22:00:15-07:00","id":231021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=230962#post230962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a good question. Not one I can answer right now because first drafts aren't due until mid-September. But oh, yes, there will be playtests.<br /> <br /> Straight talk: I <i>love</i> crossover. I have a Hunter/Mage game I visit periodically, I had a mage PC in my Changeling game for a while, and I use one character type as antagonists or contacts in another's games like mad. <b>Beast</b> is flat-out designed to allow and encourage crossover.<br /> <br /> Because to a Beast, the vampire is a sibling. Or at least a cousin.<br /> <br /> (Does that mean they're buddy-buddy? Let me put it this way: Do <i>you</i> get along with all your cousins?)</div> </div> </div> </div>is there any way we can sign up for playtests?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T22:31:55-07:00","id":231041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"