itle":"","content":"Demons have us dealing with Inferno demons, goetic demons (as well as the demons of Pandemonium), and Descent demons. Angels are just as bad: <i>qashmallim</i>, God-Machine angels, Aether angels, and Empyrean angels.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, will we ever see anything about Empyrean angels outside of one lonely page in <i>Inferno</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:17:41-07:00","id":231082,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231075#post231075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons have us dealing with Inferno demons, goetic demons (as well as the demons of Pandemonium), and Descent demons. Angels are just as bad: <i>qashmallim</i>, God-Machine angels, Aether angels, and Empyrean angels.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, will we ever see anything about Empyrean angels outside of one lonely page in <i>Inferno</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>God-Machine angels, the Qashmallim and the Empyrean are all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">In the manner they are not. Not even remotely the same.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:28:23-07:00","id":231094,"title":"","content":"I see what you did there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:29:09-07:00","id":231095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231082#post231082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God-Machine angels, the Qashmallim and the Empyrean are all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">In the manner they are not. Not even remotely the same.</span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You very nearly got a few paragraphs of impotent nerd rage out of me. This is coming from someone who thought D:tD was going to be a game about renegade qashmallim until one of the writers explicitly told me no; it's a touchy subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:37:52-07:00","id":231103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231044#post231044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover is messy and doesn't cleave well to the themes.</div> </div> </div> </div> This, so much of this. I can't stand cross over I ban it in all of the games I run and refuse anything that isn't published in respective material for that specific line. So I really hope Beast has enough content to keep the line pure otherwise it may just end up as a pretty trophy for the rest of my collection.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:38:30-07:00","id":231104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231094#post231094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you did there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I blame the letter S for being so demonic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:39:14-07:00","id":231105,"title":"","content":"Is it the following trailer or a rehashing of Werewolf the Forsaken?<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lM1o1xe5FGE\" data-code=\"lM1o1xe5FGE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lM1o1xe5FGE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:50:07-07:00","id":231110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231103#post231103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This, so much of this. I can't stand cross over I ban it in all of the games I run and refuse anything that isn't published in respective material for that specific line. So I really hope Beast has enough content to keep the line pure otherwise it may just end up as a pretty trophy for the rest of my collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think about that for a second. Would it make any financial sense to produce an entire gameline that was unplayable on its own and needed entire other game lines to work? I don't pretend to know much about business, but if I was a CCP executive, I would not approve that pitch. I'm guessing it will be built to easily facilitate crossover, but still be fully enjoyable standalone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-17-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:59:21-07:00","id":231131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231110#post231110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think about that for a second. Would it make any financial sense to produce an entire gameline that was unplayable on its own and needed entire other game lines to work? I don't pretend to know much about business, but if I was a CCP executive, I would not approve that pitch. I'm guessing it will be built to easily facilitate crossover, but still be fully enjoyable standalone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, but contrast with canon crossover-focused material in other games; usually a sidebar in this or that supplement, or maybe one weird group (a Legacy, a Bloodline, an Entitlement) for dealing with other splats. Having crossover be a central thing in the corebook is new and scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:05:38-07:00","id":231135,"title":"","content":"I'd be pretty shocked if it went beyond &quot;this is crossover friendly! here's how and why that works so well!&quot; in to &quot;You shouldn't be running Beast games. You should be running games with one or two Beasts in them.&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> I certainly understand people having bad experiences with Old World cross-over (because, you know. . .they were different systems, where pretty much each splat/genre took place in an alternate universe from one another), having that impact how you feel about New World cross-over is silly. I honestly can't even imagine playing New World without cross-over. There's, like. . .double-infinite stuff going on there, it's amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:17:42-07:00","id":231155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231135#post231135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be pretty shocked if it went beyond &quot;this is crossover friendly! here's how and why that works so well!&quot; in to &quot;You shouldn't be running Beast games. You should be running games with one or two Beasts in them.&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> I certainly understand people having bad experiences with Old World cross-over (because, you know. . .they were different systems, where pretty much each splat/genre took place in an alternate universe from one another), having that impact how you feel about New World cross-over is silly. I honestly can't even imagine playing New World without cross-over. There's, like. . .double-infinite stuff going on there, it's amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the themes get hella muddled in crossover games? If I'm running, say, a straight Werewolf game, then I know that I'm dealing with themes of duty, shame, and being a creature of two worlds who belongs in neither. If I'm running a Changeling game, I know that I'm dealing with an extended abuse survivor metaphor, and essentially running a story about picking up the pieces and building a new life.<br /> <br /> But if I have Werewolf <i>and </i>Changelings running around, what does the focus become? Almost invariably, crossover games seem to end up as more &quot;we're all magical dudes doing things together!&quot; and less potent, emotional tales with a strong thematic frame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:22:34-07:00","id":231157,"title":"","content":"Sure, I understand the pros/cons of having a single-splat game. I might have misphrased a sentence in there; it's not that I can't imagine ever playing a single game of nWoD without using multiple splats (since I do that on the regular), I just can't wrap my head around the idea of <i>never</i> having a nWoD game with multiple splats. Though, mostly, the draw of single-splat games is the lack of rules-splosion and whenever a game is going to hyper-focus on something splat-specific (the Hedge, for instance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:48:27-07:00","id":231178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231155#post231155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I have Werewolf <i>and </i>Changelings running around, what does the focus become? Almost invariably, crossover games seem to end up as more &quot;we're all magical dudes doing things together!&quot; and less potent, emotional tales with a strong thematic frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>The focus becomes trying to survive in a world which is trying to rip your head off. Personal stories of trying to stay alive because changeling A managed to coax a bane out of the the local Fire-Touched via a favor from a spring courtier in an effort to get them to stop trying to burn down the house that he and the Uratha pack live in while trying to keep a steady relationship with said pack because he saw them take down a spirit and figures that wolfy meatwalls are the best thing keeping him from being dragged back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> In short, you need to run such games as <b>Being Human</b> and add personal reasons on why the player characters are sticking together in an insane world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:02:57-07:00","id":231181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231155#post231155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the themes get hella muddled in crossover games? If I'm running, say, a straight Werewolf game, then I know that I'm dealing with themes of duty, shame, and being a creature of two worlds who belongs in neither. If I'm running a Changeling game, I know that I'm dealing with an extended abuse survivor metaphor, and essentially running a story about picking up the pieces and building a new life.<br /> <br /> But if I have Werewolf <i>and </i>Changelings running around, what does the focus become? Almost invariably, crossover games seem to end up as more &quot;we're all magical dudes doing things together!&quot; and less potent, emotional tales with a strong thematic frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you in principle - I think crossover can work great if you have a strong majority of one splat and make it explicit that you're going by said splat's themes. I have good memories of a Mage player in a Genius game I played.<br /> <br /> Basically; I'm not the biggest crossover fan but going to give Matt the benefit of the doubt here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:20:36-07:00","id":231193,"title":"","content":"Questions/concerns/thoughts:<br /> Where's the human element? The thing that I like best about the WoD games is that every single of them is in some way an exploration of the human condition, whether it's in the context of childhood or old age or death or survivors of abuse, etc.. What does Beast have to offer?<br /> <br /> I don't want Beast to be too similar, thematically, to other WoD games, particularly Werewolf. I already have that game, and it's a great game.<br /> <br /> Will there be a draconic family? Can I play a Lindwurm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:31:44-07:00","id":231200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231193#post231193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions/concerns/thoughts:<br /> Where's the human element? The thing that I like best about the WoD games is that every single of them is in some way an exploration of the human condition, whether it's in the context of childhood or old age or death or survivors of abuse, etc.. What does Beast have to offer?<br /> <br /> I don't want Beast to be too similar, thematically, to other WoD games, particularly Werewolf. I already have that game, and it's a great game.<br /> <br /> Will there be a draconic family? Can I play a Lindwurm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope Beast measures up to my earlier guesses; a game about slowly becoming a monster in play, rather than a binary change (Embrace/Awakening) or starting off as not human (Promethean, Mummy). Actually, that's my big question that I hope to see a dev answer:<br /> <br /> <b>Do Beasts start off as humans and then go through a sort of First Change, do they begin their lives as Beasts, or do they slowly become Beasts?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:38:47-07:00","id":231202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231178#post231178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The focus becomes trying to survive in a world which is trying to rip your head off. Personal stories of trying to stay alive because changeling A managed to coax a bane out of the the local Fire-Touched via a favor from a spring courtier in an effort to get them to stop trying to burn down the house that he and the Uratha pack live in while trying to keep a steady relationship with said pack because he saw them take down a spirit and figures that wolfy meatwalls are the best thing keeping him from being dragged back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> In short, you need to run such games as <b>Being Human</b> and add personal reasons on why the player characters are sticking together in an insane world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, pretty much. There are exceptionally few themes that can't work across splats. And even then, what themes aren't directly aplicable can be tweaked, or even just understood, but other splats. Sure, Changelings are in a somewhat unique position, but it's pretty similar to a newly-embraced Vampire that's had to run away from from this ancient Elder that's had him embraced for some weird reason. And so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:43:36-07:00","id":231204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231155#post231155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the themes get hella muddled in crossover games? If I'm running, say, a straight Werewolf game, then I know that I'm dealing with themes of duty, shame, and being a creature of two worlds who belongs in neither. If I'm running a Changeling game, I know that I'm dealing with an extended abuse survivor metaphor, and essentially running a story about picking up the pieces and building a new life.<br /> <br /> But if I have Werewolf <i>and </i>Changelings running around, what does the focus become? Almost invariably, crossover games seem to end up as more &quot;we're all magical dudes doing things together!&quot; and less potent, emotional tales with a strong thematic frame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or the contrast between them helps solidfy the differences making the themes of both clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:48:13-07:00","id":231206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231200#post231200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hope Beast measures up to my earlier guesses; a game about slowly becoming a monster in play, rather than a binary change (Embrace/Awakening) or starting off as not human (Promethean, Mummy). Actually, that's my big question that I hope to see a dev answer:<br /> <br /> <b>Do Beasts start off as humans and then go through a sort of First Change, do they begin their lives as Beasts, or do they slowly become Beasts?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As a guess; like Werewolves. They're born Beasts, but they don't know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T02:27:06-07:00","id":231216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231206#post231206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a guess; like Werewolves. They're born Beasts, but they don't know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I count Werewolves as a binary change; they're human, they have on crazy night, then they're a Werewolf. I know it's not <i>quite</i> true in that they were a Werewolf long before their First Change, but for narrative purposes it's kind of an instant switch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:13:28-07:00","id":231254,"title":"","content":"I'm getting gradually more excited. If they are related to vampires, then does that mean they get wassail? Can anyone become a beast? Is there a transformation mechanic? Will there be an improved haven merit, that I don't despise? SO MANY QUESTION.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T05:13:11-07:00","id":231330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231103#post231103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This, so much of this. I can't stand cross over I ban it in all of the games I run and refuse anything that isn't published in respective material for that specific line. So I really hope Beast has enough content to keep the line pure otherwise it may just end up as a pretty trophy for the rest of my collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a ST I once had started to like introduce Mages into a vampire game we had, it ruined the entire feel of it, imo. It just gets a bit too supernatural-y for me when there's a lot of different splats going on. With that being said, I do intend to have some changeling stuff in a vamp campaign I'll be running, but only as a backdrop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T06:06:09-07:00","id":231380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231200#post231200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Do Beasts start off as humans and then go through a sort of First Change, do they begin their lives as Beasts, or do they slowly become Beasts?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping it's a mixture of three lines; Werewolf, Scion, and Mage.<br /> The challenges in the age of heroes were focused much on killing monsters. The monsters were the big bad evil creatures preying on humans.<br /> But what if they weren't? The Minotaur didn't ask to be born. And Medusa's &quot;crime&quot; was that she was raped by Poseidon in Athena's temple, so Athena transforms her into a monster? (According to the Greeks this was justice.) And Fenris had a prophecy going against him, but it seems to me his greatest crime was being so big and strong that he could threaten the gods themselves if he so desired to.<br /> We see the beasts in each of them. Now bring that idea to the here and now, into the World of Darkness.<br /> /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:19:05-07:00","id":231483,"title":"","content":"From the info presented in this thread, I have a thought on how the game might be considered subversive. All the other games focus on humanity with a theme related to humanity; holding on to it, acquiring it, reacquiring it, etc. The games may tend towards players losing humanity, but there is always a struggle. This game sounds more like the players might not start out human. If they do then they must be geared towards discarding humanity. There are elements to most games with characters that lose humanity but they are designed to be &quot;bad guys.&quot; Perhaps in this case, the characters discard humanity to replace it with bestial aspects. They try to become monsters, but not the insane, evil creatures in the other games. These guys are more like sharks, large cats, wolves and all the other animals that people are irrationally afraid of. A shark doesn't bite you because it has malice. It bites you because it is hungry, and on instinct, when you came in only to start thrashing in his territory. The shark isn't evil. The victim of the shark bite might not be evil. The mob that starts killing all the local sharks so they can &quot;feel safe&quot; are the evil ones. The Heroes are antagonists. They aren't Hunters, but hunters. People looking for trophies, basically. A Beast could be evil, or dangerous, or simply trying to hide from the most dangerous predator in the real world, humans. Humans aren't the strongest or fiercest, but they are still the most dangerous. No other creature will purposely destroy it's own home permanently just to win a challenge. Humans aren't prey, they are the monsters. A Beast is just trying to survive in a world filled with monsters. They take the place humans have in all the other books. Sounds subversive to me. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:53:14-07:00","id":231503,"title":"","content":"So it is a rehash of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:59:56-07:00","id":231511,"title":"","content":"I'm utterly flabbergasted as to why people keep saying it's a rehash of Werewolf. With an understanding that we know very little, how on earth does this sound anything like being half-spirit, half-flesh creatures which engage in a holy hunt to protect the worlds of Flesh and Spirit from one another? Is it themes of alienation (read: they are in all of the World of Darkness games) and alleged (I say alleged because they have said <i>nothing </i>on the matter) animal features? How much more reductive could you possibly get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T08:10:28-07:00","id":231516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231511#post231511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm utterly flabbergasted as to why people keep saying it's a rehash of Werewolf. With an understanding that we know very little, how on earth does this sound anything like being half-spirit, half-flesh creatures which engage in a holy hunt to protect the worlds of Flesh and Spirit from one another? Is it themes of alienation (read: they are in all of the World of Darkness games) and alleged (I say alleged because they have said <i>nothing </i>on the matter) animal features? How much more reductive could you possibly get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to fandom!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T08:50:25-07:00","id":231541,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem any more a rehash of Werewolf than Werewolf is a rehash of Vampire. I'm certain there is more to the game than it is built for crossovers and subversive. I was speculating on a single element of the game. If you look at them at the right angle all the games are the same. I actually did that in my earlier post. The games share some similarities, as intended. They are meant to each be unique and I'm sure that is the intention of Beast. If you want to over-simply, I would say it is the game you would have if you took the most inhuman antagonists of all the previous game lines and played them. That might be a better description than a rehash of so-and-so. It would still be a grossly over-simplified description. Wait until you actually get some info before you jump to such conclusions as it is a rehash of something else, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T08:51:23-07:00","id":231544,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No other official word other than the synopsis.</li> <li>You playing a human that transforms into some sort of creature, more likely animal.</li> <li>This one is more regional thing that I experienced (and a couple of major websites); everybody preferring Vampire over Werewolf.</li> <li>No answer to my previous question. Is it like Creature from the Black Lagoon or a rehash of Werewolf the Forsaken?</li> <li>If it is like Creature from the Black Lagoon, why focus on humanity?</li> <li>If it is a Werewolf rehash, why repackage something that is already good?</li> </ol><br /> Don't get me wrong. I'm a fan of Werewolf. 1/3 of my WoD collection is both versions of Werewolf. But from the synopsis and the title to me suggests Creature from the Black Lagoon. Which would be awesome if you being a Creature (of any sort) trying to survive in a world were your domain is being invaded by urban expansion or those scientists trying to find a new species. However, having humanity as a focus of the game; it's just out of nowhere to the point that it feels like Werewolf. Promethean had the theme of the monster trying to understand humanity nailed; Vampire's version of humanity was always optional, you can still be the monster just either delve into being the monster or ask forgiveness for killing your juice pack. Promethean knows how to get into the mind of the monster, what makes those people human, why humans do what they do, why some humans live together while others isolate themselves, how do relationships, etc, etc. If their focusing the scene where the Creature kidnaps the lady because he wanted her as a mate, that's more of a matter of biology rather than humanity. The Creature wasn't attracted to her because she was the daughter of the scientist of the expedition, smart, and resourceful. The Creature was attracted to her because she was the best swimmer of the entire expedition (she never used the scuba gear when she swam), not to mention she was psychically attractive (which most animals go for because that meant the best genes for their offspring), to the Creature she was the best choice for his offspring. Although she was the only woman on the expedition, if you remember the captain's story about the Lagoon, the native population feared the Lagoon so the Creature couldn't determine who would be a good mate from the local populace and the Creature have evolved to the point to where he wouldn't be compatible to the fish population either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:09:15-07:00","id":231579,"title":"","content":"I've enough faith in Onyx Path (and CCP, for that matter) to assume they aren't going to announce a game that's a rehash of a gameline they're in the middle of rereleasing, all of which is taking place in the same edition.<br /> <br /> Most of your questions seem to naturally lead to positive answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:10:46-07:00","id":231581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No other official word other than the synopsis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, so speculating as to whether it's like Werewolf is useless. We know nothing and they've said nothing to suggest that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You playing a human that transforms into some sort of creature, more likely animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess Skinchangers, Thyrsus Mages, Changing Breeds and Gangrel Vampires should all go home, then. Since, if this is what we're using to define Werewolf, they are all Werewolf too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is more regional thing that I experienced (and a couple of major websites); everybody preferring Vampire over Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. What does this have to do with Beast?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No answer to my previous question. Is it like Creature from the Black Lagoon or a rehash of Werewolf the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>To your first question, we don't know.<br /> <br /> To your second question, we do know that it isn't a rehash of Werewolf. It wouldn't exist if it was a rehash of werewolf. Moreover, since you're a fan of Werewolf, I'm certain you know enough to know that this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onyx Path 2015 Schedule</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Beast: The Primordial</b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Within every one of us lies the potential of the Beast. Unleash savage powers, answer the call to your Lair, and become the thing that Heroes fear. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds <i>nothing </i>like Werewolf. We could dissect why, from the utter absence of any mention of spirits or being half-spirit, or perhaps because the potential of the Beast &quot;lies in every one of us&quot; or the focus on fighting Heroes or the utter absence of the word &quot;Hunt.&quot; This is just the start, and as they continue to post more spoilers (For instance, they spoiled a rough version of their Integrity Stat, which is only somewhat similar to Harmony in the sense that you go back and forth between two extremes, though it's better to be one or the other <i>instead </i>of in the middle like Harmony.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is like Creature from the Black Lagoon, why focus on humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because humanity is interesting and fundamentally necessary for these story games in the World of Darkness. As you'll notice, humanity, your relationship with humanity and how it makes you feel are pretty essential to every game line in one form or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231544#post231544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a Werewolf rehash, why repackage something that is already good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we wouldn't be getting Beast the Primordial and we'd instead have a different pitch entirely. They're working on a Werewolf 2nd edition, why on earth would they make a game that's a rehash at the same time?<br /> <br /> It's lazy thinking and it also assumes the incompetence of the Developer Team.<br /> <br /> Now, I can understand people making comparisons to Vampire based on what we've heard so far (though I think I'd die if they were doing it just because the game is called Beast and vampires have The Beast) because some of the spoilers (namely their Integrity Stat) are reminiscient of the Vampire template, but it's really too soon to tell, and given the Crossover friendly nature of things, it's likely they have some experiences in common anyway, which would be the game working as advertised (i.e., as a crossover friendly game)<br /> <br /> On top of all that, Matt or David A. Hill (Can't remember which!) already explicitly discussed the potential kinship of Vampires and Beasts (I believe they even used the word &quot;brothers&quot; but I think that was more experiential) so if we're gonna uselessly speculate about their relationship with any splat, it'd probably be Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:30:30-07:00","id":231590,"title":"","content":"I'm actually pleased we're getting a game that has a solid consideration of crossover, and certainly hope its more Deep One, Creature from the Black Lagoon, Dragony than others, though I wouldn't be unhappy with a Jekyll/Hyde type game either.<br /> <br /> I run primarily crossover games even though right now I'm running vampire, I don't get hung up on themes of an individual splat, but rather focus on the themes of a particular chronicle, regardless of if its a mixed game or single. In a mixed game I'm playing in (a rare thing for me to actually get to play), the main themes are the different groups struggling to work together as they've formed a supernatural government of sorts. You have resistance groups from each group, and its been quite fun. Currently we're dealing with some dissident changelings.<br /> <br /> Another game I ran was a werewolf, sin-eater, and a vampire in a small Louisianna town where residents were going missing. Didn't deal with vampire politics, didn't particularly deal with ghosts, didn't deal with spirits, but each was able to leverage those things towards finding the missing people and working to stop what was happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:35:41-07:00","id":231596,"title":"","content":"I prefer to consider many Beasts as hunters. (as opposed to those Beasts that aren't, such as bulls)<br /> I prefer to think of Vampires as the parasites they are, and incompatible, unless they are viewed as prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:42:20-07:00","id":231601,"title":"","content":"Vampires and Primordial Beasts being brothers is where I would call them idiots (cause when I say Creature from the Black Lagoon I mean Count Dracula). The Beast that Vampires have is and always have been metaphorical, that moment of weak will where you lose control and paint the room with gore. With Beast I'm hoping that it'll be a throwback or devolution, not the symbiont from Stargate. Your not gaining or learning about humanity, your losing it. Your going into the more primitive parts of your mind. For example; you need to feed, there is no small prey in this small stretch of land, not much cover, even the ponds are fruitless, but wait there is prey, walking around on the stone, very noisy, not very worried about the lack of cover, their not thirsty when they visit the ponds, their scent suggests that they are mates, they will make a fine meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:55:54-07:00","id":231615,"title":"","content":"The sooner we get more spoilers to quiet the rampant speculation, the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:56:10-07:00","id":231616,"title":"","content":"Matt said Beasts refer (or may refer) to Vampires as being, effectively, cousins. <br /> <br /> And no, the Beast isn't a metaphor for Vampires. It is an actual thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:10:02-07:00","id":231626,"title":"","content":"No. The Beast in a vampire isn't and a simple label doesn't change that.<br /> It's a demonic entity that requires blood. That's how it is to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:46:21-07:00","id":231679,"title":"","content":"Then this should be a sidebook for Vampire on the same level as Ghouls. Or call it Beast: the Vampire Symbiot. The reason why I find the Vampire's Beast as a metaphor is that not only it has always written up as a metaphor, Vampires know that the Beast is themselves but instead of admitting it they distance themselves from what makes them the blood thirsty monster as they are, which gives them a way to write off any bad deeds they done when they lose control and ask for forgiveness (depending on the Vampire). If a Vampire looks on a Beast and imagines his own Beast like the throwback that it is, that would make sense cause the Vampire will see that its not like this Primordial in front of him (add in melodramatic tone). But the Beast being blood relation to Vampire, it'll be the equivalent of coelacanths, nautilus, and other living fossils. The Beasts would have the same weakness as Vampires, both in general and specific clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:51:22-07:00","id":231706,"title":"","content":"Forget that a Vampire's beast and a Primordial Beast share the same name. We know next to nothing about Beast so far, but one thing we can be absolutely certain of is that it is completely its own game line, independent from Vampire. Yes, there was a mention that they see vampires as cousins. There was also a mention that they see ALL monsters as family. Don't read so much into it, at least not yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:56:27-07:00","id":231710,"title":"","content":"I think vampires live in denial. (<i>It's not a demon, it's a beast...</i>)That sounds so much nicer.<br /> A demon that can also hunt doesn't change what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:05:54-07:00","id":231716,"title":"","content":"Never had a problem with both having the same name. Cause like I've said, I'm hoping something along the lines of Creature from the Black Lagoon. A living fossil essentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:22:29-07:00","id":231750,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, you DO realize that Beasts considering Vampires cousins A) doesn't mean they think they are literally related, B) might just consider ALL supernatural human-hunters as part of an extended family, either because they really enjoy that hobby or, because of an extremely diversified nature, have a harder time drawing hard lines when it comes to splats (I.e. &quot;well, I can change shape and live away from people but eat people, and they do too but they're kinda deadish and are allergic to the sun, which is weird, but whatever. Jim over there can't eat non-fresh meat and he's alright).<br /> <br /> You seem to be running in to this problem where you're taking the bare minimum information (which is all that is available) and extrapolating pretty wildly, and THEN deciding that those wild extrapolations are basically facts and this game sounds dumb.<br /> <br /> Also there's a huge false dichotomy going on with this &quot;It's either rehashed werewolf or its Creature from the Black Lagoon&quot;. There's a lot of possibilities to this game, don't trap yourself between two radically different options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:22:36-07:00","id":231751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231706#post231706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget that a Vampire's beast and a Primordial Beast share the same name. We know next to nothing about Beast so far, but one thing we can be absolutely certain of is that it is completely its own game line, independent from Vampire. Yes, there was a mention that they see vampires as cousins. There was also a mention that they see ALL monsters as family. Don't read so much into it, at least not yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really think this is worth stressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:35:44-07:00","id":231791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231751#post231751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really think this is worth stressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really thought this should have been blatantly apparent, if we're honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:36:32-07:00","id":231793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231750#post231750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there's a huge false dichotomy going on with this &quot;It's either rehashed werewolf or its Creature from the Black Lagoon&quot;. There's a lot of possibilities to this game, don't trap yourself between two radically different options.</div> </div> </div> </div>What else would you think going through the roll-a-dex of horror? Especially with that title. All the major mythological archtypes are covered. Mad Scientists you could use the Mage template and remix it to science (since magic and science is one and the same). With the focus on humanity can't help but suspect a Werewolf rehash, and why I keep referring to Creature from the Black Lagoon is what the Creature is this. A ithyotic humanoid from the time species was transitioning from sea to land, a throwback to what evolution created now like a lot of living fossils, something <u>Primordial</u>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:37:04-07:00","id":231797,"title":"","content":"It really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T12:22:28-07:00","id":231860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231793#post231793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What else would you think going through the roll-a-dex of horror? Especially with that title. All the major mythological archtypes are covered. Mad Scientists you could use the Mage template and remix it to science (since magic and science is one and the same). With the focus on humanity can't help but suspect a Werewolf rehash, and why I keep referring to Creature from the Black Lagoon is what the Creature is this. A ithyotic humanoid from the time species was transitioning from sea to land, a throwback to what evolution created now like a lot of living fossils, something <u>Primordial</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really insist on making wild speculations based on almost no information, you could assume that CftBL is one of the X-splats, but I don't think there's really enough to Swamp Thing on its own to make a full game out of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: come to think of it, a game where the x-splats were different sorts of cryptids, framed as evolutionary relics or throwbacks could be pretty sweet. You've got Piscean (CftBL), Mamalian (Sasquatch, Wendigo, Yeti, etc.), Avian (Moth Man), maybe add in a lizard man... It's a pretty cool idea. I don't think we have enough evidence to suspect that's what Beast will be, by a long way, but it's still an interesting concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-17-2014, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:44:05-07:00","id":231926,"title":"","content":"If we're going to condemn the name because the &quot;Beast&quot; name is used for something unrelated, then we're in a lot more trouble than we think; look at the four or five wholly unrelated things nWoD calls Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:53:10-07:00","id":231934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231926#post231926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're going to condemn the name because the &quot;Beast&quot; name is used for something unrelated, then we're in a lot more trouble than we think; look at the four or five wholly unrelated things nWoD calls Angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling Arcadia vs Mage Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:55:48-07:00","id":231935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231934#post231934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling Arcadia vs Mage Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>DEAR GOD IN HEAVEN, Changeling Arcadia Vs. Mage Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I can see people wanting to complain that Beast sounds fangame-y(I said that to some people when I first heard it), but WoD Fans should be used to name sharing five times over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-17-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:01:41-07:00","id":231938,"title":"","content":"Not to mention Demons! Also, my last post had some weird delay issue, so oops.<br /> <br /> And what do I think? I think that there are a lot of things that can be done with this game, and I wont be able to guess at them all. Like Charlaquin said, there's not really enough to Creature to warrant an entire game line. I could see something like that as a sort of back-of-the-book antagonist with a &quot;how to play one&quot; page in some Hunter book, though. <br /> <br /> I could, however, see something like Leviathan. Or even just something not really covered in standard mainstream mythology, just some weird mutation thing going on. Or you'll be The Fly. Or its a new take on Ferals with a deeper sense of horror. <br /> <br /> But if I were to bet on anything, it'd be shapeshifting. They'll need a way to run around in public, otherwise crossover isn't going to go well at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:32:54-07:00","id":231959,"title":"","content":"&quot;You play the monster&quot; isn't subversive in WoD; it's sort of the whole point. Maybe the crossover-friendliness is, in light of previous design, but even that has groundwork laid, in Supernatural Tolerance or whatever it's called these days.<br /> <br /> For better or worse, I think all the Beauty and the Beast references say more about what we'll see than CftBL. Actually, what I'm picturing is the demonic underworld from Buffy and Angel. Beasts are the one-offs, and the extras you see in Lorne's bar, the special monsters that don't pose a threat until you see what they really are and really do. They hang with the vampires and werewolves, because that's who the hunters will go after first, these known quantities. <br /> <br /> I'd like to hear Matt's pitch, though. We've got the lonely, cursed beasts down with Vampire and Promethean, primordial monsters with Werewolf, and mythic, cyclopean potential in Changeling and Mage. What do Beasts bring to the table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:47:18-07:00","id":231973,"title":"","content":"I speculate that Beasts consider other supernaturals as cousins because Beast The Primordial might reveal some fundamental truth about the World of Darkness and how the supernatural works on the whole. Just like Demon and GMC told us about Embeds and &quot;some people use shortcuts in reality to perform superhuman feats but they don't know it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:57:47-07:00","id":231997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231935#post231935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DEAR GOD IN HEAVEN, Changeling Arcadia Vs. Mage Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I can see people wanting to complain that Beast sounds fangame-y(I said that to some people when I first heard it), but WoD Fans should be used to name sharing five times over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One could say that it sounds &quot;fangamey&quot;, but to me it sounds more like a little too bland.<br /> I kinda hope that beast is not the final title. Primordial sounds awesome though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:28:17-07:00","id":232017,"title":"","content":"Primordial: The Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:10:01-07:00","id":232055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231973#post231973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I speculate that Beasts consider other supernaturals as cousins because Beast The Primordial might reveal some fundamental truth about the World of Darkness and how the supernatural works on the whole. Just like Demon and GMC told us about Embeds and &quot;some people use shortcuts in reality to perform superhuman feats but they don't know it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that's what Embeds are, but does it say that for other things that are doing the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:49:03-07:00","id":232084,"title":"","content":"Rereading War and the Changing Breeds Pures? Hyde? Creature from the Black Lagoon? Grendel? Mythological monsters (Medusa, Minotaur)? Swamp Thing? <br /> <br /> The Archetype can be connected to another Rider War not need to possess and consume but to reform and change, destroy and survive. It will be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:56:17-07:00","id":232095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232055#post232055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that's what Embeds are, but does it say that for other things that are doing the same thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, unless that's what you want it to mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:58:23-07:00","id":232099,"title":"","content":"Wow what is going on in this thread?<br /> <br /> The only argument against the game you could make is that, by the very nature of making more game-lines, some of the games will have some blurred or overlapping themes. They did from day one, though, between a Vampire's Beast and Werewolf's bestial raging, or Hunters hunting and Werewolves Hunting. I don't think it's going to be much of an issue here because we don't really know much about the game's themes yet. The Vampires-as-cousins analogy was made in a similar vein that an Idigam Chronicle writer/developer made about how Vampires and Werewolves both hunt but for different reasons and with different prey.<br /> <br /> We know more about the mechanics than any in-depth themes. Heroes are called, Hunger morality where extremes are good and fluctuate in a single game session, PC groups are broods and might see other supernaturals as brood-mates, something about a Lair (which is what Promethean's safe place merit is called oh no!).<br /> <br /> Let's just be excited about the game-line and not worry until we know there's something to be worried about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T17:00:54-07:00","id":232102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232099#post232099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just be excited about the game-line and not worry until we know there's something to be worried about</div> </div> </div> </div>Less the WW/OP Gods be angered and we suffer another four year famine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T17:08:22-07:00","id":232113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232102#post232102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less the WW/OP Gods be angered and we suffer another four year famine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To my immense disappointment, I initially misread this as &quot;four year fanime&quot; and wondered what I missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https