message\">Ok, bit of a tangent here, but this got me wondering, &quot;Has anyone ever played one of these games in an anime style?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. We've had someone ask about it with regards to vampire in particular in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:42:13-07:00","id":232181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232176#post232176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Princess would be the next line that OP would go after :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out the Beast-slaying Heroes are magical girls!<br /> <br /> And the fandom rejoiced!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:47:28-07:00","id":232182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232181#post232181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turns out the Beast-slaying Heroes are magical girls!<br /> <br /> And the fandom rejoiced!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can already smell the cheetos dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:49:50-07:00","id":232183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232168#post232168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial: Wrath of the Id?<br /> Primordial: the Beast Within?<br /> <br /> Even just Primordial: the Beast would be okay. I think using Beast as the lead word is what's turning people away.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm on the same page. I don't really like Beast as a name, but hey. Maybe once we know more, Primordial won't make sense as the primary name.<br /> <br /> I have faith in Onyx Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T18:58:37-07:00","id":232188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232172#post232172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, bit of a tangent here, but this got me wondering, &quot;Has anyone ever played one of these games in an anime style?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, a whole tangent unrelated here, but this has been bugging me ever since I finished BESM ages ago, and was resurfaced with OVA.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, do we think anime style is within roleplaying games?<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously. On an initial surface, thinking in terms of anime means thinking in terms in animation styles, which...isn't really applicable to RPG's, but it get worse than that, because the idea of anime is actually so broad what we're really talking about is a &quot;the ideas, perspective, and procedure of a niche portion of the Japanese culture as shown through animation&quot;(on the fly, that defintion). And that's <i>just </i>assuming anime is a strict Japanese things, which with Korean and Chinese and even American productions being grouped under the umbrella(even if American stuff is hotly debated) becomes even more muddled. How does that create the groundwork for a tabletop, pen and paper role-playing game?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I don't want to be the asshole who goes around muddling a semi-pointless issue from a consumer standpoint(although I am apparently willing to be the asshole who jumps the conversation off the rails into a completely unrelated direction)-but when you start running a game in the anime style, you're the producer, and as such you might need to think a little bit about it, and it perplexes me.<br /> <br /> The main reason I bring this up is that games that try and appeal to <i>all anime</i> end up as just generic games, the only difference from GURPS being that I at least like it. I think it's possible to do games within the realms of Japanese comedy as seen in anime(Maid RPG, Teeenagers From Outer Space,etc.), or the mecha genre as seen in anime(Apotheosis Drive X is Western enough I shouldn't call it an anime-run game, but it's a really awesome setting, so I'm pimping it anyways, although Princess Drive gets closer to the mark and is even more awesome). I've seen the style of Miyazaki translated well into roleplaying games at least three times(Golden Sky Stories, Whispering Road, and Witch Quest[might have the name wrong] for <i>Kiki's Delivery Service</i>). I know other genres that are more distinctly Japanese in style and origin have good representation.<br /> <br /> Slowly getting back to the point, you say World of Darkness run in the anime style, and I can see it in my head-things like <i>Darker than Black, Gungrave/Hellsing/Ga Rei Zero</i>(I'm camping them together lazily, shut up), <i>xxxHolic </i>and <i>Kobato</i>(that last one's a little light), <i>Baccano!, Haibane Renmei, Serial Experiments Lain, Revolutionary Girl Utena, Madoka Magica, Fate/Zero, </i>and, even though it's not (psuedo-)supernatural in the slightest, <i>Cowboy Bebop-</i> but I'm not sure what exactly I'd have to do to run those sorts of stories in RPG form and still make them feel anime-esque beyond using my own understanding of Japanese perspective on the entire spliel and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> Anyways, all of this is irrelevant to the elephant in the room. Back to Beast the Primordial and its' proud anti-Hunter declarations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-17-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:18:03-07:00","id":232197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232188#post232188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, a whole tangent unrelated here, but this has been bugging me ever since I finished BESM ages ago, and was resurfaced with OVA.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, do we think anime style is within roleplaying games?<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously. On an initial surface, thinking in terms of anime means thinking in terms in animation styles, which...isn't really applicable to RPG's, but it get worse than that, because the idea of anime is actually so broad what we're really talking about is a &quot;the ideas, perspective, and procedure of a niche portion of the Japanese culture as shown through animation&quot;(on the fly, that defintion). And that's <i>just </i>assuming anime is a strict Japanese things, which with Korean and Chinese and even American productions being grouped under the umbrella(even if American stuff is hotly debated) becomes even more muddled.<br /> <br /> Snip<br /> <br /> Slowly getting back to the point, you say World of Darkness run in the anime style, and I can see it in my head-things like <i>Darker than Black, Gungrave/Hellsing/Ga Rei Zero</i>(I'm camping them together lazily, shut up), <i>xxxHolic </i>and <i>Kobato</i>(that last one's a little light), <i>Baccano!, Haibane Renmei, Serial Experiments Lain, Madoka Magica, Fate/Zero, </i>and, even though it's not (psuedo-)supernatural in the slightest, <i>Cowboy Bebop</i>, but I'm not sure what exactly I'd have to do to run those sorts of stories in RPG form and still make them feel anime-esque beyond using my own understanding of Japanese perspective the entire spliel and hope for the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't think of anime style as a formal style or anything. It's a colloquialism for the usage of tropes and ideas that are found (usually) in Japanese Anime. If you think about it, Anime has a lot of visual shorthands that people might translate into their games, or exaggerated mannerisms (I think this is the big one, though for obvious reasons <i>All Animation Does This</i>) and you'll see players who really like anime aping some of these mannerisms or incorporating elements commonly found in shounen or seinen or insert-genre-here manga/anime into their characters. These folks are those one might then say are bringing an &quot;anime style&quot; to their game. GMs might do this too. Think of the stock characters you see in a lot of Anime. Imagine someone using them in a World of Darkness game. If you're looking for the two big offenders that would lead someone to describe a game as &quot;anime style&quot; I think that stock characters, relationships and mannerisms are really where that sort of thing is evinced.<br /> <br /> While anime itself is as varied as any medium, I think people are <i>mostly </i>thinking of popular shounen stuff when they talk about things besides characterization. Namely, stuff which seems pretty high powered or involves a lot of screaming at one's enemies and the like. If people start naming their attack moves and stuff, then I think it's pretty safe to say someone might be a fan of Kamen Rider or Dragonball Z or Naruto and the like, and that they might be incorporating their fondness for it into the game.<br /> <br /> Notably, people do this stuff with genre conventions from western television and movies all the time, but I imagine that for some folks, they don't recognize that as readily as they do conventions strongly associated with anime.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's necessarily a bad thing, but I understand how it could feel a little bit weird if four of your five players made their Mages with <i>Hellblazer </i>in mind, and your fifth player just finished watching <i>Madoka </i>and wants to get their Magical Girl on. Same thing can happen with any genre, really.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apologies. Off-topic and longer than I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:18:09-07:00","id":232198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232188#post232188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, a whole tangent unrelated here, but this has been bugging me ever since I finished BESM ages ago, and was resurfaced with OVA.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, do we think anime style is within roleplaying games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anime clich\u00e9s and stereotypes? What else could it be? You'll notice Kleptomania immediately went for a school romance with gratuitous use of Japanese words.<br /> <br /> If someone described their game as &quot;American style&quot; I would assume it was a high-action game with lots of guns, using optional rules from Dudes of Legend. That, or a patriotic war story, I suppose. With lots of guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:32:11-07:00","id":232218,"title":"","content":"I'm amused that your description of American style matched perfectly(well, as perfectly as you can) what what a Chinese guy in my class described American media to be.<br /> <br /> But it's really kind of reductionist. Most of the anime I listed(not all) don't use the stereotypes and cliches normally found in Anime. Again, I can run <i>Darker than Black</i>(Chinese Electric Batman!) as a WoD game, but I'm but I'm not sure someone playing it who never saw <i>Darker than Black</i> would recognize it as anime-based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:39:54-07:00","id":232347,"title":"","content":"Back to Beast: the main reason I'm curious about if Beasts come from humans goes back to one of the dark natural conclusions of Hunter-that all monsters are effectively evolutions of sorts from humanity(Which, casually mentioning, is one of the reasons why all those conspiracies have various shades of monsters at the head of them). Beast as an anti-Hunter game(so far as we can see) seems like it might be carrying that dark conclusion as a triumphant banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> 