sts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:12:35-07:00","id":233053,"title":"","content":"Well I don't know about you cats, but I already have my first character planned with all the staggering amounts of information we have. <br /> <br /> Reckon he's gonna be a sort of Illithid sort of type of Beast. Primordial. Whatever. Insofar as he has cephalopod sort of looks and scary amounts of intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:17:47-07:00","id":233057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CodeRR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232987#post232987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555\" target=\"_blank\">http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555</a> around 36 minutes they talk about Beast</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, listening to this it makes me seem the X-splat will be human's primordial fears; so things like Darkness, Predators, Water, or things like that. Also something about Nightmares","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:42:39-07:00","id":233083,"title":"","content":"Reaper, TVTropes is unreliable as shit, so you should be careful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back to Beast: the main reason I'm curious about if Beasts come from humans goes back to one of the dark natural conclusions of Hunter-that all monsters are effectively evolutions of sorts from humanity(Which, casually mentioning, is one of the reasons why all those conspiracies have various shades of monsters at the head of them). Beast as an anti-Hunter game(so far as we can see) seems like it might be carrying that dark conclusion as a triumphant banner. </div> </div> </div>At the same time, even supernaturals that deny they are human possess traits that can be found in Humanity. Even their vices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Man is evil&quot;\u2014so said to me for consolation, all the wisest ones. Ah, if only it be still true today! For the evil is man's best force.<br /> &quot;Man must become better and eviler&quot;\u2014so do I teach. The evilest is necessary for the Superman's best.<br /> It may have been well for the preacher of the petty people to suffer and be burdened by men's sin. I, however, rejoice in great sin as my great consolation.\u2014 </div> </div> </div>This chilling excerpt from The Higher Man of Nietzsche's Zarathustra I find appropiate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 08-18-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:55:40-07:00","id":233101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=233057#post233057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, listening to this it makes me seem the X-splat will be human's primordial fears; so things like Darkness, Predators, Water, or things like that. Also something about Nightmares</div> </div> </div> </div>So people like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yao_Ming\" target=\"_blank\">Y</a>ao Ming are actually beasts of man's fear of heights....? If this is even 1/10th true I'm going to have so much fun with character creation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:01:24-07:00","id":233108,"title":"","content":"This splat looks promising anyway. As for lack of 'Heroes', I'm sure there is no need for separate splat since we have Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:39:05-07:00","id":233151,"title":"","content":"&quot;Heroes&quot; sounds to me more like a metaphorical description of the ones who end up opposing the Beasts. It might not refer to any splat or class of being with supernatural powers at all. And I don't think we really need separate splats for enemies (especially when we have rules for them), or we'd have one for Strix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=233083#post233083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, even supernaturals that deny they are human possess traits that can be found in Humanity. Even their vices.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet despite this, some supernaturals do not in fact have a Vice or Virtue, or mean different things to them than to humans. See, respectively, Vampires and Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:47:06-07:00","id":233159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet despite this, some supernaturals do not in fact have a Vice or Virtue, or mean different things to them than to humans. See, respectively, Vampires and Demons. </div> </div> </div>Mechanics vs Characterisation. If meant Vices strictly as mechanics, I would use capitalisation, YOLF,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:01:41-07:00","id":233168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CodeRR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232987#post232987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555\" target=\"_blank\">http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555</a> around 36 minutes they talk about Beast</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap is it kinda weird to listen to a seminar that I was actually at. Although since I was sitting in the back with the &quot;bad kids&quot; (as we called ourselves), I didn't hear everything Rich said, especially when the trains started running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:12:38-07:00","id":233179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=231706#post231706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there was a mention that they see vampires as cousins. There was also a mention that they see ALL monsters as family. Don't read so much into it, at least not yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANKYOU!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=232183#post232183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe once we know more, Primordial won't make sense as the primary name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder whether Primordial is more analogous to Created (the thing that distinguishes the species from other supernaturals), Forsaken (the thing that distinguishes default PC's from others of that species), or Geist (the Primordial is something inside each Beast) - or if it refers to a distant ancestor (as if Vampire the Masquerade were called Vampire the Antediluvians).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=233057#post233057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, listening to this it makes me seem the X-splat will be human's primordial fears; so things like Darkness, Predators, Water, or things like that. Also something about Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Though |'m also wondering if each X-splat will be (somewhat) parallel to a particular other critter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:25:38-07:00","id":233186,"title":"","content":"I wonder by what they mean by family is that they think they are the big older brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:10:51-07:00","id":233213,"title":"","content":"<br /> Another little tidbit from Matt McFarland at RPG.net:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I want to get away from <i>Beauty and the Beast</i> as a reference, because it's not really that applicable in tone. And I'm not ready to spoil very much about <b>Beast</b> yet, because it's still so much in flux.<br /> <br /> But! I do want to say this about Heroes.<br /> <br /> In <b>Beast</b>, &quot;Heroes&quot; are the people who are &quot;called&quot; to fight and kill Beasts. In their own stories, they'd be mighty, brave, valorous, and maybe even self-sacrificing for the greater good.<br /> <br /> This, however, is the Beast's story. So fuck those guys. They think the story is about them, but then, they <i>would</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: And some more things from the GenCon panel &quot;What's up with New World of Darkness?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;In Beast: The Primordial, you're playing a Beast. Basically you're playing one of the embodiments of the primal nightmares of humanity. So you're the Beast. Every Beast has a Hunger. You fulfill your Hungers--the Integrity analogue in Beast is called your Satiety--one of the interesting things we're doing with Beast, though, is your Satiety will fluctuate pretty wildly within a session, so don't bother bubbling in the little dots, just move the little counter.<br /> <br /> At high Satiety certain things happen, at low Satiety certain things happen. Beasts are effective in different ways basically depending on how hungry they are. At the middle is where you're kind of vulnerable. You're not hungry enough to be focused, but you're not full enough to be dangerous. But if you don't fulfill your Hunter then your soul, which is basically a primordial nightmare monster, goes romping through the dreamscape and screwing with people's lives, and nightmares. And that will eventually cause Heroes to arise, and they will eventually come and find your ass.<br /> <br /> They are not the protagonists. They think they are. The Heroes think it's all about them. And we know these guys, right? But it's not about them, it's about the Beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When I read the [...] I thought 'can you play dragons?' But as I you talk more about it, I'm thinking wendigo, and what?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So I mentioned earlier that Beasts are kind of primal fears of mankind, so if you want to make a dragon. Your character is not going to be able to turn into a dragon-dragon in the middle of Time's Square. That's kind of counter to what we're trying to do with the new World of Darkness. Now with that said, if your Beast Soul if you will wants to be a dragon, well what's scary about the Dragon that you want to bring in? Is it the fact that it's a nightmare from the sky that will just swoop down and get you? Well okay, that's this Family. Is it the thing that will just snap out and eat you in a hurry? That's that Family. As far as the Wendigo goes? I could put that into a Family and a Hunger right now. So yes, you may play a Wendigo.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:53:01-07:00","id":233289,"title":"","content":"So, not addressing every point here, because I have to go cook dinner for my gamers, but:<br /> <br /> 1) I wouldn't know an anime reference if it bit me on the face. <br /> 2) Beasts do indeed think of themselves as family to whatever supernatural creature you've got handy. <br /> 3) I know a lot of people hate crossover. <i>I</i>, however, love it, and we've gone long enough without a game that's designed to specifically encourage it. You don't want to include the other game lines, don't. It's not going to be a requirement, but crossover <i>is</i> in-theme for <b>Beast</b> (the theme in question is: &quot;You don't pick your family.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:57:11-07:00","id":233303,"title":"","content":"Hmm... embodiments of the primal nightmares of humanity?<br /> <br /> Starting to sound a bit less like Grendel, Lovecraft, dragons, and Jekyll &amp; Hyde, and more like, say, Slenderman and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Franchise/TheFearmythos\" target=\"_blank\">the Fear Mythos</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:00:01-07:00","id":233309,"title":"","content":"Will Heroes have a supernatural element at all? I'm currently picturing something between the Imbued of Hunter: the Reckoning (normal people called upon by supernatural forces to fight monsters, and granted magic powers to do so) and the Ahabs from Leviathan: the Tempest (deranged hunters who are obsessively compelled to try to destroy monsters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:21:36-07:00","id":233330,"title":"","content":"So Matt, am I right in assuming there's some level of free form design in the making Beast characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:51:08-07:00","id":233357,"title":"","content":"Dude, big shout out to <b>CodeRR</b> for the link to the nWoD Gen Con Panel Podcast.<br /> <br /> I'm even more excited now because what i'm hearing is that the Beasts will be tied to the Astral Realm/Skein similar to how Werewolves, Changelings, and Sin-Eaters are tied to the Shadow Realm, Arcadia, and Underworld. If a Beast's soul is anything like a monstrous archetype of humanity's fears then imagine what great creatures one could come up with. This is so exciting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:54:47-07:00","id":233361,"title":"","content":"So, while we might not have the form of Smaug, we can go &quot;I am Fire. I AM DEATH.&quot; l ike it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI have long since forsaken mortal blood. It offers me nothing but the stale taste of mayflies. I have partaken of Luna's ever-changing children and dined on the scholars of Magic. I have bled monsters, born and created. No more. Tonight I drink the blood of gods and slake my thirst for another thousand years of night.\u201d","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/312-grunt","name":"Grunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:40:24-07:00","id":233418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=233357#post233357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, big shout out to <b>CodeRR</b> for the link to the nWoD Gen Con Panel Podcast.<br /> <br /> I'm even more excited now because what i'm hearing is that the Beasts will be tied to the Astral Realm/Skein similar to how Werewolves, Changelings, and Sin-Eaters are tied to the Shadow Realm, Arcadia, and Underworld. If a Beast's soul is anything like a monstrous archetype of humanity's fears then imagine what great creatures one could come up with. This is so exciting!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/v4buD7D.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:15:45-07:00","id":233491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=233289#post233289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) I wouldn't know an anime reference if it bit me on the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say challenge accepted, but I'm pretty sure they call that assault in most states.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm sold on Beast now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:04:50-07:00","id":233538,"title":"","content":"Thanks Dusksage. But should I post the link on the other forums or just leave it here and have others find it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:49:26-07:00","id":233592,"title":"","content":"I'd say leave it on the nascent Beast forum, as a little reward for those who stuck with a forum based purely on the excitement of a pre-first draft game line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:12:02-07:00","id":233602,"title":"","content":"I am... kind of agog over the sheer amount of speculation here. Do we even know if Beast: The Primordial is the final title? Regardless, happy to hear about new products!<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the heavily customizable beastie, similar to Descent's Demonic Form. I think it would be very interesting if there were power &quot;slots&quot; that aligned with anatomy. So if you say, wanted eyes that saw Mage magic in addition to your eyes that see ghosts, you couldn't do that because you already have a power slotted there. Instead, you could assign your &quot;Mage sight&quot; to your ears so you could hear the magic.<br /> <br /> Alternatively... you could grow more eyes. Bwa ha haaaaaa","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:16:11-07:00","id":233606,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of &quot;ethereal&quot; claws...and shredding ghosts. And as for &quot;parasites&quot; even vampires go squish when dragons make a fist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:01:16-07:00","id":233733,"title":"","content":"So now I'm imagining Freddy Krueger &amp; White Court Vampires from Dresden Files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:04:01-07:00","id":234049,"title":"","content":"We're actually not doing a &quot;build your beast form&quot; in the same way we did with <b>Demon</b>, precisely because we just did it with <b>Demon</b>. It'll be handled a little differently, but that's an area that's still very much in flux.<br /> <br /> That said: Yes, lots of customization for any given character, depending how you want to spin it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:46:19-07:00","id":234068,"title":"","content":"So...I really want this to be the game that lets me play Croup and Vandemar.<br /> <br /> Is this that game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:41:02-07:00","id":234136,"title":"","content":"So, I know it was probably a bit of an off-hand remark, and maybe we'll see it more as the information spins out, but where's the &quot;subversive&quot; part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:47:44-07:00","id":234141,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the rest of the feral shapeshifters aren't exactly on board here?<br /> I mean if you can dot up to a fantastic-type dragon, or manticore, or lamia (suck on that one leeches), or gryphon, a werewolf isn't likely to be gracious if s/he has to give ground to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:53:29-07:00","id":234178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Papa Bear:</b> So, I know it was probably a bit of an off-hand remark, and maybe we'll see it more as the information spins out, but where's the &quot;subversive&quot; part? </div> </div> </div>So far, I would guess it's the encouraged-crossover aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:06:19-07:00","id":234191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234178#post234178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, I would guess it's the encouraged-crossover aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more the perspective. Their antagonists, as far as we know, are called Heroes. I think we're dealing with the Grendels and the Smaugs, not the Beowulfs and Bilbos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:17:52-07:00","id":234199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234191#post234191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's more the perspective. Their antagonists, as far as we know, are called Heroes. I think we're dealing with the Grendels and the Smaugs, not the Beowulfs and Bilbos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly subversive in the World of Darkness. Their start was based on playing Dracula as the &quot;hero&quot; instead of Van Helsing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:09:51-07:00","id":234260,"title":"","content":"But vampires aren't heroes per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:25:08-07:00","id":234369,"title":"","content":"Didn't they also say something about low-satiety characters having their beasts run off and mess with peoples dreams to get their fill? If that's indicitive of their nature in general, that means that our powerstat (in a sense) is going to straight up be ALIVE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:32:53-07:00","id":234379,"title":"","content":"Do you feel a certain touch of Changeling here?<br /> <br /> Primal nightmares? True fae.<br /> Narrative conflict between the monster and the hero? Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at the moment the game is not so defined in my head, and it seems like it tries to tie too much into itself. A little bit too generalist.<br /> I thought the most generalist game was Changeling, with the possibility to represent almost any kind of monster, from the vampire, to the wolfman, to a fucking dragon (the one from Autumn Nightmares, I think?), to just about everything...But now Beast seems to be even more generalist on the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:50:52-07:00","id":234403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234199#post234199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hardly subversive in the World of Darkness. Their start was based on playing Dracula as the &quot;hero&quot; instead of Van Helsing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the subversive part in the &quot;antagonist/ protagonist angle&quot; is less about if they are &quot;heroes&quot; or &quot;villain&quot;, and more about their role in the story- think about the Chronicle books. The &quot;antagonists&quot; in them is about the ones who start a story. A vampire can be monstrous, but the one who brings chaos with him and creates a story is the Owl.<br /> <br /> That also seem to be the thing in Beast- you are a dragon, or a wendigo or whatever, but the thing is that you are not drawn into some mad plot created by some dangerous thing in the dark. Instead, you are the dangerous thing in the dark. You are the one who devour babies, or kidnap maidens or guard some hidden treasure. Your presence creates Heroes who come and try to stop you, use you or steal from you. Instead of being caught in someone's plan, you are the one who makes the plan, and others are trapped in your story. YOU start the story, you are the dragon under the mountain, the giant in his fortress, the monster which swims under the dark waters. And every time you vanquish the damn hero who tried to get rid of you, you build an whole legend around you- until an hero would finally slay you, and then, and only then, they story would have its &quot;happy ending&quot;.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I see things :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:34:45-07:00","id":234437,"title":"","content":"Hearing that it sounds like in some aspect you have the spirit of the thing brought a lot of ease to my mind as otherwise it seemed to be a bit hokey. While I still go to Changeling for it I second the hope that this can be used to model characters like Croup and Vandemar. If it ends up having some of the elements i think it will. It might just be time to run A World of Darkness' League of Extraordinary Gentlemen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:45:39-07:00","id":234543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you feel a certain touch of Changeling here?<br /> <br /> Primal nightmares? True fae.<br /> Narrative conflict between the monster and the hero? Wyrd. </div> </div> </div>Most professional monsters in the WoD would argue the True Fae are a bunch of f***ing posers who need to copy from others legends because they cannot come out with their own horror stuff.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:24:18-07:00","id":234567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234379#post234379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal nightmares? True fae.<br /> Narrative conflict between the monster and the hero? Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I still think True Fae are Demons who found their own personal hell to rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:29:01-07:00","id":234585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234379#post234379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel a certain touch of Changeling here?<br /> <br /> Primal nightmares? True fae.<br /> Narrative conflict between the monster and the hero? Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at the moment the game is not so defined in my head, and it seems like it tries to tie too much into itself. A little bit too generalist.<br /> I thought the most generalist game was Changeling, with the possibility to represent almost any kind of monster, from the vampire, to the wolfman, to a fucking dragon (the one from Autumn Nightmares, I think?), to just about everything...But now Beast seems to be even more generalist on the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're different sorts of generality - that is to say, you could run more or less the entire WoD using the Changeling book along (at least aesthetically), but Beasts can narratively fit into most of the games by carefully straddling.<br /> <br /> Could be wrong, though, and it's not like we have a huge amount to go on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:31:29-07:00","id":234587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234068#post234068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...I really want this to be the game that lets me play Croup and Vandemar.<br /> <br /> Is this that game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to think about that a little more, mostly because it's been years since I read <i>Neverwhere</i>, but let me ask you this: Can you not play them in <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>?<br /> <br /> Actually, scratch that. The esteemed Messers Croup &amp; Vandemar were never human, so they're aren't really changelings. So...would they work as Beasts. Hmm. <i>Kinda</i>. It's a stretch. Ask me again after first drafts come in.<br /> <br /> And, OK, the &quot;subversive&quot; bit. What I actually said in an email to Rich was that I was looking to <i>subvert</i> the &quot;hero arising to kill the monster&quot; myth in a pretty obvious way. He used the word &quot;subversive&quot; later, and while he's not wrong, I do think the word &quot;subversive&quot; carries connotations I didn't necessarily intend.<br /> <br /> But then again, I didn't <i>not</i> intend them either. (Hey, you ask me questions about a game that's still in flux, you get wibbly answers.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Rich showed me the email, and what do you know? I actually <i>did</i> use the word &quot;subversive.&quot; This goes to show that memory is unreliable. Ah, well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","user":"blackhatmatt","date":". 08-19-2014, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:54:31-07:00","id":234608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234543#post234543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most professional monsters in the WoD would argue the True Fae are a bunch of f***ing posers who need to copy from others legends because they cannot come out with their own horror stuff.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Most professional monsters might be ignorant of the origins of those legends. True Fae aren't exactly new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:13:48-07:00","id":234628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234587#post234587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need to think about that a little more, mostly because it's been years since I read <i>Neverwhere</i>, but let me ask you this: Can you not play them in <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>?<br /> <br /> Actually, scratch that. The esteemed Messers Croup &amp; Vandemar were never human, so they're aren't really changelings. So...would they work as Beasts. Hmm. <i>Kinda</i>. It's a stretch. Ask me again after first drafts come in.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Man I love Messers Croup &amp; Vandemar. I mixed them in with a little Dark City and called them Mr Hand &amp; Mr Foot for my V:tM game. My players guessed for an age whether they were vampire, fae, Magi (I mixed a lot of NWoD with OWoD concepts) etc etc. In the end I called them <i>Other </i>and left it at that. And it freaked them the hell out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I love it when my players think they know something and then find out they don't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:26:47-07:00","id":234651,"title":"","content":"It also seems a bit subversive for the crossoverness. People have already started drawing parallels to changeling, werewolf, and vampire. While most games have a sort of &quot;accidental&quot; overlap (the changeling as everything, for example), Beast does so deliberately. Sounds to me that Beasts see those thematic overlaps, hence considering other monsters their kin and also hinting at a common origin. Doubtful itll be set in stone or solid, but it sounded like that to me with the family talk plus deliberate crossover. I do hope that the Gillman is this game's Universal Monster, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:44:28-07:00","id":234672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most professional monsters might be ignorant of the origins of those legends. True Fae aren't exactly new. </div> </div> </div>Time isn\u00b4t exactly linear in Faerie, so the Fae may had copy stuff from human dreams as well from the rest of supernaturals from the s XXI to make their own costumes (Actors) and scenarios for the Dark Ages. Remember, the lack of soul prevents them from developing imagination or ingenuity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:24:37-07:00","id":234717,"title":"","content":"I just hope that the line won't attract misguided Otherkin fandom, because normal players will have to try and chase them away with pitchforks. I know it's NWoD and thus there is a guarantee that the line will be at least decent, but I hope it won't actually attract people thinking they are actually dragons because that would be bothersome.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm okay with the theme of Beasts embodying primal fear of humanity, though personally I would also like if humanity in reverse also unnerved the heck out of Beasts, just like some monsters in the Witcherverse which are as disturbed by humans as humans by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 08-19-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:50:46-07:00","id":234743,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I don't imagine it'll be a game skewed towards that sort of thing, but if people want to make it that way, that's really their prerogative. Onyx Path is just gonna try to make the best game they can make. What people do with it is really up to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:23:02-07:00","id":234779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234717#post234717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope that the line won't attract misguided Otherkin fandom, because normal players will have to try and chase them away with pitchforks. I know it's NWoD and thus there is a guarantee that the line will be at least decent, but I hope it won't actually attract people thinking they are actually dragons because that would be bothersome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. People are family. Family's OK. <br /> <br /> I mean, you still gotta <i>eat</i>, of course...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:24:36-07:00","id":234780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234717#post234717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope that the line won't attract misguided Otherkin fandom</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't spend a lot of time on the Vampire subforum, but I've never noticed it being overrun by people who say they're real vampires. Same thing for Werewolf or any of the others. I'm not sure why you think Beast is particularly &quot;at risk&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:27:53-07:00","id":234784,"title":"","content":"So apparently Hunger is super important to Beasts. Do we have any what they Hunger for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:08:27-07:00","id":234816,"title":"","content":"I think it will be more metaphysical than literal Hunger, not craving for something physical like blood like in case of Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:36:56-07:00","id":234831,"title":"","content":"It'll probably be similar to their Changeling cousins. A base emotion that goes well with their base instincts.<br /> <br /> I'm still getting a big vibe to how the White Court Vampires are portrayed in Dresden Files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:10:53-07:00","id":234855,"title":"","content":"OK; in, what, two days? this thread has exploded and is now firmly in TL;DR territory. Could someone please summarize what\u2019s actually been revealed so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:21:32-07:00","id":234864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234855#post234855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK; in, what, two days? this thread has exploded and is now firmly in TL;DR territory. Could someone please summarize what\u2019s actually been revealed so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Egg's probably incorrect handy guide to BtP as of August 19th 2014 8:15 PM CDT<ul><li>Beasts' &quot;Family&quot; seem to represent human's primordial fears (IE, your Beast is a Dragon, why? Wings represent our lizard brain fear of being swooped back picked up?)</li> <li>It's &quot;subversive&quot; in the sense that the developer wanted to subvert the &quot;hero arising to kill the monster&quot;</li> <li>The &quot;Beast&quot; form is not going to be like Demon insofar as you build it yourself but that said &quot;Yes, lots of customization for any given character, depending how you want to spin it.&quot;</li> <li>Integrity stat is Satiety (don't bother to fill in the dots cause it should move quite a bit in the average session, bonuses on both ends)</li> <li>If a &quot;Beast&quot; doesn't indulge her &quot;Hunger&quot; it'll give like nightmares to everyone or something</li> <li>The game really supports crossovers. You don't <i>need</i> to play it as Crossover, but certain powers and whatnot really mesh well with the other soups</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:31:34-07:00","id":234876,"title":"","content":"So, they haven\u2019t actually said yet what a Beast <i>is</i>? What are the go-to mythological and/or pop-culture references at play here?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do Beasts have <a href=\"http://finalfantasy.wikia.com/wiki/Blue_Magic\" target=\"_blank\">Blue Magic</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:34:18-07:00","id":234877,"title":"","content":"Names like Gillman and Beast from Beauty and the Beast were mentioned, as was dragons, wendigo...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:40:41-07:00","id":234884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234876#post234876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they haven\u2019t actually said yet what a Beast <i>is</i>? What are the go-to mythological and/or pop-culture references at play here?</div> </div> </div> </div>No hard and fast go-to mythological references here. Hodgepodge of errythang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:40:54-07:00","id":234885,"title":"","content":"Beasts seem to embody primal human fears somehow; if you don't control your Hunger, the Beast within you rampages through peoples' dreamscapes.<br /> <br /> Here's my personal news document:<ul><li>Matt McFarland developing.</li> <li>Beasts birth splat is &quot;family.&quot; The other axis might be Hunger.</li> <li>Integrity equivalent is Satiety; it flows wildly, with both extremes being good and the middle ground being bad.</li> <li>One of Beasts themes is &quot;you don't pick your family.&quot; There's inherent crossover somehow; Beasts might well consider themselves &quot;cousins&quot; to other supernaturals.</li> <li>&quot;You're basically playing one of the embodiments of the primal nightmares of humanity.&quot;</li> <li>There's something called Heroes, which seem to be mortals who are touched by the aforementioned dreamscape romps; they want to kick your ass. Matt frequently calls them dicks, and they've been compared to Gaston more than Hercules.</li> <li>You can play a wendigo or a dragon for sure. There's an element of &quot;build your own&quot; going on here.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:32:02-07:00","id":234928,"title":"","content":"According to the recording of the meet, one type of Beast is perfect to fit a wendigo. Other types are flying death that swoops down on you and a great maw that can swallow you whole as these are ways you can represent a dragon unless you want some gigantic winged lizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:59:57-07:00","id":234994,"title":"","content":"Well I asked this over in rpgnet but it's not like everyone is on both forums, so 