rum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T22:29:16-07:00","id":235060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=234876#post234876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they haven\u2019t actually said yet what a Beast <i>is</i>? What are the go-to mythological and/or pop-culture references at play here?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do Beasts have <a href=\"http://finalfantasy.wikia.com/wiki/Blue_Magic\" target=\"_blank\">Blue Magic</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if their are beasts that can copy other supernatural powers such as a changeling contract or a demons embed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T23:29:44-07:00","id":235113,"title":"","content":"Earlier in the forum a link was left by <b>CodeRR</b> that led to a podcast of the nWoD panel at GenCon. The most solid info on Beast was given there. I'll post the link again, the discussion on Beast starts around 36 min.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/GEEKSLOGO.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555\" target=\"_blank\"> &raquo; GenCon Special &ndash; What&rsquo;s Up With the New World of Darkness?GEEKS OUT AFTER DARK </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555\" target=\"_blank\"> http://geeksoutafterdark.com/?p=555 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 08-21-2014, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T23:38:16-07:00","id":235116,"title":"","content":"I'd want to play something that lurks in dark fields and watches people in their well-lit homes, waiting for the lights to go out so it can creep up the walls and into the windows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T02:20:05-07:00","id":235221,"title":"","content":"I have nothing new, but it's the first time I recognized a new game early enough for untenable speculations, so I wish to speculate too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don\u00b4t think Beast is about another kind of changing breeds, that would not worth a whole new game. So I do not believe in something like a \u201cBeastform\u201d. I think the Beast changes more subtly. Maybe fur is growing, eyes glowing in the dark and so on. The first thing came in to my mind was Jekyll &amp; Hyde for sure. But the story of the Invisible Man by H. G. Wells is also a thing. He has hunger, he is feard for its power and get hunted by \u201cHeros\u201d in the end. I think of them because there are classical Monsters the nWoD lack of in the moment. Promethean and the Frankenstein thing had shown, that the nWoD is slightly more classical orientated than the cWoD. So we have to fill this lack.<br /> <br /> I also think that Beasts are not as visual impressive. As creatures of nightmares it is not what they look like, it's what they do. The Hero do not come for the Monster but for the stories people tell about it. Yes, it's also a H.P. Lovecraft-thing. It is not the creature, but how it effects the world. I think this too, because at the surface the WoD is just like our own world, so the Beasts have to be invisible for average people, like Demons in cover or Vampires under the tradition of the masquerade. Not to be as monstrous but have a frightening influence could be a way to handle that.<br /> <br /> Last thing I was thinking about is the crossover part. The Beast is a part of several creatures in the nWoD. Vampires, Werewolfs, Fae, the motive is not new. Beasts are maybe possessed by the same primal spirit in a human body. So there might be relationships between Beasts and all of this creatures. The Heroes (may be a kind of new/better Hunters) who are hunting Beasts searching for stories about supernatural things lurking in the shadows. But they do not know what they find in the end. It might be a Beast, but it might be a Vampire or Werewolf as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:36:41-07:00","id":235257,"title":"","content":"I agree. What if the Beast is wholly internalized? What if it is nothing more than a human acting at extremes, like an antihunter? He sees his own tentacles while others only see social ties. He sees rending claws when hes just really okay with killing someone with human hands. A beast isnt werewolf, fae, or a demon. They dont become the horror--the horror is on the inside. A humans han ds can be the crushing talons of a dragon, the drowning deep, in the right circumstance. The hunger draws you in--every human has the Primordial beast within, every one can manifest it. Some even become outward reflections of what Primordials are within--the metaphor of a dragon versus a changeling or fera.. the hunger of of flesh versus a vampire or cannibal ogre. We are all monsters, all beasts. We are all twisted by something ancient and unknowable, and yet a part of our blood. We are all family. And we must survive in a world of darkness, against the light that would burn and betrau us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{