hose that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:22:26-07:00","id":235540,"title":"","content":"So are beasts the personification of fear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:29:47-07:00","id":235552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=235458#post235458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't really think about it before..........I guess we <i>did </i>get a New WOD version of the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of awesome.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=235540#post235540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are beasts the personification of fear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in as much as all monsters are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2014, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:52:25-07:00","id":235582,"title":"","content":"Umm...Pentex was my personal fear...<br /> <br /> godsdammit!<br /> <br /> *runs screaming and laughing maniacally*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:55:36-07:00","id":235583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=235533#post235533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There, now we've made this stuff into WOD v5 (or would it be 6?). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0048127/\" target=\"_blank\">The Architect</a></i>: Denial is the most predictable of all human responses. But, rest assured, this will be the sixth time we have destroyed it, and we have become exceedingly efficient at it.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I view it the other way around. The Technocracy would've evolved if the God-Machine wasn't around to stop that &quot;Reality is belief&quot; bullshit and anchored it's self so fully into the universe that it dictated that there is and always will be a Truth that will forever spring from a guiding Principle.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:50:42-07:00","id":235611,"title":"","content":"Some more wild speculations. I find the subtitle very interesting. \u201cThe Primordial\u201d. Why not \u201cthe Primal\u201d or something? Primordial usual means the early stage of something. Could Beasts are a kind of original Monsters in the WoD and the others (or some others) descend from them. Are Vampires and Werewolfs huge Families of Beasts (Vampire = fear of the dark, hunger for Blood; Werewolfs = Fear of wild animals, hunger for hunt...) and there are some minor ones (Dragons = Fear of get swooped from the Sky, hunger for treasures; Wendigo = Fear of being eaten, hunger for flash...)?<br /> <br /> Still speculating about the crossover part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T12:55:46-07:00","id":235688,"title":"","content":"To repost something I posted earlier in Werewolf; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_fauna\" target=\"_blank\">Mega-fauna</a> And something interesting...<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creodonta\" target=\"_blank\">Creodonts</a> dominated before losing out 8 million years ago, (give or take a hot minute) to carnivorans. (Carnivorous species).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T15:23:12-07:00","id":235783,"title":"","content":"I think I have a good question that deserves a little bit of speculation. What are the Beast-Touched humans going to be called and what do you think they'll be like?<br /> <br /> Every single nWoD game has them: Ghouls for Vampires, Wolf-Blooded for Werewolf, Sleepwalker for Mage, Stigmatic for Demon, ect. The one thing that all of these humans have in common is that they've been infused/infected with the supernatural abnormality that spawned the supernatural creature itself: The Blood for Ghouls, the Spiritual Heritage for Wolf-Blooded, connection to the Supernal Realms for Sleepwalker, contact with the God-Machine for Stigmatics, ect.<br /> <br /> I can't really think of a good name for these Beast-Touched mortals but if I were to hazard a guess at their origins I'd say that they're probably created the same way Heroes are. Rather than seeking out the Beast to destroy it they probably seek it out to worship or placate it. Fear is a terrible force after all, but isn't it also true that there's nothing more fascinating than what one fears?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:03:21-07:00","id":235835,"title":"","content":"Wow,Dusksage, great question, great idea. Yes, I can imagine Humans who are obsessed by the Beast. A kind of supernatural Stockholm-Syndrome. I love it, because it do not kills me though it could easily. I could imagine the Name \u201cfamiliar\u201d. It is ambiguous for a confidant, who know your crimes, and a person in your Family (!). They maybe could learn to use the reputation and storys of their personal Beast, to inflict fear and have maybe the power to calm down and satisfy the hunger of the Beast.<br /> <br /> Other Names/Concepts i imagine are: Spawns, Remoras, Lampreys, Tamers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:24:21-07:00","id":235852,"title":"","content":"Given that the psychic impact of Beasts can negatively lead to Heroes, I'd imagine there will be a positive equivalent as well. I think Leviathan called them Beloved; a sort of Beauty to our Gaston and our Beast, a princess for the dragon to keep in the tower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:57:17-07:00","id":235975,"title":"","content":"Lol they could be called Belles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:21:28-07:00","id":236012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=235835#post235835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Remoras, Lampreys,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fledgling BtP fandom is going too gung-ho with our lust for Lovecraftian, deep sea beasties. Especially with the Dev swimming in the primordial soup with us has only given us Wendigo and Dragon examples<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:36:19-07:00","id":236088,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I'm becoming more and more convinced that the style Beast is going for is less Lovecraftian or CFtBL and more Jhon Gardener's <i>Grendel</i> (with Grendel himself being only one type of Beast and the story itself only one type as well, but the themes that they seem to be going for are all there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:13:42-07:00","id":236124,"title":"","content":"That's what I've been thinking too, though my fondness for sea creature looking stuff practically demands that I attempt to make a spooky ocean Beast anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:42:37-07:00","id":236226,"title":"","content":"I do not think Beast becomes as much Lovecraftesc. Remora and Lamprey coming in to my mind for there parasitic lifestyle. They peg to a greater fish to be safe. Grendel is definitely a thing. But I think Enkidu as well. He is the paramount example for a beastlike human Monster. Feared but becomes Gilgameshs friend in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T04:28:58-07:00","id":236324,"title":"","content":"I hope the term 'Lovecraftian' is forgotten about but nostalgically remembered by gamers everywhere as a good thing that eventually became overused","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T04:57:56-07:00","id":236332,"title":"","content":"i wonder what the y-splat will be from the quote it said Answer the call of you lair now if you lair was where you lived it wouldn't make much sense for it to call you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:18:44-07:00","id":236353,"title":"","content":"^^Lovecraft not only wrote cosmic horror, Dreamland cycle is one of his stuff that is not too cosmic horror even if within the Mythos. So, yeah, the term is used in too general way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:49:15-07:00","id":236958,"title":"","content":"I hypothesize that Beast: the Primordial will go a similar route to Vampire: the Requiem and Changeling: the Lost in that each Family will cover a single genre of Creature and that there will be another subcategory for each that will deal with more personalized aspects of primal nightmares. <br /> <br /> As a side note do you all think it's to early to speculate about the types of Factions or Philosophies that might appear in Beast? With the information at hand we can theories the general tone for the game but until we learn how solitary each Beast is I fear we may be at a speculatory impass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:07:19-07:00","id":236968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=236958#post236958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a side note do you all think it's to early to speculate about the types of Factions or Philosophies that might appear in Beast? With the information at hand we can theories the general tone for the game but until we learn how solitary each Beast is I fear we may be at a speculatory impass.</div> </div> </div> </div>as i said before i think it has something to do with the Lair, from the quote &quot;answer the call to your Lair&quot; which doesn't make much sense to me because why would answer the call to your home, why is it uppercased? anyhow the Lair could be completely different but hey I'm sticking to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":".  bad grammar 08-21-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:37:52-07:00","id":237004,"title":"","content":"That's a good point <b>Iceblade44</b>,<br /> <br /> I forgot to take into account the Beast's Lair. I find it strange too that it says &quot;answer the call <u>to</u> your Lair&quot; implying that a Beast has to be summoned or drawn to this location/concept before they can truly become a Beast. Since the Beast is tied to nightmares perhaps it's some strange equivalent to a Verge except connecting the Astral Realm to the mortal world, a place where the fear the Beast embodies is strongest? Either that or some equivalent to a Mummy's Tomb where they have some kind of mystical connection to the place locale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:50:24-07:00","id":237018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=236958#post236958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hypothesize that Beast: the Primordial will go a similar route to Vampire: the Requiem and Changeling: the Lost in that each Family will cover a single genre of Creature and that there will be another subcategory for each that will deal with more personalized aspects of primal nightmares. <br /> <br /> As a side note do you all think it's to early to speculate about the types of Factions or Philosophies that might appear in Beast? With the information at hand we can theories the general tone for the game but until we learn how solitary each Beast is I fear we may be at a speculatory impass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we're seeing Family and Hunger as the two axises (axes?) our characters are built on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:51:06-07:00","id":237019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=236353#post236353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^^Lovecraft not only wrote cosmic horror, Dreamland cycle is one of his stuff that is not too cosmic horror even if within the Mythos. So, yeah, the term is used in too general way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream-quest is my favorite story by him and one of my favorites ever so there is that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:53:00-07:00","id":237023,"title":"","content":"It would come as no surprise to me to find out that Beasts are territorial. (Its Lair?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T11:41:00-07:00","id":237186,"title":"","content":"If the call to the Lair is the equivalent to the first change (or embrace) then maybe it's a sort of....large area of a kind of fear. Like a legendary lake that drowns people or such If this holds true then the beast is a person whose soul resonates (?) with that fear or energy and is called towards it.<br /> <br /> From there I theorize that the beast is changed by the energy there (to fit the legend of the place?) to match it Ex: the drowning lake calls a local to it and as he goes into it the energy changes them into a more appropriate monster form. I think your Lair determines your form/powers and what you feed on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:29:45-07:00","id":238531,"title":"","content":"Do note that Matt mentioned, when speaking of Messrs Vandemar and Croup, that he might portray them as Changelings except that they were never men which is why they might be suitable as Beasts though it would take some twisting to make it work. That is to say it sounds like the Beasts might be creatures that never were men, so no transformation through your Lair, no first change, no Embrace etc. it's what you were born as.<br /> <br /> I personally would find it rather invigorating to finally have some truly inhuman PC's available, aside from the Prometheans who also have never been men but they still aspire to become one, instead of always playing ex-humans changed by the supernatural. And yes technically Werewolves are also born as Werewolves instead of men but they still spend their youth until the First Change as normal men so I really cannot count them here as the difference is almost academic here, it wouldn't change the psychology of becoming one whether it derived from a Curse or from birthright.<br /> <br /> Still it's all speculating and according to Matt still very much in flux anyway. Currently I find the game to sound rather fascinating especially since it's designed towards crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:41:05-07:00","id":238671,"title":"","content":"Don't forget about Demon's too, Angels are never truly human until after the Fall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:58:58-07:00","id":238680,"title":"","content":"I hypothesized that the Beasts X splat will be different types of Fear. Like maybe: Fear of self, Fear of hurt, Fear of emotional stimuli, Fear of environment, Esoteric Fear, Fear of the Unknown. <br /> <br /> I also imagined that characters can choose specific fears from amongst the General Fears (one or more may have to be a sub-fear of the main Fear) and you are able to buy more later. These probably develop the powers and probably influences what the Soul looks like when Rampaging.<br /> <br /> On a side note, another speculation of mine is that Hungers are thing that your character starts with and they get more the more the Power Stat increases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T20:23:32-07:00","id":238823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=238531#post238531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do note that Matt mentioned, when speaking of Messrs Vandemar and Croup, that he might portray them as Changelings except that they were never men which is why they might be suitable as Beasts though it would take some twisting to make it work. That is to say it sounds like the Beasts might be creatures that never were men, so no transformation through your Lair, no first change, no Embrace etc. it's what you were born as.<br /> <br /> I personally would find it rather invigorating to finally have some truly inhuman PC's available, aside from the Prometheans who also have never been men but they still aspire to become one, instead of always playing ex-humans changed by the supernatural. And yes technically Werewolves are also born as Werewolves instead of men but they still spend their youth until the First Change as normal men so I really cannot count them here as the difference is almost academic here, it wouldn't change the psychology of becoming one whether it derived from a Curse or from birthright.<br /> <br /> Still it's all speculating and according to Matt still very much in flux anyway. Currently I find the game to sound rather fascinating especially since it's designed towards crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>War Against the Pure allows for the existence of wolfweres and similar shapeshifter concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T20:47:15-07:00","id":238828,"title":"","content":"I've been working on something like this for a bit ... I've all the initial basics worked out and basically at the point of figuring out powers and what they do ... then I saw that announcement and I kinda remember posting stuff on the forums a while back and now of course I am thinking .. uh oh ... sigh .. probably just being paranoid... here's the basic idea, I've the rest if you want to see it, been a work in progress with other stuff for about 3 or 4 years now .. yes .. I know, I am a slow writer .. life sometimes has that effect.<br /> <br /> <b>THE PRIMALS </b> <br /> Over the centuries many cultures have had people who worshipped the very animals themselves, seeing them as actual gods. In some cases these were spirit animals trapped here in the mortal world from the time of the sundering, and in others they were other darker things masquerading as gods. In some cultures if one digs deep enough, you will find reference to Primals; men and women who allowed themselves to become one with the animals they worshipped.<br /> <br /> At first one might merely see this as cases of possession, what the Forsaken might call a <i>dugathim</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:45:12-07:00","id":238843,"title":"","content":"The more that I think about this kind of reminds me of fear mythos<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://thefearmythos.wikia.com/wiki/The_Fear_Mythos_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">http://thefearmythos.wikia.com/wiki/...ar_Mythos_Wiki</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:08:12-07:00","id":239025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>CodeRR:</b> If the call to the Lair is the equivalent to the first change (or embrace) then maybe it's a sort of....large area of a kind of fear. </div> </div> </div>I brought up something like this on RPGNet, and Matt confirmed that a Lair was something more supernatural than the usual &quot;residence merit.&quot; (I now find myself wondering whether the Beasts of Bethlehem from Antagonists have anything to do with the genesis of Beast's mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T06:54:55-07:00","id":239070,"title":"","content":"I think the ancient Greek deity Proteus needs mentioning. He was, in a way, the ultimate shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> Part of a progression. You'd have the basics in which animals and totemism would be a part of, then for those furthest along, Protean abilities would come into play, adding elemental, and aetherial abilities, as well as fantastic beasts. (Yeah, I guess the word 'protean&quot; is already taken by the leeches)<br /> <br /> And I don't think anyone has mentioned Jim Butcher's &quot;Shagnasty.&quot; But I wouldn't be at all surprised if there was a bit of inspiration from it. A &quot;skinwalker&quot; as well as a powerful mage, and thoroughly scary.<br /> /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:35:32-07:00","id":239618,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I'm going to have to disagree with you <b>Shadowflame</b>,<br /> <br /> The Primordials would have to be very thematically different than the other nWoD creatures, seeing as if they delve to deep into shapechanging and animism then they risk making the game to similar to Werewolf: the Forsaken. <br /> <br /> That's not to say your examples are bad though, I actually really like that you mentioned Proteus, it's just that I think with the games focus on the primeval fears of man that a Beast styled off of the Greek deity would appear more similar to John Carpenters: The Thing than the actual Olympian god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:44:57-07:00","id":239624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=239618#post239618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I'm going to have to disagree with you <b>Shadowflame</b>,<br /> <br /> The Primordials would have to be very thematically different than the other nWoD creatures, seeing as if they delve to deep into shapechanging and animism then they risk making the game to similar to Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> That's not to say your examples are bad though, I actually really like that you mentioned Proteus, it's just that I think with the games focus on the primeval fears of man that a Beast styled off of the Greek deity would appear more similar to John Carpenters: The Thing than the actual Olympian god.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that would make Kurt Russell a Hero.... That sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:57:39-07:00","id":239632,"title":"","content":"Hey, we don't know the Thing's side of the story. Maybe Kurt was lying to the audience during the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T16:02:53-07:00","id":239634,"title":"","content":"Look, you try making friends when you've been locked under the ice for a few years. Social skills kind of go to crap when all you've got is yourself and the other frozen critters to talk to. For all we know, it just wanted to be friends, then everyone around it got violent and scared it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T16:59:45-07:00","id":239675,"title":"","content":"the following is how I picture Beast games will go:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/B6qni.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/jqh0M.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:11:56-07:00","id":239755,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Beasts are things that were &quot;never human.&quot; or is that speculation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:46:11-07:00","id":239781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=239618#post239618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I'm going to have to disagree with you <b>Shadowflame</b>,<br /> <br /> The Primordials would have to be very thematically different than the other nWoD creatures, seeing as if they delve to deep into shapechanging and animism then they risk making the game to similar to Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> That's not to say your examples are bad though, I actually really like that you mentioned Proteus, it's just that I think with the games focus on the primeval fears of man that a Beast styled off of the Greek deity would appear more similar to John Carpenters: The Thing than the actual Olympian god.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I added &quot;Shagnasty&quot; in the mix. In Jim Butcher's novel, <i>Turn Coat</i>, the first thing that critter started fighting was a pack of werewolves. And they lost, badly. &quot;It&quot; then made its way to a secure hold of a Vampire Lord (actually the &quot;daughter really ran things) and pretty much tore them apart. It even started munching on a vamp's fingers. *munch crunch* There was no stopping it, especially in light of the fact that it was also a powerful mage. Shagnasty was based on a Navajo boogie man so evil that the Navajo don't even to talk about it much. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:47:07-07:00","id":239782,"title":"","content":"The Wild Things are coming, the Wild Things are coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:32:12-07:00","id":239799,"title":"","content":"Ah I see, I'm unfamiliar with Jim Butcher's work and misread the implication. That's on me and I apologize. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:59:48-07:00","id":239822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=239781#post239781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I added &quot;Shagnasty&quot; in the mix. In Jim Butcher's novel, <i>Turn Coat</i>, the first thing that critter started fighting was a pack of werewolves. And they lost, badly. &quot;It&quot; then made its way to a secure hold of a Vampire Lord (actually the &quot;daughter really ran things) and pretty much tore them apart. It even started munching on a vamp's fingers. *munch crunch* There was no stopping it, especially in light of the fact that it was also a powerful mage. Shagnasty was based on a Navajo boogie man so evil that the Navajo don't even to talk about it much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best part is that it has Were delirium cranked to stupid levels. Look at it with true vision and you just went a little Lovecraft.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:13:06-07:00","id":239838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=239799#post239799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah I see, I'm unfamiliar with Jim Butcher's work and misread the implication. That's on me and I apologize. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gah!<br /> &quot;Stormfront&quot; is the first novel, GO!<br /> <br /> The series fits in VERY well with WoD. The first couple of novels are almost formulaic as Butcher gets in the groove of writing, but then he takes off and just doesn't let up. (Wizards, werewolves, vampires, demons, fallen angels, fairies, you name it. Even a mobster so ruthless that the supernatural world steers clear of. All in modern day Chicago. And then there's &quot;Bob&quot; the talking skull, who has some of the funniest laugh out loud lines) And Butcher slowly ratchets things up with every book. (our hero &quot;Harry Dresden&quot; does level up eventually in power, but when he meets &quot;Shagnasty&quot; he is still way out of his league. <i>&quot;Bring it you dickless freak!&quot;</i> Fortunately help arrives in the form of an archmage/shaman that is a master shapeshifter and knows this enemy for what it is)<br /> <br /> I envy you that you have this series to read for the first time.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;A <i>successful murder is like a successful restaurant</i>: Ninety percent of it is about location, location, location.&quot; -- Gentleman John Marcone.</i><br /> /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:14:49-07:00","id":239839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=239838#post239838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gah!<br /> &quot;Stormfront&quot; is the first novel, GO!</div> </div> </div> </div>Storm Front. The space is important, not just because the series' titles mostly stick to a &quot;two words with the same number of letters&quot; format, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stormfront_(website)\" target=\"_blank\">but for other reasons, too.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T17:3