ts_01_10/\" target=\"_blank\">Yeah, we do.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can I say that was a great view point, and really awesome. Thanks for the link. I think I am now going to use the Thing in my next campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T15:45:25-07:00","id":245667,"title":"","content":"I just had an interesting thought, <br /> <br /> Do you guys think that the Beasts will have some kind of Mask like ability that hides their monstrous form from the rest of humanity or if they're human in appearance but have a predator's aura like the Kindred and Uratha from 2nd Edition Requiem and Forsaken?<br /> <br /> Also do you think that Heroes will be able to see/detect a Beast's true form/aura or if they're having something more similar to Disquiet where the Heroes don't have to know exactly what the Beast is but they have a clear instinct that it's the source of their troubles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T16:03:47-07:00","id":245687,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the new splat will help me with crafting Tokyo Ghoul fan splat. I have vision how to do it, buy maybe Primordial will give me some extra inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T21:46:10-07:00","id":245851,"title":"","content":"It might, they revealed that the fear of being eaten is one of the splat types in beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T22:24:42-07:00","id":245885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=245667#post245667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had an interesting thought,<br /> <br /> Do you guys think that the Beasts will have some kind of Mask like ability that hides their monstrous form from the rest of humanity or if they're human in appearance but have a predator's aura like the Kindred and Uratha from 2nd Edition Requiem and Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather them look &quot;normal&quot; but with things that hint at their monster side until they, to use an expression from another game, goes loud. Like if it is the wendigo, which we hear is easily possible, their mouth is just wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T05:47:21-07:00","id":246096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">It might, they revealed that the fear of being eaten is one of the splat types in beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now the only question would be if TG's Ghouls fall under the splat or just like other supernaturals are somehow related to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:42:07-07:00","id":246323,"title":"","content":"I'm getting a sense that Beast is gonna take a toolbox approach to supernatural construction, sort of like how demonic forms involve a lot of customization. I bet you'll be able to model whatever they do more or less using what systems they give us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:43:57-07:00","id":246324,"title":"","content":"Matt's already said they aren't doing something akin to Demonic Forms because they already did that sort of thing(It's called, ironically, Demonic Forms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T13:46:41-07:00","id":246349,"title":"","content":"I think the customizability will come from what fear you play off of and what hunger you take. From that you've got a fair bit of modability and then you get into what powers you take to enact them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T14:55:40-07:00","id":246369,"title":"","content":"I think I would explore the &quot;Straw Man&quot; (the original Scarecrow) from Marvel comics. (with a hunger manifesting as a murder of crows)<br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_Man_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/96/StrawMan.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Hmmm..Marvel comics does have a few ideas; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Marvel_Comics_demons#The_Fear_Lords\" target=\"_blank\">Fear Lords</a><br /> And then there's the old Ghost Rider that was barely controllable at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 09-01-2014, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T16:11:19-07:00","id":246419,"title":"","content":"I really wonder how the hungers are going to manifest. Is it how you feed or what you feed <i>on?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:13:30-07:00","id":246611,"title":"","content":"After listening to the podcast, I've been wondering about the primordial fears that would crop up in the World of Darkness. Besides the usual claptrap of phobias listed in DSM V that might be used by Storytellers, the fear that comes to mind for Mortal is the fear of the unknown. Also, the main fear of the other denizens would be the fear of revelation; that their secret societies may be discovered and possibly destroyed. Then another thing hit me like a ton of bricks.<br /> <br /> Remember the book Blood and Smoke? In it, WW added the Strix as an adversary for Requiem. If the podcast is right, they satiate their monstrous side by acting like vampires and they consider themselves to be the progenitors of all vampires in the World of Darkness, with an example being the character, Mother.<br /> <br /> Given that the Strix hits everything that OP said about Beasts, are the Strix a Primoridal &quot;family&quot;?<br /> <br /> Are the identities of the X-splat in Beast: The Primordial hidden in the chronicle sections of the other game lines?<br /> <br /> Think about it:<br /> <br /> A fear of the Uratha is that spirits will overtake the human world. Enter the Spirit Lords of the Idigram.<br /> <br /> Even though it's not said in Fallen World Chronicle, expect a Family based on the Abyss of Mage.<br /> <br /> The Firestorm of Promethean indicates a significant paradigm shift for the Created.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Huntsmen Chronicle for Changeling is, unless I'm missing something, is based on the Huntsman, the leader of The Wild Hunt of Faerie lore.<br /> <br /> Am I getting close?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:34:46-07:00","id":246635,"title":"","content":"I think years of fighting fans of Mage in regards to the Supernal Realms and the major templates leads to say that that is obviously not the case. Onyx Path isn't going to make that mistake <i>again</i>, particularly since they're skirting issues with Beasts thinking they're the origin point for monsters anyways.<br /> <br /> Next Track:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246119#post246119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. (For a game with a more &quot;the gang's all here&quot; kind of approach, <b>Beast</b> is coming soon.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I yoinked this from Prommie's thread.<br /> <br /> So, I've been meaning to ask, because I'm curious as hell: Considering Promethean's theme of alienation versus Beasts' 'gang's all here' mentality....how the hell are you going to reconcile the two of them?<br /> <br /> I mean, I imagine the basics of that is that Beasts offer a repreive from the Saturnine Night...which also pulls them uncomfortably away from the Pilgrimage as well. Beasts, after all, are those uncles you're never sure if you're pleased to see. But since you're developing both, I'm curious how you hold the two in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-02-2014, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:48:03-07:00","id":246639,"title":"","content":"After reading the Labor Day Monday Meeting, it's said that Beast brings together core thoughts of previously untapped horror stories. Not just Creature from the Black Lagoon, or just Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde, but something underlying in both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T00:48:19-07:00","id":246690,"title":"","content":"My reaction in a nutshell.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YWQlTRfbpzQ\" data-code=\"YWQlTRfbpzQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YWQlTRfbpzQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T01:50:49-07:00","id":246707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=246639#post246639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the Labor Day Monday Meeting, it's said that Beast brings together core thoughts of previously untapped horror stories. Not just Creature from the Black Lagoon, or just Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde, but something underlying in both.</div> </div> </div> </div> It sounds that some of us were right with there guesses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T04:08:15-07:00","id":246745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=246635#post246635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been meaning to ask, because I'm curious as hell: Considering Promethean's theme of alienation versus Beasts' 'gang's all here' mentality....how the hell are you going to reconcile the two of them?<br /> <br /> I mean, I imagine the basics of that is that Beasts offer a repreive from the Saturnine Night...which also pulls them uncomfortably away from the Pilgrimage as well. Beasts, after all, are those uncles you're never sure if you're pleased to see. But since you're developing both, I'm curious how you hold the two in your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe one of the other ways the devs described the theme of Beast is that you can't pick your family. What does it mean to a Promethean who finds acceptance from this thing that <i>has fangs in its eyes</i> and makes humans think they're gonna be eaten?<br /> <br /> And what of the Beast who finds this wayward creature? Such a responsibility to look after the young ones -- especially when they're this blank. He'll need training, molding, shaping... he might even make a proper monster one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T06:47:30-07:00","id":246775,"title":"","content":"Well, I figure at worst (barring the idea that beasts are just as vulnerable to disquiet as any one else), beasts would be a dead end on the pilgrimage, unless things are radically changing I don't think accepting that one is a monster is helpful to gaining humanity.<br /> <br /> At best, I'd see the promethean inspired to take up the road of silver, studying humanity by studying the multitude of monsters that mankind can become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T04:16:00-07:00","id":247726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dusksage:</b> Do you guys think that the Beasts will have some kind of Mask like ability that hides their monstrous form from the rest of humanity or if they're human in appearance but have a predator's aura like the Kindred and Uratha from 2nd Edition Requiem and Forsaken? </div> </div> </div>For now, I'm going to guess that they look human most of the time, but have a Predaura/Disquiet/Sybaris-alike mechanic. Their souls were described earlier on as big monstrous things that ravage the local dreamscape - whatever dreamscape means in this context - and they might be able to pull aspects of it into themselves if they need to monster out. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also do you think that Heroes will be able to see/detect a Beast's true form/aura or if they're having something more similar to Disquiet where the Heroes don't have to know exactly what the Beast is but they have a clear instinct that it's the source of their troubles? </div> </div> </div>I suspect the latter, because it has a wider range of potential plotlines. But I'm betting a Hero will know a Lair when he sees it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>StSword:</b> It might, they revealed that the fear of being eaten is one of the splat types in beast. </div> </div> </div>I think darkness is another, but that might stated more generally of the type of thing that a splat might be. I do suspect, right now, that each Family will be, or think itself to be, more closely related to a <i>particular</i> other splat or two than others. Like the splat about being eaten is most closely related to werewolves (and maybe vampires too), and if there's a darkness one, it might be related to vampires and/or sineaters - meanwhile changelings and/or Prometheans might be related to a splat about the fear of being mutilated or disfigured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:04:55-07:00","id":247811,"title":"","content":"hmf...considering how monstrous humanity can become...and all while wearing a pretty face.<br /> <br /> Sorry...got the Mideast on my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T11:18:24-07:00","id":248023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=247726#post247726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think darkness is another, but that might stated more generally of the type of thing that a splat might be. I do suspect, right now, that each Family will be, or think itself to be, more closely related to a <i>particular</i> other splat or two than others. Like the splat about being eaten is most closely related to werewolves (and maybe vampires too), and if there's a darkness one, it might be related to vampires and/or sineaters - meanwhile changelings and/or Prometheans might be related to a splat about the fear of being mutilated or disfigured.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how I feel about making different families closer to one splat or another because I don't want one Family to be the best at Vamp Kinships, while another is really good at Were Kinships. If an ST has allowed only minor crossover between Beast and one Line, and everyone is playing the other line I don't want to be stuck playing the almost Vamps if I really want to play along with my group. Also, the proposed Family for trying to create a dragon, 'nightmare from the sky that's going to swoop in and take you away' doesn't sound like something that's going to line up well with the rest of the splats. I'm looking forward to the ideas brought in by Kinships, there's a lot of interesting narrative that comes from something distinctly other that still seems to understand you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T15:59:59-07:00","id":248207,"title":"","content":"I wondered for a brief moment that Beasts are actually a superimposed template to add on to other splats, representing that those splats have 'awakened' to their Bestial nature. But, while maybe interesting, I don't think they'd give us that as the year's core game-line for a slew of reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T00:08:37-07:00","id":248674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=247726#post247726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now, I'm going to guess that they look human most of the time, but have a Predaura/Disquiet/Sybaris-alike mechanic. Their souls were described earlier on as big monstrous things that ravage the local dreamscape - whatever dreamscape means in this context - and they might be able to pull aspects of it into themselves if they need to monster out. I suspect the latter, because it has a wider range of potential plotlines. But I'm betting a Hero will know a Lair when he sees it. I think darkness is another, but that might stated more generally of the type of thing that a splat might be. I do suspect, right now, that each Family will be, or think itself to be, more closely related to a <i>particular</i> other splat or two than others. Like the splat about being eaten is most closely related to werewolves (and maybe vampires too), and if there's a darkness one, it might be related to vampires and/or sineaters - meanwhile changelings and/or Prometheans might be related to a splat about the fear of being mutilated or disfigured.</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt it will work that way, since beasts apparently categorize by how they induce fear, I find it hard to believe they wouldn't notice that the other monsters induce different kind of fears too. Vampires: the animalistic gangrel hardly induce the same kind of fear as the predatory seducers of the daeva, or the paranoia inducing mekhet, and among the mages a necromancer induces a rather different fear than that of a fate mage with an evil eye or a warlock that can bend your mind like a pretzel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T03:31:36-07:00","id":248728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hmf...considering how monstrous humanity can become...and all while wearing a pretty face. </div> </div> </div>just dropping a quote that feels relevant:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Man did not evolve naturally, as modern science teaches, either accidentally or as part of a divine plan. He is a freak of his own making. All of his actions \u2014 not only his cruelty to his own kind and his ruthless exploitation of the animal world, but even his great intellectual and artistic achievements \u2014 are the actions of a monster. </div> </div> </div>and here's what Nietzsc-, I mean Zarathustra has to say on this matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Man is evil&quot;\u2014so said to me for consolation, all the wisest ones. Ah, if only it be still true today! For the evil is man's best force.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Man must become better and eviler&quot;\u2014so do I teach. The evilest is necessary for the Superman's best.<br /> It may have been well for the preacher of the petty people to suffer and be burdened by men's sin. I, however, rejoice in great sin as my great consolation.\u2014<br /> Such things, however, are not said for long ears. Every word, also, is not suited for every mouth. These are fine far-away things: at them sheep's claws shall not grasp!</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>There are reasons why supernaturals maintain their their own &quot;masquerades&quot;. Humanity has not only advantages in numbers, is it as capable of monstrous acts as any supernatural, if not more. Slashers are the ultimate example of &quot;man's best force&quot; manifested.<br /> <br /> That's why I would love if it was emphasized that while Beasts are monsters Heroes could be equally if not more monstrous as well. Look at myths, heroic figures like Herakles fought monsters, but were capable of monstrous savagery as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:41:24-07:00","id":248913,"title":"","content":"Hmm..in a lot of myths the more intelligent &quot;monsters&quot; wanted to be left alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:48:10-07:00","id":248918,"title":"","content":"The call of the Lair, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:01:12-07:00","id":250426,"title":"","content":"Given that Beasts are seen as &quot;cousins&quot; to the other supernatural races, what do vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, sin-eaters, mummies, and demons fear? Perhaps that will be the focus of the Families that they talked about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:20:07-07:00","id":250464,"title":"","content":"Very doubtful, since the entire idea seems to be primordial fears of <i>humanity</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T22:05:41-07:00","id":250500,"title":"","content":"Although a beast might very well tap into the fears of parahumanity too when they tap into the fears of humanity, what might be scary to a human could certainly trigger the buttons of a template or two as well.<br /> <br /> A fire monster that taps into the fear of being burned alive would certainly not be something a vampire or promethean would laugh off, and a beast that turns into an angel burning with the power of the sun as the embodiment of fear of god's wrath would be no joke to a vampire or demon. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T22:52:16-07:00","id":250536,"title":"","content":"Sure, but that's coincidental.<br /> <br /> Beasts have been described implicitly as the primordial nightmares of humanity. They've also been implicitly described as seeing monsters as family. It's been heavily implied they see themselves-might even be, depending on the ST(I'll admit it, I favor the idea so far)- as being the root of all monsters, the rawest(primordial, you might say) form of monsters that all others refined themselves from.(In this sense, a comparison to the Strix makes some sense, though I imagine modern Strix take a dim view of that)<br /> <br /> Tapping into primal fears that humanity and monsters share? Sure. Tapping into the supernatural fear base? That doesn't quite seem like their place in the family tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:20:55-07:00","id":250739,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to play, like an embodiment of humanities fear of being hunted. As long as I can do that, I'm fine. Although I do wonder where the horror is going to come from. What is horrifying about being a beast? Where will our beloved angst and self-hatred come from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T11:13:04-07:00","id":250916,"title":"","content":"I think it's a similar situation to Werewolf: the Forsaken where the fear comes from self discovery. If we read into this correctly a Beast undergoes something similar to the First Change where they &quot;hear the call of their Lair.&quot; After that they become Beasts, and all the preconceptions they had about life go out the window. How can you go back to your regular life when you must satiate your hunger or else drive all those around you mad from nightmares. What happens when your best friend becomes a Hero and instinctively tries to hunt you down? How will you live with yourself when you start seeing your loved ones as food?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T23:08:23-07:00","id":251264,"title":"","content":"If the Families are only based on Humanity's fears, then unless they make a family for every phobia listed in the DSM-V, they will have to be grouped together just like the Seemings in Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T00:05:18-07:00","id":251318,"title":"","content":"That rubs me the wrong way, but I'm can't quite articulate why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T00:11:13-07:00","id":251322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251318#post251318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That rubs me the wrong way, but I'm can't quite articulate why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's an obvious statement mixed with terminological confusion and a baffling anti-rationale that ties into something that almost everyone in the thread likely understood was not the intended reading of &quot;the fears of humanity&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T00:19:32-07:00","id":251325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251322#post251322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's an obvious statement mixed with terminological confusion and a baffling anti-rationale that ties into something that almost everyone in the thread likely understood was not the intended reading of &quot;the fears of humanity&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>No-well, yes, but more I think it's the absolute certainty with which it's said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T00:31:16-07:00","id":251328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251322#post251322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's an obvious statement mixed with terminological confusion and a baffling anti-rationale that ties into something that almost everyone in the thread likely understood was not the intended reading of &quot;the fears of humanity&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be the most articulate thing I have read today. And on a forum thread based solely on hopes and speculation I must ask you to cease and desist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T04:56:21-07:00","id":251412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> cease and desist. </div> </div> </div>*stop<br /> <br /> Cause you know, I wrote a MA thesis on why legalese-derived expressions should be replaced by plainer equivalents, so I as an academic I must nitpick.<br /> <br /> But still, he does not get the point that it's about the primal fears of humanity. I doubt our nomadic ancestors deliberated about psychological terminology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T13:05:53-07:00","id":251673,"title":"","content":"I feel the single answer that would give us the most to talk about is what are humanities Primordial fears?<br /> Limiting it to the classic five by five (as guessing within a standardized system is easy.)<br /> We have Water which easily brings to mind Leviathan and Creatures form the black lagoon.<br /> Darkness; which ply's it's self towards a fear of the unknown, but seems a bit general for me to pick a &quot;beast&quot; that falls solely under it's umbrella.<br /> Fear of being Hunted which is really what werewolves represent.<br /> Those were the easy three I posit Fear of being alone and Fear losing control. Isolation and subversion yet no classical beast jumps to mind to fill in those roles. <br /> <br /> I rather hope the Y-splat is mainly visual/stylistic like basic animal groups. defining your more physical aspects. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T13:20:21-07:00","id":251683,"title":"","content":"I have not given one thought to the groups yet.<br /> <br /> It's weird, more so than any other game, when I think of Beasts, I think of islands, not archipelagos. You figure that'd be Mummy(which is the case), but that went out with Guilds(And damn the Guilds are awesome).<br /> <br /> I have no idea what beast y-splats would be like, but if the x-splat is subject matter, I could go for a y-splat that's presentation/genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T13:38:04-07:00","id":251688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=250536#post250536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but that's coincidental.<br /> <br /> Beasts have been described implicitly as the primordial nightmares of humanity. They've also been implicitly described as seeing monsters as family. It's been heavily implied they see themselves-might even be, depending on the ST(I'll admit it, I favor the idea so far)- as being the root of all monsters, the rawest(primordial, you might say) form of monsters that all others refined themselves from.(In this sense, a comparison to the Strix makes some sense, though I imagine modern Strix take a dim view of that)<br /> <br /> Tapping into primal fears that humanity and monsters share? Sure. Tapping into the supernatural fear base? That doesn't quite seem like their place in the family tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a moment: \u201cthe rawest(primordial, you might say) form of monsters that all others refined themselves from\u201d. Is that out of my speculation or where dose that came from? Source please.<br /> <br /> I think the self hate part has something to do with the hunger, because you are powerless if you are hungry and dull if you are satisfied.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile I had another idea. I think it is possible that part of the Game is, how Beasts become what they are. I believe, there is a kind of awakening moment. Like the embrace, the awakening and so on, it might be important, or even part of the game mechanic, how the (wo-) man become Beast.<br /> <br /> It has something to do with the Black Lagoon-Dr. Jekyll-Invisible Man- Statement from the Monday meeting, that I start to thinking about that. There might be a kind of activating momentum in every Beasts story.<br /> <br /> I imagine options like:<br /> <br /> Activated by chemical or other scientific Influence (Hyde, Invisible Man, Hulk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> Activated by childhood trauma or generally extreme fear (lot of Japanese horror movie children monsters).<br /> <br /> Activated by acts of soul riving cruelty or monstrosity (Eating human flash / Wendigo).<br /> <br /> Activated because raised by an Animal / Monster / Beast (maybe even supernatural Creatures, that could be the explanation, why Monsters could become Family).<br /> <br /> And the most creepy: Activated by pure choice (original Hannibal Lecter. From the books, you know).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T16:34:44-07:00","id":251760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251688#post251688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a moment: \u201cthe rawest(primordial, you might say) form of monsters that all others refined themselves from\u201d. Is that out of my speculation or where dose that came from? Source please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not faulting you, but I answered this in the same sentence.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's been <b>heavily implied</b> they see themselves-might even be, depending on the ST(I'll admit it, I favor the idea so far)- as being the root of all monsters, the rawest(primordial, you might say) form of monsters that all others refined themselves from </div> </div> </div>Which comes from, you know, the entire kinship to other monsters spoiler and the fact that 'primordial' is a hot word in the dev's talk. Oh, and the implication from Slashers that humans becoming Rippers and then Scourges is indicative of a beginning transition that leads to monsters of all kinds that sometimes gain traction and spread and breed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T18:50:50-07:00","id":251817,"title":"","content":"My guess is that the Primordial may refer to the mythical ancestor of the race, and if you believe the Beasts all human-born(-or-directly-related) supernatural beings; it is his/her blood that gives humans the power to defy humanity, to become something somewhat less but infinitely grander.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I'd say the birth splats are similar to the Fears from the Fear Mythos, embodying both a primal phobia and a more cerebral version thereof.<br /> <br /> Probably:<br /> <br /> <b>Predation: </b>On the one level, this is the fear of being eaten, the monkey hiding in the trees from hungry lions. It is also the fear of human Lions, and the loss of control to someone who gets it because they were stronger you, the nerd avoiding the bullies. The &quot;brute&quot; splat (though I expect that more intelligent, subtle members will be represented, 2nd Edition seems to have realized playing a dumb thug ain't fun).<br /> <br /> <b>Darkness: </b>There are <i>things </i>that lurk in the dark, whether wild animals, criminals, or simply pits you didn't see until you fell in. At the same time, you wish you actually knew less, because your mind invents sources of the info in your other senses; you can hear human panting, the crack of twigs, that little book bound in strange leather that you swear whispers. The very fact you can't see it makes it worse, especially if you catch glimpses out of the corner of your eye. The unknown is here, and all you know is that it is <i>out to get you.</i> The &quot;spy&quot; splat (because spies are masters of this as a matter of survival; far better you look at the scary sound over there, instead of the ninja over here).<br /> <br /> <b>Isolation: </b>Humans are a social species, it's true. That's why prison is so dreaded, actually, being stuck in the center of a cage with nothing to keep you company but grey walls and guards trained to very pointedly ignore you if that remains an option. It's also why ostracism is so feared, why the loneliest place is the center of the crowd. Having lost everyone, you have nothing but your thoughts...at least, you think they're your thoughts. Didn't shamans believe something about self-imposed exile opening themselves to other worlds? The &quot;mystic&quot; splat (existing apart from society to fully examine themselves and whoever they bring in their orbit).<br /> <br /> <b>Nature: </b>Related to Predation, the fear of natural processes differs in how personal it is; namely, not at all. The Big Bad Wolf does not eat Grandma because he wants to revel in your grief, he eats her because you pointed him to a way to survive another week or so, easily. The hurricane does not kill you because it hates you, it kills you because you were in the way of a tree it was blowing about. Considering that, how important are you (and the rest of humanity) in the grand view of things? The &quot;scholar&quot; splat (studying the amoral processes of the world),<br /> <br /> <b>Entropy: </b>Disease, moral decay, corruption, anarchy-all are built around the fear of things tomorrow being worse than they were today, and that they will never get better. Try as you might, the Second Law of Thermodynamics will have its due, all things are slouching towards heat death, and while it's an open question about whether something will be born from the universe's corpse, it will be something quite unlike anything anyone will recognize, and likely something that thinks the very <i>concept </i>of something before itself is ridiculous. The &quot;social&quot; splat (after all, really far-reaching entropy is subtle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T19:49:37-07:00","id":251875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251817#post251817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....</div> </div> </div> </div>The one thing that i hope they don't do out of this is have The social splat, The Spy splat, The brute Splat, The mystic Splat.<br /> Adding class like characteristics is narrowing and leaves a rather two dimensional feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T20:40:41-07:00","id":251929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251875#post251875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing that i hope they don't do out of this is have The social splat, The Spy splat, The brute Splat, The mystic Splat.<br /> Adding class like characteristics is narrowing and leaves a rather two dimensional feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, themes, rather than role, should dictate splat line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T22:38:13-07:00","id":251979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251817#post251817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head, I'd say the birth splats are similar to the Fears from the Fear Mythos, embodying both a primal phobia and a more cerebral version thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div>This Fear Mythos concept has been bandied about in this thread for a while now, so I finally did some research on it.<br /> <br /> That is one deep rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of material to mine there for all the gamelines, methinks -- but I certainly would love to play a game where I could play as Slenderman or something like it. Heh heh heh heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T00:34:53-07:00","id":252048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=251760#post251760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not faulting you, but I answered this in the same sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which comes from, you know, the entire kinship to other monsters spoiler and the fact that 'primordial' is a hot word in the dev's talk. Oh, and the implication from Slashers that humans becoming Rippers and then Scourges is indicative of a beginning transition that leads to monsters of all kinds that sometimes gain traction and spread and breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good morning Sethos. Don't wright postings if you are sleepy.<br /> <br /> Sorry ArcaneArts, I missed that entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:31:19-07:00","id":252467,"title":"","content":"No worries. I make mistakes all the time.<br /> <br /> Also, feel free to call me Arcane, or Arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://for