 of anyone around me with vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:07:15-07:00","id":269070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=267533#post267533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a power called 'You're in Public and All of a Sudden... You're Naked' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have that power already. It's called &quot;Paragon Shames the Weak&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T12:49:12-07:00","id":269352,"title":"","content":"Well if this power doesn't get into the book, I know the first new fan-made power that'll be coming out now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T04:56:46-07:00","id":270049,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen the music video for Maroon 5--Animals? I can't help but get an idea for a Beast in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:25:43-07:00","id":270074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=270049#post270049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone seen the music video for Maroon 5--Animals? I can't help but get an idea for a Beast in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;mfw World of Darkness forums turn into my Facebook feed<br /> &gt;mfw I have no face","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T07:59:52-07:00","id":270122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, hypothetically if I want to play as the Slender Man, should I wate for Beast, or use the True Fae rules from Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what I've seen about the legend, looks like it could be hacked out better as a True Fae, but we haven't seen enough of Beast to know for certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:02:26-07:00","id":270125,"title":"","content":"Given that Beast so far looks to have a heavy mythic slant, I'd argue for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Although some great cases can be made for Demon as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:03:15-07:00","id":270126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=269070#post269070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have that power already. It's called &quot;Paragon Shames the Weak&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you Mummy fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:46:00-07:00","id":270148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=270126#post270126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Beast so far looks to have a heavy mythic slant, I'd argue for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Although some great cases can be made for Demon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Demon personally. One of the prime antagonists in my game is basically Slenderman as an angel.<br /> <br /> I had thought that Slenderman might make a good Beast though as it's definatly hungry for something and deals with some pretty deep fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T11:40:31-07:00","id":270256,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about how Slenderman, on top of balancing between fairy tale and urban legend(if there need be a distinction), is probably one of of the first mainstream <i>quantum</i>-based folklore icons. When Slendy started, there was a lot of science bent into pusedo-science around how and what the Slenderman can do is interesting. It felt very Demon-y.<br /> <br /> Who knows, maybe Slendy is the bastard child of the concepts from both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T14:20:19-07:00","id":270356,"title":"","content":"Based on absolutely no inside knowledge whatsoever beyond what I could glean from this forum, I'm beginning to think that Dolarhyde (i.e. the Tooth Fairy) from Red Dragon/Manhunter may be a good model for a Beast, with some tweaks. He was already inhumanly strong and tough (look at the number of shots it took to kill him in Manhunter) and quite cunning; those could be jacked up further. I could also see his teeth (which were prosthetic in the book and films) actually becoming a supernatural feature that he can &quot;pop&quot; as necessary to ruin people. As Dolarhyde becomes more &quot;hungry&quot; and needs to hunt another family, people begin having nightmares about the Great Red Dragon and Will Graham becomes a Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:05:24-07:00","id":270833,"title":"","content":"I never understood the hype for Slenderman, seems like a Onryo with her head shaved and thrown in a suit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:42:43-07:00","id":270866,"title":"","content":"It was watching a new piece of folklore and mythos be spun into popular consciousness and become cemented as a cultural icon. If records remain, people will remember Slendy the way we remember the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> The entire thing is fascinating to watch. It's like watching bacteria grow and expand, except it's culture and society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:29:24-07:00","id":270901,"title":"","content":"Well Slendy already had his own episode of Supernatural. By Geek standards that is common Brothers Grimm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:28:41-07:00","id":270981,"title":"","content":"Slenderman is a tulpa, technically (by supernatural seas 1-2 standard, as well as tibetan myth) I cant remember if he was still one in &quot;his&quot; episode in seas 9. But, being that he is to me, fear of...heck...words/unknown/wild imagination...id say he seems to be a beast...or would tulpas be a beast...dang it, I want more info on Beast! Heading to Matt's twitter page to lurk a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T12:04:23-07:00","id":271017,"title":"","content":"I've got too Page like 9... and Had too Comment or Atleast Speculate.. What if the &quot;Families&quot; or Splats are Primordial Fears &quot;Of&quot; things... and what Dwells in them. Say The Deep, Above, the Dark, the Unknown and &quot;Yourself&quot;(?). Each of those categories leads into being Related more Closely with a &quot;Type&quot; of Supernatural in the WoD and likly a Type of Lair.<br /> Also gives abit of Customization... &quot;Deep&quot; Could be Oceanic or Within the bowels of the Earth, Above well... &quot;Swooping is Bad&quot; Dragon, Bat, Flying Beasty Etc.<br /> <br /> I Don't think Monsters will get a &quot;Hybrid&quot;... Theirs will be the Heroes they Spawn... their Actions Brand or Impact them so much that they become Partially Supernatural and will ALWAYS be able too Sense your Markings on the world around you (Maybe they are &quot;Embeds&quot; or something.. Not Read all of God-Machine yet so.. need to get too it).<br /> <br /> Not too Sure on the &quot;Feeding&quot; Mechanic.. but to me it Makes sense that they Will Feed on two possible things.. The Fear Generated from their Type and possibly from Killing/Eating Prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T12:33:00-07:00","id":271025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=270356#post270356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on absolutely no inside knowledge whatsoever beyond what I could glean from this forum, I'm beginning to think that Dolarhyde (i.e. the Tooth Fairy) from Red Dragon/Manhunter may be a good model for a Beast, with some tweaks. He was already inhumanly strong and tough (look at the number of shots it took to kill him in Manhunter) and quite cunning; those could be jacked up further. I could also see his teeth (which were prosthetic in the book and films) actually becoming a supernatural feature that he can &quot;pop&quot; as necessary to ruin people. As Dolarhyde becomes more &quot;hungry&quot; and needs to hunt another family, people begin having nightmares about the Great Red Dragon and Will Graham becomes a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Hannibal </i>is straight up a show about Beasts and Heroes...but the question is, who's who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:02:38-07:00","id":271088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the &quot;Families&quot; or Splats are Primordial Fears &quot;Of&quot; things... and what Dwells in them. Say The Deep, Above, the Dark, the Unknown and &quot;Yourself&quot;(?). Each of those categories leads into being Related more Closely with a &quot;Type&quot; of Supernatural in the WoD and likly a Type of Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bad, I know is pure speculation but sounds quite solid a concept to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:20:47-07:00","id":271111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=270981#post270981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slenderman is a tulpa, technically (by supernatural seas 1-2 standard, as well as tibetan myth) I cant remember if he was still one in &quot;his&quot; episode in seas 9. But, being that he is to me, fear of...heck...words/unknown/wild imagination...id say he seems to be a beast...or would tulpas be a beast...dang it, I want more info on Beast! Heading to Matt's twitter page to lurk a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thinman (the aforementioned Slenderman expy) is neither; he's a human serial killer and equally human accomplice team inspired by the Thinman myth, which was invented as a joke by the Ghostfacers.<br /> <br /> So...you want Slasher for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T16:39:47-07:00","id":271189,"title":"","content":"Sorry-i shoukd have said that according to what a tulpa is based on tibetan myth and how the season 1 or 2 episode treated it, Slenderman..would be a tulpa. Thinman, from season 9, was a serial killer. Disconnected the actual internet &quot;slenderman&quot; from the thinman episode, the former would be used for beast..I think, while the latter would be slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T16:53:15-07:00","id":271201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=271017#post271017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got too Page like 9... and Had too Comment or Atleast Speculate.. What if the &quot;Families&quot; or Splats are Primordial Fears &quot;Of&quot; things... and what Dwells in them. Say The Deep, Above, the Dark, the Unknown and &quot;Yourself&quot;(?). Each of those categories leads into being Related more Closely with a &quot;Type&quot; of Supernatural in the WoD and likly a Type of Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this a lot. One thing I would note, though, is that The Unknown covers most, if not all, fears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=271017#post271017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not too Sure on the &quot;Feeding&quot; Mechanic.. but to me it Makes sense that they Will Feed on two possible things.. The Fear Generated from their Type and possibly from Killing/Eating Prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I was thinking might be along these lines is that the need that must be Sated might be tied to the old standby of 7 Deadly Sins. Greed to accrue that hoard of gold. Lust to have that maiden sacrifice. Pride to have you ego worshipped. Gluttony to gorge and consume. Wrath for mindless destruction. Envy to sap others of their lives and belongings.<br /> <br /> But then there's Sloth, which is always a weird one. If this is the line that Beast is going down, maybe Sloth would be the ones who sleep and <i>hate </i>being awoken. Not great for player characters, but plenty of space for the ST to play there.<br /> <br /> This doesn't really tie into the whole &quot;nightmare&quot; aspect that seems to be coming out of this, but I thought it was fun enough to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:40:35-07:00","id":271317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=271201#post271201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then there's Sloth, which is always a weird one. If this is the line that Beast is going down, maybe Sloth would be the ones who sleep and <i>hate </i>being awoken. Not great for player characters, but plenty of space for the ST to play there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has this one down. Malignant Sloth isn't so much desire to not do things as complete disconnection from the world and the people in it. Sloth is the vice of true schemers, the kind of people who see the world only as a chessboard and everyone in it as a piece or an annoying rival player. No one to care about, nothing to care for. That Hunger would be raw manipulation, the monster who forms a cult around itself to bring sacrifices of food to it, because it's easier than hunting. If that food is sapient, eh, they're not ones to complain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T12:59:39-07:00","id":271698,"title":"","content":"I agree and disagree, a Slothful person probably wouldn't put the effort and thought into what a chief manipulator would to get people to do things for them, though you'd be correct a Slothful being would rather get others to do their work for them... Though even that would have the bare minimum of effort put into it. Totally agree with you on that cult aspect though, I could see a Sloth being doing that.<br /> Excuse the poke in, I just have a bit of experience with playing a Slothful Possessed from the Inferno book, I had them as a skin and bones person that didn't move much, where the demon that possessed them was more like a chubby non-moving sleepy toad thing, much like Tsathoggua from the Cthulhu Mythos. Now that is a Slothful Beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T03:01:19-07:00","id":272128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=271201#post271201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this a lot. One thing I would note, though, is that The Unknown covers most, if not all, fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Eldritch instead? Personally the one i couldn't think of a name for would be the one that Exempilfies fear of what you could do yourself.. Mirrors isn't really something people fear (Beyond the odd persons phobia) but afair few people fear Self Reflection.. Even more so in the WoD since looking at your own actions might make you out too be more of a Monster then you Think you are.. But that's just speculation. The Eldritch would kinda cover abit of the &quot;Unknown&quot; aswell as the whole God-Machine Unknowable Designs Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurrpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=271201#post271201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I was thinking might be along these lines is that the need that must be Sated might be tied to the old standby of 7 Deadly Sins. Greed to accrue that hoard of gold. Lust to have that maiden sacrifice. Pride to have you ego worshipped. Gluttony to gorge and consume. Wrath for mindless destruction. Envy to sap others of their lives and belongings.<br /> <br /> But then there's Sloth, which is always a weird one. If this is the line that Beast is going down, maybe Sloth would be the ones who sleep and <i>hate </i>being awoken. Not great for player characters, but plenty of space for the ST to play there.<br /> <br /> This doesn't really tie into the whole &quot;nightmare&quot; aspect that seems to be coming out of this, but I thought it was fun enough to post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. if you Use the Sins as the Feeding Grounds.. Pride is honestly self sufficent, and Sloth is Abit.. Meh? Maybe if you borrow the Idea that Sloth Demons had from say Dragon Age... They Made others Lazy and Tired and Gave them good Dreams.. too Keep them Dreaming. The Nightmare part of this would come from having the Dreams be Just &quot;Wrong&quot; enough too let people twig something is wrong with it then let them &quot;Escape&quot; into a New Dream that's nice and Perfect.<br /> <br /> Personally i'd Think Sloth would be great as a &quot;Resting&quot; or Torpor like Mechanic your Sleep is letting the Beast Rest but also Weakening it enough so you can Try and Control it better when you Wake with it.<br /> Hmm if you go with that then Maybe Pride can be what Causes a &quot;Hero&quot; too rise and Hunt you... that Leaves the relativly simple 5 for Feeding.<br /> Greed: Getting &quot;Stuff&quot;, Lust: Having and Working Towards an Object of Affection (Regardless of if it is Returned Affection....), Gluttony: CONSUME. IT. ALL. Wrath: Destruction, Envy: Parasitic living off of others Wealth and Goals.<br /> <br /> Anyway All just Speculation but hopefully good Speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:23:04-07:00","id":272529,"title":"","content":"I'll be happy if there's some way to make your Beast embody the fear of Freedom.<br /> <br /> Of course, fear of the Unknown or the Dark (which I guess can metaphorically stand for fear of the Unknown as well) are ones everyone is expecting, and they'll probably be there in some form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:26:24-07:00","id":272531,"title":"","content":"How, exactly, does one have a fear of freedom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:29:09-07:00","id":272532,"title":"","content":"Some people dependent on others are afraid of being forced to strike it on their own, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:41:25-07:00","id":272544,"title":"","content":"Being afraid of what having no inhibitions can do. Holding yourself back out of concern you may be capable of too much. Hiding away from making choices of your own will because you can't deal with the responsibility. Cowering at the implications that having nothing to tell you what to do also means you have no one or anything to rely on when you're unsure of what to do. The way people always create and flock to hierarchies, unable to persist in meaningful cohabitation without someone to enforce rules, regulations, and everything else that is necessary for society, but restricts one's actions.<br /> <br /> This is brainspew, but the idea is that Beasts are primal fears. And this sounds like a very doable primal fear ingrained into humanity's psyche to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T06:16:52-07:00","id":272897,"title":"","content":"I think the lower down the hierarchy of needs a fear is, the more likely it is to be in the game. As well as the more general, of course. So I think a fear of freedom, spun out the way Katsura and YeOfLittleFaith suggest will be a subset of a fear of isolation - being alone can be feared for many reasons, including the lack of structured hierarchy, but almost everyone fears it for <i>some</i> reason.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I think starvation/deprivation will be one of them. And, yes, the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T08:33:23-07:00","id":272954,"title":"","content":"I think there will be [REDACTED] because Onyx Path love themselves some [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> Also [REDACTED], but I probably shouldn't mention that, lest they unleash cyborg dobermans on me. o.o<br /> <br /> (Seriously, there are a lot of good ideas here.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:31:07-07:00","id":273050,"title":"","content":"How long until fear becomes despair?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T11:48:10-07:00","id":273124,"title":"","content":"huh! I have been sleeping on nwod of late and when I saw this thread I assumed it was another fansplat. what a pleasant surprise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T01:45:46-07:00","id":273534,"title":"","content":"Duh, it's already a megathread, so I'm surprised somebody would mistake it for a fansplat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T04:59:42-07:00","id":273621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=272531#post272531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, exactly, does one have a fear of freedom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also freedom means no restrictions, which means no reason not to do things, which means no excuses when you fail. This is something I see quite frequently in people I know personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T05:42:21-07:00","id":273665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=272531#post272531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, exactly, does one have a fear of freedom?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see a lot of ways in which somebody might fear where freedom might take them. Maybe that's what's meant. Like those guys who have been in jail for so long that it's all they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T20:58:19-07:00","id":285675,"title":"","content":"Since were on Fears here, how can we categorize Unusual Fears in Beast?<br /> <br /> For an example, here's a video on Tryptophobia, or Fear of Small Holes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4OMqoPyerc&amp;list=PLEB4B776204CBE2EC&amp;index=11\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4OMqoPyerc&amp;list=PLEB4B776204CBE2EC&amp;index=11\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4OMqoPyerc&amp;list=PLEB4B776204CBE2EC&amp;index=11\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4OMqoPyerc&amp;list=PLEB4B776204CBE2EC&amp;index=11 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Does this mean that we'll have a Beast that looks like his head is made out of Swiss Cheese like a mobster from the Dick Tracy comics?<br /> <br /> How will these types of Fears be represented in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T07:36:05-07:00","id":286604,"title":"","content":"I think if it were to address every little fear a person can have, it would bog the whole thing down.<br /> Something generic where one could &lt;insert fear here&gt; is likely how this would work to keep things moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T08:14:22-07:00","id":286623,"title":"","content":"I just want to throw in that fear of freedom is actually pretty common, just less with a notion to personal freedom and more to the idea of universal freedom. People tend to react to the idea of anarchy with horror and revulsion, because a world without restrictions is one with a large bunch of bastards willing and able to do what they want.<br /> <br /> A Beast that represents something with no fear of retribution is something that's scary; the usual defenses of civilization don't work against it. It reminds you that there's nothing in the world stopping it - or anyone else - from killing you; no invisible force field made by the police or what have you. A king's army never slays the dragon, after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T11:54:35-07:00","id":287882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A king's army never slays the dragon, after all... </div> </div> </div>And this is when individual hero steps in, though like with some heroes of ancient legends, some of them are as ruthless as those they fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:52:44-07:00","id":293534,"title":"","content":"&quot;We also kinda [don't understand the word] back into the legend of the <b>Mother of Monsters</b>...&quot; [Matthew McFarland]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10