confusing!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be a fantastic rebuttal to something that wasn't &quot;the person you're responding to is referencing this bit of in-universe speculation and so bringing up mythology from another game when oWoD Gangrel are different beasts from nWoD Gangrel is getting multiple degrees of abstraction away from OPP writers talking about evoking Echidna, the Mother of All Monsters, in Beast: the Primordial, the subject of this thread.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can only imagine such a state of affairs at present, though, because the quoted bit was in fact the thing I was saying rather than any faffing about with concern to shared nomenclature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:32:56-07:00","id":293955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=293942#post293942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would be a fantastic rebuttal to something that wasn't &quot;the person you're responding to is referencing this bit of in-universe speculation and so bringing up mythology from another game when oWoD Gangrel are different beasts from nWoD Gangrel is getting multiple degrees of abstraction away from OPP writers talking about evoking Echidna, the Mother of All Monsters, in Beast: the Primordial, the subject of this thread.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can only imagine such a state of affairs at present, though, because the quoted bit was in fact the thing I was saying rather than any faffing about with concern to shared nomenclature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really though, Satchel, we don't have much else though. Just speculation.<br /> <br /> ...So, let's get to that, then.<br /> <br /> The endgame options; I suppose one is manifesting your inner monster, the one that rampages around the dreamscape if it's hungry and frustrated, into the waking world. Another is divorcing yourself from the monster, which ties into Promethean a bit much, but I can see why a Beast might become sick of their Hunger and what it attracts.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm wondering if Beasts can create minions. Because what Hero hasn't carved through dozens of mooks to get to the big prize (and in Beast, been fatally surprised by the mooks' competence and their master becoming directly involved)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:35:06-07:00","id":293958,"title":"","content":"Lol, I planned for Gangrel in my headcanon to be spawned by aspect of Gaia called Mother of Monsters/Lilith, but if that will be considered extraheretical, I can tentatively call the first mortal transformed into a Gangrel Ennoia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:35:44-07:00","id":293959,"title":"","content":"I'm going to paraphrase a really well thought out and well written idea. All apologies to the original author-I'm going to butcher this badly.<br /> <br /> Homebrew is a fantastic part of our culture, but conversations need some directions to work with if they're going to be useful. Any navigator exploring the world needs to begin by having a point of reference.<br /> <br /> In this fantasy world we're all sharing, that point of reference is the canon.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Disregarding certain things, may I also point out about how insane* it is to be homebrewing for a game that isn't even out yet?<br /> <br /> *I'm inclined to say it's fucking insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-27-2014, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:40:55-07:00","id":293964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *I'm inclined to say it's fucking insane. </div> </div> </div>I never said anywhere I'm sane.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:43:27-07:00","id":293966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally