e(Which is also a favorite of mine), and is incredibly fun to watch with anyone regardless of age to boot. You'll be pleased by the ending.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm a little weirded out that that might be my most liked post in this thread.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And in all seriousness, Odile from Swan Lake is one of the two big concepts for my character for Beast, and I hadn't paid much attention to Odile narratively until I saw her expy in the show.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-30-2014, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:03:29-07:00","id":296572,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've been getting back into anime lately after I saw Madoka Magica. I was into it, but then I hit a bit of a period where everything was really derivative and/or predictable and/or stupid, so I drifted off. Then I, almost accidentally, saw Kotoura-san and Madoka Magica, and now I'm right back into it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Already finding it difficult to find new or interesting series', but I've been tapping reviews and such, found a few through there. Hardly 100% strike rate, but enough to keep going","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\