n't work for player beasts. Maybe for a villain beast though. Fear of the Other.<br /> <br /> Also, I think I will be fine if I get to play a best that lives and hunts in the darkness preying on adults. Not out of compassion for children, but to give them a fear of growing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T20:43:24-08:00","id":307114,"title":"","content":"kind of weird beast i thought of last week: beast representing fear of strangers, with a hunger for sex. responsible for a changeling's durance at her grandmother's house. horror concept of little red riding hood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T22:31:13-08:00","id":307196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=306996#post306996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, just read through all 46 pages of this thread...<br /> <br /> I thought of one fear that won't work for player beasts. Maybe for a villain beast though. Fear of the Other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah no. Fear of the other is rooted in fear of strangers...most of whom are perfectly normal people from a different culture, who quite possibly fear you back. It's also the root of prejudice and discrimination.<br /> <br /> Given what we know of Heroes, it's likely you won't find a more <i>protagonist-like </i>potential splat in the world. Especially given the Grendel comparisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:07:06-08:00","id":307286,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how Heroes can potentially link with Hunters of Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T07:25:48-08:00","id":307396,"title":"","content":"Heroes then MIGHT be closer to Reckoning concept of Hunters, because triggered by supernatural stimulus.<br /> <br /> But it's a loose speculation that may be likely proven wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T09:52:01-08:00","id":307527,"title":"","content":"One thing I hope to see is emphasis on the whole &quot;family&quot; aspect of Beast; to the point of making it one of the basic metaphors for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T17:57:10-08:00","id":307696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hunter has pretty even odds of being a protagonist or antagonist, and even when he's the protagonist, the Hunter has a pretty good idea that the story isn't about him, it's about the Vigil. a Hero meanwhile is an antagonist who thinks the story is about him. If I'm right, Captain Hammer from Doctor Horrible and pre-defiant Armsmaster from Worm might be good ideas of what a hero is like. If I'm wrong, eh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems agreeable.<br /> <br /> Hunter's themes is the mortal grey scale. Everything drifts from simple intense intellectual curiosity to threatening exposure, to capture and &quot;containment&quot;, to murder, and lastly, the tortured and atrocities all the while asking just how far will you go. <br /> <br /> They are the Walter E. Kurtz and the Captain Martin Walkers (Spec ops: The Line. Best Hunter story without supernatural monsters), carrying on upon a doomed path, forever alienated for what they know and later, what they've done until they break from the strain.<br /> <br /> Heroes seem more akin to something out of Mirrors. Beloved by society, morally stable, and damn hard to put down.<br /> <br /> Me thinks Heroes as Superman while Hunters are Batmen in themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T18:31:17-08:00","id":307711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=307696#post307696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heroes seem more akin to something out of Mirrors. Beloved by society, morally stable, and damn hard to put down.<br /> <br /> Me thinks Heroes as Superman while Hunters are Batmen in themes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Heroes are the template in Mirrors, and while I don't think the mechanics delve into it, they mention they're based on Greek Heroes, which, y'know, their definition of Heroic deviates from ours.<br /> <br /> So that's worth keeping in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T18:46:43-08:00","id":307718,"title":"","content":"I see heroes as those in the age of heroes. Bellerophon, Cadmus, Perseus, and the like, fighting monsters that simply wanted to be left alone.<br /> In other words, to a &quot;beast&quot; they were murderers.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder if part of the kinship thing originates from the very beginning of Order and Chaos. All that which is considered &quot;monster&quot; is derived from chaos, and it's inability to fit in with the order imposed by the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:30:23-08:00","id":307952,"title":"","content":"^I wanna see more moral ambiguity in the line. Obviously #BeastsDidNothingWrong will make me cringe.<br /> <br /> It is still part of my canon that Nimrod, Herakles and Achilles could be Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T01:08:47-08:00","id":307979,"title":"","content":"As long as beast gives us interesting rules and mechanics for the giant monster/kaiju, wrecking cities trope and enough material for aquatic/reptilian monsters i'm a happy customer.<br /> It's the only horror trope that hasn't yet received proper treatment in either nwod or cwod and the last part my wod needs to be complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T01:14:51-08:00","id":307980,"title":"","content":"^Except it was stated somewhere that there won't be such stuff like blatantly turning into a dragon in a middle of Time Square?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:20:39-08:00","id":307999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=307980#post307980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^Except it was stated somewhere that there won't be such stuff like blatantly turning into a dragon in a middle of Time Square?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not in the corebook.<br /> And if memory serves, it was more along the lines of being able to transform into something not exactly like a dragon but somewhat close yet different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","user":"Bloodspeaker","date":". 11-10-2014, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:37:58-08:00","id":308003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe not in the corebook.<br /> And if memory serves, it was more along the lines of being able to transform into something not exactly like a dragon but somewhat close yet different. </div> </div> </div>I still go by hypothesis it won't be something blatant and the monster form will be something more Uratha warform sized or mix of human and dragon characteristics.<br /> <br /> If dragonlike Beasts descend from actual dragons that will be funny indeed in the context of a Compact I make which members believe themselves to be descendants of Zmei (given there is Beast vs Heroes narrative, in Slavic mythology Zmei dragons mated with humans and spawned monster slaying humans of exceptional strength).<br /> <br /> But at this point we base on scraps of info released anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T04:30:28-08:00","id":308041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=308003#post308003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still go by hypothesis it won't be something blatant and the monster form will be something more Uratha warform sized or mix of human and dragon characteristics.<br /> <br /> If dragonlike Beasts descend from actual dragons that will be funny indeed in the context of a Compact I make which members believe themselves to be descendants of Zmei (given there is Beast vs Heroes narrative, in Slavic mythology Zmei dragons mated with humans and spawned monster slaying humans of exceptional strength).<br /> <br /> But at this point we base on scraps of info released anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We do indeed.<br /> To be honest i half expect and fear that beasts will go the route of werewolf regarding their warforms, with a variety of different/unique characteristics.<br /> But i fervently hope that this will not be the case. It would be a disservice and a missed opportunity for wod in general, to pass up on big, scary monsters (and even bigger, gigantic ones in the endgame) as warforms and &quot;alter-egos&quot; for the PCs regardless of their origin, nature or other characteristics.<br /> <br /> Plus it will have the effect of further distinguishing and reinforcing the Beats position as the common, scary family that links all supers together and fills that last horror niche that begs to be filled.<br /> At least that's the impression i get by reading the title and the scant info we have.<br /> I guess we will see in due time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T05:04:45-08:00","id":308050,"title":"","content":"There is another issue I have with idea of kaiju sized Beasts being an option. A giant monster rampaging is going to attract attention of mortals, and let's face after they in the end defeat the Beast (the bigger they are, the quicker they fall, and military response is IMO worst thing for a supernatural to face) they will start asking questions. Some Compacts and Conspiracies will be more than happy to provide answers, and if giant monsters on a rampage exist, then suddenly idea of vampires and werewolves existing does not feel so outlandish. This would potentially change the setting in a major way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:30:30-08:00","id":308159,"title":"","content":"Maybe some sort of &quot; Aura&quot; like overlay, because of the whole psychic thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:16:15-08:00","id":308226,"title":"","content":"Not explicitly mentioned, but they have the whole rampaging through the dreamscape link to people on a 'psychic' level already, so some kind of feral aura doesn't seem out of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T02:15:31-08:00","id":308904,"title":"","content":"You don't really need kaiju rules, simply use the Scale rules from the Mage Chroniclers Guide, and your beast can smash tanks and swat helicopters from the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T03:32:26-08:00","id":308919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Kat:</b> <br /> Heroes then MIGHT be closer to Reckoning concept of Hunters, because triggered by supernatural stimulus. </div> </div> </div>I did posit to Matt that Heroes sounded like a reaction to all the calls to put Reckoning hunters into Vigil by making them an antagonist to be gobbled up. He replied that it wasn't in his mind when he came up with them but that he wouldn't deny that it occurred to him later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:09:15-08:00","id":308928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did posit to Matt that Heroes sounded like a reaction to all the calls to put Reckoning hunters into Vigil by making them an antagonist to be gobbled up. He replied that it wasn't in his mind when he came up with them but that he wouldn't deny that it occurred to him later. </div> </div> </div>If I feel like running more outlandish Hunters, I apply Dudes of Legends update.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T07:08:24-08:00","id":309080,"title":"","content":"No, no kaiju.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T07:14:55-08:00","id":309088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=308050#post308050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is another issue I have with idea of kaiju sized Beasts being an option. A giant monster rampaging is going to attract attention of mortals, and let's face after they in the end defeat the Beast (the bigger they are, the quicker they fall, and military response is IMO worst thing for a supernatural to face) they will start asking questions. Some Compacts and Conspiracies will be more than happy to provide answers, and if giant monsters on a rampage exist, then suddenly idea of vampires and werewolves existing does not feel so outlandish. This would potentially change the setting in a major way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is indeed a valid concern, and kaiju monsters will surely destroy a setting that is not made to accommodate them from the beginning.<br /> So the question is if this is the game that will attempt something like that. If it does, it will certainly be very different from every other gameline that came before, one could say it would be quite subversive... :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","user":"Bloodspeaker","date":". 11-12-2014, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T07:16:20-08:00","id":309089,"tit