com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:54:22-08:00","id":387152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=386511#post386511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you mean Eclipses, sir!</div> </div> </div> </div>Err Probably... the ones that can Barter for extra Powers from Spirits and other things.<br /> (It's Been awhile since i Read/got the nerve too play Exalted) Funnily this puts them in the &quot;Oh God Yes!&quot; Category too Play/Run a game with in my Brain... Along with Princess the Hopeful.... Hmm.. Now how too do a Beast/Princess Crossover... (It could go so Wrong...)<br /> On a Side Side note is it just me or do the Second Passes of each of the Editions feel much more.. Interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T02:29:03-08:00","id":387178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=387152#post387152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Funnily this puts them in the &quot;Oh God Yes!&quot; Category too Play/Run a game with in my Brain... Along with Princess the Hopeful.... Hmm.. Now how too do a Beast/Princess Crossover... (It could go so Wrong...)<br /> On a Side Side note is it just me or do the Second Passes of each of the Editions feel much more.. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...Beasts and Magical Girls...is it wrong that I'd not be surprised if there is an anime that's already done something similar. Just hedging my bets on the likely hundreds of different magical girl animes that exist. If ArcaneArts reappears on this thread he maybe able to give us an example, is anime knowledge far surpasses my own. <br /> <br /> As for your take on Second Edition NWoD games vs their First Edition versions. I'd say that there are a number of factors involved.<br /> <br /> - With the Anniversary stuff for CWoD the NWoD does not need to adhere to some of the ideas its big-brother gameline pioneered back in the 90's.<br /> - I'd also say that the aim with the First Editions was to make settings that were very modular but had a default for you to run with. <br /> <br /> I think the Second Editions have more creative distance from their CWoD predecessors as a result and this makes them more unique in style while providing interesting alternative takes on supernatural types. Likewise, I think 8 years of the NWoD provided a lot of feedback for the earlier lines and has allowed the devs to really soak in the strengths and weaknesses of each line. As such the second editions can play up the stronger points of their game line and also address the weaknesses of the previous edition.<br /> <br /> I liked First Edition Requiem for example, but I adore Second Edition as pretty much a perfect alternative to VtM as a Vampire roleplay game. Promethean (a game I loved in its First Edition, but acknowledge was deeply flawed in some design elements) appears to be infinately more playable in the Second Edition from what we've seen of the previews as well. Demon hand-down became my joint favourite (with Vampire) game as soon as it was released because it felt like a Second Edition book straight away (very evocative, a very different take on its source material and very different from its CWoD predecessor)<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm no fan of Werewolf and for a while Second Edition of that had me almost won over that I might find the game interesting enough to run. Nearly, not quite though. Lets put it this way. I don't expect the Second Editions of say Changeling or Giest to win me over (much in the same way SE Werewolf didn't) but I expect them to be at least more interesting takes on their source material. Now SE Hunter and Mummy those are things I am really looking forward too. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I think all that makes the Second Editions more &quot;interesting&quot; and well as just having a better mechanics system on the whole and do more interesting things with it then any of the First Eds did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T03:06:35-08:00","id":387185,"title":"","content":"For me that's sorta the case aswell. Mage Doesn't Interest me.. Yes it has some Awesome background Fluff and PLENTY of Story Hooks... But.. The First Edition just.. i don't know.. (It could be that i just don't Like the whole Mage package, I Didn't really like it in OWoD either.. Again Loved the Fluff but.. something about the Actual Play was abit off to me). 1st Ed Requiem was great but.. everything seemed to be to much about calling/getting Nostalgia from the OWoD, well atleast in my Opinion.<br /> <br /> Werewolf... Yeah OWoD was awesome for it's feel but it was just too OP compared to the rest of the lines. For some reason my Favorite first Ed of the NWoD was oddly Changeling it was funny considering just How far a difference it was from the first Ed.<br /> <br /> Anyway.. No more derailing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's 