"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:41:00-08:00","id":400803,"title":"","content":"Evolve has me really wanting to play a kaiju Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:38:26-08:00","id":400990,"title":"","content":"I was about to argue that ancient Babylon would be a great setting for Beast, where humanity was building societies that kept their fears at bay, but then I realized that at least one of the Breeds traces their roots there and it very well could be discussed in the splatbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:18:21-08:00","id":401053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=400990#post400990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to argue that ancient Babylon would be a great setting for Beast, where humanity was building societies that kept their fears at bay, but then I realized that at least one of the Breeds traces their roots there and it very well could be discussed in the splatbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient Greece would be nice as well.<br /> Or portuguese and spanish settlers in South America running into monsters in the florests of the New World.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:33:09-08:00","id":402053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=401053#post401053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ancient Greece would be nice as well.<br /> Or portuguese and spanish settlers in South America running into monsters in the florests of the New World.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As a brazillian dude,seeing settlers have their ass kicked by eldritch monsters sounds goods to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:57:50-08:00","id":406324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=400990#post400990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to argue that ancient Babylon would be a great setting for Beast, where humanity was building societies that kept their fears at bay, but then I realized that at least one of the Breeds traces their roots there and it very well could be discussed in the splatbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enkidu embodied the &quot;Wildman&quot; as he was raised by beasts..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T11:37:51-08:00","id":406874,"title":"","content":"If it's anime inspiration, every time I hear about monsters who are the embodiments of Fear and are in Families, I flash back to the series, Nura: Rise of the Yokai Clan. What's interesting is that Nuraliyion (?) is so badass that his mere presence makes other yokai pause in fear, and once upon a time, he actually has a friendship with someone whose profession is hunting creatures like them, lasting past the friend's death. You have to be an Legendary Beast to create Kinships with Heroes and not get killed. You got to check it out.<br /> <br /> Since we are talking about Dark Era errata for Beast, what era would be good for them?<br /> <br /> And finally, I hope that the Fears of Race/Gender/Creed get played down or disallowed because after I read this article, I'm starting to think that these would be the Lairs of Beasts who are part of what a bigot fears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://gizmodo.com/oregon-was-founded-as-a-racist-utopia-1539567040\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://gizmodo.com/app/uploads/2025/10/gizmodo-social-1200x675-1.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://gizmodo.com/oregon-was-founded-as-a-racist-utopia-1539567040\" target=\"_blank\"> Oregon Was Founded As a Racist Utopia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://gizmodo.com/oregon-was-founded-as-a-racist-utopia-1539567040\" target=\"_blank\"> http://gizmodo.com/oregon-was-founded-as-a-racist-utopia-1539567040 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> When Oregon was granted statehood in 1859, it was the only state in the Union admitted with a constitution that forbade black people from living, working, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T11:41:52-08:00","id":406875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=406874#post406874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, I hope that the Fears of Race/Gender/Creed get played down or disallowed because after I read this article, I'm starting to think that these would be the Lairs of Beasts who are part of what a bigot fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the game remotely represents fears of race, gender, or creed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T13:04:02-08:00","id":406933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=406874#post406874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's anime inspiration, every time I hear about monsters who are the embodiments of Fear and are in Families, I flash back to the series, Nura: Rise of the Yokai Clan. What's interesting is that Nuraliyion (?) is so badass that his mere presence makes other yokai pause in fear, and once upon a time, he actually has a friendship with someone whose profession is hunting creatures like them, lasting past the friend's death. You have to be an Legendary Beast to create Kinships with Heroes and not get killed. You got to check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda hope they minimize the anime-distilled monster influence on Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T14:03:38-08:00","id":406959,"title":"","content":"Netflix has Nightbreed: the Directors Cut currently, so I just watched it. The movie itself is a classic, centering mostly around a place called Midian, the place where the Monsters go, and Boone, a guy who thinks he committed a whole bunch of murders and thus belongs there. Midian itself feels like it would be an amazing shared Lair. The monsters all all varied and individual, but also a part of a larger family of monsters that all trace their lineages back to legends of precursor races(&quot;the Tribes of the Moon&quot;) that over time have been wiped out. Led by a deranged psychiatrist/masked lunatic killer, Midian is eventually discovered by the worst monsters of all: redneck cops who think they are heroes.<br /> <br /> I feel like I am going to be drawing a lot of inspiration from that movie when I play Beast. It totally should have gotten the sequel that the end was so obviously setting up for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 02-15-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:29:15-08:00","id":407270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=406959#post406959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Netflix has Nightbreed: the Directors Cut currently, so I just watched it. The movie itself is a classic, centering mostly around a place called Midian, the place where the Monsters go, and Boone, a guy who thinks he committed a whole bunch of murders and thus belongs there. Midian itself feels like it would be an amazing shared Lair. The monsters all all varied and individual, but also a part of a larger family of monsters that all trace their lineages back to legends of precursor races(&quot;the Tribes of the Moon&quot;) that over time have been wiped out. Led by a deranged psychiatrist/masked lunatic killer, Midian is eventually discovered by the worst monsters of all: redneck cops who think they are heroes.<br /> <br /> I feel like I am going to be drawing a lot of inspiration from that movie when I play Beast. It totally should have gotten the sequel that the end was so obviously setting up for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man I am so behind...I didn't know that they finally released the extended version.<br /> <br /> The original storyline is inspiring for Beast. As opposed to the movie that was released, which was just sad. The movie was originally 145 minutes long, which was cut to 102 minutes. The extended version is I think nearly 160 minutes. I really need to see that version!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T07:43:57-08:00","id":408947,"title":"","content":"I seriously think it would be a gameline where we plays mortals who get animal (maybe cryptids ones) powers/mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:32:15-08:00","id":410205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=406933#post406933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div