gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=388126#post388126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I would like to see it too, but we can push for a Beast Dark Era PDF(or more than one)as a stretch goal when Beast gets Kickstarted right? No need to be dissappointed.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping for that and a new &quot;chapter&quot; for Hunter: Mortal Remains as a stretch goal pdf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:29:23-08:00","id":431256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=430964#post430964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Brock Lesnar is a Beast representing the fear of German Suplexes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Truly the most terrifying of all fears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:38:02-08:00","id":431574,"title":"","content":"Er, I just thought of something:<br /> <br /> How are Beasts different from werewolves as of 2E, given how Uratha are...not particularly human in the &quot;basic respect for life&quot; aspect? They're probably the most alien PCs we've had yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:47:36-08:00","id":431587,"title":"","content":"I imagine that entire &quot;I stalk you in waking and dreaming&quot; thing pushes it into new territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:13:54-08:00","id":431699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=431587#post431587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that entire &quot;I stalk you in waking and dreaming&quot; thing pushes it into new territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely; the Cahalith have Dream Hunter as a three-dot Facet, but it's unique to them.<br /> <br /> One difference that springs to mind is that where the werewolves have an affinity for the Shadow, Beasts are creatures of the dreamscape, it being where their Beast-souls dwell. And speaking of the Beast-soul, the Uratha don't have one of their aspects prone to running amuck if not satisfied.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:37:42-08:00","id":431721,"title":"","content":"New Spoilers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matthew McFarland, on RPGnet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As for this thread, I want to let you guys know: </span></span><b>Beast</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> is in development now. That means I'm not going to talk about a lot of specific systems, because those change. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Overall, though? Beasts (the Children, or the Begotten if you're feeling formal) are descendants of a great and beautiful legacy. They're their Mother's children, born of the dark, iconic nightmares that human beings have had since before they had the language to describe them. Their family is vast, and includes the werewolf hunting under the moon, the vampire drinking blood in the alley, the Promethean fleeing the mob, the changeling hiding from her former captors. Where's the Beast in that?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Beast is pointing to the werewolf's prey, smiling and drinking in the fear. He's watching the mouth of the alley so the vampire can feed in peace. He's the one that steps in front of that mob and calls down lightning, or opens up his Lair so the changeling can rest. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Of course, that's not what the Hero would say. The Hero would say that the Beast is a monster, that he hunts people down and causes nightmares, terrorizes people, steals from them. The Hero would say the Beast is the monster in the darkness, the dragon in the cave, the kraken in the boundless deeps. But this isn't the Hero's story, so, y'know, fuck that guy.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:45:02-08:00","id":431731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=431699#post431699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not entirely; the Cahalith have Dream Hunter as a three-dot Facet, but it's unique to them.<br /> <br /> One difference that springs to mind is that where the werewolves have an affinity for the Shadow, Beasts are creatures of the dreamscape, it being where their Beast-souls dwell. And speaking of the Beast-soul, the Uratha don't have one of their aspects prone to running amuck if not satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>One fifth of a populace doing stuff in dreams does not a <s>changeling</s> beast make. Vampires also have a sliver of people who can muck around dreams, but that pales to &quot;My buddies, and their buddies, and their bitches all gather together on the weekend to rampage through people's dreams so we can laugh at the morning news about a city shitting itself in the middle of the night&quot; being a seeming possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T23:05:20-08:00","id":432333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=431731#post431731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One fifth of a populace doing stuff in dreams does not a <s>changeling</s> beast make. Vampires also have a sliver of people who can muck around dreams, but that pales to &quot;My buddies, and their buddies, and their bitches all gather together on the weekend to rampage through people's dreams so we can laugh at the morning news about a city shitting itself in the middle of the night&quot; being a seeming possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rampages tends to bring out the &quot;you're a little fish in a vast ocean&quot; reminders.<br /> <br /> It could always get worse. You could be giving the local Free Council Mastigos ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T23:30:58-08:00","id":432337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matthew McFarland, on RPGnet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>...I want to do all of those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:41:55-08:00","id":432408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=431721#post431721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As for this thread, I want to let you guys know: </span></span><b>Beast</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> is in development now. That means I'm not going to talk about a lot of specific systems, because those change. </span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Overall, though? Beasts (the Children, or the Begotten if you're feeling formal) are descendants of a great and beautiful legacy. They're their Mother's children, born of the dark, iconic nightmares that human beings have had since before they had the language to describe them. Their family is vast, and includes the werewolf hunting under the moon, the vampire drinking blood in the alley, the Promethean fleeing the mob, the changeling hiding from her former captors. Where's the Beast in that?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Beast is pointing to the werewolf's prey, smiling and drinking in the fear. He's watching the mouth of the alley so the vampire can feed in peace. He's the one that steps in front of that mob and calls down lightning, or opens up his Lair so the changeling can rest. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Of course, that's not what the Hero would say. The Hero would say that the Beast is a monster, that he hunts people down and causes nightmares, terrorizes people, steals from them. The Hero would say the Beast is the monster in the darkness, the dragon in the cave, the kraken in the boundless deeps. But this isn't the Hero's story, so, y'know, fuck that guy.</span></span><br /> [/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>From this.... I make them too be the Opressive Feeling of Fear in the World once you've seen into the darkness. The &quot;Darkness&quot; of the World of Darkness.<br /> They Care for their Family, even if the family is Full of Serial Killers and rampaging Monsters.. but ya 'know you can't Pick your Family. Blood is thicker then Water and sometimes the Children need to be protected. Besides... The Family helps each other... Like a Giant Monster Mafia...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T08:10:16-07:00","id":432624,"title":"","content":"Beasts are their Mother's children... mmmmm.... I'm wanting to get my hands on Beast now just for some ideas for my Circle of the Crone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:37:04-07:00","id":432673,"title":"","content":"I kinda want to see a &quot;Mother of all monsters&quot; type beast with regenerative abilities and kinship powers that boil down to making their blood extra delicious and nutritious to Vampires, giving major returns for vitae gained per lethal damage inflicted, as a twisted and terrifying perversion of a mother nursing her children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:45:51-07:00","id":432680,"title":"","content":"I've been getting the impression, based on the Crossover play, that all beasts will have something along those lines. Granted, probably for everyone, not just vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:05:19-07:00","id":432769,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that leeches won't be feeding off them so much as getting fed upon instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","a