other supernaturals&quot; power keyed into Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:35:16-07:00","id":433318,"title":"","content":"I would like to think that the level of a beast is a bit more scaled to being more closer to scion level. And scions just scrape leeches off of their collective boots...<br /> As I see it, at best leeches should walk softly around them, figuratively speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:01:13-07:00","id":433421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433318#post433318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to think that the level of a beast is a bit more scaled to being more closer to scion level. And scions just scrape leeches off of their collective boots...<br /> As I see it, at best leeches should walk softly around them, figuratively speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a vwery funCrossover game if one guy is way stronger than everybody else, and Beasts are specifically designed for crossovers.<br /> <br /> Once more:the other Supernaturals are the Beasts family. The beasts have powers called &quot;Kinship&quot; that revolve around imitating and suporting other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> What you'd like to think is wrong, based entirely on literally everything we know about Beast so far.<br /> <br /> sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:23:16-07:00","id":433452,"title":"","content":"There in lies the rub, at least as I see things so far; Beasts can be every frightening thing not just to human, but also the boogeyman of supernaturals as well. It seems to me that those other critters aren't the worry to Beasts. Instead plain vanilla mortal humans have ever been their Achilles Heel. Those we call &quot;heroes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:35:27-07:00","id":433459,"title":"","content":"You're missing the point: Beasts are not, antagonist by default to other Supernaturals, and in fact seem to be more likely to help them, based on what we just read.<br /> <br /> &quot;Kinship&quot; Powers are meant to support, interact with, or imitate other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> What better way for a &quot;Mother of monster&quot; type Beast to support her vampire allies then by making her blood extra yummy to said vampire allies, in a twisted and horrific parody of a mother nursing her children?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:18:53-07:00","id":433509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433459#post433459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing the point: Beasts are not, antagonist by default to other Supernaturals, and in fact seem to be more likely to help them, based on what we just read.<br /> <br /> &quot;Kinship&quot; Powers are meant to support, interact with, or imitate other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> What better way for a &quot;Mother of monster&quot; type Beast to support her vampire allies then by making her blood extra yummy to said vampire allies, in a twisted and horrific parody of a mother nursing her children?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does make me wonder what the &quot;demisplat&quot; will be (like ghouls to vampires, Wolf-Blooded to werewolves, alchemists to Prometheans) will be. I assume the game wants to be standalone, so I'd expect microtemplates like David's psychic vampires-examples of minor, weird supernaturals just different enough from humans to be valid for Kinship powers. Would help bring in themes of extended family without necessitating crossovers.<br /> <br /> Also, mad scientist Beasts making microtemplates themselves. Do want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-08-2015, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:27:35-07:00","id":433543,"title":"","content":"I'm betting one of those kinship powers is to boost other supernaturals ability to extract supernatural energy. So in the presence of a beast morals blood gets thinker making them more tempting for vampires, thier emotions run deeper making the mortals emotions easier to harvest for changelings, and locii produce more essence and so on. So its not so much that supernatural brings feed on the beast as the beast enriches the feeding ground as it were.<br /> <br /> i hope beast will work with Changeling 2.0<br /> <br /> Also beast seems to be the antihunter setting, the polar opposite themetically. Beast sound like both a setting, and something you could add to other settings, to enchance say a vampire or mage game or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:16:36-07:00","id":433683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433543#post433543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also beast seems to be the antihunter setting, the polar opposite themetically. Beast sound like both a setting, and something you could add to other settings, to enchance say a vampire or mage game or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Could see a Beast Supporting some Sects of Hunters... And i Can Imagine that a Beast that loves bringing Fear to the Monsters that are it's Family, Everyone has a Big Scary Uncle/Brother/Sister that they just don't want too see coming around too Visit.<br /> I Can also see it as a Beast that Stalks the various Splats too &quot;Show them how too be a Real Monster&quot;.... Basically i see them as being useful for all Splats.. As both Support and Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T04:43:49-07:00","id":433794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433543#post433543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also beast seems to be the antihunter setting, the polar opposite themetically. Beast sound like both a setting, and something you could add to other settings, to enchance say a vampire or mage game or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, there are at least some Hunters who are &quot;part of the family&quot;, like the Lucifuge or any Wolf-Blooded Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:03:16-07:00","id":433800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433509#post433509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does make me wonder what the &quot;demisplat&quot; will be (like ghouls to vampires, Wolf-Blooded to werewolves, alchemists to Prometheans) will be. I assume the game wants to be standalone, so I'd expect microtemplates like David's psychic vampires-examples of minor, weird supernaturals just different enough from humans to be valid for Kinship powers. Would help bring in themes of extended family without necessitating crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemists aren't really a demi-splat; they're antagonists.<br /> <br /> I think micro-templates would be cool, though, but I like the Dread Power route 2nd Edition seems to be taking. I imagine any demi-splat for <b>Beast</b>, though, would be like Wolf-blooded where you fill out the Beast's extended family if you don't have access to the other gamelines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:05:48-07:00","id":434212,"title":"","content":"No immediate plans for a demi-splat. Maybe in the Players Guide, if I come up with something I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:09:53-07:00","id":434504,"title":"","content":"I always assumed Heroes were the demi-splat.<br /> <br /> But my mind works in funny ways on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:38:25-07:00","id":434571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=433794#post433794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, there are at least some Hunters who are &quot;part of the family&quot;, like the Lucifuge or any Wolf-Blooded Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>To create an analogy: Heroes and Hunters are like people who go to the same high school. There are other schools representing other splats but Heroes and Hunters are in the biggest one called Humanity. Heroes are the cocky jocks who everyone loves and everyone adores. They are the small town, home grown heroes that everyone loves.<br /> <br /> Hunters are the weird kids that no one seems to understand or does anyone care to. &quot;What's that about monsters? oh alright, bless your heart. Did you see Bobby Jenkin's play last night?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampire infestation get's nipped in the bud, they don't care.<br /> <br /> Werewolf rampage around the area. &quot;Did you see Jenkin catch that ball?! It was amazing!&quot;<br /> <br /> So on and so forth. Issues become worse if the Hero is actively involved in the Vigil. They fuck up well laid plans that get thrown into disarray due to the Hero's involvement, they demand they control how the cell moves and when the smoke clears, it was clearly they, not the cell, who gets the credit (even if the cell has lost members).<br /> <br /> This leads to issues and now we come to the last part of the analogy.<br /> <br /> Heros and Hunters are not the only roles in the school. Eventually the last role creeps in. The role of the Slasher.<br /> <br /> After all, school shootings are a sad fact of life now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 03-09-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:31:39-07:00","id":434725,"title":"","content":"Heroes are Captain Hammer. The jackass who thinks the story is about them and ruins the lives of others in an attempt to gain glory for themselves.<br /> <br /> The hunter is the guy with half a clue trying to do what he thinks is right and knows full well this is bigger than he is. Even when he screws up it's not out of malice, at least not totally.<br /> <br /> slashers are hard to place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:18:57-07:00","id":434796,"title":"","content":"Slashers are the Quiet Kids in the School who sit alone and Always get bullied... But never React. Never let it get too them.. Until they are Ready. Then the School Will Burn.<br /> <br /> I'd Personally like to have Beasts with no Demi-Splat... Instead they can make the other Demi-Splats easier too &quot;make&quot; or Control... or Whatever.... Sorta Like a Mid-Wife/Nurse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:49:45-07:00","id":435504,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder how 2E Hunter will address the issue of Beast - whether &quot;Heroes&quot; and Hunters are overlapping categories or fundamentally mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> I stand by wanting a &quot;new Mortal Remains chapter&quot; as a pdf stretch goal for Beast (along with a Dark Era).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T03:01:02-07:00","id":435506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=435504#post435504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by wanting a &quot;new Mortal Remains chapter&quot; as a pdf stretch goal for Beast (along with a Dark Era).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, those would be (in my eyes) Great Stretch goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T03:50:27-07:00","id":435527,"title":"","content":"It's starting to sound like Heroes are people who are subconsciously driven to antagonize a Beast when they've been affected by the Beast's 'Wasteland/Nimbus/Unease Sybaris' Hunger/dreamscape thing. I'm beginning to wonder if the Heroes' delusion that their conflict is <i>their</i> story is actually represented by some kind of mechanic, too.<br /> <br /> With the caveat that Hunters are all kinds of people from all kinds of life, I think Hunters make a <i>desperate choice</i> in beginning their Vigil whereas Heroes <i>subconsciously fight for delusional glory</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T04:38:01-07:00","id":435540,"title":"","content":"That'd be sort of a neat thematic divide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:12:27-07:00","id":435712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=435527#post435527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's starting to sound like Heroes are people who are subconsciously driven to antagonize a Beast when they've been affected by the Beast's 'Wasteland/Nimbus/Unease Sybaris' Hunger/dreamscape thing. I'm beginning to wonder if the Heroes' delusion that their conflict is <i>their</i> story is actually represented by some kind of mechanic, too.<br /> <br /> With the caveat that Hunters are all kinds of people from all kinds of life, I think Hunters make a <i>desperate choice</i> in beginning their Vigil whereas Heroes <i>subconsciously fight for delusional glory</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I've been thinking that it's more along the lines of humanity's desire to dominate nature, and to be the top apex predator. And that means eliminating all challengers, especially when the subconscious kicks in. Because then insanity can result.<br /> <br /> hmf...Perseus is no courageous hero defending/protecting the weak killing the sleeping Medusa in her cave. He's more a despicable assassin.<br /> <br /> Ruminating a bit;<br /> Hunger is a &quot;void.&quot; A &quot;vacuum&quot; that needs to be filled. As the darkness desires light and color. But it also could be like fire, unquenchable, untamable, constantly consuming. How similar humanity can be. Can &quot;gluttony&quot; exist in such a paradigm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:28:42-07:00","id":435999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=434212#post434212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No immediate plans for a demi-splat. Maybe in the Players Guide, if I come up with something I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd have to be something you can call a Beauty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=435712#post435712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I've been thinking that it's more along the lines of humanity's desire to dominate nature, and to be the top apex predator. And that means eliminating all challengers, especially when the subconscious kicks in. Because then insanity can result.<br /> <br /> hmf...Perseus is no courageous hero defending/protecting the weak killing the sleeping Medusa in her cave. He's more a despicable assassin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although he was when he rescued Andromeda from a sea monster. Heroes think it's all about them - and they're wrong - but it may be a mistake to think that must always make them bad guys as such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:18:11-07:00","id":436253,"title":"","content":"At that point he had the gods paying him a lot of attention and giving/loaning him some nice goodies. I have to wonder if he was really being a hero or if he was simply feeding his own ego. <i>&quot;Damsel in distress? Step aside, I got this...&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:39:17-07:00","id":436456,"title":"","content":"i think there are many way to do a interesting crossover with Beast and Promethean. We know that some Prometheans study the monsters because they want to learn about humanity by analysing which is not human. but i think a Promethean can learn more from a Beast than from other monsters. because Beast are all about Fear,they are the things every single human being is scared of. and here's the thing about Humans,Humans are defined by fear. fear guides so many of Human's actions,more often than not,the things a human fear are the base of their personality. So a promethean could learn many things about manking by being close to Beasts<br /> BUT. that raises an important question. does the Beasts would want to support th pilgrimage? after all,Prometheans are the Beast's family,A reedemed promethean is not family anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-10-2015, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:57:10-07:00","id":436537,"title":"","content":"...huh.<br /> <br /> That question is very interesting. Too interesting.<br /> I think the official answer is 'It depends on who's asking &amp; who's answering, everyone is an individual' etc. Which in turn implies that Beasts as a splat don't know about the pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:55:36-07:00","id":436570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=435506#post435506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, those would be (in my eyes) Great Stretch goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just temper that thought with the fact that it has not been decided one way or the other if <b>Beast</b> will go up on Kickstarter or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T03:30:19-07:00","id":436873,"title":"","content":"Considering how well Demon and Mummy did, it would be kind of weird if it didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T04:37:07-07:00","id":436894,"title":"","content":"New mini-spoiler:<br /> <br /> Matt said on RPGnet that if you are scared from Gozilla because you feel powerless before it, then its Family would be Anakim (named after a race of Old Testament giants).<br /> <br /> EDIT: We have 2 out of 5? now: Anakim and Namtaru (fear of powerlesness and fear of death? inevitability? respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T04:56:55-07:00","id":436904,"title":"","content":"I think the standard is that new nWoD lines and 20th anniversary cWoD books (along with choice others?) all get Kickstarters. The former to get people interested in a new game and also provide a nice hardcover copy of the book like days of yore; the latter to let people know their favorite game of yore is getting more attention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T07:33:22-07:00","id":437042,"title":"","content":"What we know from previous interviews: <br /> fear of dark (Namtaru, I believe) <br /> fear of something pouncing on you and eating you<br /> fear of being yanked down under water and drowned<br /> fear of being watched","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T07:46:58-07:00","id":437054,"title":"","content":"hmm...fear lords...I'm reminded again of Marvel:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://marvel.wikia.com/Category:Fear_Lords_members\" target=\"_blank\">Fear Lord Members</a><br /> <br /> Still, Nyx (Greek Goddess of Night) was the mother of most of humanity's fears. Nightmare, fate, death, nemesis, deceit, age, strife.<br /> Of course, she was also the mother of some good things as well; the Day, sleep...and his family of dreams (a god we all worship whether we like it or not), and in one story, she was the mother of Eros.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:34:18-07:00","id":437116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=437042#post437042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we know from previous interviews:<br /> fear of dark (Namtaru, I believe)<br /> fear of something pouncing on you and eating you<br /> fear of being yanked down under water and drowned<br /> fear of being watched</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like the Primal Fears are a little more generalized than that. Think of the Thresholds in Geist. Probably less fear of the dark, which is pretty narrow in scope, and more fear of the unknown. The examples of things pouncing down on you and drowning you are likely specific examples of a more general concept. Maybe the fear of being hunted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:48:48-07:00","id":437134,"title":"","content":"I wasn't stating my personal opinion, I was paraphrasing interviews with Matt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:02:56-07:00","id":437151,"title":"","content":"So, for sure we know the Families are: Fear of dark(Unknown?)<br /> <br /> Fear of being eaten like a prey animal<br /> <br /> Fear of drowning<br /> <br /> Fear of being watched.<br /> <br /> and Fear of being powerless.<br /> <br /> And Godzilla is given as an Example of Powerlessness.<br /> <br /> Sounds like fun<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:18:05-07:00","id":437273,"title":"","content":"Over at the Beast spoiler thread on RPG.net, BHM revealed that Lairs can lead to otherworldly places. So, here's my prediction for how Beast deals with turning into a giant monster (because let's face it, being able to turn into a giant monster would be awesome): In your Lair, have fun. If you evoke the fear of being dragged underwater and drowned, in your Lair you can actually be a kraken in the depths, with your Lair providing a suitable environment for that. If a Hero (or anyone else) chooses to fight you in your Lair, they have to fight an actual dragon, or kraken, or whatever. Presumably, Heroes are drawn to your Lair to confront you and have powers of their own that let them put up a credible fight. Also, apparently you can rampage around in people's collective dreams as a true monster, although what good this does you is dubious given that this apparently is how Heroes are made.<br /> <br /> Outside of your Lair you can call on powers that are reminiscent of your monstrous form, but you can't actually become a dragon in the middle of Times Square.<br /> <br /> Just my prediction. We'll see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:43:03-07:00","id":437294,"title":"","content":"At the least, you appear to have the power to control how hostile it is, since it's been suggested that you can use it to hide Changelings.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not sure if this has been mentioned, but apparently Lairs aren't Merits, but part of the template. I actually wonder if Lairs are the new Begotten's &quot;dreamscape&quot;(wether or not this is the Tenemos I leave up to you) spun off into its own little pocket dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:00:04-07:00","id":437307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=436253#post436253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point he had the gods paying him a lot of attention and giving/loaning him some nice goodies. I have to wonder if he was really being a hero or if he was simply feeding his own ego. <i>&quot;Damsel in distress? Step aside, I got this...&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't doubt his ego, but considering what he was fighting, courage is something I can't help but grant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as I just said on RPGNet's thread on the subject: I suspect good and evil won't figure much in the dynamics of Beasts and Heroes, outside of the Heroes' delusions of grandeur. If any morals apply, it'll the kind of things that accrued supernatural consequence in old Greek myths - kinship counts, don't betray hospitality as guest or host, and keep your promises - everything else is the scrim we use to function, and Beasts need very different things to function than do humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=437294#post437294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the least, you appear to have the power to control how hostile it is, since it's been suggested that you can use it to hide Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Matt said Beasts can &quot;give out the keys.&quot;<br /> <br /> He also said that Beasts have a &quot;Homecoming&quot; (capitalisation his) when they discover their nature and their Lair.<br /> <br /> Oh, also on the RPGNet thread, someone wondered if <i>Belle</i> might be a hero - someone determined to save a Beast from themselves, in defiance of what the Beast is and wants.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:06:40-07:00","id":438357,"title":"","content":"So, in relation to Beasts shapechanging, Matt has (cryptically) stated that they've done splats with alternate forms a lot (see, e.g., werewolves), and that they're doing something &quot;a little different&quot; with Beasts. No idea what that means, but it doesn't seem to bode well for my previous theory.<br /> <br /> However, Matt also revealed that Beasts aren't prevented from remaining in their human lives, although they still have to sate their Hunger. This brings me back to the idea I had before that Frances Dolarhyde could be a source of inspiration for a Beast. He's undeniably a person struggling with something monstrous inside him, the Great Red Dragon that has a Hunger for love and change that must be sated, and Dolarhyde (at least in <i>Manhunter</i>) arguably demonstrates some measure of low-level powers. It's not a perfect 1:1 matchup with the little we know about Beasts (i.e., we never see a Great Red Dragon rampaging through the dreams of people in St. Louis), but I just get that vibe off of what Matt is saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:52:14-07:00","id":438387,"title":"","content":"So.. I guess no Transformation when not in there Lair maybe. Maybe a &quot;Projection&quot; or the implication if your Hungry... but no Overt Transformations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T08:38:30-07:00","id":438442,"title":"","content":"Maybe some shapeshifter-like powers but not an innate ability ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T15:30:28-07:00","id":438971,"title":"","content":"A game called &quot;Beast&quot; with no shapeshifting abilities? That doesn't sound right...Yeah, I understand that in today's world (Darkness or no) that it would be dangerous to reveal oneself in all one's glory. But...I admit to being leery of having a &quot;hunger&quot; that equates to something that may be psychopathic, or sadistic. Or for that matter to have something that relies overmuch on the psychological side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:47:29-07:00","id":439427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=438387#post438387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.. I guess no Transformation when not in there Lair maybe. Maybe a &quot;Projection&quot; or the implication if your Hungry... but no Overt Transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like this idea. Some kind of projected form that's optionally controlled by the GM, whether you're aware of the projection being formed at that time or not, which is the thing terrorizing people in the dreamscape would be cool. Regardless, every splat has some kind of power that lets them turn into something - whether or not it's as innate to a Werewolf, Demon, or even Changeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:33:39-07:00","id":439613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arabidopsis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=438442#post438442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some shapeshifter-like powers but not an innate ability ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, considering beastly kinship powers, and the nwod has forsaken, cursed, changing breeds, shapeshifters, skinchangers, demons, wolfbloods, hosts, changelings, and that's just off the top of my head, I'd be shocked if it was no shapechanging at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:54:51-07:00","id":439621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=439427#post439427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like this idea. Some kind of projected form that's optionally controlled by the GM, whether you're aware of the projection being formed at that time or not, which is the thing terrorizing people in the dreamscape would be cool. Regardless, every splat has some kind of power that lets them turn into something - whether or not it's as innate to a Werewolf, Demon, or even Changeling</div> </div> </div> </div>To Further Refine the Idea, when your Hungry the &quot;Projection&quot; Would cause Issue like Raised Hackles, Paranoia and the like (In others) and would appear Stalking/Violent at/to People. When it's Sated it'd be calm and Well.. Asleep. &quot;Let Sleeping Dragons Lie&quot; could/Would be an idea at this point. Just because it's Calm and Asleep Doesn't mean it won't/isn't Dangerous when Roused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:22:19-07:00","id":441337,"title":"","content":"News over from the Hurt Locker thread. Under the entry for Supernatural Fighting Styles, there were listed:<br /> \u2022Dragonslaying (Hero; see Beast: The Primordial)<br /> \u2022Sacrificial Lamb (Cultist/Follower; see Beast: The Primordial)<br /> So it appears we're getting some sort of minor template after all. Also, re-cue the Leviathan comparisons!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T23:05:04-07:00","id":442230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=441337#post441337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">News over from the Hurt Locker thread. Under the entry for Supernatural Fighting Styles, there were listed:<br /> \u2022Dragonslaying (Hero; see Beast: The Primordial)<br /> \u2022Sacrificial Lamb (Cultist/Follower; see Beast: The Primordial)<br /> So it appears we're getting some sort of minor template after all. Also, re-cue the Leviathan comparisons!</div> </div> </div> </div>Already debunked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Also, there was the writers basically saying that there would be rules for playing heroes over someones dead body, and that beasts aren't getting a servant splat unless they come up with something interesting in the future.<br /> <br /> But I suppose changing one's mind is a writer's prerogative, but not in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-15-2015, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T03:11:29-07:00","id":442388,"title":"","content":"I want to play a Beast that's an amalgam of every ghost/demon/monster in the last 15 years of found footage horror films.<br /> <br /> My splat is whichever one represents fear of the dark or the unknown, or possibly fear of the supernatural itself. My special powers include giving people goosebumps and hairs that stand on end*, and also slamming doors purely to create edible fear for my hunger. My kinship powers are based around Mages ('witches') and spirits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*As in, providing the Unseen Sense: Whatever the Hell is Right Fucking Behind Me merit to my target for the scene, automatically giving them the Spooked condition</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T04:17:08-07:00","id":442416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=442230#post442230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Already debunked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Also, there was the writers basically saying that there would be rules for playing heroes over someones dead body, and that beasts aren't getting a servant splat unless they come up with something interesting in the future.<br /> <br /> But I suppose changing one's mind is a writer's prerogative, but not in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the Cultist/Followers might be the <i>Heroes'</i>, not the Beasts'...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T05:05:35-07:00","id":442426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=442230#post442230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Already debunked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Also, there was the writers basically saying that there would be rules for playing heroes over someones dead body, and that beasts aren't getting a servant splat unless they come up with something interesting in the future.<br /> <br /> But I suppose changing one's mind is a writer's prerogative, but not in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div> Er, sorry for wasting everyone's time then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:19:11-07:00","id":443932,"title":"","content":"Well I doubt anyone minds your enthusiasm, I certainly know I don't. <br /> <br /> I suspect cultists, are mostly normal humans, along the lines of people with supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> If someone made a &quot;I decided I want to make korra in nwod so here are four psychokinesis martial arts,&quot; I would certainly call them supernatural martial art even though technically non templated mortals could take them as long as they had the right kind of psychokinesis.<br /> <br /> Heck, deceived cultists can learn numina. <br /> <br /> Presuming that cults serve beasts and not heroes, which I am here, I admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:41:53-07:00","id":443987,"title":"","content":"I think Matt over at RPG.net said the Cult/Followers were the Hero's. Beast doesn't have a demi-splat at the moment, it seems they wont get one in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:52:10-07:00","id":444319,"title":"","content":"Assuming that cultists qualify as a demi-splat, when they haven't in vampire, or mage, or demon, or changeling, or mummy, or hunter, etc, etc, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:41:08-07:00","id":449586,"title":"","content":"The RPGNet thread has given us another Family name, Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> Of which a poster, fetfet, said: &quot;Eshmaki&quot; is the Georgian word for &quot;devil&quot;, which is probably derived from the Zoroastrian demon of wrath, Aeshma. That demon's epithet is &quot;of the bloody mace&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:18:34-07:00","id":449678,"title":"","content":"At a glance, I saw the name &quot;Ereshkigal.&quot; (Mesopotamia goddess; Greek equivalent would be Hades) ..hmm..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:58:45-07:00","id":449745,"title":"","content":"Hey, fetfet is me! I've been doing this kind of research on any spoiler that pops up.<br /> <br /> My theory is that Eshmaki are either a fear of the dark, or of blood. Or possibly deception. Aeshmer was the opponent of the angel of truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:07:54-07:00","id":449754,"title":"","content":"Some other things include:<br /> According to Developer DaveB: <br /> \u2022&quot;Unless Matt changes it from how I did the crossover rules for Prometheans, they're immune to Disquiet.&quot;<br /> <br /> According to Developer Rose Bailey: \u2022&quot;Some things individual Beasts do, from my second draft of the splats chapter:<br /> - Protect the good kids in a juvenile facility from the horrors that walk the halls at night.<br /> - Steal back an inheritance piece by piece, leaving deadly things in their place.<br /> - Guard the pool that grants wishes, and profit from the secrets it whispers.<br /> - Watch over a shore-bound lover from afar.<br /> - Keep the thing in the hospital basement at bay.&quot;<br /> <br /> According to Developer Blackhat_Matt: <br /> \u2022&quot;Heroes always seem to discover weaknesses for Beasts. Almost like the put the weakness on the Beast.<br /> <br /> (Said weaknesses are called Anathema, and the rules for placing them play into the Satiety rules.)&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Neither. You can get to your Lair any place that resonates with it. If your Lair is, like my wife's character, an ocean with a black-sand beach, good luck getting there from, like, Ohio in February (&quot;THERE IS NO WATER IN THIS AIR!&quot;), but then &quot;Flooding&quot; isn't the only Lair trait she has to work with. <br /> <br /> Plus, y'know, you could always find a swimming pool or something. &quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Yes. Beasts have two basic power types, Nightmares and Atavisms. Nightmares are highly customizable. <br /> <br /> They work just fine on people in the waking world. They work better if your Satiety is high (as opposed to Atavisms, which are usually more effective when it's low).&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022In regards to Heroes or other people getting into your Lair: &quot;2) Yes, and that's dangerous. If your Lair dies, you die with it.<br /> <br /> Well, most of you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T17:58:54-07:00","id":449953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fetfet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=449745#post449745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, fetfet is me! I've been doing this kind of research on any spoiler that pops up.<br /> <br /> My theory is that Eshmaki are either a fear of the dark, or of blood. Or possibly deception. Aeshmer was the opponent of the angel of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, welcome to the forums! Thanks for mining for tidbits.<br /> <br /> I'm feeling that the Eshmaki are more about the fear of violence and bloody dismemberment. No idea what other supernatural they would associate with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:02:23-07:00","id":449955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackhat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your Lair dies,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's certainly interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:07:30-07:00","id":449960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=449953#post449953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, welcome to the forums! Thanks for mining for tidbits.<br /> <br /> I'm feeling that the Eshmaki are more about the fear of violence and bloody dismemberment. No idea what other supernatural they would associate with...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Eshmaki were mentioned in conjunction with Vampires(more specifically, in conjunction with a question if &quot;Begotten who starts off thinking he was a certain Major Template&quot; would be a valid character concept), and he also mentioned something about how they had &quot;some stealth/darkness stuff going on&quot;, so I'd probably guess something along the line of &quot;Fear of the dark/unknown&quot; myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:33:04-07:00","id":449982,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I'm mistaken in thinking it's a one-to-one relationship with the other splats. Why couldn't they find kinship with Vampires AND Sin-Eaters, or Mages AND Prometheans? It likely has to do more with theme and style than &quot;it is simply this because they are alike&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:42:05-07:00","id":450006,"title":"","content":"Another tidbit I found looking at the rpg.net thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gangrel are more animalistic than other vampires, maybe. But human beings aren't (just) afraid of animals. They fear being watched - oh, hey, there's a Mekhet. They fear beings more powerful than they are - Ventrue! And so on.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Also, this story resonates with some of the ideas that people had earlier in the thread, and really makes me want to play this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hero tracks down the Beast (let's say it's one of my other</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">players' character, the Namtaru lawyer whose Lair is a creaky old attic filled with cobwebs). The Hero breaks into her house, kills her assistant, and waits to stab her. But then she turns into a mass of spiders, flows into the room behind him, and poisons him with a touch. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As he lies dying, he spits in her face and calls her all manner of terrible names. He pulls off his ski mask so she can see it's him, the Hero, that got into her home and killed her assistant - he might have died, but he died valiantly!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And she looks down and says, &quot;Do I know you?&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:03:38-07:00","id":450017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=449982#post449982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm mistaken in thinking it's a one-to-one relationship with the other splats. Why couldn't they find kinship with Vampires AND Sin-Eaters, or Mages AND Prometheans? It likely has to do more with theme and style than &quot;it is simply this because they are alike&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not a one-to-one relationship. The Eshmaki were brought up specifically because Matt was trying to work through whether a Beast could think it was a Vampire. So maybe another Beast could find more kinship in werewolves, or in mages, or in a variety of other monsters and supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T20:57:05-07:00","id":450084,"title":"","content":"Is there a link to the RPGnet thread somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T22:30:32-07:00","id":450166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450084#post450084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a link to the RPGnet thread somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yo! <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...-teaser-thread</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T22:39:41-07:00","id":450171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450166#post450166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yo! <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...-teaser-thread</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You ninja'd me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:07:23-07:00","id":450441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=449982#post449982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm mistaken in thinking it's a one-to-one relationship with the other splats. Why couldn't they find kinship with Vampires AND Sin-Eaters, or Mages AND Prometheans? It likely has to do more with theme and style than &quot;it is simply this because they are alike&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are enlightened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:39:17-07:00","id":450482,"title":"","content":"In reponse to &quot;Do Lairs connect to each other in a nightmarish otherworld or are they their own otherworld?&quot;<br /> <br /> Dave B answered both.<br /> <br /> And in response to &quot;Is this &quot;nightmarish otherworld&quot; one of the already recognized nWOD realms (e.g., underworld, astral, shadow, lower depths, etc.), or do Beasts' lairs reside in an entirely new realm?&quot;<br /> <br /> He also answered both.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blackhat_Matt also mentioned a Hunger for Punishment (in context, punishing other people, not being punished yourself). Though I'm not 100% sure whether he meant as a canonical Hunger or a one that would be a fitting addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:21:30-07:00","id":450642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450441#post450441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are enlightened.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of, we now know who the Dark Mother is:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt McFarland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the heart of the riddle that is the existence of Beasts is the figure known as the Dark Mother, the progenitor of their kind. While trading rumors of her sightings is a popular pastime when a number of Beasts gather, she has not been reliably sighted in centuries, possibly millennia. Nevertheless, the Begotten know on an instinctive level that she is still alive out there, somewhere. They know because the fear of her never quite goes away, for if she does return, she is far more likely to devour her children than embrace them. <br /> <br /> Who Is the Dark Mother? In the beginning, She was there. The first monster, the mother of nightmares. Lilith, Tiamat, Hekate, the Queen Mother of the West \u2014 she\u2019s been called a hundred different names in tongues still living and long dead alike, described in a thousand ways across ten thousand years, but these days her Children usually call her the Dark Mother. Some say she was the first being to travel the Primordial Dream and absorb its secrets, then brought them back to this world and formed them into her children. Others claim that she is the Primordial Dream given form, and that when she walks once more the world will know fear like it hasn\u2019t since the dawn of time. <br /> <br /> Regardless of the truth, all Beasts recognize her as the first of their kind; not only that, but the first of all monsters. As far as the Begotten are concerned, vampires, werewolves, changelings, and other stranger things are simply younger siblings, branches of the family tree that have diverged but still share common roots. While other beings may scoff, Beasts have powers and abilities that seem to back their claim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:44:15-07:00","id":450655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450482#post450482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reponse to &amp;quot;Do Lairs connect to each other in a nightmarish otherworld or are they their own otherworld?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Dave B answered both.<br /> <br /> And in response to &amp;quot;Is this &amp;quot;nightmarish otherworld&amp;quot; one of the already recognized nWOD realms (e.g., underworld, astral, shadow, lower depths, etc.), or do Beasts' lairs reside in an entirely new realm?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> He also answered both.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe there will be Kinship powers that allow allow you to create passages between your Lair and a otherworld associated with a different splat,or even gibe it some qualities of that place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:34:05-07:00","id":450797,"title":"","content":"Also this snip, from the same thread, relating to hints we've been given before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts look human outside of their Lair. In their Lair, they don't have to be separate from their Soul anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>And apparently Mages are to Beasts like the one child who went to college and whose jargon no one quite understands or cares about even though they're still family. Wonderful.<br /> <br /> Interesting that they don't seem to actually look at the Unchained as extended family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-20-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:06:59-07:00","id":450847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450797#post450797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting that they don't seem to actually look at the Unchained as extended family.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's understandable.<br /> <br /> The GM brings in Angels to do it's work and projects. Demons are really just fallen Angels and still linked to the GM in the most basic functions.<br /> <br /> Demons may be adopted family members rather than &quot;flesh and blood&quot; family as I highly doubt that Beasts would view the GM as family.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:28:09-07:00","id":450896,"title":"","content":"Actually Prometheans are the adopted ones, according to Dave! Someone suggested the criteria for how Beasts determine the degree of kinship with other supernaturals might be more closely related to the condition of the spirit or soul (and how that affects the flesh by proxy) than other factors. Hence Mages being &quot;closer&quot; to Beasts in a way than Vampires are, for example.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Unchained not being part of what Beasts see as their extended family makes some sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-20-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:53:47-07:00","id":450960,"title":"","content":"All supernatural protagonist types in the World of Darkness are transformed humans, save two: Prometheans and the Unchained. Of these, the Created are at least made out of human corpses (mostly) and share a strange connection to humanity (see the Redeemed), whereas the Unchained are remarkably adept at taking from and mimicking humanity. So I'm not surprised to learn that the Created are considered to be adopted into the extended family while the Unchained aren't. <br /> <br /> Still, I suspect that the Unchained are viewed as friends of the family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:34:48-07:00","id":451162,"title":"","content":"Technically, Demons are made of people too. Angels are created from human sacrifices, and demons are fallen angels. But, yeah, that's really a stretch. The Created have residual memories, Unchained are completely and utterly inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:20:21-07:00","id":451190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=450482#post450482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reponse to &quot;Do Lairs connect to each other in a nightmarish otherworld or are they their own otherworld?&quot;<br /> <br /> Dave B answered both.<br /> <br /> And in response to &quot;Is this &quot;nightmarish otherworld&quot; one of the already recognized nWOD realms (e.g., underworld, astral, shadow, lower depths, etc.), or do Beasts' lairs reside in an entirely new realm?&quot;<br /> <br /> He also answered both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't take this as an 'answer' so much as him screwing around with the gullible and desperate mega-cosmology readers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:31:21-07:00","id":451283,"title":"","content":"So would Beasts at least CLAIM (even if it's not objectively a demonstrable truth) that &quot;Luna&quot; of the Werewolves is the Dark Mother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:50:57-07:00","id":451291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451283#post451283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would Beasts at least CLAIM (even if it's not objectively a demonstrable truth) that &quot;Luna&quot; of the Werewolves is the Dark Mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eater: &quot;So do you believe in the all mighty Pink Pony as your ever lasting Goddess?<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;Of course I do! She's clearly the Dark Mother!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater: &quot;No she isn't!&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;Why not!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater: &quot;I just made that shit up!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:01:04-07:00","id":451295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451291#post451291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-Eater: &quot;So do you believe in the all mighty Pink Pony as your ever lasting Goddess?<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;Of course I do! She's clearly the Dark Mother!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater: &quot;No she isn't!&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;Why not!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater: &quot;I just made that shit up!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Alice's schedule is still too packed for defending some poor misguided soul\u2019s interpretation of the will of the transcendent satellite gods at the end of time, incidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:23:17-07:00","id":451303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451295#post451295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alice's schedule is still too packed for defending some poor misguided soul\u2019s interpretation of the will of the transcendent satellite gods at the end of time, incidentally.</div> </div> </div> </div>The will of the gods at the end of time is the desire get into Milliways while Disaster Area starts up their show. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T23:10:02-07:00","id":451331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451162#post451162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, Demons are made of people too. Angels are created from human sacrifices, and demons are fallen angels. But, yeah, that's really a stretch. The Created have residual memories, Unchained are completely and utterly inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: angels aren\u2019t created from human sacrifices; they\u2019re created by occult matrices. There <i>may</i> be some human sacrifice of some sort in an occult matrix; but that\u2019s a big \u201cif\u201d, as it were. A Demon who is still using the Cover he had as an angel, or who is careful to <i>only</i> get new Covers by hijacking angels, stands a good chance of saying that there\u2019s nothing human about him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T04:37:04-07:00","id":451421,"title":"","content":"I must admit I was a bit meh about this game at first, but the more I know, the more it is getting to my top three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T04:58:59-07:00","id":451434,"title":"","content":"I'm with you. I thought <b>Mummy</b> was the end-all be-all for me, but <b>Beast</b> is very clearly rocking that boat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T06:49:19-07:00","id":451484,"title":"","content":"And then what if the God-Machine is the Dark Mother? Or the God-Machine is her Dark Husband, hence the Dark Father? Or the God-Machine is just one of her infinite children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3401-uata","name":"Uata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:29:33-07:00","id":451542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451190#post451190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't take this as an 'answer' so much as him screwing around with the gullible and desperate mega-cosmology readers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but this is the gameline expressly being designed as crossover-friendly, so I'm taking &quot;both&quot; to mean &quot;easy to customise into yesses and nos.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451283#post451283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would Beasts at least CLAIM (even if it's not objectively a demonstrable truth) that &quot;Luna&quot; of the Werewolves is the Dark Mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially, though I suspect Mother Wolf might be more likely than Mother Luna (given that 2nd Ed muddies their genders). Some of them would definitely claim it about the Crone too; and I could see more than one Acolyte cult agreeing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:55:17-07:00","id":451579,"title":"","content":"Man, the Circle of the Crone is going to love these monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T11:51:24-07:00","id":451843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451484#post451484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then what if the God-Machine is the Dark Mother? Or the God-Machine is her Dark Husband, hence the Dark Father? Or the God-Machine is just one of her infinite children?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems counter to what's been said. The Machine seems outside of the family, to a point where there might even be metaphysical rifts between beasts and angels, or demons for that matter.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Which makes sense- as monsters go, angels and demons are often marked by how their sacredness and profanity set them apart from everything else. Even if beasts wanted to have them in the family, the mythological underpinnings of the divine splat demand that they just can't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-21-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:23:35-07:00","id":451976,"title":"","content":"Demons maybe can pact their way into the family. They are the in-laws that are only in for the family money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:46:28-07:00","id":451991,"title":"","content":"How exactly would one pact that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:53:09-07:00","id":451996,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Unchained are like the sitcom trope of the kid who most of the family doesn't like but who is able to get into the house even when they change the locks, and who you let stick around because you wouldn't wish their home life on anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:57:24-07:00","id":452002,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they're the punk kid no one wants.<br /> <br /> Who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T16:28:46-07:00","id":452118,"title":"","content":"Alright, so far the listed Families are Eshmaki, Namtaru,and Anakim, and the Hungers are Punishment, Prey, Power, Hoard.<br /> <br /> Broods of Beasts can share Lairs, and Lairs can include living beings, though they're more npc than person(Blackhat_Matt hinted that there might be ways to change this if he gets to expand Lairs in the Player's Guide).<br /> <br /> Also, while I can't find the actual quote, one of the devs, in response to someone asking if their would be Strix Kinship powers(or something like that) said that, while there wouldn't be any in the books, Kinship powers should be easy to make more of, and you could totally make some for other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T18:02:09-07:00","id":452191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=451996#post451996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Unchained are like the sitcom trope of the kid who most of the family doesn't like but who is able to get into the house even when they change the locks, and who you let stick around because you wouldn't wish their home life on anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining Full House with Danny Tanner as a Beast, Uncle Jessie asa Mage with music as a focus for his spells, Jessie's Wife as a Vampire, Joey asa Changeling that prefers to gather glamour from laughter, and the tanner girls as a werewolf, a promethean, and a sin-eater(you decide which is which) and Kimmy Gibbler is the Demon.<br /> <br /> I don't' know how well it fits, but I'm blaming you for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T23:39:17-07:00","id":452323,"title":"","content":"My only fear now is that the Beasts are so openended that they end up a catchall that kind of shuts down other more diverse monsters that aren't &quot;unlocked primordial darkness in the human soul&quot;. Like if Beasts cover Minotaurs (an example Matt mentioned), that might make seeing the Baal-Hadad make a 2E Werewolf cameo less likely. And I will want Naga (NOT the WtA shifters) to get a full gameline of their own till my dying breath!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:30:45-07:00","id":452385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=452323#post452323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only fear now is that the Beasts are so openended that they end up a catchall that kind of shuts down other more diverse monsters that aren't &quot;unlocked primordial darkness in the human soul&quot;. Like if Beasts cover Minotaurs (an example Matt mentioned), that might make seeing the Baal-Hadad make a 2E Werewolf cameo less likely. And I will want Naga (NOT the WtA shifters) to get a full gameline of their own till my dying breath!</div> </div> </div> </div> If the writers thought like that, there wouldn't be a mage, werewolf, mummy, geist, or demon line because vampire, inferno, and changelings all came first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:49:39-07:00","id":452732,"title":"","content":"So, having read all 63 pages of the RPGnet thread, I kind of want to know if my Beast's Lair can be an abandoned Pizzeria filled with Murderous Animatronics.<br /> <br /> Nontraditional monsters have been confirmed for beasts, and other entities being part of your lair are in, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:05:13-07:00","id":453065,"title":"","content":"I would be lying if I said I'm not totally stoked at the idea of playing a Kraken. Or maybe some sort of large spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":".  Misuse of the irrealis. 03-22-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:52:59-07:00","id":453131,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I feel like playing some sort of oversized frog monster. That or some sort of ghostly entity made out of electric energy. No idea why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:14:46-07:00","id":453407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=452732#post452732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, having read all 63 pages of the RPGnet thread, I kind of want to know if my Beast's Lair can be an abandoned Pizzeria filled with Murderous Animatronics.<br /> <br /> Nontraditional monsters have been confirmed for beasts, and other entities being part of your lair are in, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wrote up Fazbear's Pizza as a location once (including statting the animatronics). Seems like an interesting site for a one-on-one Hunter or Geist game, if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:19:25-07:00","id":453415,"title":"","content":"From Matt on the RPG.net thread: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread&amp;p=18844706#post18844706\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...6#post18844706</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Originally Posted by <b>Beast, Chapter Two</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Living with Hunger is dangerous, yes, but a dragon\u2019s gold is never a burden. The Hero might call it profane, but in his heart of hearts, he envies its glory. He\u2019d be lucky to have such a light to guide his way. Instead, he\u2019s left with the solipsism of vendetta. For Hunger is a lodestar, not an addiction as the Heroes claim. As if a Beast could detox off instinct. Grendel wars on Heorot because killing Danes is the only way he keeps his sanity stapled together. He savors the blood spattering on his skin, and the bones crumbling in his fists, but that\u2019s all empty calories. Hunger drowns out doubt. If it didn\u2019t, he\u2019d throw himself on their spears.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T01:25:04-07:00","id":453964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt McFarland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>At the heart of the riddle that is the existence of Beasts is the figure known as the Dark Mother, the progenitor of their kind. While trading rumors of her sightings is a popular pastime when a number of Beasts gather, she has not been reliably sighted in centuries, possibly millennia. Nevertheless, the Begotten know on an instinctive level that she is still alive out there, somewhere. They know because the fear of her never quite goes away, for if she does return, she is far more likely to devour her children than embrace them. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Who Is the Dark Mother? In the beginning, She was there. The first monster, the mother of nightmares. Lilith, Tiamat, Hekate, the Queen Mother of the West \u2014 she\u2019s been called a hundred different names in tongues still living and long dead alike, described in a thousand ways across ten thousand years, but these days her Children usually call her the Dark Mother. Some say she was the first being to travel the Primordial Dream and absorb its secrets, then brought them back to this world and formed them into her children. Others claim that she is the Primordial Dream given form, and that when she walks once more the world will know fear like it hasn\u2019t since the dawn of time. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Regardless of the truth, all Beasts recognize her as the first of their kind; not only that, but the first of all monsters. As far as the Begotten are concerned, vampires, werewolves, changelings, and other stranger things are simply younger siblings, branches of the family tree that have diverged but still share common roots. While other beings may scoff, Beasts have powers and abilities that seem to back their claim. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>So a couple of thoughts pop into my head reading this:<br /> <br /> 1) I wonder if one of her names is Ammut?<br /> <br /> 2) The Crone are going to be so happy that someone else shares their religious viewpoint. Alternatively they are possibly going to be freaked that some &quot;human&quot; seems to know about their creed possibly better then anyone still breathing should. <br /> <br /> 3) Does this mean Beasts are Lilin? Because I've been wanting a game about those since reading &quot;Revelations of the Dark Mother&quot; back in my VtM days about 8 years ago! <br /> <br /> 4) Does Primordial Dream scream &quot;Anima Mundi&quot; to anyone else? If one is inclined to use fancy Mage names for things. <br /> <br /> Apart from that, hearing that Lairs are their own distinct realm and also linked to pre-existing otherworldly realms we know about interests me greatly. Lairs sound pretty damn scary anyway. A Lair with a connection to Duat (Mummy related), the Abyss (Mage related) or Arcadia (Changeling related) that sounds absolutely terrifying. Even worse...what if you can have more then one link to another realm in your lair at the same time? (brain melts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T02:57:28-07:00","id":454007,"title":"","content":"Didn't Matt say the Primordial Dream had some relation to the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T05:59:34-07:00","id":454139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454007#post454007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Matt say the Primordial Dream had some relation to the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is certainly what I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:00:41-07:00","id":454216,"title":"","content":"I think we can all be positively certain that, despite being a crossover game, the Primordial Dream has roots firmly in its own mythology and probably isn't related to the Astral anymore than Duat is to the Underworld. Overlap? Possibly. Similar themes? Most likely. Canonically the same place? Definitely not.<br /> <br /> Like Matt also said in the rpg.net thread, every splat tends to think they are the 'chosen ones' and that all their beliefs and mythologies explain everyone else's. Mages will believe the Primordial Dream is the Astral, Mummies will think the Dark Mother is Ammut, Changelings will think the Primordial Dream is the Dream-realm, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:07:52-07:00","id":454254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454216#post454216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all be positively certain that, despite being a crossover game, the Primordial Dream has roots firmly in its own mythology and probably isn't related to the Astral anymore than Duat is to the Underworld. Overlap? Possibly. Similar themes? Most likely. Canonically the same place? Definitely not.<br /> <br /> Like Matt also said in the rpg.net thread, every splat tends to think they are the 'chosen ones' and that all their beliefs and mythologies explain everyone else's. Mages will believe the Primordial Dream is the Astral, Mummies will think the Dark Mother is Ammut, Changelings will think the Primordial Dream is the Dream-realm, etc</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is my understanding that's not entirely consistent with what Matt has actually stated. If I recall correctly, Matt has discussed Beast's connection to the Astral Realm, as presented in MtAw, and he has also just recently confirmed that Beast will concern both a known nWOD realm as well as something unique or different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:00:03-07:00","id":454372,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go through the thread page by page and see what's up.<ul><li>Post #88: Lairs are otherwordly</li> <li>Post #276: Lairs are something <i>like</i> the Astral, and they can access <i>other worlds</i> with kinship - implying, to me, that the Primordial Dream is separate</li> <li>Post #352: Lairs can be accessed to by 'resonating' locations</li> <li>Post #381: You can put real stuff in your Lair although it's mostly dream stuff</li> <li>Post #440: Lairs are important and Heroes (relatively mortal, presumably) can bumble into one</li> <li>Post #463: Lairs can be moved, in a way</li> <li>Post #471: Lairs have traits</li> <li>Post #474: Lairs can change</li> <li>Post #478: Lairs connect to a nightmarish otherworld but are each still their own distinctive piece of property</li> <li>Post #481: DaveB, making a silly face implying some degree of jest, says that the Primordial Dream is 'both' one of the 'already recognized nWoD' realms as well as an entirely new realm</li> </ul>I'm going to stop there, as that last bit is basically what I just said above.<br /> <br /> It's curious to me how many people think a new game-line would just come right out and say that their new other world is the other world of one other game-line's specific otherworld. Why would they say it's exactly the Astral, and then alienate all the non-Mage players? Why would they commit to that story-wise and close so many other interesting doors?<br /> <br /> You know what happened the last time we tried to get canon crossover answers published? We got the <b>Mage</b>/<b>Changeling</b> Arcadia mess. Who wants that again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:07:44-07:00","id":454375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454216#post454216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all be positively certain that, despite being a crossover game, the Primordial Dream has roots firmly in its own mythology and probably isn't related to the Astral anymore than Duat is to the Underworld. Overlap? Possibly. Similar themes? Most likely. Canonically the same place? Definitely not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you would be wrong! It is both simpler and more complicated than that. Beasts and Mages look at the Primordial Dream / Astral differently, like one blind man touching an elephant's leg while his equally-blind touches the trunk, but they're describing different observations of the same <i>thing</i>. It's closer than, say, the Skein, because Beast is the crossover-friendly game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:11:39-07:00","id":454382,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Arcadia Mess&quot; was the result of desperately trying to <i>not</i> publish a canon crossover question, to the detriment of both lines. <b>Beast</b> explains exactly how the Primordial Dream relates to the Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:19:58-07:00","id":454386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454372#post454372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would they say it's exactly the Astral, and then alienate all the non-Mage players? Why would they commit to that story-wise and close so many other interesting doors?</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't seem to have an issue with Werewolf, Mage, and the Purified sharing the Shadow. Or Geist and Mage sharing the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:30:00-07:00","id":454391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454372#post454372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go through the thread page by page and see what's up.<ul><li>Post #88: Lairs are otherwordly</li> <li>Post #276: Lairs are something <i>like</i> the Astral, and they can access <i>other worlds</i> with kinship - implying, to me, that the Primordial Dream is separate</li> <li>Post #352: Lairs can be accessed to by 'resonating' locations</li> <li>Post #381: You can put real stuff in your Lair although it's mostly dream stuff</li> <li>Post #440: Lairs are important and Heroes (relatively mortal, presumably) can bumble into one</li> <li>Post #463: Lairs can be moved, in a way</li> <li>Post #471: Lairs have traits</li> <li>Post #474: Lairs can change</li> <li>Post #478: Lairs connect to a nightmarish otherworld but are each still their own distinctive piece of property</li> <li>Post #481:<b> DaveB, making a silly face implying some degree of jest, says that the Primordial Dream is 'both' one of the 'already recognized nWoD' realms as well as an entirely new realm</b></li> </ul><b>I'm going to stop there, as that last bit is basically what I just said above.<br /> <br /> It's curious to me how many people think a new game-line would just come right out and say that their new other world is the other world of one other game-line's specific otherworld. Why would they say it's exactly the Astral, and then alienate all the non-Mage players? Why would they commit to that story-wise and close so many other interesting doors?<br /> <br /> You know what happened the last time we tried to get canon crossover answers published? We got the <b>Mage</b>/<b>Changeling</b> Arcadia mess. Who wants that again?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you doubting DaveB was being truthful, particularly in light of Matt's earlier comments about Astral realm interaction? Also, highlighting interesting or unique aspects of Lairs does not really dispositively suggest that Beast will or will not use the known Astral Reals, near limitless world(s) with few, if any, rules.<br /> <br /> More importantly, game lines commonly share otherworld realms, <i>particularly with Mage</i>. Do not forget that mages routinely access and interact with multitudes of realms besides the supernal, including the Astral, Shadow, Underworld and Lower Depths. There was even an entire book dedicated to the topic - Summoners. Does the fact that Mage uses these realms in any way diminish or confuse the other game lines that rely on certain realms as their primary, or at least important, focus. Is werewolf less exciting because mages can roam the Hisil and interact with spirits, often better than werewolves under certain circumstances? How about Geists and the Underwold (were werewolves also sometimes tread)? Changelings and dreams (i.e., Mage Oniernos)?<br /> <br /> Beasts and Mages can both easily interact with Astral space as their otherworld without stepping on each other's toes, and even dealing with each other at all. In fact, I believe many, including myself, would prefer that Beasts stick with one of the known realms, as keeping track of multitudes of realms and their unique properties and inhabitants is often difficult, arguably more realms increases &quot;bloat&quot; in the nWOD cosmology, and serves to confuse new WOD players. The fact that Beast is being designed expressly as a very crossover friendly game only emphasizes the point. <br /> <br /> If Beast ultimately uses all or some of the Astral Realm for their Lairs or anything else, both as areas in common with mages and places unique to Beasts, it would most certainly not &quot;close any interesting story doors.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:40:21-07:00","id":454399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454375#post454375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you would be wrong! It is both simpler and more complicated than that. Beasts and Mages look at the Primordial Dream / Astral differently, like one blind man touching an elephant's leg while his equally-blind touches the trunk, but they're describing different observations of the same <i>thing</i>. It's closer than, say, the Skein, because Beast is the crossover-friendly game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the response, Dave. It will certainly prevent much needless (and endless) argument, speculation and consternation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:29:11-07:00","id":454471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454216#post454216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all be positively certain that, despite being a crossover game, the Primordial Dream has roots firmly in its own mythology and probably isn't related to the Astral anymore than Duat is to the Underworld. Overlap? Possibly. Similar themes? Most likely. Canonically the same place? Definitely not.<br /> <br /> Like Matt also said in the rpg.net thread, every splat tends to think they are the 'chosen ones' and that all their beliefs and mythologies explain everyone else's. Mages will believe the Primordial Dream is the Astral, Mummies will think the Dark Mother is Ammut, Changelings will think the Primordial Dream is the Dream-realm, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside Dave's more directanswer because I wanna say this:<br /> <br /> Yeah, except that Beasts seem to be occupying a point of possible greater validity. Where the other gamelines are islands, Beast seems to be a deliberate bridge in themes and ideas, and that often translates to metaphysics and mechanics, so in this case it's actually a bad idea to assume that they don't tie in certain ways. Beasts provide a more solid way to tie things together, it seems-it's just that in doing so, everyone's going to start feeling really uncomfortable about what that means for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:16:59-07:00","id":454545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454471#post454471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, except that Beasts seem to be occupying a point of possible greater validity. Where the other gamelines are islands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snip.<br /> <br /> Beasts are the Ocean... The Rest are the Islands within the Ocean.<br /> I Can See the Beasts having some of the Most varied Themes and well... It's made as a Crossover with all the other Splats. I think they can act as the glue for the rest of them and help Bind Say a Vampire, Werewolf and Promethean with a Beast and a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:28:46-07:00","id":454560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454545#post454545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip.<br /> <br /> Beasts are the Ocean... The Rest are the Islands within the Ocean.<br /> I Can See the Beasts having some of the Most varied Themes and well... It's made as a Crossover with all the other Splats. I think they can act as the glue for the rest of them and help Bind Say a Vampire, Werewolf and Promethean with a Beast and a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think such a broad comment runs the risk of moving too far in the opposite direction and minimizing the other game lines, particularly since it is my understanding that Beast will still be an entirely self-contained game. Given the generally professed sentiments of OPP, other than basic marketing, I also doubt they would implicitly pressure purchasers into acquiring other game lines in order to fully appreciate the &quot;full Beast experience.&quot; I would imagine that crossover must still be balanced against any perception that Beast <i>requires</i> books from other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:32:36-07:00","id":454565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454545#post454545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip.<br /> <br /> Beasts are the Ocean... The Rest are the Islands within the Ocean.<br /> I Can See the Beasts having some of the Most varied Themes and well... It's made as a Crossover with all the other Splats. I think they can act as the glue for the rest of them and help Bind Say a Vampire, Werewolf and Promethean with a Beast and a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the ocean is the World of Darkness. Beasts might unite a lot of things, but this is a broad and deep world, and beasts can't hope to account for everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:41:45-07:00","id":454573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454565#post454565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the ocean is the World of Darkness. Beasts might unite a lot of things, but this is a broad and deep world, and beasts can't hope to account for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright... Maybe a Different Response is needed...<br /> <br /> The Splats are the Islands and the Beast are some of the Trade Routes, They allow Easy Access/Connect too things that they do not Normally have access too without much Wheeling and Dealing.<br /> Well.. that's what i Think.<br /> I Think they are trying too make a Decent Splat in and of itself, that can act as the &quot;Oil&quot; for a Chronicle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:01:11-07:00","id":454607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454573#post454573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Think they are trying too make a Decent Splat in and of itself, that can act as the &quot;Oil&quot; for a Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:13:27-07:00","id":454617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454607#post454607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter i See as (IF your using with others) primarily Antagonists for the others... External Conflict too Force them together.. Yeah it Works. Beast can be the... &quot;Diplomatic&quot; Tension or even the Sense of &quot;Better the Devil you Know&quot; type of Deal.<br /> <br /> Not every &quot;Monster&quot; is gonna want too Stick around Humans all the Time.. &quot;I Can Resist everything Except Temptation&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Basically Yeah, Like Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:11:30-07:00","id":454703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454375#post454375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you would be wrong! It is both simpler and more complicated than that. Beasts and Mages look at the Primordial Dream / Astral differently, like one blind man touching an elephant's leg while his equally-blind touches the trunk, but they're describing different observations of the same <i>thing</i>. It's closer than, say, the Skein, because Beast is the crossover-friendly game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This analogy sounds a bit like how it was explained in the <i>Astral Realms</i> books (ref: pg 80, 136-137) in regards to Werewolves; in contrast to the Human/Mage access going through the Oneiros&gt;Temenos&gt;Anima Mundi in relative progression, the Uratha gain access directly to the Anima Mundi as if it was a holy dream. It goes on to say that the Werewolf translation of the experience is a bit more pragmatic &amp; its practice is so unexceptional in comparison to Mages that should they cross paths; a Werewolf wouldn't really distinguish that particular Mage (or even other Uratha) as a foreign presence within their dreamscape rather simply part of their own psyche.<br /> <br /> Is this more or less the concept you are conveying in that two groups entering at opposite ends of the house will have their own interpretations of the home as a whole?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:15:41-07:00","id":454705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454565#post454565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the ocean is the World of Darkness. Beasts might unite a lot of things, but this is a broad and deep world, and beasts can't hope to account for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the lake he called home, lies a deeper darker ocean green.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:24:28-07:00","id":454716,"title":"","content":"It's possible that Beasts can interact with astral space differently than mages. Who knows, maybe Beasts can swim in the Ocean Oroboros. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:30:35-07:00","id":454722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454705#post454705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beyond the lake he called home, lies a deeper darker ocean green.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where waves are both wilder and more serene.<br /> To its ports I've been,<br /> To its ports I've been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:02:43-07:00","id":455469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=452118#post452118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so far the listed Families are Eshmaki, Namtaru,and Anakim, and the Hungers are Punishment, Prey, Power, Hoard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it seems the Anakim are giants, named after <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anakim\" target=\"_blank\">a race that terrified the Israelites</a>. Goliath was likely one of them.<br /> <br /> The Eshmaki seem to be blood-soaked monstrosities. Perhaps things like your Gmorks and Smaugs?<br /> <br /> The Namtaru seem to be inevitable, whether it be illness or death.<br /> <br /> And we seem to be definitely, <i>definitely</i> getting gillmen of some kind.<br /> <br /> Will we be getting some sort of sky folk, I wonder? Something like the Roc of old?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  Forgot to finish a thought there. 03-24-2015, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:19:01-07:00","id":455476,"title":"","content":"When I made my crack about playing the Raven from Princess Tutu, I was told that was a possibility. Whether that translates to x-splat or not, well, that's for Matt to spill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T02:03:37-07:00","id":455552,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll put my foot in my mouth if it gets a developer to lay it out for us.<br /> <br /> All I was saying was that I've read developers and writers say they'll purposely write elements into a game just to throw off any sort of grand unifying theory of the nWoD cosmology. I figured once people would still thinking, &quot;Oh, <b>Beast</b> uses <b>Mage</b>'s Astral&quot; then once again everyone is going to jump the gun about how Mages know everything - which isn't good for <b>Mage</b> or the other game-line. The World of Darkness is about mystery, and I want to see that kept is all.<br /> <br /> The most interesting story hint, to me, wouldn't be, &quot;Yes, it's the Astral&quot; or &quot;No, it's not the Astral&quot; but rather, &quot;Maybe; it could go one way or the other&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T02:07:01-07:00","id":455553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=455552#post455552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'll put my foot in my mouth if it gets a developer to lay it out for us.<br /> <br /> All I was saying was that I've read developers and writers say they'll purposely write elements into a game just to throw off any sort of grand unifying theory of the nWoD cosmology. I figured once people would still thinking, &quot;Oh, <b>Beast</b> uses <b>Mage</b>'s Astral&quot; then once again everyone is going to jump the gun about how Mages know everything - which isn't good for <b>Mage</b> or the other game-line. The World of Darkness is about mystery, and I want to see that kept is all.<br /> <br /> The most interesting story hint, to me, wouldn't be, &quot;Yes, it's the Astral&quot; or &quot;No, it's not the Astral&quot; but rather, &quot;Maybe; it could go one way or the other&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So Far it seems that it's more 2 people Viewing the same thing, One Wearing Blue Lens Glasses, one Wearing Green Lenses (And Possibly a Third Not wearing any.. Idiots Staring at the Sun)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T04:24:41-07:00","id":455652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=455552#post455552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most interesting story hint, to me, wouldn't be, &quot;Yes, it's the Astral&quot; or &quot;No, it's not the Astral&quot; but rather, &quot;Maybe; it could go one way or the other&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That was basically how Arcadia was handled during 1e. In retrospect, it didn't work out that well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:22:04-07:00","id":455928,"title":"","content":"I think it was a bit more nuanced than that. Or, perhaps, people just didn't like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:40:08-07:00","id":455950,"title":"","content":"Normally Res*, I'd agree with you. I'm normally the first to start snapping &quot;IT DOESN'T HAVE ANYTHING TO DO WITH [Insert thing here]!&quot;<br /> <br /> But Beast has been explicitly defined as breaking the rules as a crossover-centric game from the start, so it makes more sense to break the mold here.<br /> <br /> *In response to an earlier comment, not the one literally** above my head.<br /> **Well, okay, not literally, but you know what I mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:49:02-07:00","id":455962,"title":"","content":"Still, I'd just have expected for definite answers regarding how Beasts interact with the Astral. I wouldn't have suspected that the Primordial Dream is outright the Astral, even in the Big Crossover Game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:51:25-07:00","id":455965,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","