 your Lair. In your Lair, your body and your Soul are one and the same. And as your Lair grows, it becomes able to accomodate more Chambers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:22:32-07:00","id":456172,"title":"","content":"Going blind, haven't checked the thread in a second, so apologies if somebody on RPGnet already said this: My Prediction. Lair is the power stat because a powerful beast deserves a grand lair and vise versa-a beast who becomes more powerful will have a lair that grows to match, but altering the lair would also alter the beast.<br /> <br /> A stronger beast's lair would have more chambers, more features, and existing features would get stronger-in my hypothetical &quot;Your lair is freddy Fazbear's Pizzeria&quot; Beast, at Lair 1 the Beast's lair is like day one in the first game.<br /> <br /> At 10, it's 10/20 custom Night in FNAF2, except the Shadows are out to get you instead of being incidental, you don't have a mask or flashlight, you've got the fantom hallucinations from 3, and you're still on the limited battery life where if you run out, the Animatronics get you.<br /> <br /> Not sure if my Beast is The Marionette or if he's Springtrap, however.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's something I should ask: Is manifesting your lair in the real world(or a reasonable facsimile thereof) something that could be done?<br /> <br /> Because, with how much a Crapsack world the NWOD, I could honestly, iff it's possible to manifest the lair like that, see a Beast with that lair manifesting it, tweaking it to be an actual business, and then having his Lair's &quot;guardians&quot; hunt the night guards as a way of sating his hunger for predation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:36:18-07:00","id":456181,"title":"","content":"The answer is Lair","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:37:22-07:00","id":456183,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of the Power Stat interacting with Lair and essentially <i>being </i>Lair, but I hope it has an actual name that's cooler than just saying &quot;I'm a Lair 10 Beast.&quot; Y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:08:51-07:00","id":456216,"title":"","content":"The really interesting thing is that Lairs have traits. So like, the higher your Lair trait the more Lair goodies you get? And they were hinting that Beasts' Satiety might not even have breaking points, so we'll see how unique this whole game turns out. I'm excited","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:06:51-07:00","id":456241,"title":"","content":"I have the wild theory that they don't even have a Fuel Stat, that powers just need you to be at Satiety &quot;X&quot; to work and maybe that's how its reduced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:24:49-07:00","id":456254,"title":"","content":"Now I'm getting a real Nightmare on Elm Street vibe. Freddy's mutable dream world is his Lair, but it's always centered around the endless pipes and hallways of the Furnace Room.<br /> <br /> Taking a stab at his splats, I'm going to say he would be a Namtaru with a Hunger for Punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:36:08-07:00","id":456389,"title":"","content":"IIRC, this game lets you play a dragon; right? So if a dragon\u2019s Lair is its power-stat, would the accumulated gold be its fuel stat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:02:57-07:00","id":456402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456241#post456241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the wild theory that they don't even have a Fuel Stat, that powers just need you to be at Satiety &quot;X&quot; to work and maybe that's how its reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty freaking awesome. They did start playing with Fuel and Power with Mummy, and I for one would like to see a bit more of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456389#post456389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, this game lets you play a dragon; right? So if a dragon\u2019s Lair is its power-stat, would the accumulated gold be its fuel stat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there's some interplay with your Satiety and Lair. If you have a huge Horde, you need a big Lair. If your need to Punish is high, you need a potent Lair. If you have a ton of Power your Lair needs to be grandiose. And if you need Prey maybe you need space for them to run around and be terrified of you in.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the Bradbury story &quot;The Veldt&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:03:59-07:00","id":456404,"title":"","content":"Since only some Beasts have the Hunger to Hoard as their Hunger, I would suspect not as such.<br /> <br /> But I'm not the developer, so I wouldn't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T19:34:14-07:00","id":456496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456241#post456241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the wild theory that they don't even have a Fuel Stat, that powers just need you to be at Satiety &quot;X&quot; to work and maybe that's how its reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that'd be trippy.<br /> <br /> But if anyone were going to do something like that, it'd be Matt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T04:47:59-07:00","id":456740,"title":"","content":"As I said, wild theory. I think they can pull it of. It also may work with the tidbits we have about Atavisms being more potent at low satiety and Nightmares be better the higher the stat is (or I had it backwards?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 03-25-2015, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:35:18-07:00","id":456894,"title":"","content":"No,you have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:28:51-07:00","id":456963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=454391#post454391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not forget that mages routinely access and interact with multitudes of realms besides the supernal, including the Astral, Shadow, Underworld and Lower Depths. There was even an entire book dedicated to the topic - Summoners. Does the fact that Mage uses these realms in any way diminish or confuse the other game lines that rely on certain realms as their primary, or at least important, focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people think so, yeah. They're wrong of course, but the idea is hard to shake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=455552#post455552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured once people would still thinking, &quot;Oh, <b>Beast</b> uses <b>Mage</b>'s Astral&quot; then once again everyone is going to jump the gun about how Mages know everything - which isn't good for <b>Mage</b> or the other game-line. The World of Darkness is about mystery, and I want to see that kept is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point. We haven't just been told that Beast uses Mage's Astral. We've been told that <i>the Astral isn't Mage's</i>. They don't get exclusive claim to it, exclusive use to it, or exclusive understanding of it, being as they've been compared to a blind man with an elephant. As have the Beasts. Thus we've been told that the Astral is something beyond what either mages or Beasts understand. How does this translate into &quot;mages know everything&quot; - how does it translate into a lack of mystery?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, that came out as more ranty than I meant, but I do with the idea that any link between gamelines means that mage wins in some way would go away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456129#post456129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a small update. As per the Blackhatted One on RPG.net, your Lair is your power stat. Discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very interesting. Especially in light of how Beasts can share a Lair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456241#post456241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the wild theory that they don't even have a Fuel Stat, that powers just need you to be at Satiety &quot;X&quot; to work and maybe that's how its reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered about that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 03-25-2015, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:31:07-07:00","id":457361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=456963#post456963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point. We haven't just been told that Beast uses Mage's Astral. We've been told that <i>the Astral isn't Mage's</i>. They don't get exclusive claim to it, exclusive use to it, or exclusive understanding of it, being as they've been compared to a blind man with an elephant. As have the Beasts. Thus we've been told that the Astral is something beyond what either mages or Beasts understand. How does this translate into &quot;mages know everything&quot; - how does it translate into a lack of mystery?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, that came out as more ranty than I meant, but I do with the idea that any link between gamelines means that mage wins in some way would go away.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>And as repeatedly mentioned, mages <i>know </i>they don't everything. Knowing a little more and learning practical applications for your magic is the definition of Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> I am <i>so glad </i>the Supernal is going to just be the programming code of reality now, with creatures that live in it that are defined by things outside of it. That way there's something you can point to and go &quot;no, if they knew more, using <i>that </i>would not be nearly as dangerous as it is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T08:11:57-07:00","id":458065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt, Beast: the Primordial teaser thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satiety <i>is</i> the fuel trait. It has different effects on the game if it's high or low, but you have to watch that it doesn't hit 0 or 10 (unless you want some real difficulties).<br /> <br /> Beasts don't have another fuel trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hooly molley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T08:20:26-07:00","id":458068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=458065#post458065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hooly molley.</div> </div> </div> </div> HUNGER INTENSIFIES!<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, this is going to be fun. I wonder, does that mean that you actually spend Dots of Satiety to use powers, or does it mean using a power causes Satiety breaking points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T08:31:11-07:00","id":458075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=458068#post458068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> HUNGER INTENSIFIES!<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, this is going to be fun. I wonder, does that mean that you actually spend Dots of Satiety to use powers, or does it mean using a power causes Satiety breaking points?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first one. You don't <i>have</i> to spend Satiety to fuel Nightmares and Atavisms, but fun things happen if you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T16:38:45-07:00","id":458484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=458075#post458075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The first one. You don't <i>have</i> to spend Satiety to fuel Nightmares and Atavisms, but fun things happen if you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the sound of that. When you use your powers, you can play it slow and safe, or go all out and really let loose!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T03:19:04-07:00","id":459803,"title":"","content":"You know, it occurred to me that Beast is the best fit for Batman yet- A creature born of fear, driven by obsession, who partners up with other unusual characters, with a cool lair, who draws crazy antagonists like moths to the flame.<br /> <br /> As for the beast aspect, I don't know, Camazotz the bat god of death? Namtaru or Anakim with the hunger for punishment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T07:15:24-07:00","id":459910,"title":"","content":"Batman as an Eshmati with a Hunger for Punishment has been going through my head for a while now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T07:32:33-07:00","id":459918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=459803#post459803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, it occurred to me that Beast is the best fit for Batman yet- A creature born of fear, driven by obsession, who partners up with other unusual characters, with a cool lair, who draws crazy antagonists like moths to the flame.<br /> <br /> As for the beast aspect, I don't know, Camazotz the bat god of death? Namtaru or Anakim with the hunger for punishment</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting comment about Batman as a Beast. <br /> <br /> As an aside, I'm always amused how with every RPG game, WW or otherwise, there is some attempt to find or create the Batman equivalent character. The Caped Crusader has certainly left quite an indelible mark on our cultural psyche. I still fondly recall WW's Mage homage to him with the Veiled Guardinan, as part of White Wolf Presents: The Cabal, in the Mage's Chronicler's Book, p. 210-19. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:13:31-07:00","id":460519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=459918#post459918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting comment about Batman as a Beast.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'm always amused how with every RPG game, WW or otherwise, there is some attempt to find or create the Batman equivalent character. The Caped Crusader has certainly left quite an indelible mark on our cultural psyche. I still fondly recall WW's Mage homage to him with the Veiled Guardinan, as part of White Wolf Presents: The Cabal, in the Mage's Chronicler's Book, p. 210-19.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well let's see just from nwod style things, we've seen Batman as:<br /> <br /> Vampire<br /> <br /> wizard- so mage<br /> <br /> frankenstein monster, and robot- promethean<br /> <br /> gargoyle- seems rather changeling ish to me<br /> <br /> avatar of Camazotz- sounds like a possible sin-easter to me<br /> <br /> resurrected servant of an egyptian god- sounds pretty in theme for mummy there<br /> <br /> demon<br /> <br /> Considering hunters can go after regular criminals too, hunter is rather obvious<br /> <br /> And I think I remember batman as a werebat, so there's a werewolf connection<br /> <br /> Oh, I know, a beast chronicle idea- The league of batmen- A beast with a grudge against crime in a hive of scum and villainy collects some of his cousins to take a bite out of crime (perhaps literally). lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T19:53:33-07:00","id":460618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=460519#post460519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well let's see just from nwod style things, we've seen Batman as:<br /> <br /> Vampire<br /> <br /> wizard- so mage<br /> <br /> frankenstein monster, and robot- promethean<br /> <br /> gargoyle- seems rather changeling ish to me<br /> <br /> avatar of Camazotz- sounds like a possible sin-easter to me<br /> <br /> resurrected servant of an egyptian god- sounds pretty in theme for mummy there<br /> <br /> demon<br /> <br /> Considering hunters can go after regular criminals too, hunter is rather obvious<br /> <br /> And I think I remember batman as a werebat, so there's a werewolf connection<br /> <br /> Oh, I know, a beast chronicle idea- The league of batmen- A beast with a grudge against crime in a hive of scum and villainy collects some of his cousins to take a bite out of crime (perhaps literally). lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is his own splat.<br /> <br /> You got Campy batman, you got Alan Moore's Batman, you got the Nolan Batman, you got Future Bat and so on. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T22:40:49-07:00","id":460715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=460618#post460618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman is his own splat.<br /> <br /> You got Campy batman, you got Alan Moore's Batman, you got the Nolan Batman, you got Future Bat and so on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, does that make Robin the demi-splat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:01:41-07:00","id":460735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=460618#post460618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman is his own splat.<br /> <br /> You got Campy batman, you got Alan Moore's Batman, you got the Nolan Batman, you got Future Bat and so on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Miller Bat is an antagonist splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T01:40:31-07:00","id":460845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=460618#post460618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman is his own splat.<br /> <br /> You got Campy batman, you got Alan Moore's Batman, you got the Nolan Batman, you got Future Bat and so on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Batman: The Wish-Fulfillment, coming to WW from OPP atGenCon 2016 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It would certainly be &quot;interesting&quot; if OPP ever received the RPG license to Batman, or more frightening, the whole DC Universe. <br /> <br /> Then again, we'll soon have Aberrant 2e . . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, does that make Robin the demi-splat? </div> </div> </div>Too specific. The demi-split are just Sidekicks\u2122. Batman certainly has had companions other than the Robins. However, no self-respecting <i>Hero</i> should be without a sidekick to bask in the hero's glory! [At least if the heroes are the protagonists of the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T04:51:30-07:00","id":460936,"title":"","content":"You know that reminds me, while I know that beasts as written don't have a demi-splat, I was trying to think of what would work.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something in between an Igor and a minder- someone who helps move the bodies, but also reminds the beast that they need to pay their electricity bill and that their 5th year anniversary is coming up, someone completely blas\u00e9 about the nightmare aura that might spill out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:23:27-07:00","id":462038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=460936#post460936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know that reminds me, while I know that beasts as written don't have a demi-splat, I was trying to think of what would work.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something in between an Igor and a minder- someone who helps move the bodies, but also reminds the beast that they need to pay their electricity bill and that their 5th year anniversary is coming up, someone completely blas\u00e9 about the nightmare aura that might spill out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the band manager from Queen of the Damned? Or better yet, Alfred from Hudson Hawk.<br /> <br /> Also, if Sidekicks are the demi-splat in Batman: TWF I'm gonna need some hard rules to play Red Hood. Batman with guns, how can you lose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:59:43-07:00","id":462048,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that ome under the Miller Batman evil-splat? A significant variation to be sure, but why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T03:49:01-07:00","id":462073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UnjustCustos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462038#post462038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the band manager from Queen of the Damned? Or better yet, Alfred from Hudson Hawk.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, pretty much. Actually, since its been revealed that beasts have super-merits, assistants like that might be canon, they just aren't considered a demisplat.<br /> <br /> An assistant who freaks out hysterically from your nightmare aura isn't much of a super-assistant after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:39:00-07:00","id":462237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462048#post462048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that ome under the Miller Batman evil-splat? A significant variation to be sure, but why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of what Banishers are to Mages.<br /> <br /> Also, on a more relevant note, Matt added a few new spoilers on the RPG.net forum thread, including tidbits such as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><img src=\"http://forum.rpg.net/images/misc/quote_icon.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Originally Posted by <b>Spirit Reaver</b> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?p=18864065#post18864065\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://forum.rpg.net/images/buttons/viewpost-right.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></span><br /> Is Beast also interesting when you have no interests in crossover games?<br /> <br /> </span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Why would you have no interest in crossover games? </span></span><i>Weirdo</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">No, seriously, you can absolutely play </span></span><b>Beast</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> without other game lines. What you can't really do is play it without any other supernatural weirdness; a big part of </span></span><b>Beast</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> is going out and finding the strange shit that lives in the shadows. It's your family, after all. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Also, I'm doing a development pass on the Satiety rules right now, and I post this on my FB. I think you all might be interested:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Seriously, I'm really liking how these rules are coming together. You </span></span><i>can </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">get by doing Family Dinner forever, but that's never going to fill you up, and it's dangerous because you're following people around while they're doing intimate things. You </span></span><i>can </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">get by on little meals, but your Soul is always going to be grouchy and that'll lead to Heroes. You </span></span><i>can </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">eat bigger meals, but once decent roll and you're Human for a while, and that's a bitch.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Matt also confirmed that &quot;Family Dinner&quot; is the actual name of a mechanic, and that Beasts piggy back on other supernatural creatures 'feeding' their fuel stat to sate their hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-30-2015, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:56:50-07:00","id":462451,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You </span></i></span><i>can </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">eat bigger meals, but once decent roll and you're Human for a while, and that's a bitch.&quot; oO </span></i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:32:39-07:00","id":462637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462451#post462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You </span></i></span><i>can </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">eat bigger meals, but once decent roll and you're Human for a while, and that's a bitch.&quot; oO </span></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can imagine doing that intentionally has advantages though. For one, you get to take a vacation from the World of Darkness for a little bit, if you do it in a relatively safe place-you're human, after all, and that means you don't have to work to fit in with your human family. For another, being human likely means you're invisible to mystical senses-like Heroes. While they're wondering where the hell you went after gorging, you can just take a plane and move somewhere Hero-free without fear of them tracking you. Or set up an ambush right under their noses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:52:44-07:00","id":462648,"title":"","content":"Yeah, except that you're also stifled and scrammed back wholly into your old meat bag/easy-to-victimize self. I imagine, given some of the tone given to the Beasts, being human again is a really shitty proposition for most of the Eldest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:57:13-07:00","