s=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So can chimps. Do you want to be a chimp?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considerably less stressful lifestyle, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:22:13-07:00","id":462967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462947#post462947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considerably less stressful lifestyle, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather have the stress and be what I am than not have it and miss out on so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:06:27-07:00","id":462994,"title":"","content":"I hope when you go human the Heroes still have a tingle in the Self-Righteous Sense. No need to redo the Beast/Sentinel scene from Days of Future Past. &quot;Man, that guy is getting too close. Time to go human. Nom nom nom innocent-whistle.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:17:04-07:00","id":462999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462887#post462887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do note that humans can still be pretty damn dangerous if they have their wits about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but Beasts are already creatures whose souls seem to be expansive dream beasts who dwell in ever more expansive dream realms who spend their time rampaging throughout an infinite mindscape of base terror. Accessing their souls through hunger, through atavisms, through nightmares- that let's them push against the flesh bubbles they float around in, to stretch and <i>be</i>. Beasts have spent their entire lives feeling confined and now understand why, as well as how to escape that feeling.<br /> <br /> Yes, humans are still damn dangerous. But when you become such a large phatasmagorical predator, why would you ever want to be such a little thing?<br /> <br /> At least, this is what teases from chatter have indicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T00:46:39-07:00","id":463186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=462637#post462637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can imagine doing that intentionally has advantages though. For one, you get to take a vacation from the World of Darkness for a little bit, if you do it in a relatively safe place-you're human, after all, and that means you don't have to work to fit in with your human family. For another, being human likely means you're invisible to mystical senses-like Heroes. While they're wondering where the hell you went after gorging, you can just take a plane and move somewhere Hero-free without fear of them tracking you. Or set up an ambush right under their noses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd Imagine the idea is that while your &quot;Beast Soul&quot; sleeps... You can actually FEEL the Guilt and Remorse of what you've been doing... Since you've only got the Human Part telling you what is right or wrong at that point. And Feeding on Fear and making others Terrified just because your hungry would Probably ding as something a normal person would balk at.<br /> Hence the &quot;and that feels Terrible&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:21:51-07:00","id":463489,"title":"","content":"So the last Family is called Makara according to Matt over on the RPG.net thread.<br /> <br /> Also, a Beast's Lair has a Heart that destroys the Lair if it gets destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:52:04-07:00","id":463561,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the part where Matt says the Primordial Dream is not entirely synonymous with the Astral <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will be redeemed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:23:27-07:00","id":463577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463489#post463489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the last Family is called Makara according to Matt over on the RPG.net thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering the biggest hit on the subject was a Hindu mythological figure best known for ferrying the goddess of the river Ganges and the sea god around, it looks like we have the &quot;Fear of Drowning&quot; that was hinted at!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:19:51-07:00","id":463606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=453065#post453065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be lying if I said I'm not totally stoked at the idea of playing a Kraken. Or maybe some sort of large spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> I've a Shadow/fire gryphon personality I'm working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:28:07-07:00","id":463612,"title":"","content":"Makara is a Hindu sea monster and the root of the Hindi word &quot;mugger&quot; meaning &quot;crocodile&quot;; the English word &quot;mugger&quot; meaning one who sneaks up and attacks from behind is derived from this. So Makara likely represents fear of the dark/unknown/being ambushed.<br /> <br /> So if I have all the info right (feel free to correct me if not) we have Namtaru (fear of disease/the inevitable/slow creeping death?), Anakim (fear of being overpowered by something massively stronger than you), Eshmaki (fear of gore/violence?), and Makara (fear of the dark/unknown/being ambushed) as Families (X-splat), with Punishment, Prey, Power, Hoard, and Ruin as Hungers (Y-splat). Satiety as both Integrity replacement and fuel stat, Lair as power stat.<br /> <br /> More info reposted from earlier in the thread:<br /> <br /> Beasts claim descent from a being known as the Dark Mother, AKA Lilith, Tiamat, Hecate, and several other names, who entered the &quot;Primordial Dream&quot; long ago and brought forth the essences of mankind's shared nightmares, which became the souls of the first Beasts.<br /> <br /> A Beast's body appears human in the Material Plane but his soul resides in his Lair, a place inside a dream realm related to Mage's Astral Plane in some way. Said soul takes the form of a nightmare monster, which the player has a high degree of freedom to design in terms of appearance. Also, based on his soul's form, the Beast can manifest some abilities in his human form, perhaps on par with a Uratha in war form at their most extreme. Speculative example: a Beast who's a dragon in his Lair might be highly resistant or immune to heat/fire, capable of jumping really high/gliding on wings, breathing fire, etc. However, he cannot turn into a gigantic fire-breathing reptile in Times Square.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety makes you more powerful while high Satiety makes you more focused. However, hitting 10 will cause your soul to go on a rampage across the dream realm, which causes Heroes to arise and come after you. Heroes are dicks who think they're the protagonists of the story; think Gaston from <i>Beauty and the Beast</i> (Disney version), Carl Denham from <i>King Kong</i>, or Captain Hammer from <i>Dr. Horrible's Sing-Along Blog</i>.<br /> <br /> Hitting 0 Satiety is also bad for other reasons.<br /> <br /> Beasts see most of the other splats as extended family; Demons are apparently an exception. Mages are viewed as the pompous upstart who went to MIT and thinks they're smarter than everyone else; annoying, but still welcome at Thanksgiving dinner. Prometheans are the adopted sibling.<br /> <br /> We have a mechanic called &quot;Family Dinner&quot; where Beasts can gain Satiety by tagging along while other splats gain their fuel stat. Standing watch at the entrance to an alley while a Vampire feeds, pointing a pack of Werewolves.towards their prey, etc. They can also enhance other splats' powers and pick up some kind of powers based in those of other splats they encounter.<br /> <br /> Powers are divided into Nightmares and Atavisms. Nightmares work better at high high Satiety while Atavisms work better at low Satiety.<br /> <br /> Heroes are extremely good at finding a Beast's &quot;Anathema&quot; (weaknesses, probably similar to a spirit's Bans). The rules for Anathema are tied to Satiety.<br /> <br /> Lairs can be shared between Beasts and other splats can enter a Beast's lair if they're invited/&quot;have the key&quot;.<br /> <br /> A Beast's Lair can be accessed from any location that shares a resonance. Example given was a scary beach that can be accessed from any place with a lot of water, like a swimming pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-31-2015, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:38:32-07:00","id":463620,"title":"","content":"Xenu, Matt also indicated that a fifth Hunger was Ruin. Also, I believe you switched the effects for high and low Satiety. A Beast is most focused while satied, but more dangerous when hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:27:16-07:00","id":463641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463620#post463620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xenu, Matt also indicated that a fifth Hunger was Ruin. Also, I believe you switched the effects for high and low Satiety. A Beast is most focused while satied, but more dangerous when hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think you might be correct.<br /> <br /> Any indication as to whether there's a fifth Family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-31-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:38:43-07:00","id":463648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463641#post463641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I think you might be correct.<br /> <br /> Any indication as to whether there's a fifth Family?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall, and although the issue has been discussed today in the RPG.net thread, I've seen no mention of another Family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:48:37-07:00","id":463652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463648#post463648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recall, and although the issue has been discussed today in the RPG.net thread, I've seen no mention of another Family.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are five families - we've even referenced the fifth one in very early spoilers, but I don't know if their name is in the wild yet, so won't reveal it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:55:09-07:00","id":463654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463652#post463652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are five families - we've even referenced the fifth one in very early spoilers, but I don't know if their name is in the wild yet, so won't reveal it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dave, you are delightfully evil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I shall propose that the fifth family be the Bunkers, involving the fear of alienation, bigotry and isolation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn-www.i-am-bored.com/media/thumbnails/All444[1].jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:23:22-07:00","id":463667,"title":"","content":"Matt has revealed the fifth Family and some other info.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><img src=\"http://forum.rpg.net/images/misc/quote_icon.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Originally Posted by <b>BlackHat_Matt</b> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?p=18870437#post18870437\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://forum.rpg.net/images/buttons/viewpost-right.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Oh, whoops, damn. I thought I'd revealed four of five before Makara, but apparently I hadn't. Erm. <br /> <br /> Well, anyway, Makara are fear of drowning, of being dragged down into the deeps, and of the immense thing you can't quite see but you know is there. They're my favorite Family. <br /> <br /> Yeah, that'd make me uncomfortable, too. Fortunately, no one said that. <br /> <br /> Heroes aren't mentally ill. Beasts <i>exist</i>. The things they're responding to are real. You can't say, &quot;well, Heroes in the real world&quot; because <i>there aren't any</i>, because there aren't any Beasts. <br /> <br /> &quot;Homestuck&quot; is some anime thing, right?</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:01:47-07:00","id":463705,"title":"","content":"Another thing to note. Mr. Blackhat_Matt plans to do some blog posts week after nexr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:15:36-07:00","id":463718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463667#post463667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt has revealed the fifth Family and some other info.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's one more Family to be revealed (that is, the fifth), unless I missed a spoiler somewhere. My favorite one, too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:25:53-07:00","id":463724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463718#post463718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's one more Family to be revealed (that is, the fifth), unless I missed a spoiler somewhere. My favorite one, too...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oops. My mistake. He acknowledged he did reveal all five, but then only provided more info on the Makara, rather than the last Family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:47:23-07:00","id":463841,"title":"","content":"Makara as &quot;fear of drowning, of being dragged down into the deeps, and of the immense thing you can't quite see but you know is there&quot; seems very specific as opposed to the more broad portfolios I was thinking Families would encompass.<br /> <br /> Then again, Beasts are tied specifically to nightmares, and that's a fairly common one, along with &quot;being chased by a predator/pack of predators,&quot; &quot;giant monster rampaging through the area,&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> Honestly, disease and lingering death aren't really particularly prevalent nightmare fixtures AFAIK, so maybe Namtaru represent something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:53:32-07:00","id":463846,"title":"","content":"Namtaru are Revulsion, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> If the nightmare is that bugs are everywhere or something utterly revolting is present, it's Namtaru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:07:54-07:00","id":463854,"title":"","content":"It also might incorporate the ravages of disease and the malformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:09:50-07:00","id":463858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463846#post463846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Namtaru are Revulsion, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> If the nightmare is that bugs are everywhere or something utterly revolting is present, it's Namtaru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Families are fairly broad but Matt used a fairly specific example for Makara because it's more evocative?<br /> <br /> So maybe it's like... Namtaru is revulsion, Makara is being stalked in a hostile environment, Anakim is the giant creature that crushes you underfoot, Eshmaki is supernatural evil incarnate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:13:53-07:00","id":463860,"title":"","content":"Namtaru: Bitch, I'm fabulous.<br /> <br /> I just felt like saying that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:42:46-07:00","id":463953,"title":"","content":"There are still several primordial fears I think we're lacking here, and I think this product is going to suck without them! I list them here along with their requisite families for my own edification and so you all may recognize my brilliance.<ul><li>Fear of Belching (Carbonites)</li> <li>Fear of Teeth Falling Out (Dentate)</li> <li>Fear of Being Naked in Public (Nudikall)</li> <li>Fear of Eating Your Young Again (Hamtaru)</li> <li>Fear of Disappointing Your Mother (Medea)</li> </ul>But in seriousness... I am wondering if our last Family will represent the fear of falling, one of the most common nightmares and fears. Since the influences for the Families seem to be pre-Christian, you could go with the <i>shahrokh</i> from Persian myth.<br /> <br /> Take a look at this image comparing what I believe is supposed to be a &quot;thunderbird&quot; wingspan to a man ( But it's been on the net for years, so who knows). Always creeped me out a little.<br /> <img src=\"http://i2.wp.com/listverse.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/08/thunderbird.jpg?resize=550%2C355\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  clarity 03-31-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T16:51:55-07:00","id":464017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463953#post463953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fear of Belching (Carbonites)</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the fear of pissing off Jabba the Hutt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:12:22-07:00","id":464115,"title":"","content":"We finally know why humans in general don't get along with Heroes:<br /> <br /> Heroes are what hunters are afraid of most of all-the guy in the funhouse mirror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the ironies of Heroes is that they're created when Beasts are probably least harmful.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that hunters are the good Heroes, as that Heroes are the bad hunters. The stuff <i>Hunter</i> has running through it about not letting the Vigil consume your life? Heroes have already crossed that line. I'm not sure you'd actually <i>want</i> a Hero in a hunter cell, from an actual gameplay perspective, but their interests could align. (EDIT: A PC hunter cell, I mean.)<br /> <br /> For example, I had an NPC concept for my playtest game* for Jackie, a 16-year-old kid whose visions and obsession keep leading an entirely mundane group of people into conflict with the PCs. I was thinking her mini-mob could be Union.<br /> <br /> I should mention that I don't actually have a huge investment in whether people sympathize with the Heroic viewpoint. For me, Heroes are over the edge, but, hey, so are some werewolves. To Beasts they really do look pretty bad, and there are some reasons in the antagonist chapter that they don't make such hot PCs. But, y'know, if you want one that's more Clarice Starling than Gaston, sure, okay.<br /> <br /> I even have a line about Medusa conceding what you could call a... moral point... to Perseus, in one of the few places the Families stuff mentions Heroes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Which I probably won't use because the mystery involved has taken a very different direction than I was originally thinking.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:02:53-07:00","id":464141,"title":"","content":"Not really a surprise to me, it always seem to me extremely probable that they used the term heroes as in the classical hero mold, and in slasher there's the theory that the classical heroes were proof of ancient slashers.<br /> <br /> So heroes closer to slashers than hunters, that's what I've been figuring for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:17:42-07:00","id":464169,"title":"","content":"It does raise the question of what Beast focused Hunters (and focused Compact and Comspiracy) would look like and what distinction exists between them and heroes. <br /> <br /> Which segways back to be deep hope that if we get a Kickstarter for this we get a &quot;Mortal Remains chapter&quot; as a stretch goal pdf!<br /> <br /> (Same for a Dark Era)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T05:48:14-07:00","id":464607,"title":"","content":"And we now have the fifth Family from Matt, the Ugallu, associated with the fear of being watched and the fear of monsters from the sky. (According to Wikipedia, Ugallu was a storm demon with a lion's head and bird's feet. He belonged to the class of demons associated with moments of divine intervention in human life.)<br /> <br /> He's also said there's nothing stopping them from having more Families and Hungers if they have good ideas for them, which'd be material for a Player's Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 04-01-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T06:39:47-07:00","id":464629,"title":"","content":"Alright, so the Families are:<br /> \u2022Namtaru-Fear of death/disease/creepy-crawlies(?)<br /> \u2022Anakim-Fear of Insignificance/huge things(?)<br /> \u2022Eshmaki-Fear of Violence/Darkness(?)<br /> \u2022Makara-Fear of Drowning/the Water and those things that lurk within unseen<br /> \u2022Ugallu-Fear of being watched/the Sky and those things that lurk within it.<br /> <br /> And the Hungers are:<br /> \u2022Power<br /> \u2022Punishment<br /> \u2022Prey<br /> \u2022Hoard<br /> \u2022Ruin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T08:45:29-07:00","id":464713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=464629#post464629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so the Families are:<br /> \u2022Namtaru-Fear of death/disease/creepy-crawlies(?)<br /> \u2022Anakim-Fear of Insignificance/huge things(?)<br /> \u2022Eshmaki-Fear of Violence/Darkness(?)<br /> \u2022Makara-Fear of Drowning/the Water and those things that lurk within unseen<br /> \u2022Ugallu-Fear of being watched/the Sky and those things that lurk within it.<br /> <br /> And the Hungers are:<br /> \u2022Power<br /> \u2022Punishment<br /> \u2022Prey<br /> \u2022Hoard<br /> \u2022Ruin</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, we have enough info to assign a Family and Hunger to all the mythological and movie monsters you'd care to think of, with some margin of error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T10:13:45-07:00","id":464828,"title":"","content":"I don't know about you all but I feel like an itch in my brain has finally been scratched.<br /> <br /> Love that the Ugallu also deal with the &quot;something's following me&quot; feeling, though I'm interested in how that'll play with those who don't Hunger for Prey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=464607#post464607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's also said there's nothing stopping them from having more Families and Hungers if they have good ideas for them, which'd be material for a Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better watch out, gang... the Kawaii-desu Family Hungers...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...for <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b><span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">YOUR LOVE!!!</span></b></i></span> &lt;3 &lt;3 &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 04-01-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T10:39:27-07:00","id":464845,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I've been poking through the RPG.net thread, and I just wanna say?<br /> <br /> Thank you all for being sane members of society and these little communities. You guys make active participation in the fandom interesting rather than an infernal slog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:01:45-07:00","id":464899,"title":"","content":"I really like the open possibility for more Families, though I am wondering what the idea is for Beasts congregating together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:27:45-07:00","id":464921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=464845#post464845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I've been poking through the RPG.net thread, and I just wanna say?<br /> <br /> Thank you all for being sane members of society and these little communities. You guys make active participation in the fandom interesting rather than an infernal slog.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel bad for contributing to the slog on RPG.net.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm hoping for a Family that represents Fear of Aging, even though that seems like a mashup between the Namtaru and the Anakim. What with it basically being a fear of <i>becoming</i> insignificant, and also dying. Similarly, Fear of Loss. Like, losing the things that are important to you.<br /> <br /> What? No, I don't want to make a Beast who can be best friends with a Mummy, why do you ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:36:20-07:00","id":464927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463612#post463612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Beasts see most of the other splats as extended family; Demons are apparently an exception. Mages are viewed as the pompous upstart who went to MIT and thinks they're smarter than everyone else; annoying, but still welcome at Thanksgiving dinner. Prometheans are the adopted sibling.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in crossover games with Mage, would it be more fitting to look at an allied Awakened more as a &quot;Consigliere&quot; than a &quot;Cousin&quot;?<br /> <br /> ...and possibly Angels &amp; Demons as G-Men?<br /> <br /> I wonder what kind of Beast Michael Corleone would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:37:26-07:00","id":464928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=464828#post464828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love that the Ugallu also deal with the &quot;something's following me&quot; feeling, though I'm interested in how that'll play with those who don't Hunger for Prey.</div> </div> </div> </div> For Punishment maybe some sort of unseen, million-eyed THING that constantly watches you, that sees you at your vilest and most disgusting, and knows who to tell to make your life just fall into a thousand pieces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:17:10-07:00","id":464954,"title":"","content":"Or Slenderman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:54:28-07:00","id":465048,"title":"","content":"I'm now picturing an ugallu moddled after the clif racers from morrowwind. It's hunger is ruin. Ruin of your sanity that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:57:10-07:00","id":465052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=465048#post465048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now picturing an ugallu moddled after the clif racers from morrowwind. It's hunger is ruin. Ruin of your sanity that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never have I been more frightened of a monster in any game. At least until <i>Alien: Isolation</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:28:31-07:00","id":465228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=464828#post464828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love that the Ugallu also deal with the &quot;something's following me&quot; feeling, though I'm interested in how that'll play with those who don't Hunger for Prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could easily play in to all sorts of paranoia, depending of what you think you have to lose:<br /> <br /> Power: The upstart young gun who is lined up to become your boss.<br /> Punishment: The &quot;I know what you did last summer&quot; guy.<br /> Hoard: The identity thief who bankrupts a wealthy family.<br /> Ruin: The PI who has evidence of your illegal activities, and is blackmailing you to keep the secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:59:30-07:00","id":465292,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu: Makara/Ruin<br /> Smaug: Ugallu/Hoard<br /> Shelob: Namtaru/Prey<br /> The Boogeyman (Real Ghostbusters): Eshmaki/Hoard? (He feeds on fear, but doesn't have any need to harm anyone, nor does he seem to have the desire to do so. I think that rules out Prey.)<br /> The Minotaur: Anakim/Prey<br /> Pinhead: Eshmaki/Ruin<br /> Freddy Krueger: Eshmaki/Punishment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 04-01-2015, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:03:15-07:00","id":465297,"title":"","content":"are you real","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:04:27-07:00","id":465298,"title":"","content":"I. Hmm.<br /> <br /> I don't think I want to touch that expansion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:05:24-07:00","id":465299,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please respect </span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rule 9</span></a><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">, which forbids cross-forum drama.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:14:37-07:00","id":465302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=465299#post465299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please respect </span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules&amp;quot;]</a><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rule 9</span>[/URL]<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">, which forbids cross-forum drama.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops.<br /> <br /> 10chars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:30:58-07:00","id":466313,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the derail. Anyway, reposting and expanding on the actual relevant bit of that post in hopes of getting the discussion rekindled.<br /> <br /> Apparently I can only include 4 images in a post, so I'll split this into 2.<br /> <br /> Here are some famous Beasts with my take on their Families and Hungers (1/2):<br /> <br /> Cthulhu: Makara/Ruin<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://th05.deviantart.net/fs71/200H/i/2012/074/c/6/star_spawn_of_cthulhu_by_eclectixx-d4sui2d.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, according to the story, he's actually IMPRISONED under the water, which impedes his psychic powers. But his Lair is absolutely aquatic in nature; R'lyeh is described as &quot;dripping&quot;, &quot;damp&quot;, and &quot;slimy&quot;. That makes him Makara in my estimation, plus he's an unseen presence in those dreams, lurking ominously, ready to strike; that also fits Makara.<br /> <br /> In the context of Beast, Cthulhu's soul exists ONLY in the dream-world. Presumably, there's a REALLY OLD Beast passing as human, maybe one of the &quot;deathless Chinamen&quot; who leads the cult? The crew of the Emma supposedly encountering him in the real world can be explained as them entering his Lair at a site of high Resonance. Perhaps Captain Collins was a Hero who set out to hunt Cthulhu deliberately in the wake of an obvious Satiety 10 rampage? Poor bastard.<br /> <br /> Smaug: Ugallu/Hoard<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" v