nd make it hard to scroll the page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:50:54-07:00","id":466329,"title":"","content":"where is the things for the families? I missed to have never found where this info is at","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:17:13-07:00","id":466357,"title":"","content":"So ever since Beast got announced, I've been picturing <a href=\"http://www.supernaturalwiki.com/index.php?title=Leviathan\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a>and <a href=\"http://www.supernaturalwiki.com/index.php?title=Eve\" target=\"_blank\">this lady</a> as Beasts. I've got a few ideas as to what they are, too:<br /> <br /> WARNING: Large pictures<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.supernaturalwiki.com/images/2/2d/DickRoman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Dick Roman, leader of the Leviathans<br /> Family: They're gross, and have huge mouths full of teeth: but really that's probably just an Atavism of some sort that they manifest before feeding. The threat that the Leviathans posed in Supernatural was that they were everywhere, could be anybody, and controlled the media and a significant chunk of the government and large businesses. Plus they're basically impossible to kill, except by gathering up a series of nigh-impossible-to-acquire ingredients that will only work once per use.<br /> <br /> I peg them as Anakim, just barely followed by Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> Hunger: At first I was going to say Prey. The ultimate goal of Dick Roman, their leader, is to turn humanity into cattle: fat and too stupid to be anything but obedient. His M.O. however is to gather Power. Political, monetary. He practically gets off on it.<br /> <br /> So of course, he hungers for Power.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.supernaturalwiki.com/images/d/dc/EveRising.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Eve, Mother of Monsters<br /> <br /> With a name like that, you'd figure she's The Dark Mother. And I can grant you that that's not a bad guess, but she's handled without much aplomb in the show, so I think she's closer to just being a powerful Beast herself, maybe one of those Incarnates that Matt mentioned.<br /> <br /> Family: Namtaru. Her primary ability seems to be the ability to create new monsters. Not just the ones that exist already, but entirely new ones that are horrible and hard to kill (<a href=\"http://www.supernaturalwiki.com/index.php?title=Jefferson_Starships\" target=\"_blank\">Jefferson Starships</a>). The creation method resembles a virus/icky thing, so that's why I picked Namtaru.<br /> <br /> Hunger: This one was weird. At least until I remembered what her deal was: She came back out of Purgatory to find the one who had been kidnapping and torturing her family/children.<br /> <br /> So I figure it's clear that she hungers for Punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:35:56-07:00","id":466372,"title":"","content":"The Boogeyman<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://fc03.deviantart.net/fs36/i/2008/259/f/5/The_Boogeyman_by_TristJones.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>'Sup, brah? Why you lookin' at me like that? I'm just here to smoke.</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, seriously. If you're a child of the '80s like me, then this motherfucker gave you nightmares for years, full stop. If you say he didn't, then either you're a big fat liar or you didn't watch The Real Ghostbusters.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's a perfect fit for Beast. If you're not familiar with him, then first of all congratulations on the many hours of sleep you didn't miss out on! Secondly, here's the rundown:<ul><li>He lives in a crazy M.C. Escher-esque otherworldly domain filled with doors. Doors everyfuckingwhere. Each one opens into a closet in the real world.</li> <li>He eats fear. Needs it to survive. Seems to be the only form of sustenance he requires.</li> <li>His M.O. is basically to enter a child's room at night via the closet, scare the living shit out of them, then head back to his domain before repeating the process until he's full.</li> </ul><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/ghostbusters/images/c/c8/BoogiemansDomain05.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20111203080139\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>The Boogeyman's Lair.</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I mentioned above, he seems to be Eshmaki/Power. Eshmaki seems to be the &quot;demonic/classic thing-that-goes-bump-in-the-night&quot; Family, and I went with Power because he seems to enjoy terrorizing his victims, reveling in his ability to make them cower. The other Hungers don't really make much sense. He's not Prey because he doesn't harm his &quot;victims&quot;; Ruin is out unless you posit that long-term psychological trauma is the POINT of his nightly visits rather than a side effect, which is directly counter to the information given in the episodes in which he appears. Punishment makes no sense as his targets appear to be picked at random and, while he shows vindictiveness when hurt or humiliated, there's no indication that this informs his choice of victims. The only Hunger that might possibly work other than Power is Hoard, if you envision him stockpiling the fear.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://th00.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/f/2010/292/d/a/boogieman_by_ronniemick-d312oqt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>Maybe he's saving it up so he can pay a surgeon to correct that gnarly hydrocephaly he's got goin' on.</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> His &quot;harvesting fear&quot; schtick suggests a strong kinship to the Autumn Court of Changelings, while his &quot;victimizing children&quot; MO seems similar to the True Fae. I can see a crossover Chronicle where this guy takes some Ashen into his lair and protects them from the Gentry, only for them to start feeling like maybe they've merely left the fire for the frying pan... or vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 04-02-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:37:44-07:00","id":466374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466326#post466326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, I really think you should spoiler those images because they are fuckHUGE and make it hard to scroll the page.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Er, how do I do that? I looked for a spoiler button but couldn't find one.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind. Figured it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:42:48-07:00","id":466378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466374#post466374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Er, how do I do that? I looked for a spoiler button but couldn't find one.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind. Figured it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:16:33-07:00","id":466436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=463489#post463489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Beast's Lair has a Heart that destroys the Lair if it gets destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this struck me as kinda interesting at the time when I first read it. <br /> <br /> I was rereading Demon today and got to the bit about Linchpins and Infrastructure. Kinda noticed the similarity. <br /> <br /> Then I was thinking about a Demons reaction to a Beasts Lair once they were inside. Particularly since they are not considered family apparently.<br /> <br /> The confusion and misconceptions were amusing to imagine.<br /> <br /> Also Dark Mother as a &quot;rival&quot; to the God Machine is an interesting idea I feel. She comes from basic concepts of a chaotic primordial world that predates the &quot;order&quot; of human culture and civilization. Something that the God Machine is heavily invested in and embodies thematically via a cold sterile/messy body horror take on order.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that I can see the Dark Mother as a direct opponent to the GM, merely that they each represent opposing thematic forces and narratives. As such I find it interesting that their are some metaphysical similarities between their creations. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T15:02:34-07:00","id":466556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466436#post466436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So this struck me as kinda interesting at the time when I first read it.<br /> <br /> I was rereading Demon today and got to the bit about Linchpins and Infrastructure. Kinda noticed the similarity.<br /> <br /> Then I was thinking about a Demons reaction to a Beasts Lair once they were inside. Particularly since they are not considered family apparently.<br /> <br /> The confusion and misconceptions were amusing to imagine.<br /> <br /> Also Dark Mother as a &quot;rival&quot; to the God Machine is an interesting idea I feel. She comes from basic concepts of a chaotic primordial world that predates the &quot;order&quot; of human culture and civilization. Something that the God Machine is heavily invested in and embodies thematically via a cold sterile/messy body horror take on order.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that I can see the Dark Mother as a direct opponent to the GM, merely that they each represent opposing thematic forces and narratives. As such I find it interesting that their are some metaphysical similarities between their creations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know what's crazy about this?<br /> <br /> In the Demon game I'm running, one of the players is playing a Dark Hero. He's got lots of stealth-themed abilities, given to him by an ancient godlike figure called Mother Dark. She was around before the G-M, but got usurped or pushed out by it somehow and now she wants revenge. Or at least, that's how the character understands it. So imagine our surprise when we heard about this Dark Mother...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:48:32-07:00","id":466664,"title":"","content":"The problem I have with most of the above is that they're little more than socio/psychopaths. <b>Primordial</b> Beasts have to be better...have to be more than that. (Cthulhu...sure. Minotaur, yes. Those I grasp. The rest?...o no.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:57:28-07:00","id":466672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466664#post466664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with most of the above is that they're little more than socio/psychopaths. <b>Primordial</b> Beasts have to be better...have to be more than that. (Cthulhu...sure. Minotaur, yes. Those I grasp. The rest?...o no.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I dunno. We have no real info on what the Boogeyman does with his time other than scaring the shit out of little kids. Smaug the dragon spends most of his time sleeping; perhaps he's active in human form doing something cool and important while his dragon soul is napping. Pinhead only comes when summoned and his morality is... not like ours, in that he doesn't distinguish between pain and pleasure. Shelob's not <i>evil</i> per se, she's just really <i>hungry</i>.<br /> <br /> The only one I'd consider a real bad guy is Freddy, and, well... I don't think there's a rule that says Beasts can't be fairly vile individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:07:24-07:00","id":466756,"title":"","content":"ok...missed a couple. Giant spiders, dragons...on board with those. And adding an elemental aspect? Absolutely. (Shelob's shadow stuff is very evocative to me) But human monsters? No. I don't see the allure. It's just another skin for a vampire to me. And I loathe the idea of human parasites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:31:31-07:00","id":466789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466756#post466756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok...missed a couple. Giant spiders, dragons...on board with those. And adding an elemental aspect? Absolutely. (Shelob's shadow stuff is very evocative to me) But human monsters? No. I don't see the allure. It's just another skin for a vampire to me. And I loathe the idea of human parasites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Come on. The Boogeyman? THE Boogeyman? Definitive spooky story for countless centuries? Specifically in a form that ruined millions of childhoods in the mid-80s? And some of the most iconic movie monsters of the past two generations?<br /> <br /> Beasts are the embodied essence of humanity's fears given shape in the dream realm. You don't think we'd have one or two recent ones whose souls are drawn from pop culture?<br /> <br /> Think in terms of the <i>Wes Craven's New Nightmare</i> Freddy rather than the one from the main series...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:50:41-07:00","id":466816,"title":"","content":"The closest I can come to the idea is Clive Barker's &quot;Nightbreed.&quot; Just looking at that movie trailer...*sigh*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T20:19:54-07:00","id":466919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466756#post466756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok...missed a couple. Giant spiders, dragons...on board with those. And adding an elemental aspect? Absolutely. (Shelob's shadow stuff is very evocative to me) But human monsters? No. I don't see the allure. It's just another skin for a vampire to me. And I loathe the idea of human parasites.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my defense (I know you're also responding to Xenu's Paradox), the characters that I posted don't really have &quot;Beast forms&quot; ever shown in the show. Presumably Leviathans earn their name while in Purgatory, and I'm sure Eve is more than a dark-haired waif, but Beasts are explicitly humanoid when not hanging out in their lairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T21:04:21-07:00","id":466977,"title":"","content":"Beasts having a human form, yeah. No problems there. As I posted earlier about making a shadow/fire gryphon type character, he definitely has humanity as a part of his being. But he definitely knows anger, hunger, loneliness and other things that are all part of his being. A being that is always shifting between the sun's and the starry night, half lion, half eagle...But I can't see why anyone would want to roleplay Freddy Krueger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T01:25:40-07:00","id":467128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466977#post466977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts having a human form, yeah. No problems there. As I posted earlier about making a shadow/fire gryphon type character, he definitely has humanity as a part of his being. But he definitely knows anger, hunger, loneliness and other things that are all part of his being. A being that is always shifting between the sun's and the starry night, half lion, half eagle...But I can't see why anyone would want to roleplay Freddy Krueger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You must not have been a kid/teen during the 80's. Freddy was basically a superhero. Even if you aren't a fan of the movies, I recommend the documentary Never Sleep Again. It goes into not just the making of and history of the Elm Street movies, but the cultural zeitgeist that grew up around them. There were Freddy Kruger *kids pajamas*!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:43:24-07:00","id":467213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soonmot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467128#post467128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You must not have been a kid/teen during the 80's. Freddy was basically a superhero. Even if you aren't a fan of the movies, I recommend the documentary Never Sleep Again. It goes into not just the making of and history of the Elm Street movies, but the cultural zeitgeist that grew up around them. There were Freddy Kruger *kids pajamas*!</div> </div> </div> </div>As it was put earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=449754#post449754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other things include:<br /> <br /> According to Developer Rose Bailey: \u2022&quot;Some things individual Beasts do, from my second draft of the splats chapter:<br /> - <b>Protect the good kids in a juvenile facility from the horrors that walk the halls at night.</b><br /> - Steal back an inheritance piece by piece, leaving deadly things in their place.<br /> - Guard the pool that grants wishes, and profit from the secrets it whispers.<br /> - Watch over a shore-bound lover from afar.<br /> - Keep the thing in the hospital basement at bay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Krueger's origins I think we know where he belongs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:53:00-07:00","id":467220,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and later she posted something like, &quot;Who's to say the Beasts protecting the kids are good? Who determines what a 'good' kid means?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:04:30-07:00","id":467228,"title":"","content":"Silly question, since I don't have enough time to go through and double check stuff.<br /> <br /> What are the families &amp; their related fears?<br /> I've seen a few names but I don't know what they mean or where they came from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:43:02-07:00","id":467256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467220#post467220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and later she posted something like, &quot;Who's to say the Beasts protecting the kids are good? Who determines what a 'good' kid means?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was tongue in cheek.<br /> After all where does torturing and killing kids fit in anyone's view?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:18:28-07:00","id":467272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467228#post467228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly question, since I don't have enough time to go through and double check stuff.<br /> <br /> What are the families &amp; their related fears?<br /> I've seen a few names but I don't know what they mean or where they came from?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's back on page 81, but to save you time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so the Families are:<br /> \u2022Namtaru-Fear of death/disease/creepy-crawlies(?)<br /> \u2022Anakim-Fear of Insignificance/huge things(?)<br /> \u2022Eshmaki-Fear of Violence/Darkness(?)<br /> \u2022Makara-Fear of Drowning/the Water and those things that lurk within unseen<br /> \u2022Ugallu-Fear of being watched/the Sky and those things that lurk within it.<br /> <br /> And the Hungers are:<br /> \u2022Power<br /> \u2022Punishment<br /> \u2022Prey<br /> \u2022Hoard<br /> \u2022Ruin</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:21:38-07:00","id":467276,"title":"","content":"I guess I continue to look at mythological beasts and see where they fit in. Many of which I believe just wanted to be left alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:00:13-07:00","id":467329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467256#post467256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that was tongue in cheek.<br /> After all where does torturing and killing kids fit in anyone's view?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you haven't seen Let Me In/Let The Right One In?<br /> <br /> Let me propose an origin for Freddy based on having only seen the first two films and New Nightmare, and which I'm sure is absolutely inaccurate to the established canon:<br /> <br /> Those kids Freddy killed were vicious bullies who were making life a living goddamn hell for a special needs student he'd befriended. One night, they perpetrated an especially vicious &quot;prank&quot; on the poor guy and accidentally killed him. They covered it up and thought they'd gotten away with it. After all, nobody knew the &quot;retard&quot;* hadn't killed himself, right? I mean, he's so clumsy and STUPID, it'd be just like him.<br /> <br /> But Freddy knew. Oh, he wasn't there. But he KNEW.<br /> <br /> The legend says he became a monster after he burned to death, but that's not true at all.<br /> <br /> No, when that boy died, Freddy heard the call to his Lair. His rage at the injustice and his desire to see the perpetrators pay for what they'd done were heard by the Dark Mother, who smiled on his silent prayer for vengeance.<br /> <br /> And that's when Freddy became a Beast.<br /> <br /> Let me ask you something:<br /> <br /> Has Freddy ever gone after an unpopular kid?<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> *Yes, I know this is a derogatory term. I hope it's clear that I'm using it to reflect the viewpoint of some pretty unsympathetic and entirely fictional characters rather than my own. If that's still against the rules, I'll change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 04-03-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:20:27-07:00","id":467346,"title":"","content":"If you want to airbrush away Freddy's origins, which included murdering children, I'm sure there's room for it in the game. But we have plenty of real-life examples that could make the list more easily.<br /> Quite frankly I'm fairly certain that &quot;Beast; the Primordial&quot; has a lot more going for it than sadism and psychopathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:07:08-07:00","id":467398,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just had a thought. You know how the Devs have said that people who enter your Lair could destroy it, and that it wouldn't kill all of you? My thoughts is that this may mean the Begotten have a more permanent way than Satiety 10 to become human again, just like the Bound. All it takes is the one time low low cost of your sanity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:25:13-07:00","id":467477,"title":"","content":"That...doesn't sound quite right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:19:03-07:00","id":467556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467346#post467346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to airbrush away Freddy's origins, which included murdering children, I'm sure there's room for it in the game. But we have plenty of real-life examples that could make the list more easily.<br /> Quite frankly I'm fairly certain that &quot;Beast; the Primordial&quot; has a lot more going for it than sadism and psychopathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, sadism and psychopathy are the primary motivations behind player characters in tabletop RPGs.<br /> <br /> Then again, I've only actually played D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:30:34-07:00","id":467565,"title":"","content":"I've played even D&amp;D games where that statement is not true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:48:09-07:00","id":467582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467565#post467565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played even D&amp;D games where that statement is not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! Sometimes we act out of boredom!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:48:21-07:00","id":467583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467477#post467477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That...doesn't sound quite right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:23:01-07:00","id":467639,"title":"","content":"If you can survive your Lair's destruction, it's probably not a simple situation that leaves you human again. If it doesn't kill you, it's definitely not gonna leave you fine and dandy.<br /> <br /> After all, there ought to be a reason besides wanting to keep your cool powers to prevent Heroes from destroying your Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:27:39-07:00","id":467666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467639#post467639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can survive your Lair's destruction, it's probably not a simple situation that leaves you human again. If it doesn't kill you, it's definitely not gonna leave you fine and dandy.<br /> <br /> After all, there ought to be a reason besides wanting to keep your cool powers to prevent Heroes from destroying your Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! That's what everyone meant. No, I didn't mean THAT. It's why I referenced the Bound and mentioned the &quot;low low cost of your sanity&quot;. I imagined it'd kind of be like the Vacant of Geist, where the character is mentally shattered and violently willing to do anything they think could fix them(though it's rather unlikely anything actually can). Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:32:35-07:00","id":467675,"title":"","content":"We won't know until the book is out, but I could see something like that being possible, maybe. People survive poorly without their souls, and I can't imagine it's easier when you have a super monster soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:52:53-07:00","id":467698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467583#post467583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't apologize. I have no idea what's going on, I just don't think that sounds right with what's been said about Beasts. We're both speculating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:06:42-07:00","id":467717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467698#post467698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't apologize. I have no idea what's going on, I just don't think that sounds right with what's been said about Beasts. We're both speculating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wild, unfounded speculation is like, 80% of the fun of awaiting a new gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:26:19-07:00","id":467741,"title":"","content":"Hence the &quot;No need for apology&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:54:01-07:00","id":467808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played even D&amp;D games where that statement is not true.</div> </div> </div> </div> A bit off the topic but I'm reminded of the old video game Planescape; Torment. Very story-driven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:30:25-07:00","id":467910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=467808#post467808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A bit off the topic but I'm reminded of the old video game Planescape; Torment. Very story-driven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise off topic, but I keep hoping that one day OPP gets a licences to do nWoD video games, and they recruit the folks who made Torment to do a Mummy video game. Although I'm sure they could do a great Beast game too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:49:13-07:00","id":467922,"title":"","content":"I'm not a Vampire fan, but I have to say, if they could make a storyline from the character &quot;Dire McCann,&quot; that might be a winner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:05:52-07:00","id":468004,"title":"","content":"Too address the points of both <b>Shadowflame</b> and <b>Xenu's Paradox</b> have raised.<br /> <br /> On Xenu's point about being able to play morally questionable (or repugnant) psychopathic characters -<br /> <br /> I think this is a pretty interesting viewpoint. Its the viewpoint that brought us Slasher for example. Which is one of my favourite splat books for the NWoD.<br /> <br /> Its also a viewpoint that the 1st Edition NWoD did not really support all that well as a PC option. A lot of Supernatural morality traits were basically just ratified takes on Morality (a system which itself was pretty damn flawed and modelling anything resembling real world morality). There were options that could get you a more monstrous PC, playing Brood in Vampire or Pure in Werewolf for example. However, these were options fleshed out later on in the gamelines lives when the need to diversify and expand the antagonists of the respective lines became a priority.<br /> <br /> One of the real strengths of 2nd Edition NWoD is that its increasingly moving away from the idea of a default morality for everyone. Integrity for humans it outright a measure of stability rather then morality. The new take on Humanity is all about mimicking human behavior more then its about being &quot;moral&quot;. Likewise, the bane system in Vamp 2nd Ed allows you to be pretty monstrous and not devolve into an unplayable monster. Demon goes the whole hog and just removes a hierarchy of breaking points all together and has Integrity style breaking points for acting &quot;out of character&quot; for whoever your cover identity is. Its utterly subjective and that in my opinion is a very good thing.<br /> <br /> Beast seems to be going the whole hog as well. Its &quot;morality&quot; stat is all about how well fed you are. I'm hoping that a Beast can be exactly as moral or monstrous as they choose to be and are not punished for either choice. Some beasts might be kind protectors of small communities. Others might be the monster in the woods that snatches away children. Both are valid monster story archetypes after all.<br /> <br /> On Shadowflame's point about Beasts wanting to fit in, are misunderstood or just want to be left alone -<br /> <br /> I think its fine that an individual Beast character can have these motivations. I don't think its a default presumption of Beast that either is the case.<br /> <br /> From all this talk of Family I get the impression Beast is about relationships. Particularly familial relationships. While this could be seen as an aspect of &quot;fitting in&quot; I can't say its the most prominent take on the material I've seen.<br /> <br /> Likewise, all the talk of Heroes makes me think there is an obvious element of persecution. However, we have to remember that Beasts create Heroes, they create their own worst enemies. Its in their nature. Maybe we could see this as a metaphor for a self destructive or self hating aspect. Personally I see it as more tying into the narrative idea of Beasts. Every monster in every story is always challenged/defeated by a Hero, usually a Hero who has had to come deal with the monster because of the monsters actions. We know that Beast is subverting this narrative trope but that does not make the central idea that the monster &quot;created&quot; the Hero any less true.<br /> <br /> One thing I think we can say about Beasts is that they are &quot;monsters&quot; and as such are a varied bunch. Some are friendly (see &quot;good monsters&quot; in Japanese mythology), some can be bartered or parlayed with (the Djinn of middle-eastern folklore), some can be avoided (every story about a monster not seeing you if you don't look at it) and some come to end the world as people know it (Smaug burning down Laketown).<br /> <br /> For my part I've made the mistake of reading in what I WANT a game to be rather then what a game IS before. It made me waste money getting a copy of said game and ultimately made me have a very, very bad experience running said game. Followed by a continued love/hate relationship with said game. So I just wanted to hand down the advice of not reading too much into the tidbits of info we have on Beast so far and presuming what type of character does and does not work right now. Might harm your enjoyment of the game in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 04-03-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:24:13-07:00","id":468013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=468004#post468004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For my part I've made the mistake of reading in what I WANT a game to be rather then what a game IS before. It made me waste money getting a copy of said game and ultimately made me have a very, very had experience running said game. Followed by a continued love/hate relationship with said game. So I just wanted to hand down the advice of not reading too much into the tidbits of info we have on Beast so far and presuming what type of character does and does not work right now. Might harm your enjoyment of the game in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point that is easy to lose sight of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T12:27:16-07:00","id":468621,"title":"","content":"From all I've seen and heard and read about Beast, I find myself feeling potential but uncertain if it's been/being realized yet. I don't know if what I'm going to say has been said before - it's quite likely - but I find myself wanting to say it.<br /> <br /> A lot of White Wolf/Onyx Path games approach their characters from a humanistic/simply human perspective; being human is special. There's some ineffable awesomeness about being human that, while not necessarily bringing you happiness, is still fundamentally there. This is a default assumption most game lines approach from, because becoming inhuman often simply removes characters from play and/or turns them into monsters. Vampires need to hold onto their humanity to avoid becoming savage, mindless beasts; Werewolves need to hold onto their humanity to stop from losing all hold on their flesh side; Mages need to hold onto their humanity to keep from consuming themselves with hubris; Changelings need to hold onto their humanity to keep from being solipsistic nightmares; Prometheans seek humanity because it's all that gives them purpose; Mummies try to reclaim it because it gives them their liberation. I hammer on this excessively just to point out how critical humanity is to the thought process of so many World of Darkness lines.<br /> <br /> Beast, it feels to me, should ignore this completely.<br /> <br /> Beasts aren't human. Beasts are Beasts; they are things spawned from the Primordial Dream, and their wearing a human skin should be seen as convenient at best and horrendous at worst. The nature of the Beast is the thing in their Lair; their true self; their Soul self; that Hungry, inhuman nightmare that seeks to slake its thirsts on others. This inhumanity should be a central conceit of the game line. Shedding humanity should be offered as a major potential goal that is eminently attainable, just as Mages have Archmastery or Mummies have their liberation from the Judges. Inheritance should be a major path possibility and something that Beast offers a path towards.<br /> <br /> Likewise, this non-humanity should have its impacts. A possible mythos/background for the setting that's wandered through my mind is the idea that Beasts and the Primordial Dream descend from a time before Man; before humanity ever walked the Earth. They are the ur; the thing which existed before anything else. For millions of years, <i>they</i> ruled this planet. <i>They</i> were that which held dominion, drawing their strength from ancient and primal forces of the cosmos. Then, humanity appeared, and this upstart race - weak and small but many in number - arose to fight back the Beasts. Humanity's dawn was a time when monsters lay at every horizon and gods sat on every mountain peak, and humanity rose up to smite them all. In this cosmic war, the Beasts thoroughly <i>lost</i>.<br /> <br /> This would provide a resultant basis for the setting. The reason Beasts appear - initially - human is because they thoroughly lost this war for the world and now must exist in hiding. Their birth by some distant mother-force is concealed to save them from instant death when they are at their weakest and most vulnerable. Likewise, Heroes (and this is probably the most controversial thing I'm going to say here) would be something akin to humanity's unconscious defense mechanism; a tribal, unthinking backlash that sees the Other as a threat and feels it must be destroyed <i>at any cost.</i> Mind you, Beasts are, by their nature, somewhat antithetical to humanity, so they're not without reason. A Beast is a victimizer by its very nature. This is why, despite often being ruthless and sliiightly obsessive, people still adore Heroes: They're slaying monsters that feed upon them.<br /> <br /> This sort of background gives characters motive (reach Inheritance before Heroes murder you), adds extra character focus to Beasts (&quot;What is this thing you call hoo-mah-nih-tee?&quot;), and provides both them and their antagonists with a strong niche. We already have a game line about bestial predators given over to unholy urges that see them victimize people to slake their unnatural hunger, and it's awesome. Beast needs something to call its own.<br /> <br /> This would also let the writers play with some Lovecraftian themes, too. Mummy introduced those but I never felt quite like it capitalized on them fully (it has some shining sparks, mind you, but there's holes in it). We could see Beasts drawing the souls of sleeping mortals into their Lair, to become a part of their symbolism; turning their waking forms into mad cultists who seek to bring the Beast into the waking world (perhaps allowing cult rituals to bring the Beast's true form into a location; binding a path to their Lair into the waking world?). Or perhaps constructing strange monoliths that amplify the Beast's power, allowing them to feed on more people/over greater distances through their dreams; or to summon down aspects of some mighty over-being that they can draw power from? It'd be fantastic to play a Beast who bargains with or otherwise pleases Shub-Niggurath to gain the power to produce their own dark spawn; or performing the appropriate rituals to Yog-Sothoth to let them see the future. Not literally these beings, of course, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah. I might be rambling and raving in ignorance here (kinda apropos, honestly) but, if I'm not... How am I doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:08:36-07:00","id":468750,"title":"","content":"This also provides tension between the Beast and his kin: yes, the Beast who travels with a Promethean can offer some advantages that the Promethean is unlikely to get in any other way (at the very least, a companion who isn't going to develop an obsession just by sticking around); but the Beast <i>will not</i> understand the Pilgrimage. At best, it will be bemused by the Created's desire to become human; at worst, it will actively interfere and end up pushing its companion to become a Centimanus. Superficially, it looks to be the most crossover-friendly game; but just under the surface, it is inherently subversive of every other gameline's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:11:39-07:00","id":468754,"title":"","content":"I agree with Axelgear's opinion, honestly. The &quot;monster that feeds on people due to unholy hungers&quot; is already covered quite well with Vampire (and to a lesser extent Werewolf). This niche would be unique, and it'd be nice to build upon the ideals set forth in Demon. Supposedly, Beasts don't like Demons because they give off a &quot;pod person&quot; feel to them, so with that in mind I think it makes the most sense to embrace the idea of Beasts never being human and merely aping it for protective covering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:42:50-07:00","id":468799,"title":"","content":"I feel like Axel's on the right track, yeah. That said, the &quot;Unholy Hunger&quot; part has never quite seen creatures who <i>need</i> to raze towns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T17:26:33-07:00","id":468985,"title":"","content":"Maybe..but to be born with humanity, to have feelings that are obviously human...hmm...should mean something.<br /> And what we seem to know so far have Beasts very much involved with humanity, and in bits, very protective of them. <br /> In some cases from a mythological perspective that seems a little odd. (I'm pretty sure that Medusa wanted nothing to do with people after Athena's rather unfair treatment of her, assuming legitimacy of the myth. And of course, assuming she would fit in with the Beasts ideal)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T17:45:12-07:00","id":469012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=468750#post468750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also provides tension between the Beast and his kin: yes, the Beast who travels with a Promethean can offer some advantages that the Promethean is unlikely to get in any other way (at the very least, a companion who isn't going to develop an obsession just by sticking around); but the Beast <i>will not</i> understand the Pilgrimage. At best, it will be bemused by the Created's desire to become human; at worst, it will actively interfere and end up pushing its companion to become a Centimanus. Superficially, it looks to be the most crossover-friendly game; but just under the surface, it is inherently subversive of every other gameline's themes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been confirmed already that Beasys that Hang with Promethean understand why promethean cousins want to be human, and that they tend to be supportive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T17:52:23-07:00","id":469014,"title":"","content":"Huh. I actually wasn't expecting people to agree with me but I'm glad I said something interesting! I did mention this to a friend, though, and he helpfully pointed out that there is an intrinsic issue with the Beasts having set before them the clear and obvious option of &quot;KILL EVERYONE&quot; as their motive and that's just... Not diverse/interesting enough, nor does it readily encourage cooperation. To that end, I found myself proposing Shadow-over-Innsmouth-esque attempts to create Beast-human hybrids but that's really only two options and I feel like there'd be a need for many more.<br /> <br /> As for being born with humanity meaning to have obviously human feelings... I think you can include that, but I'd probably play against that. Say Beasts as children are often classified as having autism or antisocial personality disorder because they just don't relate to humans. Have relating to humanity be a struggle; be rare; be something that's typically seen as an eccentricity amongst Beasts. The attitudes towards humanity can be exceedingly varied, from hate and loathing to apathy to fascination or even love, but it would ultimately be an outsider's perspective looking in. Humanity is something the Beasts would have to decide on how to deal with, even if it's just a case of &quot;Fuck off and leave me alone!&quot;, but there's a difference between relating to humans and being human yourself.<br /> <br /> Beasts might be born looking human, but humanity is something they'd be trying to shed in this interpretation; like a straight jacket they were born wearing and are desperate to tear off like a scaly Houdini.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T19:02:23-07:00","id":469059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=468985#post468985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe..but to be born with humanity, to have feelings that are obviously human...hmm...should mean something.<br /> And what we seem to know so far have Beasts very much involved with humanity, and in bits, very protective of them.<br /> In some cases from a mythological perspective that seems a little odd. (I'm pretty sure that Medusa wanted nothing to do with people after Athena's rather unfair treatment of her, assuming legitimacy of the myth. And of course, assuming she would fit in with the Beasts ideal)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough point here Shadowflame.<br /> <br /> I'm more on board with the Axelgear point of view. Mainly because I would like another game in the NWoD besides Demon that engages with the idea of &quot;inhumanity as the norm&quot;.<br /> <br /> On a more personal tonal point, I would like the NWoD move away from having a supernatural that agonizes over either their lot in life or the lot of reality as they view it. I mean lets have a look at some of the previous NWoD games on the issue of &quot;having a bad time&quot; of being supernatural:<br /> <br /> Vampire pretty much perfectly captures the &quot;post-human&quot; state of being &quot;blessed with suck&quot; (namely being a monster that looks like a human) and having to deal with that. You have all your human memories and you still walk the same streets but you look at the people around you as food now on some instinctual level. Commence head-fuck and angst. Great game for slippery slopes, moral compromise and a lot of self-discover/hatred.<br /> <br /> Mage has people having a good time of being supernatural for the most part, but pretty much makes them view reality as a place inherently broken, degraded and fallen. Which is all the fault of human hubris that got access to too much supernatural power. So we could say its existentially angsty rather then personally angsty like Vampire.<br /> <br /> Promethean does an excellent job of getting across that being a a supernatural is not a fun thing that makes you better then humanity. It also does an excellent job of selling a humanist message and making an argument for &quot;humans are special&quot;. It's getting across its themes well and I love the humanist message in that games scope. However, it gets a double bite of the angst apple for having both personal and existential issues.<br /> <br /> Changeling has a lot of the same issues as vampire. Though less &quot;I'm a predatory monster&quot; and more &quot;I'm a broken inhuman freak&quot; and even more of an emphasis on the &quot;post-human&quot; aspect of the game. I'm not going to even go into the many ways and facets that Changeling deals with personal pain, angst and general depressing things. Needless to say they are many and central to the game.<br /> <br /> Given all the above, I could do without Beast being yet another take on the &quot;woah is me&quot; angle of being something that is inhuman or post-human. We have games that explore those themes pretty well and cover the majority of the characterful stuff you can get out of them (as detailed above). The last thing I want is to imagine a Beast sitting in his/her Lair moping/crying/lamenting about their &quot;lost humanity&quot;. I want Beast to get on with the business of being a monster, of being something that was human but is now inhuman (by which I mean something that has dropped a human viewpoint or reference), not post-human (by which I mean something that retains a human viewpoint via memory but has now had its current perceptions warped by its new nature) and is exploring that state.<br /> <br /> Some Beasts might explore it with trepidation, not even sure if they are cut out for this business of embodying fears but muddling their way through. Others might throw them selves into their new role in life, finding it natural and liberating from their &quot;laval quasi-human stage&quot; that they always felt uncomfortable in.<br /> <br /> If a Beast is being protective of humans or aiding a Promethean to become human that's all cool by me. I just want the reasons they are doing this stuff to not be immediately obvious as human motivations. I want a least a little bit of an alien mindset and motivation for these actions. Maybe the Beast is protecting these people because they fit some arcane category that makes them part of its hoard? It cares about them as property to be protected not because it hold their lives to have intrinsic meaning beyond belonging to it. Maybe the Beast is helping the Promethean because the Promethean asked it too in a particular way the means the Beast can't even contemplate refusing such a request, its just not a done thing. It could care less about the Promethean in questions eventual humanity or the alleviation of its personal and metaphysical issues. It's just got to help because its got to &quot;the rules&quot; that Beasts follow (if they have such rules) say so.<br /> <br /> In reality, I don't actually expect Beast to engage with inhuman themes as much as I want it too. That's not to say we can't both have our cake and eat it too. If Beasts can get frighteningly human (which the preview stuff seems to imply) and have a bit of disconnect between their human form and beast soul (also implied) it would be nice to have the short-sharp snap between the two. A hungry Beast is not thinking like a human it just wants to feed, but its still intelligent and a person. A sated Beast is almost completely human in mindset and likely having trouble understanding or rationalizing (or possibly even remembering) its actions while hungry.<br /> <br /> Basically, if Beast can at least manage a good Jekyll and Hyde style internal conflict depending on the Beasts Satiety rating, I'll be mostly happy.<br /> <br /> Time will tell I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T16:59:02-07:00","id":469677,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the double post but something hit me today while through skimming through first edition NWoD books to kill time. Notably I found the following in Book of the Dead:-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Leviathan </b><br /> <br /> Every human being in the world has had the nightmare, even if they can no longer remember it. The dreamer floats in the middle of the ocean, nothing around for miles, at night or <br /> during the day. Time doesn't matter. The utter hopelessness of the situation sinks in as the dreamer realizes that even if by some miracle he starts swimming in the right direction, <br /> he will tire and drown long before ever seeing land. <br /> And then, that fear is gone, replaced by a much worse one \u2014 something brushes his leg. Or perhaps he looks down and sees the shadow pass below him. The Beast Below. A <br /> shark, a sea monster, a squid, or just some nameless horror from the Deeps? It doesn\u2019t matter and the dreamer has no time to consider taxonomy. He awakens, sweating, thanking <br /> whatever deity he might believe in that it was just a dream.<br /> But the Beast Below exists, and it guards the Ocean of Fragments. It enforces the Laws of the Dominion, and despite its great size and the limitless scope of the Ocean, it can swim vast distances in an instant, dragging an unfortunate traveler down.<br /> <br /> - <b>Book of the Dead p.194</b> </div> </div> </div>So am I the only one thinking within the context of Beast that the Leviathan would make an excellent &quot;ancient&quot; Makara Beast (maybe the first of its kind a direct child of the Dark Mother) that retreated into its Lair. Said Lair was of course linked to the Underworld. Within this same context you could nicely alter things so that the Leviathan is not actually a Kerberos just that Geist's think it is. Its really just a Beast of immense age and power. <br /> <br /> Which does raise the question of using a Beast's lair that is linked to the Underworld to bypass the rivers and get deeper into the Great Below more quickly. For example having a Makara having a Lair that is a shore or lagoon with black sand (like the example Matt talked about as an example) would seem pretty easy to link to the Ocean of Fragments. That's presuming that otherworldly locations resonate with a Lair the same way suitable places in the material world do. I imagine if one decided to link ones Lair with another realm in particular in addition to the Astral it could work.<br /> <br /> Regardless I think the Ocean of Fragments would be a lot of fun for a Geist/Beast crossover game to interact with. For example<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> Oh crap...that's the Kerbero of this realm, seems we broke one of the old laws. Time to go...<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Nah that just my great-great-great-great-great-great-great gampa Leviathan, he's cool, little eccentric in his old age. (waves at Leviathan) <br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> What's wrong with you! We need to go, as in now! <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Chill man, trust me he's cool, look he just wants a hug.<br /> <br /> (Giant tentacle grasps both characters) <br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> We are so screwed...(starts to wrestle with tentacle for dear life)<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Grandpa you give the best hugs! (hugs tentacle)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T17:33:11-07:00","id":469688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=469677#post469677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the double post but something hit me today while through skimming through first edition NWoD books to kill time. Notably I found the following in Book of the Dead:-<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So am I the only one thinking within the context of Beast that the Leviathan would make an excellent &amp;quot;ancient&amp;quot; Makara Beast (maybe the first of its kind a direct child of the Dark Mother) that retreated into its Lair. Said Lair was of course linked to the Underworld. Within this same context you could nicely alter things so that the Leviathan is not actually a Kerberos just that Geist's think it is. Its really just a Beast of immense age and power. <br /> <br /> Which does raise the question of using a Beast's lair that is linked to the Underworld to bypass the rivers and get deeper into the Great Below more quickly. For example having a Makara having a Lair that is a shore or lagoon with black sand (like the example Matt talked about as an example) would seem pretty easy to link to the Ocean of Fragments. That's presuming that otherworldly locations resonate with a Lair the same way suitable places in the material world do. I imagine if one decided to link ones Lair with another realm in particular in addition to the Astral it could work.<br /> <br /> Regardless I think the Ocean of Fragments would be a lot of fun for a Geist/Beast crossover game to interact with. For example<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> Oh crap...that's the Kerbero of this realm, seems we broke one of the old laws. Time to go...<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Nah that just my great-great-great-great-great-great-great gampa Leviathan, he's cool, little eccentric in his old age. (waves at Leviathan) <br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> What's wrong with you! We need to go, as in now! <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Chill man, trust me he's cool, look he just wants a hug.<br /> <br /> (Giant tentacle grasps both characters) <br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> We are so screwed...(starts to wrestle with tentacle for dear life)<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Grandpa you give the best hugs! (hugs tentacle)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Should he... Should he be hugging me THERE?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sigh. Who brought the Japanese schoolgirl along?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:08:44-07:00","id":469746,"title":"","content":"Some updates from the Rpg.net thread:<br /> <br /> \u2022Apparently there's been some banter on the other thread about a power nicknamed &quot;Claws of the Motherf@$&amp;er&quot;. Mr. Matt has finally given some explanation about it, explaining that &quot;Any Beast can have it; it's an Atavism called Limb from Limb (it's an Eshmaki one, actually, but like I said, anyone can have it).&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022(In response to someone speculating about how the Begotten might clash with other supers, in which they wondered why a Beast wouldn't interfere with the Pilgrimage): &quot;A lot of your commentary is very much on point, but I do want to mention: A Beast doesn't want to be human again, because being human to them was always weird and uncomfortable. As such, to a Beast, a Promethean's descriptions of Disquiet and Torment might ring pretty familiar. I mean, yeah, it's too bad that our Promethean cousins don't get to be awesome like us, but that's no reason for them not to follow their bliss, right? <br /> <br /> (But on the other hand, those Hundred-Handed guys seem pretty secure in what they are. Maybe they like to party.)&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022Apparently there's going to be a Condition that can at least apply to other supers called &quot;Family Ties&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u2022Shared Lairs are apparently like that because their Beasts merged them.<br /> <br /> \u2022(While this is just someone's comment, it seemed neat enough to share): &quot;I'm imagining a campaign where a group of idealistic Beasts go out to help the poor monsters and expect everything will be Hotel Transylvania-style hijinks, except they find out that no one trusts them, everyone hates each other, and the whole situation is ridiculously complicated. Beasts have this weird modern superhero vibe? Like they're mistrusted and misunderstood but they're trying to help people? (Also they use fear as a tool and are responsible for creating their own worst enemies so they're basically Batman).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T23:53:19-07:00","id":469917,"title":"","content":"... You know, I'm disturbingly okay with the idea of Beasts being the Cursed with Awesome counterpart to Vampires Blessed with Suck.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T00:33:37-07:00","id":469946,"title":"","content":"I'm not at all interested in a World of Darkness game that *isn't* an exploration of aspects of humanity and human life in some way. Thankfully, with family being such a major theme in the game and all, it doesn't seem like Beast is going to be that game - not that I ever expect to see that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T03:19:26-07:00","id":470001,"title":"","content":"Weird Thought.... Isn't there in First Edition Vampire a &quot;City Eating Vampire Spirit&quot; that causes all the Vampires too go err.. Mad slowly with Paranoia and eventually causes all the Vampires in the City too Kill themselves?<br /> That.. Sounds like an Antagionistic Beast in a Vampire Game too me.. Feeding on &quot;Ruin&quot; of the Vampires Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T05:38:39-07:00","id":470063,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I now have the idea of a group of Beasts infiltrating a Mummy's Cult just to summon them and force them to spend time with them and tell them stories about the &quot;old times&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T05:41:44-07:00","id":470065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470063#post470063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty, I now have the idea of a group of Beasts infiltrating a Mummy's Cult just to summon them and force them to spend time with them and tell them stories about the &quot;old times&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They'd probably piss off the Judges, though, because they'd need to try and restore the mummy's memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T05:42:20-07:00","id":470067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470063#post470063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty, I now have the idea of a group of Beasts infiltrating a Mummy's Cult just to summon them and force them to spend time with them and tell them stories about the &quot;old times&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what they'd end up getting is one grumpy Mummy then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T06:27:31-07:00","id":470090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=469677#post469677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the double post but something hit me today while through skimming through first edition NWoD books to kill time. Notably I found the following in Book of the Dead:-<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So am I the only one thinking within the context of Beast that the Leviathan would make an excellent &quot;ancient&quot; Makara Beast (maybe the first of its kind a direct child of the Dark Mother) that retreated into its Lair. Said Lair was of course linked to the Underworld. Within this same context you could nicely alter things so that the Leviathan is not actually a Kerberos just that Geist's think it is. Its really just a Beast of immense age and power.<br /> <br /> Which does raise the question of using a Beast's lair that is linked to the Underworld to bypass the rivers and get deeper into the Great Below more quickly. For example having a Makara having a Lair that is a shore or lagoon with black sand (like the example Matt talked about as an example) would seem pretty easy to link to the Ocean of Fragments. That's presuming that otherworldly locations resonate with a Lair the same way suitable places in the material world do. I imagine if one decided to link ones Lair with another realm in particular in addition to the Astral it could work.<br /> <br /> Regardless I think the Ocean of Fragments would be a lot of fun for a Geist/Beast crossover game to interact with. For example<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> Oh crap...that's the Kerbero of this realm, seems we broke one of the old laws. Time to go...<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Nah that just my great-great-great-great-great-great-great gampa Leviathan, he's cool, little eccentric in his old age. (waves at Leviathan)<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> What's wrong with you! We need to go, as in now!<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Chill man, trust me he's cool, look he just wants a hug.<br /> <br /> (Giant tentacle grasps both characters)<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b> We are so screwed...(starts to wrestle with tentacle for dear life)<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Grandpa you give the best hugs! (hugs tentacle)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is amazing. <br /> <br /> (BTW, I wrote the Ocean of Fragments, so I'd love to say it was all foreshadowing for <b>Beast</b>, but that would be an utter lie.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:06:31-07:00","id":470107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470090#post470090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is amazing.<br /> <br /> (BTW, I wrote the Ocean of Fragments, so I'd love to say it was all foreshadowing for <b>Beast</b>, but that would be an utter lie.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Shush! Just smile and nod, Matt. Smile and nod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T09:27:40-07:00","id":470195,"title":"","content":"Better to remain silent and let everyone think you're a genius than to speak and confirm you're a mere mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:58:33-07:00","id":470398,"title":"","content":"We have an Estimated Release Date: Gencon 2015. There's also likely to be a Kickstarter, and we'll be getting blog posts next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:21:08-07:00","id":470427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470090#post470090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is amazing. <br /> <br /> (BTW, I wrote the Ocean of Fragments, so I'd love to say it was all foreshadowing for <b>Beast</b>, but that would be an utter lie.)</div> </div> </div> </div>BTW, is there any mechanical support for this? Is a Beast's Soul something that could merge with a ghost and become a Kerberos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T18:40:26-07:00","id":470569,"title":"","content":"Psh, as if. You'd have to break the narrative for that to happen, and monomyth is king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T08:51:08-07:00","id":471271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466436#post466436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Dark Mother as a &quot;rival&quot; to the God Machine is an interesting idea I feel. She comes from basic concepts of a chaotic primordial world that predates the &quot;order&quot; of human culture and civilization. Something that the God Machine is heavily invested in and embodies thematically via a cold sterile/messy body horror take on order.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Mother also seems to about primal fear and need, deep and immediate instincts, whereas the God-Machine is all about intricate plans and the long-term. Like you, I don't picture them as enemies - in a way, they're almost too opposite for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=466664#post466664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with most of the above is that they're little more than socio/psychopaths. Primordial Beasts have to be better...have to be more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the RPGNet thread, there was some talk of Hannibal Lecter as a Beast, but I thought it was more interesting to picture Will Graham as the Beast - he's intimate with fear and monstrosity, in such a way as takes him out of the world, and I could easily see his pursuit of serial killers in terms of a Hunger for Punishment, or even Prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:21:42-07:00","id":471332,"title":"","content":"I've always viewed &quot;Nyx&quot; as the Dark Mother. She just fits the bill too well for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:36:53-07:00","id":471698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470398#post470398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have an Estimated Release Date: Gencon 2015. There's also likely to be a Kickstarter, and we'll be getting blog posts next week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember to take that with big honkin' grains of salt. I'm sure we'll get some teasers eventually, but they'll come when they come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:56:09-07:00","id":471722,"title":"","content":"Considering Matt said final drafts are in and he basically just needs art notes it certainly looks like it'll be 'on time'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T19:41:46-07:00","id":471990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471332#post471332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed &quot;Nyx&quot; as the Dark Mother. She just fits the bill too well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is... Is there a Dark Father?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T19:54:00-07:00","id":471999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471990#post471990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My question is... Is there a Dark Father?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess would be the relative types of monsters have different &quot;fathers&quot; from each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T22:24:15-07:00","id":472211,"title":"","content":"Who is the <i>real</i> Dark Dad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T22:30:13-07:00","id":472222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=472211#post472211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is the <i>real</i> Dark Dad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanatos is the Dark Second Cousin on Mom's Side.<br /> <br /> Xanatos is the Dark Relative Who Shows Up at the Reunions but Nobody Knows How He's Related but Nobody Will Ask Because He's Rich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:46:34-07:00","id":472318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471999#post471999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My guess would be the relative types of monsters have different &quot;fathers&quot; from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T00:03:49-07:00","id":472326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471271#post471271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Mother also seems to about primal fear and need, deep and immediate instincts, whereas the God-Machine is all about intricate plans and the long-term. Like you, I don't picture them as enemies - in a way, they're almost too opposite for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me I always try to consider resources when it comes to the God Machine. The largest resource on planet Earth for its purposes is mankind (at current at least). As such it want's a monopoly on its control of mankind. I can imagine this bringing the GM into conflict with say the Exarch's, Maeljin or the True Fae, who want to either usurp control of mankind or predate on them to a unsustainable level. <br /> <br /> Things like Vampires or Beasts though? They do predate on humans, but not in the numbers to cause the GM trouble. In the formers case they usually help sure up human society so they can hind among. As for the Dark Mother, she's hardly (as far as we know) trying to control or eat all of humanity. Her aims seem more instinctual and personal then that. Or at least that's the feeling I get from the info we have. Hence no need for conflict between the two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471332#post471332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed &quot;Nyx&quot; as the Dark Mother. She just fits the bill too well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting that you gravitate towards that one primordial goddess of darkness. Considering we have Tiamat, Echidna, Lamashtu. Lilith and Gaia to all draw upon as well. Needless to say, I'm sure in NWoD fashion the Dark Mother will be all of these figures and more. Not to mention likely a good bit stranger as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471990#post471990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My question is... Is there a Dark Father?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point. Something I had not really considered. I was thinking of the Dark Mother has a being that could create without the need for a mate. Likely creating her offspring from ideas and fears that took her fancy. I guess I was thinking more in the &quot;Hera born from Zues's forehead&quot; sorta way then the traditional &quot;mated pair&quot; method. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, as glamourweaver says their may be sorta &quot;demi-fathers&quot; for each type of Beast and even the other game lines. We don't really know at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T00:07:21-07:00","id":472332,"title":"","content":"You must obey Father. Father doesn't like disobedient children.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/knd/images/6/6f/Screen_Shot_2014-03-14_at_12.34.34_AM.png/revision/latest?cb=20140314055408\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:54:43-07:00","id":472415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=472326#post472326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me I always try to consider resources when it comes to the God Machine. The largest resource on planet Earth for its purposes is mankind (at current at least). As such it want's a monopoly on its control of mankind. I can imagine this bringing the GM into conflict with say the Exarch's, Maeljin or the True Fae, who want to either usurp control of mankind or predate on them to a unsustainable level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the GM's interactions with humanity, I would say that out of all the parties, the GM cares about having control over mankind the least. Exarchs need humanity because what is tyranny if you don't have slaves? Maeljin needs Sin of some sort and humanity seems to be the only ones that can offer that. True Fae rival the God Machine in lack of caring but that's more about plundering what's there over long term planning.<br /> <br /> GM, as a whole, doesn't seem to care all that much. Sure, having humans operate things like the useful tools that they are is great but they are still tools. If something else comes along or the GM comes up with a project in which requires humanity to be &quot;wiped off the workbench&quot;, it has no problems with doing so. The GM has been here longer than humanity has and can work without them.<br /> <br /> Only reason why the GM hasn't pulled the plug on humanity in my mind is that it's a lynchpin for enough projects that are still being created or maintained to justify it's continued existence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T05:47:58-07:00","id":472581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=471990#post471990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My question is... Is there a Dark Father?</div> </div> </div> </div>Erebus was there at the beginning, alongside Mother Night.<br /> But yeah, I'd have to go with glamourweaver's post with differing fathers. (I guess Nyx and Erebus have one the those &quot;open&quot; relationships.) But together they had some of the baddest children around. (Death, Doom, Nemesis, Fate, etc..) The only other great mother that had comparable was Gaea.<br /> It's interesting that Typhon was referred to as the Father of All Monsters while Echidna was the Mother of All Monsters. The timeframes may be too different as Nyx and Erebus were there at the very beginning before humanity I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T07:52:03-07:00","id":472738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470427#post470427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BTW, is there any mechanical support for this? Is a Beast's Soul something that could merge with a ghost and become a Kerberos?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like that was actually mentioned in the book. I <i>might</i> have cut that sidebar because it felt clunky in context, but I like the idea a lot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=470195#post470195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better to remain silent and let everyone think you're a genius than to speak and confirm you're a mere mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to be a saint. I would rather be a clown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:05:15-07:00","id":473064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=472415#post472415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only reason why the GM hasn't pulled the plug on humanity in my mind is that it's a lynchpin for enough projects that are still being created or maintained to justify it's continued existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the reason is that Humanity is THE Lynchpin for the entire GM? If one considers the entire world being a single piece of Infrastructure with the purpose of maintaining the God-Machine (or in my view, re-creating the God-Machine each and every instant, I do like early Muslim atomistic ideas of creation), then the only thing important enough to be a Lynchpin would be humanity. <br /> <br /> Mind you, this could lead to strangely genocidal Demons, so maybe not such a good idea after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64