ontainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=473855#post473855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a nutshell,Beasts are [ponies].</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm totally doing the storied version of Nightmare Moon as a Beast now.(The fictional in universe one that ate foals not the real in universe one that merely tried to bring eternal midnight.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T19:02:51-07:00","id":475208,"title":"","content":"Mmm, baby eating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T19:15:56-07:00","id":475217,"title":"","content":"That sounds like some good Prey or Ruin right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T08:52:42-07:00","id":477974,"title":"","content":"So, I've not been on this thread in a good long while and am mostly skimming to get a feel for the game but I have to ask: Is beast going to be a touchy feely &quot;the real monster is you&quot; game? I assumed that &quot;Gaston&quot; was the take of the beast, not of those the Hero is helping, this along with talk of Freddy Krueger having to have been misunderstood to be a beast (seriously, he was my first thought when I heard of beasts as nightmares) and even then being too evil... am I misreading this? is it an 'inside' joke that I haven't read far enough back to get?<br /> <br /> I don't mean to be all Humbug and whatnot, its just that we already have games like that with Changeling and Promethean and my players and I like games where the monster becomes sympathetic in terms of what they They're &quot;missing&quot; a vampire is tragic BECAUSE it doesn't realize its not human anymore, a werewolf is a monster who even if he means well is still one bad day away from eating his neighbor over a poorly placed garden gnome.... etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Am I misreading this? PS: Hawthorn, you are a very, VERY bad person &quot;Grandpa&quot; had me in tears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T09:14:48-07:00","id":477979,"title":"","content":"The best way to put it is that yes, Heroes are assholes, but the Beasts aren't presented as victims.<br /> <br /> From what we've been told, Beasts accept their nature, accept what they are. They're not fighting to become human again.<br /> <br /> It's just that the Heroes who oppose them aren't heroes in the sense of being _moral_ heroes. They're more heroes in the sense of the heroes of classical myth, who by and large were assholes by modern standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T09:35:01-07:00","id":478015,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick reply<br /> <br /> and yeah, I get that Heroes are Assholes, but from what I was reading it was looking like they're the &quot;real monsters&quot; which was what was making me nervous. I never thought they wanted to be good guys I was more responding to the constant references to them actually being &quot;good guys&quot; (the Freddy Krueger reference specifically). <br /> <br /> I was thinking that Heroes followed the &quot;Good is not Nice&quot; setup and i'm a huge &quot;Affably evil&quot; set up for monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T10:10:08-07:00","id":478088,"title":"","content":"Heroes are probably not good. The example Matt gave us was a Hero murdering the ordinary human assistant of a Beast who was also a lawyer. Regardless of whether or not the Beast has done horrible things that might make it something that needs killing (and it probably has) the 'collateral damage' there is unambiguously monstrous on the Hero's part.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the assistant was probably a lawyer too... /joke","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2