nimate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahab is increasingly my go-to example for a more modern example as I think about what we've heard of them so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rose said that, essentially, a Hero is what you get when a Beast is actually at their <i>least </i>dangerous, and I think it's been mentioned they start on the wrong side of the line that divides Hunter from a more sympathetic Slasher. They aren't cures to the genuine problem, they're symptoms of it.<br /> <br /> Also, nothing stops you from making a sympathetic Hero, it's just that Matt loves to hate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T18:20:25-07:00","id":478576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/welcome-to-my-nightmare-beast-teasers/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/welcome-to-my-nightmare-beast-teasers/\" target=\"_blank\"> Welcome to My Nightmare [Beast: The Primordial] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/welcome-to-my-nightmare-beast-teasers/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/welcome-to-my-nightmare-beast-teasers/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T18:24:49-07:00","id":478579,"title":"","content":"Hm, looks like Heroes will come if you feed too much, as well as too little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T18:28:40-07:00","id":478580,"title":"","content":"It appears that some power can leave subtle signs. I wonder if what our young &quot;heroine&quot; used was a Nightmare or an Atavism?<br /> <br /> Also, it appears that Hungers exist in the psychology of the Children before their Homecoming, which seems to have some interesting implications for their mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:40:50-07:00","id":478703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=478580#post478580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that some power can leave subtle signs. I wonder if what our young &quot;heroine&quot; used was a Nightmare or an Atavism?<br /> <br /> Also, it appears that Hungers exist in the psychology of the Children before their Homecoming, which seems to have some interesting implications for their mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if the Children have any other mental traits or habits relating to their soul before their homecoming? If someone had a bigfoot soul, might they have the rather non-human habit of picking things up with their toes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:39:31-07:00","id":478780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=478580#post478580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that some power can leave subtle signs. I wonder if what our young &quot;heroine&quot; used was a Nightmare or an Atavism?<br /> <br /> Also, it appears that Hungers exist in the psychology of the Children before their Homecoming, which seems to have some interesting implications for their mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well it's a 50/50 shot, but I'd guess nightmare- water seeping in, wounds from an invisible blow, sounds nightmarish to me. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:53:21-07:00","id":478801,"title":"","content":"So are we going to have to wait for the Kickstarter to begin to get a Beast forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T01:03:35-07:00","id":478867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Welcome to My Nightmare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All your life you\u2019ve had the same nightmare</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean I'm a Beast? I'm a grown man and I've had the same nightmare of being dragged under a bed while being unable to scream as far back as I can remember. Even when I had a waterbed.<br /> <br /> Well... Need this game to come out so I can stat myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","user":"UnjustCustos","date":". 04-13-2015, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:51:22-07:00","id":478990,"title":"","content":"I greatly enjoyed the blog post and look forward to more on the topic.<br /> <br /> One thing that made me a little sad was the number of people who are already bitching about &quot;hero's being the bad guys&quot; and playing &quot;inhuman monsters&quot; off of one blog post that was designed and a very general teaser. <br /> <br /> I get the feeling that each week Matt's going to have to reiterate the same old lines like:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hero's are antagonists, but that does not make their relationship with Beast's black/white or simple. Like any antagonist in an RPG the complexity of their relationship with the protagonists varies depending on the ST's play style and the type of story being told&quot; <br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> &quot;Were not looking to make Hero's playable really, as their are other games in the NWoD that basically let you do that e.g. Mortal, Hunter and Mage.&quot; <br /> <br /> Maybe its just me, as I've been waiting for a splat that highlights the more &quot;monster&quot; or &quot;inhuman&quot; elements of the supernatural condition in a non-negative fashion for a while in the NWoD. Second edition has so far gone a long way towards letting you play those sort of characters without being punished for it mechanically e.g. the new humanity/banes system, the new harmony system, Really its one of the reasons I like Demon so much, as it has a morality system and take on being &quot;human&quot; that is utterly subjective and is a view on humanity from outside of humanity (really the one &quot;supernatural viewpoint&quot; we were lacking when the game came out).<br /> <br /> For me the WoD has never been about playing a Hero in any way. Its been about playing people. Be they people who are now dead and drinking blood for a living. Proto-people who are really working on becoming more. People who have seen the way reality really works and really don't want to go back to their old job. <br /> <br /> For me its about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Its about playing a Vampire that's having to compromise his morals to survive, having to lie, cheat and steal (at least) to get anywhere in the society of predators he finds himself in. Its about becoming selfish and justifying your actions to keep yourself alive. <br /> <br /> Its about playing a Promethean that really trying to &quot;get it&quot;, trying to figure out what it is about humans that really makes them special, that makes him want to be one so bad. Its about trying and failing and trying again and sometimes really screwing up and getting people hurt and sometimes figuring it out and having to move on. Its about feeling bad about what you might have done out of former ignorance or feeling vindicated by your actions regardless of the consequences.<br /> <br /> Its about playing a Demon that is so very grateful humanity exists, because they give him somewhere to hide and resources to use against his old boss. Its doing anything you need to to stay free and stay ahead of those hunting you. If that means destroying lives, souls and car bombing a bit of infrastructure that also happens to be a hospital then that what you do, because it need to be done. <br /> <br /> This was why the thing that made me most happy that's been posted on this forum was when Matt basically said (to paraphrase) &quot;Beasts like being Beasts, as humanity always felt uncomfortable to them and they do not want to be human again&quot;. I'd like a game that was about being a &quot;noble/good monster&quot; and enjoy their existence and their &quot;job&quot;. I'd like a splat with a little levity and pride in what they are. Rather then yet another game where the protagonists long for their lost humanity such as Vampire, Promethean (though more as a logging for humanity full stop) Changeling and in some cases Mummy. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, nothing wrong with those games. I'm a big fan of Vampire and Promethean for example, because they are engaging with the trope I described above in an interesting way. I'd just like to see the new game not be yet another take on the same trope and move onto focusing on a new facet of supernatural existence. <br /> <br /> Luckily for me, from the info we have so far, seems I'm getting my wish granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T06:20:52-07:00","id":478994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=478282#post478282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, nothing stops you from making a sympathetic Hero, it's just that Matt loves to hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's more like the whole rest of the world loves to <i>love</i> Heroes. That's why this isn't their story, it's the Beast's. This is one instance where I wouldn't really want a sympathetic villain.<br /> <br /> What about the poor Beast who's having a rough day and hasn't sated his Hunger then suddenly some rampaging murder hobo he's never met before busts down his door? What the hell, Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T07:05:38-07:00","id":479024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=478990#post478990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I greatly enjoyed the blog post and look forward to more on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part that interested me most was the seawater creeping into the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:03:57-07:00","id":479046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479024#post479024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part that interested me most was the seawater creeping into the room.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, fun fact: I actually wrote that bit a long time ago, as part of the original pitch for <b>Beast</b>. It doesn't appear in the book, although I like Eve and if we do an anthology I may write a story about her. But when I did that post for the blog, I had to read through that fiction bit and think, &quot;OK, now that the rules are written, <i>can</i> you actually do this stuff?&quot;<br /> <br /> And the answer is: Yes, though some of it is more cosmetic than anything. But Eve could have flooded that room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:41:42-07:00","id":479078,"title":"","content":"Edit: That teaser certainly made me more interested in the line, which I was previously lukewarm towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","user":"Wasteful","date":".  Turns out the question I initially asked was pretty much answered upthread. 04-13-2015, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:02:34-07:00","id":479209,"title":"","content":"You know, I don't like werewolves. They don't have a motivation. They don't have a personality. They don't talk and when they do talk, it just looks stupid. They just kill people. Vampires kill people too, but they're also actual characters. You can swap a werewolf with a normal wolf any day of the week and it wouldn't really change anything. I thought I was just going to skip Werewolf 2.0, but then I read David Hill's interview about Dark Eras where he talked about the Stonewall riots and how not having a place to belong relates to Werewolf and I got thinking.<br /> <br /> You can't tell that kind of story with Vampire. You can't tell that kind of story with Mage. You sure as hell can't tell that kind of story with Demon. I mean, you can have a story where a bunch of Mages use a nightclub as their sanctum and throw a riot when the cops come to shut the place down, but it's not going to be quite the same as the police repeatedly harassing patrons of a gay bar until the patrons decide they've had enough bullshit and start fighting back. There aren't a lot of games where you can do that, and there are even fewer games where you can do that as part of the game's central theme. So I decided Werewolf 2.0 was worth buying. <br /> <br /> There's a post on RPG.net where Matt implicitly compares Heroes to MRAs. The thread's too long and I don't know if there's a way to search through it conveniently, so I can't quote it, but it got me thinking. Is there a game out right now that subverts hegemonic cultural narratives of privilege? Not really. Exalted does it with imperialism, but I wouldn't really call it the focus of the game. <br /> <br /> We live in a world where narcissistic sociopaths demand the privilege to harass and victimize women because that's how it's been for hundreds of years and learning how to become a better person just takes too much effort. They surround themselves with parasites who go out of their way to swallow their bullshit because they enjoy being ignorant garbage. They're a cancer to our entertainment media and to our hobby. Fuck you very much, GamerGate. <br /> <br /> I don't know if it's a coincidence or if he was thinking about this when he pitched the game, but Matt thought up the tabletop game we need <i>right now</i>. We <i>need</i> a game that challenges longstanding cultural narratives. We <i>need</i> a game where the heroes are called out as assholes. The mere fact that people don't want to understand something as simple as &quot;heroes are asshole, the game isn't about them&quot; is further proof that Beast needs to happen. <br /> <br /> So fuck the heroes. The Beasts' contribution to current tabletop gaming culture is far more interesting, and far more useful. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:06:12-07:00","id":479214,"title":"","content":"The teaser sounds interesting. Although what I'm still wondering and hope that it is clear soon is if are you playing the monster itself or just a nightmare that is like the monster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:23:39-07:00","id":479224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479214#post479214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The teaser sounds interesting. Although what I'm still wondering and hope that it is clear soon is if are you playing the monster itself or just a nightmare that is like the monster</div> </div> </div> </div>You make it sound like there's a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:48:25-07:00","id":479262,"title":"","content":"Yepp if you play a full fledged dragon or &quot;just&quot; a nightmare that seems like a dragon is a difference. Like in the fiction: If you play a giant squid you can just squid out in the cafeteria and use your tentacles to feed yourself.....or you &quot;just&quot; grab someone and then wounds appear on him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:51:17-07:00","id":479264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479262#post479262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yepp if you play a full fledged dragon or &quot;just&quot; a nightmare that seems like a dragon is a difference. Like in the fiction: If you play a giant squid you can just squid out in the cafeteria and use your tentacles to feed yourself.....or you &quot;just&quot; grab someone and then wounds appear on him</div> </div> </div> </div>They've already said that this isn't a game where you'll be able to &quot;turn into a dragon in the middle of Times Square&quot;. But at the same time, there are definitely some &quot;shapeshifting&quot; powers that give you things like claws that let you tear your enemy Limb from Limb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:53:26-07:00","id":479265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479262#post479262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yepp if you play a full fledged dragon or &quot;just&quot; a nightmare that seems like a dragon is a difference. Like in the fiction: If you play a giant squid you can just squid out in the cafeteria and use your tentacles to feed yourself.....or you &quot;just&quot; grab someone and then wounds appear on him</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like you can have it both ways. In a high school cafeteria, Eve can &quot;just&quot; be a lot stronger than she looks and cause weird sucker-wounds to mysteriously appear on that other kid's flesh. If they were fighting in the ocean, Eve notes that she could crush him, eat his skin, liquify his flesh, and drink him slowly (a la the monster from <i>Deep Rising</i> whose picture graces the top of the blog post). Location, location, location (and maybe timing as well, depending on how Sated you are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:57:12-07:00","id":479269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479264#post479264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've already said that this isn't a game where you'll be able to &quot;turn into a dragon in the middle of Times Square&quot;. But at the same time, there are definitely some &quot;shapeshifting&quot; powers that give you things like claws that let you tear your enemy Limb from Limb.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I'm intrigued what it will be in the end (as the story points into both directions a bit)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479265#post479265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like you can have it both ways. In a high school cafeteria, Eve can &quot;just&quot; be a lot stronger than she looks and cause weird sucker-wounds to mysteriously appear on that other kid's flesh. If they were fighting in the ocean, Eve notes that she could crush him, eat his skin, liquify his flesh, and drink him slowly (a la the monster from <i>Deep Rising</i> whose picture graces the top of the blog post). Location, location, location (and maybe timing as well, depending on how Sated you are).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how it sounds and thus it will be interesting how it is really thus waiting for that info to come out (probalby in a few weeks^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:59:38-07:00","id":479271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479264#post479264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've already said that this isn't a game where you'll be able to &quot;turn into a dragon in the middle of Times Square&quot;. But at the same time, there are definitely some &quot;shapeshifting&quot; powers that give you things like claws that let you tear your enemy Limb from Limb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it can get more extreme than that. One of the examples we've been given involves a Beast turning into a tide of spiders to kill a Hero. That's pretty strong shapechanging-fu right there (although apparently Beasts approach it differently than were-creatures do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:02:02-07:00","id":479291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479271#post479271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it can get more extreme than that. One of the examples we've been given involves a Beast turning into a tide of spiders to kill a Hero. That's pretty strong shapechanging-fu right there (although apparently Beasts approach it differently than were-creatures do).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though that example happened within the Beast's Lair, which has been explicitly called out as a place where you can &quot;let your hair down&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:11:46-07:00","id":479298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479046#post479046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, fun fact: I actually wrote that bit a long time ago, as part of the original pitch for <b>Beast</b>. It doesn't appear in the book, although I like Eve and if we do an anthology I may write a story about her. But when I did that post for the blog, I had to read through that fiction bit and think, &amp;quot;OK, now that the rules are written, <i>can</i> you actually do this stuff?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And the answer is: Yes, though some of it is more cosmetic than anything. But Eve could have flooded that room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the seawater thing a Nightmare or an Atavism? Or neither?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:42:41-07:00","id":479314,"title":"","content":"Sounds like some sort of tell... I really liked that fiction. I've been semi-vocal about my nervousness at this game's release but that fiction just made me happy. I plan on playing up the &quot;embrace your nightmare&quot; aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:50:13-07:00","id":479319,"title":"","content":"So it looks like the five fears that correspond to the Families are, in Matt's own words:<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Hunted by a relentless predator. <br /> <br /> Makara: Dragged into the murky depths.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Dropped from great heights.<br /> <br /> Anakim: Held under the thumb of something huge and powerful.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: The knowledge that some nameless, shapeless thing out there in the dark is stalking you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:57:02-07:00","id":479324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479319#post479319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it looks like the five fears that correspond to the Families are, in Matt's own words:<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Hunted by a relentless predator.<br /> <br /> Makara: Dragged into the murky depths.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Dropped from great heights.<br /> <br /> Anakim: Held under the thumb of something huge and powerful.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: The knowledge that some nameless, shapeless thing out there in the dark is stalking you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the intellectual sides to this too:<br /> <br /> Makara: Being ignorant to nature of the danger, and knowing it.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Knowing someone is watching you.<br /> <br /> Anakim: Confronting your insignificance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:02:13-07:00","id":479330,"title":"","content":"On the RPGNet thread, someone compared a Beast to &quot;Like that elderly aunt who is up in everybody's business and is constantly dropping by unannounced to gather gossip and offer unsolicited advice... except a kraken.&quot; To which Matt replied that this was a description of the example character in the chargen chapter. I've begged him not to change this, and I think others should join me in so doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:39:16-07:00","id":479354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479319#post479319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it looks like the five fears that correspond to the Families are, in Matt's own words:<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Hunted by a relentless predator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually he said Namtaru is Revulsion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:55:24-07:00","id":479361,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I can picture a character like that:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Every night a dream of being hounded by a man,a Beautiful man,who keeps telling me i'm pathetic and he can make me free. If i agree to join his brood,a underground brood based on violence,then one day i decide to face the man in my dreams,when i say that i'm going to fight him he just says</span></span><br /> <i>&quot;Fine,hit me as hard as you can&quot;</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That was my Homemcoming,the moment i realized i was Tyler Durden&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T15:16:52-07:00","id":479537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479354#post479354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually he said Namtaru is Revulsion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but those are the five fears called out in the fiction from that preview. Eshmaki are demons/bogeymen, so they map to the nameless thing in the dark. That leaves Namtaru as the relentless predator archetype. Revulsion can fall under that umbrella as well via creepy-crawly predators (spiders, centipedes, snakes, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T16:25:44-07:00","id":479600,"title":"","content":"Is it too early to ask to see any artwork yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:28:55-07:00","id":479654,"title":"","content":"I imagine relentless predators are a matter of context, not Family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:14:23-07:00","id":479688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479654#post479654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine relentless predators are a matter of context, not Family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugallu, Anakim, and Makara map 1:1 with three of the fears mentioned (dropped from the sky, pinned under a giant's thumb, dragged into the depths,) so it's entirely reasonable to believe that the remaining two do so as well. I could be convinced that Eshmaki are the relentless predators and Namtaru are the nameless things in the dark, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:19:58-07:00","id":479693,"title":"","content":"Permit me to ask what Medusa and her kin would be then.<br /> <br /> Don't want to leave anyone out of the family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:41:04-07:00","id":479730,"title":"","content":"I think she's Namtaru? I swear I remember that from early on when they were using her as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:48:34-07:00","id":479734,"title":"","content":"Yes, Namtaru. The petrification was due to her hideous looks, conveniently overlooked by anyone who can draw and likes pretty monster girls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:07:20-07:00","id":481295,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\">Matt talks family and Families.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:15:51-07:00","id":481298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=481295#post481295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\">Matt talks family and Families.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll repost on comment I made on rpg.net:<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to get the feeling that Beast is far more tongue-in-cheek than other WW games, particularly after the repeated discussions concerning how Heroes are bad because it's not their story and now quotes such as, &quot;They seek out the unseen, the strange and arcane, not because they wish to solve the mysteries (which would be rude).&quot;<br /> <br /> I haven't yet formed a definitive opinion on whether these apparent comedic elements are a good or bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typos 04-15-2015, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:27:56-07:00","id":481299,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing anything comedic. It just sounds like Matt being Matt and including funny tidbits when talking about something that, in the book, will be presented as such. In the preview e got one little humorous aside? I don't think the game is tongue-and-cheek, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:41:07-07:00","id":481301,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think we'll get that much funny, aside from the situational. I do think that the beasts might eventually be the &quot;big bad&quot; of WoD. In every aspect, from werewolf to vampire, from uncreated to awakened, there's always that &quot;monster&quot; that they all fear, although supposed &quot;heroes&quot; not so much.<br /> It's turnabout with beasts. Monsters aren't so much a problem. &quot;Heroes&quot; however...<br /> Which is likely a concern if the rest of the WoD can't figure out which side to be on...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:54:48-07:00","id":481306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479600#post479600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it too early to ask to see any artwork yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is; I just turned in art notes last week. <br /> <br /> And as I said to branford over on RPG.Net, the book doesn't really take a comedic tone, that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:01:24-07:00","id":481311,"title":"","content":"I'm really digging the Family bits, especially the Makara. The Ugallu, too. While I might find inspiration in the more in-depth previews, I'm torn wether my first character should be Ugallu(The Witness, Fear of &quot;I know what you did last summer&quot;) or Makara(some sort of Cthulhu-Sothoth, Fear of &quot;Things man was not meant to know&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:04:06-07:00","id":481312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=481306#post481306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is; I just turned in art notes last week.<br /> <br /> And as I said to branford over on RPG.Net, the book doesn't really take a comedic tone, that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My misunderstanding about any comedy in Beast reminded me of this classic Joe Pesci moment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IWINtUCshxY\" data-code=\"IWINtUCshxY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/IWINtUCshxY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Now what kinds of Beasts are the characters in Goodfellas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:17:24-07:00","id":481391,"title":"","content":"Nobody seems to have mentioned it here yet, so I figured I would: new developer blog up, this time finally clarifying the corebook Families. Discuss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Family &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:25:41-07:00","id":481395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=481391#post481391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody seems to have mentioned it here yet, so I figured I would: new developer blog up, this time finally clarifying the corebook Families. Discuss.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Marin linked the new blog entry this morning (post #1358). However, no harm in another link. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:46:20-07:00","id":481403,"title":"","content":"So when are we going to see a dedicated beast forum now that we have preview blogs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:12:10-07:00","id":481452,"title":"","content":"We didn't get one for Demon until shortly before the KS.<br /> <br /> Cool your jets people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:27:15-07:00","id":481499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=481312#post481312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now what kinds of Beasts are the characters in Goodfellas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, man, I haven't watched that in years.<br /> <br /> Henry Hill is pretty obviously a Collector. His whole thing is that he wants the life being a Gangster provided. Maybe Power, but he seems to get hung up on things rather than position.<br /> <br /> Jimmy the Gent, probably Tyrant (Hunger for Power).<br /> <br /> Tommy DeVito is definitely a Ravager (Hunter for Ruin). He likes the girls and the booze and so on, but he feeds on killing and breaking shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","user":"blackhatmatt","date":". 04-16-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T12:59:04-07:00","id":481529,"title":"","content":"I'm really excited to hear more about Beast! I'm trying to come up with a character idea for a &quot;minotaur&quot; Beast, so based on the write-up today I'd say they'd be in the family Eshmaki, and obviously the Lair would be the Labyrinth. I think the Minotaur from Greek myth would have a Hunger for Prey, but I think a PC could have some flexibility here. I'm envisioning a school custodian who all the kids are afraid of, is the only one who enters the dangerous and winding basement beneath the school, and must chase any &quot;adventurous&quot; students out both because of school rules and to protect them from his own violent nature. Or the pampered and emotionally stunted adult son of a wealthy widow who invites new &quot;friends&quot; over to their gigantic mansion, only for many of these people to somehow get lost inside. Or the homeless person living with a group of fellows in the maintenance tunnels beneath the city, protecting them from threats that wander into their domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T13:00:44-07:00","id":481530,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">That hideousness links you back to the earliest monsters, the ones who didn\u2019t wear human shapes because they didn\u2019t care.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm taking that as reinforcement for my hypothesis that in the Neolithic Dark Eras setting, with Vinca civilization Mages, and Pre-Sundering Werewolves (in which Irem hasn't been built yet, and the only vampires are Stryx ridden corpses), the Begotten do not yet walk as humans, but instead exist freely as manifest monsters without ever being humans who have to unlock that identity.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpat