_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=482976#post482976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be kind of interested in a Demon who managed to get &amp;quot;adopted&amp;quot;, and sees life among the Beasts as the path to Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... Adopted.<br /> <br /> *Casually whispers into cuff link*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:40:07-07:00","id":483087,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of Angel from Buffy the Vampire Slayer when he was sent back into Hell. When he returned he was all feral creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T21:56:44-07:00","id":483164,"title":"","content":"If it isn't already covered by Hoard, or possibly Power, I would really like to see Knowledge as a Hunger. Knowledge of secrets. Knowledge of the occult. Knowledge of things you really shouldn't know. Knowledge of things you'd be better off not knowing. Knowledge of things the world would be better off if no one knew.<br /> <br /> Just a thought for the PG if again, it's not well served by a separate hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T05:15:20-07:00","id":483433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483164#post483164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it isn't already covered by Hoard, or possibly Power, I would really like to see Knowledge as a Hunger. Knowledge of secrets. Knowledge of the occult. Knowledge of things you really shouldn't know. Knowledge of things you'd be better off not knowing. Knowledge of things the world would be better off if no one knew.<br /> <br /> Just a thought for the PG if again, it's not well served by a separate hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you are the things people are better off not knowing about...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T05:52:23-07:00","id":483437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483164#post483164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it isn't already covered by Hoard, or possibly Power, I would really like to see Knowledge as a Hunger. Knowledge of secrets. Knowledge of the occult. Knowledge of things you really shouldn't know. Knowledge of things you'd be better off not knowing. Knowledge of things the world would be better off if no one knew.<br /> <br /> Just a thought for the PG if again, it's not well served by a separate hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that kind of beast would definitely pal around with Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:54:28-07:00","id":483533,"title":"","content":"Also, according to Mr. Matt over at the rpg.net thread, we're getting a blog on Nightmares this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:30:26-07:00","id":483630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483164#post483164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it isn't already covered by Hoard, or possibly Power, I would really like to see Knowledge as a Hunger. Knowledge of secrets. Knowledge of the occult. Knowledge of things you really shouldn't know. Knowledge of things you'd be better off not knowing. Knowledge of things the world would be better off if no one knew.<br /> <br /> Just a thought for the PG if again, it's not well served by a separate hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You <i>could</i> cover that with either Hoard or Power, I think. It might be enough it's own thing to merit being a new Hunger in the PG. Dunno yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:29:12-07:00","id":483700,"title":"","content":"So given the latest update, which Hunger do we think each of the Addams' would have? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:14:57-07:00","id":483985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483433#post483433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you are the things people are better off not knowing about...</div> </div> </div> </div>I am just working my way through all the Beast material, so forgive me if I missed this/haven't gotten to it: are mages counted as kin to Beasts? <br /> <br /> Sure, they seek knowledge and power, but they are still essentially &quot;human&quot; (just aware of the Truth of Reality). Born human (versus Prometheans, Werewolves and Demons), their soul is intact (versus Vampires and Changelings), and no supernaturally mandated compulsions (no Hunger, no Geist mandating your actions, no Judges of Duat, no Rage/Ancient Pledges). I could see them studying a Beast, but I don't think they would see them as kin. I mean, they have the same potential for good and evil as an average human (heck, Slashers and some Hunter organizations are more monsterous than the average mage), just able to exert said moral alignment on a more epic level.<br /> <br /> The Abyss, on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 04-17-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:20:48-07:00","id":483989,"title":"","content":"As far as we know, all of the major splats are Kin to beasts except Demons and Hunters.<br /> <br /> Though I think it was said that certain hunter conspiracies and some Slasher undertakings counted as Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:51:35-07:00","id":484023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483985#post483985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am just working my way through all the Beast material, so forgive me if I missed this/haven't gotten to it: are mages counted as kin to Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages apparent are definitely kin to Beasts, and in some ways closer than some other templates.<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw, one of the writers on Beast (and almost everything else recently from WW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), stated on rpg.net:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread&amp;p=18839582#post18839582\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...2#post18839582</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Beasts are people who've tapped into an unexplored depth of the human soul. They may </span></span><i>look</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> unusual, but an Awakened mage is a lot closer to them than, say, a vampire is. The analogy I used in the crossover chapter draft is that mages are like the one child in a family who went to college - she attends family gatherings with an undecipherable vocabulary and her mind on things the other attendees would never even think about, and maybe that alienates them from her, but she's still family.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:56:01-07:00","id":484028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> I guess for me, the question is then: why? I touched on my thoughts in the last post, but it just seems that a Mage is not inherently monsterous. Sure, individual mages can be nightmares, just as others can be saints. It is just that none have an inherent drive to be a monster (except Banishers and the Mad, i.e. broken mages), at least no more of a drive than any other human. They just have the knowledge and power to do more harm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nothing against the idea. I just hope it is well justified.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See my last post concerning DaveB's comments. <br /> <br /> Kinship doesn't appear to always be about how monstrous another being my be, but rather the nature and content of their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:58:08-07:00","id":484030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484023#post484023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mages apparent are definitely kin to Beasts, and in some ways closer than some other templates.<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw, one of the writers on Beast (and almost everything else recently from WW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), stated on rpg.net:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread&amp;p=18839582#post18839582\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...2#post18839582</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I was thinking from the &quot;base aspects of human fears&quot; direction, which was why mages seemed odd. I was looking at it from &quot;mages are people who had the lights turned on: they see through the darkness and have the means to rise above it.&quot; Sure, they now know all the scary stuff out there (or can find it) but have the power to confront it. And they are no more driven towards good or evil than a normal human. And with Ascension, they can become the living aspect of human nature. That is why I viewed them as the Antithesis of the Beast: they are humans souls that have the potential to combat the innate fears and transcend them.<br /> <br /> But reading Daves post, I can see why they are kin. If beasts are creatures drawn from the darker aspect of the human soul, and you look at it from that perspective of mages being those who also use the soul for power, but draw from a different well for their power... Yeah, I can see the Beasts being like &quot;Sure, you are all fancy with your philosophy, but we both draw power from the abstract concepts. Mine are just a bit less high browed, and a bit darker.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 04-17-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T17:01:04-07:00","id":484034,"title":"","content":"I believed Beasts were once normal people &quot;Blessed&quot; by the Dark Mother, for her own unfathomable reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T17:36:44-07:00","id":484053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484034#post484034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believed Beasts were once normal people &amp;quot;Blessed&amp;quot; by the Dark Mother, for her own unfathomable reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> As far as I'm aware, no. The Children were always strange and uncomfortable in their own skins, plagued by a reoccurring nightmare and a strange need that would later blossom into their Hunger. A Homecoming isn't a transformation; it's a revelation, a moment of clarity as the Begotten sees the horror at the center of their self.... And smiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T18:11:51-07:00","id":484078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484053#post484053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As far as I'm aware, no. The Children were always strange and uncomfortable in their own skins, plagued by a reoccurring nightmare and a strange need that would later blossom into their Hunger. A Homecoming isn't a transformation; it's a revelation, a moment of clarity as the Begotten sees the horror at the center of their self.... And smiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could say they were &quot;blessed&quot; from birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T04:32:12-07:00","id":484402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484078#post484078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you could say they were &quot;blessed&quot; from birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Think that underminds part of what they are going for.. These aren't Normal people who have &quot;Become&quot; something Monsterous, these are Monsters who have never understood why everything they were taught in there lives just.. Doesn't make Sense. Sure it's right for most people but it just never Clicks until they have there Homecoming then they understand why, The Rules and lessons didn't work for them because they were NEVER human, they had something inside them that just Couldn't understand why these &quot;Rules&quot; were there for them.<br /> <br /> Does this mean they are unsympathetic? Are they more Monsterous then the other Creatures in the World of Darkness? Probably not. Possibly yes.<br /> <br /> After righting this... I can't be the only one that wants too make a Beast thats a Psychologist Who's hunger is Ruin..... Scarecrow anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T08:41:24-07:00","id":484596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=479046#post479046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, fun fact: I actually wrote that bit a long time ago, as part of the original pitch for <b>Beast</b>. It doesn't appear in the book, although I like Eve and if we do an anthology I may write a story about her. But when I did that post for the blog, I had to read through that fiction bit and think, &quot;OK, now that the rules are written, <i>can</i> you actually do this stuff?&quot;<br /> <br /> And the answer is: Yes, though some of it is more cosmetic than anything. But Eve could have flooded that room.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it caught my attention. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Trying to play catch-up, as I've not been paying any attention to the upcoming releases, and are trying to get up to speed with this. Ironically, I had ideas along this line, for the game I'm working on, where there was a girl who had huge pyromancy, but felt out of place, and not quite right, no matter what she did. Because she was, in fact a dragon; in the universe she was in, they couldn't exist in their natural forms, and had to adopt other forms, like human. They could &quot;emerge,&quot; but only in times of great stress, situations like that.<br /> <br /> And by the way... thanks for sharing with us that fiction piece. Certainly was good to read, and you really felt for Eve, and her situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:01:48-07:00","id":484626,"title":"","content":"A comment from one of the writers on Kinship powers:<br /> &quot;Without giving too much away, consider that monsters are people too, at least in the World of Darkness, and there may be a difference between why mages are scary, why Mastigos mages in particular or scary, and even why Suleiman the Mastigos mage in very particular is scary. With the right Family Ties, Beasts can tap into any of those.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:35:41-07:00","id":484650,"title":"","content":"Can beasts adopt their true form while inside their lairs, or is it a specific power like protean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:51:51-07:00","id":484676,"title":"","content":"Who Makara here<br /> <br /> pleb families need not apply","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T13:20:07-07:00","id":484825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484650#post484650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can beasts adopt their true form while inside their lairs, or is it a specific power like protean?</div> </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge they are automatically their True Form inside their Lairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Who Makara here</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Comrade.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T14:44:26-07:00","id":484851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=484402#post484402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I Think that underminds part of what they are going for.. These aren't Normal people who have &quot;Become&quot; something Monsterous, these are Monsters who have never understood why everything they were taught in there lives just.. Doesn't make Sense. Sure it's right for most people but it just never Clicks until they have there Homecoming then they understand why, The Rules and lessons didn't work for them because they were NEVER human, they had something inside them that just Couldn't understand why these &quot;Rules&quot; were there for them.<br /> <br /> Does this mean they are unsympathetic? Are they more Monsterous then the other Creatures in the World of Darkness? Probably not. Possibly yes.<br /> <br /> After righting this... I can't be the only one that wants too make a Beast thats a Psychologist Who's hunger is Ruin..... Scarecrow anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the reverse can also be true, with people who fit very well into their old lives and consequently aren't taking the sudden change very well. Honestly, looking at the Hungers and the anxieties tied to the Families, Beasts sound very human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T15:01:46-07:00","id":484859,"title":"","content":"Another tidbit from the rpg.net thread: One of the writers mentioned one of his favorite Nightmares was called &quot;Behold, my True Form!&quot;. To which I can only respond ALL MY YES!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, in the comments of the &quot;Families&quot; spoiler, we have a rough schedule for the next blog posts: Tuesday and Thursday, Hungers and Nightmares respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Something new 04-18-2015, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T21:03:30-07:00","id":485045,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to Hungers. I want to see how broad they are. I'm also curious if their is anything in the way of subtypes or refinements on a specific Hunger. A character who seeks physical strength and a character who seeks authority over others can both be said to hunger for Power, but those are two very different characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T23:22:05-07:00","id":485179,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if anyone has asked this but do beasts age normally like humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T05:15:30-07:00","id":485345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485179#post485179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if anyone has asked this but do beasts age normally like humans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a very good question indeed... one that they might answer soon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:29:45-07:00","id":485391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485179#post485179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if anyone has asked this but do beasts age normally like humans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beasts age, but not as quickly as normal (something similar to changelings I'd guess), incarnates can get &quot;old as dirt&quot; longevity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T09:36:10-07:00","id":485457,"title":"","content":"So I've had two players separately come to me wondering about Nightmares about being burned alive and my instinct was for them to be Eshmaki but the write-up makes me think that might not be right. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:23:19-07:00","id":485478,"title":"","content":"For the fear of being burned alive, I'd go with Anakim, or maybe Namtaru if you want to focus on burn scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:26:02-07:00","id":485480,"title":"","content":"I could still peg it as Eshmaki, though I suppose the devil's in the details, and could lead to the Namtaru or the Anakim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:28:13-07:00","id":485483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485457#post485457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've had two players separately come to me wondering about Nightmares about being burned alive and my instinct was for them to be Eshmaki but the write-up makes me think that might not be right. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually think Anakim, of the corebook Families, since nightmares of being burned alive suggest fear of pain and agony, of being powerless to stop the pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:57:54-07:00","id":485501,"title":"","content":"My players are already planning characters, One's planning on being Jason, another a dragon and the third Cthulhu (these are vague statements of intent character creation changes everything)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:57:56-07:00","id":485502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485457#post485457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've had two players separately come to me wondering about Nightmares about being burned alive and my instinct was for them to be Eshmaki but the write-up makes me think that might not be right. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hang on...there are write-ups for this corebook? If so, where do I look for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:00:56-07:00","id":485503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485478#post485478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the fear of being burned alive, I'd go with Anakim, or maybe Namtaru if you want to focus on burn scars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anakim definitely from how I see it. To have such a fear is to be powerless to stop it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:03:10-07:00","id":485504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485502#post485502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hang on...there are write-ups for this corebook? If so, where do I look for it?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Family &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:19:36-07:00","id":485513,"title":"","content":"I have a dumb question: Why is the Anakim nightmare so much broader in scope than all the rest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:06:30-07:00","id":485563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485513#post485513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a dumb question: Why is the Anakim nightmare so much broader in scope than all the rest?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. VoidDrifter hits on a relevant explanation in the comments:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my own understanding of it, like the Makara, the Ugallu are a portamanteau of several vaguely related fears. Fear of being watched, fear of being taken by some flying monster, fear of heights, agorophobia, fear of falling, all the fears that relate to the heights, just as the Makara relate to all the fears of water and the deep darkness beneath. </div> </div> </div>The Anakim just happen to have a more basic fear sitting in the name-slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:18:19-07:00","id":485567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485504#post485504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for this! I'll try to get caught up, and see if I can understand what everyone is talking about now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T18:21:55-07:00","id":485886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485563#post485563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not. VoidDrifter hits on a relevant explanation in the comments:<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The Anakim just happen to have a more basic fear sitting in the name-slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I am still quite confused. It sounds like VoidDrifter is saying that each Family is built to evoke a cluster of basic fears, which makes sense. That said, I don't see how it addresses whether or not the Anakim theme is broader than the others. Given what little I'm aware of, it seems like the Anakim kind of overlap with the themes of all the other Families, while the other Families don't overlap with each other nearly so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T19:08:36-07:00","id":485901,"title":"","content":"Our fear at being powerless does seem a bit large in scope. But fear itself is a broad category. I think for many of us certain fears we can deal with and I think that kinda lends to a degree of confusion. Ugliness, the ocean deeps, death (obliteration), even heights, I think for a lot of us, we can overcome these fears in our real world. But to be powerless? I myself have that feeling every day. That's too real for many here. And we can easily translate that helpless feeling to the others. I believe that the idea behind the Anakim, is that word, &quot;power.&quot; I think of Dr. Doom. He doesn't fear his scars behind the mask, no fear of death, not much fear at all. But he never ever wants to feel powerless. More to do with one's ego I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T19:21:10-07:00","id":485907,"title":"","content":"Based on the source material, I wouldn't limit 'Revulsion' to 'Ugliness.' Creepy crawling things, ravages of disease, the things that have that quality to them that makes your skin crawl. Likewise the depths isn't just about ocean depths, but the unknown. The fear of the skies I think was an evolution of vulnerability. A different thing than powerlessness, more of an 'openness.' On the other thread on rpg.net, <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread&amp;p=18872736#post18872736\" target=\"_blank\">it was associated with the fear of being watched or spied upon.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-19-2015, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T19:58:41-07:00","id":485955,"title":"","content":"*nods* ok..<br /> <br /> It's kinda funny in some ways. I don't think I'm alone here when I say I relate a lot to some of these fears.<br /> I recall driving down an open stretch of road where it seemed to me that there was nothing but the sky...and it felt so strange. I didn't realize that I was a bit of an agoraphobe until that day. Felt even worse when it came to the ocean...deep...too deep! It goes on and on!! Agh! But the one fear, I've always been familiar with, well, I once had a dream of getting jumped by two guys at night at a darkened corner. When they knocked my glasses off I saw nothing but red rage, and I ripped their throats out with my teeth. I awoke with a bit of a start at that point. It bothered me a little when I realized I felt no horror at my actions. But I did feel a strange taste of victory. (Yes!...umm wait no..)<br /> I think this game is going to knock it out of the park for the reason that we are all familiar with fear in most of its categories. (Could Raistlin Majere be an example of an Anakim?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T20:04:40-07:00","id":485958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=485955#post485955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kinda funny in some ways. I don't think I'm alone here when I say I relate a lot to some of these fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most assuredly not, and that was the point, one of the inspirations for the game was <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/On-Monsters-Unnatural-History-Worst/dp/0199798095\" target=\"_blank\">On Monsters: An Unnatural History of Our Worst Fears</a>, which attempts to link a lot of mythological monsters to basic human fears.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T23:26:16-07:00","id":486046,"title":"","content":"So, a visual struck me and I find myself pondering which of the core Families <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astraphobia\" target=\"_blank\">astraphobia</a> would most readily fall into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T23:40:18-07:00","id":486054,"title":"","content":"I'd guess ugallu. It seems like it could overlap with the anakim and eshmaki because of the booming power in thunder and the destructive capability of lightning, but the fear looks to be more about this threat from the skies that could strike at any moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2015, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T00:20:00-07:00","id":486065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=229065#post229065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To quote Dave Brookshaw, and possibly the description of the book, &quot;Within every one of us lies the potential of the Beast. Unleash savage powers, answer the call to your Lair, and become the thing that Heroes fear. Onyx Path's new nWoD game line for 2015. 320 pages. PDF/PoD/Prestige Edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds like we'll get more answers at the nWoD talk tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm surprised they didn't think of this sooner. There are a bunch of legends of humans spontaneously turning into monsters for a number of reasons. Just the thought of playing as the &quot;dungeon boss&quot; and watching the little heroes play right into your trap makes me smile!<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, so you say your team once took down an entire pack of werewolves in a single night? Well then I guess you won't have any problems fighting Mazgothuk, the 126 tentacled horror from the eastern seaboard!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, this page explains we'll be playing as the children of Lamia, mother of all monsters. This is going to be euphoric!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Family &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-20-2015, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T00:57:05-07:00","id":486088,"title":"","content":"By the way, I'm going to go out on a limb and guess that those fucking dreams where I lose the ability to speak and move in slow motion the moment I spot something I'm scared of (spiders, living dolls, est) would fall under the category of Anakim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T01:32:43-07:00","id":486118,"title":"","content":"Character creation training exercise: <b>What Families would work with now supernatural creatures from the World of Darkness?</b> In the other words - <b>what fears ( and Families of Children) reflect vampires, werewolves, mages, Prometheans, changelings, sin-eaters etc.?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T01:44:00-07:00","id":486122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486118#post486118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character creation training exercise: <b>What Families would work with now supernatural creatures from the World of Darkness?</b> In the other words - <b>what fears ( and Families of Children) reflect vampires, werewolves, mages, Prometheans, changelings, sin-eaters etc.?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that...<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires &amp; Werewolves</b> - both are Raptors, in reality - you are afraid of being there victim in their hunt, and being drunk all of you blood or your limbs being torn apart by the claws of the wolf. They can snatch and killed by them, as they can look like <i>anybody</i>. So what it would be? <i><b>Ugallu</b></i>?<br /> <br /> <b>Mages</b> - I think it's fear of Unknown - this weird guy have powers you do not understand, can make anything he can wish with you, and you cannot be sure it's all he have. Or even if you killed him, if it's not just next his trick. So in this way, it would be <i><b>Makara</b></i>? Or maybe <i><b>Anakim</b></i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:40:52-07:00","id":486166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486118#post486118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character creation training exercise: <b>What Families would work with now supernatural creatures from the World of Darkness?</b> In the other words - <b>what fears ( and Families of Children) reflect vampires, werewolves, mages, Prometheans, changelings, sin-eaters etc.?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree that vamps and wolves would be raptors, since their attacks can come straight out of nowhere and where you least expect it. &quot;He's an apex predator, so he never looks up.&quot; Well until something humanity didn't expect blind sides them!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b> would be <b>Anakim</b>, obviously. A being who has all of reality as their plaything can definitely make you feel powerless. I would also suggest that Changeling would fit the same role, especially after what they experienced at the hand of the True Fae. You're taken to a world that's completely alien to you and every time you venture back there you barely escape with your life, sanity, freedom or all three!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demons</b> and <b>Prometheans</b> would be <b>Eshmaki</b>. The Prometheans being soulless constructs seeking to become more human, while Demons lose their sense of purpose and are constantly being hunted by an angry god and his angels!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mummies</b> would be Leviathans, given their origin and the fact they wake up with demi-god powers for a few years before going back into hibernation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea what Sin Eaters would be, as they don't seem to fit the roles presented.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From what I've read on Beast, it sounds like the characters you play have human bodies, but the souls of monsters. That's kind of disappointing, but at the same time it makes sense. Awfully hard to pretend knowledge of the supernatural is kept secret when you have a 50 foot tall Anakim caught on the 11 o'clock news!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:50:27-07:00","id":486171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodspeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=308041#post308041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We do indeed.<br /> To be honest i half expect and fear that beasts will go the route of werewolf regarding their warforms, with a variety of different/unique characteristics.<br /> But i fervently hope that this will not be the case. It would be a disservice and a missed opportunity for wod in general, to pass up on big, scary monsters (and even bigger, gigantic ones in the endgame) as warforms and &quot;alter-egos&quot; for the PCs regardless of their origin, nature or other characteristics.<br /> <br /> Plus it will have the effect of further distinguishing and reinforcing the Beats position as the common, scary family that links all supers together and fills that last horror niche that begs to be filled.<br /> At least that's the impression i get by reading the title and the scant info we have.<br /> I guess we will see in due time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind the Beasts having the ability to change between human and monster form. You might think the Werewolf form is pretty small, until you remember that it is 9 feet tall and weighs 400 lbs. Then, of course, you have the Gargantuan Kith who can add up to 10 levels on their Size. If a Grizzly bear is registered as a Size 7, and humans are a Size 5, imagine what a Size 15 Ogre would look like.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not impossible for us to have massive characters in WoD, it's just that only a small group of them have size alteration powers. That being said, I'm sure that the Anakim who's entire premise is descended from giant creatures will have some ability to alter their size. Perhaps not to monolythic proportions, but large enough that you feel like a power house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T04:25:21-07:00","id":486220,"title":"","content":"Stunning New Image of the Anakim.....<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://www.iwatchstuff.com/2011/09/28/bfg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:11:17-07:00","id":486276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Hungers &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:37:41-07:00","id":486283,"title":"","content":"Man, I was expecting to have to wait until tomorrow! Thank you guys!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm liking these. Punishment and Hoard seems my favorite, though all of them sound neat. I was worried that I wouldn't like Ruin, but the blurb managed to sell me. It does make me wonder about a Ravenger who destroys social groups instead of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:40:46-07:00","id":486286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=483630#post483630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i>could</i> cover that with either Hoard or Power, I think. It might be enough it's own thing to merit being a new Hunger in the PG. Dunno yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Punishment too, if your agenda with secrets is to publicise them to hurt those who keep them. But I could still see a Hunger for Secrets in its own right - maybe a Hunger for the Forbidden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:41:01-07:00","id":486287,"title":"","content":"DOUBLE POST, IGNORE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Things went wonky on my end. Sorry! 04-20-2015, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:52:55-07:00","id":486298,"title":"","content":"Its clear to me that Hungers are very open-ended, which I like. A Beast who collects secrets could be a Collector, he could be a Nemesis collecting them to punish certain sinners, or he could be a Ravager collecting them to break up relationships like you said above. Edit: Hey, he could even be a Predator who inflicts pain on his target through ruining their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:45:06-07:00","id":486357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486046#post486046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a visual struck me and I find myself pondering which of the core Families <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astraphobia\" target=\"_blank\">astraphobia</a> would most readily fall into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugallu.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">i'maghoooost</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:24:28-07:00","id":486418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486046#post486046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a visual struck me and I find myself pondering which of the core Families <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astraphobia\" target=\"_blank\">astraphobia</a> would most readily fall into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with nofather, Ugallu. Along with the reasons they suggested, I'd add that the thunder and lighting emphasise how much vaster the sky is than the world we walk on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486298#post486298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its clear to me that Hungers are very open-ended, which I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486166#post486166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mage</b> would be <b>Anakim</b>, obviously. A being who has all of reality as their plaything can definitely make you feel powerless.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Remembering the caveat that Families aren't meant to map literally to other supes] I could also see mages as Makara. Most supernaturals stick with the parts of the cosmos they have intimate connections to, but mages are interested in big pictures; they explore, which means they know and embody how unfathomable the universe is when you try to explore it. They look for the things moving beneath the surface - and there's great knowlege to be had there - but every depth you plumb is yet another suface with still more moving beneath it. And when you plumb depths getting <i>out</i> of your depth is all too easy.<br /> <br /> I could see vampires being Namtaru. Not because they're ugly - far too many of them for comfort are not - but because they're <i>poison</i>. When they entice, it's because something of them has got under your skin and changed you - literally so, in the case of blood bonds. They make you into their image in lesser or greater degrees, from dominate to ghouls to the embrace.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, I'd see as Eshmaki. You're being hunted, and the thing hunting you won't stop, won't give up, and won't lose you. People say they fear being alone, or the unknown - but what they mean is that they fear they <i>aren't really alone</i>, and that whatever lurks out of sight will come forth and make itself known - and when the werewolves are after you, that's your life, for as long as it lasts.<br /> <br /> I agree about changelings as Anakim. The way pledges can bind you up is a big one there.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, I think I see Prometheans as Ugallu. Mostly because they're very much creatures of outside, and of empty places (and the places they go tend to become emptied out). They bring storms with them - literal in the case of Wastelands, psychological and social in the case of Disquiet, and inside themselves with their Torment. And they're attended by angels.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't one of the families. Bloody gold-digging pretenders.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sineaters I think I'd see as Makara. There's another being beneath the surface of every one of them, and another world beneath the surface of this one, which they're all part of - caves don't look much like watery depths, but can generate much of the same feel. And an endless past, represented by both the Underworld and ghosts, lurking beneath the surface of the present.<br /> <br /> And mummies I'd see as Anakim. They're implacable, driven by purposes neither you nor they can gainsay. They represent a world that's older, bigger, grander, and just... <i>more</i>... than the one you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:49:30-07:00","id":486481,"title":"","content":"When Fears are diffcult to pin point as easy equivalents to other supernaturals, shown in blog post <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/\" target=\"_blank\">Hungers </a>are much simpler anolouges.<br /> <br /> ( Links are based on general sterotypes of respective gamelines )<br /> <br /> <i>Vampires</i> are Tyrants, controling your life from shadows.<br /> <i>Werewolves</i> are Predators, hunting on you in the middle of night.<br /> <i>Mages</i> are Collectors, doing anything for next supernal pice of knoglede.<br /> <i>Fae</i> ( and Changelings ) are Nemeses, punishing those that brake the &quot;rules&quot;. ( Example character even hangs out with Lost from the Ogre Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <i>Prometheans</i> are Ravangers, that destroy things just by they own existance and Ravange is part of their Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-20-2015, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:32:46-07:00","id":486565,"title":"","content":"Man, there are a probably lot of Beasts with no patience for pretty much all the organizations in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:37:18-07:00","id":486570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486565#post486565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, there are a probably lot of Beasts with no patience for pretty much all the organizations in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question is though:</b> Will heroes usually be solo, or will they attack in parties?<br /> <br /> If the heroes travel alone, then Beast sounds like they're pretty weak. If they hunt in parties, then Beasts can be pretty powerful to take them head on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:44:28-07:00","id":486575,"title":"","content":"I should think that an angry mob would be pretty scary to all involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T12:23:29-07:00","id":486613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486570#post486570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Question is though:</b> Will heroes usually be solo, or will they attack in parties?<br /> <br /> If the heroes travel alone, then Beast sounds like they're pretty weak. If they hunt in parties, then Beasts can be pretty powerful to take them head on.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I gather, Heroes aren't pals with other Heroes. Their egos are too large (I'm also of the theory to become a Hero, you have to do something that the Children find inexcusable, and something Matt loves to hate them for-then I remembered how many mythical heroes are kinslayers).<br /> <br /> They get Followers, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T12:23:44-07:00","id":486614,"title":"","content":"TL; Did R. Very excited. I could see mortals getting drawn to a Beast's Lair and becoming trapped, and changed, by it, but I don't really care if that ever gets put in the book. Also, I'd argue the phantasmal sea water in the fiction was probably a Nightmare power; the sucker-marks, an Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T12:26:16-07:00","id":486615,"title":"","content":"More like an angry raid. That should be a fun obstacle for Beast players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T12:50:08-07:00","id":486648,"title":"","content":"Also: my ideal Beast would be an Acid Rainer. So, Ugallu with a Hunger for Punishment. Thinking of being a Dirigible Pilot by day, Radical Environmentalist by night. Wonder if some of the higher level Atavisms will allow for poisons, or flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custo