":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:29:18-07:00","id":486669,"title":"","content":"Okay, so after reading a bit. We have &quot;Lairs, Hearts, and Chambers&quot; that Beasts reside in....<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/Dungkeep.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Squee!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:25:54-07:00","id":486763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486666#post486666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to aid in character creation:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://abookofcreatures.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://abookofcreatures.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *reads entry on Al-mi'raj*<br /> <br /> BRB, must make Beast based on Mythological Rabbit of Carennabog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:02:28-07:00","id":486790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486481#post486481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Fears are diffcult to pin point as easy equivalents to other supernaturals, shown in blog post <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/beasthungers/&quot;]Hungers</a> [/URL]are much simpler anolouges.<br /> <br /> ( Links are based on general sterotypes of respective gamelines )<br /> <br /> <i>Vampires</i> are Tyrants, controling your life from shadows.<br /> <i>Werewolves</i> are Predators, hunting on you in the middle of night.<br /> <i>Mages</i> are Collectors, doing anything for next supernal pice of knoglede.<br /> <i>Fae</i> ( and Changelings ) are Nemeses, punishing those that brake the &quot;rules&quot;. ( Example character even hangs out with Lost from the Ogre Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <i>Prometheans</i> are Ravangers, that destroy things just by they own existance and Ravange is part of their Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I thought more along these lines:<br /> <i>Mages</i> are Tyrants, beings of ungodly power, who seek to further their power to ascend to a point where they literally define reality.<br /> <i>Prometheans</i> are Collectors, constantly seeking what will let them be whole. (Milestones and the Pilgrimage)<br /> <i>Vampires</i> are Ravagers, who literally must drain the life blood of others to survive, and can only procreate by destroying the life of another.<br /> <br /> Agree with the Werewolf and Changing tags. Any idea for the Sineaters? I could see them fitting with the Nemeses, as they too try to punish those who break the the rules (Get ghosts to pass on or destroy abmortals). <br /> <br /> (Though I will admit, the Prometheans could be Ravagers. One word- Wastelands)<br /> <br /> That said, I feel it will come down to the individual drives of the member of each group, with just some natural tendency of members to lean towards one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":".  beware the trap of copy and paste 04-20-2015, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:29:49-07:00","id":486804,"title":"","content":"guys it's &quot;ravager.&quot; no &quot;n&quot; and no etymological commonality with &quot;revenge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Minimal indulgence of prescriptivism aside\u2026<br /> <br /> I disagree with the view that Prometheans resonate with Ravagers just because they're powered by an inherently ruinous force \u2014 remember that the Hungers <i>feed</i> Beasts.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, positing that Sin-Eaters have the most resonance with that Hunger by the nature of their duty and motifs \u2014 whether it's undoing stagnation or supporting it, the Underworld runs and runs on loss. Werewolves are Nemeses as a function of basic territorial policy and mythological dictates.<br /> <br /> Closer to home, which Family/Hunger pairs do y'all see as best-fits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:36:14-07:00","id":486830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486804#post486804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closer to home, which Family/Hunger pairs do y'all see as best-fits?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, which Family fits best with which Hunger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"