werlessness, feeding by making others feel powerless seems like a no-brainer.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Eshmaki, who seem to best represent the fear of being hunted, seem like natural Predators. <br /> <br /> Ugallu, with their apparent associates with paranoia and surveillance seem like they'd make terrifying Nemeses.<br /> <br /> The Namtaru's connection to such horrors as death and rot seems like they'd make good Ravagers.<br /> <br /> And Makara would be Collectors, because of the whole eldritch lore and ancient underseas treasure thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:55:49-07:00","id":486859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486852#post486852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very same. Anakim Tyrants seem like a natural fit, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anakim Ravagers are really intuitive for me.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadow Over Innsmouth</i> makes me think of Makara Tyrants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486854#post486854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Y'Know, in a fangame-friendly version of WoD, I would guess that the Leviathans are the closest &quot;cousins&quot; to the Beasts, possibly even &quot;brothers&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think you wanted to link to this page: <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/LeviathanTheTempest\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...thanTheTempest</a></div> </div> </div> </div>No, they meant Leviathan as in the Makara Family; it is their nickname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 04-20-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:59:24-07:00","id":486864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486859#post486859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anakim Ravagers are really intuitive for me.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadow Over Innsmouth</i> makes me think of Makara Tyrants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, they meant Leviathan as in the Makara Family; it is their nickname.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhhhh. My mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:04:44-07:00","id":486866,"title":"","content":"Also, since underclassman shares my confusion I thought I might as well put it to the thread: anybody have a good bare-bones explanation of the Eshmaki and Predators? I'm just this side of grokking them, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:14:59-07:00","id":486874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486852#post486852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very same. Anakim Tyrants seem like a natural fit, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anakim might also be good Predators. When you're the size of a house you need a lot of food to keep your energy up. And you can easily feel powerless when confronted with a bigger, meaner predator who's evolved to conquer its environment! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-20-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:43:15-07:00","id":486882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486866#post486866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since underclassman shares my confusion I thought I might as well put it to the thread: anybody have a good bare-bones explanation of the Eshmaki and Predators? I'm just this side of grokking them, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>My best guess, given the information we have, is that Predators feed off reminding humanity that they're not at the top of the food chain. A bit confusingly, with the Vanessa example, they don't actually need to eat their prey, so long as the prey understands that it's prey. In contrast, in my mind, a Tyrant would require a gesture of submission from their target, while a Nemesis needs their mark to transgress before they make their move.<br /> <br /> So, as bare bones as possible, Predators are all about the thrill of the hunt.<br /> <br /> As for the Eshmaki, imagine that oft-recurring scene in horror movies where a character believes they are alone, but the camera reveals to the audience that this is not the case. Alternatively, they're that feeling you get when you're walking home alone at night and there's no one around and part of you understands that there's no one else around but another part of you is absolutely certain that someone is about to jump out of the shadows and mug/beat/etc you.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also, it seems that, like Families, Hungers have a lot of potential for overlap, which is interesting. The boundaries between, say, Ravagers and Nemeses, Predators and Tyrants, seem quite fuzzy. (Unless they're only fuzzy to me because I'm missing something crucial, so, caveat emptor.) If this is the case, I imagine it is intentional, considering what happens when one goes about filling in maps. I also imagine at least once some hapless chump has been targeted by five different Beasts to satiate all five Hungers at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 04-20-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:57:24-07:00","id":486887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486866#post486866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since underclassman shares my confusion I thought I might as well put it to the thread: anybody have a good bare-bones explanation of the Eshmaki and Predators? I'm just this side of grokking them, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I feel what the Eshmaki represent pretty strongly, so let me try. The Eshmaki are the knife that presses against your throat out of nowhere, and the hand that covers your mouth when you try to scream. They are the gun in the dark, following you or lurking in alleyways, waiting for you to let your guard down for just one second. When you wake up from a fitful slumber and you see a bestial THING on the edge of your bed, looking at your throat like it's the tastiest thing in the world, you have known the Eshmaki. When you lie awake at night, neither moving nor breathing, not crying out or even just crying because you know the second the demons sense you you will die, know that the Eshmaki have supped upon your dreams, with the jagged teeth of wolves or the curves fangs of vampires. Their names are Thug and Violence, Darkness and Lurker, Isolation and No-one Can Hear You Scream. They are the Eshmaki. Don't bother running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:04:13-07:00","id":486892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486882#post486882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My best guess, given the information we have, is that Predators feed off reminding humanity that they're not at the top of the food chain. A bit confusingly, with the Vanessa example, they don't actually need to eat their prey, so long as the prey understands that it's prey. In contrast, in my mind, a Tyrant would require a gesture of submission from their target, while a Nemesis needs their mark to transgress before they make their move.<br /> <br /> So, as bare bones as possible, Predators are all about the thrill of the hunt.<br /> <br /> As for the Eshmaki, imagine that oft-recurring scene in horror movies where a character believes they are alone, but the camera reveals to the audience that this is not the case. Alternatively, they're that feeling you get when you're walking home alone at night and there's no one around and part of you understands that there's no one else around but another part of you is absolutely certain that someone is about to jump out of the shadows and mug/beat/etc you.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also, it seems that, like Families, Hungers have a lot of potential for overlap, which is interesting. The boundaries between, say, Ravagers and Nemeses, Predators and Tyrants, seem quite fuzzy. (Unless they're only fuzzy to me because I'm missing something crucial, so, caveat emptor.) If this is the case, I imagine it is intentional, considering what happens when one goes about filling in maps. I also imagine at least once some hapless chump has been targeted by five different Beasts to satiate all five Hungers at once.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The description for Anakim says that &quot;size is secondary&quot; what counts is that you overwhelm your victims with shear power. A predator can certainly be powerful without being the largest creature in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Besides, every incarnation of the WoD series from what I have seen has a way to divide the same monster into multiple different archetypes and categories. A vampire can be seductive, terrifying, dominating or elusive. Changelings represent dreams, and Beasts represent nightmares. So with that in mind, it's not the family that's important, it's what your character represents that determines the Hunger you should choose for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, the Anikem Punisher. Maybe they embody the sense of guilt weighing a person down and messing up their ability to stay focused or make rational decisions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or an Eshmaki Tyrant. Perhaps they embody the sense of paranoia. The constant fear that once somebody makes it to the top, everyone is jealous and plotting their downfall. They can't trust anybody, so they're alone in the world!<br /> <br /> <br /> And for my final example, a Namtaru Hoarder. They might embody the desire to mask one's physical imperfections by amassing great wealth. Look at Hugh Hefner, he's a wrinkly old man, yet because of his wealth he's got countless naked women clinging to him.<br /> <br /> <br /> It all comes down to your imagination. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:55:16-07:00","id":486957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486852#post486852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very same. Anakim Tyrants seem like a natural fit, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you kidding? THe ones with the secrets are king, these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T19:03:22-07:00","id":486960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486648#post486648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: my ideal Beast would be an Acid Rainer. So, Ugallu with a Hunger for Punishment. Thinking of being a Dirigible Pilot by day, Radical Environmentalist by night. Wonder if some of the higher level Atavisms will allow for poisons, or flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Ruin instead.<br /> <br /> Also, any hints on what elements of Lair design the character can control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T20:11:54-07:00","id":486976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486957#post486957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you kidding? THe ones with the secrets are king, these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am in fact completely serious when I suggest that the Nightmares of Powerlessness are an obvious fit for the guys who Hunger For Power.<br /> <br /> <br /> It could be the sample Lurker skewing my perspective, but it seems like the Eshmaki archetype suits itself most to the Nemeses \u2014 there's overlap with the Ugallu by way of the fear of being watched, but one of the things that makes breaking the taboo worth reconsidering is the threat of retribution even in the face of no obvious witnesses. Am I far off the mark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T20:18:36-07:00","id":486981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486960#post486960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Ruin instead.<br /> <br /> Also, any hints on what elements of Lair design the character can control?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I said previously, the lair will include a Heart and Chambers, but the info I came across didn't go into further detail. It did, however, state that multiple Beasts can share the same Lair, and that a Beast can not assume their full monster form <i>outside</i> of their Lair. Which leads me to believe these lairs can be labyrinthine is size and a place where the Beasts are at their most powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:57:58-07:00","id":487043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486981#post486981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said previously, the lair will include a Heart and Chambers, but the info I came across didn't go into further detail. It did, however, state that multiple Beasts can share the same Lair, and that a Beast can not assume their full monster form <i>outside</i> of their Lair. Which leads me to believe these lairs can be labyrinthine is size and a place where the Beasts are at their most powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope that it can be shaped to fit whatever a player wishes, as far as what's thematic for the character. I know I'd like an oubliette of clouds and freefall, with few, if any tangible features, and the option to shape a few, as needed, for my allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:56:06-07:00","id":487074,"title":"","content":"Found an interesting documentation about Family and Hunger. Didn't know that Beast is based on historical figures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5l7KbMVdN7E&amp;feature=player_detailpage#t=54\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5l7KbMVdN7E&amp;feature=player_detailpage#t=54\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"u