2858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T06:07:07-07:00","id":487212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487043#post487043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just hope that it can be shaped to fit whatever a player wishes, as far as what's thematic for the character. I know I'd like an oubliette of clouds and freefall, with few, if any tangible features, and the option to shape a few, as needed, for my allies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That may be possible, actually. It seems that Lairs will not exist on the physical plane, similar to Changelings and their Hallows.<br /> <br /> <br /> OH, I also found out that Beasts will have a collection of powers specifically geared towards interaction with other splats. Which means crossovers are encouraged! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT<br /> <br /> <br /> Atavism</b>: physical, based powers, apparently connected to your Beast's body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> ephemeral based powers, apparently connected to your Beast's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-21-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:43:21-07:00","id":487867,"title":"","content":"And innate kinship powers to sense, empower, and vicariously feed with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And advanced merits, so beasts have quite the grab bag of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:27:10-07:00","id":487911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487867#post487867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And innate kinship powers to sense, empower, and vicariously feed with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And advanced merits, so beasts have quite the grab bag of powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wonder since beast use kinship on other supernaturals do spirits and ghosts count among the supernaturals can they affect the smaller splats like immortals or slashers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:32:29-07:00","id":487913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487076#post487076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens when a Collector and a Mekhet get together.</div> </div> </div> </div>A polite but excited conversation over who has the biggest RPG collection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:47:44-07:00","id":487922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487911#post487911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wonder since beast use kinship on other supernaturals do spirits and ghosts count among the supernaturals can they affect the smaller splats like immortals or slashers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmm, well if the Mother was the first ever monster and Fae are considered to be relatives of the Children, I don't see why Spirits wouldn't be either. Ghosts, probably not, since they're lingering souls of mortals.<br /> <br /> This also brings up something I'm curious about<b></b>: how powerful are Beasts going to be compared to the other splats?<br /> <br /> When you're the descendant of a Kraken or a Frost Giant, you'd better have some top notch abilities compared to blood sucking corpses and half breed fairies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-21-2015, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:18:50-07:00","id":487949,"title":"","content":"Here's something:<br /> <br /> What Hunger, do you think, would a Beast who's appointed himself the guardian of the dead who helps them resolve their anchors have?<br /> <br /> My idea is that he collects anchors to store in his Lair (a church taking after the Manor of Sleep in Fatal Frame 3, it even comes with an Avernian Gate in the basement), but Hoard doesn't seem that fitting; an anchor is just a random item once the ghost has let go of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:27:57-07:00","id":487952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487949#post487949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something:<br /> <br /> What Hunger, do you think, would a Beast who's appointed himself the guardian of the dead who helps them resolve their anchors have?<br /> <br /> My idea is that he collects anchors to store in his Lair (a church taking after the Manor of Sleep in Fatal Frame 3, it even comes with an Avernian Gate in the basement), but Hoard doesn't seem that fitting; an anchor is just a random item once the ghost has let go of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassionate Ravager for the win?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:32:57-07:00","id":487954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487922#post487922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, well if the Mother was the first ever monster and Fae are considered to be relatives of the Children, I don't see why Spirits wouldn't be either. Ghosts, probably not, since they're lingering souls of mortals.<br /> <br /> This also brings up something I'm curious about<b></b>: how powerful are Beasts going to be compared to the other splats?<br /> <br /> When you're the descendant of a Kraken or a Frost Giant, you'd better have some top notch abilities compared to blood sucking corpses and half breed fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably between Lost and Created. Home-Field advantage, hidden strengths and whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:41:42-07:00","id":487974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487949#post487949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an anchor is just a random item once the ghost has let go of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a backwards way of looking at it, particularly given that the example Anakim appears to be a safe-cracker who collects <i>the wreckage of safes</i>.<br /> <br /> History matters, especially to supernatural beings in the World of Darkness. Remember that the Tooth Fairy of Discworld has built an empire on collecting what are effectively just little bits of outgrown bone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T22:32:44-07:00","id":487988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487949#post487949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something:<br /> <br /> What Hunger, do you think, would a Beast who's appointed himself the guardian of the dead who helps them resolve their anchors have?<br /> <br /> My idea is that he collects anchors to store in his Lair (a church taking after the Manor of Sleep in Fatal Frame 3, it even comes with an Avernian Gate in the basement), but Hoard doesn't seem that fitting; an anchor is just a random item once the ghost has let go of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Punisher. A lot of people don't die peacefully...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T22:37:15-07:00","id":487992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487954#post487954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably between Lost and Created. Home-Field advantage, hidden strengths and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It would be appropriate if the Children were on even terms with Mages, actually. The creatures who they are descended from didn't simply terrorize mortals, they clashed with the gods themselves. Then, of course, we have the popular stories of monsters who were so powerful the only way to defeat them was to banish them to magical prisons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Damn this has a lot of interesting possibilities!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T22:46:11-07:00","id":487997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487988#post487988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punisher.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term is Nemesis. Which, as Brick Top informs us, is\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A righteous infliction of retribution manifested by an appropriate agent. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T23:00:07-07:00","id":488001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487997#post487997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The term is Nemesis. Which, as Brick Top informs us, is\u2026<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry, haven't memorized them all yet. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T00:21:20-07:00","id":488046,"title":"","content":"Faintly embarrassed at not getting the Predators now, since looking back at the first blog entry there's a bit that basically runs down the list of Hungers in order:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A drive so strong they would do most anything to satisfy it, even if it costs friends, family, fame, or fortune in the process. That insatiable need to dominate, to possess, <b>to devour</b>, to punish, to destroy. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T04:25:30-07:00","id":488161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487911#post487911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wonder since beast use kinship on other supernaturals do spirits and ghosts count among the supernaturals can they affect the smaller splats like immortals or slashers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering all the major splats but demons count as kin, I believe that spirits don't normally count as kin unless they claim someone (since like demons they have no connection to humanity), ghosts and other minor supernatural beings probably do count.<br /> <br /> After all, Matt mentioned that Beast wasn't designed to require other gamelines, so that suggests to me that in a solely beast and blue book game that beasts would have kinship to scourges, revenants and ghosts, claimed, demon possessed, enfants, changing breeds, skinthieves, psychics, thaumaturges, immortals, dark heroes, infected, dreamers, doppelgangers, aswang, and those suffering from the hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-22-2015, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T07:54:35-07:00","id":488273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488161#post488161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering all the major splats but demons count as kin, I believe that spirits don't normally count as kin unless they claim someone (since like demons they have no connection to humanity), ghosts and other minor supernatural beings probably do count.<br /> <br /> After all, Matt mentioned that Beast wasn't designed to require other gamelines, so that suggests to me that in a solely beast and blue book game that beasts would have kinship to scourges, revenants and ghosts, claimed, demon possessed, enfants, changing breeds, skinthieves, psychics, thaumaturges, immortals, dark heroes, infected, dreamers, doppelgangers, aswang, and those suffering from the hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only things in the WoD (so far) that Beasts are explicitly *not* kin to are the Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:06:17-07:00","id":488279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488273#post488273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only things in the WoD (so far) that Beasts are explicitly *not* kin to are the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question then, would they consider Cryptds and Stigmatics kin? After all their gifts come from the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:12:35-07:00","id":488281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488273#post488273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only things in the WoD (so far) that Beasts are explicitly *not* kin to are the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, even normal humans? I've been really curious about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:21:17-07:00","id":488286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488281#post488281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, even normal humans? I've been really curious about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's just simple genetics. You have a human body after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:29:31-07:00","id":488290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=487992#post487992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be appropriate if the Children were on even terms with Mages, actually. The creatures who they are descended from didn't simply terrorize mortals, they clashed with the gods themselves. Then, of course, we have the popular stories of monsters who were so powerful the only way to defeat them was to banish them to magical prisons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Damn this has a lot of interesting possibilities!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to disagree. Granted, we have only seen a glimpse of what the Begotten are capable of, but what we have seen strikes me being more focused and linear than the broad, geometric growth inherent to the Forsaken and the Awakened. Deep powers, definitely, but I imagine basic fundamental control of the Elements or Causality, for example, will not be something your typical Beast will be capable of, at least, not at an early point in their character arc, or not in an all-encompassing fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:04:07-07:00","id":488417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=486887#post486887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their names are Thug and Violence, Darkness and Lurker, Isolation and No-one Can Hear You Scream. They are the Eshmaki. Don't bother running.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than any other, the Eshmaki are the terrors that are intimate - the ones the quote &quot;their habitation is even one with your guarded threshold&quot; were talking about.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Makara's habitation is the descent into the Underworld - it might be water rather than caves, but it's crushing, inimical, full of ancient secrets and ancient terrors. The Ugallu's habitation is vastness - the world you thought you knew opening in different directions, different vistas, different vantages, so you can never know what direction the terror will come from, or even that there is a terror until it's too late. (The Anakim aren't about habitations, unless it's &quot;go where the fuck they want because you can't stop them&quot; - and the Namtaru aren't really about habitations either).<br /> <br /> That's my takeanyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488161#post488161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, Matt mentioned that Beast wasn't designed to require other gamelines, so that suggests to me that in a solely beast and blue book game that beasts would have kinship to scourges, revenants and ghosts, claimed, demon possessed, enfants, changing breeds, skinthieves, psychics, thaumaturges, immortals, dark heroes, infected, dreamers, doppelgangers, aswang, and those suffering from the hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt said in the same post that Beast <i>did</i> require a certain amount of other supernatural weirdness to nose about in, which supports your point (adding that they're also interested in urban legends, mysterious places, and do on. I'm wondering if there's going to be a Dread Powers analogue in the game for assembling such things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:58:53-07:00","id":488555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488417#post488417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More than any other, the Eshmaki are the terrors that are intimate - the ones the quote &quot;their habitation is even one with your guarded threshold&quot; were talking about.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Makara's habitation is the descent into the Underworld - it might be water rather than caves, but it's crushing, inimical, full of ancient secrets and ancient terrors. The Ugallu's habitation is vastness - the world you thought you knew opening in different directions, different vistas, different vantages, so you can never know what direction the terror will come from, or even that there is a terror until it's too late. (The Anakim aren't about habitations, unless it's &quot;go where the fuck they want because you can't stop them&quot; - and the Namtaru aren't really about habitations either).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anakim's habitats are the places made to make you feel insignificant. Grand castles, imposing cathedrals, and ivy covered halls. You aren't worthy to be here, and you know it.<br /> <br /> The Namtaru's habitats are the places that make your skin crawl just thinking of them. Quarantine Zones, apartments overrun with vermin, the portapotties at Coachella. You'll never feel clean again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T13:47:18-07:00","id":488656,"title":"","content":"Matt,<br /> <br /> Hopefully you can answer my question about a character concept based upon your blog postings. Say I want to make a character who cuts his prey down mercilessly through words. This could either be in the form a lawyer verbally tearing his opponents defense to pieces or a hostage negotiator breaking down a gunmans desire to follow through with his deadly act. Would these concepts fit more under the Anakim or Eshmaki family? Also, do you think this would fit more under the hunger for prey, power, or punishment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5284-sanaelar","name":"Sanaelar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5284_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:30:27-07:00","id":488721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488286#post488286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's just simple genetics. You have a human body after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but Hunters I thought I read that Hunters aren't kin, even though they are humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:53:26-07:00","id":488809,"title":"","content":"I tend to toss out the rules and let ideas dominate as often as not. That's especially the case were I to think that the story that others want to roll with is going in the direction of awesome. Now, I suppose one could just make three vertical lists representing Hungers, Fears, and Families...assign a number to each and roll the dice to see who gets this particular Hunger-Fear-Family...but...hmm...I guess one could play out the hand s/he's dealt with and see where that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:37:28-07:00","id":488824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488721#post488721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but Hunters I thought I read that Hunters aren't kin, even though they are humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that that would be entirely dependent on the Endowment you're attempting to duplicate. Most of the item-based powers strike me as inappropriate for Kinship, while some of the blatantly supernatural abilities wouldn't bother me in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think a Hunter/Beast crossover could work, especially if the event that brings the group together is some variant of &quot;your princess is in another castle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:02:08-07:00","id":488845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488555#post488555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Anakim's habitats are the places made to make you feel insignificant. Grand castles, imposing cathedrals, and ivy covered halls. You aren't worthy to be here, and you know it.<br /> <br /> The Namtaru's habitats are the places that make your skin crawl just thinking of them. Quarantine Zones, apartments overrun with vermin, the portapotties at Coachella. You'll never feel clean again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lairs won't exist in the physical world, though. They're part of the dreamscape, as I understand it. However, they can be accessed by places that have a strong enough connection to the Lair itself. The door of a cathedral, for example, can be used as a gateway to access the Anakim's lair, but the actual lair itself could be a full fledged palace or subterranean kingdom. Besides, they need the breathing room, they have the soul of a Giant, after all!<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, the surface of the water might be the gateway to Leviathan's Lair, where those who go scooba diving find themselves exploring a bottomless lake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:26:52-07:00","id":488863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488721#post488721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but Hunters I thought I read that Hunters aren't kin, even though they are humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the rpgnet thread, it was mentioned that some endowments could be enhanced with that kinship feature, so apparently some hunters can count as kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488273#post488273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only things in the WoD (so far) that Beasts are explicitly *not* kin to are the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was just trying to extrapolate from there. If it was just a matter of being made by the god-machine, and the god-machine has no connection to the dark mother, well if the principle is another god-machine (which is an option) why would the dark mother have any connection to that god-machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-22-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:47:37-07:00","id":488880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488824#post488824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that that would be entirely dependent on the Endowment you're attempting to duplicate. Most of the item-based powers strike me as inappropriate for Kinship, while some of the blatantly supernatural abilities wouldn't bother me in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think a Hunter/Beast crossover could work, especially if the event that brings the group together is some variant of &quot;your princess is in another castle.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Endowment part which makes me suspect it isn't about humans being kin, since that would include an organization of people descended from demons (which provides a more obvious link to a Dark Mother).<br /> <br /> But yeah, there are a lot of possibilities for a Hunter/Beast crossover!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:54:05-07:00","id":488885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488863#post488863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just trying to extrapolate from there. If it was just a matter of being made by the god-machine, and the god-machine has no connection to the dark mother, well if the principle is another god-machine (which is an option) why would the dark mother have any connection to that god-machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do remember that the Unchained effectively become what they are due to an angel's momentary decision to <i>deny the reason for their existence.</i> The Unchained are a bunch of different families of one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:43:53-07:00","id":488919,"title":"","content":"I'm anxious to see what kind of monsters the Beasts can be descended from, or if they take the Changeling route and leave it up to the player's imagination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I want a leviathan ooze monster who's Atavisms let him consume people through bodily contact, i.e absorbtion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:48:55-07:00","id":488942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488885#post488885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do remember that the Unchained effectively become what they are due to an angel's momentary decision to <i>deny the reason for their existence.</i> The Unchained are a bunch of different families of one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except as far as we know, a beast could run into the The Thief and still feel kinship with him despite the possibility that he's the only thief that's ever existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:26:45-07:00","id":488980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488863#post488863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just trying to extrapolate from there. If it was just a matter of being made by the god-machine, and the god-machine has no connection to the dark mother, well if the principle is another god-machine (which is an option) why would the dark mother have any connection to that god-machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Principle has nothing to do with the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> Easiest answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:27:23-07:00","id":488981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488942#post488942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except as far as we know, a beast could run into the The Thief and still feel kinship with him despite the possibility that he's the only thief that's ever existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odds are low that even the solitary version of the Thief exists because something else decided to <i>stop</i> existing and now only possesses metaphysical reality due to its own declaration of ego. You're trying to argue this when the Begotten claim family ties to <i>the Created.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:48:26-07:00","id":489460,"title":"","content":"We've got Nightmares!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastnightmares/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastnightmares/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Nightmares &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastnightmares/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastnightmares/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Interesting, if a bit bare bones seeming. I also like the naming conventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:00:44-07:00","id":489492,"title":"","content":"These are very, very powerful, especially the enhanced versions. Are there any limitations on how often a Beast can use NIghtmares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:10:29-07:00","id":489497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489492#post489492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are very, very powerful, especially the enhanced versions. Are there any limitations on how often a Beast can use NIghtmares?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't actually see them as all that powerful. They're potent, sure, but not to the point that I read them and go, &quot;now <i>hold on</i>.&quot; What concerns you specifically? <br /> <br /> Also, there's no particular limit to how often they can used; by default they last a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:39:52-07:00","id":489520,"title":"","content":"Now, what Nightmares to give my flying jellyfish? I'm hoping for something involving falling, being eaten alive/dissolved, or rag-dolled by something big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:19:07-07:00","id":489572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489492#post489492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are very, very powerful, especially the enhanced versions. Are there any limitations on how often a Beast can use NIghtmares?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the hard fuel cap of 10 will be the big balancing factor. That, and as near as I can tell, these are mostly Pass/Fail powers.<br /> <br /> Also, Matt, will the cutoff for High/Low Satiety be 8/3 like Harmony? Also, will there be mandatory feeding or spending Breaking Points at or above/below those levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:28:50-07:00","id":489579,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> Would a Mage Kinship Nightmare be, say, You Don't Know What's Going On? Would a Werewolf one be You Are Small And Weak?<br /> <br /> Love the very concept, and the previously unseen role Beasts have of being debuffers; fits with the Nightmare aspect (also, Your Teeth Are Falling Out fits with my guy, he temporarily makes his targets suffer the effects of extreme age; the Son of Charon has a fitting power). I'll assume that Atavisms, likewise, are self-buffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:41:56-07:00","id":489606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489497#post489497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually see them as all that powerful. They're potent, sure, but not to the point that I read them and go, &quot;now <i>hold on</i>.&quot; What concerns you specifically? <br /> <br /> Also, there's no particular limit to how often they can used; by default they last a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the only thing that stood out and caused a &quot;now wait a second&quot; was the <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satiety Expenditure: The player may spend multiple Satiety on this effect. For every Satiety spent, the Beast may reflexively cause the victim to fail a single Physical action. </div> </div> </div>. It is not that it is overpowered, just that I am trying to recall anytime you can ever guarantee a failure, as there always is a chance die for most basic actions. Even if mechanically an action would be doomed (like trying to punch an Archmage with Mage armor in 1e) you could still attempt it, and gods willing, there was a 1 in a million chance for success.<br /> <br /> Note, I could be wrong in my recollection. It just was the first time I have ever seen an ability with those conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:46:52-07:00","id":489612,"title":"","content":"Heh, kinship nightmare, They Keep Bringing Up Dicks.<br /> <br /> More relevant than it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:16:31-07:00","id":489630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489572#post489572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the hard fuel cap of 10 will be the big balancing factor. That, and as near as I can tell, these are mostly Pass/Fail powers.<br /> <br /> Also, Matt, will the cutoff for High/Low Satiety be 8/3 like Harmony? Also, will there be mandatory feeding or spending Breaking Points at or above/below those levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Low Satiety is 1-3, high is 7-9 (10 is...a problem. Eat to live, don't live to eat). <br /> <br /> Mandatory feeding does happen. Breaking points aren't something Beasts have to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:33:06-07:00","id":489695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488845#post488845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lairs won't exist in the physical world, though. They're part of the dreamscape, as I understand it. However, they can be accessed by places that have a strong enough connection to the Lair itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the talk of habitations was more about illustrating the Families than anything literal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:21:15-07:00","id":489775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489612#post489612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, kinship nightmare, They Keep Bringing Up Dicks.<br /> <br /> More relevant than it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the need to ask..... who or what is this kinship power derived from? I feel like I'm missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:27:52-07:00","id":489779,"title":"","content":"It's a reference to a game I ran where, for some reason, this kept happening*. Alternatively, it's the only explanation for Utena you need. Alternatively, kinship with Hellblazer's Fuckpig.<br /> <br /> All three make me chuckle, for various reasons and with various intensity.<br /> <br /> *Weirdest part was that it started off with none of us trying for it**. Once the inevitable became clear, we ran with it. Still not as weird or as bad as the game of Don't Rest Your Head we killed the president in.<br /> **Though it must be noted that I am, at all times, something of an immature git. Fart jokes are still funny to me on occasion, for Pete's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-23-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T14:46:28-07:00","id":489878,"title":"","content":"Wondering if an Inventive Beast could be... Abit well OTT with Kin Nightmares Maybe mixing 2 or more &quot;Kin Types&quot; into one Nightmare say Vampire and Werewolves... &quot;You are Prey regardless of which Jungle&quot; Although they probably already have one like that. Or say a Mage/Changeling one &quot;The Hounds are Coming, Trust me I know&quot;<br /> <br /> I Suspect it could get messy if they can though... Then again, Maybe not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:10:41-07:00","id":489973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489878#post489878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wondering if an Inventive Beast could be... Abit well OTT with Kin Nightmares Maybe mixing 2 or more &quot;Kin Types&quot; into one Nightmare say Vampire and Werewolves... &quot;You are Prey regardless of which Jungle&quot; Although they probably already have one like that. Or say a Mage/Changeling one &quot;The Hounds are Coming, Trust me I know&quot;<br /> <br /> I Suspect it could get messy if they can though... Then again, Maybe not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I'd never allow Kinship Nightmares at Character Creation, IDC how you try to justify knowing NPCs from every major splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:27:52-07:00","id":490001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=489973#post489973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I'd never allow Kinship Nightmares at Character Creation, IDC how you try to justify knowing NPCs from every major splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never would on Character Creation.. Mostly because too me I'd want too See what powers the others have and theme them based on those that I'm with.<br /> Also.. It'd be too Easy too Make shit up in Creation &quot;I Know a Werewolf and a Vampire and a Changeling and a Mummy......&quot; Yeah. No. Unless your doing that with Merit Points.... No. and even then No MAYBE with one person but not with all of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:32:49-07:00","id":490082,"title":"","content":"Maybe if you knew them prior to becoming a Beast or if you met them shortly afterward. But a new Beast fresh out of char gen isn't going to know the whereabouts of all the supernaturals in the city, much less be on good terms with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, I'd say a good kinship Nightmare for an Anakim + Werewolf would be &quot;You are Domesticated&quot; in which the Beast form-locks their victim into their human state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:42:23-07:00","id":490087,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, anyone think up any ideas they want to see if they can work into Kinships? I've got a couple for Prometheans.<br /> <br /> \u2022You Are A Object(Golem/Unfleshed, whichever is appropriate in 2e): Makes the target subject of a form of the lineage's Disquiet, causing others to treat them like things, and attempt to &quot;own&quot; them at all costs.<br /> <br /> \u2022Do You Hear The Walls Thinning?(Ulgan): A targeted version of the Ulgan Wasteland, damaging the Gauntlet in a local area.<br /> <br /> \u2022You Are The Outsider(General): Makes the target the subject of a general Disquiet-like effect, making everyone hate and distrust them.<br /> <br /> \u2022You Can't Drink Lightning?(General): Protects the user from electric damage, and can even heal them at a cost.<br /> <br /> \u2022You Can't Control Yourself(Any Lineage): Less of a Nightmare in and of itself and more of a vague template, the idea is that it forces the target to experence the Torment of a particular Lineage. For example, the one that inflicts the Torment that belonged to the Tammuz in first edition might be called &quot;You Aren't Going To Take That, Are You?&quot;, while the Galateid version might be &quot;Tell Me I'm Pretty!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:03:23-07:00","id":490095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490087#post490087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, anyone think up any ideas they want to see if they can work into Kinships?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We Need a Donor (Vampire): The subject is placed under the delusion that they are severely ill and require a blood transfusion to stay healthy. Doctors may refuse to give such treatment to a &quot;healthy&quot; patient, driving them to further desperation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fever Dream (Changeling): The subject is assaulted by wild, incoherent hallucinations that drives them into a disoriented state. Can possibly inflict the subject with a temporary Derangement!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How did That Get Here? (Mage): The user has the ability to conceal an object or objects small enough to fit in their hands from the senses of others. Unless a thorough inspection is performed or the inspector knows what they're looking for, their minds will be tricked into ignoring the object(s) during a search. The objects can not be concealed while they are in use, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Naked in Public (Werewolf): The victim feels as if they are wearing little or even no protection and this carries over into battle as well. Naked in Public allows their attackers to bypass the armor rating of the victim. The amount of armor that can be ignored depends upon the successes rolled. Only mundane armor (i.e clothing) is affected by this Nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-23-2015, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:08:30-07:00","id":490096,"title":"","content":"a good one for Mummy kinship (I intend Batman to have learned this during his time with ra's al ghul)... You Have Been Judged--the victim rolls for their relative integrity stat. they dont risk losing a point, but if they suceed, fail, or dramatically fail, they take a condition as normal without risking any dots. the high satiety version might cost wp points, while the fueled version might force them to actually risk integrity facing their judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:08:43-07:00","id":490097,"title":"","content":"As it is, knowing other creatures at chargen is a player/ST decision. I didn't want to represent it with Merit because that felt cheesy to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:16:50-07:00","id":490102,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine at, chargen, the only Kinships that could be feasible would be Ghost or Spirit. For one, it let's you use Numina as a guide. For two, its relatively easy to justify.. like.. &quot;after my Homecoming, I started seeing my dead grandma/sister/wife, etc.&quot; Or &quot;a spirit was attracted to my Primordial nature. It hungered for what I hungered for, its Family is my Family&quot;. That way, there's no assumption of having other books. Its 100% core compatible. And it kinda is a startup with the whole.. &quot;demons and angels aren't kin&quot; right off the bat, as angels (also in the core) arent available as kin .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:35:37-07:00","id":490110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490087#post490087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, anyone think up any ideas they want to see if they can work into Kinships? I've got a couple for Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine:<br /> <br /> You've Been Living A Lie (Mage): The world suddenly seems a lot stranger, and you realize that feeling that someone's been using you is there because, well, someone's been using you. You don't know who or what to trust anymore, you've become aware of the fact your senses are being deceived every hour of every day. The target gains the Maddened Condition, with a stimulus chosen by the Beast as its trigger.<br /> <br /> Someone Else Is Controlling Your Body (Deceived): The implication of certain advanced physics, namely the fact that everything that can happen has happened, forces itself on your mind. You are a product of random chance and things that have already happened, your free will is simply an idle illusion you came up with because you can't quantify the full majesty of the cosmos. The target becomes easily suggestable and obedient, opening the first two Doors of any Social Manuvering attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T19:17:27-07:00","id":490132,"title":"","content":"As basic ideas: 'Your Thoughts Betray You' (Mastigos Mage, Mekhet Vampire, essentially any supernatural with a form of mind reading.), causing the victim's mind to become as though an open book to the Beast; 'Your Flesh Is Wrong' (Legion Scelesti), inflicting severe and otherworldly body dysphoria on the victim; and 'No Masks For You' (Strix), stripping all disguises and facades of civility and selflessness from a victim.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:00:14-07:00","id":490146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490102#post490102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it kinda is a startup with the whole.. &quot;demons and angels aren't kin&quot; right off the bat, as angels (also in the core) arent available as kin .</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I've missed something, there hasn't been anything said about angels or the Machine not being kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:00:27-07:00","id":490147,"title":"","content":"This one is actually pretty similar to Lelial's, but I had just read parts of the Slasher book and couldn't resist.<br /> <br /> 'You Know You Want To' (Slasher, Maniac) - You know you shouldn't be listening to the guy telling you what a good idea it is to kill your neighbor, but it just makes so much sense. His dog does keep peeing on your rosebush, and you did warn him there would be hell to pay. He's right, a man is only as good as his word. Time to get the lighter fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:12:20-07:00","id":490157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490146#post490146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I've missed something, there hasn't been anything said about angels or the Machine not being kin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Matt mentions it in a comment on the Nightmares blog post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:36:06-07:00","id":490164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490087#post490087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, anyone think up any ideas they want to see if they can work into Kinships?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Life Means Nothing (Mummy): The target feels the crushing weight of his own mortality, inflicting him with either a deep depression or a sudden desperate need for religion.<br /> <br /> You Hear Voices (Sin-Eater): The target can hear the gibbering moans of the dead, driving her batty and keeping her from concentrating.<br /> <br /> No One Appreciates Your Hard Work (Wizened): For the duration, people overlook the target, treating them at best as hired help, at worst as a member of an undesirable caste.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:00:06-07:00","id":490171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490087#post490087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, anyone think up any ideas they want to see if they can work into Kinships?</div> </div> </div> </div>You Don't Know Your Own Strength (Obrymos/Frankenstein/Ogre/Iron Masters): tools and objects malfunction in the target's hands.<br /> <br /> Your Face is not Your Own (Frankenstein/Nosferatu/Thyrsus): the target can't recognize themselves.<br /> <br /> Your Gold is Lead (Changing Breeds/Acanthus/Moros): the target loses what value they hold for an object.<br /> <br /> Your Shadow Betrays You (Moros/Mekhet/Nosferatu): Stealth and Subterfuge attempts against the Beast are difficult.<br /> <br /> You Can't Touch Him (Daeva/Darkling/Acanthus/Mastigos): attempts to grapple or touch the Beast are severely penalized.<br /> <br /> You are Surrounded (Daeva/Mastigos): the target sees the Beast everywhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:12:12-07:00","id":490177,"title":"","content":"Here are some water based ideas for possible Leviathans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Deep Blue (Nosferatu):</b> The victim feels as if they are cast adrift upon the waves and begins to suffer a panic attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wave of Anger (Werewolf):</b> The Beast can provoke violent reactions in others by projecting feelings of hatred, anger and destruction into their minds. If successful, the victim will immediately begin attacking everything in sight, starting with the last target who upset them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gloomy Downpour (Darkling):</b> the subject is instilled with feelings of apathy and sorrow, temporarily gaining the Depression derangement or upgrading it to the severe version if they already have it. Additionally, their body feels heavy, as if something is pressing down against it for the rest of the duration, imparting a -2 penalty to Strength.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T22:21:29-07:00","id":490212,"title":"","content":"So I'm a little confused by what one of the nightmares in the update actually does. &quot;All Your Teeth Fall Out&quot; says at high satiety normal successes only generate a single success and exceptional successes generate 2. I'm a bit confused does this mean if I had a dice pool of 5 and I rolled 4 normal successes then I would only get 1 success, or am I remembering terms incorrectly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:42:13-07:00","id":490285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=488161#post488161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering all the major splats but demons count as kin, I believe that spirits don't normally count as kin unless they claim someone (since like demons they have no connection to humanity), ghosts and other minor supernatural beings probably do count.<br /> <br /> After all, Matt mentioned that Beast wasn't designed to require other gamelines, so that suggests to me that in a solely beast and blue book game that beasts would have kinship to scourges, revenants and ghosts, claimed, demon possessed, enfants, changing breeds, skinthieves, psychics, thaumaturges, immortals, dark heroes, infected, dreamers, doppelgangers, aswang, and those suffering from the hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thieves, liars, pirates, maniacs, Methodists, serial killers, rustlers, cut throats, murderers, bounty hunters, desperados, mugs, pugs, thugs, nitwits, halfwits, dimwits, vipers, snipers, con men, Indian agents, Mexican bandits, muggers, buggerers, bushwhackers, hornswogglers, horse thieves, trekkies, trekkers, and simple carnival folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:39:12-07:00","id":490540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490212#post490212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm a little confused by what one of the nightmares in the update actually does. &quot;All Your Teeth Fall Out&quot; says at high satiety normal successes only generate a single success and exceptional successes generate 2. I'm a bit confused does this mean if I had a dice pool of 5 and I rolled 4 normal successes then I would only get 1 success, or am I remembering terms incorrectly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpreted it as meaning that, at Satiety 7+, the disfigurement caused by the power is so extreme that it makes Physical actions next to impossible for the <u>target</u>, exactly the way you say above. Since at a minimum, your Target's Physical pool is down 2 dice, odds are that at High Satiety, they are never rolling more than 1 success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:56:53-07:00","id":490554,"title":"","content":"@StSword: Chatter has indicated that spirits count for kinship, so I'm inclined to believe it's literally just anything from your friendly neighborhood God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T08:40:52-07:00","id":490599,"title":"","content":"<b>One, two, Beasties coming for you</b>(Slashers in general) The victim suffers from &quot;delusions&quot; that the Beast is in someway an unstoppable killing machine with a massive hate on for the victim. Said victim drives themselves crazy trying to &quot;escape&quot; the &quot;rampage&quot;. High Satiety makes the Victim do stupid things like go off alone, smoke weed/have sex when they know you're around, not actually leave the dangerous place. Burning Satiety prevents them from calling the police, and makes them forget to double tap if they find themselves actually fighting the beast and manage to incapacitate it.<br /> <br /> <b>You talkin Shit about me?</b>(Legend) The beast can place the &quot;eavesdropped on&quot; condition on a number of victims. Until the condition is resolved the Beast is automatically aware if any of the victims are talking about them, and the nature of the conversation. At High Satiety the Beast recalls the conversations held about it word for word and if mortal victims believe it posses certain powers it can save that conversation in it's memory and use it to develop further nightmares based on those stories. For a point of Satiety, the Beast may instinctively know the fastest routes and best time to approach the target.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm the Juggernaut, Bitch(</b>Mask) A victim of this power has their perceptions altered so as to perceive the Beast as an unstoppable juggernaut-bullets that in truth missed the beast are perceived as bouncing off, injuries and signs of exhaustion are not apparent, and the victim in general perceives the beast as being much bigger and stronger than they are in truth.<br /> <br /> <b>The Man in the Mirror...And on the sidewalk.</b>(Mutant) The victim perceives themselves and everyone they meet as being cursed with vile and hideous deformities.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm in your head</b>(Maniac) The Beast marks a single victim and ads their legend to all rolls to read that person or predict their actions. At high satiety the beast can also predict with actions of that personals allies based on their reading of the victim, but on;y with a half legend(rounded down) bonus. For a pint as Satiety, the beast can add their total satiety to their bonus(or half satiety if they're at high satiety already)<br /> <br /> I couldn't think of one for Psychos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:11:38-07:00","id":490655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/47890-god-machine-rules?p=49059#post49059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't think of one for Psychos.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>You Can't Live Without Me: </b>The Target is treated as being under the effects of the Swooning condition in the presence of the Beast; Beaten Down around others. High Satiety inflicts the Addiction and Lethargic conditions, respectively. Spend Satiety to drain Willpower from the target and recover your own on a 1:1 rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:19:08-07:00","id":490659,"title":"","content":"Here are some nightmares based on dreams I've actually had! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Paralyzing Fear (General):</b> The victim perceives themselves to be moving in slow motion. Their movements become sluggish and easy to read. This Nightmare has a greater chance of taking hold if the victim is confronted with a phobia of theirs!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backseat Driver (Spirits):</b> The victim loses partial or even total control of their bodily functions, yet remains conscious of their actions. For the rest of the duration, the Beast is able to perform a contested roll to telepathically influence the victim's movements each round. On an exceptional success, the Beast gains full control over the victim's movements for the rest of the duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Your Friends Don't Care (Changeling):</b> A power that is as cruel as it is disturbing. With this Nightmare, the Beast is able to compel the victim's allies to refuse aid no matter how much they beg, scream and plead. The Beast supplants the victim with a subtle aura that causes those around the victim to feel apathy and disinterest, even when the victim is being attacked right before their eyes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T13:28:38-07:00","id":490884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=490285#post490285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thieves, liars, pirates, maniacs, Methodists, serial killers, rustlers, cut throats, murderers, bounty hunters, desperados, mugs, pugs, thugs, nitwits, halfwits, dimwits, vipers, snipers, con men, Indian agents, Mexican bandits, muggers, buggerers, bushwhackers, hornswogglers, horse thieves, trekkies, trekkers, and simple carnival folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was beautiful, man!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T14:56:58-07:00","id":490979,"title":"","content":"<b>Shadow Slayer (Werewolf):</b> The target becomes a an unnatural predator, his body attuned to the Shadow. If spirits dream, the target has become their worst nightmare. The target's unarmed attacks deal lethal damage to the corpus of spirits. On an exceptional success, the target deals <i>aggravated</i> damage against spirits with their unarmed attacks, as if by the spirit's bane.<br /> <br /> Not all the Nightmares need to be negative, now do they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:40:47-07:00","id":491003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbc