ling she'd be. As for Beast, its harder to pinpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T21:40:26-07:00","id":491274,"title":"","content":"Almost like a recurring nightmare...<br /> <br /> Embrace your Lair, Arc; only then will it end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T21:46:37-07:00","id":491277,"title":"","content":"I embraced my Soul and all I got was this lousy t-shirt.<br /> <br /> Which turned out to be an Astral symbol for illness, so all I really got for my trouble was, well, sick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but it's pretty easy to guess what kind of Changeling she'd be. As for Beast, its harder to pinpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) If you inadvertently resurrect <i>that </i>nightmare, I will be cross. Which means I'll pout. And that's it.<br /> <br /> 2) You'd have thought it was, but we were having to argue against WyrdHamster* and [Sanguine Information], so it was....<br /> <br /> ...well, a recurring nightmare, yes.<br /> <br /> *I'm dogging on then Wyrd, not now Wyrd, to clarify, and I mean that sincerely. Looking at the threads in question, I am now impressed how more on the nose his...questions are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T06:31:39-07:00","id":491600,"title":"","content":"So far, based on very limited information about Nightmares, it seems they are very other-focused powers. That is, you have to have a target. So if the problem can be solved by fucking with someone, you're golden. Need to sneak into the museum? Sure, the guard is too busy arguing with his dead mother to really stop you. Firefight at the warehouse? Let see them find their way out of a burning labyrinth. On the other hand, it seems that if it's a physical obstacle, they aren't going to help you much. So it's not very effective against the security cameras, and if that warehouse is actually on fire, it's likely not going to help you escape. You can't make a rock think it's teeth are falling out.<br /> <br /> So I'd think that if you need to surpass a physical obstacle, like a locked door or a wall to climb, or if you need to affect yourself with a power, you need an Atavism. So when that Hero snipes you from half a mile a way and you are now bleeding to death, you may need an Atavism to get over there and make him regret that decision. This is why you never leave your cave, younglings.<br /> <br /> I think a good source of Nightmare inspirations would come from the Silent Hill series. I also like to use monsters from that series as inspiration for Pandorans, so I think I might allow a crossover Nightmare that awakens all the local Pandorans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:37:55-07:00","id":491907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=491277#post491277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If you inadvertently resurrect <i>that </i>nightmare, I will be cross. Which means I'll pout. And that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alice could work as Begotten in the same way as you can recreate Dracula, Werewolf of London or Frankenstein Monster as one of them. <b>BtP</b> setting seems so open to let you emulate almost any kind of monster our popculture can ran in to. I would put Demonic Alice as the Anakim ( she looks higher, more bloody, really scary with horns in &quot;direct&quot; and &quot;confrontional&quot; kind of way ) and maybe Hunger for Power - she becomes real Tyrant in Wonderland, ending the reign of Queen of Hearts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=491277#post491277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) You'd have thought it was, but we were having to argue against WyrdHamster* and [Sanguine Information], so it was....<br /> <br /> ...well, a recurring nightmare, yes.<br /> <br /> *I'm dogging on then Wyrd, not now Wyrd, to clarify, and I mean that sincerely. Looking at the threads in question, I am now impressed how more on the nose his...questions are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I do not remeber any of this. Beside you got some weird convictions about me, lately. Maybe we should not dwell in to it more, if you are more cool with mine Internet persona...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T14:54:50-07:00","id":491966,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd peg her as a Makara. During the Mcgee games, Alice doesn't really come across as being helpless, as she takes it upon herself to explore the depths of her own mind and confront the source of her insanity. There's also a heavy focus on forgetting the past and what really happened to her family, which is something the Makara also embody, knowledge lost to time. Alice resides in the sea, the Sea of Madness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dracula would be an Eshmaki obviously. Betrayed by his own subjects, forsaken by God, he has 3 wives and still wants to make Mina Harker into his lover. And, of course the monsters he brainwashes into servitude. Clearly Dracula has abandonment issues!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:39:08-07:00","id":492314,"title":"","content":"Castlevania Dracula, though, is a pretty clear Anakim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:44:57-07:00","id":492316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=492314#post492314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castlevania Dracula, though, is a pretty clear Anakim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for clarity's sake, are we assuming the title character is his Soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:02:54-07:00","id":492333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=492316#post492316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just for clarity's sake, are we assuming the title character is his Soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely. Odd case where it comes with his personality, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:18:09-07:00","id":493180,"title":"","content":"Reading through what's available currently. Here's my current chip-ins.<br /> <br /> Inspiration - Film &amp; Tv; Search for the Lost Giants - Two brothers seeks out the evidence of Giant skeletons. It's a step above Finding Bigfoot, when viewed under the lens of World of Darkness, two Heroic brothers are setting out to prove the existence of Giants and the Children.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1 opening Quote - Cause mama, Mama I'm coming home, Ozzie Osbourne","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:39:36-07:00","id":493190,"title":"","content":"Obviously, Kaiju flicks and more than a few Lovecraft films will make the cut. Soul Taker, Neo Ranga, and Evangelion also seem to have the right feel to me as do more than a few Beowulf adaptations.<br /> <br /> I wonder which Nightmares and Atavisms would be good for a Tarrasque.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:43:10-07:00","id":493253,"title":"","content":"I'll be disappointed if Sharktopus isn't a possibility in this game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:57:19-07:00","id":493262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=491966#post491966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd peg her as a Makara. During the Mcgee games, Alice doesn't really come across as being helpless, as she takes it upon herself to explore the depths of her own mind and confront the source of her insanity. There's also a heavy focus on forgetting the past and what really happened to her family, which is something the Makara also embody, knowledge lost to time. Alice resides in the sea, the Sea of Madness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dracula would be an Eshmaki obviously. Betrayed by his own subjects, forsaken by God, he has 3 wives and still wants to make Mina Harker into his lover. And, of course the monsters he brainwashes into servitude. Clearly Dracula has abandonment issues!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to arbitrarily argue against this, buuuuuuuuuut.<br /> <br /> Consider that in the beginning, and in fact for years, she <i>does</i> suffer dreams of powerlessness. The games are a transition point when she she begins overcoming her dreams and triumphs over them, taking in what her friends are saying and conquering her self-deception and despair.<br /> <br /> It's...a little worrisome. She could be an Anakim(fits her brutish fighting style), as she comes to terms with her trauma. She could also be a Hero, building an ego out of the affliction of her nightmare.<br /> <br /> Well, to be fair, I don't you can Self-Hero.<br /> <br /> Yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:13:37-07:00","id":493265,"title":"","content":"She's definitely a Beast; taking into account that in the first game, the Red Queen has her face. I can't think of a better confirmation than that! In the second game, the queen explains that the destruction of Wonderland is the destruction of Alice, and vice versa. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But yeah, first game suggests Anakim, second game suggests Leviathan. Tough call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:20:32-07:00","id":493268,"title":"","content":"I always favor the former to the latter, both for it's chronological importance and the simple fact it's a better story.<br /> <br /> Still, without Madness Returns, we wouldn't be able to get Otherlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T03:09:37-07:00","id":493407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=493268#post493268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always favor the former to the latter, both for it's chronological importance and the simple fact it's a better story.<br /> <br /> Still, without Madness Returns, we wouldn't be able to get Otherlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.. Madness Returns the Doctor/Dollmaker is a &quot;Hero&quot; using Psychology too destroy Alice's Lair, And the Game is her coming too Realise that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":".  Edit for Spelling 04-27-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T08:18:05-07:00","id":493650,"title":"","content":"So the first game is her Homecoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:23:38-07:00","id":493940,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of nightmares I've had and which Family they might correspond to, and it's taking a bit. I'm one who hasn't had a nightmare since I was young, so it's taking a bit to recall where to really go with them. First one that comes to mind is my house was covered in these huge blue flies with pink eyes. They kind of bounced around like an idle animation from a video game, left to right. They seemed to be laughing constantly. The thing that really horrified me was that if I were to squish them they'd explode in this impossibly sticky tar like substance, holding me to the walls.<br /> <br /> Next one is not really a full on nightmare in that it didn't leave me waking frightened so much as confused about my actions. Basic summary is Death came to me to be an undercover agent for the local spirits as a tutor for the young daughter of a new family in town, trying to turn her toward a more spiritually beneficial way of life. When she eventually told me my ideas of trying to help the spirits was silly and I should just take what I want without thought for anyone else I backhanded her skull in and walked out of the house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:43:08-07:00","id":493955,"title":"","content":"The only recurring nightmare I remember is one that I had a bunch of times when I was a kid. There was this big body of water with only a pale light shining over it all, but it was grainy like a noir film. Then something big began to rise unseen from beneath the water ... and I would wake up in varying stages of heightened alertness and tension. I never got to see what that thing was.<br /> <br /> So I am almost certainly a Makara of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:53:38-07:00","id":493965,"title":"","content":"Ooooh, I hope there's a nightmare that can inflict people with sleep paralysis. I've had that multiple times, and if you don't recognize what's going on, it's terrifying!<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's another nightmare I came up with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Puppet Master:</b> A less powerful version of Backseat Driver but one that is almost as terrifying. This nightmare gives the Beast the power to telekinetically manipulate humanoid constructs, specifically dolls or action figures.Puppet Master can not force a subject to move in a way that is physically impossible for them, which means statues are not controllable, and toys are limited by their plastic molds and joints. Still, the thought of your lifeless dolls turning into serial killers has traumatized adults and children alike!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-27-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T21:41:51-07:00","id":494357,"title":"","content":"Can someone help me with the Families? I mean, what really is the distinction between an Eshmaki and a Makara? I get some of the distinctions (sea and sky, hidden and hideous), but are there more subtle distinctions that I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T22:02:39-07:00","id":494375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494357#post494357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone help me with the Families? I mean, what really is the distinction between an Eshmaki and a Makara? I get some of the distinctions (sea and sky, hidden and hideous), but are there more subtle distinctions that I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it in overly simplistic terms, the Eshmaki are fear of the dark, whereas the Makara are fear of the deep.<br /> <br /> The foundation of the Lurkers isn't that you're going to be swallowed up by the tide, it's that your little boat has a murderous stowaway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:17:06-07:00","id":494636,"title":"","content":"I think how such things are defined will be an eye opener for many curious about the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:30:49-07:00","id":494777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494375#post494375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To put it in overly simplistic terms, the Eshmaki are fear of the dark, whereas the Makara are fear of the deep.<br /> <br /> The foundation of the Lurkers isn't that you're going to be swallowed up by the tide, it's that your little boat has a murderous stowaway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just seems pretty ambiguous to me; being 'swallowed up by the tide' strikes me as being as much about Powerlessness as the Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:56:29-07:00","id":494798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494636#post494636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think how such things are defined will be an eye opener for many curious about the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:42:33-07:00","id":494863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494777#post494777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems pretty ambiguous to me; being 'swallowed up by the tide' strikes me as being as much about Powerlessness as the Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tide can't get you unless you go to the sea; the kraken can't get you unless you go swimming or sailing (or hang around on docks, I suppose). The depths are symbolic of the doom you somewhat invite on yourself - you have to take a step into that world, probably in search of rewards (the lost secrets and treasures and so on), but the terrors get you instead. Cf the Ugallu who can strike at any time from an ever-present vantage, the Eshmaki who are already with you, and the Anakim who implacably come for you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:59:51-07:00","id":494976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494863#post494863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tide can't get you unless you go to the sea; the kraken can't get you unless you go swimming or sailing (or hang around on docks, I suppose). The depths are symbolic of the doom you somewhat invite on yourself - you have to take a step into that world, probably in search of rewards (the lost secrets and treasures and so on), but the terrors get you instead. Cf the Ugallu who can strike at any time from an ever-present vantage, the Eshmaki who are already with you, and the Anakim who implacably come for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an interesting way of looking at it. From that path of thought, the Makara are representative of taking a chance, even though you know it is risky, and losing. The primordial fear of water isn't necessarily the fear of not knowing what lies under the waves, but from knowing exactly what waits for you if you fall overboard, and attempting it anyways.<br /> <br /> Now I want to make a Makara who runs high stakes dice games, offering winners the opportunity for double or nothing with a devilish grin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:49:13-07:00","id":495063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=494976#post494976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I want to make a Makara who runs high stakes dice games, offering winners the opportunity for double or nothing with a devilish grin.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Now, friend, I know it seems like a lot to wager, but with your circumstances, you really can't afford to not take the plunge. You understand? Good! Now, care to shake a poor sinner's hand?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:33:15-07:00","id":495298,"title":"","content":"&quot;Anyone caug