ss/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498063#post498063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastatavisms/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/beastatavisms/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me think of the worm dude from <i>Buffy: the Vampire Slayer</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:47:17-07:00","id":498122,"title":"","content":"Am I only one to see some problems with &quot;Atavisms are not seen by humans&quot; rule? If spoiled <i>Infestation</i> power ( change in to hive of bugs ) is indication, characters can become <i>very</i> in-human in <b>actions</b>. Sadiety Expenditure can make so supernatural things that I cannot imagine <i>how</i> mortals cannot see them. Like in Infestation, with Expenditure, <b>your entire body disintegrates into a mass of insects or spiders, leaving his clothing and worldly possessions behind.</b> How can something like that be &quot;overlooked&quot; by mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2015, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:48:29-07:00","id":498124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=496942#post496942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, that's how I feel whenever I offer my players the choice to make a failure dramatic in exchange for a beat. They take the offer far more than they should.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish my players would do that. I have two that I can count on to take dramatic failures, but everyone else is hit-or-miss. I try to get them to embrace failure more often, but so far, no go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:00:33-07:00","id":498137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498122#post498122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I only one to see some problem with &quot;Atavisms are not seen by humans&quot; rule? If spoiled <i>Infestation</i> power ( change in to hive of bugs ) is indication, characters can become <i>very</i> in-human in <b>actions</b>. Sadiety Expenditure can make so supernatural things that I cannot imagine <i>how</i> mortals cannot see them. Like in Infestation, with Expenditure, <b>your entire body disintegrates into a mass of insects or spiders, leaving his clothing and worldly possessions behind.</b> How can something like that be &quot;overlooked&quot; by mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are completely misunderstanding what was explained in the post. If an Atavism activation has an obvious, otherwordly and nigtmarish effect, then a regular human will naturally see it - but that is all they will see, and they will likely not understand it. A supernaturally aware being, on the other hand, will <i>see the monster that is the Beast's Soul</i> as the power shows itself (even though they too may not understand what they're looking at, they certainly discern its true nature more clearly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atavisms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Beast can pass for human because his Atavisms are <b>typically subtle</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, bold is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-30-2015, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:03:30-07:00","id":498139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498137#post498137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are completely misunderstanding what was explained in the post. If an Atavism activation has an obvious, otherwordly or nightmarish effect, then a regular human will obviously see it - but that is all they will see, and they will likely not understand it. A supernaturally aware being, on the other hand, will <i>see the monster that is the Beast's Soul</i> as the power shows itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. In the example given to explain the perception issue, normal humans still see the character BREATHING FIRE, but those with supernatural perception see a DRAGON breathing fire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:12:15-07:00","id":498146,"title":"","content":"I feel like my explanation actually suffers a bit from departamental department of redundancy in its phrasing, but I am going to chalk that up to the fact it is very late right now.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure sleeping will come easy with the sample Atavism in mind though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:54:37-07:00","id":498248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498139#post498139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. In the example given to explain the perception issue, normal humans still see the character BREATHING FIRE, but those with supernatural perception see a DRAGON breathing fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to wonder if that reference of a dragon in New Zealand and Alaska (Hunter Core and Damnation City-Blurb about anchorage respectively) was a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:30:54-07:00","id":498272,"title":"","content":"I am now even more excited. Beast is looking good!<br /> <br /> Now not to push a cross-over questions, but it was kinda invited it with the mention of how Atavisms interact with other templates:<br /> Can a Mage use their Mage Sight to study a Beast and see what they are, even if the Beast isn\u2019t activating an Atavism? Maybe not reflexively, but in a similar manner to how a Mage studying a Changeling could potentially see past the Mask (not easy but with persistence they can get through)? The same question extends to Auspex or other supernatural abilities that let you investigate the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-01-2015, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T00:46:38-07:00","id":498463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498139#post498139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. In the example given to explain the perception issue, normal humans still see the character BREATHING FIRE, but those with supernatural perception see a DRAGON breathing fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in our Infestation Atavism example both humans will see men becoming hive of spiders, but supernaturl will see what else? They <i>literally</i> see spiders that are his Beast Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:30:30-07:00","id":498494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498122#post498122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I only one to see some problems with &quot;Atavisms are not seen by humans&quot; rule? If spoiled <i>Infestation</i> power ( change in to hive of bugs ) is indication, characters can become <i>very</i> in-human in <b>actions</b>. Sadiety Expenditure can make so supernatural things that I cannot imagine <i>how</i> mortals cannot see them. Like in Infestation, with Expenditure, <b>your entire body disintegrates into a mass of insects or spiders, leaving his clothing and worldly possessions behind.</b> How can something like that be &quot;overlooked&quot; by mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts apparently have to deal with a little thing called <b>Panic</b>.<br /> Which starts with a P.<br /> Which rhymes with D.<br /> And D stands for <b>Disquiet</b> (or Lunacy's twin, <b>Delusion</b>).<br /> <br /> I imagine that a prior to a Hero arising, there will be moments where mortal NPCs will get an inkling that something's not right. Probably at mid to high Satiety, this Panic will be mostly individual, and most of the time, the victim will forget, rationalize, or go a bit crazy. Rarely, they'll fully and clearly remember what they saw, start putting 2 and 2 together, and eventually, although not satisfying the Hunger exacerbates the process, that NPC goes Hero and starts stalking the Beast. There may even be a vector and compounding mechanic, but I can only speculate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, I might be reading too much into this \ud83d\ude1c.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-01-2015, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:37:05-07:00","id":498495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498463#post498463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in our Infestation Atavism example both humans will see men becoming hive of spiders, but supernaturl will see what else? They <i>literally</i> see spiders that are his Beast Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think that Beastial spiders are ever <i>just</i> spiders in the mundane sense - there's a difference between a giant squid and a <i>kraken</i>. So supernaturals will see the true primordial horror behind what the mortals see as 'merely' spiders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T03:07:51-07:00","id":498582,"title":"","content":"I must say I wasn't sure how I feel about Beast until now- but Atavism just won my heart. It sounds awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T04:10:56-07:00","id":498603,"title":"","content":"So a normal spider, but everyone gasps really loudly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T04:16:57-07:00","id":498605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498603#post498603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a normal spider, but everyone gasps really loudly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's quite fair. Because if it's a normal spider I will already be shrieking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T04:44:13-07:00","id":498620,"title":"","content":"Humans sees the Beast fall apart, dissolving into a swarm of black spiders, skittering towards them like a ravenous carpet as though they were a single amorphous being.<br /> And those with supernatural sensitivity also see the great, hairy, many legged aracnid with hungry eyes around a gaping maw, its chitinous carapace glistening like the abyss as light and warmth sink into it; the approach casting all into darkness as the swarm seems to walk forward in its shape.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine it's something like that, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-01-2015, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T04:51:54-07:00","id":498639,"title":"","content":"This is both glorious and horrifying; I can't wait to see more!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Eve used an Atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Remembered something 05-01-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:56:20-07:00","id":498744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=498620#post498620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans sees the Beast fall apart, dissolving into a swarm of black spiders, skittering towards them like a ravenous carpet as though they were a single amorphous being.<br /> And those with supernatural sensitivity also see the great, hairy, many legged aracnid with hungry eyes around a gaping maw, its chitinous carapace glistening like the abyss as light and warmth sink into it; the approach casting all into darkness as the swarm seems to walk forward in its shape.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine it's something like that, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> The supernatural folk I would think see an expression of the Beast's soul, even if symbolic. But likely terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:23:26-07:00","id":498755,"title":"","content":"Human: &quot;You Just Saw that guy Dissolve in a Tide of Spiders! Holy Shit.... It's Crawling towards you!&quot;<br /> Human with Sixth Sense: &quot;That.... Thing just Became a Swarm of 8-Legged Mosters with Hundreds of Eyes and A Bite that can strip Flesh, And it's Hungry.... So Hungry... Your Food&quot;<br /> Mage/Other Supernaturals: &quot;A Wave of energy from the Dreamlands indicates that this is his &quot;Real&quot; Form, Hundreds of Tiny Biting Abyssal Monsters that only JUST appear to be Spiders too your Senses. They are something MUCH Worse&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd Imagine it's something like that....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:40:04-07:00","id":498771,"title":"","content":"*eyes glinting*<br /> <i>Sees a small ocean wave in a night of glittering red stars. The stars reflected in the water...No! They are eyes! Ocean...sky? No horizon to see.</i><br /> <br /> Hmf...suitable for any swarm I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","cust