Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:02:41-07:00","id":506232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=506217#post506217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, there are an awful lot of Anakim, aren't there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well they embody the fear of being powerless. And against the Hulk, you're certainly outclassed in brute force!<br /> <br /> <br /> Amusingly enough, I would imagine that quite a few Anakim have the Nerd Rage from being weak and helpless prior to their inheritance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-06-2015, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T18:29:22-07:00","id":506296,"title":"","content":"I think they're also very... Main character-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:17:30-07:00","id":506357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=506296#post506296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're also very... Main character-y.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at it from Rosencrantz and Guildenstern's perspective.<br /> <br /> What could be more hopeless than facing down someone who the plot has decided at least deserves to die with meaning-and you're a completely random goon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:55:23-07:00","id":506368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=506357#post506357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take a look at it from Rosencrantz and Guildenstern's perspective.<br /> <br /> What could be more hopeless than facing down someone who the plot has decided at least deserves to die with meaning-and you're a completely random goon?</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I have an idea for an Anakim who represents the feeling of being a extra in your own life story. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T21:33:57-07:00","id":506387,"title":"","content":"I was talking to a player and hit upon an idea for a foster family led by a hoarder who was actually a lurker who hoarded everything... including children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T04:28:46-07:00","id":506604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=506357#post506357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take a look at it from Rosencrantz and Guildenstern's perspective.<br /> <br /> What could be more hopeless than facing down someone who the plot has decided at least deserves to die with meaning-and you're a completely random goon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't trying to suggest that Anakim can't be supporting or minor cast! There's just a very hero-like element to their themes, much moreso than the other Families (as far as I know, of course). Do you have a character who feels powerless, but later becomes powerful and triumphs? You might have an Anakim! Like Anakin, come to think of it.<br /> <br /> Edit: On further consideration, it may just be that the Hero's Journey is very power-oriented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","user":"Wasteful","date":". 05-07-2015, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T03:15:03-07:00","id":507898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=506088#post506088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He <i>does</i> want to be Hokage ...</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd go for collector for Naruto- Why does he play pranks, why does he seek to be hokage? So people will notice hiim.<br /> <br /> Why does he want people to notice him? To be his friend.<br /> <br /> So Naruto collects friends- hence his going all Misery on Sasuke. Collectors don't like it when they lose their stuff, even when it's their stuff having a mind of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T07:50:15-07:00","id":508029,"title":"","content":"Hmm As there seemingly wasn't an update this thursday and I saw no notice there: Will there be another update at all before the kickstarter goes live?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:21:05-07:00","id":508182,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Sasuke left the village and became evil because of forces outside of Sasuke's control.<br /> <br /> Magic tattoo that gives you power at cost of being mentally influenced to join a madman, that has part of said madman's soul in it, and will kill him if he doesn't go to said madman. Reciving said tatoo put his mind back on gaining power to get revenge after deciding to give it up, as well, proving mental influence.<br /> <br /> Then there was the mind rape.<br /> <br /> and the other lunatic that pushed his buttons in just the right way to turn him into a psychopathic pawn<br /> <br /> So it's not Naruto's toy leaving of his own accord. It's other people taking his toy from him. particularly since these people intended to abuse the toy for their own gain instead enjoying it on it's own merits. They'll never enjoy playing with the toy-never love it as much as he and his other toys will.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, this is fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:58:57-07:00","id":508230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=508182#post508182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that Sasuke left the village and became evil because of forces outside of Sasuke's control.<br /> <br /> Magic tattoo that gives you power at cost of being mentally influenced to join a madman, that has part of said madman's soul in it, and will kill him if he doesn't go to said madman. Reciving said tatoo put his mind back on gaining power to get revenge after deciding to give it up, as well, proving mental influence.<br /> <br /> Then there was the mind rape.<br /> <br /> and the other lunatic that pushed his buttons in just the right way to turn him into a psychopathic pawn<br /> <br /> So it's not Naruto's toy leaving of his own accord. It's other people taking his toy from him. particularly since these people intended to abuse the toy for their own gain instead enjoying it on it's own merits. They'll never enjoy playing with the toy-never love it as much as he and his other toys will.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, this is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Really, the tattoo put his mind back on revenge? You sure it wasn't the 72 hour mind rape of having his family slaughtered by his brother who snapped his arm and left him in a coma?<br /> <br /> The tattoo would have only killed Sasuke if he didn't use the Sound Four's method to achieve level 2. Left by itself, the mark would have progressed to stage 2 on its own, but he would have had no control over it, and thus his life energy would have been exhausted. Once he popped out of the barrel, there was no reason for him to go to Orochimaru except for him to learn more power. 2 and a half years later, he even treats Orochimaru like crap, and proceeds to kill him (or try to), so the mark had nothing to do with him leaving, he just wanted as much power as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the other lunatic pushing his buttons, all he did was give the backstory of the Uchiha. His family were planning to take over the village because they're saiyan-er-warriors. His brother was a &quot;pacifest&quot; (way to screw up the continuity, there, btw), and killed his entire family tree in order to save everybody else. Once he found out that the leaders of the village ordered his brother to wipe out his family, I don't think that qualifies as manipulation, that's a legit reason to hate them. Especially since there were a bunch of family members who had no idea about the plan and were just as innocent as Sasuke. (like I said, way to fuck up the continuity).<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> I could go on about my hatred for the &quot;plot&quot; of Shipuuden, but this is not the place for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:17:38-07:00","id":508253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=508230#post508230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Really, the tattoo put his mind back on revenge? You sure it wasn't the 72 hour mind rape of having his family slaughtered by his brother who snapped his arm and left him in a coma?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you would reread or rewatch the orest of Death Arc, Sasuke gave up on revenge when fightin Orochimaru, but imediatly started talking about using the curse mark's power to get his revenge when he woke up.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the other lunatic pushing his buttons, all he did was give the backstory of the Uchiha. His family were planning to take over the village because they're saiyan-er-warriors. His brother was a &quot;pacifest&quot; (way to screw up the continuity, there, btw), and killed his entire family tree in order to save everybody else. Once he found out that the leaders of the village ordered his brother to wipe out his family, I don't think that qualifies as manipulation, that's a legit reason to hate them.. </div> </div> </div>It's more the way Tobi said it than what he said.<br /> <br /> Sasuke was in rather emotionally fragile state at the time.<br /> <br /> And really none of that contradicts the point I was making with beastified Naruto-Sasuke was at the very least heavily coerced into leaving the village and joiing the various bad guys. someone was taking Naruto's toy away from him and wasn't even going to treat it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:08:52-07:00","id":511905,"title":"","content":"What Family would you use to model Shub-Niggurath, the Black Goat of the Woods with a Thousand Young? It's one of the concepts I keep coming back to for Beasts, but I'm not sure what to use. Eshmaki?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:15:21-07:00","id":511945,"title":"","content":"Why an eshmaki? The obvious choices to me would be Anakim (humans are but microbes to her), or Namtaru (she's a lovecraftian deity, she's so repulsive she drives men mad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:40:31-07:00","id":511965,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely call her Namtaru, representing the icky sides of fertility and childbirth and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:49:15-07:00","id":511989,"title":"","content":"I'm making Dagon and a Star-Spawn of Cthulhu as Makara when this comes out, first thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=511965#post511965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd definitely call her Namtaru, representing the icky sides of fertility and childbirth and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to have to second this, but as said above you could definitely get a good Anakim out of the concept too due to the sheer scale and helplessness some of the artwork and text implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:14:16-07:00","id":512040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=511945#post511945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why an eshmaki? The obvious choices to me would be Anakim (humans are but microbes to her), or Namtaru (she's a lovecraftian deity, she's so repulsive she drives men mad).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Eshmaki description emphasizes the fear of being alone, is the only one which focuses on the presence or absence of interpersonal relationships, and its example concept is an administrator who goes after things that might harm his &quot;kids&quot;. I feel like it gets more at the idea of a terrifying, alien mother-goddess or fertility deity than the Anakim's focus on power or the Namtaru's emphasis on disgust. You could certainly go Anakim for &quot;is strong&quot; or Namtaru for &quot;is hideous&quot;, but I don't know if that captures what makes Shub-Niggurath Shub-Niggurath. I'm not sure Eshmaki does either, it just seems closest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:15:54-07:00","id":512499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=512040#post512040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Eshmaki description emphasizes the fear of being alone, is the only one which focuses on the presence or absence of interpersonal relationships, and its example concept is an administrator who goes after things that might harm his &quot;kids&quot;. I feel like it gets more at the idea of a terrifying, alien mother-goddess or fertility deity than the Anakim's focus on power or the Namtaru's emphasis on disgust. You could certainly go Anakim for &quot;is strong&quot; or Namtaru for &quot;is hideous&quot;, but I don't know if that captures what makes Shub-Niggurath Shub-Niggurath. I'm not sure Eshmaki does either, it just seems closest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of an eshmaki you find so compelling is about the beast's hunger (Either collector, or nemesis), it doesn't have a single thing to do with his family. The family relevant part of his description is that he stalks the facility at night, hiding in every shadow, waiting behind every corner, under every bed, in every closet, <br /> <br /> What's relevant to a beast's family is what makes them scary.<br /> <br /> The goat with a thousand young doesn't induce paranoia, she doesn't hide at all, she's large and in charge and in your face. Eshmaki is pretty much one of the least appropriate families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 05-12-2015, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T02:41:17-07:00","id":512753,"title":"","content":"Do we have any idea what the ghoul equivalent will be for beasts? I can't really imagine a 'half-beast' but something like proximi might work a bit??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:41:16-07:00","id":512792,"title":"","content":"There are no demi-splats planned for Beast, at least on the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T05:14:36-07:00","id":512830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=512499#post512499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goat with a thousand young doesn't induce paranoia, she doesn't hide at all, she's large and in charge and in your face. Eshmaki is pretty much one of the least appropriate families.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Most stories and descriptions I've read featuring the Black Goat With A Thousand Young essentially have her just lurking somewhere. She eats, produces monsters, and that's about it. She's this thing in the woods or caves, sitting and breeding, feasting upon or transforming the beings her followers present. I mean, she is usually large, and I guess she's a figure of authority within cults, but she's certainly not in your face. Nor does she have anything to do with the air, predation, water, secret knowledge, dominance, or might. That leaves Namtaru and Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> As for the bit about Hunger, would you mind explaining your thinking? I didn't use any material from outside the Family article, so I'd like to learn more about how you weave together the posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:28:57-07:00","id":513127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastlairs/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastlairs/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Lairs &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastlairs/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastlairs/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:33:45-07:00","id":513146,"title":"","content":"If you go down to the woods today you're in for a big surprise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:46:52-07:00","id":513166,"title":"","content":"If I get a chance to run Beast, one of my requirements will be for players to draw their Lairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:50:03-07:00","id":513169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513166#post513166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I get a chance to run Beast, one of my requirements will be for players to draw their Lairs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suggested that the character sheet have room for a bubbles-and-lines Lair diagram, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:56:10-07:00","id":513174,"title":"","content":"Neat! So, Lair Traits have to be Tilts? Does that mean I can't have , say, &quot;Occult&quot;, &quot;Mystical&quot;, or &quot;Learning&quot; as Traits?<br /> <br /> For the Integrity loss requirement, it must be fun to run about with Uratha. Lunacy is your friend, especially if they have Gaze of the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Wrong Gift! 05-13-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:57:54-07:00","id":513180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513174#post513174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat! So, Lair Traits have to be Tilts? Does that mean I can't have , say, &quot;Occult&quot;, &quot;Mystical&quot;, or &quot;Learning&quot; as Traits?<br /> <br /> For the Integrity loss requirement, it must be fun to run about with Uratha. Lunacy is your friend, especially if they have Glorious Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>First time, however, it could really freak out your werewolf friends, who realise that some wolves are Bigger and Badder than they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:42:40-07:00","id":513241,"title":"","content":"The more I read about the primordial dream and lairs, the more I want to learn how it relates to the Astral Realms and the Changeling Skein. <br /> I mean:<ul><li>a soul crafted into realms, which are both a part of the Beast and something he and others can enter</li> <li>These are carved into and connected to the world of dreams</li> <li>They connect to certain parts of our world, which share at least some element of the area they are connected to</li> </ul><br /> Sounds somewhat familiar to another entity in the WoD (*cough*Archmages *cough*). Just saying, it will be interesting to see how they might relate, since we know that their are some an affinities between beasts and the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> I am excited though to see more of Beast. Come on kickstarter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-13-2015, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T13:47:40-07:00","id":513270,"title":"","content":"If not today, then either next Wednesday or the one after that. I was really hoping today, as my players and I are taking this week off and it would give me time to read it. With the release of this spoiler I'm guessing its not today, which give me, literally the biggest sad I've had in months,.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:00:18-07:00","id":513274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513241#post513241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds somewhat familiar to another entity in the WoD (*cough*Archmages *cough*).</div> </div> </div> </div>*coughcough*StrangersfromLostdiditfirst*cough*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:06:16-07:00","id":513282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513274#post513274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*coughcough*StrangersfromLostdiditfirst*cough*</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:10px\">*tinycough* Firstborn dens, yo.</span><br /> <br /> And if we're to avoid being metatemporal about this, the Begotten are literally the first ones at bat in this particular game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:07:19-07:00","id":513285,"title":"","content":"And this is why I defer to Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:10:27-07:00","id":513290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513241#post513241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read about the primordial dream and lairs, the more I want to learn how it relates to the Astral Realms and the Changeling Skein.<br /> I mean:<ul><li>a soul crafted into realms, which are both a part of the Beast and something he and others can enter</li> <li>These are carved into and connected to the world of dreams</li> <li>They connect to certain parts of our world, which share at least some element of the area they are connected to</li> </ul><br /> Sounds somewhat familiar to another entity in the WoD (*cough*Archmages *cough*). Just saying, it will be interesting to see how they might relate, since we know that their are some an affinities between beasts and the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> I am excited though to see more of Beast. Come on kickstarter!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the explanation given in Princess: the Hopeful;<br /> <br /> Basically, the Astral Realm, and similar places may be the same plane of existence, as viewed from different perspectives, like how different web browsers might render the same web site in different ways. Changelings see the Dream World how a Fairy would see it (A story to be exploited and manipulated), Mages view it through a Supernal lens (complex arcane symbolism), and Beasts see them as a primal predator would (as a lair and hunting ground). It's all about perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:16:18-07:00","id":513291,"title":"","content":"I want to know what happens when Beasts try to conquer each others' Lairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:20:55-07:00","id":513294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513241#post513241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read about the primordial dream and lairs, the more I want to learn how it relates to the Astral Realms and the Changeling Skein.<br /> I mean:<ul><li>a soul crafted into realms, which are both a part of the Beast and something he and others can enter</li> <li>These are carved into and connected to the world of dreams</li> <li>They connect to certain parts of our world, which share at least some element of the area they are connected to</li> </ul><br /> Sounds somewhat familiar to another entity in the WoD (*cough*Archmages *cough*). Just saying, it will be interesting to see how they might relate, since we know that their are some an affinities between beasts and the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> I am excited though to see more of Beast. Come on kickstarter!</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the name, the Primordial Dream is inside the collective soul of the world, not inside the consciousness of dreamers like the Skein -- Beasts' souls do draw sleeping victims in when they get hungry enough, but they'll happily feed on people in comas, people meditating, people tripping on heavy drugs...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, mages exploring the Temenos sometimes wander into Lairs by accident - from the Awakened's point of view, Lairs are part of the Astral Realms. And a Changeling dreamwalking into someone who then gets picked by a hungry soul will find herself in the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:20:59-07:00","id":513295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513290#post513290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the explanation given in Princess: the Hopeful;<br /> <br /> Basically, the Astral Realm, and similar places may be the same plane of existence, as viewed from different perspectives, like how different web browsers might render the same web site in different ways. Changelings see the Dream World how a Fairy would see it (A story to be exploited and manipulated), Mages view it through a Supernal lens (complex arcane symbolism), and Beasts see them as a primal predator would (as a lair and hunting ground). It's all about perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to disparage one ofthe few fan games i like, but, well, it's a fan game-doesn't really have bearing on the -<br /> <br /> Wait, am I about to argue definition to a mystery-based cosmology? Nope, nevermind, Hopeful it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:26:31-07:00","id":513314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513294#post513294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the name, the Primordial Dream is inside the collective soul of the world, not inside the consciousness of dreamers like the Skein -- Beasts' souls do draw sleeping victims in when they get hungry enough, but they'll happily feed on people in comas, <b>people meditating, people tripping on heavy drugs</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is both awesome and horrifying. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:29:46-07:00","id":513326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513294#post513294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Despite the name, the Primordial Dream is inside the collective soul of the world, not inside the consciousness of dreamers like the Skein -- Beasts' souls do draw sleeping victims in when they get hungry enough, but they'll happily feed on people in comas, people meditating, people tripping on heavy drugs...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, mages exploring the Temenos sometimes wander into Lairs by accident - from the Awakened's point of view, Lairs are part of the Astral Realms. And a Changeling dreamwalking into someone who then gets picked by a hungry soul will find herself in the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave, this has made me so happy. I am looking forward to the game where a mage wanders into a Lair while exploring the Tenemos, and then the Lair's owner comes home...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:31:31-07:00","id":513327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513295#post513295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to disparage one ofthe few fan games i like, but, well, it's a fan game-doesn't really have bearing on the -<br /> <br /> Wait, am I about to argue definition to a mystery-based cosmology? Nope, nevermind, Hopeful it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understand, I was just stating where the explanation came from. I know it wouldn't be &quot;canon&quot;, I just liked how it explained things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513326#post513326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave, this has made me so happy. I am looking forward to the game where a mage wanders into a Lair while exploring the Tenemos, and then the Lair's owner comes home...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey cousin! Nice of you to drop by. Please excuse the carnivorous trees, they're a bit peckish around this time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:00:22-07:00","id":513343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513166#post513166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I get a chance to run Beast, one of my requirements will be for players to draw their Lairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>During playtesting, we drew a lot of Lairs. Layers of Lairs, really.<br /> <br /> Being subject to dream logic, they're a lot more free form than you might think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:11:53-07:00","id":513349,"title":"","content":"So, what is the strength in more chambers, other than a bigger lair?<br /> <br /> Is it the potential to develop a wider variety of Lair traits? If one of your chambers is a spooky dark forest and an other is a cabin in the woods, that's potential for similar but distinct traits, as is a chamber that's a cave in that forest.<br /> <br /> Wait, is that viable? You start as some cave dwelling monster, but as you grow, interact with some of your changeling friends and develop fairly like Nightmares-maybe even a few atavisms that to buy wouldn't have otherwise gained, thus changing your soul you add a chamber based on the forest where one mortal had a break down when he saw one of the true fey emerge from the hedge and drag away a friend kicking and screaming. The Chamber looks like the Mythological Version of The Dark Forest, a maize of tall trees and taller shadows, inhabited by Trolls, Goblins, and, other Fair folk who are mischievous at best. The only place safe from the Fae is a deep, dark cave hidden in the Forrest... Where the monster of the woods, a horribly Ogre lives...<br /> <br /> Then the Beast encounters and has to fight Slashers. Freaks, and Mutants, nand Brutes, and Masks and even a fw Avengers and Legends. The sort of Characters you see in the true blue slasher movies. The Giant cave dwelling Ogre has to change again, to be like his foes. The Cabin is yet an other Chamber-The perfect, Archetypal Slasher Movie Set. Now the Ogre is less of a literal Ogre and more of a giant of a man with an ugly visage and supernatural powers that evoke the darkest of Fairy Tales...<br /> <br /> The only way to defeat this monstrous killer, who Calls himself the Ogre is to escape his Cabin, brave his haunted forest, and find the cave where he keeps his Heart... But be warned becuase in that Cave he takes his True form and is his most dangerous.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:21:08-07:00","id":513483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513349#post513349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what is the strength in more chambers, other than a bigger lair?<br /> <br /> Is it the potential to develop a wider variety of Lair traits? If one of your chambers is a spooky dark forest and an other is a cabin in the woods, that's potential for similar but distinct traits, as is a chamber that's a cave in that forest.<br /> <br /> Wait, is that viable? You start as some cave dwelling monster, but as you grow, interact with some of your changeling friends and develop fairly like Nightmares-maybe even a few atavisms that to buy wouldn't have otherwise gained, thus changing your soul you add a chamber based on the forest where one mortal had a break down when he saw one of the true fey emerge from the hedge and drag away a friend kicking and screaming. The Chamber looks like the Mythological Version of The Dark Forest, a maize of tall trees and taller shadows, inhabited by Trolls, Goblins, and, other Fair folk who are mischievous at best. The only place safe from the Fae is a deep, dark cave hidden in the Forrest... Where the monster of the woods, a horribly Ogre lives...<br /> <br /> Then the Beast encounters and has to fight Slashers. Freaks, and Mutants, nand Brutes, and Masks and even a fw Avengers and Legends. The sort of Characters you see in the true blue slasher movies. The Giant cave dwelling Ogre has to change again, to be like his foes. The Cabin is yet an other Chamber-The perfect, Archetypal Slasher Movie Set. Now the Ogre is less of a literal Ogre and more of a giant of a man with an ugly visage and supernatural powers that evoke the darkest of Fairy Tales...<br /> <br /> The only way to defeat this monstrous killer, who Calls himself the Ogre is to escape his Cabin, brave his haunted forest, and find the cave where he keeps his Heart... But be warned becuase in that Cave he takes his True form and is his most dangerous.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth</div> </div> </div> </div>On a long enough timescale, my Acid-Rainer's Lair will look like a loop of the Boglodite invasion sequence from MIB3. Corrosive is tempting, but I really want wind and gravity manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:34:37-07:00","id":513496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513349#post513349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what is the strength in more chambers, other than a bigger lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say it with me now:<br /> <br /> Water Temple.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:37:08-07:00","id":513500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513496#post513496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say it with me now:<br /> <br /> Water Temple.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is evil. I pity the hero who enters (especially if they lack their iron boots)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:54:02-07:00","id":513513,"title":"","content":"Normally I don't don't go in for &quot;Gasp! I want this more now&quot; kind of feelings, but dang it all they made me feel one when I read the lairs spoiler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:56:55-07:00","id":513544,"title":"","content":"I smell another brainstorm situation coming on!:<br /> <br /> <b>The Vicar's Lair: The Temple of Sleep</b><br /> <br /> It's not a loud place, the Reverend Grebert's soul and home. In fact, it seems to eat sound, ambient indoor light, the sensation of motion (nobody actually moves any slower, but it feels like they are); it's actually fittingly sleepy, and laying on its many stones will reveal that it's actually quite comfy, too; the stones are flat as boards and smooth as skin, and the grass that seems to sit everywhere cradles the body. One could very easily have the best rest of their lives here, if one could ignore the ghosts and the deathly Resonance that permeates the entire edifice and its grounds. Naturally, its lord is one of them; the Son of Charon finds that he's been long spoiled by his home. He no longers sleeps in his flesh-side house, no; his bedroom is vestigial except as a portal to here, where the bony, cloaked priest dozes upon an altar of asphodel and slate, a sleeping statue overlooking his precious Avernian Gate and the abandoned anchors of those he has helped move past the Gate's other side.<br /> <br /> <b>Traits; Lethargic, Unquiet, Open, Sacral<br /> <br /> Lethargic: </b>The Temple is almost a physical lullaby. Simply looking at the pedals dancing in the quiet breeze is almost hypnotic, and what sound the breezes make sounds like a mother's cooing. It's hard for even its master to think quickly here, and should one upset the peace, it turns its full power on the heretical swine who dare disturb its tranquility. Meditation rolls gain a +2 bonus, and anyone who initiates a fight in a location under the influence of the Lethargic tilt is suddenly overcome with the desire to rest and sleep, suffering a -3 to all actions until they willingly surrender (at which point they instantly fall asleep). As a side note, changeling may use the Temple as a way to enter the dreams of others, much like the Hedge, although Grebert doesn't know this.<br /> <br /> <b>Unquiet: </b>The dead here, while as desperate and eccentric as usual, are not hostile, not most of them. In fact, were it not for their translucent and obvious signs of death, the ghosts seem...normal. Something about the Temple turns ghosts <i>sane, </i>and returns much of their living personality. On one hand, this allows them to approach the difficulty of moving on rationally and accept help more readily...and on the other hand, it makes them more dangerous, since a sane ghost is also a ghost who knows exactly how their Numina and other powers work. A ghost who is in (or has an anchor which is in) a location affected by Unquiet has normal Virtues and Vices (they may regain one Willpower by indulging their vice and all Willpower by acting in accordance with their Virtue), and a +2 bonus to any rolls involving ghostly Manifestations or Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Open: </b>The Temple welcomes all. All ghosts may treat the Temple as Open for their Manifestations.<br /> <br /> <b>Sacral: </b>Some Children revel in their seemingly demonic nature and willfully Ruin churches, Punish holy people, and Hoard the Satanic. The Vicar thinks these Beasts are still stuck in a teenager mentality and probably lashing out against a far more mortal enemy than God. No, he and the other Begotten are the bloodline of the two creations of God, men and angels, and its his job to take up the latter's slack when it comes to escorting people to their eternal reward. The Temple agrees with him; it counts as holy ground for all purposes, and holy powers meant to harm him or his charges automatically fail, with the added insult that the triggering individual of their weakness is suddenly overcome with a sense of incredible shame and guilt (this has no game effect, it's a plot hook).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:22:44-07:00","id":513559,"title":"","content":"@Leliel: Can I use him, someday? It'll probably be &quot;Reverend&quot; rather than &quot;Vicar&quot;, but otherwise this guy is just far too cool not to want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:27:29-07:00","id":513564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513500#post513500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is evil. I pity the hero who enters (especially if they lack their iron boots)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a distinct lack of Zora's Tunic is a bigger issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:39:19-07:00","id":513574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513559#post513559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Leliel: Can I use him, someday? It'll probably be &quot;Reverend&quot; rather than &quot;Vicar&quot;, but otherwise this guy is just far too cool not to want to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Do as you may.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:52:57-07:00","id":513583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513564#post513564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a distinct lack of Zora's Tunic is a bigger issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is no longer deserving pity. That is just pure foolishness. Natural selection has its place, after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:48:41-07:00","id":513649,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure we're going to get at least one Springtrap or Freddie Fazbear soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:07:04-07:00","id":513658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513649#post513649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm pretty sure we're going to get at least one Springtrap or Freddie Fazbear soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I suggested a Pizzeria full of murderous animatronics as a lair before.<br /> <br /> Springtrap as the beast, with the Phantoms being one of the Lair traits, which is consistent with the theory that the ghost haunting Springtrap is more powerful than the ghosts of the murdered children.<br /> <br /> Of course, in this scenario, the beast would't have had his homecoming until after he died...<br /> <br /> Unless his beast form is a giant murderous rabbit and that' s why he used the Spring Bonnie suit, and instead of the corpse/endoskeleton, costume hybrid being possessed by the Murderer's ghost, he's got some kind of atavism that results in him being technically still alive despite the horrific trauma and the fact that he's a ruptured mummy.<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;Nightmare&quot; animatronics would be better beasts? Depends who 4 is going to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-13-2015, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:07:28-07:00","id":513659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513544#post513544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I smell another brainstorm situation coming on!:<br /> <br /> <b>The Vicar's Lair: The Temple of Sleep</b><br /> <br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>That was brilliant, so I wrote up what I would like for my prospective Beast character:<br /> <br /> <b>The Acid-Rainer\u2019s Lair: the Moor-Spire</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> At the end of the hall, built into the wall of Riggs\u2019 floor of his high-rise apartment, is set a red fire door. Through it, though, the building\u2019s Brutalist concrete gives way to black basalt before ending in a rain-slick, scorched deadfall. Impossibly high, far higher than the tenement that houses its only entrance, the spire stretches in imposing verticality toward both a jaundiced, nacreous sky, and laughably intangible landscape below. Storm clouds and hoarfrost wreathe the edifice, while flocks of bird-things, and stranger creatures, congregate within the alcoves carved into its smoldering hide. The thing that men know as Riggs floats there too, bracing himself against the wind\u2019s tides with his caustic embrace.<br /> <br /> <b>Traits: Bottomless, Corrosive, Oubliette, Windscarred</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bottomless: </b>The Spire stretches relentlessly into space, forcing visitors to experience it as an ever-moving vector of solidity rather than a mere object. Within the cultivated infinity of that Lair\u2019s stretch of Dreamland, the ground is a distant mirage, but gravity is constant, oriented perpendicularly to the Spire\u2019s faces. Creatures without a natural Flying speed must contend with this by passing a Dexterity + Athletics roll, moving laterally relative to the Spire 10 yards per success. Creatures that attempt this roll must forgo defending themselves during their turn. Creatures that are clinging to the Spire, or are capable of flight may act normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Corrosive: </b>Acid Rain regularly batters the flanks of the Spire, and etches craters into its surface.<br /> <br /> <b>Oubliette: </b>Unwelcome guests to the Spire suffer the full effects of the Lost condition, as the walls contain many alcoves, each containing red doors, but only one contains a means of escape. Only by accepting the futility of escape, can an intruder hope to gain an exit.<br /> <br /> <b>Windscarred: </b>The Spire is constantly buffeted by winds of tropical storm intensity. Intruders are subject to the Heavy Winds Tilt, subtracting 1 die from all Physical rolls, and suffering 1 Bashing damage per turn while in the air or on the Spire\u2019s surface. The alcoves provide shelter enough to mitigate this Tilt.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-13-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:16:20-07:00","id":513667,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that stories can't cross boundaries, particularly since one of my favorite actual plays has Rose Bailey using faerie tales as the groundwork for her vampires.....<br /> <br /> But I am curious why people are keen on turning what is perhaps this decade's premier <i>ghost story</i> into a groundwork for characters in a <i>mythic/epic horror </i>game.<br /> <br /> It's weird, for me at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:25:19-07:00","id":513671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513667#post513667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I am curious why people are keen on turning what is perhaps this decade's premier <i>ghost story</i> into a groundwork for characters in a <i>mythic/epic horror </i>game.<br /> <br /> It's weird, for me at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually played the game in question, I believe the reason is that it exemplifies what Lairs might be like for intruders, not to mention the resonance the game has with the innate, primal fear(similar to that of darkness, or drowning) any sane person has of animatronic pizzerias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:39:34-07:00","id":513718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513667#post513667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that stories can't cross boundaries, particularly since one of my favorite actual plays has Rose Bailey using faerie tales as the groundwork for her vampires.....<br /> <br /> But I am curious why people are keen on turning what is perhaps this decade's premier <i>ghost story</i> into a groundwork for characters in a <i>mythic/epic horror </i>game.<br /> <br /> It's weird, for me at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Animatronics, even in the prequel where the first few nights were Pre-Haunting, and including Springtrap who might be a zombie instead of a proper animatron, pretty well embody the Fear of helplessness.<br /> <br /> You can't really stop them, you can just delay them, fool them, and hoe it works long enough for you to be able to last long enough.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a good Anakim to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:56:57-07:00","id":513751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513718#post513718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Animatronics, even in the prequel where the first few nights were Pre-Haunting, and including Springtrap who might be a zombie instead of a proper animatron, pretty well embody the Fear of helplessness.<br /> <br /> You can't really stop them, you can just delay them, fool them, and hoe it works long enough for you to be able to last long enough.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a good Anakim to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That, and minus Springtrap, all the animatronics are misguided rather than evil; a security guard murdered them, you're a security guard, they can't tell the difference. Sounds like a Hunger for Punishment without proper direction to me; if Mike underwent a Homecoming, I'd expect him to make fast friends with them once Kinship kicks in and they calm down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T22:40:19-07:00","id":513837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=513751#post513751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That, and minus Springtrap, all the animatronics are misguided rather than evil; a security guard murdered them, you're a security guard, they can't tell the difference. Sounds like a Hunger for Punishment without proper direction to me; if Mike underwent a Homecoming, I'd expect him to make fast friends with them once Kinship kicks in and they calm down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also implied that the Killer Tampered with the Toy's Facial Recognition software. They know there's a child predator, but they can't tell who it is and thus become trustful of all adults.<br /> <br /> That software was later repurposed when the original animatronics, the ones that were haunted, were repaired and put back in use.<br /> <br /> Meaning they can't, in fact, tell the difference between <i>anyone</i>. All they know is that the killer keeps coming back, so if they keep killing people eventually they'll get him. Neither vengeful spirits nor small children tend to be very rational.<br /> <br /> And Springtrap, being haunted by a child predator, hungers for Prey. Possibly also some kind of arrogance to him, since there was literally no reason for him to head back to Fazbear's and destroy the animatronics after the place closed down for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T00:30:18-07:00","id":513945,"title":"","content":"Is Springtrap really the best canidate for beast status at this point? I mean I think there might be objections now.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/YiAna9L.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/YiAna9L.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/YiAna9L.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i.imgur.com/YiAna9L.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T02:01:35-07:00","id":513970,"title":"","content":"I'd still Flag the Whole lot of the Animatronics as Pandorans from Promethean, And the Security Guard (the one you play) is a Constantly Returning Promethean that killed the Kids and Tried Raising them as Prometheans but Sadly Failed. The Pizzeria falling apart and the like is the Wasteland Effect, Being Fired is the Torment getting at the owners Etc.<br /> <br /> That Said.. The Ghosts of the Kids ARE Likely Still around and keep Haunting people, Leading too Tales of the Haunted Dinner Etc. Maybe the Mannequin/Puppet is a Beast.... And the Rest is History....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T04:43:46-0