i know i've read it before enough times))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":".  Given the Correct Quote/Phrase, Edited it in. 05-14-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T15:27:12-07:00","id":514551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514541#post514541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;And in the strange Aeons, Even that which is Dead may Eternally Die...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> (Horribly Mangled i Suspect... Can Never Remember the Quote Fully)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That is not dead which can eternal lie,<br /> And with strange aeons even death may die.&quot; Not too far off it seems you basically put the start of the second line at the start and tried to correct for the oddity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:00:07-07:00","id":514588,"title":"","content":"Thought i'd Add in/on with the Lair Traits, Considering the Subject Matter of the last few posts i've done... Cthulhu's Lair/Traits of R'lyeh:<br /> <br /> Traits: Flooded, Unfathomably Deep, Non-Euclidean.<br /> <br /> Unfathomably Deep: R'lyeh lays at the unexplored and unexplorable Depths of the oceans, where the Pressure is normally lethal too mortals, Those operating without support or a time too adjust will suffer a -3 penalty too any Physical action until they can become accustomed too the pressure (Roll Against Stamina once a Scene while exposed, To grow fully accustomed you would need 10 successes over an extended action) Once Accustomed you may operate without Penalty except for single Turn Transitions.<br /> <br /> Non-Euclidean: Why does that Corner reach that side but... it doesn't travel the distance in between? That Space inside is too Large, And that Edge is too small to contain that door-frame. Paying too Much Attention too the Lair is Dangerous too your Sanity, If you Ever Fail a Perception Test while within the Lair (Or Basic Maths is the GM is Feeling Particularly cruel) you suffer a temporary Derangement/Condition that is themed towards the Breakdown of geometry, Gm Gets too pick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably worded/written up Horribly... But I have a weird &quot;Blank&quot; whenever i try too put things down even if i can word it perfectly in my head....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:39:02-07:00","id":514611,"title":"","content":"\u2026and now I'm thinking of Labyrinth, as Sarah confronts the Goblin King in a \u201ccavern\u201d inspired by an Escher painting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T17:12:17-07:00","id":514632,"title":"","content":"Since Beasts don't have a traditional fuel stat, I've got a mental image of a few beasts using their atavisms for the most trivial and mundane bullshit, just because it's much less costly for them to use their powers often than it is for other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> It culminated in a hypothetical 5 star restaurant, run by and employing Supernatural Creatures who collectively benefit from the rich and famous coming to eat at their establishment for various reasons, where the star chef is a dragon who uses his fire breath when lighting up the grill for his trademark steaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-14-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:10:22-07:00","id":514761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514632#post514632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Beasts don't have a traditional fuel stat, I've got a mental image of a few beasts using their atavisms for the most trivial and mundane bullshit, just because it's much less costly for them to use their powers often than it is for other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> It culminated in a hypothetical 5 star restaurant, run by and employing Supernatural Creatures who collectively benefit from the rich and famous coming to eat at their establishment for various reasons, where the star chef is a dragon who uses his fire breath when lighting up the grill for his trademark steaks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Are you saying you wouldn't want to eat a steak that's been roasted to perfection with dragon's fire? You know there are knights who would kill to have a sword forged in that stuff!<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, it finally dawned on me that we have the chance to play as Dragons... fuggin DRAGONS in a modern, gothic setting. I can't help but smile at the idea of some big, bad supernatural talking shit about your character, then you drag them into your lair and address him as &quot;Baggins&quot; for the rest of the scene!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-15-2015, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:55:39-07:00","id":514789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514761#post514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Are you saying you wouldn't want to eat a steak that's been roasted to perfection with dragon's fire? You know there are knights who would kill to have a sword forged in dragon fire!<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, it finally dawned on me that we have the chance to play as Dragons... fuggin DRAGONS in a modern, gothic setting. I can't help but smile at the idea of some big, bad supernatural talking shit about your character, then you drag them into your lair and address him as &quot;Baggins&quot; for the rest of the scene!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh its more fun than that. If you trigger an atavism they see it anyway. Big bad supernatural thing trying to intimidate the &quot;mortal&quot; ends with having to dodge fire and the a distinct image of a dragon standing over the mortal for reasons they don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:57:40-07:00","id":514790,"title":"","content":"Me, I just realized &quot;physical body of the Dark Mother&quot; is an awesome final boss.<br /> <br /> She even has her own phases in the form of evolutionary states; her reborn form is initially a puddle of prokaryotic slime (the first life form capable of deliberately preserving its own existence-the first thing to feel fear), and as she devours nightmares from across the world she keeps on increasing in complexity until she stabilizes at the life form most capable of feeling acute and complex fear; humanity.<br /> <br /> I can't help but see her as a &quot;demon lord to be resurrected by her loyal cultists&quot;, existing normally as a creature of living dream and sapient instinct, with the proper rituals allowing her to take physical form and finally eat her fill. Said eating of fill involves driving somewhere between a country and a continent insane from fear, and the birthing of new and powerful monsters into the world.<br /> <br /> It's nothing personal, honestly, she's just hungry. And she doesn't hate you for trying to stop her; prey fighting for its right to exist is natural, and she can't hate people following their instincts without feeling like a complete hypocrite. Honestly, she respects you; bravery is the ability to face fear after all, and she <i>is </i>fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:57:47-07:00","id":514791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514761#post514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying you wouldn't want to eat a steak that's been roasted to perfection with dragon's fire? You know there are knights who would kill to have a sword forged in dragon fire!</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said I wouldn't want to, I said I got the mental image of it happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T22:15:43-07:00","id":514798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514761#post514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, it finally dawned on me that we have the chance to play as Dragons... fuggin DRAGONS in a modern, gothic setting. I can't help but smile at the idea of some big, bad supernatural talking shit about your character, then you drag them into your lair and address him as &quot;Baggins&quot; for the rest of the scene!</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful there Smaug, the Chiefest and Greatest of All Calamities. That didn't end well for many a dragon. Pride and greed are usually how they go, and dragging someone into your soul might not go well if they aren't easy prey. They might not have magic rings, but I could definitely see it being unwise to meddle in the affairs of wizards, for they are subtle and quick to anger. <br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I could see Beasts being more cautious with creatures who can hit back hard. Predators usually don't like to get wounded if they can avoid it, cause it makes catching food that much harder and means you lose energy fighting and healing. Sure, some creatures may not be too dangerous to said dragon (fire does not agree with Prometheans, Mummies or Vampires), but I think that Beasts may want to avoid both pissing of the local supernaturals and inviting a potential threat into his home. I get not taking shit, but if they are a true big, bad supernatural like the a 3rd degree master Mage, high psyche Geist, or some other high powered splat...well, a Lair 10 Dragon may have no issue with this, but a starting PC might want to avoid angering that Mage or Geist... For now.<br /> <br /> That said. I love the idea of Dragons too! And I will admit, even after stating my concerns above, a part of me wants to go full Smaug when I play <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T23:34:57-07:00","id":514848,"title":"","content":"One of the things I'm most curious about is the concept of taking on your true form when you enter your lair. Turning into a giant, a kraken, a dragon, a gorgon or whatever is going to be interesting, to say the least. I like to imagine the Namtaru who has Infestation is actually a giant insect queen and her lair is filled with egg sacs containing her larval offspring! And sculpting your lair based on places you've been to makes it sound like typical Beast chronicles will involve lots of traveling in order to flesh out your lair. Which can work very well as a reason for them to interact with different supernaturals and thus have a chance to utilize their sympathy powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what manner of creatures would a Hero be to hunt and kill Beasts as a hobby / profession? If they're like some video game hero where they hack and slash their way through monsters, then yeah, they could pose a major threat to the Children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-15-2015, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:03:41-07:00","id":514877,"title":"","content":"........ A Weird idea Struck me.... How about &quot;Kevin&quot; from the Cabin in the Woods?<br /> A Beast who's True Form is that of a perfectly normal Man who is Somehow Absolutely terrifying when he smiles or talks too you. He would represent the fear of the Mundane, the normal people on the Street that make people paranoid.... Damnit... Now i need to see if i can Stat him....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T04:35:00-07:00","id":515043,"title":"","content":"Hmf...I'm reminded of Beckett in VtM who once stated that vampires are monsters only if they choose to be.<br /> Despite bestial &quot;hunger&quot; among a few other things, I don't think Beast needs to go in a direction that makes monsters of &quot;monsters.&quot; I'm pretty sure that the &quot;hero&quot; will be more than happy to do that all by him/herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:56:40-07:00","id":515114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514877#post514877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">........ A Weird idea Struck me.... How about &quot;Kevin&quot; from the Cabin in the Woods?<br /> A Beast who's True Form is that of a perfectly normal Man who is Somehow Absolutely terrifying when he smiles or talks too you. He would represent the fear of the Mundane, the normal people on the Street that make people paranoid.... Damnit... Now i need to see if i can Stat him....</div> </div> </div> </div>When did they reveal what kevin was? I thought the best thing about kevin is that he was left up to your imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:08:29-07:00","id":515119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=515114#post515114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When did they reveal what kevin was? I thought the best thing about kevin is that he was left up to your imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to say that Goddard or someone said that Kevin was, like, a guy who works at Wal-Mart and then goes out and kills people for fun. so in WoD terms he might fit better as a slasher than a Beast. But if you want him as a Beast, I ain't gonna stop you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:19:29-07:00","id":515127,"title":"","content":"Fascinating. Now make with audio and talk Rob into posting the kickstarter today so I can read this weekened and introduce a pc's foster next weekend! (mwahahaha)<br /> <br /> Raymer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:43:03-07:00","id":515139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=514798#post514798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful there Smaug, the Chiefest and Greatest of All Calamities. That didn't end well for many a dragon. Pride and greed are usually how they go, and dragging someone into your soul might not go well if they aren't easy prey. They might not have magic rings, but I could definitely see it being unwise to meddle in the affairs of wizards, for they are subtle and quick to anger.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but then again, how many stories of slaying dragons begin with catching it sleeping in its lair? I don't think I've heard of somebody rushing a dragon who's prepared for a conflict, at least not without having an army behind their back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> This is getting good! Every teaser they give out has me juggling between Beast or Changeling!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:20:58-07:00","id":515312,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Nyrufa;n515139]<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, but then again, how many stories of slaying dragons begin with catching it sleeping in its lair? I don't think I've heard of somebody rushing a dragon who's prepared for a conflict, at least not without having an army behind their back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Why, Good Sir John Lambton facing the great Worm forded into the River Wear in his thorny armour, intending to be coiled about by the beast, which would cut itself to ribbons on the spearheads welded to his armour!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:31:22-07:00","id":515318,"title":"","content":"&quot;Good&quot; Sir John Lambton was cheating!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:08:01-07:00","id":515332,"title":"","content":"Its not cheating when your fighting a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:23:47-07:00","id":515347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=515119#post515119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want to say that Goddard or someone said that Kevin was, like, a guy who works at Wal-Mart and then goes out and kills people for fun. so in WoD terms he might fit better as a slasher than a Beast. But if you want him as a Beast, I ain't gonna stop you.</div> </div> </div> </div>He does fit the slasher mold better. According to the novelization (I looked it up) he's described as looking perfectly normal if a bit unsettling. He shows up if someone looks at a film strip all the way through,he apparently walked through the purge casually until he came upon an injured guard who got Kevin's attention. According to the wiki &quot;He then proceeds to 'exsanguinate him in a second.&quot; The guard is later described as looking unharmed but the person seeing the corpse&quot;had never seen anyone more dead.&quot; So I think he fits the slasher mold better as far as what he is, but on the other hand I can see a few different types of beast you could build with him as the model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"d