um.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=522128#post522128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, Skin/Skull?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man/Monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:04:21-07:00","id":522164,"title":"","content":"Goofus/Gallant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:26:52-07:00","id":522228,"title":"","content":"Liechtenstein/Lefranc?<br /> <br /> Wait, what are we doing again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:41:54-07:00","id":522418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=522228#post522228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liechtenstein/Lefranc?<br /> <br /> Wait, what are we doing again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guessing at the alliteration hinted at by Matt:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=519445#post519445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody get into &amp;quot;The Skull Beneath the Skin&amp;quot; at GenCon?<br /> <br /> (Also, the Virtue/Vice analogue is, indeed, alliterative in <b>Beast</b>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:47:10-07:00","id":522451,"title":"","content":"I still think its going to be Ham and Honey-Glaze","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:55:23-07:00","id":522611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=522008#post522008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I think the concept of human nightmares is a term applied to Beasts, but it is not their fundamental nature. Their lair is in the Astral after all, which is the realm of the Soul, not the realm of Dreams. And from what we have been told, even in the Astral they do not sit in the Temenos, which would relate the to humankind and their collective fears, but in the Anima Mundi &quot;the Soul of the World&quot;. Which means Beasts' souls connect to something far older and more primal than just human fears and nightmares.<br /> Which makes them a lot more awesome in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the game is called the Primordial, indicating that they predate human existence and possibly most forms of life on the planet. Which does pose a lot of interesting questions and theories. The Beasts were here before anybody else. They ruled this land with an iron claw / tentacle / talon / whatever. Then something happened (probably those ass hole mages) that struck them down from power. Forced to live in a separate dimension while <i>their</i> planet is over run with creatures who barely register as infants compared to their kind. Well the Beasts may not be able to return to their former glory, but they can do the next best thing, making these would-be kings of the earth suffer for their insolence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:15:06-07:00","id":524259,"title":"","content":"Why do I get the feeling that at some point down the line, we'll be introduced to dark father, Typhon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:51:54-07:00","id":524295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=522611#post522611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then something happened (probably those ass hole mages) that struck them down from power. Forced to live in a separate dimension while <i>their</i> planet is over run with creatures who barely register as infants compared to their kind. Well the Beasts may not be able to return to their former glory, but they can do the next best thing, making these would-be kings of the earth suffer for their insolence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder...<br /> <br /> I don't think that is necessarily true. A quiet fade from this WoD could be just as true. Living in another world say...of creodonts where hypercanes and other super weather phenomena would exist and a primal life where mankind doesn't exist at all. Of course the reason for returning to the WoD...umm<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 05-22-2015, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:46:02-07:00","id":524343,"title":"","content":"I'm still interested in making Slenderman as an Ugallu. He might not be a flying creature, but nothing else says &quot;fear of being watched&quot; quite so strongly.<br /> <br /> On that note, though, what Hunger do you guys think he would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:46:19-07:00","id":524344,"title":"","content":"Because you think there might be one?<br /> <br /> I don't exactly see the Dark Mother as being monogamous,myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:25:35-07:00","id":524740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524343#post524343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still interested in making Slenderman as an Ugallu. He might not be a flying creature, but nothing else says &quot;fear of being watched&quot; quite so strongly.<br /> <br /> On that note, though, what Hunger do you guys think he would be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Slenderman screams Anakim. He's unnaturally tall, there's presumably nothing you can do against him, and you can't escape. Even if you collect all the pages and make it to the tower, you still die. He's a fear of powerlessness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:43:54-07:00","id":524759,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much true of most monsters, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:56:55-07:00","id":524784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524759#post524759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much true of most monsters, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Some monsters can be outfoxed, outrun, or killed. Not the Slenderman. He's not an <i>enemy</i>, so much as an <b>eventuality</b>. That's totally Anakim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-22-2015, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:38:47-07:00","id":524915,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure! Honestly, he could well be Anakim even if he wasn't an eventuality. I mean, giants are clearly Anakim, and there are tons of stories in which they are slain. Honestly, I'm slightly confused as to what isn't Anakim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:53:43-07:00","id":524929,"title":"","content":"I honestly would put slender man as a Eshmaki. I mean, read their description: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eshmaki, the Lurkers, the Nightmares of Destruction: Everyone fears being alone. Not just being deserted by lovers, not just being an outcast from society, but being literally alone. Being the only one in a room, listening to the house settle or the pipes creak. Thinking they see the shadows move, even when nothing in the room did. When they\u2019re afraid, most of them worry about the surprise, about the moment that their fear of not being alone will be suddenly confirmed. But you know better. You know that the moment you step into the light, the moment you breathe hard enough that they can really hear it, that you\u2019re about to unleash ungodly hell on the poor bastard who crossed you. Or might have crossed you, had he known you existed. </div> </div> </div>I am just saying. Slender man is the guy who is always just out of sight, not an unstoppable physical monstrosity. Anakim seem all about being much more about the fear of a physically unstoppable force, while a Eshmaki is much more the fear of them <i>being right behind you</i>. It is the difference between being chased by a T-Rex and realizing that the call came from inside your house:both will make you shit your pants but the methods are different. Slender man is scary not because he is a juggernaut but because no matter where you hide or how alone you are, he could be right there behind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-22-2015, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T18:22:04-07:00","id":524966,"title":"","content":"So The Rake would be Anakim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T18:37:36-07:00","id":524970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524929#post524929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly would put slender man as a Eshmaki. I mean, read their description:<br /> <br /> I am just saying. Slender man is the guy who is always just out of sight, not an unstoppable physical monstrosity. Anakim seem all about being much more about the fear of a physically unstoppable force, while a Eshmaki is much more the fear of them <i>being right behind you</i>. It is the difference between being chased by a T-Rex and realizing that the call came from inside your house:both will make you shit your pants but the methods are different. Slender man is scary not because he is a juggernaut but because no matter where you hide or how alone you are, he could be right there behind you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, that's exactly what I associate with the Ugallu. The Slenderman of Marble Hornets (the incarnation I'm most familiar with) never actually does anything \u2013 that we can see at least. He's just... <i>there</i>. Watching.<br /> Granted, I made this connection before they emphasized the flight stuff. So Esmaki might work too. <br /> <br /> At any rate, I'm still stuck on Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T18:55:16-07:00","id":524973,"title":"","content":"It inspires others to attempt murder. So there's the influencing of impressionable minds, loss of control of kids, fear of people believing in a fictional character to the point they'd try to end someone's life over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T19:04:29-07:00","id":524976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524970#post524970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, that's exactly what I associate with the Ugallu. The Slenderman of Marble Hornets (the incarnation I'm most familiar with) never actually does anything \u2013 that we can see at least. He's just... <i>there</i>. Watching.<br /> Granted, I made this connection before they emphasized the flight stuff. So Esmaki might work too. <br /> <br /> At any rate, I'm still stuck on Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I am thinking along the versions of the myths where he takes and kills children(or inspires others to do so). Which could fit several hungers. It depends on the why. If he is just another Predator, that is easy. If it is to target a group who fear him, and children are an easy group, he makes sense as a Tyrant. And if he does it to inspire the fear and terror of losing a child in their parents, and to spread that fear beyond his initial kill... Then he is a Ravager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-22-2015, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T19:34:25-07:00","id":524986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524966#post524966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So The Rake would be Anakim?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would almost say Namtaru Ravager. The few things I have read on it focus on it being an ugly, misshapen entity, and the stories all focus on it driving the people to being exceptionally fearful by destroying things or threatening to take them. <br /> <br /> I think modern urban legends focus less on the nature of the Anakim because we no longer fear physical forces like we used to. With the advent of modern weaponry, the idea that there is a force we couldn't defeat in a physical confrontation is relatively absent. Instead, it is the things we cannot fight that we fear, which is why the idea of the slender man is so much worse. <br /> <br /> That said, it is the idea of safety and might. Doesn't mean individuals aren't scared anymore. Just that after the creation of the atom bomb, the modern unstoppable monster is man, not a dragon or ogre... Which just means when one shows up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T19:40:49-07:00","id":524992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524966#post524966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So The Rake would be Anakim?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most likely. He's all about physical power plus sadistic if obvious mind games. Expanding the net a little, so's the Archangel (inevitability's a form of powerlessness).<br /> <br /> The Convocation is Ugallu as they come, EAT might as well be the example Makara given her intellect and water themes...<br /> <br /> Come to think of it you can mine the Fear Mythos for a lot of this stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T05:58:37-07:00","id":525362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=524970#post524970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, that's exactly what I associate with the Ugallu. The Slenderman of Marble Hornets (the incarnation I'm most familiar with) never actually does anything \u2013 that we can see at least. He's just... <i>there</i>. Watching.<br /> Granted, I made this connection before they emphasized the flight stuff. So Esmaki might work too.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I'm still stuck on Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I heard that he stalks you for months or even years on end, driving you mad before he finally kills you. Seems kind of Predatory to me, savoring the hunt and kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T10:19:51-07:00","id":525579,"title":"","content":"Who says he kills you?<br /> <br /> Sometimes people who he disappears return. Changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T15:12:30-07:00","id":526007,"title":"","content":"The story that I head says after he catches you, he impales you on a tree branch and leaves you to rot in the forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com