 make a Makara/Tyrant cult leader who deals with the crushing weight of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-25-2015, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T01:33:47-07:00","id":527421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=527399#post527399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious about Kinship with the Arisen.<br /> <br /> May well make a Makara/Tyrant cult leader who deals with the crushing weight of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how long the Arisen is walking around and what the goals are of the Beast and Arisen.<br /> <br /> I could see a Makara getting in his head that she is the true leader of the cult and screw the Judges which leads to the Arisen rising...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T01:52:33-07:00","id":527441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=527395#post527395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless &quot;exactly like the Hedge/Underworld/Hollow&quot; can be statted out as an environmental tilt, and thus applied as a lair trait, which could be applied around the time the Beast makes a chamber like the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really makes me ask a question I'd already put forth in the RPG.net thread. Could some Beast traits actually be positive? Take this for example: <br /> <br /> <b>Reveals Forbidden Knowledge (Environmental)</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Any Academics, Investigation, Occult, or Science rolls made within this area gain a +3 bonus. While within this area, all exceptional successes on these rolls also trigger breaking points in addition to their regular effects as the character uncovers something fundamentally disturbing or wrong about the nature of reality.<br /> <br /> Instead of adding a negative to the rolls, it instead adds a positive that makes breaking points more likely. Would such a trait be possible? Would the Beast only reap the benefits of this tilt, or would it not be impacted either way? Hopefully we get the answers on Wednesday. </span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div cla