nkedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T06:35:32-07:00","id":531923,"title":"","content":"We got Blog Post!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastcrossover/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastcrossover/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Beast]Crossover &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastcrossover/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/beastcrossover/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T07:19:25-07:00","id":531947,"title":"","content":"I've always taken a sort of &quot;Endless Forms Most Beautiful&quot; approach to WoD, so the big surprise right now is that I <i>haven't</i> run a crossover game yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T07:31:31-07:00","id":531951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=531848#post531848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just had a wonderful moment where I thought one of the supplements was a Dark Eras book where all of the eras were Beast or Beast crossovers. And the Mage/Beast Era was Rome and Alexandria during the life of Valentinus and the height of Gnostisim. And it was good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope some Dark Eras are one of the stretch goals, and, judging by that book's success and fan rave, I would be very surprised if we didn't get one somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T07:41:20-07:00","id":531954,"title":"","content":"In truth at this point, I find it less likely that it'll be a Dark Era addition and more likely that it'll be a stand-alone historical setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T08:14:26-07:00","id":531963,"title":"","content":"I really think a book the size of Heirs to Hell would work well for Beast Dark Eras. You could probably fit two or three eras in there. I don't think it'd be possible to add to the Dark Eras book or the Companion without significantly disrupting its publication process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T08:31:02-07:00","id":531972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=531704#post531704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seriously cannot wait to pledge the second they launch the KS. Really interested in seeing what sort of material they've got lined up for stretch goals, too. And like, what other books they have planned for the line. AND TO PLAY THIS GAME.</div> </div> </div> </div>:/ that would be wednesday my time then....way too long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T10:33:30-07:00","id":532042,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned in the blog comments, I really like the crossover writeup there. And I'm glad to hear one of the onyx path developers at least takes the Changeling/mage Arcadia are the same stance by default. Regardless, this has my psyched for the kickstarter and the unformatted text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:06:46-07:00","id":532077,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Nuts to that. They're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:13:19-07:00","id":532080,"title":"","content":"Mine re-post from comments, but I think it's very important point to make:<br /> <br /> <i>I love idea of crossovers and I'm very glad the Beast will be crosses-friendly. However, this particular Werewolf section is leaving with a bit of deficiency - we see how Beasts and Uratha could compete and react as &quot;next threat in the neighberhood&quot;. We do not see how Wolves can greet the Child in to their pack, how they can share the huntings and what Beasts get of it, beside Kinship powers. In other words - we have reasons why Uratha and Beasts would be affraid about each other on first meet, but we do not have mentioned things that could benefit on their collaboration. Second draft could point to this more, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-29-2015, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:37:23-07:00","id":532088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532077#post532077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Nuts to that. They're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You tell 'em Dave!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:40:53-07:00","id":532090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532077#post532077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Nuts to that. They're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth (and I know it still doesn't match your own view) I tend to treat it as the same place, but that the Mage Arcadia is one location within the larger flux of it. That is, the Oracle themself has created a Realm, Props, Avatar, and Wisps of its own that follows similar methods to how the Gentry work, and that realm is more or less 'walled off' from the rest of Arcadia, though that doesn't mean there's never any interaction or oddities between them. It does mean that going to Arcadia through the hedge likely won't help a mage, nor will a Changeling likely ever end up there (or most Gentry for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:46:32-07:00","id":532091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532088#post532088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You tell 'em Dave!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but Dave's obviously become drunk on his own power. Arcadia's obviously Arcadia. Its like Paris, France not Paris, Texas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:58:50-07:00","id":532102,"title":"","content":"I think the point is that you can screw up Mage's astrology as much as you want as long as you're not running Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:15:08-07:00","id":532110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532102#post532102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point is that you can screw up Mage's astrology as much as you want as long as you're not running Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do whatever you want with any game you're running","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:43:34-07:00","id":532124,"title":"","content":"Unless you're agreeing with Dave. Because that's wrong-bad fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:45:32-07:00","id":532125,"title":"","content":"Can't wait to make a crocodilian Makara who acts as the &quot;bad cop&quot; to an Arisen cult. And then weep, because the only thing less likely than playing Mummy is playing Mummy crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:18:52-07:00","id":532175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532077#post532077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Nuts to that. They're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the opinion that the Fae Arcadia is both a Fallen reflection of Supernal Arcadia, as well as being Supernal Arcadia. Basically, the Hedge of Changeling is a massive Arcadian Verge that acts as sort of a bridge across the Abyss, and the Arcadia of Changeling is a sort of &quot;Fallen Verge&quot; into the True Arcadia, a place where the Fair Folk can safely keep their pets and toys without them getting flattened across the Supernal symbol-scape.<br /> <br /> Of course, If this <i>were</i> the case, that brings up the question as to whether there are other people who've ended up in other Supernal realms, because we haven't seen any such creatures, and if not, why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:26:40-07:00","id":532179,"title":"","content":"In my world of darkness Falco's pretty close. Arcadia's a mad world crafted by and from the twisted dreams of the True Fae that by dint of its very nature is able to cross the abyss<i> and</i> is fastened to the Supernal by the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn. its a pylon of 'order' (in the form of Fate and time) in a sea of causality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:30:56-07:00","id":532187,"title":"","content":"Different places for me. Different metaphysics, different descriptions, different inhabitants, got their names from different groups of people.<br /> I honestly never saw them having much in common apart from the name. For one, Mage Arcadia isn't a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:55:22-07:00","id":532250,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You know, I just realized that Beast might be my best chance to play as a Dracopyre in a game other than AQ.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Though the Dracowerepyre from AQW might be a better bet for fluff.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T14:50:47-07:00","id":532364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532080#post532080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine re-post from comments, but I think it's very important point to make:<br /> <br /> <i>I love idea of crossovers and I'm very glad the Beast will be crosses-friendly. However, this particular Werewolf section is leaving with a bit of deficiency - we see how Beasts and Uratha could compete and react as &quot;next threat in the neighberhood&quot;. We do not see how Wolves can greet the Child in to their pack, how they can share the huntings and what Beasts get of it, beside Kinship powers. In other words - we have reasons why Uratha and Beasts would be affraid about each other on first meet, but we do not have mentioned things that could benefit on their collaboration. Second draft could point to this more, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrdhamster, buddy? First off: Beast The Primordial is long past the second draft stage. We are extremely unlikely to actually see any re-writes at this point.<br /> <br /> Second, the excerpt already gives plenty of food for thought on how Beasts and Werewolves benefit from cooperation and closeness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast Crossover Blog Post</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an Uratha pack, a Beast finds the closest expression of Kinship outside her own kind. While a brood lacks the purity of purpose of the family she knows, a lone Uratha might find solace there. Individual characters in a crossover chronicle can build powerful stories about surrogate families and finding a place of acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most obvious call to that, one that in addition gives very pertinent suggestions on how to enrich a story in which they mingle, and what themes to focus on that come naturally to both splats.<br /> <br /> The paragraph that follows tells us of consequences that might become very relevant to a chronicle where both Beasts and Werewolves are present, and how those might bring them into conflict. But there is a huge amount of potential in what is left unspoken there. Reading that left my mind spinning at the possibilities. For example, the many ways Werewolves could <i>take advantage</i> of the effect the Beast has in the Shadow. The excerpt doesn't talk about that, but it <i>offers you the facts you need to consider</i> <i>it. </i>You can't expect the storytelling section to spoonfeed you everything. You need to find your ideas and your own way to explore the game in what it lays out for you.<br /> <br /> Also, Beasts, like any other supernatural that could join a pack (regardless of the level), bring as many benefits as their diversity allows. That is to say, the reasons a pack might be interested in a Beast are entirely dependent on who that particular Beast is and what they alone can offer. There are no universal advantages a pack and a Begotten might obtain from cooperating anymore than a team of researchers in hiring someone new to join them for any number of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-29-2015, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T15:07:23-07:00","id":532375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532187#post532187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different places for me. Different metaphysics, different descriptions, different inhabitants, got their names from different groups of people.<br /> I honestly never saw them having much in common apart from the name. For one, Mage Arcadia isn't a place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally see it that way too... it was even true in one of my games. I was more celebrating the modularity of the setting (... and picking on Dave because he needs a picking on)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:34:16-07:00","id":532600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=532250#post532250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You know, I just realized that Beast might be my best chance to play as a Dracopyre in a game other than AQ.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Though the Dracowerepyre from AQW might be a better bet for fluff.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Blood drinking Dragon seems very doable, I don't see why it would be hard to recreate that. Just that a vampire dragon isn't something most people imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast seems to have a similar level of creativity to Changeling in that it's limited only by what we can dream up. Which, of course makes it awesome from a sandbox point of view!<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to see Beasts who model themselves after alligators or snakes and design their lairs in the image of sewers and aqueducts. You go to use the bathroom and a snake lunges out of the toilet and bites you, or a gator chases you down the filth covered tunnels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:19:27-07:00","id":532623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=531954#post531954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth at this point, I find it less likely that it'll be a Dark Era addition and more likely that it'll be a stand-alone historical setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. I didn't mean to imply that it'd find its way into the book. Like Tiresias said, I would expect a small companion supplement like <b>Lore of the Deceived</b> or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:29:01-07:00","id":532627,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dracopyre&quot; done'st mean blood drinking dragon.<br /> <br /> It means &quot;Humanoid Hybrid of Vampire, Werewolf, and Dragon&quot;<br /> <br /> It comes from an AE browser game called AdventureQuest. The First was a &quot;Werepyre&quot;(Equally Vampire and Werewolf) who was also half-dragon on top of that, but the second generation and the PC if you so choose are more even mixes<br /> <br /> But the similar but unrelated Dracowerepyre from AQworlds might be a better choice from a fluff standpoint-it was a dragon that was inflicted with Lycanpyrism.<br /> <br /> So, a Beast that's a dragon who hangs out with or comes into conflict with Kindred and Uratha and develops Kinship Nightmares and maybe even a few atavisms similar to their cousins and eventually changes from a dragon with vampire and werewolf like powers to &quot;hybrid&quot; of the three, allowing for Atavisms and Nightmares that normally wouldn't fit on a dragon becoming available without major refluffing.<br /> <br /> I mean, Matt did say over on RPGNet that if a Beast takes an Atavism that doesn't fit their soul. one option os for the soul to change to better fit.<br /> <br /> If the soul can change for one atavism, then it can probably slowly change over time as a result of learning new Nightmares and Spending Time around certain kinds of supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> That makes sense, right?<br /> <br /> I was thinking of that when I had my realization.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that Beasts could easily be used to get the feal of Template Stacking without having to worry about how powerful that would make a character or having to make adjustments to rules or fluff, because the character is't actually template stacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:00:00-07:00","id":532643,"title":"","content":"I know, I played AQ a long time ago. Even had a level 67 Dracopyre. But the lore behind the Dracopyre is they started off as a Werepyre who gorged on the blood of dragons and eventually mutated into the creature it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:06:05-07:00","id":532650,"title":"","content":"And the scenario I presented for my &quot;dracopyre&quot; beast is the inversion-start as a dragon and become the hybrid creature due to interaction with vampires and werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T06:07:37-07:00","id":533100,"title":"","content":"The update regarding crossovers brought up a good point, I hadn't given much thought to before now. Just because the Beasts are family, doesn't mean they're going to get a warm welcome. After all, if all monsters are family, well they certainly have no qualms about slaughtering each other on sight. I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack, so why then should Beasts get any special treatment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:00:20-07:00","id":533156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533100#post533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you generalize like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3771-damoqles","name":"damoqles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:01:57-07:00","id":533158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533100#post533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack, so why then should Beasts get any special treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead Wolf bloodline notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T08:38:19-07:00","id":533232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533100#post533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The update regarding crossovers brought up a good point, I hadn't given much thought to before now. Just because the Beasts are family, doesn't mean they're going to get a warm welcome. After all, if all monsters are family, well they certainly have no qualms about slaughtering each other on sight. I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack, so why then should Beasts get any special treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Joining a Pack is a bit more complicated than that. For most other Supes, it's quite difficult. Vampires have the disadvantage of not being as active in the real world, and being blind to the spirit world early on, so in a Pack, they tend to have responsibilities more inline with those of mortals or Shadow-blind Wolf-blooded: gathering resources, working contacts and occasionally manning the walls.<br /> <br /> Beasts, on the other hand, are still creatures of this world, although their powers and their Lair give the pack an alternative route to a target and new tactical options when Essence is tight and they can't safely travel through the Shadow. Obviously, the challenge comes from earning a place in the Pack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T08:42:17-07:00","id":533234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533100#post533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, if all monsters are family, well they certainly have no qualms about slaughtering each other on sight. I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player of Werewolf and ST of vampire, unless they were specifically a band of vampire hunters like Black Moon eXtreme, or the vampire was a rampaging monster, there wouldn't likely be an instant antagonism. If they didn't know the vampire, sure, they'd probably laugh in his face since it's such a crazy idea, but nothing suggests a vampire can't become allies with werewolves outside of certain circumstances like the BMX or the Eaters of the Dead lodge.<br /> <br /> Vampires are even called out as potential packmates in the alternative pack members sidebar, 'A sorcerer, a vampire, or a patchwork creature could join a pack of werewolves. Unless a totem has a particular prejudice, there\u2019s no reason it couldn\u2019t happen.'<br /> <br /> I see potentially more problems from an out of character perspective. If everyone's playing werewolf, but one person wants to be a Beast, without the weaknesses or investment that a werewolf has to deal with, they're going to stand out, like, a lot. It seems like it would be worse with vampire, since it doesn't seem like Beasts are going to have to deal with the issues the others are. Who wants to play a game where one person is a daywalker? Or Promethean, where one player doesn't have Disquiet or Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-30-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T08:45:29-07:00","id":533239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533100#post533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The update regarding crossovers brought up a good point, I hadn't given much thought to before now. Just because the Beasts are family, doesn't mean they're going to get a warm welcome. After all, if all monsters are family, well they certainly have no qualms about slaughtering each other on sight. I can't imagine a vampire would make it very far strolling up to a wolf den and asking to join with the pack, so why then should Beasts get any special treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Cause they're so gosh darn likable?<br /> <br /> 2) Why wouldn't a vampire make it very far? It's a matter of context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T12:14:55-07:00","id":533510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533239#post533239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Cause they're so gosh darn likable?<br /> <br /> 2) Why wouldn't a vampire make it very far? It's a matter of context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm thinking with Apocalypse rules in which they didn't get along well, if at all. It just seemed like if werewolves are about keeping the balance between spirit and flesh, then a race of the walking dead who feeds on the blood of the living, commonly enslaves them, and erects a shadow government to manipulate their thoughts wouldn't be on speaking terms with the lupine.<br /> <br /> But in hindsight it sounds like I'm assuming the wolves know anything about vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-30-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T12:39:51-07:00","id":533544,"title":"","content":"Well, remember, Werewolves are more focused on spirits, their related entities, the Shadow, and themselves than anything else in 2nd edition. So, sure, Vampires might manipulate mortals and feed on blood, but just because that's not entirely a great thing to do doesn't mean it really affects the werewolves or that any individual pack cares, depending on their own outlook. Sure, they may spawn spirits, but the few blood, greed, and similar spirit types are lost amongst the ranks of similar types in larger cities.<br /> <br /> (As a note, yes, Glasswalkers have other supernaturals in their purview, but like their primary trget of mortals, they don't go and hunt down every one that does 'bad' things, it's mainly if it affects the Uratha or the spirit world.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:05:52-07:00","id":533601,"title":"","content":"They're about finding a balance between spirit and flesh in themselves, not necessarily the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:22:33-07:00","id":533644,"title":"","content":"All of the above, and Uratha aren't Garou; they hunt because they are hunters rather than any higher goal. They can, and will, give themselves higher goals to their hunts, but the ultimate reason they start is the Wolf Must Hunt.<br /> <br /> Another hunter by necessity, such as a vampire, understands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T18:42:23-07:00","id":533871,"title":"","content":"I will never see a vampire as a hunter.<br /> More like a parasite.<br /> Hunters are part of an ecology. Parasites aren't in my world.<br /> <br /> I should wonder if a &quot;beast&quot; would know the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:07:16-07:00","id":533886,"title":"","content":"I'd be surprised if they care, it seems like Beasts see vampires and werewolves both as distant relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:45:36-07:00","id":533928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533871#post533871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will never see a vampire as a hunter.<br /> More like a parasite.<br /> Hunters are part of an ecology. Parasites aren't in my world.<br /> <br /> I should wonder if a &quot;beast&quot; would know the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since by definition parasites are part of their ecology, I'd go with no beast with even rudimentary knowledge of biology would make that mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T22:57:49-07:00","id":534075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533871#post533871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will never see a vampire as a hunter.<br /> More like a parasite.<br /> Hunters are part of an ecology. Parasites aren't in my world.<br /> <br /> I should wonder if a &quot;beast&quot; would know the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are only parasites if they keep their victims alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T01:48:01-07:00","id":534141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534075#post534075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are only parasites if they keep their victims alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the ppl who die due to parasites on the world daily that their killer is no parasite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T06:48:42-07:00","id":534276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=533928#post533928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since by definition parasites are part of their ecology, I'd go with no beast with even rudimentary knowledge of biology would make that mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rudimentary knowledge of biology never accepts parasites as part of an ecology because as defined there's no contribution to the whole. If the fleas, mosquitos, ticks, mites, what have you, disappear from the face of the earth nothing will mourn them. It seems even Mother Nature makes mistakes. I recall seeing a pic of a rabbit that was so flea infested...ugh...it brings to mind vampires and a city populace...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T07:50:01-07:00","id":534321,"title":"","content":"Guys, <i>humans</i> are hunters(as in hunter gatherers, not slayers of monsters). That's kind of how we got our start. And despite the divide now, the Uratha still use humans in their pack.<br /> <br /> Debating about whether vampires are hunters or parasites is a little silly, given the context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:11:55-07:00","id":534326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534141#post534141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell that to the ppl who die due to parasites on the world daily that their killer is no parasite</div> </div> </div> </div>A parasite that kills it's host is a really shitty parasite, since it's shooting itself in the foot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:01:14-07:00","id":534427,"title":"","content":"This discussion is getting a bit out of hand. Vampires are hunters, some of which do so in parasitical sorts of ways, but they are HUNTERS, and that word is used most often in their own book (Parasite tends to just be used as an external insult). Considering how mystic they are in origin and capabilities, it's rather silly to debate how closely they fit to real world biological definitions....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:24:06-07:00","id":534478,"title":"","content":"So, since we have around 48 hours until the proposed Kickstarter date, anyone have any interesting character ideas? I guess I'll start, with the first character idea I really started working on.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Witness&quot;: An Ugallu Nemesis, abet an unconventional one. Rather than focusing on the flying aspects, he focuses on the feelings of surveillance. He specifically represents the Fear of &quot;I Know What You Did Last Summer&quot;, the fear that someone knows all your darkest secrets. I'm not sure what he does for a day job, but his true calling is as an online blogger, seeking out those people with hidden sins and dragging them out, kicking and screaming into the light. His Lair appears as a washed out city, like someone sketched a urban landscape and then covered it in watered down paint. Here he appears in his true form, a grayish-white silhouette that can only be seen out of the corner of your eye, and who communicates through the feeling of hot breath on the back of your neck and a whisper that appears to be spoken right into your ear. In some ways, he was inspired by this song(<a href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 05-31-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:10:36-07:00","id":534740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534276#post534276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the fleas, mosquitos, ticks, mites, what have you, disappear from the face of the earth nothing will mourn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the animals that are natural enemies and hunters of mosquitoes, mites etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3771-damoqles","name":"damoqles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:29:54-07:00","id":534770,"title":"","content":"Plus it's not as if Beasts aren't parasitical or vampiric in nature. They just exchange blood for fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:09:07-07:00","id":534800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534478#post534478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since we have around 48 hours until the proposed Kickstarter date, anyone have any interesting character ideas? I guess I'll start, with the first character idea I really started working on.<br /> <br /> \u2022&amp;quot;The Witness&amp;quot;: An Ugallu Nemesis, abet an unconventional one. Rather than focusing on the flying aspects, he focuses on the feelings of surveillance. He specifically represents the Fear of &amp;quot;I Know What You Did Last Summer&amp;quot;, the fear that someone knows all your darkest secrets. I'm not sure what he does for a day job, but his true calling is as an online blogger, seeking out those people with hidden sins and dragging them out, kicking and screaming into the light. His Lair appears as a washed out city, like someone sketched a urban landscape and then covered it in watered down paint. Here he appears in his true form, a grayish-white silhouette that can only be seen out of the corner of your eye, and who communicates through the feeling of hot breath on the back of your neck and a whisper that appears to be spoken right into your ear. In some ways, he was inspired by this song(<a href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Plaecholder name is The Rager. He's a Makara Tyrant and a member of an Arisen cult; their immortal master promised a blissful afterlife in exchange for dutiful service. The Rager has made himself the flipside to that dogma; disobey the Arisen, and face an eternity of pain within his jaws. He works with the mummy and his high priest to keep the cult loyal and scared. His Lair is a water-stained ancient ruin, crumbling and open to a starless black sky; it evokes feelings of one's insignifigance in the face of the unyielding march of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:32:21-07:00","id":534816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534478#post534478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since we have around 48 hours until the proposed Kickstarter date, anyone have any interesting character ideas? I guess I'll start, with the first character idea I really started working on.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Witness&quot;: An Ugallu Nemesis, abet an unconventional one. Rather than focusing on the flying aspects, he focuses on the feelings of surveillance. He specifically represents the Fear of &quot;I Know What You Did Last Summer&quot;, the fear that someone knows all your darkest secrets. I'm not sure what he does for a day job, but his true calling is as an online blogger, seeking out those people with hidden sins and dragging them out, kicking and screaming into the light. His Lair appears as a washed out city, like someone sketched a urban landscape and then covered it in watered down paint. Here he appears in his true form, a grayish-white silhouette that can only be seen out of the corner of your eye, and who communicates through the feeling of hot breath on the back of your neck and a whisper that appears to be spoken right into your ear. In some ways, he was inspired by this song(<a href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=rUuNjyitK2Q&amp;autoplay=1</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Miss Land,&quot; an Anakim Nemesis. A strident anti-gnostic and ally of the Seers of the Throne, she strives to defend mages from Paradox by preventing them from publicly or privately using magic, using everything from surveillance to evicting them from their Hollows via group focus - after all, the Abyss is the home of creatures foreign even to the Dark Mother, and it is Miss Land's duty to defend her family, even if that means denying them their heritage. Thus, she fulfills her hungers by seeking out those who meddle too deeply in dangerous magic and punishing their hubris. She represents the fear that the laws of physics aren't just indifferent or set up without regard for human values, but actively malicious towards specific individuals; her monstrous form manifests as a iron statue, its skin inscribed with commandments, forbiddances and punishments, in a Lair that is a vast, decrepit amusement park, where all manufactured or handmade objects slowly crumble into dust, and all movement is downward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:54:21-07:00","id":534851,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering about the mysterious &quot;Beast Within Revised&quot; thing that has been in the Monday Meeting notes for the past few weeks. Could this be our Beast quickstart or is it a cWoD thing that I'm unfamiliar with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:21:08-07:00","id":534904,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Vicar&quot;, an Anakim Collector. He was-is-an Anglican priest, and he's still very religious, thanking God for every day. It's just that the nuances of his personal religion don't resemble anything orthodox by any human standard. He enrolled in the priesthood as a desperate attempt to quell his angry, prideful urges to tear down all those who offended him, and the faith helped; it gave him an explanation and a reason when he finally stood up to the cloaked, stone-faced spectre with wings of shadow and a scythe of purest light that forever overlooked his nightmares, staring at him with the severe starkness of the inevitible. He knows now his birthright, that of the terrifyingly mighty and horrifyingly beautiful giants born of men and angels, sheltered and hidden away by the Dark Mother Lilith. And it is his duty to redeem the name of his fallen ancestors, and take up the bloodline's duties to Heaven; as his true form suggests, he has become a self-appointed angel of Death, here to guide those lost souls trapped on earth or the Purgatory of the Underworld to their just rewards, and to finish what binds their spirits to the mortal coil. All he asks is that he be allowed to keep their anchors, to further decorate his Lair; a placid, sleepy cathedra resting atop a field of asphodel where all, living and dead, may find rest. And protection, for its lord and guardian finds those who would further torment the dead to be most offensive indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-31-2015, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T17:10:59-07:00","id":534961,"title":"","content":"Riggs, the Acid-Rainer, an Ugallu Ravager: Possessed of a cutting and relentless wit, Riggs never could form lasting relationships. Too smart and too independent, his only true love is the sky, which he explores from the gondola of his airship. The skies of his dreams haunted by an impossible thing of acid disdain and endless tendrils, he now hangs from above the clouds, senses sharp like that eyeless horror that lives within, ready to deliver a smoking, noxious demise to those who profane his true home. Let the fools choke on their pride, drown in his burning ichor, and be crushed by their fallen towers, for his is the vengeance of a blighted sky, and only when they humble themselves will he be satisfied.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Concept: Airship Pilot<br /> Legend: Unexpected<br /> Life: Honest<br /> Kinship: Forsaken<br /> Family: Ugallu<br /> Hunger: Ruin<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> Mental Skills: Crafts 2 (Repairs), Investigation 3, Occult 3<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 2 (asset, Dodge), Brawl 2 (Touching), Drive 3 (asset, Dirigibles), Stealth 2 (asset, Tailing), Survival 2<br /> Social Skills: Empathy 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> Merits: Contacts 2 (Contract Couriers, Sports Venues, PT benefit), Crack Driver 3, Direction Sense, Advanced Direction Sense, Professional Training 3 (Stuntman), Trained Observer 1<br /> Atavisms: Basilisk's Touch, Wings of the Raptor<br /> Nightmares: Behold, My True Form!, You Cannot Run<br /> Lair : 1 (Thin Air, Currents)<br /> Health: 8<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Satiety: 2<br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Armor: 0<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-04-2015, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T17:31:34-07:00","id":534971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=534851#post534851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering about the mysterious &quot;Beast Within Revised&quot; thing that has been in the Monday Meeting notes for the past few weeks. Could this be our Beast quickstart or is it a cWoD thing that I'm unfamiliar with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a CWoD thing; it's nothing to do with <b>Primordial</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T18:06:23-07:00","id":534988,"title":"","content":"I think it was an old VtM anthology... so no idea why it is being revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:09:54-07:00","id":535005,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nature Jr.&quot; A Makara Collector. Before his homecoming, NJ was a nature activist who dedicated his life to protecting the environment. Only to have his pleas fall on deaf ears when confronted with the wealth and power of corporations and their lawyers. Now he satisfies his hunger by sabotaging industrial machinery and pirating valuables from private yachts and cruise ships. He represents the fear of consequences, that one day mankind's arrogance will come back to bite them in the ass. His lair is a filthy, polluted ocean with garbage littering the surface so clustered you can't even see the water. Yet beneath the thick layer of trash, the ocean floor is sparkling with gold, silver, jewels, and other fine treasures he has plundered as &quot;reparations&quot; for the damage caused to his home.<br /> <br /> The creature who lurks within his soul is beyond description, because he leaves no survivors to provide one. Those dragged into his lair watch in horror as the garbage mound rises and falls as something moves beneath the surface, and as they panic and try to swim through the filth, it senses their presence and closes in. Finally, something grabs their leg and they are dragged into the putrid waters below, never to resurface!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:52:02-07:00","id":535104,"title":"","content":"The Alley Serpent: Anakim Nemesis. A poor kid from Gary, Indiana who was plagued with nightmares about snakes all his life. His parents blamed the local gang, the Cobras, for this nightmare, but the dream was far more primal. He was always a shy, unassuming kid, who got his fair share of bullying, but no more than most other kids. He grew up, always silently bubbling with discontent at the poverty and violence around him, but he always knew there was nothing he could do about it. Then, one day, when he was 17, he was mugged on his way home from cashing his very first paycheck. Normally, he would have just put his head down and walked home in dejection, but at that moment, something snapped. He followed the mugger to his home, an old, run-down house he shared with a few other addicts and thieves, and in the dead of night, slew him and anyone who dared to stand in the way. Since then, bodies of gang-bangers, drug dealers and petty thieves have been found, mutilated, stripped of all valuables, and with necrotic wounds resembling the bite of a massive and brutally poisonous snake.<br /> <br /> In dreams, The Alley Serpent is a great, terrible snake of a thousand colors, with vestigial limbs on the side of its body. Or, perhaps, the limbs are not vestigial, but human-sized, and tiny compared to the huge beast. His fangs are slender, straight, and shine like stainless steel, resembling hypodermic needles, and his head flares into a wide cobra's hood with ever-shifting patterns, showing a tapestry of the viewer's sins.<br /> <br /> His Lair is a geometrically impossible series of streets and alleys, twisting upon themselves in constant night. Despite the illusion of size given by the infinite looping, the Lair is incredibly claustrophobic, as the tall buildings trap you in at all times. The lair is swarming with reptiles and the vermin they hunt, all animals built of living urban refuse. Every window in this nightmare city is broken, every door locked, and every shop looted and abandoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 06-01-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T23:54:32-07:00","id":535328,"title":"","content":"By the way, I had a funny mental image of Heroes acting <a href=\"https://youtu.be/brs6-uQMfGU\" target=\"_blank\">like this</a> when they show up in your stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T00:02:55-07:00","id":535330,"title":"","content":"The Dark Sister, Anakim Predator<br /> <br /> As long as she could remember, her dreams were haunted by her dark sister, the gaunt figure that waited for her wherever she turned, ragged and ravaged, terrible and inescapable, the face ever hidden, ever concealed, she dared not meet for fear of what she might see.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, she thought her dark sister was the twin who should have been born with her. In her darker moments, she thought maybe her dark sister was supposed to have been born _instead_ of her, angry at being denied her rightful place in the world.<br /> <br /> She remembers the dream when everything changed. When she faced her dark sister and said &quot;Come back. Come home.&quot;<br /> <br /> She knows, now. They were incomplete before, missing their other halves, their other selves. Now they are together and whole, close as any sisters could be.<br /> <br /> She seeks out prey for her sister. If she's honest - and why wouldn't she be? - there's not a little vindictiveness in her targets, terrorising the assholes and bullies around her, showing them that there are real monsters in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:26:00-07:00","id":535569,"title":"","content":"Warning.... This is Maybe abit Dark but.. My Mind Wandered there and well.. i needed to get it out or have it Fester.<br /> Spoilered because of its Nature.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Mr Johnson&quot; A Eshmaki Predator, In his everyday life &quot;Johnson&quot; couldn't escape his twisted Dreams of being hunted as a child, defenseless and alone the &quot;Smiling Man&quot; that chased him in his dreams just wanted something from him, something sweet, Innocent... something that couldn't be taken or given, At least by children. As he grew he came too realise his dreams were closer too home then he wanted. He was having Sympathetic Nightmares of his Sisters Abuse from his Stepfather, When he finally Accepted this and Took the &quot;Smiling Man's&quot; hand he learned the price this has on people.<br /> <br /> Now Grown up, Mr Johnson is the Headmaster of a School for Children who have suffered from abuse, looking out for them and Preying on those that would pray on them... Many Of his charges are also Orphans from a rash case of Disappearing Abusers, Only afew of the Children have tales of what happened too there Parents or abusers, but because of the Delusions of the obviously broken children Tales of a Calm and terrifying &quot;Smiling Man&quot; (the children cannot give a better description) are growing as an Urban Legend..... </div></div> </div> </div><br /> His Lair:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Lair of the Smiling Man is like a Toybox filled with broken and damaged Toys, there is something off about them though, Regardless of where you stand they watch you, silent, innocent, Judging. Scattered about are areas of broken dreams and battered promises, small lies told too children to let them think everything is fine.<br /> <br /> When the Smiling Man is in his lair the Toys are animate, Alive. Capable of walking and interacting with others, they will follow people wherever they go whispering and singing a Melancholic tune about the secrets and tortures they inflict on their Victims.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-01-2015, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:00:09-07:00","id":535658,"title":"","content":"The Wicked Idol: A Makara Ravager. She is the fear that your sins are irredeemable, the crushing panic when the church closes it's doors on you. She knows the dirty, fetid secrets that the righteous hold in their hearts and she knows the horrid things they do in the dark. Slowly, she wears away at their resolve, hiding temptation in their duties and hedonism in their houses. She hooks the priest on on crack and makes the campaigner an alcoholic, driving them further down the road to damnation with every caress. In the dark hours, when they sob and shake in fear of their lives and faith being ruined, she feasts.<br /> <br /> In dreams, she is a giant rainbow scaled woman, with a dozen tentacles to soothe and bind her victims and seven eyes to see all their sins. Her Lair is a lake of shimmering acid that reeks of whisky and solvents. A storm lashes out on the waters, spitting psychedelic drugs into the waters. Sometimes, mountains of peace and stability, glowing in the darkness, can be seen on the horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:00:49-07:00","id":535718,"title":"","content":"Think we'll still get the ks tomorrow? I'm going to wear out my phones battery checking back as often as I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T12:58:38-07:00","id":535852,"title":"",