ition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T13:23:12-07:00","id":535897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=535852#post535852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought this was supposed to be a game? You know, as in a fun game?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't quite understand what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:47:42-07:00","id":535954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=535852#post535852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought this was supposed to be a game? You know, as in a fun game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrifying puny mortals is all kinds of fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:25:50-07:00","id":536007,"title":"","content":"<b>Mr Daniel Teague, a Makara Predator.</b><br /> As a young boy, Daniel lived in the port city of St Ives, in Cornwall, England. His father, a crab catcher by profession, was not a pleasant man. He would be gone for days at a time out on work, but would always come home, reeking of cheap whiskey and rotten fish, and whenever Daniel's mother would complain about his state, he would thrash the boy in punishment and make her watch. Needless to say, Daniel grew up hating his father, until one night at the age of thirteen.<br /> <br /> The Great Storm of '87 it was called. It was hard to sleep that night, the wind howling outside and waves crashing upon the rocks like the jaws of some monster, gnashing, struggling to break free of its bonds. While young Daniel lay there, tossing and turning trying to get some sleep, he started to see things out in the world. Glimpses of the storm, out at sea, far worse than even at home. And in the midst of all this rage, sailed a small fishing boat, which Daniel recognised as his father's. Seeing it sway around, he observed the terrified crew and his hated father, scramble for their lives attempting, in vain, to sail to the shore. A rogue wave, smashed against the side of the tag, and Daniel's father was thrown overboard, but not so far as to be unrescuable. The crew, scrambled for their captain, reaching against hope that they could pull him back up, when Daniel, despite being miles away, reached out in his bed, and pulled his father's leg from beneath the waves, down towards the deep.<br /> <br /> Years on now, Daniel has turned his lust for vengeance against the corrupt and hateful towards his profession. Now a ruthless prosecution lawyer, he works tirelessly to send those villains where they belong. But, now and again, when the crime is too heinous, or when his appetite rears its head, he'll make a couple of mistakes, a mishandling of evidence here, a dodgy witness there, and they'll slip through the cracks. And he waits, and watches, and when they get too close to the water, he's waiting.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair: </b><br /> Imagine a body of water, stretching as far as the eye can see. The water is perfectly placid and pure. It is a beautiful day and not a cloud in the sky. It is exactly midday, all the time. There are islands of haven in this vast ocean, small sandy banks covered in palm trees. There is no wind at all, it is perfectly still. When you enter the lair, you come up through the water, and then rest on top of it, and may stand on it. However, if you make too much noise, move too fast or break the tranquillity, you will fall through the water. In the water, there are beautiful, tropical fish of all kinds, and are constantly swimming and moving, seemingly at peace, but should you fall through the ocean into the depths, they swarm upon you like piranhas, tearing at flesh and bone until nothing of you remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6