{"date":"2015-06-02T12:09:46-07:00","id":537303,"title":"","content":"Pledged. The art is gorgeous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:10:18-07:00","id":537305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537265#post537265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting to solidify how the Unchained are thoroughly not an organic part of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, the fact they were robots didn't tip you off, squishy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:33:25-07:00","id":537317,"title":"","content":"After reading through the full Family writeups, I've decided that my Slenderman Beast is definitely an Eshmaki, not an Ugallu.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Isaac is an Eshmaki Nemesis. His Soul has declared that the forest is not the domain of man, and anyone who trespasses on it cannot truly return from it until they have been punished for their transgressions. People who wander off the path in his territory find themselves lost, the way back having disappeared behind them. Even if they manage to physically leave the forest, he ensures that the places they once regarded as safe become labyrinthine and unfamiliar. Doors no longer lead where they should, paths turn back on themselves, and their memories of their movements become obscured. And then, as they desperately attempt to trace their own passage, they become aware of a figure in the background, a silhouette thin enough to be mistaken for the shadow of a dead tree, only noticeable in retrospect. Watching. Only when they surrender to the directionless expanse of the forest is his Soul sated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2449,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","user":"One Tin Soldier","date":". 06-02-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:58:53-07:00","id":537341,"title":"","content":"Since there is a Beast Dark Eras stretch goal, would that include Beasts also being listed on the different era sidebars like the other gamelines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:59:40-07:00","id":537343,"title":"","content":"Doesn't look like I'm backing this one; I hate to say that I just don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:00:42-07:00","id":537344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537305#post537305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, the fact they were <s>robots</s> <b>profanely/sacredly apart</b> didn't tip you off, squishy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537238#post537238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all supernaturals are family of the beast? interesting perspective. However my mage would say to the beast that he does not need to terrorize people and feed on their nightmares to survive. They have nothing in common, at all. After that he would give the beast the middle finger and prepare himself to wipe out this unholy abomination from the face of the earth, making sure that it does not hurt people ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Then why are you so desperately diving into the Fallen World?&quot; says the Collector of Secrets with a toothy grin.<br /> <br /> Mages are just as hungry as anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537237#post537237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lobbying again for a <b>&quot;Mortal Remains&quot; chapter pdf</b>, and a Dark Era chapter pdf to be stretch goals!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I'd write that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537341#post537341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there is a Beast Dark Eras stretch goal, would that include Beasts also being listed on the different era sidebars like the other gamelines?</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Where is that mentioned?</s> Found it, nevermind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537343#post537343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't look like I'm backing this one; I hate to say that I just don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-02-2015, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:04:27-07:00","id":537357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537305#post537305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, the fact they were robots didn't tip you off, squishy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Robot <i>ghosts </i>from another universe entirely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:07:46-07:00","id":537358,"title":"","content":"@Arc: Central themes just feel a bit muddy to me. I'm not sure what all the Begotten /do/ beyond sate their Hungers. The crossover material feels a little shallow.<br /> <br /> It's not bad, it just isn't hooking me, and that's fine. Not every game can be Promethean or Mummy, and it seems like tons of folks are already in love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:10:06-07:00","id":537362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537358#post537358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Arc: Central themes just feel a bit muddy to me. I'm not sure what all the Begotten /do/ beyond sate their Hungers. The crossover material feels a little shallow.<br /> <br /> It's not bad, it just isn't hooking me, and that's fine. Not every game can be Promethean or Mummy, and it seems like tons of folks are already in love.</div> </div> </div> </div>They find a way to beat the cycle of violence, and maybe their Hungers to boot.<br /> <br /> But that's me.<br /> <br /> And hey, yeah, I get it. I love all the games, Beast included, but Vampire and Mage are always a little short-sold on my end. Different strokes for different folks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although the new cover descriptor, A Storytelling Game of Endless Hunger, somewhat supports your point of view. Eh, it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:17:50-07:00","id":537372,"title":"","content":"I think that the Primordial Dream offers a lot of opportunity to take campaigns beyond satisfying individual hungers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I haven't fully read the crossover material, but your view seems a little pessimistic, ata. You can essentially draw on any of the themes of the other game lines, any of their goals, and come up with a way to incorporate Beasts. Does the BtP corebook not flesh this out enough? Even so, with a little creativity and ingenuity I'd imagine the possibilities are pretty limitless, which to me is a very exciting idea.<br /> <br /> The Beasts think they are the original monsters. What happens when this clashes with the views of the other splats? nWoD was always about &quot;this is one take on how things are, and this is another,&quot; and BtP offers a personification of that conflict (dialectic?). What your Beast &quot;is&quot; is completely up to the player. They themselves gets to decide what kind of monster they are in a much more open-ended way than any of the other splats IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","user":"n_a_anyon","date":". 06-02-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:25:28-07:00","id":537381,"title":"","content":"I love Patrick and Ahmed from the Hunger for Punishment section far too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:31:03-07:00","id":537388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537358#post537358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Arc: Central themes just feel a bit muddy to me. I'm not sure what all the Begotten /do/ beyond sate their Hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, if sating hunger wasn't as important as it is, Gordon Ramsay wouldn't be on TV nearly as much. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:33:16-07:00","id":537393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537080#post537080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BlackHatMatt's Hunger is confirmed. He's a Collector of our Kickstarter money.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope. I get a very small percentage of that. <br /> <br /> My Hunger is Actual Play reports. Get on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:34:49-07:00","id":537395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537237#post537237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lobbying again for a &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; chapter pdf, and a Dark Era chapter pdf to be stretch goals!</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, I would love to see how Hunters have to deal with Heroes mucking up the place.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck your story. Fuck your insane antics. God damn it, we want to study the damn thing! Not kill it!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:37:48-07:00","id":537397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537344#post537344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Then why are you so desperately diving into the Fallen World?&quot; says the Collector of Secrets with a toothy grin.<br /> <br /> Mages are just as hungry as anyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh you know we all like to think that we are better than monsters, even if we have little bit of them in us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:43:47-07:00","id":537401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537393#post537393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope. I get a very small percentage of that. <br /> <br /> My Hunger is Actual Play reports. Get on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Now* I understand what all that bone chilling laughter was about when I sent you our playtest write ups...<br /> <br /> It seems so obvious in hindsight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:44:38-07:00","id":537404,"title":"","content":"God damn, do I love the Inheritances, particularly the Incarnates. Strider, your many nights of stressing paid off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:57:06-07:00","id":537411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537401#post537401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Now* I understand what all that bone chilling laughter was about when I sent you our playtest write ups...<br /> <br /> It seems so obvious in hindsight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kept hearing low chuckling every time we met. I thought Strider had ghosts or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T14:26:46-07:00","id":537429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537372#post537372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Primordial Dream offers a lot of opportunity to take campaigns beyond satisfying individual hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what? They seem to be able to get into the Primordial Dream, but I'm not seeing anything on what to do there, or what it's like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T14:38:40-07:00","id":537434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537404#post537404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God damn, do I love the Inheritances, particularly the Incarnates. Strider, your many nights of stressing paid off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, sir!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:19:26-07:00","id":537452,"title":"","content":"Debating on if I want to go in on this. I'm working my way through the preview and not feeling it as much as I'd like to. I'm picking up on two dominant tones so far wrt Beasts: one of innocence and one that's very unapologetic. I feel like this would be fine except Beasts are predators by nature and an innocent, unapologetic predator is going to start feeling <i>really</i> dissonant <i>really</i> quick if you aren't careful. (For example, it feels like the text is reluctant to acknowledge that anyone would have a good/rational reason for wanting to kill a Beast.) <br /> <br /> There's also some pretty unsettling implications when Heroes start getting compared to oppressors of various stripes. If the villain is depicted as a M'ladying, fedora-wearing MRA, what does that make his nemesis, the primordial, kinda-sadistic-deep-down, nightmare monster that feeds on people/ruin/power/etc? And what does it say when that kind of villain's target is also the reason that villain exists in the first place? I feel like whoever wrote that part of the Hero stuff's intentions were in the right place and I get what they were going for, but it really rubs me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a more positive note, the general concept is pretty interesting and I really dig Lairs and some of the powers (a few are a bit too gonzo for me, but that's just taste so its not a big deal). Also major bonus points for including that X-Card/safeword sidebar. Haven't finished reading up on Inheritances and the crossover stuff, but what I've seen so far also looks interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:33:00-07:00","id":537463,"title":"","content":"Can we get a Beast: The Primordial forum or something, now that we have the text and the Kickstarter is going?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:36:03-07:00","id":537467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537452#post537452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debating on if I want to go in on this. I'm working my way through the preview and not feeling it as much as I'd like to. I'm picking up on two dominant tones so far wrt Beasts: one of innocence and one that's very unapologetic. I feel like this would be fine except Beasts are predators by nature and an innocent, unapologetic predator is going to start feeling <i>really</i> dissonant <i>really</i> quick if you aren't careful. (For example, it feels like the text is reluctant to acknowledge that anyone would have a good/rational reason for wanting to kill a Beast.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, the first paragraph where Heroes are mentioned?<br /> <br /> They explicitly state that if Heroes were more self-aware and less egotistical, the Beasts really wouldn't hate them so much. They fully admit they <i>are </i>the bad guys, and that means there's not any real answer to the question of their existence. It's natural for humans to want to kill the Other, and the Begotten are the reason that instinct exists.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Heroes want all the perks of being the good guy without any of the responsibilities. They're not the dogged but proud Bat-family and Starks, trying desperately to keep to honor and virtue in a world that rewards treachery and vice. They're the Tribulation Militia and Mary Sues reveling in power and carte blanche to be &quot;the protagonists&quot; in a world not written by someone who buys into their narcissism.<br /> <br /> Particularly the Militia. After all, Nicolae Carpathia makes an excellent Beast, what with using his demonic inheritance and Hunger for Power to enforce world peace and mutual understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:38:03-07:00","id":537468,"title":"","content":"I'm at the hungers in the preview.<br /> <br /> I do believe that my corpus was insufficiently prepared for the shear amount of awe inspiring content within said file.<br /> <br /> I both fear and anticipate the final product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:53:31-07:00","id":537479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537463#post537463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get a Beast: The Primordial forum or something, now that we have the text and the Kickstarter is going?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was actually anticipating that the start of the Kickstarter would be when Onyx Path decided it was forum time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ah, well. Maybe soon!<br /> <br /> That being said: I'm outlandishly excited about this. This will be the first Kickstarter I've ever participated in and I couldn't be happier. This might have something to do with the &quot;Add a corebook for 15 dollars&quot; part. And also the Storyteller screen. It's like some kind of Second Edition shopping center and it's <i>amazing</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T16:14:39-07:00","id":537487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537429#post537429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like what? They seem to be able to get into the Primordial Dream, but I'm not seeing anything on what to do there, or what it's like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, one of the obvious routes would be to place the Primordial Dream at the center of your world's cosmology, so any sort of &quot;mysteries of the universe&quot; stories could take place there. Or maybe the Dark Mother is hiding there, and your Brood has to seek her out for some reason (a necessary step to reach Incarnate status perhaps). Maybe there's a way to burrow into an antagonist Beast's Lair by traveling through the Dream, but the Dream is where the things live that even Beasts fear... Maybe a Beast who hungers for power can use the Primordial Dream to (try to) grow their Lair into some sort of pan-supernatural hegemony.<br /> <br /> But personally, I like the small scale stories Beast is offering. Hunger, fear, self-preservation. These are universal things, and I appreciate the new spin on them that BtP is providing. There is no Beast society, but Beasts can participate in the societies of the other splats for their own reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T16:25:44-07:00","id":537494,"title":"","content":"At the risk of stealing Beast's thunder, I have to say I have the idea swimming in my head about a Hunter compact which uses lobotomized Heroes to hunt down Beasts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:02:42-07:00","id":537518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537452#post537452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debating on if I want to go in on this. I'm working my way through the preview and not feeling it as much as I'd like to. I'm picking up on two dominant tones so far wrt Beasts: one of innocence and one that's very unapologetic. I feel like this would be fine except Beasts are predators by nature and an innocent, unapologetic predator is going to start feeling <i>really</i> dissonant <i>really</i> quick if you aren't careful. (For example, it feels like the text is reluctant to acknowledge that anyone would have a good/rational reason for wanting to kill a Beast.)<br /> <br /> There's also some pretty unsettling implications when Heroes start getting compared to oppressors of various stripes. If the villain is depicted as a M'ladying, fedora-wearing MRA, what does that make his nemesis, the primordial, kinda-sadistic-deep-down, nightmare monster that feeds on people/ruin/power/etc? And what does it say when that kind of villain's target is also the reason that villain exists in the first place? I feel like whoever wrote that part of the Hero stuff's intentions were in the right place and I get what they were going for, but it really rubs me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a more positive note, the general concept is pretty interesting and I really dig Lairs and some of the powers (a few are a bit too gonzo for me, but that's just taste so its not a big deal). Also major bonus points for including that X-Card/safeword sidebar. Haven't finished reading up on Inheritances and the crossover stuff, but what I've seen so far also looks interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I completely agree -- I'm really enjoying the mechanics and powers Beasts have access too -- and it's nice to return to a very down-to-earth them, like &quot;EAT EVERYTHING&quot; (not that Mummy and Promethean's themes aren't engaging, but sometimes you just need a game about eating stuff, okay?) but the way Heros have been handled so far kind of make me go &quot;. . .Ugh?&quot; -- especially seeing Durga listed as inspiration for Heroes, which just seems really. . . inappropriate, given that she's kind of a very loved part of a very alive religion (and very large religion) -- tying her to the villains seems kind of like a bad step. Then making those villains <i>incredibly</i> flat . . . *sighs*<br /> <br /> But on top of that, the whole write up for Heroes is just very . . . under-nuanced. At least with Banishers, you got motives that made sense, but the writing for Heroes just makes me wince whenever I see them mentioned now. The write ups for Heroes read almost like really bad comedy, more than anything.<br /> <br /> I'm torn. On the one hand, a game that makes it possible to literally play a unicorn, but on the other . . . Heroes as written make me really uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:08:35-07:00","id":537520,"title":"","content":"There's a preview? Did I miss something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"}