page, there's a link to the &quot;99% complete&quot; preview document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:12:07-07:00","id":537524,"title":"","content":"KICKSTARTER \\o/<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/beast-the-primordial-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...estige-edition</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:19:17-07:00","id":537526,"title":"","content":"I've been adoring everything, Beasts and Heroes and all so far without any reservation. Still reading into Chapter 3.<br /> <br /> The only place where I would have done things a little differently is to give some more Legend and Life examples, but I understand the demands of wordcount on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:20:57-07:00","id":537527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537518#post537518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree -- I'm really enjoying the mechanics and powers Beasts have access too -- and it's nice to return to a very down-to-earth them, like &quot;EAT EVERYTHING&quot; (not that Mummy and Promethean's themes aren't engaging, but sometimes you just need a game about eating stuff, okay?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which puts me in an interesting predicament, considering <b>Promethean</b> and <b>Mummy</b> are my two favorite lines. In some ways <b>Beast</b> is a welcome refreshment where it not only slides to the other end of the spectrum, but it crashes right through it and does a pose at the end.<br /> <br /> In some ways I wish the tone was more unashamed and they didn't try to justify the 'goodness' of Beasts or the 'badness' of Heroes so much. It's okay to play 'the evil campaign' once in a while. I'm mostly with atamajakki, though, except I think the game is kinda cool (having read the leak in April) and I'll still back it for the pdf...and get the <b>Promethean</b> 2e core out of it as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:24:04-07:00","id":537529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the Beast: the Primordial Kickstarter Draft</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Void is Waiting</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Xc90UhV6hJA?t=3s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Xc90UhV6hJA?t=3s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Xc90UhV6hJA?t=3s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Xc90UhV6hJA?t=3s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-03-2015, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:26:27-07:00","id":537531,"title":"","content":"Apparently my bale hound has been an Anakim Tyrant-Collector-Predator-Ravager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:47:47-07:00","id":537539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537527#post537527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which puts me in an interesting predicament, considering <b>Promethean</b> and <b>Mummy</b> are my two favorite lines. In some ways <b>Beast</b> is a welcome refreshment where it not only slides to the other end of the spectrum, but it crashes right through it and does a pose at the end.<br /> <br /> In some ways I wish the tone was more unashamed and they didn't try to justify the 'goodness' of Beasts or the 'badness' of Heroes so much. It's okay to play 'the evil campaign' once in a while. I'm mostly with atamajakki, though, except I think the game is kinda cool (having read the leak in April) and I'll still back it for the pdf...and get the <b>Promethean</b> 2e core out of it as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean and Mummy are both excellent lines, and very, very story centered, which is always great -- but Beast does make a good palate cleanser between the two, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I agree -- I think Beast tries too hard to follow in the footsteps of Demon or Mummy, by having definite go-to villains who are definitely badder than the main characters at least, but the concept would work a lot better if Beasts were either allowed to just be monsters or legitimately had a deeper premise than &quot;hungry for nightmares&quot;.<br /> <br /> In game terms, Beast's Satiety is at about 5. It's not hungry enough to go for broke, but not full enough to provide deeper material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:03:06-07:00","id":537574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537518#post537518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I completely agree -- I'm really enjoying the mechanics and powers Beasts have access too -- and it's nice to return to a very down-to-earth them, like &quot;EAT EVERYTHING&quot; (not that Mummy and Promethean's themes aren't engaging, but sometimes you just need a game about eating stuff, okay?) but the way Heros have been handled so far kind of make me go &quot;. . .Ugh?&quot; -- especially seeing Durga listed as inspiration for Heroes, which just seems really. . . inappropriate, given that she's kind of a very loved part of a very alive religion (and very large religion) -- tying her to the villains seems kind of like a bad step. Then making those villains <i>incredibly</i> flat . . . *sighs*<br /> <br /> But on top of that, the whole write up for Heroes is just very . . . under-nuanced. <b>At least with Banishers, you got motives that made sense,</b> but the writing for Heroes just makes me wince whenever I see them mentioned now. The write ups for Heroes read almost like really bad comedy, more than anything.<br /> <br /> I'm torn. On the one hand, a game that makes it possible to literally play a unicorn, but on the other . . . Heroes as written make me really uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bold part is making me tilt my head.<br /> <br /> The Storytelling chapter put this out in plain English; they're conspiracy theorists turned vicious, and they desperately need something, anything, to make them feel like their life has a point and a purpose. Given how said purpose is <i>murderhoboing, </i>they're never really sane or nuanced about it. That's a motive that makes perfect sense, even if it depends on a rather illogical thought process.<br /> <br /> Watch <i>Steven Universe</i>, specifically that episode Keep Beach City Weird. Ronaldo Fryman? Yep, he's a Hero, and as Pearl pointed out rather bluntly, his ultimate motive for pursuing the sneople is selfish; he wants to feel more important than he is.<br /> <br /> That doesn't change the fact you kinda have to feel sorry for Ronaldo; he's ultimately a rather sad individual, because of just how desperate he is for his life to be meaningful after it kind of fell apart. It also shows how he can be <i>really dangerous, </i>because his personal mythology allows him to do very murderous and stupid things in pursuit of &quot;freeing humanity from serpent person oppression.&quot;<br /> <br /> I see Heroes in largely the same way; broken, desperate people who have latched on to a very dark way of thought because it's better than being as they are. I outright pity two out of the three examples (Miriam and Sleeping Beauty).<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Heroes can't be real asses as well (the one out of three I don't pity, and in fact rather laugh at).<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that most of the book, barring the part on Heroes from the perspective of Heroes, is written from the view of Begotten, who it should be mentioned, <i>are the people Heroes are trying to kill. </i>That tends to bias people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:20:38-07:00","id":537588,"title":"","content":"Second thing that makes me go 'huh' is how short the default lifespan of a Beast is. I was honestly expecting longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:21:23-07:00","id":537589,"title":"","content":"It does expressly state that heroes are broken, degraded individuals, before the nightmares of the Beasts spurred them into action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:29:42-07:00","id":537590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537539#post537539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree -- I think Beast tries too hard to follow in the footsteps of Demon or Mummy, by having definite go-to villains who are definitely badder than the main characters at least, but the concept would work a lot better if Beasts were either allowed to just be monsters or <u>legitimately had a deeper premise than &quot;hungry for nightmares&quot;</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I keep thinking, &quot;...and then what?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages explore Mysteries. Werewolves must Hunt. Beasts feed their Hunger. Okay, and then what?<br /> <br /> Vampires do a lot more than just suck blood - they have to figure out what to do with themselves for the next few centuries while they degenerate into monsters trying to retain a shred of Humanity. Beasts, though, largely seem content with their lot in life - in fact, it's pretty explicit that their lives sucked <i>before</i> they had their Homecoming and, now that they've had it, things make more sense and are more <i>comfortable</i>.<br /> <br /> The Incarnates are really cool but, with the <b>Vampire</b> analogy again, how rare is it for a Beast to seek or achieve them? Vampires have some vague legendary Golconda but a lot of <b>Mummy</b>'s themes are balanced by the possibility of Apotheosis and the steep cost of eternal, miraculous power.<br /> <br /> Even their reason for getting involved with other splats seems to boil down to them being nosy and saying, &quot;Hey, we're family, right? So what're you guys up to?&quot; with no greater reason.<br /> <br /> I think Beasts are really cool - the powers, Lair, Incarnates, Kinship - but I guess it's hard for me to imagine a two year long campaign of the game, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:34:59-07:00","id":537593,"title":"","content":"My gut feeling is that Beast works better in an episodic format unless you want to really flesh out the setting to get them involved in supernatural politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T18:57:00-07:00","id":537605,"title":"","content":"Jesus, this thing updated fast! 6 pages since I last checked!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:14:39-07:00","id":537622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537217#post537217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/beast-the-primordial-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...estige-edition</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Dude, I love the pic in the video where the werewolf is approaching the guy who's just chilling with a dragon behind him. Oh and what I can only guess is a personal harem at his feet.<br /> <br /> Although unfortunately the music becomes excessively loud near the end of the video, I had to strain to understand the narrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2015, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:26:28-07:00","id":537637,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I'm surprised the Ephemeral being rules in the book cover Angels instead of something like Astral Entities. I see the latter being far more likely to occur in a Beast game than the former...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:35:26-07:00","id":537639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537590#post537590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I keep thinking, &quot;...and then what?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages explore Mysteries. Werewolves must Hunt. Beasts feed their Hunger. Okay, and then what?<br /> <br /> Vampires do a lot more than just suck blood - they have to figure out what to do with themselves for the next few centuries while they degenerate into monsters trying to retain a shred of Humanity. Beasts, though, largely seem content with their lot in life - in fact, it's pretty explicit that their lives sucked <i>before</i> they had their Homecoming and, now that they've had it, things make more sense and are more <i>comfortable</i>.<br /> <br /> The Incarnates are really cool but, with the <b>Vampire</b> analogy again, how rare is it for a Beast to seek or achieve them? Vampires have some vague legendary Golconda but a lot of <b>Mummy</b>'s themes are balanced by the possibility of Apotheosis and the steep cost of eternal, miraculous power.<br /> <br /> Even their reason for getting involved with other splats seems to boil down to them being nosy and saying, &quot;Hey, we're family, right? So what're you guys up to?&quot; with no greater reason.<br /> <br /> I think Beasts are really cool - the powers, Lair, Incarnates, Kinship - but I guess it's hard for me to imagine a two year long campaign of the game, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>They become FAMILY. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beasts are compose of Broods - and those all hail to the Dark Mother. I envision you make your Brood, your mythos, and become LEGEND of it ( like how every story need a big bad monster - and it's you now ). You can join the other supernaturals societies and work with them for the&quot;re-engagment&quot; them to the cause of Dark Mother ( think about Circle of Crones-like missionaries ). OR you build your family with other Beasts - and you longer the species. I think, that on the outside, &quot;the later&quot; part of the <b>Beast</b> game is a soup opera mixed with organized crime thriller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Johnny, you reskined your life, you are monster under childrens bed, you sate your Hunger with their fears. What will you do now?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Now I will find mine bride, And then, we will have many, many, many more Johnny's to take care of. And <b><i><u>then</u></i></b> we will take up the city! Cosa Nostra!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Family IS Primodial - it's fundation of every society cell. Tell me, what kind of stories you can talk about your family only? About your grandprnets seazing teritory in hometown? About how your fathers show love to your mother? How you all had taught times when neighbors from around come to your land and demand part of it? About your wierd cousin join cult and you all need to save him?<br /> <br /> And now on this family-themed stories put an incarnation of base fears and Primodial Dream. Add some <b>Mage</b>-like &quot;Astral&quot; shenigans. And here you got your next story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I'm Hungry - I need to consume so Hopes and Secrets. Be right back! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-02-2015, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:50:23-07:00","id":537651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537590#post537590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I keep thinking, &amp;quot;...and then what?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Mages explore Mysteries. Werewolves must Hunt. Beasts feed their Hunger. Okay, and then what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then\u2026 Family? Aside from their Hunger, the single biggest thematic element I got out of Beast is that these guys desperately do not want to be <i>alone</i>. One might reasonably say that they're willing to consider people \u201cfamily&quot; who <i>hate their guts</i> and who actively work against them \u2014 heck, they even show a modicum of sympathy toward the Heroes who hunt them! (Though the latter sympathy quickly gets trumped by \u201cif only they weren't so narcissistic and deluded\u201d.)<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> get where you're coming from, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537637#post537637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I'm surprised the Ephemeral being rules in the book cover Angels instead of something like Astral Entities. I see the latter being far more likely to occur in a Beast game than the former...</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I'm guessing that Angels made it in because the rules were copy-pasted from GMC; but I would strongly recommend excising Angels and replacing them with Astral Entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:54:39-07:00","id":537655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537651#post537651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. I'm guessing that Angels made it in because the rules were copy-pasted from GMC; but I would strongly recommend excising Angels and replacing them with Astral Entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have to agree here. A lot. Hopefully it's not too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:00:02-07:00","id":537658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537651#post537651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. I'm guessing that Angels made it in because the rules were copy-pasted from GMC; but I would strongly recommend excising Angels and replacing them with Astral Entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thought too. Dunno if it's too late for such a major change though. Though I guess it'd just be copy pasting from a different book instead (Mage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:14:25-07:00","id":537675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537574#post537574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should also be noted that most of the book, barring the part on Heroes from the perspective of Heroes, is written from the view of Begotten, who it should be mentioned, <i>are the people Heroes are trying to kill. </i>That tends to bias people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's the parts that aren't from the perspective of the Beasts which bother me the most. The writers make it very clear that if you want to a sympathetic antagonist, or even one who just undergoes personal growth of any kind, you should not use Heroes. It's kind of baffling, seeing as its the opposite of the approach basically used by every other New World of Darkness line. I could see it as a small antagonist group (like something in a Night Horrors supplement), but this is the major antagonist group for the gameline, and by writer edict they must be weak-willed losers incapable of actual friendship (or even wishing they could). That's kind of weird, and I wish there was some way I could find out why.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, I'm really glad you found two of the example Hunters to be sympathetic. I really left that chapter feeling like it was a bit hypocritical for the game to be so anti-intolerance while also providing a group of people who basically should all be killed. Also, I like the Anathema mechanics. A lot of the Hero mechanics are pretty cool, and that's of course on top of the Beast stuff. I think if I can get the money together, I'll buy the book and just refluff Heroes so they can potentially be round, dynamic characters, instead of... I don't know, magical 4chan stereotypes? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Man, this paragraph went the opposite of how I wanted it to.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:20:04-07:00","id":537677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537675#post537675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it's the parts that aren't from the perspective of the Beasts which bother me the most. The writers make it very clear that if you want to a sympathetic antagonist, or even one who just undergoes personal growth of any kind, you should not use Heroes. It's kind of baffling, seeing as its the opposite of the approach basically used by every other New World of Darkness line. I could see it as a small antagonist group (like something in a Night Horrors supplement), but this is the major antagonist group for the gameline, and by writer edict they must be weak-willed losers incapable of actual friendship (or even wishing they could). That's kind of weird, and I wish there was some way I could find out why.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, I'm really glad you found two of the example Hunters to be sympathetic. I really left that chapter feeling like it was a bit hypocritical for the game to be so anti-intolerance while also providing a group of people who basically should all be killed. Also, I like the Anathema mechanics. A lot of the Hero mechanics are pretty cool, and that's of course on top of the Beast stuff. I think if I can get the money together, I'll buy the book and just refluff Heroes so they can potentially be round, dynamic characters, instead of... I don't know, magical 4chan stereotypes? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Man, this paragraph went the opposite of how I wanted it to.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I suspect the writers were in kind of an internal war. On the one hand, you have Matt's utter hatred of egotists and bigots of all stripes (I <i>assume </i>it's him writing the Storytelling chapter given his posts on RPGnet), but on the other, you have whoever recognized that a Hero got like that by being a fundamentally broken person who often was a direct victim by a callous or reckless Beast.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I suspect there may have been a bit of dissonance over the writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:20:30-07:00","id":537678,"title":"","content":"Nightmares guven form stalk the world, preying upon the fear and flesh alike of the common man. Brave sorts arise to stop the threat... and they're the bad guys?<br /> <br /> Heroes don't feel &quot;bad&quot; in any way ityer than the game telling us to view them as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:25:34-07:00","id":537679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537675#post537675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers make it very clear that if you want to a sympathetic antagonist, or even one who just undergoes personal growth of any kind, you should not use Heroes. It's kind of baffling, seeing as its the opposite of the approach basically used by every other New World of Darkness line.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of Heroes is that they're narcissistic psychopaths who refuse to take responsibility for their lives and who can only validate themselves by acting like textbook abusers because it's the only way they can feel good about themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:31:50-07:00","id":537683,"title":"","content":"They really don't seem like psychopaths or even textbook abusers, though narcissistic certainly fits. The very act of being a Hero seems like they're taking responsibility for their lives, in the face of the threat of the Beast.<br /> <br /> One can't even be a Hero without suffering several breaking points, meaning they're usually witnesses or victims of horrible trauma. The Collector's Hero seems like a Beast with a Hunger for Punishment. The Predator's Hero is someone who refuses to suffer any more abuse, the Tyrant's refuses to 'know their place.' The Nemeses' and Ravager's Heroes seem more selfishly malign.<br /> <br /> Someone said earlier in this thread that the book is mostly from the point of view of the Beasts, and so it is biased. I'm not sure if that's true, but it seems to be, with the constant talking down of Heroes. But considering the soul of Heroes have been overwhelmed by the Beast, it being no more their fault than the Beast becoming a Beast, and the only way to stop it from happening is killing Beasts, as well as the fact that they can be 'cured' and go on to become a hunter or maybe just live a normal life by getting more than 4 Integrity, they're not exactly unsympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-02-2015, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:32:28-07:00","id":537684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537678#post537678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes don't feel &quot;bad&quot; in any way ityer than the game telling us to view them as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the impression I got from reading the book at all, which includes explicit statements as the motives and behavioral tendencies of Heroes which are decidedly rather monstrous. I'm not sure why anyone gets your impression from it.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying your impression is necessarily wrong, but I don't just can't see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:44:19-07:00","id":537688,"title":"","content":"Maybe we can get some stereotype quotes/interstitial fiction that has Beasts doing things other than chuckle paternally at the &quot;poor ignorant fools&quot; that everyone who isn't that Beast or Brood specifically are or constantly blame their victims? I almost feel like it's not the <i>Heroes</i> who are narcissistic sociopaths. If they're all supposed to have this &quot;family&quot; theme, the Beast fiction and quotes so far are from that one relative who thinks the family would fall apart without them and in reality the only thing that keeps the family together is their mutual disgust at how pathetically idiotic said relative is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:57:09-07:00","id":537704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537688#post537688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we can get some stereotype quotes/interstitial fiction that has Beasts doing things other than chuckle paternally at the &quot;poor ignorant fools&quot; that everyone who isn't that Beast or Brood specifically are or constantly blame their victims? I almost feel like it's not the <i>Heroes</i> who are narcissistic sociopaths. If they're all supposed to have this &quot;family&quot; theme, the Beast fiction and quotes so far are from that one relative who thinks the family would fall apart without them and in reality the only thing that keeps the family together is their mutual disgust at how pathetically idiotic said relative is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I've been getting from the write up. The Hero in the Courtroom especially (and the entire article leading up to it) has a Beast goading the Hero to act like a misogynistic hateful monster. All of this <i>after</i> you realize that Heroes are <i><b>victims </b></i>of the Beast. &quot;we realize we're crazy&quot; the beasts say, well duh, you <b>chose </b>this lot. The heroes are poor lonely bastards you <i>drove to madness </i>and then continue to poke at. <br /> <br /> I brought to mind ex-cons who were goaded by POs and arresting officers into breaking their parole 'because they're the bad guy'. <br /> <br /> Add to that the fact that the Beasts bragging about how Happy they are but keep crying victim <i>while eating people</i> just rubs me wrong.<br /> <br /> I really wanted to love this game, and the system is <i><b>GREAT </b></i>but between the game making me actually root for the 'bad guy' (when did horror games from the point of view of the monster get bad-guys instead of antagonists?) and the uneven writing I'm not sure I want to back this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:08:02-07:00","id":537709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537238#post537238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all supernaturals are family of the beast? interesting perspective. However my mage would say to the beast that he does not need to terrorize people and feed on their nightmares to survive. They have nothing in common, at all. After that he would give the beast the middle finger and prepare himself to wipe out this unholy abomination from the face of the earth, making sure that it does not hurt people ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Neither do beasts, they can vicariously feed off of the mage regaining mana from meditation or eating literal magic mushrooms. <br /> <br /> And of course, if the beast is in the know about mags, can reply &quot;Pretty funny, you guys judging us. We're beasts, inhuman souls in human bodies, and we can feed our hunger without hurting anyone if we so choose. But you? You lot are 100% human, you guys include people who choose to step on the collective neck of the world for a good 401K package, and mages who turn to cannibalism and soul consumption for no other reason than you can choose to do so. <br /> <br /> So which of our peoples are the monsters here? The monsters who can choose to be benign, or the humans who choose to be monsters?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:12:49-07:00","id":537714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537709#post537709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So which of our peoples are the monsters here? The monsters who can choose to be benign, or the humans who choose to be monsters?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you answer, 'Not <i>all </i>Beasts,' with, 'Not <i>all </i>humans.'?<br /> <br /> The writing is a bit uneven, which may be what's causing the different views on things.<br /> <br /> But the game is what it is, you play a Beast, a true nightmare in the flesh of a person. You get to terrorize without losing your Humanity. You can eat people without worrying about the Oath of the Moon. Use your powers to do what you want without losing Wisdom and so forth, unless you want to use it to fuel your power and make it really nasty. You're not on a quest to become human. You're not running from your tormentor. You're not running from your other tormentor. You're not caught in an eternal cycle of memory loss and the demands of a lost homeland. You get to be a monster.<br /> <br /> Heroes can clearly be sympathetic, but above all they're obsessed with killing you, and that's the part that matters to a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-03-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:14:17-07:00","id":537717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537677#post537677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I suspect the writers were in kind of an internal war. On the one hand, you have Matt's utter hatred of egotists and bigots of all stripes (I <i>assume </i>it's him writing the Storytelling chapter given his posts on RPGnet), but on the other, you have whoever recognized that a Hero got like that by being a fundamentally broken person who often was a direct victim by a callous or reckless Beast.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I suspect there may have been a bit of dissonance over the writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wrote the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> Honestly? The way I see it, Heroes aren't inherently, black or white bad. Sometimes they're totally in the right. In my experience with playing Beast so far, the problem with Heroes isn't that they're wrong and bad and whatever, it's that they're doing it for the wrong reasons. They're going after Beasts &quot;because they're monsters&quot;, not because of their individual behaviours. They're doing it for what ultimately amounts to ideology, which is right the same way a broken clock is. Does everyone that does bad things deserve to be slain? No. Heroes are not creatures of compromise and nuance, and that's their utter failing. <br /> <br /> This is my opinion, mind you. I wrote Storytelling. I didn't write the actual text on Heroes. But that's the ethos I took with me when I was writing how to make their actions work within the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:16:03-07:00","id":537718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537704#post537704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly what I've been getting from the write up. The Hero in the Courtroom especially (and the entire article leading up to it) has a Beast goading the Hero to act like a misogynistic hateful monster. All of this <i>after</i> you realize that Heroes are <i><b>victims </b></i>of the Beast. &quot;we realize we're crazy&quot; the beasts say, well duh, you <b>chose </b>this lot. The heroes are poor lonely bastards you <i>drove to madness </i>and then continue to poke at.<br /> <br /> I brought to mind ex-cons who were goaded by POs and arresting officers into breaking their parole 'because they're the bad guy'.<br /> <br /> Add to that the fact that the Beasts bragging about how Happy they are but keep crying victim <i>while eating people</i> just rubs me wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um...where do they play victim?<br /> <br /> They state outright in the beginning that Beasts accept that the <i>idea </i>of a Hero is an okay one, humans have a right to defend themselves. <br /> <br /> And that Courtroom scene?<br /> <br /> I think you've been taken in by the Unreliable Narrator mate. And the fact that Hero <i>explicitly mentioned </i>he killed that lady's brood and/or friends.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it may be a dick move <i>if things happened that way, </i>but it's not one born out of a motive to torture him (not purely, anyway)-it's revenge against someone who already hurt her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:29:03-07:00","id":537726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537717#post537717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually wrote the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> Honestly? The way I see it, Heroes aren't inherently, black or white bad. Sometimes they're totally in the right. In my experience with playing Beast so far, the problem with Heroes isn't that they're wrong and bad and whatever, it's that they're doing it for the wrong reasons. They're going after Beasts &quot;because they're monsters&quot;, not because of their individual behaviours. They're doing it for what ultimately amounts to ideology, which is right the same way a broken clock is. Does everyone that does bad things deserve to be slain? No. Heroes are not creatures of compromise and nuance, and that's their utter failing.<br /> <br /> This is my opinion, mind you. I wrote Storytelling. I didn't write the actual text on Heroes. But that's the ethos I took with me when I was writing how to make their actions work within the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saving my ability to enjoy being part of this discussion. That's an excellent, and much more well-worded explanation of what I took from the earlier chapters' descriptions of Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:29:37-07:00","id":537727,"title":"","content":"Hunters aren't mentioned in the Stereotypes? are they going to be part of the Hero antagonists?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:42:49-07:00","id":537736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537717#post537717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually wrote the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> Honestly? The way I see it, Heroes aren't inherently, black or white bad. Sometimes they're totally in the right. In my experience with playing Beast so far, the problem with Heroes isn't that they're wrong and bad and whatever, it's that they're doing it for the wrong reasons. They're going after Beasts &quot;because they're monsters&quot;, not because of their individual behaviours. They're doing it for what ultimately amounts to ideology, which is right the same way a broken clock is. Does everyone that does bad things deserve to be slain? No. Heroes are not creatures of compromise and nuance, and that's their utter failing.<br /> <br /> This is my opinion, mind you. I wrote Storytelling. I didn't write the actual text on Heroes. But that's the ethos I took with me when I was writing how to make their actions work within the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to include that in the final printing. It seem to fly over a lot of people's heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:45:04-07:00","id":537738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537727#post537727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters aren't mentioned in the Stereotypes? are they going to be part of the Hero antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the third chapter. There is a lengthy section that details the difference between the two.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:45:50-07:00","id":537739,"title":"","content":"The way I put earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult. Heroes wouldn't happen if Beasts didn't do their thing, but Beasts are driven by their Hunger to do what they do. Heroes often have to cope with Beasts by compensating and developing the jerkass mentality that elicits the &quot;Fuck Gaston&quot; mentality, but on the other hand, it's in response to being exposed to the Beast's Hunger, and in fact you could almost describe it as the Hunger lightly infecting them...and it's not like Beast's hunger don't drive them to being gigantic pricks either.<br /> <br /> Older and wiser Beasts can accept it as just the way things are, the way of the world, but it's really hard to not see why any Beast could get personally invested in eating the heart of a Hero.<br /> <br /> THe sad part, on Heroes side, is that they might be more or less incapable of ever reaching that state. Beasts fuck people up just to get by.<br /> <br /> But despite all the sympathy in the world for Heroes, I still kind of hate them, and it comes down to how much I think on a given day is the fault of the Beast. They give just as much as they take.<br /> <br /> It's a shit cycle with shit people on each side, I suppose is the easiest way to put it. This is very much a game where the best intentioned people will still get dragged down by their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T22:15:38-07:00","id":537753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a shit cycle with shit people on each side, I suppose is the easiest way to put it. This is very much a game where the best intentioned people will still get dragged down by their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; and that's pretty much why, since the revival of the new World of Darkness started, this will be the first new gameline that I will not be buying. No offense to those of you who are enjoying it; but I'm simply not finding anything in it that I can latch on to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-03-2015, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T22:21:24-07:00","id":537759,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's not a cheery game. This is the splat where the <i>best </i>victory condition (aside from &quot;die of old age&quot;) is you becoming an exceedingly alien monster-god through the power of cosmic horror stories.<br /> <br /> The sorry state of the Heroes plays into the dour mood, which is part of the reason I don't mind it so much.<br /> <br /> Though, I realized; it's not actually that harmful to a Hero's self-image if they realize they're the ones invoking Anathema (&quot;Holy shit, I'm taking ancient gobbledygook and turning it true through the power of thought and justice! This is awesome!&quot;). Does make me wonder what happens if they become more self-aware about it (I'd say they easy lose access to a couple of the mind-altering ones, because the realization they're just making the Beast act that way awkwardly raises the question of how, but gain the ability to choose what Anathema they'd prefer).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T22:30:19-07:00","id":537761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537759#post537759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's not a cheery game. This is the splat where the <i>best </i>victory condition (aside from \u201cdie of old age\u201d) is you becoming an exceedingly alien monster-god through the power of cosmic horror stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>That's</i> an understatement. Prior to this, <b>Vampire</b> was my least favorite of the nWoD gamelines, because it was so depressing. But compared to <b>Beast</b>, it's positively upbeat! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537759#post537759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sorry state of the Heroes plays into the dour mood, which is part of the reason I don't mind it so much.<br /> <br /> Though, I realized; it's not actually that harmful to a Hero's self-image if they realize they're the ones invoking Anathema (\u201cHoly shit, I'm taking ancient gobbledygook and turning it true through the power of thought and justice! This is awesome!\u201d). Does make me wonder what happens if they become more self-aware about it (I'd say they easy lose access to a couple of the mind-altering ones, because the realization they're just making the Beast act that way awkwardly raises the question of how, but gain the ability to choose what Anathema they'd prefer).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if they're real jerks (which seems to be the theme), they'll do it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T22:42:05-07:00","id":537782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537759#post537759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's not a cheery game. This is the splat where the <i>best </i>victory condition (aside from &quot;die of old age&quot;) is you becoming an exceedingly alien monster-god through the power of cosmic horror stories.<br /> <br /> The sorry state of the Heroes plays into the dour mood, which is part of the reason I don't mind it so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy it all so very much. Although I admit my initial draw to the game is, and somewhat remains, its potential for facilitating Crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:02:50-07:00","id":537798,"title":"","content":"Reading over the PDF I came across the Tyrants and thought about Sabertooth. How he tracked down Wolverine every year on his &quot;birthday&quot; and beat the crap out of him. Mmmm, hold me closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:16:01-07:00","id":537800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537759#post537759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's not a cheery game. This is the splat where the <i>best </i>victory condition (aside from &quot;die of old age&quot;) is you becoming an exceedingly alien monster-god through the power of cosmic horror stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could just cut the beast soul loose and be free from you.<br /> <br /> Reduces you to a puny human but that has advantages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:27:31-07:00","id":537803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537800#post537800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could just cut the beast soul loose and be free from you.<br /> <br /> Reduces you to a puny human but that has advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you had to die for that one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:36:12-07:00","id":537818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537803#post537803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you had to die for that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently there's a point where Beasts reach a point called inheritance. At this junction there are 3 ways a Beast can end up going. Sometimes the Beast ends up overwhelming the human portion and the two are merged into a shadowy nightmare figure haunting the primordial pathways. (The Unfettered) There's retreat which basically causes the Beast to take a chunk out of the person's soul ,since it was actually part of their soul when they were born, but leaves the person behind in a sort of hollowed out state. The third is a mixed state where the Beast and Human merge into a glorious hole more than either essentially the pinnacle of legend and one of the more dangerous beings around. I will point out though that the pdf seems to give the indication that these choices are things that happen at the point of inheritance,so it isn't like one of the begotten can just sever their Beast whenever they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:39:12-07:00","id":537820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537651#post537651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then\u2026 Family? Aside from their Hunger, the single biggest thematic element I got out of Beast is that these guys desperately do not want to be <i>alone</i>. One might reasonably say that they're willing to consider people \u201cfamily&quot; who <i>hate their guts</i> and who actively work against them \u2014 heck, they even show a modicum of sympathy toward the Heroes who hunt them! (Though the latter sympathy quickly gets trumped by \u201cif only they weren't so narcissistic and deluded\u201d.)<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> get where you're coming from, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which puts them at a weird thematic parallel with <b>Promethean</b>. The protagonists of <i>that</i> game don't want to be alone and yet that's all they get. Beasts, at worst, might not want to be alone but <i>they aren't</i> alone because they think every fucking thing under the sun is their relative except the Unchained <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So that either makes an interesting theme to play with in a crossover game or it means that <b>Beast</b> didn't really think through the themes in the way you're suggesting, for better or worse.<br /> <br /> But let's say it is &quot;then family.&quot; Even my post was saying that, if you indeed went that route, the game itself presents their interest in family more as 'nosy curiosity' rather than 'desperate avoidance of loneliness' which isn't a very strong theme to be a foundation of a game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:11:19-07:00","id":537824,"title":"","content":"The work and ideas you present have interested me. Please sir, take some of my money.<br /> <br /> By which I mean I'm in for $90.<br /> <br /> Aside, is the video worth watching? Or is it just a clip show of the art with a cringeworthy voiceover like every other kickstarter vid I've watched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:13:39-07:00","id":537844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537727#post537727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters aren't mentioned in the Stereotypes? are they going to be part of the Hero antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Some can be kin, like VASCU, the Lucifuge, maybe even Cheiron, Maleus Malificarum, or the Cainite Heresy, but most can't. Most of the Compacts have a passing interest, or become the unwitting dupes of Heroes, though, as I read it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:25:31-07:00","id":537847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537818#post537818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently there's a point where Beasts reach a point called inheritance. At this junction there are 3 ways a Beast can end up going. Sometimes the Beast ends up overwhelming the human portion and the two are merged into a shadowy nightmare figure haunting the primordial pathways. (The Unfettered) There's retreat which basically causes the Beast to take a chunk out of the person's soul ,since it was actually part of their soul when they were born, but leaves the person behind in a sort of hollowed out state. The third is a mixed state where the Beast and Human merge into a glorious hole more than either essentially the pinnacle of legend and one of the more dangerous beings around. I will point out though that the pdf seems to give the indication that these choices are things that happen at the point of inheritance,so it isn't like one of the begotten can just sever their Beast whenever they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Retreat and the Merger can be undertaken at any time (but honestly, why would you), while the Incarnation requires Lair 8 and destroying a Hero utterly without taking Lethal Damage or being struck by Anathema (tip: don't go for it with Satiety 5). It's easiest with a lot of planning and a Satiety below 3. It basically should play out like a war of assassins, until all he has left is his bare hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:25:40-07:00","id":537848,"title":"","content":"So after reading over the Kickstarter document. Damn....Beasts are far creepier than I was expecting. I want to make a Leviathan now. Might have to make this my first NWoD game I was won over to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:30:21-07:00","id":537850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537847#post537847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Retreat and the Merger can be undertaken at any time (but honestly, why would you), while the Incarnation requires Lair 8 and destroying a Hero utterly without taking Lethal Damage or being struck by Anathema (tip: don't go for it with Satiety 5). It's easiest with a lot of planning and a Satiety below 3. It basically should play out like a war of assassins, until all he has left is his bare hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the part of the pdf I'm at has only defined what they are not necessarily the mechanical rules attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:32:42-07:00","id":537851,"title":"","content":"just read the Kickstarter preview. I must say that I've found it really interesting- all of the families were wrote in a very appealing way, and the Atavisms are now one of the powers I like the most in WoD. I also liked all of the crossover sidebars, and that it presented both how the Beasts look on the other monsters and how those monsters look on Beasts (and in the case of Hunter, how they look on Heroes). The Inheritance was something I didn't expected, and I like it. Also- Japanese Lucifuge! I hope to see more of them in Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:41:26-07:00","id":537871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537522#post537522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, have I just not found it yet, or is there no Aura mechanic for Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's under Kinship. Family Resemblance allows you to spot other Supernaturals (although Unchained are harder and riskier to detect) and Passing Resemblance lets you disguise yourself as another template, provided you have established Kinship with them. These are all innate qualities of the Begotten template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:46:55-07:00","id":537874,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one mentions how Beasts are utter badasses at Dream travel, what with using their best Attributes and using their Trait limit to determine their effective Size and Corpus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T01:05:33-07:00","id":537880,"title":"","content":"I think everyone is just getting swallowed up by different parts. Once I'm done fantasizing about different feeding methods I'll have to check out their dream travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T02:03:16-07:00","id":537922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537874#post537874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised no one mentions how Beasts are utter badasses at Dream travel, what with using their best Attributes and using their Trait limit to determine their effective Size and Corpus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast also reveals how Dream/Astral Travel works in second edition games - which Changeling and Mage also use. No more using your Willpower as Health when in the Astral. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T02:33:40-07:00","id":537939,"title":"","content":"Didn't give much thought to the Gorgons, but after reading the kickstarter, I'm interested enough to try playing one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T03:04:31-07:00","id":537961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537803#post537803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you had to die for that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. To undergo the Retreat, the Beast must die. No hollowed-out human is left...well, unless you count the corpse, I suppose...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T03:07:07-07:00","id":537962,"title":"","content":"Funded in 16 hours! Sweet! <br /> <br /> I'm digging it so far. I know some people have said that this game doesn't really have hooks for them to sink into on first blush, but for me the supernatural relationships are more than enough. Beast may be a game of hunger, but the family theme really speaks to me. You could have a really neat game where the Beast considers its kin to be Ghosts, the Deceived, the Shuankhsen, or the Mad. There are plenty of ways to play with this game and twist it to tell nontraditional stories. <br /> <br /> I also notice that the new Integrity stat for Prometheans is Pilgrimage instead of Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T03:34:55-07:00","id":537972,"title":"","content":"Coming back to this in the light of day and yeah, the conflicting tones and the implications about The Other are definitely dealbreakers for me. Alas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537717#post537717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually wrote the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> Honestly? The way I see it, Heroes aren't inherently, black or white bad. Sometimes they're totally in the right. In my experience with playing Beast so far, the problem with Heroes isn't that they're wrong and bad and whatever, it's that they're doing it for the wrong reasons. They're going after Beasts &quot;because they're monsters&quot;, not because of their individual behaviours. They're doing it for what ultimately amounts to ideology, which is right the same way a broken clock is. Does everyone that does bad things deserve to be slain? No. Heroes are not creatures of compromise and nuance, and that's their utter failing.<br /> <br /> This is my opinion, mind you. I wrote Storytelling. I didn't write the actual text on Heroes. But that's the ethos I took with me when I was writing how to make their actions work within the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said earlier, bonus points for including X-Cards/safewords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T03:46:16-07:00","id":537977,"title":"","content":"Odd..... Somehow reading the Opening Chapter puts me in the Mind of Isaac from The Binding of Isaac.... It's his Homecoming.....<br /> <br /> Edit: And Now just Reading a Paragraph on the Dark Mother makes me think of Marmee Noir from Anita Blake series.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-03-2015, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:08:57-07:00","id":538135,"title":"","content":"That there's no easy or definite answer to the Hero-Beast dilemma is genuinely one of the most interesting things in the game, far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> Heroes are undoubtedly victims. When confronted with the nightmare that is the Beast, their broken ego latches on to the notion that the Begotten is an absolute monster, and that they alone know the truth. They compose themselves through the idea that it's their responsibility to end the Beast. Why else would they know? Why else would their heart scream so that the Begotten are enemies of mankind? This is more than just responsibility - it's their role. They know because they are meant to destroy the monster. And that means they're the hero, with everything it entitles them to.<br /> <br /> It's not a willful reaction. It's one born of desperation, an unconscious measure on the part of would-be-Heroes to not collapse into themselves. Their already shaken life sublimes into an enemy of Beasts. They are driven by these ideas, husks moved by their assumed righteousness against the one who made them this way. Against this imperative taken to support their existence after a traumatic experience, nothing else matters.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't make them right by default. Every living being in the world takes from elsewhere in order to survive. Humans take not only from the world, but from each other, often not even for survival, but just because it pleases them; to satisfy their desires. Arguably, Beast take more meaningfully and deeply than many humans do, but they at least can say they do it to survive. Of course, this doesn't always make them right by principle either.<br /> <br /> Heroes are irredeemably tragic figures despite their individual misgivings and their universal willingness to walk over everything to destroy the Beast, because they have no real escape from the cycle they are pulled into. But the bane of a Hero, what might antagonize even the noblest of Beasts against them, is that they don't even realize <i>they're all puppets, tangled in strings</i>. A Hero is as much of a slave as the Beast, if not more, to the perpetual narrative of the monster and the savior. But they do not, cannot recognize their position in this system; they make themselves believe it is about them, that they own this story. In the eyes of Beasts, they are ignorant - maybe offensively so, on a deep existential level that any person who truly lives should be able to understand. They accept the cycle and push it forward of their own vollition, in their weakness nothing more than prisoners seeking to drag everyone else down with them, unable to even struggle to be more.<br /> <br /> You can't really fault Beasts for feeling that way. Of course, you can't really fault Heroes for not having a conscious choice in the matter either. But the bottom line is, being a Beast doesn't make one inherently wrong, and being a Hero doesn't make one inherently justified; ultimately, it's understandable that they are enemies. It's hardly a fair situation for anyone involved. And it is understandable the Children could think they have the worst side of the deal and hate their counterparts for their perspective on the Hero Cycle. There is some bliss to be found in ignorance, but self-awareness only makes the inevitable more painful.<br /> <br /> And yet, they would rather know and curse their destiny than mindlessly go along with it.<br /> <br /> Also see David's explanation, which is fantastic and I will second on being a very comprehensive rundown of the impression the book left on Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-03-2015, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:18:18-07:00","id":538141,"title":"","content":"What I dislike about the age, is the fact that Heroes have a potentially longer lifespan than Beasts have. I'd say that instead of only increasing the expected life duration for Lair 6+, I'd do it for every increase of Lair, with perhaps beasts of Lair 9-10 being unable to die of old age (but still getting older). Just imagine that old ancient","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:30:48-07:00","id":538210,"title":"","content":"......... My Mind is Having Evil Ideas.... I'm Wondering what would happen if a Pre-Beast was effected by the Nightmares of another and became a &quot;Hero&quot; in their own Dreams......<br /> (By this i mean instead of Embracing the Monster that is their Soul they Face it and Slay it Without looking or Caring what it is.....)<br /> <br /> Something Horrific i'd think if it Could Happen...<br /> <br /> Then again i've only got a little bit into the first chapter of the Preview so this is hopefully answered...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:45:07-07:00","id":538227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538135#post538135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That there's no easy or definite answer to the Hero-Beast dilemma is genuinely one of the most interesting things in the game, far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> Heroes are undoubtedly victims. When confronted with the nightmare that is the Beast, their broken ego latches on to the notion that the Begotten is an absolute monster, and that they alone know the truth. They compose themselves through the idea that it's their responsibility to end the Beast. Why else would they know? Why else would their heart scream so that the Begotten are enemies of mankind? This is more than just responsibility - it's their role. They know because they are meant to destroy the monster. And that means they're the hero, with everything that entitles them to.<br /> <br /> It's not a willful reaction. It's one born of desperation, an unconscious measure on the part of would-be-Heroes to not collapse into themselves. Their already shaken life sublimes into an enemy of Beasts. They are driven by these ideas, husks moved by their assumed righteousness against the one who made them this way. Against this imperative taken to support their existence after a traumatic experience, nothing else matters.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't make them right by default. Every living being in the world takes from elsewhere in order to survive. Humans take not only from the world, but from each other, often not even for survival, but just because it pleases them; to satisfy their desires. Arguably, Beast take more meaningfully and deeply than many humans do, but they at least can say they do it to survive. Of course, this doesn't always make them right by principle either.<br /> <br /> Heroes are irredeemably tragic figures despite their individual misgivings and their universal willingness to walk over everything to destroy the Beast, because they have no real escape from the cycle they are pulled into. But the bane of a Hero, what might antagonize even the noblest of Beasts against them, is that they don't even realize <i>they're all puppets, tangled in strings</i>. A Hero is as much of a slave as the Beast, if not more, to the perpetual narrative of the monster and the savior. But they do not, cannot recognize their position in this system; they make themselves believe it is about them, that they own this story. In the eyes of Beasts, they are ignorant - maybe offensively so, on a deep existential level that any person who truly lives should be able to understand. They accept the cycle and push it forward of their own vollition, in their weakness nothing more than prisoners seeking to drag everyone else down with them, unable to even struggle to be more.<br /> <br /> You can't really fault Beasts for feeling that way. Of course, you can't really fault Heroes for not having a conscious choice in the matter either. But the bottom line is, being a Beast doesn't make one inherently wrong, and being a Hero doesn't make one inherently justified; ultimately, it's understandable that they are enemies. It's hardly a fair situation for anyone involved. And it is understandable the Children could think they have the worst side of the deal and hate their counterparts for their perspective on the Hero Cycle. There is some bliss to be found in ignorance, but self-awareness only makes the inevitable more painful.<br /> <br /> And yet, they would rather know and curse their destiny than mindlessly go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love everything about this, it's exactly what I was thinking. Also it's the very reason why beast is not a game for me. Oh I have put money in the kickstarter because I find the idea fascinating and I will use the material in my other games but I will not play it. It's a tragic story about two beings who cannot fight against their nature and role in life, they are doomed to reenact it over and over again till the eventual tragic ending. The hero is a deluded psychopath and the beast just rolls its eyes because on an instinctual level it knows, it thinks &quot;Ok we both know this dance, let's just get this over with&quot;. Such lack of freedom and enslavement to fate is completely anathema to me, it's unfair and I can't stand it. However I want to make it clear that this is just my personal preference, I don't find the idea wrong per se. It's just a different perspective, a different way to tell stories. Just not the kind of stories I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:55:53-07:00","id":538234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538210#post538210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">......... My Mind is Having Evil Ideas.... I'm Wondering what would happen if a Pre-Beast was effected by the Nightmares of another and became a &amp;quot;Hero&amp;quot; in their own Dreams......<br /> (By this i mean instead of Embracing the Monster that is their Soul they Face it and Slay it Without looking or Caring what it is.....)<br /> <br /> Something Horrific i'd think if it Could Happen...<br /> <br /> Then again i've only got a little bit into the first chapter of the Preview so this is hopefully answered...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that could be a nasty villain! I like the way you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:55:58-07:00","id":538235,"title":"","content":"I love Yolf and I cannot lie.<br /> <br /> But yeah, for me, the Beast-Hero conflict is actually a very broad one that covers a black and white moral struggle all the way down to a murky dingy grey. Are Heroes assholes who deserve to be put down before they do more harm than you do? Then play it that way. Is there a deep examination of fault that reveals all the things that explore humanity's failings and imperfection in the face of conflict? Play it that way.<br /> <br /> It helps that Family Dinner and the crossover aspect gives Beasts a dial on the direction. A Beast in crossover settings has better odds of controlling their hunger than one who isn't.<br /> <br /> It's a game that meditates a lot about the cycle of violence, about the needs and wants that fuel them, and asks questions about if there's a time and reason to these things. We all want things, all want good positions in life and justice in the world.We all come across people who make us angry, people we think deserve to be taken down a peg, whether that person be a roommate who pisses us off or a political figure who seems intent on ruining the way things ought to be. At what point should those be pursued and when should we let up? And at what point do we trangress others enough to warrant the same question? This game asks a lot of interesting questions about the lot of it.<br /> <br /> It helps that it's also non-normative with it's conclusions. Using Incarnates as the example, the way out is to break the cycle by completely dominating it. A <i>lot</i> of people take this view to problems in life, and you have to ask, because you play as the Beast, <i>are they wrong?</i> It's not an easy game, but that's what I like about it.<br /> <br /> When I got with the playtest materials, I really asked how anyone could get around the Hungers, because they seem to demand a certain evil. When I realized that was sort of the point, <i>that was when I came to love this game</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-03-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T06:56:01-07:00","id":538236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538227#post538227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such lack of freedom and enslavement to fate is completely anathema to me, it's unfair and I can't stand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The Fate is that the Hero kills the Beast. It gets overturned when the Beast kills the Hero instead. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:01:37-07:00","id":538242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538236#post538236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. The Fate is that the Hero kills the Beast. It gets overturned when the Beast kills the Hero instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's part of the fate to me. Either you kill or get killed. No other way around it. It's equally tragic to me, and besides even if you kill the hero another one will appear, and another, and another, and another etc....A cycle of violence and horror that never ends and in which you have no control about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:31:15-07:00","id":538275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=538242#post538242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of the fate to me. Either you kill or get killed. No other way around it. It's equally tragic to me, and besides even if you kill the hero another one will appear, and another, and another, and another etc....A cycle of violence and horror that never ends and in which you have no control about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite true. The (excellent) Storyteller section has rules and advice for Beasts helping rehabilitate Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/