:"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T12:55:39-07:00","id":539858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539831#post539831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soon he'll be an ashtray.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Samuel Haight jokes will never get old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:20:41-07:00","id":539908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539858#post539858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the Samuel Haight jokes will never get old.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He could be less CWoD Haight and more CWoD Rasputin - no one's sure what he is and so everybody claims him.<br /> <br /> My favorite answer on CWoD Rasputin was that while in life he was probably a mortal (maybe a Mage, but probably a mortal), he became a Puppeteer Wraith in death, and the reason there are so many stories of him running around as Vampires of different Clans, Garou, Fomori, etc etc etc, is because he's a master of possession and body hops between supernaturals to do his work in the Skinlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:11:29-07:00","id":539966,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing it, but I should hope that there's a difference between a monster and a beast...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:22:23-07:00","id":539971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539966#post539966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing it, but I should hope that there's a difference between a monster and a beast...</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are Monsters, But not all Monsters are Beasts. Not all of them are Begotten/The Children.<br /> <br /> I See Slashers as Monsters even though they are purely human, Vampires can be monsters, As can Uratha. The Main Difference is Choice. Beasts HAVE too Feed but they have a Choice on how/why/when. The Hungers they have might make them need too kill/Destroy Etc but they can Pick how too do it (Honestly i suspect any combination Brood that has one with a Hunger for Punishment and another with a Hunger for Destruction will be feeding quite abit if they work together)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:29:28-07:00","id":539979,"title":"","content":"Huh. A Lair 10 Anakim with Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence and has reached apex, if they spend 2 of either satiety or willpower, according to circumstances, can lift and throw an object of size 396. You'd be starving afterwards, but still, size 396.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6232-astrolapse","name":"Astrolapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:33:50-07:00","id":539985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astrolapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539979#post539979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. A Lair 10 Anakim with Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence and has reached apex, if they spend 2 of either satiety or willpower, according to circumstances, can lift and throw an object of size 396. You'd be starving afterwards, but still, size 396.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't fully understand the scale of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:37:23-07:00","id":539989,"title":"","content":"Well, considering that the moon is about size 128, and it works on an exponential scale, it's pretty damn big. I've lost the size equation somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6232-astrolapse","name":"Astrolapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:41:27-07:00","id":539995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astrolapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539989#post539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, considering that the moon is about size 128, and it works on an exponential scale, it's pretty damn big. I've lost the size equation somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something the Size of Saturn/Jupiter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:43:00-07:00","id":539998,"title":"","content":"So, I've noticed something in the Merits section.<br /> <br /> Advanced Iron Skin and Epic Iron Skin do not include the base merit among their prerequisites.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit iffy on How Base Iron Skin works with The Advanced Version. I mean, unless I'm remembering it wrong, Armor doen'st stack, so do they just not interact at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:46:04-07:00","id":540001,"title":"","content":"With all this talking about Temenos and the Primordial Nightmare, I've been thinking about an Eshmaki based on the Corinthian.<br /> <br /> And an Anakim which is a really big snake, but that is neither really creative nor a Sandman reference. Still cool, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:54:23-07:00","id":540006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539998#post539998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've noticed something in the Merits section.<br /> <br /> Advanced Iron Skin and Epic Iron Skin do not include the base merit among their prerequisites.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit iffy on How Base Iron Skin works with The Advanced Version. I mean, unless I'm remembering it wrong, Armor doen'st stack, so do they just not interact at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it just doesn't interact at all. The Advanced and Epic versions make up for not requiring the previous version by requiring a full dot more of Stamina each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:09:41-07:00","id":540028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539998#post539998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've noticed something in the Merits section.<br /> <br /> Advanced Iron Skin and Epic Iron Skin do not include the base merit among their prerequisites.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit iffy on How Base Iron Skin works with The Advanced Version. I mean, unless I'm remembering it wrong, Armor doen'st stack, so do they just not interact at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that due to them being essentially Supernatural effects, they would in fact stack, although the basic Merit would not stack with mundane Body Armor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:15:17-07:00","id":540037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astrolapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539979#post539979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. A Lair 10 Anakim with Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence and has reached apex, if they spend 2 of either satiety or willpower, according to circumstances, can lift and throw an object of size 396. You'd be starving afterwards, but still, size 396.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it basically falls into the Promethean problem.<br /> <br /> Sure you can lift and throw anything and everything. The problem is trying to find something that will survive being lifted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:16:53-07:00","id":540039,"title":"","content":"The bit on Hercules in the Heroes section made me laugh out loud. Listing &quot;having many children from his heterosexual relationships&quot; among his litany of 'crimes.'<br /> <br /> There's a definite current of &quot;Heroes represent th heteronormative patriarchy!&quot; without much mind paid to the fact that such an assumption makes oppressed identities out to be flesh-eating incarnate nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:34:15-07:00","id":540080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540039#post540039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit on Hercules in the Heroes section made me laugh out loud. Listing &quot;having many children from his heterosexual relationships&quot; among his litany of 'crimes.'<br /> <br /> There's a definite current of &quot;Heroes represent th heteronormative patriarchy!&quot; without much mind paid to the fact that such an assumption makes oppressed identities out to be flesh-eating incarnate nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was pretty much my view until a few hours ago. Something <i>just</i> clicked for me.<br /> <br /> Beasts aren't being mapped to &quot;The Other.&quot; Think about it. They're predatory, have incredible power that is inherited from ancient times, have connections to nearly every group of shadowy monsters in the WOD, and their actions generate monsters personified by the worst of humanity.<br /> <br /> They're the 1%. The deck is stacked in their favor from the start and they still don't feel like its enough. Actions against them are treated as irrational and villainous no matter how justified they may be.<br /> <br /> Heroes aren't meant to be seen as oppressors, they're the products of a corrupt system. They're the PIC/Tea Party/etc. While they have the power to harm Beasts, they're largely too unstable and disorganized to do so. Meanwhile the masses are either blind to the true nature of their predators or too scared/overwhelmed to make any serious moves against them.<br /> <br /> Its a bit too depressing for me, but it makes a lot more sense in this light. Also explains why Unchained and Begotten don't get along. Unchained are revolutionaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","user":"Illuminated Minutia","date":". 06-04-2015, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:40:55-07:00","id":540083,"title":"","content":"<i>Alternatively</i>, it's just a game about playing as monsters with no deep meaning about what the monsters represent, beyond their own hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:43:41-07:00","id":540086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540039#post540039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit on Hercules in the Heroes section made me laugh out loud. Listing &quot;having many children from his heterosexual relationships&quot; among his litany of 'crimes.'<br /> <br /> There's a definite current of &quot;Heroes represent th heteronormative patriarchy!&quot; without much mind paid to the fact that such an assumption makes oppressed identities out to be flesh-eating incarnate nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one could argue that the Heroes do oppress them, to an extent. A Beast that fills his Hunger as a Nemesis by putting violent criminals away wouldn't deserve to get repeatedly stabbed in the eyes with a steak knife, now would he?<br /> <br /> Punishing a class of people for what only a portion of that class does is ostensibly oppression.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the Heroes are necessarily unjustified in their hunt, but they aren't interested in doing good so much as killing for glory, making it sort of a supernatural hate crime.<br /> <br /> As a side note, &quot;Supernatural Hate Crime&quot; is a great name for a metal band.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:45:48-07:00","id":540088,"title":"","content":"Has anyone else tried mapping a family and hunger to themselves as if they were Beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:46:44-07:00","id":540091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540039#post540039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The bit on Hercules in the Heroes section made me laugh out loud. Listing &quot;having many children from his heterosexual relationships&quot; among his litany of 'crimes.'</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:54:44-07:00","id":540099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540083#post540083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Alternatively</i>, it's just a game about playing as monsters with no deep meaning about what the monsters represent, beyond their own hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one. Let's go with this one, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540088#post540088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone else tried mapping a family and hunger to themselves as if they were Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why yes, I have! I remember having nightmares as a child that were pretty fitting for a Makara, so I would probably be one of those. And considering some of my behavior when I was younger (though perhaps not as far from the present as I might like) I would probably have a Hunger for Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 06-04-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:02:37-07:00","id":540105,"title":"","content":"Heroes are deeply unstable people who, upon having a nightmare about a monster, decided that the monster was both real, and had to die just because it was a monster.<br /> <br /> Meaning the Average Hero will be hunting Beasts regardless of if a Beast is hurting people.<br /> <br /> since the nightmares are otherwise no more harmful than regular nightmares, and nightmares happen most often when the beast is hungry, then a beast is most likely to create a hero when he is not feeding enough.<br /> <br /> Meaning when he is doing the least harm.<br /> <br /> Compare this to the description of heroes, which notes that 1: Repeated exposure to the Supernatural does not usually lower Integrity low enough for someone to be able to become a hero, and two that Bullies and Abusers are both in the category of people who are likely to have the requisite low integrity to become Heroes.<br /> <br /> Two people have urges that are negative and harmful. One of them is aware of the nature of the urges, can try to control them, to limit the damage he causes, and ultimately try and direct his damage towards positive ends. The other is either gleefully unaware of the harm his urges cause or just doen'st care because he's so important.<br /> <br /> A Beast could be either of those people. a Hero is always the second person. That's what I'm getting from it.<br /> <br /> The fact that the crossover section mentions that hunters are likely to compare Heroes to Slashers(and if the Slasher Morality Rules carry over to Integrity, then they both have to be at 4 to become what they are, it's not a stretch) tells me that Hunters, whatever they were, are not good people. At best, they are Byronic Heroes-deeply, deeply flawed individuals doomed to a terrible fate.<br /> <br /> And finally: &quot;You're a monster, you hurt people&quot; is a good reason to want to kill a beast. sometimes, it might even be both completely true and the beast in question is gleeful about it. but That's not the reason the Hero is hunting the Beast, even if that's what he's telling himself and others. He's hunting the Beast because the Beast is a Beast and therefore deserves to die, and he, the Hero, is the one who deserves to kill them.<br /> <br /> Just becuase a rationalization is a valid reason in it's own right does not mean it's not a rationalization. A serial Killer who rationalizes his killings by only victimizing criminals is still a serial killer. Especial when not every crime is worthy of death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:13:54-07:00","id":540113,"title":"","content":"Hey, we got a new stretch goal on the line! $80,000 and we get a Beast Dark Era for the Dark Era Companion. Anyone who pledges high enough for at least a Beast pdf will get a pdf copy of that Dark Era for free.<br /> <br /> No, we have no idea what time period the era will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:20:09-07:00","id":540122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540091#post540091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't, because that's not a list of crimes at all.<br /> <br /> It's boasting, and boasting the ancient Greeks would totally view as boasting (&quot;Hah! My seed is as strong as my muscles!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:24:37-07:00","id":540127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540122#post540122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You shouldn't, because that's not a list of crimes at all.<br /> <br /> It's boasting, and boasting the ancient Greeks would totally view as boasting (&quot;Hah! My seed is as strong as my muscles!&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:34:07-07:00","id":540154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540122#post540122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You shouldn't, because that's not a list of crimes at all.<br /> <br /> It's boasting, and boasting the ancient Greeks would totally view as boasting (&quot;Hah! My seed is as strong as my muscles!&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and I also see it as a way for the writers to mention the fact that Hercules probably would also have male lovers. Which, considering the culture of the time, is a honest way to imagine a hero from ancient Greece and yet something most represention of Hercules in modern culture prefer to avoid altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:35:57-07:00","id":540156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540105#post540105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes are deeply unstable people who, upon having a nightmare about a monster, decided that the monster was both real, and had to die just because it was a monster.<br /> <br /> Meaning the Average Hero will be hunting Beasts regardless of if a Beast is hurting people.<br /> <br /> since the nightmares are otherwise no more harmful than regular nightmares, and nightmares happen most often when the beast is hungry, then a beast is most likely to create a hero when he is not feeding enough.<br /> <br /> Meaning when he is doing the least harm.<br /> <br /> Compare this to the description of heroes, which notes that 1: Repeated exposure to the Supernatural does not usually lower Integrity low enough for someone to be able to become a hero, and two that Bullies and Abusers are both in the category of people who are likely to have the requisite low integrity to become Heroes.<br /> <br /> Two people have urges that are negative and harmful. One of them is aware of the nature of the urges, can try to control them, to limit the damage he causes, and ultimately try and direct his damage towards positive ends. The other is either gleefully unaware of the harm his urges cause or just doen'st care because he's so important.<br /> <br /> A Beast could be either of those people. a Hero is always the second person. That's what I'm getting from it.<br /> <br /> The fact that the crossover section mentions that hunters are likely to compare Heroes to Slashers(and if the Slasher Morality Rules carry over to Integrity, then they both have to be at 4 to become what they are, it's not a stretch) tells me that Hunters, whatever they were, are not good people. At best, they are Byronic Heroes-deeply, deeply flawed individuals doomed to a terrible fate.<br /> <br /> And finally: &quot;You're a monster, you hurt people&quot; is a good reason to want to kill a beast. sometimes, it might even be both completely true and the beast in question is gleeful about it. but That's not the reason the Hero is hunting the Beast, even if that's what he's telling himself and others. He's hunting the Beast because the Beast is a Beast and therefore deserves to die, and he, the Hero, is the one who deserves to kill them.<br /> <br /> Just becuase a rationalization is a valid reason in it's own right does not mean it's not a rationalization. A serial Killer who rationalizes his killings by only victimizing criminals is still a serial killer. Especial when not every crime is worthy of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Lex Luthor/Superman dynamic, in that Luthor's monomaniacal obsession with Superman has nothing to do with Supe's ascribed &quot;selfishness,&quot; (which, by the way, is a typical Individualistic projection), and everything to do with Luthor's own self-hatred and delusions of powerlessness. Ironically, it's never really about the Beast, but the reflection the Beast's Soul shows the nascent Hero of himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:39:53-07:00","id":540159,"title":"","content":"Y<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540156#post540156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the Lex Luthor/Superman dynamic, in that Luthor's monomaniacal obsession with Superman has nothing to do with Supe's ascribed &quot;selfishness,&quot; (which, by the way, is a typical Individualistic projection), and everything to do with Luthor's own self-hatred and delusions of powerlessness. Ironically, it's never really about the Beast, but the reflection the Beast's Soul shows the nascent Hero of himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's a much shorter and simpler way to say what I was trying to.<br /> <br /> Thank you.(not sarcasm)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:52:04-07:00","id":540165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540039#post540039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit on Hercules in the Heroes section made me laugh out loud. Listing &quot;having many children from his heterosexual relationships&quot; among his litany of 'crimes.'<br /> <br /> There's a definite current of &quot;Heroes represent th heteronormative patriarchy!&quot; without much mind paid to the fact that such an assumption makes oppressed identities out to be flesh-eating incarnate nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're comparing cold sociopathy to garden-variety, if a bit visceral, obsessive compulsion. It's not just that Herc is a serial rapist, but he's also a serial mass-murderer, a drunk, and a spousal abuser among other things. One recognizes and moderates their behavior, the other parties hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:34:46-07:00","id":540203,"title":"","content":"Primordial Dream...yet...no dreams per se, but only nightmares....hmf...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:38:46-07:00","id":540205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540203#post540203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial Dream...yet...no dreams per se, but only nightmares....hmf...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream is explicitly for nightmares. Other dreams are in other parts of the Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:44:19-07:00","id":540212,"title":"","content":"Someone was just pointing out on the rpg.net forums that it isn't just nightmares that cause the change to hero. A Beast can create one from just meeting people, though the examples suggest it's from feeding off of them, as they are supposed to really enjoy the taste of fear from someone who might become a hero. Also a dramatic failure when using the Under your Bed ability.<br /> <br /> And it isn't exactly 'just' a nightmare. They're dragged out of their body and into the Beast's Lair, where their dream form is then killed.<br /> <br /> And, again, low Satiety doesn't mean a Beast is doing the least amount of harm, it just means they have low Satiety, which you can get from expending it to empower nightmares or atavisms. It could just mean the Beast just threw a bunch of planes through a bunch of skyscrapers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:02:05-07:00","id":540251,"title":"","content":"There is no mechanical support for it happening just from meeting someone. Only for Under the Bed and for it happening due to Low Satiety-induced nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:04:50-07:00","id":540253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540212#post540212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone was just pointing out on the rpg.net forums that it isn't just nightmares that cause the change to hero. A Beast can create one from just meeting people, though the examples suggest it's from feeding off of them, as they are supposed to really enjoy the taste of fear from someone who might become a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>.Page number with mechanics, please. Fluff doen'st count. All I see is that a potential hero might become such by seeing a Beast in the process of feeding on somebody else. Nothing about making a hero just from meeting people.<br /> <br /> And we still have word of mat that most Heroes come from the nightmares.<br /> <br /> Also, they still have to be integrity 4. meaning they were screwed up to begin with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it isn't exactly 'just' a nightmare. They're dragged out of their body and into the Beast's Lair, where their dream form is then killed. </div> </div> </div>The description of the dreams which describes that for most non heroes, the experience is <b>effectively</b> just a particularly vivid nightmare disagrees with you. Regardless of what it actually is, for everybody but a hero it's just a bad dream as far as they're concerned.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, again, low Satiety doesn't mean a Beast is doing the least amount of harm, it just means they have low Satiety, which you can get from expending it to empower nightmares or atavisms. It could just mean the Beast just threw a bunch of planes through a bunch of skyscrapers. </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. Right in the book it says your soul only goes ravaging immediately if you have a very high lair trait and you've hit satiety 0. Everybody else it takes at least a few days. Since I doubt that the majority of Beasts are at a lair higher than five, that means that the majority of beasts who cause nightmares did so after being at low satiety for a few days or weeks.<br /> <br /> The Beasts who are likely to be at low satiety for days or weeks at a time are the one who are just plain not feeding. that's just logic.<br /> <br /> And once more, I feel the need to point out, that Mat, the Developer of the game, has said that heroes are usually created when the beast is at their least harmful. Dev Quotes mean that yes, a Beast is usually doing the least harm when it creates a hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:15:01-07:00","id":540263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540251#post540251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no mechanical support for it happening just from meeting someone. Only for Under the Bed and for it happening due to Low Satiety-induced nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>P275. 'It\u2019s not only in dreams that Beasts can stumble across Heroes. Heroes can also encounter Beasts manifesting themselves in the real world. Some simply find themselves in the wrong place at the wrong time, while a Beast is reaping the fears of another in a more direct manner. Other times, they find themselves at the wrong end of the Beast\u2019s barbs.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540253#post540253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page number with mechanics, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>P110. 'Dramatic Failure: The Beast is unable to enter the Primordial Pathways through the target\u2019s nightmares, and the resulting psychic turmoil reverberates through the Primordial Dream. The target, or someone sleeping within a mile of him, becomes a Hero if able (that is, the subject is a normal human being with Integrity 4 or lower).'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The description of the dreams which describes that for most non heroes, the experience is <b>effectively</b> just a particularly vivid nightmare disagrees with you. Regardless of what it actually is, for everybody but a hero it's just a bad dream as far as they're concerned. </div> </div> </div>P121. 'The Soul draws the targeted individual into the Lair so successfully that a Primordial Pathway opens and drags the unfortunate in. If he loses all Astral Health within the Lair, the Beast gains the victim\u2019s Willpower dots in Satiety. When the victim awakens, he is traumatized but emboldened by the experience \u2014 he becomes a Hero '<br /> <br /> People aren't traumatized by 'just' particularly vivid nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fluff doesn't count. Matt has said. Dev Quotes. </div> </div> </div>Unless Matt is going to come with the book to tell everyone otherwise, when people get the book, they're going to go by what the book says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:19:43-07:00","id":540268,"title":"","content":"Does Inheritance remove the Lair traits? No more Environmental Immunities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:20:33-07:00","id":540269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540263#post540263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P275. 'It\u2019s not only in dreams that Beasts can stumble across Heroes. Heroes can also encounter Beasts manifesting themselves in the real world. Some simply find themselves in the wrong place at the wrong time, while a Beast is reaping the fears of another in a more direct manner. Other times, they find themselves at the wrong end of the Beast\u2019s barbs.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am aware of that passage. Where are the mechanics for it? Every other method has mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:21:54-07:00","id":540270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540268#post540268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Inheritance remove the Lair traits? No more Environmental Immunities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of them do. The Apex does not; you retain your Lair stat, and so logically you still have the other aspects that come with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:34:32-07:00","id":540307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540263#post540263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P110. 'Dramatic Failure: The Beast is unable to enter the Primordial Pathways through the target\u2019s nightmares, and the resulting psychic turmoil reverberates through the Primordial Dream. The target, or someone sleeping within a mile of him, becomes a Hero if able (that is, the subject is a normal human being with Integrity 4 or lower).'</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I asked for. I asked for mechanics of a someone becoming a hero just from meeting a hero. You have not privided sucha thing. Put your money where your mouth is, or close that mouth<br /> <br /> also, that's only applicable if the dreamer or somebody within a mile of them is at integrity 4. That is, already screwed up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P121. 'The Soul draws the targeted individual into the Lair so successfully that a Primordial Pathway opens and drags the unfortunate in. If he loses all Astral Health within the Lair, the Beast gains the victim\u2019s Willpower dots in Satiety. When the victim awakens, he is traumatized but emboldened by the experience \u2014 he becomes a Hero '<br /> <br /> People aren't traumatized by 'just' particularly vivid nightmares. </div> </div> </div>You've clearly never had a particularly vivid nightmare.<br /> <br /> Also, this is directed directly at heroes. I <b>specifically</b> mentioned that for people who do not become heroes, it's just a nightmare, which is in the book, though I'm having a hard time remembering the page number.<br /> <br /> a potential hero is also, as stated, already a deeply disturbed or unstable individual. So a Vivid Nightmare could have devastating effects upon them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:49:50-07:00","id":540338,"title":"","content":"I think arguing over the degree of mind rape is kind of besides the point, guys. Whether it's super bad or merely bad for people who don't turn into Heroes is besides the point. Does this mean Beast is kind of weirdly victim-blaming? Sure, it's a game about predators. Are Heroes still really evil? Of course! The game openly says that any degree of affection, moral concern, or remorse expressed by the Hero is just part of their Legend, not representative of their actual feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:05:33-07:00","id":540351,"title":"","content":"A victim stops being a victim when they get to a point where they plot to murder anyone even remotely like the one who hurt them and take disproportionate revenge, such as plotting to murder the person who gave them a bad dream.<br /> <br /> Even in the cases where a Hero is one hundred percent justified in killing their originating Beast, once they move onto killing beasts indiscriminately just because they're beasts, or if they cause significant collateral damage or loss of life in the process, they stop being a victim and start being just another monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:05:51-07:00","id":540353,"title":"","content":"Heroes can recruit followers, but I don't think they can make other Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:07:39-07:00","id":540354,"title":"","content":"So in my home campaigns there is an entity known as &quot;The Radio.&quot; You can tune into it through any dead channel as long as you've been exposed. I think for the first Beast game I run, this is the song The Radio will play when they've created a Hero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wC5g9M5FAq4\" data-code=\"wC5g9M5FAq4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wC5g9M5FAq4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:18:22-07:00","id":540360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540269#post540269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I am aware of that passage. Where are the mechanics for it? Every other method has mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't instinctively recognize heroes*, so the part about finding themselves at the wrong end of the barbs just means the Beast chose to feed and picked the hero as the target. The manifesting in the real world just means the hero is exposed to the Beast when it is trying to feed on someone in the real world. It could also be talking about the fact that heroes all have the power to track at least the beast that awakened them in which case it means tracking down the person in the material world.<br /> <br /> So it isn't really a case of bumping into a Beast at the mall and awakening. It does require the proto-hero to at least encounter a beast using atavism. I think the idea is if the Beast causes the proto-hero to suffer a breaking point then it could result in the heroes awakening,<br /> <br /> *And Heroes to be aren't on the list at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 06-04-2015, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:18:29-07:00","id":540361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540338#post540338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are Heroes still really evil? Of course! The game openly says that any degree of affection, moral concern, or remorse expressed by the Hero is just part of their Legend, not representative of their actual feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that they can become 'cured' by getting their Integrity above 4, and above 5 start living a normal life again.<br /> <br /> And even disregarding that, Heroes are capable of breaking their narrative in favor of their Life.<br /> <br /> 'A Hero\u2019s Life represents his human nature, the part of him that is still the same mortal that he was before his heroic calling. In this regard, Heroes are not so different from the Beasts they fight, subject to all the same small quirks and traits that represent their last hold on humanity.'<br /> <br /> But if they don't give into their Legend, they are haunted by nightmares every night until they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:31:02-07:00","id":540387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540361#post540361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that they can become 'cured' by getting their Integrity above 4, and above 5 start living a normal life again.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how many of them do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:45:01-07:00","id":540406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astrolapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=539989#post539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, considering that the moon is about size 128, and it works on an exponential scale, it's pretty damn big. I've lost the size equation somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where does that figure come from? Because I've never heard it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:02:01-07:00","id":540436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540387#post540387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how many of them do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same as the number of Beasts that refuse to kill people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:11:38-07:00","id":540438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540436#post540436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same as the number of Beasts that refuse to kill people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page number, please. Give me the exact quote and page number that says that the number of heroes who can raise their integrity higher than the threshold for hero hood.<br /> <br /> Or are you just talking about in your chronicles instead of what's in the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:20:24-07:00","id":540440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540083#post540083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Alternatively</i>, it's just a game about playing as monsters with no deep meaning about what the monsters represent, beyond their own hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this, with the caveat that it doesn't mean there aren't deeper themes to the game, just that those themes don't map to social justice politics directly. It's about our own relationships to our fears, including what we fear about our own dark side.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say you can't do a great story that DOES explore themes of racism/sexism/etc. Imagine a PoC wrestling with internalized racism, who finally faces those fears and how they're socially taught and rises as a Gorgon with a Hunger for Punishment. Or a poor white racist whose fears of social impotence, scapegoated onto people of color (and other minorities), eventually manifest in him assuming the mantle of a Giant with a Hunger for Power (this would probably be an antagonist).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:27:50-07:00","id":540444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540351#post540351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A victim stops being a victim when they get to a point where they plot to murder anyone even remotely like the one who hurt them and take disproportionate revenge, such as plotting to murder the person who gave them a bad dream.<br /> <br /> Even in the cases where a Hero is one hundred percent justified in killing their originating Beast, once they move onto killing beasts indiscriminately just because they're beasts, or if they cause significant collateral damage or loss of life in the process, they stop being a victim and start being just another monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stepping away from the issue of the morality of intentionally inflicting traumatic experiences on people, since we clearly just have very different views on the weight of that, I don't buy that victims ever stop being victims barring changing history. That event, that position, still exists no matter how many horrible things they do. What changes is the weight of that condition in the consideration of others.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd argue that this understanding is very important to how Heroes are written in Beast, where so much focus is put on how they lack self-awareness, and how they interpret that initial encounter with the Beast. Part of what makes Heroes so insufferable is that they refuse to see themselves as compromised. Even Thaddeus Pearson, who thinks that everything in his life is someone else's fault, has this problem: It would never occur to him that any of the things &quot;done&quot; to him have changed him. It's why that step to Integrity 5 is characterized as a realization that he or she is &quot;messy, complicated, and unfair&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:28:13-07:00","id":540445,"title":"","content":"Not to get off topic, but does anyone know when the character sheet is going to be available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/430-moonshadow","name":"Moonshadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:30:08-07:00","id":540446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540438#post540438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page number, please. Give me the exact quote and page number that says that the number of heroes who can raise their integrity higher than the threshold for hero hood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Hero can raise their integrity higher, p400. But there's no numbers for how many have, just as there's no numbers for how many Beasts are pacifists, or even how many Beasts or Heroes exist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:34:09-07:00","id":540449,"title":"","content":"Okay first it really isn't valid to say heroes aren't evil because they can stop being heroes. Heck retiring from being a Hero doesn't even mean that a Hero has stopped hunting Beasts in spite of the drive to do so, there are stories that include the hero slaying the monster and then going back to live a peaceful life. Best we can say on that is that some Heroes choose to end their stories.<br /> <br /> I do believe it is fair to say that Heroes retiring is an uncommon if not rare event, since the pdf does say the idea never really occurs to most Beasts that a Hero might retire without being forced into it. Though in response to nofather I'd say its probably rarer than Beasts that refuse to kill, as a few of the feeding methods seem to discourage killing if only because it leaves fewer people to feed off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:40:48-07:00","id":540473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540446#post540446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any Hero can raise their integrity higher, p400. But there's no numbers for how many have, just as there's no numbers for how many Beasts are pacifists, or even how many Beasts or Heroes exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said that the numbers were equal. You have admitted that you have no evidence for this claim.<br /> <br /> No number given for either does not mean both are equal.<br /> <br /> In fact, given as heroes are consistently described as lacking self awareness of their own harmful nature while such awareness of the potential harm caused by their monstrous nature is and the ability to mitigate it is brought up as one of the differences between Beast's and heroes, I'd say that the number of heroes who raise their integrity is much lower than the number of beasts who can mitigate the harm their feeding causes, based on the simple logic that all Beasts are stated to have the necessary self awareness while a Hero with the requisite self awareness must be, by the definitions given in the book, be an exception to the normal hero parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:50:11-07:00","id":540483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540449#post540449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay first it really isn't valid to say heroes aren't evil because they can stop being heroes. Heck retiring from being a Hero doesn't even mean that a Hero has stopped hunting Beasts in spite of the drive to do so, there are stories that include the hero slaying the monster and then going back to live a peaceful life. Best we can say on that is that some Heroes choose to end their stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>They lose the obsessive drive to do so. And the obsessive drive is what people are claiming is evil. From then on, if an ex-Hero kills a Beast, it's not because they're obsessed or driven to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540473#post540473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You said that the numbers were equal. You have admitted that you have no evidence for this claim.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh no?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No number given for either does not mean both are equal. </div> </div> </div>I said it was the same. None is the same. Just as, 'Whatever number you want,' is the same as, 'Whatever number you want,'</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In fact, given as heroes are consistantly described as lacking self awareness of their own harful nature while such awareness of the potential harm caused by their monsterous nature is and the abillity to mitigate it is brought up as one of the diferances between Beast's and heroes,</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Except, Heroes do break from their Heroic obsession and act in the nature of their human self. They have a Legend and Life just like Beasts. The fact that they're driven by nightmares to fulfill their Legend doesn't mean they don't follow their Life.<br /> <br /> '</span></span></span>A Hero\u2019s Life regains him 1 Willpower when he puts himself or his mission at significant risk to break with the narrative of the Hero and act in accordance with his more human self, but it can never allow him to regain more than 1 Willpower per scene. A Maternal Hero regains 1 Willpower when she stops to comfort one of her foe\u2019s victims rather than advancing on the Beast, and a Cautious Hero regains 1 Willpower when he backs out of a dangerous situation rather than pursuing his foe into a dramatic conflict.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:53:20-07:00","id":540486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter Preview, pg 400</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if a Hero\u2019s Integrity were to rise above four dots, his soul would gain enough strength to ignore the Beast and develop other interests. At that point, it is possible that the Hero continues to focus on his quest to kill Beasts, but he gains no gifts or benefit from doing so (and indeed, might even lose Integrity, allowing the cycle to continue). If he abandons the hunt and continues to live his life in a way that allows for further Integrity gain, he can strengthen his soul the way any normal human being can. Good, bad, or otherwise, the ex-Hero gains enough psychic definition that he no longer needs to pursue his role as \u201cslayer of monsters.\u201d Likewise, a Hero who raises his Integrity to 5 or more loses his Legend/Life and replaces them with the more standard Virtue and Vice (p. XX). In effect, the character is no longer a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes are Heroes because of a time of weakness. The weakness can be overcome, but it is a choice to not Hunt. As said above, that choice is independent of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:53:24-07:00","id":540487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moonshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540445#post540445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to get off topic, but does anyone know when the character sheet is going to be available?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably close to when the book is actually ready to see release. Probably +/- a week from when the book comes out. That's my hope anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:54:47-07:00","id":540489,"title":"","content":"All the back and forth here is making the game less appealing...*muses* I hope after I finish reading the preview things will look far better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:58:59-07:00","id":540493,"title":"","content":"Yes, this back and forth is quite unpleasant. It's creating a rather toxic environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:06:47-07:00","id":540508,"title":"","content":"Alright. You don't need me to point out things, everyone's got access to the same book I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:13:44-07:00","id":540532,"title":"","content":"Huh, I just realized that the set up of how the Begotten work actually resolves the contradiction between the traditional Greek Medusa myth, and Ovid's version. She was born a mortal woman, who was a priestess of Athena, who transformed after being raped; AND she was the monstrous daughter of Ceto, never human to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:24:54-07:00","id":540542,"title":"","content":"So I'm reading through the Hungers and I get to the Hunger for Punishment and my brain suddenly clicks, &quot;That explains the DMV! No wonder people who have DUI's and Suspensions tend to file the wrong paperwork, they are given it 'on accident' by Hag-Beasts who feed their Hunger for Punishment by sending them chasing their tails through paperwork for months!&quot;<br /> <br /> Dear god, those hags could spend Satity like it was going out of style, that would be the best feeding ground ever. And any hero's who attack get overwhelmed by the coven of Hag-Beasts with the massive home advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:49:33-07:00","id":540581,"title":"","content":"It's interesting how the Unfettered section doesn't say anything about the Rank of the Lurker only going up to 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:51:21-07:00","id":540582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540581#post540581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"