main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540588#post540588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any 2e book has yet to provide mechanics for ephemeral beings of Rank 6+, which is what your Rank would be if your Lair was that high</div> </div> </div> </div>Missing the horrifying point there a bit. We hardly need mechanics for that to understand its significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:18:37-07:00","id":540592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540588#post540588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any 2e book has yet to provide mechanics for ephemeral beings of Rank 6+, which is what your Rank would be if your Lair was that high</div> </div> </div> </div>The God Machine Chronicle has a Rank 6 archangel in it. It only has its title, its Ban, and its Bane listed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:30:09-07:00","id":540599,"title":"","content":"the ephemerals above rank 5 are strictly plot devices, they don't get stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:40:32-07:00","id":540601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=537738#post537738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check the third chapter. There is a lengthy section that details the difference between the two.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I looked in Ch 3... couldn't find anything .. is it further in? I'm just about to go into the chapter on heroes .. I am assuming its in there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:02:09-07:00","id":540625,"title":"","content":"You Are Meat.<br /> <br /> Page 180.<br /> <br /> Gives Soulless to anything you use it on, even beings that explicitly have <i>no soul </i>to begin with.<br /> <br /> Can be made more or less impossible to fix.<br /> <br /> Does this bother anyone else?<br /> <br /> Looks to me like a way to effectively kill anyone in the entire World of Darkness with a single roll, given how potent Soulless is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:16:28-07:00","id":540665,"title":"","content":"It gives it <b>temporarily</b>, unless you spend Satiety in which case it's<i> mostly</i> permanent.<br /> And given it's nature, who said Heroes needed souls? That is one way to force Integrity degeneration after all. Plus a large number of the Family (were-wolfs, mages, changelings, sin-eaters &amp; even vamps) don't take kindly to soul snatching.<br /> <br /> It is not something I would allow to be used all willy-nilly...<br /> <br /> But I can see why making it so accessible is an issue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:12:16-07:00","id":540726,"title":"","content":"I'm not really talking about heroes. They can use it on, say, Demons just fine. Who don't even have souls. There's a sidebar that explicitly says it works on beings without souls.<br /> <br /> The whole family thing is a separate issue. I see only reasons why most splats would hate Beasts, not welcome them with open arms. For now I'm talking about removing (apparently just suppressing) the souls of beings that don't even have them, when soul removal has been rare and difficult thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:25:36-07:00","id":540731,"title":"","content":"Are you sure it's Soulless in universe and not just mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:38:02-07:00","id":540737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540625#post540625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You Are Meat.<br /> <br /> Page 180.<br /> <br /> Gives Soulless to anything you use it on, even beings that explicitly have <i>no soul </i>to begin with.<br /> <br /> Can be made more or less impossible to fix.<br /> <br /> Does this bother anyone else?<br /> <br /> Looks to me like a way to effectively kill anyone in the entire World of Darkness with a single roll, given how potent Soulless is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I thought that was weird, considering most other gamelines can't touch the souls of others. I get not focusing on game balance, but some things do need to be universal, or at least far far more difficult (Though I do think I saw something that says Mages can steal Beast souls as if they were Mage ones, somewhere in there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:42:48-07:00","id":540739,"title":"","content":"Well one of their abilities does actually have it so unless something has happened to poison the relationship most splats tend to default to viewing the Beast as not an enemy even if they aren't going to recognize them as friends. Obviously we're also talking on a case by case basis. I mean a tyrant beast is probably not going to get on well with a vampire who fancies itself king of the world. Whereas a collector beast might end up being considered a useful &quot;pet&quot; for the same vampire since it can be paid off with information on where certain objects are.<br /> <br /> I'm not so sure on the You Are Meat Nightmare since I'm not totally familiar with the Ennervated state and the like, but yeah that does seem rather powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:43:45-07:00","id":540740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540726#post540726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole family thing is a separate issue. I see only reasons why most splats would hate Beasts, not welcome them with open arms. For now I'm talking about removing (apparently just suppressing) the souls of beings that don't even have them, when soul removal has been rare and difficult thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most splat do not acknowledge they have common Family Maternal Figure as a whole race creator. The only ones with strong Maternal Myth ( werewolves, Circle of Crone vampires ) would meet Beasts with open arms on start. BUT they all, on long meeting, could understand that Beasts are really their cousins. And Kinship powers should &quot;sell&quot; the PC in other races group ( coterie, pack, cabal, motley, etc ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:51:08-07:00","id":540744,"title":"","content":"So I'm trying to get the hang of the Primordial Pathways rules, and\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026is Skeleton Key actually a more consistently effective means of getting into one's Lair away from one's Chambers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:52:05-07:00","id":540745,"title":"","content":"Mmm... Interested to see how a Beast can sell that Maternal connection to a Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:31:20-07:00","id":540774,"title":"","content":"They are the adopted ones; not directly descended from the Dark Mother but they are 'close enough' to be Kin.<br /> &quot;The world may reject you, but I don't. You are family and I am sure the Dark Mother would be happy enough to embrace you. It's ok Cousin, you are home now.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...Ooooh! Wastelands are kinda like Environmental Tilts right? The same kind as make up the Lair traits? PtC 2nd ed is going to be very useful...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:57:03-07:00","id":540779,"title":"","content":"As for Primordial Pathways, it seems to be a Wits+Resolve roll with an instant action to open a Pathway for a character's Resolve in turns, though it ends up penalised if not in the Primordial Dream, the <i>Temeros</i> or having Lair Traits enacted at this newly made entrance.<br /> <br /> The Skeleton Key is more expensive... It needs a point of Willpower, then it's a contested roll against the Supernatural Tolerance of the gate's creator. Sure, it's Resolve+Occult+Lair as the Beast's pool, though there is more chance of the Key failing, especially if trying to use the Key on a supernatural with a higher tolerance. It seems more like that it could be used for busting into another Beast's Lair, though I do not see it as a way to make a Primordial Pathway to your Beast's own Lair, rather into other Beast's Lairs if you wanted to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T03:32:45-07:00","id":540835,"title":"","content":"Looking over the powers more closely about the only house rule I am seeing so far is You Are Meat is not going to work on Deathless in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T04:29:06-07:00","id":540938,"title":"","content":"I might have missed it, but on pondering the opening of a Primordial Pathway, how would a Beast enter the <i>Temeros</i> to begin with to make an attempt at making a Pathway? Through the Skeleton Key ability does seem to be the main way, though that seems somewhat <i>limiting</i>?<br /> I know the Beast (human in real world) can vanish from the material world to inhabit their Primordial-based Soul, though I guess they can make a Pathway leading from their Lair once within it outwards to where they choose, right? So a Beast could go into the Lair and then make a Pathway outwards to material world and because the Lair is the external entry point through the Pathway, it gets a bonus to reach there... Correct?<br /> <br /> So the Beast vanishes from their position, merges with their Soul in their Lair, then from there they can open a Pathway to somewhere else, which the Beast can then wander outwards to, unmerging with the Soul...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:21:46-07:00","id":541071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540105#post540105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the crossover section mentions that hunters are likely to compare Heroes to Slashers(and if the Slasher Morality Rules carry over to Integrity, then they both have to be at 4 to become what they are, it's not a stretch) tells me that Hunters, whatever they were, are not good people. At best, they are Byronic Heroes-deeply, deeply flawed individuals doomed to a terrible fate.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Why are you here?</i> the voice over the loudspeaker asked as it's voice echoed down the halls. <i>What prods you down this maze? </i><br /> <br /> Angelica give a brief hiss before continuing on, sniffing the acidic for a scent, for anything.<br /> <br /> <i>I know what you seek but why do you seek it? You have no blood relation. You have no romantic relation. Is it </i><i>vengeance</i> <i>you're after? One last hangnail to clip? One last scab to rip open? </i><br /> <br /> The Beast gave a roar as it punched into the left wall of the blood soaked corridor. Ripping and tearing with all it's might into the room beyond. It slowly work it's way inside before being confronted with another corridor.<br /> <br /> <i>The princess, or I should say Hero, is in another castle. </i><br /> <br /> She howled in frustration. She spend time unknown crawling in this maze of a mind. The being that called it's self <i>The Deconstructionist </i>had the Hero she wanted and was refusing to give it up.<br /> <br /> <i>The exit is right behind you. It always was. </i><br /> <br /> She continued, sniffing the air, hunting for her prey.<br /> <br /> <i>And yet... You continue. Why? Whywhywhywhywhywhy?<br /> Subverting you own Myth perhaps? Changing the actors and twisting the roles? Can Fate handle that? Does Fate break that? </i><br /> <br /> Angelica turned a corner to see polished reinforced glass and beyond it lay her prize. A broken figure thrashed and writhed upon a table while a darken one operated.<br /> <br /> <i>Such weak prey, these Heroes are. Reminds me of the people that I once worked with. Cheap. Fearful. Unable to do what needed to be done to gain the knowledge to wield to fight back. Blinded by self righteous morality when the world is being set upon by monsters outside. Is it not logical to throw those who are unable to see into the maw of the enemy to gain knowledge? Is it not logical to rip the secrets</i> <i>of your enemies out by any means necessary</i>?<br /> <br /> The Beast growled and began to claw into the glass, it's talons punching barely punching through it. The Slasher continued his work below.<br /> <br /> <i>After a while, the mind starts to see patterns. Roles, actors. themes, and moods. You start being able to grasp just what strings are being toyed with and occasionally subvert the roles. Is it wrong to dismiss the lives of the worthless that were serving no purpose anyways? Is it wrong to use those who were just occupying space? Your kind after all dines on terror and horror. You above all should understand. </i><br /> <br /> The Beast climbed into the hole that it had made only to find it's self confronted with another glass wall. A foot closer to it's prey.<br /> <br /> <i>So why are you here? The monomyth has been subverted. The Hero is being saved by the Beast and thus is not a Hero, if he ever was at all. </i><br /> <br /> Anglica redoubled her efforts, smashing and breaking her fists into a bloody stumps. She smelled death in the air, she smelled impending doom. She broke through glass room by glass room. Each just a little bit closer, each just beyond her reach.<br /> <br /> <i>Do you not feel it? The man before me has lost his status. He is nothing more than a broken wreak. A shell. There is nothing heroic about him. No desire to harm you now. </i><br /> <br /> The Beast finally had the slasher in the same room as it. It raised it's bloody claw to strike.<br /> <br /> <i>Why are you here? I am just killing a man. </i><br /> <br /> The Slasher's body was crushed as Anglica brought her claw down upon it. The edges of the corpse hissed as the dreamscape quivered and wavered. She grabbed the groaning body of the man and took a step back. She felt the rushing wind of the Astral as she was ejected from the dream.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the world, a man in a coma stirred to wakefulness.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the world, a Beast roused it self to the material.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the world, a Slasher awoke and reaches for a set of notes, the answer to his question escapes him still.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-05-2015, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:43:44-07:00","id":541079,"title":"","content":"So Ron Swanson is some kind of Anakim Tyrant, right? Incredibly powerful and impressive callback to a previous age with a recurring interest in &quot;besting&quot; people? He even spends one episode trying to prove that fear is a better motivator than joy and optimism, sows distrust in his staff because they were getting &quot;too chummy&quot;, and pretends to pull his tooth out during a meeting because &quot;it's always good to demonstrate to your co-workers that you are capable of withstanding a tremendous amount of pain&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:54:35-07:00","id":541096,"title":"","content":"Hmf...Why would a &quot;beast&quot; care about souls? A monster I could understand...but a beast? (I could create my own reasons I suppose)<br /> <br /> The more I read the more things don't make any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:15:25-07:00","id":541134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541071#post541071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ***Freaking Awesomesauce***<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You see, stuff like this is exactly why I don't get how people are saying they don't know what to do with Beast stories. Beasts versus Slashers would awesome, especially if it was used to subvert the hero-beast dynamic! I know its different strokes for different folks, and I'm so crossover obsessed that I'm building a timeline detailing every detail of the world of darkness... but Beast seems so rich with potential storylines. I can't wait to actually run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:32:25-07:00","id":541164,"title":"","content":"Why, in universe, Beast are able to restrain themselves at least enough to avoid becoming complete monsters, while heroes are forced to become remorseles psychopaths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:38:23-07:00","id":541172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541164#post541164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in universe, Beast are able to restrain themselves at least enough to avoid becoming complete monsters, while heroes are forced to become remorseles psychopaths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Heroes are Already Damaged BEFORE they become what they are. If they could ignore the Call they Wouldn't be Heroes in the Narrative Sense, they'd be i don't know... Seekers? Seers?<br /> <br /> ...... I'm Almost tempted too make a Template for Heroes who have recovered AND kept their Powers... I'd call them Bards.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:38:46-07:00","id":541173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541164#post541164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in universe, Beast are able to restrain themselves at least enough to avoid becoming complete monsters, while heroes are forced to become remorseles psychopaths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause the Dark Mother is a bad parent, but at least she has some mercy on her direct offspring? I don't know, haven't quite made it that far yet. <br /> <br /> Stretch goal has been passed! Fingers crossed that we get to poll for the Dark Era now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:38:54-07:00","id":541174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541164#post541164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in universe, Beast are able to restrain themselves at least enough to avoid becoming complete monsters, while heroes are forced to become remorseles psychopaths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Heroes don't realize that what they're doing is wrong. They believe they're the hero, and they don't see any reason to question that. Like any sort of moralistic crusader, they are utterly unaware of their own failings and hypocrisy. If you don't know you're doing wrong, it's a lot harder to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:46:11-07:00","id":541182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541134#post541134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, stuff like this is exactly why I don't get how people are saying they don't know what to do with Beast stories. Beasts versus Slashers would awesome, especially if it was used to subvert the hero-beast dynamic! I know its different strokes for different folks, and I'm so crossover obsessed that I'm building a timeline detailing every detail of the world of darkness... but Beast seems so rich with potential storylines. I can't wait to actually run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is that Beast isn't self contained and doesn't really have a system of drama between Beasts much akin to Mage's Orders or Changeling's Freeholds. The other issue for a few people is a lack of morality system to add the pain of being a Beast. Even werewolf, with it's telling of &quot;You are not human&quot; has it's harmony yardstick. Sure, you're a monster but some part of you must want human contact or perhaps some shot at being remotely human. As it stands, I see most of WoD's supernaturals would not even consider allying with Beasts but rather putting them down like rabid dogs if they have no concept of why they shouldn't be monsters. <br /> <br /> There is also the lack of a new ground being broken (Vampire has it's cities/cages, Werewolf has the Shadow, Mages have the Astral, Prometheans have themselves, Changelings have the Hedge, Giests have the underworld, Mummies have History of the world, and demons have the God-Machine). It makes complete sense to break the Astral open (yet again) as Mage is going to be more focused on the Supernal than the Astral but idk. It hones with a laser focus on one antagonist but that's it.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Beast throws it's self into an area which it seems to be the game line that attempts to bind all the game lines together (insert Lord of the Rings joke here) but offers somewhat little on what it offers in that direction. In truth, Hunter is ironically the best option to do so as it has organizations focused on dealing with all the game lines in a somewhat understandable fashion. Cherion is a supernatural chopshop that is built for profit, The Union is the everyman who simply wants supernaturals to get off their lawn, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Beasts, in contrast, have no underlining grander organization or ethos in dealing with other supernaturals which is odd considering they are the game line that has the most sense to do so other than Hunter.<br /> <br /> In short, Beast has it's (ironically) self inflicted flaws but I'm not going to crucify it like some people have but rather like to see what it grows into.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:48:10-07:00","id":541184,"title":"","content":"Becuase a Beast has always had the pscyho-spiritual infrastructure to cope with their Hungers-they can handle the strain of the Astral influence. Heroes, getting somewhat infected by the Hunger in a feeding that already hurt them to some degree, just don't have the necessary support to not collapse under the weight of that Hunger infection. They should be down and out for a while. Instead, Heroes consolidate themselves into a a more cohesive whole that stems from their survival instinct, exacerbating the sense of their self-importance to the universe, and instead become psycho-spiritual-and-flesh combos like the Beasts, but at this point they've still suffered the damage that makes them more dangerous in their mentality.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether the Hunger ever goes away or not, a Hero <i>can</i> over time grow their personal Astral Space enough to become more complete and sturdy,and this is likely why some Heroes end up just quitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:49:35-07:00","id":541187,"title":"","content":"Because beasts are sane. Beasts don't do anything they aren't willing to do to feed their hunger. A beast chooses exactly how they feed their hunger, whether it's as a crusading lawyer or mass murderer.<br /> <br /> Herodom is something that can be cured by therapy. <br /> <br /> You want someone relatively sane hunting beasts, there's an entire gameline called hunter the vigil, there's also a book about cops in nwod, heroes aren't a replacement The beast equivalent of a promethean's disquiet fueled mob, or mages summoning abyssal spirits accidentally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:55:44-07:00","id":541208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540744#post540744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm trying to get the hang of the Primordial Pathways rules, and\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026is Skeleton Key actually a more consistently effective means of getting into one's Lair away from one's Chambers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Skeleton Key opens <i>other doors</i>? No. I never got from the reading Skeleton Key was intended to use on the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:59:21-07:00","id":541209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540726#post540726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really talking about heroes. They can use it on, say, Demons just fine. Who don't even have souls. There's a sidebar that explicitly says it works on beings without souls.<br /> <br /> The whole family thing is a separate issue. I see only reasons why most splats would hate Beasts, not welcome them with open arms. For now I'm talking about removing (apparently just suppressing) the souls of beings that don't even have them, when soul removal has been rare and difficult thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>it's a liiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiie</i><br /> <br /> But seriously, Nightmares, being Astral powers, are more about convincing someone Soul-Deep that something is happening rather than causing something to happen. Demons don't have souls because their bodies <i>are</i> their souls(that entire flesh/spirit dichotomy), so while they can't actually lose their souls, they can be convinced of something to that effect. It's all mimicry and shadow play and getting people to invest in a narrative that is fundamentally false.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now, how this works for something like Prometheans, I have no idea. And in fact, since I haven't looked at the power yet, I don't want to postulate about all the other things that break my own logic here. But, in this case, this is how I understood the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-05-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:08:25-07:00","id":541229,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised the chapter on Heroes doesn't discuss superheroes and contemporary interpretations of the monomyth. Superman's a bit straightforward, but he does think he is objectively better than humanity, plus his obsession with Lex Luthor sometimes causes him to do some particularly unwise things. Then, of course, there is Batman and his menagerie of themed villains, many of whom would make interesting Beasts. What with how disconcertingly popular Marvel movies have become, there must be at least one Hero out there running around in spandex + cape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:09:29-07:00","id":541230,"title":"","content":"The last thing I'm going to say about Heroes is this: The first half of the book goes a long way to say hoe <i>evil </i>Heroes are, and how mean and cruel and sadistic they are and isn't that awful. But then you read the Hero chapter and the (HOLY SHIT THIS IS BRILLIANT) Storytelling chapter and you see that Heroes are <i>almost literally </i>reflections of the beast that made them, and <i>that</i> is why Beasts hate them so (they kill them and are mean yadda yadda yadda even good Beasts traumatize people to get their fill at best and they do it far more often then heroes get their kill on). <br /> <br /> Add to this that the Hero <i>can</i> move on. that they <i>can </i>escape the narrative, and I think I like them as antagonists. <br /> <br /> also, the best Hero on TV right now? Oliver Queen. Bar Non. *ducks*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:09:52-07:00","id":541231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540105#post540105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two people have urges that are negative and harmful. One of them is aware of the nature of the urges, can try to control them, to limit the damage he causes, and ultimately try and direct his damage towards positive ends. The other is either gleefully unaware of the harm his urges cause or just doen'st care because he's so important.<br /> <br /> A Beast could be either of those people. a Hero is always the second person. That's what I'm getting from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. A nuanced sympathetic person who's been victimised by a Beast's predation and decides to fight back against those Beasts that commit such crimes, and protect their other victims, is the backstory for a <i>hunter</i> - a <i>Hero</i> is something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541182#post541182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts, in contrast, have no underlining grander organization or ethos in dealing with other supernaturals which is odd considering they are the game line that has the most sense to do so other than Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that Beasts are rather like mortals in how they engage with the world at large. Most other lines more or less suggest that a supernatural's former human life will largely disappear - though they might keep it up, or maintain another one, it's more a cover story than a real life. Whereas for a Beast, they don't have an &quot;imposed&quot; new life to replace it - new abilities, and a new pressing need, but no new world to go along with it and replace their old one - their former lives feel more real to them than most supernaturals, even mechanically, via their Life. So my answer to what a Beast does it it's the same as what a (PC) mortal does. Live their life, try to get by, dig into the dark corners that surround them, hope to make things a little more comfortable for them and theirs - just that they have a big addition to the second of those things, and lots more talent for the third.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:14:23-07:00","id":541234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541208#post541208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Skeleton Key opens <i>other doors</i>? No. I never got from the reading Skeleton Key was intended to use on the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Finally, the Beast can use Skeleton Key to <b>force a supernatural gateway to open to the Primordial Dream</b>, even if it normally connects to another realm. The Soul casts a shadow across all realities \u2014 just like in a nightmare, <b>no matter what path a victim takes, he might wind up walking into the monster\u2019s hunting ground.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A gateway can only be connected to one realm at a time \u2014 either its normal destination or the Primordial Dream. If the Beast wishes to switch the destination, <b>she must end the current use of Skeleton Key </b><b>and activate it once again.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Seeing as this seems to incentivize the Begotten to squat around supernatural real-estate I figured it was intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:15:33-07:00","id":541236,"title":"","content":"D'oh, forgot about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date