<a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:00:54-07:00","id":541456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541359#post541359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any rules as to how big a beast's soul is, or is that a player's choice? And when in the underworld/hedge/whatever, does a beast stay in their human shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream Logic, therefore Size is meaningless. A good narrative rule of thumb is that all Dream Travelers have a Species factor added to their Health based upon their Trait limit, and the Beast retains full access to all of their Atavisms at all Satiety levels, and can activate Satiety Expenditure effects with Willpower. Therefore, your effective Size for your Beast Soul is 5 + 1 for every point of Lair above 5 + Twice your Lair Rating if you took Looming Presence.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, unless you draw your Lair into a given area via a Primordial Pathway, you are always in human form, Inheritance not withstanding. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:28:52-07:00","id":541499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541229#post541229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised the chapter on Heroes doesn't discuss superheroes and contemporary interpretations of the monomyth. Superman's a bit straightforward, but he does think he is objectively better than humanity, plus his obsession with Lex Luthor sometimes causes him to do some particularly unwise things.</div> </div> </div> </div> Point with the others, but I feel this first example does better flipped. <br /> Superman is an Anakim, represent the fear of someone being just plain better than you. He's either a Nemesis that makes sure to do good alongside fighting transgressors or a Tyrant who gets his fix through the envy and awe of those who see him as a paragon of morality and power. Lex,however, is a definite Hero, and the worst possible depiction at that; in most versions of the character, destroying or hurting Superman consumes his life utterly, all out of mindless jealousy and xenophobic hatred. Really, the only reason he isn't a textbook Hero is that he can pretend to be normal enough to have something like a normal social life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:33:16-07:00","id":541522,"title":"","content":"Huh. That's an interesting interpretation. I'm down with that clown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:43:20-07:00","id":541525,"title":"","content":"I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:50:15-07:00","id":541528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I treat it the same way I did when Awakening did it, only I like Beasts more than Mages as a whole: Namely that everybody else politely smiles and nods because they're not gonna stop prattling about how right they are, but when the Beast/Mage turns their back the listener pantomimes the speaker with funny faces while making a wank-off motion with their hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:54:16-07:00","id":541533,"title":"","content":"If it helps, consider such statements to come not from the authors of the text but from the Begotten for whom justifications of the kind form the structure of their cultural mythos. In the same way that werewolves tend to assume other monsters are Claimed, or how changelings wonder if everything supernatural is the work of Arcadia, Beasts contextualize their experiences as always returning to the Dark Mother. The strong crossover focus of the book just pushes that particular chauvinism front and center. So, whenever the text claims something like &quot;Father Wolf was one of the first Eshmaki,&quot; it might be good to append &quot;Many Beasts think that--&quot; to the front of such sentences. On a second read-through, on reflection, I think that practice might be helpful for basically everything in the first few chapters. The Storytelling chapter implies that the Children aren't nearly as self-aware as they like to style themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:57:15-07:00","id":541534,"title":"","content":"Just because this is what they believe does not make it the complete truth, or even a part of the truth. Hell, what even is truth? I've always thought of truth as a little wibbly wobbly, timey wimey ball of stuff that is very subjectively interpreted by all who see it. That is why everyone who sees something has a different story, because there is never one &quot;truth&quot;, there are many &quot;truths&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:58:01-07:00","id":541535,"title":"","content":"Hmm...I'm having a similar problem. I'll write out a more detailed post later, but I'm all about narrative, not the mechanics bit. And so <b>far</b> all I'm really seeing is that someone took Jim Butcher's skinwalker (naagloshii = evil super shapeshifting mage type character) and decided to build around it...on top of it and tried to recreate it into a protagonist of a sort. And in so far as I've read into the preview, it's not really all that pretty. (Yeah, I know the writeup is still in the raw stages) It's like we cheer the monster because s/he's fighting worse monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:17:25-07:00","id":541556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541534#post541534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because this is what they believe does not make it the complete truth, or even a part of the truth. Hell, what even is truth? I've always thought of truth as a little wibbly wobbly, timey wimey ball of stuff that is very subjectively interpreted by all who see it. That is why everyone who sees something has a different story, because there is never one &quot;truth&quot;, there are many &quot;truths&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised, though I should not be that people are bringing this up. Saw this in another thread and I'll repeat what I said there. Nothing in the Beast Kickstarter document says to me that Beasts have any sort of objective truth on the matter. They have ideas, beliefs,etc. No different from the conjectures, beliefs,etc of other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:18:12-07:00","id":541557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the Beasts' stories of the Dark Mother are not the ultimate 100% truth of the setting. They are just the present creation-myths spread by Beasts around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:18:32-07:00","id":541559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think its UTTER bupkis. mostly because, as written, Beasts don't have any sort of society outside of the Brood and therefor are basing this knowledge on... well nothing. They're the &quot;original&quot; evil, the first monsters, so OF COURSE everything stems from them, THATS why they have kinship powers et al. It can't have anything to do with their 'kinship' being traced to the fact that they are drawn to the fears and legends engendered by those creatures (which explains why Demons have no kinship [except they do] because they're too 'new' too far outside the context of what men think of as monsters). There's even a line in the ST chapter that reveals that they're connected to <i>Slashers</i> which shouldn't be because they're COMPETELY human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:20:13-07:00","id":541560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541528#post541528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I treat it the same way I did when Awakening did it, only I like Beasts more than Mages as a whole: Namely that everybody else politely smiles and nods because they're not gonna stop prattling about how right they are, but when the Beast/Mage turns their back the listener pantomimes the speaker with funny faces while making a wank-off motion with their hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening didn't do it. In fact Mages have a ton of names they give places specifically because giving them names helps many of them feel more comfortable with the fact those names are labels for &quot;Places we don't know fuck-all about.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:24:22-07:00","id":541564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just not seeing what you're seeing here, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:30:46-07:00","id":541636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>This Could be because the Beasts (Who 90% of the Book is written from that Perspective) want too feel important and Connected. The Dark Mother is a Nice Ideal/Religious Figure that they can use for that and because she was the &quot;First&quot; Then obviously her Children are the original Monsters, and all the others are imitations.<br /> <br /> Mostly they only have feeling and are Grasping at Straws, looking for an Answer. The entire conflict with Heroes is likely this at it's core, They need too know they aren't Wrong, They hate the Fact that Heroes even though they are Damaged come for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:52:13-07:00","id":541653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541234#post541234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Finally, the Beast can use Skeleton Key to <b>force a supernatural gateway to open to the Primordial Dream</b>, even if it normally connects to another realm. The Soul casts a shadow across all realities \u2014 just like in a nightmare, <b>no matter what path a victim takes, he might wind up walking into the monster\u2019s hunting ground.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A gateway can only be connected to one realm at a time \u2014 either its normal destination or the Primordial Dream. If the Beast wishes to switch the destination, <b>she must end the current use of Skeleton Key </b><b>and activate it once again.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Seeing as this seems to incentivize the Begotten to squat around supernatural real-estate I figured it was intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've mentioned before on p.156 how I think it's tougher and more expensive to use Skeleton Key. I suppose it's good if you so happen to find a supernatural gateway if your Beast can't make Lair Tilts and they're stuck somewhere to heavily penalise them, though I'd go for Primordial Pathways as they're much easier to achieve and less situational than a Skeleton Key is. Your Beast still needs either a supernatural gateway or a Family member supernatural to have opened some pathway for the Beast to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:46:29-07:00","id":541700,"title":"","content":"I had a thought. So far a few have recreated some tentacled makara to reflect HP Lovecraft's iconic works, but what if HP Lovecraft himself was a beast who never had his homecoming and lived the whole of his life just on the verge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:50:48-07:00","id":541703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541700#post541700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought. So far a few have recreated some tentacled makara to reflect HP Lovecraft's iconic works, but what if HP Lovecraft himself was a beast who never had his homecoming and lived the whole of his life just on the verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he <i>did </i>have his Homecoming, and he feeds his Hunger for Ruin by scaring the bejeezus out of everyone through his books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:57:07-07:00","id":541706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541700#post541700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought. So far a few have recreated some tentacled makara to reflect HP Lovecraft's iconic works, but what if HP Lovecraft himself was a beast who never had his homecoming and lived the whole of his life just on the verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually got a sheet for him as a mortal that I've been thinking of using to make him as an Ugallu. He can be a Night Gaunt like from his childhood and adolescent night terrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:01:49-07:00","id":541715,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about the question on Skeleton key and using it to travel through your lair. I get that we would need mechanics for traveling between chambers in a lair since antagonists would have to deal with it and of course someone in the group might end up going into someone else's lair for whatever reason. Where is the part that indicates we would need these for traveling between the different chambers in our own lair?<br /> <br /> The mechanic I'm seeing seems to work more for entering your lair from outside of it as opposed to going room to room inside of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:03:14-07:00","id":541719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541700#post541700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought. So far a few have recreated some tentacled makara to reflect HP Lovecraft's iconic works, but what if HP Lovecraft himself was a beast who never had his homecoming and lived the whole of his life just on the verge?</div> </div> </div> </div> Speaking of which, has anyone tried to pin down any of Lovecraft's other works? The Daemon Sultan, the Key and the Gate, the Emperor in Yellow, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:17:57-07:00","id":541736,"title":"","content":"The lair bit mentions you can reflexively let someone through burrows. Presumably that also applies to yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:20:25-07:00","id":541741,"title":"","content":"Are any of you familiar with Gogo Bomango? As I was jogging today I was thinking of the character in terms of Beast. Which fits surprisingly well.<br /> <br /> While Gogo adores a dragon, she comes off as an Anakim with a hunger for punishment despite her talent for ruining things. Thinking of the other other two main characters in WoD terms. Gog's sister, Didi, comes off as a Mage, and Andy, her human best friend/leash/something... to borrow the phrase, her Other, would be a mortal and the human reflecting Gogo's Trusted Friend merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:24:11-07:00","id":541756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541719#post541719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speaking of which, has anyone tried to pin down any of Lovecraft's other works? The Daemon Sultan, the Key and the Gate, the Emperor in Yellow, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnarly Nyarly and the Yellow King are both mentioned in Mummy, though not by name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:39:11-07:00","id":541769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>are</i> flaws with the argument, not the least of which is the glaring fact that Beasts seem to be tied to <i>human</i> fear, while certainly spirits like Father Wolf and Luna precede humanity by a whole shit ton.<br /> <br /> Their ability to interface with mulltiple systems that the World of Darkness works with is persuasive, but it's not <i>conclusive</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:48:19-07:00","id":541774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings are not born, however,<br /> <br /> but made out of Durance from the True Fae, whose behavior exemplifies the obsessive nature of<br /> <br /> Hungers. That is a secret the Children would dearly love to possess. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9zhKt9iyXDs\" data-code=\"9zhKt9iyXDs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9zhKt9iyXDs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I think.. I need to go for a walk and think long and hard about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-05-2015, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:04:11-07:00","id":541784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=540726#post540726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole family thing is a separate issue. I see only reasons why most splats would hate Beasts, not welcome them with open arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to return to this.<br /> <br /> I've used the metaphor of the uncle who lets you do cool stuff but also is probably doing illegal stuff around you before, and it largely sticks. When you first meet a Beast, it's thrilling. They've got a sort of animal magnetism that makes them cool, they make you tougher and more powerful, they can go anywhere and take you with them <i>and</i> not upset the locals. They aren't inclined to judge you for your monstrous needs, and in fact can help you do it-they're happy to!<br /> <br /> But then you find out about their hungers and their theories and their mentalities, and it's no longer as fun as it used to be. You have this friend who has given you the &quot;Whole New World&quot; experience, and now it turns out their possibly the worst people you could know. What do you do? It's a good question, and one both sides need to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:05:21-07:00","id":541786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are flaws with the argument, not the least of which is the glaring fact that Beasts seem to be tied to human fear, while certainly spirits like Father Wolf and Luna precede humanity by a whole shit ton.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, that's one thing among so many other things I've a problem with. &quot;Beast the Primordial&quot; refers to an existence at the beginning, but at the beginning of what? Humanity? I guess that would have to be it since they need humans to feed off of....o wait...what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:21:52-07:00","id":541793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541786#post541786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, that's one thing among so many other things I've a problem with. &quot;Beast the Primordial&quot; refers to an existence at the beginning, but at the beginning of what? Humanity? I guess that would have to be it since they need humans to feed off of....o wait...what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, persuasive, not conclusive.<br /> <br /> The simple fact of the matter is that we don't <i>quite</i> know the chronology of monsters, or the exact mechanics of how the Dark Mother and her Children can interface with everything. Remember, the Primordial Dream borders the Soul of the World and the Collective Soul of Humanity-it's quite possible the Dark Mother crossed over from the World Soul into the Collective Soul, and with that it's possible that she really <i>does</i> precede anything else. Then again, it could be she's younger and leverages human elements and involvement with the other systems alongside the World Soul and uses that to worm in.<br /> <br /> It's a very <i>persuasive</i> argument, because a lot of the precedents exist within Beast's framework. While having their own distinctive, rough but epic take on things, there is still many, many facets that mirror the others and create the possibility. Yes, they evoke human nightmares, but their incarnations aren't inclined to modern fears, but the roots of them, as well as brutal, basic desires that just aren't as prioritized today...superficially, anyways. It <i>could</i> be true. It's one of the simpler stories that could unite the World of Darkness that you could hope to find.<br /> <br /> But it's not conclusive, because no one can really know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:25:49-07:00","id":541798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541164#post541164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in universe, Beast are able to restrain themselves at least enough to avoid becoming complete monsters, while heroes are forced to become remorseles psychopaths?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Beast has enough self awareness to realize that they're a monster. The text outright says that most of them know this instinctively.<br /> <br /> Heroes, on the other hand, are both already screwed up in the head, and lack that self awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:26:55-07:00","id":541799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541784#post541784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to return to this.<br /> <br /> I've used the metaphor of the uncle who lets you do cool stuff but also is probably doing illegal stuff around you before, and it largely sticks. When you first meet a Beast, it's thrilling. They've got a sort of animal magnetism that makes them cool, they make you tougher and more powerful, they can go anywhere and take you with them <i>and</i> not upset the locals. They aren't inclined to judge you for your monstrous needs, and in fact can help you do it-they're happy to!<br /> <br /> But then you find out about their hungers and their theories and their mentalities, and it's no longer as fun as it used to be. You have this friend who has given you the &quot;Whole New World&quot; experience, and now it turns out their possibly the worst people you could know. What do you do? It's a good question, and one both sides need to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great story seed based on Family theme. And yes, Beasts are like a Family's Black Sheep Uncle to resto supernaturals - you know, he listen to hard rock or even metal, is a bit New Age, and smoke cigarates riding on his bike. He tells you totally diffrent moral stance to &quot;mainstrame&quot; Family, and you want to be like him. You want to belive him. Until you understand he has lousy job, he has no girlfriend, has problem to get up somedays from the bed and is totally unraliable to help you when you need it. But, hey, he is ssssoooo great to hang out, yes?<br /> <br /> This gives me idea for next topic to talk about...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:29:33-07:00","id":541802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541786#post541786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, that's one thing among so many other things I've a problem with. &quot;Beast the Primordial&quot; refers to an existence at the beginning, but at the beginning of what? Humanity? I guess that would have to be it since they need humans to feed off of....o wait...what?</div> </div> </div> </div>First fears of Humanity? I see a very nice parallel to Idigams of Werewolf in the Beasts ancestors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:30:58-07:00","id":541807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541799#post541799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great story seed based on Family theme. And yes, Beasts are like a Family's Black Sheep Uncle to resto supernaturals - you know, he listen to hard rock or even metal, is a bit New Age, and smoke cigarates riding on his bike. He tells you totally diffrent moral stance to &quot;mainstrame&quot; Family, and you want to be like him. You want to belive him. Until you understand he has lousy job, he has no girlfriend, has problem to get up somedays from the bed and is totally unraliable to help you when you need it. But, hey, he is ssssoooo great to hang out, yes?<br /> <br /> This gives me idea for next topic to talk about...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wholly, but yes: He's the rebel of the family, with the catch that unlike most rebels, this one can actually pull off bringing the family together than most.<br /> <br /> Which just makes everyone all the more uncomfortable, because that says a few things about them-but it can't, can it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:40:19-07:00","id":541831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541525#post541525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying my hardest, but I just can't get around how insistent Beast seems to be on having the &quot;truth&quot; behind everything else. I really don't like what the Dark Mother narrative does to every other gameline.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;Father Wolf was an Archmage's pet!&quot; all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the world of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It's only true if you want it to be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:58:15-07:00","id":541844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Beast has enough self awareness to realize that they're a monster. The text outright says that most of them know this instinctively. Heroes, on the other hand, are both already screwed up in the head, and lack that self awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Too convenient...It's semantically the same as &quot;Heroes are too stupid.&quot; And considering the monster that needs to dole out nightmares regularly to...anyone...Feeding off of humanity in such a fashion is even worse than blood-sucking leeches. Which leads to yet another problem I have; terminology. The word &quot;Beast&quot; doesn't work here at all. To me, these are monsters, not beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 06-05-2015, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:07:23-07:00","id":541848,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bad dreams that occasionally make deeply unstable people want to kill you&quot; and &quot;causing fear in ways that does not always cause harm to people&quot; is worse than &quot;mug people for their blood?&quot;<br /> <br /> Not all Beasts cause actual physical harm to people-I'm really only seeing it in predators, nemesis, and maybe tyrants, and then not all predators or tyrants.<br /> <br /> I don't see how &quot;hunting down and punishing people who break rules&quot; &quot;breaking the windows of rich jerks&quot; &quot;playing mean pranks on people to feed on their altruism&quot; &quot;being ambitious&quot; &quot;or making your prey know it's prey&quot; are worse than &quot;literally stealing the blood from people's veins&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires are worse. They'd cause more harm. A beast, if they so choose, could direct their hunger to positive ends far more easily, and the hunger for collection doen'st require hurting people at all.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't see how &quot;these people who are deeply unstable to the point of lacking self awareness(as shown by Integrity 4-) lack self awareness is the same as &quot;heroes are too stupid.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's um. Not at all the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:09:51-07:00","id":541852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541844#post541844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...And considering the monster that needs to dole out nightmares regularly to...anyone...Feeding off of humanity in such a fashion is even worse than blood-sucking leeches....</div> </div> </div> </div> While I do respect your opinion, my main issue with this is that the &quot;nightmares&quot; Beasts cause can often be reduced to the level of &quot;petty annoyance&quot;, like(to use examples from the Hunger for Power) being an exacting and incorruptible Health Inspector, or outperforming people who look down on you. Some Kindred would give their left arm for that privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:10:22-07:00","id":541853,"title":"","content":"Is like to point out that the Prey of a Predator does not need to know it was prey. The Predator just needed to be able to kill the prey at some point. They do not have to actually do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:19:07-07:00","id":541873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Bad dreams that occasionally make deeply unstable people want to kill you&quot; and &quot;causing fear in ways that does not always cause harm to people&quot; is worse than &quot;mug people for their blood?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> As someone that's familiar with what &quot;night terrors&quot; are; a monster feeding off the soul...is worse than a monster feeding off of blood. That's how I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:35:49-07:00","id":541880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541844#post541844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Too convenient...It's semantically the same as &amp;quot;Heroes are too stupid.&amp;quot; And considering the monster that needs to dole out nightmares regularly to...anyone...Feeding off of humanity in such a fashion is even worse than blood-sucking leeches. Which leads to yet another problem I have; terminology. The word &amp;quot;Beast&amp;quot; doesn't work here at all. To me, these are monsters, not beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you so hung up on the difference between &quot;monster&quot; and &quot;beast?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:49:14-07:00","id":541889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541873#post541873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As someone that's familiar with what &quot;night terrors&quot; are; a monster feeding off the soul...is worse than a monster feeding off of blood. That's how I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing.<br /> <br /> The beast only causes Nightmares when they don't feed.<br /> <br /> The nightmares might even be why they have to.<br /> <br /> Unless you have an integrity of 4 or below, all that happens when a Beast's soul ravages your dreams is you have a particularly vivid nightmare. not a Night Terror. Just a regular nightmare.<br /> <br /> So, physical harm that takes days to recover from, or a bad dream?<br /> <br /> Now, keep in mind that Beast's do not have to cause bad dreams to feed. Bad dreams come from not feeding.<br /> <br /> Beast feeding can be harmful, but does not have to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:51:52-07:00","id":541894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541844#post541844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Too convenient...It's semantically the same as &quot;Heroes are too stupid.&quot; And considering the monster that needs to dole out nightmares regularly to...anyone...Feeding off of humanity in such a fashion is even worse than blood-sucking leeches. Which leads to yet another problem I have; terminology. The word &quot;Beast&quot; doesn't work here at all. To me, these are monsters, not beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Um. Of course they're monsters. What game do you think we're playing here?<br /> <br /> 2) Of the numerous responses, why focus on this one? There were <i>lots</i> of answers that went into a lot of depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:54:57-07:00","id":541896,"title":"","content":"Considering what the Beast is in Vampire the term seems pretty appropriate.<br /> <br /> Though when they drink from people the people at least usually feel good afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:59:36-07:00","id":541912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541880#post541880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are you so hung up on the difference between &quot;monster&quot; and &quot;beast?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantically, &quot;monster&quot; implies &quot;evil&quot;, while &quot;beast&quot; implies &quot;animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, I put Vampires and Beasts on an even level, morally. Yes, a nightmare can be very traumatic, especially when elevated to the levels of night terrors, but one nightmare, even nightmares for a straight month, is unlikely to kill a healthy person, although admittedly torturous. One greedy or stupid Vamp can drink you right to death on the first bite.<br /> <br /> Although, to be fair, am I evil for eating a chicken sandwich? A chicken or a tomato might say yes, but I kind of have to eat to survive.<br /> <br /> The Begotten <i>need</i> to terrify to live. They can do everything they can to mitigate the suffering and harm they cause, and do so responsibly, but in the end, they must do it to continue existing.<br /> Moralize all you want, there's no vegetarian option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:11:59-07:00","id":541917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541912#post541912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantically, &quot;monster&quot; implies &quot;evil&quot;, while &quot;beast&quot; implies &quot;animal&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed that was the point, considering that the thesis of Beast is to subvert the heroic narrative in which the monster is just an animal that must be killed to further the hero's legend. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:13:42-07:00","id":541918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541912#post541912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantically, &quot;monster&quot; implies &quot;evil&quot;, while &quot;beast&quot; implies &quot;animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, I put Vampires and Beasts on an even level, morally. Yes, a nightmare can be very traumatic, especially when elevated to the levels of night terrors, but one nightmare, even nightmares for a straight month, is unlikely to kill a healthy person, although admittedly torturous. One greedy or stupid Vamp can drink you right to death on the first bite.<br /> <br /> Although, to be fair, am I evil for eating a chicken sandwich? A chicken or a tomato might say yes, but I kind of have to eat to survive.<br /> <br /> The Begotten <i>need</i> to terrify to live. They can do everything they can to mitigate the suffering and harm they cause, and do so responsibly, but in the end, they must do it to continue existing.<br /> Moralize all you want, there's no vegetarian option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, because the need to demonize <i>something</i> and why people have that need is a prominent theme in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:21:07-07:00","id":541927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541912#post541912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, to be fair, am I evil for eating a chicken sandwich? A chicken or a tomato might say yes, but I kind of have to eat to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The next time a chicken or tomato says yes, I'll consider granting your point on the matter \u2014 although in the former case, I might suggest that you go vegan. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Begotten <i>need</i> to terrify to live. They can do everything they can to mitigate the suffering and harm they cause, and do so responsibly, but in the end, they must do it to continue existing.<br /> Moralize all you want, there's no vegetarian option. </div> </div> </div>\u2026which argues that Heroes might have a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:26:48-07:00","id":541932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541912#post541912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantically, &quot;monster&quot; implies &quot;evil&quot;, while &quot;beast&quot; implies &quot;animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, I put Vampires and Beasts on an even level, morally. Yes, a nightmare can be very traumatic, especially when elevated to the levels of night terrors, but one nightmare, even nightmares for a straight month, is unlikely to kill a healthy person, although admittedly torturous. One greedy or stupid Vamp can drink you right to death on the first bite.<br /> <br /> Although, to be fair, am I evil for eating a chicken sandwich? A chicken or a tomato might say yes, but I kind of have to eat to survive.<br /> <br /> The Begotten <i>need</i> to terrify to live. They can do everything they can to mitigate the suffering and harm they cause, and do so responsibly, but in the end, they must do it to continue existing.<br /> Moralize all you want, there's no vegetarian option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is rather how it was presented more so than anything else. The kindred inflict arguably inflict more harm than any of the Beasts but other than the most deluded kindred, most understand that they are into some pretty fucked up shit. Beasts were/are presented as oppressed by Heroes rather than realizing that they are the natural outcome of very screwed up stuff. There is something very dark about abusers blaming their victims. Vampire simply calls that yes, they are monsters and are trying to hold on to what scraps of humanity remain while Beast seems to have nothing wrong with their actions until Hunters/Heroes start kicking in the door.<br /> <br /> The fact that the book pointed out the process of which True Fae make Changelings and stated the fact that Beasts are looking into creating the process for themselves simply highlighted and made me say &quot;Shit. Now they're just running the game about abusers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:28:19-07:00","id":541935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541927#post541927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026which argues that Heroes might have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of echoing superficial arguments for real world matters that might give the impression that I see an analogue I'm not pushing, my response to this is always &quot;Why? It's not their fault they're born that way.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can see why Heroes would argue that, and I can even conceive of a demonstrable effect on the grand future if Beasts were just let free to eat, but it's not like they chose this. Why condemn a monster for a life they didn't choose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:30:27-07:00","id":541936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541932#post541932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the book pointed out the process of which True Fae make Changelings and stated the fact that Beasts are looking into creating the process for themselves simply highlighted and made me say &quot;Shit. Now they're just running the game about abusers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, that part always made me squirm.<br /> <br /> Then again, survival of the species is a hell of a counter-argument. Dangerous, but still a hell of an argument.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:30:52-07:00","id":541937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541935#post541935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why? It's not their fault they're born that way.&quot;<br /> Why condemn a monster for a life they didn't choose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why condemn a Hero when the Beast's actions and inaction creates them? They didn't have a choice in the matter either.<br /> <br /> And Beasts do have ways to isolate themselves from causing nightmares to nearby humans. There's other worlds they can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:35:34-07:00","id":541945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541937#post541937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why condemn a Hero when the Beast's actions and inaction creates them? They didn't have a choice in the matter either.<br /> <br /> And Beasts do have ways to isolate themselves from causing nightmares to nearby humans. There's other worlds they can go.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I know, right? It really is a game where no one's at fault, and yet someone's gotta die. Terrible, brutal, vicious cycle of violence.<br /> <br /> 2)Also as mentioned, this is why the crossover thing is important-it gives you that dial to turn up and tone down aspects of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:37:38-07:00","id":541948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541945#post541945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I know, right? It really is a game where no one's at fault, and yet someone's gotta die. Terrible, brutal, vicious cycle of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's directly the fault of a Beast that the Hero is created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:39:15-07:00","id":541949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541948#post541948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it's directly the fault of a Beast that the Hero is created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Beast needs to eat and <i>will</i> eat even more recklessly if he doesn't.<br /> <br /> Cycles suck.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Unless, of course, it's avoided with Family Dinner. Which involves predation on other things and in other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:46:23-07:00","id":541954,"title":"","content":"My goodness it's looking like an argument is coming back up that I could swear we <i>just got done saying was turning into a toxic back-and-forth.</i><br /> <br /> Nofather, your opinion is known and your arguments have been presented and have not swayed anyone who disagrees with you. Please stop clogging the thread.<br /> <br /> Everyone else, please stop contributing to the clog in the thread that is this back-and-forth. It is fruitless, tedious, and unpleasant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Re: semantics: Y'all do remember that this game started out being about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serpents_in_the_Bible#Ancient_serpent\" target=\"_blank\">dragons</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Second_Coming_(poem)\" target=\"_blank\">right</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:50:27-07:00","id":541964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541954#post541954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My goodness it's looking like an argument is coming back up that I could swear we <i>just got done saying was turning into a toxic back-and-forth.</i><br /> <br /> Nofather, your opinion is known and your arguments have been presented and have not swayed anyone who disagrees with you. Please stop clogging the thread.<br /> <br /> Everyone else, please stop contributing to the clog in the thread that is this back-and-forth. It is fruitless, tedious, and unpleasant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Re: semantics: Y'all do remember that this game started out being about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serpents_in_the_Bible#Ancient_serpent\" target=\"_blank\">dragons</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Second_Coming_(poem)\" target=\"_blank\">right</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. it's a busy day/week, and I haven't kept up with everything going on in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:16:01-07:00","id":541988,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many different ways you can make Dragons with the rules here ...?<br /> <br /> Or rather, what Atavisms would everyone think were best suited to making a dragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 06-05-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:33:19-07:00","id":542003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541988#post541988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many different ways you can make Dragons with the rules here ...?<br /> <br /> Or rather, what Atavisms would everyone think were best suited to making a dragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonfire and Wings of the Raptor are both classics, of course. Basilisk's Touch is good for the poison-breathers. Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable are good for the invulnerable, while Limb From Limb, Titanic Blow, and Cyclopean Strength provide the raw muscle. Heart Of The Ocean and Monster From The Deep are good for the &quot;sea serpent&quot; type. Looming Presence adds both size and social prowess, Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song make you good at manipulating people, Mimir's Wisdom makes you a cunning dragon...<br /> <br /> Okay, to be blunt, there isn't a single Atavism that I think wouldn't work for a dragon. Except maybe Infestation. Even then, it might work for a dragon made out of a lot of tiny dragons, or one whose scales are actually hundreds or scarabs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:35:41-07:00","id":542028,"title":"","content":"Depending on the Dragon, any and all of the Atavisms apply. I'm letting a player in my Hunter game become a Beast and she's creating Godzilla. Imposing Visage, Dragon Fire, Cyclopean Strength, Limb from Limb, Monster from the Deep, Relentless Hunter, Titanic Blow, and Unbreakable work best for her. but add in Wings of the Raptor and you have a perfect dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:36:33-07:00","id":542031,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Infestation is the only Atavism that doesn't apply to dragons very well. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:37:07-07:00","id":542033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541927#post541927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next time a chicken or tomato says yes, I'll consider granting your point on the matter \u2014 although in the former case, I might suggest that you go vegan.<br /> <br /> \u2026which argues that Heroes might have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they would, if they were hunting Beats for that reason. But they arne't.<br /> <br /> They're hunting Beasts because it's literally the only way they can think to verify their existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:41:59-07:00","id":542039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541937#post541937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why condemn a Hero when the Beast's actions and inaction creates them? They didn't have a choice in the matter either..</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Beast isn't killing anybody who gets in their way just becuase they're in their way?<br /> <br /> And doesn't think they're the center of the universe?<br /> <br /> And does not blame all of their problems on everybody but them.<br /> <br /> Again, unless you seriously fuck up one Nightmare and have the bad fortune to do it to a psychopath, sociopath, or somebody who always has to find someone else to blame for his misfortunes, the only and most common way for Heroes to be created is a Beast to be consistently at low satiety, meaning they aren't feeding, meaning they aren't causing harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:44:55-07:00","id":542044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542028#post542028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the Dragon, any and all of the Atavisms apply. I'm letting a player in my Hunter game become a Beast and she's creating Godzilla. Imposing Visage, Dragon Fire, Cyclopean Strength, Limb from Limb, Monster from the Deep, Relentless Hunter, Titanic Blow, and Unbreakable work best for her. but add in Wings of the Raptor and you have a perfect dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looming Presence. the &quot;I'mma big Motherfucker&quot; power, is missing form this list.<br /> <br /> You kinda need that for a Kaiju.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:13:01-07:00","id":542065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542044#post542044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looming Presence. the &quot;I'mma big Motherfucker&quot; power, is missing form this list.<br /> <br /> You kinda need that for a Kaiju.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever reason I called it Imposing Visage instead of presence. But its there. And its awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:31:18-07:00","id":542071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541912#post541912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantically, &quot;monster&quot; implies &quot;evil&quot;, while &quot;beast&quot; implies &quot;animal&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> As I posted before I have a problem with the terminology.<br /> And I see a huge difference between taking bites out of a person's soul, and sucking a pint of blood out that person's body.<br /> <br /> So far, the only way to satisfy hunger is through psychological torture. What a person's playing at being here? Jeffrey Dahmer?<br /> Sure a monster would need to be around humans. Beasts however live without them. Which returns to my question &quot;Why Primordial?&quot; The word refers to the very beginning. I can only assume that means the beginning of humanity. Heck, maybe it should be called &quot;Monsters; the Horrors&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541927#post541927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026which argues that Heroes might have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. If people are terrorized by a monster then there is justification to go all mob justice.<br /> <br /> I'm still reading the pdf but there are some things I'm seeing that display that the writing is still pretty raw.<br /> <br /> From the pdf: <i>It\u2019s not easy being the monster everyone was raised to hate and destroy.</i><br /> Seriously? If people hate you and want to destroy you it should be hellishly easy! Feast away!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Anakim...I tried to justify them in an earlier post. But...really they should be the big guns in every way. The category is just too general. Why fear anything if I've all the power I need?<br /> <br /> The family listing for &quot;Eshmaki&quot; begins with the fear of being alone. But then the rest of the article seems contradictory.<br /> <br /> Hmf..maybe I should stop reading...These just aren't the beasts I was hoping for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:39:53-07:00","id":542077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542071#post542071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, the only way to satisfy hunger is through psychological torture. What a person's playing at being here? Jeffrey Dahmer?</div> </div> </div> </div>As ArcaneArts pointed out, you can use Family Dinner to feed too. With this method, if you think another splat's method of hunting is more moral, your character can spy on them while they do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still reading the pdf but there are some things I'm seeing that display that the writing is still pretty raw. </div> </div> </div>Yes, a lot is going to have to be cleared up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:50:02-07:00","id":542088,"title":"","content":"Concerning the Begotten's relation to the Unchained, I notice that the extent to which Beasts are driven to be around people \u2014 leveraging a Family Dinner requires the Beast be physically present, there's an overt range limit on who a hungry Soul afflicts with its nightmares, and generally speaking Beasts are incentivized to be imposing in both senses of the word \u2014 directly contrasts with demonic detachment.<br /> <br /> By the by, making sure I've got the Primordial Pathways rules straight:<br /> <br /> You can spend 1 Willpower and roll Wits + Resolve as though imposing Lair Traits, in which case the roll is subject to the same penalties for spiritual, narrative, or descriptive similarity, as well as the set of modifiers based on where in the cosmology you're attempting to reach your Soul from, unless you you're going to the seed of one of your Chambers or an exact facsimile thereof. Satiety Conditions further modify this roll.<br /> <br /> (You can grant someone else this ability to someone else via Be My Guest by spending a point of Satiety for each visitor so authorized.)<br /> <br /> This also works for attempting to create a Primordial Pathway out of your Lair, though going out blind imposes a hefty penalty to the roll on top of the usual difficulties with going anywhere other than the Temenos or another Lair.<br /> <br /> You can also leverage an existing supernatural gateway to lead to your Lair by spending 1 Willpower and rolling the Skeleton Key pool of Resolve + Occult + Lair vs the associated Supernatural Tolerance of a given gate.<br /> <br /> That about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-05-2015, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:56:31-07:00","id":542089,"title":"","content":"To clarify my position on Heroes: I'm not saying that Heroes should be, well, the heroes; I get that the game is intended to subvert the traditional hero/beast narrative. But I think that a lot of the condemnation of the Heroes involves overcompensating and needlessly characterizing them as cardboard cut-out villains for fear that if you <i>don't</i> completely and utterly discredit them, they'll steal the show. To me, that's every bit as flat as the traditional monster slayer narrative that this game is intended to subvert. <br /> <br /> To clarify my position on Beasts: the answer to \u201cit's not their fault they were born that way\u201d is \u201ctell that to their victims\u201d. Sir or madam: I'm sorry you were attacked or tortured by a Beast; but you have to understand that she had to hurt <i>someone</i> in order to continue living; if it wasn't you, it would have been someone else. <br /> <br /> In a way, it's a bit like the plight of a Promethean; and I'd say that it's a tossup as to whose existence sucks more of the two, save only for one thing: Prometheans have a way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:59:36-07:00","id":542090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542089#post542089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my position on Heroes: I'm not saying that Heroes should be, well, the heroes; I get that the game is intended to subvert the traditional hero/beast narrative. But I think that a lot of the condemnation of the Heroes involves overcompensating and needlessly characterizing them as cardboard cut-out villains for fear that if you <i>don't</i> completely and utterly discredit them, they'll steal the show. To me, that's every bit as flat as the traditional monster slayer narrative that this game is intended to subvert.<br /> <br /> To clarify my position on Beasts: the answer to \u201cit's not their fault they were born that way\u201d is \u201ctell that to their victims\u201d. Sir or madam: I'm sorry you were attacked or tortured by a Beast; but you have to understand that she had to hurt <i>someone</i> in order to continue living; if it wasn't you, it would have been someone else.<br /> <br /> In a way, it's a bit like the plight of a Promethean; and I'd say that it's a tossup as to whose existence sucks more of the two, save only for one thing: Prometheans have a way out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beasts have Inheritance. If they reach Apex, they no longer create Heroes, their Soul never rampages uncontrolled or falls asleep, and so they never end up Ravenous or Human.<br /> <br /> Or if they reach Satiety 10, they become Slumbering, which makes them essentially human. They just don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:05:27-07:00","id":542092,"title":"","content":"Nomenclature note: there should probably be a different name for the Inheritance that results from the Retreat, since it doesn't do to have the Eshmaki mixed up with the <i>other</i> Lurkers in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:08:02-07:00","id":542094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542090#post542090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their Soul never rampages uncontrolled or falls asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording of Apex imlies that rampages still happen, but that soul is more careful about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety</b>: The Beast Incarnate must still feed, but never loses control of its Soul. <b>It can venture<br /> through nightmares, feeding carefully,</b> or it can take larger meals if it wishes to put in the effort.<br /> The Beast Incarnate never becomes Ravenous or Human; if it falls to Satiety 0, it remains<br /> Starving. If it rises to Satiety 10, it remains Gorged<br /> <br /> PG 344","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:13:55-07:00","id":542096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542094#post542094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording of Apex imlies that rampages still happen, but that soul is more careful about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being immune to becoming Ravenous goes a long way toward surviving starvation \u2014 you don't automatically roll a chance die when Inflicting Nightmares, you don't need more oomph to restart the upward climb and you don't take damage from going hungry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:16:54-07:00","id":542099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542089#post542089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my position on Heroes: I'm not saying that Heroes should be, well, the heroes; I get that the game is intended to subvert the traditional hero/beast narrative. But I think that a lot of the condemnation of the Heroes involves overcompensating and needlessly characterizing them as cardboard cut-out villains for fear that if you <i>don't</i> completely and utterly discredit them, they'll steal the show. To me, that's every bit as flat as the traditional monster slayer narrative that this game is intended to subvert.<br /> <br /> To clarify my position on Beasts: the answer to \u201cit's not their fault they were born that way\u201d is \u201ctell that to their victims\u201d. Sir or madam: I'm sorry you were attacked or tortured by a Beast; but you have to understand that she had to hurt <i>someone</i> in order to continue living; if it wasn't you, it would have been someone else.<br /> <br /> In a way, it's a bit like the plight of a Promethean; and I'd say that it's a tossup as to whose existence sucks more of the two, save only for one thing: Prometheans have a way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there <i>is </i>a way out, it's called out as unreliable and the Hero tends to fight it every step of the way (not to mention the template itself-it requires Experience to raise Integrity, after all), so that's the disconnect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:19:36-07:00","id":542102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542003#post542003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonfire and Wings of the Raptor are both classics, of course. Basilisk's Touch is good for the poison-breathers. Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable are good for the invulnerable, while Limb From Limb, Titanic Blow, and Cyclopean Strength provide the raw muscle. Heart Of The Ocean and Monster From The Deep are good for the &quot;sea serpent&quot; type. Looming Presence adds both size and social prowess, Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song make you good at manipulating people, Mimir's Wisdom makes you a cunning dragon...<br /> <br /> Okay, to be blunt, there isn't a single Atavism that I think wouldn't work for a dragon. Except maybe Infestation. Even then, it might work for a dragon made out of a lot of tiny dragons, or one whose scales are actually hundreds or scarabs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or having an entire horde of Kobolds at your beckon-call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:22:04-07:00","id":542104,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time believing that in the entirety of fictional dragons there is not one made of smaller dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:35:59-07:00","id":542176,"title":"","content":"I feel at this juncture that I should point out that nothing in this book that can be taken as the consensus among Begotten is necessarily the absolute metaphysical reality of the game canon. While a given Brood might have a passing relationship with a handful of other supernatural creatures, that never implies anything better than secondhand, if not falsified, information about how another template works. And given the decentralized, horizontal power structure of Begotten society, such as it is, there's just no way to corroborate anything a given Kin tells them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:45:17-07:00","id":542198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542089#post542089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my position on Beasts: the answer to \u201cit's not their fault they were born that way\u201d is \u201ctell that to their victims\u201d. Sir or madam: I'm sorry you were attacked or tortured by a Beast; but you have to understand that she had to hurt <i>someone</i> in order to continue living; if it wasn't you, it would have been someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>After years of vampires draining people of their blood, werewolves forcibly terraforming both the physical and spiritual world, and changelings engineering extremely emotional scenarios for Glamour, <i>how am I supposed to find this a drastic change</i><i>?</i><br /> <br /> But putting that aside, this comes back to my constant refrain about this game: <i>this is about the cycle of violence</i>. It <i>literally</i> is the tale as old as time, the earliest narrative filled with tension and drama. <i>Everyone has needs, and when these needs are in opposition to one another,conflict emerges</i>. Every story Beast's live draws from the early days of survival, when surviving another day often meant someone having to suffer in kind. Even if it isn't as drastic this day, don't we have whole <i>wars</i> over needs? Is it too far fetched to have a game that acts as a metaphor for how the simple fact that, as creatures of need, we will inevitably have conflict over them?<br /> <br /> Because yes, I sympathize for the victims. I don't endorse the Beast who just feeds. I expect Beasts to wrestle with a correct way to eat. But I'm also not going to be the one who tells a Child that he can't eat. I sympathize with the Beasts as well. I can do both. I can also think that both sides are assholes, Heroes for reducing things to violence and Beasts for....well, objectively I don't have a good reason too(which may be the problem), but I can still hate them for having to do what they have to do even as I sympathize with them. It's a shit situation that feeds itself.<br /> <br /> But/And Speaking as a story? That's one of the best recipes for a story. There's a reason I rather like this game, at least as much as I like Hunter, Werewolf, and Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:51:52-07:00","id":542200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542104#post542104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time believing that in the entirety of fictional dragons there is not one made of smaller dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this one of those &quot;Would you rather <i>fight 100 duck</i>-sized horses or 1 horse-sized duck\u201d&quot; questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:54:20-07:00","id":542229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542200#post542200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this one of those &quot;Would you rather <i>fight 100 duck</i>-sized horses or 1 horse-sized duck\u201d&quot; questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bring on the duck. Horses of any size are murder beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:57:38-07:00","id":542232,"title":"","content":"Just an observation. Dragons are everywhere in fiction. Swarms aren't that far behind. Fantasy RPGs must have dozens of Monster Manuals between them.<br /> <br /> Surely there's a dragon made of other dragons somewhere. Even if it isn't a swarm, something like Voltron or Power Rangers where a bunch of dragons combine to make one particularly large dragon? Or a dragon that is so massive that other dragons just spawn off it like flakes of skin might off a person, red dragons oozing out like blood and taking flight. It's had to have come up somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:00:22-07:00","id":542233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542232#post542232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an observation. Dragons are everywhere in fiction. Swarms aren't that far behind. Fantasy RPGs must have dozens of Monster Manuals between them.<br /> <br /> Surely there's a dragon made of other dragons somewhere. Even if it isn't a swarm, something like Voltron or Power Rangers where a bunch of dragons combine to make one particularly large dragon? Or a dragon that is so massive that other dragons just spawn off it like flakes of skin might off a person, red dragons oozing out like blood and taking flight. It's had to have come up somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If there's a Fenrir made of snakes out there, there's a flight of dragons that like to huddle next to each other that breathe out even more dragons.<br /> <br /> God, this is a thing now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:07:37-07:00","id":542244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542198#post542198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After years of vampires draining people of their blood, werewolves forcibly terraforming both the physical and spiritual world, and changelings engineering extremely emotional scenarios for Glamour, <i>how am I supposed to find this a drastic change</i><i>?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The Changeling example is a bit of a stretch, as changelings aren't forced to prey on others. As for vampires and werewolves, let me just note right now that they're not exactly my favorite games in the nWoD; and to the extent that I <i>do</i> like them, it's because I can get around that aspect. Up until I read Beast, Vampire was easily my least favorite nWoD gameline precisely because victimizing humans was so ingrained in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:14:26-07:00","id":542245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542244#post542244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling example is a bit of a stretch, as changelings aren't forced to prey on others. As for vampires and werewolves, let me just note right now that they're not exactly my favorite games in the nWoD; and to the extent that I <i>do</i> like them, it's because I can get around that aspect. Up until I read Beast, Vampire was easily my least favorite nWoD gameline precisely because victimizing humans was so ingrained in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. This I can understand.<br /> <br /> As a note, if it seems like I'm getting aggresive, let me know. As I said, I do rather like this game, and I'm prone to respond as sharply here as I did for Demon(though I still like Demon more than Beast), but when I get out of the &quot;RARGH!&quot; mentality, it is easy to remember that I started off openly admitting this is not going to be a game for everyone.<br /> <br /> But god, it's conflict is so simple and easy while still being neatly rich for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:18:13-07:00","id":542252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542245#post542245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. This I can understand.<br /> <br /> As a note, if it seems like I'm getting aggresive, let me know. As I said, I do rather like this game, and I'm prone to respond as sharply here as I did for Demon(though I still like Demon more than Beast), but when I get out of the &quot;RARGH!&quot; mentality, it is easy to remember that I started off openly admitting this is not going to be a game for everyone.<br /> <br /> But god, it's conflict is so simple and easy while still being neatly rich for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been having this same problem in every Beast teaser thread so far (though I think I like Beast more than I like Demon, even if I really like Demon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 06-06-2015, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:38:12-07:00","id":542279,"title":"","content":"After reading a lot of critiquing of BtP here and on rpgnet I have to say... frankly I don't get what people are surprised by or complaining about most of the time. I do sympathize somewhat with the &quot;OK you feed your hunger and then what?&quot; questions, but nWoD has always had an element of player/ST creativity required to make it playable. The lack of explicit socio-political groups contributes to this, but I appreciate that they're choosing to move away from that model of conflict with this game. I haven't read the storytelling chapter yet, so there may very well be great suggestions for chronicles in there, but I find the general ideas and mechanics inspiring enough so far. A lot of the other criticisms just seem to be based on... it's hard for me to summarize but it's combination of &quot;this game is too dark/amoral&quot; and vague complaints about how Heroes are treated in the text.<br /> <br /> In my view, you're either interested in playing humans with Souls that embody primordial fears and have to feed off of regular people in some fashion, or you aren't. From my reading, the vast majority (if not the entirety) of the text portrays a game that fulfills that wish, and as always any details one doesn't like can be changed as one sees fit.<br /> <br /> Like, what more do people want from an rpg company?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:38:32-07:00","id":542280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aiden said</b><br /> I've been having this same problem in every Beast thread so far (though I think I like Beast more than I like Demon, even if I really like Demon). </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that makes it that much more of a challenge to play Beast really. For example, I'm making a tooth fairy Beast character at the moment, and thinking of ways that he can feed his Hunger to Hoard teeth <b>without</b> actually hurting anyone. One way that I thought of was for him to be a dentist, another was to actually pretend to be the tooth fairy; there were other less savory ways for when the Hunger takes over as well, but the idea of fighting that Hunger seems to be central to Beast. At least so it seems to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:43:08-07:00","id":542284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542245#post542245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. This I can understand.<br /> <br /> As a note, if it seems like I'm getting aggresive, let me know. As I said, I do rather like this game, and I'm prone to respond as sharply here as I did for Demon(though I still like Demon more than Beast), but when I get out of the &amp;quot;RARGH!&amp;quot; mentality, it is easy to remember that I started off openly admitting this is not going to be a game for everyone.<br /> <br /> But god, it's conflict is so simple and easy while still being neatly rich for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, your posts have been helpful. Thinking it over some more, my main squick factor is the forced victimizing of <i>innocents</i>; and I think I could get behind a Batman-like Beast who Hungers to punish the wicked \u2014 so long as he can maintain a \u201clet the punishment fit the crime\u201d approach (so no sawing off a jaywalker's legs, for instance). There's a reason why the WoD games I gravitate toward the most are Promethean, Mage, and Changeling. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which: how would you apply Family Dinner to mages or Prometheans? The text seems to assume that some sort of zero-sum game is involved: if the Kin gains what he or she desires, someone else must lose something \u2014 there's always a victim. But with mages and Prometheans, the things they desire most aren't zero-sum games: mages are addicted to Mystery, and nobody has to suffer for them to feed their addiction; Prometheans, likewise, seek Mortality \u2014 again, they don't have to victimize anyone to advance their Pilgrimage. So are they ineligible for the Family Dinner, or do they provide a loophole by which a Beast can sate its Hunger without hurting anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:49:13-07:00","id":542285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542096#post542096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being immune to becoming Ravenous goes a long way toward surviving starvation \u2014 you don't automatically roll a chance die when Inflicting Nightmares, you don't need more oomph to restart the upward climb and you don't take damage from going hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what that has to do with soul rampages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:49:46-07:00","id":542286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542280#post542280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I'm making a tooth fairy Beast character at the moment, and thinking of ways that he can feed his Hunger to Hoard teeth <b>without</b> actually hurting anyone. One way that I thought of was for him to be a dentist, another was to actually pretend to be the tooth fairy; there were other less savory ways for when the Hunger takes over as well, but the idea of fighting that Hunger seems to be central to Beast. At least so it seems to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They could be a Dentist slash Tooth Fairy, who sneaks into peoples houses at night, gasses them, then removes all their teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:51:26-07:00","id":542288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542286#post542286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They could be a Dentist slash Tooth Fairy, who sneaks into peoples houses at night, gasses them, then removes all their teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lZ3fsb3ak1I\" data-code=\"lZ3fsb3ak1I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lZ3fsb3ak1I/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:54:12-07:00","id":542289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nofather said<br /> They could be a Dentist slash Tooth Fairy, who sneaks into peoples houses at night, gasses them, then removes all their teeth. </div> </div> </div>And there lies the challenge, not letting your Beastly Hunger rule you, because if it does Heroes will be attracted to you left and right......and if you get overt enough Hunters too. Being that monstrous would also be bad in other ways as well, it could make it difficult to get allies other than spirits or low humanity vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:58:27-07:00","id":542295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542289#post542289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there lies the challenge, not letting your Beastly Hunger rule you, because if it does Heroes will be attracted to you left and right......and if you get overt enough Hunters too. Being that monstrous would also be bad in other ways as well, it could make it difficult to get allies other than spirits or low humanity vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Heroes find it harder to locate high Satiety Beasts, they get a bonus locating low ones. And you start with a good impression with any supernatural you meet, not including Demons from Descent, providing you don't act hostile or rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:00:07-07:00","id":542298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542280#post542280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that makes it that much more of a challenge to play Beast really. For example, I'm making a tooth fairy Beast character at the moment, and thinking of ways that he can feed his Hunger to Hoard teeth <b>without</b> actually hurting anyone. One way that I thought of was for him to be a dentist, another was to actually pretend to be the tooth fairy; there were other less savory ways for when the Hunger takes over as well, but the idea of fighting that Hunger seems to be central to Beast. At least so it seems to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bOtMizMQ6oM\" data-code=\"bOtMizMQ6oM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bOtMizMQ6oM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-06-2015, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:00:37-07:00","id":542299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542284#post542284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, your posts have been helpful. Thinking it over some more, my main squick factor is the forced victimizing of <i>innocents</i>; and I think I could get behind a Batman-like Beast who Hungers to punish the wicked \u2014 so long as he can maintain a \u201clet the punishment fit the crime\u201d approach (so no sawing off a jaywalker's legs, for instance). There's a reason why the WoD games I gravitate toward the most are Promethean, Mage, and Changeling.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which: how would you apply Family Dinner to mages or Prometheans? The text seems to assume that some sort of zero-sum game is involved: if the Kin gains what he or she desires, someone else must lose something \u2014 there's always a victim. But with mages and Prometheans, the things they desire most aren't zero-sum games: mages are addicted to Mystery, and nobody has to suffer for them to feed their addiction; Prometheans, likewise, seek Mortality \u2014 again, they don't have to victimize anyone to advance their Pilgrimage. So are they ineligible for the Family Dinner, or do they provide a loophole by which a Beast can sate its Hunger without hurting anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, without having looked at the old rules recently enough to remember even a general direction nor knowing properly how they work in Second Edition, still I think it's somewhat off to suggest that Mages and Prometheans don't harm anyone when they 'feed'. Mages can and will evict people living in a place to access their resources, and Vitriol can come from rather inhumane acts.<br /> <br /> As for the providing perspective, Thanks! That's what I like to hear.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can explain how I came up with Gwyneth Warren tomorrow morning as well as who she is, which also catalogues my experience with Hunger. Spoilers: it involves Swan Lake, emotional abuse, tropes I think I are overdone, and the sins of 2% milk.<br /> <br /> Seriously, who the fuck buys 2% milk. Psychopaths, that's who.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:02:13-07:00","id":542300,"title":"","content":"I started reading beast today. But it's not as exciting as reading these comments. Not to indicate I don't like what I already read. But well. I've already contributed and will be getting a pod when that's available. My favorite aspect about beast so far is the lair system. So I think when I run the game I'm going to try and set the plot up for the players to build up their lairs in a sort of way where they're trying to recreate a lost world or even building a new one with them as gods. And Heros acting the part of their version of lucifer and the rebelling Angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:03:06-07:00","id":542302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542280#post542280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that makes it that much more of a challenge to play Beast really. For example, I'm making a tooth fairy Beast character at the moment, and thinking of ways that he can feed his Hunger to Hoard teeth <b>without</b> actually hurting anyone. One way that I thought of was for him to be a dentist, another was to actually pretend to be the tooth fairy; there were other less savory ways for when the Hunger takes over as well, but the idea of fighting that Hunger seems to be central to Beast. At least so it seems to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>another option would be to forego literal teeth... maybe he hoards pictures of peoples teeth that he takes without their permission, or hoards teeth from the already deceased, or hoards the feeling of growing up that comes from children losing their baby teeth, or the feeling of aging and fearing death that comes from adults losing their teeth to rot and decay...<br /> <br /> I think it's a somewhat important part of the game that Beasts are victimizers, but that need not be physical or violent (and is IMO far more interesting when it isn't).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:08:15-07:00","id":542338,"title":"","content":"So the section on Conspiracy Theories says the following.<br /> <br /> &quot; Look to the most popular conspiracy theories in the real world; they don\u2019t hold up to even a moderate scientific inquiry&quot;<br /> <br /> Are the Beast devs seriously saying they think JFK's magic bullet is a scientifically sound concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:13:41-07:00","id":542339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542338#post542338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the section on Conspiracy Theories says the following.<br /> <br /> &quot; Look to the most popular conspiracy theories in the real world; they don\u2019t hold up to even a moderate scientific inquiry&quot;<br /> <br /> Are the Beast devs seriously saying they think JFK's magic bullet is a scientifically sound concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure how you got the impression from a statement that popular conspiracy theories don't hold up to scientific inquiry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:26:22-07:00","id":542347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542229#post542229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bring on the duck. Horses of any size are murder beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, yes! Why does no one else see that horses are the natural enemy of all mankind? They were designed for killing, people!<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I totally agree that After Vampires and Werewolves, soul munching monsters from before time began isn't especially evil. The problem is that they're claiming &quot;But I was born this way&quot; is malarkey. Vampires admit their monsters, werewolves just don't care but these guys excuse their actions and THAT is a pretty big turn off. (and this is from a guy who, after finishing the book went back and re-backed the game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:30:26-07:00","id":542348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542284#post542284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which: how would you apply Family Dinner to mages or Prometheans? The text seems to assume that some sort of zero-sum game is involved: if the Kin gains what he or she desires, someone else must lose something \u2014 there's always a victim. But with mages and Prometheans, the things they desire most aren't zero-sum games: mages are addicted to Mystery, and nobody has to suffer for them to feed their addiction; Prometheans, likewise, seek Mortality \u2014 again, they don't have to victimize anyone to advance their Pilgrimage. So are they ineligible for the Family Dinner, or do they provide a loophole by which a Beast can sate its Hunger without hurting anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't... unless you're present when a Mage makes a blood sacrifice. I think that Mummies too might stymie a Beasts attempt to feed vicariously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:33:53-07:00","id":542349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542300#post542300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started reading beast today. But it's not as exciting as reading these comments. Not to indicate I don't like what I already read. But well. I've already contributed and will be getting a pod when that's available. My favorite aspect about beast so far is the lair system. So I think when I run the game I'm going to try and set the plot up for the players to build up their lairs in a sort of way where they're trying to recreate a lost world or even building a new one with them as gods. And Heros acting the part of their version of lucifer and the rebelling Angles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! I'm letting a player in my Hunter game who is particularly broken have a homecoming, we'll see how it goes... The Lair system is by far the coolest thing I can think of in a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:40:29-07:00","id":542350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542244#post542244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling example is a bit of a stretch, as changelings aren't forced to prey on others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which just reinforces that Beasts don't necessarily need to inflict harm to feed.<br /> The book is weird on that, stating Beasts as always requiring torture to feed, and then having rules that give lots ways around that.<br /> Mages, Changelings, Prometheans, etc... lots of ways for a Beast to get by without ever inflicting harm on a human being.<br /> <br /> A Tyrant Anakim Bodyguard to a Changeling Street Artist can not only can get by on Family Dinnering on the joy his ward causes, but get extra Satiety from when he stops the Fae Hunters that come to drag his friend back into the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542348#post542348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't... unless you're present when a Mage makes a blood sacrifice. I think that Mummies too might stymie a Beasts attempt to feed vicariously.</div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB noted somewhere that Beasts can feed on Mages fulfilling their Obsession. No blood sacrifice necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:45:26-07:00","id":542373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542347#post542347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that they're claiming &quot;But I was born this way&quot; is malarkey. Vampires admit their monsters, werewolves just don't care but these guys excuse their actions and THAT is a pretty big turn off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how it's at all a different situation from vampires being able to say &quot;But I was embraced this way.&quot; I mean, low-level vampires can feed off of non-human animals, but that only works for so long. The game is still pushing you to be a monster whether you like it or not. I also didn't really see in the book that Beasts were even claiming &quot;but I was born this way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:52:50-07:00","id":542376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542348#post542348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't... unless you're present when a Mage makes a blood sacrifice. I think that Mummies too might stymie a Beasts attempt to feed vicariously.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't work, blood sacrifices are for bonus dice, not mana in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:57:50-07:00","id":542377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542348#post542348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Mummies too might stymie a Beasts attempt to feed vicariously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shuankhsen, tho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542376#post542376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't work, blood sacrifices are for bonus dice, not mana in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\">Using a blood sacrifice as a Yantra</a> gives bonus dice equal to <b>the amount of mana otherwise gained.</b> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of Family Dinner, anyone else catch that by all appearances you don't need to be a non-Beast to be a viable proxy?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p21</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sating one\u2019s Hunger is also easier with a brood, as the group can collectively derive sustenance when one member feeds.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T01:37:07-07:00","id":542388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542284#post542284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of which: how would you apply Family Dinner to mages or Prometheans? The text seems to assume that some sort of zero-sum game is involved: if the Kin gains what he or she desires, someone else must lose something \u2014 there's always a victim. But with mages and Prometheans, the things they desire most aren't zero-sum games: mages are addicted to Mystery, and nobody has to suffer for them to feed their addiction; Prometheans, likewise, seek Mortality \u2014 again, they don't have to victimize anyone to advance their Pilgrimage. So are they ineligible for the Family Dinner, or do they provide a loophole by which a Beast can sate its Hunger without hurting anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions for Mages; Disquiet for the Created. If it causes terror and strife, it should work, especially if it's reflects satisfying a primal urge. Disquiet works in a weird but not unusable fashion, in that a Beast would be more interested in failing to relate positively to people than in succeeding.<br /> <br /> Side Note: do you think Begotten will view Alchemists the same way they view Heroes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:14:08-07:00","id":542400,"title":"","content":"Afew things have come too mind... for me anyway.<br /> <br /> 1: Beasts Hate Heroes, this is somewhat true, but this comes down too envy. Beasts ARE Monsters that need too feed on fear, some of them might not like the Idea of a &quot;Hero&quot; Rising too defeat them, But can understand it. Heroes never Have too Question why they are hunting because EVERYWHERE you look in fiction &quot;The Good Guys&quot; are always Right So why would they Question when they find they are the Chosen One. Beast's hate this Fact Because it Essentially Says &quot;You and all Monsters Are Wrong and Deserve too Die&quot; Even if there are worse things out there then them or their Family. (Let's get real... Humans are Far Far Worse 70-80% of the time because that makes the Stories more interesting)<br /> <br /> 2: Beasts can Feed on helping others Feed... &quot;Yeah we get it&quot;, how about if i say they can Also feed by helping others self destruct... Or Say feed a Mage more Knowledge more things too Feed their Addiction.... Feed on a Promethean by helping Sow Torment/Disquiet and the Fear that creates of/for the Prommie. Not so Sure about Geists... But Think of the Possibilities for Subversion for a &quot;Monster too Monsters&quot; Beast could be like....<br /> <br /> 3: Incarnate Beasts are Horrifying. True Monsters that Set-up Shop and Could in Theory feed from an Entire City from the Fear they can Generate. Great too know if you're Hungry... Not so great if they are creating an Area of Paranoia. Pretty Sure we have an Example of this already in one of the Vampire Mythology Books.. a &quot;Super-Vampire&quot; that causes Kindred all over the City too start growing paranoid (more then usual) and slowly cause entire cities population of Vamps too Implode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:44:21-07:00","id":542403,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about You Are Meat, and while I really like the Normal and High Satiety effects, I've got to agree that the Satiety Expenditure effect is, in technical terms, hella OP. Permanently severing a supernatural character's soul with almost no chance of recovery (and in the case of the Deceived, literally no chance of recovery, since the Deceived are barred from the Primordial Dream) should take more effort than spending one point of Satiety and passing a dice roll that's usually stacked in the Beast's favor anyways. That goes double for Mages, since they permanently lose their magic under the effects of You Are Meat; compare with Excision, the lobotomy Tactic from <i>Witch Finder</i>s, which is significantly harder to pull off, significantly easier to recover from, and noticeably in theme for H:tV, illistrating that (unlike Heroes) Hunters can approach the Vigil in ways that don't involve murder (I was genuinely disappointed that <i>Night Stalkers</i> didn't have a <i>Dracula</i>-esque Tactic for treating vampires with blood transfusions. Likely a bridge too far, but still).<br /> <br /> The most straightforward fix, I think, would be to say that most supernatural characters are immune to the Satiety Expenditure effect. Beasts are already immune due to their souls being &quot;far to powerful&quot; and it would make sense for other supernaturals to be exempt on the grounds that their souls are to powerful/weird/nonextant to be permanently affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:47:27-07:00","id":542404,"title":"","content":"...I can't seem to find the default duration for Nightmares. Please help me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:49:49-07:00","id":542405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542403#post542403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about You Are Meat, and while I really like the Normal and High Satiety effects, I've got to agree that the Satiety Expenditure effect is, in technical terms, hella OP. Permanently severing a supernatural character's soul with almost no chance of recovery (and in the case of the Deceived, literally no chance of recovery, since the Deceived are barred from the Primordial Dream) should take more effort than spending one point of Satiety and passing a dice roll that's usually stacked in the Beast's favor anyways. That goes double for Mages, since they permanently lose their magic under the effects of You Are Meat; compare with Excision, the lobotomy Tactic from <i>Witch Finder</i>s, which is significantly harder to pull off, significantly easier to recover from, and noticeably in theme for H:tV, illistrating that (unlike Heroes) Hunters can approach the Vigil in ways that don't involve murder (I was genuinely disappointed that <i>Night Stalkers</i> didn't have a <i>Dracula</i>-esque Tactic for treating vampires with blood transfusions. Likely a bridge too far, but still).<br /> <br /> The most straightforward fix, I think, would be to say that most supernatural characters are immune to the Satiety Expenditure effect. Beasts are already immune due to their souls being &quot;far to powerful&quot; and it would make sense for other supernaturals to be exempt on the grounds that their souls are to powerful/weird/nonextant to be permanently affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once I get the chance to look over Mage 2e I'm going to look into how I feel about the power in regards to mages. I know I'm going to have Deceived &amp; Arisen be immune due to their souls being tied to the Rite of Return &amp; the Judges/Temakh's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T03:21:57-07:00","id":542416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542404#post542404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I can't seem to find the default duration for Nightmares. Please help me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally one scene. Right above the &quot;Eye Contact&quot; sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:55:58-07:00","id":542448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542279#post542279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, what more do people want from an rpg company?</div> </div> </div> </div>A thoughtful and emotional engagement with the concepts of monstrosity, &quot;monstrosity&quot;, and living with compulsion, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T05:58:41-07:00","id":542477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542279#post542279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, what more do people want from an rpg company?</div> </div> </div> </div>A narrative that makes sense.<br /> *lifts hands in surrender* I gave up on reading the pdf after I realized the narrative wasn't going to get any better.<br /> For all the reasons listed before and more not listed (and I'll delineate them later if anyone cares) I just won't support this project at this time.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:13:21-07:00","id":542483,"title":"","content":"I was hoping for a game that didn't take the side of horrifying monsters; the way Vampire doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:24:04-07:00","id":542491,"title":"","content":"Yeah...a person that may have been raped, a teenager that has been abused, a transgender that has been bullied since ever...may be one nightmare away from being put into the role of &quot;hero,&quot; i.e. the antagonist... and none of which has a choice in the matter. The way things are written now it posits the opposite, but the reverse can happen just as easily. So this goes from &quot;Beast the Primordial, to &quot;Blame Game the Victimization.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:33:47-07:00","id":542495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542448#post542448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A thoughtful and emotional engagement with the concepts of monstrosity, &quot;monstrosity&quot;, and living with compulsion, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Did we not get that in the current write up? I believe it explicitly states that Predators don't actually have to eat their victims, they just have to remind them they're prey. Beasts don't need to harm people to get their meal, and it even suggests this is only a short term solution at best. Yeah, you have to spread terror on a regular basis in order to keep your hunger under control, but that doesn't mean you need a body count to accomplish it; unless you're trying to become an urban legend or something. And you may not enjoy what you do, but you must do it regardless, or else people around you start to lose their shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:43:02-07:00","id":542497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542495#post542495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Did we not get that in the current write up? I believe it explicitly states that Predators don't actually have to eat their victims, they just have to remind them they're prey. Beasts don't need to harm people to get their meal, and it even suggests this is only a short term solution at best. Yeah, you have to spread terror on a regular basis in order to keep your hunger under control, but that doesn't mean you need a body count to accomplish it. And you may not enjoy what you do, but you must do it regardless, or else people around you start to lose their shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>A low satiety collector doesn't even need a to mug a person just go into a stire and buy whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:50:52-07:00","id":542522,"title":"","content":"@Shadowflame, Wasteful: I see those two things just fine in Beast. As Nyrufa pointed out, there is already sizeable nuance in how the book presents a lot of things. But then, that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> On a side note: though I'm loving the book, I see what some people mean when they say the writing is uneven. I see it, but I don't share the sentiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:02:00-07:00","id":542536,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, playing Beast is kind of like Johnny the Homicidal Maniac. If he doesn't paint the wall with fresh blood (literally), the collective madness of humanity will escape from it and terrorize the world!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev_PNWHlfXM\" data-code=\"Ev_PNWHlfXM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ev_PNWHlfXM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:04:28-07:00","id":542537,"title":"","content":"Just wondering are atavisms customed made as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:07:03-07:00","id":542552,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* I was looking for entertainment, an escape from reality...A game where victimization is a large part of the story isn't either of those. Nuance be damned.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:08:33-07:00","id":542553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542491#post542491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...a person that may have been raped, a teenager that has been abused, a transgender that has been bullied since ever...may be one nightmare away from being put into the role of &quot;hero,&quot; i.e. the antagonist... and none of which has a choice in the matter. The way things are written now it posits the opposite, but the reverse can happen just as easily. So this goes from &quot;Beast the Primordial, to &quot;Blame Game the Victimization.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the devs could put in a blurb up-front explicitly saying &quot;this game is not meant to be played this way&quot; and it would clear a lot of this up, right? I mean, everything I've seen from the present writers at Onyx Path has shown them to be on the side of humans of all varieties, I don't see them intending this kind reading at all, and think they would rather like to shut down people who would want to abuse real players (as telling such a story as you describe would be effectively doing given our ignorance of the histories of the people sitting at a gaming table with us).<br /> <br /> IMO, this lack-of-clarity is due to Beast being &quot;the crossover game,&quot; so they straddled all the themes they've touched on already. Without a bit of a disclaimer, I do see why some are reading it as a bit unsettling thematically, though I still don't really think the parallels between Beasts and MRAs, transphobes, racists etc. actually make sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:11:08-07:00","id":542555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542491#post542491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...a person that may have been raped, a teenager that has been abused, a transgender that has been bullied since ever...may be one nightmare away from being put into the role of &quot;hero,&quot; i.e. the antagonist... and none of which has a choice in the matter. The way things are written now it posits the opposite, but the reverse can happen just as easily. So this goes from &quot;Beast the Primordial, to &quot;Blame Game the Victimization.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I finally get why the game isn't hooking me or is just making me uncomfortable with liking it.<br /> <br /> I can't get over the dissonance between the glorification of the Beasts and the sheer contempt for Heroes. So much victim blaming. And then there's the Heroes on the Beast dynamic and it just becomes a mess. The fact that the portrayal of the Beasts throughout the entire text is really not that self-aware gives it that extra squick factor that Other Terrible Splats (e.g. Vampires, Demons, et al) avoid by virtue of owning what they are.<br /> <br /> The whole game just gives me an uncomfortable &quot;no, I don't want to go there&quot; feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:12:48-07:00","id":542565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542552#post542552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* I was looking for entertainment, an escape from reality...A game where victimization is a large part of the story isn't either of those. Nuance be damned.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that perspective, but then how is Beast any different from Vampire if we don't care about nuance? This is where critics lose me. I mean, all action-oriented fiction involves violence which means victimizing <i>someone</i>, and part of the buy-in is that the protagonist is mostly justified in their choices (though certainly not always, and reflecting on where they cross the line is an important part of processing such stories).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:20:31-07:00","id":542570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542555#post542555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I finally get why the game isn't hooking me or is just making me uncomfortable with liking it.<br /> <br /> I can't get over the dissonance between the glorification of the Beasts and the sheer contempt for Heroes. So much victim blaming. And then there's the Heroes on the Beast dynamic and it just becomes a mess. The fact that the portrayal of the Beasts throughout the entire text is really not that self-aware gives it that extra squick factor that Other Terrible Splats (e.g. Vampires, Demons, et al) avoid by virtue of owning what they are.<br /> <br /> The whole game just gives me an uncomfortable &quot;no, I don't want to go there&quot; feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the contempt for heroes is that while Beasts may be dangerous and terrifying, they at least have the decency to admit this and they don't hold any significant grudge towards Heroes as they can understand the reason behind their reaction to Beasts existing. Even if they won't lay down and die for them, they at least admit its natural to retaliate.<br /> <br /> Heroes don't have the same level of respect or decency. They are right and you are wrong. You're with them or against them. They can do whatever the hell they want because <i>&quot;its for the greater good.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Heroes are self righteous, arrogant, merciless and vain. When a Hunter kills, they do it to protect humanity. When a Hero kills, they do it for self gratification, bragging rights and glory. Hunters fear becoming Heroes because that would mean they start caring more about themselves than the people they serve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-07-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:29:07-07:00","id":542577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542570#post542570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters are self righteous, arrogant, merciless and vain. When a Hunter kills, they do it to protect humanity. When a Hero kills, they do it for self gratification, bragging rights and glory. Hunters fear becoming Heroes because that would mean they start caring more about themselves than the people they serve.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'd normally agree, the fact that they're caused by what is functionally cthulhu makes it hard for me to read them as anything but victim-turned-torturer, more likely suffering from serious issues. It's layers of messed up and not in that 'enjoyable thought experiment' a lot of the other WoD game lines can be.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I chose 'squick' as my adjective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:29:43-07:00","id":542578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542570#post542570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes don't have the same level of respect or decency. They are right and you are wrong. You're with them or against them. They can do whatever the hell they want because <i>&quot;its for the greater good.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the divides among the people talking about the game is the creation of Heroes.<br /> <br /> Some people think it's unfair that a Beast creates a Hero, no matter how, and suddenly that person is obsessed, because of the Beast, and so is an unsympathetic, scum of the earth type.<br /> <br /> Others don't seem to think it's a big deal, and seem gung-ho in the 'Heroes are assholes,' belief.<br /> <br /> Another issue seems to be the lack of, 'Things to do,' the fact that the text contradicts itself in places, the Charisma they have when it comes to other supernatural splats, and some people seem to have an issue with the myth, which they feel is more 'canon' than other books.<br /> <br /> Before I'm replied to being called toxic, or by someone thinking these are my arguments, I'm just stating an observation, since many people say they don't understand the problem people have with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:29:58-07:00","id":542579,"title":"","content":"A beast didn't ask to become a beast any more than a hero asked to become a hero. Both have their hungers that they can't really control. <br /> <br /> I don't really see how fighting a hero is victim blaming though. They're generally trying to murder you when that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:46:29-07:00","id":542615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542373#post542373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't see how it's at all a different situation from vampires being able to say &quot;But I was embraced this way.&quot; I mean, low-level vampires can feed off of non-human animals, but that only works for so long. The game is still pushing you to be a monster whether you like it or not. I also didn't really see in the book that Beasts were even claiming &quot;but I was born this way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you a vampire CAN try to say that, but no one bats an eye when a Hunter shows up to stake his ass, Beast as written in the first 200 or so actually talks about Heroes Oppressing them and &quot;if they just understood&quot; Heroes may be extremist assholes, but eating people is eating people. A hero's a 'villain' because he'd blow up a building full of people to kill the CEO's Silithid Personal Assistant, not because He's trying to kill the Her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:47:40-07:00","id":542617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542416#post542416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally one scene. Right above the &quot;Eye Contact&quot; sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, btw seems shockingly short considering the effects of some of the nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:50:01-07:00","id":542619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542350#post542350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> DaveB noted somewhere that Beasts can feed on Mages fulfilling their Obsession. No blood sacrifice necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Nifty!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:50:25-07:00","id":542620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542555#post542555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I finally get why the game isn't hooking me or is just making me uncomfortable with liking it.<br /> <br /> I can't get over the dissonance between the glorification of the Beasts and the sheer contempt for Heroes. So much victim blaming. And then there's the Heroes on the Beast dynamic and it just becomes a mess. The fact that the portrayal of the Beasts throughout the entire text is really not that self-aware gives it that extra squick factor that Other Terrible Splats (e.g. Vampires, Demons, et al) avoid by virtue of owning what they are.<br /> <br /> The whole game just gives me an uncomfortable &quot;no, I don't want to go there&quot; feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just can't quite accept that dragons, unicorns, gryphons, and such, tap into humanity's deepest fears, but...but not into the sense of wonder that humanity also has for these creatures...<br /> Things can go into various directions, but for some reason they only go into the negatives; Fear, Nightmare, etc..And our &quot;heroes&quot; have to be some self-righteous jerk that we hate, because there would be too much empathy from some person who has borne a life of abuse and just had that one nightmare that put him/her into the role of the antagonist.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:54:47-07:00","id":542622,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel any better the Hero probably murdered their abusers too. &quot;If you're against me you're with the beasts&quot; and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:03:03-07:00","id":542632,"title":"","content":"...why exactly can't the Begotten also embody hope &amp; wonder? It was how the Western medieval mindset rationalized monsters; proof that God could work miracles. There is more in the Primordial Dream than just the Primordial Nightmare.<br /> Beasts represent the negative, because they are meant to inspire the positive. Heroes are that positive gone wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:15:45-07:00","id":542634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542632#post542632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...why exactly can't the Begotten also embody hope &amp; wonder? It was how the Western medieval mindset rationalized monsters; proof that God could work miracles. There is more in the Primordial Dream than just the Primordial Nightmare.<br /> Beasts represent the negative, because they are meant to inspire the positive. Heroes are that positive gone wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't work from the victims' perspective.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:17:16-07:00","id":542635,"title":"","content":"Nothing works from the victim's perspective. The victim has gone soaring off the deep end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:19:48-07:00","id":542636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542635#post542635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing works from the victim's perspective. The victim has gone soaring off the deep end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only after s/he was traumatized by having a nightmare...and having no choice but to become this &quot;hero.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:37:30-07:00","id":542641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542620#post542620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just can't quite accept that dragons, unicorns, gryphons, and such, tap into humanity's deepest fears, but...but not into the sense of wonder that humanity also has for these creatures..</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a horror game. That's the only answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:44:20-07:00","id":542645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542491#post542491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way things are written now it posits the opposite, but the reverse can happen just as easily. So this goes from &quot;Beast the Primordial, to &quot;Blame Game the Victimization.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not saying I haven't explored aspects of what you're talking about, I think you're taking this a little too far. Granted, I get that what Beasts do hits really close for you,and I will freely admit, this is not a game for everyone.<br /> <br /> But may I remind you that this game is designed by <i>Matthew McFarland</i>? The Black Hat does a lot of dark stuff, but he seriously doesn't tolerate that sort of crap. You should have seen his response to someone making a dog-fighting joke, it was one of the firmest shutdowns I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, because you don't get a copy of Black Hat Matt(Cloning stretch goal maybe?) with the game, THe problem is not the victim, the problem is the victim becoming the victimizer, and that's also what this game is heavily about. Neither Hero-to-Be nor Beast is responsible for their lot in life, it happens, but they have control over their actions from there. A Nemesis can be a policeman and dispense punishment readily that way. A Tyrant can rise through a corrupt organization and clean up it's practices as he goes along. A Ravager can remind dictators and oppressors that they aren't untouchable.<br /> <br /> It's a little harder for Heroes/-to-be, because of the entire &quot;Hunger infection/lack of soul infrastructure/consolidation with roots in survival instinct&quot; thing, but considering that Hungers have root in a Mage thing, is it too much to expect that like calls to like? A Nemesis Hero-to-be usually has, buried beneath their fear, a desire to be the one who decides what deserves punishment, to be the moral judge so they don't have to be guilty. A Tyrant Hero-To-Be wants to master the hierarchy like his Beast, but is too afraid of it. A Ravager Hero wants to be self-sufficient, but has misplaced his view of how to be that and is afraid of moving away from the things he's used so far. When the hero-response comes, they consolidate, and the result is to <i>brutally take what they think they deserve</i>. Heroes <i>don't</i> just come from people who are traumatized-they come from people who are just a few steps away from <i>being the Beast themselves</i>.<br /> <br /> And in fact, that's something. Beasts exist to <i>allow people to confront their fears</i>. An experience with a Beast can be freeing, because the change in perspective can lead to appreciation of what one has, growth as an individual, recognition of hamartia, and so on. A beast can shake up their lives for a bit, but humanity can come out stronger for...without a need for violence. Beast, as a game, is about the, say it with me, the cycle of violence, and it condemns it quite readily.<br /> <br /> Again, No one's really at fault, but the people involved aren't squeaky clean either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* I was looking for entertainment, an escape from reality...A game where victimization is a large part of the story isn't either of those. Nuance be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, and you thought the <i>World of Darkness</i> was a good place to get that? A gameline about exploring dark themes from a company that asks of its' fans to take simple gaming and push it into an artform?<br /> <br /> Man, I make it a policy not to question people's play styles, but I feel I must suggest you're in the wrong neighborhood regardless. Kudos if it works for you, but still seems really backwards to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...why exactly can't the Begotten also embody hope &amp; wonder? It was how the Western medieval mindset rationalized monsters; proof that God could work miracles. There is more in the Primordial Dream than just the Primordial Nightmare.<br /> Beasts represent the negative, because they are meant to inspire the positive. Heroes are that positive gone wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can embody those things But not everyone does. At the roots, those stories have to do with fear, fairly universally. Not all of them embody hope and wonder. So, all Beasts have something to do with fear.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a monster that embodies hope and wonder, then you can. But that depends on you <i>being the monster who inspires</i>. The game won't do that for you, because it comes to the character to be those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:54:41-07:00","id":542649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542578#post542578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the divides among the people talking about the game is the creation of Heroes.<br /> <br /> Some people think it's unfair that a Beast creates a Hero, no matter how, and suddenly that person is obsessed, because of the Beast, and so is an unsympathetic, scum of the earth type.<br /> <br /> Others don't seem to think it's a big deal, and seem gung-ho in the 'Heroes are assholes,' belief.<br /> <br /> <b>Another issue seems to be the lack of, 'Things to do,' the fact that the text contradicts itself in places, the Charisma they have when it comes to other supernatural splats, and some people seem to have an issue with the myth, which they feel is more 'canon' than other books.</b><br /> <br /> Before I'm replied to being called toxic, or by someone thinking these are my arguments, I'm just stating an observation, since many people say they don't understand the problem people have with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded text is a problem I have with a lot of the posts here. Folks keep assuming that if it's not explicitly said by a character, then it must be the unvarnished truth, which is a ridiculous notion. All the evidence points to most of the stuff in the book relating to how things work is largely secondhand information, or outright lies, so trusting it, let alone being angered by it, is a waste of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:02:35-07:00","id":542650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542495#post542495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we not get that in the current write up? I believe it explicitly states that Predators don't actually have to eat their victims, they just have to remind them they're prey. Beasts don't need to harm people to get their meal, and it even suggests this is only a short term solution at best. Yeah, you have to spread terror on a regular basis in order to keep your hunger under control, but that doesn't mean you need a body count to accomplish it; unless you're trying to become an urban legend or something. And you may not enjoy what you do, but you must do it regardless, or else people around you start to lose their shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes to Ye of Little Faith's comment as well, but I don't really see how those nuances really form a thoughtful engagement with the subject matter. It's the equivalent of vampires being able to drink from squirrels and blood bags, and writing a sentence about how sometimes they feel bad about it anyhow. I mean, especially the bit about Predators not having to kill their prey. That's not engagement, that's just &quot;can we make it so this Hunger isn't solely comprised of serial killers?&quot;<br /> <br /> If it would be helpful, I can put together something elaborating on what I mean by &quot;thoughtful and emotional engagement&quot;. I haven't here because it might be unnecessary and long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:04:39-07:00","id":542654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542615#post542615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you a vampire CAN try to say that, but no one bats an eye when a Hunter shows up to stake his ass, Beast as written in the first 200 or so actually talks about Heroes Oppressing them and &quot;if they just understood&quot; Heroes may be extremist assholes, but eating people is eating people. A hero's a 'villain' because he'd blow up a building full of people to kill the CEO's Silithid Personal Assistant, not because He's trying to kill the Her.</div> </div> </div> </div> Some beasts are complete monsters, they don't need heroes to take them on, there's such a thing as hunters, cops, angry mobs, other beasts, and other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Heroes want to commit genocide for a power up and an ego boost, and don't care if their target is a complete monster or a living saint. <br /> <br /> They don't just want to kill beasts, they objectify them.<br /> <br /> I very much doubt that many of the people complaining about heroes being villains would be too charitable if someone wanted to kill them and all their friends and justified it with &quot;It's not like you're really people or anything.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:05:14-07:00","id":542655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542649#post542649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bolded text is a problem I have with a lot of the posts here. Folks keep assuming that if it's not explicitly said by a character, then it must be the unvarnished truth, which is a ridiculous notion. All the evidence points to most of the stuff in the book relating to how things work is largely secondhand information, or outright lies, so trusting it, let alone being angered by it, is a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I am seriously having trouble spotting anything in the category of certain metaphysical statements about Kinship that that isn't in the immediate vicinity of &quot;Beasts believe&quot; or an equivalent.<br /> <br /> Jakki brought up &quot;Father Wolf was an archmage's pet!&quot; from when Imperial Mysteries came out. Thing is, I <i>remember</i> that happening, and <i>it was fandom histrionics rather than anything the book did more than indirectly indicate was possible</i>, which is more on the sort of person who plays a starting Thyrsus and tries to summon Luna to proclaim their superiority over the werewolves in their crossover game than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:07:21-07:00","id":542657,"title":"","content":"Also, do people here just not understand what Integrity and Breaking Points represent? You aren't as likely to lose Integrity by being a victim per se, but mainly by being a perpetrator, or having your worldview challenged. So it doesn't exactly work that a history of victimization is a prerequisite for becoming a Hero, while a history of antisocial behavior is a much more common determinant, exposure to other supernatural phenomena not withstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  fact-checking 06-06-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:15:14-07:00","id":542664,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what Matt thinks of all of this discussion that's been going on. I'm not saying he has to come down and tell us, but I'm still curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:25:26-07:00","id":542685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542664#post542664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what Matt thinks of all of this discussion that's been going on. I'm not saying he has to come down and tell us, but I'm still curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it's a bit more nuanced than 75% of what I've found myself saying aloud while reading this thread, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:26:28-07:00","id":542686,"title":"","content":"Matt curses in iambic pentameter. True story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:28:55-07:00","id":542689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542634#post542634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't work from the victims' perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that this discussion is taking place in good faith and is only about the philosophical concepts involved. I'm also agreeing to your buy-in that Heroes are victims, which does not sit well with me but is not the point I'm attempting to contest.<br /> <br /> The book <i>does</i> idicate that it is at least partially the Hero's choice to become a Hero. In the form of the <b>Hunter's Response</b>. IC the Begotten don't know why some people become Heroes but not others. Hunters are known to exist. It takes a damaged soul to even possibly transform into a Hero, but anyone can become a monster slayer. One does not have to continue the cycle of abuse, they have other legitimate options. Why don't they become keepers of the Vigil?<br /> On some level the Hero chooses to not only fight back; but that the ends justify any means because <i>they say so</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying hunters are any better, but they retain the capaicity to be better. To develop new tools (Endowments) and techniques (Tactics), to build a better world. Heroes can't see big picture, because they are so focused on what happened to them, how they are going to step up and do what no-one has, what no-one else can.<br /> <br /> Heroes are objectively tragic.<br /> <br /> Beasts, on the other hand, are trapped in their own skin. They don't just suffer the same sort of nightmares that create Heroes for <i>years on end</i>. They have to accept that the thing that frightens them, that has been hunting them is <i>themselves</i>. No wonder they are relieved when they have their Homecoming, they literally figured out how to stop self-harming. Not to mention those strange urges that they have always been living with, that society tells them are unnatural and immoral are not going away, are normal...and ignoring them is painful both for themselves and the people around them. The Begotten have to deal with the fact that they don't belong in their own bodies, their world and their human families will probably never understand.<br /> Why do you think Family &amp; Kin play such a large role for them? For the first time in forever, they aren't alone.<br /> <br /> However, I've gone off-topic. Fear can be a great motivator. It motivates the Hero's initial journey, the Beast's Homecoming, weapons, clothes, agriculture and argumentally the founding of civilization itself. It's not too far fetched to say that it can be used to motivate people to do great things. There is no reason that cannot be present in the game. The Begotten are strange beings that can go almost anywhere, be almost anything...why shouldn't those who look upon their Souls feel wonderment as well as terror?<br /> <br /> In the end though, you have to decide what the game means to you. It does no-one any good to remove all positive options from the table. Consider how you would play it and still have fun. It might be a struggle for your personal tastes, but often the best stories are struggles, characters torn between their own conflicting motivations. At least give it a try.<br /> <br /> @ArcaneArts: I disagree. Hope, wonder and inspiration are coming from the audience not the Beast. The Begotten was just there, being seen. What the viewers take away from the experience is their own thoughts and feelings. Besides, I never said the Begotten ever stopped being scary.<br /> Godzilla might be amazing to behold in the flesh. I'm still going to run away as fast as I can though. Afterwards, reflecting on the matter, I may geek out and wonder if this means if there is other kaiju out there but Fear still played a role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-06-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:37:47-07:00","id":542692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542657#post542657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do people here just not understand what Integrity and Breaking Points represent? You don't lose them by being a victim per se, but mainly by being a perpetrator, or having your worldview challenged. So it doesn't exactly work that a history of victimization is a prerequisite for becoming a Hero, while a history of antisocial behavior is a fairly common determinant, exposure to other supernatural phenomena not withstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I think Integrity is better than Morality was, its flexibility causes huge problems when Heroes are introduced. You can get to 4 by being a huge jerk, by having people be increasingly huge jerks to you, by any mixture of the two, or by mixture of the two plus seeing the supernatural. Beast realizes this, but doesn't really want to deal with the repercussions, so you get pg. 399's incredibly weird &quot;Heroes and Integrity&quot; section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:39:44-07:00","id":542694,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat perplexed by two things.<br /> <br /> One, that people conflate Vampire feeding to Beast feeding.<br /> Two, that the common position seems to be that these actions are approximately equivalent.<br /> <br /> I posit that they are not, not even slightly.<br /> <br /> See, Vampire assumes one of two primary feeding methods:<br /> <br /> First and foremost that you will convince your &quot;victim&quot; to consent. Herds, blood dolls, ghouls, old-fashioned seduction, whatever. The Kiss is pleasurable and has no more adverse side-effects than donating blood (usually less, if the vampire is careful). It is not harmful by default. As with most things in life, the dose makes the poison, and a little Kiss does no harm at all. A vampire's food can be willing and left unharmed by the experience. You can't condemn willing vampire bites any more than you can condemn alcohol or a tattoo. It's the same level of &quot;harm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, and admittedly worse, is feeding from the unaware (mostly Mekhet and Nosferatu do this). Still, though, if the vampire takes care not to over-feed, they are never even aware that something happened and experience no negative effects from the bite.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that vampire bites are never bad. Done aggressively, or without restraint, or in a frenzy, there are victims being made. It can and does happen. In fact, it almost certainly will happen at least once for every vampire. And, I suppose similarly to Beasts, taking this path is going to lead to people out to kill you. Hunters. Friends of the victim. Police. Whatever.<br /> <br /> The difference is the default for Beast is explicitly harmful, and they take specific powers and effort to not harm.<br /> <br /> The default for vampires is explicitly mutually (if not equally) beneficial or neutral, and it takes specific effort or lack of good judgment to harm.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure someone will bring up lethal damage from feeding. 1: If it was consented to, it's still no worse than anything else people can consent to that causes physical damage, like alcohol or even extreme sports. 2: Given that the Kiss leaves no physical marks, one has to assume the damage is just a crude mechanical representation of blood loss and the time it takes the body to replace it, not actual physical injury.)<br /> <br /> I think the line of thinking that Beasts feeding are no worse than Vampires is a bit misleading or ill-informed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:58:07-07:00","id":542717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542650#post542650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This goes to Ye of Little Faith's comment as well, but I don't really see how those nuances really form a thoughtful engagement with the subject matter. It's the equivalent of vampires being able to drink from squirrels and blood bags, and writing a sentence about how sometimes they feel bad about it anyhow. I mean, especially the bit about Predators not having to kill their prey. That's not engagement, that's just &quot;can we make it so this Hunger isn't solely comprised of serial killers?&quot;<br /> <br /> If it would be helpful, I can put together something elaborating on what I mean by &quot;thoughtful and emotional engagement&quot;. I haven't here because it might be unnecessary and long.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a single example of the many strokes of nuance you might find in the text. Far from the only one or even the most engaging.<br /> <br /> We may have different ideas of what constitutes nuanced writing with thoughtful and emotional engagement, but I still find the best of it in the relationship between Beasts and Heroes. I won't go into detail because, well, at this point it's really been discussed and elaborated enough and I doubt repeating will suffice to change a deeply different opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-06-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T10:37:54-07:00","id":542740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542694#post542694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm somewhat perplexed by two things.<br /> <br /> One, that people conflate Vampire feeding to Beast feeding.<br /> Two, that the common position seems to be that these actions are approximately equivalent.<br /> <br /> I posit that they are not, not even slightly.<br /> <br /> See, Vampire assumes one of two primary feeding methods:<br /> <br /> First and foremost that you will convince your &quot;victim&quot; to consent. Herds, blood dolls, ghouls, old-fashioned seduction, whatever. The Kiss is pleasurable and has no more adverse side-effects than donating blood (usually less, if the vampire is careful). It is not harmful by default. As with most things in life, the dose makes the poison, and a little Kiss does no harm at all. A vampire's food can be willing and left unharmed by the experience. You can't condemn willing vampire bites any more than you can condemn alcohol or a tattoo. It's the same level of &quot;harm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, and admittedly worse, is feeding from the unaware (mostly Mekhet and Nosferatu do this). Still, though, if the vampire takes care not to over-feed, they are never even aware that something happened and experience no negative effects from the bite.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that vampire bites are never bad. Done aggressively, or without restraint, or in a frenzy, there are victims being made. It can and does happen. In fact, it almost certainly will happen at least once for every vampire. And, I suppose similarly to Beasts, taking this path is going to lead to people out to kill you. Hunters. Friends of the victim. Police. Whatever.<br /> <br /> The difference is the default for Beast is explicitly harmful, and they take specific powers and effort to not harm.<br /> <br /> The default for vampires is explicitly mutually (if not equally) beneficial or neutral, and it takes specific effort or lack of good judgment to harm.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure someone will bring up lethal damage from feeding. 1: If it was consented to, it's still no worse than anything else people can consent to that causes physical damage, like alcohol or even extreme sports. 2: Given that the Kiss leaves no physical marks, one has to assume the damage is just a crude mechanical representation of blood loss and the time it takes the body to replace it, not actual physical injury.)<br /> <br /> I think the line of thinking that Beasts feeding are no worse than Vampires is a bit misleading or ill-informed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;default,&quot; you mean having the most favorable Opportunity Cost, then you are comparing apples and oranges. It's far easier to utilize Family Dinner for Satiety recovery than it is to actuate the Hunger mechanic, and less overtly harmful. Even if you aren't explicitly running a Crossover game, Kinship can still be a factor in determining how a Beast survives. It's only fair to compare all of their feeding options, not just the ones you only perceive as requiring the same amount of effort.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:01:23-07:00","id":542748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542740#post542740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by &quot;default,&quot; you mean having the most favorable Opportunity Cost, then you are comparing apples and oranges. It's far easier to utilize Family Dinner for Satiety recovery than it is to actuate the Hunger mechanic, and less overtly harmful. Even if you aren't explicitly running a Crossover game, Kinship can still be a factor in determining how a Beast survives. It's only fair to compare all of their feeding options, not just the ones you only perceive as requiring the same amount of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's try default as &quot;in the absence of extenuating/non-standard factors which may include, but are not limited to, supernatural powers not ubiquitous to the splat or magical wingmen to leech off of.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is, a vampire who is not frenzying, who is not on an extreme fringe of Humanity, who has no access to powers that provide alternate feeding methods, who does not have a benefactor that hand-feeds them, will almost certainly feed in one of the two above methods. Violent, victim-making feeding is the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> The opposite is true for Beasts. Barring non-standard circumstances (like having a power that grants alternate feeding methods, or having a buddy from another splat that lets him play remora), a Beast feeding is a harmful act, unless I missed a standard power Beasts have to let them feed without extra help from powers or other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> If Beasts do have such an easy, benevolent option, then they are more like Vampires than I gave credit. The part I take issue with, however, is the idea that vampire feeding is innately harmful. The comparison between Beasts and Vampires doesn't bother me so long as it's accurate, so I'm not particularly bothered if it turns out I missed something on the Beast side.<br /> <br /> It'd be rather hypocritical for me to continue to perpetuate bad information on Beasts when I'm trying to stop that very thing vis-a-vis vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:12:10-07:00","id":542759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542740#post542740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by &quot;default,&quot; you mean having the most favorable Opportunity Cost, then you are comparing apples and oranges. It's far easier to utilize Family Dinner for Satiety recovery than it is to actuate the Hunger mechanic, and less overtly harmful. Even if you aren't explicitly running a Crossover game, Kinship can still be a factor in determining how a Beast survives. It's only fair to compare all of their feeding options, not just the ones you only perceive as requiring the same amount of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he means default in terms of its usage in the text. When Beast talks about a just-born Hero &quot;watching the Beast feeding or otherwise wreaking havoc&quot; (pg. 275), it pretty clearly doesn't refer to Family Dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:33:18-07:00","id":542779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542748#post542748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's try default as &quot;in the absence of extenuating/non-standard factors which may include, but are not limited to, supernatural powers not ubiquitous to the splat or magical wingmen to leech off of.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is, a vampire who is not frenzying, who is not on an extreme fringe of Humanity, who has no access to powers that provide alternate feeding methods, who does not have a benefactor that hand-feeds them, will almost certainly feed in one of the two above methods. Violent, victim-making feeding is the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> The opposite is true for Beasts. Barring non-standard circumstances (like having a power that grants alternate feeding methods, or having a buddy from another splat that lets him play remora), a Beast feeding is a harmful act, unless I missed a standard power Beasts have to let them feed without extra help from powers or other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> If Beasts do have such an easy, benevolent option, then they are more like Vampires than I gave credit. The part I take issue with, however, is the idea that vampire feeding is innately harmful. The comparison between Beasts and Vampires doesn't bother me so long as it's accurate, so I'm not particularly bothered if it turns out I missed something on the Beast side.<br /> <br /> It'd be rather hypocritical for me to continue to perpetuate bad information on Beasts when I'm trying to stop that very thing vis-a-vis vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, on the Beast side of things, there is no culturally mandated expectation of secrecy that necessitates killing, kidnapping, or other morally/ethically suspect behaviors on the part of the Beast. There's no Masquerade to breach, so there's no extra incentive to remove victims or witnesses. And not all feedings by Beasts do lasting harm, beyond causing emotional trauma. Some, particularly the example High Satiety feedings for Tyrants and Nemeses, and most of those for Collectors, are hardly traumatizing at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:36:40-07:00","id":542780,"title":"","content":"Playing a Collector or Tyrant and only feeding when you get low seems to be the most humane options. You can get away with just buying shit or exerting authority over someone, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:43:16-07:00","id":542783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542780#post542780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing a Collector or Tyrant and only feeding when you get low seems to be the most humane options. You can get away with just buying shit or exerting authority over someone, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, a low-Satiety Nemesis can feed by <i>giving an offender a stern warning</i>, and Predators who stay hungry can feed by engaging in <i>regular hunting.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:48:02-07:00","id":542787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542783#post542783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, a low-Satiety Nemesis can feed by <i>giving an offender a stern warning</i>, and Predators who stay hungry can feed by engaging in <i>regular hunting.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am currently imagining a hungry Predator feeding by playing the most HARDCORE game of Laser Tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:58:55-07:00","id":542816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542787#post542787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am currently imagining a hungry Predator feeding by playing the most HARDCORE game of Laser Tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's called warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:09:11-07:00","id":542825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542338#post542338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the section on Conspiracy Theories says the following.<br /> <br /> &quot; Look to the most popular conspiracy theories in the real world; they don\u2019t hold up to even a moderate scientific inquiry&quot;<br /> <br /> Are the Beast devs seriously saying they think JFK's magic bullet is a scientifically sound concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally the opposite of what they said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:12:52-07:00","id":542826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542347#post542347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, yes! Why does no one else see that horses are the natural enemy of all mankind? They were designed for killing, people!<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I totally agree that After Vampires and Werewolves, soul munching monsters from before time began isn't especially evil. The problem is that they're claiming &quot;But I was born this way&quot; is malarkey. Vampires admit their monsters, werewolves just don't care but these guys excuse their actions and THAT is a pretty big turn off. (and this is from a guy who, after finishing the book went back and re-backed the game).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing &quot;but I was born this way&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm seeing &quot;yeah, I'm a monster I've got to do this to live. At least I'm aware of it can can do something about it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:19:57-07:00","id":542848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542780#post542780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing a Collector or Tyrant and only feeding when you get low seems to be the most humane options. You can get away with just buying shit or exerting authority over someone, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think Collectors can't purchase things to sate their Hunger, but they're still one of the most humane options far as feeding goes. Especially if they stay at low satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:24:19-07:00","id":542859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542787#post542787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am currently imagining a hungry Predator feeding by playing the most HARDCORE game of Laser Tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be honest we all know people like that anyway. It'd be a pretty good way to maintain a low cover though- I don't think a hero would think to check the local laser tag place for Smaug the Terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:27:28-07:00","id":542861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542859#post542859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be honest we all know people like that anyway. It'd be a pretty good way to maintain a low cover though- I don't think a hero would think to check the local laser tag place for Smaug the Terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMy armor is like tenfold shields, my teeth are swords, my claws spears, the shock of my tail a thunderbolt, my wings a hurricane, and my breath-, hey, let go of my vest, that's cheating!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:28:29-07:00","id":542862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542779#post542779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh, on the Beast side of things, there is no culturally mandated expectation of secrecy that necessitates killing, kidnapping, or other morally/ethically suspect behaviors on the part of the Beast. There's no Masquerade to breach, so there's no extra incentive to remove victims or witnesses. And not all feedings by Beasts do lasting harm, beyond causing emotional trauma. Some, particularly the example High Satiety feedings for Tyrants and Nemeses, and most of those for Collectors, are hardly traumatizing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't the flip-side of this that Beasts have no culturally mandated reason not to kill or kidnap? Removing witnesses draws attention. Vampires are quite capable of shutting up witnesses without hurting them, even without ethically dubious methods like Dominate. They have plenty of time to build up a mundane powerbase, after all, or to know another vampire who already has.<br /> <br /> You can bring up all kinds of special cases if you like, but without extenuating circumstances, Vampires feeding do not cause harm, and without extenuating circumstances, Beasts feeding do. The circumstances that make Beasts harmless or Vampires harmful may be fairly common, but they're still mirror images of jerkish behavior. Drinking blood isn't innately harmful or monstrous. It's just a fairly easy leap to make. Beast feeding is innately monsterous, but it's possible (I still wouldn't say easy from the evidence provided) for it to be harmless. Are Hungers personal choices like Covenants? I wouldn't think so, but it makes the ones that choose &quot;wrong&quot; even more unethical. If they can't, then it's just another exception to the rule. You can't really make the argument that one or two types of Beast feeding harmlessly makes them all, or even most, harmless, when you're using exceptions. I'll admit I've only skimmed; it's why I'm primarily arguing on the Vampire side, not the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:29:53-07:00","id":542863,"title":"","content":"I am going to just throw in my 2 cents on the Beast/Hero debate:<br /> <br /> What I got from this book is the idea of a mythic arc drawn from the Astral given flesh. The Beast acts as the central point, providing the &quot;antagonist&quot; and the setting (their lair). They create a &quot;whirlpool&quot; around them that pulls those who lack identity (due to low integrity) into the work by giving them the identity of a hero.<br /> <br /> And Beasts are aware, or at least learn, that they are the villains in a story. That is where their claims of victimization comes in: they were cast in the role at birth of being the monster in a story, and they don't find that as fair. Especially if they try to avoid the role that was cast for them, and yet are still forced to play along. They don't view the heroes as victims so much as others caught in the same myth as they are, but the heroes don't fight off the effects. They don't always realize that these humans aren't quite in control, or that they could be rehabilitated, but jit's psychopaths who are playing along with the classic story. Even those who do realize they don't have control seem (based on the way the book is written) to view them as weak minded men and women who were forced into becoming . <br /> <br /> And the thing is, the heroes are assholes, at least from the viewpoint of the Beasts and anyone around them. It doesn't matter why or how they became an asshole, because most people aren't aware of the metaphysics driving them. When they blow up a bus to kill the Beast driver, or kill the mage who they thought was serving the dragon (they just grabbed drinks once), both the mortals and supernaturals are going to view the Heroes as jerks. This doesn't mean everyone views the beasts as being good, just that the Heroes aren't good guys. The beasts can be just as horrible as the heroes claim, it is just that the hunters don't realize how horrible they are as well.<br /> <br /> And it makes sense that the heroes are so one-dimensional and the story they are in is making them into the role of a myth. The fact that they can recover by reasserting their own identity by regaining integrity points to the behavior as due to the overlaying of the &quot;heroic&quot; trappings in a lot of cases, or exaggerating existing &quot;heroic&quot; traits at the cost of being a well developed human.They act like soliphistic jerks because the story being woven by the beast <i>is </i> making them the center of a story. It is just beasts don't like where that story leads, and everyone else just sees them as self-centered zealots.<br /> <br /> A Beasts &quot;win condition&quot; (become Incarnates) is defined as them hijacking the classic &quot;hero fights monsters and win&quot; myth so thoroughly that they reset themselves as the focus of the story (versus the hero). Doing do frees them from creating new Heroes. I think an incarnate is a beast who has taken on the role of both beast and hero, thus ending the cycle. This seems to point to the idea that there is some higher metaphysical element driving the hero/beast dichotomy than just the Beasts nightmares making someone becoming a Beast-hunter. <br /> <br /> Then again, I may be putting too much thought into it. I do think that more emphasis needs to be put on the &quot;this is how it is&quot; v. &quot;this is what beasts think is the case&quot;, but I don't mind the hero/ beast dichotomy when it is cast in a tragic, myth spinning where only one party is aware of what fate is forcing them towards.<br /> <br /> **changing gears**<br /> <br /> As for the crossover, I play mage, so the wide open cosmology is an issue. I feel that (as I said above) the &quot;beasts believe&quot; v. &quot;This is the case&quot; could be better defined. I do feel that the book does create the feel that the Beasts don't really understand the mechanics of their world, or at least not in as a systematic way as the mages do, and a lot of their &quot;explanations&quot; are more akin to &quot;myths and legends&quot;. <br /> <br /> I mean, I could come in as a mage, who after hearing their explanation of kinship, then (ic) ties the Beasts existence to a fallen supernal symbols of primordial fear and epic myths that is trapped in the Astral realm, which shapes souls in a manner akin to awakening and allows for kinship by drawing on the aspects of other splats that relate to those fallen supernal symbols in a manner akin to how mages use the supernal. And the beast (ic) would nod his head politely and later talk about how mages have to make everything more complicated than they have to be, since it <i>obviously </i> is just that we all descend or draw upon the dark mothers powers. <br /> <br /> And as for why the other splats put up with them? I don't think they all do on the social level. Or at least they don't view them as family. Mages would likely see a new Mystery to solve, or at best a powerful ally that may not earn him points with the Orders. Vampires likely see a new pawn in the politics, or a hunting buddy. Werewolves see this being that seems like one of the claimed, but isnt, and I could see them kill a beast as readily as have one join the hunt. Sine ates probably would be okay with them (they seem to be okay with most splats, if most aren't okay with them... see claimed and werewolves). And the other splats (except demon) are so rare that each wouod interact on an almost individual basis.<br /> <br /> I think the emphas is should be on that the Beasts view everyone as their best buds (except those soulless robot demons/angela, thank you very much), but this doesn't mean that view is reciprocated by the other communities as a whole. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, I love how Demon's don't get along with the Beasts and vice versa... on a meta level, it is fun to think of them as 2 of Matt kids not getting along)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:31:19-07:00","id":542865,"title":"","content":"I have laundry/work to do, but I want to point out the delicious irony of how years after years of hearing arguments about how vampires are perhaps the most harmful supernatural type for humanity, we're now getting the exact opposite argument.<br /> <br /> No bearing on how this plays out with Beast, just highly amusing for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:35:42-07:00","id":542869,"title":"","content":"EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542717#post542717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a single example of the many strokes of nuance you might find in the text. Far from the only one or even the most engaging.<br /> <br /> We may have different ideas of what constitutes nuanced writing with thoughtful and emotional engagement, but I still find the best of it in the relationship between Beasts and Heroes. I won't go into detail because, well, at this point it's really been discussed and elaborated enough and I doubt repeating will suffice to change a deeply different opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can still help to communicate an idea, though. I clearly could have used more examples of what you meant, because the one Nyrufa mentioned really didn't really address my concerns at all. It's certainly an element of nuance, and one of many situations in which multiple options are presented. However, it does not provide much that much insight into the different approaches and beliefs of Beasts.<br /> <br /> I don't know if Beast actually needed a section on social organizations, but that's usually the part of the book which provides a lot of insight into life as a supernatural entity. That's where Refinements come up in Promethean, and with them a real glimpse at how the Created approach their inquiry into Humanity. It's where Courts are explained in Changeling, and alongside it a sense of the way Changelings react to and try to move on from their trauma.<br /> <br /> Beast talks a lot about the monomyth, but only as a plot structure. It's also about the ways in which people develop as people (which, ironically enough, Heroes don't). Beast talks a lot about humans inheriting the stories of Hercules, but not about the 2014 movie imagining Hercules as wandering hero who may or may not be super strong and have killed supernatural beasts, but is certainly horrified that he killed his children. Beauty and the Beast fits in the game's narrative, but not Monsters Inc. That's what I mean when I say it doesn't feel like a thoughtful and emotional engagement with its concepts. This is also, I think, part of the reason why its treatment of Heroes is rubbing at least a very vocal minority the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:35:57-07:00","id":542870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542848#post542848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I think Collectors can't purchase things to sate their Hunger, but they're still one of the most humane options far as feeding goes. Especially if they stay at low satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: The Primordial page 134</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety: The Collector can seek out anything that generally fits within the scope of his<br /> desire. A Collector who hoards gold can walk into any jewelry shop with a bit of cash</div> </div> </div> </div>Right there in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:54:05-07:00","id":542878,"title":"","content":"Huh. I forgot about that. I was only remembering this bit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: The Primordial page 45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the Hoard\u2019s nature, Collectors satisfy their Hunger by acquiring new objects for it. Even for a very rich Collector, this is never as simple as going out to a store and buying a new diamond necklace. That\u2019s not acquiring something new, it\u2019s merely trading one thing of value for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which implied regular, legal acquisition isn't enough to satisfy a Collector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:57:06-07:00","id":542892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542491#post542491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...a person that may have been raped, a teenager that has been abused, a transgender that has been bullied since ever...may be one nightmare away from being put into the role of &quot;hero,&quot; i.e. the antagonist... and none of which has a choice in the matter. The way things are written now it posits the opposite, but the reverse can happen just as easily. So this goes from &quot;Beast the Primordial, to &quot;Blame Game the Victimization.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. No.<br /> <br /> One, as with reaching Integ 4 from exposure to the supernatural, that's all both unlikely and not appropriate for the tone the books have.<br /> <br /> A Hero has to be at Integrity 4 before they actually become a hero from the Nightmare.<br /> <br /> The Way Heroes are described, that's a &quot;barely functional in society, one bad say away from shooting up a mall/school/church/post office&quot; levels of integrity.<br /> <br /> If the average integrity is 7, one rape isn't enough to bring someone low enough-it's just one breaking point. Maybe two if the victim has to testify and you get a scenario like in Law in Order where the rapists is a sociopathic asshole and represents himself. a worst case scenario would bring her close, but chances are, if she hits Integrity 4 or below from one rape, she was already running low.<br /> <br /> The Abused Teenager... There are plenty of ways to react to abuse. Only a few of them result in actions one could expect from an integrity 4. And besides, a sympathetic backstory does not excuse being a murderous asshole, unless you want to say that Freddy Kruger(Implied to molest and murder children because he was bullied for being the &quot;bastard son of 100 maniacs&quot;) has an excuse for being a child molesting serial killer.<br /> <br /> The Transgendered victim of bullying. Plenty of bullying victims don't' become borderline murderous assholes. If you are at a point where having a bad dream gives you a new purpose as a self centered murderous asshole, it took a bit more than mundane bullying to get to that level. And as before, a sympathetic backstory does not excuse murder or collateral damage.<br /> <br /> So, in all of those cases, it's incredibly unlikely that any of those, by themselves, would result in a hero. Even in freak cases, that's not an excuse for going out to kill the &quot;monster&quot; from your dream and possible causing large amounts of collateral damage and civilian casualties.<br /> <br /> At best, I could see an extreme example of the &quot;bullying victim&quot; scenario producing one of the &quot;byronic hero&quot; type of Heroes. The ones that might kill their Beast and then either die or give up heroing, and eventually work up enough integrity to lose the hero template. But if their Beat is't one of the rare cases where it's not a Hungry Beast's nightmares making a hero and this guy is an asshole who deserves to die, or if they keep hunting and cause collateral damage or civilian casualties, then they still have to pay for that, because a sympathetic backstory is not an excuse.<br /> <br /> As I said before: A Serial Killer who only targets criminals is still a serial killer. Especially if he kills more than just murderers and rapists, becuase the last time I checked vandalims and petty theft don't get you the death penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:57:25-07:00","id":542893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542650#post542650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This goes to Ye of Little Faith's comment as well, but I don't really see how those nuances really form a thoughtful engagement with the subject matter. It's the equivalent of vampires being able to drink from squirrels and blood bags, and writing a sentence about how sometimes they feel bad about it anyhow. I mean, especially the bit about Predators not having to kill their prey. That's not engagement, that's just &quot;can we make it so this Hunger isn't solely comprised of serial killers?&quot;<br /> <br /> If it would be helpful, I can put together something elaborating on what I mean by &quot;thoughtful and emotional engagement&quot;. I haven't here because it might be unnecessary and long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Please do, because I'm having a little bit of trouble understanding where you're coming from. To me, it seems like a Hero is that one guy who had a couple bad encounters with a different ethnicity, and decides to join the Klan. And remember the Ravager sample was just a guy who smashed out windows and spray painted the walls. A rational member of society would simply bring them up on vandalism charges. A Hero would burn their house down with molotov cocktails screaming &quot;Burn, you fucking freak!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Heroes aren't just humans that had a bad day, they are the worst example of human arrogance. They take what they want, when they want and screw the consequences until it's biting them in the ass. Humanity can capture and tame animals for entertainment and research, but the second that animal retaliates, well it's time to put it down because its a danger to the community. They burn down forests and wildlife because they're so overpopulated they need more room, and think nothing of the endangered species or medicinal ingredients they just destroyed.<br /> <br /> This is how I view Heroes, they are humanity's arrogance personified, and it works from a monster's perspective. And that is what WoD has always been about, playing as the monster. Well except for Hunter and possibly Mage side of things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:57:30-07:00","id":542894,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is an official thing; but I'm thinking of playing it this way regardless:<br /> <br /> \u2022 the Hunter phenomenon is when a mortal gets exposed to the supernatural and <i>doesn't</i> shy away from it the way the Curse would normally compel her to do<sup>*</sup>, but instead fights back against it. While these guys are not Sleepwalkers, they have a little something extra that lets them be proactive in the face of the Curse. <br /> \u2022 a Hero is not <i>merely</i> the result of an Integrity 4 human being exposed to the Primordial Dream; it's the result of an Integrity 4 human <i>who would have become a hunter if the supernatural encounter had been anything else</i> encountering a Beast. That is, the Hero is someone who was already predisposed to strike back; but the combination of his mental instability (represented by his low Integrity) <i>and</i> whatever it is that causes Beasts to inspire Heroes \u2014 three separate factors that must <i>all</i> be met \u2014 is what turns him into a Hero. This puts more of the responsibility for being a Hero on the <i>Hero's</i> shoulder, because he <i>is</i> the one who decided to be proactive when confronted by the Beast. <br /> \u2022 I'm now toying with an idea for a Hunter \u201cConspiracy\u201d<sup>\u2020</sup> with an Endowment that mimics what Heroes can do, but without necessarily being limited to Beasts: for instance, these guys can place Anathema on <i>anyone</i> that Beasts would consider Kin. Being hunters, not Heroes, they're also not delusional about who and what they are \u2014 though on the downside, if they ever drop to Integrity 4 they automatically <i>become</i> Heroes, whether or not they've ever encountered a Beast. Actually, instead of creating a <i>new</i> Conspiracy, I might just upgrade Ashwood Abbey to Conspiracy status. Still debating it. <br /> <br /> The idea behind this third point is to provide an alternative to Heroes who are a response to the Beasts and who are still sane (and all the more dangerous for it), but who <i>don't</i> get to blame the Beast for what he has become. They still tend to be first-order jerks; but that's more of a cultural thing than a supernaturally imposed thing. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> * It has been confirmed by Dave that the Curse is a thing throughout the nWoD, not just in relation to Mage, and is largely responsible for why the supernatural remains in the shadows: most people who encounter it pointedly ignore it. <br /> \u2020 In quotes because I don't see them as being any more organized than Les Mysteres, or whatever the name of the Conspiracy from <b>Spirit Slayers</b> is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:58:18-07:00","id":542896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542869#post542869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast talks a lot about humans inheriting the stories of Hercules, but not about the 2014 movie imagining Hercules-</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that movie was <i>terrible</i>.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm not contributing to the conversation. I'll go now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:01:10-07:00","id":542897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542894#post542894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 I'm now toying with an idea for a Hunter \u201cConspiracy\u201d<sup>\u2020</sup> with an Endowment that mimics what Heroes can do, but without necessarily being limited to Beasts: for instance, these guys can place Anathema on <i>anyone</i> that Beasts would consider Kin. Being hunters, not Heroes, they're also not delusional about who and what they are \u2014 though on the downside, if they ever drop to Integrity 4 they automatically <i>become</i> Heroes, whether or not they've ever encountered a Beast. Actually, instead of creating a <i>new</i> Conspiracy, I might just upgrade Ashwood Abbey to Conspiracy status. Still debating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, you mean sort of like the Cainite Heresy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:03:38-07:00","id":542898,"title":"","content":"I hope there's a player's guide in the works. Lair Traits, Lives, Legends, Atavisms, Nightmares... I really wish there was more of everything to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:05:14-07:00","id":542899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542898#post542898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's a player's guide in the works. Lair Traits, Lives, Legends, Atavisms, Nightmares... I really wish there was more of everything to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view?pli=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Scroll waaaay down there, bud. Has at least a basic explanation of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:07:04-07:00","id":542900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542898#post542898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's a player's guide in the works. Lair Traits, Lives, Legends, Atavisms, Nightmares... I really wish there was more of everything to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, the only thing I've heard Matt talk about on the supplement front is a player's guide-though I might be imagining things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:08:38-07:00","id":542901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542878#post542878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which implied regular, legal acquisition isn't enough to satisfy a Collector.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It makes no implication about how they need to acquire it at all. The method they get it isn't what matters. The text makes it very clear the only thing that matters is that the object matters to someone other than the Beast. The Beast could very well be a rich person who goes to auctions and buys out objects from under other after learning they have been seeking it for years. Which is entirely legal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:08:56-07:00","id":542902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542577#post542577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'd normally agree, the fact that they're caused by what is functionally cthulhu makes it hard for me to read them as anything but victim-turned-torturer, more likely suffering from serious issues. It's layers of messed up and not in that 'enjoyable thought experiment' a lot of the other WoD game lines can be.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I chose 'squick' as my adjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast didn't cause it. It's very clear that it's caused by the hero to be being so damaged, for whatever reason, that having a bad dream and feeling that the monster from the dream is real is enough to give them a purpose in life.<br /> <br /> That, and the fact that it doen'st happen every time, but only when you fuck up on a dream feeding or do too well(a different kind of fucking up) makes it an accident.<br /> <br /> and really, the reading I got was &quot;the most likely people to become heroes are extreme narcissists, bullies*, abusers*, and th kind of asshole who never went to college and slacks off, and then blames the fact that he doen'st have a good job on illegal immigrants instead of his own laziness and lack of education.&quot;<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">Explicitly named as potential heroes in the text.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">That last one in particular, because overwhelmingly the vibe I'm getting is &quot;Yes! Monsters! That's why my life is terrible. The very existance of these monsters is why I'm poor, not a sheer accident of birth! They're why I can't get a good job, not my lack of education and poor work ethic! They're the reason I can't get a promotion, not because my boss hates me for fucking his daughter! Geese, why would he hate me. I'm a catch. Monsters make so much more sense.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:18:36-07:00","id":542911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542901#post542901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It makes no implication about how they need to acquire it at all. The method they get it isn't what matters. The text makes it very clear the only thing that matters is that the object matters to someone other than the Beast. The Beast could very well be a rich person who goes to auctions and buys out objects from under other after learning they have been seeking it for years. Which is entirely legal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know the strict requirement is that whatever the Beast collects needs to matter to someone else. But I mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast The Primordial Page 45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the Hoard\u2019s nature, <b>Collectors satisfy their Hunger by acquiring new objects for it</b>. Even for a very rich Collector, <b>this is never as simple as going out to a store and buying a new diamond necklace</b>. That\u2019s <b>not acquiring something new</b>, it\u2019s <b>merely trading one thing of value for another.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If that doesn't imply purchase isn't quite enough to sate a Collector's Hunger, I don't know what does. Mind you, it makes more sense that the meal just isn't as worthwhile if you acquire it through trading someone normally, and that's still line with what the first chapter says in the above quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:19:12-07:00","id":542912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542902#post542902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That last one in particular, because overwhelmingly the vibe I'm getting is &quot;Yes! Monsters! That's why my life is terrible. The very existance of these monsters is why I'm poor, not a sheer accident of birth! They're why I can't get a good job, not my lack of education and poor work ethic! They're the reason I can't get a promotion, not because my boss hates me for fucking his daughter! Geese, why would he hate me. I'm a catch. Monsters make so much more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Boom, battleship sunk!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:22:01-07:00","id":542914,"title":"","content":"A Beast &quot;triggering&quot; the birth of a Hero does not mean the Hero was a victim of the Beast. Some (maybe most) will be, but that is not the same as all. The protoHero may or may not have ever been a victim in their life. The presumption that they have Integrity 4 due to being victimized is not only boring, it's a premise unsupported by reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:25:43-07:00","id":542928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542636#post542636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only after s/he was traumatized by having a nightmare...and having no choice but to become this &quot;hero.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only happens if she's already fucked up in the head. It's hardly the Beast's fault if the person their soul ravaged without any conscious choice on the Beast's part just so happened to be so screwed up that having a particularly vivid nightmare was enough to make the go all &quot;narcissistic serial killer&quot;on them,.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:27:39-07:00","id":542932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542902#post542902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Beast didn't cause it. It's very clear that it's caused by the hero to be being so damaged, for whatever reason, that having a bad dream and feeling that the monster from the dream is real is enough to give them a purpose in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you explain &quot;The Quest In Progress&quot;, and the succeeding five sections talking about how the Beast's &quot;Hunger infuses the Hero, making him the type of adversary best suited to defeat her, even if it takes years do to so?&quot; (pg. 278)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:37:52-07:00","id":542950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542694#post542694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, that's not to say that vampire bites are never bad. Done aggressively, or without restraint, or in a frenzy, there are victims being made. It can and does happen. In fact, it almost certainly will happen at least once for every vampire. And, I suppose similarly to Beasts, taking this path is going to lead to people out to kill you. Hunters. Friends of the victim. Police. Whatever.<br /> <br /> The difference is the default for Beast is explicitly harmful, and they take specific powers and effort to not harm.<br /> <br /> The default for vampires is explicitly mutually (if not equally) beneficial or neutral, and it takes specific effort or lack of good judgment to harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Vampire feeding does at least one point of Lethal Damage, yes?<br /> <br /> Meaning it is explicitly harmful in every case.<br /> <br /> The same is not true for a Beast, who depending on hunger at least has the option to avoid causing harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:39:31-07:00","id":542951,"title":"","content":"Heroes are very clearly victims of a Beast. That is a fact. But that alone doesn't make them justified in their pursuits, especially if they take easily to more extreme methods. It doesn't make the Beast automatically worthy of elimination or their retribution, but it certainly doesn't excuse wrongdoings outside of the natural consequences of their existence either. Even their presence makes a case for antagonizing them depending on the exact effects, but the reason one may have to to hunt Beasts is important to the dillemma. Especially from the perspective of the Begotten.<br /> <br /> But I'm just reiterating things pointed out earlier in the thread so I'll bow out of the discussion now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:41:13-07:00","id":542955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542645#post542645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in fact, that's something. Beasts exist to <i>allow people to confront their fears</i>. An experience with a Beast can be freeing, because the change in perspective can lead to appreciation of what one has, growth as an individual, recognition of hamartia, and so on. A beast can shake up their lives for a bit, but humanity can come out stronger for...without a need for violence. Beast, as a game, is about the, say it with me, the cycle of violence, and it condemns it quite readily.<br /> <br /> Again, No one's really at fault, but the people involved aren't squeaky clean either.</div> </div> </div> </div>My God.... Lil Slugger from Paranoia Agent is a Beast if you go with this....<br /> <br /> Hell... Maybe that's the Response....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:54:48-07:00","id":542966,"title":"","content":"Here's a thought:<br /> <br /> Some beasts regularly victimize people to sate their hungers.<br /> <br /> Some beasts create Heroes.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, <i>these are not the same beasts. </i>Heroes inevitably arise around, and are drawn to target, those who have <i>not</i> done as much to earn their ire. The true monsters are always full and therefore get off scot free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:56:44-07:00","id":542967,"title":"","content":"While Low Satiety Beasts are more likely to be found by Heroes, High Satiety Beasts aren't invisible to their radar. Specifically, there's a bonus to finding one and a penalty to finding the other.<br /> <br /> The game isn't for everyone. None are. If some people have a problem with it, you don't need to try convince them they're wrong, just as they don't need to try and convince you.. If someone doesn't want to play the game, they just won't play the game, haranguing them about it won't make a difference, not everyone is going to go for the buy in, just like not everyone goes for the buy in in Vampire, World of Darkness, or RPGs in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2015, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:00:02-07:00","id":542969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542955#post542955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My God.... Lil Slugger from Paranoia Agent is a Beast if you go with this....<br /> <br /> Hell... Maybe that's the Response....</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect example, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:00:05-07:00","id":542970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542932#post542932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you explain &quot;The Quest In Progress&quot;, and the succeeding five sections talking about how the Beast's &quot;Hunger infuses the Hero, making him the type of adversary best suited to defeat her, even if it takes years do to so?&quot; (pg. 278)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy.<br /> <br /> The Nightmare caused by a Soul going rampaging is likely to be a Nightmare about the Beast's hunger.<br /> <br /> The hero responds appropriately to the Hunger demonstrated in the Nightmare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Heroes are very clearly victims of a Beast. That is a fact.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> It really isn't.<br /> <br /> It's clear that Heroes are victims of the Beast being hungry enough to trigger the unintentional and involuntary side effect of their existance and having shitty enough luck that their soul decides to give a nightmare to a deeply unstable person and screw up the nightmare giving.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:01:24-07:00","id":542971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542966#post542966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a thought:<br /> <br /> Some beasts regularly victimize people to sate their hungers.<br /> <br /> Some beasts create Heroes.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, <i>these are not the same beasts. </i>Heroes inevitably arise around, and are drawn to target, those who have <i>not</i> done as much to earn their ire. The true monsters are always full and therefore get off scot free.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I've been saying for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:05:38-07:00","id":542974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542862#post542862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't the flip-side of this that Beasts have no culturally mandated reason not to kill or kidnap? Removing witnesses draws attention. Vampires are quite capable of shutting up witnesses without hurting them, even without ethically dubious methods like Dominate. They have plenty of time to build up a mundane powerbase, after all, or to know another vampire who already has.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would require a homogeneous, self-policing culture that all Begotten are part of, which on a macro-level just does not exist. Also, I was under the impression that this argument was discounting social ties, but hey, it's your party. Also, even if psychology no longer holds any power over the Begotten, the elements of their old life are still going to inform a lot of their decision making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can bring up all kinds of special cases if you like, but without extenuating circumstances, Vampires feeding do not cause harm, and without extenuating circumstances, Beasts feeding do. The circumstances that make Beasts harmless or Vampires harmful may be fairly common, but they're still mirror images of jerkish behavior. <b>Drinking blood isn't innately harmful or monstrous.</b> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, Morbus, and other Vampires passing on blood-borne diseases, by accident or design is still a thing, so yes, drinking blood does carry more than a risk of harm. Also, could you point me to a real world culture that doesn't view the non-ritualistic consumption of blood, especially <b>human </b>blood, as monstrous on general principle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just a fairly easy leap to make. Beast feeding is <b>innately</b> monsterous, but it's possible (I still wouldn't say easy from the evidence provided) for it to be harmless. Are Hungers personal choices like Covenants? I wouldn't think so, but it makes the ones that choose &quot;wrong&quot; even more unethical. If they can't, then it's just another exception to the rule. You can't really make the argument that one or two types of Beast feeding harmlessly makes them all, or even most, harmless, when you're using exceptions. I'll admit I've only skimmed; it's why I'm primarily arguing on the Vampire side, not the Beast. </div> </div> </div>Under what metric? Raw destruction? Callousness? What is <i>innately monstrous</i> about pursuing a target, challenging a rival or superior, obsessively acquiring treasure by any means necessary, or watching something, or better yet someone, come to ruin? There is a very Propertarian angle to this discussion, which would be laughable if it weren't also devolving into tee-totaling.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:13:34-07:00","id":542979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542950#post542950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire feeding does at least one point of Lethal Damage, yes?<br /> <br /> Meaning it is explicitly harmful in every case.<br /> <br /> The same is not true for a Beast, who depending on hunger at least has the option to avoid causing harm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I try to be open-minded and considerate towards alternate arguments when I discuss things on a forum.<br /> <br /> One thing that drives me up a wall, though, is when people do not read my whole post and then try to argue against me with arguments I already addressed. This happens far too often. It expresses that one is arguing in bad-faith and not really trying to hold a discussion at all. It wastes everyone's time.<br /> <br /> Given that Onyx Path's forums tend to operate in far better faith than other places I discuss things, I will give you the benefit of the doubt and re-post my answer to your argument. Normally I would assume you are a troll and ignore you. This time I will just assume you were in a rush for whatever reason. It was rather long and posted several pages ago, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542694#post542694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm sure someone will bring up lethal damage from feeding. 1: If it was consented to, it's still no worse than anything else people can consent to that causes physical damage, like alcohol or even extreme sports. 2: Given that the Kiss leaves no physical marks, one has to assume the damage is just a crude mechanical representation of blood loss and the time it takes the body to replace it, not actual physical injury.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":".  formatting 06-06-2015, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:20:58-07:00","id":542982,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry. I missed that, but still, consented to harm is still harm, particularly since &quot;consent&quot; in the case of a vampire could include, in addition to genuine consent, &quot;thinking you're going to have sex when she just wants your blood&quot;, &quot;being addicted to her blood&quot;, &quot;having been fed her blood so often that you're are obsessively infatuated with her&quot; &quot;having been brainwashed to want it&quot; &quot;she's too hot to ignore because of her vampire powers&quot; or &quot;memory was altered to make you thing I consented&quot;<br /> <br /> And still, given the choice between &quot;always caused physical harm(blood loss) that takes days to heel&quot; versus &quot;might cause physical harm but done'st have to&quot; I'd think the one that doen'st have to cause physical harm is the least harmful.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between assault and vandalism/burglary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:40:43-07:00","id":542987,"title":"","content":"Actually, validly consented to injury or pain isn't harm. Harm is a setback to one's interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:48:58-07:00","id":543026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542987#post542987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, validly consented to injury or pain isn't harm. Harm is a setback to one's interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the point is that consent is dubious at best when a vampire is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:00:19-07:00","id":543058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542974#post542974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would require a homogeneous, self-policing culture that all Begotten are part of, which on a macro-level just does not exist. Also, I was under the impression that this argument was discounting social ties, but hey, it's your party. Also, even if psychology no longer holds any power over the Begotten, the elements of their old life are still going to inform a lot of their decision making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discounting social ties, vampires have no Masquerade beyond self-preservation. Because of the desire for self-preservation, they will still not go on a mass-murdering spree and should prefer the non-violent feeding methods. A vampire with a modicum of self-preservation instinct won't be causing dangerous witnesses in the first place. If they are, they will likely die quickly, either to Hunters, mortals, or Kindred. Non-violent feedings are simply logical. Doing things that cause dangerous witnesses that need to be killed are not an every day part of Kindred existence. Frenzy is the wildcard here, but if we accept it to be part of &quot;standard behavior&quot; that's still a tiny fraction of feedings compared to Beast's standard of every feeding being harmful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542974#post542974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, Morbus, and other Vampires passing on blood-borne diseases, by accident or design is still a thing, so yes, drinking blood does carry more than a risk of harm. Also, could you point me to a real world culture that doesn't view the non-ritualistic consumption of blood, especially <b>human </b>blood, as monstrous on general principle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly cannot speak for Morbus. 2e is my entry point into VtR (though I had a bit of experience with Masquerade before that). I would expect vampires to put down a whole bloodline of Plaguebearers just like they would an individual one. If they didn't in old fluff, I couldn't say why. Morbus feeding could be considered worse than Beasts. Non-morbus plaguebearers, though, fall under the criminal negligence we've already discussed. At first taste of blood, vampires can know whether said blood carries any disease. Then deciding to knowingly spread it goes along the same lines as purposefully draining people to death or frenzying in a crowded mall. Non-standard behavior where I'll agree it can be considered as bad or worse than Beasts. But it's still non-Standard behavior. Vampire's don't run around eating Aids victims trying to spread it to all the foolish mortals.<br /> <br /> As for blood, a few religions partake in the ritual drinking of blood, including a subculture called Sanguinarians. Hard to find much beyond that, because searches tended to go to vampire myths. That said, cultures that practice cannibalism are easier to find. Still typically limited to ritual cases (not all the time as Hollywood depicts), eating the flesh of deceased human beings is hard to see as less taboo than drinking the willing blood of living ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542974#post542974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under what metric? Raw destruction? Callousness? What is <i>innately monstrous</i> about pursuing a target, challenging a rival or superior, obsessively acquiring treasure by any means necessary, or watching something, or better yet someone, come to ruin? There is a very Propertarian angle to this discussion, which would be laughable if it weren't also devolving into tee-totaling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it hurt a person against their will, psychologically or physically? Then it is bad. Vampires can go their entire unlives without harming someone against their will. Without even using mind-altering Disciplines. Frenzy, admittedly, skews that to &quot;every vampire will harm someone against their will at some point,&quot; but once in a hundred is still not as bad as every single time, and barring Frenzy vampires do not usually harm anyone against their will, and that's the debate. Vampires tend to only harm people with outside circumstances (frenzy, disciplines, abnormal morality). Beats tend to only <i>not </i>harm people with outside circumstances (powers not every Beast will have, a couple of non-universal Hungers, a lackey they can hang around while they feed).<br /> <br /> I suppose one could argue that instead violent feedings are the default, but every violent feeding is a potential Masquerade Breach that will call or create Hunters (a similarity to Beast, I suppose?), and so I do not think Vampires would exist to the modern nights if that was the standard MO.<br /> <br /> You could also argue that Dominate/Majesty/vinculum is the default to acquire feedings. I disagree that it's that common, but I will admit that I find mind control worse than anything any splat can do short of soul destruction. If it weren't temporary, I'd consider it equivalent. A vampire that feeds this way can join the Morbus as &quot;terrible and evil,&quot; fine by me. It's not like I think vampires are all angels. I just don't think feeding is morally wrong by any stretch of the imagination without additional factors.<br /> <br /> @Rater202: I don't really feel that your analogy is quite right. It's more like an issue of rape vs. rough BDSM sex with safewords. They both look terrible to onlookers, but one is morally repugnant and illegal and harms people without question. The other is performed with consent and is not immoral in the slightest. Indeed, it can be done between two people who love each other dearly. A vampire feeding may look terrible to onlookers, but if the blood doll enjoys it and is consenting, it's not really anyone's place to judge.<br /> <br /> Geeze. Used to post no more than a sentence, typically. Now I'm spamming up the forums. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:00:39-07:00","id":543059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543026#post543026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the point is that consent is dubious at best when a vampire is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:11:45-07:00","id":543093,"title":"","content":"1.) Last I checked getting drunk doesn't inflict L<b>ethal</b> damage in the system, unless you meant to refer to the effects of heavy alcohol abuse, which are <b>very</b> <b>severe and long lasting</b>. Additionally, agreeing to do something that might get you hurt (sports in general) doesn't mean that you aren't actually hurt when you shatter a bone.<br /> <br /> 2.) The Kiss leaving behind no visible marks is entirely irrelevant. Nor does the Vampire being able to heal the puncture wounds to the neck mean they never <b>bit open someones neck.</b>*<br /> <br /> Vampires feeding, <i>at minimum</i>, will <b>always</b> cause physical harm, no matter how &quot;minor&quot;. A Beast feeding, <i>at minimum</i>, causes no harm at all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*I use neck as a stereotypical example. The same applies to any site of feeding.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:48:37-07:00","id":543149,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to this. I hope they get this on Amazon Prime since I'm a Prime customer, I won't pay for a PDF, and I want it shipped fast. =P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:48:44-07:00","id":543150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543058#post543058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @Rater202: I don't really feel that your analogy is quite right. It's more like an issue of rape vs. rough BDSM sex with safewords. They both look terrible to onlookers, but one is morally repugnant and illegal and harms people without question. The other is performed with consent and is not immoral in the slightest. Indeed, it can be done between two people who love each other dearly. A vampire feeding may look terrible to onlookers, but if the blood doll enjoys it and is consenting, it's not really anyone's place to judge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the difference.<br /> <br /> The Whole Point of BDSM is to experience forced sex/rough sex/sex while restrained in an environment where you don't actually get hurt. That is nothing at all like vampire feeding.<br /> <br /> Even if you consent to vampiric feeding, you are still suffering an injury. This is not the case in Even Rough BDSM, unless you screw up.<br /> <br /> Another issue is the matter of consent: Consent means jack shit if it's not given after receiving full disclosure and if it's not given with full disclosure.<br /> <br /> I seriously doubt that a vampiric seductress is going to flat out say to her mark &quot;hey, I'm an honest to god vampire and I'm going to feed off you while we have sex Also we won't really be having sex. Still wanna go?&quot;<br /> <br /> Not informed consent, and thus not real consent. He agreed to getting laid, not having his blood taken.<br /> <br /> A blood doll is probably more like the hooker who can't quit because her number one John controls when she gets her next hit of her narcotic of choice than someone in a conceptual but kinky relationship, and may have an extreme unnatural infatuation with her vampiric John/Dealer, which could be compared to stockholm syndrome in a certain light. In either case, consent is dubious at best.<br /> <br /> Even if neither scenario is the case, and the mark is both fully aware of the vampire's vampirism and not addicted to their blood or under vinculum, vampires have two entire disciplines that can easily be used to mind fuck a &quot;yes&quot; out of somebody regardless of what they were going to say. Dominate can even make them think they consented when they didn't.<br /> <br /> So, in your metaphor, the Vampire is always closest to the rapist than he is to the dom in the BDSM relationship.<br /> <br /> Meaning on average, the Vampiric Feeding which always requires inflicting injury does more harm than the Beast feeding that does not always require inflicting injury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:15:07-07:00","id":543185,"title":"","content":"A vampire may have several dozen methods to force &quot;consent&quot;, but they're under no obligation to <i>use</i> them. Some people genuinely get off on blood play and shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:18:49-07:00","id":543189,"title":"","content":"Plus they can offer limited immortality in exchange for a steady supply. Or feed off of ghosts or spirits.<br /> <br /> That said, Maina's expressed their opinion, there's no need to hassle them over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2015, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:21:24-07:00","id":543190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543058#post543058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I honestly cannot speak for Morbus. 2e is my entry point into VtR (though I had a bit of experience with Masquerade before that). I would expect vampires to put down a whole bloodline of Plaguebearers just like they would an individual one. If they didn't in old fluff, I couldn't say why. Morbus feeding could be considered worse than Beasts. Non-morbus plaguebearers, though, fall under the criminal negligence we've already discussed. At first taste of blood, vampires can know whether said blood carries any disease. Then deciding to knowingly spread it goes along the same lines as purposefully draining people to death or frenzying in a crowded mall. Non-standard behavior where I'll agree it can be considered as bad or worse than Beasts. But it's still non-Standard behavior. Vampire's don't run around eating Aids victims trying to spread it to all the foolish mortals.<br /> <br /> As for blood, a few religions partake in the ritual drinking of blood, including a subculture called Sanguinarians. Hard to find much beyond that, because searches tended to go to vampire myths. That said, cultures that practice cannibalism are easier to find. Still typically limited to ritual cases (not all the time as Hollywood depicts), eating the flesh of deceased human beings is hard to see as less taboo than drinking the willing blood of living ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Geeze. Used to post no more than a sentence, typically. Now I'm spamming up the forums. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the book explains the reason the Morbus haven't been wiped out... they control disease. All it takes is one Morbus to create a city wide plague and contaminate the food supply of any Princedom stupid enough to move against them. They can even inflict these diseases on vampires directly, turning them into more Plaguebearers, so pissing them off is probably not a smart decision.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you have other bloodlines such as the Niktuku who actually hunt and eat fellow vampires, and yet they're still roaming the world instead of being put to the torch. There's lots of bloodlines you think might get the axe in society, but they're either too scattered, powerful, or otherwise impossible to stamp out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:20:58-07:00","id":543244,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543093#post543093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Last I checked getting drunk doesn't inflict L<b>ethal</b> damage in the system, unless you meant to refer to the effects of heavy alcohol abuse, which are <b>very</b> <b>severe and long lasting</b>. Additionally, agreeing to do something that might get you hurt (sports in general) doesn't mean that you aren't actually hurt when you shatter a bone.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543093#post543093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2.) The Kiss leaving behind no visible marks is entirely irrelevant. Nor does the Vampire being able to heal the puncture wounds to the neck mean they never <b>bit open someones neck.</b>*</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampires feeding, <i>at minimum</i>, will <b>always</b> cause physical harm, no matter how &quot;minor&quot;. A Beast feeding, <i>at minimum</i>, causes no harm at all.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">*I use neck as a stereotypical example. The same applies to any site of feeding.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I Find a fundamental problem with the beast feeding at &quot;minimum&quot; causing no harm.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A vampire doesn\u2019t have to bite harm his food supply either. Many neonates turn to the blood banks and such. And if we really wanna stretch it a vampire can feed from someone who is already hurt. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I find a beast hunger could maybe only be understood by vampire outside of beasts themselves and vice versa. A vampire and beast and find a common ground in their hungers. Same as a beast can find \u201cfamily ties\u201d in a pack of werewolves. It finds understanding and \u201cfeeding\u201d with a vampire or coterie. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feeding in my opinion and what i understand in WoD setting is not a nice thing. It\u2019s suppose to be harmful it\u2019s suppose to have consequences. Yes rocking the systems of low satiety (i.e a hoarder buying something to feed himself, a hunter killing a deer) isn\u2019t very harmful but how long can you starve yourself going of scraps. Beast\u2019s aren\u2019t good guys they don\u2019t go around planting flowers and making family dinners. They feast on fear they inflict mental and emotional scars on their victims. In the end i feel like the argument (you and many others) are making are very isolating and specific in general a Beast will hurt his food just as quickly as a Kindred is. There is no nice guys in WoD. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:50:39-07:00","id":543271,"title":"","content":"Bit offtopic: This game could use it's own forum already. 170+ pages of discussion is kinda crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:53:09-07:00","id":543273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543271#post543271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit offtopic: This game could use it's own forum already. 170+ pages of discussion is kinda crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been brought up quite a few times.<br /> <br /> And while we're adding new fora, I'd also <i>ideally</i> want to see a subforum for homebrew stuff. Ideally. I know it probably won't happen, but it'd be nice to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:57:06-07:00","id":543278,"title":"","content":"What fundamental problem with a Beast feeding causing no harm? You not liking something is not a fundamental problem.<br /> <br /> As for neonates getting blood from blood banks, where do you think that blood is coming from? Magically conjured? No, it is harvested and &quot;donated&quot;. Not to mention how long will a Vampire be able to go consuming only the minimum blood needed to survive? What happens after the get into a turf war? After fighting some Hunters? Are they just going to starve or stay injured until they slowly heal a little bit at a time? Asking that question of Beasts without also asking it of Vampires is disingenuous.<br /> <br /> You also presume that by stating a Beast is <i>capable</i> of feeding with out causing physical harm, that I am suggesting that they <i>will</i>. I never said Beasts were <i>good guys</i>. I never said that there feeding <i>would not</i> cause harm. I said it <i><b>did not have to</b></i>, which is not true of Vampires*.<br /> <br /> I was calling out the assertion that the feeding of a Beast was intrinsically more harmful than that of a Vampire*. Practically speaking, both Vampire and Beast feeding habits will cause a great deal of harm in the long run regardless of how carefully they both feed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Ordo Dracul not withstanding</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:17:07-07:00","id":543285,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Granted my reading comprehension might of fell short when trying to understand what you wanted to get across. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your original statement was:</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;\u201c&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;Vampires feeding, &#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;&#91;I&#93;at minimum&#91;/I&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;, will &#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;&#91;B&#93;always&#91;/B&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93; cause physical harm, no matter how &quot;minor&quot;. A Beast feeding, &#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;&#91;I&#93;at minimum&#91;/I&#93;&#91;/FONT&#93;&#91;FONT=Arial&#93;, causes no harm at all.\u201d&#91;/FONT&#93;</pre> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">always is nice and bold. I feel like my example clearly breaks the always. (i may be getting stuck on wording but there seems to be less wiggle room for context in the above statement) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also Saying that the nurse digging the needle in a person is the vampires fault? Is like saying the man enjoying his steak went out to the farm and slit the cow's throat.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What I am trying to say is that a vampire can cause just as little </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>physical </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">harm as a beast when it comes to feeding. I believe that's important to bring up especially since the large portion of the last 20 pages is about vampires causing more harm than beasts. (alot of my post was directed at this, and seems to have fallen short :P) </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:28:40-07:00","id":543293,"title":"","content":"Stealing blood from a blood bank also causes harm.<br /> <br /> That was going to go to a person who needed a transfusion, meaning that person is less likely to receive a transfusion, meaning that person is more likely to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:30:10-07:00","id":543295,"title":"","content":"You example does not break that because the blood is not magically appearing in a bag, and stealing it from a legitimate blood bank also causes harm because that's blood people need to stay alive. <br /> <br /> Contrast that to a Beast being able to get by by handily beating you in a chess match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:31:34-07:00","id":543296,"title":"","content":"Blood banks do sell blood legitimately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:33:51-07:00","id":543298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543296#post543296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood banks do sell blood legitimately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when do Blood banks sell blood for transfusions to random people off the street?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:34:29-07:00","id":543299,"title":"","content":"Yes, and even if the vampires legitimately buy it, it still isn't going into those people needing blood transfusions is it? Making the legality of it irrelevant doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:36:11-07:00","id":543302,"title":"","content":"Vampires are hardly random people off the street, but blood banks are a billion dollar business, with a lot of waste. A lot of donated blood is likely going to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Not every vampire is the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckner_Cambronne\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire of the Caribbean</a>, but that doesn't mean there aren't harmless ways to feed.<br /> <br /> Can a Beast feed from scaring animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:37:12-07:00","id":543303,"title":"","content":"A Predator at low satiety can.<br /> <br /> If blood isn't good for transfusion, who says it's good enough to feed a vamp?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:40:10-07:00","id":543307,"title":"","content":"If they're going to throw it out, why not take it before it goes bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:43:18-07:00","id":543312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543307#post543307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're going to throw it out, why not take it before it goes bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I asked.<br /> <br /> let me rephrase: If the blood is no longer good for transfusion, then what makes you think it will provide sustenance to a vampire? Preserved blood is already less filling than fresh blood. The blood the banks throw out is thrown out because it's gone bad or is about too.<br /> <br /> At that point, it's just water and dead tissue. nothing vital about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-06-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:44:27-07:00","id":543313,"title":"","content":"There's no mechanics for technologically stored blood going bad. As you said yourself, if there's no mechanics for it, it doesn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:48:15-07:00","id":543314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543313#post543313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no mechanics for technologically stored blood going bad. As you said yourself, if there's no mechanics for it, it doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I said. I said there were no mechanics for Heroes becoming that way just because they met a beast.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, if blood isn't going bad, it's not being thrown out.<br /> <br /> Meaning either it goes bad and is thus worthless to vampires, or it never goes bad and thus can always be given to patients who need it.<br /> <br /> In the first case, a vampire cna't feed that way. in the second, not only is it not even an option, but feeding from presurved blood at all is putting somebody's life at risk.<br /> <br /> Can't have it both ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:49:31-07:00","id":543315,"title":"","content":"What is even going on in this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:52:50-07:00","id":543319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543315#post543315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is even going on in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>A discussion on whether or not vampiric feeding is more harmful than Beast feeding.<br /> <br /> Since Vampire Feeding either involves inflicting lethal damage to somebody or putting a transplant/transfusion patient at risk of death at bare minimum, while Beast feeding at bare minimum involves not hurting anybody at all, the answer is &quot;vampire feeding does more harm&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:53:43-07:00","id":543320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543315#post543315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is even going on in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was around page 168 did the drugs begin to take hold....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:56:04-07:00","id":543321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543315#post543315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is even going on in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. I was lost when someone used a creature that has been a rape metaphor as an example of good parasitism vs Beast feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:56:24-07:00","id":543322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543315#post543315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is even going on in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>People arguing over morality concerning a game about being humanity's most primal fears made manifest. It all seems a bit silly to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:57:02-07:00","id":543325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543314#post543314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not what I said. I said there were no mechanics for Heroes becoming that way just because they met a beast.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, if blood isn't going bad, it's not being thrown out.<br /> <br /> Meaning either it goes bad and is thus worthless to vampires, or it never goes bad and thus can always be given to patients who need it.<br /> <br /> In the first case, a vampire cna't feed that way. in the second, not only is it not even an option, but feeding from presurved blood at all is putting somebody's life at risk.<br /> <br /> Can't have it both ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that, dear friends, is how a conspiracy theory gets started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:00:05-07:00","id":543327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543325#post543325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that, dear friends, is how a conspiracy theory gets started.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the logic in this statement.<br /> <br /> I'm merely pointing out a hole in someone else's logic.<br /> <br /> Either donated blood eventually goes bad, and thus is thrown out but is either nonviable for feeding or at least not an appetizing or efficient way to feed.<br /> <br /> Or it never goes bad, and thus doen'st get thrown out, meaning it's always there for transfusions, meaning taking it is putting a transferee's life at risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:00:12-07:00","id":543329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543322#post543322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People arguing over morality concerning a game about being humanity's most primal fears made manifest. It all seems a bit silly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The morality of it is not the point of discussion. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:07:52-07:00","id":543336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543313#post543313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no mechanics for technologically stored blood going bad. As you said yourself, if there's no mechanics for it, it doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never said that so I'll ask. If the blood has gone bad, why would you assume that the Vampires would be capable of gaining sustenance from it?<br /> <br /> Also, does a Vampire feeding off an animal hurt it? That would be harming something by feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:11:27-07:00","id":543340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543302#post543302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are hardly random people off the street, but blood banks are a billion dollar business, with a lot of waste. A lot of donated blood is likely going to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Not every vampire is the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckner_Cambronne\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire of the Caribbean</a>, but that doesn't mean there aren't harmless ways to feed.<br /> <br /> Can a Beast feed from scaring animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the fact that Beasts aren't even directly scaring people, in a way that would be directly translatable to non-sentient life the way acquiring Vitae, Essence, or Mana are, how does the fact that you can harvest those fuels from animals seem any less cruel than doing likewise to people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:13:07-07:00","id":543341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543340#post543340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside from the fact that Beasts aren't even directly scaring people, in a way that would be directly translatable to non-sentient life the way acquiring Vitae, Essence, or Mana are, how does the fact that you can harvest those fuels from animals seem any less cruel than doing likewise to people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also add that just because a vampire goes to some lengths to try to find non invasive ways to obtain blood. It's still going against the grain of the vampiric nature, which is not at all pleasant for humanity. &quot;Nice&quot; vampires are still monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:16:26-07:00","id":543359,"title":"","content":"I've always interpreted VtR 2e as having any blood outside of the body for more than a few minutes loses potency and becomes entirely unpalatable after a single night. I've never really considered blood banks an option for that reason. Always figured the rules were just there for if someone tries it during an emergency. Doesn't work like VtM:Bloodlines where they're portable health potions anymore.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I'm out of this discussion. Once people start saying that things done with consent are always universally worse than something done without consent, there really is no rational discussion to be had anymore. The worldviews involved are too different to find any common ground.<br /> <br /> It is my view that anything done with consent is not harmful to the person who consented. With that view, the non-consensual feeding of beasts will never be &quot;better.&quot; Especially not when the in-book fluff uses poisoning, running over people's pets, choking people nearly to death, and abusing children at school as examples. Especially not when Vampires own what they are and Beasts pretend blaming the victim is acceptable. No matter what someone does, they do <b>not </b><i>deserve </i>what happens to people in the Beast books.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the rant. Vampires can and do get consent. Beasts cannot and do not. Non-consensual is not more moral than consensual, sorry. My mind won't really be changed on that, so I am going to attempt to respectfully bow out now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:17:27-07:00","id":543360,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, you guys might want to compare a Beast's feeding habits to those of a Changeling, since they are so very closely related. Hell, the Autumn Court should be welcoming a Beast with open arms, since they both feed on terror and use it to fuel their abilities.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Summer Court who feeds on rage, and the Winter Court who feeds on sorrow. I can't imagine either of those emotions are any less harmful than fear, possibly even more harmful to their victims when you think about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> We can all agree that emotional damage and physical damage are two very different themes and aren't really good for a moral comparison. Instead, we should be looking at the ways a Changeling can satisfy their Glamour without hurting others, and then try to apply that to a morally upstanding Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:20:49-07:00","id":543363,"title":"","content":"Morality wise i think everyone agree's they're both horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:21:53-07:00","id":543364,"title":"","content":"I went back, and I am trying to figure out exactly why the &quot;vampire (now changeling) vs. Beast: who is worst?&quot; has any relevance. Sure, you can give examples from both of those who don't harm humans and those whose very existence is a reason to kill them due to the innate harmful. <br /> <br /> But I don't really see why this would sway those humans who do hunt them why they should be killed. Nor why it would mean that the supernaturals being hunted wouldn't feel persecuted, especially if they aren't one of the supernarural who live up to stereotypes. And even those who are monsters don't think they are in many cases, or think it is natural, so they are as likely to feel persecuted as those who aren't monsters.<br /> <br /> The difference between a hunter and hero is not the value their target nor the method of their creation. Plenty of hunters take up the vigil due to being victims of the Supernatural, such as loosing a lover to a vampire, a child to the fae, or a friend to obe of the other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> The difference is the how and the why. The Hunters might not know what they are getting into, but it is an active choice. They aren't compelled by anything beyond normal human emotion and reason. Heroes are those who have a lack of identity that allows their role as a Beast Slayer due to a mythic compulsion. And as such, hunters pursue their targets and use human emotion and reason to pursue the monsters, while heroes are driven by their role in a story. <br /> <br /> Plus, hunters can be as bad as Heroes. Heroes simply start out that bad. People seem to like to cast the hunters as good guys, but they are just as prone to being monsters as the good guys. The more extreme hunters are going be no different than a Hero, which makes sense: both are low integrity humans. And both can recover their humanity by regaining their integrity. The key is that the Heroes only come about at that low integrity because they have been drawn into the beasts mythos.<br /> <br /> So if I am missing the point of the &quot;Vampire harm vs. Beast Harm&quot; argument, I am sorry. But it just seems odd to argue who deserves to be killed more based on the harm, thus justifying the Hunters vs. Heroes. Hunters will kill good supernaturals ( there is an entire compact dedicated to killing the forsaken and helping the pure and spirits wanting to posses people!) as much as the bad. Some supernaturals are &quot;good&quot; while others should be killed on sight. But arguing one splat inherently bad based of examples, and thus its splats human monster slayers as being more or less justified, is an effort in futility at best.<br /> <br /> (Note, I am not saying it needs to end. I just don't really follow where this debate is going. Please fill me in if it seems I completely am missing the point)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:23:21-07:00","id":543365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543359#post543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always interpreted VtR 2e as having any blood outside of the body for more than a few minutes loses potency and becomes entirely unpalatable after a single night. I've never really considered blood banks an option for that reason. Always figured the rules were just there for if someone tries it during an emergency. Doesn't work like VtM:Bloodlines where they're portable health potions anymore.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I'm out of this discussion. Once people start saying that things done with consent are always universally worse than something done without consent, there really is no rational discussion to be had anymore. The worldviews involved are too different to find any common ground.<br /> <br /> It is my view that anything done with consent is not harmful to the person who consented. With that view, the non-consensual feeding of beasts will never be &quot;better.&quot; Especially not when the in-book fluff uses poisoning, running over people's pets, choking people nearly to death, and abusing children at school as examples. Especially not when Vampires own what they are and Beasts pretend blaming the victim is acceptable. No matter what someone does, they do <b>not </b><i>deserve </i>what happens to people in the Beast books.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the rant. Vampires can and do get consent. Beasts cannot and do not. Non-consensual is not more moral than consensual, sorry. My mind won't really be changed on that, so I am going to attempt to respectfully bow out now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consent=/=morally sound. In fact Vampires are one of the worst sort of splats in general, and of the NWoD to try to argue are in a position to set up consent that really is a horrifying, dangerous, parasitic, manipulative situation. I make no arguments that monsterously abusive Beasts are not awful. But vampires as an example of not awful is disturbingly inaccurate. In a serious, not even remotely funny, these are creatures that are metaphors of drug addiction and rape. If people are going to try to evoke contrast to Beasts, don't use vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:27:31-07:00","id":543370,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that &quot;nice&quot; Beasts are still monsters, too. I do not intend to indicate otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to point out that the process of a Beast feeding does not <i>necessitate</i> injury of any sort (physical or other). The consumption of blood does. In one way or another, someone or something is going to suffer injury of some kind. Therefore the position that the feeding of a Vampire is less harmful than that of a Beast is false.<br /> <br /> However, in the course of &quot;real world&quot; scenarios, as it were, I doubt that the mortals of the WoD would see any distinction between the them. As an whole, each group will leave a trail of bodies behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:32:58-07:00","id":543378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543359#post543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from that, I'm out of this discussion. Once people start saying that things done with consent are always universally worse than something done without consent, there really is no rational discussion to be had anymore. The worldviews involved are too different to find any common ground.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not what's being argued.<br /> <br /> The argument is that something that innately causes physical injury is universally more harmful than something that does not require physical injury, and that consent means jack if it wasn't given by a mentally sound person with full knowledge of what they're agreeing to of their own free will.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is my view that anything done with consent is not harmful to the person who consented. With that view, the non-consensual feeding of beasts will never be &quot;better.&quot; Especially not when the in-book fluff uses poisoning, running over people's pets, choking people nearly to death, and abusing children at school as examples. Especially not when Vampires own what they are and Beasts pretend blaming the victim is acceptable. No matter what someone does, they do <b>not </b><i>deserve </i>what happens to people in the Beast books. </div> </div> </div> Injury, including blood loss, is innately harmful.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd argue that someone who runs a really shitty restaurant deserves to have his place shut down for health code violations(Tyrant feeding) and I'd expect serial killer to deserve death(Nemesis) I'd expect someone who makes long dedicated and detailed plans to opres others to deserve the terror that comes from his plans crashing down around him(Ravager) A Collector isn't mandated to hurt people at all, and a predator that seduces virgins into a one night stand is innately less harmful than a vampire who does the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apologies for the rant. Vampires can and do get consent. Beasts cannot and do not. Non-consensual is not more moral than consensual, sorry. My mind won't really be changed on that, so I am going to attempt to respectfully bow out now. </div> </div> </div>How many vampirs do you think can get informed consent from mentally healthy individuals without the person being coerced into it by force or supernatural power?<br /> <br /> Being mind fucked into saying yes is not consent.<br /> <br /> Agreeing to have sex is not consent to have your blood removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:39:07-07:00","id":543383,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, people, seriously. Unless a vampire drains somebody into a coma, it's not causing serious harm to their victims. Have you ever had your blood tested or donated to charity? Just drink some orange juice and you're recovered in a day or two. Most vampires drink only what they need to survive in order to keep themselves in check, and they are capable of closing the wounds left by their bites instantly. An &quot;evil&quot; vampire would just leave their victim to bleed out.<br /> <br /> A vampire feeding causes a brief moment of pain, followed by mind bending pleasure and then a day or two of recovery. Compare this to a Beast who's feeding invokes terror in the minds of their victims that can take years of therapy to recover from if such a thing is even possible. How do you tell your doctor you had a vivid dream of being digested alive or raped by a 7 headed bear? It's a joke to think vampires are any more harmful than Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:39:53-07:00","id":543384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543364#post543364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went back, and I am trying to figure out exactly why the &quot;vampire (now changeling) vs. Beast: who is worst?&quot; has any relevance. Sure, you can give examples from both of those who don't harm humans and those whose very existence is a reason to kill them due to the innate harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone claimed that Vampires were less harmful than Beasts.<br /> <br /> This is false, as a Vampire innately inflicts lethal damage on their victim and while one may claim that it was consented to, physical injury is still harm and consent given to a vampire is always dubious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:41:13-07:00","id":543385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543365#post543365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consent=/=morally sound. In fact Vampires are one of the worst sort of splats in general, and of the NWoD to try to argue are in a position to set up consent that really is a horrifying, dangerous, parasitic, manipulative situation. I make no arguments that monsterously abusive Beasts are not awful. But vampires as an example of not awful is disturbingly inaccurate. In a serious, not even remotely funny, these are creatures that are metaphors of drug addiction and rape. If people are going to try to evoke contrast to Beasts, don't use vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting further bogged down by explaining how we're all misinterpreting each other, I would argue that either the Lost or the Created are better points of comparison to the Begotten in terms of interests and impact on Mortal society, with the Created having a better connection in regards to social organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:45:41-07:00","id":543386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543383#post543383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, people, seriously. Unless a vampire drains somebody into a coma, it's not causing serious harm to their victims. Have you ever had your blood tested or donated to charity? Just drink some orange juice and you're recovered in a day or two. Most vampires drink only what they need to survive in order to keep themselves in check, and they are capable of closing the wounds left by their bites instantly. An &quot;evil&quot; vampire would just leave their victim to bleed out.<br /> <br /> A vampire feeding causes a brief moment of pain, followed by mind bending pleasure and then a day or two of recovery. Compare this to a Beast who's feeding invokes terror in the minds of their victims that can take years of therapy to recover from if such a thing is even possible. How do you tell your doctor you had a vivid dream of being digested alive or raped by a 7 headed bear? It's a joke to think vampires are any more harmful than Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I walked into a place to donate blood. It didn't include an ambulatory corpse beset with a monsterous aspect of itself that is quite possibly from the Lower Depths, has an addiction to the vital life fluids of living beings, preferably human, existing in a parasitic relationship with the rest of the world and possessing of mental ,emotional and physically manipulative powers set to wrest these vital fluids from beings that often are much younger than themselves(to Catch a Vampiric Predator anyone?). If you know anything about the literary history of vampires and the mythic underpinnings of vampires. Thinking that the nature of the &quot;consent&quot; in that is healthy is far more disturbing to me than what some people are attempting to derive from the preview text. Like, this isn't funny at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:46:30-07:00","id":543388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543383#post543383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, people, seriously. Unless a vampire drains somebody into a coma, it's not causing serious harm to their victims. Have you ever had your blood tested or donated to charity? Just drink some orange juice and you're recovered in a day or two. Most vampires drink only what they need to survive in order to keep themselves in check, and they are capable of closing the wounds left by their bites instantly. An &quot;evil&quot; vampire would just leave their victim to bleed out.<br /> <br /> A vampire feeding causes a brief moment of pain, followed by mind bending pleasure and then a day or two of recovery. Compare this to a Beast who's feeding invokes terror in the minds of their victims that can take years of therapy to recover from if such a thing is even possible. How do you tell your doctor you had a vivid dream of being digested alive or raped by a 7 headed bear? It's a joke to think vampires are any more harmful than Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An &quot;Evil&quot; Vampire wouldn't leave a victim to bleed out-a stupid vampire would. That's one less person to feed from in the future and one obvious vampire vicitm to attract the hunters.<br /> <br /> Now, answer me this. Would you rather suffer one significant injury's worth of blood loss, or have something stolen from you? Be intimidated by an authority figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:52:42-07:00","id":543389,"title":"","content":"1) When I started off this train of comparison, I used Vampire, Werewolf, and Changeling as comparisons. Had I time, I would have tied it into every single splat. My grand point is that predation is one of the many, many prevalent themes of the entire World of Darkness, and that Hungers are not thematically out of place. Can we please stop the fucking game of who's the bigger monster with their predation? All the splats have lovely penises, thank you.<br /> <br /> 2) In fact, can we all just stop for, like, a day or so? Give the thread a rest on the deep schisms? Get away, think on other things, cook something lovely with mushrooms and wine, have a picnic, come back after a while? At this point we have assembled a monster that puts anything the Devs had in mind to shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:57:51-07:00","id":543390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543383#post543383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, people, seriously. Unless a vampire drains somebody into a coma, it's not causing serious harm to their victims. Have you ever had your blood tested or donated to charity? Just drink some orange juice and you're recovered in a day or two. Most vampires drink only what they need to survive in order to keep themselves in check, and they are capable of closing the wounds left by their bites instantly. An &quot;evil&quot; vampire would just leave their victim to bleed out.<br /> <br /> A vampire feeding causes a brief moment of pain, followed by mind bending pleasure and then a day or two of recovery. Compare this to a Beast who's feeding invokes terror in the minds of their victims that can take years of therapy to recover from if such a thing is even possible. How do you tell your doctor you had a vivid dream of being digested alive or raped by a 7 headed bear? It's a joke to think vampires are any more harmful than Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Vampires use the Kiss, let alone use it proficiently.<br /> <br /> In point of fact I have, several times over the past 22 years. And all situational stress aside, the experience is not remotely comparable to having what you thought was another human being bite you and drink your blood.<br /> <br /> Likewise, your example Beast Feeding is not a typical example, just one that exploits the maximum possible circumstances to satisfy both your point and granting a favorable bonus to the roll to feed. It's the difference between playing a character and playing a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:01:18-07:00","id":543411,"title":"","content":"Lets change direction. What about beast do you really like? Let's show the writers what they got right. <br /> <br /> I love lair, love it. It has got to be the most interesting powerstat ever in a WW/OP game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:02:53-07:00","id":543420,"title":"","content":"So, anyone want to talk about something else for a bit? How about Atavisms? More specifically, any sort of &quot;niche&quot; that future Atavisms might fill. The two most obvious to me are:<br /> 1) Action at a Distance: It doesn't matter if it's a Giant who's force of will is strong enough to lift mountains or a Gorgon with a freakishly long and dexterous tongue, an effect that allows you to do things like melee attack or lift things at range seems like a good idea. Anakim seems like the best Family.<br /> 2) Super speed: While Imposing Presence improves speed as a Expenditure effect, it isn't really focused on it as a whole. An Atavism based on boosting Speed and Initiative seem like it would be good for those who are all about being terrifyingly swift. Eshmaki seems like a good fit.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I may be missing something with these. Anyone got any ideas of their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:06:00-07:00","id":543423,"title":"","content":"I feel like there is a speed Atavism, but I haven't checked yet(Hooray video editting!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:07:02-07:00","id":543424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543411#post543411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets change direction. What about beast do you really like? Let's show the writers what they got right.<br /> <br /> I love lair, love it. It has got to be the most interesting powerstat ever in a WW/OP game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lairs are awesome. I love the idea of the human monster with the soul of a primordial creature. That base concept itself just works for me. I keep picturing a man in a robe, in rich surroundings, a study filled with artifacts from across the globe. Sitting by a fire narrating some nautical tale and the listeners fail to see that he is casting shadows on the wall that writhe with the shape of a Kraken. For me Beasts are throwbacks. Creatures of a supernatural prehistoric era in the modern era. While there is psychological horror aspects to pull from Beast. I think if I use them in a game it will be as go-betweens and psychopomp foils to certain other lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:09:50-07:00","id":543425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543385#post543385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without getting further bogged down by explaining how we're all misinterpreting each other, I would argue that either the Lost or the Created are better points of comparison to the Begotten in terms of interests and impact on Mortal society, with the Created having a better connection in regards to social organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't making a statement relating the place of various monster splats in the NWoD. I was making a statement about not white washing the place of vampires in the setting and in particularly the nature of the relationship of vampires to sentient prey and how disturbing it is to make such a mistake. I'm not comparing them or any of them to Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:12:59-07:00","id":543427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543411#post543411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets change direction. What about beast do you really like? Let's show the writers what they got right.<br /> <br /> I love lair, love it. It has got to be the most interesting powerstat ever in a WW/OP game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? I mean, how often do you, as a player, get to set the stage, particularly with all the craziness you could hope for from a psycho-spiritual landscape that is both personal and universal?<br /> <br /> I also like it's implementation in game. Some Atavisms let you bring in big effects, but so long as you've got traction, you can bring down your Lair anywhere for the big effects. It's like instant drama-appropriate scene dressing.<br /> <br /> Plus I think a lot of gamers do have some background in dungeon design, and I liked having a return to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:16:29-07:00","id":543429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543411#post543411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets change direction. What about beast do you really like? Let's show the writers what they got right.<br /> <br /> I love lair, love it. It has got to be the most interesting powerstat ever in a WW/OP game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that Beasts are very XP-efficient. And that they don't get loaded down with extraneous kit.<br /> <br /> I also love that the central named character has a complete story arc, makes it past Lair 5, and get's the girl inside the limited space of the Chapter Prologue fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:16:34-07:00","id":543430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543384#post543384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone claimed that Vampires were less harmful than Beasts.<br /> <br /> This is false, as a Vampire innately inflicts lethal damage on their victim and while one may claim that it was consented to, physical injury is still harm and consent given to a vampire is always dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so it is mostly just a thread derailment. Gotcha. <br /> <br /> Though (and I hate myself for doing this, since I don't want to stoke this debate further...):<br /> Vamps can be harmless if they work to keep the or BP low and only eat animals. It isn't a pleasant existence, but it is possible. And on the more powerful end, they gain nothing from hunting mundane humans and essentially become Hunters, seeking and destroying other supernaturals. But most will have to eat people, which is (on a species level) going to be harmful for humanity, even if they only tried to target &quot;bad guys&quot; and those who consented (not getting into whether it was coerced, uniformed or fully informed consent). Beasts can be relatively harmless or even more destructive in their appetites than any vampire, and it really just depends on their satiety and their personal predilection. <br /> <br /> But that said, this really is a debate that seems to have sidetracked. It is focusing on something that I don't think will get us anything but in a loop on morality (at best) or annoyed and completely derailed (at worst). I suggest we move back towards the original discussion, and if this debate is really important, make a new thread for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: it seems I delayed long enough in posting my reply that we have already moved on (or at least are attempting to)... so my apologies.<br /> <br /> I have to second the love for Lairs. I was most skeptical about this part (specifically, it's mechanics), so I am happy with how it turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:18:33-07:00","id":543431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543423#post543423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there is a speed Atavism, but I haven't checked yet(Hooray video editting!)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are there not two that effect speed? I know the Looming Presence does. Wait, the other was a Beast only Merit maybe? Also, the Beast Merits are <i>awesome</i>~<br /> <br /> I punch you, now take Agg damage. Nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, being able to have permanent armor at 5/2 also <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:22:24-07:00","id":543436,"title":"","content":"Since we're on lairs maybe someone can help me out with something. In the writing it says you can have an undiscribied lair and in return your given 2xp. So what happens to that lair is it forever closed of? Can the players later in describe it? 2xp also seems like a sizable chunk of xp for a minor setback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:28:04-07:00","id":543437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543436#post543436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on lairs maybe someone can help me out with something. In the writing it says you can have an undiscribied lair and in return your given 2xp. So what happens to that lair is it forever closed of? Can the players later in describe it? 2xp also seems like a sizable chunk of xp for a minor setback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that your character has not yet opened that chamber, but can go through the process during play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:28:20-07:00","id":543438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543436#post543436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on lairs maybe someone can help me out with something. In the writing it says you can have an undiscribied lair and in return your given 2xp. So what happens to that lair is it forever closed of? Can the players later in describe it? 2xp also seems like a sizable chunk of xp for a minor setback.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you <i>start without any extra Chambers</i> then you get two Experiences. Seeing as this leaves you with relatively little in the way of easy access to Primordial Pathways and requires the usual things for such additions to remedy, I hope you have a trustworthy broodmate to piggyback off of to get to your own Heart or don't mind needing to break people's minds or talk your way into regular access to magical real estate.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I feel like there's a story to be had from a Beast whose Chambers are overwhelmingly &quot;stolen&quot; Hearts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:32:09-07:00","id":543440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543436#post543436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on lairs maybe someone can help me out with something. In the writing it says you can have an undiscribied lair and in return your given 2xp. So what happens to that lair is it forever closed of? Can the players later in describe it? 2xp also seems like a sizable chunk of xp for a minor setback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why this made it jump to mind. But I just realized that Beasts can in fact have......a Volcano Lair! This is overly humorous to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:32:28-07:00","id":543441,"title":"","content":"Lair is just such a lovely thing. It's interesting and very flavorful in everything it does. I'm a big fan of how deeply personal and flexible the benefits are, which makes Lair unique and defining to each Beast.<br /> <br /> It's also lovingly designed in that you have very strong and natural incentive to level it, but in conjuction with the rest of the mechanics the player always has reason to purchase Attributes or invest in Merits rather than simply dump all Experiences into supernatural powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:34:32-07:00","id":543442,"title":"","content":"I am just wondering can their be enough to make custom made atavisms that would seem intersting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:37:16-07:00","id":543446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543431#post543431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are there not two that effect speed? I know the Looming Presence does. Wait, the other was a Beast only Merit maybe? Also, the Beast Merits are <i>awesome</i>~<br /> <br /> I punch you, now take Agg damage. Nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, being able to have permanent armor at 5/2 also <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, just plain-Jane Fleet of Foot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:37:41-07:00","id":543447,"title":"","content":"Now I want a Lurker who talks like Bruce from Family Guy. &quot;I'm a Dragon!~ Oh no!~ Rawr!~&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:44:03-07:00","id":543450,"title":"","content":"On the flip side a Beast based of comic book guy from the Simpson who treats his lair like a dungeon crawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:56:00-07:00","id":543451,"title":"","content":"Calling back something mention earlier in this thread, the idea that Oliver Queen from Arrow is the best Hero on tv right now, it got me thinking and going through the shows characters and I came up with a break down of the characters as Beasts or Heroes:<br /> Oliver Queen- he is an Eshmaki Nemesis in my view, filling his Hunger in more violent ways, before eventually filling it without killing as time went on.<br /> <br /> Malcolm Merlyn- a Hero, who is later reformed and then becomes a Namtaru Predator at the end of season 3 (taking that Soul from Ra's Al Ghul after he becomes Unfettered)<br /> <br /> Slade Wilson- Another Hero against Oliver, he is not reformed.<br /> <br /> Thea Queen- Malcolm tried to turn her into a Hero, but it eventually led to her becoming an Ugallu Nemesis<br /> <br /> Roy Harper- He is a Anakim Tyrant<br /> <br /> Jon Diggle- He is a Eshmaki Nemesis<br /> <br /> Ray Palmer- As the Atom he is definitely a Ugallu either Collector or Ravager (given how many building he destroyed)<br /> <br /> Felicity Smoak- she is an Ugallu (the internet/cyberspace is her sky) either a Ravager (given all the hacking/network wrecking she does) or a Collector (given all the various romantic relationships she has been in)<br /> <br /> Laurel Lance- she is an Ugallu Predator<br /> <br /> Oliver, Jon, Felicity are all in a Brood together (Roy, Laurel, Ray and Thea all joined the Brood at later times, but Roy has left the Brood now)<br /> <br /> I don't know why this go stuck in my mind, but it had to get written out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:07:50-07:00","id":543453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543450#post543450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the flip side a Beast based of comic book guy from the Simpson who treats his lair like a dungeon crawl.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And it works, since he'd be a collector and taunt heroes with &quot;epic loot!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:11:28-07:00","id":543454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543453#post543453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it works, since he'd be a collector and taunt heroes with &quot;epic loot!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>*dispatches a Hero* Worst. Murderhobo. Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T22:06:43-07:00","id":543472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543451#post543451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling back something mention earlier in this thread, the idea that Oliver Queen from Arrow is the best Hero on tv right now, it got me thinking and going through the shows characters and I came up with a break down of the characters as Beasts or Heroes:<br /> Oliver Queen- he is an Eshmaki Nemesis in my view, filling his Hunger in more violent ways, before eventually filling it without killing as time went on.<br /> <br /> Malcolm Merlyn- a Hero, who is later reformed and then becomes a Namtaru Predator at the end of season 3 (taking that Soul from Ra's Al Ghul after he becomes Unfettered)<br /> <br /> Slade Wilson- Another Hero against Oliver, he is not reformed.<br /> <br /> Thea Queen- Malcolm tried to turn her into a Hero, but it eventually led to her becoming an Ugallu Nemesis<br /> <br /> Roy Harper- He is a Anakim Tyrant<br /> <br /> Jon Diggle- He is a Eshmaki Nemesis<br /> <br /> Ray Palmer- As the Atom he is definitely a Ugallu either Collector or Ravager (given how many building he destroyed)<br /> <br /> Felicity Smoak- she is an Ugallu (the internet/cyberspace is her sky) either a Ravager (given all the hacking/network wrecking she does) or a Collector (given all the various romantic relationships she has been in)<br /> <br /> Laurel Lance- she is an Ugallu Predator<br /> <br /> Oliver, Jon, Felicity are all in a Brood together (Roy, Laurel, Ray and Thea all joined the Brood at later times, but Roy has left the Brood now)<br /> <br /> I don't know why this go stuck in my mind, but it had to get written out</div> </div> </div> </div>DoooD! SPOILERS!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T22:17:37-07:00","id":543474,"title":"","content":"Okay, had some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Was there a place where it mentioned why Beasts have human bodies, because if so I missed it.<br /> <br /> I'd like more alternative theories in Beast, like Gaia is listed as one of the names some beasts call the Dark Mother by. So what if the connection to the werewolves is through Luna? You can't tell me the goddess of shapeshifting and insanity and Gaia mother of monsters wouldn't be related. <br /> <br /> Also, the beast views are too clean, if they know enough about werewolves to know that they believe they are descended from Father Wolf and Mother Moon, then they should also know that not all werewolves believe that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:00:36-07:00","id":543481,"title":"","content":"Okay I think I figured out the whole thing on Beasts with a hunger for collecting something and shopping. So early in the book it says that a collector with a gold hunger can't just walk into a jewelry store and later it mentions a Beast with a collection hunger going into a pawn shop with a wad of cash. What I think the rule for feeding low satiety collectors is that object has to have significance to someone. Meaning a collector is rarely going to be in a situation where a brand new ring at K's or some jewelry store will have the appropriate significance to work for a collection. A pawn shop by comparison tends to be where people go to trade their possessions for money and while sometimes this is a case of not wanting the object there's a fair chance that the object used to, if not still does, have importance to the person selling it because the money is more important at the time allows it to be used for feeding.<br /> <br /> So the $3000 white gold ring at K's might not be a valid target for a feeding, but the $350 gold ring that Mr. Smith gave his kid when he graduated that was pawned for $250 is a viable target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:02:00-07:00","id":543482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543389#post543389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) In fact, can we all just stop for, like, a day or so? Give the thread a rest on the deep schisms? Get away, think on other things, cook something lovely with mushrooms and wine, have a picnic, come back after a while? At this point we have assembled a monster that puts anything the Devs had in mind to shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>B:tP - The Nerd Rage</b>&quot; is corebook that is self-writing on our eyes. One is sure - this &quot;game&quot; is engagint all the fandom in extreme emotions - like good World of Darkness game should. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:08:45-07:00","id":543486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543474#post543474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay, had some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Was there a place where it mentioned why Beasts have human bodies, because if so I missed it.<br /> <br /> I'd like more alternative theories in Beast, like Gaia is listed as one of the names some beasts call the Dark Mother by. So what if the connection to the werewolves is through Luna? You can't tell me the goddess of shapeshifting and insanity and Gaia mother of monsters wouldn't be related.<br /> <br /> Also, the beast views are too clean, if they know enough about werewolves to know that they believe they are descended from Father Wolf and Mother Moon, then they should also know that not all werewolves believe that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking the Beast is human when not in their lair. In the lair one of the Children normally fuses with their Soul ,the monster part, to wander or do whatever its going to do. Atavisms are about drawing part of that soul into the human body out of the Primordial Dream, and why the book says that a Beast can use all aspects of its Atavisms as it wants in the lair. (Though I'm 99% sure the part where you have to spend satiety for the big effect will still cost satiety.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:10:36-07:00","id":543487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543474#post543474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like more alternative theories in Beast, like Gaia is listed as one of the names some beasts call the Dark Mother by. So what if the connection to the werewolves is through Luna? You can't tell me the goddess of shapeshifting and insanity and Gaia mother of monsters wouldn't be related.<br /> <br /> Also, the beast views are too clean, if they know enough about werewolves to know that they believe they are descended from Father Wolf and Mother Moon, then they should also know that not all werewolves believe that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about this yasterday - in my POV, Beasts should equate <b>Luna</b> with Dark Mother. Luna is known as Mother of Werewolves, is personification of Shapeshifting, Night and Madness - very sutabe to Dark Mother figure. Also, the rumors that Idigams are first children of Luna, makes sense as her as Mother of Monsters.<br /> <br /> I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game\">proper topic on Werewolf forum</a> to dwell on this more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:31:01-07:00","id":543527,"title":"","content":"I saw this; thought it was intriging so I decided to share it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nezumi-chan on rpg.net</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've finally formulated what I like about the game, so far, give or take. (Crosspost from Tumblr, plus some additions I may cross-edit back to there)<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. I\u2019m still reading <i>Beast: The Primordial</i>, and there are a few worrisome things about the handling of Heroes (the fact that it\u2019s not really a choice ups the horror and tragedy, but has some really unfortunate implications), and I can definitely see why some people are upset by making the \u201coppressed/marginalized group\u201d analogue literal monsters that scare people to survive\u2026 but the entire game and metaphor are really, really resonating with my experiences as a trans woman and autistic person. Heroes are <b>uncomfortably</b> similar to eugenics and Autism cure advocates, to MRAs and other misogynistis, to TERFS and other anti-transers.<br /> <br /> And in a world where I keep getting told I hurt people just by existing, a character who <b>owns that</b> \u2013 that can minimize their harm or go all out, but who is what they are and doesn\u2019t have to apologize or deny themselves \u2013 comes across as hugely appealing.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that I can absolutely get behind monsters who are actually <b>monsters</b> as PCs in an RPG -- who can be good or bad, who can try to channel it positively and minimize it or go rampaging, but who absolutely <b>have</b> to scare and hurt people, because they're monsters and that's what monsters do and why should we gloss that over or ignore it?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:02:35-07:00","id":543582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543486#post543486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally speaking the Beast is human when not in their lair. In the lair one of the Children normally fuses with their Soul ,the monster part, to wander or do whatever its going to do. Atavisms are about drawing part of that soul into the human body out of the Primordial Dream, and why the book says that a Beast can use all aspects of its Atavisms as it wants in the lair. (Though I'm 99% sure the part where you have to spend satiety for the big effect will still cost satiety.)</div> </div> </div> </div> You do realize that doesn't do a single iota to answer my question, right?<br /> <br /> My point still stands- Why the @#$#$# do beasts have human bodies? Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:09:17-07:00","id":543584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543582#post543582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that doesn't do a single iota to answer my question, right?<br /> <br /> My point still stands- Why the @#$#$# do beasts have human bodies? Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unfettered lack Lairs and are not the base state of the Soul as embodied in the Begotten, besides the matter of the Primordial Dream being a weird nonstandard layer of the Astral.<br /> <br /> Chill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:12:29-07:00","id":543587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543582#post543582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that doesn't do a single iota to answer my question, right?<br /> <br /> My point still stands- Why the @#$#$# do beasts have human bodies? Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watsonian-They aren't Goetia, As werewolves are of both the flesh and of the spirit, and Sin-Eaters are of both the Flesh and the Dead, so are Beasts of the Flesh and of the Astral. Its' just, they go about it in a manner that's a little different from the other two.<br /> <br /> Doyalist-For the same reasons that an Angel falling and becoming a Demon stops being an ephemeral being and starts being a being with a meat body with the attendant complexity of stats-because it's a template applied over a character made in the default manner, and WoD character creation only handles things that can pass for human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:42:00-07:00","id":543595,"title":"","content":"Shadowed Soul, transport to any shadow in sight. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'll see you on the dark side of the moon.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:47:52-07:00","id":543598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543582#post543582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that doesn't do a single iota to answer my question, right?<br /> <br /> My point still stands- Why the @#$#$# do beasts have human bodies? Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Misread thought you asked if they have human bodies and figured you were asking if the soul existed as a different being inside the lair when the human was outside. Besides I imagine the whole masquerade and keeping the existence of other splats becomes a whole lot harder if the local pool had to be closed down after a Kraken moved in. Otherwise I think Satchel and Rater have it handled pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T01:40:32-07:00","id":543624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UnjustCustos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543595#post543595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowed Soul, transport to any shadow in sight. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'll see you on the dark side of the moon.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can see the dark side of the moon? (No Pink Floyd jokes, please)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T02:01:37-07:00","id":543637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543624#post543624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can see the dark side of the moon? (No Pink Floyd jokes, please)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not from Earth, hence the reason it is called the dark side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T02:09:36-07:00","id":543640,"title":"","content":"Technically that's the <i>far</i> side. The <i>dark</i> side is whichever side is dark, and we can see <i>that</i> most of the time, at least partially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T02:49:17-07:00","id":543675,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking, well that and Been Playing The Secret World abit... and well John/The Black Signal is a Beast, As are the Dreamers.<br /> <br /> The Twisted and Black Filth could be a Lair Effect... Dreamers are Incarnates that want too turn the Entire Earth into their Lair (The Dreamers are Likely a Brood that All Incarnated)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T04:43:27-07:00","id":543723,"title":"","content":"Random thought: All splats have to potential to basically end up creating Heroes, they are just not as focused on killing their creator and they are called Psychos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Ex-hunters who become Psychos often suffered at the hands of a supernatural creature, but not physically. One Psycho might have become bound by blood to vampire. Another was the mate of a werewolf. A Psycho might have been magically enslaved, unable to reach out for help due to spells placed on her mind. The Psycho hates the supernatural, and that hate spills over into every other aspect of his being.<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"> (Slashers, p. 110)</span></i><br /> <br /> As others have mentioned Slashers also have the same morality stats prerequisites as Heroes, and Psychos do have an even more explicid connection to Heroes than other Slashers.<br /> Given that Beast is crossover focused I think it is a missed oppurtunity they didn't have Hero creation more explicidly connected to Slasher creation and have all Heroes start with the abilities of one of the Slasher templates. A Mask with Hero abilities on top of their Slasher abilities would certainly make for one hell of an opponent for a Beast, and might for example be a possible result of a Dramatic Failure (or success!) on trying to make the Beast's Soul stealing ability permanent on a mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T05:14:12-07:00","id":543753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543723#post543723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought: All splats have to potential to basically end up creating Heroes, they are just not as focused on killing their creator and they are called Psychos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Ex-hunters who become Psychos often suffered at the hands of a supernatural creature, but not physically. One Psycho might have become bound by blood to vampire. Another was the mate of a werewolf. A Psycho might have been magically enslaved, unable to reach out for help due to spells placed on her mind. The Psycho hates the supernatural, and that hate spills over into every other aspect of his being.<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"> (Slashers, p. 110)</span></i><br /> <br /> As others have mentioned Slashers also have the same morality stats prerequisites as Heroes, and Psychos do have an even more explicid connection to Heroes than other Slashers.<br /> Given that Beast is crossover focused I think it is a missed oppurtunity they didn't have Hero creation more explicidly connected to Slasher creation and have all Heroes start with the abilities of one of the Slasher templates. A Mask with Hero abilities on top of their Slasher abilities would certainly make for one hell of an opponent for a Beast, and might for example be a possible result of a Dramatic Failure (or success!) on trying to make the Beast's Soul stealing ability permanent on a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have thought one purpose of Heroes being mechanically distinct was partly so that people didn't need a second book to make the line's basic antagonist. It would have been really cool, though. I like the idea of more counter-supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:21:09-07:00","id":543885,"title":"","content":"Hey, has anyone else noticed that about half the example Unfettered mentioned in the book <i>don't</i> sound like they were at satiety 10 when they died? What's going on there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:29:48-07:00","id":543886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543587#post543587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watsonian-They aren't Goetia, As werewolves are of both the flesh and of the spirit, and Sin-Eaters are of both the Flesh and the Dead, so are Beasts of the Flesh and of the Astral. Its' just, they go about it in a manner that's a little different from the other two.<br /> <br /> Doyalist-For the same reasons that an Angel falling and becoming a Demon stops being an ephemeral being and starts being a being with a meat body with the attendant complexity of stats-because it's a template applied over a character made in the default manner, and WoD character creation only handles things that can pass for human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sin-eaters have human souls, which beasts don't seem to have, werewolves have this synergistic hybrid vigor thing going on, which beasts, with their completely human bodies, don't really share.<br /> <br /> So I was thinking more along the lines of where the advantage comes in.<br /> , <br /> Beasts are smarter than goetia, but that leads to 'Why does the Dark Mother want intelligent children?&quot; While I quite value intelligence, the loss doesn't really seem to hamper ephemeral beings like goetia. <br /> <br /> Another advantage is the power trait, lair which goes up to 10, which can lead to goetia with rankings over 5. So perhaps like the green sun princes of exalted, beasts are embryonic gods, the next generation of dark mothers and fathers. <br /> <br /> Of course that leads to the question, what are all these dark gods of fear and hunger up to, surely beasts must have resulted in some unfettered of rank above 5 by now?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:54:44-07:00","id":543896,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm gonna go ahead and say the Dark Mother is a Beast who Ascended at lair 9 or 10. Maybe she was the first, just a freak accident in the astral where some poor human's oneiros got slammed into the anima mundi or something. After ascending she decided to make more of her kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:55:46-07:00","id":543897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543582#post543582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. They're humans with souls that are made from primordial fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:04:48-07:00","id":543903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543886#post543886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sin-eaters have human souls, which beasts don't seem to have, werewolves have this synergistic hybrid vigor thing going on, which beasts, with their completely human bodies, don't really share.<br /> <br /> So I was thinking more along the lines of where the advantage comes in.<br /> ,<br /> Beasts are smarter than goetia, but that leads to 'Why does the Dark Mother want intelligent children?&quot; While I quite value intelligence, the loss doesn't really seem to hamper ephemeral beings like goetia.<br /> <br /> Another advantage is the power trait, lair which goes up to 10, which can lead to goetia with rankings over 5. So perhaps like the green sun princes of exalted, beasts are embryonic gods, the next generation of dark mothers and fathers.<br /> <br /> Of course that leads to the question, what are all these dark gods of fear and hunger up to, surely beasts must have resulted in some unfettered of rank above 5 by now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Human forms do grant a modicum of social camouflage, even if that's hampered by certain Atavisms (Alien Allure, and Looming Presence in particular). Granted the Forsaken have more than a few tricks that have more finesse when dealing with mundane humans, Beasts aren't subject to having people immediately lose their shit when they utilize the more monstrous aspects of their power set.<br /> <br /> As to your question, even if one of the Begotten held on in the face of despair that long, odds are that they'd necessarily spend more time haunting the Anima Mundi and Temenos than any other Realm of existence, as those are easier to access and don't require a link to the Primordial Dream to support the Beast Soul's presence. Generally speaking, they'd stay where the food is abundant, competition is minor, and enemies are few to nonexistent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:42:45-07:00","id":543917,"title":"","content":"The Children benefit from humanity and human intelligence because it gives them access to Nightmares. The Soul by itself can only use Atavisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:23:16-07:00","id":543944,"title":"","content":"They dont have human bodies. They have Beast bodies. Beasts are not human. Just because their bodies are a lot like a humans dos t really matter, because a human body can't pick up a car and throw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:43:25-07:00","id":543960,"title":"","content":"They do in fact have human bodies. Atavisms are simply the Soul intruding on/mixing with their otherwise normal bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:47:31-07:00","id":543971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543582#post543582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that doesn't do a single iota to answer my question, right?<br /> <br /> My point still stands- Why the @#$#$# do beasts have human bodies? Beasts are goetia in human bodies (if the unfettered are anything to go by), goetia don't need human bodies, the astral plane is filled with goetia without bodies of any sort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well one of the Inheritance paths mentions the body and soul fusing completely and seems to indicate the Beast turns into the physical avatar of their soul. I don't know if this means they transform fully into a monster, or if their soul is just controlling the body, but a Beast who performs this loses any trace of their humanity and goes on a feeding spree until it's finally put down. In other words, same thing as a vampire Revenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:01:07-07:00","id":543976,"title":"","content":"Without having read the book, what makes heroes so dangerous for Beasts and their power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:15:54-07:00","id":543987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543976#post543976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without having read the book, what makes heroes so dangerous for Beasts and their power?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can inflict weaknesses on Beasts called 'Anathema' that compel them to behave in certain self-destructive ways, or which make them vulnerable to certain substances or circumstances. Heroes believe (and cannot be convinced otherwise) that they are discovering pre-existing weaknesses inherent to a Beast, but something about them creates the weaknesses instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:23:43-07:00","id":543989,"title":"","content":"Man, I love how a Beast&lt;-&gt;Demon meeting can end up with both of them getting the Spooked Condition. It just hilarious to imagine two of these staring at each other in mutual discomfort and horror. Wouldn't want to lose that bit of mechanics for anything.<br /> <br /> My only critique about how Demons and Beasts interact is that they really need at least <i>one</i> other type of Supernatual creature that Beasts react to in the same way as to Demons. Ideally make one up just for Beasts as additional Antagonists, or use one of the existing Antagonist factions from another gameline (Abyssal creatures would fit for the 'not-kin' effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:28:17-07:00","id":543990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543989#post543989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I love how a Beast&lt;-&gt;Demon meeting can end up with both of them getting the Spooked Condition. It just hilarious to imagine two of these staring at each other in mutual discomfort and horror. Wouldn't want to lose that bit of mechanics for anything.<br /> <br /> My only critique about how Demons and Beasts interact is that they really need at least <i>one</i> other type of Supernatual creature that Beasts react to in the same way as to Demons. Ideally make one up just for Beasts as additional Antagonists, or use one of the existing Antagonist factions from another gameline (Abyssal creatures would fit for the 'not-kin' effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, they seem to count Abyssal Intruders as kin as much as anything. After all, one of their Nightmares allows them to fiddle with the Abyss within all of us ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:32:08-07:00","id":543993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543990#post543990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, they seem to count Abyssal Intruders as kin as much as anything. After all, one of their Nightmares allows them to fiddle with the Abyss within all of us ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. Didn't mean to imply Abssals aren't kin by RAW. I am saying they need at least one additional 'not-kin' faction, and Abyssals would fit if they don't make up a new faction whole-cloth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-07-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:38:03-07:00","id":543995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543993#post543993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I know. Didn't mean to imply Abssals aren't kin by RAW. I am saying they need at least one additional 'not-kin' faction, and Abyssals would fit if they don't make up a new faction whole-cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it makes Demons stand out as particularly strange and alien entities. Which is something I rather like. Plus, Angels and other God-Machine things are pretty clearly not-kin, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:39:26-07:00","id":543996,"title":"","content":"Plus that entire aspect of the divine being sacred/profane and apart. Cause, you know, it's important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:40:29-07:00","id":543997,"title":"","content":"Maybe a &quot;Dreamless&quot; Human Type... that hunt Beasts for the Nightmares they generate.. Because even that is Better then NEVER Dreaming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:44:04-07:00","id":543999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543997#post543997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a &quot;Dreamless&quot; Human Type... that hunt Beasts for the Nightmares they generate.. Because even that is Better then NEVER Dreaming?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having Star Trek flashbacks.<br /> <br /> Like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:49:21-07:00","id":544014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543999#post543999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much like. Although I could see some Beasts cultivating such people as friends (or slaves) as well. After all, they can go Under the Bed with them and give them such lovely nightmares that way ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:51:57-07:00","id":544030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543995#post543995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, it makes Demons stand out as particularly strange and alien entities. Which is something I rather like. Plus, Angels and other God-Machine things are pretty clearly not-kin, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of most other settings I'd agree. But not for the New World of Darkness. It one of the most important things about this world just how filled to the brim with unexplainable horrors and wonders it is. It's a setting where even the most powerful and wise entitities of all are never more than grasping at straws in a dark room full of dangers.<br /> Demons aren't that special within the greater NWoD, they are just one more unexplainable horror among many, and every Beast should come across a lot of things that leave it utterly stumped over the course of its existence. Giving more than one non-kin faction actually does a lot more to help the unique nature of the World of Darkness than having them stand out like that. It would also enable them to put Demons specific form of non-kin weirdness into a much shaper focus and give them more definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:59:05-07:00","id":544032,"title":"","content":"Can't say I'm thrilled with Beast. Reading the comments on RPG.net and Something Awful it appears I'm not alone. It's a shame because I was really looking forward to it, but it seems the author's let their political axe to grind kinda destroy a great concept.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I think with some minor changes, Heroes would make an awesome Tier 3 Hunter Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Get rid of all the Strawman &quot;They're all horrible people, really!&quot; stuff, and keep the fact they're people who are broken and have been beaten down. People who have been abused, and then by some chance run across a Beast. Finally they decide to stand up for themselves and their fellow humans when faced with this monstrous creature who exists only to create more misery around it...<br /> <br /> Killing it, they count coup and gain more power. They are &quot;buying into the narrative&quot; as the means of gaining their abilities. Throw in the possibility of them becoming completely self obsessed ego maniacs, rather than Heroes of story and legend, and you end up with a pretty cool Hunter splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:06:56-07:00","id":544037,"title":"","content":"Well, okay. Not everyone is going to like this game, and the mass of similar comments will undoubtedly help with supplements.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I was thinking of Relenetless Hunter, and it doesn't quite do what I was thinking of. Oops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:08:39-07:00","id":544038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544032#post544032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it seems the author's let their political axe to grind kinda destroy a great concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen comments to this effect a few times. <br /> <br /> I have <i>no idea</i> what it is supposed to be referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:10:28-07:00","id":544040,"title":"","content":"And down the abyssal rabbit hole we go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:18:09-07:00","id":544054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544040#post544040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And down the abyssal rabbit hole we go.</div> </div> </div> </div> At least I get to imagine the cross looking on Rey's face as he says that? I'm sure we could get some interesting sample Beasts out of some of Gunnerkrigg's characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:18:31-07:00","id":544055,"title":"","content":"Must we do this again? If people do not like the book, can they please refrain from saying they 'ruined the entire concept'? Does it need to be like this, or can people just be content with going 'this is not to my taste, I'm bowing out'? Because it has been quite irritating for the past few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:19:18-07:00","id":544056,"title":"","content":"It's not worth killing the calm we've had for the past few pages.<br /> <br /> THe worst part is that I have no wine and no mushrooms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:23:44-07:00","id":544061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544038#post544038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen comments to this effect a few times.<br /> <br /> I have <i>no idea</i> what it is supposed to be referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, that Heroes are a stand in for Gamergate, MRA's and Anti-feminists. Beasts are suppose to be a stand in for those who are &quot;Othered&quot; by our society. Transgendered inividuals, minorities, homosexuals, ect....as the text claims &quot;they just want to be left alone&quot; except for the Heroes who hunt them down and are singled minded. The Heroes are the stand in for perceived Hate movements in our society...Hell one of the example Heroes is a Trillby wearing neckbeard who actually says &quot;M'lady&quot; to people...you can't get more blatant than that..<br /> <br /> The problem of course comes down to the fact Beasts ARE in fact terrible people to the world. They have to feed on pain and misery, they are responsible for the creation of Heroes...<br /> <br /> This results in this very strange dichotomy where essentially it's being said &quot;Feminists create anti-Feminists with their very presence and actions by abusing non-Feminists&quot;... Since Beasts do infact abuse people, it paints the &quot;Other&quot; they're suppose to be championing as being responsible for some pretty horrible things.... By contrast the text goes so far out of it's way to demonize Heroes and paint them as terrible people, it ends up making them more sympathetic.... A hero is someone with Integrity 4...and while that can mean a bad person, it can also mean a victim of abuse...someone who has been raped, or lived in poverty all their life, abused....and other such things...and then a Beast ends up scaring the shit out of them, and they supposedly become a self obsessed ego-maniac..<br /> <br /> This could have been handled with far more nuance... If Heroes were written to be more sympathetic, or if Beasts were given more clear options that doesn't make them just unrepetenant terrible monsters, the narrative would work...but at the end of the day you end up with a situation where nobody is happy..<br /> <br /> Well except for those who love the game...which there are quite a few, and kudos to those who do... the above is just the general sentiment of those of us who have problems with the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","user":"Orphan81","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:33:52-07:00","id":544067,"title":"","content":"I'm going to hate myself for this, but if I didn't have something to self-loathe I'd become the king of arrogance, so here we go.<br /> <br /> Considering that Beasts <i>are</i> terrible people or at least have strong drives towards doing terrible things and how that contradicts certain points in the thesis, and considering that Matt has said <i>several times over</i> that Heroes are not a stand in for any of the things you've listed, can we at least have a concession that while it can be read that way, it is in no means the only one way to read it, and in fact probably not the intention of the developer and the writers?<br /> <br /> Because either we end a conversation that has been beaten into a dead-horse paste and move on with our lives or we devolve into another pit of now meaningless discussion because the book isn't going to change much at the content level at this point.<br /> <br /> I would really like to avoid the ages of countless repetition getting nowhere and generating nothing but vitriol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:43:15-07:00","id":544091,"title":"","content":"I've said my piece and opinion, I don't want to drag down the thread, so feel free to move on. My views are my own and I make no claim to it being the &quot;only&quot; interpretation of the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:44:15-07:00","id":544092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544061#post544061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially it's being said &quot;Feminists create anti-Feminists with their very presence and actions by abusing non-Feminists&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, no it isn't. Beasts only create heroes when they're starving, so what would be being said if that was the metaphor is &quot;Feminists create anti-Feminists with their very presence and actions by NOT abusing non-Feminists ENOUGH&quot;. Which is clearly an utterly bonkers sentiment to express.<br /> <br /> A hero isn't just an abuse victim lashing out at their oppressors. They've had an astral spirit attack their soul and have <i>gone crazy. </i>They have a Hunger, as real and as impossible to ignore as a beast's that drives them to single-mindedly hunt them to the exception of all else. Except unlike a beast they don't even have the option to sate it through harmless channels. They <i>need</i> to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:44:36-07:00","id":544093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544067#post544067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really like to avoid the ages of countless repetition getting nowhere and generating nothing but vitriol.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that this discussion has disquieted a few people. A few people may end up having to do some soul searching. May end up having to go on a pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Ok, I'll stop :P<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:46:00-07:00","id":544094,"title":"","content":"Hmm while heroes don't replace hunters, hunters are more or less likely to use heroes just as soon as they'd use any other minor template. I think Heroes are interesting and broken enough we'll probably see a book similiar to slashers at some point. <br /> <br /> Also on another note. Beast character functionally have no Integrity system they can be as bad as they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:51:30-07:00","id":544101,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Oh, we're all in agreement. Nevermind!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:52:46-07:00","id":544104,"title":"","content":"Putting everything aside, I think the real message of Beast The Primordial can be expressed in a single phrase:<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck You I am a Dragon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:55:52-07:00","id":544110,"title":"","content":"<div