ck and get elected mayor of Toronto.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Rob Ford has gotta be an astoundingly blatant Anakim Tyrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:06:26-07:00","id":544123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544121#post544121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you smoke some crack and get elected mayor of Toronto.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Rob Ford has gotta be an astoundingly blatant Anakim Tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a classical Tyrant. Shits more like &quot;Eh, Fuck it. I don't care.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:07:53-07:00","id":544124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544120#post544120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am kind of surprised that no one has mentioned bloodborne what with all the monsters and beasts in that game. The enemies are literally<br /> called beasts<br /> <img src=\"https://psmedia.playstation.com/is/image/psmedia/bloodborne-bestiary-blood-starved-beast-two-column-01-ps4-us-20mar15?$TwoColumn_Image$\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>About 5-6 Pages Back.. someone was Saying about Running a Game In The Bloodbourne City, I Posted afew Connections/Creatures = as (IE Great Old Ones are Incarnated Beasts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:11:16-07:00","id":544125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544114#post544114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm Reminded of the Dark Sun D&amp;D Campaign, Specifically the Part of Dying of Thirst &quot;Alignments are Momentarily Suspended until you are no-longer Dying of Thirst&quot; Basically a Beast is Always Hungry and the Hunger Dominates their actions. High Satiety and they can Regret it like anyone would, Low and they Don't Care. I Believe i said it before.... &quot;When their Full their human and That Sucks because you can Feel everything you've done and Regret it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now.. How about Homebrewing/Making a Spell too Set a Beast at Satiety 10 temporarily? Or Even a Nightmare..... Hmm....<br /> <br /> Edit: Notice this is a Running theme with Characters with Hungers in NWoD.... When Hungry alot of them are Straight up... &quot;MUST FEED!&quot; i can Understand that abit. (Also not using this as an Excuse for Beasts, Just an Example) Also Makes Beasts abit more of &quot;Kin&quot; too Pandorians.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm but what would a beast be willing to do when his not feeding his hunger. Say Saitey 4 and some drunk asshole picks a fight. They would be all brawrafafasg MURDERFACE~ I'm a monster yo. Of course that's a quick way to get unneed attention but i figure it just paints Beasts as probably one of the more dangerious splats which could be fun to explore with its focus on cross over element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:17:34-07:00","id":544131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544125#post544125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm but what would a beast be willing to do when his not feeding his hunger. Say Saitey 4 and some drunk asshole picks a fight. They would be all brawrafafasg MURDERFACE~ I'm a monster yo. Of course that's a quick way to get unneed attention but i figure it just paints Beasts as probably one of the more dangerious splats which could be fun to explore with its focus on cross over element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means they Should also be Rarer, And the Good ones Should be Less common (PC Characters) Heroes are Much Likely too be Wanted by the Good Ones so they don't have too kill their &quot;Brothers/Sisters&quot; Atleast in my Eye. A Group of say 5-6 In a City will drive the City into Paranoia if they ALL Start making Big Plays for Fear... If they Aren't Careful Hunters WILL come after them and they might Spawn afew Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:19:34-07:00","id":544135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=543486#post543486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Though I'm 99% sure the part where you have to spend satiety for the big effect will still cost satiety.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think that? You said it yourself: the effects of Atavisms are about drawing part of the Soul from the Primordial Dream into the Beast's physical body.<br /> <br /> They're natural abilities or traits of the monster the Begotten truly is. The normal effect is simply from the portion of the Soul's power that seeps from the Lair and into the Beast's flesh at all times. When the Soul is hungry, it becomes restless and driven. Its power in the Primordial Dream increases, and more bleeds out, sharpening the Atavisms of the Beast in the physical world.<br /> <br /> The final effect pulls the majority of strength of the Atavism into the physical world, in a normally very drastic and unsubtle way. The sheer potency involved is evident in how anyone with appropriate sensitivity can perceive the form of the Soul when a Beast activates it, and is why it costs Satiety to do so in the first place.<br /> <br /> But in the Lair, the Soul is completely present. The Beast doesn't need to be hungry or to expend their metaphysical fuel to manifest Atavisms. They're already there in their full capacity, as part of the Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:27:41-07:00","id":544150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544032#post544032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get rid of all the Strawman &quot;They're all horrible people, really!&quot; stuff, and keep the fact they're people who are broken and have been beaten down. People who have been abused, and then by some chance run across a Beast. Finally they decide to stand up for themselves and their fellow humans when faced with this monstrous creature who exists only to create more misery around it..</div> </div> </div> </div>And what about all of the people who are naturally at Integrity 4 because they're extremely sociopathic or psychopathic?<br /> <br /> What about the ones who degenerated that low because they committed murders?<br /> <br /> What about all of the bullies or abusers? you know, the people who are flat out called as being likely to become heroes? I mean, Things like Abuse and Supernatural Encounters are unlikely to bring integrity <i>that </i>low-then the abuser is more likely to become a hero than the abusee.<br /> <br /> What about the assholes who sit around blaming everybody but themselves for their problems? The other people called out as being likely to become heroes?<br /> <br /> What about the fact that integrity 4 is Slasher Territory, and as soon as you hit &quot;serial killer&quot; levels of integrity you don't get to play the victim card as an excuse anymore-you get to play the &quot;mad dog who needs to be put down before he hurts someone&quot; card.<br /> <br /> And Heroes do not come from &quot;a chance encounter with a beast&quot; They come from 1: A Beast not feeding long enough for their soul to go rampaging, having the misfortune for their soul, and being unlucky enough to fuck it up, or 2: A Beast fucking up one Nightmare and having the poor luck to do it to a person who is deeply mentally unstable.<br /> <br /> Considering that the Nightmares caused by soul ravaging are, for everybody but a hero, harmless, that means that a hero is not a victim of the Beast, they're a victim of a accident.<br /> <br /> And an other thing: As has been pointed out, their are Beasts who thrive on causing fear, seriously hurt people. And there are the beasts who generate the nightmares that sometimes turn potential serial killers into Heroes.<br /> <br /> THESE ARE NOT THE SAME BEASTS<br /> <br /> The Beasts who deserve to be killed are not the ones who make the hero making nightmares. They are not the ones with heroes coming to kill them(at least at first).<br /> <br /> And heroes can and will kill anyone they perceive as being on the Beast's side.<br /> <br /> So, you have a deeply unstable person, most likely a bully, abuser, sociopath, psychopath, or extreme narcissist, with Serial Killer levels of Integrity, who after having a bad dream, decided to go hunt down a monster. This &quot;monster&quot; is real, but does not deserve death. The person hunting it will kill anyone who gets in their way.<br /> <br /> sounds a fucking lot like a Slasher.<br /> <br /> I think people are getting hung up on the &quot;:but you can lose integrity from abuse/supernatural&quot; and not stopping to think how unlikely it is to get that low from anything but natural degeneration or deliberately doing things that lower integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:30:45-07:00","id":544155,"title":"","content":"Someone named Paradim posted a comic over at the rpg.net thread, and I'd thought I'd share it here, considering the parallels some have been drawing for the Begotten. <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/gallery/NuqGD\" target=\"_blank\"> Here it is!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:30:59-07:00","id":544156,"title":"","content":"Concerning the resurgence of the recently toxic topic: can we please get a subforum for Beast so that posters will be more comfortable spreading their discussions out over multiple topics instead of feeling the need to keep it all in a handful of topics? Then people could go to, say, the &quot;Heroes: evil or misunderstood?&quot; thread and know what they're getting into, and mods could feel more comfortable shutting it down if it gets out of hand.<br /> <br /> And this thread could die of old age instead of continuing to wander from topic to topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:45:55-07:00","id":544198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544061#post544061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basically, that Heroes are a stand in for Gamergate, MRA's and Anti-feminists. Beasts are suppose to be a stand in for those who are &quot;Othered&quot; by our society. Transgendered inividuals, minorities, homosexuals, ect....as the text claims &quot;they just want to be left alone&quot; except for the Heroes who hunt them down and are singled minded. The Heroes are the stand in for perceived Hate movements in our society...Hell one of the example Heroes is a Trillby wearing neckbeard who actually says &quot;M'lady&quot; to people...you can't get more blatant than that..</div> </div> </div> </div>Prove it. I'm seeing heroes as a stand in for &quot;sociopathic assholes and serial killers, some of whom <i>might</i> have been sympathetic at one point but are not anymore&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem of course comes down to the fact Beasts ARE in fact terrible people to the world. They have to feed on pain and misery, they are responsible for the creation of Heroes... </div> </div> </div> They don't have to hurt people to feed, the Beasts with heroes coming after them are are most likely the ones who are not feeding at all and thus not hurting people, and hero creation is very clearly just an accident of fate, not the fault of any one being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This results in this very strange dichotomy where essentially it's being said &quot;Feminists create anti-Feminists with their very presence and actions by abusing non-Feminists&quot;... </div> </div> </div> I think you're reading to much into something.<br /> <br /> This could have been handled with far more nuance... If Heroes were written to be more sympathetic[/quote] Sympathetic backstories are less likely to bring someone to serial killer morality [/quote]or if Beasts were given more clear options that doesn't make them just unrepentant terrible monsters[/quote] They're given plenty, you're just overlooking them.<br /> <br /> How is a Health Inspector whose extra strict to make absolutely sure a restaurant is up to code a terrible unrepentant monster? Or a Vice-Principal who takes great joy in giving out strict but fair punishments to the children in her school(Tyrant Feeding) How about the Predator who lures people out, makes them think she drowned, and feeds on their altruism when they try to rescue her? Also she's done is play a somewhat cruel prank. Not an unrepentant monster deserving death. Collecting requires at worst theft, not a monster, I hardly see how breaking windows and scaring the people in the house makes you an unrepentant monster, especially if you only do it to rich people who can easily afford repairs(example ravager) And a Nemesis can feed their hunger in little increments by being a Cop.<br /> <br /> Again, the problems I'm seeing that make people not like the game seems to be a case of painting all of the heroes with the &quot;abuse victim&quot; brush, the one that only rarely applies and is thus a minority o f heroes, and then painting all Beasts with the &quot;Unrepentant murderous monster&quot; brush, despite plenty of evidence that at least half of Beasts are not that bad, and I'd expect the majority of Beasts don't, since Unrepentant murderous monster tends to attract negative attention from free range heroes, hunters, mortal authorities, and pissed of vampires/werewolves/mages/other who think you're a security risk. That tends to thin out the herd a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-07-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:50:56-07:00","id":544201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544155#post544155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone named Paradim posted a comic over at the rpg.net thread, and I'd thought I'd share it here, considering the parallels some have been drawing for the Begotten. <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/gallery/NuqGD\" target=\"_blank\"> Here it is!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Someone posted that in this thread already. It's dozens of pages back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:08:00-07:00","id":544207,"title":"","content":"Or, since this particular topic keeps coming up over and over and over again, could we at least move it to its own thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:18:05-07:00","id":544212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544201#post544201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone posted that in this thread already. It's dozens of pages back.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologizes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:37:39-07:00","id":544220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544212#post544212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologizes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you don't need to apologize. There are a lot of pages and considering we've had jumps into the repeated vitriol filled topics like are Heroes bad guys, or just victims; is a Beast's feeding more harmful than a vampire's; and complaining about the sociopolitical hammer someone insists is being beaten over the readers head. It is kind of understandable that something would get lost in the shuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:45:04-07:00","id":544224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544135#post544135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you think that? You said it yourself: the effects of Atavisms are about drawing part of the Soul from the Primordial Dream into the Beast's physical body.<br /> <br /> They're natural abilities or traits of the monster the Begotten truly is. The normal effect is simply from the portion of the Soul's power that seeps from the Lair and into the Beast's flesh at all times. When the Soul is hungry, it becomes restless and driven. Its power in the Primordial Dream increases, and more bleeds out, sharpening the Atavisms of the Beast in the physical world.<br /> <br /> The final effect pulls the majority of strength of the Atavism into the physical world, in a normally very drastic and unsubtle way. The sheer potency involved is evident in how anyone with appropriate sensitivity can perceive the form of the Soul when a Beast activates it, and is why it costs Satiety to do so in the first place.<br /> <br /> But in the Lair, the Soul is completely present. The Beast doesn't need to be hungry or to expend their metaphysical fuel to manifest Atavisms. They're already there in their full capacity, as part of the Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure one way or the other now. It mentions the lair counts as &quot;resonant&quot; to itself (duh) so at the very least they cost willpower in there and not satiety.Also by default Apex beasts still spend satiety (as they have a power that means they don't for a specific atavism once a chapter) and their souls are as present in reality as they are in their lair. On the other hand it's not clear if they get to use the low satiety effects whenever they want either so maybe there's still a difference there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:58:56-07:00","id":544232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544212#post544212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologizes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not passing judgement. Just making a statement, it had already posted. Nothing to apologize for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:07:20-07:00","id":544235,"title":"","content":"I believe in the lair the only time you'd spend satiety is you want to get the high satiety effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:36:33-07:00","id":544294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544235#post544235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe in the lair the only time you'd spend satiety is you want to get the high satiety effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 120</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls have access to the Beast\u2019s Atavisms (but not Nightmares, which require more finesse than the Soul can manage). The Soul can use any aspect of an Atavism \u2014 normal, low Satiety, or Satiety expenditure. Also, the Beast counts as always being in a Lair-resonant location when acting inside the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 156-7</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an area resonates with a Beast\u2019s Lair, the Beast\u2019s Atavisms are more dangerous. She can use the Satiety expenditure aspect of her Atavisms by spending a point of Willpower, rather than Satiety. She can do this once per scene per dot of Lair.<br /> <br /> Note that this only applies in the physical realm. Inside its Lair, the Soul has access to the full range of the Beast\u2019s abilities, as does the Beast when she and the Soul merge inside the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Costing Satiety to use the Satiety Expenditure effects of your Atavisms inside your Lair would mean that iconic tricks like Wings of the Raptor or Monster From The Deep are inaccessible to a Beast when their Atavisms are nominally at their most effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:43:34-07:00","id":544296,"title":"","content":"Heyo, noob question here: Do you guys think a minor splat could go through a Homecoming and become a Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:55:05-07:00","id":544310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544296#post544296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heyo, noob question here: Do you guys think a minor splat could go through a Homecoming and become a Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much, I believe. They'd lose the template, liquidating any powers that aren't explicitly retained(like a Wolf-Blooded's Tells) back into XP. I'd generally rule it could only be spent on Supernatural traits, but I think that's up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:56:52-07:00","id":544311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544294#post544294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bunch of quotes +<br /> <br /> Costing Satiety to use the Satiety Expenditure effects of your Atavisms inside your Lair would mean that iconic tricks like Wings of the Raptor or Monster From The Deep are inaccessible to a Beast when their Atavisms are nominally at their most effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. that makes sense. I think I skipped that last bit by accident because it was over the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:12:54-07:00","id":544410,"title":"","content":"Going back over the Primordial Pathways rules again:<br /> <br /> Am I reading it correctly that a Willpower point isn't required on the Wits + Resolve roll to open a Pathway from the seed locations of your Chambers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:14:24-07:00","id":544412,"title":"","content":"That seems to be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:32:00-07:00","id":544468,"title":"","content":"I'm on page 117-118 and i haven't seen anything that overides that 1WP cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:32:45-07:00","id":544469,"title":"","content":"Yep. It's cheap to do, though usually a quite heavily penalised roll (depending on your character's planned destination, of course), though Lair Traits helps some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:37:46-07:00","id":544471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544468#post544468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm on page 117-118 and i haven't seen anything that overides that 1WP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not in the section describing the roll itself, but it's repeated in two different places in the text.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p117</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opening a Pathway to the exact location the Beast created a Chamber from is easiest, but desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use locations that are similar <b>by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt</b> and incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the location matches (see p. XX.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p123</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with opening a Primordial Pathway, Beasts may attempt to use a Chamber in locations that are similar, if not exactly the same,<b> by spending a Willpower point.</b> To impose Traits into a substitute location like this, the player must succeed on a Wits + Resolve roll, with a dice penalty based on how dissimilar the location used is.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:38:11-07:00","id":544472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544468#post544468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm on page 117-118 and i haven't seen anything that overides that 1WP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Opening a Pathway to the exact location the Beast created a Chamber from is easiest, but desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use locations that are similar <b>by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt. </b>&quot;<br /> <br /> If it cost a willpower normally that bold bit wouldn't make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:43:03-07:00","id":544476,"title":"","content":"@ELFiveI think the bold part is just repeating the cost and a case of the book just needing editing/simplifying. I mean there's no way around the <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Cost: 1 willpower</pre> </div>(so it must just be repeating it self i would think)<br /> <br /> @Satchel I can't really make heads and tail of that paticular quote. At first i'm thinking okay pay 1 WP to effect the destination than 1WP to open the pathway if your trying to reduce the dice penalty. But i don't think that's quiet it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","user":"Mal","date":". 06-07-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:48:15-07:00","id":544480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544125#post544125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm but what would a beast be willing to do when his not feeding his hunger. Say Saitey 4 and some drunk asshole picks a fight. They would be all brawrafafasg MURDERFACE~ I'm a monster yo. Of course that's a quick way to get unneed attention but i figure it just paints Beasts as probably one of the more dangerious splats which could be fun to explore with its focus on cross over element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of Satiety 4-6, the question becomes &quot;how much effort do I need to end this fight?&quot; If you focus on Atavisms, the hungrier you are, the less effort you need, whereas a Nightmare focused Beast has an easier time when nearly full. Inside 4-6, everything requires effort to be effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:50:44-07:00","id":544482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544476#post544476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ELFiveI think the bold part is just repeating the cost and a case of the book just needing editing/simplifying.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Grammar does not work that way. &quot;BUT x CAN do y BY z&quot; implies a conditional exception. I really can't see how you could read it any differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:00:26-07:00","id":544484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544482#post544482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grammar does not work that way. &quot;BUT x CAN do y BY z&quot; implies a conditional exception. I really can't see how you could read it any differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's established before hand 5 or so pages that there is a cost to the action.<br /> <br /> So saying it costs willpower 5/6 pages later to me is simply repeating the fact that opening pathways costs 1WP and not introducing a cost. Would it make sense(more so) if the bold part was left out? Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:04:10-07:00","id":544486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544114#post544114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm Reminded of the Dark Sun D&amp;D Campaign, Specifically the Part of Dying of Thirst &quot;Alignments are Momentarily Suspended until you are no-longer Dying of Thirst&quot; Basically a Beast is Always Hungry and the Hunger Dominates their actions. High Satiety and they can Regret it like anyone would, Low and they Don't Care. I Believe i said it before.... &quot;When their Full their human and That Sucks because you can Feel everything you've done and Regret it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now.. How about Homebrewing/Making a Spell too Set a Beast at Satiety 10 temporarily? Or Even a Nightmare..... Hmm....<br /> <br /> Edit: Notice this is a Running theme with Characters with Hungers in NWoD.... When Hungry alot of them are Straight up... &quot;MUST FEED!&quot; i can Understand that abit. (Also not using this as an Excuse for Beasts, Just an Example) Also Makes Beasts abit more of &quot;Kin&quot; too Pandorians.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from life experience, having had profound Combined Type ADHD and Type 1 Diabetes since childhood, I can say that when you're forced to be conscientious about your urges, it sucks more when you <u>aren't</u> satisfied, something STs and players should keep in mind when making Feeding rolls. You aren't far wrong if you approach Family Dinner like buying a candy bar at a convenience store in lieu of purchasing a proper meal, while those high level feedings should feel like a home-cooked meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:07:30-07:00","id":544491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544484#post544484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's established before hand 5 or so pages that there is a cost to the action.</div> </div> </div> </div>The notation indicating the Willpower cost applies to inexact Chamber resonance comes <i>before</i> the roll description. That is the earliest mention of a Willpower cost for the normal means of opening a Pathway; everything preceding that is part of alternative methods like Skeleton Key or Under The Bed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:10:23-07:00","id":544505,"title":"","content":"I think the book is saying if you wish to open a Primordial Pathway from a Chamber to a place that is dissimilar to it, then you would spend a WP point. Otherwise it's a quick roll with a likely penalty and it doesn't cost willpower to open the Pathway to a place directed linked with the Chamber or what have you.<br /> <br /> Skeleton Key costs willpower, though thats forcing open a gateway normally to somewhere else, like a Hedge-Gate or Avernian Gate to lead into the Primordial Dream instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:19:57-07:00","id":544520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544094#post544094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm while heroes don't replace hunters, hunters are more or less likely to use heroes just as soon as they'd use any other minor template. I think Heroes are interesting and broken enough we'll probably see a book similiar to slashers at some point.<br /> <br /> Also on another note. Beast character functionally have no Integrity system they can be as bad as they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd likely get the same response from Matt that people got when Alchemists where announced as Promethean's main Antagonist splat, i.e.: that's not the game they're writing, so stop asking. I have only a little distaste at the possibility of PC Heroes, but I don't think it's beyond the realm of possibility.<br /> <br /> It's too bad though. They did Rational Egoism so well in Dark Ages Vampire (Via Adversarius FTW<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, Satiety is just another in a long line of &quot;no, but at the same time yes,&quot; that really endears this splat to me. The fact that the consequences range from not regaining fuel to some asshole's out to get you is just enough reality to make things fresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T00:42:57-07:00","id":544892,"title":"","content":"Personally I think playable Heroes are doable, but if you want to play a sociopath who levels up from killing monsters D&amp;D will probably give you a better range of options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:53:34-07:00","id":545094,"title":"","content":"Just a heads up (and not trying to stir things), but Rich just posted this in the Kickstarter comments. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">90-99% done doesn't mean we cant or won't edit sections that require it, or rewrite material that didn't come across as intended. Part of the reason for putting out the text with the KS is so we can hear and respond to comments about the book before we have gone into the next phase of the production process. We are aware of folks' concerns and are discussing what tweaks to the material could help to resolve any issues where the authors' intent didn't come through. Thanks.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>On another interesting (and likely irrelevant note), I've been comparing the Beast and Demon pledge levels via kicktraqs for each day. Barring the first day and the third day, Beast has been getting more dollars and backers each day, although Demon is still overall doing better at this point (the difference on the first day is huge) but the margin keeps narrowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:59:10-07:00","id":545097,"title":"","content":"Rich is the man. I don't know how he does it sometimes.<br /> <br /> I despise people who post stuff like: &quot;well, I was going to pledge more, but not if the book stays in the shape it's in now.&quot; Or &quot;I was really going to pledge for this, but it really bothers me that the book seems to support ___________(blah blah blah, insert whatever issue you'd like).&quot;<br /> <br /> The book is fine. The concept is fun. The writing is good. People are going to complain, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:06:05-07:00","id":545100,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's not much you can do to appease people who seem to have formed a negative opinion of your work by reading the mechanics <i>backwards. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:18:53-07:00","id":545104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545097#post545097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rich is the man. I don't know how he does it sometimes.<br /> <br /> I despise people who post stuff like: &quot;well, I was going to pledge more, but not if the book stays in the shape it's in now.&quot; Or &quot;I was really going to pledge for this, but it really bothers me that the book seems to support ___________(blah blah blah, insert whatever issue you'd like).&quot;<br /> <br /> The book is fine. The concept is fun. The writing is good. People are going to complain, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this a rather harmful perspective that does everyone involved a disservice.<br /> <br /> Complaints are valid even if you do not like or agree with them. Likewise, your complaints are valid even if other people do not like and agree with them.<br /> <br /> The situation can't get better if only praise is allowed. That paints a false picture. That's doing a disservice to the developers. They can't improve themselves and their work if they never receive views other than their own.<br /> <br /> Contradictory viewpoints is how we all grow as people, even if the modern presumption is that all critique is mean-spirited and bad by its very nature.<br /> <br /> I critique because I love OPP and the work they do and want to see it kept to that excellent standard it's had since I first became a customer. I don't critique because I want to tear them down and be mean. I don't think most other people do, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:24:02-07:00","id":545106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545097#post545097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rich is the man. I don't know how he does it sometimes.<br /> <br /> I despise people who post stuff like: &quot;well, I was going to pledge more, but not if the book stays in the shape it's in now.&quot; Or &quot;I was really going to pledge for this, but it really bothers me that the book seems to support ___________(blah blah blah, insert whatever issue you'd like).&quot;<br /> <br /> The book is fine. The concept is fun. The writing is good. People are going to complain, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? It's actually good if people post why they're not backing it and how can it be improved. It provides information to the developers to make an informed decision. Knowing what the community likes/dislikes is super important for any developer. <br /> The only question here is what's the tone of the post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T07:12:33-07:00","id":545144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545106#post545106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It's actually good if people post why they're not backing it and how can it be improved. It provides information to the developers to make an informed decision. Knowing what the community likes/dislikes is super important for any developer.<br /> The only question here is what's the tone of the post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like in All things, Constructive Critism is ALWAYS Useful. One of the Issues i Think people have Hang-ups on is the Fact People WANT too put a Black and White Morality on Essentially Sociopaths and Murders. As Written Most Heroes Aren't Victims that suddenly decide too hunt Monsters because of a Bad Dream, they are instead People who THINK they are Victims that want too have something too Blame and So Do once a Beast gives them a Bad Dream. Most of them anyway.<br /> <br /> If you (As a GM) WANT a sympathetic Hero then write one.. It's not Hard too do. Hell... Here's a Freebie. Isaac from Binding of Isaac is Both a Beast (With his Dream Selves being Blue Boy and/Or Satan) or a Hero that is Trying too Slay the Monster that is Constantly Hounding him (Mum/Mum's Heart/It Lives/Satan/Isaac/The Lamb Etc... They could all be different Forms of the Same Beast OR Different Beasts that he is Projecting onto). If no-one Knows why i say him... Look up the Alternative Interpretations of the Story.<br /> (In Short, Isaac was Playing with his Sister and Locked her in his Chest by accident, She Died, He Didn't Know, His Mom and Dad found her, after awhile they Split up, Isaac see's his mum Drinking and is Shouting at him/the TV and Thinks she is coming too kill him.)<br /> <br /> I Think that Beasts need another Adversary honestly, something so that Heroes AREN'T the only focus on why they are Monsters. Something that Preys on them would be Good (Hence the Earlier Comment on a Dreamless Human type that Feeds on beasts because Even Nightmares are better then Nothing would be Good (Could Even Tie them in with Mages/The Abyss and have them as a Constantly Growing Living &quot;Dreamless Black Hole&quot; that needs to feed just As Much as Beasts After the First Taste)).<br /> <br /> Point i'm Making is Discussion is Fine Aslong as people have something that's not just &quot;Don't Like it&quot; more useful is &quot;I don't like it because of X, or Y isn't very cohesive&quot; &quot;Y Needs too be explained better&quot; Etc. Alot of the Posts prior too the 99% Version being shown had the Fear that Heroes are Flat Characters... They Are and That's because it's a Defense Mechanism for them. Post 99% people are Saying its All About Them being Victims. Again the Book Explains that later on, But some Haven't read that OR don't feel it's justified/Right. Giving Constructive Critism can help them Decide that need too Clarify things/Expand upon them so people can get the original intentions.<br /> <br /> Blah. Too Serious for me... Sorry. Generally don't like too blather like this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T07:24:22-07:00","id":545150,"title":"","content":"I'm still picking through the 99% copy, but is there even that hard of guidelines on who a Hero needs to be? There are a lot of ways to reach Integrity 4, after all, and the easiest way to get and stay there is to commit murder or simply be exposed to a violent supernatural act. From what I remember it was more like a natural reaction; the people who become heroes are reacting to a negative experience that most people just shrug off because of a past experience. Their become heroes are triggered not by what the Beast does, but rather by what has already happened to them since most people will experience the Beast's nightmares and not become a hero. Why are people making such a big deal about them? They're a general templet, your the one who's suppose to fill them in and make them interesting. <br /> <br /> That was just my reading of it though, and I really need to reread that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T07:41:50-07:00","id":545159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545150#post545150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still picking through the 99% copy, but is there even that hard of guidelines on who a Hero needs to be? There are a lot of ways to reach Integrity 4, after all, and the easiest way to get and stay there is to commit murder or simply be exposed to a violent supernatural act. From what I remember it was more like a natural reaction; the people who become heroes are reacting to a negative experience that most people just shrug off because of a past experience. Their become heroes are triggered not by what the Beast does, but rather by what has already happened to them since most people will experience the Beast's nightmares and not become a hero. Why are people making such a big deal about them? They're a general templet, your the one who's suppose to fill them in and make them interesting.<br /> <br /> That was just my reading of it though, and I really need to reread that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes and Integrity (Page 399-400)<br /> In Chapters Two and Five, we mention that in order for a person to become a Hero, his Integrity<br /> rating can be no greater than four. For purposes of creating Hero characters, that\u2019s all you need<br /> to know, but it\u2019s important to unpack that idea so that you understand why that\u2019s the case and<br /> what it means for Heroes.<br /> Integrity, as explained in Chapter Four, is a game trait measuring the health of a person\u2019s soul<br /> and self-image. Integrity does not, by itself, measure whether a person is \u201cgood\u201d or not. It is not<br /> a measure of kindness or compassion. Certainly people with high Integrity traits tend to be strong<br /> of character, and strength of character leads to empathy and compassion, but it is possible to<br /> have a high Integrity rating and be harsh, cruel, or even violent. It simply means that the<br /> character is well aware of who and what he is.<br /> Incipient Heroes, though, lack that awareness. Their souls are weak, whether by nature or by<br /> difficult lives whittling away their Integrity. They tend to be shortsighted, self-centered (but not<br /> self-aware), and unfocused. A person can fall to this level of Integrity in any number of ways;<br /> when you are designing Heroes for your Beast chronicle, it\u2019s worthwhile to consider how it<br /> happened. You don\u2019t need to design breaking points for the character (though you can), nor do<br /> you need to detail how any given dot of Integrity was lost, but just a general sense of what<br /> happened to the character is enough. Did the character avoid talking to people out of belief that<br /> he was better? Did the character suffer some hardship and look for someone else to blame? Or is<br /> the answer more basic \u2014 is the character an abuser or a bully?<br /> <br /> Copied from the Text.. Hopefully sums it up?<br /> The Way i Read it is That Mostly the people who Become Heroes/Have a Mythic Reaction are generally those who 1, Blame things on Others/Fate rather then their own Failings. 2, Are More likely too be generally immoral in the First Place (Abusers not Abusees, Bully's not Bullied). 3, Likely Might have had a Brush with the Supernatural. 4, MORE THEN LIKELY ALWAYS TAKE THE SIMPLE OPTION WHEN DOING ANYTHING. They Probably have a Really easy too Fulfill Vice in the First place.. and Will indulge it most chances they get.<br /> <br /> This of Course is only a Generalisation and might be Missing afew things, Also It's not impossible for a Hero too have been an Victim and became what they are.. But i suspect they won't have, IF the GM/You want too have a Sympathetic one.. It's Possible too do, you just need a reason why they Suddenly Decided that &quot;If I kill this monster I Will recover/Have a better life&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:09:24-07:00","id":545451,"title":"","content":"Hey, can someone tell me if a Beast who starts the game with a Kinship, HAS to pick a Kinship Nightmare, or if they just CAN pick one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:14:21-07:00","id":545454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545451#post545451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, can someone tell me if a Beast who starts the game with a Kinship, HAS to pick a Kinship Nightmare, or if they just CAN pick one?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be a <b>can, </b>not a <b>must.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:15:40-07:00","id":545455,"title":"","content":"Started a Recruiting post for Beast. If you want to, come on over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:37:08-07:00","id":545516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545454#post545454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'll be a <b>can, </b>not a <b>must.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:09:34-07:00","id":545552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545104#post545104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this a rather harmful perspective that does everyone involved a disservice.<br /> <br /> Complaints are valid even if you do not like or agree with them. Likewise, your complaints are valid even if other people do not like and agree with them.<br /> <br /> The situation can't get better if only praise is allowed. That paints a false picture. That's doing a disservice to the developers. They can't improve themselves and their work if they never receive views other than their own.<br /> <br /> Contradictory viewpoints is how we all grow as people, even if the modern presumption is that all critique is mean-spirited and bad by its very nature.<br /> <br /> I critique because I love OPP and the work they do and want to see it kept to that excellent standard it's had since I first became a customer. I don't critique because I want to tear them down and be mean. I don't think most other people do, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with complaints. I never said I did. I have a problem with people LOOKING for things, that are not there, to complain about. Some people actively try to find things that bother them, and then present those things in such a toxic way, that it does NOTHING to help the developers, or the fans of the product.<br /> <br /> I was also focused mostly on what I've seen on other message boards, not this one. Critiquing is fine. Trying to find some socio-political agendas(where there are none) and using it to attack the developers or the book? Yeah, that's not cool.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say the modern presumption is that all critique is mean-spirited and negative. Not at all. But it CAN be(see Exalted, Beast, etc.).<br /> <br /> I will, however, say that in this hobby, there is a growing number of people who's primary goal is to attack and destroy material for no logical reason. To find things that simply do not exist, and then attack it, ten-fold. The things the devs for Beast have been accused of has baffled me(and others).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-08-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:18:11-07:00","id":545559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545552#post545552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have a problem with complaints. I never said I did. I have a problem with people LOOKING for things, that are not there, to complain about. Some people actively try to find things that bother them, and then present those things in such a toxic way, that it does NOTHING to help the developers, or the fans of the product.<br /> <br /> I was also focused mostly on what I've seen on other message boards, not this one. Critiquing is fine. Trying to find some socio-political agendas(where there are none) and using it to attack the developers or the book? Yeah, that's not cool.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say the modern presumption is that all critique is mean-spirited and negative. Not at all. But it CAN be(see Exalted, Beast, etc.).<br /> <br /> I will, however, say that in this hobby, there is a growing number of people who's sole goal is to attack and destroy material for no logical reason. To find things that simply do not exist, and then attack it, ten-fold. The things the devs for Beast have been accused of has baffled me(and others). So I'm not sure if I'm outgrowing this hobby, or if perhaps the people who play it are changing too fast for me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've waded through a great chunk of the stuff on RPG.net and I have to disagree about people looking for things to complain about. While their have been some strange interpretations, there have also been many that are valid for what was written, if not what was intended. A game of horror is supposed to provoke visceral emotions, and clearly Beast has for some many people who both like it and dislike it. Understanding if and where it crosses the line for some people is important, not just for this game, but for Onyx Path in general. Even though I don't agree with them on all of their points, I've had different life experiences than them, so I have no intention of brushing those opinions off. There's always bad apples, yes, but I think that for the majority it's safe to assume that their commentary and concerns are both legitimate and expressed with the best of intentions.<br /> <br /> In less controversial news, we have a Dark Era! Wonder which on it is... (Go Zanzibar Sultinate!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-08-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:32:55-07:00","id":545579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545559#post545559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I've waded through a great chunk of the stuff on RPG.net and I have to disagree about people looking for things to complain about.</b> <b>While their have been some strange interpretations</b>,</div> </div> </div> </div>To each his/her own, then. I definitely saw some valid criticisms/concerns as well. But then I also saw some that were baffling to the point where I had to question if I was drunk or not when reading the same thing. It saddens me.<br /> <br /> Regardless, 80k and another stretch goal.<br /> <br /> Full steam ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:48:40-07:00","id":545590,"title":"","content":"So with Dark Era's reached, do you guys think we'll get a say in which era they go with? I wasn't involved with the Dark Era kickstarter but they voted on some of them then, didn't they? Also, who wants to bet we'll get some good old fashion Cold War McCarthism? I sure hope we do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:02:42-07:00","id":545602,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Crusades as the Dark Era","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:09:41-07:00","id":545605,"title":"","content":"Any Aslong as i get too see a Side-bar on Post/Pre/War London (WW2) Although that's just cause I think that works... Cold War Works too though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:17:29-07:00","id":545615,"title":"","content":"I just want it because I'm a filthy hipster at heart and I really love the history and politics of the world (especially America, as biased as that is). I'd give a limb to be able to play in McCarthy era DC or Hollywood.Or even better, just paranoid small town America. Though, WW2 would also be amazing, though I get the feeling it would bring up some issues people wouldn't feel comfortable addressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:18:45-07:00","id":545617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545602#post545602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Crusades as the Dark Era</div> </div> </div> </div>I could dig that, particularly as a Beast vs Beast focused setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:35:09-07:00","id":545644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545104#post545104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complaints are valid even if you do not like or agree with them. Likewise, your complaints are valid even if other people do not like and agree with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complaints are only valid if they contain valid criticism.<br /> <br /> complaints of &quot;All heroes/beasts a X/Y&quot; contain &quot;invalid&quot; criticisms because the books contain plenty of examples of heroes who are not X and Beass who are not Y, so to make the argument is to either complain about something you haven't read, ignore significant portions of the text you're complaining about, or just complaining just to complain.<br /> <br /> All three cases make the complaint invalid.<br /> <br /> I have yet to see a complaint that doen'st necessitate ignoring part of the book before it has a leg to stand on.<br /> <br /> Heroes are victims!-You stop being a victim when you become a serial killer.<br /> <br /> Heroes could have been abused to get that low-statistically unlikely, the abuser is called out as more likely to hero.<br /> <br /> Beasts are all unrepentant monsters who only hurt people-book calls out that Beasts still have a human conscience, a bunch of the example Beasts don't have to hurt people at all.<br /> <br /> Beasts are a metaphor for oppressed &quot;others&quot; but act like unrepentant monsters that only hurt people-Okay, one, show me in the book where Beasts are compared explicitly in text to ethnic minorities, the poor, or any :category&quot; in the LGBT* community, because I do not see once word that makes the explicit comparison. Two, see above with the bit about plenty of Example Beasts who don't hurt people and/or still demonstrate human conscience<br /> <br /> Heroes are metaphors for the Heteronormative Majority-No, they're metaphors for the sociopaths, psychopaths, abusers, jerks, bullies, deeply unstable individuals who are threats to themselves or others, and assholes that are present in every culture and subculture on earth to some degree. Except instead of being a metaphor that's quite explicitly what they are.<br /> <br /> Heroes have no free will-Except they're called out several times ans not even trying to fight the role they're given, some heroes are said to just stop after a while, and it's possible for heroes to be rehability. All three cases require the hero to be able to make a choice, thus necessitating the hero having free will.<br /> <br /> Did I miss any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-08-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:35:33-07:00","id":545646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545602#post545602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Crusades as the Dark Era</div> </div> </div> </div>Good place to introduce a Beast-focused Hunter Conspiracy, even if it's only a subsect, or precursor, of the Maleus Maleficarum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:26:10-07:00","id":545718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545644#post545644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Complaints are only valid if they contain valid criticism.<br /> <br /> complaints of &quot;All heroes/beasts a X/Y&quot; contain &quot;invalid&quot; criticisms because the books contain plenty of examples of heroes who are not X and Beass who are not Y, so to make the argument is to either complain about something you haven't read, ignore significant portions of the text you're complaining about, or just complaining just to complain.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You should really give people the benefit of the doubt more.<br /> <br /> This is fairly simple.<br /> <br /> Beast contradicts itself in tone, theme, and text more than once.<br /> <br /> As such, any argument made for or against beast by nature has to ignore part of the book. The book is impossible to reconcile as a whole.<br /> <br /> I don't like Beast. I know I'm biased against it. I'm trying to keep my discussions in this thread on the peripheral because of that. Stuff like vampire bites and the fact that we're all better off trying to understand one another instead of calling each other poopy heads and covering our ears. Not direct discussions on Beast. Before anyone calls me out, I said I'm trying. Sometimes I open my big mouth against my better judgement. This post may or may not be one of those times.<br /> <br /> But Beast contradicts itself. It does so often and gratuitously. I think this is the root of 99% of the conflicts over its contents. Everyone cherrypicks the text that supports their side, whether their side is defending or critiquing Beast.<br /> <br /> Neither critique nor compliment of Beast is &quot;valid&quot; by your definition. But I think they <i>are </i>valid. Why? Because such an intense divide and such utterly different interpretations of the same book and the discussion that evolves from that shows the developers where the text needs to be tightened. Where it is (I presume) unintentionally contradicting itself.<br /> <br /> If you need an example, look no further than the two threads spawned by the fact that the &quot;integrity 4&quot; stipulation for Heroes was added late in the development, and a lot of the text doesn't take that into account, fluff or crunch. The people arguing that Heroes are tragic figures are justified because of parts of the text. Their opinion is valid. The people who think Heroes are horrible people the Beasts are justified in defending themselves against are also justified. Their opinions are also valid. Both sets of opinions also contradict parts of the book.<br /> <br /> There is no One True Opinion, Rater202. The sooner people on both sides accept that, the happier everyone is going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:42:08-07:00","id":545733,"title":"","content":"Saying that the book contradicts itself over and over again doesn't make it true. I see no contradiction, I see &quot;Beasts and heroes are variable&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't ignore part of the book because &quot;contradiction&quot; because there is no contradiction. The book at no time makes a statement about &quot;all beasts&quot; or &quot;all heroes&quot; It merely gives examples bfo behavior while talking in <b>generalities</b> and giving exceptions to those generalities.<br /> <br /> There is no contradiction..<br /> <br /> And please don't accuse m of claiming that there's a &quot;one true opinion&quot; because I'm not.<br /> <br /> I'm just pointing out that complaints are unfounded, thus making <i>some</i> of the opinions I've seen invalid as they are based on poor understanding of the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-08-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:53:36-07:00","id":545741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545718#post545718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is fairly simple.<br /> <br /> Beast contradicts itself in tone, theme, and text more than once.<br /> <br /> As such, any argument made for or against beast by nature has to ignore part of the book. The book is impossible to reconcile as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you would like to actually provide examples of these supposed conridictions? Rather than say, &quot;Lool people are arguing about it!&quot; as evidence. Every supposed contridiction I have seen only exists when text is ignored, as opposed to the other way around. Which Rator has actually pointed out. Multiple times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:03:06-07:00","id":545756,"title":"","content":"Have to admit, I lose confidence in the validity of a position once &quot;you'd have a good point <i>on opposite day</i>&quot; has been an entirely valid criticism of it's proponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:03:56-07:00","id":545759,"title":"","content":"Well, there's the examples of Heroes-to-Be that make it very clear Heroes were created by direct, physical confrontations of Feasting Beasts starting on p278. I was told the fluff doesn't count.<br /> <br /> Or this one, 'Before their first contact with the Children, a Hero could be any given human walking down the street on any given day.' Which doesn't really fit considering the Integrity scale goes from 1 to 10.<br /> <br /> There's the idea that Heroes are both single-mindedly obsessed with killing Beasts, but also capable of enough memory of their former Life to get Willpower through acts resounding from it.<br /> <br /> Also the fact that Integrity is not morality, and Heroes are not justified in their hatred of Beasts, but one of the ways to lose Integrity is to become a victim of a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-08-2015, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:13:29-07:00","id":545770,"title":"","content":"Some of the Arguements are made without reading all the book ( I know I'm capable of Sprouting Bollocks without Reading it all) and most of the text supports itself from what I've seen. Again though I've not read the whole thing, i can see how Both sides can have issues with it as is. Like i said.. CONSTRUCTIVE Critism is always Useful, If you have doubts or don't understand thats fine, Say What and Why and suggest what you think it needs too help it. 99% Done isn't &quot;This is It as your Getting it&quot; It's &quot;This is Close too finished, Most of the Content is there, it just needs Finalising&quot; which does mean it can be altered too fix issues and Clarify things More.<br /> <br /> Give Examples and Reasons, Not just &quot;I don't like it&quot; Why don't you like it? What is it that puts you off? What can you Suggest that might help it?<br /> <br /> Personally i've said afew times.. it Needs a Secondary Antagonist too give something other then Heroes too Focus on. Heroes themselves seem too be the main Sticking point for people. &quot;Their all Victims&quot; &quot;They Are Flat Characters&quot; &quot;They Have no Agency&quot; All arguements I've seen for them, Are they Wrong? Yes AND No. They Are Flat Characters because thats how they survive, They CAN be Victims pushed too far and Decide that the Monster Must Die (In this case the Monster is a scapegoat for a Lifetime of Abuse and Might not Actually be at Fault) They DO have Agency... But that Agency is that of Reactionary... Heroes React, Villains Act. Villains are the thing the Hero Rises Against. In General though they are Bullies who see a Monster and Think &quot;Ahha! I must be the Chosen One! It must Die by my Hand!&quot; Is that a Generalisation? Yes.<br /> Does it Mean ALL Heroes Have too be that way? Hell No.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beasts have nothing to do other then Feed&quot; Neither Do Vampires if you get down too it, They play the Political Game... BECAUSE otherwise they'd have nothing too Distract them from the Long Nights and Blood. They Make something for Themselves. Strix HATE/LOATHE them because they are Monsters... they Shouldn't be Playing at Human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:17:10-07:00","id":545775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545770#post545770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Beasts have nothing to do other then Feed&quot; Neither Do Vampires if you get down too it, They play the Political Game... BECAUSE otherwise they'd have nothing too Distract them from the Long Nights and Blood. They Make something for Themselves. Strix HATE/LOATHE them because they are Monsters... they Shouldn't be Playing at Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they say that, they likely aren't talking about things to do in their life. They're probably talking about when you get the book, and look through it, vampire offers many options for things you can do, whether its politics, exploring the beliefs of your covenant, conspiring against other members of your court or other courts, find touchstones, and so forth. When you look at the Beast book, it really offers you Feasting, and dealing with Heroes. There are hints that you can do other things, such as explore the Astral Realms, but little in the way of how or why or, for a Storyteller, how to present those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:19:50-07:00","id":545778,"title":"","content":"I really am getting pissed off that people are saying this book endorses abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","user":"n_a_anyon","date":".  removed cross-forum reference 06-08-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:20:14-07:00","id":545780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545718#post545718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither critique nor compliment of Beast is &quot;valid&quot; by your definition. But I think they <i>are </i>valid. Why? Because such an intense divide and such utterly different interpretations of the same book and the discussion that evolves from that shows the developers where the text needs to be tightened. Where it is (I presume) unintentionally contradicting itself.<br /> <br /> If you need an example, look no further than the two threads spawned by the fact that the &quot;integrity 4&quot; stipulation for Heroes was added late in the development, and a lot of the text doesn't take that into account, fluff or crunch. The people arguing that Heroes are tragic figures are justified because of parts of the text. Their opinion is valid. The people who think Heroes are horrible people the Beasts are justified in defending themselves against are also justified. Their opinions are also valid. Both sets of opinions also contradict parts of the book.<br /> <br /> There is no One True Opinion, Rater202. The sooner people on both sides accept that, the happier everyone is going to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>One it would probably help your ability to debate if you actually read the source as opposed to just assuming &quot;people are arguing therefore its a flaw&quot; and are basing this on people's arguments in the forum then you are also likely to miss points where someone has forgotten a mid point somewhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> Two no the Hero thing you're arguing doesn't work because one person is arguing that they want heroes to be anti-beast Hunters and is literally disregarding evidence in the book that contradicts his claim that Heroes have no agency or choice and the other is just questioning whether or not a Hero needs to be a jerk. The integrity 4 thing is whether or not Hero's being able to cease being Heroes qualifies as more of a moral imperative on the part of Beasts to try and help someone suffering a dangerous potential side-effect of feeding, or witnessing a Beast feeding, or if the fact that the Hero drive compels the Hero to murder the Beast exonerates a Beast of responsibility for the Hero.<br /> <br /> Third the vampire bite thing was a bit of a problem from you're own writing. You had pointed out that you didn't like the comparison of a Beast feeding to a Vampire feeding and argued the two were basically apples and oranges. Which actually is a valid statement, belief, and perfectly understandable due to differences in how the two species function. The issue came when you then contradicted your statement and argued that Vampire feeding was less monstrous and harmful than Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:23:19-07:00","id":545785,"title":"","content":"It needs an appendix. Beasts can go <i>anywhere</i>. So we need at least a brief overview of what everywhere is like. They're explorers. Bottom of the ocean, depths of the astral, the shadow, the hedge, you name it. <br /> <br /> To provide a comprehensive list of every story opportunity beast presents would require another book twice the size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:24:07-07:00","id":545787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545778#post545778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yay I got banned from rpgnet for getting pissed off at people saying this book endorses abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casual reminder that cross-forum/website drama is thing to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:26:22-07:00","id":545788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545787#post545787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casual reminder that cross-forum/website drama is thing to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted, thanks. Just frustrated that people anywhere are so insistent on attacking this game for IMO ridiculous reasons. Not trying to start drama, just venting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I removed the reference from my original post, thanks for the advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","user":"n_a_anyon","date":". 06-08-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:28:53-07:00","id":545791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545775#post545775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When they say that, they likely aren't talking about things to do in their life. They're probably talking about when you get the book, and look through it, vampire offers many options for things you can do, whether its politics, exploring the beliefs of your covenant, conspiring against other members of your court or other courts, find touchstones, and so forth. When you look at the Beast book, it really offers you Feasting, and dealing with Heroes. There are hints that you can do other things, such as explore the Astral Realms, but little in the way of how or why or, for a Storyteller, how to present those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair Enough, so it needs abit more in that direction in any Stretch goals we might get after the next. Maybe something like a... Primordial Pathways book/chapter on Charting Notable Dreams/location etc.<br /> <br /> Really the Second Ed of Vampire has added alot too do. Even the First Ed had Stuff.. but it Felt lacking, Not in a &quot;Urrgh I Hate this&quot; Way, just a &quot;So.. I feed and Go to court? What else?&quot; way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-08-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:30:40-07:00","id":545794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545785#post545785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To provide a comprehensive list of every story opportunity beast presents would require another book twice the size.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one asked for one. The other books don't have them and manage to give you plenty to do. Usually in the Storyteller section, which in this case is sort of dominated by Inheritance, an end-game proposition, Heroes, and crossover. Or in the splat section, which in Beast's case tells you some great and inspiring ways to feed that are, in the end, only ways to feed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545788#post545788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noted, thanks. Just frustrated that people anywhere are so insistent on attacking this game for IMO ridiculous reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, this is a pretty mature board. It isn't 4chan. People aren't rabid hatemongers urging people to stop playing games. When they propose criticisms, it's not an attack on a game. It's explaining that they see something wrong with the book in the hopes that it gets clarified or fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:34:11-07:00","id":545800,"title":"","content":"But sometimes that attack is unjustified due to being based on an opinion that is in turn based on a lack of proper understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:39:29-07:00","id":545804,"title":"","content":"All that being said, more than a passing reference to how versatile this splat is at traveling, and some more detail on how Family Dinner interacts with other splats, would be useful, if not in the Core book, then in a player's/Storyteller's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:41:47-07:00","id":545807,"title":"","content":"I wasn't talking about anyone on this board, nofather. Suffice it to say, elsewhere people are IMO unfairly making statements about whether things like abuse are are implied to be justified by this text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:42:52-07:00","id":545809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545794#post545794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, this is a pretty mature board. It isn't 4chan. People aren't rabid hatemongers urging people to stop playing games. When they propose criticisms, it's not an attack on a game. It's explaining that they see something wrong with the book in the hopes that it gets clarified or fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about the OP forums and not rpg.net forums, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:45:00-07:00","id":545813,"title":"","content":"I would like to ask if we could please cut down on some of the dismissiveness of other peoples' viewpoints and, in particular, maybe roll back the reluctance to consider that their reading of the text might not be down to malice or mental delusion. I am not a mod or anything, of course, so feel free to ignore me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:48:28-07:00","id":545815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545813#post545813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to ask if we could please cut down on some of the dismissiveness of other peoples' viewpoints and, in particular, maybe roll back the reluctance to consider that their reading of the text might not be down to malice or mental delusion. I am not a mod or anything, of course, so feel free to ignore me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chris, were you one of the writers for Beast, and if so, what sections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:49:55-07:00","id":545816,"title":"","content":"Well, I haven't begun phase two quite yet. I can drop some perspective.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting that I have had two times where I had to sit long and hard with the game and figure out if it was justifiable. The first was upon initially reading Hunger, and my conclusion was that, for me, manipulating and side stepping the Hunger was a big part of the game-finding a balance between accepting the Hunger and not being ruled by it.<br /> <br /> The second was actually Shadowflame and one his arguments. There was a point when I suddenly thought I didn't have a leg to stand on, around the but* on paragraph 4 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=542645#post542645\">here</a>. I just hit that word and I didn't quite know where to go. And that's with having a lot of the book a lot of time before y'all got it. Truth be told, I still think my defense was a little weak around that point, but I also think it's valid given some of the way Mage works(I don't <i>exactly</i> know if the principles I applied from Mage can directly apply to the Astral, but commonalities and such).<br /> <br /> My point is that I can really strongly see what people are getting at. It's a dangerous balance Beast goes for, and I'm willing to concede it doesn't toe it perfectly. But I know the people involved were not going for that sort of thing, and in the end my critical reading doesn't end that way. But it's <i>tough</i> for Beast, particularly given the story form it's emulating(How many heroes do we have who only do something <i>after</i> something tragic occurs to them, <i>Spiderman/Batman/Oh, screw it, most of the American Superheroes, and an even larger portion of Western protagonists in general</i>).<br /> <br /> I suppose what I'm saying is that it's not ridiculous, but it's also not intended. Beast is supposed to read a different way, and it's tough to make it read that way. My biggest problem, at this moment, is really not that people have the argument, but that people aren't quite reading this in good faith, as it were. It's like they can't they see another side to it**, and that always annoys me (See my fury over &quot;DEMON IS ABOUT ROBOTS!&quot; arguments)<br /> <br /> *No, not the ogre's butt, but thanks for asking, Quest For Camelot.<br /> <br /> **I'm avoiding the suggestion that some people are deliberately not looking at it, because that's a dick move, but I would be foolish if I didn't mention the possibility as well, so here it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:51:45-07:00","id":545817,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or is the Heracles bit about his children clumsily written? Couldn't they have left it as &quot;The only thing to rival his kill count are the number of children he sired&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:56:10-07:00","id":545820,"title":"","content":"I'll stop. I'm very frustrated by this whole discussion, and think I've already said most everything useful I could say. To me, this is simply a dark game that doesn't force any morality, and it is up to the players to judge the actions of characters in the game. Playing as the embodiment of a primordial fear is a very interesting narrative device to me, and I wish those who are drawing IMO unjustified conclusions about the text would keep this foundational aspect of the game in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:59:01-07:00","id":545824,"title":"","content":"&quot;but that people aren't quite reading this in good faith&quot;<br /> <br /> Thank you, I felt the same about a lot of the discussion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:59:02-07:00","id":545825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545820#post545820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll stop. I'm very frustrated by this whole discussion, and think I've already said most everything useful I could say. To me, this is simply a dark game that doesn't force any morality, and it is up to the players to judge the actions of characters in the game. Playing as the embodiment of a primordial fear is a very interesting narrative device to me, and I wish those who are drawing IMO unjustified conclusions about the text would keep this foundational aspect of the game in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with ya man. It's a tough game, but it has such potential to be really rewarding too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:00:48-07:00","id":545827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545813#post545813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to ask if we could please cut down on some of the dismissiveness of other peoples' viewpoints and, in particular, maybe roll back the reluctance to consider that their reading of the text might not be down to malice or mental delusion. I am not a mod or anything, of course, so feel free to ignore me.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a viewpoint includes statements that are objectively false (such as, in this context, &quot;Beasts are all unrepentant monsters&quot; despite statements of having a human conscience, &quot;Beasts have to hurt people&quot; despite at least a dozen examples of beasts that don't hurt people when they feed,) then the viewpoint itself is erroneous.<br /> <br /> an erroneous viewpoint is one that can have two origins-deliberate misunderstanding or misrepresentation for the purpose of provoking argument, or insufficient understanding of the thing being believed.<br /> <br /> I choose to believe in the good of people, and thus assume that it's misunderstanding rather than malice.<br /> <br /> The objective facts of the game contradict most of the complaints about the game.<br /> <br /> when your complaints are not supported by genuine examples from the text, your complaints are invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:04:22-07:00","id":545833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545815#post545815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Chris, were you one of the writers for Beast, and if so, what sections?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, although some friends were writers on it. I feel confident that they are adults and capable of handling criticism in a level fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:06:51-07:00","id":545834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545817#post545817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or is the Heracles bit about his children clumsily written? Couldn't they have left it as &quot;The only thing to rival his kill count are the number of children he sired&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too hot on Heracles' stories and mythology... I'd agree with this statement if Heracles was never written to have any homosexual encounters. If he <i>was</i> bisexual in his mythos, I do kind of wonder why it needs bringing up in such a way as it was written, as the discussion is more on him being a Hero and the clarification isn't <i>really</i> needed for a throwaway line.<br /> <br /> On brighter news, I've only just started reading the Heroes part where this is and I do love how Heroes with 12 kills get a title of Hercules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:07:42-07:00","id":545835,"title":"","content":"Well, all I know is that my players are excited about this game in a way they were not from years and if all goes the way it should we're going to run a playtest made of an handful of stories in a couple of weeks. Be it the one whose in-game morality is usually comparable to that of Superman or the one that has to be restrained from hitting those who look at him the wrong way (and all that exists in between within my little group), they can't wait to play the game and I kinda feel it all reduces to this, at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-08-2015, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:07:59-07:00","id":545837,"title":"","content":"So, has anyone considered the option of making a Beast with a pre-established legacy? I think a reincarnated Beast sounds like a really fun idea, a game based around a Brood that is literally Loki's Brood sounds really fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:11:31-07:00","id":545845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545827#post545827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a viewpoint includes statements that are objectively false (such as, in this context, &quot;Beasts are all unrepentant monsters&quot; despite statements of having a human conscience, &quot;Beasts have to hurt people&quot; despite at least a dozen examples of beasts that don't hurt people when they feed,) then the viewpoint itself is erroneous.<br /> <br /> an erroneous viewpoint is one that can have two origins-deliberate misunderstanding or misrepresentation for the purpose of provoking argument, or insufficient understanding of the thing being believed.<br /> <br /> I choose to believe in the good of people, and thus assume that it's misunderstanding rather than malice.<br /> <br /> The objective facts of the game contradict most of the complaints about the game.<br /> <br /> when your complaints are not supported by genuine examples from the text, your complaints are invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would posit that since such a sufficiently large number of people, most of whom are WW fans and are familiar with at least some of the authors and developer, share these purported &quot;misunderstandings or misrepresentations&quot; that the text of Beast might be at fault, and not the intelligence or good faith of the readers. The authors might have honestly intended to convey certain messages or ideas, and simply not succeeded with a portion of the audience. In fact, open development and release of drafts is primarily intended to remedy these types of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:14:09-07:00","id":545847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545845#post545845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would posit that since such a sufficiently large number of people, most of whom are WW fans and are familiar with at least some of the authors and developer, share these purported &quot;misunderstandings or misrepresentations&quot; that the text of Beast might be at fault, and not the intelligence or good faith of the readers. The authors might have honestly intended to convey certain messages or ideas, and simply not succeeded with a portion of the audience. In fact, open development and release of drafts is primarily intended to remedy these types of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, there's that tight balance again.<br /> <br /> But also to be fair, a lot of people arguing about it don't seem like regulars to me. Maybe I'm out of touch with the hip, young crowd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:20:47-07:00","id":545855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545834#post545834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not too hot on Heracles' stories and mythology... I'd agree with this statement if Heracles was never written to have any homosexual encounters. If he <i>was</i> bisexual in his mythos, I do kind of wonder why it needs bringing up in such a way as it was written, as the discussion is more on him being a Hero and the clarification isn't <i>really</i> needed for a throwaway line.<br /> <br /> On brighter news, I've only just started reading the Heroes part where this is and I do love how Heroes with 12 kills get a title of Hercules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heracles was an ancient Greek. Being bisexual is the default and his males lovers are mentioned in legend. Iolaus for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:24:58-07:00","id":545872,"title":"","content":"L<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545847#post545847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair, there's that tight balance again.<br /> <br /> But also to be fair, a lot of people arguing about it don't seem like regulars to me. Maybe I'm out of touch with the hip, young crowd?</div> </div> </div> </div>i am trying to think of a good joke involving the old crowd and replacement hips but my extremely spotty internet connection is enraging me too much to come up with a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:27:18-07:00","id":545874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545872#post545872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">L<br /> <br /> i am trying to think of a good joke involving the old crowd and replacement hips but my extremely spotty internet connection is enraging me too much to come up with a good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit of the joke is received, if not the corpse. Er, form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:28:01-07:00","id":545875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545845#post545845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would posit that since such a sufficiently large number of people, most of whom are WW fans and are familiar with at least some of the authors and developer, share these purported &quot;misunderstandings or misrepresentations&quot; that the text of Beast might be at fault, and not the intelligence or good faith of the readers. The authors might have honestly intended to convey certain messages or ideas, and simply not succeeded with a portion of the audience. In fact, open development and release of drafts is primarily intended to remedy these types of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would counter-posit that the text is quite explicit in cases of confusion, and thus would argue that at best a lot of these arguments are coming from insufficient attention being paid when the relevant passages are read.<br /> <br /> One of the first things the book says about Beasts is that they know they're monsters, feel bad about it sometimes, and that many of them try to mitigate the harm they cause due to still having a human conscience.<br /> <br /> That invalidates the &quot;Beasts are all unrepentant monsters&quot; statement, so arguments built on that statement are invalid.<br /> <br /> I'll be posting in a bit about the &quot;beasts have to harm people&quot; statement and the passages from the book that render it false, as soon as I can skim through the book to get exact quotes, because I'm getting tired of having to argue points I've already made over and over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-08-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:36:57-07:00","id":545885,"title":"","content":"L<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545875#post545875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would counter-posit that the text is quite explicit in cases of confusion, and thus would argue that at best a lot of these arguments are coming from insufficient attention being paid when the relevant passages are read.<br /> <br /> One of the first things the book says about Beasts is that they know they're monsters, feel bad about it sometimes, and that many of them try to mitigate the harm they cause due to still having a human conscience.<br /> <br /> That invalidates the &amp;quot;Beasts are all unrepentant monsters&amp;quot; statement, so arguments built on that statement are invalid.<br /> <br /> I'll be posting in a bit about the &amp;quot;beasts have to harm people&amp;quot; statement and the passages from the book that render it false, as soon as I can skim through the book to get exact quotes, because I'm getting tired of having to argue points I've already made over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boiling down criticisms into single sentence sound bites so that you can knock them down is building straw men and precisely the opposite of constructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:37:39-07:00","id":545888,"title":"","content":"&quot;My dragon is Batman, your argument is invalid.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:50:19-07:00","id":545905,"title":"","content":"I mentioned this in another forum concerning one of my criticisms of Beast.<br /> <br /> I believe the crossover-heavy nature of Beast, with included mechanics of varying quality, was intended to replace the importance of social and political factions which characterize every other major and beloved nWOD game line. Beasts were supposed to piggy-back and insinuate themselves within Covenants, Consilia, Freeholds, Protectorates, etc. <br /> <br /> It was a bold design decision that sadly may have failed to achieve its purpose. The lack of these species-specific groups feels like a void in the Beast setting, creates ambiguity in Beasts' motivations and overall goals, and creates other problems such as the hyper-focus on Heroes (which has been discussed here in detail). It also may unfairly presume a substantial knowledge about the other nWOD splats and an actual desire by most player groups and ST's for crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:56:01-07:00","id":545913,"title":"","content":"Tyrants<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jo doesn\u2019t tower over her prey \u2014 she\u2019s short, but she\u2019s all muscle. She enjoys letting other<br /> people challenge her, especially men. The challenge isn\u2019t always or even usually physical.<br /> Sometimes they try to test her knowledge on topics they think she shouldn\u2019t understand, or try to<br /> explain things to her that it\u2019s obvious she knows. She destroys them; she knows what they know<br /> and she pokes holes in their beliefs and their facts, showing them sides of the topic they never<br /> considered. Secretly, though, she relishes the rare times when a man gets so mad he tries to touch<br /> her, because then she can beat him in a way that leaves no room for argument. </div> </div> </div>Usually done'st harm those she feeds from, unless they try to harm her first.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reynold is a health inspector for the city. When his Soul hungers, he dons rubber gloves and<br /> tests everything. He quizzes employees, he looks for the slightest bit of mold or dirt, and he<br /> happily provides miles of appeals forms to the owner. He refuses bribes and dutifully reports any<br /> attempt. He isn\u2019t after money, after all. He\u2019s after the frustration and defeat in their eyes </div> </div> </div>Does not inflict harm to people who do not deserve. Hurts no one. Indirectly protects people.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dave worked his way up. He started out delivering packages, but then he got promoted to<br /> supervisor, went to school, got his MBA, and now he\u2019s got a corner office. But he\u2019s got his<br /> sights set higher \u2014 he wants top floor. He wants to look down at the whole city. He\u2019s patient,<br /> though. He figures there are about six more positions between his and the big boss, and he wants<br /> to have them all. It\u2019s not having the top floor that will make him happy. It\u2019s taking it. </div> </div> </div> Feeds by earning promotions the hard way.Hurts no one.<br /> <br /> Collectors<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rose collects teeth. She\u2019ll take them from a victim\u2019s skull, if she needs to, but that\u2019s messy and<br /> difficult. She\u2019d rather take them from people \u2014 a lot of parents keep their children\u2019s baby teeth,<br /> at least for a while. She\u2019s taken them from the dead, too, and sometimes she breaks into dentists\u2019<br /> offices. The shape of human teeth fascinates her. Hers, after all, feel so sharp. She wonders if a<br /> vampire\u2019s teeth might feel more like hers, but she likes most of the vampires she\u2019s met too much<br /> to rip their fangs out. </div> </div> </div> Neither requires harming others, no is it her preference to harm others<br /> <br /> Predators<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brianna came to her Homecoming early. Now in middle school, she spends summers with her<br /> brood, traveling the coastlines. She visits beaches, swims out too far, and waits for some poor<br /> soul to come and try to save her. Some Predators feel on flesh and blood. Brianna feeds on<br /> altruism. She doesn\u2019t drown her would-be saviors, of course, she just dives deep and swims<br /> away, letting them either keep looking or swim back to land thinking that she drowned. </div> </div> </div> That's a mean prank, but it's not hurting anybody.<br /> <br /> Nemesis<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jess\u2019 brood doesn\u2019t know much about zir. They don\u2019t know zir\u2019s real name or zir assigned<br /> gender, and Jess isn\u2019t interested in sharing. Jess also doesn\u2019t participate in group hunts \u2014 it\u2019s not<br /> personal, Jess just takes hunting seriously and prefers to do it alone. Ze finds the people who<br /> have committed crimes that went unreported \u2014 date rape, domestic violence, child abuse, the<br /> really unpleasant stuff. Those are the people Jess punishes, and ze doesn\u2019t linger over the act. </div> </div> </div> Feeds by hurting people who deserve to be hurt.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Angela went to law school to represent the people who wouldn\u2019t otherwise have representation.<br /> She represents the victims of bullies, the victims of the beautiful, the rich, the popular, the<br /> charming, the privileged. She doesn\u2019t always win, of course \u2014 she has a small practice and she\u2019s<br /> just as overworked as any other attorney. But she\u2019s got a superlative method of negotiation, and<br /> it involves putting the fear of God (or at least a billion little spiders) into opposing counsel. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good guy to me.<br /> <br /> Ravager<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grace watches with amusement as people take care of their cars with a tenderness they never<br /> show to people. Few things provide so much sustenance with so little work as damaging an<br /> expensive car. When Grace really feels the need to treat herself, she turns a car upside down, and<br /> watches as the owner goes crazy trying to figure out how it happened. </div> </div> </div> Rather mean spirited, but not harmful, and she on;y does it to jerks<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lester loves the sound of glass breaking. Human beings forget how flimsy windows are \u2014 they<br /> are enough to keep out the rain, yes, but not enough to keep out bricks, branches, or a determined<br /> intruder. Lester smashes the windows in the homes of the rich in the dead of night, and watches<br /> the security come running. Sometimes he writes his message on a wall or a mirror: YOU ARE<br /> NOT SAFE. </div> </div> </div>Scares the bejesus, but done'st hurt people.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Amon finds fungus fascinating. He knows that certain types of fungus turn insects into zombie<br /> slaves, and other types can drive people from their houses in fear of their health. The fungus that<br /> grows in his Lair and that festers in the eyes and mouth of his Soul could overtake and reclaim a<br /> city in days if he ever let it out. He wouldn\u2019t \u2014 he has friends who run as wolves, and they have<br /> to live here, too. He has a deal with them, though. If their enemies ever attempt to take territory,<br /> they\u2019ll establish a spiritual quarantine zone and Amon will let his fungus spread. </div> </div> </div>This ones a borderline case, depending on the Werewolves this guy is friends with.<br /> <br /> Plenty of examples of Beasts who don't have to hurt people, or at least don't have to hurt innocent people, and some of them even help people.<br /> <br /> Thus disproving the &quot;Beasts are monsters who must hurt people&quot; statement, rending any argument based upon it invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:00:06-07:00","id":545924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545885#post545885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">L<br /> <br /> Boiling down criticisms into single sentence sound bites so that you can knock them down is building straw men and precisely the opposite of constructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>what you call &quot;boiling down criticism into a single sentence&quot; I call &quot;picking out the thesis of that critism so that I can provide evidence to counter it&quot; which is the hallmark of debate.<br /> <br /> and that is nowhere near the same thing.<br /> <br /> Nobody is going to parse a paragraph sentence by sentence to provide complete evicdence tha tproves it wrong when countering the thesus proves the rest of the paragraph wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:15:44-07:00","id":545943,"title":"","content":"Is this a game of Endless Hunger or beating a dead horse? Because that's what this topic has turned into. I'm not saying that you guys don't have valid points, but it kind of feels like this argument is killing off any other conversation and it's really frustrating. There are other topics for talking about heroes and their design flaws (and the flaws of the game), can we please talk about something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:21:13-07:00","id":545954,"title":"","content":"We aren't talking about heroes anymore.<br /> <br /> We're specifically talking about Beasts and the fact that some people are saying that they are an entire splt of unrepentant monsters despite the text disagreeing with them.<br /> <br /> This is a topic that's been around for like, two or three pages, and another conversation has been going on at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:21:43-07:00","id":545955,"title":"","content":"Okay, wow, what is making everybody dive on this thread lately? I keep having to re-bookmark this topic several times a day because we rack up pages so fast!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:34:05-07:00","id":546001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545924#post545924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what you call &amp;quot;boiling down criticism into a single sentence&amp;quot; I call &amp;quot;picking out the thesis of that critism so that I can provide evidence to counter it&amp;quot; which is the hallmark of debate.<br /> <br /> and that is nowhere near the same thing.<br /> <br /> Nobody is going to parse a paragraph sentence by sentence to provide complete evicdence tha tproves it wrong when countering the thesus proves the rest of the paragraph wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Criticism or praise of Beast is not a zero sum game, and treating discussion as a thing you need to win is part of what is contributing to making Beast threads so unpleasant at the moment. Building straw men that you can easily knock down and then declare victory over doesn't help at all and, presuming you genuinely don't think you're doing that, I would suggest taking a step back for a bit and having a very thorough think over how you are coming across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:39:00-07:00","id":546011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545943#post545943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a game of Endless Hunger or beating a dead horse? Because that's what this topic has turned into. I'm not saying that you guys don't have valid points, but it kind of feels like this argument is killing off any other conversation and it's really frustrating. There are other topics for talking about heroes and their design flaws (and the flaws of the game), can we please talk about something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beating a dead horse is the forum-wide pass time of the White Wolf/Onyx Path forums.<br /> <br /> Though it might say something that most of the record holders aren't here due to banning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-08-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:41:43-07:00","id":546016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546001#post546001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Criticism or praise of Beast is not a zero sum game, and treating discussion as a thing you need to win is part of what is contributing to making Beast threads so unpleasant at the moment. Building straw men that you can easily knock down and then declare victory over doesn't help at all and, presuming you genuinely don't think you're doing that, I would suggest taking a step back for a bit and having a very thorough think over how you are coming across.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not treating discussion as a thing to win, and nor am I trying to win.<br /> <br /> I'm making factual statements.<br /> <br /> I'm pointing out that some common, but specific, criticisms of this product are invalid.<br /> <br /> Permitting invalid criticism to be treated as valid to risk them being taken seriously by the people in charge, and addressing invalid criticisms wastes time and page count and thus can only harm the product.<br /> <br /> If the criticisms were &quot;this thing can easily be misunderstood as this thing&quot;, then that would be a valid criticism. But that's not the statement being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:54:06-07:00","id":546063,"title":"","content":"Your approach and methods will not have the effect you desire, and are simply making these threads even less pleasant than they already were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:58:11-07:00","id":546097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546016#post546016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not treating discussion as a thing to win, and nor am I trying to win.<br /> <br /> I'm making factual statements.<br /> <br /> I'm pointing out that some common, but specific, criticisms of this product are invalid.<br /> <br /> Permitting invalid criticism to be treated as valid to risk them being taken seriously by the people in charge, and addressing invalid criticisms wastes time and page count and thus can only harm the product.<br /> <br /> If the criticisms were &quot;this thing can easily be misunderstood as this thing&quot;, then that would be a valid criticism. But that's not the statement being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to say how much I appreciated this point. Well put, to the point and something important to point out imho. I think the discussion hasn't been TOO bad. The similar rpg.net discussion has had numerous red text because of &quot;If you don't interpret the text the way I do.&quot; issues and that hasn't really happened here thankfully. I'd say there are a few things on the nature of Beast society( if there is such a cohesive enough thing) and Heroes that could use clarification but I don't think they were planning on editing the text. Has the line developer stopped in at all here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:41:31-07:00","id":546158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545905#post545905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned this in another forum concerning one of my criticisms of Beast.<br /> <br /> I believe the crossover-heavy nature of Beast, with included mechanics of varying quality, was intended to replace the importance of social and political factions which characterize every other major and beloved nWOD game line. Beasts were supposed to piggy-back and insinuate themselves within Covenants, Consilia, Freeholds, Protectorates, etc.<br /> <br /> It was a bold design decision that sadly may have failed to achieve its purpose. The lack of these species-specific groups feels like a void in the Beast setting, creates ambiguity in Beasts' motivations and overall goals, and creates other problems such as the hyper-focus on Heroes (which has been discussed here in detail). It also may unfairly presume a substantial knowledge about the other nWOD splats and an actual desire by most player groups and ST's for crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot can be learned from other splats that don't treat the Y-axis (or in the cases of Demon, Promethean and, I think, Geist, the X-axis) of the template as another avenue of power. In most of these splats, interactions with other members of those axes is not exactly essential to character growth the way it is for other templates, so you don't end up with the kinds of axial monoculture that other games (particularly Requiem, and Forsaken 1.0) either fall prey to or rely on in order to maintain the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Also, it's incumbent upon the Storyteller to challenge any notions of Setting Mastery that may arise and embrace the possibility of a crossover in whichever method they see fit. Preconceptions are fine, so long as you are willing to let them be challenged, and a Beast holding a position of power within an established Supernatural power structure should always be the start of a story or Chronicle, not the end. Look at the Vancouver section of the Beasts in the World chapter. The stranglehold that the Leviathans have over the region is an opportunity to subvert core assumptions about how Supernaturals interact with each other, and gives the troupe something to deal with besides the standard threats posed by mortals and non-Begotten adversaries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:29:37-07:00","id":546265,"title":"","content":"Question this is something that may have been mentioned in a different thread or it may have just been something someone said that caused me to think this. I know Hunters are capable of becoming Heroes, but are the other splats capable of it? Just wondering since while I can always make exceptions in my own games it would be nice to know if setting default allows for accidental spawning of a Werewolf Hero, or if its only a risk of really cheesing one off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:30:09-07:00","id":546266,"title":"","content":"So. Another bit of delayed comprehension-slash-is-this-intentional occurred to me today:<br /> <br /> Given statements about how the more Chambers a Lair has the farther the hungry Soul ranges, can it be assumed that the [Lair] mile radius for the Inflicting Nightmares roll applies to both the Beast's location and the basis of any Chambers she has?<br /> <br /> (I really feel like the whole spread of systems for the Lair needs to be reorganized on a macro level, not least because the two sets of penalties for opening Primordial Pathways are five pages apart.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:43:07-07:00","id":546275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546266#post546266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Another bit of delayed comprehension-slash-is-this-intentional occurred to me today:<br /> <br /> Given statements about how the more Chambers a Lair has the farther the hungry Soul ranges, can it be assumed that the [Lair] mile radius for the Inflicting Nightmares roll applies to both the Beast's location and the basis of any Chambers she has?<br /> <br /> (I really feel like the whole spread of systems for the Lair needs to be reorganized on a macro level, not least because the two sets of penalties for opening Primordial Pathways are five pages apart.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I assume so but then most of the powers that beast have besides nightmares such as atavism and the birthrights requires to be touched or at least seen by someone to work that would make nightmares more important if it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:45:20-07:00","id":546278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546011#post546011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beating a dead horse is the forum-wide pass time of the White Wolf/Onyx Path forums.<br /> <br /> Though it might say something that most of the record holders aren't here due to banning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Beating a Dead Horse&quot; sounds like a great name for a Kinship Nightmare, possibly for Mummy or Geist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:49:58-07:00","id":546288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546265#post546265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question this is something that may have been mentioned in a different thread or it may have just been something someone said that caused me to think this. I know Hunters are capable of becoming Heroes, but are the other splats capable of it? Just wondering since while I can always make exceptions in my own games it would be nice to know if setting default allows for accidental spawning of a Werewolf Hero, or if its only a risk of really cheesing one off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. In fact, I'm pretty sure you need an Integrity rating and no Supernatural power to become a Hero, although you could argue for Stigmatics, Wolf-blooded, or Sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider