ode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546275#post546275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well I assume so but then most of the powers that beast have besides nightmares such as atavism and the birthrights requires to be touched or at least seen by someone to work that would make nightmares more important if it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the Lair + Power - Composure roll on page 120, not the Invoking Nightmares systems summary on page 175.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T20:11:24-07:00","id":546380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546302#post546302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would actually be an interesting story especially if anathema could have effects on other supernaturals suddenly a vampire gets damaged by garlic. Heck since beasts have there own version of golcanda why not make one for heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;I have become Mary Sue, destroyer of worlds!&quot;<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, it might be neat to include a sort of &quot;Apex Hero&quot; as a story threat in a future supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T20:17:27-07:00","id":546385,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to read 188 pages to see if what I'm going to say has already been said, so i'll sum it up.<br /> <br /> Firstly, all the authors of Beast are individuals that I've immensely enjoyed reading in the past.<br /> <br /> Beast will be the first OPP product I don't back and, in the future, won't allow at game sessions.<br /> <br /> I'll ignore the the victim-abuse/victim-blaming criticism, which I think is valid, but it doesn't bother me. I think art should explore the dark corners of human behavior, though I perfectly understand how people are disturbed by it. I don't think the authors condone victim blaming or anything like that, and I'm perfectly fine roleplaying an evil SOB that spreads hate and pain...but not when the system itself is not self-aware enough to call a spade a spade and say &quot;ya, you're evil&quot;. Gamers like to talk about 'ludonarrative dissonance', mostly in attempt to sound like they understand literary theory, but I think in this case, it's the best description I can find in terms of the contradictory messages of the author, the Beast's actions, and the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I don't think the late addition of Integrity makes the book's tone about Heroes justified either, as both a Beasts' actions can lower this, AND Integrity can be low by things such as PTSD and abuse. It says a lot when people sympathize and would rather play the Heroes than the Begotten.<br /> <br /> I don't like how Beasts fit into the rest of the world, and basically says &quot;all your vampire, werewolf, etc..that rich history of separate philosophies, creation myths, and politics are really bullshit..you're all under the dark mother, except Demons&quot;. Oh, and all you guys get along great with Beasts.<br /> <br /> I really really don't like how they fit in with Changelings, since a Changeling would take one look at a Beast's action and say &quot;no way, i've see this shit before&quot; and run or rip the Begotten apart. I won't even get into some of the other specifics, like a Begotten's ability to shape the Hedge and their willingness to participate in the Hunt.<br /> <br /> Beasts seem like they have all the advantage of every other system, with none of the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> I usually really enjoy the fiction in the books...but the fiction in Beast is...bad.<br /> <br /> Torturing a guy to death for not tipping a waitress? <br /> Being an assistant Principle that likes to torture little kids that joke around in class?<br /> Poisoning a little boy for stealing candy, then suffocating him with a plastic bag, then turning his house into a torture den? Seriously...he's trick or treating...he's probably like 11 or 12.<br /> <br /> I think even some of the old school evils like the baali would even be like &quot;uh, chill dude&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T20:42:49-07:00","id":546403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546385#post546385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torturing a guy to death for not tipping a waitress?<br /> Being an assistant Principle that likes to torture little kids that joke around in class?<br /> Poisoning a little boy for stealing candy, then suffocating him with a plastic bag, then turning his house into a torture den? Seriously...he's trick or treating...he's probably like 11 or 12.<br /> <br /> I think even some of the old school evils like the baali would even be like &quot;uh, chill dude&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: one example of a particularly brutal nemesis<br /> 2: Ni implications that she's torturing the children, merely disciplining them<br /> 3: Page please.<br /> <br /> Everything else has already been addressed this and other threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T20:56:10-07:00","id":546433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546385#post546385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really really don't like how they fit in with Changelings, since a Changeling would take one look at a Beast's action and say &quot;no way, i've see this shit before&quot; and run or rip the Begotten apart. I won't even get into some of the other specifics, like a Begotten's ability to shape the Hedge and their willingness to participate in the Hunt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with a lot of stuff you said, but especially this point.<br /> <br /> Changelings would, at a first glance, friggin cringe at what beasts do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T21:14:57-07:00","id":546448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546403#post546403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: one example of a particularly brutal nemesis<br /> 2: Ni implications that she's torturing the children, merely disciplining them<br /> 3: Page please.<br /> <br /> Everything else has already been addressed this and other threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darth is misreading or otherwise fibbing since the text does not say he is a little boy. It's explicitly an older person probably 17+ who is stealing kids candy .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T21:29:42-07:00","id":546457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546300#post546300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a hard attitude to understand, especially considering the number of people who have read it (myself included) <b>and found that reading the material has been viscerally unpleasant and made unfortunate implications, regardless of how deliberate the authoring of the implications was.</b><br /> <br /> I've seen enough of the various OPP Authors' work and community interaction to know that they're definitively not doing that in any fashion, but divorced from interaction with the author of the text, it is not difficult to ascribe the motivations of the writers with what they observe in the text. Remember, we're on the OPP forums - we get to regularly interact with the writers and we get the advantage of having the extra explanations that mean that we often get to see <i>what they meant</i> instead of <i>what they wrote</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which parts of the text gave led you to these conclusions? Serious question as I'd like to see what you found unpleasant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:02:01-07:00","id":546555,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing none of the detractors really get addiction, or impulsive behavior. Perhaps they should do some outside media consumption, say, The Number 23, or any of the Hannibal Lechter movies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:06:29-07:00","id":546562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546403#post546403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: one example of a particularly brutal nemesis<br /> 2: Ni implications that she's torturing the children, merely disciplining them<br /> 3: Page please.<br /> <br /> Everything else has already been addressed this and other threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>p.136<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'm preaching to the converted of a different religion, but I'm just laying this out here for anyone that is at OPP and wants a fan's suggestions:<br /> <br /> I'm the morality question they can be explained away in a number of ways, that's not my main point (I'm fine playing completely evil characters).<br /> <br /> - a conflicting description of Beasts from the author's point of view, their mechanics, and their actions...at least the ones given in the text. The question of good/evil is hard to define precisely because parts of the book don't even agree. <br /> <br /> - a complete lack of awareness of any sort of internal conflict in the character to make them interesting. They feed, they exist, they're happy, they're boring. There is no wrestling with Paradox or the beast (vampire) or the shadow (wraith)...just no inner drama anywhere, the Begotten are totally okay with what they are. That's it. They just feast and fend off Heroes. They're just monsters who do scary-monster stuff, but lack the existential dread VtM or the grungy/punk rage of werewolves, and the result is a very powerful but also very bland sort of creature who lacks motivation to do anything besides eat and stay alive<br /> <br /> - a complete lack of consideration of other game system's core themes, what their logical reactions to Beasts would be, and why they would even want to associate with them (Changeling is the most egregious, probably second is Promethian but werewolf, mage and vampire all have their problems).<br /> <br /> - Heroes are a completely uninteresting antagonist, I just don't find forced villains compelling, especially not with this archetype. Furthermore, the Begotten are completely overpowered, even giving Mage a run for their money. Their natural enemy, Heroes, are pretty much wimps in comparison.<br /> <br /> I had really high hopes for this game, but as it stands, I'm not seeing grand and terrible beasts of legend, a creature born from the fire of cruel circumstance, working through a crisis of personal and outward difficult conflict. I'm seeing an endless parade of cruel, petty, spiteful people, whose miserable compulsions drive them to make the world around them a sadder, uglier place. To me, it felt like a set of rules for the banality of evil.<br /> <br /> I may be 'reading it wrong' or 'not getting it', but I've read every WW/OPP book, and grasped the themes and core concepts of each one with little difficulty. If I, and many others, interpret the system a particular way that's not intended, then the core concept either needs to be re-worked because it fails in its purpose, or re-worded to make the point clearer.<br /> <br /> And with that, I&quot;m bowing out here. Thanks for listening and I truly hope beast is changed for the better. I won't fund it, but I'll definitely pick it up from driveThru if it improves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:24:32-07:00","id":546574,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain how the Guilty Pleasure and Fist of Nightmare Merits work, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:36:36-07:00","id":546587,"title":"","content":"Umm Darth the book says that while Beasts do somewhat relate to Changelings the part of them they really relate to is the Gentry and it flat out says that this terrifies Changelings. <br /> <br /> Plus the whole thing of retreat or merger is dealing with the fact that Beasts are not just at peace with themselves or lack conflict involved with their inner monster. I grant though it is less than other splats by a significant amount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:50:12-07:00","id":546599,"title":"","content":"@darthcoffee<br /> [QUOTE][Mrs. Winters, Magda\u2019s character (detailed starting on p. XX), is running a little low \u2014 she\u2019s<br /> only got two dots of Satiety and she\u2019d rather not risk becoming Ravenous. She Hungers for<br /> Punishment, and her particular favorite flavor is punishing those who harm the children in her<br /> neighborhood. As it happens, Halloween was last week, and she noted a young man named Brent<br /> snatching bags of candy from some of the youngsters.<br /> Magda decides Mrs. Winters doesn\u2019t need to be subtle or elaborate about her punishment, not<br /> this time. She breaks into Brent\u2019s house while he\u2019s away and notes that he\u2019s got a bunch of<br /> candy on his coffee table. She grabs a few soft candies and injects them with a mild poison \u2014<br /> nothing fatal, but enough to make the bully very ill. She lurks upstairs for a while, and waits until<br /> she hears him start to retch. She then creeps up behind him with a thick plastic bag (one of the<br /> bags of candy he stole from a child) and holds it over his face until he nearly blacks out. As he<br /> lies there panting, she whispers, \u201cNow, you behave. We see what you do on All Hallow\u2019s Eve,<br /> and we remember.\u201d/QUOTE] It refers to him as a &quot;young man,&quot; which in general refers to 18-25. He's also described as owning a house.<br /> <br /> This isn't a little kid taking candy from his fellow trick-or-treaters. This is a grown ass man stealing candy from little kids. The poison is explicitly only something that will make him sick, and since he's later described as a potential hero, he's already at Integ 4 or below. Yeah, choking him out is kinda disproportionate retribution, but Mrs. Winters seems to be a dark grey character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a conflicting description of Beasts from the author's point of view, their mechanics, and their actions...at least the ones given in the text. The question of good/evil is hard to define precisely because parts of the book don't even agree. </div> </div> </div>I don't really see what you're getting at here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a complete lack of awareness of any sort of internal conflict in the character to make them interesting. They feed, they exist, they're happy, they're boring. There is no wrestling with Paradox or the beast (vampire) or the shadow (wraith)...just no inner drama anywhere, the Begotten are totally okay with what they are. That's it. They just feast and fend off Heroes. They're just monsters who do scary-monster stuff, but lack the existential dread VtM or the grungy/punk rage of werewolves, and the result is a very powerful but also very bland sort of creature who lacks motivation to do anything besides eat and stay alive </div> </div> </div>Just because there are no mechanics for the inner struggle doen'st mean an inner struggle is not present. There are several places where it's mentioned that Beasts sometimes struggle to reconcile their knowledge that they're monsters with their human conscience and finding ways to manage their Hunger without hurting their loved ones.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a complete lack of consideration of other game system's core themes, what their logical reactions to Beasts would be, and why they would even want to associate with them (Changeling is the most egregious, probably second is Promethean but werewolf, mage and vampire all have their problems </div> </div> </div>Thank you, a criticism that makes sense. What would you think that the other supernaturals reactions would be<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Heroes are a completely uninteresting antagonist, I just don't find forced villains compelling, especially not with this archetype. Furthermore, the Begotten are completely overpowered, even giving Mage a run for their money. Their natural enemy, Heroes, are pretty much wimps in comparison. </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you mean about &quot;forced villains?&quot; As for the power dependency between the Beasts, that's very much intentional-as I said in the &quot;Anemic Heroes&quot; thread, the original intention with heroes, regardless of mine, yours, or anybody else thoughts on the presentation, was &quot;arrogant asshole&quot; and being weaker than the heroes feeds into that-they think they're great and legendary heroes, but in actuality they're way over their heads. a Green Hero is going to need luck, skill, or just plain cheating to kill his first Beast. Furthermore, Beast has three &quot;end game&quot; scenarios in the book, and the most viable option requires utterly dominating a hero and turning them from threat to nuisance. For that to be possible, the Heroes template has to be something that is possible to turn from a threat to a nuisance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm seeing an endless parade of cruel, petty, spiteful people, whose miserable compulsions drive them to make the world around them a sadder, uglier place. To me, it felt like a set of rules for the banality of evil. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545913#post545913\">I would politly direct you to a post of mine from a few pages back</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:02:51-07:00","id":546610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546574#post546574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain how the Guilty Pleasure and Fist of Nightmare Merits work, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty Pleasure allows you to gain extra Satiety by doing something compromising while attempting to feed.<br /> <br /> Fist of Nightmare lets you deliver a targeted nightmare with a touch that you've invoked in advance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:16:51-07:00","id":546614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546599#post546599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@darthcoffee<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Mrs. Winters, Magda\u2019s character (detailed starting on p. XX), is running a little low \u2014 she\u2019s<br /> only got two dots of Satiety and she\u2019d rather not risk becoming Ravenous. She Hungers for<br /> Punishment, and her particular favorite flavor is punishing those who harm the children in her<br /> neighborhood. As it happens, Halloween was last week, and she noted a young man named Brent<br /> snatching bags of candy from some of the youngsters.<br /> Magda decides Mrs. Winters doesn\u2019t need to be subtle or elaborate about her punishment, not<br /> this time. She breaks into Brent\u2019s house while he\u2019s away and notes that he\u2019s got a bunch of<br /> candy on his coffee table. She grabs a few soft candies and injects them with a mild poison \u2014<br /> nothing fatal, but enough to make the bully very ill. She lurks upstairs for a while, and waits until<br /> she hears him start to retch. She then creeps up behind him with a thick plastic bag (one of the<br /> bags of candy he stole from a child) and holds it over his face until he nearly blacks out. As he<br /> lies there panting, she whispers, \u201cNow, you behave. We see what you do on All Hallow\u2019s Eve,<br /> and we remember.\u201d </div> </div> </div>It refers to him as a &quot;young man,&quot; which in general refers to 18-25. He's also described as owning a house.<br /> <br /> This isn't a little kid taking candy from his fellow trick-or-treaters. This is a grown ass man stealing candy from little kids. The poison is explicitly only something that will make him sick, and since he's later described as a potential hero, he's already at Integ 4 or below. Yeah, choking him out is kinda disproportionate retribution, but Mrs. Winters seems to be a dark grey character.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't really see what you're getting at here.<br /> <br /> <b>Just because there are no mechanics for the inner struggle doen'st mean an inner struggle is not present. There are several places where it's mentioned that Beasts sometimes struggle to reconcile their knowledge that they're monsters with their human conscience and finding ways to manage their Hunger without hurting their loved ones.</b><br /> <br /> Thank you, a criticism that makes sense. What would you think that the other supernaturals reactions would be<br /> <br /> What exactly do you mean about &quot;forced villains?&quot; As for the power dependency between the Beasts, that's very much intentional-as I said in the &quot;Anemic Heroes&quot; thread, the original intention with heroes, regardless of mine, yours, or anybody else thoughts on the presentation, was &quot;arrogant asshole&quot; and being weaker than the heroes feeds into that-they think they're great and legendary heroes, but in actuality they're way over their heads. a Green Hero is going to need luck, skill, or just plain cheating to kill his first Beast. Furthermore, Beast has three &quot;end game&quot; scenarios in the book, and the most viable option requires utterly dominating a hero and turning them from threat to nuisance. For that to be possible, the Heroes template has to be something that is possible to turn from a threat to a nuisance.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=545913#post545913\">I would politly direct you to a post of mine from a few pages back</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ in regards to the position being responded to by the bold text: there very much is an internal struggle at play within the Satiety system; one of self-control. As I've been pointing out, to my mind, this is a game about addiction and impulse, and managing those addictions and impulses is where the internal struggle presents itself. The consequences are more immediate and impactful than the madness and loss of traits that Darth is used to, but they're there, if you're willing to play them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:19:19-07:00","id":546616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546356#post546356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious, just what was &quot;viscerally unpleasant?&quot; I only ask because I thoroughly enjoyed the draft, layout aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found a lot of the real-world abuse and abusive tactics inflicted by many of the beasts in the fiction writing made my stomach churn. Far too many relate to things I've seen the effects of to ever want to even explore that in a <i>game</i> perspective. I don't really want to discuss it much further because it mirrors too many bad situations in the past (or present which I'm not realistically capable of changing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:23:07-07:00","id":546618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546614#post546614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I beg to differ in regards to the position being responded to by the bold text: there very much is an internal struggle at play within the Satiety system; one of self-control. As I've been pointing out, to my mind, this is a game about addiction and impulse, and managing those addictions and impulses is where the internal struggle presents itself. The consequences are more immediate and impactful than the madness and loss of traits that Darth is used to, but they're there, if you're willing to play them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how this difers from my point.<br /> <br /> &quot;just because there's no &quot;inner struggle&quot; mechanic comparable to Paradox of vampiric rage or werewolf rage, doen'st mean there isn't an inner struggle.&quot; what I tried to say, could have worded that better.<br /> <br /> And he's right, there is no inner struggle mechanic. Satiety, is a hunger mechanic. thats not an inner struggle that every beast is going to have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:27:50-07:00","id":546619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546616#post546616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I found a lot of the real-world abuse and abusive tactics inflicted by many of the beasts in the fiction writing made my stomach churn. Far too many relate to things I've seen the effects of to ever want to even explore that in a <i>game</i> perspective. I don't really want to discuss it much further because it mirrors too many bad situations in the past (or present which I'm not realistically capable of changing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I honestly avoided those parts, but I'll take your word on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:32:34-07:00","id":546625,"title":"","content":"I didn't really see anything in there any worse than what the other splats get up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T01:06:54-07:00","id":546646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546618#post546618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how this difers from my point.<br /> <br /> &quot;just because there's no &quot;inner struggle&quot; mechanic comparable to Paradox of vampiric rage or werewolf rage, doen'st mean there isn't an inner struggle.&quot; what I tried to say, could have worded that better.<br /> <br /> And he's right, there is no inner struggle mechanic. Satiety, is a hunger mechanic. thats not an inner struggle that every beast is going to have</div> </div> </div> </div>More differing from his than from yours. And I'm not convinced that Satiety, and the consequences of not managing it properly, does not constitute an inner struggle mechanic. It may be a bit inverse of Integrity and the like, but the function is largely the same: guiding a player's decision making by providing consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T03:03:11-07:00","id":546695,"title":"","content":"Subversive. How appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T05:06:57-07:00","id":546751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546618#post546618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how this difers from my point.<br /> <br /> &quot;just because there's no &quot;inner struggle&quot; mechanic comparable to Paradox of vampiric rage or werewolf rage, doen'st mean there isn't an inner struggle.&quot; what I tried to say, could have worded that better.<br /> <br /> And he's right, there is no inner struggle mechanic. Satiety, is a hunger mechanic. thats not an inner struggle that every beast is going to have</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Darth is talking less about struggle mechanics and more about how they interact with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T06:21:32-07:00","id":546953,"title":"","content":"I would point out: has anyone here ever had to struggle with being hungry? Or to stay on a regimented diet? <br /> <br /> Starvation leads your brain to focus on good. While your cognitive function doesn't decline (otherwise, how would human, without tooth or claw, get food). But it does distract you from tasks that are not centered on food. They have shown starvation is akin to withdrawal, while food triggers similar pathways to recreational drugs (and some suspect obesity to be due to these pathways firing too much, creating literal addictions).<br /> <br /> And then you have diets, where you are willingly starving yourself and depriing yourself of things that give you pleasure. Therr is a reason most people fail their diet regimines, and it is because you are essentially pitting your individual discipline against millions of years of evolutionary instinct. To top it off, even the discipline can undermine you, as flawed thoughts: &quot;I can't eat this&quot; is more likely to lead you to cheat, as such a denial leads to part of your brain rebelling against the part telling it it can't do something (it is like when you tell a 6 year old he can't have a cookie... he will then want it even more).<br /> <br /> And the obvious inverse is over eating and poor consumption control, when you keep eating when full or to often. I mean, the obesity crisis is there in part because a lot of processed foods trigger the reward process <i>too well </i> (I still remember my button class in Medical School showing an FMRI of someone on coke and someone who was both overweight and eating some form of processed desert (name wasnt given)...the overlap was scary). Point being, not eating too much is only a bit easier than keeping yourself from eating, due to the same pathways triggering the reward part of the brain and thus making you <i>happy </i>that you are eating.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that it isn't something physical, but metaphysical. Your soul literally thirsts for something, and is starving. And <i>it feels good to sate it </i>, just like a cheeseburger would taste like nirvana after being in the desert for a week without food. It isn't something you can fully control, because if you don't feed it, it will hijack the dreams of others and feed itself. And feeding it to the point of it literally falling into a metaphysical &quot;food coma&quot; is nearly as dangerous as letting it starve. And the issue is, you have to let it be hungry unless you are willing to act in the dark manners to fulfill it, harming mankind (even if it is a non-persistent manner to only those who &quot;deserve it&quot;) in someway to instill the fear you need to feed. <br /> <br /> Beasts have an inner struggle, just like anyone on a diet. There diet simply is &quot;not instilling terror into humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, the MD in me slipped out a bit there. But trust me, when working with both morbidly obese 14 year Olds and anorexics, you learn how much the hunger/reward response can mess things up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-09-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T06:58:13-07:00","id":547011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldq