and eating some form of processed desert (name wasnt given)...the overlap was scary). Point being, not eating too much is only a bit easier than keeping yourself from eating, sue to the same pathways.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that it isn't something physical, but metaphysical. Your soul literally thirsts for something, and is starving. And <i>it feels good to sate it </i>, just like a cheeseburger would taste like nirvana after being in the desert for a week without food. It isn't something you can fully control, because if you don't feed it, it will hijack the dreams of others and feed itself. And feeding it to the point of it literally falling into a metaphysical &quot;food coma&quot; is nearly as dangerous as letting it starve. And the issue is, you have to let it be hungry unless you are willing to act in the dark manners to fulfill it, harming mankind (even if it is a non-persistent manner to only those who &quot;deserve it&quot;) in someway to instill the fear you need to feed.<br /> <br /> Beasts have an inner struggle, just like anyone on a diet. There diet simply is &quot;not instilling terror into humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, the MD in me slipped out a bit there. But trust me, when working with both morbidly obese 14 year Olds and anorexics, you learn how much the hunger/reward response can mess things up).</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that an explicit thing in Beast, or merely an angle we can easily imagine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:05:58-07:00","id":547067,"title":"","content":"Well, given that they have a stat that is based exicity on how hungry they are\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:08:43-07:00","id":547069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546562#post546562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had really high hopes for this game, but as it stands, I'm not seeing grand and terrible beasts of legend, a creature born from the fire of cruel circumstance, working through a crisis of personal and outward difficult conflict.<b> I'm seeing an endless parade of cruel, petty, spiteful people, whose miserable compulsions drive them to make the world around them a sadder, uglier place.</b> <b>To me, it felt like a set of rules for the banality of evil.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I won't bother responding to the rest of your post, out of respect to everyone on this forum. But you DO know that this is the <u>World of Darkness</u>, right?<br /> <br /> Like, it's a setting with vampires, werewolves, ghosts, demons, slashers, etc. If you were looking for something more light in tone, I don't think the World of <b>Darkness</b>(new or classic) is the best place to look.<br /> <br /> Just an FYI.<br /> <br /> And as others have also said, you don't have to create a Beast continually strives for cruelty and brutality and misery, just like you don't have t play a Gangrel that rips people into shreds. There can be plenty of personal crisis and a strive to be &quot;better.&quot; Again, I feel like this keeps getting kicked around on an hourly basis.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously wondering if most of this is coming from new fans of the <u>World of Darkness</u> or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-09-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:11:28-07:00","id":547075,"title":"","content":"Hunger is not of the body, it is of the Soul.<br /> <br /> 'Beasts hunger. The Soul doesn\u2019t just want to eat; it wants to consume, to devour. Beasts consume things, creatures, concepts. They hunger for power, or violence, or possession, like the monsters they are. Their Hungers aren\u2019t biological urges, but jealous, vicious needs.'<br /> <br /> Though I will point out they are implied to eat regular food and drink, and the book is so sparse on mentioning that it's easy to miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:29:28-07:00","id":547099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547075#post547075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger is not of the body, it is of the Soul.<br /> <br /> 'Beasts hunger. The Soul doesn\u2019t just want to eat; it wants to consume, to devour. Beasts consume things, creatures, concepts. They hunger for power, or violence, or possession, like the monsters they are. Their Hungers aren\u2019t biological urges, but jealous, vicious needs.'<br /> <br /> Though I will point out they are implied to eat regular food and drink, and the book is so sparse on mentioning that it's easy to miss.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the psychology is the same. Not addressing it leads to a slow death, and to Heroes, while overindulgence leads to being left exposed, and unable to access their own powers and advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:33:03-07:00","id":547103,"title":"","content":"Those are the effects of starvation and over-eating, not the psychology of hunger or Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:34:57-07:00","id":547104,"title":"","content":"The weight of Hunger and what it means to a Beast are absolutely explicit and align, if not entirely then in at least in part, with the points Freemind brought up. At least in my reading of it. <br /> <br /> I will say that, far as I'm concerned, explanations in the genre do not need to be explicit to this degree of detail - existential horror is best served with a mixture of subtle and obvious, but should avoid being 'in your face' lest it lose the impact. It should evoke terror to see and when you ponder on it, not tell you to feel terror. <br /> <br /> Exploring the implications on your own is in great part where the feeling dawns for me, and in that respect Beast offers the essential information in the writing and elaborates adequately to support that type of reading without overextending itself; it gives just enough to immediately understand, but not so much that it eliminates the potential for major exploration.<br /> <br /> In that sense, you could argue the amount of discussion BtP has prompted so far about Heroes and the position of its protagonists (leaving aside the toxicity some developed into) speaks wonders of how accomplished the text is in the regard above.<br /> <br /> The book may have its flaws, but I think highly of it and its difficult themes (the cycle of violence, justification and true monstruosity, who you are versus what you are, what we hate to see in mirrors, the subversion of the narrative, etc), and I believe it is sufficiently transparent about its intended tones that it should not invite the amount of objection and controversy we're seeing.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand not everyone feels that way, and that's fine, because different strokes for different people and there would not be legitimate concerns if parts of the book weren't troublesome from at least one valid perspective. Ultimately, if adjusting the final product so it is more faithful or clearer to the intention of the team alleviates these issues, then I'll be alright with that and OPP has all of my support. This whole thing is probably quite hard on them, and they have to worry about things like sales as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really didn't mean to turn that into a rant but whelp! Okay, I got it out my system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:35:40-07:00","id":547107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546953#post546953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would point out: has anyone here ever had to struggle with being hungry? Or to stay on a regimented diet?<br /> <br /> Starvation leads your brain to focus on good. While your cognitive function doesn't decline (otherwise, how would human, without tooth or claw, get food). But it does distract you from tasks that are not centered on food. They have shown starvation is akin to withdrawal, while food triggers similar pathways to recreational drugs (and some suspect obesity to be due to these pathways firing too much, creating literal addictions).<br /> <br /> And then you have diets, where you are willingly starving yourself and depriing yourself of things that give you pleasure. Therr is a reason most people fail their diet regimines, and it is because you are essentially pitting your individual discipline against millions of years of evolutionary instinct. To top it off, even the discipline can undermine you, as flawed thoughts: &quot;I can't eat this&quot; is more likely to lead you to cheat, as such a denial leads to part of your brain rebelling against the part telling it it can't do something (it is like when you tell a 6 year old he can't have a cookie... he will then want it even more).<br /> <br /> And the obvious inverse is over eating and poor consumption control, when you keep eating when full or to often. I mean, the obesity crisis is there in part because a lot of processed foods trigger the reward process <i>too well </i> (I still remember my button class in Medical School showing an FMRI of someone on coke and someone who was both overweight and eating some form of processed desert (name wasnt given)...the overlap was scary). Point being, not eating too much is only a bit easier than keeping yourself from eating, sue to the same pathways.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that it isn't something physical, but metaphysical. Your soul literally thirsts for something, and is starving. And <i>it feels good to sate it </i>, just like a cheeseburger would taste like nirvana after being in the desert for a week without food. It isn't something you can fully control, because if you don't feed it, it will hijack the dreams of others and feed itself. And feeding it to the point of it literally falling into a metaphysical &quot;food coma&quot; is nearly as dangerous as letting it starve. And the issue is, you have to let it be hungry unless you are willing to act in the dark manners to fulfill it, harming mankind (even if it is a non-persistent manner to only those who &quot;deserve it&quot;) in someway to instill the fear you need to feed.<br /> <br /> Beasts have an inner struggle, just like anyone on a diet. There diet simply is &quot;not instilling terror into humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, the MD in me slipped out a bit there. But trust me, when working with both morbidly obese 14 year Olds and anorexics, you learn how much the hunger/reward response can mess things up).</div> </div> </div> </div>I deal with this every day, and it's hard. This is part of why Beast appeals to me, this resonance with my lived experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:59:44-07:00","id":547119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547103#post547103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are the effects of starvation and over-eating, not the psychology of hunger or Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean how hungry the Beast is affecting their behavior isn't psychological? It is almost like that statement is ridiculous. I mean we wouldn't what a roleaying game to allow the player to determine how their character is going to react to starvation or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:09:19-07:00","id":547125,"title":"","content":"Good thing the game doesn't, then.<br /> <br /> Because if you are starving, your Soul will go out and get a meal on its own, and its new Satiety will be determined by a die roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:26:42-07:00","id":547148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=546625#post546625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really see anything in there any worse than what the other splats get up to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it deals with doing psychological damage. I know people who are petty who like to lord their power over people, delight in minor punishments, take things people want just to deny them, and people who revel in destruction of things people love... I don't want to be forced to do that stuff in a game, I have been on the receiving end of that and even doing it to someone who \u201cdeserves\u201d it seems wrong. <br /> <br /> I read the preview and I had no ideas for characters or campaigns staring Beasts. I could see a Hunter game storming into the nightmare realm of the soul and fighting the true form monster that has been terrorizing the community.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:27:53-07:00","id":547150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547069#post547069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I won't bother responding to the rest of your post, out of respect to everyone on this forum. But you DO know that this is the <u>World of Darkness</u>, right?<br /> <br /> Like, it's a setting with vampires, werewolves, ghosts, demons, slashers, etc. If you were looking for something more light in tone, I don't think the World of <b>Darkness</b>(new or classic) is the best place to look.<br /> <br /> Just an FYI.<br /> <br /> And as others have also said, you don't have to create a Beast continually strives for cruelty and brutality and misery, just like you don't have t play a Gangrel that rips people into shreds. There can be plenty of personal crisis and a strive to be &quot;better.&quot; Again, I feel like this keeps getting kicked around on an hourly basis.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously wondering if most of this is coming from new fans of the <u>World of Darkness</u> or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until now I've tried to stay out of the discussions about Beast, mostly because I haven't read the text, but I'd really like people to use actual good arguments while arguing, and like them to argue in good faith. I'm willing to believe you didn't intend it that way, but your last sentence almost sounds like an ad hominum. It could be interpreted as you saying that the some arguments do not have to be considered, as the people leveling them are not &quot;real&quot; fans (whatever that means).<br /> <br /> About your assessment of the World of Darkness: The tone of the new World of Darkness is not necessarily very dark. In much of the material &quot;dark&quot; is instead interpreted as &quot;hidden&quot;. A secret world people do not know about. Of course terrible things happen in the darkness, but not all that happens in darkness is necessarily terrible. The level of horribleness varies per game line and campaign.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this post also comes across as negative. I don't have anything against you, but I think your post could be interpreted in ways that are bad for the discussion, even if not intentionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:29:56-07:00","id":547153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547125#post547125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing the game doesn't, then.<br /> <br /> Because if you are starving, your Soul will go out and get a meal on its own, and its new Satiety will be determined by a die roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanic you've described and the fact of players determining how their characters react to starvation are not mutually exclusive things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:30:59-07:00","id":547154,"title":"","content":"Actually, what happens if you hit the countdown time-out for your soul feeding itself while you're <i>in</i> it? Does it have to wait until you separate?<br /> <br /> Can you defer a feeding indefinitely by holing up in your lair? Possibly sending your broodmates out for pizza so you don't <i>starve</i> starve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-09-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:32:34-07:00","id":547157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547011#post547011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But is that an explicit thing in Beast, or merely an angle we can easily imagine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the fluff makes a point about how different levels of hunger shape the beasts actions, and that the system imparts conditions on the Beast depending on the Satiety, which in turn act as a means for Beats (i.e. XP) in the current system... I don't see an issue with it. I mean, rhe fact that both ends and the middle reflect different levels of rhw beasts actions and your susceptibility to Anathema's all point to reasons to have a mechanic (Low means the Soul ravages dreams and drives you, 5 is most susceptible to Heroes, and High means the Beast leaves you be but you have difficulty sating it, and it may not respond). Plus, satiety is also your power pool, so it is essential mechanically in that respect as well.<br /> <br /> And here is the thing: the central theme reflecting the core conflict of each splats setting. I mean, you have:<ul><li>Mortals/hunters have Integrity (holding onto your sense of self in the face of the horror of the world, some if with you perpetrated or experienced)</li> <li>Werewolves and Harmony (balance the world's of flesh and spirit)</li> <li>Mage has Wisdom (Not abusing your semi-phenomenal, nearly cosmic power)</li> <li>Sineaters and Synergy (don't piss off that ancient ghost that brought you back, but stay human (ish))</li> <li>Humanity (cling to what you were-Vampire/Become what you want to be-Promethean)</li> <li>Changelings have clarity (hold on to reality after being the play thing of beings who defined both it and you before you eacaped)</li> </ul>(If I am forgetting anyone, I apologize.)<br /> <br /> I mean, you could make the argument &quot;but do we really need a gauge to determine that? Why not just role play it? &quot; But i could make that point for everything in nWoD. Do you need Harmony or Synergy, Humanity or Integrity? No, nor do you need to play with them, as they all could be reflected by game play and the PCs thoughts and actions. For example, I dropped the morality aspect from my 1e mage games for the most part, focusing more on how you used vulgar magic and let the abyss into the world. But the games do have those systems for a reason in 2e beyond moral judgement, which is to have mechanical factors that attempt to reflect the central theme of conflict of each line and reward players both for optimizing those tracks and for playing their characters failure on them (via Beats and conditions).<br /> <br /> Sure, you can act hungry IC, but with the current system, you get a condition that reflects it that grants you XP for both acknowledging as you play and when it resolves, thus offering a reward for playing your character. It also offers guide posts so the player, other PCs and the ST has an understanding of where characters are on the scale and what actions might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> As for why satiety, it fits the conflict best. I mean, other lines have &quot;hungers&quot;, but those aren't the central theme, or at least not the one that drives conflict. Mages thirst for knowledge, power and Mystery, but the conflict comes from how they use that knowledge and power, not it's acquisition (unless acquired via said misuse). Vampires have their Hunger, but the conflict isn't fighting it so much as trying to cling to being human when you are not one any longer (and I would argue that since their soul is still human, if scarred and twisted, that they face a dissonance that beasts don't). Werewolves have the need to hunt, but their conflict is the balance of the spirit vs. the flesh, and how that shapes their hunt (not the need hunt itself). And so on.<br /> <br /> The point is, the central theme of Beast's conflict is that you have the soul of a powerful, <b><u>hungry</u></b>, and totally inhuman monster that <i>is </i> a part of you. The Souls hunger is your hunger, and it is the conflict of the setting because if how you need to fill it: harming humans to create the appropriate type of fear or loss. And you are still human enough to recognize those things as both harmful and necessary for your existence, and must balance sating yourself and sparing those around you.<br /> <br /> The Beasts are driven by and must fight their hunger, balancing it against everything else. And that hunger shapes both how far they are willing to go for their principles and a reason to forgo them. For example, to compare it to a human: cannibalism as even a concept is appalling to even think about while you sit in a cafe while down the street from the supermarket (at least, I would hope it is), but when trapped on a snowy mountain with no resources but the frozen guy next to you, you find your principles challenged as you starve to death. Beasts are beings that literally have a hunger that resides in the Core of their being, that transcends the physical needs of their body as their very Soul demands sustenance. They potentially face the conundrum of forsaking their principles to eat every day, not just when trapped on a snowy maintain, because holding to the principle of not harming humans (even if only metaphysically) is what starves them. Some might be able to go and maintain hunger strikes to the point of being willing to die for their principles, though the beast won't let that happen (and will ravage humanity in their dreams anyway). Others give in to their hunger, and gorge themselves, guilt setting in as they realize what they did. And others try to funnel it into morally justifiable acts, while others don't care and accept being monsters. The thing is, the Hunger is what drives their conflict with the world and in themselves. The fact that denying your Hunger leads to the Mythic Arc initiating the creation of a Hero, and thus drives the games central external conflict, also makes it appropriate.<br /> <br /> Tl;DNR: Mechanically, Satiety is important as both the power pool for abilities and as a source of conflict for beats, as well as defining your susceptibility to Anathemas. It also fits thematically as the core driver of the Beasts conflict, both internally and with the world, as it reflects the state of the Soul and it's influence on the Beast as well as the Soul's actions in the Astral (which in turn leads to the creation of Heroes, the one of the key elements of the games external conflict).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":".  Wrote on phone. Trying to make it look pretty at home. Will likely take more than one attempt. 06-09-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:39:08-07:00","id":547167,"title":"","content":"Beasts can keep their Lair low (3 max) and if they keep to themselves and balance correctly, they can just do a feed once a week and as mentioned, depending on the Hunger and their personality, they don't have to be a dick about it when they do that weekly take in. They do need to feed because if the Soul goes Ravenous, they take lethal damage eventually, though a Beast could potentially live a fairly normal life if they stick to Starving as a Condition, just having that once a week a nibble.<br /> <br /> But then, personally... I'd rather play a Lestat figure enjoying their Beasthood than a Louis figure feeding off rats and only when the hunger gets too much. Thats just me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:13:02-07:00","id":547247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547125#post547125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing the game doesn't, then.<br /> <br /> Because if you are starving, your Soul will go out and get a meal on its own, and its new Satiety will be determined by a die roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which means by not eating, you are choosing let the monster that is inside of you ravage the dreamscape/personal souls of those humans a fund yu, amd also possibly create a hero bent on destroying you. <br /> <br /> Hunger does drive your psychology in real life. Human culture has entire portions of itself driven by it, from fasting and taboo foods in religions to just day to day social influence. Starvation and satiety both trigger neurological changes that shape the thought process of the person undergoing them. <br /> <br /> This game has the hunger be due to a primordial soul that is a manifestation of humans darkest fears. If that doesn't effect the psyche of a something who has human thought and emotion, especially when your hunger is for the emotions of fear, powerlessness, loss, vengence and hopelessness... then that thing is likely not very human anymore. Sure, these hungers could all be sated with non-physical or lasting means (turn in a their, don't kill him, as a means of punishment) but you are still inflicting psychological harm by targeting the most basic fears of humanity. <br /> <br /> The fact that you once considered yourself one of them, even if you never truly were one, means that you will still feel the tugging of your psyche saying what you do is wrong, along with (if you so choose) your efforts to prove you are more than a monster, means that you will face the effort of combating giving in to your hunger. At the same time, that growing hunger will put you in further conflict with that primordial soul, as it's hunger (and thus your own) grows. Eventually, you either choose to give in or you allow it to rampage and attack the Oneiros of the humans around you to sate it's hunger. And while that may sound preferable, rhe fact that you are letting a monster ravage the personal soul of everyone around you and possibly create someone whose soul purpose is to kill you... seems like it might not be a good call either.<br /> <br /> And if your players choose to ignore the influence of the hunger, that is their perogative. They can let their PC starve. But it simply means they arent really acknowledging the core concept, nor does it mean they are saints who don't allow harm to come to humanity (see the &quot;Beasts ravaged the Astral&quot; above). The fact that actual conditions exist at each stage to reflect your hunger means that players ignoring these means missing out on Beats and traits that exist within their PC. <br /> <br /> If your players decide instead to give up their humanity and not care about the harm they do, then that is all good. This game doesn't punish you for morality failings, at least internally. Beasts know that they are monsters, and their cruelty and dark acts are to them the same as a lion chasing down a gazelle: it is what happens, no matter how bad you feel for the gazelle. The punishment isnt internal, as they likely are more in line with their Soul, and I would argue that this is a far more accurate way to play a PC, based on the way this game is described (as an aside, for all those who hate the fact that this game makes the protagonists at best y grey and on average monsterous entities... I always got the feeling that was the point: play as the bad guy, a la Dungeon Keeper, or at least someone with horribly dark tendencies, a la V or Alan Moore's Batman). There are other dangers, such as the beast subsume ng any trace of your humanity, but this is much more in line then playing the game as the &quot;Beast who never hungers&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yes, you can just let it hit zero, and roll. But that is ignoring both the in game consequences of the choice to do so and the fact that it means players are forgoing XP and playing their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-09-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:14:23-07:00","id":547250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547167#post547167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can keep their Lair low (3 max) and if they keep to themselves and balance correctly, they can just do a feed once a week and as mentioned, depending on the Hunger and their personality, they don't have to be a dick about it when they do that weekly take in. They do need to feed because if the Soul goes Ravenous, they take lethal damage eventually, though a Beast could potentially live a fairly normal life if they stick to Starving as a Condition, just having that once a week a nibble.<br /> <br /> But then, personally... I'd rather play a Lestat figure enjoying their Beasthood than a Louis figure feeding off rats and only when the hunger gets too much. Thats just me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have a fairly safe and rewarding career as a Beast if you keep Satiety below 4 and focus on Atavisms, but occasionally, you want those high Satiety Nightmare effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:15:36-07:00","id":547251,"title":"","content":"From what I've read, Beasts do have an inner struggle, just not one against their nature. The struggle is in the dichotomy between a Beast's Legend and her Life. A Beast knows she's a monster and that acting like it is what the world expect from her, but she can challenge this fate by connecting with her humanity, by being more than a slave to her Beastial nature.<br /> I think it is made even more poignant and important because the Beast doesn't need to deny or transcend the monster inside; it is entirely her choice, there is no penalty, no degeneration, nothin to lose, and yet she can say: &quot;I am more than this&quot; and do her best to prove it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:23:53-07:00","id":547269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547251#post547251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've read, Beasts do have an inner struggle, just not one against their nature. The struggle is in the dichotomy between a Beast's Legend and her Life. A Beast knows she's a monster and that acting like it is what the world expect from her, but she can challenge this fate by connecting with her humanity, by being more than a slave to her Beastial nature.<br /> I think it is made even more poignant and important because the Beast doesn't need to deny or transcend the monster inside; it is entirely her choice, there is no penalty, no degeneration, nothin to lose, and yet she can say: &amp;quot;I am more than this&amp;quot; and do her best to prove it.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>This is true as well. The Life/Legend dichotomy is the central conflict, but what drives it is your hunger. It is hard to be human when the beast inside is snarling from hunger at all the potential meals around it, while a connecting with your legend is hard if the Soul is slumbering and not active. <br /> <br /> I mean, it is easy to protect a loved one from something when you are full, but when you are starving, it may be hard to ignore the Soul inside demanding &quot;just a taste&quot; of the fear that loved one is feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:25:15-07:00","id":547271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">About your assessment of the World of Darkness: The tone of the new World of Darkness is not necessarily very dark. In much of the material &quot;dark&quot; is instead interpreted as &quot;hidden&quot;. A secret world people do not know about. Of course terrible things happen in the darkness, but not all that happens in darkness is necessarily terrible. The level of horribleness varies per game line and campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div> The setting does draw a lot upon Gothic fantasy, which is defined by attraction to and fascination with the grim, the macabre and the horrifying from a safe distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:29:42-07:00","id":547277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547269#post547269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true as well. The Life/Legend dichotomy is the central conflict, but what drives it is your hunger. It is hard to be human when the beast inside is snarling from hunger at all the potential meals around it, while a connecting with your legend is hard if the Soul is slumbering and not active.<br /> <br /> I mean, it is easy to protect a loved one from something when you are full, but when you are starving, it may be hard to ignore the Soul inside demanding &quot;just a taste&quot; of the fear that loved one is feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and it is the very fact that itt is hard, and that mechanically, it would cost the Beast nothing to succomb, that makes her not giving in so extraordinary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:32:45-07:00","id":547279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547154#post547154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, what happens if you hit the countdown time-out for your soul feeding itself while you're <i>in</i> it? Does it have to wait until you separate?<br /> <br /> Can you defer a feeding indefinitely by holing up in your lair? Possibly sending your broodmates out for pizza so you don't <i>starve</i> starve?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably run it as a clash of wills.Basically have Soul fight your influence in the merger to go on a rampage. If you can win you manage to postpone the rampage, but if you lose well you'll have a nice black out period while the Soul goes and gets some snacks.<br /> <br /> Slightly related note when the soul does rampage does anyone recall if there was a chart or something mentioning how far the Soul's rampage range is, or is it just locked at the one mile limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:59:22-07:00","id":547333,"title":"","content":"One mile per dot of lair. If you want to shake it up a bit you could say it's within [dots] miles of the <i>soul</i>, and so that range can be centered on either the beast (if it's in the heart) or the location corresponding to the chamber the soul is in at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:45:52-07:00","id":547378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547333#post547333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One mile per dot of lair. If you want to shake it up a bit you could say it's within [dots] miles of the <i>soul</i>, and so that range can be centered on either the beast (if it's in the heart) or the location corresponding to the chamber the soul is in at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or within <i>Lair</i> miles of a place that shares Resonance with your Lair, if you really want things to be dire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:59:23-07:00","id":547387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547150#post547150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until now I've tried to stay out of the discussions about Beast, mostly because I haven't read the text, but I'd really like people to use actual good arguments while arguing, and like them to argue in good faith. I'm willing to believe you didn't intend it that way, but your last sentence almost sounds like an ad hominum. It could be interpreted as you saying that the some arguments do not have to be considered, as the people leveling them are not &quot;real&quot; fans (whatever that means).<br /> <br /> About your assessment of the World of Darkness: The tone of the new World of Darkness is not necessarily very dark. In much of the material &quot;dark&quot; is instead interpreted as &quot;hidden&quot;. A secret world people do not know about. Of course terrible things happen in the darkness, but not all that happens in darkness is necessarily terrible. <b>The level of horribleness varies per game line and campaign.</b><br /> <br /> Sorry if this post also comes across as negative. I don't have anything against you, but I think your post could be interpreted in ways that are bad for the discussion, even if not intentionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I don't mean any of what I typed to be negative, either. Apologies if that's how you take it.<br /> <br /> So you haven't read the text, yet are critical of my opinion of someone else's understanding of it? As others have stated, I'm not saying NOT to critique Beast. By all means, do so. Maybe you find the rules difficult to understand, or perhaps the mechanics of it seem a bit confusing. That's fine.<br /> <br /> But to rally against the game's &quot;horror&quot; or &quot;dark&quot; themes, is absurd when you consider the rest of the splats in the World of Darkness. It's fine, though. Others who are far more intelligent than I am have already expressed what I've been thinking time and again. It's like beating a dead horse(too dark?), by now.<br /> <br /> And as for your comment on the tone of the NWOD? I disagree. Heavily. The NWOD is extremely dark--at least, in the games I play it is. Slashers, Lancea Sanctum, Ashwood Abbey etc. do things that are all horrific in nature. The NWOD is very, very dark. And of course it's hidden. It's largely supposed to be. Much like how the things Beasts can do can be &quot;hidden.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you said it yourself: &quot;the level of horribleness varies per game line and campaign.&quot; Yes. I agree. And like many Vampire, Werewolf and Changeling campaigns, Beast can be extremely disturbing.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly tired of this, though. It's all very frustrating. I'm going to follow the game on the Kickstarter page a bit more than here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-09-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:31:05-07:00","id":547463,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of vitriol and snark to my two posts. I'll give people the benefit of the doubt and just assume it's due to a 190+ thread and the general back-and-forth from each side's inability to see the other's point (as is usual).<br /> <br /> As I said..many times...I don't have a problem with the dark nature of the game, and I generally enjoy playing horrible, dark characters. The root cause to all the general problems (other than mechanics and crossover issues) is the dissonance/conflicting themes in the book<br /> <br /> So, since I have seemed to fail getting my original thoughts across with the original posts, I'll just steal Rand Brittain's post from a different forum, since Rand is far more eloquence I could ever hope to be.<br /> <br /> If this is against the rules, or has already been posted, I'm sorry in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> Rand Brittain<br /> Okay, I was linked to a movie review that helps me really express where Beast's problems stem from.<br /> <br /> The first two problems are ultimately intertwined. The first problem is that Beasts are incredibly unsympathetic. This exacerbates the second problem, which is that the text and subtext of the game are decoupled.<br /> <br /> I think the writers of Beast would agree that it's a darker game even than Requiem. Vampires prey on humans, but they're still ultimately human in psyche and a large part of their condition revolves around how they try to justify their new relation to humanity. Beasts don't come across as human. From the Introduction onward, Primordial revels in the inhuman nature of the Children, and each splat description gives loving attention to numerous examples of their sadism and lack of empathy. (There are positive examples, but they don't really stick out when they're sharing space with &quot;Abusive Scorpion Principal&quot; and &quot;I Invented Some Crimes So I Could Drown You For Committing Them.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Beasts are just not likeable. They are nastier than Kindred, nastier than Seers, nastier than anything in the game line that I can think of. They even come across as worse than Slashers, because Slashers weren't in a book that took their pretensions seriously. Of course, it's not exactly wrong for a horror game's protagonists to be nasty, but this is the first time a game has tried to clear a hurdle so viscerally awful.<br /> <br /> (I think part of this is the result of how Beasts tend to commit literal acts of abuse where other games couch their monsters in metaphor: a vampire's Kiss can stand in for sexual, physical, or financial predation, but it doesn't actually require anybody to act out the sources of real-life trauma at the gaming table.)<br /> <br /> How did this happen? I think it derives from, while also exacerbating, the second problem: the game's text and subtext are decoupled.<br /> <br /> The relationship between text and subtext is complicated because a game's subtext tends to be layered and include multiple metaphors that sometimes contradict rather than a single straightforward allegory. Vampires, for instance, resonate with toxic relationships, addiction, and a number of other things.<br /> <br /> Requiem, of course, has a huge body of art and culture to draw on in establishing the subtext of what vampires can stand on. Primordial didn't have that kind of shoulders to stand on, and it suffers, because the subtext of the game doesn't grow organically from the text.<br /> <br /> On a text level, Beasts are children of nightmare who sate their hunger by tormenting humanity. On a subtext level, they stand for such things as outcasts and people who generally don't fit into society's prescribed roles and are looking for a home. There's a clear intended link between the Children and LBGT persons or those with nonbinary gender identity.<br /> <br /> This is where the book starts to fall apart, because while there is a link between the socially noncompliant and the monster, it's not strong enough to bridge the gap between &quot;sympathetic outsider&quot; and &quot;sadistic beast.&quot; Some readers have been willing to suspend their disbelief and leap over the gap, but it's very clear that a large number have not been willing.<br /> <br /> This, I think, is key. The portion of the audience that has reacted negatively to Primordial hasn't failed to see the subtext in the book; it has rejected that subtext. The book is written under the assumption that readers will accept the sympathetic subtext and judge its protagonists in that light, but because the presentation of those protagonists is so jarring (honestly, reading the book makes me feel dirty), they are unwilling to do so. When viewed without that subtext, the Children are... well, they're pretty much just a bunch of gribbly serial killers with an overinflated sense of their own specialness.<br /> <br /> This leads to a related problem, the problem of Heroes. In the light of what I've already said, the problem seems pretty obvious. Heroes are, subtextually, the bigots and reactionaries who persecute the outcasts as represented by Beasts. They even have examples identifying Heroes with notable geek unlovelies, mens' rights activists.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, on a textual level, Heroes and Beasts are nearly identical, except that Beasts are worse. Beasts torment, stalk, and kill humans; Heroes do the same thing, but only to Beasts, who they see as monsters responsible for their problems. (They generally aren't very far wrong.)<br /> <br /> When you view Heroes in light of the intended subtext, everything snaps into place. Readers who have rejected that subtext, will wonder why the book hates Heroes so much when they're undeniably &quot;the good guys&quot;?<br /> <br /> The book does hate Heroes. You can almost see the drops of spittle staining the page whenever it mentions them. The authorial voice is on a very high horse about the superiority of Beasts to small-minded Heroes. Since plenty of readers long ago arrived at the conclusion that chopping off a Beast's head is probably the best way to handle one, this attitude is jarring at best. As it stands, Heroes add very little value to the game.<br /> <br /> In Conclusion:<br /> <br /> How can Primordial's problems be fixed?<br /> <br /> Sadly, there's no easy patch. The first step would have to be a careful going-over of the text to increase its consistency and to sell the reader more effectively on the Children as protagonists.<br /> <br /> The book also needs to work on the link between the Children as monsters and the Children as outcasts. As it stands, Beasts are too powerful, too unconcerned with other peoples' feelings, and too socially connected to make the metaphor connect.<br /> <br /> Finally, to be blunt, Primordial needs to jettison its hate-boner for Heroes. A protagonist derives status from the power and allure of its enemies; Beasts derive no status at all from their implacable straw foes. If the writers aren't willing to ascribe depth to MRAs or high school bullies, then the connection between those things and Heroes needs to be dropped like a rock.<br /> <br /> (I would honestly be pretty okay with a game where villainous Beast protagonists work against noble Hero antagonists; certainly there are plenty of stories around where the antagonist is &quot;the good guy&quot; by normal standards.)<br /> <br /> Fixing these problems is going to require more work than Onyx Path is going to be happy about doing, but I think that doing so now (rather than waiting for Beast 2e in 2019) will help make the game into something that reflects well on the second phase of the nWoD.<br /> <br /> The responses we've seen from the readers who were able to find something to identify with the game show that there's definitely a gem in there somewhere, and it would be a shame if half the audience were driven away because nobody polished all the blood off.<br /> ------------------","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","user":"darthcoffee","date":".  formatting 06-09-2015, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:40:41-07:00","id":547473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547387#post547387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't worry, I don't mean any of what I typed to be negative, either. Apologies if that's how you take it.<br /> <br /> So you haven't read the text, yet are critical of my opinion of someone else's understanding of it? As others have stated, I'm not saying NOT to critique Beast. By all means, do so. Maybe you find the rules difficult to understand, or perhaps the mechanics of it seem a bit confusing. That's fine.<br /> <br /> But to rally against the game's &quot;horror&quot; or &quot;dark&quot; themes, is absurd when you consider the rest of the splats in the World of Darkness. It's fine, though. Others who are far more intelligent than I am have already expressed what I've been thinking time and again. It's like beating a dead horse(too dark?), by now.<br /> <br /> And as for your comment on the tone of the NWOD? I disagree. Heavily. The NWOD is extremely dark--at least, in the games I play it is. Slashers, Lancea Sanctum, Ashwood Abbey etc. do things that are all horrific in nature. The NWOD is very, very dark. And of course it's hidden. It's largely supposed to be. Much like how the things Beasts can do can be &quot;hidden.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you said it yourself: &quot;the level of horribleness varies per game line and campaign.&quot; Yes. I agree. And like many Vampire, Werewolf and Changeling campaigns, Beast can be extremely disturbing.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly tired of this, though. It's all very frustrating. I'm going to follow the game on the Kickstarter page a bit more than here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you are getting tired of this discussion, and I hope I didn't contribute too much to that. As for me being critical, I only try to criticise things or part of arguments non-specific to Beast because otherwise I'd just feel hypocritical.<br /> <br /> As for the themes part, I'm not trying to rally against the &quot;horror&quot; and &quot;dark&quot; themes as you call them. I actually agree that nWoD is a horror game with some dark themes. As Isator said, it draws upon a Gothic fantasy. The problem I had with your argument is that you seemed to equal &quot;does not like the dark tone&quot; with &quot;is not a fan of nWoD.&quot; I disagree with this as the nWoD contains a multitude of different themes. The core rulebook for example explicitly calls out dread as the main mood, there interpreted as the fear of the unknown and the dark. This is a more subtle theme than the gothic horror of Vampire. So there exist themes in the nWoD that do not require in your face horribleness.<br /> <br /> Thus even while the nWoD contains many horrific things, like the examples you mentioned, not all these things are important to every campaign. When they are not part of the story, they do not necessarily impact its mood and theme. But if Beast contains such things by default, I guess the game isn't suited for people who want horror that is less directly in your face, which I guess is the point you were trying to make.<br /> <br /> But I'll stop this line of argument now, as it is close to derailment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I made in error in my representation of Dude's point, so I changed &quot;does not like beast&quot; into &quot;does not like the dark tone.&quot; Furthermore, just to make it clear, this was my interpretation of what Dude said, and not necessarily the point he was trying to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 06-09-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:52:53-07:00","id":547478,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Based on deathcoffee's last post, I'm curious on the following piece of data.<br /> <br /> What is the correlation between those who hate Beast and those who read the fluff stories before or &quot;in order&quot; while going through the book as opposed to reading the crunchier and setting bits before even touching the fluff stories?<br /> <br /> I wonder if they may be the issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 06-09-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:54:38-07:00","id":547481,"title":"","content":"So, this &quot;subtext&quot; of the protagonists being somehow different to those around them, with a group dedicated to wiping them out or otherwise oppressing them. <br /> <br /> How is this different to <i>every other gameline</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:05:29-07:00","id":547499,"title":"","content":"Oh, this may be an unpopular opinion, I like heroes. However, I view them as force of nature antagonists instead of narrative antagonists. They are an antagonist in the same way that blindly setting the house you're in on fire makes the fire in the house an antagonist. They don't need to be anything but what they are, but force of nature antagonists need to be used in the story in a particular...<br /> <br /> Actually. here you go.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ^ Should help when thinking about how to handle Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:08:31-07:00","id":547506,"title":"","content":"Where do people keep getting Scorpion VP as being abusive? Seriously. Nothing in the story goes one way or the other about how she gets everyone to behave. Just being an intimidating person with a pet scorpion alone would gets most kids to behave just to not have to interact with them. The presumption that she is actually abusing her students is entirely bad faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:12:23-07:00","id":547512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547463#post547463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of vitriol and snark to my two posts. I'll give people the benefit of the doubt and just assume it's due to a 190+ thread and the general back-and-forth from each side's inability to see the other's point (as is usual).<br /> <br /> As I said..many times...I don't have a problem with the dark nature of the game, and I generally enjoy playing horrible, dark characters. The root cause to all the general problems (other than mechanics and crossover issues) is the dissonance of the theme's in the book</div> </div> </div> </div>The Problem hasn't been the Discussion.. It's Been that some don't make comments too HELP the Situation. I've said repeatedly that Constructive Critism is useful, you just need too Give something beyond &quot;I don't like this&quot;. Giving context to what you don't like and how it can be improved helps get your point across, Some people just refuse too give context too what they dislike if it's the general tone, Fine. Say that, but say WHY.<br /> <br /> As too what you copied and posted, It's been retreaded repeatedly over the 190+ pages. Some who disliked the idea in the original posts have come around too be the strongest supporters of the game. I've not been following the RPG.net thread but, IF it's worse then this thread, I can imagine Its degenerated down too Integrity 1 or 2....<br /> <br /> The Main points I can Agree with is:<br /> <br /> Tone: &quot;It's Too Dark&quot; Yes, Yes it is, But only if you refuse too make it lighter yourself. Use the REALLY Dark Monsters as highlights too the players too show them what they could become if they don't be careful.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Begotten aren't good Guys&quot; .......... Neither Are Vampires, Werewolves, Frankenstein Monsters, or Demons. Yet people have less issues with them because &quot;Some of them can be Good guys&quot; so can the Begotten. It's Harder... MUCH Harder, but... that makes the ones who are BETTER Heroes (In my Eye anyway), Borrowing from Skyrim...<br /> <i><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0553409/\" target=\"_blank\">Paarthurnax</a></i>: What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?<br /> <br /> &quot;Heroes Are Abuse Victims&quot; and &quot;Heroes aren't Interesting&quot; Both of these... CAN be true. If you Want them too be uninteresting Flat People Who Rush headlong into Danger and Death then fine, that's what they are. Personally I'd play them as people who are willing too Wait too get the &quot;Monster&quot; so they can Learn about it, Find it's Weaknesses (Apply Banes from a distance while watching it), Break into it's lair while it is &quot;Sleeping&quot; (While the Player is doing something else, the &quot;Beast&quot; is going too be there in it's Lair just not active Atleast thats what I'd Say.) and Take something of its, or Trap it. And the Abuse Victim's Part... I can see it as a thing. Someone who's gone though Hell and Snapped.... it's unfortunate. The Beast SHOULD Feel sorry... Should Be MADE too Suffer for his Choice of not Feeding. Beast's are gonna want too know about who's trying too kill them. They May even End up Agreeing with them that they Hurt People.<br /> <br /> Those are the Main 3 Points that this thread has... &quot;Beaten too death and Flayed it's Corpse&quot; And really need too be adressed sometime soon I think. Rewrites/Clarification would help in some of these things.<br /> <br /> Blah. Ranting. Sorry....<br /> <br /> *When I say you, I don't actually mean &quot;you&quot; I mean &quot;you&quot; in general. I'm not trying too call anyone out, Even if I do seem too be doing it.<br /> Also apologise's for over Capitalisation, it's a bad Habit, that i do when i start typing too fast too realise I'm doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:22:00-07:00","id":547518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547481#post547481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this &quot;subtext&quot; of the protagonists being somehow different to those around them, with a group dedicated to wiping them out or otherwise oppressing them.<br /> <br /> How is this different to <i>every other gameline</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The zeitgeist in which the gameline comes out, the fact many people can't differentiate the subtext they see in the draft (admittedly, one which is really easy to see) from the clearly stated declaration that any resemblance to real person or organization is purely coincidental, the always hard to fathom difference between a vocal minority (still symptomatic of a problem, no doubt) and an almost universal rejection of a project and the far too easily forgotten &quot;You don't have to love each gameline and that's perfectly fine&quot; thing<br /> <br /> I won't even consider the hard mission to make mythological monsters <i>potentially</i> sympathetic and playable, because that's what happened with each gameline since Vampire: The Masquerade and whoever says Beasts are unequivocally the worst we've seen between CWoD <i>and</i> NWoD and they are forced to be terrible unrepentant assholes it's either misinformed, ignoring part of the books or, and I hate to but I've got to consider the option, a liar which is willingly feeding the flames of the controversy.<br /> <br /> P.S. Please, please, please, the last paragraph is only referring to the idea that, out all the gamelines, Beasts are all terrible beings that ALWAYS enjoy their hungers and gleefully spread misery in the world with no option or reason whatsoever to struggle with their nature. I'm not going to call people misinformed or ignorant for their interpretation of the text or other kinds of criticism, but that one is factually wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-09-2015, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:46:44-07:00","id":547566,"title":"","content":"If beasts were as bad as some people seem to think there wouldn't <i>be</i> any heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:31:33-07:00","id":547678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547566#post547566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If beasts were as bad as some people seem to think there wouldn't <i>be</i> any heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony of the fact that some of the complainers have chosen a situation that is simultaneously the worst case scenario narratively, and the best possible scenario mechanically, as their hill to die upon is not lost on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:33:09-07:00","id":547681,"title":"","content":"Edited: We're fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-09-2015, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T17:11:58-07:00","id":547767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547566#post547566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If beasts were as bad as some people seem to think there wouldn't <i>be</i> any heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>After some thinking why are people complaining about Beasts and not about Demons and how they make contracts especially custom made ones or Werewolf were everything is and can be hunted including humans especially humans or slashers and how they are pretty much worse thing than anything else and you can play as them with mechanic help this is not me jabbing Werewolf especially loving on how they did gifts or Demons being my favorite book. But comparing it to the other game lines how exactly different are they.<br /> <br /> @SoulGambit after watching the video I kind of agree with you I prefer heroes as a force of nature then narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:37:55-07:00","id":547851,"title":"","content":"You know, I hate to say it, but I'm sort of hoping that Matt and the other Devs/writers for Beast just ignore all of the criticism.<br /> <br /> I've seen like, <i>four</i> valid criticisms for the book vs a whole bunch that can only have come from misunderstanding and/or not paying attention to the relevant passages, and if too much time is spent on those invalid criticisms, it's just going to kill the game.<br /> <br /> The Valid criticism I've seen, by the way, are &quot;Passages don't make it clear what's really going on&quot; which is what's leading to the misunderstanding that lead to the invalid critisims<br /> <br /> The Bit about ugalu Vs Namtaru Birthrights<br /> <br /> And the Power of the Nightmares seems inconsistent<br /> <br /> And some people have claimed that supernatural creatures should interact differently based on their themes and culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:38:27-07:00","id":547852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547157#post547157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[A very well-written discussion of Satiety in Beast]</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that's really good. *Sigh* Alright. I think I'm just missing the days of the social groups, and I'm missing whatever the manifestation of this tension within the Beast community. I keep expecting to read about a Hunger AA-equivalent, or something. Thank you for your time, folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:28:00-07:00","id":547880,"title":"","content":"Given how people offering criticism get multiple people demanding them to defend their opinions, I can really see why there isn't much constructive criticism. I don't personally agree with &quot;Beast is about abusers&quot; and creates a dynamic of &quot;the Other is good, the norm is evil.&quot; I do see why a person would have that opinion. Those elements do exist within the game. If you can't see it then you don't want to see it. That is fine. I think the criticism here is generally good for the developers and writers to see. I don't expect them to do anything about it. The game is not for everyone. Everyone should be able to accept that fact. OP seems to have done just that. If the &quot;attacking&quot; of people that say why they hate the game stops then maybe the people that have criticism that can actually be addressed in the book will start to appear. Basically, chill out. The game does seem to have issues. I'm still reading, but I guarantee I won't bother to try to address the issues any time soon because the environment isn't really conducive for critical analysis. Ideally, there are some things that need to be tightened up with this game because not everything seems clear. It isn't broke, but at about the midpoint of the text I'm still trying to figure some things out that I should already know. I'll have to wait and see what gets clarified. The game seems playable, but I'm not sure it is up to par. It's still early. I don't see why it can't be one of the best, even if less accessible to a wider audience.<br /> <br /> Some people don't like the game. I think that was expected. It certainly should have been. The game has no white hats. The best you can hope for in a character is gray. That works for many. That doesn't work for others. People are expressing this and the &quot;proper&quot; response is &quot;I think you haven't grasped the full potential, but I understand the vibe just isn't right for you.&quot; The &quot;big&quot; issues that have been brought up are not debatable (practically speaking, there is no purpose to it). Let people say their peace and you move on. Arguing over how abusive the game is hasn't really solved anything. How about the people that like the game focus on what needs to be fixed? That would really help out. Peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:45:56-07:00","id":547893,"title":"","content":"Mr. McFarland has made an anouncement!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sent a long email to Rich, Rose, and Michelle (the editor of Beast) tonight. I'm not going to go into the contents (yet) because I need to actually have some feedback from folks, but basically it was a proposed batch of changes/fixes to the material, based in large part on the discussions happening here and elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Now, I could be flip and say that these discussions might have happened anyway, or I could be contrite and say that we really want all y'all to love the game so we're changing it, but neither of those things is precisely true. The truth of the matter is: This game is generating discussion. It's generating controversy. It's challenging people. I think that's good...but I also think that some of the criticism that's come up is entirely valid. Beasts do need a more defined struggle and culture. They do need specific things to do. Their relationship with Heroes does require some more scrutiny. <br /> <br /> So: To the people who have read the game and made their opinions clear without being hostile, to the people who have shared what they feel works as well as what doesn't, to to the people who have been constructive with their criticism: Thank you. I tell my authors all the time, &quot;kill your darlings,&quot; but sometimes it's hard to know which darlings to kill without some outside perspective. I won't say that this discussion hasn't stung; it has. I'm a writer and I'm as sensitive as any other writer. But at the same time, as I was scribbling notes in my li'l red notebook last night, I also found myself really getting excited to run Beast (starting up a chronicle when I get back from vacation). <br /> <br /> I think the changes are going to strengthen the game, and I'll be talking with the rest of the team about how best to communicate those changes to the backers and the readers so you'll get a quick sense of what we're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:56:06-07:00","id":547905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547851#post547851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen like, <i>four</i> valid criticisms for the book vs a whole bunch that can only have come from misunderstanding and/or not paying attention to the relevant passages</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to sound rude or aggressive, but if I need to cautiously read 400 pages cover to cover in order to evaluate this game's potential and/or the feelings coming from it, then something's wrong. Something should be adressed so that I don't read 399 pages of things that make me cringe to finally read the last one and understand that this wasn't all that bad after all.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as mechanics go, I don't like the Hunger states to be represented by Conditions. It will drive players to constantly go from satiety 3 to 5 and back again. Non stop. They'll craft the story around the idea that they must find a way to use Atavisms, and then make an easy feed. I know it's not every players that will, but since the Condition system was built to encourage players to resolve them, well then the easiest way to do so is to jump between Satiety 2 and 5 as many times as possible.<br /> <br /> Also, for some odd reason, Satiety is stated to represent the connection that the Beast has with the physical world, with his human self (page 92, first sentence), which honestly makes no sense and is referenced nowhere else. Then there's the Life and Legend (Virtue and Vice) which are supposed to represent the Human and the Monster, but which really don't. Life is the sole mechanical &quot;morality&quot; trait, and it's really not.<br /> <br /> I think what I'm trying to say here is that people (including myself) complain about Beast's Evil-Only tendencies and the counter-argument is that all monsters in the WoD are amoral monsters.<br /> <br /> My point, then, is that this is completelly true, but not mechanically encouraged in their respective games. Sociopath murdering monsters all face consequences both mechanically and in a role-play sense.<br /> <br /> -Vampires lose Humanity and risk Masquerade Breach<br /> -Werewolves risk unbalancing themselves and getting the ire of their Tribe<br /> -Wanton Mages lose Wisdom, causing their Nimbus to grow and become stronger<br /> -Prometheans lose Humanity, getting farther from their goal<br /> -Changelings risk Clarity and getting banned from their Court<br /> -Sin-Eaters risk their sanity whenever they kill someone not deserving<br /> -Hunters lose their Integrity in a downward spiral into madness<br /> -Demons must follow the code of their Cover of risk being targeted by the Eye Of Sauron<br /> -Beasts....get bonus XP<br /> <br /> I think that's really the point that many people dislike. Not the fact that it's dark or grim or an endless cycle of abuse. Simply the fact that trying to be good has nothing to it. At least in Vampire, if you only feed on animals or from blood banks, using your powers as a vigilante, you'll probably be able to go out in the sun, to chat with an old friend and to look at the other players while saying &quot;My Humanity is at 8!&quot;. Sure they get to use their powers more often, can do horrible things without consequences (thanks to Banes) and are more in tune with the Danse Macabre, but the Good-Guy-Vampire still has a feeling of success from a mechanical standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:57:02-07:00","id":547907,"title":"","content":"And now, we wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:03:12-07:00","id":547912,"title":"","content":"Losing Humanity is mechanically encouraged by 2nd edition of Vampire, because any Conditions gained and resolved in service of the story grants Beats. The story is about stuff like falling humanity and managing the Conditions that come along with it.<br /> <br /> While Beast is due for some focusing based on Matt's post, it's pretty clear that fluctuating Hunger is very much a part of the game, so Conditions reflecting levels of Satiety and the resolutions that accompany them seems pretty clearly to be a desired state. Your Hunger is very, very important for a game. Satisfying that hunger, expending Satiety, they want you to do that, hence Conditions which incentivize it.<br /> <br /> If you think these games encourage you to be a bad person solely by granting Beats, you're missing the point. You get Beats when you lose your Integrity, you get them when you keep it. Demons gain Conditions when they risk their Cover and when they lose it. Beats are rewards for playing into and resolving Conditions because doing so <i>adds drama to the story</i>. In all reality, it <i>is </i>the story most of the time.<br /> <br /> If you feel your players are &quot;gaming&quot; the system by playing the game, you can see how that's a little wonky, can't you?<br /> <br /> I really, really hate to play this card, but I think you're thinking &quot;simulationist&quot; when the 2nd edition trends towards &quot;narrativist.&quot; That is, the bad things that happen to characters like Losing Humanity or Integrity or Cover are encouraged because they make story, drama and the game. If you were never losing any of these things, then you're probably not playing the game at all, because the act of going out and doing things necessitates risking all of them. It's considered a <i>good </i>thing, because you're trying to tell a story, and story results from stuff happening, from these things being risked and lost, from the up and down. Beast seems <i>very </i>keen on this, to the degree that Matt said early on that Satiety is likely fluctuating regularly in a given session.<br /> <br /> If you just don't like that, it's fine, but don't make the mistake of thinking it's some kind of exploit or loophole for players to get Teh Sick Beatz.<span style=\"font-size:10px\">(tm) </span> It's part of the game. If you feel like your players are &quot;gaming&quot; hungers and not actually developing story, then don't give them the Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-09-2015, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:15:14-07:00","id":547920,"title":"","content":"Watching my Roommate play Overlord, I couldn't help but notice parallels. What should be a black and white game, with you on the black side, actually turned out to be quite muddled.<br /> <br /> Also, Freemind, your treatise on Satiety is fucking <i>awesome.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.yaylife.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/internet-high-five-place-hand-here-480x444.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:19:28-07:00","id":547922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547912#post547912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing Humanity is mechanically encouraged by 2nd edition of Vampire, because any Conditions gained and resolved in service of the story grants Beats. The story is about stuff like falling humanity and managing the Conditions that come along with it.<br /> <br /> While Beast is due for some focusing based on Matt's post, it's pretty clear that fluctuating Hunger is very much a part of the game, so Conditions reflecting levels of Satiety and the resolutions that accompany them seems pretty clearly to be a desired state. Your Hunger is very, very important for a game. Satisfying that hunger, expending Satiety, they want you to do that, hence Conditions which incentivize it.<br /> <br /> If you think these games encourage you to be a bad person solely by granting Beats, you're missing the point. You get Beats when you lose your Integrity, you get them when you keep it. Demons gain Conditions when they risk their Cover and when they lose it. Beats are rewards for playing into and resolving Conditions because doing so <i>adds drama to the story</i>. In all reality, it <i>is </i>the story most of the time.<br /> <br /> If you feel your players are &quot;gaming&quot; the system by playing the game, you can see how that's a little wonky, can't you?<br /> <br /> I really, really hate to play this card, but I think you're thinking &quot;simulationist&quot; when the 2nd edition trends towards &quot;narrativist.&quot; That is, the bad things that happen to characters like Losing Humanity or Integrity or Cover are encouraged because they make story, drama and the game. If you were never losing any of these things, then you're probably not playing the game at all, because the act of going out and doing things necessitates risking all of them. It's considered a <i>good </i>thing, because you're trying to tell a story, and story results from stuff happening, from these things being risked and lost, from the up and down. Beast seems <i>very </i>keen on this, to the degree that Matt said early on that Satiety is likely fluctuating regularly in a given session.<br /> <br /> If you just don't like that, it's fine, but don't make the mistake of thinking it's some kind of exploit or loophole for players to get Teh Sick Beatz.<span style=\"font-size:10px\">(tm) </span> It's part of the game. If you feel like your players are &quot;gaming&quot; hungers and not actually developing story, then don't give them the Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I could make a suggestion for keeping that kind of play under control, I'd suggest that the game give better rewards for novel behavior, and diminishing returns for habitual acts, in the form of growing penalties to Feeding rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:26:12-07:00","id":547931,"title":"","content":"Well for better or worse Im excited to see how this turns out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:31:22-07:00","id":547935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547893#post547893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. McFarland has made an anouncement!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly why I backed Beast, even though there are some sections that I think need some smoothing over. I love most of the game, and I know Matt had the best of intentions when writing it, so if tons of people said that there were issues with the text, he'd be going back in to find a way to make it work. The amount of love that these people put into their work and into their fans is incredible, so there could be no other possible outcome. I also never ended up backing the Mummy and Demon Kickstarters, the first because I wasn't really into nWoD at the time, and the latter because I wasn't sure about the entire GMC and techgnosis aesthetics. Now I love both of them, they may even be my two favourite gamelines (Prommie 2e will likely change that though). Together, Mummy and Demon actually got me playing nWoD, instead of just skimming the books when I was at friend's. I think that at this point Onyx Path's team has earned my trust, and I have no intention of making a third mistake. I'm backing Beast to the hilt, because even if the text needs some polishing, I know it will be something incredible in the end.<br /> <br /> Just don't change Vancouver at all, cause its awesome. And please make a Vancouver city book!<br /> <br /> <u><b>Edit</b></u>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter Description</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If we pass </span></span></span><b>$90,000</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> of contributions, we will begin the creation of a </span></span></span><b>Beast: the Primordial fiction anthology</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> with three short stories that further explore the characters and stories possible with </span></span></span><b>Beast</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. The PDF and electronic versions of the anthology will be sent to every backer who pledged for a Reward Tier that includes a PDF of </span></span></span><b>Beast: The Primordial</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-09-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:08:22-07:00","id":547965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547893#post547893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. McFarland has made an anouncement!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:17:55-07:00","id":547970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547965#post547965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where was this?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?751112-Beast-the-Primordial-teaser-thread&amp;p=19088152#post19088152\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...2#post19088152</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:14:30-07:00","id":547997,"title":"","content":"Is Beast showing up in the Crossover Sidebars in Dark Eras?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:20:31-07:00","id":548062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547920#post547920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching my Roommate play Overlord, I couldn't help but notice parallels. What should be a black and white game, with you on the black side, actually turned out to be quite muddled.<br /> <br /> Also, Freemind, your treatise on Satiety is fucking <i>awesome.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.yaylife.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/internet-high-five-place-hand-here-480x444.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually gave my screen a high five. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I think beast needs some cleaning up. I think that if they clarified the themes, and the nature of the beasts roles in the WoD, the game would be great. But I do think Satiety is one of the stronger elements of the game and fits quite well. <br /> <br /> Things I think need that clarification are:<ul><li>What is the driving element of the Beast and Heroes origins? A lot of people viewed the story as the beasts going &quot;whoa is us, why does everyone want to kill us&quot; while also being &quot;I kill puppies for the lulz&quot;, and their hatred of the Heroes that hunt them despite knowing they created them. The theme seemed &quot;Eat and don't get killed&quot; and &quot;make friends with the other splats&quot;, with a smattering of other themes at different points.<ul><li>I could have been wrong in my reading, but one of the themes that seemed to be present was the idea that the Beasts are cast in a role by the Primordial Dream, the classic heroes tale. They are the monster, the manifestation of humanities fears, their lair the setting and their role is to be the villain killed by the hero. The tragedy is that they are aware that this is their role, and yet even if they don't play along, every other part of the setting, even their Soul, wants to follow through with the story. So they essentially either have to give in, fight their role and possibly die for their efforts, curl up and surrender to it, or overcome the myth and change the story to make them the protagonist. <br /> <br /> Emphasizing this wouldn't change the setting, the need for satiety, or even the end game. What it would achieve though is giving a constant theme beyond the hunger and struggle to both sate it and control it. It would add the nuance of being the only one who realized they are trapped in a story and who doesn't like how it is supposed to end for them.<ul><li>Whats more, it would help make heroes cleaner while both keeping their traits, creation and even role as victims<ul><li>Heroes are those who was cast as the Hero in the story around the Beast.<ul><li>The reason they are cast is because their soul (their onieros) was exposed to the Beasts soul while it fed in the Astral, and due to their lack of personal identity, their identity gets subsumed into the myth by the primordial dream. This forms a bond with the primordial dream and the story, and as they follow the path the story set out for them, it follows the traditions of the myth. Hence why their powers grow, or their ability to define the Beasts weaknesses with Anathema: it follows the conventions of the mythology that is centered around the Beast.<ul><li>So they are victims just as the Beasts: people drawn in to the role in a living myth by the Soul of the Beast. They just lack an awareness of what this means</li> <li>Whats more, their lack of awareness and certainty of their role in the story irks beasts, as these heroes seem to be people who are killing them because the plot demands it, and the heroes are too weak willed to realize this</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>It would also explain their &quot;all about me&quot; attitude: it is, at least in some sense. They <i>are</i> part of a story, and they are at least innately aware of their role in it as &quot;the hero&quot;. They just don't have much more insight because they are being defined fully by the role, and it controls them as they lack enough spiritual fortitude to realize what they are.</li> <li>It would also explain their lack of characterization. They are people with poor self-identities who are being driven by an epic narrative driven by a realm based on the world of concepts. It is like the gentry almost, turning a human into the role needed. He is a hero, he hunts the monsters because it is what heroes do. The fact that this role is what gave him the drive and unifying focus means that it is the central core of his being, and unless he gains enough integrity to rise above the role and embrace his role as a human being, he basically becomes the hero prince from a story...which is fine in literature and entertainment, but would be unpleasant to deal with in real life.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Then again, I could be full of shit.</li> </ul></li> <li>Clarify what is the beast cultures opinions and what are cold hard facts.<ul><li>Some of this was unclear. I know I read parts where I couldn't tell if I was being told &quot;this is what the beasts believe&quot; and &quot;this is how it is&quot;.</li> </ul></li> <li>Make the crossovers less &quot;easy&quot;.<ul><li>This game is a crossover game, so people being upset by that are missing the point. But the idea of alliances should be something that are not common nor are they something that the cultures on the other side are okay with collectively, if even aware of it. It also should make clear how much insight the Beasts have into the other splats, and how much is their own mythos.</li> </ul></li> <li>The fact that the Beasts are &quot;bad guys&quot;<ul><li>I think this is mostly personal taste</li> <li>That said, I do think the book should clarify that their examples represent the gamut of the types of beasts, from those who use their powers to minimize their harm while others revel in their roles as monsters. And make the point that Beasts are like people: Some are psychopaths, and others are decent people. They just have to deal with a monster whose hunger pushes them towards being the psychopath, meaning there are more of those than in the general human population.</li> </ul></li> <li>Heroes<ul><li>Already touched on this above, but maybe give a less &quot;this is how Beasts see them&quot; and &quot;this is what they are, and the beasts see them as monsters because the Beasts are being killed by these people&quot;.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> (also, I was trapped in clinic without any patients...I had to do something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:24:21-07:00","id":548065,"title":"","content":"I took the time to give Beast a strong reading, and for the most part I definitely enjoy it. 7.8 out of 10.<br /> Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> While I can see some members of the LGBT community identifying with some of the situations Beast brings up, it is clear to me that this was an accidental parallel because they happen to share some bad circumstances. Not an intentional effort by the writers to generate controversy on that front.<br /> <br /> Beasts seem to lack direction beyond just surviving from day to day. Vampires have their politics, Werewolves have their wars, Mages have their exploration, Changelings have their Fetch and their paranoia and their coping / recovery and their courts.<br /> <br /> The relationship with other supernaturals seems very forced and sometimes inappropriate, especially regarding Changelings. The Dark Mother metaphor feels like it should be much more obviously unreliable narrator.<br /> <br /> Some of the powers feel like they really step on the toes of other splats. Primordial Pathways and Skeleton Keys are the biggest example, since any starting Beast can go to the Hedge or one of the Towers if they have some time on their hands to align resonance. This was a really big deal for the respective splats. It's less noticeable for other splats, but I was able to make a Werewolf themed beast that was somewhat better at combat and tracking than a Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 06-10-2015, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:27:55-07:00","id":548069,"title":"","content":"I know I'm late to the party, and I'll keep my thoughts brief:<br /> <br /> I like Beast as a standalone game. I think Beast can support a single non-Beast Supernatural if that splat's player tailors their character to the game.<br /> <br /> I feel the best Beast in X xsplat is either Vampire or Hunter. The themes are fairly close with Vampire and Beasts have to manage Satiety in a way similar to Vampires managing Vitae. More human-friendly Beasts could help Hunters in hunting &quot;evil&quot; Supernaturals in a unique way.<br /> <br /> I feel the Changeling xsplat is workable. Both can influence dreams, both can use each other to feed, and Beasts can consciously choose to be less abusive rather than more to allay the Lost's fears. Beast's can also empathize with the inner them and the outer them not matching. Both also are bound up in the ancient narrative thing.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Beasts are capable of successfully cross-splating with:<ul><li>Sin-eaters - too much of the Sin-eater's job is interacting with Ghosts, something Beats have no ability to do. They're also pretty limited in their ability to enter the Underworld. What's a Krewe going to do with one of the Begotten?</li> <li>Mummies - difference in power levels, difference in goals, the whole Mummy managing memories thing.</li> <li>Werewolves - same issue as with Sin-eaters, how is the Beast supposed to cross over in the <i>Hisil</i>? Interact with Spirits, especially those that haven't manifested? This one isn't too bad, though, because at least the Beast can select a Hunger that can be sated while hunting with Werewolves.</li> <li>Mages - zero ability for Beasts to interact with the Supernal. Zero ability to protect themselves against spells. No real way to help a Cabal investigate a Mystery other than by being a guinea pig. Same power issues that come up with Mummy, but worse because versatility. The least workable, IMO, unless all the Mage players cater to the Beast... in which case why play a Mage game?</li> </ul><br /> The easiest fix for most of these is to give Beasts some way (Atavism?) of interacting with things like Spirits and Ghosts and crossing over into the Shadow or Underworld. Perhaps Nightmares that cause Power Incontinence in Mages and Mummies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:33:25-07:00","id":548075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548069#post548069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest fix for most of these is to give Beasts some way (Atavism?) of interacting with things like Spirits and Ghosts and crossing over into the Shadow or Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordial Pathways are specifically <i>easier</i> to open to other supernatural realms than they are to the material world and Skeleton Key lets you get through any point of entry to another world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-10-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:37:53-07:00","id":548079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=547852#post547852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, that's really good. *Sigh* Alright. I think I'm just missing the days of the social groups, and I'm missing whatever the manifestation of this tension within the Beast community. I keep expecting to read about a Hunger AA-equivalent, or something. Thank you for your time, folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that the beasts society needs some fleshing out. We know they form broods. They can add other splats to these broods...And that is it. There really isn't much in the way how they operate internally. I mean:<ul><li>Vampires fight over blood and political power</li> <li>Mages fight over mysteries, political power and abuses of power</li> <li>Werewolves have whole crusade against the Pure, and have a tendency to be rather violent culturally as a whole</li> <li>The Demons trust no one</li> <li>The changelings have an entire feudal court system, plus other changelings might sell them out to the Fae or take them back themselves</li> <li>Hunters fight each other, thinking they are monsters, or because they don't agree with the tactics used. Even before fighting, they will get into arguments over topics just like humans, especially about what to do with their targets</li> <li>Mummies may fight if their orders demand they do, though Mummy v mummy is rare (though their followers may go back and forth).</li> <li>Prometheans...hold grudges? (Okay, I am tired and ran out ideas)</li> </ul>One of the things Rose and Matt emphasized is that Beast v. Beast was going to be a big component of conflicts. What I don't see is the &quot;why?&quot; in the text. Conflict needs a reason, whether a competition for resources or the threat to the existence of either part or something they cherish. Beasts don't seem to be shown competing for food or other resources. They don't seem to go after one another. The only issue is where the group in the story demands the beast resolve the vampire issue, and he is pissed by this, or the fact that beasts seem to intercede when they note someone is putting them at risk by creating heroes.<br /> <br /> And culturally, there isn't much there in the way of Beast. I don't know how they interact with one another, and have a better idea about how they might integrate with other splats than with one another.<br /> <br /> I am not saying Beasts need the &quot;5 societies&quot; model. Just a bit more to the &quot;how do these things interact?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: An idea, tying back to the idea of emphasizing the mythic arc as being the &quot;higher theme&quot; that transcends the &quot;scare and eat or starve and ravage&quot; day to day theme: Have the Society based on the approaches to the myths and their views on how the Beast should deal with their role as the villain and their Soul's hunger. Sure, the final results are known (Merger, Incarnate and...the other one) but not how the Beasts view their inheritances nor their different takes on their responsibilities as beasts. This means you could add the role of morality as a part of one particular &quot;clans&quot; code, while another thinks that all that matters is being at peace with the Soul, no matter how disgusting it is to achieve said peace. And one could think that Beasts should accept their roles as monsters in the story and enjoy being the villain, another to fight the role, and the third who caves and wants the story to just end already before they hurt anyone else. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-10-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:38:31-07:00","id":548080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548075#post548075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial Pathways are specifically <i>easier</i> to open to other supernatural realms than they are to the material world and Skeleton Key lets you get through any point of entry to another world.</div> </div> </div> </div>! Thank you, I forgot about skeleton keys, I spent a few days digesting each section and forgot.<br /> <br /> So I guess my only real qualms are: their inability to interact with Spirits and Ghosts and their lack of thematic usefulness to Mages or Mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T00:03:36-07:00","id":548114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Mages - zero ability for Beasts to interact with the Supernal. Zero ability to protect themselves against spells. No real way to help a Cabal investigate a Mystery other than by being a guinea pig. Same power issues that come up with Mummy, but worse because versatility. The least workable, IMO, unless all the Mage players cater to the Beast... in which case why play a Mage game?</span> </div> </div> </div>That's something that really stuck out for me. Beasts might be able to blend in with other supernaturals, but it's all but impossible for a Beast to masquerade as a Mage. Even if their aura looks like that of a mage, they still can't imitate any of a Mage's basic powers, nor are they capable of understanding any of a Mage's discussions on the nature or experience of magic, and the first use of an Atavism will immediately give them away, since it's obviously not Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> Moreover, there's an even bigger issue - Mage culture. Mage society is extremely paranoid of rogue Mages. Mages make it a point to study people well before they awaken, and even prevent their awakening if their personality is too dangerous or unstable. They are also highly unlikely to accept a Mage who was indoctrinated by another group first, unless they can be absolutely sure that they're not a danger. Even if a Beast was able to convince a group of Mages that he is a Mage, they'd still be more likely to reject him than to accept him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-10-2015, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T00:24:30-07:00","id":548127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548080#post548080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ! Thank you, I forgot about skeleton keys, I spent a few days digesting each section and forgot.<br /> <br /> So I guess my only real qualms are: their inability to interact with Spirits and Ghosts and their lack of thematic usefulness to Mages or Mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Void is Waiting is a beautiful if a little petty way to surreptitiously deflect spells, and other targeted supernatural powers. And it's not like they can't learn the First Tongue, or see spirits or ghosts already. Translation into Twilight is really the only ability they don't have, but they could learn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T00:42:43-07:00","id":548138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548127#post548127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Void is Waiting is a beautiful if a little petty way to surreptitiously deflect spells, and other targeted supernatural powers. And it's not like they can't learn the First Tongue, or see spirits or ghosts already. Translation into Twilight is really the only ability they don't have, but they could learn it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tapping the Abyss so blatantly is unlikely to endear them to Pentacle Mages (the &quot;default&quot; mages), the Guardians of the Veil would take particular exception. And they still have no way to interact with Mysteries.<br /> <br /> And they can't see spirits or ghosts unless they're manifested, in which case even a Mortal can see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:18:42-07:00","id":548150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548138#post548138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tapping the Abyss so blatantly is unlikely to endear them to Pentacle Mages (the &quot;default&quot; mages), the Guardians of the Veil would take particular exception. And they still have no way to interact with Mysteries.<br /> <br /> And they can't see spirits or ghosts unless they're manifested, in which case even a Mortal can see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't endear them to the Seers either. I imagine even most nameless orders probably wouldn't want anything to do with them. Only Banishers, the Scelesti, and ignorant apostates would be willing to associate with them overtly. Pretty much any other mage who allied with such a Beast and was found out would likely be killed or exiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-10-2015, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:22:47-07:00","id":548152,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm glad to see Matt has been looking carefully at the feedback (although that was expected), and has made a preliminary decision about Beast.<br /> <br /> I'm excited to see what will come out of it, but wary. I'd be lying if I said I wasn't worried, since Beast The Primordial is already a <i>huge</i> book with a lot of content; I can't help but fear that revision of the text to account for some of the valid critiques Matt pointed out might take up space currently dedicated to other important parts. Or on certain details and elaborations to topics in the writing I'm fond of, to be entirely honest.<br /> <br /> However, to reiterate from an earlier post: I do trust the team, and I think OPP is handling the discussion around Beast very well. So I wish them the best of luck with that and look forward to the final result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:25:44-07:00","id":548154,"title":"","content":"I'd say a Beast should be able to reach Twilight/Shadow and therefore interact with all ephemera if they use their Primordial Pathway ability. Not sure how they'd react to Underworld Rivers, though if their gateway powers can't help them cross, then a Sin-Eater with the requisite Psyche probably could walk them across, same as they can with anyone else. Though I wonder if a Beast can walk as many Rivers as they have Lair, their own power stat. Like Changelings, Beasts should be able to pop into Dying Dream under certain circumstances and that seems like a fairly deep Domain of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:50:26-07:00","id":548161,"title":"","content":"Twilight isn't a place, it's a state of matter. <br /> <br /> \u200bBut yeah, the lack of any power to see un-manifested things in the material struck me as a bit of a blind spot. Maybe it was an intentional one though. Beasts can still meet spirits and ghosts, but only on their home turf. They might not even realize that these otherworldly beings can cross over. They have trouble fitting in with mages, but again there's actually a decent justification for that in the text. They don't consider themselves as closely related. Their biggest connection is that they share an ability to access the astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:06:52-07:00","id":548169,"title":"","content":"Another thing that bothered me was the idea of Beast/Changeling crossovers. Changelings are already extremely xenophobic and paranoid, so a Beast associating with them at all is already a pretty big jump. But then you combine that with the fact that Beasts relate more to True Fae than to Changelings, and it seems totally ludicrous that Changelings would accept one into their midst.<br /> <br /> The book tries to justify this by saying that a Beast ally would be a good defense against True Fae hunting parties. Well yeah, but having a True Fae ally would also be a good defense against that, but you certainly don't see any changelings trying to earn favors from True Fae. The way I see it, Beasts are a huge threat and an unknown for Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:13:25-07:00","id":548172,"title":"","content":"True, I imagine a beast telling a changeling that the gentry are their younger siblings, the changelings are going to be &quot;Oh, don't mind that almond taste to that drink I just gave you, it's totally not poison.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:22:24-07:00","id":548174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548169#post548169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are already extremely xenophobic and paranoid</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548169#post548169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts relate more to True Fae than to Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? I think these two facts might be connected.<br /> <br /> And anyway, I like my True Fae complex. You might not see changelings jumping to trust the True Fae, but making deals with them? I can see that happening. They're powerful. Maybe you could get protection from a keeper my making a deal with one of their rivals. It's stupid and risky, but that's never stopped people before now, has it? And a True Fae is capable of being amicable when it suits them. Sure, they'll turn on you in a flash if they get bored, but that might take <i>years</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:54:58-07:00","id":548185,"title":"","content":"Remembered two things I wanted to say about current discussion:<br /> <br /> The text does actually have several examples and mentions of Beasts competing or otherwise coming to blows due to their Hunger. Not saying this to disencourage the notion of elaborating on conflict among Beasts, but it's worth remembering.<br /> <br /> And I don't think the Begotten need to be able to interact with Twilight. Their kinship with ghosts is fainter than with spirits, and they can already access the Shadow and the Underworld. It's also a damned if you do damned if you don't case because some people think they're lacking in not being able to interact with twilight, but some would complain they can do too much if they were able to. Nothing in their nature seems to strongly justify it either (as Elfive pointed out they're closer to the astral rather than the ephemeral), so I wouldn't give them an inherent, universal ability to interact with Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-10-2015, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T03:06:47-07:00","id":548194,"title":"","content":"I have been reading BtP text again, the Heroes section especially, and really think that they are like the Banishers, both in intentions, vibe, and origins. Yeah, they are really a lot similar.<br /> <br /> The difference is though, the Banishers are only a small part of Mage's rogue's gallery, which also consists really well built-up, big-shot enemies of the Seers, the Scelesti, and the Nefandi, all in the core as well. I mean, all those criticism against the Heroes, (I made many of them as well) would just go away if the Heroes were either a) a lot more diverse, scarier, and multi-dimentional, or b) only a part of the line's bigger pool of villains.<br /> <br /> I think Beast can be a better line if they had many different antagonists, including intra-Begotten conflicts, because the Heroes really do look less intimidating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T03:52:23-07:00","id":548232,"title":"","content":"I have a question concerning the dream form of the Beast's soul. Do I understand it correctly that the dream form of a Beast with a low lair trait is rediculously weak ?<br /> <br /> Your soul form may be towering Giant but actually you probably have less health levels in this form than in human form (highest resistance attribute + lair instead of Stamina + 5) ? Your soul form does not have any special abilities other than Atavisms ? The book contains vast sections on strange crossover stuff but does not run a section on abilities for your soul form regardless of the fact that Heros (and sometimes other people) try to follow you to and hunt you down in your lair ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 06-10-2015, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:05:04-07:00","id":548235,"title":"","content":"You got it wrong. Health in Dream Form for Beasts (i.e the Soul) is highest resistance attribute (or Resolve for everyone else except noted otherwise) + attribute maximum (which for normal humans is always 5, and is never less than 5 for any splat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-10-2015, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:11:19-07:00","id":548268,"title":"","content":"It says on page 119, that dream health is Resolve + your attribute maximum, which for humans is 5, but for Beasts can be higher.<br /> <br /> Abilities for the soul are on page 120.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548235#post548235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got it wrong. Health in Dream Form for Beasts (i.e the Soul) is highest resistance attribute (or Resolve for everyone else except noted otherwise) + attribute maximum (which for normal humans is always 5, and is never less than 5 for any splat).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't actually say that health is based on the maximum resistance stat as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-10-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:15:12-07:00","id":548269,"title":"","content":"Plus it can use all of your atavisms, at any level, for free. This can make some beast's souls <i>astoundingly</i> hard to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:16:54-07:00","id":548270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548174#post548174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might not see changelings jumping to trust the True Fae, but making deals with them? I can see that happening. They're powerful. Maybe you could get protection from a keeper my making a deal with one of their rivals. It's stupid and risky, but that's never stopped people before now, has it? And a True Fae is capable of being amicable when it suits them. Sure, they'll turn on you in a flash if they get bored, but that might take <i>years</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationship with True Fae seems superficial at best. They are creatures born of narrative power and driven by narrative desires. Beasts are specifically mentioned as undermining those narratives, <i>&quot;That doesn\u2019t mean they play along, however. Beasts call out narratives. They undermine them. They break them over the heads of Heroes.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Honestly, Beasts should be absolutely terrified of the True Fae and Changelings.<br /> They have to be extremely careful or Talecrafting is going to rock them.<br /> The Heroes are going to win, because the Beast always loses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:18:59-07:00","id":548285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548268#post548268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't actually say that health is based on the maximum resistance stat as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's based on resolve. You ask the soul to roll resolve, what would it roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:28:52-07:00","id":548294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548270#post548270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Beasts should be absolutely terrified of the True Fae and Changelings.<br /> They have to be extremely careful or Talecrafting is going to rock them.<br /> The Heroes are going to win, because the Beast always loses.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Gentry's performance, they are the Jester that Doesn't do what they want or Expect.They do what they Want/Feel, not what the Story tells them.<br /> Going back a page or so... this is the Problem player that the GM had too deal with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T04:29:43-07:00","id":548296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548268#post548268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't actually say that health is based on the maximum resistance stat as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I was mixing it up with the the Soul since it uses the highest resistance attribute as Resistance. Hence Resolve, for most cases.<br /> <br /> ... That's debatable now that I think about it actually, even though the text specifies the Beast's Resolve and even gives an example.<br /> <br /> On a different note, the True Fae are frankly very similar to Beasts. Even down to Hunger there are resemblances: the Gentry may not understand it as Begotten do, but they too are driven to action by their very natures; reliant on /conflict/ to exist separately from the Wyrd, to give their individuality a meaningful edge that justifies it and feeds it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-10-2015, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:34:34-07:00","id":548444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548235#post548235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got it wrong. Health in Dream Form for Beasts (i.e the Soul) is highest resistance attribute (or Resolve for everyone else except noted otherwise) + attribute maximum (which for normal humans is always 5, and is never less than 5 for any splat).</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it, <i>attribute maximum granted by lair,</i> not just <i>lair</i>. Thank you.<br /> <br /> I still don't understand why the Mythic Creature Form is not fleshed out more in this game. They could simply have used the rules for the Beast Incarnate ? The soul never leaves its lair, but in the lair it should have about the same abilities as those described on p. 342 ff. for the Apex. They could have introduced starting form abilities, merits etc. A missed opportunity in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:58:37-07:00","id":548460,"title":"","content":"I think atavisms cover a lot of that. Your beast form has Wings of The Raptor, it can fly whenever. Those &quot;effective&quot; size points Looming presence grants? Not so illusionary in the lair. That Cyclopean Strength? Who needs extra dice when you've got bonus successes on everything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:07:25-07:00","id":548773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548169#post548169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book tries to justify this by saying that a Beast ally would be a good defense against True Fae hunting parties. Well yeah, but having a True Fae ally would also be a good defense against that, but you certainly don't see any changelings trying to earn favors from True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost as though one of these is overtly the worst type of breaking point trigger possible for Clarity and the other is just a Well-Connected Weird Supernatural Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-10-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:15:55-07:00","id":548787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548138#post548138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tapping the Abyss so blatantly is unlikely to endear them to Pentacle Mages (the &quot;default&quot; mages), the Guardians of the Veil would take particular exception. And they still have no way to interact with Mysteries.<br /> <br /> And they can't see spirits or ghosts unless they're manifested, in which case even a Mortal can see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how that power works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 186</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Void Is Waiting (Low-Wisdom Mage) </b><br /> A book that is a universe. A set of mathematical formulae that graph nonexistence. A million chittering, hungry things desperate to be. They\u2019re all out there. And they\u2019re all waiting for you.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The victim\u2019s mind is plunged into a <u>vision</u> of the Abyss, the toxic anti-reality that lurks between the World of Darkness as Beasts know it and the pure realm of abstract symbolism from which mages draw their power. <u>This vision calls to the tiny sliver of the Abyss that lurks in every human soul, drawing that realm\u2019s attention. </u><br /> The Abyss seeks to draw magic into itself in order to fuel its own existence; any time a supernatural power is used in the victim\u2019s vicinity (including by the victim himself if he has such abilities) provokes a Clash of Wills. The victim rolls Resolve + Composure if human, or Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance if not. Success for the victim means the power targets the victim rather than its intended target.<br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>When the victim succeeds on a Clash of Wills triggered by this Nightmare, the user of the supernatural power takes lethal damage equal to the number of successes rolled.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The player may spend multiple Satiety on this effect. For every Satiety spent, the Beast may cause one attempt at activating a supernatural power in the victim\u2019s presence to automatically fail.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Each time the victim absorbs a supernatural effect in the Beast\u2019s presence, it counts as fulfilling the Beast\u2019s Hunger. See Satiety, p. XX, for more information on fulfilling Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast is using an existing connection to The Abyss, essentially forcing a controlled Havoc to manifest. This is really better used to hinder an enemy that has powers of their own than to lightening rod an ally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:24:56-07:00","id":548799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548269#post548269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it can use all of your atavisms, at any level, for free. This can make some beast's souls <i>astoundingly</i> hard to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it just you can use WP for Satiety expenditure? Same as if you are in a resonant location?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:32:30-07:00","id":548807,"title":"","content":"No, the Soul just has access to every Atavism effect at all times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:00:17-07:00","id":548842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548270#post548270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The relationship with True Fae seems superficial at best. They are creatures born of narrative power and driven by narrative desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text calls this as the reason <i>why</i> many (not most, let alone all) Beasts empathise with the Fae.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:06:32-07:00","id":548868,"title":"","content":"Sleeping Beauty was one tough teenager.<br /> <br /> The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots on all Strength related rolls for the remainder of the scene, not just feats of strength. <br /> <br /> That's an automatic hit in melee combat, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:11:22-07:00","id":548912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548807#post548807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Soul just has access to every Atavism effect at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that this makes a Soul with Relentless Hunter functionally indestructible, I feel comfortable saying that the text following the note on Lair Resonance is referencing the [Lair]-times-per-chapter limit on spending Willpower instead of Satiety rather than saying the cost for Satiety Expenditure effects is completely waived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:33:56-07:00","id":549000,"title":"","content":"That's about the only one that it doesn't seem to work with. Everything else makes perfect sense, and agrees with the text.<br /> <br /> I actually meant to ask about that, but I forgot amid all the discussion. Is the Satiety Use of Relentless Hunter meant to only work once per scene like the Low Satiety effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:36:50-07:00","id":549004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548868#post548868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleeping Beauty was one tough teenager.<br /> <br /> The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots on all Strength related rolls for the remainder of the scene, not just feats of strength.<br /> <br /> That's an automatic hit in melee combat, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they don't Dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:39:29-07:00","id":549006,"title":"","content":"At low Lair full Relentless Hunter would only grant something just over Gauru-tier regeneration. That's tough, but not insurmountably so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:44:50-07:00","id":549010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548912#post548912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that this makes a Soul with Relentless Hunter functionally indestructible, I feel comfortable saying that the text following the note on Lair Resonance is referencing the [Lair]-times-per-chapter limit on spending Willpower instead of Satiety rather than saying the cost for Satiety Expenditure effects is completely waived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:50:02-07:00","id":549019,"title":"","content":"Except I don't think the soul can spend your willpower or satiety on its own. So in order for &quot;the soul has access to all levels of its atavisms&quot; to be true they can't cost anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:07:50-07:00","id":549033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549019#post549019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except I don't think the soul can spend your willpower or satiety on its own. So in order for &quot;the soul has access to all levels of its atavisms&quot; to be true they can't cost anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Soul's access to Atavism effects is described in two places: the Soul Itself sidebar on page 120, where it notes that the Lair always counts as a Lair-resonant location immediately afterwards, and at the end of the Lair Resonance section on page 157. Neither of these sections specifically state that the Satiety Expenditure effect of the Beast's Atavisms are costless when the Soul uses them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Incarnate's Superior Atavism bonus makes little sense if taken in combination with their ability to draw down the Lair anywhere; if this wasn't a change to the basic way things worked, it wouldn't be a demarcated power.<br /> <br /> I'd think a life-or-death struggle happening in your soul would be sufficient to warrant a couple points of Willpower being spent for your Soul to use its scenelongs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:14:06-07:00","id":549039,"title":"","content":"If it was that simple to call down their lair anywhere they wouldn't need the ability to transform at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:34:33-07:00","id":549094,"title":"","content":"Do you gain a Beat when you resolve the Satiety Conditions, moving from one to another?<br /> <br /> 'Each Condition has criteria for resolution. Take a Beat when you resolve a Condition.'<br /> <br /> These guys are Beat machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:41:13-07:00","id":549097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548787#post548787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how that power works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast is using an existing connection to The Abyss, essentially forcing a controlled Havoc to manifest. This is really better used to hinder an enemy that has powers of their own than to lightening rod an ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's a blatant connection to the Abyss, like I said. Thanks for clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-10-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:53:58-07:00","id":549320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549097#post549097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's a blatant connection to the Abyss, like I said. Thanks for clarifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a Blatant Connection too the Abyss that ALL Mages and every Human has even if they don't want too admit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:54:24-07:00","id":549321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=548787#post548787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how that power works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast is using an existing connection to The Abyss, essentially forcing a controlled Havoc to manifest. This is really better used to hinder an enemy that has powers of their own than to lightening rod an ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter. Any use of the Abyss tears apart the fabric of reality, and would get the Beast marked as kill-on-sight by most mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549320#post549320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a Blatant Connection too the Abyss that ALL Mages and every Human has even if they don't want too admit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages (and other supernaturals) don't have it, only Sleepers. And it really doesn't matter either way because screwing with the Abyss intentionally is still going to get you branded as evil and a major threat to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-10-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:01:10-07:00","id":549328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549320#post549320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a Blatant Connection too the Abyss that ALL Mages and every Human has even if they don't want too admit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just asking, but don't mages lose their connection to the abyss upon awakening? And other supernaturals, which is why they act as sleepwalkers in regards to paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:04:04-07:00","id":549329,"title":"","content":"Not sure About 2nd Ed but i was under the Impression they kept the connection, it's Weakened, but there. And Mages would hate too Admit it.<br /> Could be Wrong though<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549321#post549321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages (and other supernaturals) don't have it, only Sleepers. And it really doesn't matter either way because screwing with the Abyss intentionally is still going to get you branded as evil and a major threat to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, Fair enough, and yeah, I can see that any Tampering with the Abyss is bad asfar as Mages are concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-10-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:55:30-07:00","id":549403,"title":"","content":"These two Atavisms, with their normal effect basically summed up.<br /> <br /> <b>Alien Allure</b>: Adds Lair dots to all Social rolls where looks or attractiveness helps, cumulative with Striking Looks. Always starts with a Good Impression. If Beast has caused harm to target, must wait a day for it to work.<br /> <br /> <b>Siren's Treacherous Song</b>: Add Lair dots as a bonus on all Social rolls involving speech or song. Always counts as tempting their Vice whenusing Social maneuvering rules. Voice carries unnaturally well.<br /> <br /> Since you're not confined to looking good or talking in a single act, can these two stack? Specifically adding Lair dots as a bonus on Social rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T15:00:21-07:00","id":549408,"title":"","content":"Siren's also allows you to do perfect vocal mimicry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T15:01:27-07:00","id":549409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549408#post549408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siren's also allows you to do perfect vocal mimicry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I overlooked that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T15:47:42-07:00","id":549462,"title":"","content":"What do they do? Why do we care? Heroes seem....off. I think the satiety rules and tweeking the relationship between the Primordial, Beast and Hero could help...<br /> <br /> The Satiety rules(specifically the bit where one loses control of the Primordial if ones does not feed it) reminds be of an OWOD story(of a dubious nature) about the Baali. That most of the horrific things they did were to keep the Great Old Ones( or whatever) asleep with lovely dreams of atrocity so as they don't wake up and actually get on with some mega-death horror. Better to do nasty things to thousands than billions and the magical perks arent bad either. Anyway, Got me thinking that the Beast could have a bit more justification for the things they do. <br /> <br /> &quot;If this primordial wasnt chained to me it would be tearassing across the pyschosphere doing G-M knows what to countless peoples dreams. So me being a dick once a week is a pretty good deal all things considered. &quot;<br /> <br /> Of course its a slippery slope as the Beast will grows comfortable with its role and it justification it would probably slide...downward. But even then when faced with the reality of its actions and an angry Hero its justifications would hold, and the fact that killing the beast only sets the primordial free and even if it ends up chained to some other beast in the future, who can say if the next beast will be as kind and humane as you try to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Hero! I think I'm doing a pretty good job of keeping a lid on this particular can of primordial evil. Killing me will just let it out...Could you do a better job?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which leads me to heroes. Heroes need to have made a choice. It may have been a bad and uninformed choice, but seems to be a sticking point for a number of people. Something is finding people who have had run ins with beasts. Contacting them in their dreams and offering a faustian bargain.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll take away your self doubt and give you superpowers if you take up the fiery sword and hunt those things that made you feel small.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something want the Primordial cut free from the Beasts(maybe its the Primordial themselves, or Enchidna) and they are exalting Heroes and and convincing them that they are saving the world, when in fact they are jail breaking ancient evils.<br /> <br /> TLDR Beasts are primordial prison cells. Heroes have been tricked into jailbreaking them. Beasts have a purpose and shred of justification and Heroes have some responsibility for being where they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2161-nadir","name":"Nadir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:02:41-07:00","id":549474,"title":"","content":"That'd be kind of a very different game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:29:26-07:00","id":549502,"title":"","content":"Personally I think a lack of distinct factions is no reason for the game to not focus on inter-beast conflicts. They're pretty individualistic, so it wouldn't make sense to name any groups but nonetheless you can definitely divide beasts between those who try not to hurt people and those who revel in their monstrosity. Maybe you could have a brood that goes around feeding by taking out the sort of beasts Heroes <i>think</i> they're fighting all the time? And of course there's the Merged beasts, who honestly probably need to be put down a fair amount of the time.<br /> <br /> There's your &quot;kill me and it'll get worse&quot; angle. The main problem with heroes is they can't tell the difference between beasts who feed as humanely as possible (and I could come up with about a dozen ways each hunger could be sated in an acceptable manner) and those who act like unrepentant monsters. In fact they're more likely to go for the nicer ones. And the nicer ones are the ones less likely to kill them on sight, which does nothing to deter them. So really, the biggest problem with Heroes is that they ultimately don't solve the problem they dedicate their lives to solving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:01:41-07:00","id":549548,"title":"","content":"Philosophies would be good. I'm having difficulty relating to Beasts. They seem so dehumanized. I know it's there somewhere (humanity), but I have a hard time seeing it. I would think Maleficent would be a Beast tale. I tend to think the kings make good examples of Heroes. The fact that I feel like I'm stretching things to fit Maleficent as a Beast/Hero relationship is what leaves me scratching my head about the text given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:02:24-07:00","id":549549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549321#post549321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't matter. Any use of the Abyss tears apart the fabric of reality, and would get the Beast marked as kill-on-sight by most mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mages (and other supernaturals) don't have it, only Sleepers. And it really doesn't matter either way because screwing with the Abyss intentionally is still going to get you branded as evil and a major threat to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why, pray tell, does that Nightmare affect all supernatural powers and does not restrict its targeting to Sleepers? Plus, who said it <i>really </i>was the Abyss they were tapping, anyway? And why should we even care that one splat doesn't actuate the driving elements of another's plots anyway? Wouldn't proving that there are some things that the Awakened definitively aren't aware of be a Mystery in of itself? Does crossover require everyone involved pursuing the same things for the same reasons? No. It doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:36:32-07:00","id":549567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549548#post549548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophies would be good. I'm having difficulty relating to Beasts. They seem so dehumanized. I know it's there somewhere (humanity), but I have a hard time seeing it. I would think Maleficent would be a Beast tale. I tend to think the kings make good examples of Heroes. The fact that I feel like I'm stretching things to fit Maleficent as a Beast/Hero relationship is what leaves me scratching my head about the text given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair their wasn't much philosophy used in some games such as demon or in werewolf unless you wanted to use philosophy in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-10-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T19:37:12-07:00","id":549599,"title":"","content":"So, basically, we want:<br /> <br /> -Nuanced heroes at various stages of corruption, corruption coming from our own existence, and these heroes are all trying to hurt us in various ways<br /> -Many different Antagonists including the monsters of monsters, interesting mortals, fanatics and even the creatures of nightmare given form<br /> -Philosophies to describe the various ways one can go about being a monster<br /> -Playing a game of being the outsider, outcast, the person that always was a monster<br /> -Playing a game with strong ties to the LGBT<br /> -Playing a game which reverts the genre of Monster-Hero<br /> -A game in which morality is vague and fluctuent<br /> <br /> So...Why aren't we all playing Promethean already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T19:39:47-07:00","id":549601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549549#post549549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why, pray tell, does that Nightmare affect all supernatural powers and does not restrict its targeting to Sleepers? Plus, who said it <i>really </i>was the Abyss they were tapping, anyway? And why should we even care that one splat doesn't actuate the driving elements of another's plots anyway? Wouldn't proving that there are some things that the Awakened definitively aren't aware of be a Mystery in of itself? Does crossover require everyone involved pursuing the same things for the same reasons? No. It doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I am going to go a bit Meta on this, but I hope it helps with this discussion a bit. <br /> <br /> Kinship seems to be tied to the the Primordial dream tapping into the Astral Reflections that correspond to the different splats. The Astral Realms is a conceptual space, where the collective ideas of humanity and the concepts of the world find representation. Everything from realms representing the whole of humanity, from different religions, political ideas, philosophies, fears, dreams, etc. exist in the Temenos, and the Anima Mundi is reflection of the concepts of the world itself. And while more personal, each onieros contains different reflections and symbolic representations of that person.<br /> <br /> My theory is that when a Beast is calling on Kinship powers, they are connecting the Primordial Dream to Realms representative of the other splats and entities, channel concepts related to those supernaturals through the lens of the Primordial Dream. If I was a mage, I would describe it as akin to how mages use magic, but utilizing Astral Symbolism rather than Supernal Symbols, with the Primordial Dream forging those connections by utilizing sympathy between the Supernatural that the Beast had developed a kinship bond with and the respective Astral concepts and/or realm (while the Beast hearing this would roll his eyes and wonder why mages overthink and try to explain everything). This is why nightmares aren't just &quot;replicate a power&quot; but draws on concepts associated with the splats in question Thus, it is going to not quite follow the same rules, or even be the same energies, as they aren't tapping into the original source of those things but the astral representation instead. Whats more, they can only draw on the concepts that resonate with the Primordial Dream, meaning that their connections and applications will always be through the lens of being tied to primordial fear. <br /> <br /> So for the concept of the Nightmare that replicates the effects of the Abyss:<br /> This nightmare is drawing on the Astral concepts of the Abyss <i>as it is perceived by mages</i> and then projecting this astral concept. The vision of the abyss and the effects aren't actually drawing on the Abyssal spark or abyss, but the ideas of these things and what they represent to mages, and using these astral concepts to create an effect that duplicates these concepts more broadly. Thus, you have a force that creates something that embodies the traits of havoc but effecting all of the supernatural, not just the supernal magics, because it isn't actually the abyss but the astral concept of the Abyss. <br /> <br /> I also look at this as to why Demons don't really have kinship: they lack any real Astral Reflections. They destroy a human soul and merge with the metaphysical void, and the soul is what connects most to the Astral. Furthermore, discussion have made the God Machine and its products as metaphysical manifestations of human concepts of technology, logistics and infrastructure that developed an alien intelligence, akin to the astral entities, but existing in the material realm. Thus, it lacks a true astral representation, as do the demons since they are derived from it. While they can invade the Astral, they don't have a conceptual space reflecting them and their mythos that can be tapped by the beasts connection to them, as they themselves are that conceptual space.<br /> <br /> And Beasts don't really look at it this way at all, as their own ideas of the Astral beyond the primoridal dream is limited to whatever exposure they get following a mage or chamber into it. <br /> <br /> Though, this is is all just conjecture and I could be completely wrong. Beast makes me seek connections based on other game lines, and I will admit that I do turn to mage since the Astral is their thing (The Beasts may exist in it, but the Mages can go anywhere they want in it). <br /> <br /> Tl<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />NR- My theory is that the thing tapped into is the Astral Concept of the Abyss, which the Beast draws on after being with a mage whose nature associates him with said concept and allows the beast to call on it through their kinship. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:07:46-07:00","id":549625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549599#post549599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Why aren't we all playing Promethean already?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I am, but what I want from Beast is to explore a game focused on our relationship to our own primal fears, rather than experimenting to discover what it means to be human. As well as a game rooted in kinship rather than isolation. So there's a lot to be gained here that Promethean doesn't do.<br /> <br /> On the LGBT theme comment - I'm all for strong LGBT representation in the games, amongst all supernatural types and mortals - but I'm honestly tired of &quot;monsters as metaphor for queer identity&quot; or any other minority group. It doesn't actually work. Note that I'm not saying this is what Beast does, I'm responding to people trying to cram it in that hole. I think it was True Blood that destroyed that trope for me once and for all. You can't use something that IT'S COMPLETELY REASONABLE FOR PEOPLE TO FEAR as a metaphor for a people oppressed by unjust fear.<br /> <br /> Also, while this isn't so much an issue with rpgs, in other cases, all too often genre media uses supernatural/alien/whatever metaphor for sexual or racial politics in order to tell a story about racism... with white central protagonists - or a story about homophobia... with straight central protagonists, and so on. I'm looking at you X-Men movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-10-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:08:13-07:00","id":549626,"title":"","content":"Thing is, it's also been pointed out in Summoners that anything <i>like </i>the Abyss is <i>of </i>the Abyss, so it makes little difference.<br /> <br /> There's a reason 2E acamoth live in the Astral image of the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:10:05-07:00","id":549627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549502#post549502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think a lack of distinct factions is no reason for the game to not focus on inter-beast conflict</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the text address whether Beasts can prey on each other to feed? That might be something worth adding or playing up to bring more focus on inter-Beast conflict. Tyrants dominating multiple Broods under their rule. Nemeses policing Beasts for how they feed. Powerful Collectors extracting tribute from the hoards of others. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:17:36-07:00","id":549633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549627#post549627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the text address whether Beasts can prey on each other to feed? That might be something worth adding or playing up to bring more focus on inter-Beast conflict. Tyrants dominating multiple Broods under their rule. Nemeses policing Beasts for how they feed. Powerful Collectors extracting tribute from the hoards of others. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>does this work PG 28<br /> <br /> She doesn\u2019t care for the label;<br /> she doesn\u2019t look at the world as her colonial playground. But she does love her trophies, the<br /> antlers and ivory and even skulls she\u2019s torn from their flesh by her own two hands. She doesn\u2019t<br /> like weapons. She lives for the hunt and the kill, the contest of predator against the closest thing<br /> to a monster that isn\u2019t her kin. Maybe one day she\u2019ll snap and take another Beast\u2019s head for her<br /> wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:20:20-07:00","id":549635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549625#post549625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while this isn't so much an issue with rpgs, in other cases, all too often genre media uses supernatural/alien/whatever metaphor for sexual or racial politics in order to tell a story about racism... with white central protagonists - or a story about homophobia... with straight central protagonists, and so on. I'm looking at you X-Men movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually in the one of the comics of x men they featured a gay marriage on the cover of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:47:00-07:00","id":549718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549626#post549626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, it's also been pointed out in Summoners that anything <i>like </i>the Abyss is <i>of </i>the Abyss, so it makes little difference.<br /> <br /> There's a reason 2E acamoth live in the Astral image of the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I would go that far, and I am not sure what in summoners you are referring to. It also doesn't seem to jive with the cosmology. There are plenty of things that are alien and &quot;like the abyss&quot; that don't have origins from it, even in that book (looking at you, Men in Black). <br /> <br /> Yes, the Abyss is an anti-reality. But what I was talking about is the <i>idea</i> of it that mages have, the concept of it in their cosmology, the impact it has on their psyche. These things are based in reality, even if the thing that triggered these thoughts and concepts <i>isn't</i>. It is like how you have Astral Mars reflecting the actual mars, but also &quot;Mars as humans have perceived it&quot; which includes UFOs and Wars. I am not talking about drawing on the Orroboros, the actual Astral manifestation of the Abyss, but a realm or concept of the temenos, or possibly even a mages Onieros, that represents their perceptions of the abyss and mage's view of that horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:48:24-07:00","id":549720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549627#post549627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the text address whether Beasts can prey on each other to feed? That might be something worth adding or playing up to bring more focus on inter-Beast conflict. Tyrants dominating multiple Broods under their rule. Nemeses policing Beasts for how they feed. Powerful Collectors extracting tribute from the hoards of others. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the 2 Incarnates described explicitely does it. I don't see why other Beasts couldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:05:08-07:00","id":549732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549635#post549635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually in the one of the comics of x men they featured a gay marriage on the cover of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said X-Men movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:06:24-07:00","id":549734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549720#post549720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the 2 Incarnates described explicitely does it. I don't see why other Beasts couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out that the modifiers chart for the Feeding roll only applies a penalty for supernatural targets that you've got direct or indirect Family Ties to, and that despite their qualification for a lot of Kinship abilities, the Begotten explicitly can't have Family Ties.<br /> <br /> Basically the only means of gaining Satiety that explicitly can't be channeled through other supernatural beings is Inflicting Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:16:14-07:00","id":549740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549549#post549549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why, pray tell, does that Nightmare affect all supernatural powers and does not restrict its targeting to Sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mage's abyssal powers aren't restricted to sleepers either. Sleepers are what trigger the Abyss normally, but once you've drawn the Abyss down directly, anything goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, who said it <i>really </i>was the Abyss they were tapping, anyway? And why should we even care that one splat doesn't actuate the driving elements of another's plots anyway? Wouldn't proving that there are some things that the Awakened definitively aren't aware of be a Mystery in of itself? Does crossover require everyone involved pursuing the same things for the same reasons? No. It doesn't. </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is absolutely core to the entire concept of Mages. It's the fundamental force that drives the theme of hubris. Removing or handwaving it would be like ignoring the fact that Vampires drink human blood. They just become unbridled superheroes. Everything that made them a monster is erased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:32:38-07:00","id":549756,"title":"","content":"Is it mentioned anywhere how long Satiety Expenditure lasts for Atavisms? A lot of the Satiety Expenditure powers like Looming Presence sound like they should be scene-long, but it doesn't seem to be specified anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:32:43-07:00","id":549757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549626#post549626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, it's also been pointed out in Summoners that anything <i>like </i>the Abyss is <i>of </i>the Abyss, so it makes little difference.<br /> <br /> There's a reason 2E acamoth live in the Astral image of the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, we're resorting to corner cases and system mastery to justify dismissing crossover as unplayable?<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, can anybody think of a good reason for a given splat to not team up with a Beast that is not contingent upon having absolute character knowledge of how the nWoD universe works, or of what the impressions section of Beast, or any other part, has to say about the splat in question?<br /> <br /> I can understand if, as a player or Storyteller, you don't want to run an explicit crossover with Beast. It's your game. But don't mistake evocative language for trustworthy language, or statements of prevailing opinion as dogma, let alone policy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:34:15-07:00","id":549758,"title":"","content":"I was saying philosophies instead of factions common in other game lines, a little something to emphasize the human side of a Beast. I don't know. I'm just not seeing the humanity of Beasts coming through. The perspective of the Soul is well covered. I think that part is extremely clear. Players need something to relate to on the human side though. I'm fairly certain the players are going to be human after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:37:04-07:00","id":549760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549758#post549758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saying philosophies instead of factions common in other game lines, a little something to emphasize the human side of a Beast. I don't know. I'm just not seeing the humanity of Beasts coming through. The perspective of the Soul is well covered. I think that part is extremely clear. Players need something to relate to on the human side though. I'm fairly certain the players are going to be human after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Life/Legends I find it strange no mentioned this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:43:53-07:00","id":549761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549740#post549740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage's abyssal powers aren't restricted to sleepers either. Sleepers are what trigger the Abyss normally, but once you've drawn the Abyss down directly, anything goes.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is absolutely core to the entire concept of Mages. It's the fundamental force that drives the theme of hubris. Removing or handwaving it would be like ignoring the fact that Vampires drink human blood. They just become unbridled superheroes. Everything that made them a monster is erased.</div> </div> </div> </div>You miss what I was asking. If the Abyss is the reason that Mage spells malfunction, and it is, and the presence of the Abyss within a Sleeper's soul is why Disbelief happens, and it is too, than why does this power work on other Supernatural powers, even those cast upon or by those that have no connection to the Abyss?<br /> <br /> And I was not saying to remove the Abyss from the setting. All I was asking is why should the value of a splat in a crossover be measured in how well it supports the other splats plot points? Why does Beast have to interact with Mysteries at all?<br /> <br /> Also: where in the Beast draft are there any consequences related to this power that look like anything at all to do with using the Abyss? I don't have any Mage material related to the Abyss or 2e in front of me, so I can't tell if this is a legit concern or simply a literal reading of the power's fluff text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:55:33-07:00","id":549774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549761#post549761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You miss what I was asking. If the Abyss is the reason that Mage spells malfunction, and it is, and the presence of the Abyss within a Sleeper's soul is why Disbelief happens, and it is too, than why does this power work on other Supernatural powers, even those cast upon or by those that have no connection to the Abyss?<br /> <br /> And I was not saying to remove the Abyss from the setting. All I was asking is why should the value of a splat in a crossover be measured in how well it supports the other splats plot points? Why does Beast have to interact with Mysteries at all?<br /> <br /> Also: where in the Beast draft are there any consequences related to this power that look like anything at all to do with using the Abyss? I don't have any Mage material related to the Abyss or 2e in front of me, so I can't tell if this is a legit concern or simply a literal reading of the power's fluff text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the things added in beast besides demon relies on 2e books but the problem is we don't have any of the books for 2e minus demon mage, and vampire take for example beast and changeling PG 316: Around the Makara, the Hedge becomes a sucking mire,replete with hidden depths and sinkholes that can swallow the unwary traveler whole. Use the rules found in Changeling: The Lost Second Edition problem is we don't have Changeling 2e or Mage 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:56:17-07:00","id":549775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549757#post549757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, we're resorting to corner cases and system mastery to justify dismissing crossover as unplayable?<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, can anybody think of a good reason for a given splat to not team up with a Beast that is not contingent upon having absolute character knowledge of how the nWoD universe works, or of what the impressions section of Beast, or any other part, has to say about the splat in question?<br /> <br /> I can understand if, as a player or Storyteller, you don't want to run an explicit crossover with Beast. It's your game. But don't mistake evocative language for trustworthy language, or statements of prevailing opinion as dogma, let alone policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons and Beasts. They can't form kinships and Beast seem to really not like them...So they may not team up :P The book pretty much says so, though it is nice enough to give us examples of instances that <i>might</i> make them team up, but also why they would make great antagonists.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I get punchy while on call. I get what you are saying. I will say that Beast may need to make sure its tone is more &quot;beasts think this is the case&quot; versus being the nWoD know it alls (I mean, mages arent right and they went to college for this stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but I think none of that precludes crossovers. Just look at Hunter and its portrayal of mages and their powers compared to actual awakened. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549740#post549740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage's abyssal powers aren't restricted to sleepers either. Sleepers are what trigger the Abyss normally, but once you've drawn the Abyss down directly, anything goes.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is absolutely core to the entire concept of Mages. It's the fundamental force that drives the theme of hubris. Removing or handwaving it would be like ignoring the fact that Vampires drink human blood. They just become unbridled superheroes. Everything that made them a monster is erased.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I pointed out, it could be they are replicating the effects of the Abyss based on the mages deep connection to it informing the Beast's Soul as to its conceptual nature. The actual force that is felt and acting on the target is like any other nightmare: Projections of the Primordial Dream, except these draw on the nightmares and dark aspects associated with the Astral Concepts of mages. The text is describing what the person feels and experiences using the terminology of what the effect replicates, because it is replicating the <b>terror </b><i>that</i> <i>a mage experiences when his magic has paradox, </i>and bring that into full effect. <br /> <br /> I mean, this fits the other nightmares. The ones that are available without kinship are tied to basic human fears, flaws and sinister elements of humanity, making the fears so real they physically manifest: &quot;all your teeth falling out&quot; plays up the fear of aging and feeling old that it literally makes that fear manifest. Kinship powers seem to draw on those traits (human fears, flaws and sinister elements) of the supernatural, and then making them universal fears, just like aging. <br /> <br /> It is way to balance the cosmology without violating either one's settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T22:11:51-07:00","id":549782,"title":"","content":"Freemind, I agree with a whole lot of what you've said here.<br /> <br /> However, I don't consider Demon a corner case precisely because there are canonical, and easily understood, reasons why they just don't work well together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T22:27:27-07:00","id":549787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549782#post549782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freemind, I agree with a whole lot of what you've said here.<br /> <br /> However, I don't consider Demon a corner case precisely because there are canonical, and easily understood, reasons why they just don't work well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I was being punchy. It was intentionally evoking the canon &quot;these don't work&quot; since it was intentionally ignoring the actual point of the question just so I could be a bit of a smartass. Hence it leading into my actual points.<br /> <br /> Also, 2 quick follow ups. The fact that the Nightmare uses the phrasing &quot;This vision calls to the tiny sliver of the Abyss that lurks in every human soul, drawing that realm\u2019s attention&quot; means that it does seem to be actually evoking the real abyss via the abyssal shard with a vision of it. I interpret that thought the lens I described, but it does indicate that the actual a abyss is what is being called upon. <br /> <br /> And everything is a Mystery to Mage. They want to know it all, and anything offers insight. Doesn't mean they know everything or solve all the Mysteries...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-11-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T00:57:37-07:00","id":549868,"title":"","content":"An issue is that Nightmares seem inconsistent with respects to how &quot;real&quot; they are. Behold, My True Form! can potentially turn someone into real stone. You Are Drowning (the hypothetical Nightmare mentioned on page 174) can leave the victim with real seawater in their lungs. You Are Meat, which nominally only inflicts the <i>sensation </i>of soullessness (thus allowing it to work on victims regardless of whether they're even <i>supposed </i>to have souls), doesn't work on Beasts because &quot;their Souls are far too powerful.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T01:28:39-07:00","id":549887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549868#post549868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An issue is that Nightmares seem inconsistent with respects to how &quot;real&quot; they are. Behold, My True Form! can potentially turn someone into real stone. You Are Drowning (the hypothetical Nightmare mentioned on page 174) can leave the victim with real seawater in their lungs. You Are Meat, which nominally only inflicts the <i>sensation </i>of soullessness (thus allowing it to work on victims regardless of whether they're even <i>supposed </i>to have souls), doesn't work on Beasts because &quot;their Souls are far too powerful.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual description at the head of the Nightmares section actually explains that.Essentially the part about them that isn't real is that others can't see or be effected by one person's Nightmare. Other than that the Nightmare is real. Essentially they are real to the person they are effecting thus why &quot;You are Drowning&quot; can cause a person to actually have sea water in their lungs. As for why &quot;You are Meat*&quot; can't effect Beasts well I'm guessing it is more that The Begotten have to deal with the fact that their soul rampages. Basically the soul of a Beast is more disconnected than that of most other splats and will very quickly remind you of it's presence if it wasn't in a food coma at the time you were subjected to it.<br /> <br /> *I think general consensus seems to be that it could use some tweaking, as it seems far more powerful than it was likely intended to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T01:31:39-07:00","id":549888,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to suppress a soul that can bite your face off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T02:07:55-07:00","id":549912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549888#post549888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult to suppress a soul that can bite your face off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that DaveB mentioned somewhere else that a Beast and its soul are so closely connected that stealing their soul kills them outright. So suppressing it would have a somewhat different result than for anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T03:48:58-07:00","id":549944,"title":"","content":"<b>Freemind</b> (Highfive) for the subtle &quot;Mages are the family members who went to college&quot; joke.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Beast/Mage crossover I am just thrilled at the prospect of running a 2E Beast/Mage game in the near future. From that I've read both games have a delightful running theme about exploring the world's mysteries and understanding how one's actions affect the world around them. Really loved the Banisher/Hero paralell and can't wait to see the changes made to them in 2E Awakening. But most of all I can't wait for the first time a Mage loses Wisdom thanks to aiding a Beast in indulging their Hunger. Thanks to Beast's morality system being purely reactionary to the players actions rather than immediate they only have rewards to reap when the Mages begin to realize that these Begotten are bound by no higher code other than their endless hunger. So excited! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T05:19:25-07:00","id":549972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549757#post549757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, we're resorting to corner cases and system mastery to justify dismissing crossover as unplayable?</div> </div> </div> </div>A) That isn't what I was saying at all,<br /> <br /> B) It's not a corner case so much as lore, and by the looks of it going to be right there in the new corebook,<br /> <br /> C) It's a single Nightmare, one a Beast might never develop,<br /> <br /> D) Even if they did, I can see mages deciding the play with fire anyway, as they are wont to do. The Abyss isn't Chaos, you don't turn into a Scelesti simply by knowing or existing near it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:18:06-07:00","id":550082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=549972#post549972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) That isn't what I was saying at all,<br /> <br /> B) It's not a corner case so much as lore, and by the looks of it going to be right there in the new corebook,<br /> <br /> C) It's a single Nightmare, one a Beast might never develop,<br /> <br /> D) Even if they did, I can see mages deciding the play with fire anyway, as they are wont to do. The Abyss isn't Chaos, you don't turn into a Scelesti simply by knowing or existing near it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That was a thoughtful response. It had just upset me how flippant people were getting about Mage/Beast crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:04:15-07:00","id":550234,"title":"","content":"Ookay.. finally read it back to back and... I am really less than impressed.<br /> <br /> - Like a lot of people has pointed out, the Hero mechanic IS really flawed in its contexts and analogies, that leads to really unfortunate implications.<br /> - Even without that, the Heroes are really underwhelming and unentertaining as antagonists go. And they are the only antagonists in the book.<br /> - Intra-Begotten society is almost never visited, despite the line's emphasis on 'family.'<br /> - Despite the developers' goals, Beast is actually the line that is least crossover viable game. This actually killed all enthusiasm for me.<br /> <br /> - EDIT: and yeah, immune to disquiet, immune to multitudes of mind control effects, immune to soul pacts, because their souls are friggin strong?<br /> What the hell? The Mary Sue quotient of this is reaching DtF level.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am still going to back it (whole lot less money than I was planning though) , if only for arts and fictions or maybe some antagonist ideas, (being Beasts) but I am likely never play it, and never allow it if I run as a storyteller. Unless Matt really do something about those problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:25:40-07:00","id":550242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550234#post550234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Despite the developers' goals, Beast is actually the line that is least crossover viable game. This actually killed all enthusiasm for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate? I thought the crossover viability was extremely high given the number of mechanics that encourage and support it, like Family Ties, Family Dinner, and Mother's Kiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:31:22-07:00","id":550250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550242#post550242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you elaborate? I thought the crossover viability was extremely high given the number of mechanics that encourage and support it, like Family Ties, Family Dinner, and Mother's Kiss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, there are mechanics, but all those mechanics are making Beasts cooler at the expense of literally making other splats as &quot;little brothers/sisters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not only that, Beasts don't add to other splats' themes by being added into their games, and often takes away key themes. Take Promethian, Changeling and Vampire for example.<br /> And also, the mechanic that states that the first impressions are 'always good?' Hardly any logic behind it, (often counterproductive even) and the powers and traits do suggests that the Beasts are 'Big Brother' splat, which likely WILL damage storytelling and inter-PC relations.<br /> <br /> Do you know how people say Mage is, both mechanically and thematically hard to do right in crossover games?<br /> Beast has similar problems, but at least three times bigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:33:37-07:00","id":550251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550234#post550234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">immune to multitudes of mind control effects,</div> </div> </div> </div>Which power is that? I made a search for &quot;mind&quot; through the pdf and couldn't find anything.<br /> <br /> They are immune to Disquiet because, ironically, that strengthens Prometheans theme of loneliness. Basically, the Promethean section doesn't buy what Beasts are selling, their acceptance of their monstrous state is terrible for any Promethean looking to become human. Any friendship a Beast can offer is something a Promethean has to leave behind if they want to be able to continue on their journey. For a Promethean, a Beast friend is like a weight around their ankle holding them back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:36:03-07:00","id":550253,"title":"","content":"If I were to make a beast for a vampire chronicle, I'd try to make it a vampire-like beast. That strikes me as the sort of beast likely to hang around with a bunch of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:38:15-07:00","id":550258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550251#post550251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which power is that? I made a search for &quot;mind&quot; through the pdf and couldn't find anything.<br /> <br /> They are immune to Disquiet because, ironically, that strengthens Prometheans theme of loneliness. Basically, the Promethean section doesn't buy what Beasts are selling, their acceptance of their monstrous state is terrible for any Promethean looking to become human. Any friendship a Beast can offer is something a Promethean has to leave behind if they want to be able to continue on their journey. For a Promethean, a Beast friend is like a weight around their ankle holding them back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't have PDF with me now, but I might have made a mistake. It could have been one of the Beast powers, that can Fxxk everyone's soul/mind except for the Beasts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the power &quot;You can give Soulless condition, even to those other supernaturals who inherently do not have Souls,&quot; without giving any logical backing. Inversion is almost always not true. Mary Sue much?<br /> <br /> About Disquiet.<br /> You know, thematically, right, but that still seems really very Mary Sue things to put in, because,things like dead people and half-machine people ARE subjective to Disquiet, because, it's the consistency.<br /> Moreover, Beast nature of its acceptance of being a monster, wouldn't it actually make Promethians dispise, or at least disagree hard, on Beasts? But yeah, Beasts are still big brothers, liked by everyone(except for Demons) on sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:49:43-07:00","id":550266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550250#post550250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, there are mechanics, but all those mechanics are making Beasts cooler at the expense of literally making other splats as &quot;little brothers/sisters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not only that, Beasts don't add to other splats' themes by being added into their games, and often takes away key themes. Take Promethian, Changeling and Vampire for example.<br /> And also, the mechanic that states that the first impressions are 'always good?' Hardly any logic behind it, (often counterproductive even) and the powers and traits do suggests that the Beasts are 'Big Brother' splat, which likely WILL damage storytelling and inter-PC relations.<br /> <br /> Do you know how people say Mage is, both mechanically and thematically hard to do right in crossover games?<br /> Beast has similar problems, but at least three times bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a quick niggle: The First Impressions thing are only assuming everything is equal when the &quot;target' supernatural meets a Beast for the first time. I guarantee you a vampire from Vancouver vacationing in New Jersey will react in a hostile manner to any Beast, Makara or otherwise.<br /> <br /> I always figured that the First Impressions thing represented the Beast showing up in a manner that doesn't immediately offend the target (walking up to a vampire and saying, &quot;Hey Leech! Nice to meet you!&quot; will likely also result in pain/death) and trying to be nice. Like, most supernaturals probably aren't used to somebody coming up and just wanting to chat. It's intriguing.<br /> <br /> That aside, I think that all crossover requires a degree of tossing out some of the themes of each game. But I can see any other supernatural party being just fine with the addition of a Child or two. Even Prometheans. They don't afflict each other with Disquiet after all, so it's not that strange. Hell, do Prometheans even affect other supernaturals with Disquiet? Is that ever explicitly detailed? I always assumed that they didn't.<br /> <br /> Not trying to convince you that your reading was somehow wrong, I just don't see the Mary Sue-ness that others have mentioned. But I acknowledge that y'all have been noticing it.<br /> <br /> PS: They're immune to a host of various powers? I did a search for &quot;immune&quot;, &quot;unaffected&quot;, etc... in the document, and I saw a small handful of stuff mostly about physical Tilts related to Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:53:23-07:00","id":550267,"title":"","content":"The reason you can't take a beast's soul is that the version of soulless a beast gets is called &quot;dead&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:54:49-07:00","id":550268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550266#post550266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hell, do Prometheans even affect other supernaturals with Disquiet? Is that ever explicitly detailed? I always assumed that they didn't.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethian books explicitly say that they do. I am 98% sure that the books that came later, such as Demon, also states that Demons are affected by Disquiet. (I am actually not sure about Mummy though, but everyone else is affected, yes.<br /> <br /> I mean, it could be changed in Promethian 2E, but as of Demon, (which is sorta in line with 2E books) yeah, everyone except Beast IS subject to Disquiet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:57:45-07:00","id":550294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550234#post550234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> immune to soul pacts, because their souls are friggin strong?<br /> What the hell? The Mary Sue quotient of this is reaching DtF level.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Immune&quot; to <i>pacts, period.</i> As in &quot;neither party is getting anything out of the documentation.&quot;<br /> <br /> When the Unchained are already disincentivized from stepping into supernatural souls because <i>it gets them a human identity with a few boxes of aggravated damage</i>.<br /> <br /> Not being able to benefit from a supernatural bargain that primarily works off of manipulating connections to the mortal world is kind of part and parcel of being a crossover-friendly game built around establishing connections to <i>other supernatural beings</i> at the increasing expense of your mortal life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:57:59-07:00","id":550295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550268#post550268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> everyone except Beast IS subject to Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sort of. IIRC werewolves don't actually suffer disquiet like mortals do. They become more prone to death rage, but when not in death rage they act normally.<br /> <br /> Given sharp changes to how Kuruth works in second edition I suspect we could be looking at a heavy shake up in the mechanics here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-11-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:58:07-07:00","id":550296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550258#post550258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mary Sue</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you even mean by that?<br /> I know the literal definition, but your use doesn't fit that at all. So I am not sure what you are getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:59:31-07:00","id":550298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550268#post550268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethian books explicitly say that they do. I am 98% sure that the books that came later, such as Demon, also states that Demons are affected by Disquiet. (I am actually not sure about Mummy though, but everyone else is affected, yes.<br /> <br /> I mean, it could be changed in Promethian 2E, but as of Demon, (which is sorta in line with 2E books) yeah, everyone except Beast IS subject to Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'll have to go over my books (Prommie core and DtD in this case) when I get home, because I've been drastically misreading Promethean this whole time otherwise.<br /> <br /> I just assumed that Disquiet was the sort of thing that only affected people with an &quot;Integrity&quot; score, or &quot;Fundamentally human&quot; as Beast would put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:00:03-07:00","id":550299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550268#post550268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethian books explicitly say that they do. I am 98% sure that the books that came later, such as Demon, also states that Demons are affected by Disquiet. (I am actually not sure about Mummy though, but everyone else is affected, yes.<br /> <br /> I mean, it could be changed in Promethian 2E, but as of Demon, (which is sorta in line with 2E books) yeah, everyone except Beast IS subject to Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean also suggested ways that Supernaturals could become immune to Disquiet. Not saying that's equal with Beasts, but it also sets a precedence for a type of Supernatural that is naturally immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:00:27-07:00","id":550300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550295#post550295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sort of. IIRC werewolves don't actually suffer disquiet like mortals do. They become more prone to death rage, but when not in death rage they act normally.<br /> <br /> Given sharp changes to how Kuruth works in second edition I suspect we could be looking at a heavy shake up in the mechanics here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Disquiet does SOMETHING to them. Something to everyone, except for the Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:07:59-07:00","id":550305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-