a search through the book and as far as I can tell it never mentions it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:22:38-07:00","id":550319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550317#post550317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget sin eaters dont think prometheans talk about them. tried to check both books no mention of eighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I should check about them tonight. Yeah... and Mummy too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:25:57-07:00","id":550322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550318#post550318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually <i>do</i> Demons suffer from disquiet? I just ran a search through the book and as far as I can tell it never mentions it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something that could be taken that way in the Integrator Stereotypes sidebar, but otherwise nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:31:33-07:00","id":550325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550322#post550322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's something that could be taken that way in the Integrator Stereotypes sidebar, but otherwise nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I remember that.<br /> It went like... &quot;I studied under one for two years before I killed her. I still don't know why...&quot; or somethinglike that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:37:42-07:00","id":550328,"title":"","content":"Weeks. Still, in a wider context that could mean anything. Maybe an angel made him do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:37:49-07:00","id":550329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550318#post550318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually <i>do</i> Demons suffer from disquiet? I just ran a search through the book and as far as I can tell it never mentions it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually looked through all the Demon books as well and couldn't find anything. No luck with google either, though I am pretty sure I remember something about how only their Covers are affected by Disquiet, and it slips the moment they go into Demonic form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:04:25-07:00","id":550353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550296#post550296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you even mean by that?<br /> I know the literal definition, but your use doesn't fit that at all. So I am not sure what you are getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mary Sue archetype has many, many indicators. It is never expected or implied that a given &quot;Mary Sue&quot; exhibit all of them. That said, three of the oldest and most universal are:<br /> <br /> Bending or breaking the established rules of the universe to the benefit of the Sue.<br /> Being loved by all with minimal justification or merit.<br /> Less universal but part of the original inspiration for the term: tearing the focus away from the established characters of the setting and putting it on the Mary Sue. The term Mary Sue originally referred to a specific author-insert character in a Star Trek fanfic, and she did precisely this. Mary Sue has since expanded beyond just fanfics, which is why this is less universal.<br /> <br /> Things like the &quot;suppressing souls of creatures that don't have any&quot; could be interpreted as the first. So could their mechanically supported unifying mythos.<br /> <br /> The second is a power that Beasts have, I assume for the benefit of crossovers.<br /> <br /> The third is what Beast may do in a given crossover, due to their incredibly high power levels and ability to mimic or simply do better at a lot of things the other splats specialize in. Not everything, mind, but there's enough that it's a viable concern in a crossover game. The Beast background mythos could also be this, depending on how you look at things.<br /> <br /> This is, I assume, what people mean when they call Beast a Mary Sue splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:06:40-07:00","id":550358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550329#post550329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually looked through all the Demon books as well and couldn't find anything. No luck with google either, though I am pretty sure I remember something about how only their Covers are affected by Disquiet, and it slips the moment they go into Demonic form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right &quot;Flowers of Hell&quot; mentions that a Demon in a cover has to actually deal with the biological issues and complications that come from being human. It actually mentions that Demons are only vulnerable to stuff like fear when they're in a cover, so I guess its kind of a case of it working on humans with a demon being basically human while wearing a cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:09:01-07:00","id":550363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550353#post550353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, I assume, what people mean when they call Beast a Mary Sue splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may assume, but Mary Sue has long been used as the go to catch-all damning term. So I I'd like to hear torete describe what she means when using that term in her own words.<br /> In most cases these days, Mary Sue means &quot;I don't like it, and I want to give my subjective dislike an illusion of being based on objective facts&quot;. I am curious if more is intended in this case.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:19:25-07:00","id":550370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550234#post550234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Like a lot of people has pointed out, the Hero mechanic IS really flawed in its contexts and analogies, that leads to really unfortunate implications.<br /> - Even without that, the Heroes are really underwhelming and unentertaining as antagonists go. And they are the only antagonists in the book.<br /> - Intra-Begotten society is almost never visited, despite the line's emphasis on 'family.'<br /> <b>- Despite the developers' goals, Beast is actually the line that is least crossover viable game. This actually killed all enthusiasm for me.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>While I largely agree with your other three points, I can't really get behind this last one. Beast is fine in crossover, just no better than any other splat. They still require the storyteller to perform setting control, and vet characters a little more closely, and they still require common themes (which they certainly have). They certainly don't lend themselves to &quot;Five Adventurers Meet In A Tavern&quot; play, but that's almost universally true across nWoD lines.<br /> <br /> Indeed, if there's a major crossover issue it lies in the <b>necessity </b>of crossover to facilitate Beast play. The near total absence of a setting or baked in hooks beyond &quot;eat, or don't, your call&quot;, does not lead to exciting standalone stories. Or, at the very least, none come to mind, which is absolutely unheard of for me and a corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:26:24-07:00","id":550386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550370#post550370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I largely agree with your other three points, I can't really get behind this last one. Beast is fine in crossover, just no better than any other splat. They still require the storyteller to perform setting control, and vet characters a little more closely, and they still require common themes (which they certainly have). They certainly don't lend themselves to &quot;Five Adventurers Meet In A Tavern&quot; play, but that's almost universally true across nWoD lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue with this is that, when you have a Beast in your crossover game, that Beast has the ability to deal with what would otherwise be antagonists from a position of good impression. So if your Changeling is being hunted down by a loyalist, the Beast can talk to them and use the social maneuvering system to cool it. And if the loyalist returns to their True Fae overlord, then the Beast can talk them out of it as well. At least mechanically. Thicker Than Water isn't limited to traditional player splats, which makes sense considering how they have more in common with things like the Pure and Seers, but it also means that when you're running a game, most splat antagonists could be dealt with completely disregarding the traditional animosity they usually bring to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-11-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:46:07-07:00","id":550451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550386#post550386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue with this is that, when you have a Beast in your crossover game, that Beast has the ability to deal with what would otherwise be antagonists from a position of good impression. So if your Changeling is being hunted down by a loyalist, the Beast can talk to them and use the social maneuvering system to cool it. And if the loyalist returns to their True Fae overlord, then the Beast can talk them out of it as well. At least mechanically. Thicker Than Water isn't limited to traditional player splats, which makes sense considering how they have more in common with things like the Pure and Seers, but it also means that when you're running a game, most splat antagonists could be dealt with completely disregarding the traditional animosity they usually bring to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify.<br /> <br /> Everything you said is true and correct. That's why I said Beasts don't crossover any <b>better </b>than other splats. You certainly can't randomly drop a Beast into a Changeling game and expect the Lost setting to go unchanged, at least no more than a Thrysis could join a wolfpack and leave the Forsaken game as is.<br /> <br /> Crossover inherently muddles the waters and screws with expectations, that can be fun, but it's more work for the storyteller.<br /> <br /> Edit: Does the book's storytelling chapter not go into this? Because it's really important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 06-11-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:53:56-07:00","id":550454,"title":"","content":"Kickstarter update with the Family art for the Namtaru! Quite a nice one. Also comes with an interesting version of the tale of the Minotaur.<br /> <br /> @Pendragon: the Crossover section of the storytelling chapter goes into it. Mostly in the &quot;Anchor On Theme&quot;, &quot;Game Balance?&quot; and &quot;Find Universal Motivators&quot; topics. Doesn't specifically mention the ability or advantages of Beasts in dealing with say, Gentry in a Changeling chronicle, but it discusses pertinent points of crossover and Beast involvement in other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-11-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:22:08-07:00","id":550513,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that contrary to what some people think the Thicker than Water bonus isn't actually that big. It means that when you use soft leverage it takes <i>days</i> to pull someone around instead of <i>weeks. </i>You need to start from a non-hostile position too, and what that means can vary depending on who you're talking to. I don't think I'd count an encounter with people trying to kill your buddies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:30:16-07:00","id":550547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550454#post550454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Pendragon: the Crossover section of the storytelling chapter goes into it. Mostly in the &quot;Anchor On Theme&quot;, &quot;Game Balance?&quot; and &quot;Find Universal Motivators&quot; topics. Doesn't specifically mention the ability or advantages of Beasts in dealing with say, Gentry in a Changeling chronicle, but it discusses pertinent points of crossover and Beast involvement in other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good.<br /> <br /> I've actually got a Beast PC in my current game (or a character so beast like that he will shortly be converted without any perceptible change in character) the splat does add some very cool elements of mystery and psychology to the mix. They also antagonize brilliantly, and as someone whose games thrive on player-vs-player conflict (not violence, but conflict) Beasts can work quite nicely.<br /> <br /> Not sure how they'd handle in a Superfriends sandbox...my guess is poorly. For all the talk of Thicker Then Water, Beasts antagonize with their very presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:31:18-07:00","id":550549,"title":"","content":"It only needs you to start without hostility, not them. And days instead of weeks is a big difference.<br /> <br /> But the big thing is how it's meant to be represented in the game. Because it does seem like supernaturals aren't going to be inherently aggressive towards Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-11-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:00:49-07:00","id":550586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550547#post550547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts antagonize with their very presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read several statements to that effect, but I still don't get it. Beasts seems to be built to avoid just such a thing. They don't need to compete for resources, and indeed benefit from helping other supernatural creature access places of power and feeding opportunties which can allow them to replenish Satiety without doing anything too shocking. They naturally begin their interactions with Kin from a good position. They can help Kin in their magical endeavours. That's plenty of reasons to get along, IMHO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:39:15-07:00","id":550623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550549#post550549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> days instead of weeks is a big difference.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not when you're trying to convince a bunch of forsaken and pure to not rip each others throats out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:51:51-07:00","id":550634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550623#post550623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not when you're trying to convince a bunch of forsaken and pure to not rip each others throats out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is your solution to force everyone to try and kill each other at first sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:07:16-07:00","id":550676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550623#post550623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not when you're trying to convince a bunch of forsaken and pure to not rip each others throats out.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Back the Fuck off or I WILL Hunt Both of you punks Across anywhere you go. Now Get Back into your own camps... This Place is MINE.&quot;<br /> Hecatonhire, Anakim Tyrant.<br /> <br /> Edit/Added: Just pointing out that Uratha and the Pure Both understand Territory, and might not want too piss off someone/thing that Likely CAN hunt and Kill them wherever they go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-11-2015, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:12:13-07:00","id":550692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550676#post550676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Back the Fuck off or I WILL Hunt Both of you punks Across anywhere you go. Now Get Back into your own camps... This Place is MINE.&quot;<br /> Hecatonhire, Anakim Tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hecatonhire, forensics didn't stand a chance figuring out what happened to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:17:58-07:00","id":550697,"title":"","content":"The point is that Thicker Than Water will do precisely fuck all in this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:39:44-07:00","id":550723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550586#post550586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read several statements to that effect, but I still don't get it. Beasts seems to be built to avoid just such a thing. They don't need to compete for resources, and indeed benefit from helping other supernatural creature access places of power and feeding opportunties which can allow them to replenish Satiety without doing anything too shocking. They naturally begin their interactions with Kin from a good position. They can help Kin in their magical endeavours. That's plenty of reasons to get along, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>H'okay, this will take some explaining, and may not be true for every group. But here's the way I see it:<br /> <br /> Beast's domain, its core concept and thematic area, is in psychology. Beasts in crossover don't interact with the splat's setting so much as they interact with the splat itself. This is most evident in their Nightmares, which manipulate and exploit key features of the kin. They have hungers, certainly, but those more serve to facilitate group activity. What keeps the Beast around is curiosity, and the experienced gained by plumbing the psychological depths of those they deem family. <br /> <br /> Looking at this through the eyes of the kin, while the Beast may seem attractive at first, they will in time be revealed to possess a dangerous and totally remorseless interest in their family's darkest natures, and the power to exploit them in terrible, taboo ways. This is Beasts's point, it's purpose in a crossover. They represent the unbridled hungers of the other splats, and force those splats to ask some very uncomfortable questions. For instance, how many Mages really want to ponder how far they're willing to go for knowledge?<br /> <br /> And then we get to Heroes, the gaggle of randomly occurring antagonists that pop up to bother the Beast and all his friends. Sure, they might not be a huge threat, but most splats see killing in a slightly harsher light than the Begotten, and may begin to ask important questions like &quot;Is my dragon friend turning me into a horrible person as well?&quot;. Indeed, Heroes might well be a bigger hassle for the Beast's family than the Beast itself, because unlike the Begotten, those splats have <i>their own fucking problems to deal with. </i><br /> <br /> Now I'd ask you to take this with a grain of salt. I haven't read the book thoroughly, and from what I read their themes are a tad...underdeveloped. Can you play a nice buddy buddy Beast who doesn't want to cause problems for his family? Yes...tragically you can. But the spirit of the text is clear, Beasts are assholes unrepentant. The devil on the shoulder asking &quot;why not?&quot; and taking steps to prove it. Does that mean they are unpalatably evil? I like to think evil is a perspective, but I expect a lot of characters (and probably players) would strongly disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:01:30-07:00","id":550771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550723#post550723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">H'okay, this will take some explaining, and may not be true for every group. But here's the way I see it:<br /> <br /> Beast's domain, its core concept and thematic area, is in psychology. Beasts in crossover don't interact with the splat's setting so much as they interact with the splat itself. This is most evident in their Nightmares, which manipulate and exploit key features of the kin. They have hungers, certainly, but those more serve to facilitate group activity. What keeps the Beast around is curiosity, and the experienced gained by plumbing the psychological depths of those they deem family.<br /> <br /> Looking at this through the eyes of the kin, while the Beast may seem attractive at first, they will in time be revealed to possess a dangerous and totally remorseless interest in their family's darkest natures, and the power to exploit them in terrible, taboo ways. This is Beasts's point, it's purpose in a crossover. They represent the unbridled hungers of the other splats, and force those splats to ask some very uncomfortable questions. For instance, how many Mages really want to ponder how far they're willing to go for knowledge?<br /> <br /> And then we get to Heroes, the gaggle of randomly occurring antagonists that pop up to bother the Beast and all his friends. Sure, they might not be a huge threat, but most splats see killing in a slightly harsher light than the Begotten, and may begin to ask important questions like &quot;Is my dragon friend turning me into a horrible person as well?&quot;. Indeed, Heroes might well be a bigger hassle for the Beast's family than the Beast itself, because unlike the Begotten, those splats have <i>their own fucking problems to deal with. </i><br /> <br /> Now I'd ask you to take this with a grain of salt. I haven't read the book thoroughly, and from what I read their themes are a tad...underdeveloped. Can you play a nice buddy buddy Beast who doesn't want to cause problems for his family? Yes...tragically you can. But the spirit of the text is clear, Beasts are assholes unrepentant. The devil on the shoulder asking &quot;why not?&quot; and taking steps to prove it. Does that mean they are unpalatably evil? I like to think evil is a perspective, but I expect a lot of characters (and probably players) would strongly disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I get it. It's true that the fluff gives more example of scary, downright villainous Beasts, than of the antiheroes that many of the WoD's fans prefer playing. But that's just fluff.<br /> Your Beast could take all her sustenace from watching her Spring Court Kin stripping nightly as the local Changeling owned strip club. She could dedicate her life to the protection of the Freehold, terrorizing its ennemies and exploring the mysteries of the fae to make sure she can keep her Lost friends safe. With such a plentiful source of Satiety, no risk of creating Heroes.<br /> This is mechanically as likely as her being a serial killer inciting a Promethean throngs to greater and greater dephts of depravity in their search for understanding or rejecting humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:17:56-07:00","id":550793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550771#post550771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I get it. It's true that the fluff gives more example of scary, downright villainous Beasts, than of the antiheroes that many of the WoD's fans prefer playing. But that's just fluff.<br /> Your Beast could take all her sustenace from watching her Spring Court Kin stripping nightly as the local Changeling owned strip club. She could dedicate her life to the protection of the Freehold, terrorizing its ennemies and exploring the mysteries of the fae to make sure she can keep her Lost friends safe. With such a plentiful source of Satiety, no risk of creating Heroes.<br /> This is mechanically as likely as her being a serial killer inciting a Promethean throngs to greater and greater dephts of depravity in their search for understanding or rejecting humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said a few pages back that I wasn't always 100% satisfied with Beast. This <i>is</i> a major source of dissatisfaction.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, most splats can be played in an 'uncharacteristic' manner. It's partially the storyteller's job to bring that fluff to bear. But again, on the hole I agree that Beasts could use some more concrete motivators towards antagonism. Perhaps something like Arcane Experience, rewarded for plumbing their kins' psyche...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:35:24-07:00","id":550822,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say they need motivators (concrete or not) towards <i>antagonism</i> because that would defeat one point of their seeking out Kin in most cases. But I wouldn't be opposed to some more concrete motivators to plain explore the worlds and psyche of their kin, as well as delve through the World Of Darkness and leave their mark through the lenses of her Legend. I understand the amount of fluff references to Beasts exploring their Legend mostly seems to be a (good) abstract description of the ways the Begotten grow more powerful by engaging the world, but I wouldn't have been surprised to see associated Beat rewards in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Not that Beasts need them, mind you, they're beat machines by virtue of the Satiety Conditions alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:42:18-07:00","id":550828,"title":"","content":"I think the themes of fear, hunger and kinship have a strong focus throughout the text and were presented in an intriguing way. I think the characters are presented with a different tone in each half of the book. Beasts/Heroes are clarified in the end, but in the beginning they come across to me as unrelatable with alien mindsets. I view them now as truly amoral creatures with some human characteristics. I think that is still playable.<br /> <br /> The first half was well written and an interesting read. I just didn't find it appealing as a game, so if I was trying to convince someone to get into Beast I would tell them to read Chapter 5 earlier. I might put it before Chapter 3 or concurrent with Chapter 2. I think that would eliminate much confusion. But I'm not one that cares if Chapter 3 covers X because that is the way it has been done. It requires a hard sell to convince someone to make it through 300-400 pages before making a decision on whether you actually like the characters.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think this game could manage without additions, but the points that are being looked at by Matt wouldn't be hurt by some additional work. I also give a nod to the writers.<br /> <br /> Lingering Questions<br /> <br /> The sample hero Mariann appears to go from high integrity to hero overnight. What happened there? A segue might be in order.<br /> Beasts seem a tad listless. I'm not sure what they do aside from feeding and dodging Heroes. I'm assuming there is more to them.<br /> There was early talk of Beasts searching the occult in the beginning of the text and I don't know what happened with that. Missing element?<br /> Do Souls use Satiety to fuel Atavisms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:54:09-07:00","id":550837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550793#post550793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said a few pages back that I wasn't always 100% satisfied with Beast. This <i>is</i> a major source of dissatisfaction.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, most splats can be played in an 'uncharacteristic' manner. It's partially the storyteller's job to bring that fluff to bear. But again, on the hole I agree that Beasts could use some more concrete motivators towards antagonism. Perhaps something like Arcane Experience, rewarded for plumbing their kins' psyche...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't saying Beast should be more antagonistic. To the contrary, I like how they can mostly choose the kind of conflict, and the kind of story they will involve themselves in. Kinship is a large part of that, since it allows Beast to integrate with their Kin and their narratives.<br /> But an equivalent to arcane experience could indeed motivate players to explore more esoteric themes rather than the more utilitarian ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:59:08-07:00","id":550842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550258#post550258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I don't have PDF with me now, but I might have made a mistake. It could have been one of the Beast powers, that can Fxxk everyone's soul/mind except for the Beasts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the power &quot;You can give Soulless condition, even to those other supernaturals who inherently do not have Souls,&quot; without giving any logical backing. Inversion is almost always not true. Mary Sue much?<br /> <br /> About Disquiet.<br /> You know, thematically, right, but that still seems really very Mary Sue things to put in, because,things like dead people and half-machine people ARE subjective to Disquiet, because, it's the consistency.<br /> Moreover, Beast nature of its acceptance of being a monster, wouldn't it actually make Promethians dispise, or at least disagree hard, on Beasts? But yeah, Beasts are still big brothers, liked by everyone(except for Demons) on sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Liked&quot; is a strong word. I think the devs should imply that they are merely not viewed automatically as a threat by other Supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:02:28-07:00","id":550845,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I have to nth the voices unimpressed by the preview text of Beast. My main issues with it are:<br /> <br /> - The subtext is questionable at best, particularly when you consider that the &quot;outcast&quot; and &quot;hunted&quot; Beasts are actually in a position of personal and social power that they use to torment the people around them and are distinctly more powerful than their main antagonists.<br /> <br /> - The way the crossover stuff is done leaves a bad taste in my mouth\u2014it feels like a total Poochie thing, with the totally coolrad character suddenly inserted into the scene and treated as the best thing ever by everyone.<br /> <br /> - Beasts are, frankly, kind of boring. If you cross off the crossover stuff, there's just not much there: do unpleasant things to people to charge up your power meter (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those normal humans are just suckers who deserve everything they get!), and kill Heroes (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those Heroes are just egomaniacs who deserve everything they get!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:15:43-07:00","id":550852,"title":"","content":"After reading through a large section of this thread, not the entirety but over 150 pages mostly starting around page 35-40ish, and having read through the Kickstarter document I'm in agreement with some of what I'm seeing. I feel the tone needs to be tightened up. I agree with some of what's been said that Beasts aren't really sympathetic so being an anti hero feels harder. Fluff is thankfully easy to change at a whim, but the Mechanics back up basically being a dick on some level. I'm more of a mechanics guy than fluff guy as I can just change whatever fluff I don't like. <br /> <br /> I made a comment on kickstarter about the Satiety conditions and how Satiety is our power pool and also our &quot;integrity/morality&quot; stat. I feel that the extremes of Ravenous and Slumbering are suitably terrible conditions to ever get and you'll want to avoid them. My issue is that the other 3 conditions are just more crapsack. The only winner out of the 5 is Starving. It doesn't feel right that Starving is kind of your badass I want to live here state of existence. At Starving: Anathema penalties are lessened, Atavisms are stronger, Your condition penalty is a minor penalty to open Pathways, and while Starving your soul will accept a whole lot of things to feed your hunger.<br /> <br /> By comparison Sated isn't too bad, it's the window of opportunity for Heroes to apply Anathemas. No bonuses, but no real penalties besides Anathemas at this level. So still a crapsack but it's a story driven crapsack in that Anathemas have to have a window or they don't really matter. <br /> <br /> Gorged on the other hand blows so many chunks why would you really want to be there? You get a +2 to open Pathways, stronger Nightmares, oh and lose Lair to your supernatural defense vs mind affecting things. So because I'm feeling refreshed from eating and not starving myself I become more easily influenced by mind buggery magic? It clashes with my image of a Dragon fresh off the feast immense in his power, secure in his home, but because he's not hungry he's no harder to Dominate than a Mortal. The real disconnect comes from the fact that these Conditions all still apply to the Beast Incarnate.<br /> <br /> If you become an Incarnate, the pinnacle endgame of beast, you can no longer hit Ravenous or Slumbering. You can still be Gorged, Sated, and Starving. Why is an Incarnate at Satiety 7-10 losing their bonus Supernatural Tolerance to mindbuggery? These are supposed to be the badass monsters that other Beasts are wary of and look up to. When they're fed though, easier to slap you with a Nightmare! Not exactly thrill/fear inducing.<br /> <br /> The players at my table will unfortunately look at things the same way, as cool as Nightmares are being a Dragon is more about breathing Fire and wrecking shit to them. And since you get beats from these Conditions I see them feeding and dropping back to 3 fast as they can just spending satiety to drop, resolving the conditions and making a Beat farm happen.<br /> <br /> I've only read through Atavisms and Nightmares once so far as I spent more time working to understand Lair, Hero/Beast stuff, Crossover themes, and then Satiety and it's associated Conditions. From what I've read they're pretty cool and flavorful, some are more open to re-skinning between the Families than others, but that's the nature of the beast. I think a little more time in development could flesh out some of the hiccups in the text. The overall tone, coverage of crossover material could use a little more meat in that section, some defining direction for the game beyond &quot;the crossover splat&quot;, a revisit of Satiety conditions and their balance against the system and each other, and some work on Heroes and other antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6403-ahzouroshadow","name":"ahzouroshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:38:52-07:00","id":550862,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm gonna have to disagree with some of these. They've been addressed a lot though, so I'll be brief.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550845#post550845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The subtext is questionable at best, particularly when you consider that the &quot;outcast&quot; and &quot;hunted&quot; Beasts are actually in a position of personal and social power that they use to torment the people around them and are distinctly more powerful than their main antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beasts are not meant to represent the outcast or the underdog or that sort of thing, so this isn't a case of &quot;It's wrong to persecute this person just because they're different. Even if he's a psycho who likes eat people's hearts out of their chests while the person is still using it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550845#post550845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Beasts are, frankly, kind of boring. If you cross off the crossover stuff, there's just not much there: do unpleasant things to people to charge up your power meter (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those normal humans are just suckers who deserve everything they get!), and kill Heroes (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those Heroes are just egomaniacs who deserve everything they get!).</div> </div> </div> </div> It has already been mentioned that the dev's are working on tightening things to give Beasts something more to do than just eat, fight heroes, live and die. The interpretation of normal humans being &quot;suckers who deserve everything they get&quot; is held but some Beasts, but the splat portrays it more as the Beast is just attempting to keep itself fed and not let its soul go on a rampage. Hero killing is not considered justified because you're special it is considered justified because the Hero is trying to murder the crap out of you and no splat is going to argue self defense is a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:40:32-07:00","id":550866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550845#post550845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, I have to nth the voices unimpressed by the preview text of Beast. My main issues with it are:<br /> <br /> - The subtext is questionable at best, particularly when you consider that the &quot;outcast&quot; and &quot;hunted&quot; Beasts are actually in a position of personal and social power that they use to torment the people around them and are distinctly more powerful than their main antagonists.<br /> <br /> - The way the crossover stuff is done leaves a bad taste in my mouth\u2014it feels like a total Poochie thing, with the totally coolrad character suddenly inserted into the scene and treated as the best thing ever by everyone.<br /> <br /> - Beasts are, frankly, kind of boring. If you cross off the crossover stuff, there's just not much there: do unpleasant things to people to charge up your power meter (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those normal humans are just suckers who deserve everything they get!), and kill Heroes (and be totally justified in it because you are special and those Heroes are just egomaniacs who deserve everything they get!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll play Devil's Advocate here, because 2 points of view are often better than 1.<br /> <br /> -Beasts don't have to torment people. Some do, some don't. Why only focus on those who do?<br /> <br /> -Beasts are built to be useful to other splats, but they don't have to upstage them. There's no reason for a Beast to take center stage unless it serves the story. Even with Thicker than Water, they just make a good first impression. Their Children of tthe Dark Mother thing can look patronizing, but they could merely be misinterpreting what their Kinship means, like those Werewolf hunting hippies from Hunter misinterpreat what their Unseen Sense means.<br /> <br /> -I don't see how Beast are more boring than any other splat, even afterr depriving them from one of their primary themes (the Crossover stuff). Even your stance on them claiming justified in hurting people ca be interestin to explore. It's like people arguing for their right to pollute the environnement because it brings profit. Do you have the right to hurt other to survive?How far can you go before you can't justify your actions even to yourself? There's a whole thematic to explore if you want to. Even without that, you have a whole World of Darkness to explore and a panoply of cool powers to help you. You have no inherent mission, but that just means you can do anything you want!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:53:36-07:00","id":550869,"title":"","content":"You know what I really find most questionable about this &quot;subtext&quot; people keep banging on about?<i> Its existence.</i><br /> <br /> You are not a persecuted minority. You are a fucking dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:03:56-07:00","id":550873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550793#post550793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said a few pages back that I wasn't always 100% satisfied with Beast. This <i>is</i> a major source of dissatisfaction.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, most splats can be played in an 'uncharacteristic' manner. It's partially the storyteller's job to bring that fluff to bear. But again, on the hole I agree that Beasts could use some more concrete motivators towards antagonism. Perhaps something like Arcane Experience, rewarded for plumbing their kins' psyche...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Arcane XP would work, because the template is pretty XP efficient in the RAW. Now, special Beats for expanding the Lair or developing new Nightmares makes sense, as would more permanent investments in the Beasts Kinship group. They should also do a better job of tying the kinds of actions necessary to recover Satiety to the levels of Satiety where those acts become necessary. Only Starved or Gorged Beasts should feel compelled to do actions with a High Satiety potential, while anyone else should have a flags raised when they try to do something that extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:05:18-07:00","id":550874,"title":"","content":"See except that's my actual only issue with the game as it stands. You're not a fucking dragon, you're a fucking dragon with crap tons of baggage and silly hindrances that don't logically follow based on how hungry you may or may not be. The ability to waltz into any of the game lines, sans Demon, and play nice if you like is pretty awesome. The fact that there's not a direct correlation between powers is awesome, I don't recall seeing a power that essentially increased your speed or actions in a round so no Celerity type thing though I very well may have missed it. <br /> I don't know how many folks have read The Dresden Files, but I want to BE Ferrovax. I want to be a Dragon not exactly like those in DnD/Pathfinder, but I want to be on that scale of things when it comes to being a Dragon. I want to mingle through the supernatural world secure in my power and be a mysterious force in the world. I like the idea of making new powers based on the powers of other supernatural entities, I like making those allies across the splats and dabbling in their squabbles, I really really really like the idea of exploring the World of Darkness. I think that could be a grand focus. I can't recall where I've seen it, but Demon is the Spy genre to Mage's pulp noir Detective genre. Mages poke around uncovering secrets of the World and trying to learn more. That overlaps a bit, but a focus on just Exploring the world would be pretty fantastic. The line is thin between the two ideas, but it does exist. At least in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6403-ahzouroshadow","name":"ahzouroshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:07:52-07:00","id":550877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahzouroshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550874#post550874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See except that's my actual only issue with the game as it stands. You're not a fucking dragon, you're a fucking dragon with crap tons of baggage and silly hindrances that don't logically follow based on how hungry you may or may not be. The ability to waltz into any of the game lines, sans Demon, and play nice if you like is pretty awesome. The fact that there's not a direct correlation between powers is awesome, I don't recall seeing a power that essentially increased your speed or actions in a round so no Celerity type thing though I very well may have missed it.<br /> I don't know how many folks have read The Dresden Files, but I want to BE Ferrovax. I want to be a Dragon not exactly like those in DnD/Pathfinder, but I want to be on that scale of things when it comes to being a Dragon. I want to mingle through the supernatural world secure in my power and be a mysterious force in the world. I like the idea of making new powers based on the powers of other supernatural entities, I like making those allies across the splats and dabbling in their squabbles, I really really really like the idea of exploring the World of Darkness. I think that could be a grand focus. I can't recall where I've seen it, but Demon is the Spy genre to Mage's pulp noir Detective genre. Mages poke around uncovering secrets of the World and trying to learn more. That overlaps a bit, but a focus on just Exploring the world would be pretty fantastic. The line is thin between the two ideas, but it does exist. At least in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Become an Incarnate, then. That's what they're all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:12:07-07:00","id":550881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550869#post550869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I really find most questionable about this &quot;subtext&quot; people keep banging on about?<i> Its existence.</i><br /> <br /> You are not a persecuted minority. You are a fucking dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally just spit cereal all over my desk. Both, because you're right and because it was funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:14:38-07:00","id":550883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550877#post550877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Become an Incarnate, then. That's what they're all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or at the very least, remember your matches, lighter fluid, hot dogs and marshmallows<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:18:56-07:00","id":550884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550869#post550869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I really find most questionable about this &quot;subtext&quot; people keep banging on about?<i> Its existence.</i><br /> <br /> You are not a persecuted minority. You are a fucking dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they really wanted to play that up, there'd be an Aura mechanic or something more general than Heroes to make the persecution more pervasive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:22:56-07:00","id":550885,"title":"","content":"Incarnate still suffer from Satiety conditions, which means that minimum of Lair 8 to even become one? Yeah you lose that anytime you're at Satiety 7-10. Losing 8-10 dice to resist mental coercion just because your'e not hungry does not scream Dragon Incarnate at me. The majority of the game won't be played at the Incarnate stage, and the text even suggests retiring the character after becoming one due to the power increase, I feel if the mechanics are backing the fluff then I should be able to make a Dragon like Ferrovax was in Dresden. Someone that the supernatural community, at least locally, knows about respects/fears/hangs out with or somesuch and is a player in the game. Maybe not at Char gen, but the way the book reads Beasts are supposed to be kinda badass. There's some badassness going on in here, but then it's nickled and dimed by other things. I'd like to see the nickle and dimes get a re tuning so you can literally bust out with I'm a Fucking Dragon. And have that mean something more than what &quot;penalties am I currently suffering from?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6403-ahzouroshadow","name":"ahzouroshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:22:58-07:00","id":550886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550866#post550866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I'll play Devil's Advocate here, because 2 points of view are often better than 1.<br /> <br /> -Beasts don't have to torment people. Some do, some don't. Why only focus on those who do?<br /> <br /> -Beasts are built to be useful to other splats, but they don't have to upstage them. There's no reason for a Beast to take center stage unless it serves the story. Even with Thicker than Water, they just make a good first impression. Their Children of tthe Dark Mother thing can look patronizing, but they could merely be misinterpreting what their Kinship means, like those Werewolf hunting hippies from Hunter misinterpreat what their Unseen Sense means.<br /> <br /> -I don't see how Beast are more boring than any other splat, even afterr depriving them from one of their primary themes (the Crossover stuff). Even your stance on them claiming justified in hurting people ca be interestin to explore. It's like people arguing for their right to pollute the environnement because it brings profit. Do you have the right to hurt other to survive?How far can you go before you can't justify your actions even to yourself? There's a whole thematic to explore if you want to. Even without that, you have a whole World of Darkness to explore and a panoply of cool powers to help you. You have no inherent mission, but that just means you can do anything you want!</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's the quest to thwart the Heroes coming to get you, depending on how well characterized the storyteller makes them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:45:14-07:00","id":550921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/X7rAnaKId3E\" data-code=\"X7rAnaKId3E\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X7rAnaKId3E/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Totally appropriate to have playing in the background in a Beast's Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:54:41-07:00","id":550926,"title"