th.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550869#post550869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I really find most questionable about this &amp;quot;subtext&amp;quot; people keep banging on about?<i> Its existence.</i><br /> <br /> You are not a persecuted minority. You are a fucking dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember before Maleficient came out and was worried they were going to &quot;Wicked&quot; the plot to make her a tragic victim (that is what happened, and I was a tad disappointed, but it did work better than I feared), my exact words were...<br /> <br /> &quot;She shouldn't be a victim. She can turn into a dragon! You know who are never victims in life? PEOPLE WHO CAN TURN INTO DRAGONS!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:47:25-07:00","id":550973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550967#post550967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;She shouldn't be a victim. She can turn into a dragon! You know who are never victims in life? PEOPLE WHO CAN TURN INTO DRAGONS!!!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This has made my day.<br /> <br /> But I should note that one of my favorite scenarios from GSS's Fantasy Friends setting hack is &quot;Save the Dragon from the Princess!&quot; It totally works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:57:26-07:00","id":550976,"title":"","content":"This thread is suddenly taking a turn for the awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:02:20-07:00","id":550977,"title":"","content":"Loose idea for an additional, more socially defined splat axis - in the tradition of Agendas, Archetypes, and Refinements (I.e. philosophies without in built organization or hierarchy).<br /> <br /> (these are placeholder names)<br /> <br /> Imperials want the broods to be unified, even if only on a territorial basis. Paradoxically they're amongst the most likely to fight with other Beasts as they compete for power, and try to dominate other Broods. Obviously there is a Tyrant plurality in this faction, but Collectors looking to collect tribute from other hoards (or more egalitarianly create a greater shared hoard), or Nemeses wanting a system that holds the Begotten to account for their actions, are also common.<br /> <br /> Faithful are dedicated to the search for the Dark Mother, in lore, in the nature of their kin, in the depths of the Primordial Dream, or chasing down sightings on earth.<br /> <br /> Caretakers want to integrate seemlessly into mortal society, and stay as sated and safe as possible as continuously as possible. To this end they build or attach themselves to small cults of humans that they can use for satiation, and protect their resources.<br /> <br /> Primals believe aping humanity is a fools errand. They are the things beyond the light of fire that humans are meant to dread. They abandon all semblance of mortal life and society to live as the monsters they were meant to be, and in more extreme cases work to destroy the lie of mortal civilization, erected to protect humanity from the truth of their primal fears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I want at least one more, but that's what I've got so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:05:11-07:00","id":550980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550973#post550973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has made my day.<br /> <br /> But I should note that one of my favorite scenarios from GSS's Fantasy Friends setting hack is &quot;Save the Dragon from the Princess!&quot; It totally works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a Princess: the Hopeful/Beast Crossover, with a Princess opposing a young Beast with a Hunger for candy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:24:00-07:00","id":550992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550980#post550980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see a Princess: the Hopeful/Beast Crossover, with a Princess opposing a young Beast with a Hunger for candy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, Nobility and Beasts could be considered two sides of the same coin. Both are connected to primordial dreams, one to nightmares and one to hopeful ones. And I get the feeling that Princesses would <i>not</i> like the comparison. Especially since the way Begotten feed is not that different from how Darkspawn corrupt those around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:24:14-07:00","id":550993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550977#post550977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> <br /> I want at least one more, but that's what I've got so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with the notion of giving Beasts a stronger cultural identity and slightly more concrete social/philosophical grounds to stand on, both with diversity, but I don't think a 4 or 5-way subsplat division is the way to go about it. Personally, I find it unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Functional enough draft but eh. I'm very lukewarm to that model for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-11-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:30:10-07:00","id":550998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550993#post550993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree with the notion of giving Beasts a stronger cultural identity and slightly more concrete social/philosophical grounds to stand on, both with diversity, but I don't think a 4 or 5-way subsplat division is the way to go about it. Personally, I find it unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Functional enough draft but eh. Very lukewarm to that model for Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using it as a framework to imagine behaviors and viewpoints to create conflict, so I wanted the potentially opposing options. I'm definitely down for more than 5 ala Geist Archetypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:32:25-07:00","id":551000,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:41:31-07:00","id":551005,"title":"","content":"Looks like there's going to be some changes. Some major. Some not.<br /> <br /> Not very happy right now. We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:43:52-07:00","id":551006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550980#post550980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see a Princess: the Hopeful/Beast Crossover, with a Princess opposing a young Beast with a Hunger for candy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually planned to make both princess and beast kin just to frighten princesses just imagine the princess lose her mind finding out her powers are related to a beast. Plus it makes them think is the darkness really evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:50:31-07:00","id":551008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551005#post551005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like there's going to be some changes. Some major. Some not.<br /> <br /> Not very happy right now. We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I know the two things I've seen Matt mention are play up Beast v Beast conflict, and clarify the nature of Heroes (not to make them work better with the metaphor people are complaining about, but to clarify that's not what they are). I wouldn't worry about Matt doing anything to throw out the things that make the game great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:52:39-07:00","id":551011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551008#post551008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I know the two things I've seen Matt mention are play up Beast v Beast conflict, and clarify the nature of Heroes (not to make them work better with the metaphor people are complaining about, but to clarify that's not what they are). I wouldn't worry about Matt doing anything to throw out the things that make the game great!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this is the case.<br /> <br /> If so, that's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:15:01-07:00","id":551021,"title":"","content":"So tl;dr so the whole deal with this game is you get to play rawhead rex and maurad for flesh? Or is it more like nightbreed and you hang out apart from humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:32:05-07:00","id":551029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551006#post551006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was actually planned to make both princess and beast kin just to frighten princesses just imagine the princess lose her mind finding out her powers are related to a beast. Plus it makes them think is the darkness really evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, that could create all sorts of interesting situtions and plot hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:37:25-07:00","id":551030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551021#post551021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So tl;dr so the whole deal with this game is you get to play rawhead rex and maurad for flesh? Or is it more like nightbreed and you hang out apart from humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former rather than the latter, sorta.<br /> There is no separate mini-society like with (Vampires, Changelings, Mages, etc.), more of a collection of small, tight groups. Think W:tF pack structure without the Tribes. That doesn't mean you couldn't have a tier 2/regional organization of Beasts show up or run your own Midian-eske town for monsters. It's just not part of the default assumptions.<br /> <br /> But Rawhead Rex strikes me as a Rampant Inheiritor; a Beast who has Merged with their Soul and destroyed their Lair. The story in question appears to be more the failed endgame of the Beast in question.<br /> I have no idea what you mean by &quot;maurad for flesh&quot; and google didn't help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:46:18-07:00","id":551032,"title":"","content":"Travel the countyside consuming/maiming/killing all you encounter,so its the monster version of slasher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:53:50-07:00","id":551039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551032#post551032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Travel the countyside consuming/maiming/killing all you encounter,so its the monster version of slasher?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I mean you COULD do that, but most Beasts don't. They have different Hungers. Power, Hoard, Prey, Punishment, and Ruin are in the core ( Matt's mentioned others are possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:56:00-07:00","id":551041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551032#post551032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Travel the countyside consuming/maiming/killing all you encounter,so its the monster version of slasher?</div> </div> </div> </div>You meant maraud, then.<br /> Beasts can do that, but that's not what the game is about. <br /> You're better off reading the draft and making your own opinion, since it seems many of us don't see the same thing in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:58:36-07:00","id":551044,"title":"","content":"Ah, spelling errors; the Anathema of the Internet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:13:17-07:00","id":551126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550862#post550862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are not meant to represent the outcast or the underdog or that sort of thing, so this isn't a case of &quot;It's wrong to persecute this person just because they're different. Even if he's a psycho who likes eat people's hearts out of their chests while the person is still using it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To grab a couple of quotes...<br /> <br /> Talking about Beasts in general:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts are born, not made, and reared in a world that instinctively fears them. It does not matter if she is rich or poor, hideous or lovely, gay or straight or somewhere in between. People look askance at what they know is not human even though, objectively speaking, they have no reason to fear. Not at first.<br /> <br /> Even as children, Beasts feel like outsiders. A Makara dreams of the deep ocean where she sleeps in solitude, far from the demands of her needling peers. An Ugallu\u2019s eyes stray to a sky forever out of reach. At night, an Eshmaki runs on all fours through a darkened forest, only to wake up once again in a stifling human world.<br /> <br /> Even a Beast\u2019s body betrays her. She knows this lump of flesh is not her. She is a prisoner of her own skin and blood. </div> </div> </div>Talking about storytelling for Beasts:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead, look to stories about outsiders, about disenfranchised people, and about communities that exist on the outskirts of the mainstream. </div> </div> </div>Talking about Beasts' role in relation to the Anima Mundi:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For millennia, lepers were reviled as harbingers of plague and corruption, both moral as well as physical. Homosexuals became the lepers of the AIDS generation and were victimized by the same moralist hysteria. Immigrants, Muslims, transgender, and impoverished people have all been vilified in the modern era, turned into scapegoats by bigoted \u201ccrusaders\u201d with narrow minds and selfish agendas. The next pandemic or culture shift will produce its own outcasts and they, too, will be blamed for their plight. </div> </div> </div>Talking about Heroes:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, the Beast needs a Hero. In the usual story, a Hero believes himself the central character. The Beast is a simple creature, with easily discernable goals and desires. It is only there for the Hero to kill. Obviously, the tale is about the \u201cgood guy,\u201d the upstanding, handsome, proper protagonist. The creature, as the outcast, the pariah, serves only to validate the Hero\u2019s existence. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550869#post550869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I really find most questionable about this &quot;subtext&quot; people keep banging on about?<i> Its existence.</i><br /> <br /> You are not a persecuted minority. You are a fucking dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I would like Beast way more if it didn't try to gussy it up with bad comic antihero justifications about how Beasts are totally justified in what they do and how Heroes just deserve what they get for daring to go after one.<br /> <br /> I'd also like it a lot more if it wasn't so focused on hurting people, specifically, and instead used more general god-monster themes - hoarding, territorialism and control of property, fame and rumor, etc - with actual harm to people being a side effect. This way you can get some genuine moral ambivalence in there, in the &quot;player characters are always tempted to slip a little further down the slope in search of power&quot;, instead of &quot;good&quot; Beasts just being petty assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:50:04-07:00","id":551154,"title":"","content":"Roadie,<br /> <br /> You literally just cut and pasted only fragment quotes to support your claim. That's an incredibly dangerous thing to do since it takes them out of context, and without context we cannot even begin to question what the subtext implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T00:08:22-07:00","id":551155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551154#post551154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roadie,<br /> <br /> You literally just cut and pasted only fragment quotes to support your claim. That's an incredibly dangerous thing to do since it takes them out of context, and without context we cannot even begin to question what the subtext implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly since the lepers quote is just mined from the middle of the section describing how the Astral works and comes immediately after a note about how the symbolism of Jack the Ripper exists disproportionate to the actual magnitude of his actions.<br /> <br /> It's part of a larger observation on how Beasts' relation with the collective unconscious affects their capacity for fame and thus not all that supportive of any point about the Begotten standing in for marginalized groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-12-2015, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T02:31:01-07:00","id":551209,"title":"","content":"Holy shit, I just figured it out. <br /> <br /> They're not supposed to represent the minorities. <br /> <br /> They're supposed to represent the <i>vilification itself</i>. The fear of the &quot;other&quot;. <br /> <br /> The destruction they wreak is the destruction that bigots <i>think</i> the minorities cause to society. Their power is the power bigots <i>think</i> minorities have. A Hero isn't a hypocrite, they're hypocrisy itself. They're the bigots' self-image, bent on taking down the very forces they created. But in the end it doesn't work. Their hate just contributes to the forces in the temenos, and breeds more beasts for them to fight. <br /> <br /> Beast's create Heroes, but &quot;heroes&quot; are the reason beasts exist at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T02:55:36-07:00","id":551215,"title":"","content":"The thing is, people are not just seeing what is there; they are seeing their interpretations. This doesn't invalidate their concerns but it is worth remember that it is no more valid than any other interpretation. It would be nice if they remember that.<br /> <br /> Any of the splats can be horrible; vampires can be life-sucking, a mind-raping one person conspiracy; a werewolf can be a heartless marauding monster, tearing anyone who takes their fancy limb-from-limb; a mage can play sorcerer-king, bending the world to their will regardless of anyone else's desires.<br /> The point is they don't have to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:12:37-07:00","id":551221,"title":"","content":"Hey, how do you think a rule along the lines of &quot;Unbeknownst to anyone, whenever a Hero slays a Beast two more inevitably arise in its place&quot; would affect the narrative? I think it would be a good way to get rid of the &quot;Heroes are the good guys&quot; problem, because then regardless of what you think of the Beasts the Heroes are Not. Helping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:17:03-07:00","id":551222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551221#post551221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, how do you think a rule along the lines of &quot;Unbeknownst to anyone, whenever a Hero slays a Beast two more inevitably arise in its place&quot; would affect the narrative? I think it would be a good way to get rid of the &quot;Heroes are the good guys&quot; problem, because then regardless of what you think of the Beasts the Heroes are Not. Helping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd Say one for one... I'd Also say a New one Arises even if they become Unfettered and/or Incarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:35:25-07:00","id":551225,"title":"","content":"My take on you idea <b>Elfive</b> is that if you want to get rid of the &quot;Heroes are the good guys&quot; narrative than your Heroes inadvertantly create Beasts idea would work wonders since it's a Beast's Hunger that brings out the Heroic urge in those lacking self-worth. You could have it be that as a Hero grows by each Beast slain that Beast's hunger disperces back into the Primordial Dream, and from the bloody remains new Souls emearge Hungry for more blood and fear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:09:08-07:00","id":551274,"title":"","content":"So Rose mentioned in the Kickstarter comments that they're looking at fleshing out the Primoridal Dream in response to some of the critiques to Beast. I for one am stoked, and hope this also means that the Angels in the core section get replaced with something more Astrally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:15:39-07:00","id":551297,"title":"","content":"Replacing Angels with Astral beings in the core section would actually be really welcome. And it would be interesting, but I'm somewhat worried about expanding on the Primordial Dream because of, well, space. The impression I got was that it's for the most part comprised of the Lairs of the Begotten, which doesn't leave all that much that /needs/ to be explored in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-12-2015, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:23:16-07:00","id":551300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551297#post551297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Replacing Angels with Astral beings in the core section would actually be really welcome. It woukd be interearing, but somewhat worried about expanding on the Primordial Dream because of, well, space. The impression I got was that it's for the most part comprised of the Lairs of the Begotten, which doesn't leave all that much that /needs/ to be explored in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Plus, when the book repeatedly makes note that the GM and it's workings, as well as Demons, are things that Beasts don't quite get, it seemed odd that there was a good bit of focus on them over the Realm which the Beasts arise from. Though with GMC, I guess it makes sense to explain the antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:24:57-07:00","id":551302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551215#post551215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, people are not just seeing what is there; they are seeing their interpretations. This doesn't invalidate their concerns but it is worth remember that it is no more valid than any other interpretation. It would be nice if they remember that.<br /> <br /> Any of the splats can be horrible; vampires can be life-sucking, a mind-raping one person conspiracy; a werewolf can be a heartless marauding monster, tearing anyone who takes their fancy limb-from-limb; a mage can play sorcerer-king, bending the world to their will regardless of anyone else's desires.<br /> The point is they don't have to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, except, the whole point of VtR is acknowledging that, and trying to preserve a modicum of humanity. A werewolf's point is precisely not to be a mindless monster, and the mage thing? Their integritystat is called 'wisdom,' and playing sorcerer-kings is both a wisdom sin and people like GotV will sic you.<br /> <br /> All the games, the point is more 'not being a monster,' while a pretty big premise of Beast is, you know, being one and being proud of it, to the point of making Heroes, jerkass with a point, to be acceptable targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:34:43-07:00","id":551318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551221#post551221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, how do you think a rule along the lines of &amp;quot;Unbeknownst to anyone, whenever a Hero slays a Beast two more inevitably arise in its place&amp;quot; would affect the narrative? I think it would be a good way to get rid of the &amp;quot;Heroes are the good guys&amp;quot; problem, because then regardless of what you think of the Beasts the Heroes are Not. Helping.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Cut off one head, Two more shall take its place. Hail HYDRA!&quot; <br /> <br /> (In a game where you actually can be a Hydra <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:42:18-07:00","id":551334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551302#post551302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm, except, the whole point of VtR is acknowledging that, and trying to preserve a modicum of humanity. A werewolf's point is precisely not to be a mindless monster, and the mage thing? Their integritystat is called 'wisdom,' and playing sorcerer-kings is both a wisdom sin and people like GotV will sic you.<br /> <br /> All the games, the point is more 'not being a monster,' while a pretty big premise of Beast is, you know, being one and being proud of it, to the point of making Heroes, jerkass with a point, to be acceptable targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly; the point is to be more than a monster. That does not mean you can't be proud of it; a Blood Talon Rahu is most certainly proud of slaying a Predator King in single combat. This is equally applicable to Beasts.<br /> As for what makes Heroes 'acceptable targets', I never considered their 'jerkishness' to be a defining factor. More of an 'icing on the cake' thing. It was always more a case of self-defense to me; the Hero wants to kill the Beast and the Beast doesn't want to die. (Unfettered excused, naturally).<br /> Yes the Beast creates the Hero, but not on purpose. Not normally anyway; unless said Beast has gone too far. There is a reason why Esmee Childress is presented primarily as an antagonist; she might be a sympathetic figure to some character concepts, (which I would find distasteful and request that they not be played at my table), she places her goals above not only human morality but her Kin; fellow Beasts, Ghist, the vampires of New Orleans...<br /> <br /> Also heartless does not equal mindless. A high Harmony werewolf doesn't have a problem killing people for trespassing in what it considers it's territory. That doesn't mean it automatically will do so. This same principle can apply to the Begotten feeding their Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-12-2015, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:52:02-07:00","id":551356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551302#post551302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm, except, the whole point of VtR is acknowledging that, and trying to preserve a modicum of humanity. A werewolf's point is precisely not to be a mindless monster, and the mage thing? Their integritystat is called 'wisdom,' and playing sorcerer-kings is both a wisdom sin and people like GotV will sic you.<br /> <br /> All the games, the point is more 'not being a monster,' while a pretty big premise of Beast is, you know, being one and being proud of it, to the point of making Heroes, jerkass with a point, to be acceptable targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue the point of Requiem is the /inevitability/ of becoming detached from humanity, and the way a Kindred deals with it. And being or not being a 'monster' misses the point of Forsaken - the wolf must hunt, and each Uratha must find their balance with that. Bit comparing apples and oranges there.<br /> <br /> But this tangent is besides the original point you seem to be missing: what you are needn't match up to who you are. You can be anything from a Vampire to a Beast and not /need/ to be a horrible person.<br /> <br /> But also the premise of Primordial is that you're a nightmarish monster, so if someone can't stomach that inherent notion, maybe they're criticizing the wrong game for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-12-2015, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:57:33-07:00","id":551362,"title":"","content":"A Werewolf's &quot;not being a monster&quot; thing has about as much relevance to their harmony as a beasts does to their satiety. You can maintain harmony 5 (which is the optimal point) by carefully making sure to alternate between torture and cannibalism when you murder people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:02:25-07:00","id":551366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551356#post551356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue the point of Requiem is the /inevitability/ of becoming detached from humanity, and the way a Kindred deals with it. And being or not being a 'monster' misses the point of Forsaken - the wolf must hunt, and each Uratha must find their balance with that. Bit comparing apples and oranges there.<br /> <br /> But this tangent is besides the original point you seem to be missing: what you are needn't match up to who you are. You can be anything from a Vampire to a Beast and not /need/ to be a horrible person.<br /> <br /> But also the premise of Primordial is that you're a nightmarish monster, so if you're can't stomach that inherent notion, maybe you're criticizing the wrong game for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, except i was not exactly criticizing this aspect of the Beast. The monster-as-a-monster attitude is actually a part of Beast that I do like about.<br /> <br /> However there are points in the text that does kind of portray Beasts as (and shoehorn prospective Pcs into) dark heroes, / also portraying them as oppressed minority, something I think clashes somewhat thematically with 'you're a nightmarish monster' premise. I do think that Beasts inherently being monsters out of mortal moral boundary is not a bad thing, at all, but mixing them with the other theme is not actually helping. I mean, yeah, a lot of time mentioned are the cases of beasts who only hurt the 'deserving,' and that of course delivers sympathy, but that kind of goes against &quot;I am a dragon&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> Pardon me. I am babbling.<br /> <br /> Granted, publishing a line of all-terrifying-amoral-monsters is probably not viable at all, (Slasher, a designated Picaresque semi-splat, is a notable exception to this, and the developers acknowledge that) so yeah, I can't criticize the devs for promoting even in-game amorality, but at times I think it could have been presented better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:13:47-07:00","id":551388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551209#post551209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, I just figured it out.<br /> <br /> They're not supposed to represent the minorities.<br /> <br /> They're supposed to represent the <i>vilification itself</i>. The fear of the &quot;other&quot;.<br /> <br /> The destruction they wreak is the destruction that bigots <i>think</i> the minorities cause to society. Their power is the power bigots <i>think</i> minorities have. A Hero isn't a hypocrite, they're hypocrisy itself. They're the bigots' self-image, bent on taking down the very forces they created. But in the end it doesn't work. Their hate just contributes to the forces in the temenos, and breeds more beasts for them to fight.<br /> <br /> Beast's create Heroes, but &quot;heroes&quot; are the reason beasts exist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, they're intended to be a stand in for villains, or more accurately, crazy wonderful creatures just doing their thing who need to die because it looks impressive on the resume.<br /> <br /> Looks guys, I like repressed minority stories as much as anyone, but this is turning into Frozen all over again. It <i>can</i> be used that way, but it's not <i>wholly</i> about that. It's a deconstruction and subversion of the monomyth theory, that much is apparent. It has a lot of things to say about the violent cycles in our lives, that's fairly prominent subtextually. But saying &quot;Beasts are the viification of the lesbians/Mexicans/Muslims/etc.&quot; strikes me as confusing the vehicle for the passengers, particularly since much of the World of Darkness as a whole, and not just this game, place a lot of stock in the fear of the other and the use of monsters as a metaphor for anyone who feels outside of societies norms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:21:06-07:00","id":551400,"title":"","content":"@torete: I don't entirely see the Beasts as dark heroes or oppressed minority, but whatever clashes in the text in that regard is something I believe is necessary, especially in the perspective of the Begotten against a wider and more neutral one.<br /> <br /> It's on topic thoughtful babbling, so it's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:24:24-07:00","id":551402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551302#post551302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm, except, the whole point of VtR is acknowledging that, and trying to preserve a modicum of humanity. A werewolf's point is precisely not to be a mindless monster, and the mage thing? Their integritystat is called 'wisdom,' and playing sorcerer-kings is both a wisdom sin and people like GotV will sic you.<br /> <br /> All the games, the point is more 'not being a monster,' while a pretty big premise of Beast is, you know, being one and being proud of it, to the point of making Heroes, jerkass with a point, to be acceptable targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. It is more &quot; be in control of your monsterousness&quot; in most cases, or &quot;avoid being too extreme&quot; for most lines. The game lines split between those that hate what they are and those that embrace it.<br /> <br /> Mages, Geists, Demons, and Werewolves all embrace their supernatural role, and look in askance at those who try to deny what they are (Banishers, Integrators, etc). Their focus is on using their power and abilities with insight, and avoiding going off the deep end. For example, per Dave, the new Wisdom system can have a Seer who is high Wisdom while manipulating the world for selfish ends, while the selfless Arrow named Harry Dresden is teetering at the low end: their ability to control and efficiently use their abilities define them, not their morality. I put Demons here because they don't even think of themselves as humans; they only act as such because the GM will come down on them like a ton of bricks if they are too blatant.<br /> <br /> Then you have the &quot;But I don't want to be a monster&quot; groups, who try to stave it off (usually): vampires and prometheans. And even there there is a split, where one is trying to hold on to what thry lost and the other finding what they can become. These games are the closest (besides Hunter) on being focused on &quot;morality&quot; and not being the monster, as the Vampires realize they are damned and fear losing themselves to their Beast, while Prometheans want to be a human and thus try to emulate them. <br /> <br /> Changelings and hunters are the neutral parties. Hunters are human (mostly), so they come at this differently. For them, it is determining how far they are willing to go and how much they are willing to become what they hunt. Morality is going to come into play here. Not 1e capital M morality, but more the general elements of human ideas about what is right and wrong, and what the Hunter can personally tolerate. Changelings run the gamut from self hatred and fully embracing what they now are, and there is no consistent cultural association one way. I mean, when you sometimes aren't even sure if you escaped the Fae, their focus is more on recovering from their trauma and finding what empowers them (like actual abuse victims).<br /> <br /> And mummies... mummies are wierd and complex. They are monsters, no question. They, as they regain Memories, become less monsterous and against what they are, but not because they view themselves as monsters per se, but because they realize the nature of the cycle and the fact that they are trapped. Some are okay with this, accepting their role under the Judges, while others seek freedom through Aptothesis. And yet others turn towards forgetting everything and going back to being automatons. <br /> <br /> My point is that Beast falls into the same category as the first. In fact, their mechanic is similar to Harmony or Synergy, in that it is more of a representation of you balance between two extremes that each have merit. They aren't exceptions, but fall in with a half of the gamelines, where the question isn't about not being a monster (it is too late to avoid that) but what type of monster you want to be. Do you want to be:<ul><li>Smaug: the proud and selfish force of destruction, who has no doubts about his superiority and right to be what he is.</li> <li> Slenderman: a quiet intelligent force that stalks and kills it's pray without a trace, but doesn't seem to revel in what it is. It just does what it does.</li> <li>the Kingpin (Netflix Daredevil): a powerful force who sees himself as beneficial and his evil as necessary ro allow a better world, bur who deep down is a disturbed individual</li> <li>Batman: a force that knows they can never be truly healed, turning theor darkness into a means for good whose discipline prevents them from going to far</li> <li>Or someone else?</li> </ul>Cause while Beasts are monsters and accept this, they still have the power to define <i> what type of monster they will be </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:36:41-07:00","id":551426,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, at their core monsters are all manifestations of this fear of the &quot;others&quot;. For as long as humans existed we've had this &quot;us vs them&quot; mentality. It worked in small tight-knit tribes, where anyone you didn't know, anyone &quot;different&quot; was likely from a rival tribe and therefore probably competition for scarce resources at the very least, and therefore &quot;the enemy&quot;. As our society grew this fear remained, with nothing to attach it to, so we started to invent our own. <br /> <br /> While the other monsters are &quot;them&quot;, I see beasts as the fear itself. Fear of the unknown. It festers beneath the surface, grows fangs and claws. The collective unconsciousness thought &quot;here there be dragons&quot; and lo and behold, there they sprang up. They're not <i>really </i>vilification incarnate, not originally, but that's how the fear that birthed them manifests most prominently in modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:37:55-07:00","id":551427,"title":"","content":"@Freemind: Good point. I sorta concentrated on the hunger/satiation aspect for the Beast, which kind of railroaded me into thinking like... Vampire mindset.<br /> But you are correct. Beast mentality would be more similar to Mage mentality.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, though, the book actually talks a lot about cases of Beasts 'only abusing who deserves it,' which IS kind of more vampire and less mage way to go about their monstrous life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:42:36-07:00","id":551429,"title":"","content":"I think I read something but not sure: With geists do the sin eaters see beasts for what they truly are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:13:45-07:00","id":551531,"title":"","content":"Also, I want to touch on something that keeps bugging me (especially since I just gave a lecture on this topic): Victimization is not Justification. Specifically, citing that the Heroes have a right to kill beasts as they are victims or that the Beasts are harmful is not okay.<br /> <br /> Being a victim is a seperate and isolated experience from the means of coping and acts that follow after. Even if the acts are directly linked to the act, if unhealthy or inappropriate they should not be tolerated. At the same time, you have to recognize that the event was traumatic and that the person is a victim. <br /> <br /> For example, I had a an adolescent patient who attempted to kill his father, who had been physically and verbally abused by his father since he was 3. His mother had also suffered abuse and had been afraid to come forward or protect her son because of fear of reprisal. This father was a horrible person, had a criminal and substance abuse history, and is as far from a sympathetic. Yet the son's response is still not the appropriate response, no matter what. As much as the Dad might seemed to have deserved it, the response was not an effective coping mechanism, nor would it be beneficial in the long run. What's more, it was the cusp of other violent tendencies that the son had begun to manifest as his outlet for frustrations, especially towards autority figures, and he likely would have gone in to hurt others too. <br /> <br /> With him, the whole thing was seperating his response from him being a victim. Which is hard. You felt for this kid. But while I can sympathize, and did acknowledge his suffering, I also had to rebuild his world view to not being defined by his anger and fear of his father. <br /> <br /> And there are myriad other examples of this. One of the biggest pedictors violent and predatory behavior in adults was being victimized as a child or adolescent. This is due to the fact that their identities are still forming and thus they are susceptible to having such acts lead to inappropriate development, especially if they had co-morbid conditions that make then more susceptible to having poor coping mechanisms Even adults have these breaks, though it is less common as their identities and coping mechanisms are more fixed and defined. But in all cases, you do not allow them to justify their actions through their nature as victims, as it validates that their response is appropriate. You acknowledge their suffering and the evils of what was done to them, but then must make it clear that said events do not make their current actions or thoughts okay. <br /> <br /> This is the nature of the heroes. They are victims of the Beasts. As much as I like the idea of them being puppets in the Mythic Arc that surrounds the Beasts (just as the Beast is) they are still victims even in that scenario, as they susceptible humans who were cast in a role after having their soul attacked by a Beast's Soul. To pretend that the heroes aren't victims or deserved it is wrong, as it is ignoring the fact that their soul was ravaged, likely more then once. But one also needs to acknowledge their coping mechanism and response is excessive and unhealthy, especially since their quest doesn't end with the death of their tormentor, and will usually leas them to their own destruction. Their delusions and single minded focus on their hatred of the monsters can be explained by the Beasts attack on them, and it is unfortunate that it happened, but these thoughts and the resulting actions are not healthy nor good things to have. <br /> <br /> To parrallel it with an extreme example, a hero is akin to a rape victim who has decided to kill off all men to prevent anyone ever from being raped again*. Rape is never ever okay, the perpetrators are (in my mind) some of the worst people on earth, but the single minded and excessive response is not okay either. To target not only the perpetrator but all who are just associated with the ability to be such perpetrators as needing to die is not a healthy nor justified response. <br /> <br /> TL;DNR (like half the Medical Students in my lecture): Beasts can be violators. Heroes are the victims of those Beasts who are. This part is tragic. The heroes actions after , however, are not justified nor healthy.<br /> <br /> *note, this isn't hyperbole: I had a colleague who was called in to treat a girl who tried to rundown several boys crossing the street who cited this as her reasoning to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":".  Stupid, crappy, old phone 06-12-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:28:23-07:00","id":551560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551427#post551427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Freemind: Good point. I sorta concentrated on the hunger/satiation aspect for the Beast, which kind of railroaded me into thinking like... Vampire mindset.<br /> But you are correct. Beast mentality would be more similar to Mage mentality.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, though, the book actually talks a lot about cases of Beasts 'only abusing who deserves it,' which IS kind of more vampire and less mage way to go about their monstrous life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I would still say it is accepting what you are and deciding how you are going to use it. A beast who hunts and beats up criminals using his powers is not pretending he isn't a monster. He knows he is. He just is choosing who is going to fear him, and how far he is willing to go. I mean:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am vengeance! I am the night! I. AM. BATMAN! </div> </div> </div>There is no doubt or shame of who or what he is, or even what drives him. I am sorry i keep going back to him, but Batman just works so well as Beast who has directed his darkness towards good an entire city of criminals who fear him, driven by vengeance and the need to punish criminals, but never going to far. He is an example of a Beast who uses his powers and hunger to achieve something positive (and might even have a pretty high satiety... Gotham has a ton of criminals and a prison with revolving doors).<br /> <br /> The reason it is different from vampires is that even targeting the bad guys reminds them of their monstrosity at higher humanity, as this means they are still acknowledging that <i>they are monsters</i> who are making concious efforts not to be. Beasts don't have that problem: they never deny they are monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-12-2015, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:42:59-07:00","id":551583,"title":"","content":"And I just realized something: The Joker is a good example of a hero. Though the origin story varies(which, like the movie, is varied and all contradictory), Batman almost always played a part in his creation, chasing the man who would be Joker into a chemical plant, where the man fell into a vat while trying to escape. He became the Joker, and his insanity is fixed on besting or hating the Batman. His entire nature is defined by this fixation, and he even becomes sane and gives up crime in one story when he thinks batman was dead. He sees his actions as part of a dualistic game between him and batman, and all the evil he does as just part of playing that game.<br /> <br /> Though... he also would be a fun beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:45:46-07:00","id":551588,"title":"","content":"<i>Thank you</i> for delving into that important topic in such a comprehensive manner, Freemind. It's been brought up before but quite a few people seemed to still be missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-12-2015, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:51:07-07:00","id":551604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551583#post551583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I just realized something: The Joker is a good example of a hero. Though the origin story varies(which, like the movie, is varied and all contradictory), Batman almost always played a part in his creation, chasing the man who would be Joker into a chemical plant, where the man fell into a vat while trying to escape. He became the Joker, and his insanity is fixed on besting or hating the Batman. His entire nature is defined by this fixation, and he even becomes sane and gives up crime in one story when he thinks batman was dead. He sees his actions as part of a dualistic game between him and batman, and all the evil he does as just part of playing that game.<br /> <br /> Though... he also would be a fun beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joker came to my mind as well, but I thought of him first as a Beast... although Batman was too decent a person to be a WoD Hero. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then again, yeah. Batman also is a great Beast, considering his main theme IS manipulating the fear in others. Granted, he uses his power and prowess for good, but definite Beast theme right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:59:01-07:00","id":551615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551604#post551604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, he uses his power and prowess for good, but definite Beast theme right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So can Beasts. He's an Ugallu Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:01:13-07:00","id":551619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551615#post551615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So can Beasts. He's an Ugallu Nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of what I meant to say, but went right out of my brain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yeah Ugallu Nemesis indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:16:49-07:00","id":551661,"title":"","content":"Batman fits in pretty well since more than a few members of his rogue's gallery have targeted him as an enemy, rather than committing crime. Many are obsessed with him to a point that seems similar to Heroes.<br /> <br /> Though he's been depicted in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tpu6yPAFHrs\" target=\"_blank\">many different ways</a> throughout his 76 years.<br /> <br /> Video is probably NSFW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:23:17-07:00","id":551671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551583#post551583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I just realized something: The Joker is a good example of a hero. Though the origin story varies(which, like the movie, is varied and all contradictory), Batman almost always played a part in his creation, chasing the man who would be Joker into a chemical plant, where the man fell into a vat while trying to escape. He became the Joker, and his insanity is fixed on besting or hating the Batman. His entire nature is defined by this fixation, and he even becomes sane and gives up crime in one story when he thinks batman was dead. He sees his actions as part of a dualistic game between him and batman, and all the evil he does as just part of playing that game.<br /> <br /> Though... he also would be a fun beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>If i was too do the Joker in WoD he would be a Hero, His Origin is and has always been &quot;Multiple Choice&quot; for this i'd have him as a constant Victim that's Pysche has shattered from abuse from multiple people/Supernaturals. Domination, Mind Arcana, Lunacy Etc... Every Type of Supernatural has attacked him and broken him. Only one hasn't..... Batman, The Beast that gave him form.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mostly I use that as Jusification for why the Joker refuses too kill Bat's, he's too important for his Self-Image, he just can't Destroy him... Doesn't mean he can't make his life &quot;Interesting&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-12-2015, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:57:19-07:00","id":551744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551225#post551225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on you idea <b>Elfive</b> is that if you want to get rid of the &quot;Heroes are the good guys&quot; narrative than your Heroes inadvertantly create Beasts idea would work wonders since it's a Beast's Hunger that brings out the Heroic urge in those lacking self-worth. You could have it be that as a Hero grows by each Beast slain that Beast's hunger disperces back into the Primordial Dream, and from the bloody remains new Souls emearge Hungry for more blood and fear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do have some Mythological precedent for that phenomenon (i.e.: Pegasus and Chrysaor), so it wouldn't be incongruous to add that in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-12-2015, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:10:43-07:00","id":551788,"title":"","content":"Also, the book mentions that Hercules was responsible for creating a vast number of children. And with this idea, Hercules Heroes would be responsible for creating a vast number of Children. <br /> <br /> Illuminati Confirmed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:16:00-07:00","id":551791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551366#post551366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, except i was not exactly criticizing this aspect of the Beast. The monster-as-a-monster attitude is actually a part of Beast that I do like about.<br /> <br /> However there are points in the text that does kind of portray Beasts as (and shoehorn prospective Pcs into) dark heroes, / also portraying them as oppressed minority, something I think clashes somewhat thematically with 'you're a nightmarish monster' premise. I do think that Beasts inherently being monsters out of mortal moral boundary is not a bad thing, at all, but mixing them with the other theme is not actually helping. I mean, yeah, a lot of time mentioned are the cases of beasts who only hurt the 'deserving,' and that of course delivers sympathy, but that kind of goes against &quot;I am a dragon&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> Pardon me. I am babbling.<br /> <br /> Granted, publishing a line of all-terrifying-amoral-monsters is probably not viable at all, (Slasher, a designated Picaresque semi-splat, is a notable exception to this, and the developers acknowledge that) so yeah, I can't criticize the devs for promoting even in-game amorality, but at times I think it could have been presented better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immorality. Werewolves might be more properly described as amoral, in that the moral implications behind what they do hold little or no concern for their spiritual wellbeing, whereas both Slashers, and potentially Beasts, pursue villainous behavior for its own ends, which is definitely immoral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-12-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:29:23-07:00","id":551817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551791#post551791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immorality. Werewolves can be more properly described as amoral, in that the moral implications behind what they do hold little or no concern for their spiritual wellbeing,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true, in fact what they do has a great impact on their spiritual wellbeing, the thing is they don't work off the common moral system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:46:51-07:00","id":551832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551604#post551604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joker came to my mind as well, but I thought of him first as a Beast... although Batman was too decent a person to be a WoD Hero. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then again, yeah. Batman also is a great Beast, considering his main theme IS manipulating the fear in others. Granted, he uses his power and prowess for good, but definite Beast theme right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that second bit was my point: the focus on how Beasts have to be <b>evil</b> monsters because they feed by inflicting fear and harm is overlooking that they, with discipline, can be... while not nice, not evil at least. I mean, Batman even admits he isn't a good guy:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Clark wanted to, he could use his superspeed and squish me into the cement. But I know how he thinks. Even more than the Kryptonite, he's got one big weakness. Deep down, Clark's essentially a good person... and deep down, I'm not. </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is how I view the way Beasts approach it: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I decided early that I would never take a life. Right around the time I decided that I wanted to live. It wasn't an arbitrary decision and it was more than moral. It's about identity. As long as you can choose that, choose who you are in the world... you can choose to call yourself sane </div> </div> </div><br /> PS. I think my Batman binge is coming from this cool kid I got called to on a consult. Batman is his icon and he dresses up as him (he is 6). Kid is pretty bad ass: he is fighting ALL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-12-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:49:07-07:00","id":551836,"title":"","content":"I Fixed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:55:21-07:00","id":551842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551604#post551604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joker came to my mind as well, but I thought of him first as a Beast... although Batman was too decent a person to be a WoD Hero. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then again, yeah. Batman also is a great Beast, considering his main theme IS manipulating the fear in others. Granted, he uses his power and prowess for good, but definite Beast theme right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight derailment, the thing i fond Funny about Batman is the Fact he Qualifies for 2 of the Lantern Corps, almost 3 of them if not for the other 2 emotions. Fear and Willpower, Anger and Disipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:56:49-07:00","id":551844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551531#post551531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DNR (like half the Medical Students in my lecture): Beasts can be violators. Heroes are the victims of those Beasts who are. This part is tragic. The heroes actions after , however, are not justified nor healthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that, as written, Heroes literally don't have the free will to choose to act differently. The only way they can break free of the role forced on them is to rise above Integrity 4.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is also something where the book suffers for being farmed out piecemeal to different writers, since different sections seem to have different basic assumptions about how the mindset of being a Hero works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a