ts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:14:14-07:00","id":551862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551845#post551845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://media.comicbook.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/batman-wonder-woman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>...... Diana is a Anakim Tyrant......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:20:05-07:00","id":551865,"title":"","content":"Wonder Woman is really not about fear, though I guess you could say she inspires fear in people afraid of powerful women, that's a bit of a stretch. Though it would explain her rogues gallery.<br /> <br /> In that story she was being influenced by the power of the Black Lantern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:57:27-07:00","id":551911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551671#post551671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If i was too do the Joker in WoD he would be a Hero, His Origin is and has always been &amp;quot;Multiple Choice&amp;quot; for this i'd have him as a constant Victim that's Pysche has shattered from abuse from multiple people/Supernaturals. Domination, Mind Arcana, Lunacy Etc... Every Type of Supernatural has attacked him and broken him. Only one hasn't..... Batman, The Beast that gave him form.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mostly I use that as Jusification for why the Joker refuses too kill Bat's, he's too important for his Self-Image, he just can't Destroy him... Doesn't mean he can't make his life &amp;quot;Interesting&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Though he did attempt to kill off all the bat family to make batman into the ultimate hero, a force force if vengeance aimed at him, thr ultimate supervillian. The coup de grace being their mutual destruction. <br /> <br /> And in general, he doesn't try to not kill Batman. So he will set up the traps and situations with the full intent to kill batman. He just isn't broken up when he &quot;gets to keep playing the game.&quot; <br /> <br /> But yeah. No metaphor is perfect. But I like your idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:09:35-07:00","id":551956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551911#post551911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice. Though he did attempt to kill off all the bat family to make batman into the ultimate hero, a force force if vengeance aimed at him, thr ultimate supervillian. The coup de grace being their mutual destruction.<br /> <br /> And in general, he doesn't try to not kill Batman. So he will set up the traps and situations with the full intent to kill batman. He just isn't broken up when he &quot;gets to keep playing the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah. No metaphor is perfect. But I like your idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>He Also gets jealous if he thinks someone else has taken his Toy away.<br /> The Bat Family isn't Batman, They aren't his Obsession, so they are his target since he Thinks they weaken Ol' Battsi. And your right, he Doesn't pull his punches, since he knows Bats can handle it. He's actually pretty menacing when it's anyone but Bat's he's against, He will not care about them or play &quot;Fair&quot; against them because Bat's doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:35:15-07:00","id":552008,"title":"","content":"In an attempt to make things a little less problematic, here is how I'm going to pitch it to my group:<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is home to terrible things, most of them wrought by mortal hands, but what mortals do leaves lasting impressions on dreams. Urban legends drift into truth, nightmares turn real, and life imitates fiction, becomes legend, and the circle continues. Beasts and Heroes are both victims, trapped in their own cyclic narrative; they were each once mortals, and they were each exposed to the supernatural. For the Beasts, what they learned and found tormented them until they became like it. For Heroes, what they found terrified them that they have broken themselves trying to stay away from it - and destroy that which has become it. To them, the Beasts have switched sides. To the Beasts, however, in becoming the legend they have prevented something far worse, and in feeding, they protect other mortals from falling into the same terrible revelations that turned them into what they are today.<br /> <br /> so you have Beasts as people who saw the darkness and in order to halt the spread, became it, and try to hide it because they know the situation (supernatural stuff hiding itself) is not permanent, but that no one is prepared for it, and Heroes as people who saw the darkness for what it was and recoiled from it so violently that they want to destroy everything in it, but they can't. They come up against Beasts because they are dressed like the enemy and because Heroes are loose cannons: they will use their supernatural abilities publicly and dangerously - in their attempts to save lives, they will ruin lives instead.<br /> <br /> Beasts try to track down supernatural things and either help them be less destructive/hide them/prepare nearby mortals to face it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:06:19-07:00","id":552053,"title":"","content":"I know the post has moved past this point but I still feel that expanding the section describing the Primordial Dream shouldn't mean eliminating the section with Angels. In order for Beast to be truly Crossover friendly they need to have a way to build Angels since that's an integral part of Demon. It's true that Beast and Demons have little reason to get along, but the God Machine can be anywhere. And you cannot have a God Machine Chronicle without Angels.<br /> <br /> I feel that cutting back some of the fluff involving the Beasts's Hungers that they repeat like three times about would be a much better use of trimming the text to expand the Dark Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:42:14-07:00","id":552104,"title":"","content":"If there's space for both Astral Entities <i>and</i> Angels, then sure; include them both. But if you have to choose between them, please favor the Astral Entities over the Angels. <br /> <br /> In particular, it's worth noting that Demons are the one crossover that Beast deliberately <i>doesn't</i> cater to; and if you <i>are</i> doing a crossover featuring demons and/or the God-Machine, then <b>Demon</b> and/or <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> will supply the necessary rules for Angels. Conversely, Astral Entities are likely to show up even in a <b>Beast</b> chronicle that doesn't feature <i>any</i> crossovers: if your Lair is anything at all like a mage's Oneiros, it's likely to have creatures in it; and those creatures would be Astral Entities by definition. As such, I would argue that their inclusion in the game is even more important than the inclusion of ghosts and spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:45:47-07:00","id":552105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551844#post551844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem here is that, as written, Heroes literally don't have the free will to choose to act differently. The only way they can break free of the role forced on them is to rise above Integrity 4.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is also something where the book suffers for being farmed out piecemeal to different writers, since different sections seem to have different basic assumptions about how the mindset of being a Hero works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heroes are entirely capable of choosing to act differently. They suffer for it, yes, but it is a choice they can make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:46:26-07:00","id":552106,"title":"","content":"It still caters to Demon, just not in the same way.<br /> <br /> Let's not mistake benefiting for catering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:12:05-07:00","id":552165,"title":"","content":"You guys make excellent points, and in retrospect if they had to cut something Angels would be a good choice since they only occupy one paragraph and add little but a bit of fluff and the basic mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:13:55-07:00","id":552167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552053#post552053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the post has moved past this point but I still feel that expanding the section describing the Primordial Dream shouldn't mean eliminating the section with Angels. In order for Beast to be truly Crossover friendly they need to have a way to build Angels since that's an integral part of Demon. It's true that Beast and Demons have little reason to get along, but the God Machine can be anywhere. And you cannot have a God Machine Chronicle without Angels.<br /> <br /> I feel that cutting back some of the fluff involving the Beasts's Hungers that they repeat like three times about would be a much better use of trimming the text to expand the Dark Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The GM has become a big part of the WoD, it would be absurd to ignore it just because Beast find Demons creepy. Which makes me think: Do we know how Beasts react to stigmatics and vice-versa? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:21:31-07:00","id":552172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552167#post552167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. The GM has become a big part of the WoD, it would be absurd to ignore it just because Beast find Demons creepy. Which makes me think: Do we know how Beasts react to stigmatics and vice-versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's not so much &quot;find Demons creepy&quot; as it is &quot;Demons and Angels are man-flavored robot ghosts from the alien future outside of time and sideways, and therefore not from the same stock.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mother could be, though &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:22:30-07:00","id":552174,"title":"","content":"From the kickstarter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matthew McFarland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heya, Matt here.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So, first of all, I want to thank all (as of this writing) 1,147 folks who have backed Beast. Your support means everything to the project, not just in the form of your hard-earned cash, but also in the form of the comments and discussion here. It\u2019s been a real pleasure to watch people talk about Beast, analyze it in terms of media, discuss what Dark Eras would be cool, and plan out the characters they want to make. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">But not all Beast discussion has been quite so positive, and I want to talk about that. Stay with me a minute. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">With Beast, we tried doing a bunch of things differently. Some of those things were purely mechanical; the game doesn\u2019t have a \u201cfuel trait\u201d the way our other games do, for instance, nor does its Integrity analogue function the way that other such traits do. Moreover, it was always our intention to take a light touch with Beast \u201csociety;\u201d I didn\u2019t want the same kind of structure that, say, Vampire or Changeling uses. The Hero/Beast dynamic, too, came out differently than I was intending. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The result of that is the game has some issues. If you\u2019ve followed discussion of the game on various online forums, you\u2019ve probably seen it. I\u2019m not going to repeat every point, here, mostly in the interests of time (I\u2019ve got a development pass to get started on!), but here\u2019s the gist: We hear you. There are problems with the game as it stands. Some of those problems come from the fact that we did try and break some new ground on the game, and that always carries a chance of something coming out different that one planned. Some of it just the nature of game development; at this stage of the process, things are getting tweaked. The difference is that it\u2019s more public than it\u2019s ever been. And some of it is that, honestly, when you\u2019re as close to the material as I and the other writers have been, it\u2019s easy to lose perspective. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Of course, the game hasn\u2019t been received wholly negatively. I\u2019ve had the pleasure of watching folks who really like the game talk about their inspirations, their character ideas, and the mechanical innovations we\u2019ve made. We\u2019ve heard those voices, too, and as we move forward, we\u2019re listening to the positive feedback as well as the criticism. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">What all that means is this: I\u2019m doing another development pass on Beast. I\u2019m going to add about 15,000 words of text (give or take), and do some heavy revision on parts of the game. My plan is to have that done by next Friday, June 19, but if that changes during the week, I\u2019ll let you know. As I revise chapters, I\u2019m going to give them to Rose to link from the Kickstarter, and I\u2019ll be putting them up on Google Drive and doing posts on the Onyx Path blog so you can see what we\u2019re doing. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Here\u2019s a quick list of the overarching things we\u2019re addressing. Note that I\u2019m enumerating specific changes here (that is, I\u2019m saying what we\u2019re changing but not how), because I\u2019m still compiling my notes and making a plan. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Resolving the \u201care you born a Beast or not?\u201d question. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Defining Beast culture; we\u2019re not adding social splats, but we are giving Beast society some structure and giving Storytellers something more to work with (this is where a lot of the extra word count is going)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Further definition of the Primordial Dream, its relationship to Beasts and Heroes, and what you can do with it in play (this is where a lot of the rest of the word count is going)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Hand in hand with that point, we\u2019re underlining Beast-on-Beast conflict more</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Redefining the Beast/Hero relationship, and (more to the point), revising how the text treats Heroes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Looking at the crossover sections and making sure they reflect the other game lines well, and that they get across our intent with making Beast crossover friendly</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Making sure that in-character opinions are clearly reflected as such; all of the World of Darkness games include unreliable narrators, but it\u2019s important (especially for a new game) that the reader understands what the game assumes to be true and what a character within the game assumes to be true</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022 Giving Beasts something specific to do. That was definitely the most exciting part of the meeting that we had last night. I think you\u2019ll like it. It addresses one of the biggest points of criticism we\u2019ve had, which is that a Beast sating its Hunger is pretty much just cruel and abusive for the sake of it. I want characters in my game to be monstrous; they\u2019re Beasts, after all. But I want there to be a point. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There are other, minor revisions that\u2019ll happen, too, most of them logical outgrowths of the list above. Stay tuned, watch this space, and thank you for all your feedback. This is going to make for an intense week for me, but I\u2019m excited to do the work. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Watch this space (regardless of what space you\u2019re seeing this on, it\u2019ll at least get linked) for more information, and again, thank you for your support and your feedback. Criticism stings, but it teaches a lesson. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And that\u2019s an appropriate note to end on, I think.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:27:29-07:00","id":552180,"title":"","content":"Was literally just about to share that. Much to dwell on! Much goodness forthcoming, one could hope","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:32:15-07:00","id":552182,"title":"","content":"Any time you encounter something, whether it's new or not, you change. That change can be better or worse, and while there are times where you can't decide if the change makes you worse, like losing your house or your car or getting some money stolen. Other times you can decide, based on the incident. Like waking up from a nap and finding you don't have the food you want to eat, so you make something good with what you've got left, or your car runs out of gas in some town in the middle of nowhere, but you decide to just have your vacation right there on the road.<br /> <br /> Story.<br /> <br /> There's this boy out hunting for some peccary, and he runs across a rattlesnake on the road. Rattlesnake calls out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, hey, you!&quot; rattlesnake says.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, what?&quot; boy answers.<br /> <br /> &quot;My den, it's all the way up that straight cliff,&quot; rattlesnake says. &quot;Do you think you can carry me up there?&quot;<br /> <br /> Boy says no, and that he's afraid of getting bitten. Rattlesnake says he won't bite, he swears. Eventually they work out a deal, the boy'll take the rattlesnake up the cliff if the rattlesnake tells him where to find peccary. Then, real careful, the boy picks up the snake and starts climbing. They get about two-thirds the way up when the snake bites the boy in the arm.<br /> <br /> &quot;You promised you wouldn't bite me!&quot; boy shouts.<br /> <br /> &quot;You knew what I was!&quot; snake shouts.<br /> <br /> They land, boy breaks his legs, feels the snake venom running through his body, rolls to the snake.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to die!&quot; boy shouts.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think I can solve this,&quot; snake says, and slithers off into the bushes.<br /> <br /> Snake comes back with a dress covered in diamonds.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wear this,&quot; snake says.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's a girl's dress,&quot; boy says.<br /> <br /> Snake gives him the &quot;I am disappoint&quot; stare and the boy puts it on. Immediately the boy starts screaming in pain, feeling his body distort and become something else. He realizes he's turned into a woman, and then he starts stretching and stretching and his arms and legs get sucked up into his body and now he's a lady snake.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was saving it for a girl I liked,&quot; snake says. &quot;But at least you're alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> The new snake's understandably upset, but figures there's at least some good can come out of it. Another hunter comes along.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you!&quot; the new snake says. &quot;Our den's up on that cliff, think you can take us up there?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, you know, you can't avoid getting bit. That already happened. Now all you're getting asked is if you want to bite through the pain and hope the venom doesn't drive you crazy, or you going to put on that dress?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:48:31-07:00","id":552188,"title":"","content":"I really want Beasts to be the splat that keeps reinforcing the masquerade, because they are trying to scare people into not looking too deeply into particular things because those things are way more dangerous than Beasts, while also testing and preparing people for when the masquerade does eventually break down so it's not a huge mess - like Delta Green except you're playing Medusa and the Orochi, and Heroes as the dangerous outliers who don't care if they have to tear the goddamn masquerade down, because Destroy All Monsters!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The many men, so beautiful!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And they all dead did lie:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And a thousand thousand slimy things</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lived on; and so did I.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:04:05-07:00","id":552226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552104#post552104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's space for both Astral Entities <i>and</i> Angels, then sure; include them both. But if you have to choose between them, please favor the Astral Entities over the Angels.<br /> <br /> In particular, it's worth noting that Demons are the one crossover that Beast deliberately <i>doesn't</i> cater to; and if you <i>are</i> doing a crossover featuring demons and/or the God-Machine, then <b>Demon</b> and/or <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> will supply the necessary rules for Angels. Conversely, Astral Entities are likely to show up even in a <b>Beast</b> chronicle that doesn't feature <i>any</i> crossovers: if your Lair is anything at all like a mage's Oneiros, it's likely to have creatures in it; and those creatures would be Astral Entities by definition. As such, I would argue that their inclusion in the game is even more important than the inclusion of ghosts and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see so many thematically appropriate ways to include Astral Entities in a Beast game, including but not limited to the aforementioned Dragon-worshipping Kobolds scenario. I wonder if you could eat/lead them for cheap Satiety recovery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:09:29-07:00","id":552228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552188#post552188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want Beasts to be the splat that keeps reinforcing the masquerade, because they are trying to scare people into not looking too deeply into particular things because those things are way more dangerous than Beasts, while also testing and preparing people for when the masquerade does eventually break down so it's not a huge mess - like Delta Green except you're playing Medusa and the Orochi, and Heroes as the dangerous outliers who don't care if they have to tear the goddamn masquerade down, because Destroy All Monsters!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The many men, so beautiful!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And they all dead did lie:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And a thousand thousand slimy things</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lived on; and so did I.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That'd work well, and it would better help splats that can't magically enforce their Masquerade or are badly affected by Mortals hanging around, like Mages and Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:16:41-07:00","id":552238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=551844#post551844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem here is that, as written, Heroes literally don't have the free will to choose to act differently. The only way they can break free of the role forced on them is to rise above Integrity 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow. Are you implying that people choose to develop maladaptive and unhealthy psychiatric states choose to? <br /> <br /> Because that wasn't what I said, nor is it true. People don't choose to go off the deep end, nor does everyone who experiences trauma develop significant crises. But few people come through unscathed and have behavioral changes that are their means to cope, which aren't a choice, it is what people need to do as thinking organisms. <br /> <br /> But some do develop problems. These individuals are often susceptible and have already had other events or poor coping skills that made them vulnerable, and the trauma is the final straw. These patients develop maladaptive behaviors, delusions, and even full blown psychiatric conditions that result in maladaptive and possibly dangerous behavior. But once again, this isn't a choice.<br /> <br /> Yet while not a choice, it doesn't mean the actions are permissible or justified. Even in criminal law, where there is a plead of insanity, this doesn't excuse the actions or say that they are justified, merely that the person doesn't even have the capability to grasp how bad the action is and needs treatment so they might be able to one day. No matter what, you work to curb the maladaptive behaviors, and <br /> <br /> The thing is, heroes literally follow the classic model of those who develop maladaptive psych. They are individuals who have a lowered threshold and poor sense of identity, which is represented by their lowered integrity. They are exposed to a massive destabilizer, which causes them to decompensate and develop maladaptive behaviors and thought processes, which like many trauma victims, are focused on the incident that destabilized them. Even a Hero's recovery mimics how we work with such patients: it is about rebuilding their sense of self that is separate from the incident, and helping them break from the maladaptive behavior (in other words, recovering someone who sees nothing wrong back to above integrity 4).<br /> <br /> But also note that I am not saying the Beasts &quot;kill the heroes, cause they are bastards&quot; is okay either. While the heroes actions aren't excusable, they also are still victims. The optimal solution would be rehabilitation, and the game even gives mechanics for this, but I amssume since this is the WoD that rehabilitation is rare. And Beasts are much like the general population on mental health: They have difficulty either seeing past the actions, or if they do, don't get that the hero can't help it and that they must just be assholes or people who need to be put down or locked away.<br /> <br /> It's not a perfect analogy. They never are, but the parallels are there. I know I am working with a very difficult subject, and while I have a lot of experience with this type of stuff, I am not a final authority nor do I even pretend to know the game designers intent. <br /> <br /> PS. I also want to point out, before people counter with Matt's comments on &quot;but heroes aren't crazy&quot;, there is a difference between insanity, maladaptive behavior, and delusions. People with maladaptive behaviors and delusions can beotherwise highly cognitive and rational, but work from a distorted view of things regarding the topic of their delusions. I view heroes in the same lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:23:36-07:00","id":552268,"title":"","content":"I'm really looking forward to the changes Matt is making, I really liked the original for it's flaws, but I think that this will just make me like it more. Now, if we got a crossover based supplement that focused on groups like the Strix and the Pure, I'd be even happier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:47:34-07:00","id":552285,"title":"","content":"A Beast is similar to a Sin-Eater, just, instead of dying, you see something scary and you react to it. If you react to it by letting it overwhelm you, you're out of the game. If you own it and consume it, you become a Beast. If you recoil in disgust and want everything to go back the way it was, you become a Hero. A Beast is like a Vampire, in that it must do terrible things to survive. It's like a Changeling, in that everything it knew is gone. It's like a Promethean, because it's trying to figure out what being alive means. It's like a Werewolf, because the Beast must hunt. It's like a Mage, because it must find the hidden pathways to wisdom. The Beast is like a Hunter, because it knows what's there to lose. It's like a Demon, in that it's a stranger in its own skin.<br /> <br /> Whether you own it or not, Beast or Hero, you start recognizing the world for what it is. You see the problems and the monsters and you feel the hunger in your stomach. You have a choice there \u2013 you can become the monster, abuse the abusers, kill, maim, or terrify people who don't really deserve it, or you can find the monsters and see what they're doing, what they need, what you can get for them. But you know mortals, too, and you know they're just trapped in the middle. Everyone who could have helped them has been doing nothing but hiding for so long that if everyone knew what was going on, there'd be anarchy. So your other choice comes into play: keep things secret while preparing everyone else to see what you did, to experience it. This means you have to scare people away from things more dangerous than you, while also teaching them how to handle it if it comes down to that, but without them knowing. Become the monster and grow the legend, because if you don't, the whole thing comes crashing down.<br /> <br /> Heroes, on the other hand, they went a little crazy. They don't want it to be true. They're afraid of what's real, or they think that what's real is a lie. They're a little bit right, the world is terrible and you have to do terrible things to live in it, but that doesn't mean you should burn it all down \u2013 that hurts more than it helps. So, even if you, the monster, are trying to make things better, you have to deal with Heroes one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","user":"raygungoth","date":". 06-12-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:23:09-07:00","id":552327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552238#post552238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow. Are you implying that people choose to develop maladaptive and unhealthy psychiatric states choose to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only issue that I have with requiring Heroes to have Integrity 4 or below is your overlapping with Slashers (which to be honest, far more interesting than Heroes) and are weaker for it given their current state.<br /> <br /> Really, as it currently stands, anything I see a Hero is useful for, a Slasher can do and will do better so that needs to be fleshed out a bit (which is one of Matt's points are thankfully).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:41:30-07:00","id":552334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552327#post552327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only issue that I have with requiring Heroes to have Integrity 4 or below is your overlapping with Slashers (which to be honest, far more interesting than Heroes) and are weaker for it given their current state.<br /> <br /> Really, as it currently stands, anything I see a Hero is useful for, a Slasher can do and will do better so that needs to be fleshed out a bit (which is one of Matt's points are thankfully).<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that is a different thing. Mechanics is a whole other mess, and not what I was responding to. I also think Beast makes a good point that you shouldn't compare splats of combat. <br /> <br /> But if that is the issue, I think it is a good thing to bring up here too.<br /> <br /> Though I need to ask(since I can't remember): can Slashers recover? Or is it a permanent state? Cause the fact that Heroes can recover (not saying they do) and get back to some normalcy is a good thing (from an objective standpoint of &quot;this person is now mentally stable).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:50:46-07:00","id":552336,"title":"","content":"Rippers, maybe.Scourges? Hell no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:01:10-07:00","id":552353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552334#post552334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that is a different thing. Mechanics is a whole other mess, and not what I was responding to. I also think Beast makes a good point that you shouldn't compare splats of combat.<br /> <br /> But if that is the issue, I think it is a good thing to bring up here too.<br /> <br /> Though I need to ask(since I can't remember): can Slashers recover? Or is it a permanent state? Cause the fact that Heroes can recover (not saying they do) and get back to some normalcy is a good thing (from an objective standpoint of &quot;this person is now mentally stable).</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast does make a point of not comparing splats to &quot;White room&quot; fights but it looses the argument with it's abilities. The ability to simply shred a soul due to a good die roll is the example that comes to mind which is a plain &quot;FU&quot; to introducing them to any Mage game.<br /> <br /> Issue is that the theme of games naturally reflect their mechanics. Vampire is abuser/social predator, Werewolf is hunting people/spirits down, etc. Beast tries to intrude in all the game lines and have abilities which usually outmatch splat that it's trying to have kinship with. When a Beast is a better hunter (little h) than a Uratha or a better at shutting down Magic than an Awakened, you got problems.<br /> <br /> Beast tries to play Robin to everyone's Batman but ends up looking like Superman because of the abilities that it has. It's that conflict that makes me wonder if the Kinship powers that Beasts has should be more of a supporting role than such an active one.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that you have several splat factions of whom would simply murder the Beast due to it's actions than befriend it.<br /> <br /> As for Slashers. Slashers &quot;can&quot; recover but you always run the risk of them snapping and going back down the murder slide that they're on. The thing that is played up in the book though is that once a person loses empathy for other human beings, it is damn near impossible for them to regain it (usually reflected by either twisting their own internal moral code or discarding it entirely).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:25:44-07:00","id":552377,"title":"","content":"For Heroes, I'm assuming what I believe the intent was rather than the impression I got since it has been made clear the intent wasn't conveyed precisely. A Hero is the kind of person that after significant interaction you would think should seek out therapy. A Slasher after the same period is the person you think belongs in a mental hospital. The evolved Slashers are bat shit crazy. When they say Heroes are not crazy, I think they mean they aren't <i>that</i> bad off. Character models for a Slasher are Hannibal Lector and Michael Meyers. My model for a Hero is Ahab. He didn't completely flip out until the end of the story. It is the difference between saying in hindsight &quot;that guy was nuts&quot; and calling the cops to report a possible missing mental patient. Heroes are supposed to be sorta reasonable. Beasts are supposed to prefer not to have to kill a Hero. Nobody cares if you kill a Slasher, except the pacifists and they might be willing to make an exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:22:27-07:00","id":552425,"title":"","content":"I find that there is one major difference between Heroes and whatever analogy people want to compare them with on a given day:<br /> <br /> Heroes have no other recourse. There is no legal system, mortal or supernatural, that they can turn to. There is no way to get protection. There is no way to non-violently prevent a Beast from hurting them again, such as jail or rehabilitation.<br /> <br /> The only choice any victim of a Beast has is to either roll over and take it or fight back. Self-defense is not immoral.<br /> <br /> Of course, then people bring up how they attack even the Beasts that didn't make them. I say it's important to realize that people in the World of Darkness, Hero or otherwise, do not have the benefit of reading the books. They only have what they see. And they see primordial monsters masquerading as human beings who abuse others. They see it because that's what made them. Beasts look like people, but Heroes aren't going after people. They're going after Beasts.<br /> <br /> This goes double for Heroes who regularly see Beasts in their Lairs, like the infamous Sleeping Beauty. If they look like the monsters of legend, act like the monsters of legend, and live in lairs made of nightmares, and you don't have the benefit of getting the full picture from the book, what else can you do? You can't report these monsters to the police. If you're one of the few people in the world that knows this threat even exists, and you know you're capable of stopping it, don't you have a moral obligation to do what you can to stop it? Beasts may not all be evil, but given what Heroes know and have experienced and how they don't have any other way to go about it, I feel the only moral option they have is to fight.<br /> <br /> The only time I'd consider otherwise is if a Beast went out of their way to show the Hero that they aren't evil, but even then a Hero has every reason to believe they're just hiding it to get the upper hand. You have to look at this from an in-universe perspective. Heroes don't have the book. Heroes have no other way. I do think they're justified.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm glad Matt is open to clarifying things and seems intent on changing it. Which I suppose makes a lot of the debate about a lot of things moot until we see what the changes are.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Morality isn't Integrity. They each do and represent different things. That's where the Heroes = Slashers mentality falls apart completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:39:46-07:00","id":552441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552425#post552425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that there is one major difference between Heroes and whatever analogy people want to compare them with on a given day:<br /> <br /> Heroes have no other recourse. There is no legal system, mortal or supernatural, that they can turn to. There is no way to get protection. There is no way to non-violently prevent a Beast from hurting them again, such as jail or rehabilitation.<br /> <br /> The only choice any victim of a Beast has is to either roll over and take it or fight back. Self-defense is not immoral.<br /> <br /> Of course, then people bring up how they attack even the Beasts that didn't make them. I say it's important to realize that people in the World of Darkness, Hero or otherwise, do not have the benefit of reading the books. They only have what they see. And they see primordial monsters masquerading as human beings who abuse others. They see it because that's what made them. Beasts look like people, but Heroes aren't going after people. They're going after Beasts.<br /> <br /> This goes double for Heroes who regularly see Beasts in their Lairs, like the infamous Sleeping Beauty. If they look like the monsters of legend, act like the monsters of legend, and live in lairs made of nightmares, and you don't have the benefit of getting the full picture from the book, what else can you do? You can't report these monsters to the police. If you're one of the few people in the world that knows this threat even exists, and you know you're capable of stopping it, don't you have a moral obligation to do what you can to stop it? Beasts may not all be evil, but given what Heroes know and have experienced and how they don't have any other way to go about it, I feel the only moral option they have is to fight.<br /> <br /> The only time I'd consider otherwise is if a Beast went out of their way to show the Hero that they aren't evil, but even then a Hero has every reason to believe they're just hiding it to get the upper hand. You have to look at this from an in-universe perspective. Heroes don't have the book. Heroes have no other way. I do think they're justified.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm glad Matt is open to clarifying things and seems intent on changing it. Which I suppose makes a lot of the debate about a lot of things moot until we see what the changes are.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Morality isn't Integrity. They each do and represent different things. That's where the Heroes = Slashers mentality falls apart completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got an amusing mental image of an amazingly short lived Hero in court going,&quot;You don't understand that thing isn't human. Its a massive conglomerate of sentient worms that feeds on random desecration and using its evil worm powers to corrupt people into littering and tagging. It's pure evil and it needs to die!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:53:26-07:00","id":552450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=550353#post550353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is a power that Beasts have, I assume for the benefit of crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, no it's not.<br /> <br /> Beasts have a power that, all things equal, makes other supernaturals less likely to fear and hate them.<br /> <br /> If the Beast does something to anger or insult an other supernatural, the other supernatural can and will still react appropriately.<br /> <br /> It's just, if the Beast is friendly, the supernatural is more likely to accept that friendliness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:09:24-07:00","id":552475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552425#post552425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that there is one major difference between Heroes and whatever analogy people want to compare them with on a given day:<br /> <br /> Heroes have no other recourse. There is no legal system, mortal or supernatural, that they can turn to. There is no way to get protection. There is no way to non-violently prevent a Beast from hurting them again, such as jail or rehabilitation.<br /> <br /> The only choice any victim of a Beast has is to either roll over and take it or fight back. Self-defense is not immoral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self defense is not immoral. No. But it cuts both ways. A Beast who's only crime is smashing windows every so often fully has the right to fight back against the deranged &quot;Hero&quot; that's trying to murder him because he had a bad dream about him.<br /> <br /> And here's another thing, The Beasts who make the Heroes, most of the time, are not the Beasts that are hurting people.<br /> <br /> As the nightmares a Beast creates, in every case except where the sufferer has an integrity lower than five and the Beast's soul fucks up, is, regardless of what's' happening on a metaphysical level, just a particularly vivid nightmare.<br /> <br /> The most harm this causes is a night that is particularly unrestful.<br /> <br /> Thus, Heroes are not a the victim of a beast.<br /> <br /> Considering how unlikely it is for a Hero to be created <i><b>at all, </b></i>from a logical basis<i><b>, </b></i>a Hero can only be considered the &quot;victim&quot; of both the hero and the beast having incredibly shity luck.<br /> <br /> Now, as, in most cases, the Hero is not the victim of the Beast, the Mundane Equivalent of the average hero is a Man having a Nightmare about a murderer, becoming a Vigilante, and then trying to murder a petty thief because he happens to look like the murderer from his dream.<br /> <br /> Is that self defense? No, That's Murder.<br /> <br /> If anything,t he Beast/Petty Thief is exercising Self Defense when he kills the Hero/Vigilante that's trying to murder them.<br /> <br /> Now, I thought this conversation had ended.<br /> <br /> Edit: And yes, I read the rest of you post, but you ignored the bit about Heroes in most cases not actually being the Beast's victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:33:39-07:00","id":552485,"title":"","content":"No, Heroes hunt Beasts because that is what heroes do. &quot;He's a Hero...and Heroes kill monsters.&quot; They <i>have</i> a choice, which is why the game has mechanics for what happens when a Heroes chooses not to hunt Beasts. It's a shit choice, yes, but the choice is there. They <i>can</i> choose to fight their obsession. Most will not. Not with out some outside push anyway.<br /> <br /> The Heroes can rationalize why they are murdering people all they want. Slashers do that too. It does nothing to change <i>why</i> they are <i>really</i> doing it. It is not even about the Beast, it is an inherently selfish act that is all about them. The Heroes likely even know the real reason they do it, but by their very nature, rather then try and actually better themselves they will shift the blame.<br /> <br /> Most Heroes are no more a &quot;victim&quot; of a Beast's Soul (<i><b>not</b></i> the Beast himself) then those who have suffered a hurricane are the victims of the hurricane. Continuing to see attempts to paint Heroes as <i>all</i> poor souls who should be given sympathy (they very well deserve pity), to make them the very archetype they are <i>meant to deconstruct and subvert</i>, are frankly baffling. <i>Some</i> will be victims yes. Most are not. Many will have been terrible people before the Beast ever came along.<br /> <br /> Open Season has a perfect example of most Heroes. The hunter. He believes he's killing away for everyone's own good. Funny how no one else seems to agree aside from all the other Heroes/hunters.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Lets all remember the mother who decided she needed to murder her <b>son</b> because she had a bad dream and heard a voice in her head. She was <i>totally</i> a victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:41:21-07:00","id":552486,"title":"","content":"Great example.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm just so sick of how like, at least 75% of the Criticisms boil down to Dressing the Heroes up in<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DracoInLeatherPants\" target=\"_blank\"> Draco Malfoy's Leather Pants</a> and Branding Beasts with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RonTheDeathEater\" target=\"_blank\">Ron Weasley's Dark Mark.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:05:10-07:00","id":552499,"title":"","content":"Welp, I just want to throw a comment in, then run off.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beasts have nothing to do&quot; and &quot;Beasts need more antagonists&quot; thoughts - I think that they do, both from the same source. Crossover. Beast: the Primordial isn't quite a game I'm comfortable doing a Superfriends style game, where everyone is a different supernatural. What I am comfortable with, however, is having the Beasts driven to seek out other supernaturals to interact with, and that cause drama.<br /> <br /> Beasts, to my mind, are like Overlords, in that they're building up an Army of Darkness. Culturing contacts and support among other supernaturals, and making their enemies yours, or failing and getting into battles, building a grand Dungeon/Lair connected that's a home for all of them. The central drive is to build a Family. You're like Dracula building up his Castlevania fortress. Its like playing the game Overlord, or Dungeon Keeper, and their spiritual successors. It literally nourishes your soul to do this. And, like those games, you can be as evil or good as you like, though your powers and methods are still dark.<br /> <br /> In a way, Beast is a lot like Mage and Hunter. The Awakened go out to find mysteries to study, which can include supernaturals (though, more often. its just the realms and the ephemeral beings). Hunters seek out supernaturals because they're the Enemy - you're standing up to the night. Both those games revolve around exploring things from the other game lines. Beast takes that tendency, and runs with it as the main story hooks.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't a crossover game because you're expected to play Beast x Mage in the same party. Its a crossover game because dealing with other supernaturals is as critical to the game as the hunt is to a werewolf. At least, that's my opinion. So, if you ignore or diminish that crossover element, of course there's less for Beasts to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:21:14-07:00","id":552507,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider: Heroes are the only antagonist written up in Beast because any other Antagonists(Mortals, Mortal Hunters, other Supernaturals) would be in other books or made with the same ruels as Beast PCs(Due to being Beasts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:29:14-07:00","id":552512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552499#post552499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, I just want to throw a comment in, then run off.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beasts have nothing to do&quot; and &quot;Beasts need more antagonists&quot; thoughts - I think that they do, both from the same source. Crossover. Beast: the Primordial isn't quite a game I'm comfortable doing a Superfriends style game, where everyone is a different supernatural. What I am comfortable with, however, is having the Beasts driven to seek out other supernaturals to interact with, and that cause drama.<br /> <br /> Beasts, to my mind, are like Overlords, in that they're building up an Army of Darkness. Culturing contacts and support among other supernaturals, and making their enemies yours, or failing and getting into battles, building a grand Dungeon/Lair connected that's a home for all of them. The central drive is to build a Family. You're like Dracula building up his Castlevania fortress. Its like playing the game Overlord, or Dungeon Keeper, and their spiritual successors. It literally nourishes your soul to do this. And, like those games, you can be as evil or good as you like, though your powers and methods are still dark.<br /> <br /> In a way, Beast is a lot like Mage and Hunter. The Awakened go out to find mysteries to study, which can include supernaturals (though, more often. its just the realms and the ephemeral beings). Hunters seek out supernaturals because they're the Enemy - you're standing up to the night. Both those games revolve around exploring things from the other game lines. Beast takes that tendency, and runs with it as the main story hooks.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't a crossover game because you're expected to play Beast x Mage in the same party. Its a crossover game because dealing with other supernaturals is as critical to the game as the hunt is to a werewolf. At least, that's my opinion. So, if you ignore or diminish that crossover element, of course there's less for Beasts to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. And if you don't want to buy the other corebooks to do crossovers, it's not too difficult to stat out other splats with Beast mechanics:<br /> <br /> A Vampire, for example, might have any of the the Alien Allure, Cyclopean Strength, Limb From Limb, Needs Must, Shadowed Soul, and Unbreakable Atavisms and any of You Deserve This, You Must Obey, or any Vampire-based Kinship Nightmare. They have Fire and Sunlight as Anathema at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:00:45-07:00","id":552518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552486#post552486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great example.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm just so sick of how like, at least 75% of the Criticisms boil down to Dressing the Heroes up in<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DracoInLeatherPants\" target=\"_blank\"> Draco Malfoy's Leather Pants</a> and Branding Beasts with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RonTheDeathEater\" target=\"_blank\">Ron Weasley's Dark Mark.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>People aren't bending over backwards to suggest there is a problem with how Heroes are suggest Rater, they're pointing out that there is a fundamental disconnect between what the fluff insists is true and how the mechanics work out.<br /> <br /> The fluff tells use Heroes are always wrong, they're bad people fundamentally. While I think this is lazy and uninspired, that's not really the heart of the problem, what is the problem is that Heroes are created when a Beast starves and runs off into someone elses Dreams and kills/terrorizes their dream self or if a Beast victimizes them or someone in their presence. Mechanically Heroes become NPCs who's sole goal is to kill all Beasts.<br /> <br /> This is the heart of the problem, if you only read how it works you come away feeling bad for them. Some asshole monster either murdered them violently in their dreams in a way that caused real psychic trauma or hurt them or someone in their presence. In both of those cases that totally normal human standing up to the Beast and fighting back should be by definition heroic. But the book tells use otherwise, that actually they were a bad person is why they became a Hero. So that by association means the only reason they could fight back was because they were a bad person.<br /> <br /> More troubling, look at the mechanics, they were made a Hero because a Beast fucked them up, again they suffered real psychic trauma in a dream or saw a monster attacking people in real life, or they were attacked. Removed from what the book tells us about this situation, we get that the Beast damaged that person, made them a Hero and gave them a drive to kill, this is all on the Beast. That makes Heroes tragic and sympathetic figures, until the book tells us, &quot;No, they're all evil horrible bastards.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem was made worse when people telling the Devs Heroes seem very sympathetic tried to force Heroes to be bad people by adding the Integrity 4 rule and added text saying it had to be from being a bad person. We know this is a late addition (I know, because full disclosure I was in the playtest and raised these issues then) and it not only brings us back to Morality mechanics, but serves to retroactively justify Beasts when they kill Heroes. There's no drama in fighting a Hero, he was a bad person anyway so when you kill him why does it matter?<br /> <br /> This isn't me going into Beast yelling, &quot;Lets undermine this game!&quot; I want to like Beast. There are some neat ideas in here, but its mechanics don't line up with the story its trying to tell. Right now the text proudly proclaims that Beasts are the real good guys and Heroes are the real bad guys, while Beasts in the book run around cackling evilly while they torture people and the way to create Heroes are made resembles people reacting to trauma.<br /> <br /> Now the good news for me is that the Devs have said they are going to address my issues. The good news for you is that I don't see how them expanding on any of the content in the game can hurt your enjoyment if your already on board. I realize that this is the heartland of OPP support, people here are the most devoted followers because lets face it, if you post on this forum you are on some level personally invested in the product. So I don't blame people here from being one hundred percent behind OPP, but please do no just dismiss concerns with some TVTropes links. If people see an issue simply saying, &quot;Well I don't see it&quot; isn't helping anybody. We all want the best game possible out of Beast, not to sink it. Unless you believe that the repeated pointing out of the exact same issues is part of some sinister conspiracy, at some point you have to assume something just isn't working. Thankfully the Devs did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552512#post552512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree. And if you don't want to buy the other corebooks to do crossovers, it's not too difficult to stat out other splats with Beast mechanics:<br /> <br /> A Vampire, for example, might have any of the the Alien Allure, Cyclopean Strength, Limb From Limb, Needs Must, Shadowed Soul, and Unbreakable Atavisms and any of You Deserve This, You Must Obey, or any Vampire-based Kinship Nightmare. They have Fire and Sunlight as Anathema at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Beasts promises that it is a complete game that is rich and full of life without any other books. Beast is provably not rich and full of life, its focus on Crossover left it very skeletal. In the playtest I tried to encourage them to add a Dread Powers sections ala Hunter for making other supernaturals if you lack the tools. I have no idea if they ever even read that Email, I got no response, but this was around the time of the leak when they stopped all communication.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't think its unreasonable to expect Beast to be playable out of the box and not require you to have to mod it to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5558-greaterheron","name":"GreaterHeron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:51:05-07:00","id":552540,"title":"","content":"Yeah no.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fluff tells use Heroes are always wrong, they're bad people fundamentally. While I think this is lazy and uninspired, that's not really the heart of the problem, what is the problem is that Heroes are created when a Beast starves and runs off into someone elses Dreams and kills/terrorizes their dream self or if a Beast victimizes them or someone in their presence. Mechanically Heroes become NPCs who's sole goal is to kill all Beasts. </div> </div> </div>Fluff: Heroes are deeply mentally unstable people who most commonly are born when a Beast is starving and goes too long without eating, which in all probability means that he's causing the least harm as is possible to be a beast. Heroes inevitably choose to hunt and kill that beast, and other Beasts like him, the ones that are statistically causing the least harm, are the ones easiest for him to detect and thus most likely for him to try and murder.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: Exactly the same as above.<br /> <br /> The Beasts soul is the part o a beast that is a fundamental force of nature. Someone who is soul ravaged is not the victim of the Beast. They are the victim of that fundamental force of nature. Or is someone driven into rage by Disquiet the victim of a promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the heart of the problem, if you only read how it works you come away feeling bad for them. Some asshole monster either murdered them violently in their dreams in a way that caused real psychic trauma or hurt them or someone in their presence. In both of those cases that totally normal human standing up to the Beast and fighting back should be by definition heroic. But the book tells use otherwise, that actually they were a bad person is why they became a Hero. So that by association means the only reason they could fight back was because they were a bad person. </div> </div> </div>There are no rules for the second, and the first only makes a hero if the person is already three or more levels of integrity lower than the Beast.<br /> <br /> Also, it's explicitly called out that, other than the origin in the soul ravaging, that the Beast's Soul ravaging a mortals dreams is, for the mortal experiencing it, just a fucking Nightmare. I'll provide a quote as soon as I can find the fucking page it's on. If an otherwise ordinary Nightmare Counts as Psychic Trauma, then so does a horror movie.<br /> So they aren't the Beasts victim.<br /> <br /> Now. What do you call a man, who, after having a Nightmare, decides to become a vigilante, but he only hunts down and murders petty crooks while the far worse monsters get off scot free?<br /> <br /> A Fucking Psychopath.<br /> <br /> How is the Hero who has a nightmare and starts hunting the &quot;Monsters&quot; who cause the least amount of harm any different from the vigilante who only murders petty crooks.<br /> <br /> Now.<br /> <br /> I'm going to peace through the book.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to get all of the fluff about Heroes that says they're bad people.<br /> <br /> and then I'm going to do a quote post, with all of the fluff that says that Heroes are bad people.<br /> <br /> Because if the Fluff says it and the Mechanics say it, then there's no disconnect, and it means that they're bad people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T22:31:26-07:00","id":552557,"title":"","content":"Quote Post proving Heroes bad people only with Fluff.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At best, Heroes bear a strong resemblance to the heroes of ancient<br /> epics: deeply flawed people doomed to a terrible but glorious fate. At worst, Heroes are<br /> gibbering, gore-spattered maniacs whose obsessive quest to destroy the Beast twists their minds<br /> and makes them dangerous to everyone around them. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coupled with the fact that many of these self-styled Heroes are capable<br /> of any number of atrocities in the name of the greater good \u2014 after all, what isn\u2019t justified to<br /> stop a dragon preying on your town? \u2014 it can be very hard to tell who the villain is in the<br /> situation. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroes, on the other hand,<br /> never question their own heroism \u2014 and that is why Beasts hate them. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Living with Hunger is dangerous, yes, but a dragon\u2019s gold is never a burden. The Hero might call<br /> it profane, but in his heart of hearts, he envies its glory. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take a high school bully, mate him with a rabid dog, and a Hero is born. The saying goes that<br /> fanatics redouble their efforts when they lose sight of their aims; if so, Heroes are an exceptional<br /> breed of fanatic. Their efforts leave no room to be redoubled, and their aims are barely coherent<br /> to begin with.<br /> Strip down the layers of a Hero\u2019s ego, and all one finds is murder. Murder is his only end,<br /> regardless of bystanders. He\u2019ll bloviate about the little girls and puppies he saves, but at the best<br /> of times, protecting the innocent is incidental. He pursues the Beast because she dares to live and<br /> breathe and occupy the same world he does, not because some fool needs rescuing. It\u2019s an<br /> imperative a serial killer might understand. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To a degree, the Begotten understand the Heroic drive. Whether it\u2019s for piles of gold or<br /> slaughtered prey, Beasts are equally slaves to instinct. The difference between a Beast\u2019s lust and<br /> a Hero\u2019s obsession is self-awareness. A Beast knows she\u2019s crazy. She learns to live with it or she<br /> suffers. Justifications miss the point of having a Hunger in the first place. A Hero, on the other<br /> hand, will twist his brain to rationalize his hatred. It\u2019s the same defense abusers cling to: blame<br /> the victim. Understanding that pathology makes the difference between a Beast with a Legend<br /> and a Beast with an encyclopedia entry. </div> </div> </div>This last one is particularly egregarious-I've literally seen people claiming that Beasts Victim Blame Heroes when it's very clearly written that it's the other way around.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroes are hardly social animals, though. It\u2019s called a monomyth for a reason. Heroes have no<br /> use for friends, no matter how fanatical their followers may be. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, loved ones may be excess baggage to Heroes, but at least they\u2019re still loved. A Hero<br /> saves his spite for his other fellow Heroes. Wars are more congenial than the alliances Beast<br /> slayers make. Their egos might be able to handle short partnerships in the name of a greater<br /> good, but a smart Hero always keeps a spare knife ready in case his allies decide that honor is for<br /> chumps. No Hero really wants to share in the glory of the kill. They\u2019d rather have fawning<br /> lackeys than an equal to share their victory. </div> </div> </div>I'll post more quotes later. It's getting late where I am and I need to be up early in the morning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T22:35:54-07:00","id":552558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552540#post552540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah no.<br /> <br /> Fluff: Heroes are deeply mentally unstable people who most commonly are born when a Beast is starving and goes too long without eating, which in all probability means that he's causing the least harm as is possible to be a beast. Heroes inevitably choose to hunt and kill that beast, and other Beasts like him, the ones that are statistically causing the least harm, are the ones easiest for him to detect and thus most likely for him to try and murder.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: Exactly the same as above.<br /> <br /> The Beasts soul is the part o a beast that is a fundamental force of nature. Someone who is soul ravaged is not the victim of the Beast. They are the victim of that fundamental force of nature. Or is someone driven into rage by Disquiet the victim of a promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what the fundamental difference between Promethean and Beast is here? Promethean own that they are the problem. Promethean don't sit around and justify that they are faultless in causing Disquiet, they realize that they are hurting these people by just existing. Its part of what drives Promethean onwards towards humanity.<br /> <br /> A Beasts soul that goes wild is a Beast who is starving, yes, it's not his fault realistically, something went wrong that forced them there. Going, &quot;Well it's a force of nature&quot; doesn't justify what happens afterwards, it just provides context. It doesn't matter how it happened, the Beast fucked up and let his soul hurt people and these people get up broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552540#post552540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no rules for the second, and the first only makes a hero if the person is already three or more levels of integrity lower than the Beast.<br /> <br /> Also, it's explicitly called out that, other than the origin in the soul ravaging, that the Beast's Soul ravaging a mortals dreams is, for the mortal experiencing it, just a fucking Nightmare. I'll provide a quote as soon as I can find the fucking page it's on. If an otherwise ordinary Nightmare Counts as Psychic Trauma, then so does a horror movie.<br /> So they aren't the Beasts victim.<br /> <br /> Now. What do you call a man, who, after having a Nightmare, decides to become a vigilante, but he only hunts down and murders petty crooks while the far worse monsters get off scot free?<br /> <br /> A Fucking Psychopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not just a nightmare, it's the most traumatic Nightmare they've ever experienced, it felt all to terribly real and broke them fundamentally. They very well could be a psychopath, but it doesn't change the fact that they weren't a psychopath before they went to bed. They woke up fundamentally changed because the Beast fucked up. I wouldn't expect many Beasts to see it as anything other than, &quot;How dare he rise up against me&quot; but it doesn't change the tragedy that the Beast destroyed a functional human being.<br /> <br /> Then let us remember that you can also spawn heroes by wiping out your magic powers in public and hurting people with them. What do you call someone who has seen that there are real monsters in the world and rises up against them? A Hero. That they are left broken by the experience and will never be functional members of humanity again only makes them more sympathetic for their sacrifice.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that the fluff insist that the Heroes are wrong. But they're right. There are monsters out in the dark and they are hunting down and hurting people. The fluff insists that Heroes are bad people because they see an issue with this. Who wouldn't see an issue with this? And remember, Heroes don't get to read the core book and go, &quot;Oh, there are good and bad monsters out there, I should only fight the bad ones.&quot; They just know there are monsters. Worse, the monster broke their brains so they can't see the difference. All of this is the Beasts fault, he didn't want to do any of it, but hey, here we are. The Beast and Hero relationship should be complex and full of tragedy. Instead Heroes are always Chaotic Evil Orcs that occasionally pop up to be trivially killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552540#post552540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the Hero who has a nightmare and starts hunting the &quot;Monsters&quot; who cause the least amount of harm any different from the vigilante who only murders petty crooks.<br /> <br /> Now.<br /> <br /> I'm going to peace through the book.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to get all of the fluff about Heroes that says they're bad people.<br /> <br /> and then I'm going to do a quote post, with all of the fluff that says that Heroes are bad people.<br /> <br /> Because if the Fluff says it and the Mechanics say it, then there's no disconnect, and it means that they're bad people.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will actually prove nothing. You can pull a thousand quotes from the fluff that say, &quot;They're bad people&quot; and I can just point to how they are made and ask does these line up?<br /> <br /> The answer is simply no they don't properly align. The integrity rule for instance is the best example, its a big awkward out of place rule trying to retroactively justify Beasts. What makes it so awkward? Integrity does not measure morality anymore, its part of it, but Integrity is not Morality, Integrity was designed to be more complex and better express the themes of WoD. Namely human beings break under stress and the assault of the supernatural. So this rule has to have awkward clarification text to make its point. Its terrible, inelegant design. Its all the proof you need that Heroes aren't working.<br /> <br /> Now you are obviously on the same page as the Devs, you've read their posts, probably kept up with the game through development and you're letting that guide your reading. Not everyone is like you and they aren't going to look for Dev clarification. The fluff is to strong, trying to desperately to paint Heroes as black and Beasts as white. The mechanics are muddled and confused.<br /> <br /> But here's the other thing, the Devs have already said they're making changes to this. So there isn't an argument as much as me trying to show you the other sides thought process. It's not an attempt to subvert the game or sabotage it. Its not that I haven't read the rules, I was in the playtest for god's sake. It's that what the Devs thought they wrote and actually wrote don't match. And that's all anyone wants fixed, if Heroes are just mindless villains at least make Beasts own their hand in creating them, because let us not forget, that a Hero exists is the Beasts fault, I'm not saying that the only way to deal with this for the Beast is suicide, I'm saying that Beasts replying with what right do you have to oppose me is insane when Beasts know full well that they made the Hero. Sure maybe that Beast didn't make him, but some other asshole Beast did. Or better yet, change how Heroes are created. I have no idea how they'll go about it and wish them the best in making the game better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5558-greaterheron","name":"GreaterHeron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:13:14-07:00","id":552583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552486#post552486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great example.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm just so sick of how like, at least 75% of the Criticisms boil down to Dressing the Heroes up in<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DracoInLeatherPants\" target=\"_blank\">Draco Malfoy's Leather Pants</a> and Branding Beasts with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RonTheDeathEater\" target=\"_blank\">Ron Weasley's Dark Mark.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I find the irony to be that this accusation is being leveled when discussing a game that is <i>fundamentally built on</i> the Draco's Leather Pants and Ron Weasley's Dark Mark tropes. That is, after all, the whole premise: the Beasts wear leather pants while the Heroes have the dark mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  fixed links 06-16-2015, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:17:18-07:00","id":552585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That will actually prove nothing. You can pull a thousand quotes from the fluff that say, &quot;They're bad people&quot; and I can just point to how they are made and ask does these line up? </div> </div> </div>You're the one who complained about the fluff portraying Heroes as good people and the mechanics not backing it up.<br /> <br /> I've provided half a book's worth of the fluff that depicts them as the bad people that the mechanics say they are.<br /> <br /> And I see you've admitted that that, reasonably, a Beast is not responsible for creating a hero, and at admitting this the Hero was not victimized by the Beast(thus removing one of the &quot;rationalizations&quot; heroes use-and they are rationalizations, as I have repeatedly explained)<br /> <br /> Now, as for Beasts not owning up to being monsters<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, with relief comes horror, as the Beast realizes her terrible Hunger must be fed to keep<br /> the Soul appeased. Everything a Beast has learned since she was a child tells her the monster is<br /> evil. The monster is at best a vicious animal to be slain by a victorious Hero. In most cases, the<br /> monster is an analog for Satan, lust, greed, or whatever other quality or being society wishes to<br /> demonize. The monster is vile, she is wrong; every story the Beast knows ends with the<br /> monster\u2019s destruction. The Beast has to come to terms with knowing that she is the monster, and<br /> in most stories, she\u2019s the villain. </div> </div> </div>That, the multiple lines about Beasts having to balance their human and Beast sides, and line about managing hunger, and the lines that state that the difference between HEroes and Beasts is that Heroes lack self awareness of what they really are, all of that tells me that Beasts do, in fact, own up to what they are, by trying to manage their hungers.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd argue that Beasts are far less the problem than a promethean-Disquiet works on almost everyone. Only the deeply unstable can become heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it's not just a nightmare, it's the most traumatic Nightmare they've ever experienced, it felt all to terribly real and broke them fundamentally. They very well could be a psychopath, but it doesn't change the fact that they weren't a psychopath before they went to bed. They woke up fundamentally changed because the Beast fucked up. I wouldn't expect many Beasts to see it as anything other than, &quot;How dare he rise up against me&quot; but it doesn't change the tragedy that the Beast destroyed a functional human being. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> For everybody but the Integ 4 person who is unlucky enough to become a hero(which is not every integ 4 person), it is Explicitly just a vivid nightmare. It might be the worst nightmare you ever had, but it's still just a nightmare, mundane in every way except what caused it.<br /> <br /> It's only Integ 4 people who are &quot;traumatized&quot;(find me a quote, please, becuase I've got nothing) and become Heroes. If it was as you say, <b>Everyone</b> would become a hero.<br /> <br /> <i>Explicitly </i>not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-13-2015, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:26:32-07:00","id":552589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552583#post552583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the irony to be that this accusation is being leveled when discussing a game that is <i>fundamentally built on</i> the Draco's Leather Pants and Ron Weasley's Dark Mark tropes. That is, after all, the whole premise: the Beasts wear leather pants while the Heroes have the dark mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> In universe, it's perfectly logical for the Beasts to, with some exceptions, be the light Grey to the Heroes' Dark Grey to Black.<br /> <br /> Those Tropes are about a Dark Grey or Black morality character being depicted as stark white for reasons that amount to &quot;I think they're hot/cute&quot;/I like them&quot; and light grey to white character being depeicted as jet black morally for the reason of &quot;I have an (irrational) hatred of them&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:27:21-07:00","id":552591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552583#post552583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the irony to be that this accusation is being leveled when discussing a game that is <i>fundamentally built on</i> the Draco's Leather Pants and Ron Weasley's Dark Mark tropes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Data, the game is incredibly up-front about the fact that you're playing a being whose nature all but demands either a certain degree of borderline-to-not-even-borderline criminal behavior or the facilitation or tacit enabling of other supernatural predation as a matter of survival due to hunger pangs giving rise to narratively-empowered individuals intent on murdering you.<br /> <br /> What you're doing here is as damaging to the discussion as the recurring confusion between Awakened mages and people who think Mage's cosmology trumps everything. Don't be that guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:45:00-07:00","id":552612,"title":"","content":"As for the &quot;Beasts are responsible for creating Heroes&quot; argument: remember MADD? It was an 80s activist group based on the notion that Dungeons &amp; Dragons was responsible for kids going crazy and doing stupid stuff. It turns out that to the extent that the problem existed at all, the kids in question were already having trouble distinguishing fantasy from reality; and to the extent that D&amp;D was responsible at all, it merely provided the final nudge to an already unstable individual. <br /> <br /> That's how I think Heroes should be portrayed: they should be people who are already being driven toward the Heroic mindset long before any Beast gets near them. They already have an urge to slay monsters (whether literal or figurative), and it should be the sort of urge that drives someone to experience Breaking Points of the \u201cethical infractions\u201d variety. That aspiration, not Integrity 4 per se, should be the necessary ingredient for becoming a Hero. The Beast doesn't create Heroes per se; he merely serves as the catalyst that tips the wannabe slayer across the final threshold to become a Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-13-2015, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:50:57-07:00","id":552615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552591#post552591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Data, the game is incredibly up-front about the fact that you're playing a being whose nature all but demands either a certain degree of borderline-to-not-even-borderline criminal behavior or the facilitation or tacit enabling of other supernatural predation as a matter of survival due to hunger pangs giving rise to narratively-empowered individuals intent on murdering you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know; and you misunderstood my point. I didn't say that there's anything wrong with the role-reversal; I was merely commenting that I find it ironic that someone's crying foul about role-reversals when discussing a game that's built around role reversals. Nothing more. Look at my last post (#3138) which was ninja'd by the two posts before it to get a fuller idea of where I'm coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:04:12-07:00","id":552625,"title":"","content":"Another wild theory: what if Heroes are failed Beasts? That is, the &quot;special ingredient&quot; that allows one to become a Hero is that he was born of the Primordial Dream just like a Beast; and just like a Beast, he has had recurring nightmares of monsters stalking him all his life. And left to his own devices, he might have eventually had a Homecoming and become a Beast. But then a Beast's Soul inadvertently disrupted the process; and instead of accepting that he is himself a Beast, he <i>slays the monster of his nightmares</i>, destroying his own Soul before he ever discovers the truth, and finds that he now has a hole that can only be filled (albeit briefly) by slaying Beasts, starting with the one who interfered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:15:30-07:00","id":552635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552615#post552615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know; and you misunderstood my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That tends to happen when you borrow terminology without understanding it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't say that there's anything wrong with the role-reversal; I was merely commenting that I find it ironic that someone's crying foul about role-reversals when discussing a game that's built around role reversals. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about role-reversals, either \u2014 &quot;Draco in Leather Pants&quot; and &quot;Ron the Death Eater&quot; are fandom-behavior trends, not simple &quot;the antagonist is the good guy and the protagonist is the bad guy&quot; tropes and so your claim doesn't connect with either end of the comparison on the grounds of nomenclature failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing more. Look at my last post (#3138) which was ninja'd by the two posts before it to get a fuller idea of where I'm coming from. </div> </div> </div>People I have blocked have posted in this thread with sufficient frequency that the post number you're alluding to is in the future at the time of this writing, so that's going to be kind of difficult.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could be missing something, but is it my imagination or do the Unfettered not have a defined band of Twilight to occupy via Nightmare Apparition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-13-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:20:51-07:00","id":552636,"title":"","content":"Great Heron, &quot;wiping&quot; out your powers do not cause Heroes to arise. Staying below Satiety 4, then rolling a DF or XS on a Power + Lair - Composure on someone Integrity 4 or lower is the only way to do it. (Sidenote: Devs should come up with a more evocative, less confusing term for that; I vote Rampage)<br /> And Heroes are wrong, in that they operate under the delusion that they're the protagonist of the story, that it's all about them. Also, it's a stretch to assume that that single encounter with the Beast's Soul would grant any knowledge of a Beast's particular Hunger, or how they go about satisfying it, let alone enough context to form an opinion beyond &quot;I need to kill that thing.&quot; There's no altruism, no concern in a Hero's motivation per se, just obsession, and no amount of rationalization will change that. Now, if you want to have a Hero gain that info, or form those opinions, go right ahead, just understand that as written, a freshly arisen Hero shouldn't have any of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  responding to wrong poster 06-13-2015, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:29:22-07:00","id":552675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552612#post552612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the &quot;Beasts are responsible for creating Heroes&quot; argument: remember MADD? It was an 80s activist group based on the notion that Dungeons &amp; Dragons was responsible for kids going crazy and doing stupid stuff. It turns out that to the extent that the problem existed at all, the kids in question were already having trouble distinguishing fantasy from reality; and to the extent that D&amp;D was responsible at all, it merely provided the final nudge to an already unstable individual.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0084314/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Mazes and Monsters</i></a> exists and starred Tom Hanks, ergo D&amp;D is literally Satan, QED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:30:42-07:00","id":552677,"title":"","content":"Hexmeister Vic: I'm not talking about the manuscript as written; I'm suggesting alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:02:38-07:00","id":552683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreaterHeron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552558#post552558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what the fundamental difference between Promethean and Beast is here? Promethean own that they are the problem. Promethean don't sit around and justify that they are faultless in causing Disquiet, they realize that they are hurting these people by just existing. Its part of what drives Promethean onwards towards humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore. Disquiet and Wasteland aren't &quot;you chose the wrong splat&quot; effects as Matt said here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Disquiet and the Wasteland: Everything and Everyone Hates You [Promethean: The Created</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]<br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Matthew McFarland - October 28th, 2014, 11:04 am</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Every Promethean burns with an inner fire so intense, it scorches the land around them. It makes people uncomfortable, even if they can\u2019t figure out why. The Divine Fire, the energy that ultimately allows the alchemy of the Great Work, also sets Prometheans apart from the world they want to join.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>In 2nd Edition, we\u2019re moving away from Disquiet and the Wasteland being products of the Prometheans being \u201cthings that should not be.\u201d Part of that is because the semantics always bugged me; who </b><b><i>says</i></b><b> they shouldn\u2019t be? They\u2019re here, so there\u2019s really no \u201cshould\u201d about it, and I\u2019m not into punishing characters on a moral level for their very existence, thanks. Instead, the reasons for the Wasteland and for Disquiet have more to do with the world not being able to handle the intensity of the Divine Fire. It burns too hot, and people sense that during interactions with the Promethean. They respond with spite, possessiveness, jealousy, or paranoia. The blanket term for these responses is </b><b><i>Disquiet</i></b><b>.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Likewise, Prometheans have to be careful how they interact with the world around them. If they let too much of their inner Fire out at once, they can scorch the land, beginning an inexorable process of creating a <i>Wasteland</i>. As Wastelands grow more extreme, it can cause weird elemental effects \u2013 thunderstorms rage, water thickens and sours, the veil between spirit and flesh grows thin. It depends on the humours of the Promethean in question (which also means that Prometheans of the same Lineage, sharing as they do the same humours, can make the effect worse).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Disquiet, by itself, doesn\u2019t progress beyond a certain point. People feel suspicious, fascinated, or just disdainful with regards to the Promethean, and might go out of their way to cause minor inconveniences, but it doesn\u2019t rise to the level of physical violence. Within a Wasteland, though, Disquiet festers. The human mind responds not only to the intensity of the Divine Fire within the Promethean, but to the changes she is wreaking on the environment. Left unchecked, Disquiet becomes contagious, and ends with the victims trying to purge the corrosive element from their midst (this is colloquially known as the \u201ctorches and pitchforks\u201d stage of Disquiet).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[\u2026]</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-13-2015, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:52:50-07:00","id":552758,"title":"","content":"I've become much more hopeful for Beast based on the recent posts from Mathew McFarland.<br /> <br /> In particular, naming &quot;Tucker and Dale vs Evil&quot; as an inspiration really helps me click with the &quot;Hero&quot; relationship. I seriously love the idea of Tucker and Dale being two Beasts just trying to enjoy themselves in the wild, and the camping kids getting whipped up into a frenzy by the &quot;Hero&quot; leader whose labeled them as Monsters and thinks they deserve to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T02:22:55-07:00","id":552769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552758#post552758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've become much more hopeful for Beast based on the recent posts from Mathew McFarland.<br /> <br /> In particular, naming &quot;Tucker and Dale vs Evil&quot; as an inspiration really helps me click with the &quot;Hero&quot; relationship. I seriously love the idea of Tucker and Dale being two Beasts just trying to enjoy themselves in the wild, and the camping kids getting whipped up into a frenzy by the &quot;Hero&quot; leader whose labeled them as Monsters and thinks they deserve to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god how did I not think of that movie as an example I mean at the very least you have a good example of Hero behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:47:23-07:00","id":552904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552683#post552683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not anymore. Disquiet and Wasteland aren't &quot;you chose the wrong splat&quot; effects as Matt said here:</div> </div> </div> </div> That bit you quoted from Matt actually supports what GreaterHeron said, not negates it. Prometheans are still the cause of Disquiet (even if its their internal Fire instead of the Uncanny Valley effect), and they own it. They keep on the Pilgrimage to minimize damage. If the sample settings are any indication, Beasts don't - the SAS presents mass murder as something the PCs should consider allowing. <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> You know, one thing I'm having trouble nailing down with Beast is the whole society connection thing. Vampires are about politics, night life, and relationships. Werewolf deals a lot with the transgender community. Mage has some privileged upper class vibes to it. Changeling and trauma / abuse. So... what's the Beast's vibe?<br /> <br /> <br /> Human sadists? Put aside the word Hunger for a moment. We're talking about satisfying a psychological urge to cause others pain and distress. They get a voyeuristic thrill from watching others hunt. Are we looking at a splat based around bullies? And, if we are, are we looking at Heroes as the Columbine-type kids, who snapped and shot up the place in revenge? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:48:17-07:00","id":552905,"title":"","content":"Oh no. I actually liked how Disquiet was handled in 1e. I guess I really don't fit well with Blackhatmatt, though not at all to his fault.<br /> <br /> Let me elaborate though; isn't an absolutely huge part of Promethean and Disqueat the concept of Uncanny Valley? I mean, 'hated because they are the things that should not be' sounds pretty much like a central idea of Promethean.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-13-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:50:08-07:00","id":552907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552905#post552905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no. I actually liked how Disquiet was handled in 1e. I guess I really don't fit well with Blackhatmatt, though not at all to his fault.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't it the same thing, though? Seems to me the change is just semantics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:56:33-07:00","id":552910,"title":"","content":"Also, there should be non-Hero mortals who fight beasts, right? But with better judgments and without shiny Hero-powers?<br /> <br /> I think it would be good if the devs added even a paragraph about non-Hero mortal antagonists, because at the moment the definition of Hero is a little bit narrow and strawman-ish, and those eventually lead them to being unimpressive antagonists.<br /> <br /> Like... if we take Beast/Mortal mirror narrative, Hunters would be at the narrow end of the spectrum opposite of which lies the meanest, the most brutal beasts lie, and I don't think that's a good way to handle the major antagonists for a line. I mean, sure, people like Banishers and VII are like that, but these are only (kind of more flat) part of many antagonists that the lines provide.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know... If I were a dev, I could have made things like... having one single, special, designated Hero against each Beast, who grows in power and magnitude with the Beast, whose quest is pursuing that particular PC beast if it meant his life. Then give the PC to subvert or deconstruct the heroic epic, either by defeatinging him, 'rehabilitating' him, befriending him, or even ignoring him. (i.e., anything but letting him kill you, but a good story could even be made out of that.) I think it might be better solution in the lategame than making heroes 'mere footnotes.' (actual words)<br /> <br /> It... could give Beasts things to do, as well? I don't know. I think as much as the story of Beowulf IS about Grendel, the subversion of the story of Grendel should not just be.. Grendel killing heroes and hanging out with other monsters. If the mechanics are given to Heroes, I think they deserve better narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-13-2015, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:58:40-07:00","id":552911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552907#post552907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Isn't it the same thing, though? Seems to me the change is just semantics.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it may have been a theory often cited by the Hundred-Handed last edition, the idea being it doesn't put the burden on the Created, but blames mortals for when things go wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:16:03-07:00","id":552920,"title":"","content":"@MCN : I will be waiting for 2E to come out... yeah, I think the theme should stay, but what Matt is suggesting kind of... blows some flavour out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:21:16-07:00","id":552924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Craig shoots Todd on the head because Todd is a monster.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am very, very sorry to jump in what is not my argument.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't see Craig described as a villain is bad at all... <br /> But, I think defining the entire antagonist group as people like Craig actually hurts the game. (just my opinion though, but I am entitled, right? )<br /> <br /> I do think having the entire antagonist group within that small window kind of hurts the fun of the game, and that's my problem of heroes. I (personally) believe that Heroes (or chief mortal antagonists of any other name) should be of wider spectrum both in power and intentions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:41:50-07:00","id":552956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552910#post552910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there should be non-Hero mortals who fight beasts, right? But with better judgments and without shiny Hero-powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are.<br /> <br /> They're called &quot;Hunters&quot; and they have an entire Gameline about them.<br /> <br /> I'm reasonably certain that Hunters get touched on in the crossover sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:51:26-07:00","id":552958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552956#post552956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are.<br /> <br /> They're called &quot;Hunters&quot; and they have an entire Gameline about them.<br /> <br /> I'm reasonably certain that Hunters get touched on in the crossover sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have been more clear about this.<br /> <br /> Non-Hero, non-human mortal antagonists.<br /> <br /> Because, I think, being a hunter is still different than being hurt by Beast and feeling like they should do something about it,<br /> and chooses not to go Hero- way, and say, like attacking only murderous Beasts and such.<br /> <br /> Seriously, non-Hero mortal antagonists merits a lot more than being mentioned in a crossover section. It is a very important theme that should not be neglected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:58:59-07:00","id":552961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552958#post552958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have been more clear about this.<br /> <br /> Non-Hero, non-human mortal antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non human by default means non-mortal in a NWoD context.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552958#post552958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, I think, being a hunter is still different than being hurt by Beast and feeling like they should do something about it,<br /> and chooses not to go Hero- way, and say, like attacking only murderous Beasts and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. Heroes are not harmed by Beasts, unless you count a particularly bad dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:00:54-07:00","id":552962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552961#post552961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non human by default means non-mortal in a NWoD context.<br /> <br /> Again. Heroes are not harmed by Beasts, unless you count a particularly bad dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>O shit, sorry. I meant Non-Hunter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, psychological damage is not being 'hurt' now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:01:19-07:00","id":552963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552910#post552910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there should be non-Hero mortals who fight beasts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>*incoherent begging for a &quot;Hunter - Mortal Remains&quot; chapter as a pdf released as a Beast stretchgoal*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:07:15-07:00","id":552964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552963#post552963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *incoherent begging for a &quot;Hunter - Mortal Remains&quot; chapter as a pdf released as a Beast stretchgoal*</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just thinking about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hunter conspiracy about Beasts!<br /> <br /> I mean, but also, Hunter seems really like a group with philosophy, almost like a night-job.<br /> I want to read write-ups about normal people, doing something against the Beasts, but who are not Hero-level fanatics.<br /> I think.. just (seeming to) put any anti-Beast mortal into Hero lump is the weak part of the write-up as it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:32:09-07:00","id":553018,"title":"","content":"Stretch goals I want to see:<br /> Mortal Remains- Beast Chapter<br /> A book about Broods(singular) and Broods banding together(analog to a protectorate of werewolfs and a vampire domain) with Vancouver fleshed out as an example.<br /> Another Dark Era wouldn't hurt<br /> With there isn't going to be a supplement about it, then a small book about Kinship powers from minor splats, and how Beasts relate to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 06-13-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:33:43-07:00","id":553020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552962#post552962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, psychological damage is not being 'hurt' now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody else takes &quot;Psychological Damage&quot; from the dreams, becuase they're just bad dreams.<br /> <br /> The Hero to be doen'st become hero becuase he was traumatized.<br /> <br /> He became a hero becuase he's so screwed up that having a nightmare about a Monster was enough to give him a purpose.(That purpose being murder.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:36:24-07:00","id":553028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553020#post553020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody else takes &quot;Psychological Damage&quot; from the dreams, becuase they're just bad dreams.<br /> <br /> The Hero to be doen'st become hero becuase he was traumatized.<br /> <br /> He became a hero becuase he's so screwed up that having a nightmare about a Monster was enough to give him a purpose.(That purpose being murder.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This... is something we'll just have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast DO cause damage. it's part of satiating their hunger.<br /> Some people damaged by that, might just decide to fight back. The book as of now does not mention it except for the Hero cases, leading to very unfortunate implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:43:01-07:00","id":553031,"title":"","content":"Question for the Kickstarter people.<br /> <br /> I want to invest at the $35+ level and get Changeling 2nd Edition for the additional reward. But it says I might have a chance of getting Changeling 1st Edition instead of the one I want depending on which edition is current at the time the rewards are being sent out. I already own Changeling 1st Edition. I don't like gambling, so can I just wait however long it takes for 2nd Edition to come out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:45:50-07:00","id":553032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553028#post553028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This... is something we'll just have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast DO cause damage. it's part of satiating their hunger.<br /> Some people damaged by that, might just decide to fight back. The book as of now does not mention it except for the Hero cases, leading to very unfortunate implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the ones who are damaged by a Beast's feeding and choose to fight back are HUNTERS.<br /> <br /> Heroes are the jackasses who had a nightmare and decided to go murder a guy who isn't hurting anyone because he looks like the monster from his dream, while completely ignoring the Murderous Cousins on the &quot;monster&quot; the Hero chose to hunt.<br /> <br /> Heroes are <b>not</b> victimized by a Beast in the majority of Cases.<br /> <br /> In the Majority of Cases, they're just the asshole who started &quot;hunting monsters&quot;(read, murdering people) because he had a <i>fucking nightmare.</i><br /> <br /> That's the disconnect.<br /> <br /> People keep assuming that Heroes are the Victims of a Beast, when the Mechanics and most of the Fluff make it abundantly clear that Heroes are the victims of nothing but a Starving Beast having really shitty luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-13-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:58:17-07:00","id":553039,"title":"","content":"Well, the fluff does seem to think people can become heroes after encountering a beast in the real world in a couple of places, but there's absolutely no mechanism for how this happens, and it kinda jars with the idea that their onieros has been infected by the beast's hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-13-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:23:57-07:00","id":553061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553031#post553031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the Kickstarter people.<br /> <br /> I want to invest at the $35+ level and get Changeling 2nd Edition for the additional reward. But it says I might have a chance of getting Changeling 1st Edition instead of the one I want depending on which edition is current at the time the rewards are being sent out. I already own Changeling 1st Edition. I don't like gambling, so can I just wait however long it takes for 2nd Edition to come out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that you can leave your reward level undecided until near the end of the Kickstarter, not that that would help much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:24:06-07:00","id":553063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553020#post553020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody else takes &quot;Psychological Damage&quot; from the dreams, becuase they're just bad dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> My wife suffers night terrors (of the extremely potent variety). She has more than one occasion woken up traumatised and suffering &quot;psychological damage&quot; from something that is &quot;just bad dreams&quot;.<br /> <br /> Night terrors powered by a supercharged primordial soul that wants to feast on humanity? That's terrifying and to claim that &quot;bad dreams&quot; don't hurt anyone is ignorant at best and downright dismissive at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:40:07-07:00","id":553084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553063#post553063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> My wife suffers night terrors (of the extremely potent variety). She has more than one occasion woken up traumatised and suffering &quot;psychological damage&quot; from something that is &quot;just bad dreams&quot;.<br /> <br /> Night terrors powered by a supercharged primordial soul that wants to feast on humanity? That's terrifying and to claim that &quot;bad dreams&quot; don't hurt anyone is ignorant at best and downright dismissive at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Night Terrors are something different from proper Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A </span></span></span><b>night terror</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><b>sleep terror</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or </span></span></span><i><b>pavor nocturnus</b></i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is a </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parasomnia\" target=\"_blank\">parasomnia</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep_disorder\" target=\"_blank\">sleep disorder</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, causing feelings of terror or dread, and typically occurs during the first hours of stage 3-4 </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-rapid_eye_movement\" target=\"_blank\">non-rapid eye movement</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (NREM) </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep\" target=\"_blank\">sleep</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Night terrors tend to happen during periods of arousal from delta sleep, also known as </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slow-wave_sleep\" target=\"_blank\">slow-wave sleep</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-Bjorvatn-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-Guzman-3\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-Szelenberger-4\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> During the first half of a sleep cycle, delta sleep occurs most often, which indicates that people with more delta sleep activity are more prone to night terrors.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-Guzman-3\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> However, they can also occur during daytime naps.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_terror#cite_note-DSM-5\" target=\"_blank\">[5]</a></sup> </div> </div> </div>There's no evidence that the Nightmares caused by a Beast's soul is anything but a mundane Nightmare, other than it's origin.<br /> <br /> Particularly since the book flat out says that unless you're at integ 4, it's just an ordinary, if vivid, nightmare.<br /> <br /> A Night Terror is not an ordinary Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:46:59-07:00","id":553100,"title":"","content":"At this point I don't even know why I even bothered. My apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:08:01-07:00","id":553122,"title":"","content":"Didn't we already cover this Night Terror territory once and conclude that there was one instance where the book used night terror, and the rest said it was normal nightmare? Because otherwise I'm getting bad enough d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu that I'm going to start watching my back for Agent Smith and the God Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:44:33-07:00","id":553146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552920#post552920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MCN : I will be waiting for 2E to come out... yeah, I think the theme should stay, but what Matt is suggesting kind of... blows some flavour out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. I always thought it was part of the flavor in the first place. Ah, well, I played the game once and haven't touched it again, so its not like I have a horse in that race. No triple crown for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552910#post552910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... If I were a dev, I could have made things like... having one single, special, designated Hero against each Beast, who grows in power and magnitude with the Beast, whose quest is pursuing that particular PC beast if it meant his life. Then give the PC to subvert or deconstruct the heroic epic, either by defeatinging him, 'rehabilitating' him, befriending him, or even ignoring him. (i.e., anything but letting him kill you, but a good story could even be made out of that.) I think it might be better solution in the lategame than making heroes 'mere footnotes.' (actual words)<br /> <br /> It... could give Beasts things to do, as well? I don't know. I think as much as the story of Beowulf IS about Grendel, the subversion of the story of Grendel should not just be.. Grendel killing heroes and hanging out with other monsters. If the mechanics are given to Heroes, I think they deserve better narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do agree that Heroes should get better stuff. I made the comparison to D&amp;D before - we should have enough mechanics so we could make up a paladin-esk Hero, a magical companion, etc. Something that's actually making us feel like we're dealing with a Legendary Hero archetype. I think they should be as scary as the Beasts.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, definitely some rules on rehabilitating Heroes. We do'nt even need mechanics, but some guidelines and ideas for how to deal with them other than killing would be lovely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552958#post552958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have been more clear about this.<br /> <br /> Non-Hero, non-hunter mortal antagonists.<br /> <br /> Because, I think, being a hunter is still different than being hurt by Beast and feeling like they should do something about it, and chooses not to go Hero- way, and say, like attacking only murderous Beasts and such.<br /> <br /> Seriously, non-Hero mortal antagonists merits a lot more than being mentioned in a crossover section. It is a very important theme that should not be neglected.</div> </div> </div> </div> What is the difference between a mortal that's fighting against the monsters that go bump in the dark, and a hunter? As far as I'm aware, mortals standing up to the monsters ARE hunters. It seems like we're dealing with the same thing.<br /> <br /> And, in Vampire, there's not a lot of discussion about mortals as antagonists either. I think they're just kind of assumed here, in some games. They're talked about in Demon, because cultists are a huge thing there. Werewolf, we have one of the five sacred prey. In Vamp, mortals are food, not antagonists. So, I'm kinda just assuming the same thing with beasts - mortals aren't a critical thing on their own, if not a hunter or hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552961#post552961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again. Heroes are not harmed by Beasts, unless you count a particularly bad dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to agree with others that this sentence is not true. &quot;Particularly bad dreams&quot; are causing distress and suffering. Its not a physical wound, but the damage is real. Dismissing it as just a &quot;bad dream&quot; is doing a disservice to both the game, and those who suffer from such problems.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with torete; feeding your so-called Hunger is inflicting torment. Beasts are naturally sadists. The &quot;good&quot; Children try to channel their sadistic tendacies in positive (or, at least neutral) directions, but we're still talking about creatures that get off on hurting others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553084#post553084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night Terrors are something different from proper Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right. Proper Nightmares are worse than night terrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-13-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:51:26-07:00","id":553152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553146#post553146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between a mortal that's fighting against the monsters that go bump in the dark, and a hunter? As far as I'm aware, mortals standing up to the monsters ARE hunters. It seems like we're dealing with the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, yeah, you're right.<br /> I was too preoccupied with Compact and Conspiracies to forget that Tier 1 hunters essentially ARE mortals standing up and fighting whatever.<br /> Thanks for reminding me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't know... I keep comparing and contrasting Prometheans with Beasts.<br /> It's my opinion that either Heroes should have more diverse dimentions,<br /> or if Heroes were to stay that way, non-Hero struggles against hunter/mortals should be mentioned right along with hero section, and not just two-three paragraphs in the crossover section. I mean, yeah, hunters are their own line and all, but the text as it is written... kind of says that the victims either suck it up or become assholes. Unfortunate implications.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-13-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:51:50-07:00","id":553153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552964#post552964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hunter conspiracy about Beasts!<br /> <br /> I mean, but also, Hunter seems really like a group with philosophy, almost like a night-job.<br /> I want to read write-ups about normal people, doing something against the Beasts, but who are not Hero-level fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>...... That Literally describes Hunters........<br /> <br /> Hunters are perfectly normal Mortals who have decided to take up &quot;The Vigil&quot; IE Hunt the monsters they kill and Harm people.<br /> That is Literally what they do. Yes Some have special abilities.. but they are still normal people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:52:27-07:00","id":553154,"title":"","content":"A lot of people said they wanted to see Mortal Remains chapter for Beasts as a Kickstarter Stretch Goal.<br /> <br /> I'm now one of them, especially if it helps alleviate the whole &quot;not enough antagonist variety&quot; problem some people have noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:55:02-07:00","id":553156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553152#post553152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, yeah, you're right.<br /> I was too preoccupied with Compact and Conspiracies to forget that Tier 1 hunters essentially ARE mortals standing up and fighting whatever.<br /> Thanks for reminding me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> No, thank you. Its easy to get caught up in the Compacts and Conspiracies - I know people that can't wrap their minds around a tier 1 hunter game, and get all angsty if I bring it up. They just get so wrapped up in how hunters are different from base mortals, they stopped thinking of hunters as humans and just another supernatural.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-13-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:56:02-07:00","id":553158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552904#post552904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That bit you quoted from Matt actually supports what GreaterHeron said, not negates it. Prometheans are still the cause of Disquiet (even if its their internal Fire instead of the Uncanny Valley effect), and they own it. They keep on the Pilgrimage to minimize damage. If the sample settings are any indication, Beasts don't - the SAS presents mass murder as something the PCs should consider allowing.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> You know, one thing I'm having trouble nailing down with Beast is the whole society connection thing. Vampires are about politics, night life, and relationships. Werewolf deals a lot with the transgender community. Mage has some privileged upper class vibes to it. Changeling and trauma / abuse. So... what's the Beast's vibe?<br /> <br /> <br /> Human sadists? Put aside the word Hunger for a moment. We're talking about satisfying a psychological urge to cause others pain and distress. They get a voyeuristic thrill from watching others hunt. Are we looking at a splat based around bullies? And, if we are, are we looking at Heroes as the Columbine-type kids, who snapped and shot up the place in revenge?</div> </div> </div> </div>But neither effect is automatic anymore, just like the Rampage. Also, I'm pretty sure that one of the story goals in the SAS was to prevent the mass murder rather than being accessory to it. Again, you mistake mechanical advantage for narrative license. Any decent storyteller would deliver consequences for that sort of behavior, which is where that argument, like those of MADD and the like, fall flat.<br /> <br /> Like I said on this past Monday Meetings post, there needs to be a discussion of addiction, obsession, and the interplay between underworld subcultures when talking about Beast. That's what they're about. If Vampires are the Mob, then Beasts are the Drug-addled fences, fixers, and leg-breakers that truck with them for their next fix while arranging meet-ups with other, more or less law-abiding groups.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:01:56-07:00","id":553161,"title":"","content":"Totally unrelated to the ongoing discussion, but what I really wanted to see now is an Innocent game that involves a Beast. (either as the PC or the antagonist.)<br /> Right there along with the Changeling, I think Beast as a huge fun-potential in that game, with even somewhat toned-down-yet-scary children's horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 06-13-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:18:30-07:00","id":553176,"title":"","content":"I feel like the discussion's starting to get a little circular again, so maybe we should wait for the revisions to be done before continuing to spin circles in circles and mandalas in mandalas in a tapestry of inevitability.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: And the discussion has kinda moved on, which tends to happen when you have a post you started to write hanging for several hours. Blergh.)<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that is a really ambitious goal for an unplanned development pass Matt and team set. 15 thousand words plus some rewriting and rewording in <i>a week?</i> No one can claim they don't work hard after this. You can tell they love this book.<br /> <br /> In another topic I'm surprised no one commented on, I thought the story of the minotaur in the Namtaru update for the Kickstarter was pretty good. I appreciate that while it can be interpreted as Minos being a good father within what he thought was in his reach (and the tale is all the more moving for of it), it also has a healthy degree of ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Also lonely Minotaur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-13-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:23:03-07:00","id":553183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553158#post553158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div> You misread what I said. That's not what I was saying at all. <br /> <br /> Irregardless, they're changing up some things, so it doesn't matter. Moving on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said on this past Monday Meetings post, there needs to be a discussion of addiction, obsession, and the interplay between underworld subcultures when talking about Beast. That's what they're about. If Vampires are the Mob, then Beasts are the Drug-addled fences, fixers, and leg-breakers that truck with them for their next fix while arranging meet-ups with other, more or less law-abiding groups. </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... its missing too much. While vamps do have much in common with drug cultures, they do step out and away from just gangs and mobs. And Beasts have more than just being thugs for vamps; doesn't touch on too many of the other sadistic hungers. Feels too small. Doesn't feel right. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-13-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:27:51-07:00","id":553188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553176#post553176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the discussion's starting to get a little circular again, so maybe we should wait for the revisions to be done before continuing to spin circles in circles and mandalas in mandalas in a tapestry of inevitability.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: And the discussion has kinda moved on, which tends to happen when you have a post you started to write hanging for several hours. Blergh.)<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that is a really ambitious goal for an unplanned development pass Matt and team set. 15 thousand words plus some rewriting and rewording in <i>a week?</i> No one can claim they don't work hard after this. You can tell they love this book.<br /> <br /> In another topic I'm surprised no one commented on, I thought the story of the minotaur in the Namtaru update for the Kickstarter was pretty good. I appreciate that while it can be interpreted as Minos being a good father within what he thought was in his reach (and the tale is all the more moving for of it), it also has a healthy degree of ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Also lonely Minotaur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really really love Minotaur as Beast analogy, cause MINOTAURS....<br /> <br /> Seriously. If one monster in a myth is both disgustingly, hilariously abusive and yet capable to earning sympathy, it's the Minotaur. So much depth.<br /> <br /> And I am a hardcore <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">House</span> of Leaves fan, so there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:33:05-07:00","id":553193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553183#post553183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, no. You get a choice of trying to prevent it, or not. The fact that its an option at all is kind of horrifying at the mentality of Beasts in general.<br /> <br /> Now, Rose has said that the writers tend not to suggest that violence not be the ultimate answer in the WoD... however, it IS being suggested rather casually as the best answer in Beast. If that's not the intent, its the intent a lot of people are walking away with, which is an issue.<br /> <br /> I frankly don't care if you think its right or wrong. In this case, perception is reality. If people are perceiving it that way, then that will be their reality. If you're not seeing it that way, then that, too, is your reality.<br /> <br /> Again? This is the first time its come up with me, and no, I didn't. This and that are separate issues. I'm not talking about delivering consequences at all! You completely and utterly misread what I put down. I'm talking about cultural trends, which is an entirely different manner.<br /> <br /> Ehhh.... its missing too much. While vamps do have much in common with drug cultures, they do step out and away from just gangs and mobs. And Beasts have more than just being thugs for vamps; doesn't touch on too many of the other sadistic hungers. Feels too small.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. That's the argument: that the option to do evil encourages people to do evil. Which is not always the case in reality.<br /> <br /> 2. I was using the plural you, because that argument has been made several times before on this thread.<br /> <br /> 3. That was an example, but that's the real-world parallel I draw, that Beasts are all addicts to one degree or another, and those addictions inform how they interact with other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:45:31-07:00","id":553211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't compare all of the Begotten to addicts anymore than I'd compare any being that needs to hunt and eat to survive to addicts. Withdrawal can kill past a certain point, but drug addicts aren't born or inevitably drawn to become that, far as I know.<br /> <br /> It's likely valid to say some are addicted to their Hungers, but claiming that's true for all of them doesn't seem right. Well, in part a matter of personal interpretation there, but it's not uniformly accurate to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus if you say that all vampires are addicts the werewolves should be considered addicts for hunting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:47:04-07:00","id":553220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553193#post553193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. That was an example, but that's the real-world parallel I draw, that Beasts are all addicts to one degree or another, and those addictions inform how they interact with other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was going to address the other parts, but honestly, it doesn't matter. Perception is reality, and the perception that poeple walk away with of the game is real to them. Argue for or against what you think they're saying, it doesn't address the underlying issue.<br /> <br /> This part, however, deserves an answer. Beasts aren't addicts. Not only is that covered by vampires already, but it doesn't match what Hungers feel like. This is a psychological <i>need</i> that the Beasts possess, much in the same way we need food and water. Addicts can only think about their next hit, and that really doesn't feel like the theme in the game. Suffering is their spiritual drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:26:26-07:00","id":553264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553161#post553161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally unrelated to the ongoing discussion, but what I really wanted to see now is an Innocent game that involves a Beast. (either as the PC or the antagonist.)<br /> Right there along with the Changeling, I think Beast as a huge fun-potential in that game, with even somewhat toned-down-yet-scary children's horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I proposed some time ago to get <i>WW2 Bliz Britain</i> as <b>Innocents</b>/<b>Beast</b> crossover era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496951#post496951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About <b>London Blitz Era</b>: I would point out this combination is golden, as you can be loneley child thrown in alien surrounding, monster under it's bed or just that thing that watch out from the window both of them to sate it's Hunger, in the times of great terror on the world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The victim of fear ( child), the source of fear ( supernaturals/monsters? Beasts? ), the guardian of this fear ( the other Begotten ) or even to play the fear of eveyone of those groups in times of war. What even more disturbing Homecoming to have is that your repeating child nightmares are <b>your very own Beast Soul</b>?<br /> <br /> And even then random vampire that raised from grave on battlefield, totally lost in their undead condition. Or werewolf that slaughter battalion pressed to anger, and now left without guidence. The both literal children and metaphorical Children need to take care of them or confront them.<br /> <br /> Looks I finally got idea for mine first chronicle in Beast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Really, I need this setting right now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And WE REALLY NEED <b>BEAST</b> SUBFORUM, as this topic is very interesting, but a big mess now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:30:11-07:00","id":553266,"title":"","content":"Late to the party...but has there been any discussion of a demi-human splat for this game? I'm wondering because I'm reading the preview copy and noticing a lack of psuedo-Beast or Beast-affiliated characters. The Beast's minions, stewards, and guardians figure prominently into some stories as additional obstacles (mid-bosses) that the Hero must overcome. From that perspective it feels like Beast is lacking something vital. What of the Beast's mortal kin? The mother that suspects what her son is and protects him? What of the Beast's own monstrous children, the deep ones that come from the sea, Leviathan's daughters gathering sacrifices to feed her? What about the hounds that drive the prey to the hunter?<br /> <br /> It seems like another vital societal aspect to Beasts is missing from the game since not everyone in the Beast's family is going to be a Beast or a &quot;Kin&quot;. It would be nice if there was a section that fills this in, much like the sections on Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, Proximi, etc. If such a section isn't planned for the book then the pages discussing Integrity, Virtue, and Vice aren't actually needed and could be subtracted out of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 06-13-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:34:40-07:00","id":553268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553266#post553266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late to the party...but has there been any discussion of a demi-human splat for this game? I'm wondering because I'm reading the preview copy and noticing a lack of psuedo-Beast or Beast-affiliated characters. The Beast's minions, stewards, and guardians figure prominently into some stories as additional obstacles (mid-bosses) that the Hero must overcome. From that perspective it feels like Beast is lacking something vital. What of the Beast's mortal kin? The mother that suspects what her son is and protects him? What of the Beast's own monstrous children? What about the deep ones that come from the sea, Leviathan's daughters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt's said there won't be one for Beast. I think this was because they couldn't come up with anything that they liked for the demi-supernatural, although I feel like it may also have been a deliberate design choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553266#post553266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like another vital societal aspect to Beast's is missing from the game since not everyone in the Beast's family is going to be a Beast or a &quot;Kin&quot;. It would be nice if there was a section that fills this in, much like the sections on Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, Proximi, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably too much word count for not enough payoff in most games to include in the main book. I bet you it shows up in a dedicated crossover book, or barring that, in the Storyteller's Handbook. For now, I'm content with exploring as many of the different vampire kinships from Night Horrors as possible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:09:51-07:00","id":553323,"title":"","content":"Monsters do not have minions. Not the Monomyth styled ones anyway. They don't need them. They may have siblings, but that's covered by Brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:13:24-07:00","id":553356,"title":"","content":"Yep. These are the kinds of beasts that would not have minions. The game doesn't really have a place for them either. Innocent and Beast is a good idea for a Stretch Goal. You should comment that on the Kickstarter. Wasn't it the same Matt that made Innocents? Sounds like something that will appear in a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:59:40-07:00","id":553397,"title":"","content":"New Introduction is up on the Kickstarter; some interesting changes. Heroes, especially, are now much more a part of the narrative weft of the Dream rather than spawned by Beasts. Some more evocative terminology too. Homecoming is now The Devouring, Soul is now The Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:37:37-07:00","id":553415,"title":"","content":"After reading the new intro I feel as if Beast has taken a step backwards. I liked that beasts were living nightmares and that realizing this about themselves was like coming home. Them reveling in their nature as monsters was a big part of the draw for me. Please don't let this be the actual intro for the book. I'm overcome with disgust at the moment and having a hard time putting my thoughts into words. Will probably come back after I've calmed down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:41:33-07:00","id":553421,"title":"","content":"One thing I hope gets touched in the rewrite: the Kinship sections for Changeling and Mummy. The former feels like a bit of a waste, focusing on the Gentry instead of actual changelings, while the latter was basically &quot;neither side gets much out of it, move along.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553415#post553415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the new intro I feel as if Beast has taken a step backwards. I liked that beasts were living nightmares and that realizing this about themselves was like coming home. Them reveling in their nature as monsters was a big part of the draw for me. Please don't let this be the actual intro for the book. I'm overcome with disgust at the moment and having a hard time putting my thoughts into words. Will probably come back after I've calmed down.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason it got a rewrite, friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-13-2015, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:46:28-07:00","id":553443,"title":"","content":"The Hero change is good. The Beast change is <i>really</i> bad, and even contradicts the implications of the (unchanged) opening narrative.<br /> <br /> I don't like the idea that a Beast has to have another Beast act as a catalyst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:49:23-07:00","id":553444,"title":"","content":"I dunno; the Beast is still marked from birth. It's more of a...I don't know, a mentoring? The Beasts are seeking out their family and guiding them to their destiny. To me, it implies a cultivation of potential. The Beast isn't the catalyst; he's merely the hand that finally helps you over the threshold.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure that there's the potential to simply give in independently of another Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:51:12-07:00","id":553445,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think spontaneous devourings should at least be possible, even if they're not required.<br /> <br /> Maybe that can be something Unfettered do now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:52:36-07:00","id":553446,"title":"","content":"To clarify a point from earlier in the thread: I wrote some of the stuff about nightmares (small 'n'). My intention was that the nightmares spread by Beasts were not actually worse than &quot;normal&quot; nightmares, so not scarring or torturous.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As in, last night, I actually had a nightmare about being chased by a monster. Pretty <i>Beast</i>-appropriate. I woke up fairly unhappy, but it evaporated in the light of morning. That kind of thing. Not, like, say, the sleep paralysis episode where a demonic shadow was hovering over my bed, which was seriously affecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 06-13-2015, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:54:00-07:00","id":553447,"title":"","content":"There are a lot more words that still have to written and revealed, people. And I'm saying that to both those who disliked the book before and those who are perplexed or don't like the new introduction.<br /> <br /> I'm wary about some aspects of it, for example. Some things don't exactly click in the same way they did before for me (though I do like other parts) but I'm going to wait for the complete picture before expressing a definitive judgement.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I just came back from Jurassic World and watching that movie while Beast haunts my thoughts is already having consequences. Bad or good, I can't really say.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553445#post553445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think spontaneous devourings should at least be possible, even if they're not required.<br /> <br /> Maybe that can be something Unfettered do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I just don't like that part now. I get that it helps the social aspects, renforces the &quot;Family&quot; whole deal and gives older Beasts an important role, but not having spontaneous devourings as a possibility is something I sadly miss. A moment of mythical self-realization that now sounds more as an ordinary recruitment. Devourings are fine and have a reason to be, but I really do believe spontaneus ones should be a thing, even a rare one. I hope this is not the whole deal, but the intro is not giving me reasons to believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-13-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:58:56-07:00","id":553448,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% happy with the update, myself, but for different reasons. I am happy with a lot of the changes made, though: Beasts now have a raison d'etre besides being bad people doing bad things. I'm not sure if the teaching aspect is exactly the choice I'd make but it <i>is</i> a valid one and definitely one that fits Beasts' place in the setting, both cosmically and in terms of power. Personally, I liked Beasts being born, and being relatively inhuman, but that's something I can live with.<br /> <br /> I'm at the very least curious to see what further changes are made. There's fine-tuning to be done, but we're not off to a bad start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:59:39-07:00","id":553451,"title":"","content":"Ok, had a bit of a stew and a think. What's turning me off of this new intro was that the homecoming is part of what really sells me on Beast. A beast is something you are, it's something you have to realize and come to terms with. The new intro has turned that moment of self realization into a job offer. It feels so much weaker this way and frankly leaves a bad taste in my mouth.<br /> <br /> Now, I like that using fear as a teaching tool has been brought to the fore where as before it was very much a background thing that seemed to be quickly glossed over in the initial write up. Going to have to reread the new intro now that my head has cleared a bit and see how the rest of it shapes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:04:33-07:00","id":553456,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of family seeking out family and helping them to understand what they've always been. Though when I put it like that, it kind sounds like Hagrid turning up with a letter. I like the idea that sometimes this is what happens but think that they need to be clear that sometimes Beasts just accept the dream and get devoured. More often than not, I would think, that self-realisation and strength of will should shine through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:07:36-07:00","id":553458,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm digging the new intro. If the rest of the revisions are at this level I'm in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:14:05-07:00","id":553461,"title":"","content":"And once again, Beast delivers everything I wanted with a large helping of what I needed. I love the fleshed out treatment of Heroes and of the Primordial Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:17:18-07:00","id":553463,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Sleep Paralysis - I'm surprised there isn't a NIghtmare that deals with that specifically. I guess there's You Can't Run, but there's still a pretty specific experience separate from that worth exploring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:26:16-07:00","id":553471,"title":"","content":"I can probably sum up my issue with the new intro with just the word &quot;devoured&quot;. The idea that the beast soul has always been a part of you and was just waiting for you to realize what you are is to me a great concept. It's coming of age for monsters and the lack of this concept in the new write-up bothers me. It feels like the strongest part of Beasts narrative was removed and what it was replaced with just seems inferior. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this seems ranty but I've grown attached to the game over the past few days and I'm having trouble parsing this change in a positive light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:27:48-07:00","id":553474,"title":"","content":"I like the new intro. I know the Intro was suggesting that Beasts Devour you like a job offer and all that jazz, but even <i>EVEN </i>with this being a major revision of a revision, I'd bet good money that the text will get cleaned up again further, since these re-writers are in part a big conceptual overhaul. Polishing the wording around that will probably come.<br /> <br /> I'll probably run my games a bit more abstract than Joe Beastman helping Jill Beastman become a Beastman if I run Beast, but the idea of fear being instructional really jives with me and feels more distinctive. If the story about the monster in the darkness outside your hut teaches you not to go outside at night when the <i>actual predators </i>are out there stalking to kill the shit out of you, than that story which seems to prey on the imaginations of children and the supersticious is serving a valuable function of protecting the people from the real night predators. I think tapping into that is a great way to offer Beasts a weird sort of place in a supernatural ecosystem, though I like to think of the New World of Darkness as being more mysterious than a simple ecosystem of spooky things.<br /> <br /> One of the things I'd like to see, if nothing else than to help people's ability to comprehend Beast with regards to other splats, would be that in the section discussing Kinship, there be some examination of how the Primordial Dream and the Astral writ large occupy a sort of conceptual space rather than a literal one. The relationship between the Dark Mother and the Awakened or Vampires isn't something as simple as &quot;She was here first&quot; but rather that the symbolism that these creatures all have as components of their identity interacts heavily with the primordial ideas that the Primordial Dream embodies. Supernal Magic, the Curse, Father Wolf, all of these things aren't literally descended from the Dark Mother, so much as they all have some sympathy with elements of the Primordial Dream, and that this is probably the basis for Kinship.<br /> <br /> People that think Mage's cosmology overwrites other WoD games are dumb. I'm pretty sure Beast doesn't overwrite anything anyway, but I'd prefer it if it's clear for people on the fence, and to avoid the low reading comprehension issue that Mage has had to contend with for years. Beast is a cool idea and doesn't need that getting in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:30:42-07:00","id":553477,"title":"","content":"I get where you're coming from, CM; I like the notion that Beasts are inhuman in some way. It's just hard to reconcile that Beasts would give a damn about humanity with the notion of being completely inhuman. I'd prefer it if we could have the former <i>and</i> the latter, but a character with a (cosmic) reason to not be a complete and utter bastard-coated bastard is worth more to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:30:56-07:00","id":553478,"title":"","content":"I'm mixed. I love the new Heroes, and I think the role of &quot;Dark Teacher&quot; seems like it's fun and new. Horror's okay as a term. I <b>really</b> don't like Devouring. I preferred being a Beast to be something more innate, and I really hate that it's now a transformation(that you can't even achieve on your own!) instead of a realization. I mean, I know you guys put a lot of effort into this rewrite, and I feel terrible for saying it isn't perfect, but I'm just not feeling parts of it. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:40:59-07:00","id":553486,"title":"","content":"I can only look at the teaching angle as good news for my spider-Raptor TA.<br /> <br /> Anybody else notice the shift in definition of Chambers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:42:58-07:00","id":553487,"title":"","content":"Yeah, definitely to do with expanding on the Primordial Dream. I remember thinking there was probably something like that in the Astral anyway, so I'm excited to see what more they give us about it as a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:45:14-07:00","id":553488,"title":"","content":"Reading it again, I don't think the beast necessarily has any <i>direct </i>involvement in the transformation. They just sort of tell the newbie how to do it themselves. It seems logical that some beasts can figure it out without help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:50:04-07:00","id":553490,"title":"","content":"I'd have to ask Matt for a definitive answer, but, yeah, I think it's something that can probably happen without help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:55:09-07:00","id":553492,"title":"","content":"Hey a question I'm a little fuzzy on if someone would mind clarifying it for me,so I can be sure. It was mentioned in both versions that a Beast's hunger can occasionally change, but that it is usually set and the change is a dramatic thing. So just for clarification are we talking a like a tyrant Beast one day becoming a collector, or are we talking a collector who focused on books switching over to collecting weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:03:50-07:00","id":553497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553446#post553446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify a point from earlier in the thread: I wrote some of the stuff about nightmares (small 'n'). My intention was that the nightmares spread by Beasts were not actually worse than &quot;normal&quot; nightmares, so not scarring or torturous.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As in, last night, I actually had a nightmare about being chased by a monster. Pretty <i>Beast</i>-appropriate. I woke up fairly unhappy, but it evaporated in the light of morning. That kind of thing. Not, like, say, the sleep paralysis episode where a demonic shadow was hovering over my bed, which was seriously affecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:07:40-07:00","id":553498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553490#post553490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to ask Matt for a definitive answer, but, yeah, I think it's something that can probably happen without help.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why I tend to have faith in you, Onyx Path overlords.<br /> <br /> Even if I have some reservations about the new intro (though the parts I like more exceed the ones I like less), I'll wait to the very end before setting the ship on fire and jumping into the sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:09:42-07:00","id":553499,"title":"","content":"Extremely disappointed with the new changes. This...just feels far more inferior to me as a horror game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:14:55-07:00","id":553501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553499#post553499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely disappointed with the new changes. This...just feels far more inferior to me as a horror game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">The material in the new intro preview is not the game I was hyped up for. This is not what I was promised in the blog teasers, in the RPG.net teasers, or anywhere else. This is not the game I got into when I read the document originally posted up on Kickstarter, which made me feel like pledging my money to this project.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I do not like the Devouring; I want the Homecoming where you are the only player involved in becoming what you are. I do not like the 'teacher' thing, which feels like an unnecessary effort to justify the Hungers of Beasts. I want the Beast I was sold on before.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:16:43-07:00","id":553502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553478#post553478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mixed. I love the new Heroes, and I think the role of &quot;Dark Teacher&quot; seems like it's fun and new. Horror's okay as a term. I <b>really</b> don't like Devouring. I preferred being a Beast to be something more innate, and I really hate that it's now a transformation(that you can't even achieve on your own!) instead of a realization. I mean, I know you guys put a lot of effort into this rewrite, and I feel terrible for saying it isn't perfect, but I'm just not feeling parts of it. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought's, exactly. Only I mark that if Devouring is more a thing &quot;it can be done spontenous, the Older Siblings are only often to help when they can&quot; I think it's totally okay. I'm missing a bit realisation of &quot;you are a monster from the ancient times&quot;, but, in the end, being Devored by the Horror from the Primodrial Dream <b>does</b> have a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Only other question on Devouring in revision - <b>Does Older Sibling's Family need to be the same as yours?</b> So Anakim helps proto-Anakim in change or Namataru guides proto-Namataru? Or does any Beast can help you unleash a Horror that hunts your mortal self? Great would be to get confirmation from <b>Matt</b> on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-13-2015, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:18:35-07:00","id":553504,"title":"","content":"The thing is though, without some sort of overarcing idea of what a Beast stands for, then there was literally nothing to restrain you. Nothing. It's like with the introductory adventure they included; why should Beast-as-was care about any of that? Why care enough to get involved and stop her when its something that I could very easily want to do?<br /> <br /> Beast needed something to provide a degree of nuance between reasonable Beasts and Beasts that get their kicks from suffering. There had to be something that added depth rather than &quot;I'm hungry&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:25:58-07:00","id":553509,"title":"","content":"I'm mad that they chose to sacrafice the Homecoming ( a key part of the game ) in order to insert a social structure. Yes, Beast needed a social structure. No, they shouldn't have changed such a key part of the game in order to do it. Now, every Beast chooses to be a Beast, it's not something they are born as. I would much rather have seen groups connected through shared goals and desires, there are no reason like minded Beasts couldn't band together or try to govern each other. The Homecoming was the heart of the game, without it I'm not sure this is still the same game I fell in love with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:30:33-07:00","id":553514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553509#post553509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mad that they chose to sacrafice the Homecoming ( a key part of the game ) in order to insert a social structure. Yes, Beast needed a social structure. No, they shouldn't have changed such a key part of the game in order to do it. Now, every Beast chooses to be a Beast, it's not something they are born as. I would much rather have seen groups connected through shared goals and desires, there are no reason like minded Beasts couldn't band together or try to govern each other. The Homecoming was the heart of the game, without it I'm not sure this is still the same game I fell in love with.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still born as a Beast, it's just a matter of accepting it. I also really can't see it as &quot;sacrificing&quot; the Homecoming to insert a social structure, because that really isn't how it comes across for me. The social aspect comes more into the regional Alphaing thing that they seem to have went for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:31:39-07:00","id":553530,"title":"","content":"List of things I Like<br /> -------------------------------<br /> Opening Pitch<br /> *The Main thing I like is the sort of discussion what fear does, how fear acts as a teacher and crucible for development. THere's some good clarity and sense of place here-it reminds me of a good bit from Dresden Files in Ghost Story. But not all monsters are-well, I'll save that for the torn section.<br /> <br /> Overview<br /> *You know, it just occurred to me that Beasts were kind of 'justified victims' as well from a certain point of view in the old read. This avoids that. I'm not sold on the seperate soul taking the place of yours, but I think having the full claiming of one's Soul in context removes a troublesome element.<br /> <br /> The Devouring<br /> *Oh god, some of those dreams are <i>visceral</i>. Good story fodder there. You experience the nightmares of others, and you just <i>know</i> what it means, and you try to do something about it, but you aren't equipped yet to do it. I like that as a tie into desire to improve humanity through fear, questioned as that might be.<br /> <br /> Heroes<br /> *Aaaand that's the right angle. It fit well before, but now it's smoother, like there were bubbles underneath the surface I wasn't aware of that got popped.<br /> <br /> List of things I don't like<br /> -----------------------------------<br /> Opening Pitch<br /> *What's with this &quot;Being devoured/chosen by the Beast/your Big Brother Or Sister&quot; stuff? You have an expansive Soul that draws from the soul of the world and of humanity as a whole, you can have wisdom from your Homecoming without divorcing your Soul from yourself. Plus you can parody the Chosen Ones narrative a little, and somewhat mirror Heroes more(parallels are great!). I mean, it <i>does</i> tie into the family frame, but still.<br /> <br /> Overview<br /> *Too much humanity, not enough monstrosity(?). You wanna sell me on Beasts bringing the Family home and become better teachers-by-fear, sure, but let's keep the ugliness of the monstrous family in view.<br /> <br /> Hunger<br /> *Okay, confusion. The Horrors call on the Beast to teach humanity through fear, and then says it doesn't care and will eat anything wholly, regardless of if that thing survives to get wisdom or not. Pick a party line, Horrors-are you teachers or eaters?<br /> <br /> List of things I'm torn on<br /> -----------------------------------<br /> Opening Pitch<br /> *On the one hand, I <i>liked</i> the entitlement of Beasts. It felt real and risky to me-it rang true that a Beast has a sense of....not quite entitlement, but freedom to claim things for themselves now. It also really fed into their need to defy the cycle. On the other hand, the monstrous mentor thing is really cool to me too, and it's one of my preferred archetypes, but I have a harder time buying into the need to deviate from the cycle. I dunno, I like the 'altruism', but I also like the brutal liberation. Hmm.<br /> <br /> THings that I just want to comment on without assigning a qualifier on.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> The Horror<br /> *I could dig the idea of Horrors as a sort of incubator for the Beast's Soul. It expands the personal mythology of Beasts a bit, going from Beasts, to Unfettered, Rampant, Incarnates to the Horrors to the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Overall Impression<br /> ------------------------------<br /> The first version thrilled me. This one does...less so, but at the same time it is a wiser approach. It isn't as sharp edged, but it is still interesting. Color me cautiously optimistic about the changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:32:47-07:00","id":553533,"title":"","content":"I preferred the Homecoming, but also see how a mentor could make a meaningful difference in the education of a new Beast.<br /> I think it would be best if we could have it both ways:<ul><li>Every Beast is destined to have a Homecoming. The ones who have a Teacher tend to integrate into Beast society the easiest.</li> <li>That leaves plenty of narrative room for PC Beasts who have no teacher to be played, while also leaving room for wild and savage NPC Beasts.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:42:01-07:00","id":553537,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like these changes on the whole. Part of them I'm sure as hell I don't like.<br /> <br /> The changing of the Homecoming to the Devouring is... too significant for me to swallow. The latter seems to mean and have entirely different implications than the former, and those changes honestly diminish the idea that Beast presented to me since OPP started to talk about it in the detail, and that the 99% text gave us.<br /> <br /> These changes don't sound like the Beast I was excited for, and they feel like trying to force justification where none was needed and trade-off in purpose where there was already purpose in the consumption itself.<br /> <br /> This took a bit to write even though I read the update immediately because I might actually be churning a little bit at considering it. And it just clicked to me. I feel betrayed by these proposed changes to the text. I'm genuinely sorry to say it, but I do.<br /> <br /> I will wait until we've reached the end of this development pass, and Matt and co. have discussed the feedback again, to say if I'll withdraw my support of Beast or not. But for now, I am very wary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:44:59-07:00","id":553541,"title":"","content":"It's beginning to sound like if Onyx Path want to please everyone they're going to have to release two versions of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:45:41-07:00","id":553542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553537#post553537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will wait until we've reached the end of this development pass, and Matt and co. have discussed the feedback again, to say if I'll withdraw my support of Beast or not. But for now, I am very wary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I am right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:46:10-07:00","id":553544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553541#post553541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's beginning to sound like if Onyx Path want to please everyone they're going to have to release two versions of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very fortunately, Onyx Path never has the intention of pleasing everyone. Trying to do so is impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:46:55-07:00","id":553545,"title":"","content":"I'm going to rant freely. I hope I don't cross a line..<br /> <br /> Why? Why change the Homecoming? Why Change the Beasts Soul to something as Generic as a Horror?<br /> <br /> and Speaking of horror-Here's the implication I'm getting: A Monster invades somebody's dreams, scares the Bejesus out of them, and convinces them to become a Monster.<br /> <br /> Then a Disembodied Monster shows up and eats the first persons soul and then jacks there body.<br /> <br /> That's a fucking Pod Person.<br /> <br /> Meaning that all Beasts have committed at least one Unforgivably Immoral Act, just to come into existance..<br /> <br /> That completely derails the Grey and Grey Morality into Grey and Black-And the Beasts are the black.<br /> <br /> Even if I'm wrong about the Implications of the Devouring, there's still the fact that it being a case of a Spiritual Entity Merging with Someone, as opposed to have always had a Primordial Soul,... We already have a game about Spiritual Entities Merging with a Mortal Host wo is perceptive to them-It's Called Geist the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> And about the Beasts new Motivation-Scaring People to Impart Wisdom. Isn't that Exactly what Vampires on the Path of Lilith did in the CWoD? And I think The Lancea Et Sanctum did something similar(being the monster that scares the mortals into following His Divine Wisdom) at least in 1E<br /> <br /> So the changes to Beast in the document are &quot;Change the Name of their Primordial Soul to the incredibly Bland and Generic &quot;Horror&quot;, either changed them from the Reborn Primordial Monsters to evil Pod People who con people into being Replaced or into a Geist Rip off. And they rip off the Motivation of Two different Vampire Subplots.<br /> <br /> There were better ways to fix Beasts problems than this, Matt.<br /> <br /> You said a Beast's motivations were &quot;To feed and explore the world of Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> You could have given the Beasts Direction by not changing anything about their Origins and then just giving them some more insentive to explore the world of Darkness-Eldritch Locations to find, or Maybe include an Appendix with a bunch of minor templates/Simplified Monster Rules/Merits for Mortal Psychich so that you didn't have to go full crossover to have a game about going out and Finding Kin.<br /> <br /> This was not the way to go Matt. I am Disappoint.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553504#post553504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is though, without some sort of overarcing idea of what a Beast stands for, then there was literally nothing to restrain you. Nothing. It's like with the introductory adventure they included; why should Beast-as-was care about any of that? Why care enough to get involved and stop her when its something that I could very easily want to do?<br /> <br /> Beast needed something to provide a degree of nuance between reasonable Beasts and Beasts that get their kicks from suffering. There had to be something that added depth rather than &quot;I'm hungry&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There were better ways to do it.<br /> <br /> In providing restraint in this manner, they killed <b>Beast's</b> Soul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:48:31-07:00","id":553547,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now that I've had a chance to go back over the new intro without being blinded by rage I can say I like pretty much everything you've changed other than the Homecoming, as mentioned above, and I'm not really sure what to think about Heroes. I was one of those that was fine with the original Hero write-up, the new one will take some time to digest.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:52:28-07:00","id":553549,"title":"","content":"I think the personally amusing thing for me is that I'm fairly happy with either interpretation. A little tweak on the Devouring would be enough to bring it into line with what it was, easy enough. I think that it's been really amusing to see the shift in hyperbole from one side of the controversy to the other. And I'm sorry, but saying that this has killed Beast's soul is hyperbolic.<br /> <br /> I would very much love to hear how you would have mediated the rampant abuse inherent in Hungers though; what approach would you have used to rein in the worst of Beast's nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:54:44-07:00","id":553550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553549#post553549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would very much love to hear how you would have mediated the rampant abuse inherent in Hungers though; what approach would you have used to rein in the worst of Beast's nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely nothing. It was fine as it was. <br /> <br /> That is my stance, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:55:55-07:00","id":553551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553533#post553533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I preferred the Homecoming, but also see how a mentor could make a meaningful difference in the education of a new Beast.<br /> I think it would be best if we could have it both ways:<ul><li>Every Beast is destined to have a Homecoming. The ones who have a Teacher tend to integrate into Beast society the easiest.</li> <li>That leaves plenty of narrative room for PC Beasts who have no teacher to be played, while also leaving room for wild and savage NPC Beasts.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I support this with both hands - we do not need to lose the Homecoming to have Older Siblings taking big part in Beast transformation. I easily could see that preHomecoming Beast is strugling with the nightmares her Horror is inducuing their whole life - and when the Older Sibling is showing her Atavisms, or even Nightmares - the preHomecoming just click and finally understand she was a monster all along. The Older Sibling is training new Beast about base of mythology, Dark Mother and Kinship - and is describing need to making Lessons in the feast their Horror makes on people.<br /> <br /> And we still can have feral Beast that needed to get to this on their own, totally alone, probably as partially antagonistic faction - &quot;<i>What do you mean <b>only</b> Hunger is important? What about restraining your Horror? What about Lessons to contain the Heroes, for a f@#$ sake!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> We do not need to have Devouring that is mixed idea to this day. Let there be Homecoming still in it's place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-13-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:56:17-07:00","id":553553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553550#post553550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely nothing. It was fine as it was.<br /> <br /> That is my stance, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly that didn't jive with Matt, and I can see why. This is a wiser approach. Maybe less evocative, but it's more mature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:59:57-07:00","id":553555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553553#post553553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly that didn't jive with Matt, and I can see why. This is a wiser approach. Maybe less evocative, but it's more mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have to agree there. Greater nuance brings greater potential, and less potential for abuse- while leaving enough leeway for people who do want to be the shameless revel glutton.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:08:39-07:00","id":553560,"title":"","content":"Okay, now that I've taken a step back I'm going to try and take another go at this. <br /> <br /> I liked the Homecoming, I loved what it meant for the characters and the stories they would create. It makes me very sad to see it go. I will need to be sold on the Devouring, but at the very least they should look into renaming it. I want the birth of the Beast to be a homecoming, an awakening if you would, a moment of clarity and self idendification. I'm not sold on the mentor aspect, and mostly right now I'm worried about what else was changed. I really want to like this book, I've spent the last few months madly in love with it and I want to keep being in love with it. But I won't be able to make that call until I see the rest of the changes. They did good on the heroes, here hopes they did as well on the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:14:06-07:00","id":553564,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, I'm okay with Homecoming and Devouring being synonymous. I can even make the transition and go completely with Devouring.<br /> <br /> It's Horror in the place of Soul, and the context of it, that bugs me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:18:22-07:00","id":553566,"title":"","content":"Why not make both homecoming and devouring optional","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:21:08-07:00","id":553569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553564#post553564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, I'm okay with Homecoming and Devouring being synonymous. I can even make the transition and go completely with Devouring.<br /> <br /> It's Horror in the place of Soul, and the context of it, that bugs me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, an entire species created just to enforce some primal moral is kind of junky. It would have worked much better as like, a school of thought among the Children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:22:22-07:00","id":553570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553268#post553268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt's said there won't be one for Beast. I think this was because they couldn't come up with anything that they liked for the demi-supernatural, although I feel like it may also have been a deliberate design choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was intentional. A few of us brought up the possibility during initial discussions. Matt said he didn't want them. So nothing ever really got discussed at length. Promethean similarly doesn't have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:26:52-07:00","id":553574,"title":"","content":"I had a bit of a kneejerk negative reaction there, and now that I'm cooling down a little and reading more into it, I'm not as... cross with these changes to the text. I actually think some of them might be good, even if there is a significant portion that still bothers me and from my perspective alters fundamental pieces of the premise.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to post something I just said in the blog comments that I think is pertinent, especially to the &quot;how else would the writers restrain the worst of the Beast's nature or mediate the burning needs of Hunger&quot; question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YOLF, Beast Revisions</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The kickstarter preview even says \u201cjustifying Hunger misses the point\u201d. And that brings me to the question I have to ask about this information that\u2019s being revealed. Why justify Hunger? Why justify terror? I can understand and even get behind the concept of fear as a lesson. It\u2019s a cool thing that builds on the importance of Beasts and the Primordial Dream itself to the world. But I don\u2019t think that should justify them, and in the text originally in the kickstarter it didn\u2019t. It also makes me ask, \u201cwhy do the Horrors care?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Horrors that dwell in the Primordial Dream don\u2019t seem to have any real reason to be invested. Unless I\u2019m misunderstanding something very fundamental, they\u2019re a natural byproduct of the wisdom taught by fear, and they\u2019re that lesson itself in what they represent as primordial nightmares. But what that lesson means to the people that receive it shouldn\u2019t be of any consequence to them. That is not what this draft feels like it\u2019s trying to say, especially in the details of the Devouring, and it seems to be contradicting itself in that way.<br /> <br /> <b>It should be the prerogrative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /<i>that/</i> should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves <i>/don\u2019t care</i>/.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The (bolded) last paragraph is something I feel is very important now that I'm carefully considering the revised introduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-13-2015, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:30:43-07:00","id":553576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553574#post553574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The (bolded) last paragraph is something I feel is very important now that I'm carefully considering the revised introduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could have easily been included without horribly derailing the everything about Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:32:39-07:00","id":553579,"title":"","content":"Well it seems I'm not alone in the 'unhappy that Homecoming &amp; the Soul have been replaced by Devouring &amp; the Horror respectably'.<br /> <br /> May I ask why such a tone change was required? The mentoring angle could have been added independently, or even incorporated into the reason you have a Primordial Soul in the first place.<br /> I admit I'm not happy about the change but I might be less opposed to it if I knew the reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:49:32-07:00","id":553583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553570#post553570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was intentional. A few of us brought up the possibility during initial discussions. Matt said he didn't want them. So nothing ever really got discussed at length. Promethean similarly doesn't have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may do one (or more) later. Demons got stigmatics in the core book, but also got the various heirs to hell later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the children of demons were an idea that came up during the KS itself. Somebody asked for an <i>Innocents </i>tie-in, and I was like &quot;holy shit Matt, we have to do this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T18:08:42-07:00","id":553594,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the Introduction, but I did read the bullet points at the end and I have to agree I'm not keen on the Beast not being Beast all along and it does take away from the premise originally proposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T18:14:39-07:00","id":553597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553569#post553569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, an entire species created just to enforce some primal moral is kind of junky. It would have worked much better as like, a school of thought among the Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not it. I have hang-ups on that, too, but I feel by and large more positively towards it. And truth be told, I'm okay with the word Horror too, although I reserve a right use it ina different context in the following explanation. No, it has to do with-<br /> <br /> Okay, before I procede, I need to acknowledge I'm about to run the risk of sounding like an asshole. I apologize if I do in advance.<br /> <br /> In society, we have gatekeepers for a lot of different things. We have gatekeepers for literature, we have them for the culinary arts and the workers unions and the teachers and such, people who define the terms and the access of it. THis applies to families too, within the looseness of the words. A drill sergeant decides who and who isn't allowed into the military family, a Mormon Mission President decides who belongs to what zone 'family' at what time, a group of friends usually has someone who is the final voice of whether someone is in the group or not, a child can marry someone into the family, and the parents in an actual family decide whether to adopt someone in or not(and is often sought after for their blessing in regards to the aforementioned marriage). It's not always an active thing, quite often it's just casually accepted, if even noticed, but there are gatekeepers in families, people who decide whether someone belongs in or not.<br /> <br /> Beasts are adopted in, or perhaps married into by will of the Horror, the Primordial Family in this write up. By itself, that's okay, but it loses potency when it comes to the Crossover/Family aspect of the game. Why? (This is where I risk being an asshole, hear me out) Because the authority and sense of wholeness of a character who brings someone into the family is weakened when that person is adopted/married in.<br /> <br /> Now, that's a shitty, shitty thing to believe in in real world circumstances, that someone brought in that way will never have a truly weighty and substantive opinion as someone born into the family. It's bullshit...But there is still a sense of it, and that sense becomes more important for the Crossover thing than it ever would in real life. See, let's say I marry, creating a person here, Known Sciences, and have been accepted into the Science Family at large*. By all rights, I have a certain authority to allow someone into the Arts Family, particularly under my purview...but do I have the authority to bring someone into the Science's family simply because they conceded to let me in? Technically, the answer is Yes, but you can feel the iffyness around that subject. I am not actually a Science, I am a sort of honorary Science, granted access to the circle, but not the keys to let other people in.<br /> <br /> Now, like I said, that's bollocks in a real world society regardless of how squirmy it makes you feel. That said, it has weight in this kind of narrative, and it comes to one simple reason: Werewolves. Confused, I know, I'll explain. Werewolves bring other things into their family too, their pack, things they recognize as not being Uratha but as being Pack. Humans, Wolf-blooded, Spirits, GHosts, mages, vampires, everything of that sort. We <i>have</i> a family bring-inner of that sort. Beast makes a different claim-you are not part of the family because you have been invited in, you are part of the family because <i>you were born into it</i>, which as has been stated by some of the critics <i>is a bold claim on a cosmological front</i>. It has vast implications. Of course, it need not be true, but it need have some weight to feel possible. In <i>this sense</i>, having someone whose soul was replaced by a Horror is less effective at telling the supernatural that than someone whose soul was always an Astral Manifestation.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a Beast being brought into the family, but I want their soul to be their own**. I like the idea of a new class of being who incubates that soul of a Beast until it's about awakened, leading them to a choice to accept their soul or consolidate it into a simpler soul(or maybe even a Heroic Soul), and who can mentor the Beast and act as an official gatekeeper and can really set the bar of &quot;The Dark Mother aspires for the teaching of humanity through fear&quot;, but that doesn't have to happen-the Soul is connected to the Soul of the World and the Soul of Humanity, and being Devoured can impart that sort of stuff intrinsically. If you add in an incubator of sorts, that also allows for Beasts to have that expectation of teaching and still have a soul that isn't necessarily inclined to it, as it is young in the moment.<br /> <br /> I dunno, this is what I think. I feel like I can take the crossover family claim more seriously if the Beast has always had their soul be their Soul, rather than being consumed into the family.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Let me be clear, I can take everything else, but this is the one thing that makes me go &quot;ERGH&quot;. I'm still planning on buying this game regardless, because all the things I love are still in there.<br /> <br /> *Man, what were they drinking when they made that decision?<br /> <br /> **This isn't to say that reincarnation/&quot;I am the new incarnation of Fenrir***&quot; can't happen, but those souls need to be awakened still.<br /> <br /> ***Oh hush, you hardcore Werewolf fans, there can be multiple Fenrirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-13-2015, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T18:40:06-07:00","id":553606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553597#post553597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's not it. I have hang-ups on that, too, but I feel by and large more positively towards it. And truth be told, I'm okay with the word Horror too, although I reserve a right use it ina different context in the following explanation. No, it has to do with-<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Don't worry, I don't think you come off as an asshole. I am, however, having trouble responding. I agree with everything your saying, my reading of the preview has been very shallow and you've brought up some good points that have made me consider it in a more complex matter. It does feel like it weakens a Beast's claim that their soul isn't their own, it also bothers me that as a character you start out trading a major part of yourself vs awakening to your fuller self like in the original. But again, at this point I'm waiting until I can get my hands on the rest of the changes before I make up my mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, I still say a Brood made of Loki's children (and grandchildren) would be a wicked fun game. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T18:42:41-07:00","id":553607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div 