d to be awakened through the right method. Keeps the social aspects while also allowing the true bonds of Family from the initial version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1965-joebobjoe","name":"joebobjoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:24:48-07:00","id":553649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553634#post553634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not go faultily associating &quot;Bad ST's&quot; with &quot;people who work with the canon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, one of the deal making aspects of NWoD for me was a <i>seeming</i> lack of metanarrative to hold to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:25:01-07:00","id":553650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hammbone87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553622#post553622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im kinda surprised at the levels of anger at the fluff changing...<br /> <br /> I liked the homecoming more than the devouring, that why ill be using the homecoming in my games.<br /> <br /> but this isnt like disappointment, im seeing alot of anger... and THAT is the actuall disappointing part. i must be spoiled with good STs cause not one of us uses the text and &quot;meta-lore&quot; verbatim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not angry, so at least you are not alone. Reminds me of the old saying &quot;He who shouts makes his angry heard; not his words.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:27:45-07:00","id":553652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553643#post553643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite anime of all time, Revolutionary Girl Utena, is Shoujo. A lot of my favorite animes are Shoujo.<br /> <br /> Yer gonna have to explain the embarrassment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Utena rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:28:30-07:00","id":553653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553576#post553576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could have easily been included without horribly derailing the everything about Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I call foul on this.<br /> <br /> Having seen Matt's commentary on Beasts, and in my own experience, I suspect the whole Reading Beasts As Minorities was not only wrong, but actively poisonous to the game.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt about this; pre-Revision Beasts made my skin crawl, and not in the &quot;wow, that's scary&quot; sense, but in the &quot;these people are kind of disgusting&quot; sense. &quot;I have a right to exist&quot; doesn't make good stories, and to be frank? In our game, I deliberately wrote my character to be someone who resolves issues with Heroes as peacefully as he can, because he's ultimately the cause of a rather dark psychosis (paper-thin antagonist deliberately my foot, mental illness doesn't make someone what is effectively an orc). I'm fucking happy the game has gone and be rejiggered, because at least I can play a &quot;Pod Person&quot; (which is unlikely or at least askew, given how the Devouring process is voluntary) without feeling like I'm the goddamned Joker. Supervillains are great and all, but I'd rather be someone with the capacity to be honorable and friendly in his personal life, and has the support structure needed for that.<br /> <br /> Did Matt go a little far? Maybe, the Devouring could be Homecoming and I think he still wants born latent Beasts. Were these changes <i>utterly necessary </i>so I could enjoy the game as a whole, rather than just the rules? <b>Hell. <i>Yes.</i></b><br /> <br /> So yeah, I support the revision. I expect and want it to be refined further, but as a starting point? Thank <i>God, Dark Mother, the Crone, Oracles, Luna, and every other semi-benevolent divine figure </i>he's facing this direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 06-13-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:37:27-07:00","id":553660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553619#post553619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read the revised intro. I'm feeling kind of... uneasy about it. Mostly, I don't like the channges very much; they feel a bit like they fell short of what they aimed for, or perhaps they merely fall shor of my expectations. I was very, very enthusiastic about the first draft, so perhaps, it's just a knee-jerk reation to seein something I liked change.<br /> Still I'll try to explain what bothers me with the revision:<br /> <br /> 1) The Devouring:<br /> -I dislike the fact that Beasts can just ask people to become one of them. I don't feel like iit mesh with the Legendary Monster theme. Dragons, Giants and Tentacled Abominations don't invite people to join the club.<br /> -It now really feels like the Beasts are possessed, or claimed, or whatever, as if the Horror is an alien invader replacing the person the Beast was before, and worse! they do it with the pre-Beast permission. That just feels like a suicide, and for no reason.<br /> -How does it work, really? Why does it need a Beast to have the future Begotten agree to it? What kind of monster wait for permssion before eating?<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits. Most real-world animistic traditions have similar initiation rites, wherein the perspective shaman must allow an entity to take over. That kind of jives with what the Beast's role was in the past, as written in the new fluff, and better encapsulates a latent role for Beasts that in 1e was strictly Mage/Changeling turf: dealing with Dreams.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:37:53-07:00","id":553661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553542#post553542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is where I am right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to say I'm in the same situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:48:15-07:00","id":553664,"title":"","content":"I would like to reserve judgement on the changes until maybe seeing the rational behind them. First impressions are not good for the Devouring though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:50:02-07:00","id":553665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553653#post553653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I call foul on this.<br /> <br /> Having seen Matt's commentary on Beasts, and in my own experience, I suspect the whole Reading Beasts As Minorities was not only wrong, but actively poisonous to the game.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt about this; pre-Revision Beasts made my skin crawl, and not in the &quot;wow, that's scary&quot; sense, but in the &quot;these people are kind of disgusting&quot; sense. &quot;I have a right to exist&quot; doesn't make good stories, and to be frank? In our game, I deliberately wrote my character to be someone who resolves issues with Heroes as peacefully as he can, because he's ultimately the cause of a rather dark psychosis (paper-thin antagonist deliberately my foot, mental illness doesn't make someone what is effectively an orc). I'm fucking happy the game has gone and be rejiggered, because at least I can play a &quot;Pod Person&quot; (which is unlikely or at least askew, given how the Devouring process is voluntary) without feeling like I'm the goddamned Joker. Supervillains are great and all, but I'd rather be someone with the capacity to be honorable and friendly in his personal life, and has the support structure needed for that.<br /> <br /> Did Matt go a little far? Maybe, the Devouring could be Homecoming and I think he still wants born latent Beasts. Were these changes <i>utterly necessary </i>so I could enjoy the game as a whole, rather than just the rules? <b>Hell. <i>Yes.</i></b><br /> <br /> So yeah, I support the revision. I expect and want it to be refined further, but as a starting point? Thank <i>God, Dark Mother, the Crone, Oracles, Luna, and every other semi-benevolent divine figure </i>he's facing this direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of half-owned/half-redirected the entire monstrosity thing with the idea for Gwyneth. My original idea that I still wanted to explore in the final draft was to try and make her signature Hero(a stand-in for Siegfried/Odette) eventually emotionally dependent on her. Of course, I also intended for the Hero to win in the end.<br /> <br /> Anyways, point is good on you for playing someone out to break the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:54:08-07:00","id":553673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553660#post553660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits. Most real-world animistic traditions have similar initiation rites, wherein the perspective shaman must allow an entity to take over. That kind of jives with what the Beast's role was in the past, as written in the new fluff, and better encapsulates a latent role for Beasts that in 1e was strictly Mage/Changeling turf: dealing with Dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but I just do't see it. Shamans commune with spirits true but it's a temporary union. They don't sell their souls as food to Nightmare monsters. Also, spirits usually demand things (sacrifices, offerings, rituals). They don't ask, and they certainly don't wait for approval from people. Except in Exalted, sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:56:55-07:00","id":553675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553649#post553649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, one of the deal making aspects of NWoD for me was a <i>seeming</i> lack of metanarrative to hold to.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a meta-narrative, but there are structures within the framework of each line that carry certain amounts of loads.<br /> <br /> Nothing about the Devouring necessitates that harsh of a change, it handles the load almost as well as Homecoming, and it's an easy shift. It's not like, say, changing Clarity to a Hamonry-esque mechanic coughcoughshouldn'thavegonetherepretendIdidn'tcoug hcough.<br /> <br /> All of that is irrelevant to the elephant. My point is I'm not wild about the idea that in order to be a good ST, you have to deviate from what the books say, particularly since I actually rather like working my way back into what the text posits in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:12:15-07:00","id":553681,"title":"","content":"What I like about the rewrite: Beasts and Heroes have a common origin, both being people who \u201cdream deep\u201d. They differ in terms of how they deal with that: Beasts find a way to accept the Primordial Dream, and set up shop there; Heroes reject the Primordial Dream and develop a talent for destroying it and everything connected to it, including but not limited to Beasts. Heroes are drawn to Beasts not because Beasts somehow created them, but because Beasts bring the Primordial Dream into the waking world. <br /> <br /> This suggests a possibility for a demi-splat: those mortals who \u201cdream deep\u201d but are still on the fence about what to do about it, or who have chosen a third option that lets them retain their human nature without going \u201cmonster slayer\u201d. <br /> <br /> What I'm not quite so fond of: the specific raison d'etre that makes Beasts something more than feeding machines. I like that there <i>is</i> such a thing; but \u201cteachers\u201d feels\u2026 off, somehow. Maybe it's just the presentation? I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-13-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:14:31-07:00","id":553683,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've finally made my way through the new intro. There are still a couple of rough spots I think, but overall I'm pleased. The switch been Homecoming and Devouring does strike me as being jarring, and I do prefer that the Beasts have always been Beasts, rather than being changed into one. Likewise, I find the Soul/Horror shift a it offputting, but I could see that needing to be done for clarity's sake, and with time will get used to it. Beasts definitely have better motivation now, and the relationship with the Heroes is much, much better. <br /> <br /> All in all, I'm okay with everything. I don't think the outcry we've seen is warranted, but to each her/his own, and hey... its the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:16:52-07:00","id":553685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553683#post553683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I'm okay with everything. I don't think the outcry we've seen is warranted, but to each her/his own, and hey... its the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>OH DEAR GOD, I'M ON THE INTERNET IT ALL MAKES SENSE NOW WHEN WAS I DRAGGED BACK HERE MUST ESCAPE HAAAAAAAAAAALP!<br /> <br /> But seriously, internet, why does everything have to warrant a &quot;You're tearing me apart, Lissa!&quot; reaction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:16:52-07:00","id":553686,"title":"","content":"It's funny to see the tide shift. Some that were defending the text before, claiming that you could play good guys or bad guys and that it was fully supported now seem to act as if including a goal to a splat removes the whole Monster aspect from this game.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, I'll be banking some money and pledging for this - something I'd have never done before the intro rework.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">PS: I'd rather keep the Homecoming too.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:21:33-07:00","id":553691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553681#post553681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I like about the rewrite: Beasts and Heroes have a common origin, both being people who \u201cdream deep\u201d. They differ in terms of how they deal with that: Beasts find a way to accept the Primordial Dream, and set up shop there; Heroes reject the Primordial Dream and develop a talent for destroying it and everything connected to it, including but not limited to Beasts. Heroes are drawn to Beasts not because Beasts somehow created them, but because Beasts bring the Primordial Dream into the waking world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this gets me on board with the loss of Homecoming. The dichotomy between Heroes and Beasts is good. What I would suggest though is that the Devouring is less a destruction of the soul and more a merging/birthing to create the new Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:23:45-07:00","id":553693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553681#post553681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm not quite so fond of: the specific raison d'etre that makes Beasts something more than feeding machines. I like that there <i>is</i> such a thing; but \u201cteachers\u201d feels\u2026 off, somehow. Maybe it's just the presentation? I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the teaching angle makes for a better rationale for Kinship Nightmares, feeds nicely into the introduction of Advanced Library, and offers a good cultural explanation for why a Beast might aim to be Gorged rather than Starving while still leaving the folks who hang around low Satiety in roughly the same place they were before in terms of understandability.<br /> <br /> I do confess to a certain mild consternation that Satiety still appears to be pronounced differently than the dictionaries tell me it's supposed to be pronounced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:24:17-07:00","id":553694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553643#post553643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite anime of all time, Revolutionary Girl Utena, is Shoujo. A lot of my favorite animes are Shoujo.<br /> <br /> Yer gonna have to explain the embarrassment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know why, but I expected an attack. Impulsive posting is not the best idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:24:39-07:00","id":553695,"title":"","content":"Devouring vs. Homecoming: I prefer Homecoming. It works much better once Beasts have something to them that a reasonable person might want to be a part of, and especially if the Homecoming is a choice (which is why I like the \u201cHeroes are what happens when a proto-Beast rejects the Primordial Dream\u201d concept).<br /> <br /> Or, put another way: I prefer Homecoming as \u201caccept what you are and become a Beast, or reject what you are and become a Hero.\u201d (Side note: could we maybe rename the Heroes as \u201cSlayers\u201d instead?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-13-2015, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:26:52-07:00","id":553699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553695#post553695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devouring vs. Homecoming: I prefer Homecoming. It works much better once Beasts have something to them that a reasonable person might want to be a part of, and especially if the Homecoming is a choice (which is why I like the \u201cHeroes are what happens when a proto-Beast rejects the Primordial Dream\u201d concept).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a happy medium between the two, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:28:09-07:00","id":553700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553694#post553694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't know why, but I expected an attack. Impulsive posting is not the best idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, most posters here aren't afraid of cooties anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:30:05-07:00","id":553705,"title":"","content":"<b>Possible Beast?</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/a42ffbca3aa787618a809381239327e1/tumblr_mt02viZpIV1qi1wjmo1_r1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:30:17-07:00","id":553706,"title":"","content":"The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are part of the same family of primal nightmares that have haunted humanity forever.<br /> The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are born the way they are, and that the Hunger is a basic need of life. <br /> <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that there is a family of primal fears in the Primordial Dream which Beasts are a part of. <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that imminent Beasts have a family in the form of an older sibling figure who can support them. <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts choose to face their fears head on in order to deal with their problems. <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts can serve an extremely useful function to ordinary people by giving them a chance to face their problems while they dream. <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Heroes choose not to face their fears and instead feed upon the fears of ordinary people and that it's in the Hero's best interest for people not to deal with their problems. <br /> <br /> The Devouring cuts off the inborn nature of Beasts in order to provide extensive support for Beasts' relationship with mortals and for the conflict between Beasts and Heroes, and it still has some room for Beasts' family theme. From a design perspective, it's a huge bargain. <br /> <br /> And really, anyone who thinks teaching through fear isn't an appropriate role for Beasts needs to read up religions. &quot;Get your shit together or else you're going to get genocided&quot; is something of a recurring theme in the Old Testament. <br /> <br /> Hell, you know who else works as a Beast? <i>The Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future</i>. That's right. Anyone who doesn't want Beasts to give people horrifying nightmares to teach them a lesson <i>hates Christmas</i>. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:31:38-07:00","id":553707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553699#post553699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a happy medium between the two, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; I don't think we're quite at that happy medium yet. On the other hand, it is just the Intro. The rest of the re-write can change that.<br /> <br /> Also saw this on the Kickstarter Comments section; posting here because I think it's worth sharing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jason Something</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I hope I can be forgiven for having the idea of 'Devouring v. Homecoming' being an in-universe debate now. Because that feels like a good way to both honour the authors, keep the parts I like and maintain both themes. The question of whether or not you were just Coming Home or were Devoured by another Beast (Big Brother/Sister) is one of the Begotten's own mindset, at least at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:33:02-07:00","id":553709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553705#post553705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Possible Beast?</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/a42ffbca3aa787618a809381239327e1/tumblr_mt02viZpIV1qi1wjmo1_r1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><i>kill it with fire and more fire and lots of pointy sticks and kill it until death then kill it some more.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:33:24-07:00","id":553710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553699#post553699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a happy medium between the two, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would hope.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's a better place to quantify why Beasts and Demons don't like each other, as well as clearing up the moral ambiguity between Pacting and inflicting nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:34:45-07:00","id":553714,"title":"","content":"<b>Dataweaver</b>, in response to the second post before you're last one. (Damn there's posts flying everywhar! O - O' )<br /> <br /> Well, it does sound a bit weird at first. But, it's true though isn't it? Nightmares do teach us valuable lessons about our own subconscious fears and flaws do they not? I feel that this direction helps to enforce the focus that's starting to take shape in the revised material: A Beast is a living nightmare.<br /> <br /> Because let's face it, one of the flaws with the original text is that it truly had little focus on what a Beast actually was and how they relate to eachother. This I feel was in part because of how much freedom we got with choosing what our Horror (and another thing, I know it's nit-picky but doesn't Horror roll of the tongue sooo much better than Soul did?) looked like and how it fed. Giving Beasts as a whole an imperative besides feed is far more thematic and appropriate for a game claiming you get to play an ancient nightmare of legend.<br /> <br /> It does seem like it takes some of the bite out of what made Bests such horrifying monsters, but then again it also creates a subconsious connection with the other two supernatural creatures that the Begotten are most in common with mechanically: Werewolves and Sin-Eaters. Both have imparatives besides the wolf must hunt/party like it's the last night of your life that deal specifically with the link they possess to the supernatural otherworlds that they draw their powers from (being enforce the laws of the Shadow and police the lingering dead respectably.) Each of those gamelines are better for it because they add additional layer on to what those supernatural creatures are, and I feel that this new focus on reminding humanity why they're instincually afraid of the dark is a great way of doing that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Wait for meeeeee.... 06-13-2015, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:35:31-07:00","id":553722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553706#post553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are part of the same family of primal nightmares that have haunted humanity forever.<br /> The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are born the way they are, and that the Hunger is a basic need of life.<br /> <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that there is a family of primal fears in the Primordial Dream which Beasts are a part of.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that imminent Beasts have a family in the form of an older sibling figure who can support them.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts choose to face their fears head on in order to deal with their problems.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts can serve an extremely useful function to ordinary people by giving them a chance to face their problems while they dream.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Heroes choose not to face their fears and instead feed upon the fears of ordinary people and that it's in the Hero's best interest for people not to deal with their problems.<br /> <br /> The Devouring cuts off the inborn nature of Beasts in order to provide extensive support for Beasts' relationship with mortals and for the conflict between Beasts and Heroes, and it still has some room for Beasts' family theme. From a design perspective, it's a huge bargain.<br /> <br /> And really, anyone who thinks teaching through fear isn't an appropriate role for Beasts needs to read up religions. &quot;Get your shit together or else you're going to get genocided&quot; is something of a recurring theme in the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> Hell, you know who else works as a Beast? <i>The Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future</i>. That's right. Anyone who doesn't want Beasts to give people horrifying nightmares to teach them a lesson <i>hates Christmas</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel incredibly disarmed with this. I don't want to hate Christmas.<br /> <br /> Well, more than I already do. Point is, this is really compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:35:32-07:00","id":553723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553705#post553705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Possible Beast?</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/a42ffbca3aa787618a809381239327e1/tumblr_mt02viZpIV1qi1wjmo1_r1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Who is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:37:36-07:00","id":553724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553723#post553723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Griffith from Berserk. He's pretty much the embodiment of the idea that fueled &quot;Heroes are fucking assholes who need to die&quot;. He's...Well, he's a terrible person by the end of the series.<br /> <br /> <i>but seriously murderkill his face until he stops twitching and then kill him with fire thrice</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:37:54-07:00","id":553726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553699#post553699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a happy medium between the two, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>A really good happy medium was posted a few pages back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553533#post553533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I preferred the Homecoming, but also see how a mentor could make a meaningful difference in the education of a new Beast.<br /> I think it would be best if we could have it both ways:<ul><li>Every Beast is destined to have a Homecoming. The ones who have a Teacher tend to integrate into Beast society the easiest.</li> <li>That leaves plenty of narrative room for PC Beasts who have no teacher to be played, while also leaving room for wild and savage NPC Beasts.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:38:18-07:00","id":553727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553706#post553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are part of the same family of primal nightmares that have haunted humanity forever.<br /> The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are born the way they are, and that the Hunger is a basic need of life.<br /> <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that there is a family of primal fears in the Primordial Dream which Beasts are a part of.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that imminent Beasts have a family in the form of an older sibling figure who can support them.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts choose to face their fears head on in order to deal with their problems.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts can serve an extremely useful function to ordinary people by giving them a chance to face their problems while they dream.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Heroes choose not to face their fears and instead feed upon the fears of ordinary people and that it's in the Hero's best interest for people not to deal with their problems.<br /> <br /> The Devouring cuts off the inborn nature of Beasts in order to provide extensive support for Beasts' relationship with mortals and for the conflict between Beasts and Heroes, and it still has some room for Beasts' family theme. From a design perspective, it's a huge bargain.<br /> <br /> And really, anyone who thinks teaching through fear isn't an appropriate role for Beasts needs to read up religions. &quot;Get your shit together or else you're going to get genocided&quot; is something of a recurring theme in the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> Hell, you know who else works as a Beast? <i>The Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future</i>. That's right. Anyone who doesn't want Beasts to give people horrifying nightmares to teach them a lesson <i>hates Christmas</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You have a very compelling argument there.<br /> <br /> Also, LOL, BURN!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:43:59-07:00","id":553731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553724#post553724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Griffith from Berserk. He's pretty much the embodiment of the idea that fueled &quot;Heroes are fucking assholes who need to die&quot;. He's...Well, he's a terrible person by the end of the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also grew up feeling somewhat apart and different from those around him, was subtly guided and later outright taught by older Beasts, then undergoes his Homecoming / Devouring in spectacular / horrific fashion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:50:18-07:00","id":553739,"title":"","content":"I mentioned this before, but thinking of different mythologies, what if the Dark Mother is Gaia?<br /> <br /> In greek mythology, Gaia is the mother of monsters: the hundred handed, the cyclops, the gigantes, and the erinyes, Echidna and Typhoon are her kids, so Echidna's children are her grandchildren. <br /> <br /> In Norse myth, the world was made from Ymir's corpse, and Ymir is the father of the dwarves and jotun.<br /> <br /> In Aztec myth, the gods made the world from Cipactli, an all consuming monster with a mouth at every joint. <br /> <br /> Even in the Tiamat myth, Tiamat while being the chaotic primordial sea is also the mother of Ki, the land, which is appropriate since she's the mother of all creation, so obviously including monsters and the earth. <br /> <br /> And that's just the relevant myths I can remember offhand, the idea that the natural state of the world is a monstrous one seems oddly popular. <br /> <br /> This is the world of darkness, maybe the fact that humans are hardly the top of the food chain is no cosmic accident but a feature, nature is red in tooth and claw and full of nastiness<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:53:19-07:00","id":553742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553739#post553739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mentioned this before, but thinking of different mythologies, what if the Dark Mother is Gaia?<br /> <br /> In greek mythology, Gaia is the mother of monsters: the hundred handed, the cyclops, the gigantes, and the erinyes, Echidna and Typhoon are her kids, so Echidna's children are her grandchildren.<br /> <br /> In Norse myth, the world was made from Ymir's corpse, and Ymir is the father of the dwarves and jotun.<br /> <br /> In Aztec myth, the gods made the world from Cipactli, an all consuming monster with a mouth at every joint.<br /> <br /> Even in the Tiamat myth, Tiamat while being the chaotic primordial sea is also the mother of Ki, the land, which is appropriate since she's the mother of all creation, so obviously including monsters and the earth.<br /> <br /> And that's just the relevant myths I can remember offhand, the idea that the natural state of the world is a monstrous one seems oddly popular.<br /> <br /> This is the world of darkness, maybe the fact that humans are hardly the top of the food chain is no cosmic accident but a feature, nature is red in tooth and claw and full of nastiness<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>THe Primordial Dream borders the Soul of the World and the Collective Soul of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:55:50-07:00","id":553743,"title":"","content":"So here's some dramatic irony for you. Beasts' closest relatives are Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:57:43-07:00","id":553747,"title":"","content":"...I could have sworn I said that <i>ages ago</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:59:11-07:00","id":553766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553706#post553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are part of the same family of primal nightmares that have haunted humanity forever.<br /> The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are born the way they are, and that the Hunger is a basic need of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a big part of what I liked about Beast. It lets characters say &quot;I am a monster, now what am I going to do about that?&quot; There's still plenty of narrative room here for the whole teaching through fear angle. This is the point where the Big Sibling pops up and says &quot;Let me show you a way to fulfill your needs and help the world at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> The difference between the old and the new is being born with a great gift and having to make a choice about how you'll use it vs being inducted into a mystical cult that wants to make the world better through fear and terror. It's changed the entire narrative feel of the game by changing the starting conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:00:37-07:00","id":553779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553743#post553743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's some dramatic irony for you. Beasts' closest relatives are Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like the idea that a Hero that hunts down and murders a Beast risks becoming a Beast himself.<br /> Either because his soul was that of a slumbering Beast all along, drawn into the narrative by the dream...<br /> Or because the terrible deeds that some Heroes use to slay the Beast open them up to being Devoured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:01:38-07:00","id":553782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553766#post553766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was a big part of what I liked about Beast. It lets characters say &quot;I am a monster, now what am I going to do about that?&quot; There's still plenty of narrative room here for the whole teaching through fear angle. This is the point where the Big Sibling pops up and says &quot;Let me show you a way to fulfill your needs and help the world at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> The difference between the old and the new is being born with a great gift and having to make a choice about how you'll use it vs being inducted into a mystical cult that wants to make the world better through fear and terror. It's changed the entire narrative feel of the game by changing the starting conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This. So much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:08:50-07:00","id":553789,"title":"","content":"Could we maybe start calling them Slayers instead of Heroes? The latter is still very descriptive, possibly moreso than \u201chero\u201d, but lacks any moral judgment either way; the former is more vague, and carries the implication that the game has been fighting against, that a Hero is someone to be admired. You can even keep \u201cHeroes\u201d as a secondary term that some of the more sarcastic Beasts use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:13:59-07:00","id":553798,"title":"","content":"I had been watching news about the game for a while waiting for more info, it interested me. Then when the Kickstarter went up and I got a chance to see the initial draft I was elated. This seemed like a game for me. Even a game I could love running for other people. I backed the project as soon as I had the opportunity to. Heck I even started talking to friends about setting up a group to run for them. We had the Kickstarter draft and I was getting the book anyway so why not start soon.<br /> <br /> The idea behind the Homecoming just resonated with me. I liked the fact that A Beast's moment of awaking was in essence accepting a part of themselves. It wasn't thrust on them by an outside source, as it is now with the Devouring. From there a Beast could be a decent person and try to deal with their hungers in the best was possible or they could be a terrible monster reveling in the pain they cause others. It was a choice they made and that a player could explore. They didn't have some driving goal or a supernatural purpose they just needed to survive and it left it to the players to discover what the character wanted to do with their new found revelations.<br /> <br /> Being tied to the Primordial dream and the existence of Heroes implied there was a Narrative power to the Beast's life; something outside their control trying to force meaning on their existence and the game held hints of fighting against this. Part of it was about not allowing something else to take control of your life. This made the Hero all the more terrible for a player. For a player this was a person who had become completely consumed by the power of narrative. A person had lost what they were in favor of a story (even if it was a pleasant lie) because a Beast had either been so unwilling to cause harm that they starved themselves or they were so negligent that they starved from over exertion or showed themselves off to others as the monster the narrative wanted them to be.<br /> <br /> Sure a lot of Beasts turned out to be complete monsters but that makes sense, it's hard not to be what everyone expects you to be. It's easier to follow those expectations after all and the rules kind of express that pretty well.<br /> <br /> Even the cross over stuff seemed good. I saw this as a perfect opportunity to use all my knowledge of the other nWoD games to get some of my friends who don't know much about the setting involved. The fact that the Beasts seemed to be able to interact with the other supernaturals without instantly being put on the s**t list by them made it a unique opportunity to do so without stretching things too far.<br /> <br /> Now we get the new introduction and it seems to put a knife to everything I liked about the old one. Now the Homecoming is gone. It's no longer a person accepting what they are but a person choosing to be something else. You now have a calling, you have a purpose given to you by some outside force. No more searching for meaning for you. Now the nightmares you cause and the victims you make are for a reason! You're teaching them lessons now! Oh and if you kill and main and devolve into sadistic mayhem it's wrong, not for any personally held moral reasons, it's wrong because The Dark Mother doesn't think you are doing your job right.<br /> <br /> Changing the Homecoming to the Devouring changes the tone. It makes it feel like it is no longer a moment of clarity for the character it is instead a moment of loss. It's giving up, it's giving in. The Soul becoming the Horror makes it the outside force and implies it is a bad thing (like the Vampire's Beast). As an outside force that takes it's toll on the character and is something they could have avoided rather than just a part of themselves they must come to terms with.<br /> <br /> Even the purpose given to the Beasts seems unneeded. It was obvious that the \u201cNarrative\u201d I spoke of earlier wanted them to be that warning in the Dark; that source of fear but the previous introduction and text hinted that they could be more than that. The new one clearly states that yes that's what they are supposed to be and that's what you are supposed to play them as. Either \u201cGood\u201d and following that purpose or \u201cBad\u201d and not doing that. It also doesn't help that the stated goal now seems to be what 1<sup>st</sup> Edition Autumn Court in Changeling was all about.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest if I had picked up a book and read the current version of the intro I would have set it down thinking this game had little interest for me. Those friends I have shared the new intro with have expressed similar disinterest with the changes. I can only say that I am happy I got the original preview text from Kickstarter so that we can still use the information from it instead. On the other hand if things continue in the current direction I may very well remove my backing from the Kickstarter I didn't decide to donate to the current vision of the game after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6352-bible","name":"Bible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:14:22-07:00","id":553799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553742#post553742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordial Dream borders the Soul of the World and the Collective Soul of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I ask of thee: Art thou mankind?<br /> <br /> Nay! I am the world \u2014 the world inside the gourd.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:17:25-07:00","id":553821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553739#post553739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mentioned this before, but thinking of different mythologies, what if the Dark Mother is Gaia?<br /> <br /> In greek mythology, Gaia is the mother of monsters: the hundred handed, the cyclops, the gigantes, and the erinyes, Echidna and Typhoon are her kids, so Echidna's children are her grandchildren.<br /> <br /> In Norse myth, the world was made from Ymir's corpse, and Ymir is the father of the dwarves and jotun.<br /> <br /> In Aztec myth, the gods made the world from Cipactli, an all consuming monster with a mouth at every joint.<br /> <br /> Even in the Tiamat myth, Tiamat while being the chaotic primordial sea is also the mother of Ki, the land, which is appropriate since she's the mother of all creation, so obviously including monsters and the earth.<br /> <br /> And that's just the relevant myths I can remember offhand, the idea that the natural state of the world is a monstrous one seems oddly popular.<br /> <br /> This is the world of darkness, maybe the fact that humans are hardly the top of the food chain is no cosmic accident but a feature, nature is red in tooth and claw and full of nastiness<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting interpretation.<br /> <br /> I would not, however, want an OPP book to demonize a deity that several faiths worship to this day. Echidna is already the Mother of Monsters, so I'd draw the parallel there, not with Gaia.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that the World of Darkness has played host to fairly negative depictions of various deities that people venerate at one point or another, but I'd rather avoid it going forward.<br /> <br /> Personal interpretations by Storytellers at a table are, of course, fine and not anybody else's business. I'd just rather it not be an official comparison.<br /> <br /> Just need to be careful to remember that one person's &quot;mythology&quot; is another's faith, particularly with all the reconstructionist faiths cropping up these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:17:37-07:00","id":553823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553789#post553789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we maybe start calling them Slayers instead of Heroes? The latter is still very descriptive, possibly moreso than \u201chero\u201d, but lacks any moral judgment either way; the former is more vague, and carries the implication that the game has been fighting against, that a Hero is someone to be admired. You can even keep \u201cHeroes\u201d as a secondary term that some of the more sarcastic Beasts use.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, no. Just... no.<br /> No way we're also losing the deconstuction of Monster vs Hero aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:17:50-07:00","id":553824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553789#post553789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we maybe start calling them Slayers instead of Heroes? The latter is still very descriptive, possibly moreso than \u201chero\u201d, but lacks any moral judgment either way; the former is more vague, and carries the implication that the game has been fighting against, that a Hero is someone to be admired. You can even keep \u201cHeroes\u201d as a secondary term that some of the more sarcastic Beasts use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the name &quot;Slayers&quot; is already in use for a different splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:20:23-07:00","id":553825,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:20:46-07:00","id":553826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553789#post553789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we maybe start calling them Slayers instead of Heroes? The latter is still very descriptive, possibly moreso than \u201chero\u201d, but lacks any moral judgment either way; the former is more vague, and carries the implication that the game has been fighting against, that a Hero is someone to be admired. You can even keep \u201cHeroes\u201d as a secondary term that some of the more sarcastic Beasts use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehhh...I like keeping them Heroes. I like that there's a value judgment attached. Of course, I only just came around on the Devouring change, so maybe I'm still just trying to hang out to the raw, ragged edges that I liked so much about the original document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:22:47-07:00","id":553828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553821#post553821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An interesting interpretation.<br /> <br /> I would not, however, want an OPP book to demonize a deity that several faiths worship to this day. Echidna is already the Mother of Monsters, so I'd draw the parallel there, not with Gaia.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that the World of Darkness has played host to fairly negative depictions of various deities that people venerate at one point or another, but I'd rather avoid it going forward.<br /> <br /> Personal interpretations by Storytellers at a table are, of course, fine and not anybody else's business. I'd just rather it not be an official comparison.<br /> <br /> Just need to be careful to remember that one person's &quot;mythology&quot; is another's faith, particularly with all the reconstructionist faiths cropping up these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really demonizing Gaia, here. She is indeed one of the Mothers of Monsters from Greek myth, along with, Nyx, Ceto, Echidna, Kampe and perhaps others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:27:16-07:00","id":553845,"title":"","content":"<b>cmwatford</b>,<br /> <br /> I would like to point out that it explicidly mentions that the Horror (the Soul) only cares about being fed. It's the dreamer who inturprets the lessons that underline the Primordial Dream. Even in the example origin it's the Beast who informs the Beat-to-be that they'd have to make a tough choice, giving the impression that it's the Life that seeks to inform the rest of humanity, while the Legend is still virtually unchanged from the original doc in it's single minded desire to feed. A great<br /> analogue for this would be the difference between the Changelings of the Autumn Court and the True Fae from 1E. The Leaden Mirror grows fat on the Glamour generated by fear, but their goal is to warn the humans about the dangers of the world. Even to the point of recreating brutal killings and hollywood slasher tropes in order to rob the Gentry of their majesty and tricks. The True Fae on the other hand will never try to scare away their prey (Unless...well, it looked fun) that would be counter productive. The Others want their victims to come with them to Arcadia, the fact that mortals never learn gives them the means to procure slaves and entertainment so easily.<br /> <br /> However, you do make a great point about how this does change the starting mindset for the game. While I personally feel that this new version tightens the focus the game but it does unquestionably change a lot about that originally made the Children the Children, to the point that even the crossover section will need a massive overhaul in order to correct the changes made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Thought up a good paralell. Kinda get's rambly though 06-14-2015, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:36:17-07:00","id":553851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553799#post553799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I ask of thee: Art thou mankind?<br /> <br /> Nay! I am the world \u2014 the world inside the gourd.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know there was someone else here who had seen that!<br /> <br /> And okay, having cooled down some more I'll give that Tiresias's argument has strength. Still prefer the Homecoming because it presents the Begotten as someone who always was a monster rather than someone who becomes one, and I think that removing that part of the premise and essentially making the Beasts adopted/married severely weakens the theme of finding your true family. I also still don't see why the dreamer has a choice at all when confronted with a Horror.<br /> <br /> I admit there are more interesting things in the introduction now. The importance of the Primordial Dream to mankind as a whole is one. But the details make me feel like the tone of the game has become significantly different, even if that wasn't supposed to happen*. And overall I'm left very conflicted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*It makes me think that if the information and perspectives (some anyways) added with the update had been introduced in a Book Of The Deceived style supplement and presented in a different way, they might have blown me away instead of causing me personal grief*.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">**Curse my first world problems.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:36:35-07:00","id":553852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553706#post553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, you know who else works as a Beast? <i>The Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future</i>. That's right. Anyone who doesn't want Beasts to give people horrifying nightmares to teach them a lesson <i>hates Christmas</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admission time: I hate Christmas, but that's only due to close to two decades in retail at this point. That will kill that holiday for anyone.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah, those three <i>absolutely</i> work at Beasts, I'd say. In fact, since they're ephemeral (I mean, they're ghosts), they could be Beasts that underwent the Retreat. (Pending any revisions, of course.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:43:43-07:00","id":553855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553653#post553653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I call foul on this.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>It should be the prerogrative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /<i>that/</i> should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves <i>/don\u2019t care</i>/.</b> </div> </div> </div>That line.<br /> <br /> That's what my comment was addressed to.<br /> <br /> That was something that could have been added directly to Beasts, as they were.<br /> <br /> It could have been added to Beasts, <i>without</i> completely 180ing them from &quot;Monsters who explore the world of darkness to learn more about themselves and their family&quot; to &quot;Teach Mortals by scaring the fuck out of them incidentally ripping off the Motivation of a CWoD Vampire Subsplat <i>and </i>an NWoD Vampire Subsplat&quot;, <i>Without </i>turning them from &quot;The Reincarnated Primordial Soul of a Legendary Monster&quot; to &quot;Either a Pod Person who had an other pod person con the original person into letting them replacment kill them&quot; or &quot;Geist Ripoff&quot;, <i>Without </i>hanging the name of the Primordial Soul into something as utterly generic and uninspired as &quot;Horror&quot;, <b><i>and WITHOUT </i></b>mandating that Beasts now have to hurt people when they feed.<br /> <br /> since, you know, that was one of the things people were bitching about bEfore, when it was <b>not</b> a mandatory thing<br /> <br /> Oh, and the new Social Structure, with old Beasts Teaching new Beasts? That could have been added just as easily by declaring that part of Kinship is being able to sense when a nearby Beast is about to have his homecoming and thus would not utterly derail a Beasts Origin Story.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously Going from &quot;reincarnated Primordial Monster who realizes what they are after they finally stop running from themselves&quot; to &quot;&quot;Person who got his soul eaten by a Monster, then an other Monster slithered into their body to take their place?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a Protagonist Splat in WoD. That's a god damned Strix!<br /> <br /> And the line, that my original comment was based on, conflicts with the fact that Beasts are now mandated to be awful, awful people now, when they weren't before.<br /> <br /> It's a line that needs to be included. Because people kept missing the implications of it.<br /> <br /> But seriously, adding it did not have to change everything about what a Beast is.<br /> <br /> The Homecoming was better than the Devouring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-14-2015, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:49:20-07:00","id":553860,"title":"","content":"Rater, you had the excuse of &quot;I'm going to rant openly for a bit&quot; acting as a bulwark against censure the first time with the unspoken understanding that further discussion would be more measured.<br /> <br /> <i>Calm your shit and use an argument that isn't raw inflammatory anger with two pips of a point in it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:50:39-07:00","id":553862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553699#post553699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a happy medium between the two, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Homecoming as normal, but add an option to reject what you are and stay 'mortal'&quot; with <i>maybe</i> the cave eat that certain people can screw it up and become a Hero in the process<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:51:51-07:00","id":553864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553855#post553855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That line.<br /> <br /> That's what my comment was addressed to.<br /> <br /> That was something that could have been added directly to Beasts, as they were.<br /> <br /> It could have been added to Beasts, <i>without</i> completely 180ing them from &quot;Monsters who explore the world of darkness to learn more about themselves and their family&quot; to &quot;Teach Mortals by scaring the fuck out of them incidentally ripping off the Motivation of a CWoD Vampire Subsplat <i>and </i>an NWoD Vampire Subsplat&quot;, <i>Without </i>turning them from &quot;The Reincarnated Primordial Soul of a Legendary Monster&quot; to &quot;Either a Pod Person who had an other pod person con the original person into letting them replacment kill them&quot; or &quot;Geist Ripoff&quot;, <i>Without </i>hanging the name of the Primordial Soul into something as utterly generic and uninspired as &quot;Horror&quot;, <b><i>and WITHOUT </i></b>mandating that Beasts now have to hurt people when they feed.<br /> <br /> since, you know, that was one of the things people were bitching about bEfore, when it was <b>not</b> a mandatory thing<br /> <br /> Oh, and the new Social Structure, with old Beasts Teaching new Beasts? That could have been added just as easily by declaring that part of Kinship is being able to sense when a nearby Beast is about to have his homecoming and thus would not utterly derail a Beasts Origin Story.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously Going from &quot;reincarnated Primordial Monster who realizes what they are after they finally stop running from themselves&quot; to &quot;&quot;Person who got his soul eaten by a Monster, then an other Monster slithered into their body to take their place?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a Protagonist Splat in WoD. That's a god damned Strix!<br /> <br /> And the line, that my original comment was based on, conflicts with the fact that Beasts are now mandated to be awful, awful people now, when they weren't before.<br /> <br /> It's a line that needs to be included. Because people kept missing the implications of it.<br /> <br /> But seriously, adding it did not have to change everything about what a Beast is.<br /> <br /> The Homecoming was better than the Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:53:51-07:00","id":553866,"title":"","content":"That was...<br /> <br /> the exact <i>opposite </i>of my reading.<br /> <br /> It was key to the Beast beforehand that the Soul <i>didn't care</i>. In fact, the reason they turned to Sating their Hungers was that the Soul <i>didn't care. </i>In fact, the Soul <i>didn't care </i>so much it turned on the Beast's friends and family because they were the closest, and thus the most easy food sources. It <i>created Heroes </i>because the potential Hero was a food source. What was the real sticking point for me, and a <i>hell </i>of a lot of a different people, was that the Children <i>apparently didn't care either.</i><br /> <br /> In the revision, it's not only made quite clear they <i>do, </i>and feel utterly <i>awful </i>about it, but that their society is based around trying to turn it into <i>something productive.</i><br /> <br /> <i>That's </i>personal horror. <i>That's </i>a protagonist in a horror setting, one who has either discovered he's the unwilling villain of humanity's story or the tragic individual who was forced to make herself thus to save someone very near and dear, depending on future drafts. <i>That </i>is something the average vampire, if they possess <i>any </i>self-awareness at all, will understand. <i>Not a Strix</i>. Strix, after all, don't seek productive things, and in fact actively hate the idea, because it's Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:58:23-07:00","id":553869,"title":"","content":"I like Heroes having a connection to the Primodial Dream. I hate the idea of Heroes just being failed Beasts. I also dislike becoming a Beast being a choice, which greatly devalues the concept of family. <br /> <br /> I honestly do not see how this change, in particular, was needed. All of the other changes I either liked as much or more than what was written before. But the Devouring currently is sitting as something that will be utterly ignored. Which is something I don't really like to do as it can cause mix ups when trying to get games going. <br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying it is a bad concept. It is actually pretty neat. I just feel like it is something that not Beast. Which, honestly, isn't the best way to put it but it's all I got right now. <br /> <br /> Now, obviously this is a hazard of reading material before it is finalized, because I fully aglnowlege that had I not read the text before this revision, I'd be all onboard. But that's how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:58:49-07:00","id":553875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553706#post553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are part of the same family of primal nightmares that have haunted humanity forever.<br /> The Homecoming emphasizes that Beasts are born the way they are, and that the Hunger is a basic need of life.<br /> <br /> The Devouring emphasizes that there is a family of primal fears in the Primordial Dream which Beasts are a part of.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that imminent Beasts have a family in the form of an older sibling figure who can support them.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts choose to face their fears head on in order to deal with their problems.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Beasts can serve an extremely useful function to ordinary people by giving them a chance to face their problems while they dream.<br /> The Devouring emphasizes that Heroes choose not to face their fears and instead feed upon the fears of ordinary people and that it's in the Hero's best interest for people not to deal with their problems.<br /> <br /> The Devouring cuts off the inborn nature of Beasts in order to provide extensive support for Beasts' relationship with mortals and for the conflict between Beasts and Heroes, and it still has some room for Beasts' family theme. From a design perspective, it's a huge bargain.<br /> <br /> And really, anyone who thinks teaching through fear isn't an appropriate role for Beasts needs to read up religions. &quot;Get your shit together or else you're going to get genocided&quot; is something of a recurring theme in the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> Hell, you know who else works as a Beast? <i>The Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future</i>. That's right. Anyone who doesn't want Beasts to give people horrifying nightmares to teach them a lesson <i>hates Christmas</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> I strongly dislike your strawman argument.<br /> <br /> At best, Beasts teaching humans through Fear should be something that some Beasts do, not something that All Beasts are required to do. Especially since Beasts are now required to hurt people when they were not before and that hurts the game by taking a game about gray morality and skewing the protagonist splat far deaper into the black then they were before.<br /> <br /> I'd even go as far as to say that it's now a game about one group of evil duchebags who hurt innocent people but think they're in the right fighting an other group that is exactly the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:59:22-07:00","id":553876,"title":"","content":"I'd like to start by saying I'm fairly new to the nWoD setting. I've read up a bit about Changeling the Lost, but that's more or less the limit of my knowledge of the setting. A friend of mine who knows a great deal more about the setting showed me the original introduction to beast and I was quite excited. After reading through the Homecoming and the various types of families and hungers I thought &quot;Here's a chance for me to explore the setting as someone just coming in to it, both in and out of character.&quot;<br /> <br /> With the Homecoming it seemed, to me at least, that the beasts as a whole didn't have an over-arching goal other than survival. As far as I was concerned that was great, it meant a group of players could have much more diverse goals working within the same brood. Some of the players may want to use their new found powers for personal gain, others may want to actually do some good with them, and others still might just try to survive while doing as little harm as possible, and all of these goals would be equally valid.<br /> <br /> Now the Homecoming has been changed to the Devouring, and I feel that freedom of choice has been largely limited. Rather than coming in to your own as a beast and figuring out who you are, and what you want to do with the power, it seems more like you've been given a night job. I'll grant there's still room for choice when it comes to what type of beast you want to be, and what sort of methods you're going to use, but if you're playing by the rules the Horror has set for you, everyone is going to have the same end goal aren't they? Now rather than my character deciding what it means to be a beast and choosing their own path, they just decide whether to do a good job or not.<br /> <br /> I know that previously some of the other people interested in this setting had been complaining that the heroes seemed too one dimensional, but I'm not sure that it's wrong if that's the case. It seems proper to me that for a story told from the Beasts perspective the hero comes about because of the beast. This isn't the Hero's story after all, history is generally written by the victors, and we have plenty of examples of the Hero's stories.<br /> <br /> As it stands at present I'm no longer certain if the game is something I'll want to back, as the direction of the game seems to have changed fairly dramatically with the addition of a goal given to all Beasts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6443-roryunin","name":"Roryunin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:01:08-07:00","id":553877,"title":"","content":"Umm, to be fair Rater, what I said there was already present in the book as shown in the kickstarter preview before we got into the new development pass. Sure we didn't have the whole terror as a lesson/forewarning for betterment thing then, but Beasts already had to balance their Hunger and their true self as monsters with their human identity.<br /> <br /> It's dangerous to take that comment out of context; I said that specifically because the updated intro seemed to tell me (especially with the implications of the Devouring) that the Horrors of the Primordial Dream cared for the message of their predations and the bestowing of wisdom through fear (as opposed to something that is simply carried by their existence intrinsically), while <i>also</i> saying they only lived for Hunger and it was the Beast's (the dreamer who understands the truth and accepts it) duty to manage it.<br /> <br /> Also, you really don't need to be blowing up like this. To reiterate, cool it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-14-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:04:46-07:00","id":553879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553828#post553828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really demonizing Gaia, here. She is indeed one of the Mothers of Monsters from Greek myth, along with, Nyx, Ceto, Echidna, Kampe and perhaps others.</div> </div> </div> </div> According to a quick wikipedia search, monsters born by Gaia: The Three cyclopes, the three hecatonchires, the entire gigantes race, the three furies/erinyes, Antaeus, Charybdis, the laistrygonians, Typhon, Echidna, Campe, and the Python. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, I'd agree, it's hardly unfair to portray someone as a mother of monsters when they've done it 17 times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:11:08-07:00","id":553887,"title":"","content":"Before:<ul><li>Many things were unclear, vague, left to interpretation. Many liked that because it created a game of discovery and personal discovery about what it meant to be a monster</li> <li>This created discomfort in many because of the lack of social structure or goals, which people from the point above stated was not an issue: you just had to create your own goals, and being evil is not an obligation!</li> </ul>Now:<ul><li>Things are clearer. There's a social structure, a link between the various supers in town, a basic goal to the Beasts</li> <li>People complain that they now cannot explore the same things as before</li> </ul><br /> Tables have turned, as I said a few posts back. The game now gives you basic directions, but it's up to you to follow them or not. Same argument I was given for a week about the Hungers from 1st draft &quot;You don't have to be evil, you know!&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, with the second draft: You don't have to be good, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:12:13-07:00","id":553890,"title":"","content":"Gaea is specifically called out as a facet of the Dark Mother on the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:16:42-07:00","id":553894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553877#post553877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's dangerous to take that comment out of context; I said that specifically because the updated intro seemed to tell me (especially with the implications of the Devouring) that the Horrors of the Primordial Dream cared for the message of their predations and the bestowing of wisdom through fear (as opposed to something that is simply carried by their existence intrinsically), while <i>also</i> saying they only lived for Hunger and it was the Beast's (the dreamer who understands the truth and accepts it) duty to manage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, we've got a fairly established body of work in the existing gamelines telling us that &quot;your soul has replaced by someone/something else's&quot; doesn't have much in the way of overt impact on your personality at the start.<br /> <br /> I also feel like a character concept that I had thought was kind of against the grain is less of an immediate concern now \u2014 before, the Dark Mother's &quot;gifts&quot; made semirandom people need to terrify their neighbors to live and the main outroads were chiefly creative forms of ego-death despite the dev's avowed disagreement with &quot;the only moral thing to do as a monster is die&quot; as a takeaway; it seems unlikely that some Begotten wouldn't be more motivated to find Mother Dearest to ask her <i>what the hell</i>.<br /> <br /> The Devouring offers a framework where the grind of spreading nightmares is something you opted into and Echidna can be reasonably portrayed as an archetypal personage who saw a point of interface between humanity and the many terrors of the outside world and turned it into a tool of instruction \u2014 it lends weight to the &quot;Hecate as the First Beast&quot; theory where before the Dark Mother was pretty much just a sentimental name for entropy with the occasional bit of bizarre cryptozoology on top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:19:15-07:00","id":553899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553875#post553875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> I strongly dislike your strawman argument.<br /> <br /> At best, Beasts teaching humans through Fear should be something that some Beasts do, not something that All Beasts are required to do. Especially since Beasts are now required to hurt people when they were not before and that hurts the game by taking a game about gray morality and skewing the protagonist splat far deaper into the black then they were before.<br /> <br /> I'd even go as far as to say that it's now a game about one group of evil duchebags who hurt innocent people but think they're in the right fighting an other group that is exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um Rater they still aren't required to hurt anyone. You teach a lesson how you teach that lesson is up to you and hell from what I gathered it seems like the message Beasts are supposed to teach is at its core, &quot;The world can be dangerous, scary, and you should be careful what you do lest it destroy you.&quot; Granted some some hungers are still harder not to be a douchebag with than others, but it was always going to be a bit of trick not coming off as kind of a jerk when you have the goal of reminding someone that they are prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:20:10-07:00","id":553900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553866#post553866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was...<br /> <br /> the exact <i>opposite </i>of my reading.<br /> <br /> It was key to the Beast beforehand that the Soul <i>didn't care</i>. In fact, the reason they turned to Sating their Hungers was that the Soul <i>didn't care. </i>In fact, the Soul <i>didn't care </i>so much it turned on the Beast's friends and family because they were the closest, and thus the most easy food sources. It <i>created Heroes </i>because the potential Hero was a food source. What was the real sticking point for me, and a <i>hell </i>of a lot of a different people, was that the Children <i>apparently didn't care either.</i><br /> <br /> In the revision, it's not only made quite clear they <i>do, </i>and feel utterly <i>awful </i>about it, but that their society is based around trying to turn it into <i>something productive.</i><br /> <br /> <i>That's </i>personal horror. <i>That's </i>a protagonist in a horror setting, one who has either discovered he's the unwilling villain of humanity's story or the tragic individual who was forced to make herself thus to save someone very near and dear, depending on future drafts. <i>That </i>is something the average vampire, if they possess <i>any </i>self-awareness at all, will understand. <i>Not a Strix</i>. Strix, after all, don't seek productive things, and in fact actively hate the idea, because it's Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first Draft, the Soul was an unthinking thing of instinct and hunger inflicted on the Beast. It was in its nature to feed and rampage, and not something the Beast chose to have it do. The harm the soul did was a consequence of the Beast's nature, not a deliberate agression.<br /> <br /> The Horror, now? The Beast chooses to accept it. The Beast chooses to align with its goal. There is no reason for reluctance or unwillingness, here. No real moral dilemma. The Beast chooses to inflict horror and terror or people to force her nightmarish lessons on them.<br /> <br /> That's what I see with the revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:20:47-07:00","id":553901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553866#post553866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was...<br /> <br /> the exact <i>opposite </i>of my reading.<br /> <br /> It was key to the Beast beforehand that the Soul <i>didn't care</i>. In fact, the reason they turned to Sating their Hungers was that the Soul <i>didn't care. </i>In fact, the Soul <i>didn't care </i>so much it turned on the Beast's friends and family because they were the closest, and thus the most easy food sources. It <i>created Heroes </i>because the potential Hero was a food source. What was the real sticking point for me, and a <i>hell </i>of a lot of a different people, was that the Children <i>apparently didn't care either.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It should be the prerogrative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves <b>/don\u2019t care/. [</b></span></span></span>/QUOTE]<br /> The &quot;Soul&quot; quite explicitly still doen'st care.<br /> <br /> And the children did care before, unless you completly ignored the comments that stated that they still had a human conscience and that many of them disliked being what they are.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the revision, it's not only made quite clear they <i>do, </i>and feel utterly <i>awful </i>about it, but that their society is based around trying to turn it into <i>something productive.</i> </div> </div> </div>And ther ewer plenty of examples of Beasts trying to be productive with their feeding in the orignal eddition.<br /> <br /> Like, say the Nemeisis Defence Atourny or the Tyrant Health Inspecter given right from the hunger sectin in the first chapter.<br /> <br /> Beasts Pre revision were only Unrepenetant Monsters who ddin' care&quot; if you selectivly ignored everything that said they werren't.<br /> <br /> Really, the fack that Beasts are now mandated to hurt people, when before they were not, in fact, required to hurt people to feed, means they're already morally worse than before<br /> <br /> &quot;Always hurts people&quot; is always worse than &quot;does not always have to hurt people&quot; especially when you consider that there are still going to be Beasts who don't care and hurt people becuase they don't give a shit.<br /> <br /> The entire cdhange in motivation is pointless. All it does is change it so now, if a Beast tries to make their hunger positivly productive in antyway that isn't &quot;Be the monster in the cautionary Tale&quot; They are now doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> and really, mandating you play a role in a story in a game about subverting, inverting, and deconstructing a story? Step backwards.<br /> <i>That's </i>personal horror. <i>That's </i>a protagonist in a horror setting, one who has either discovered he's the unwilling villain of humanity's story or the tragic individual who was forced to make herself thus to save someone very near and dear, depending on future drafts. <i>That </i>is something the average vampire, if they possess <i>any </i>self-awareness at all, will understand. <i>Not a Strix</i>. Strix, after all, don't seek productive things, and in fact actively hate the idea, because it's Humanity. </div> </div> </div>1: Yeah, um. A Beast agreed to become a Beast in the revision. That by default means that they chose to be something that hurts people.<br /> <br /> 2: The Strix Comment was more about the &quot;Inhuman Monster that Jacks Bodies&quot; part than the &quot;shoehorn in a cautionary tale&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:25:43-07:00","id":553903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553899#post553899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um Rater they still aren't required to hurt anyone. You teach a lesson how you teach that lesson is up to you and hell from what I gathered it seems like the message Beasts are supposed to teach is at its core, &quot;The world can be dangerous, scary, and you should be careful what you do lest it destroy you.&quot; Granted some some hungers are still harder not to be a douchebag with than others, but it was always going to be a bit of trick not coming off as kind of a jerk when you have the goal of reminding someone that they are prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>You teach a lesson by being the monster from a cautionary table.<br /> <br /> This by default requires you to cause problems for otherwise innocent people, when before a Beast could easily feed themselves by only hurting jackasses who deserve it or by not hurting anybody at all.<br /> <br /> Being the villain ina cautionary story tends to, um, require you to hurt people.<br /> <br /> So everything people complained about being mandatory when it wasn't is now mandatory for real.<br /> <br /> Where are the people complaining about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:30:41-07:00","id":553907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553900#post553900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the first Draft, the Soul was an unthinking thing of instinct and hunger inflicted on the Beast. It was in its nature to feed and rampage, and not something the Beast chose to have it do. The harm the soul did was a consequence of the Beast's nature, not a deliberate agression.<br /> <br /> The Horror, now? The Beast chooses to accept it. The Beast chooses to align with its goal. There is no reason for reluctance or unwillingness, here. No real moral dilemma. The Beast chooses to inflict horror and terror or people to force her nightmarish lessons on them.<br /> <br /> That's what I see with the revision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> It's gone from a game where &quot;some of the assholes trying to murder you might have a point, since you are a monster and many of your kind do hurt people without a care&quot; to &quot;One group of jackasses who thinks they're doing the greater good while they hurt everyone around them fights another group that's almost exactly like them-except one is called out as the arbitrary good guys because their name is on the book&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:30:49-07:00","id":553908,"title":"","content":"I'm responding to both of you:<br /> <br /> 1) We don't know if this is the final draft yet, and it was cranked out in under a week, so I suspect greater nuance is in store. It happened already, after all.<br /> <br /> 2) ...And yet somehow this invalidates sympathy? There's such a thing as a devil's deal that was the only reasonable solution to a problem. It could also mean the potential Child didn't know what he or she was getting into, or that she or he decided the nightmares were a good thing for them, so it must be a good thing for others, or it was a genuinely better way than remaining as they were as humans, or...<br /> <br /> Really, this shows just how toxic the pre-revision was, if you're calling them evil now because there's an element of choice. In other words, the only justification for their monstrousness and desire to feed on fear was the fact they didn't have a choice. That's not something a lot of players can stomach, particularly if there isn't a tone of ambivalence throughout the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:33:38-07:00","id":553911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553903#post553903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You teach a lesson by being the monster from a cautionary table.<br /> <br /> This by default requires you to cause problems for otherwise innocent people, when before a Beast could easily feed themselves by only hurting jackasses who deserve it or by not hurting anybody at all.<br /> <br /> Being the villain ina cautionary story tends to, um, require you to hurt people.<br /> <br /> So everything people complained about being mandatory when it wasn't is now mandatory for real.<br /> <br /> Where are the people complaining about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to the clip from <i>Hot Fuzz</i> posted earlier, I decided that I really don't like the whole purpose angle either, and it makes me think more of pre-Revision Heroes: a bunch of terrible people doing terrible things and then justifying it to themselves by saying &quot;It's for the greater good.&quot; Sure, they might mean it now, but I think it makes Beasts look weaker and more deluded than they were.<br /> <br /> They were supposed to be big on self-awareness, and I loved the &quot;I reject the narrative that says I don't get to live&quot; element. I know some people say that it doesn't give them much to work with as a game, but nuts to that. &quot;Scare people for their own good,&quot; is awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:37:37-07:00","id":553913,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> We calling them Evil because in a situation between &quot;Born a monster, can carfully manage their feeding and might not even have to hurt people if they're careful&quot; to &quot;Chose to be a monster, must hurt people, and chose to do so in order to force your views of morality on people&quot; the second is objectivly more evil than the first.<br /> <br /> Beasts were justified before by the fact that they did not choose what they were, and many of them chose to try and make their predations productive in their won way, or at least prey in sauch a way as to minimize the harm they were forced to cause.<br /> <br /> Now, they deliberately chose to be something that is mandated to hurt people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:40:04-07:00","id":553915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553908#post553908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm responding to both of you:<br /> <br /> 1) We don't know if this is the final draft yet, and it was cranked out in under a week, so I suspect greater nuance is in store. It happened already, after all.<br /> <br /> 2) ...And yet somehow this invalidates sympathy? There's such a thing as a devil's deal that was the only reasonable solution to a problem. It could also mean the potential Child didn't know what he or she was getting into, or that she or he decided the nightmares were a good thing for them, so it must be a good thing for others, or it was a genuinely better way than remaining as they were as humans, or...<br /> <br /> Really, this shows just how toxic the pre-revision was, if you're calling them evil now because there's an element of choice. In other words, the only justification for their monstrousness and desire to feed on fear was the fact they didn't have a choice. That's not something a lot of players can stomach, particularly if there isn't a tone of ambivalence throughout the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I don't follow your logic. I'm really trying, but I'm beginning to think we're not talking about the same thing.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that you think someone who choses to use terror to make people think or act the way she think they should, is on the same level morally as someone who unintentionally inflict nightmares on people?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:41:24-07:00","id":553916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553903#post553903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You teach a lesson by being the monster from a cautionary table.<br /> <br /> This by default requires you to cause problems for otherwise innocent people, when before a Beast could easily feed themselves by only hurting jackasses who deserve it or by not hurting anybody at all.<br /> <br /> Being the villain ina cautionary story tends to, um, require you to hurt people.<br /> <br /> So everything people complained about being mandatory when it wasn't is now mandatory for real.<br /> <br /> Where are the people complaining about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the entire branch of cautionary tales that deal with why someone shouldn't commit evil just slipped by you? A cautionary tale doesn't mean be dick to people for no reason it means people do something that they shouldn't are given a reminder that they shouldn't do it. No it doesn't require you to be evil, yeah that happens, but it is not required now chill out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:42:18-07:00","id":553922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553911#post553911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks to the clip from <i>Hot Fuzz</i> posted earlier, I decided that I really don't like the whole purpose angle either, and it makes me think more of pre-Revision Heroes: a bunch of terrible people doing terrible things and then justifying it to themselves by saying &quot;It's for the greater good.&quot; Sure, they might mean it now, but I think it makes Beasts look weaker and more deluded than they were.<br /> <br /> They were supposed to be big on self-awareness, and I loved the &quot;I reject the narrative that says I don't get to live&quot; element. I know some people say that it doesn't give them much to work with as a game, but nuts to that. &quot;Scare people for their own good,&quot; is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you prefer &quot;scare people for no good reason other than the fact I need to eat&quot;?<br /> <br /> You're drawing kind of a false equivalency here, new Beasts scare people because they need to, so might as well scare for a purpose. They know damn well that's what they're doing, and from that flows the implication that they wrestle with the question of what is the &quot;greater good&quot; to begin with. Also, scaring does not necessarily involve, oh, what was it...<i>murder</i>.<br /> <br /> In fact, here's an idea for the Theme section to any reading Beast author: The Nature of Morality and Social Norms, both their flaws and strengths, and deciding what to keep and what to rend.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:43:43-07:00","id":553932,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">That line, what wit The Beasts being motivated to force their morality on people, comes off as being very hypocritical.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">I think the next revision should be to take the Heroes from this revision, and the social structure for the Beasts(older Beasts teaching new Beasts) and then throw out literally everything else ad go back the last draft.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">The quoted line makes more sense in the context of beasts who have something forced on them and then choose to be positive and productive than on somebody who chose to be a monster so that he can force his morality on people.<br /> <br /> Especially because in both cases, you're going to have Beasts who decided &quot;fuck it, I'm a monster. Let's have fun&quot; and not give two sits about the people they hurt.<br /> <br /> In the first draft, they were kind of jackasses by Beast standards. In this, those folks would just be being honest with themselves</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:49:11-07:00","id":553941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553922#post553922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you prefer &quot;scare people for no good reason other than the fact I need to eat&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I would definitely prefer &quot;Must scare people because I need to eat, but am not mandated to hurt them and can turn it to genuinely positive ends&quot; to &quot;Since I have to hurt people to eat, I might as well force my arbitrary standards of morality on people and then do nothing else positive or productive&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially since the first person is making the best of a bad situation while the second guy chose what he is now.<br /> <br /> Scare/Hurt People for no good reason&quot; is going to be in the game no matter what.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd rather the game where he's the asshole who doen'st care who he hurts to the game where the only difference between him and the &quot;goodguys&quot; is that he's honest with himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:51:02-07:00","id":553943,"title":"","content":"I really take the &quot;teaching people by inflicting fear&quot; to be in large part a cultural rationalization around their actual need to feed. They're drivent to turn what they do in the world by their very nature into something positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:54:48-07:00","id":553946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553941#post553941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> I would definitely prefer &quot;Must scare people because I need to eat, but am not mandated to hurt them and can turn it to genuinely positive ends&quot; to &quot;Since I have to hurt people to eat, I might as well force my arbitrary standards of morality on people and then do nothing else positive or productive&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to explain where &quot;Stay away from the pond in the park between midnight and dawn, because a monster lives there and it eats people&quot; is a matter of morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:56:53-07:00","id":553948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553916#post553916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the entire branch of cautionary tales that deal with why someone shouldn't commit evil just slipped by you? A cautionary tale doesn't mean be dick to people for no reason it means people do something that they shouldn't are given a reminder that they shouldn't do it. No it doesn't require you to be evil, yeah that happens, but it is not required now chill out.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It did not.<br /> <br /> But not every Beast is going to be sustained on those tales, and really, a lot of those are rather extreme(children dieing for not listening to their parents. Children dying <i>because </i>they listened to their parents. Being maimed or killed for petty theft&quot; That's the sort of thing Beasts have to be now.<br /> <br /> And again, I'd say that deliberately choosing to be something that has to hurt people, regardless of your reasoning, is significantly less moral than the one who had it forced on them and can then choose how they want to manage their hunger and mitigate the harm they cause.<br /> <br /> We have people whose only option for mitigating harm is &quot;force my morals on other people, causing them harm in the likelihood&quot;<br /> <br /> And we have people whose options for mitigating harm is &quot;whatever they want to do to mitigate harm, up to an including not actually casudiing any harm at all as well as doing genuine good&quot;<br /> <br /> which is better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:00:27-07:00","id":553951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553946#post553946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to explain where &quot;Stay away from the pond in the park between midnight and dawn, because a monster lives there and it eats people&quot; is a matter of morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, I'm talking about the other kind of cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> But it does become about the<i> Beasts</i> morality,Because the monster in the pond is a human being who chose to become a monster and is sitting in the pond between midnight and dawn specifically to eat the people who show up.<br /> <br /> Since, you know, the Beast is taking the place of the Monster in the cautionary tale, that's the role they have to take.<br /> <br /> He's kind of the bad guy in this kind of story.<br /> <br /> Yet by the Beast revision he's now, in fact, the default protagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:01:57-07:00","id":553952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553903#post553903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You teach a lesson by being the monster from a cautionary table.<br /> <br /> This by default requires you to cause problems for otherwise innocent people, when before a Beast could easily feed themselves by only hurting jackasses who deserve it or by not hurting anybody at all.<br /> <br /> Being the villain ina cautionary story tends to, um, require you to hurt people.<br /> <br /> So everything people complained about being mandatory when it wasn't is now mandatory for real.<br /> <br /> Where are the people complaining about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can accomplish that by either pulling a Yuuko, and brokering more Faustian arrangements, or being a Lil' Slugger, and taking a more hands on approach. And who says you have to be a villain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:03:05-07:00","id":553954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553946#post553946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to explain where &quot;Stay away from the pond in the park between midnight and dawn, because a monster lives there and it eats people&quot; is a matter of morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess? &quot;a monster <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">lives there and it eats people&quot; doesn't sounds like a good indication on the monster's good moral standing.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:03:24-07:00","id":553955,"title":"","content":"While I'll agree that the version of Beast presented in the new version of intro has its rough spots, I like it <i>much</i> better than the original.<br /> <br /> In particular,<br /> - the awkward attempt at presenting Beasts as outsiders despite being best buddies with other supernaturals is gone,<br /> - the implicit sense of superiority to other supernaturals is gone (and seems to be replaced by a more pleasantly crossover-play-enabling &quot;student of other supernaturals&quot; theme), and<br /> - the whole &quot;dream imposed on the real world&quot; thing as a theme played through with both Beasts and Heroes removes the worst of the thematic conflicts inherent in &quot;you are a primordial monster yet are totally human physically by default&quot;, and<br /> - Beasts feel much more like actual characters by default instead of petty assholes and/or edgelord strawman revenge fantasy placeholders.<br /> <br /> Also, there have been a number of complaints about the way Devouring is presented in the new draft.<br /> <br /> Here's a thought:<br /> <br /> <b>What if it was reversed?</b> What if it wasn't the monster Devouring you, but instead you Devouring the monster?<br /> <br /> Of course, this would probably be quite a dangerous process, liable to kill or drive utterly mad someone who isn't properly prepared. It would make being a Beast feel less like &quot;joining a club&quot; and more like a mystical initiation of the kind historically practiced in the real world, or like the initiation rites of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maw\u00e9_people\" target=\"_blank\">Maw\u00e9 people</a>, where a boy ready to become a man sticks his hand into hundreds of (incredibly painful) live bullet ants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553941#post553941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> I would defintly prefer &quot;Must scare people becuase I need to eat, but am not mandated to hurt them and can trun it to genuinly potivive ends&quot; to &quot;Since I have to hurt people to eat, I might as well force my arbitrary standards of morality on people and then do nothing else positive or pruductive&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially since the dfirst person is making the best of a bad situation while the second guy chose what he is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. Having that kind of self-conflict as a default element, instead of the sort of smug self-satisfied inhumanity of the first version, makes this version's Beasts much more compelling as characters dealing with horrific things on a personal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","user":"Roadie","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:04:40-07:00","id":553957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553954#post553954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess? &quot;a monster <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">lives there and it eats people&quot; doesn't sounds like a good indication on the monster's good moral standing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Rampant and the stranger anthropophages of the World of Darkness tend not to be, yes. You'll recall that claiming custodianship of particular terrifying real estate was already an established thing the Begotten do.<br /> <br /> You and Rater seem to have forgotten that the entire basis of Kinship Nightmares is &quot;find another Scary Thing and distill What Makes It Scary into a power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember the night nurse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:04:43-07:00","id":553958,"title":"","content":"Something totally totally unrelated though,<br /> but I think some of the advanced and epic merits should have requirements of 'supernatural' instead of 'beast.'<br /> <br /> I mean, I see no thematic reason for a mage not to be able to have Epic Potential, a demon or a vampire not to be able to have Advanced Striking looks, a werewolf or a slasher not to be able to have advanced killer instincts.<br /> <br /> Why only beasts though?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I think things like Advanced Safe Place (this one only for Beasts) related to Lair could be really really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:07:44-07:00","id":553959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553952#post553952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you can accomplish that by either pulling a Yuuko, and brokering more Faustian arrangements, or being a Lil' Slugger, and taking a more hands on approach. And who says you have to be a villain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explain those terms please.<br /> <br /> I on't really see how making &quot;Faustian Bargains&quot; makes you the good guy.<br /> <br /> and by default the monster ina cautionary tale is the villain.<br /> <br /> Really, going from &quot;you can mitigate the damage you are required to inflict in any manner you can think of and maybe even not cause harm at all&quot; to &quot;you must mitigate your harm in this specific way that we tell you and made the whole game about&quot; is a bad move in general, even when the manner chosen of avoiding harm is in itself not immoral.<br /> <br /> The fact that in this case, it is, and worse, the person chose to be that way?<br /> <br /> Really, if I wanted to play that kind of character, I'd play a Slasher-Avenger or Legend, Maybe Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:11:06-07:00","id":553961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553957#post553957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You and Rater seem to have forgotten that the entire basis of Kinship Nightmares is &quot;find another Scary Thing and distill What Makes It Scary into a power.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't forgotten about anything. I hardly see how &quot;learn how a monster is scary in order to create a psychic attack based on it&quot; has anything to do with &quot;either be the monster in the lack that eats people or be the kind of asshole who terrorizes people in order to force their sense of morality on said people.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:13:20-07:00","id":553963,"title":"","content":"I'm really loving the changes to the Introduction of &quot;Beast&quot; It's actually a game I've become excited for and want. Having a quote from &quot;Preacher&quot; as part of the introduction really helps sell it too.<br /> <br /> The whole change in the dynamic between Heroes and Beasts is awesome and provides an excellent oppertunity for nuanced stories rather than the simple &quot;Evil vs Evil&quot; that Heroes and Beasts represented before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:16:36-07:00","id":553968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553961#post553961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't forgotten about anything. I hardly see how &quot;learn how a monster is scary in order to create a psychic attack based on it&quot; has anything to do with &quot;either be the monster in the lack that eats people or be the kind of asshole who terrorizes people in order to force their sense of morality on said people.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The monster in the pond after dark is not you. The monster in the pond after dark is a preexisting phenomenon that you can distill the terror of into a big flashing sign that tells people to <i>stay away from the pond after dark because there is a monster in there.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:17:45-07:00","id":553971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553963#post553963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really loving the changes to the Introduction of &quot;Beast&quot; It's actually a game I've become excited for and want. Having a quote from &quot;Preacher&quot; as part of the introduction really helps sell it too.<br /> <br /> The whole change in the dynamic between Heroes and Beasts is awesome and provides an excellent opportunity for nuanced stories rather than the simple &quot;Evil vs Evil&quot; that Heroes and Beasts represented before.</div> </div> </div> </div>IT wasn't evil Vs. Evil before.<br /> <br /> It was &quot;Light Gray Vs. Dark Gray to Evil while other Evil got off scot free.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:23:20-07:00","id":553973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553968#post553968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The monster in the pond after dark is not you. The monster in the pond after dark is a preexisting phenomenon that you can distill the terror of into a big flashing sign that tells people to <i>stay away from the pond after dark because there is a monster in there.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not a viable feeding pattern for a Cautionary Beast. Or any Beast.<br /> <br /> That's a Scarecrow Minister's job.<br /> <br /> eventually, people are gonna stop going to the pond on their own, and leaching off another monster's play pin isn't gonna give you much, unless &quot;Family Dinner&quot; is still in play, in which case it's in your best interest to let ti keep eating people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:24:53-07:00","id":553974,"title":"","content":"Guys, seriously?<br /> <br /> Calm yer ruddy selves down.<br /> <br /> In regards to the change, regardless of opinion, let's keep in mind that Matt had to kill some darlings and work through the block that probably came with the comment shock to produce this revision. Let's keep in mind the work the entire team has done in writing this and responding to it, and have a mind open and ready to search for positives as much as negatives.<br /> <br /> There are things I like about the first draft. There are things I like about the second draft. Cool yer shit and make this a goodplace to talk about what we like in order to make an excellent game and an excellent community.<br /> <br /> Please and thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:31:26-07:00","id":553979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553957#post553957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rampant and the stranger anthropophages of the World of Darkness tend not to be, yes. You'll recall that claiming custodianship of particular terrifying real estate was already an established thing the Begotten do.<br /> <br /> You and Rater seem to have forgotten that the entire basis of Kinship Nightmares is &quot;find another Scary Thing and distill What Makes It Scary into a power.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about a Beast using Kinship to benefit from another monster's kills? <br /> It doesn't change anything anyway. The issue is with the nature of Beasts not their actions. Beasts from the 1st Draft and the revision can both be evil monstrosities. The problem is that those from the revision get a hell of a headstart in that direction. <br /> They have the same tools, but neither the same origins nor the same purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:32:49-07:00","id":553981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553959#post553959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain those terms please.<br /> <br /> I on't really see how making &quot;Faustian Bargains&quot; makes you the good guy.<br /> <br /> and by default the monster ina cautionary tale is the villain.<br /> <br /> Really, going from &quot;you can mitigate the damage you are required to inflict in any manner you can think of and maybe even not cause harm at all&quot; to &quot;you must mitigate your harm in this specific way that we tell you and made the whole game about&quot; is a bad move in general, even when the manner chosen of avoiding harm is in itself not immoral.<br /> <br /> The fact that in this case, it is, and worse, the person chose to be that way?<br /> <br /> Really, if I wanted to play that kind of character, I'd play a Slasher-Avenger or Legend, Maybe Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuuko solves other people's problems by mediating the metaphysical influences that cause them; Lil' Slugger does so by triggering Karmic realignment, generally by causing accidents or removing bad people.<br /> <br /> Only if the person being taught is innocent, or rather, undeserving.<br /> <br /> And now you are delving into the same slippery slope the critics were not 10 hours ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:36:12-07:00","id":553984,"title":"","content":"Things I liked about revision:<br /> <br /> This line&quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.</span></span>&quot; since it's a thing that was present in the first draft that a lot of people overlooked.<br /> <br /> The Social Structure that encourages Older Beasts to help out younger beasts and educate him.<br /> <br /> Things I like about the initial draft. Everything the revision got rid off to either make room for the new social structure(that could have fit into the old origin much more easily with just a small change to Kinship) or that makes the &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.</span></span>&quot; line seem hypocritical at best and completely inapplicable to the new Beasts at worst.<br /> <br /> I'll reserve judgement on Revision Heroes until we see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:43:43-07:00","id":553987,"title":"","content":"Hey, can people stop telling others to cool it? Whether you mean it or not, it's basically the same as going, &quot;You mad bro?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:44:26-07:00","id":553988,"title":"","content":"I'm really glad they changed Homecoming to the Devouring because now truly anyone can become a Beast, even Ex-Heroes.<br /> <br /> I was never a fan of how in CWoD you were either born a Werewolves or you weren't. And while Beast's original draft shyed away from those murky depths by having who's born a Beast seem cryptic at best and random at worst it still had that out of place hurdle that had been so seemlessly absent from all of the other NWoD game line up until now. I'm even glad that the creation process is even more horrifying now that one's humanity is devoured by the Horror of the Primordial Dream, to me it helps reinforce the concept of nightmares and the underlining morals that can be found within. For instance, the first lesson all newly reborn Beasts learn: There is always a consiquence for one's actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:45:38-07:00","id":553989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553981#post553981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yuuko solves other people's problems by mediating the metaphysical influences that cause them; Lil' Slugger does so by triggering Karmic realignment, generally by causing accidents or removing bad people.</div> </div> </div> </div> Both of which were things that could have been done under the original model. Meanwhile the Health inspector and the Defense attorney and all of those Beasts who didn't have to hurt people, the ones I posted the quotes from a while ago, can't do what they do anymore. Hell, depending on how you define cautionary tail, you're not going to be able to do what you suggested either.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, any Beast who wants to mitigate there hunger on their own terms can't-they have to do it by being the monster from a cationary tail.<br /> <br /> and that still ignores the issue that this is still somebody who chose to have their soul removed and replaced with a monster so that they can arbitrarily enforce their personal moral codes on people.<br /> <br /> And really, Limiting characters to cationary tail monsters is um, a huge limitation. By default plenty of characters are no longer viable..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only if the person being taught is innocent, or rather, undeserving. </div> </div> </div>Which, by modern morality, is in most cautionary tales.<br /> <br /> Can you name one little girl who deserves to be eaten alive because she listened to her parents? Think of one person who deserves to be maimed or killed because he committed petty theft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:47:23-07:00","id":553992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553948#post553948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It did not.<br /> <br /> But not every Beast is going to be sustained on those tales, and really, a lot of those are rather extreme(children dieing for not listening to their parents. Children dying <i>because </i>they listened to their parents. Being maimed or killed for petty theft&quot; That's the sort of thing Beasts have to be now.<br /> <br /> And again, I'd say that deliberately choosing to be something that has to hurt people, regardless of your reasoning, is significantly less moral than the one who had it forced on them and can then choose how they want to manage their hunger and mitigate the harm they cause.<br /> <br /> We have people whose only option for mitigating harm is &quot;force my morals on other people, causing them harm in the likelihood&quot;<br /> <br /> And we have people whose options for mitigating harm is &quot;whatever they want to do to mitigate harm, up to an including not actually casudiing any harm at all as well as doing genuine good&quot;<br /> <br /> which is better?</div> </div> </div> </div>First you have continually argued that the old way for Beast including only hurting people that deserved it. Which is actually still inflicting your own moral values on others. Second none of the options have gone away this is the explanation that is used for why Beasts exist. Third yeah you did miss them. The ones on where a person is punished for murder, carrying any vice to self-destructive levels, caring too much about your appearance. That entire branch of cautionary tale apparently slipped your mind because you're sticking to the boogeyman that is told to children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:51:03-07:00","id":553993,"title":"","content":"I can totally understand someone saying &quot;you mad, bro?&quot; at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:57:33-07:00","id":553995,"title":"","content":"And here we come to the heart of the problem.<br /> <br /> Rater, &quot;cautionary tale&quot; is broader than you're making it out to be and spreading said tales can be done in more varied ways than you're suggesting and the limited spread you're operating under is woefully narrow.<br /> <br /> Everyone is going to know about and dread the visits from the health inspector who could crush their livelihood if so much as one thing isn't up to par and they will prepare accordingly. The privileged (or at least their lawyers) will think twice about going to court with their victims in a locale where the terrifying prosecutor has set up shop and if they're particularly canny they might figure victimizing people around town or isn't worth the risk of litigation.<br /> <br /> Not everything is about missing persons and mutilation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:02:46-07:00","id":553997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553992#post553992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First you have continually argued that the old way for Beast including only hurting people that deserved it. Which is actually still inflicting your own moral values on others. Second none of the options have gone away this is the explanation that is used for why Beasts exist. Third yeah you did miss them. The ones on where a person is punished for murder, carrying any vice to self-destructive levels, caring too much about your appearance. That entire branch of cautionary tale apparently slipped your mind because you're sticking to the boogeyman that is told to children.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I didn't<br /> <br /> I continually pointed out that Beasts were in no way mandated to hurt people at all, or could at least limit themselves to people who <i>arguably deserve it</i> (The Health Inspector who is extra strict is only hurting Restaurateurs who are putting people's lives at risk to make a buck, the Attorney who makes absolutely sure that justice is found is only hurting criminals and is doing so in a way that is entirely legal)<br /> <br /> Now they are, and they <b>chose</b> that life.<br /> <br /> That's one of my biggest points of contention on the new focus. Not only are you mandated to cause harm when you were not before, you are mandated to cause harm in a way that is guaranteed to get innocent people hurt in the crossfire, especially since plenty of cationary Tales include morals that are abhorrent to modern society.<br /> <br /> And The &quot;Children's Boogeymen&quot; <b>are </b>the cationary tales.<br /> <br /> and again.Forcing Players to limit themselves to people who feed by being the Monster of a cationary Tale is a bad move, because there are only so many characters who can be made with that theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:08:18-07:00","id":553999,"title":"","content":"I just realized what I don't like about the Devouring so much.nit even that it's the choice to actively go out and be a monster. Its that they faced a fear, fought back and now they have a super super piggy backing on them. Just like a Son-Eater. <br /> <br /> I can now describe them as Changling Sin-Eaters. <br /> <br /> The reason I have grown to dislike the lesson teaching is that by giving them an &quot;end goal&quot; Beast is now just like any other splat. Before it wasn't about the end. It was about the story. The destination didn't matter it was the journey, the Legend. <br /> <br /> If I wanted to be a fairy tale monster I'd play a Changling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:08:19-07:00","id":554000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553995#post553995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here we come to the heart of the problem.<br /> <br /> Rater, &quot;cautionary tale&quot; is broader than you're making it out to be and spreading said tales can be done in more varied ways than you're suggesting and the limited spread you're operating under is woefully narrow.<br /> <br /> Everyone is going to know about and dread the visits from the health inspector who could crush their livelihood if so much as one thing isn't up to par and they will prepare accordingly. The privileged (or at least their lawyers) will think twice about going to court with their victims in a locale where the terrifying prosecutor has set up shop and if they're particularly canny they might figure victimizing people around town or isn't worth the risk of litigation.<br /> <br /> Not everything is about missing persons and mutilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But those are not the cautionary tales with Monsters, and furthermore they are not, in fact, presented as a cationary tale.<br /> <br /> Well, the Nemesis is, if you squint, by the Health Inspector is a Tyrant<br /> <br /> And a Beast is, under this Paradigm, forced to be the monster from a Cautionary Tale, which by defualt means they have to be the kind of cationary tale with a monster<br /> <br /> That probably sounds like circular reasoning, but it's not. IT's a case of 1=1.<br /> <br /> And there's still the matter of being mandated to prey on people, when they were not before.<br /> <br /> And the lack of Freedom to pursue you hunger the way you want to.<br /> <br /> Great Example: I'm trying to start a game going now. We have one Tyrant who exercises complete control over his restaurant and an other who thrives on proving her physical superiority.<br /> <br /> Neither of these are viable characters under this paradigm, and that is a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-14-2015, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:13:32-07:00","id":554002,"title":"","content":"Rater, none of the mechanics of Hunger and Satiety have changed yet. All that's changed is the first chapter of the book. Until they actually state that each Hunger must, at its most basic level, be satisfied through the use of violence, killing, or bullying, the argument that cruelty is the resting heartbeat of Begotten society is just not true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:27:39-07:00","id":554009,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it would be appropriate for a Lair to be affected by the inclusion of a Kin in a brood like it is by the presence of a strong supernatural in the region? That part was one of the things I liked about the revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 06-14-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:33:11-07:00","id":554012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revised Introduction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger<br /> <br /> All Beasts have a primal drive called Hunger, which they must indulge to sate the appetite of the Horror. Hunger can be a very simple, direct thing, such as a drive to stalk and kill prey, or it can be more abstract, such as a need to punish others for their transgressions. Though the primal drives are the same, how Beasts interpret them can vary \u2014 instead of literally hunting prey to consume them, for example, a Beast might more metaphorically stalk a target and \u201cconsume\u201d their trust.<br /> <br /> However it is interpreted, Hunger must always feed the Horror\u2019s appetite. Put another way, as older Beasts sometimes tell younger ones, \u201cif someone eats, something gets eaten.\u201d A Beast may console herself by thinking that she only hurts \u201cbad people\u201d to sate her Hunger (either to scare the subject straight or make an example of him), for example, but deep down she knows that as far as her Horror is concerned, really anyone would do \u2014 and one day they just might. It is rare for a Beast\u2019s Hunger to change, though it can happen in certain extreme circumstances and always signals a profound struggle to reconcile with the Horror.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts sate their Hungers to feed the Horror, but also to teach a lesson from the Primordial Dream. Every Beast has a lesson that it imparts in various ways; the lesson comes from the intersection of the Beast\u2019s Family and Hunger. In order to teach the lesson, though, the subject of the lesson has to survive it and internalize it. A nightmare is only useful if the dreamer awakens, and wisdom is only useful if someone survives to use it. </b>The Horror doesn\u2019t understand this (or doesn\u2019t care); it is just as happy if the Beast kills to feed it. Beasts that simply indulge their Horror\u2019s whims, though, tend to come to a bad end. Some face the judgment of their kin. Others attract Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lessons are not a harm mitigation tactic; they're a modus operandi. What specific fear your Beast represents informs how they hunt, and the default assumption is that most of the time, <u>no one dies.</u><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:41:48-07:00","id":554014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554009#post554009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it would be appropriate for a Lair to be affected b the inclusion of a Kin in a brood like it is by the presence of a strong supernatural in the region? That part as one of the things I liked about the revision.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Beasts in the World of Darkness&quot; section of Chapter Five (p311-19) has some decent groundwork for this sprinkled throughout, which is nice.<br /> <br /> There is the question of whether, say, Chambers built around a supernatural feature replicate that feature themselves \u2014 a friend of mine has a Leviathan Collector of magical human/animal/vegetable remains he's working on and we've discussed whether some kind of nightmare-infusing bog might reasonably be claimed for her Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:48:15-07:00","id":554018,"title":"","content":"Okay. I'm going to try and sum up what about this revision Ruffles my Jammies, so I can get all of my thoughts down so I don't get confused and end up contradicting myself<br /> <br /> 1: Beasts are now Mandated to harm people, when it was entirely possible to make a Beast who could spread his necessary emotions to feed without causing harm<br /> <br /> 2: Beasts are mandated now to be the monsters from Cautionary Tales. There may be a great degree of flexibility. but a lot of those tales contain morals that are utterly abhorrent, most of them are the so called &quot;Children's Boogy Men&quot; the majority of those tales involves disproportionate retribution(Seriously, In the Original Story Little Red Riding Hood was forced to strip naked and crawl into bed with a stranger impersonating her grandmother who proceeded to &quot;devour her&quot; when her only crime was choosing to listen to her parents instead of her gut. That is the opposite of a good cautionary tale)<br /> <br /> 3: The Fact that Beasts, to a man, chose to be what they are, in addition to complete reversing the assumptions we'd been going in with, boils each one of them down to &quot;asshole who decided that he has the right to arbitrarily enforce his morality on others, while before he was someone who was born that way and may have been trying to make the best of it. They might have a point, but the mere fact that they chose it is a huge tonal shift that adversely impacts morally gray theme of the game.<br /> <br /> There's a major moral difference between &quot;Somebody who is born a monster and has to hurt someone choosing to hurt people who might deserve it in order to mitigate the harm he causes and direct tit to good ends and a person who chose to be a monster specifically to do so because another monster convinced them to<br /> <br /> The first comes across as someone trying to make the best of a bad situation. The second comes across as an asshole trying to force his arbitrary view of morality on people.<br /> <br /> It's not even necessarily true, but it's the tone, the way it comes across.<br /> <br /> 4: Mandating Beasts to be monsters from Cautionary Tales pretty much kills dead a lot of concepts.<br /> <br /> I can't think of one concept that is both the monster from a Cautionary Tale and fits the hungers.<br /> <br /> Not even a Nemesis, since Nemesi don't care for justice, they just care for the punishment<br /> <br /> Meaning the Hungers all have to be rewritten, because there's not a single Tyrant, Collector, Predator, Ravager concept I can think off that could be motivated by serving as or providing examples of what you bad behavior can get you and still qualify as their hungers, and with Nemesi you have to squint to get it to fit.<br /> <br /> 5. Making it something you choose, as opposed to something you're born with, is far inferior to being the Reincarnated Soul of a Primordial Monster. As is the &quot;The Soul has utterly no connection to you until you agree to merge with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 6. The &quot;Horror&quot; moving into your body after another Beast has talked you into letting them eat your soul, at best, Makes Beasts a Pod Person. At worst, it makes it a rip off of Geist.<br /> <br /> 7. The &quot;Seve as a cautionary Tale&quot; runs complete counter to the Original Documents theme of subverting and deconstructing the Heroic Narrative, since you're just trading one story for an other. It is also a complete 180 from the stated theme of exploring the world of Darkness o learn more about yourself and your family(teaching others VS Teaching yourself.)<br /> <br /> 8. The term &quot;Horror&quot; is incredibly bland and Generic. Soul was better.<br /> <br /> 9: The Devouring, by it's nature, requires a significant change in how a Beast is played and what kind of Backstories a character can have, and the involvement of a preexisting Beast seems like just an excuse to shoehorn in a new social structure, even though that social structure would have fit very easily into the original Beast with minimal adjustment.<br /> <br /> 10: This line &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.</span></span>&quot; which I like because this apparently needed to be said out right, since a bunch of people missed it last time around, feels quite hypocritical with the knowledge that every Beast chose to be someone who is mandated to hurt people.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, I personally feel that New Beasts are morally worse than Old Heroes, because the Beast <i>chose</i> to be a monster and <i>chose</i> to hurt people for the &quot;greater good&quot;<br /> <br /> 11. In both drafts, both paradigms, you're going to have to have Beasts who say &quot;fuck it, I'm a monster&quot; and go around hurting people with no remorse. In the First Draft, these people are clearly in the wrong. In the revision, coupled with the people who chose to be Beasts, the mandate to sate your hunger by hurting people, and the hypocrisy mentioned above, really makes it sound like the asshole Beasts are just being honest with themselves.<br /> <br /> I think that's everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:51:47-07:00","id":554019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554002#post554002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rater, none of the mechanics of Hunger and Satiety have changed yet. All that's changed is the first chapter of the book. Until they actually state that each Hunger must, at its most basic level, be satisfied through the use of violence, killing, or bullying, the argument that cruelty is the resting heartbeat of Begotten society is just not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the hungers fit the new paradigm.<br /> <br /> Meaning the Hungers <i>will</i> have to be rewritten or even scrapped entirely, and that means that those characters will not be a viable concept in the new paradigm, since none of the hungers fit the new paradigm, since none of them are, currently, about anything that will allow a motivation that fits a &quot;Cautionary Tale Monster&quot; motivation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:54:58-07:00","id":554020,"title":"","content":"Hope people were not too attached to any of the fiction because that's pretty much all going to need to be rewritten. Bye bye Minotaur. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:58:13-07:00","id":554022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554012#post554012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lessons are not a harm mitigation tactic; they're a modus operandi. What specific fear your Beast represents informs how they hunt, and the default assumption is that most of the time, <u>no one dies.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>And none of the hungers allow for a Beastly motivation that is appropriate for teaching a lesson.<br /> <br /> Not even the Nemesis, since they care more about the punishment than the morality of the &quot;rules&quot;<br /> <br /> And in any case, mandating that Beasts be the villains from cationary Tales still means that dozens of character concepts, especially the ones that revolve around not hurting people ar all(like Petty Vandalism man&quot; can't be done, and the ones like Tyrant Health Inspector and Nemesis Atourny have to be twisted to fit.<br /> <br /> This is a theme that should be an <b>Option</b> for a player to take. Not something that you are forced to be just to play the game.<br /> <br /> That's a huge deal. That is taking choices about what a Character is out of a player's hands, and that is the wrong move for a game to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:58:17-07:00","id":554023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554014#post554014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;Beasts in the World of Darkness&quot; section of Chapter Five (p311-19) has some decent groundwork for this sprinkled throughout, which is nice.<br /> <br /> There is the question of whether, say, Chambers built around a supernatural feature replicate that feature themselves \u2014 a friend of mine has a Leviathan Collector of magical human/animal/vegetable remains he's working on and we've discussed whether some kind of nightmare-infusing bog might reasonably be claimed for her Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it would depend on wether there is an appropriate Lair trait. I'm not quite sure how you could mimic a Goblin Market, for exemple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:00:21-07:00","id":554025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554020#post554020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope people were not too attached to any of the fiction because that's pretty much all going to need to be rewritten. Bye bye Minotaur. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an other thing that makes the changes in Beast Origin and there shoehorned in &quot;purpose&quot; a bad move to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:04:13-07:00","id":554026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554019#post554019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the hungers fit the new paradigm.<br /> <br /> Meaning the Hungers <i>will</i> have to be rewritten or even scrapped entirely, and that means that those characters will not be a viable concept in the new paradigm, since none of the hungers fit the new paradigm, since none of them are, currently, about anything that will allow a motivation that fits a &quot;Cautionary Tale Monster&quot; motivation</div> </div> </div> </div>YOU CLEARLY HAVE LOST THE ABILITY TO COMPREHEND WHAT YOU ARE READING, BECAUSE YOU ARE WRONG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:11:26-07:00","id":554031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554026#post554026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> YOU CLEARLY HAVE LOST THE ABILITY TO COMPREHEND WHAT YOU ARE READING, BECAUSE YOU ARE WRONG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I'm a link you a character sheet.<br /> <br /> Without changing <b>anything</b> about her, tell me how exactly she can serves as the monster fro m a cationary tale(keep in mind, she doen'st give a fuck about what other people do)<br /> <br /> Now. If you can provide an example of her being a cationary tale monster, one that I can accept, I will concede this one point.<br /> <br /> None of the others, just this one, specifically about the Hungers needing to be rewritten<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bNstwSwtCfCUWUygOXaDtsfBJQWxeRQg3UdP1b5SEX4/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...EX4/edit?pli=1</a>.<br /> <br /> Also, All Caps and telling people that they're &quot;wrong&quot; tends to be the kind of thing that loses you an argument.<br /> <br /> Even without that, it's still very rude and I'm trying to be civil.<br /> <br /> The point of the matter is, mandating characters to be a monster from a cationary tale limits expressions of the hungers and takes control of a character's motivations out of a player's hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-14-2015, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:23:37-07:00","id":554036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554022#post554022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And none of the hungers allow for a Beastly motivation that is appropriate for teaching a lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Collectors</b> - &quot;Every of your belongings can be snapped from you every single minute by something more powerful than you. Deal with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Tyrants</b> - &quot;There is always someone higher in food chain, even if you think you are on top.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Nemiesis</b> - &quot;Rules/Laws should not be broken, or your bones <b>will</b> be broken with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Predators</b> - &quot;You can in every second be hunt down and fight for your live - and now RUN!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Ravengers </b>- &quot;All your civilization if nothing compared to Darkness of the world. Get used to it.&quot;<br /> <br /> And those are only of top of my head. I also was prepering example Beast for mine RPG club presentation - it's based on Batman in frist version. But in revision it has even more sense:<br /> <br /> <b>Batman-as-Beast</b> - <b>Ugallu/Nemesis</b> - <b>Lesson: </b>He hunts criminals to remind them they are always watched, from the night sky, and that law of Gotham need to be abided - or they will get themselves hurt.<br /> And each night patrol, each broken bone of criminal - he teach them the Lesson and sates Hunger of Bruce Wayne's Horror - the Bat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554022#post554022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even the Nemesis, since they care more about the punishment than the morality of the &quot;rules&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My Batman example still stands with both Nemesis and revision's take on Hunger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-16-2015, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:26:14-07:00","id":554037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554022#post554022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And none of the hungers allow for a Beastly motivation that is appropriate for teaching a lesson.<br /> <br /> Not even the Nemesis, since they care more about the punishment than the morality of the &quot;rules&quot;<br /> <br /> And in any case, mandating that Beasts be the villains from cationary Tales still means that dozens of character concepts, especially the ones that revolve around not hurting people ar all(like Petty Vandalism man&quot; can't be done, and the ones like Tyrant Health Inspector and Nemesis Atourny have to be twisted to fit.<br /> <br /> This is a theme that should be an <b>Option</b> for a player to take. Not something that you are forced to be just to play the game.<br /> <br /> That's a huge deal. That is taking choices about what a Character is out of a player's hands, and that is the wrong move for a game to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) A Beast teaches a lesson. Meaning a Nemesis can teach lessons of not violating rules. Morality is not explicitly tied into it.<br /> 2) You seem to missing a massive thing that Beasts are not required to teach to feed.<br /> 3) That depends on how central the theme is to the game. Demon ends up a very different game if you decide paranoia, and concern for discovery should be thrown out the window.<br /> 4) A lesson does not mean morality is needed. Punishment does not mean maiming, killing, or torture are needed. Cautionary tales do not require you to be psychopath to be the antagonist. Those fictions you say need to be twisted horribly to fit require no such effort.<br /> 5) It is talking about the reason they exist not that Beasts can't do anything if they aren't teaching.<br /> 6) You've quoted it yourself the Horror does not care if a lesson is taught to feed since it is more interested in feeding. So you aren't going to be getting objections from it because you decide you don't want to try and teach people anything unless you decide you're not going to feed it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:32:45-07:00","id":554039,"title":"","content":"2: But Beasts are Required to Teach, which is taking part of the Character's motivation out of player hands<br /> 3: Seems pretty central in the revised intro<br /> 4: A Cautionary Tale does imply morality<br /> 5: And that reason that they exist is toxic to the game, because it takes control from the player and puts it in the hands of a book's writers<br /> 6: Doesn't matter if it's the Soul or not. Beasts are apparently supposed to teach lessons, it's the &quot;reason for their existance&quot; and that's a bad thing, because it takes agency away from the character because they have to build characters that fit that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:36:06-07:00","id":554041,"title":"","content":"Ok, you seem to have missed a point. The Horror doesn't care how you sate it, right? So you have beasts who go entirely too far and just murder people without teaching anything, but you can <i>also</i> have beasts who feed subtly without affecting people at all. These beasts are also lacking in their lesson quota, but are more tolerated because they're just slackers and not unrepentant monsters who need to be put down. <br /> <br /> And you know what else? I think you can easily spin the devouring as a transformation. Your human soul dies, and a Horror (why is everyone complaining about this word? &quot;Soul&quot; is a generic as they come.) takes its place. In much the same way that Anakin Skywalker died and Darth Vader took his place. It's a <i>rebirth. </i><br /> <br /> I've started picturing it like Eren's first transformation in Attack on Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:40:58-07:00","id":554048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554031#post554031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I'm a link you a character sheet.<br /> <br /> Without changing <b>anything</b> about her, tell me how exactly she can serves as the monster fro m a cationary tale(keep in mind, she doen'st give a fuck about what other people do)<br /> <br /> Now. If you can provide an example of her being a cationary tale monster, one that I can accept, I will concede this one point.<br /> <br /> None of the others, just this one, specifically about the Hungers needing to be rewritten<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bNstwSwtCfCUWUygOXaDtsfBJQWxeRQg3UdP1b5SEX4/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...EX4/edit?pli=1</a>.<br /> <br /> Also, All Caps and telling people that they're &quot;wrong&quot; tends to be the kind of thing that loses you an argument.<br /> <br /> Even without that, it's still very rude and I'm trying to be civil.<br /> <br /> The point of the matter is, mandating characters to be a monster from a cationary tale limits expressions of the hungers and takes control of a character's motivations out of a player's hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of your argument is what's wrong, but I'll attempt to indulge you.<br /> <br /> Short answer: Icarus story. This character is a typical unjustifiably wealthy person and has a lot of smug bastard going on, so her cautionary tale would be about underestimating your adversary.<br /> <br /> And nowhere in the introduction are the words &quot;monster from a cautionary tale&quot; mentioned. What's implied, is that in order for the Horror to be nourished, the act in question must resonate both with Hunger and Family, i.e. an Anakim Tyrant will almost always seek to prove that physically, they are the best and anyone who takes exception does so at the risk of a sudden, brutal and ignominious demise, whereas a Ravager of the same family literally tears things down in order to curb foolish pride, and an Namtaru Tyrant establishes control by fomenting betrayal and distrust among their rivals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:42:33-07:00","id":554049,"title":"","content":"I'm Torn, I like some of the changes, but not all, then again i can understand why they made the changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:45:16-07:00","id":554051,"title":"","content":"Devouring is sorta weaksauce, if you kids still say that these days. Homecoming has a bittersweet feel, like seeing yourself in the birth parent you just meet. Devouring just seems like an offer even your sleeping self would reject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:47:17-07:00","id":554052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554041#post554041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, you seem to have missed a point. The Horror doesn't care how you sate it, right? So you have beasts who go entirely too far and just murder people without teaching anything, but you can <i>also</i> have beasts who feed subtly without affecting people at all. These beasts are also lacking in their lesson quota, but are more tolerated because they're just slackers and not unrepentant monsters who need to be put down.<br /> <br /> And you know what else? I think you can easily spin the devouring as a transformation. Your human soul dies, and a Horror (why is everyone complaining about this word? &quot;Soul&quot; is a generic as they come.) takes its place. In much the same way that Anakin Skywalker died and Darth Vader took his place. It's a <i>rebirth. </i><br /> <br /> I've started picturing it like Eren's first transformation in Attack on Titan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your soul being eaten to make room for something else to crawl in is not a transformation , especially with the implcation that the &quot;Horror&quot; was a preexisting entity.At best it's a pod person, at worst ti's a geist rip off<br /> <br /> a &quot;Soul&quot; is far more evocative and far more descriptive for the Imperial, astral based Monster that is literally your soul than &quot;Horror&quot; which is incredibly generic and not not at all descriptive.<br /> <br /> And I don't think I missed a point.<br /> <br /> The fact that it's an assumed things that Beasts are supposed to do, something that specific, takes agency from the player's hands.<br /> <br /> when your options are taking one of three options(Unrepentant Monster, Force your idea of Morality/Ethics on people*, or Lazy Fucker who doen'st do the thing he signed on to do) and dressing them up in different hats, you have insufficient agency when it comes to your character for a tabble top role playing game.<br /> <br /> and Eren Yeager didn't get to chose weather or not he became a titan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Once again, the fact that the Monster Chose to be a monster heavily taints the morality of anything they do in relation to their hunger</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:53:02-07:00","id":554056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554052#post554052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your soul being eaten to make room for something else to crawl in is not a transformation , especially with the implcation that the &quot;Horror&quot; was a preexisting entity</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>NOT</i> a preexisting entity. It's created at the <i>exact moment</i> your old soul &quot;dies&quot;. A soul which is said to look straight into the eyes of the Dark Mother and then wake up in their Lair for the first time.<br /> <br /> You didn't die. You just grew claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:53:14-07:00","id":554057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554048#post554048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The premise of your argument is what's wrong, but I'll attempt to indulge you.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;A Character must be built around the themes of the game&quot; is a wrong premise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Short answer: Icarus story. This character is a typical unjustifiably wealthy person and has a lot of smug bastard going on, so her cautionary tale would be about underestimating your adversary. </div> </div> </div>No. Doesn't count. She's not the one teaching the lesson, as Beasts are apparently supposed to do, she's the one learning the lesson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:04:13-07:00","id":554060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554039#post554039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: But Beasts are Required to Teach, which is taking part of the Character's motivation out of player hands<br /> 3: Seems pretty central in the revised intro<br /> 4: A Cautionary Tale does imply morality<br /> 5: And that reason that they exist is toxic to the game, because it takes control from the player and puts it in the hands of a book's writers<br /> 6: Doesn't matter if it's the Soul or not. Beasts are apparently supposed to teach lessons, it's the &quot;reason for their existance&quot; and that's a bad thing, because it takes agency away from the character because they have to build characters that fit that reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>3) That's because there wasn't a point to them originally.<br /> 4) No a cautionary tale implies that you should be cautious about something. That's why there are stories where the lesson amounts to don't go into the woods alone at night and remember to bring a light source.<br /> 5) No it doesn't. It just says that Beast's originally came into the world to teach.<br /> 6) *Buzzer* Wrong a lesson is just a lesson. They don't need to be crushing moral things that dominate your entire character. They can actually be rather simple.<br /> -Tyrant lesson: Someone is better than you (probably me).<br /> - Collector lessons: Get better security. There is nothing you possess that can not be taken from you*<br /> - Ravager lesson: You know this is a lot more fragile than you think it is.<br /> -Predator lesson: You are prey and you can not escape. (Heck I think that one is basically phrased as a lesson in the original draft anyway.)<br /> -Nemesis lesson: You have done wrong and for that you will be punished. / Don't do that again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and the part where you're trying to be smug about arguing with Hex. The part of your premise that is flawed is that a Beast must be a cautionary tale. A lesson doesn't require it be a cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> *Yes yes &quot;Raiders of the Lost Arc&quot; I'm weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 06-14-2015, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:11:07-07:00","id":554062,"title":"","content":"3) Oh, but they had a point: Explore the World of Darkness to learn my about yourself and your Family. The problem is, that focus was heavily dependant on the crossover element. That can be easily solved by including an appendix full of simplified templates, minor templates, or simplified monster rules( like the Dread Powers from Hunter) so that you don't have to crossover to find the weird things in the WoD and learn from them. Instead, Matt chose to throw out the prexisting theme for one that is the opposite of the one that we were told about for over a year. Furthermore, it's a very restricting theme.<br /> 5) Which means you have to either build a character that conforms to that theme or is specifically a rejection of it. That greatly restricts the permissible character concepts, which is taking agency out of Player Hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:14:56-07:00","id":554064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554056#post554056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>NOT</i> a preexisting entity. It's created at the <i>exact moment</i> your old soul &quot;dies&quot;. A soul which is said to look straight into the eyes of the Dark Mother and then wake up in their Lair for the first time.<br /> <br /> You didn't die. You just grew claws.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Horror is a monster from the Primordial Dream, and it rushes up to merge with the dreamer. </b><br /> <br /> It splits the dreamer\u2019s nightmare off from her Big Brother or Sister, and the dreamer \u2014 now a<br /> <br /> Beast \u2014 finds herself in her new Lair. The Horror is now part of her. She sees the Primordial<br /> <br /> Dream stretching before her, replete with the hard-fought wisdom that humanity has earned since<br /> <br /> the dawn of time. They are part of a great brood, a family of monsters the world over. </div> </div> </div> Implies it's a prexisting Entity that come sin to take the place where your soul used to be.<br /> <br /> you might not have died, but you're not all you anymore.<br /> <br /> Which means, again, at best, it's a game about pod people(though bodyjackers might be better) and at worst it's a ripoff of Geist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:15:27-07:00","id":554066,"title":"","content":"Cautionary tale is mentioned exactly one time in the revised text and it is under the section describing Heroes. You made up the theme then you want everyone else to work around it. That is an incorrect premise. Cautionary tales have nothing to do with it. Rephrase or accept that your requests are unreasonable.<br /> <br /> The text from Introduction to Overview is from an in character perspective. It is how Beasts see Beasts. It may or may not be the Truth. If the perspective Beasts take on their role, birth, and existence is hypocritical then they are not very different than many people in the World of Darkness. Actually, they wouldn't be that different from many real people. That section of text is supposed to make Beasts seem relatable to players and put Beasts in the best possible light.<br /> <br /> The in character Introduction never invalidates what follows. Absolutely, none of the fiction needs be changed because of it. The character examples need not be changed. Hungers would be exactly the same. Beasts can come up with whatever bullshit justifications they want. The out of character part says some of them give exactly zero fucks about teaching people anything. They would not be hypocrites. They would read the Introduction, laugh, and call it a giant steaming crock of shit.<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to try to explain the Introduction, but I would prefer to see more to view it in a larger context. All I can really say is all in character explanations are intended to be taken skeptically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:17:45-07:00","id":554068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554066#post554066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cautionary tale is mentioned exactly one time in the revised text and it is under the section describing Heroes. You made up the theme then you want everyone else to work around it. That is an incorrect premise. Cautionary tales have nothing to do with it. Rephrase or accept that your requests are unreasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't make it up, I went with what an other person said about the theme, and really, &quot;monster that teaches a lesson&quot; and &quot;monster from a cautionary tail&quot; is up, kind of different ways to say the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-14-2015, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:24:21-07:00","id":554069,"title":"","content":"I kind of think that if certain vocal detractors (I have in mind the people who implied that those who liked the first draft condoned horrible stuff IRL) had exercised a little more critical judgment toward the text instead of taking it as face value, a heavy re-writing such as the one we're seeming to get wouldn't have been necessary. Beasts are kind of awful, and know and embrace it even if they can choose to work hard to minimize damage; Heroes are not awful for defending themselves, they're awful for desiring to apply murder as the only possible punishment against a group of people whose crimes aren't all deserving of death penalty (and, depending on the Hero, causing collateral damage against innocents, and not caring about it).<br /> (Admittedly that there was ambiguity over the free will of Heroes was a problem and did deserve clarification, but whether they have a choice or not, I consider that if your sole crime is vandalism/theft, you don't deserve to be callously murdered.)<br /> I sure as hell don't remember anybody crying out that Demons were irredeemable for regularly destroying mortals' souls and very existence for their own interests, and how that painted a terrible picture of gears in the system who don't want to blindly follow orders anymore.<br /> That I saw, of all supernaturals, Vampires being used as an example of harmless feeding was also jarring, and I'd like to know where the hell that came from. If somebody commits what's essentially a physical aggression on you (measurable by blood loss) without your consent, even if you don't remember it, even if it felt good at some point, even if you don't notice consequences or injuries, even if the aggressor felt the need to do it, that's still a physical aggression. If they prey on animals instead of humans, then they tend to kill a lot of animals during their existence as a consequences; and as it turns out, there's several Beasts that similarly kill animals to satisfy their Hunger as well, not all of them pets belonging to grieving owners but wild, untamed beasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I understand that many people saw uncomfortable stuff, but frankly? That several readers managed to make fans of the first draft feel like shit, and that the final text seems to take a wholly different direction than the one that had seemingly been intended for months, rubs me the wrong way. I command the writers for reacting so fast and taking in account the discomfort of potential players, I really do.<br /> But unless the next revisions change my mind, I'm growing afraid that, just as much as the first draft wasn't a game for everyone, the final version might not be a game for me. (The biggest shame is that, maybe, if I hadn't read the development thread for months and had ignored the very first draft, I might have liked what was published just now, but there's a lot from the first version that I liked that appears to be excised.)<br /> You can't please everybody, and I'm just one potential customer out of hundreds, if not thousands.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: yes, I mad bro. Well, not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:27:07-07:00","id":554071,"title":"","content":"Ahem: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever its form, whatever its origins, however, when a Horror Devours a human\u2019s soul, in the moment of oblivion,<b> a new Horror is born</b>. The newborn Beast joins with <b>this</b> Horror, and becomes one of the Begotten. </div> </div> </div>You stare into the abyss. It stares back. No possession here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:33:43-07:00","id":554075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554071#post554071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahem:<br /> <br /> <br /> You stare into the abyss. It stares back. No possession here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joining implies possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:40:16-07:00","id":554079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554062#post554062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Oh, but they had a point: Explore the World of Darkness to learn my about yourself and your Family. The problem is, that focus was heavily dependant on the crossover element. That can be easily solved by including an appendix full of simplified templates, minor templates, or simplified monster rules( like the Dread Powers from Hunter) so that you don't have to crossover to find the weird things in the WoD and learn from them. Instead, Matt chose to throw out the prexisting theme for one that is the opposite of the one that we were told about for over a year. Furthermore, it's a very restricting theme.<br /> 5) Which means you have to either build a character that conforms to that theme or is specifically a rejection of it. That greatly restricts the permissible character concepts, which is taking agency out of Player Hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so a Beast only game becomes rather less interesting since all anyone is doing is exploring the world. There is no reason to explore the world other than find new things to feed on, and you're saying that original point of Beast was to step on the toes of Mage by trying to explore and understand the world they live in.<br /> Your response to &quot;5&quot; isn't even a bloody argument. You are arguing that it is too restrictive of a concept to have vampires drink blood for all the complications &quot;Beasts teach a lesson&quot; throws into character creation and concept unless your ST is sadist who insists that every single aspect of the character must be dedicated to one specific lesson and you are not allowed any variation ever and no part of the character can deviate from that lesson.<br /> <br /> @Chairkicker The vampire thing got kind of crazy. Basically it had started with the person having issues that Beast and Vampires kept having their feedings compared to eachother when this individual felt they weren't really comparable outside of favored food source. Then they made a case that since a Vampire could ,in theory, feed predominantly off minor amounts (say the amount of blood one donates in a blood drive or for a blood test) from willing subjects it was potentially less harmful than a Beast's feeding which can not have a willing target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:45:31-07:00","id":554080,"title":"","content":"What does it even matter if the soul is replaced anyway? That doesn't mean the beast and the dreamer aren't the same entity. That's not how souls work here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:48:37-07:00","id":554082,"title":"","content":"I've read the intro. I'm ok with making Heroes more sympathetic (even if I didn't feel the need), but the premises of the game have changed too much for my taste. I don't like that becoming a Beast is a choice. I think that if Beast really had to change for Heroes, Homecoming could still stay. The game feels very different reading the intro.<br /> And this &quot;beast are there to teach philosophical lessons&quot; doesn't appeal to me and my friends.<br /> <br /> Too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:54:37-07:00","id":554085,"title":"","content":"I'll grab what I wrote on the kickstarter and give it some editing so it sounds better.<br /> <br /> I just said this on the Onyx Path homepage, but I wanted to say it here since I'll hopefully reach some more folks in this medium, but I'm not a big fan of the tonal shift in the rewritten introduction. Like no doubt a few have said, the Devouring versus Homecoming seems a lot weaker an introduction to the supernatural setting of Beast from an in character perspective.<br /> <br /> A Homecoming gives an innate feeling of alienation for characters, you were always different and now that you embrace your monstrous soul, you finally realise why. You always were alien, you were a monster all along, you just didn't know it and didn't know what made you different.<br /> <br /> With the Devouring, you're offered a choice to become a monster and accept a duty to show humanity the true horrors lurking in the world. So, you basically are playing Lancea et Sanctum: the Guides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 06-14-2015, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:59:12-07:00","id":554086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554079#post554079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Chairkicker The vampire thing got kind of crazy. Basically it had started with the person having issues that Beast and Vampires kept having their feedings compared to eachother when this individual felt they weren't really comparable outside of favored food source. Then they made a case that since a Vampire could ,in theory, feed predominantly off minor amounts (say the amount of blood one donates in a blood drive or for a blood test) from willing subjects it was potentially less harmful than a Beast's feeding which can not have a willing target.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's how it started?<br /> I could as well make the case that a Beast could theoretically only feed off deserving targets (see: Batman who terrorizes villains, and too many protagonists to count, plus you could ask every person out there who has an &quot;eye for an eye&quot; philosophy toward crime*). Or do something even less harmful: use Family Dinner. Hang out with Changelings, Werewolves, or other supernaturals who are very capable of &quot;feeding&quot; without harming people, and bam. If you make it a point not to be an asshole toward your &quot;relatives&quot; (particularly Changelings, since they &quot;feed&quot; often but have the most reasons to mistrust Beasts), it shouldn't be hard.<br /> The best Vampires can do in comparison is raid blood banks. Not only it's going to be harmful to mortals who do need the blood since there's nowhere as many donors as there are patients, but I'm not even sure you can get decent Vitae, or Vitae at all, from it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Not that I agree with them, but I know way too many people who argue that aggressors should be beaten up, rapists should be raped, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:03:30-07:00","id":554087,"title":"","content":"Beasts always chose to become Beasts. If joining implies possession then Homecoming was possession as well. But that is another point.<br /> <br /> A cautionary tale is a method of teaching a lesson. The concepts are not the same. If you want to know how Taylor can teach someone a lesson, the answer is a long list. I'm guessing you want something specific. I'm still working on understanding all the mechanics, and I'm not sure how they might change, if at all. Does using a Nightmare seem appropriate? She can show her true form briefly. Her lesson can be &quot;don't try to bully Taylor.&quot; A more general lesson could be &quot;don't underestimate women.&quot; She could even go with &quot;fear women.&quot; Those would more or less be in line with a Power Hunger too. The setup is obvious, no? Find someone, give them the opportunity to show they need teaching, and hit them with the Nightmare. Depending on the particulars, it could be a cautionary tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:04:37-07:00","id":554088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554080#post554080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it even matter if the soul is replaced anyway? That doesn't mean the beast and the dreamer aren't the same entity. That's not how souls work here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one, there's the &quot;you're not quite who you were before&quot; implication and the &quot;something else slithered into you&quot; implication, the first implies partial loss of agency(from an in character perspective) while the second makes the game a bit too similar to Geist.<br /> <br /> For Two, as has been said several times, mosrst recently by Gullinbursti, Thw whole concept of the Devouring feels inferior to the Homecoming, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Me, my biggest problems with it are the fact that by choosing to be a monster, you're choosing to have to hurt people and that taints any moral point you might have, te fact that somebody other than you is involved in the process, and the bit about it being something that comes in and replaces your soul instead of you having always been a monster and just realizing it sort of conflicts with Beasts theme of Family","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:05:44-07:00","id":554089,"title":"","content":"I wonder what makes a person agree to the devouring, and under the new structure(?) could you possibly have an antagonist Beast based off the bad guy in Dead Silence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:09:44-07:00","id":554093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554079#post554079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, so a Beast only game becomes rather less interesting since all anyone is doing is exploring the world. There is no reason to explore the world other than find new things to feed on, and you're saying that original point of Beast was to step on the toes of Mage by trying to explore and understand the world they live in.<br /> Your response to &quot;5&quot; isn't even a bloody argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 is a point, and a valid one, with a theme like &quot;This is what you were made to do and you have to buy into it to become an X&quot;, then any character you make has to buy into X, or be a specific rejection of X, and I would contend that &quot;explore the world&quot; is a much better theme because it promotes more variety because it can be done in more numerous ways.<br /> <br /> It's also a less formal thing in character so you character isn't looked down upon for not doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are arguing that it is too restrictive of a concept to have vampires drink blood for all the complication </div> </div> </div>I am arguing no such thing. &quot;Vampires drink blood&quot; is not a very restrictive thing. &quot;Beasts must tach lessons&quot; is far more restricting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:11:12-07:00","id":554095,"title":"","content":"Unless you assume the developers are bold faced liars (I do not), then it is actually unfair to say any changes were made because of people did not approve of something in the first version, except maybe for the teaching bit. People conveyed their impression of what Beast was. The developers realized that their intention was not being recognized. Whether it was by people that hating or loved the tone, it wasn't what they wanted the game to be. I'm thinking the teaching thing was in response to criticism, specifically that Beasts didn't seem to have any motivation to do anything except feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:12:03-07:00","id":554097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554087#post554087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts always chose to become Beasts. If joining implies possession then Homecoming was possession as well. But that is another point..</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A Beast was quite explicitly always a Beast, they just needed to realize it. That's like, the opposite of possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:14:04-07:00","id":554098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554095#post554095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you assume the developers are bold faced liars (I do not), then it is actually unfair to say any changes were made because of people did not approve of something in the first version, except maybe for the teaching bit. People conveyed their impression of what Beast was. The developers realized that their intention was not being recognized. Whether it was by people that hating or loved the tone, it wasn't what they wanted the game to be. I'm thinking the teaching thing was in response to criticism, specifically that Beasts didn't seem to have any motivation to do anything except feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they could have gien a motivation that's less restrictive.<br /> <br /> I don't see anybody complaiining the Promeatheans don't have a motivation to do anything but become human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:23:23-07:00","id":554100,"title":"","content":"If you ask me, the old homecoming was as much a choice as the devouring is. A beast was always running from the monster in their dreams. Then they realize that they <i>are</i> the monster. At that point, they stop running. And the monster devours them, and they merge for the first time. <br /> <br /> What can happen now is that another beast can notice a nascent beast and tip them off that they need to stop running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:26:27-07:00","id":554103,"title":"","content":"I've only read a bit of the last 8 or so pages. So please take my next statement in the spirit of co-operation and an attempt to understand.<br /> <br /> It appears that some members of our community are conflating the changes with other concepts which may or may not be effected.<br /> Beasts requiring another Beast to gain the template - Not relevant to name change.<br /> Beasts having to decide to become Begotten - Not related to name change.<br /> Heroes being connected to the Primordial Dream - has nothing to do with name change.<br /> Becoming Begotten is a sacrifice - <b>Is implied by name change</b><br /> Pod People - <i>Not a result of the name change but tightly connected, I grant you.</i><br /> Begotten being mini-bodhisattvas of the <a href=\"http://www.google.com.au/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0CB0QFjAAahUKEwijs4_y9o7GAhUkI6YKHVUzAGc&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwhitewolf.wikia.com%2Fwiki%2FAutumn_Court_%28CTL%29&amp;ei=EVF9VePmKKTGmAXV5oC4Bg&amp;usg=AFQjCNHzfigPBDGjHrfUVgfmvjWDUOzHcw&amp;sig2=p8dgh0ZnE9qSJ3OY84BflA&amp;bvm=bv.95515949,d.dGY\" target=\"_blank\">Autumn Court</a> - Not related to the name change.<br /> <br /> What the name change, from Homecoming to Devouring does is change the tone of the transformation. Before it was implied to be a relief of sorts...now it appears to at least some to be a form of <i>suicide</i>.<br /> <br /> I am not pleased by <b><i>all </i></b>the changes but I will not blame a label for ruining a concept.<br /> <br /> Take for example this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast revised Introduction - Devouring</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then one day, a Beast finds her. How the Beast knew about her dream, she has no idea, at least not at first. The Beast demonstrates its power and its nature, and she sees the Horror beneath...and recognizes it. Maybe she\u2019s never seen that particular monster, but she\u2019s seen its brothers and sisters in her dreams. Some people recoil in horror at coming face to face with the thing in the dark, but some feel a rush of gratitude. The nightmares were terrifying, yes, but they brought catharsis and good lessons.<br /> <br /> The Beast explains that the dreamer feels the knowledge of the Primordial Dream more deeply than most, and that she is therefore equipped to become one of the Children. If she chooses to join the family, though, she gives up her soul. She will become inhuman, seemingly a person but possessed of a Horror. She will never dream again. Instead, she will become the nightmare that teaches the harsh lessons. She will become the Primordial incarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the new concepts can be used with Homecoming with only minor tweaking;<br /> <br /> <i>The Beast explains that the dreamer feels the knowledge of the Primordial Dream more deeply than most, and that she is therefore one of the Children. If she chooses to join to come Home, she releases her Soul. She will become inhuman, seemingly a person but possessed of a horror within. She will never dream again. Instead, she will become the nightmare that teaches the harsh lessons. She will become the Primordial incarnate.</i><br /> <br /> Not exactly world shattering, but the tone changes dramatically...and only one paragraph was altered. So please, try to remember that Devouring is not the other changes; it is a shift in tone from the reconciliatory to a darker, less apologetic hue.<br /> <br /> I have faith that dispite whatever changes they make, the authors will produce something amazing that I am able to (and probably will) enjoy. I know nothing I can do will alter the content. I know this is the same for almost all of us. With that in mind; can we please agree that is ok to disagree and everyone is allowed to have their own interpretations &amp; share them here?<br /> No rants, no rubbing opinions or facts in each other's faces. Just polite-ish discourse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:33:41-07:00","id":554105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554085#post554085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not a big fan of the tonal shift in the rewritten introduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, its not a mechanical shift, at least as far as I know so far, but the tonal shift that I'm not a big fan of. Instead of being a non-human who discovers his heritage during his Homecoming (a Werewolf's First Change), its more akin to a Mage's Awakening or a Vampire's Embrace. You had a spark within that had the potential to let you become a Beast (Mage), but it takes an outside source to trigger it, the Devouring (Awakening, being Embraced etc).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:39:57-07:00","id":554107,"title":"","content":"Here are some Comments I took from the Kickstarter because they deserve to be shared;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paige</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I backed the project finally, just to voice my intense dislike for Devouring vs Homecoming. There is a story in the original draft, of a Makara woman who falls in love with her childhood friend; the bond she shares with that woman seems to be the only thread tying her to her humanity. But, after her childhood naivety wears off, she realizes that her true love will always live in a world apart from her, because you are born a beast. And as a Rampaging Soul typically goes after those closest to you, there's some deeply implied danger.<br /> If anybody can become a beast, the story changes drastically. Now, her goal would be what, to find a way to slip the red pill to her wife and intentionally replace her lifelong partner's soul with that of a monster? That just screams Vampire.<br /> My take was that the Soul was always an adversary, if you read enough into the text -- realizing that when I read the draft really caught me off guard. It did not care what happened to You. The woman who dies, alone, scared, and pathetic because her Soul was gorged and sleeping when the hunter followed her into her Lair -- her Soul objectively doesn't care at all as it goes off Unfettered. Same with the Sphinx who lets herself die. The soul feels no bond or obligation to You. In the fluff, Ben seems to retain some sense of himself, but in mechanics, Merger completely obliterates you and the Soul steals your body. An animal that you share a bond with seeks to comfort or protect you. Pets threaten those who threaten their owner. Your Soul doesn't even care about getting revenge on your murderer.<br /> I actually wanted to see revising more towards the soul not being so hostile to your interests. Even in a bestial, animalistic way, it should care for you in some fashion. Instead, it felt more like you were under demonic possession. Now with the revision, you literally have your soul destroyed and a ghost parasite possessing you.<br /> I've spent months hanging on every scrap of info regarding the game, and I have great interest in the project. I mean no disrespect, and of course you can't please everybody, but this feels so anti-beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone else mentioned that with the changes, most of the fiction in the book no longer makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-14-2015, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:46:26-07:00","id":554121,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm Sean Martin and shared my post last page <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:56:12-07:00","id":554123,"title":"","content":"The Lancea et Sanctum don't disperse wisdom, they scare people into the arms of the Almighty like frightened sheep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:04:10-07:00","id":554125,"title":"","content":"I think that, when looking at the Lancea or the Scarecrow Ministry in comparison to Beasts, it's important to consider 'what lessons do we teach?' If they're the things in the dark, the dwellers in the unknown, then the things that they ward against can be myriad. Plenty of people have mentioned the idea of Beasts as Guardians of things that man was not meant to know, or arbiters of the overall Masquerade. From my point of view, especially with this as an introduction, I see no reason why all of these things and more can't be equally true.<br /> <br /> What lessons do we teach? Do we all really need the same lesson? And that, right there, is where I see a lot of philosophical potential and conflict within Beast society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:07:27-07:00","id":554127,"title":"","content":"Homecoming V. Devouring<br /> <br /> I guess I'll play this game too. I thought Homecoming was very evocative and appropriate. It added absolutely nothing to the game, but not everything needs to do that. Sometimes cool imagery is reward enough. I think the revision needs some final polishing, so I can't compare the writing without being unfair. I will say that Devouring does actually add to the game. I would prefer the names actually be reversed. I think the new way would better be called Homecoming. The name would eliminate that distasteful &quot;job offer&quot; feeling. It would be &quot;welcome to the family.&quot; It also downplays a Beast &quot;making&quot; another Beast. I don't hate it, but I don't love it either. I think Devouring would fit the old method as an appropriate title that fits better there. Obviously, that would mean both methods are valid. I actually haven't seen anything to suggest otherwise. Devouring is, obviously, the standard method now. It improves the game even if it does &quot;kill a darling&quot; as Matt said.<br /> <br /> Sometimes semantics matter. There are a few words changed here or there that I think were changed unnecessarily that would weaken the possibility of the old Homecoming being a possibility. It is still reasonable, but a more solid footing. I think Beasts being born human instead of like a human and anybody could become a Beast does dilute the title character. I would love for that bit to backtrack, but if it was the original intent then I'll live with it. Let's assume Beasts retained that &quot;special at birth&quot; feel.<br /> <br /> I would say a Beast is born and raised like a normal human. At some point, the nightmares start and they get the alienated feelings, all the usual stuff. This is the point Devouring and Homecoming would differ. If the proto-Beast happens upon a Beast then they can choose Devouring. If they don't it will be more difficult and take longer but eventually they will have the choice of Homecoming. Both are in fact choices. They always were. What is not a choice is the Beast having the opportunity to make the choice. A Beast would keep getting the nightmares until they choose Homecoming or Devouring.<br /> <br /> Before a Devouring a Beast must be as much a Beast as just before a Homecoming. It is even more explicit in the new text. A proto-Beast can actually recognize a true Beast and see their powers activate as a normal Beast could. They can't be mortal because mortals are incapable of recognizing Beasts and seeing Horrors/Souls. Devouring would be the default because it is the easy path. Homecoming would still be an option. It isn't like anyone that has seen the first version doesn't know how to run with Homecoming. Of course, it would be nice if Homecoming at least got a mention. It could be elaborated upon in a later book if there isn't room in the core.<br /> <br /> Now assume the new changes stand. Absolutely nothing about the dual paths changes. If a person is Beast enough to be Devoured then they could manage a Homecoming too. This is what happens when you try to look more for similarities than differences, aka keeping an open mind.<br /> <br /> This isn't something I think is worth pitching a fit over. It is a section of the game that many people will skip over. It would only matter if it actually affected the story. Homecoming, Devouring are important to the character. They mean much less to the player. Nobody can suck Homecomings from your mind and I think I have justified them as a possibility. It then is left to the group to decide what they want. Unless the book specifically states that Beasts do not spontaneously occur, you can have your Devouring and Homecoming too. Players are special so even if most Beasts were Devoured, you can Come Home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:08:59-07:00","id":554129,"title":"","content":"My dislike of this though is that in the case of the Lancea et Sanctum and the Scarecrow Ministry, they are merely splats (or sub-splats) within a setting, here, the &quot;terrorise the flock so they learn&quot; schtick seems to now be the overriding stance of the entire setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:14:18-07:00","id":554135,"title":"","content":"@nalak42 I really wish you people would quit calling me disturbed and suggesting that I'm a terrible human being for thinking that non-harm done with consent isn't as morally reprehensible as harm done without it. I dropped the discussion. Would appreciate it not being brought up again.<br /> <br /> But then, that's the level of &quot;discussion&quot; this thread has taken for a while now, so I think I'll just quit visiting. I'm sure it'll make both of us much happier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:20:07-07:00","id":554137,"title":"","content":"Reading all the comments and opinions here I'm starting to feel sorry for the developers. This game is becoming one hell of a headache for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-14-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:52:14-07:00","id":554150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554018#post554018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10: This line &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, Calibri, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.</span></span>&quot; which I like because this apparently needed to be said out right, since a bunch of people missed it last time around, feels quite hypocritical with the knowledge that every Beast chose to be someone who is mandated to hurt people.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=553984#post553984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things I liked about revision:<br /> <br /> This line&quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">It should be the prerogative of the Begotten who possess the souls of these Horrors to consider the matter, and /that/ should be what drives their moderation. The fact that they understand that\u2019s what they are and what their souls represent, but their Horrors themselves /don\u2019t care/.</span></span>&quot; since it's a thing that was present in the first draft that a lot of people overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind not pulling my words out of context to justify your arguments?<br /> <br /> This thought was presented in Beast before, and from my understanding it's still intended to be important (possibly more so). Rich even answered that far as he knows, the Horror really does not care about the purpose of Beasts beyond satisfying its Hunger. I said that specifically to point out that the idea might need clarification, because in my reading the updated introduction didn't seem entirely consistent about where the Horrors stand in this.<br /> <br /> On follow up readings, I may have misunderstood some things (even if I don't like the tone of the Devouring as opposed to the Homecoming) and missed a detail or two. Even then, I think the point is valid, but <i>in the context it was written.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:24:10-07:00","id":554189,"title":"","content":"About the tone<br /> <br /> Since the writers recognize the old tone was not what they intended, I feel more comfortable describing the original tone. From the Introduction, character examples, and basically the first few hundred pages, the tone was Beasts are &quot;irredeemable assholes&quot; as one person put it. Some people liked that, some hated it. The purpose of a Beast's existence seemed to be solely to feed its hunger and whatever it might like to do in its free time, not spent feeding. As a whole, the tone slapped you in the face while asking &quot;why would you ever act morally?&quot; It made a person feel like they must be stupid, stupid, stupid if they didn't play a Beast as a sadistic monster.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness has a paradigm. Part of it would be while the World is dark, a player may be as good or evil as they wish. Generally, good is a struggle. That is a function of the World. Sadistic monster has always been an option. Beast did not seem to fit the paradigm. Sure you could play as good or as evil as you wanted. Of course, you were required to do evil acts to feed your hunger or let them be done in your name, as it were. A character is less about good and evil and more about mitigating required evil. Practically everything in the book makes you feel like you are <i>supposed</i> to play the sadistic monster. That was never the intent.<br /> <br /> Beasts have a piece of sadistic monster inside and they need to feed it. That was intended. You can play as good or evil as you want, provided you feed the monster. That is required to be a game line in WoD. The difference is the game has at least a few pages devoted to countering the notion that you are <i>supposed</i> to be a sadistic monster, unrepentant. The teacher bit is new. Unlike feeding, it is a soft goal. There is no penalty if you blow it off.<br /> <br /> The tone is different. There is no denying that. Did Matt go too far away from the original? Perhaps. We only have a few pages this time around. If he is setting a trend for changes then I think he is over-correcting. If this is just the counter balance to all the rest that remains the same then maybe not. There are many examples left to show what sadistic monsters Beasts can be. They do not need to be changed. Sadistic monster is a part of Beast. It was not meant to be the all-consuming part though.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the example characters don't illustrate what sadistic monsters Beasts can be? I'm using &quot;sadistic monsters&quot; as that is how Beasts are unabashedly described in this game. However, you might like to described it. Are the examples not some nasty pieces of work? I think so. I don't know if they are good teachers. I know that old lady taught that punk not to steal candy from kids. I know Ben taught that bully not to mess with people. How much of their actions was about teaching and how much was about feeding? I think only the player knows. The cautionary tale, don't get on a Beast's radar. They will fuck you up. Are they imposing their morality upon others? Maybe, but they have to decide on some method to choose victims-- I mean prey. Are Beasts hypocrites? Maybe, but so are many of the Kin.<br /> <br /> Can't we give the guy a break? I don't mean to say we shouldn't express are opinions, but we can be realistic. We know why the revision would be less catchy, months vs. days. I don't get the outrage. From a handful of pages suddenly it is apparent that the whole rest of the book is invalidated? Ridiculous. I don't know what some people expected. Atavisms and Nightmares don't do it for you? Nope, they changed the Introduction section so they fucked up the whole book. One of your favorite parts is changed and I can understand somebody getting angry about it. I don't see how that destroys your image of the entire book. You must not have liked it that much then. I'm still not going to call you &quot;bro.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:31:37-07:00","id":554190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554137#post554137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading all the comments and opinions I'm starting to feel sorry for the developers. This game is becoming one hell of a headache to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right with you on that one. These people have slaved over their baby, gone back in an cut stuff out, while rebuilding other parts in an attempt to make it better. Let's not jump down their throats. I liked the first draft. I like what I've seen of the second draft, and I think they're going to knock it out of the park when all is said an done. The response I've seen has actually been overwhelmingly positive, and while I wasn't sold on everything 11 hours ago when I woke up, I think I've come all the way around to the changes that have been made. Hopefully others will too. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, one thing that really jumped out to me in the last hour is the role of the Beast as an educator. We can now actually do the Addams Family with Beasts. Before, they never really thematically fit, but now its perfect. The show has always been about a family that is different, but supportive and well meaning of one another. With the tweek in the Beast's role as a teacher (showing that different isn't always wrong) as well as the change in attitude towards Heroes (cause Gomez could never hate anyone anyhow) I really think its doable now, if a few shades darker than the show was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:34:23-07:00","id":554192,"title":"","content":"I think the first &quot;controversy&quot; was enough to give headaches. I think people are just punchy at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:39:16-07:00","id":554193,"title":"","content":"I didn't feel like the tone was &quot;irredeemable assholes&quot;, but that's my opinion. I'm not criticizing the tone of the rest of the book, just of the event that makes a Beast, well, come into their own. I'm trying to be fair and not judge the rest of the revisions beforehand, but I'm left a bit wary because the Homecoming was very defining for the book from my perspective. I do like the added importance of the Primordial Dream to humanity, for one.<br /> <br /> This must be an absolute headache to Matt and team. I have no doubts of that, and I wish it wasn't. It might be a necessary headache given the discussion Beast was surrounded by from early on, but that doesn't make any nicer.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to offer my piece as a fan in hopes that the final product is as fantastic as everyone hoped. Sometimes I may sound like a jerk because I'm getting too emotional about it. I apologize for those times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:47:55-07:00","id":554196,"title":"","content":"I am pleased about the role as Teacher, or Attendant of Fears.<br /> But i liked more the Homecoming genesis, really.<br /> <br /> The idea of Heroes as deluded men and women is great and hit hard the theme of self acclaimed role can be source of corruption.<br /> BUT.<br /> MORE WAY to handle the roles are a boon, not a bane.<br /> <br /> I like think as a four based type of characters.<br /> Beast (or Monster), Vs Hero (or Slayer): the difference is not based on the role of the horror story, but about the self awareness and self limit of the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-14-2015, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:54:10-07:00","id":554199,"title":"","content":"Well since I stayed out of every discussion of Beast barring, I believe, one comment a couple weeks ago, I don't think I'm coming in especially &quot;punchy&quot; at this point. I've merely stated where, I hope, Rich and Matt will see it, that I'm not a big fan of the Devouring when compared to Homecoming. Also, a major tonal shift in the introduction setting of a book does actually influence how the rest of the material is seen. I'm not decrying Beast as ruined, I personally left that to the initial folks who complained bitterly about aspects of the first draft (especially Heroes), but this looks like its going to become a very different beast (forgive the pun) during these rewrites and I'm not a fan of modern social media allowing people an outlet to bully authors/directors/etc into changing their visions. I personally feel Promethean is one of the best games I'll probably never run because the style of the game is very different from the sort of games I run, but I'd never have asked it to be changed to fit better with my play style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T06:36:09-07:00","id":554250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554137#post554137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading all the comments and opinions I'm starting to feel sorry for the developers. This game is becoming one hell of a headache to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, but I don't. Some people made an uproar(which I'd argue were in the minority, but hey), which then it was decided to make some revisions. The revisions that I thought were coming? Nothing like this. Not wholesale changes to the entire IDEA of what it is to be a Beast.<br /> <br /> This was not the game that was teased to us. This was not the game that was promoted by Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> And if, IF this was truly the game Matt wanted in the first place, then why were those teasers so far away from what we have now? Seriously.<br /> <br /> As someone else said, even the fiction doesn't make sense anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-14-2015, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T06:37:14-07:00","id":554252,"title":"","content":"My thoughts -<br /> <br /> I am personally glad Homecoming is gone. Its the same exact thing with Werewolves. You were born a wolf, you just didn't know it. And then, when you Changed that first time, you understood. You were finally in your true skin. Now, for some, this is fine on the surface, but it was an irritation to me - I like every supernatural having a unique origin. Not only that, though, but Werewolves actually supports that true skin idea - you not only shapeshift into a more comfortable animal form, but you can change your physical appearance or gender to something you feel comfortable in. You can even claim to be a werecyote, werejackle, or weredog if it suits you, instead of wolf. The symbolism is just deeper there. In Beast, it was lacking. The whole Family thing wasn't very strong with the Homecoming. It was just... there. There was nothing Family-like about becoming a Beast by realizing you were a Nightmare. The Homecoming did nothing for me, or the game, imho.<br /> <br /> I also like how we're emphasizing the nightmarish aspects of the game. Beast, while it had the Homecoming, meant that they were sadists. They were at home with spreading fear and terror, just because. Your Hunger drove you to be a petty tyrant, a thief, a destroyer without a moral compass. You don't have to play that way, but... well, you know what they say. Power corrupts, and absolute power corrupts absolutely. (Mage's themes.) Now, you could play the game by skimming over the darker parts and just use it to explore the WoD as a generic monster, but again, I feel like that was already covered by another game: Mage. That's the raison d'etre of the line - exploring the mysterious things in the WoD. And I don't really feel the need for that kind of overlap.<br /> <br /> Some people are bashing the new Beast direction because of the Lancea et Sanctum. While I did think of another game when I read the new Intro, my first thought wasn't vampire. It was Changeling's Autumn Court. And I absolutely love, love, love the Autumn Court. Now, we have an entire game that revolves around that kind of that theme, which is actually really attractive to me. And, before I'm accused of hypocracy, yes, I know I said I don't like reinventing the wheel with games. However, there's no other entire gameline with this focus, which changes things. Otherwise, would we ever need Werewolf: the Forsaken since we have Crone Gangrel? Or Prometheans since we have vampire Golconda chronicles? Clearly that didn't happen.<br /> <br /> Now, as well, we can have a Beast game without crossover if we wanted too as well. Which is good too.<br /> <br /> I also like how Saiety now reflects what kind of Beast you are - one who teaches by nightmares, or one who revels in the sheer power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-14-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T06:50:51-07:00","id":554256,"title":"","content":"Well I think I'm the only one who mentioned the Lancea et Sanctum, and another person mentioned the Scarecrow Ministry, but as I said before, the thing with those, they're a single aspect of their game lines. From my current reading Beast sounds like the central theme of the game is now playing Lancea/Autumn with a dash of Mage mystery exploration thrown in. These aren't necessarily bad, but it is a major tonal shift from the initial draft and I'm a little concerned as to how much will be changed. As some have already said, the change between Devouring and Homecoming is going to change a lot as a knock on effect throughout the setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:10:05-07:00","id":554266,"title":"","content":"The entire splat seems like it has become the Lancea Sanctum.<br /> I really enjoy the Lancea Sanctum, but there should be more encouraged options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:21:22-07:00","id":554269,"title":"","content":"Beasts are no more Lancea et Sanctum than Mages are Bone Shadows or Circle of the Crone. You can have a faction that emulates a splat's major themes without rendering them redundant. <br /> <br /> Like, maybe someone likes the Lancea et Sanctum idea, but doesn't feel it's appropriate to tack onto Christianity. I can think of a few reasons some Christians might be uncomfortable with the notion that God would do the things they claim he did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:32:34-07:00","id":554273,"title":"","content":"What was the central theme before? And &quot;punchy&quot; was a reference to the immediate reaction of the revision. Calmed down, mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:33:55-07:00","id":554275,"title":"","content":"Family &amp; Survival...<br /> It was more of an aspiration than a theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:49:00-07:00","id":554287,"title":"","content":"Family is sticking around. Was it reduced in any way? Survival is pretty much a constant theme in role playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:51:05-07:00","id":554288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554269#post554269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are no more Lancea et Sanctum than Mages are Bone Shadows or Circle of the Crone. You can have a faction that emulates a splat's major themes without rendering them redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The important thing is that Vampires have other word-count supported goals that they can choose, in addition to the Lancea Sanctum modus operandi. I really enjoy the Lancea Sanctum and have no problem with Terrorism being one of the driving societal goals of Beast.<br /> <br /> But there should be more options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:07:16-07:00","id":554315,"title":"","content":"Technically, it is two in one with the aspect. First you have inflict fear to teach others. Second you have learning about fear. Then you have the more mundane. Eat, live, support your family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:12:37-07:00","id":554317,"title":"","content":"I think I prefer Homecoming to Devouring, honestly.<br /> <br /> I haven't backed yet, and I'm not sure I'm going to. It's not so much that I dislike the new changes as I'm not sure how I feel about a project that might potentially keep switching horses mid-stream on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:30:15-07:00","id":554326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554199#post554199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well since I stayed out of every discussion of Beast barring, I believe, one comment a couple weeks ago, I don't think I'm coming in especially &quot;punchy&quot; at this point. I've merely stated where, I hope, Rich and Matt will see it, that I'm not a big fan of the Devouring when compared to Homecoming. Also, a major tonal shift in the introduction setting of a book does actually influence how the rest of the material is seen. I'm not decrying Beast as ruined, I personally left that to the initial folks who complained bitterly about aspects of the first draft (especially Heroes), but this looks like its going to become a very different beast (forgive the pun) during these rewrites and I'm not a fan of modern social media allowing people an outlet to bully authors/directors/etc into changing their visions. I personally feel Promethean is one of the best games I'll probably never run because the style of the game is very different from the sort of games I run, but I'd never have asked it to be changed to fit better with my play style.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If Matt had said he was changing his vision, you <i>might </i>have a point.<br /> <br /> As it is, that whole &quot;marginalized people metaphor&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Man Himself on RPGnet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had meant to do it, it would have been done better.</div> </div> </div> </div>So no, we critics didn't &quot;force him to change his vision&quot;, according to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:32:43-07:00","id":554327,"title":"","content":"The plan listed 8 changes. 5 are clarifications. 1 is something that was going to be added in a later book. 1 is completely new and I don't know about the last one. That means the switching is really from our point of view and not theirs. No idea if that affects a decision to back or not. Pretty sure everyone misses Homecoming, at least to an extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:33:53-07:00","id":554328,"title":"","content":"^^I said y'all were stretching with that one. A lot of us did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-14-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:44:56-07:00","id":554345,"title":"","content":"Well this has turned in a lovely little clusterfuck again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:53:10-07:00","id":554352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554135#post554135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@nalak42 I really wish you people would quit calling me disturbed and suggesting that I'm a terrible human being for thinking that non-harm done with consent isn't as morally reprehensible as harm done without it. I dropped the discussion. Would appreciate it not being brought up again.<br /> <br /> But then, that's the level of &quot;discussion&quot; this thread has taken for a while now, so I think I'll just quit visiting. I'm sure it'll make both of us much happier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't call you disturbed or say anything to that effect and have no clue where you got that idea. I said that situation got crazy and was explaining what happened because chair brought it up and thought you were arguing that unwilling feeding wasn't harmful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:12:23-07:00","id":554390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554326#post554326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If Matt had said he was changing his vision, you <i>might </i>have a point.<br /> <br /> As it is, that whole &amp;quot;marginalized people metaphor&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So no, we critics didn't &amp;quot;force him to change his vision&amp;quot;, according to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just by changing the introduction, the entire time and theme of the game have changed. That's a change in vision. <br /> <br /> Addiontional, why are you talking about &quot;marginalized people metaphor&quot;? It has nothing to do with what is being discussed. <br /> <br /> The problem with Beast being meant to teach lessons is not the goal of reaching lessons. The issue is no that the Beast chose to do so. The argument that, &quot; But they don't have to,&quot; while true, is irrelevant. By choosing to become a Beast after getting a &quot;mentor&quot; the option to not do if basically taken away. It's something you can do, but it will<br /> Make no damn sense. It would be no different then making a Hunter and then not hunting. <br /> <br /> It really all does boil down the changing from the Homecomong to the Devouring. It has nothing to do with the terms used but what they each represented. <br /> <br /> Further more, the Hungers no longer work. Beasts, according to the new introduction, feed off the catharsis caused by their &quot;victim&quot; gaining wisdom. This only reinforces that they will have to teach leasons to survive even if the Beast no longer wishes to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:13:41-07:00","id":554392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554345#post554345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this has turned in a lovely little clusterfuck again.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as everyone stays polite, what's the harm? Just ignore the parts of the discussion that annoys you. I think mos people are aware they won't cchange anyone's mind, no matter what aguments they present, good or not; that's just not how most people work. But it feels good to at leat express one's views, so tthe arguments will probably continue until the frustration goes away, which will probably mean that at least most of one side of the argument will lose interest in the subject and by association the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:21:53-07:00","id":554422,"title":"","content":"Everyone is making a fuss about this and I don't even see a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:24:05-07:00","id":554424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554392#post554392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as everyone stays polite, what's the harm? Just ignore the parts of the discussion that annoys you. I think mos people are aware they won't cchange anyone's mind, no matter what aguments they present, good or not; that's just not how most people work. But it feels good to at leat express one's views, so tthe arguments will probably continue until the frustration goes away, which will probably mean that at least most of one side of the argument will lose interest in the subject and by association the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were quite a few moments where it risked going off the rails, and I'm not wholly convinced we're intent on avoiding the cliff on the side of the road.<br /> <br /> But I'm a person still trying to overcome his innate pessimism with years of seeing these sorts of things happen who just woke up and has the unfortunate habit of being stupid in the morning even when I'm reading academic journals, so I might have the skewed view on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:35:33-07:00","id":554444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554424#post554424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were quite a few moments where it risked going off the rails, and I'm not wholly convinced we're intent on avoiding the cliff on the side of the road.<br /> <br /> But I'm a person still trying to overcome his innate pessimism with years of seeing these sorts of things happen who just woke up and has the unfortunate habit of being stupid in the morning even when I'm reading academic journals, so I might have the skewed view on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, someone is due to end up going too far, it's par the course for this kind of things. People got really invested emotionally, which makes us less likely to be obective and tolerant of others' opinions. But this isn't 4chan, we can expect at least some maturity about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:42:16-07:00","id":554451,"title":"","content":"A comment from the rpg.net thread on the new Beast/Hero dynamic that seems appropritate;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> &quot;rikalous&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I got from the new intro is that the actors are supposed to be on the same side, but now something's gone wrong and Santa's snapped and is trying to bash the Krampus's head off with a baseball bat from his sack because he's forgotten that they're both actors. So now Krampus, who takes his job seriously, is trying to get across the moral of the skit without getting splattered by Santa, except for the times when Krampus is being played by an asshole who just gets off on scaring kids. And while all this is going on the kids are working really really hard on ignoring Krampus and murder-Santa both in hopes that it'll make them go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:48:08-07:00","id":554457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554444#post554444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this isn't 4chan, we can expect at least some maturity about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now morbidly curious as to what the /tg/ thread for this looks like. *Dons HAZMAT suit*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:53:04-07:00","id":554461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554457#post554457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now morbidly curious as to what the /tg/ thread for this looks like. *Dons HAZMAT suit*</div> </div> </div> </div>You cray cray. Totally cray cray. You need at least three HAZMAT suits and a standard issue Indiana Jones fridge for that.<br /> <br /> Anyhow... Has anyone taken a shot at statting the Krampus as a Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:54:07-07:00","id":554463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554057#post554057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;A Character must be built around the themes of the game&quot; is a wrong premise?<br /> <br /> <br /> No. Doesn't count. She's not the one teaching the lesson, as Beasts are apparently supposed to do, she's the one learning the lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is if what you are assuming are the themes of the game aren't.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry if taking down prideful persons through physical means doesn't sound like teaching a lesson to you, but again, you don't seem to be understanding the book the way I do. I was giving you a reason why people would want to challenge that character's authority, not suggesting that she be the target of the lesson. Besides, you made her rich and cocky for no discernible reason, I just ran with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-14-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:56:59-07:00","id":554465,"title":"","content":"So I finally just finished reading the initial preview copy and (this has probably been said by others but) while I like the overall ideas and feel the text is trying to do too many things at the same time. The two biggest factors are the competing notions of monomyth and family. With regards to the latter, the preview goes to great lengths to integrate the other nWoD game's splats as &quot;kin&quot;, providing ample ammunition for the &quot;fitting in&quot; aspect of family. Unfortunately the flipside -- obligation -- is neglected in its entirety. Alot of missed opportunities for providing additional avenues and tools for game-play there. <br /> <br /> Similarly, while the nature of Heroes as these pseudo-humans is relatively well developed, any treatment of other denizens in the Primordial Dream as Heroes, the Gentry as Heroes (this is such an obvious one, dragon hunting is sport for them), and other supernaturals as Heroes is completely lacking. No deeper consideration for what monomyth means and plays out in a true-crossover WoD is developed and so as above, there are a lot of missed opportunities.<br /> <br /> Finally, the rule section for ephemeral beings (i.e., ghosts, spirits, and angels), just kind of sits in the middle of the text like a painfully large gall stone. While I get that all of the game lines are supposed to be specializations of the core WoD setting, using the same core rules, I don't think it's a good idea to include rules just for their own sake. What roles ghosts, spirits, and angels play in Beast are never actually suggested or even alluded to. This entire section could be replaced with another chapter that expands upon the game's core concepts of Family and Monomyth or, it could be replaced by a chapter that describes the other ephemeral beings that dwell in (and sometimes escape from) the Astral realms of the Primordial Dream, Temenos, and Oneiros.<br /> <br /> That's my 3-pence anyway. I'm looking forward to seeing how this project evolves and shape up. It'd be nice if it turns out to be something I have to tweak not at all (like V:tR 2nd ed) or only slightly tweak (like it seems M:tA 2nd ed is going to be). I do realize it's going to be impossible to match the peerless perfection that is W:tF 2nd ed but, one can hope. (I swear that game is like 1000-piece tool kit, so many endless permutations of the stories that can be told with it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:04:20-07:00","id":554486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554457#post554457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now morbidly curious as to what the /tg/ thread for this looks like. *Dons HAZMAT suit*</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably better for everyone's sanity not to think about it. \\tg\\ is the place where the Necronomicon came alive powered by sheer spite and malice, and with a pitiful whimper, promptly committed suicide in despair, faced with the horrible vision of its impotence and irrelevance in the face of bottomless nerd rage and fathomless bigotry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:05:52-07:00","id":554487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554390#post554390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just by changing the introduction, the entire time and theme of the game have changed. That's a change in vision.</div> </div> </div> </div> The entire tone of the game has shifted, yes. But we don't know if its a change in vision. This might be part of the vision that simply failed to be conveyed originally.<br /> <br /> Well, I think that the general shift is a good one, but only if they don't go too far. That's always a danger, over correcting, that is. <br /> <br /> What I'd love to hear is what the intention of this shift in tone is from the developers. What's the idea here, what their goals are, what is the actual vision that they wish to convey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-14-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:12:19-07:00","id":554490,"title":"","content":"I had problems with beast as written. I wasn't going to back it, as I'm cutting down on my spending, and realistically, I don't need another book i won't ever get to play. With the rewrites, I'm definitely not spending any money on it any time soon. <br /> <br /> I'm just throwing this out there - my opinions and a few suggestions.<br /> <br /> What I liked: Beast lets you play an &quot;other.&quot; An &quot;Other&quot; that has always been alienated, that has always known something was off, and then finally gets WHY. That speaks to me. Granted, I Didn't like the otherkin-tendencies.<br /> What I liked: Lairs. While I'm not a fan of them being mostly-inaccessible other-realm locations, the concept is great. Let me Take you to the Maze Of Leviethan &lt;/cenobite&gt;.<br /> What I Liked: Heroes as antagonists - cWoD captial-H Hunters with a purpose.<br /> What I Liked: Mythic nature, no mythic purpose - You Feed. I'm not a werewolf fan, so the &quot;hunt&quot; aspect doesn't overlap for me. I liked the variable reasons and ways a Beast fed.<br /> What I Liked: Much as I don't care for the seven deadlies, Feeding the Greed. Letting all that Wrath out. Envy leading to destruction. Letting lust devour them. Building something worthy of all-eclipsing pride.<br /> <br /> What I Didn't Like: Otherkin tendencies - Hear me out, I have a very specific reason - I Didn't want the gnostic &quot;I'm REALLY a Harpy in the Otherworld&quot; crap - I wanted physical transformation. I'm still annoyed that the nWoD (aside from vampires) doesn't like to let anyone BE a monster. Vampire powers are limited to animal forms, the crinos-equivalent has a timer, etc. I want MONSTERS. &quot;Timmy with spirit tentacles&quot; doesn't do it for me.<br /> What I didn't like: still seem stuck in the 5 x 5 grid.<br /> What I didn't like: the 3 &quot;Endings&quot; - Either become a physical monster(yay!) and get murdered (boo), become a dream-monster (boo), and get written out of the story (ugh), or Merge and become...written out of the story (Ugh^2).<br /> What I didn't like: Family as a theme - I don't see how this works. Legendary monsters may have lineages, but they're rarely encountered in small groups. Most stories apply something like the Conservation of Ninjutsu trope: One monster is a threatening rival. Five are a difficult, but not too-taxing encounter. A hundred are mooks to be mowed down on your way to the end-of-level encounter. Beasts should be End-bosses, not cluster-enemies. Most of the fiction I read felt like beasts were loners, stand-offish, and that makes more sense to me than a bubbly social butterfly flitting between branches of her Addams Family reunion.<br /> <br /> Now, with the revision:<br /> <br /> The &quot;Beastbrace&quot; - silly. Just silly. This kills the one thing that really spoke to me - &quot;You Are Not Them.&quot; A literal Soul-selling, for a role that makes no sense.<br /> The &quot;Teaching&quot; goal - This is... wrong. A person is not a lesson. I would not want to run a game where players are Anthropomorphic cautionary tales. WHY does the dark mother make children, just to teach these lessons? I can see this as a faction goal, but not a whole game. There has to be a better &quot;Goal&quot; for the splat. Survival would have worked just fine.<br /> The Heroes - I'm fine with them having a similar origin type to the beast- they can be humans with &quot;potential&quot; - But I think the original, &quot;You survived, and your brush with the primordial affected you with supernatural PTSD&quot; is superior. I was far happier with them as Driven, Angry, former victims. If they're a broken half of a humanoid Morality Play system, why haven't beasts lost their part of the task too? What is this lesson that was so important?<br /> The Big Brother/Sister Role - No. You want to be a transformational catalyst? you want to let your wife come with you into the Dark? That should be a possibility, but not the ONLY way.<br /> The Big Brother/Sister name - Awful. Sempai/Kohai is better. Mentor is better. Devourer is better. Hell, Soul-stealer is better.<br /> <br /> <br /> Suggestion: You need a name for the potential beasts/hunters, and they're your beast-ghoul type - Dreamwalkers or something. Oneiroprancers? Give these undifferentiated bedroom brain intruders a name.<br /> Suggestion: Have a supernatural force, an enemy for the Dark Mother - much weaker (or otherwise incapable of direct interference), but one that, like the Gods of old, Arms heroes, teaches them a few tricks, and sends them out after her with a Mistletoe Missile, Silver Athames soaked in virgin's blood, or some other Bane in hand. The Gods (or the Dark Mother's other &quot;family&quot;) may not strike against her and her work directly, but giving a few gifts to those already fighting her kind? No rules against making the game more sporting.<br /> Suggestion: Goal - Overall? Survive.<br /> Suggestion: Goal - Be the Enforcers of the &quot;Veil&quot;/Shroud/Etc. Be the force that keeps the supernatural apart from the Human. Be the Gauntlet. Plant the Hedge. Keep digging the abyss.<br /> Suggestion: Goal - A single splat being &quot;Teachers&quot; and &quot;Lessons.&quot;<br /> Suggestion: Give The Monsters The Power to Be Monsters. Physically.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":55,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/55-necrotek","user":"necrotek","date":". 06-14-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/55-necrotek","name":"necrotek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar55_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:14:11-07:00","id":554502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554068#post554068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't make it up, I went with what an other person said about the theme, and really, &quot;monster that teaches a lesson&quot; and &quot;monster from a cautionary tail&quot; is up, kind of different ways to say the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who?<br /> <br /> Second, no, they are not the same. A &quot;monster that teaches a lesson&quot; is a passive statement that implies that what the monster does must have a metaphysical weight, in the form of inspiring catharsis in its witnesses, whereas the &quot;monster from a cautionary tale&quot; is an active statement that implies that Beasts define themselves as taking a specific role in a narrative, and must live up to that role at all times. The latter is limiting and precludes certain character concepts, the former is not &amp; does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:20:00-07:00","id":554539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrotek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554490#post554490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I Didn't Like: Otherkin tendencies - Hear me out, I have a very specific reason - I Didn't want the gnostic &quot;I'm REALLY a Harpy in the Otherworld&quot; crap - I wanted physical transformation. I'm still annoyed that the nWoD (aside from vampires) doesn't like to let anyone BE a monster. Vampire powers are limited to animal forms, the crinos-equivalent has a timer, etc. I want MONSTERS. &quot;Timmy with spirit tentacles&quot; doesn't do it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an inherent requirement of the modern world setting - a Manticore wouldn't be able to interact with the world at all. And in all honesty, it thematically works with the Jungian themes of the game.<br /> <br /> That said: Achieve Incarnation! There you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:21:05-07:00","id":554542,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading the revised intro. I think it's mostly fine. <br /> <br /> As I believe has already been pointed out, some sense of the Beast's agency has been lost in the transition to the new draft. One possible solution would be to reverse who's soul is eaten in the Devouring. A Beast becomes a Beast not because they offer their soul up to be consumed but because they consume the soul of the thing that stalked them in their nightmares. This preserves the best things about the Homecoming and also adds the spice of the whole &quot;become the thing I fear&quot; trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:22:20-07:00","id":554543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554457#post554457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now morbidly curious as to what the /tg/ thread for this looks like. *Dons HAZMAT suit*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554486#post554486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably better for everyone's sanity not to think about it. \\tg\\ is the place where the Necronomicon came alive powered by sheer spite and malice, and with a pitiful whimper, promptly committed suicide in despair, faced with the horrible vision of its impotence and irrelevance in the face of bottomless nerd rage and fathomless bigotry.</div> </div> </div> </div>*pops head out of a mole tunnel*<br /> <br /> /tg/ actually tends to be one of the most pleasant and overall enjoyable boards from my experience. But dear lord the /wodg/ threads degenerate from uninformed opinions and powerlevel arguments into insults and toxicity really fast most of the time.<br /> <br /> Good luck venturing there, Elfive. Try not to be overwhelmed by its negativity.<br /> <br /> *pops back in and returns to waiting*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-14-2015, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:23:20-07:00","id":554544,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Beast have its own forum now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:24:29-07:00","id":554547,"title":"","content":"Do we have any idea when the rest of the updated preview will be released? After more time to come to terms with it, I'm actually looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:25:40-07:00","id":554549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554543#post554543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *pops head out of a mole tunnel*</div> </div> </div> </div> *gasp* <br /> Where's my mallot! Its whack-a-faith! <br /> *takes a swing*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *pops back in and returns to waiting* </div> </div> </div> *misses* <br /> Dang!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:27:40-07:00","id":554553,"title":"","content":"My idea is to play with the idea that &quot;consumption&quot; actually involves union (that's why its so often sexualized... just ask any given Vampire writer).<br /> <br /> Uniting the idea of the Homecoming with the Devouring - a potential-Beast carries a human soul AND a newborn horror since birth - or from some traumatic event that connected them with the Primordial Dream, allowing said horror to be lain within them. They can then go their entire lives without ever being realized - but sometimes on their own, but often with the guidance of another Beast, they eventually turn and embrace the horror as themselves in their nightmare and are &quot;devoured&quot;.<br /> <br /> So Bruce Wayne connected with the Primordial Dream, allowing a newborn Ugallu to be conceived into him when he was eight and saw his parents murdered. It persued him for the following decade +. Eventually another Beast (who depends on the continuity, but lets say Ra's) taught him to turn and embrace the bat, born from his own fear, ever pursuing him as himself, and his soul was consumed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:29:51-07:00","id":554559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554539#post554539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an inherent requirement of the modern world setting - a Manticore wouldn't be able to interact with the world at all. And in all honesty, it thematically works with the Jungian themes of the game.<br /> <br /> That said: Achieve Incarnation! There you go.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554539#post554539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an inherent requirement of the modern world setting - a Manticore wouldn't be able to interact with the world at all. And in all honesty, it thematically works with the Jungian themes of the game.<br /> <br /> That said: Achieve Incarnation! There you go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree that that's a requirement. If a werewolf warform works, a manticore works. If a changeling can have feathers, a manticore can work. <br /> <br /> Achieving &quot;incarnation&quot; doesn't do much good, if it kicks you out of the rest of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/55-necrotek","name":"necrotek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar55_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:29:53-07:00","id":554560,"title":"","content":"I'm actually alright with the &quot;beastbrace&quot; now. It's sort of a hybrid of the werewolf and vampire entry mechanisms, and it's thematic that something supposedly connected to all the other monsters takes a bit from each. Plus apparently there's debate among beasts themselves whether the Devouring replaced their soul or just reshaped it into the form it was always meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:31:37-07:00","id":554562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554543#post554543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *pops head out of a mole tunnel*<br /> <br /> /tg/ actually tends to be one of the most pleasant and overall enjoyable boards from my experience. But dear lord the /wodg/ threads degenerate from uninformed opinions and powerlevel arguments into insults and toxicity really fast most of the time.<br /> <br /> Good luck venturing there, Elfive. Try not to be overwhelmed by its negativity.<br /> <br /> *pops back in and returns to waiting*</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... not the memory I have of it. At all.<br /> You're perhaps more thick-sinned than I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:34:04-07:00","id":554566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrotek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554559#post554559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree that that's a requirement. If a werewolf warform works, a manticore works. If a changeling can have feathers, a manticore can work.<br /> <br /> Achieving &quot;incarnation&quot; doesn't do much good, if it kicks you out of the rest of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, so you are counting those, I thought you said they didn't count - ok, I can see the value of being physically a Manticore but having a human illusion over yourself ala Changelings, Prometheans, or Demons. I think at this point it was a desire not to be redundant with those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:45:10-07:00","id":554573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554566#post554566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, so you are counting those, I thought you said they didn't count - ok, I can see the value of being physically a Manticore but having a human illusion over yourself ala Changelings, Prometheans, or Demons. I think at this point it was a desire not to be redundant with those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am counting those. I can see where I might have been unclear, but I'm fine with even a timer ala werewolf. I just want a character that can actually BE a monster, at least part of the time. . <br /> <br /> I'm Ok with multiple forms. I'm OK with the &quot;illusion&quot; cover (and for demons, Cover is arguably not an illusion), if that's what gets me a real monster instead of a &quot;But my SOUL is a....&quot; Otherkin. I think the &quot;But my soul is a ....&quot; is what brings about the Otherkin problem in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/55-necrotek","name":"necrotek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar55_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:59:55-07:00","id":554581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrotek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554573#post554573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am counting those. I can see where I might have been unclear, but I'm fine with even a timer ala werewolf. I just want a character that can actually BE a monster, at least part of the time. .<br /> <br /> I'm Ok with multiple forms. I'm OK with the &quot;illusion&quot; cover (and for demons, Cover is arguably not an illusion), if that's what gets me a real monster instead of a &quot;But my SOUL is a....&quot; Otherkin. I think the &quot;But my soul is a ....&quot; is what brings about the Otherkin problem in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the &quot;draw down the Primordial Dream to don the guise of Horror&quot; angle is a little too restrictive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:13:53-07:00","id":554603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554581#post554581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the &quot;draw down the Primordial Dream to don the guise of Horror&quot; angle is a little too restrictive?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It smacks of the worst parts of awakening. It shouldn't be a guise. It's not supposed to be a mask. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/55-necrotek","name":"necrotek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar55_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:32:13-07:00","id":554621,"title":"","content":"Quoth the wise, wild Rose...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose, Kickstarter comments</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'd ask that we not get too hung up on the Devouring/Homecoming issue until you've seen a few more pieces of text... some of chapter one, and also chapter two. Because the idea that you can be both different and make a choice is going to figure in there.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:40:50-07:00","id":554624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554621#post554621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoth the wise, wild Rose...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for posting the quote in here.<br /> I've got my fingers crossed!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:05:40-07:00","id":554658,"title":"","content":"In looking at the original and the new intro, I've got a couple thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. The fiction that precedes the intro now makes very little sense due to the Embracey details of turning into a Beast.<br /> 2. Most of the overall Family motif in the book doesn't work very well if being a Beast isn't an inherent condition IMO. (and the Big Brother/Sister thing is somewhere between cheesy and creepy IMO)<br /> 3. I like the general idea of needing/wanting to behave as a corrective mechanism, but I'm uncertain this is the best way to phrase things.<br /> <br /> For my own games I'm probably going to treat them a bit like a mixture of C:tD and the Devil-Tiger Dharma from Kindred of the East. (The following is offered as both a suggestion to other Storytellers and potentially to Onyx Path as well. Feel free to use all or part of this however you like, I'm interested in improving the game, not fighting over IP rights.)<br /> <br /> A Beast is what they've always been, rather than something they are made. While some go through a Homecoming on their own, others are catalyzed similarly to a Hero when one of their cousins bumps up against their dreams and the recognition of kinship with the horror they see wakes them with a revelation of their true selves.<br /> <br /> The Hungers then, are half satisfying the monster you are beneath the skin and half about karma and forced perspective for the wicked. You are not merely a monster born from the collective depths of the most basic of human fears. A cursory glance might make it appear that way, but it is not so simple. More than simple fear is mixed into the Primordial Dream, there are other primal drives as well.<br /> <br /> For every person who has screamed in the grasp of a giant or been dragged beneath inky waves in their dreams, there is another who has toiled thanklessly under the lash of a pitiless master or been cast adrift by treachery or felt irreparably soiled by the touch of something repulsive lurking in a fairer guise. Someone who dreams of vengeance. Whose fantasies, waking or asleep, are filled with the terror of those who have wronged them. Their minds craft a champion of sorts, a monster who Hungers not for the powerless, but for the flesh and fear of the lesser monsters who have preyed on the weak.<br /> <br /> The Beasts are driven by their Hunger, an endless gnawing need that must be fed. When they are starving, even the smallest wrong is enough to satisfy. A small flicker of greed tugs at their mind, guiding them to the meager wealth of a man whose only crime was ignoring a panhandler that morning or blasting someone with the Nightmares of swimming through a sea of salty glass for having shouted at their children that morning. When fat on the pain of the deserving, only the choicest morsels will do... blood diamonds stolen from the private vaults of a remorseless magnate, stalking and tormenting a wealthy serial rapist until their terror forces a confession even their overpaid lawyers can't get them out of.<br /> <br /> Not all Beasts agree on what punishment fits a crime, not all agree on what even <i>constitutes</i> a crime. Most don't even consciously view their Hunger in the light crime and punishment anymore than the average person analyzes the exact reason they like oranges more than grapes, they simply prefer a certain flavor of fear and know how to get it. The billion scattered fears and hopes of humanity are hardly a unanimous chorus, and each Beast feels their Primal urges through the lens of their life before the Homecoming. Some are even so broken themselves, or formed from such distorted imaginings, that they Hunger simply for blood and shrieks, caring little for the lesson it might teach or the example to the rest of the herd.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heroes are their cousins in a sense, not born, but called into being when the currents of the Primordial Dream draw too near and break into their souls like a sudden unexpected wave. A Hero forms when a mind that cries out for vengeance, for agency, for the power to matter again is exposed to the wake of a monster who hungers for the wrongs the Hero suffered. In their scattered dreaming the Hero sees not an ally or an answer to their wish for justice, but a wrong given flesh. A young man sees in a sudden shock of what he mistakes for clarity, not the desire to batter and rend and despoil the uncle who molested him, but the embodiment of his pain. Not just <i>an</i> abuser but Abuse itself, a slithering hateful thing that sullies the world with its every breath. Helpless, hopeless, for too long the Hero knows what must be done. What THEY must do, because no other will see the thing for what it is until he has torn out it's heart to mend his own. Their connection to the Primordial allows them to strike out and reshape a vulnerable Beast to better match their personal narrative, rather than it's own. Their need guides them toward the weakness the Beast <i>must</i> have, as surely all foul things do. Nothing so vile could be perfect, could it? Anathema exist because if they did not, there would be little hope.<br /> <br /> Pain is a private thing, and so Heroes rarely work well together, but they frequently have the power to convince and gather others who have suffered similar fates to their own. An alcoholic might convince his AA group that perhaps there ought to be a new first step in their program. A recently jobless steel worker who has recently seen Greed far too close at hand speaks to his friends on their way to the unemployment lines. The homeless see Exposure, or Indifference, or Poverty and draw together the other forgotten to take back a chance at their lives.<br /> <br /> The threat of a Hero is a serious one, because humanity has always found it's strength in numbers and in certainty. Alone their powers are potentially dangerous but of little use against an entire Warren. With the aid of others though... weapons are easy to come by in the modern World of Darkness, and when they cannot be purchased or stolen, fire and stones have served mankind well since they first left the trees. A Beast may have the power to scour them with flaming breath or crush their minds in Nightmares, they find it sits uneasily with them at best.<br /> <br /> Whatever their true family, Beasts lived as humans once, and still live among them. Better by far to duel the Hero and what followers they may have found, to battle them closely and carefully, striving not to slay the would-be slayer, but to guide them back to sanity. To remind them that no matter how much blood they spill, there is no simple answer, no single foe to slay that will quiet the call of the bottle or the memories that make their skin crawl at the touch of a lover. Some are too far gone to hear reason, some simply develop a stronger grudge against the nemesis that will not obligingly die before their righteous assault... but others can be calmed and saved from a life of obsession and bloodshed.<br /> <br /> (Possible rules sidebar here: Only by defeating and <i>convincing the Hero of their error</i> can a Beast remove an Anathema placed on them. Killing the one who saddled them with the new weakness will make it a permanent part of the Beast, cementing the role of the defeated Hero in their legend as someone who once wounded them, paving the way for a later champion to succeed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":". 06-14-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:15:54-07:00","id":554662,"title":"","content":"Re: the above, I'm planning to frame the God-Machine and it's minions as something of an opposing force to the Beasts. It seems to me like the God-Machine has a vested interest in keeping the bulk of humanity toiling along on the fumes of hope and imagination it allows, conforming to it's grand design (whatever it is) but never stepping out of their place. It relies on the abusers and despoilers of the world to function as part of it's Infrastructure, a guiding mechanism to ensure the rest stays in line. Shaking that pattern isn't good for its plans, nor is something whose very existence is meant to rattle the bars of the cage it is making.<br /> <br /> Beasts and their cousins are bursts of color and strangeness in the grey oatmeal mundanity that is meant to drown the world, and they cannot be tolerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:17:52-07:00","id":554663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554542#post554542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished reading the revised intro. I think it's mostly fine.<br /> <br /> As I believe has already been pointed out, some sense of the Beast's agency has been lost in the transition to the new draft. One possible solution would be to reverse who's soul is eaten in the Devouring. A Beast becomes a Beast not because they offer their soul up to be consumed but because they consume the soul of the thing that stalked them in their nightmares. This preserves the best things about the Homecoming and also adds the spice of the whole &quot;become the thing I fear&quot; trope.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:30:19-07:00","id":554671,"title":"","content":"The idea of sell own soul and became a beast (but with a purpose of course) or combat the monster to become a hero ... could be less attractive of the old homecoming.<br /> Sell your soul Vs Accept your real self... mh!<br /> This is my 20 cents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Oh Matt: i LOVE your work, just saying ^^ )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:32:24-07:00","id":554674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who was critical of the earlier draft due to some issues of choice and compulsion, both for Beasts and Heroes, and appreciate the new Introduction and look forward to more, I have no idea how anyone could suggest than Beasts now have <i>less</i> self-determination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:33:48-07:00","id":554675,"title":"","content":"I'm going to give the rest of the revised material a chance to come out before I make any final decisions. But for the moment the new intro has moved me from planning to back to not. Honestly I just don't really care for the idea that becoming a Beast is a choice that you make. Nor do I like the idea that your soul is devoured and replaced by a horror. Regardless of the connotations of souls in the wider world of darkness. Beast doesn't make clear that &quot;Oh you're still you even though you don't have a soul.&quot; which I'll admit is never something that really clicked for me when I played Mage.<br /> <br /> All that aside. I do like the changes to heroes. Don't care for Devouring vs Homecoming. And don't really like the idea of whoever the big power in the city is encroaching on my lair. It just kinda removes a degree of the personal nature of it for me. Beyond that I do hope there is a lot more expanding on the Beast's purpose. Since at current saying they're all about teaching is well and good but that isn't reflected anywhere to me. I don't see how they do it or the like. Anyways just my thoughts. And my feelings after reading the intro compelled me to share in hopes they're seen. I hope that there's another rewrite of the intro as Beast as a game really clicked for me before and now doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:33:59-07:00","id":554677,"title":"","content":"I like Ninjar's suggestion from the kickstarter, of a human's Integrity setting the base Satiety potential of a feeding. Target moral and decent people and you're at far more risk of ending up with your Soul/Horror Slumbering. It means you'd be policing the worst dregs of humanity in a way, and potentially sterring ttem towards a better path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:36:57-07:00","id":554680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554671#post554671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of sell own soul and became a beast (but with a purpose of course) or combat the monster to become a hero ... could be less attractive of the old homecoming.<br /> Sell your soul Vs Accept your real self... mh!<br /> This is my 20 cents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Oh Matt: i LOVE your work, just saying ^^ )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A &quot;proto-Beast&quot; does not choose between becoming a Beast or a Hero. It appears Heroes are those who reject the wisdom of their nightmares and lash out.<br /> <br /> However, I'm still not sure of what happens to people who learn from their nightmares, are offered the Devouring, but still decline and keep their soul? Do they continue as before, forget everything that happened, become a tasty snack for the Beast who offered them the Devouring, or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:40:53-07:00","id":554684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554677#post554677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Ninjar's suggestion from the kickstarter, of a human's Integrity setting the base Satiety potential of a feeding. Target moral and decent people and you're at far more risk of ending up with your Soul/Horror Slumbering. It means you'd be policing the worst dregs of humanity in a way, and potentially sterring ttem towards a better path.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with this is that unlike the old Humanity stat, Integrity is a measure of how mentally stable and resilient you are, not of your morality. You can be a (relative) saint at Integrity 2-3, you'll just be a little nuts, where a person with Humanity 3 is by definition on the Baby Eating end of the Mother Theresa/Baby Eating scale of good and evil.<br /> <br /> You can't cleanly tie this sort of thing to a concrete stat anymore (which I think is a good thing, TBH) but I think people can and should give some form of bonus or penalty based on how much of a monster your 'meal' is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:45:54-07:00","id":554686,"title":"","content":"Right because choosing to reject the &quot;wisdom&quot; of fear is totally not a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:01:47-07:00","id":554724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554103#post554103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only read a bit of the last 8 or so pages. So please take my next statement in the spirit of co-operation and an attempt to understand.<br /> <br /> It appears that some members of our community are conflating the changes with other concepts which may or may not be effected.<br /> Beasts requiring another Beast to gain the template - Not relevant to name change.<br /> Beasts having to decide to become Begotten - Not related to name change.<br /> Heroes being connected to the Primordial Dream - has nothing to do with name change.<br /> Becoming Begotten is a sacrifice - <b>Is implied by name change</b><br /> Pod People - <i>Not a result of the name change but tightly connected, I grant you.</i><br /> Begotten being mini-bodhisattvas of the <a href=\"http://www.google.com.au/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0CB0QFjAAahUKEwijs4_y9o7GAhUkI6YKHVUzAGc&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwhitewolf.wikia.com%2Fwiki%2FAutumn_Court_%28CTL%29&amp;ei=EVF9VePmKKTGmAXV5oC4Bg&amp;usg=AFQjCNHzfigPBDGjHrfUVgfmvjWDUOzHcw&amp;sig2=p8dgh0ZnE9qSJ3OY84BflA&amp;bvm=bv.95515949,d.dGY\" target=\"_blank\">Autumn Court</a> - Not related to the name change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, um. Just becuase people are complaiing about the Name Change <i>and</i> the other stuff doens't mean that they're blaiming everything on the name change.<br /> <br /> It's just the whoel package that includes the name and the everything else about the devouring.<br /> <br /> And I don't see anybody complaining about heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:03:21-07:00","id":554728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554100#post554100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ask me, the old homecoming was as much a choice as the devouring is. A beast was always running from the monster in their dreams. Then they realize that they <i>are</i> the monster. At that point, they stop running. And the monster devours them, and they merge for the first time.<br /> <br /> What can happen now is that another beast can notice a nascent beast and tip them off that they need to stop running.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it never was. It wasn't a choice, it was a realization.<br /> <br /> And The Devouring isn't fluffed like &quot;helping an other Beast realize what they are&quot; it's fluffed like &quot;convince an otherwise ordinary human to become a beast&quot;, and that is not, at all, thematic compared to &quot;reincarnated monster soul realizing what it is&quot;:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:07:53-07:00","id":554733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554542#post554542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished reading the revised intro. I think it's mostly fine.<br /> <br /> As I believe has already been pointed out, some sense of the Beast's agency has been lost in the transition to the new draft. One possible solution would be to reverse who's soul is eaten in the Devouring. A Beast becomes a Beast not because they offer their soul up to be consumed but because they consume the soul of the thing that stalked them in their nightmares. This preserves the best things about the Homecoming and also adds the spice of the whole &quot;become the thing I fear&quot; trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Are you high?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:13:04-07:00","id":554738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554123#post554123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea et Sanctum don't disperse wisdom, they scare people into the arms of the Almighty like frightened sheep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, from a Religious Fundementalist perspective, is Dispensing Wisdom","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:18:04-07:00","id":554741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554738#post554738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, from a Religious Fundementalist perspective, is Dispensing Wisdom</div> </div> </div> </div>I-buh-wut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:22:13-07:00","id":554742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554135#post554135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@nalak42 I really wish you people would quit calling me disturbed and suggesting that I'm a terrible human being for thinking that non-harm done with consent isn't as morally reprehensible as harm done without it. I dropped the discussion. Would appreciate it not being brought up again.<br /> <br /> But then, that's the level of &quot;discussion&quot; this thread has taken for a while now, so I think I'll just quit visiting. I'm sure it'll make both of us much happier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody called you mentally disturbed.<br /> <br /> They merely pointed out that you seem to be under the impression that major blood loss is harmless, and the fact that a vampire getting genuine informed consent is incredibly unlikely.<br /> <br /> And again, in the old Document, it was entirely possible to feed without hurting people at all.<br /> <br /> &quot;Always inflicts a major injury&quot; is more harmful than &quot;doesn't even have to inflict injury&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:28:55-07:00","id":554749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554273#post554273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the central theme before?</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't one.<br /> <br /> It had multible themes: Explore Your Family, Explore the World, and Survive.<br /> <br /> This revision, instead of making them more prominent so you have something to do other than feed or crossover, through them out for something completly new, and that new centralized theme is incredibly restricting of character concepts.<br /> <br /> eally, an RPG should not have a single centralized theme that every character has to be built around, like this one does. A game meant for Crossovers definintly shouldn't, becuase then you can only have friendly relations with fraction of the supernatural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:33:08-07:00","id":554752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554658#post554658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In looking at the original and the new intro, I've got a couple thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. The fiction that precedes the intro now makes very little sense due to the Embracey details of turning into a Beast.<br /> 2. Most of the overall Family motif in the book doesn't work very well if being a Beast isn't an inherent condition IMO. (and the Big Brother/Sister thing is somewhere between cheesy and creepy IMO)<br /> 3. I like the general idea of needing/wanting to behave as a corrective mechanism, but I'm uncertain this is the best way to phrase things.<br /> <br /> For my own games I'm probably going to treat them a bit like a mixture of C:tD and the Devil-Tiger Dharma from Kindred of the East. (The following is offered as both a suggestion to other Storytellers and potentially to Onyx Path as well. Feel free to use all or part of this however you like, I'm interested in improving the game, not fighting over IP rights.)<br /> <br /> A Beast is what they've always been, rather than something they are made. While some go through a Homecoming on their own, others are catalyzed similarly to a Hero when one of their cousins bumps up against their dreams and the recognition of kinship with the horror they see wakes them with a revelation of their true selves.<br /> <br /> The Hungers then, are half satisfying the monster you are beneath the skin and half about karma and forced perspective for the wicked. You are not merely a monster born from the collective depths of the most basic of human fears. A cursory glance might make it appear that way, but it is not so simple. More than simple fear is mixed into the Primordial Dream, there are other primal drives as well.<br /> <br /> For every person who has screamed in the grasp of a giant or been dragged beneath inky waves in their dreams, there is another who has toiled thanklessly under the lash of a pitiless master or been cast adrift by treachery or felt irreparably soiled by the touch of something repulsive lurking in a fairer guise. Someone who dreams of vengeance. Whose fantasies, waking or asleep, are filled with the terror of those who have wronged them. Their minds craft a champion of sorts, a monster who Hungers not for the powerless, but for the flesh and fear of the lesser monsters who have preyed on the weak.<br /> <br /> The Beasts are driven by their Hunger, an endless gnawing need that must be fed. When they are starving, even the smallest wrong is enough to satisfy. A small flicker of greed tugs at their mind, guiding them to the meager wealth of a man whose only crime was ignoring a panhandler that morning or blasting someone with the Nightmares of swimming through a sea of salty glass for having shouted at their children that morning. When fat on the pain of the deserving, only the choicest morsels will do... blood diamonds stolen from the private vaults of a remorseless magnate, stalking and tormenting a wealthy serial rapist until their terror forces a confession even their overpaid lawyers can't get them out of.<br /> <br /> Not all Beasts agree on what punishment fits a crime, not all agree on what even <i>constitutes</i> a crime. Most don't even consciously view their Hunger in the light crime and punishment anymore than the average person analyzes the exact reason they like oranges more than grapes, they simply prefer a certain flavor of fear and know how to get it. The billion scattered fears and hopes of humanity are hardly a unanimous chorus, and each Beast feels their Primal urges through the lens of their life before the Homecoming. Some are even so broken themselves, or formed from such distorted imaginings, that they Hunger simply for blood and shrieks, caring little for the lesson it might teach or the example to the rest of the herd.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heroes are their cousins in a sense, not born, but called into being when the currents of the Primordial Dream draw too near and break into their souls like a sudden unexpected wave. A Hero forms when a mind that cries out for vengeance, for agency, for the power to matter again is exposed to the wake of a monster who hungers for the wrongs the Hero suffered. In their scattered dreaming the Hero sees not an ally or an answer to their wish for justice, but a wrong given flesh. A young man sees in a sudden shock of what he mistakes for clarity, not the desire to batter and rend and despoil the uncle who molested him, but the embodiment of his pain. Not just <i>an</i> abuser but Abuse itself, a slithering hateful thing that sullies the world with its every breath. Helpless, hopeless, for too long the Hero knows what must be done. What THEY must do, because no other will see the thing for what it is until he has torn out it's heart to mend his own. Their connection to the Primordial allows them to strike out and reshape a vulnerable Beast to better match their personal narrative, rather than it's own. Their need guides them toward the weakness the Beast <i>must</i> have, as surely all foul things do. Nothing so vile could be perfect, could it? Anathema exist because if they did not, there would be little hope.<br /> <br /> Pain is a private thing, and so Heroes rarely work well together, but they frequently have the power to convince and gather others who have suffered similar fates to their own. An alcoholic might convince his AA group that perhaps there ought to be a new first step in their program. A recently jobless steel worker who has recently seen Greed far too close at hand speaks to his friends on their way to the unemployment lines. The homeless see Exposure, or Indifference, or Poverty and draw together the other forgotten to take back a chance at their lives.<br /> <br /> The threat of a Hero is a serious one, because humanity has always found it's strength in numbers and in certainty. Alone their powers are potentially dangerous but of little use against an entire Warren. With the aid of others though... weapons are easy to come by in the modern World of Darkness, and when they cannot be purchased or stolen, fire and stones have served mankind well since they first left the trees. A Beast may have the power to scour them with flaming breath or crush their minds in Nightmares, they find it sits uneasily with them at best.<br /> <br /> Whatever their true family, Beasts lived as humans once, and still live among them. Better by far to duel the Hero and what followers they may have found, to battle them closely and carefully, striving not to slay the would-be slayer, but to guide them back to sanity. To remind them that no matter how much blood they spill, there is no simple answer, no single foe to slay that will quiet the call of the bottle or the memories that make their skin crawl at the touch of a lover. Some are too far gone to hear reason, some simply develop a stronger grudge against the nemesis that will not obligingly die before their righteous assault... but others can be calmed and saved from a life of obsession and bloodshed.<br /> <br /> <b>(Possible rules sidebar here: Only by defeating and <i>convincing the Hero of their error</i> can a Beast remove an Anathema placed on them. Killing the one who saddled them with the new weakness will make it a permanent part of the Beast, cementing the role of the defeated Hero in their legend as someone who once wounded them, paving the way for a later champion to succeed.)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would play a game with the bolded text as part of the mechanics, optionally or otherwise, and it wouldn't hurt my immersion one bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:33:31-07:00","id":554753,"title":"","content":"Erm... &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt?&quot; C'mon, dude, a central theme isn't <i>that</i> restrictive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:35:28-07:00","id":554760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554738#post554738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, from a Religious Fundementalist perspective, is Dispensing Wisdom</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect: no, it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:36:41-07:00","id":554761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554463#post554463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is if what you are assuming are the themes of the game aren't.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry if taking down prideful persons through physical means doesn't sound like teaching a lesson to you, but again, you don't seem to be understanding the book the way I do. I was giving you a reason why people would want to challenge that character's authority, not suggesting that she be the target of the lesson. Besides, you made her rich and cocky for no discernible reason, I just ran with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't word it as her teaching people a lesson. You worded it as though she was an undeservingly rich and arrogant person who deserves to be taken down a peg, and I took it as such. and &quot;I can kick anybody's ass&quot; is a good reason to be cocky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:39:17-07:00","id":554769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554749#post554749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There wasn't one.<br /> <br /> It had multible themes: Explore Your Family, Explore the World, and Survive.<br /> <br /> This revision, instead of making them more prominent so you have something to do other than feed or crossover, through them out for something completly new, and that new centralized theme is incredibly restricting of character concepts.<br /> <br /> eally, an RPG should not have a single centralized theme that every character has to be built around, like this one does. A game meant for Crossovers definintly shouldn't, becuase then you can only have friendly relations with fraction of the supernatural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does this new theme restrict character actions or concepts in any way? What can't they do now, but could do before? In fact, the new Introduction specifically discussed how some Beasts completely reject the &quot;teach through fear&quot; schtick, and there are no major organized social groups to enforce compliance. <br /> <br /> The new focus simply creates a paradigm somewhat unique to Beasts that gives characters a default motivation besides feeding and crossover, both of which had their own issues in the first draft. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:42:08-07:00","id":554788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554502#post554502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who?<br /> <br /> Second, no, they are not the same. A &quot;monster that teaches a lesson&quot; is a passive statement that implies that what the monster does must have a metaphysical weight, in the form of inspiring catharsis in its witnesses, whereas the &quot;monster from a cautionary tale&quot; is an active statement that implies that Beasts define themselves as taking a specific role in a narrative, and must live up to that role at all times. The latter is limiting and precludes certain character concepts, the former is not &amp; does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diferent forum.<br /> <br /> And really, that seems to be your own biases talking.<br /> <br /> The purpose of a cationary tale is to teach a lesson. The Purpose of the Monster in the tale is to enforce that lesson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:44:24-07:00","id":554790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554761#post554761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't word it as her teaching people a lesson. You worded it as though she was an undeservingly rich and arrogant person who deserves to be taken down a peg, and I took it as such. and &quot;I can kick anybody's ass&quot; is a good reason to be cocky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I only brought it up because Resources 4 on an a character focused on Unarmed Combat struck me as a little odd, but then again, it's not my character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:49:14-07:00","id":554811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Before, the Beast was a born that way, and got they powers when <b>they </b>realizied what they were.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>somebody else </b>chose to make you a beast, and you agreed to it. The simple fact that somebody else is involved now and had to make a decision before you get to make yours makes it a loss of agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:53:26-07:00","id":554817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554811#post554811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before, the Beast was a born that way, and got they powers when <b>they </b>realizied what they were.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>somebody else </b>chose to make you a beast, and you agreed to it. The simple fact that somebody else is involved now and had to make a decision before you get to make yours makes it a loss of agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>...are you high?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:59:35-07:00","id":554844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554811#post554811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before, the Beast was a born that way, and got they powers when <b>they </b>realizied what they were.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>somebody else </b>chose to make you a beast, and you agreed to it. The simple fact that somebody else is involved now and had to make a decision before you get to make yours makes it a loss of agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...<br /> <br /> What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:00:17-07:00","id":554846,"title":"","content":"Being born that way didn't grant agency. That was the whole point. You didn't choose to be a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:00:54-07:00","id":554847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554741#post554741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I-buh-wut?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lancea Et Sanctum is a Religious Sect, primary derived from Early Christianity but with factions based on other manifestations of the Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> The most active embers devote themselves to scaring mortals into accepting the Abrahamic God and His wisdom.<br /> <br /> So, from the perspective of a Fundamentalists Sanctified, scaring mortals into become good christians/muslims/jews/other religion based on the Abrahamic Faiths is giving them wisdom.<br /> <br /> I'd explain in more detail, but there's a massive chance that giving more details could lead me to accidentally offend someone, and that's something I've done before, and accidentally offending people is not fun so I won't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:02:36-07:00","id":554849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt, I want take take a second to say that I congratulate on your work thus far and continuing to navigate the dark waters to make Beast a stronger and better game line. Thank you for it.<br /> <br /> As for my feelings thus far, I'll sit upon my high mountain top of the mildly interested consumer and watch the ruckus below until the new version has been handed out.<br /> <br /> <br /> The white dog can come too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:04:01-07:00","id":554850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554753#post554753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt?&quot; C'mon, dude, a central theme isn't <i>that</i> restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not complaining about a central theme.<br /> <br /> I'm complaining about &quot;Beasts exist for the sole purpose of teaching mortals lessons&quot; to be far too restrictive of a Central Theme, when the before themes were more permissive to variety and really only needed to be expanded upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:12:30-07:00","id":554856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554847#post554847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea Et Sanctum is a Religious Sect, primary derived from Early Christianity but with factions based on other manifestations of the Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> The most active embers devote themselves to scaring mortals into accepting the Abrahamic God and His wisdom.<br /> <br /> So, from the perspective of a Fundamentalists Sanctified, scaring mortals into become good christians/muslims/jews/other religion based on the Abrahamic Faiths is giving them wisdom.<br /> <br /> I'd explain in more detail, but there's a massive chance that giving more details could lead me to accidentally offend someone, and that's something I've done before, and accidentally offending people is not fun so I won't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, dude, irregardless of my opinion of the validity or lack thereof (it's complicated), You need to stop, step away, and take a second to breath.<br /> <br /> 1)-, no, wait.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>1) You're running risks with the Forum Rules, and I don't want you to get kicked for this. I'M NOT A MOD, but I'm worried about you on these terms.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> 2) You aren't making sense. Lots of people are just now openly going &quot;What the hell are you talking about?&quot; in regards to this. You need to stop for a second and rethink how you're going to make your points, because we're getting lost in the logic.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to approach anything else you've brought, nor do I know if I want to. But I'm worried about you staying here, and I'm worried about how you come across, and I think you'd be well served to just take a breather.<br /> <br /> Like I advised everyone to do last night. And I will advise everyone do it again now. I think this will help us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:17:27-07:00","id":554859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554850#post554850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Beasts exist for the sole purpose of teaching mortals lessons&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not even close to being something the new intro suggests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:17:41-07:00","id":554860,"title":"","content":"So, I was going through my tumblr (don't judge) and I noticed I had accumulated a lot of art that was very Beastly in the years I've been there. Do you guys think we should make a character inspiration thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:18:26-07:00","id":554861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554860#post554860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was going through my tumblr (don't judge) and I noticed I had accumulated a lot of art that was very Beastly in the years I've been there. Do you guys think we should make a character inspiration thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:26:45-07:00","id":554870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554850#post554850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not complaining about a central theme.<br /> <br /> I'm complaining about &quot;Beasts exist for the sole purpose of teaching mortals lessons&quot; to be far too restrictive of a Central Theme, when the before themes were more permissive to variety and really only needed to be expanded upon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the first draft, there were really no central guiding themes or motivations. Beast fed and maybe engaged with other supernaturals for no clearly understood reasons. There was also no prominent reasons mechanically for a Beast to restrict their predations. That's precisely why Matt, Rich and others at OPP acknowledged the criticisms as valid and added the material.<br /> <br /> What you call a &quot;permissive&quot; setting, many others call absent, contradictory or little more than an unintentional foundation for juvenile and shallow revenge fantasies.<br /> <br /> In any event, nothing about this new theme restricts how you can play the game or portray Beasts. In fact, the Horror explicitly cares nothing about teaching, and simply wants to feast. A Beast can ignore or resist the Horror at their discretion. Beats can and may behave exactly as they did in the first draft, only now they might have some reasons not to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:28:55-07:00","id":554871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554769#post554769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How does this new theme restrict character actions or concepts in any way? What can't they do now, but could do before? In fact, the new Introduction specifically discussed how some Beasts completely reject the &quot;teach through fear&quot; schtick, and there are no major organized social groups to enforce compliance.<br /> <br /> The new focus simply creates a paradigm somewhat unique to Beasts that gives characters a default motivation besides feeding and crossover, both of which had their own issues in the first draft.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In this Paradigm, all Beasts exist to Teach Lessons.<br /> <br /> Meaning any character made either has to have a lesson they could teach, or, alternatively, must be built in a rejection of Teaching lessons.<br /> <br /> Furthermore,a Beast who doen'st teach lessons would be looked down upon by Beasts who do, which would be the majority if that's the purpose of the Beasts.<br /> <br /> For Comparison, a Changeling who done'st want to scare mortals away from dangerous places for their own good has how many Entitlements, other than Scarecrow Ministry, that they could choose from? Or just not take an Entitlement at all? Or hell, not even take a Court.<br /> <br /> I'd be fine if it was &quot;Some Beasts believe that their Purpose is to scare mortals in order to teach them lessons&quot; and teaching lessons was just a thing some Beasts did, among the other things Beasts did before, but as a central theme it leaves much to be desired.<br /> <br /> And you'd have to drop the &quot;ordinary humans who chose to be a monster when it's offered&quot; because that changes the tone a bit.<br /> <br /> Really, if it was just the &quot;Homecoming&quot; with you already having been a monster and just realizing it, but then you had a choice to accept what you are or deny it, with denying it meaning you stay &quot;mortal&quot; that right there would add character agency without shifting the tone.<br /> <br /> and the new social structure, the older Beasts helping younger beasts get used to what they are and teach them things, yeah, that could easily have been put in by just adding a &quot;Can tell when a nearby mortal is actually a little brother or sister about to come home&quot; power to Kinship or maybe as a merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:35:01-07:00","id":554876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554790#post554790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. I only brought it up because Resources 4 on an a character focused on Unarmed Combat struck me as a little odd, but then again, it's not my character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to create parallels between her Mortal Life and her Beastly Self.<br /> <br /> She's a dragon, and dragons tend to have massive hoards of gems and precious metals.<br /> <br /> In some stories the Dragon guards it jealously(Collector) while in others, in others, it's food, and in others it's s symbol of Status.<br /> <br /> Taylor's money is a sign of her status, and she really done'st care about it beyond that.<br /> <br /> The fact that her &quot;Dragons hoard&quot; in her lair is damaged by the extreme heat as well as the fact that it's made of every kind of precious or semi-precious metals, is paralleled back-Her soul doen'st care about it except that it's there and a symbol of her status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:39:59-07:00","id":554882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554817#post554817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...are you high?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very.<br /> <br /> The only reason a prospective Beast has a choice, is becuase somebody else made a choice to offer them that choice.<br /> <br /> Meaning the shift focuses from &quot;one day you don't run/fight back and thus learn that the monster has already been you&quot; to &quot;somebody else made you a monster&quot;<br /> <br /> That makes you a major reactor, instead of a minor actor.<br /> <br /> That's, depending on perspective, either a loss of agency, or at least a shift of agency in a diferant direction without changing it's value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:42:18-07:00","id":554885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554846#post554846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being born that way didn't grant agency. That was the whole point. You didn't choose to be a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a realization is still something you did.<br /> <br /> Now the choice is being offered to you.<br /> <br /> The only reason you have any agency in the decision is because somebody else offered you a choice.<br /> <br /> That puts the agency on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:46:34-07:00","id":554889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554859#post554859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not even close to being something the new intro suggests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then where did the thought come from? Because I got it from my extended discussion with Hexmeister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:48:42-07:00","id":554890,"title":"","content":"Agency is a conserved quantity. In order to increase the agency of the beast (making their transformation an entirely conscious choice) one must create some anti-agency as well (placing the onus of granting that choice upon another Beast). On a fundamental level, however, it all balances out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:51:16-07:00","id":554892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554856#post554856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, dude, irregardless of my opinion of the validity or lack thereof (it's complicated), You need to stop, step away, and take a second to breath.<br /> <br /> 1)-, no, wait.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>1) You're running risks with the Forum Rules, and I don't want you to get kicked for this. I'M NOT A MOD, but I'm worried about you on these terms.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> 2) You aren't making sense. Lots of people are just now openly going &quot;What the hell are you talking about?&quot; in regards to this. You need to stop for a second and rethink how you're going to make your points, because we're getting lost in the logic.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to approach anything else you've brought, nor do I know if I want to. But I'm worried about you staying here, and I'm worried about how you come across, and I think you'd be well served to just take a breather.<br /> <br /> Like I advised everyone to do last night. And I will advise everyone do it again now. I think this will help us.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Should I try to claify what I meant, or should I just drop this particular tangent about the Sanctified spreading Wisdom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:52:35-07:00","id":554893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554890#post554890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agency is a conserved quantity. In order to increase the agency of the beast (making their transformation an entirely conscious choice) one must create some anti-agency as well (placing the onus of granting that choice upon another Beast). On a fundamental level, however, it all balances out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it balances out to roughly the same amount of agency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:55:18-07:00","id":554894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554547#post554547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any idea when the rest of the updated preview will be released? After more time to come to terms with it, I'm actually looking forward to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As soon as it can be written/rewritten. They might not release updates of the entire thing. Many whole chapters would only have some name changes. There is still the promised culture/society, primordial dream, and hero parts to look forward to. Exciting stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:58:18-07:00","id":554899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554892#post554892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Should I try to claify what I meant, or should I just drop this particular tangent about the Sanctified spreading Wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I were you I'd probably just drop it. Potentially a super touchy subject to begin with, and people are already a touchy at the moment. Better to just leave it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:59:56-07:00","id":554901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it makes you feel better, I think Beasts have <i>gained</i> agency. Tonally I would say they gained it in spades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:00:14-07:00","id":554902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554892#post554892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Should I try to claify what I meant, or should I just drop this particular tangent about the Sanctified spreading Wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should rethink how you want to go about arguing the similarity between the Sanctified spreading wisdom at the least. I don't agree with you, at least on a one-to-one, but I think this opinion matters to you. But I think you need to rethink how you approach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:02:33-07:00","id":554904,"title":"","content":"For those who are interested, Matt gave a short interview on Gamer-XP about Beast, including the new revisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__ur