/div> </div>Weren't you saying something about cliffs earlier? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;...are you high?&quot;<br /> re: &quot;not very.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have to say thank you. I couldn't stop laughing for 5 minutes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-14-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:15:45-07:00","id":554912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554902#post554902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should rethink how you want to go about arguing the similarity between the Sanctified spreading wisdom at the least. I don't agree with you, at least on a one-to-one, but I think this opinion matters to you. But I think you need to rethink how you approach it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna drop it.<br /> <br /> I cna't think of a way to explain my point without accidentally offending people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:20:06-07:00","id":554914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554547#post554547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any idea when the rest of the updated preview will be released? After more time to come to terms with it, I'm actually looking forward to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Rose and Matt, they'll be up by Friday if all goes well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:26:58-07:00","id":554935,"title":"","content":"Why does everything have to go up when I'm working! Oh, yeah, because my schedule doesn't make any sense. It's good that all this happened now, for all the turbulence it's caused, with all the time we still have left on the kickstarter. Though I'm not sure the changes have made much of difference in it's progress. After the release of the edited preview it felt like what little was lost was quickly recovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:34:47-07:00","id":554940,"title":"","content":"As to &quot;Agency re: Devouring&quot;, I think there are two different kinds of agency getting confused here: Player agency and character agency.<br /> <br /> <i>Character</i> agency has been expanded with the change from Homecoming to Devouring, as the character has now <i>chosen</i> their Beastly state, and a character can choose to accept or refuse the &quot;gift&quot; of the Devouring.<br /> <i>Player</i> agency, however, has arguably diminished, as now you have to play a character that chose the life of a Beast, with all attendant features. Quite frankly, the deal itself is damn near Faustian, and either the Beast didn't disclose all the terms of Beast-hood to the proto-Beast, or the person is the kind of person that's totally fine becoming a spirit-monster that feeds on the fear of others. So you're basically stuck playing the fool, or somebody who willingly chooses to become a monster.<br /> <br /> I think that maybe Homecoming and Devouring should both be present. Marrying into the family, vs. being born into it.<br /> <br /> <b>Unrelated tangent:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not to mention, your soul is being <i>annihilated and replaced with a monster</i>. I'm frankly amazed that what comes out of something like that resembles the original person in any way, to the point that it somewhat stretches my suspension of disbelief.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:53:56-07:00","id":554951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554940#post554940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unrelated tangent:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not to mention, your soul is being <i>annihilated and replaced with a monster</i>. I'm frankly amazed that what comes out of something like that resembles the original person in any way, to the point that it somewhat stretches my suspension of disbelief.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>You have to remember that in NWoD your soul is not the seat of your ego. It is an important part of what makes humans Human but is not the core of your identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:06:27-07:00","id":554953,"title":"","content":"If Mage cosmology is applied, while souls are important, they're still entirely fungible, even for those possessing &quot;important&quot; souls like mages.<br /> <br /> You are still you in the nWOD, even without a soul, and any potential diminishment from soul loss is ameliorated by the Horror replacement. In fact, many would consider it a soul &quot;upgrade,&quot; particularly those people who are the proto-Beasts and accepted and learned from their nightmares, since you now will gain some nifty new powers. It's nothing like the bargains from Demon or other mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:07:32-07:00","id":554954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554951#post554951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to remember that in NWoD your soul is not the seat of your ego. It is an important part of what makes humans Human but is not the core of your identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is true, but the way I see it is that if you swap out the engine of your car for a jet turbine, it's gonna be a fundamentally different ride, and if switch the OS on your computer, you're going to have different sets of features, and possibly run into compatibility issues with old software.<br /> <br /> Also, the bastards will want you to connect your computer account to an email account <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and they send your data to a shoe company in Hong Kong, <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and suddenly cartoon you is hawking knockoff Reeboks made by child workers, then you get sued when the shoes explode and radda radda radda...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:14:15-07:00","id":554970,"title":"","content":"They need to clarify if the Horror consumes and replace your soul or if the Horror joins with and creates a new soul as a result. The text says both and they need to make up its mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 06-14-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:24:04-07:00","id":554972,"title":"","content":"Both, neither, not even beasts know. *Fistfight ensues*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:27:27-07:00","id":554974,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure it consumes your soul and joins with you. Your Soul is more like an item of clothing for your consciousness than the source of <i>you </i>and all that. It might be an item of clothing your consciousness needs to function normally, but you can live without it. It sounds like the Horror devours your soul and sort of replaces it. The Horror is sort of like a soul too, I guess. I wonder how magic around the soul might interact with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:27:29-07:00","id":554975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554970#post554970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need to clarify if the Horror consumes and replace your soul or if the Horror joins with and creates a new soul as a result. The text says both and they need to make up its mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the difference is immaterial. A Beast no longer has a <i>human</i> soul. <br /> <br /> The difference is little more than theological interest, and similar inquiries could be made about changeling, vampire and werewolf &quot;souls,&quot; that even mages cannot answer, despite their setting-specific knowledge of the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:29:20-07:00","id":554977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554972#post554972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both, neither, not even beasts know. *Fistfight ensues*.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Breaks bottle, walks up to Elfive.*<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can live with that, leaving it canonically ambiguous and providing in-character explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:30:42-07:00","id":554978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of it as a limitation on agency, but it is definitely a psychological shift.<br /> <br /> Previously, Beasts were born and discovered who they were: This means every Beast must ask themselves difficult questions about the morality of their survival.<br /> Currently, Beasts must choose to become Beasts: This means every Beast has already made a Faustian bargain to gain power from terrorism.<br /> Though it's certainly possible your teacher lied to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:37:59-07:00","id":554984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554978#post554978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think of it as a limitation on agency, but it is definitely a psychological shift.<br /> <br /> Previously, Beasts were born and discovered who they were: This means every Beast must ask themselves difficult questions about the morality of their survival.<br /> Currently, Beasts must choose to become Beasts: This means every Beast has already made a Faustian bargain to gain power from terrorism.<br /> Though it's certainly possible your teacher lied to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This choice strongly disassociates Beasts as analogous to certain oppressed minority groups, with all the very negative baggage and troublesome connotations that implied, and purportedly wasn't the intention of Matt and the other writers.<br /> <br /> I personally believe this change is a notable improvement, and prevents Beast from becoming little more than a disturbing revenge fantasy, all without altering any of the intrinsic horror of the first draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:40:53-07:00","id":554986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554984#post554984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This choice strongly disassociates Beasts as analogous to certain oppressed minority groups, with all the very negative baggage and troublesome connotations that implied, and purportedly wasn't the intention of Matt and the other writers.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Like Werewolves?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:47:53-07:00","id":554987,"title":"","content":"Werewolves get away with it because they're an established monster and also because their primary antagonists are both werewolves themselves and basically nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:59:56-07:00","id":555005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554986#post554986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Like Werewolves?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all splats have to represent all things. Every spat need not be a metaphor for oppressed, minority or alienated people. <br /> <br /> Beast deals with subjects often more realistic and personal than other splats, and therefore had greater risk of offense. In real life, people do not shapeshift, spirits do not possess people, no one of sound mind drinks blood, etc. However, we all have nightmares, and are well acquainted with the perils of bullying and abuse in its myriad forms, These subjects are certainly part of the horror genre and narrative, but were not handled well in the first draft. They were encouraged without mechanical restraint. Now, the terror at least has a default purpose and Beasts have a identifiable motivation and reason to not always be sadistically terrible, just like most other splats. <br /> <br /> Beasts in the first draft are also inimical by their very existence and apart from their actions. If they represented oppressed groups, the implications are extremely troubling to say the least, and certainly not what Matt would ever intend to convey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:05:36-07:00","id":555006,"title":"","content":"Plus, in the World of Darkness if you want to play a minority or whatever you can just <i>do </i>that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:09:59-07:00","id":555010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555006#post555006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, in the World of Darkness if you want to play a minority or whatever you can just <i>do </i>that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now, that's just crazy talk...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:15:10-07:00","id":555013,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is someone else's baby. I think Beasts were intended to be outsiders, but in a broad sense that most people could relate to. Readers started to identify Beasts with groups and Heroes too. It seemed like people were elevating the characters to symbolic representations of groups. I think it was realized that Matt could not continue to create his game if he had to worry about offending people by &quot;misrepresenting&quot; or &quot;bashing&quot; their symbols. People brought that into the game and it wasn't on a personal level. It was supposed to be the individual player identifying with the outsider concept. That just wasn't working out. Some people liked the way it was, but since they would not have felt comfortable continuing to make the game, it would have screwed over everyone that wants to play Beast. I don't like the dilution but I understand and agree with the decision, from that perspective. It isn't about the critics in this case, but the people that were so vocally supportive. The game just didn't come across as intended in some ways. No choice but to change it. Better now than later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:26:43-07:00","id":555034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555013#post555013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game just didn't come across as intended in some ways. No choice but to change it. Better now than later.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons open development was instituted was to listen to customer feedback and improve game quality for everyone. Although it's unlikely that Matt and Rich anticipated such a &quot;diverse&quot; and &quot;expressive&quot; level of criticism about Beast, I commend them for acknowledging it and seeking to improve the product. If successful, they will have strongly demonstrated OPP's commitment to their fans and improved the marketability and saleability of Beast.<br /> <br /> Godspeed and I look forward to reading the other revisions to the draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:35:50-07:00","id":555042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555005#post555005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have a identifiable motivation and reason to not always be sadistically terrible, just like most other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>The change actually seems to encourage more sadism than before, but I can absolutely understand the need to avoid having too many accidental similarities to certain oppressed groups for the sake of human decency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:40:39-07:00","id":555044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555042#post555042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The change actually seems to encourage more sadism than before, but I can absolutely understand the need to avoid having too many accidental similarities to certain oppressed groups for the sake of human decency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although not perfect, the nature of monster myths as cautionary tales makes the teaching through fear theme understandable and relatable. The potential risk and inherent abuse of using fear to teach potentially enhances role-playing opportunities, and unlike before, at least provides a reason why Beasts might not be slavishly sadistic all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:43:05-07:00","id":555046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554977#post554977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Breaks bottle, walks up to Elfive.*</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys are goofy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:00:34-07:00","id":555073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555044#post555044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and unlike before, at least provides a reason why Beasts might not be slavishly sadistic all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually do not understand where you are getting this. It seems to be the opposite to me. The majority of Beasts agreeing to teach lessons through terrorism seems to enhance the potential for sadism, instead of a theoretically larger number of Beasts who would do the minimum amount of terrorism needed to survive in the previous version and the theoretically less malicious psychology. Could you explain your thoughts on this further?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:03:26-07:00","id":555076,"title":"","content":"People will choose against their interests as long as they believe they have a choice. Players need to feel like they control their character's level of sadism at all times. As long as that feeling is there, they can go torture porn if they want. Personally, not my bag, but to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:09:36-07:00","id":555079,"title":"","content":"So basically a case of &quot;Human psychology is fucked up?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:10:24-07:00","id":555080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555073#post555073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually do not understand where you are getting this. It seems to be the opposite to me. The majority of Beasts agreeing to teach lessons through terrorism seems to enhance the potential for sadism, instead of a theoretically larger number of Beasts who would do the minimum amount of terrorism needed to survive in the previous version and the theoretically less malicious psychology. Could you explain your thoughts on this further?</div> </div> </div> </div>The connection of rampages with &quot;you are doing a shitty job at teaching a deeper lesson,&quot; taken in combination with the basic structure of &quot;higher Satiety necessitates more particular meals&quot; suggests a greater degree of care is culturally incentivized along with more regular use of Family Dinner in the company of other Begotten.<br /> <br /> The Devouring model is presented as a cultural framework built to mediate the less inherently exacting standards of the Horror rather than as a change in the metaphysics and fundamental psychology of the Begotten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555079#post555079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically a case of &quot;Human psychology is fucked up?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/baddreams.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-14-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:23:13-07:00","id":555088,"title":"","content":"Family Dinner is another thing, now that we have this whole &quot;Beast as Teacher&quot; paradigm introduced.<br /> <br /> Why would that feed your hunger? What lesson are you teaching by watching somebody chew on somebody else?<br /> <br /> I mean, you could argue that you're getting the leftover catharsis of learning something like &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot;, but that's outstandingly flimsy. What does anybody learn from watching a former dead guy stand in a lightning storm?<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, I'm adding &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot; to my sig, because it is my greatest thing that I have said ever in any context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:27:47-07:00","id":555090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555088#post555088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family Dinner is another thing, now that we have this whole &quot;Beast as Teacher&quot; paradigm introduced.<br /> <br /> Why would that feed your hunger? What lesson are you teaching by watching somebody chew on somebody else?<br /> <br /> I mean, you could argue that you're getting the leftover catharsis of learning something like &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot;, but that's outstandingly flimsy. What does anybody learn from watching a former dead guy stand in a lightning storm?<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, I'm adding &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot; to my sig, because it is my greatest thing that I have said ever in any context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to the new Introduction, a Beast does not need to teach any lesson in order to feed. In fact, the Horror does not care about anything but feasting on fear, which Family Dinner is generally capable of providing.<br /> <br /> We also don't know if Matt intends to make any changes to the Family Dinner fluff or crunch. Your concerns might very well be addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:37:25-07:00","id":555091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555090#post555090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to the new Introduction, a Beast does not need to teach any lesson in order to feed. In fact, the Horror does not care about anything but feasting on fear, which Family Dinner is generally capable of providing.<br /> <br /> We also don't know if Matt intends to make any changes to the Family Dinner fluff or crunch. Your concerns might very well be addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair 'Nuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:45:07-07:00","id":555094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555088#post555088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family Dinner is another thing, now that we have this whole &quot;Beast as Teacher&quot; paradigm introduced.<br /> <br /> Why would that feed your hunger? What lesson are you teaching by watching somebody chew on somebody else?<br /> <br /> I mean, you could argue that you're getting the leftover catharsis of learning something like &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot;, but that's outstandingly flimsy. What does anybody learn from watching a former dead guy stand in a lightning storm?<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, I'm adding &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man&quot; to my sig, because it is my greatest thing that I have said ever in any context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you get to count it as being taught the lesson, in which case I vote the lesson be learning to delegate responsibility is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:49:27-07:00","id":555098,"title":"","content":"The teaching is a social thing rather than a nature thing. The millenia of evaluation lead to the inclination that it's for the best for Beasts to be Teachers with their Hungers.<br /> <br /> The Horror eats, the Beast teaches, in short.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I have no idea what's happening in this thread anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:56:22-07:00","id":555100,"title":"","content":"The in character Beast perspective on watching others feed would be to learn about the fear the Kin are supposed to teach. The others exist to perpetuate fear as well. They have lost touch with whatever lesson they were meant to impart. A Beast would figure out what lesson a werewolf is supposed to teach people. It may be &quot;don't be unlucky and get dead by a wolf-man.&quot; Nobody has the answer to that one. Beasts are not just teachers of fear, they are students as well. They just can't learn like a human can. They need Family to teach them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:12:45-07:00","id":555105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555080#post555080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The connection of rampages with &quot;you are doing a shitty job at teaching a deeper lesson,&quot; taken in combination with the basic structure of &quot;higher Satiety necessitates more particular meals&quot; suggests a greater degree of care is culturally incentivized along with more regular use of Family Dinner in the company of other Begotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>The need to teach a lesson suggests a longer than necessary amount of time spent on any individual nightmare in order to teach said lesson. This, in combination with the psychology inherent in being the kind of person who would make the choice to terrorize others in exchange for power (even if that power is rationalized as making you better at teaching lessons), suggests far more sadistic predator mentalities on average than the previous version.<br /> <br /> Interesting thoughts on how a more involved society would reduce the number of sloppy feedings due to Family Dinner, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:25:18-07:00","id":555109,"title":"","content":"Someone linked this earlier, and I just finished reading it : <a href=\"http://www.gamer-xp.com/understanding-the-monsters-interview-with-beast-the-primordial-creator-matthew-mcfarland/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gamer-xp.com/understandin...hew-mcfarland/</a><br /> <br /> After everything, it still does feel like the main thrust of the game is going to revolve around dealing with other supernatural critters as antagonists and counterpoints. Even more than Heroes and other Beasts, especially when Heroes are still feeling like extremist hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:42:35-07:00","id":555127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555109#post555109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone linked this earlier, and I just finished reading it : <a href=\"http://www.gamer-xp.com/understanding-the-monsters-interview-with-beast-the-primordial-creator-matthew-mcfarland/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gamer-xp.com/understandin...hew-mcfarland/</a><br /> <br /> After everything, it still does feel like the main thrust of the game is going to revolve around dealing with other supernatural critters as antagonists and counterpoints. Even more than Heroes and other Beasts, especially when Heroes are still feeling like extremist hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Matt gives a better explanation of the Teaching thing, which oddly enough, doesn't seem to invalidate anything from the first draft, to me at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:43:32-07:00","id":555128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555105#post555105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The need to teach a lesson suggests a longer than necessary amount of time spent on any individual nightmare in order to teach said lesson. This, in combination with the psychology inherent in being the kind of person who would make the choice to terrorize others in exchange for power (even if that power is rationalized as making you better at teaching lessons), suggests far more sadistic predator mentalities on average than the previous version.<br /> <br /> Interesting thoughts on how a more involved society would reduce the number of sloppy feedings due to Family Dinner, though!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By this, are you saying you prefer Beasts to be less sadistic, or to use a more neutral term, monstrous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:47:36-07:00","id":555130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555109#post555109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone linked this earlier, and I just finished reading it : <a href=\"http://www.gamer-xp.com/understanding-the-monsters-interview-with-beast-the-primordial-creator-matthew-mcfarland/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gamer-xp.com/understandin...hew-mcfarland/</a><br /> <br /> After everything, it still does feel like the main thrust of the game is going to revolve around dealing with other supernatural critters as antagonists and counterpoints. Even more than Heroes and other Beasts, especially when Heroes are still feeling like extremist hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In light of the time frame and word count, I did not have any reasonable expectation that we would suddenly receive a whole new panopoly of new antagonists with the revisions. Hopefully, we'll see more in any sourcebooks. Besides, there's enough work to be done to improve the current material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:51:51-07:00","id":555138,"title":"","content":"I was told Beast will have supplements. I think the additional stuff about the Primordial Dream was planned to be in one, but they thought it would be better to pull it in now after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:53:29-07:00","id":555139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555127#post555127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Matt gives a better explanation of the Teaching thing, which oddly enough, doesn't seem to invalidate anything from the first draft, to me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, no. It seems pretty easy to drop the parts of Beast culture you don't like. Heroes still feel like hunters, and so on. Still a tonal change, but I don't think there's anything that's more restrictive than before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:01:51-07:00","id":555144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555130#post555130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In light of the time frame and word count, I did not have any reasonable expectation that we would suddenly receive a whole new panopoly of new antagonists with the revisions. Hopefully, we'll see more in any sourcebooks. Besides, there's enough work to be done to improve the current material.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, but I was thinking more that Heroes, despite everything, really won't make a very good long-term campaign on their own. They're best when used subtly instead of directly (mostly because they'll die). Even with an expanded Beast culture, I can't imagine we'll have something on par with the Seers or Pure as antagonists.<br /> <br /> Its a crossover game, the vast chunk of mechanics revolve around dealing with other supernaturals (followed by the Lair) in some way. When all is said and done, that makes it the most important thing in a Beast game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:15:45-07:00","id":555148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555138#post555138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was told Beast will have supplements. I think the additional stuff about the Primordial Dream was planned to be in one, but they thought it would be better to pull it in now after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Some of it maybe. I still bet we get a supplement on the Primordial Dream. Too rich of a ground not to give it its own book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:19:08-07:00","id":555149,"title":"","content":"Well I guess one could use the Incarnate, Unfettered and Rampant as antagonists as well. And who knows what we can get with the Primordial Dream being expanded on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:21:50-07:00","id":555151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555128#post555128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By this, are you saying you prefer Beasts to be less sadistic, or to use a more neutral term, monstrous?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't made any value statements yet, and I have not yet decided which version I like more. I feel like we have traded accidental comparison to oppressed minorities to accidental comparison to religion, especially with the similarities to Lancea et Sanctum mentioned previously. Not better or worse, but different flavor entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:26:06-07:00","id":555152,"title":"","content":"I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:32:19-07:00","id":555159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554904#post554904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who are interested, Matt gave a short interview on Gamer-XP about Beast, including the new revisions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.gamer-xp.com/understanding-the-monsters-interview-with-beast-the-primordial-creator-matthew-mcfarland/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gamer-xp.com/understandin...hew-mcfarland/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This interview makes me think, that I in fact didn't understand what the writers wanted to do with the game.<br /> <br /> A lot more accent is put on causing fear, making it clear that the writers want this to be a central par of the game. The 1st draft really made it more an option than an obligation: here Matt states clearly that it is something Beast have to do to feed their Horrors. I guess I'll see how it impacts the game's mechanics, to see if it's more than fluff I could ignore. <br /> <br /> Other Beasts opposing you for not bothering with the teaching thing is now a major source of antgonism? That feels kind of oppressive in a cWoD Camarilla kind of way (this is not necessarily a bad thing, I love V:tM). I didn't peg Beast society as being this cohesive.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they wanted to do things like this from the start but failed at first, or if they changed their original intent because of the critics. In any case, I feel disconnected from the product Matt describes in the interview. I'm going to stick around until we get more substantial material to objectively evaluate the changes, but I've truly lost all the exitation I felt at the 1st Draft release.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:33:35-07:00","id":555161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555152#post555152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to have both actually. Homecoming and Devouring. One representing the angle of the family you are born into, and the other representing the family you marry into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:39:30-07:00","id":555191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555152#post555152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brought that up a few pages ago, but yeah, that is a thing.<br /> <br /> Not that it's a dealbreaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:53:52-07:00","id":555224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555151#post555151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't made any value statements yet, and I have not yet decided which version I like more. I feel like we have traded accidental comparison to oppressed minorities to accidental comparison to religion, especially with the similarities to Lancea et Sanctum mentioned previously. Not better or worse, but different flavor entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no comparison to religion. We have no indication what &quot;lessons&quot; a Beast is supposed to teach. Given that Kin were meant to teach through fear, according to Beasts, I think it is safe to say the lessons might not be based on morality unless a Beast chooses that approach. Hunger is likely to play a role. Collectors teach to keep your stuff secure. Predators teach people have not evolved beyond being prey. Ravagers teach to fear nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:06:40-07:00","id":555256,"title":"","content":"Religion has no inherent tie to morality. Religion is nothing more then a set of practices. So yes, the method of teaching through use of horror is comparable to a religious practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:10:55-07:00","id":555263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555161#post555161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to have both actually. Homecoming and Devouring. One representing the angle of the family you are born into, and the other representing the family you marry into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, both would be ideal. That gives you both a &quot;You can't choose your family&quot; bit and a &quot;marriage/adoption&quot; thing going on. Then you don't lose out on what I think the purpose of Devouring is (which is to give Beasts more reason to socialize) and yet still keep several of the thematic elements of Homecoming, as well as being less restricted to the character types of Gullible Rube/Psychotic Asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:47:51-07:00","id":555281,"title":"","content":"&quot;religion is nothing more than a set of practices&quot; is not only a gross mischaracterization, but an offensive comment which I would hope was unintentional. Language is a set of practices. I don't see the connections. A Beast feeding is a set of practices. Is a Beast feeding comparable to religion? We are getting into mind boggling territory now. If feeding or even the teaching thing is in a person's mind comparable to religion then every single game has the same problem and there wasn't any problems. I wouldn't worry about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:22:50-07:00","id":555312,"title":"","content":"No it wasn't unintentional. Theism and religion are not the same thing. Furthermore, Beast feeding practices are comparable to religion. Or, more specifically, they can be. If both feeding and/or teaching methods of an individual Beast are a consistent set of practices, which seems to be the presumption, then they would be comparable to religion. They very well may be straight out religious. I also did not say, not imply, it was a problem. <br /> <br /> Your assertion that the aspect of Beasts teaching through use of fear was not comparable to religion on the bases that it was not informed of morality was based on flawed presumption. The two are in fact comparable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You also do well not to confuse what the word religion means with religious practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 06-15-2015, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:27:24-07:00","id":555314,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the forum rules, guys. That's all I ask,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:44:04-07:00","id":555320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555159#post555159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Beasts opposing you for not bothering with the teaching thing is now a major source of antgonism? That feels kind of oppressive in a cWoD Camarilla kind of way (this is not necessarily a bad thing, I love V:tM). I didn't peg Beast society as being this cohesive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't necessarily have to mean that the society is that cohesive. Basically could just mean that when a Beast becomes one they get told that the reason their kind exists is to teach the inhabitants of the world. After that you end up with some who decide they'll stick with the job, some who decide to hell with the job, and all the matters in between.Obviously you'll end up with some conflict between those who think feeding without any lesson should be nothing more than just a last resort to keep your horror under control and those who decide feeding is a solid goal in and of itself and there's not really a need to over complicate stuff with a lesson (or some variant.) You only really need it to be cohesive enough to get the introduction out of the way and after that they can be fully justified in doing like the sea turtle and letting them find their own way in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:08:21-07:00","id":555417,"title":"","content":"I don't get why the devouring makes the claim that beasts are any less &quot;older cousins&quot;. They inherited a shard of primordial nightmare. They're no less legitimate than vampires or sin eaters in their ties to monstrosity. <br /> <br /> In fact, the notion that beasts chose their place resonates with sin eaters, who did the same. It seems to be a feature of the more cheerful splats, which Beast seems to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:23:47-07:00","id":555422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555417#post555417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why the devouring makes the claim that beasts are any less &quot;older cousins&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before: You are literally an ancient monster reborn.<br /> <br /> Now: You are some random guy who when asked if they wanted to be a monster, was made into a monster.<br /> <br /> when you're born with the soul of a dragon or a jotun or a cthulhu, you have a decent claim to the title of &quot;ancient race from which all other monsters are descended.<br /> <br /> When you start out as pure human and then get made into a monster via a process that, apparently, creates a brand new monster soul(since I apparently misread that part)? You're some upstart mortal who is aping the shit of all the <i>real</i> monsters and then claiming to be this Super Awesome progenitor.<br /> <br /> And,now that I think about it, with Kinship and the fact that the devouring kinda rips off Geists origins, and Beast culture aping The Lancea et Sanctum and the Scarecrow Ministry's things... Kinda makes New Beasts a bit of a Mary Sue Splat.<br /> <br /> The Self-Insert Copy everyone else but better kind of Mary Sue.<br /> <br /> That right there is reason enough to drop devouring and go back to &quot;You were always a monster, you just didn't realize it until now&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:26:54-07:00","id":555423,"title":"","content":"It makes sense for something which claims kinship with everything to have features of everything. They're the missing link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:33:42-07:00","id":555426,"title":"","content":"Well, what with the new cosmology of Beast, coming up with minor splats for Beast shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Dreamers can become Beasts, they can become Heroes, what else could they become?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:50:04-07:00","id":555430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555423#post555423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense for something which claims kinship with everything to have features of everything. They're the missing link.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It does. If they were <i>always</i> like that.<br /> <br /> When you start as an ordinary human and then choose to be a monster, it just makes you the guy who is taking a bit of everything from the other splats when he becomes a monster.<br /> <br /> The first is the missing link.<br /> <br /> The second is a self insert mary sue.<br /> <br /> Am I clear on why I think that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:56:09-07:00","id":555431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555224#post555224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no comparison to religion. We have no indication what &quot;lessons&quot; a Beast is supposed to teach. Given that Kin were meant to teach through fear, according to Beasts, I think it is safe to say the lessons might not be based on morality unless a Beast chooses that approach. Hunger is likely to play a role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please consider the following:<ul><li>A (hopefully) benevolent member of Beast society discovers you because you went searching for answers or you are the kind of person they want to join them.</li> <li>Said member of Beast society attempts to convert you by explaining their system of beliefs and offering supernatural perks.</li> <li>You agree to their belief system and undergo a process where you are reborn.</li> <li>Your new job requires you to seek out others and teach them your system of beliefs (at least the basic tenets).</li> <li>While you do so, you are also on the look out for potential converts.</li> </ul>There are probably numerous different systems of belief across the various types of beasts and geographical locations, so this does not suggest similarity to any <b>singular</b> religion. But it is quite similar to the behavior of <b>many</b> throughout history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:58:32-07:00","id":555434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555430#post555430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I clear on why I think that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no.<br /> <br /> For one thing beasts weren't &quot;ordinary&quot; people. They had a certain potential, a spark of the primordial that allowed the transformation to take place. And what said transformation involves is accepting a spirit of nightmares into yourself, a primordial force of fear born into a dynasty of monsters. The Horror is you now. When they say they are the missing link, that's what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Beasts may have existed like this for longer than any other supernatural, if what they claim is true. Their origins don't matter as far as that is concerned. What matters is that they are the the fear of unknown, manifest. They're not taking things from other splats, they're taking things from the primordial dream, which they claim other splats do too, in a sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:02:45-07:00","id":555435,"title":"","content":"More and more, I find myself wishing Beasts were a &quot;never human to begin with&quot; splat...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:10:30-07:00","id":555437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555422#post555422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And,now that I think about it, with Kinship and the fact that the devouring kinda rips off Geists origins, and Beast culture aping The Lancea et Sanctum and the Scarecrow Ministry's things... Kinda makes New Beasts a bit of a Mary Sue Splat.<br /> <br /> The Self-Insert Copy everyone else but better kind of Mary Sue.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a grossly unfair accusation. I preferred the old origins too, but the new way has far more potential than 'Mary Sue: nWoD edition'. What we have is a taste, I think we can wait until we see the whole meal before laying down that judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:53:30-07:00","id":555444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555434#post555434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts may have existed like this for longer than any other supernatural, if what they claim is true. Their origins don't matter as far as that is concerned. What matters is that they are the the fear of unknown, manifest. They're not taking things from other splats, they're taking things from the primordial dream, which they claim other splats do too, in a sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>But claims of such hold 0.0 grams of weight when you're a human being that got turned into a monster as opposed to naturally a monster<br /> <br /> When you're born a monster, claims of being the primordial progenitor race holds weight.<br /> <br /> when you're human and made into a monster, you could very well be some Archmaster's pet project two hybridize the splats that took on a life of it's own after a test subject found out how to make more of itself, as far as anyone is concerned.<br /> <br /> The family theme is heavily diluted by Beasts not being born Beasts anymore, and with th family theme gone, you've just got the &quot;Similar to everybody&quot; splat<br /> <br /> when you've got he &quot;similar to everybody splat&quot; that believes it's the progenitor but has no support for this due to having used to be human, used to be a mostly normal human, chose to be a monster, was made a monster, has a motivation that is incredibly similar to not one but two subsplats that already exist, and the origin story is very similar to the origin of an other gameline.<br /> <br /> That's the kind of thing that, when unique, would get called off for being a mary sue, and is easy to wright as a mary sue.<br /> <br /> The monster who was born a monster and is the reincarnated soul of a primordial monster, and did not choose to be what he is, that's the kind of character that you have to be a bad writer to make a sue.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, or course. Not arguing facts this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:59:07-07:00","id":555446,"title":"","content":"Being born a monster does nothing to prevent you being an archmaster's pet project. And in fact now they're <i>more</i> of a family because, unlike before, they now have an <i>actual traceable fucking lineage</i>. Beast was a club in version 1. Now you actually <i>are</i> a family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:01:29-07:00","id":555448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555446#post555446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being born a monster does nothing to prevent you being an archmaster's pet project. And in fact now they're <i>more</i> of a family because, unlike before, they now have an <i>actual traceable fucking lineage</i>. Beast was a club in version 1. Now you actually <i>are</i> a family.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have it backwards.<br /> <br /> Before, you were born into a family.<br /> <br /> Now, you joined a club after receiving an invitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:05:03-07:00","id":555449,"title":"","content":"Except you weren't. You were just a bunch of random people with the same condition. <i>Now</i> part of your very soul was created in a moment of monstrous genesis. You have a direct connection to another beast that never existed before now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:11:16-07:00","id":555450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555449#post555449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you weren't. You were just a bunch of random people with the same condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And now your a bunch of random people who were mostly normal and then developed the same condition after joining a special club.<br /> <br /> Trust me &quot;You were always different and born that way, and found others like you&quot; is more family than &quot;normal guy who becomes special after joining a club&quot;, no matter what kind of connection you have to the guy who invited you to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 06-15-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:20:27-07:00","id":555455,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they are bothe valid ways to read it, so can we please stop this constant back and forth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:23:28-07:00","id":555456,"title":"","content":"Beasts are as much a family as Vampire clans. You know, the ones who actually refer to each other as children and siblings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:25:21-07:00","id":555459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555152#post555152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being &quot;born&quot; and accepting the Soul doesn't really add up to the family angle either. You're not raised with other Beasts, you don't really share any parents or blood relations with any Beasts, you don't have anything adopted. <br /> <br /> After you become a Beast, and you link Lairs, its like you're all living together, so the brood does become a kind of family, but that's after the Homecoming / Devouring, and equally applies. Same with the whole Dark Mother thing - you're still linked to her, though why its a thing is open to debate, its not like it matters if a Beast doesn't think it.<br /> <br /> Homecoming isn't like being born to a family of monsters. You figure it out yourself, on your own, until you happen to come across others. If you're lucky - you could be the only Beast in a tiny town in the middle of nowhere, or maybe a group of powerful heroes and hunters killed everyone in an area and moved on before any new Beast came around. The point is, solitary Homecomings are more than possible - where's your family there? <br /> <br /> The issue with Homecoming is that its pretty much neutral. It doesn't do anything for the story, but it doesn't really do anything against it either. Its just a feel-good piece (a well written one, yes, but still). Congrats, you're a monster, go have fun. It doesn't support or hurt any thing. Its was just... there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555312#post555312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it wasn't unintentional. Theism and religion are not the same thing. Furthermore, Beast feeding practices are comparable to religion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Religion is defined, at minimum, by a set of related beliefs and practices. Feeding is, at best, just practices. Now, saying that Beasts should feed only to teach lessons because the Dark Mother commanded it is, yes, religious. That includes a belief. Doing it because you think its a good idea, and not because of any particular beliefs, is not religious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:29:44-07:00","id":555467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555459#post555459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being &quot;born&quot; and accepting the Soul doesn't really add up to the family angle either. You're not raised with other Beasts, you don't really share any parents or blood relations with any Beasts, you don't have anything adopted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can be born into a family and you're still a blood relation, even if you never meet your distant cousins.<br /> <br /> Homecoming is youralizing you have cousins who are like you.<br /> <br /> Devouring is joining a club and becoming similar to the other members after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:34:55-07:00","id":555469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555456#post555456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are as much a family as Vampire clans. You know, the ones who actually refer to each other as children and siblings?</div> </div> </div> </div> Less so, actually. Vampires have literal shared blood between them, and mystical connections to their siblings and cousins. Beasts actually don't have any connection to other Beasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555467#post555467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be born into a family and you're still a blood relation, even if you never meet your distant cousins.<br /> <br /> Homecoming is youralizing you have cousins who are like you.<br /> <br /> Devouring is joining a club and becoming similar to the other members after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that Homecoming isn't realizing you have cousins. Its like realizing, say, that there are other people who are into asphyxiation in the world. Sure, you feel part of a group. But that's still club-like, no matter which way you go.<br /> <br /> My distant cousins still share my blood, my DNA, my ancestors. There's nothing linking a Beast to other Beasts, okther than &quot;we're all from the Primordial Dream.&quot; And that remains true in both versions.<br /> <br /> There's nothing about Homecoming to make one feel that another Beast is a cousin. Its everything else that did it, and the Devouring doesn't change those things.<br /> <br /> I get it, you like Homecoming better. The problem is that Homecoming didn't actually have anything to do with Family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-15-2015, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T05:19:39-07:00","id":555506,"title":"","content":"Now, don't get me wrong. I'm not trying to say that there isn't a tonal shift in the game. There is. Simply renaming the Soul to the Horror has some pretty big changes beyond semantics argument. A Soul is just part of who you are. A Horror is something that you are scared of, and the word implies its something that you should be rejecting. At least, that's a valid perception.<br /> <br /> That's something that I think may be an issue. That, I think, is the heart of the issue. We went from being at peace with being a monster, to something that's uncomfortable. That is not an insignificant change.<br /> <br /> You're still merging with a primordial soul through your dreams, but its being given a darker cast instead of the lighthearted, accepting one.<br /> <br /> Has the game shifted in tone from something lighthearted, to being very vampire-like? Where families work like clans, where you know you have an inner monster (call it the Beast, call it the Horror, whatever) you have to balance? Did the writers over correct? Likewise, this wisdom angle - does it feel forced? Is it appropriate to have a shard break off from anther Beast, ala vamp clans or prommie lineage, or draw something unique out of the Primordial?<br /> <br /> That is a discussion worth having on a deeper, analytical level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-15-2015, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:19:32-07:00","id":555569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555506#post555506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, don't get me wrong. I'm not trying to say that there isn't a tonal shift in the game. There is. Simply renaming the Soul to the Horror has some pretty big changes beyond semantics argument. A Soul is just part of who you are. A Horror is something that you are scared of, and the word implies its something that you should be rejecting. At least, that's a valid perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the difference if one says soul or horror? In the end here none as the horror replaces your soul in the new version. The only difference comes from the beginning as now the horror is not the soul that you began your life with.....it is there instead of the soul and in the original version it was your soul to begin with you just accepted it when you became a beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:29:27-07:00","id":555573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555569#post555569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference if one says soul or horror?</div> </div> </div> </div> The difference isn't mechanical, its tonal and perception. When you -read- the words, it carries connotations and feelings. Our brains come hard wired with preconceptions and associations, and that changes our perception of things. Despite what Shakespeare would have people think, a rose by any other name <i>would</i> <i>not </i>smell as sweet. <br /> <br /> I mean, lets be honest. If there wasn't a difference, would they have changed it from Soul in the first place? Individual perceptions make up our reality. If someone thinks the book is saying one thing, then, for that person, the book is saying that. For literature, the tone and feel are critical. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:33:05-07:00","id":555575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555506#post555506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something that I think may be an issue. That, I think, is the heart of the issue. We went from being at peace with being a monster, to something that's uncomfortable. That is not an insignificant change.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also an extremely important tonal shift that you are choosing to be an abuser, instead of doing so because you need to survive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:33:58-07:00","id":555576,"title":"","content":"For beasts, a horror is a part of what you are, and is something <i>other people</i> are scared of. At the end of the day it's a chunk of the temenos/anima mundi. The soul of humanity/the world. So your chunk of the soul of humanity is ripped out and replaced with... another chunk of the soul of humanity. Not to mention the intro is in-character. What actually happens is that the beast perceives themselves being eaten, blacks out, and wakes up with a monster where their soul used to be and a vague memory of something reaching out to them from some primordial nightmare realm. Can you <i>really</i> say with any degree of certainty that anything was replaced? <br /> <br /> Sometimes terminology is just that. A horror <i>is </i>a soul. And it may even be yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:05:14-07:00","id":555620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=552905#post552905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no. I actually liked how Disquiet was handled in 1e. I guess I really don't fit well with Blackhatmatt, though not at all to his fault.<br /> <br /> Let me elaborate though; isn't an absolutely huge part of Promethean and Disqueat the concept of Uncanny Valley? I mean, 'hated because they are the things that should not be' sounds pretty much like a central idea of Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that kind of concept doesn't work very well for RPG's because its inherently anti-social and leads to anti-social behaviors. One could even say that it's diametrically opposed to the entire point of an RPG, which is inherently social in nature.<br /> <br /> This concept works best in a video game, which can easily be a single player experience, and moderately well in a board game.<br /> <br /> Also, YMMV, but I always thought that estrangement and prejudice were the central themes to Promethean. The whole game is like the X-Men, an allegory for racism and discrimination.<br /> <br /> That being said, it took some massive rewrites on my part to make it into something that was both true to those themes and playable. Among these things was reduction of the Wasteland's area by an order of magnitude, nerfing of some of the passive Disquiet effects, and the introduction of humans who are simply immune to the effects of both (because they're innocents -- think little girl in the old B&amp;W frankenstein movie).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 06-15-2015, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:20:16-07:00","id":555627,"title":"","content":"The element of choice is there, yes, but categorizing the Beasts as abusers is a rather unfair one. There's a bit of dissonance involved in the matter of choosing to be a monster, and knowing its evil, yes. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think that you can start throwing around the word abuse without issues. If you do that, then you'll have to say the game before the changes was about abuse as well (could just get Satiety 10, live as effective human), so that's an entirely different discussion. That's more of a complaint against the very basis of the game as a whole, and not germane to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:35:56-07:00","id":555637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555627#post555627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The element of choice is there, yes, but categorizing the Beasts as abusers is a rather unfair one. There's a bit of dissonance involved in the matter of choosing to be a monster, and knowing its evil, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's completely fair and appropriate. Many of them are literally abusers. In order to get what they need to survive, many of them need to inflict emotional distress on another sapient creature or allow someone else to do so. There are some fringe cases involving other supernaturals, such as a Beast who seeks out and associates with Spring Court Changeling or Prometheans. But making all Beasts seek out those less harmful methods of getting a Family Dinner would probably not make a very good RPG. Instead we have a society of abusers who abuse for what they believe to be the greater good. That's the kind of rationalization that makes for a good RPG, but it's definitely still abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 06-15-2015, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:44:18-07:00","id":555643,"title":"","content":"Not if they're vigilantes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:45:09-07:00","id":555644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=554663#post554663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, what?<br /> <br /> Being a Beast is now something that is, at least partially, a choice. How you feed your Horror is <i>entirely</i> a choice. What being a Beast means to you and how you express is a choice (character's and player's). How has anyone <i>lost</i> agency?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you say choice I'm not sure how to take it. Basically you're saying that the player chooses to eaten by the Horror. They choose to be the victim. <br /> <br /> The problem is that being a victim is, in and of itself, a good indicator that agency has been lost. There's a much bigger problem though -- that the players <b><i>choose</i></b> to be victims. This is not the reason most people play RPGs (or games at all). Playing an RPG where, up front, I know that my character chose to be a victim doesn't sound that interesting to me. Now YMMV, but this actually sounds quite disturbing. To make some simple analogies to the (now) core tenant of the game, imagine if the Horror is trying to rape your character. To become the Beast you must choose to let it happen. Or we can go with a less utter dark analogy, the Horror is trying to murder you and to become the Beast you must choose to let it happen. The character must surrender to their fate. Surrender is the very definition of loss of agency.<br /> <br /> Now I'm pretty sure that you didn't realize that the new intro could be read this way. And I'm sure this issue is going to get fixed in future drafts because I have every confidence that your not going to give me a game where the core tenant is everyone's a victim. Right? As storyteller's we would never come to the table with a chronicle that opens up with -- you're all victims of rape (or insert slightly less terrible crime here). Because that isn't going to be a very fun chronicle. We might be able to deconstruct such things -- crimes and victimhood -- in literature but, games aren't a literary form, even if the storytelling part seems like it is. There are some themes that we simply can't bring to the table because it simply isn't going to be fun. Remember, whatever you do, this is still going to be a game, and you have to make it so people are going to want to play it. <br /> <br /> I do still think that there's a simple fix. Just flip who does the Devouring and you're pretty much good to go.<br /> <br /> If you want to score extra points and work the Family / Dark Mother concept back in, you could make some additional alterations a la, <br /> The Dark Mother's seeds drift through the endless seas of the Astral Realms coming to rest in the dreams of some children. These seeds are the source of many of our childhood terrors. The bogeyman beneath the bed, the monster in the closet. Most of the time these seeds whither and die, destroyed by mind's natural defenses. A very few of these seed bearers are fed upon by other Beasts, germinating the seed within them. In these very few, a Horror hatches that hounds them throughout their dreams until at last, they turn and face it. A Beast is born when a hounded soul stands against the Horror that has stalked their dreams for so long and not only defeats it but descends to its level, consuming it in a great Devouring in the exact manner that Horror continuously threatened to do unto them.<br /> <br /> ...or something along those lines anyway, preserving some of the things from the Homecoming and Family.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this thread is really too long so I probably won't return to this conversation (because it's going to be too hard to find again) so PM me if you want to discuss the whole agency / victimhood issue more. I'll warn you though, I'm a PhD student in the midst of preparing my reading list for my quals so I might be slow in responding (I'll be reading through dozens upon dozens of articles on semantics, phil. o. lang., info. org., info. theory, linked data, and similar topics this summer so my response rate will be downright atrocious at times).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:46:06-07:00","id":555651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555459#post555459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religion is defined, at minimum, by a set of related beliefs and practices. Feeding is, at best, just practices. Now, saying that Beasts should feed only to teach lessons because the Dark Mother commanded it is, yes, religious. That includes a belief. Doing it because you think its a good idea, and not because of any particular beliefs, is not religious.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Or, rather they can be.&quot; <br /> <br /> Either you didn't actually rea what I wrote or you are intentionally misrepresenting it by quoting out of context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 06-15-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:48:34-07:00","id":555654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555637#post555637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's completely fair and appropriate. Many of them are literally abusers. In order to get what they need to survive, many of them need to inflict emotional distress on another sapient creature or allow someone else to do so. There are some fringe cases involving other supernaturals, such as a Beast who seeks out and associates with Spring Court Changeling or Prometheans. But making all Beasts seek out those less harmful methods of getting a Family Dinner would probably not make a very good RPG. Instead we have a society of abusers who abuse for what they believe to be the greater good. That's the kind of rationalization that makes for a good RPG, but it's definitely still abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, kind of like <a href=\"https://www.google.com.au/search?q=battery+hen&amp;client=ubuntu&amp;hs=0tC&amp;channel=fs&amp;tbm=isch&amp;tbo=u&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CCQQsARqFQoTCLKsmuf2kcYCFYtIvAodzvsApw&amp;biw=1366&amp;bih=671\" target=\"_blank\">battery cage hens</a> are abused? Or <a href=\"http://www.hsvma.org/facts_veal_calves\" target=\"_blank\">milk-fed veal cattle</a>?<br /> As long as the Begotten <i><b>need </b></i>to feed their Hunger, it can be a gray issue. There is a reason people earlier in the thread compared it to vampires hunting for blood, it is an apt analogy.<br /> <br /> The fact that not feeding causes unmitigated harm to people than feeding just compounds the issue.<br /> <br /> That doesn't magically make their actions OK; but it does help to put them in perspective. It's still abuse from a human perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T07:59:10-07:00","id":555664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555320#post555320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't necessarily have to mean that the society is that cohesive. Basically could just mean that when a Beast becomes one they get told that the reason their kind exists is to teach the inhabitants of the world. After that you end up with some who decide they'll stick with the job, some who decide to hell with the job, and all the matters in between.Obviously you'll end up with some conflict between those who think feeding without any lesson should be nothing more than just a last resort to keep your horror under control and those who decide feeding is a solid goal in and of itself and there's not really a need to over complicate stuff with a lesson (or some variant.) You only really need it to be cohesive enough to get the introduction out of the way and after that they can be fully justified in doing like the sea turtle and letting them find their own way in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the whole repression thing that appeared out of nowhere.<br /> The 1st draft had the Beasts be small groups sharing a sense of kinship born of innate similarity, mostly accepting, or a least non-judgemental of each others' more or less gruesome habits; now they're a cult whose members may beat you up if you don't conform to their pseudo-moralistic dogma after you're inducted.<br /> Having a body of people feeling they have a right to punish you for not respecting their rules is already a sign that a certain form of higer authority exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:01:11-07:00","id":555667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555644#post555644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When you say choice I'm not sure how to take it. Basically you're saying that the player chooses to eaten by the Horror. They choose to be the victim.<br /> <br /> The problem is that being a victim is, in and of itself, a good indicator that agency has been lost. There's a much bigger problem though -- that the players <b><i>choose</i></b> to be victims. This is not the reason most people play RPGs (or games at all). Playing an RPG where, up front, I know that my character chose to be a victim doesn't sound that interesting to me. Now YMMV, but this actually sounds quite disturbing. To make some simple analogies to the (now) core tenant of the game, imagine if the Horror is trying to rape your character. To become the Beast you must choose to let it happen. Or we can go with a less utter dark analogy, the Horror is trying to murder you and to become the Beast you must choose to let it happen. The character must surrender to their fate. Surrender is the very definition of loss of agency.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What the <i>hell</i> are you talking about? A beast-to-be doesn't choose to be a victim, they choose to undergo a rather traumatic transformation that leaves them more powerful than they've ever been. And the whole point of devouring is that it's quite literal. The beast <i>eats</i> you. No rape or anything involved here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:06:36-07:00","id":555687,"title":"","content":"The Devouring seems to be what the Beasts did to souls of Heroes in the first revision, except Heroes didn't have a choice and their nightmares didn't go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:23:17-07:00","id":555713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555637#post555637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's completely fair and appropriate. Many of them are literally abusers. In order to get what they need to survive, many of them need to inflict emotional distress on another sapient creature or allow someone else to do so. There are some fringe cases involving other supernaturals, such as a Beast who seeks out and associates with Spring Court Changeling or Prometheans. But making all Beasts seek out those less harmful methods of getting a Family Dinner would probably not make a very good RPG. Instead we have a society of abusers who abuse for what they believe to be the greater good. That's the kind of rationalization that makes for a good RPG, but it's definitely still abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div> First, I want to point out that feeding off supernaturals is NOT a fringe case. Its a core part of the game. <br /> <br /> Vampires play social games. To that effect, we have innate frenzy issues, blood bonds, and physical strength. Werewovles hunt. So, the game revolves around tracking, different shapes to identify, hunt down, and &quot;kill&quot; prey with. Mages study mysteries. Mage sights and the academia to support those themes. <br /> <br /> The core aspects of Beast's mechanics are finding and interacting with other supernaturals. Its something that every single Beast does. Its so interwoven into the game that not having the supernaturals would be like having a vampire that didn't drink blood. That's <i>not</i> a niche. Its the norm. If you think that most supernaturals are abusive in their hunts, then I have to look askance - werewolves tracking down and eating a rabbit counts for two points, and that's far from abusive. Autumn fae jumping out and scaring someone isn't abuse, nor is attending a sport's competition. Mages tracking down mysteries is abusive? Its debatable with vampires, and they're the worst of the lot!<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, you missed the entire part where I said its unfair because if you're going to talk about Beasts being abusers, you have to admit that they were abusers before and after the changes. You're taking what I said out of context. Calling what Beasts do abuse is an issue with the game as a whole, not the discussion of changes. Trying to make the changes about abuse is nothing more than using a hot button word to make it sound worse than it is. It doesn't invite discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Third, its debatable if its abuse. We haven't seen the revisions of how Hungers are going to work, so that's just a guess on your part on how they're going to survive. Even if we assume the five Hungers remain mostly the same? A Collector would be more like a thief, which is no where near abuse. Tyrants can establish power by picking a fair fight with a school bully. Its sadistic, yes. Abuse? That's not so clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:26:39-07:00","id":555718,"title":"","content":"That is not, at all, what the Beasts Soul did to Heroes. The Beast's Soul was present in a Nightmare which the psyche/soul of the Hero then latched onto to give itself purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:45:07-07:00","id":555743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555643#post555643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if they're vigilantes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much the definition of the Hunger for Punishment, I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555654#post555654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the Begotten <i><b>need </b></i>to feed their Hunger, it can be a gray issue. There is a reason people earlier in the thread compared it to vampires hunting for blood, it is an apt analogy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except, unlike vampires, the target of the Hunger doesn't have to be a human. And, in many cases, its not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555664#post555664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except for the whole repression thing that appeared out of nowhere.<br /> The 1st draft had the Beasts be small groups sharing a sense of kinship born of innate similarity, mostly accepting, or a least non-judgemental of each others' more or less gruesome habits; now they're a cult whose members may beat you up if you don't conform to their pseudo-moralistic dogma after you're inducted.<br /> Having a body of people feeling they have a right to punish you for not respecting their rules is already a sign that a certain form of higer authority exist.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humans have bodies of people who feel they have the right to punish you for not respecting rules. They're called police/juries/judges/prison guards, and the rules are called laws. No cult or higher power necessary, unless your higher power is &quot;the good.&quot; There's no need to assume differently for Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555651#post555651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Or, rather they can be.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either you didn't actually rea what I wrote or you are intentionally misrepresenting it by quoting out of context.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, I don't even remember what I was trying to get at, so I couldn't say what I was doing. I think it was something along the lines of &quot;just because a Beast chooses a moral way to feed doesn't make it automatically religious.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:46:53-07:00","id":555744,"title":"","content":"Debates about morality, agency, etc aside my problem with the whole Devouring angle boils down to this: nobody in their right mind is going to say yes to the question &quot;is it cool if I <i>eat your soul</i> and turn you into a living Scared Straight program?&quot; The mechanical necessity/function of a soul in the NWoD notwithstanding, the popular conception of what constitutes your soul is a pretty big deal, enough so that most people aren't going to use it as a bargaining chip regardless of the payoff.<br /> <br /> At least with Vampires the pitch is a relatively easy sell. You can see how someone would be willing to change their diet and give up tanning in exchange for wealth, immortality and some incidental super powers. With Beast though? &quot;In addition to having your soul replaced with a Horror From Man's Darkest Imaginings, you'll have a slightly extended lifespan, some powers that are mostly good for smashing things and/or scaring the poo out of people, and sometimes the neighborhood loser will spontaneously come unglued and obsessively try to murder you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:00:22-07:00","id":555751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555152#post555152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only works with an orthodox, dictionary definition of family, which this game clearly would have more interest in subverting than supporting.<br /> <br /> Consider Werewolf. In 1st ed., it was a given that a Werewolf character had at least other Wolf-blooded, if not full Werewolves, as blood relatives, and consequently, undergoing the First Change was an increase in status within the family. An unfortunate side effect of that familial connection was that Tribes, in the narrative, had a dynastic, monolithic hold over regions, which forced Chronicles to either involve the Pack being drawn from a single Tribe, or being the narratively rare Mixed Tribe Pack. In 2nd ed., this is not an issue, due primarily to the narrative shifting away from Tribes being cohesive, world-spanning organizations, but also due to there being more vectors to becoming Wolf-blooded than mere blood relation.<br /> <br /> Beast, as presented in the new draft of the introduction, will benefit similarly from decoupling acquiring the template's powers from blood relations in that Broods will have more agency in choosing their own power structures rather than adhering to an imposed, paternalistic framework, be it based on blood ties or Mythological hierarchy. This fluid power dynamic also aids in regulating the behavior of broodmates in a similar fashion to how the low-level antagonism that pervades Vampire courts aids in preserving the Masquerade. Additional, this non-orthodox family model avoids having members being beholden to toxic power dynamics, a very real problem with conventional family models.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:03:00-07:00","id":555755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555152#post555152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to bring up something I saw on an other forum: Beasts being made instead of born, and choosing to become a Beast, kinda screws with the family angle.<br /> <br /> You're not the older cousin. You're the new guy who isn't actually related to any of them and is just aping their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except your &quot;Horror&quot;, your Beast Soul, was LITERALLY born from another Beast. So it actually plays up a heritage that presumably stretches back to the Mother doing the first Devourings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:03:15-07:00","id":555756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555654#post555654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, kind of like <a href=\"https://www.google.com.au/search?q=battery+hen&amp;client=ubuntu&amp;hs=0tC&amp;channel=fs&amp;tbm=isch&amp;tbo=u&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CCQQsARqFQoTCLKsmuf2kcYCFYtIvAodzvsApw&amp;biw=1366&amp;bih=671\" target=\"_blank\">battery cage hens</a> are abused? Or <a href=\"http://www.hsvma.org/facts_veal_calves\" target=\"_blank\">milk-fed veal cattle</a>?<br /> As long as the Begotten <i><b>need </b></i>to feed their Hunger, it can be a gray issue. There is a reason people earlier in the thread compared it to vampires hunting for blood, it is an apt analogy.<br /> The fact that not feeding causes unmitigated harm to people than feeding just compounds the issue.<br /> That doesn't magically make their actions OK; but it does help to put them in perspective. It's still abuse from a human perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the analogy to battery cage hens and milk-fed veal cattle really works. It would take some stretching. Mostly because you made the specific choice to become something that primarily eats those things, and were previously something that never ate those things before. But you don't just eat them, you need to actually make them feel terrible or watch someone else making them feel terrible. This can depend on the type of hunger of course.<br /> <br /> Vampires have the option at character creation between having made a choice, or having no choice at all.<br /> Every Beast seems to have made the choice to become an abuser (even under false pretenses).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:12:42-07:00","id":555766,"title":"","content":"Or a vigilante.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:21:32-07:00","id":555785,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there is room for a sixth Family, centered around will-o-the-wisps, rusalki, yuki-onna, and other passive-aggressive trickster Beasts, whose danger is not in what they will do to you, but in leading you into danger, representing the fear of deception or something of the kind. This is already half-covered by the Makara and their out-of-your-element style, but the Leviathans seem to be pulling double-duty, concept-wise (plus, what use are grappling maneuvers to a siren?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:22:49-07:00","id":555787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555785#post555785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(plus, what use are grappling maneuvers to a siren?).</div> </div> </div> </div>They help with the drowning bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:24:14-07:00","id":555790,"title":"","content":"There is that, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:37:09-07:00","id":555805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555743#post555743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans have bodies of people who feel they have the right to punish you for not respecting rules. They're called police/juries/judges/prison guards, and the rules are called laws. No cult or higher power necessary, unless your higher power is &quot;the good.&quot; There's no need to assume differently for Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err, I was talking about a higher social order, the existence of a level of social organization cohesive enough to try to impose dictats, such as what you describe, not a higher spiritual, or moral power, really.<br /> Sorry if I was unclear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 06-15-2015, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:49:46-07:00","id":555814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555713#post555713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I want to point out that feeding off supernaturals is NOT a fringe case. Its a core part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossover was never a core intention of NWoD. If a storyteller can make it happen, then that is an awesome and can make for some good stories. Just because Beast tries to be crossover friendly does not mean the other splats intend it. The crossover friendly nature of Beast is probably an attempt to avoid the Promethean trap and make them more marketable, not an intentional effort to make their society less abusive through the use of Family Dinner.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555713#post555713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, you missed the entire part where I said its unfair because if you're going to talk about Beasts being abusers, you have to admit that they were abusers before and after the changes. You're taking what I said out of context. Calling what Beasts do abuse is an issue with the game as a whole, not the discussion of changes. Trying to make the changes about abuse is nothing more than using a hot button word to make it sound worse than it is. It doesn't invite discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with that admission. Sometimes you have fringe cases where the older Beast tricked the younger Beast into accepting a Faustian bargain that involved something completely different than what they expected. That is as close to innocent as Beast can manage.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555713#post555713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we assume the five Hungers remain mostly the same? A Collector would be more like a thief, which is no where near abuse. Tyrants can establish power by picking a fair fight with a school bully. Its sadistic, yes. Abuse? That's not so clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already covered this, but Collectors are the only ones who seem really capable of escaping the abuse angle that most Beasts have going on. But I am interested to see how the hungers may or may not change with the coming revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 06-15-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:51:10-07:00","id":555815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555744#post555744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debates about morality, agency, etc aside my problem with the whole Devouring angle boils down to this: nobody in their right mind is going to say yes to the question &quot;is it cool if I <i>eat your soul</i> and turn you into a living Scared Straight program?&quot; The mechanical necessity/function of a soul in the NWoD notwithstanding, the popular conception of what constitutes your soul is a pretty big deal, enough so that most people aren't going to use it as a bargaining chip regardless of the payoff.<br /> <br /> At least with Vampires the pitch is a relatively easy sell. You can see how someone would be willing to change their diet and give up tanning in exchange for wealth, immortality and some incidental super powers. With Beast though? &quot;In addition to having your soul replaced with a Horror From Man's Darkest Imaginings, you'll have a slightly extended lifespan, some powers that are mostly good for smashing things and/or scaring the poo out of people, and sometimes the neighborhood loser will spontaneously come unglued and obsessively try to murder you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><br /> While I have yet to meet anyone swayed by a sales pitch for a defining metaphysical change being presented in the form of a reductive, pop-culture referential, I have seen more than a few RPG players choose to have their characters endure unthinkably drastic psychic and spiritual harm in the name of acquiring power. You don't choose that path because you're antisocial or masochistic; you choose it because it's the kind of character you'd like to explore.</span><br /> <br /> Also, you used the word &quot;most.&quot; Player Characters seldom qualify as &quot;most&quot; people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:00:50-07:00","id":555823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555785#post555785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there is room for a sixth Family, centered around will-o-the-wisps, rusalki, yuki-onna, and other passive-aggressive trickster Beasts, whose danger is not in what they will do to you, but in leading you into danger, representing the fear of deception or something of the kind. This is already half-covered by the Makara and their out-of-your-element style, but the Leviathans seem to be pulling double-duty, concept-wise (plus, what use are grappling maneuvers to a siren?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those sound more like Namtaru or Eshmaki to me, but just about any Family would work, save maybe the Ugallu, since the others have the social powers and indirect powers that make those concepts viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:09:12-07:00","id":555828,"title":"","content":"Even Collector's can't really go out of the abusive that easily. They can't just steal random shit. The stuff they steal must be valuable to someone for it to count. And if it's valuable.. well, all the Beasts take away value from you (whenever it's stuff, hp, dignity or whatever else)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:31:15-07:00","id":555837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555828#post555828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Collector's can't really go out of the abusive that easily. They can't just steal random shit. The stuff they steal must be valuable to someone for it to count. And if it's valuable.. well, all the Beasts take away value from you (whenever it's stuff, hp, dignity or whatever else)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. If something is genuinely valuable to you, then it's probably going to hurt to lose it. Maybe not PTSD level horror like some Hungers, but more than a few people have gotten divorced or committed suicide due to sudden poverty, or driven to depression because they lost something that meant the world to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:32:33-07:00","id":555839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555718#post555718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not, at all, what the Beasts Soul did to Heroes. The Beast's Soul was present in a Nightmare which the psyche/soul of the Hero then latched onto to give itself purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul of a Hero is engulfed by the Soul of the Beast. The soul of a dreamer is Devoured by a Horror. Both come out of it changed and with purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555744#post555744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debates about morality, agency, etc aside my problem with the whole Devouring angle boils down to this: nobody in their right mind is going to say yes to the question &quot;is it cool if I <i>eat your soul</i> and turn you into a living Scared Straight program?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably the first chapter will get into this more, but they've already been having dreams where they were the monster. The offer is probably less of, 'Can I eat your soul?' and more, 'Will you leave your mortal shell behind to fulfill your destiny?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2015, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:43:05-07:00","id":555848,"title":"","content":"The whole Nightmares teach wisdom things feels really tacked on. Right now, I feel like I don't want to play a Beast. I want to play someone who hunts down and kills Beasts, because they seem built to spread misery and fear in the name of &quot;wisdom&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to see a take on them in the view of the God Machine with the idea that the Dark Mother is a figure in opposition to the God Machine. Nightmares produce fear. Fear triggers the fight or flight response in people. It is or can be a call to action. Nightmares are how the Beasts try to awaken humanity to action against the Machine that lulls them into sleeping obedience. Heroes are humans touched by the Machine (or one of its Angels) and driven to seek out and destroy Beasts in order to maintain Humanity's obedient slumber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:47:26-07:00","id":555852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555848#post555848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to see a take on them in the view of the God Machine with the idea that the Dark Mother is a figure in opposition to the God Machine. Nightmares produce fear. Fear triggers the fight or flight response in people. It is or can be a call to action. Nightmares are how the Beasts try to awaken humanity to action against the Machine that lulls them into sleeping obedience. Heroes are humans touched by the Machine (or one of its Angels) and driven to seek out and destroy Beasts in order to maintain Humanity's obedient slumber.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Dark Mother is in any way an analogue to the God Machine, but all we have is the introduction and from that it looks like a character could do that. Still, I wouldn't want an entire, new game revolving around fighting the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:59:26-07:00","id":555858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555848#post555848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Nightmares teach wisdom things feels really tacked on. Right now, I feel like I don't want to play a Beast. I want to play someone who hunts down and kills Beasts, because they seem built to spread misery and fear in the name of &quot;wisdom&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to see a take on them in the view of the God Machine with the idea that the Dark Mother is a figure in opposition to the God Machine. Nightmares produce fear. Fear triggers the fight or flight response in people. It is or can be a call to action. Nightmares are how the Beasts try to awaken humanity to action against the Machine that lulls them into sleeping obedience. Heroes are humans touched by the Machine (or one of its Angels) and driven to seek out and destroy Beasts in order to maintain Humanity's obedient slumber.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then play a Hunter.<br /> <br /> And it isn't capital N nightmares that teach wisdom, it's satisfying Hunger that does. <br /> <br /> Also, that GM hates the DM angle does nothing to support the enmity between the Begotten and the Unchained, and almost turns the game into Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:14:39-07:00","id":555864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555858#post555858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that GM hates the DM angle does nothing to support the enmity between the Begotten and the Unchained</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually I think that one's pretty easy to make work. They're still <i>of</i> the GM, even if they rebelled, so there's this instinctive wariness they have toward beasts and vice-versa. The fact that they rebelled is why they can have good relations at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:24:09-07:00","id":555869,"title":"","content":"I know the discussion itself has kind of drifted from it, but I'm a little confused why Beast's would stop being related on the grounds that now they're a human fragment that's fused with a fragment of the Primordial Dream. I mean the silliest would of course be arguing the relation is from the human side, as with the exception of Prometheans, the splats tend to have human as part of the initial life phase then the supernatural kicks in.*<br /> <br /> So more likely the relation ,at least from the belief of Beasts, comes from the Horror aspect you've merged with. Which to my knowledge a few of the other splats require you to be made and not born anyway, so discounting Beasts because they weren't always monsters doesn't really work.**<br /> <br /> *Unless you're a wolfwere garou then you were a wolf and one day you gained the power to become human and have thumbs.<br /> **The list as I understand it: Made splats: Vampires, Changelings (NWoD), Geists, Prometheans, Mummies. Born splats: Mages, Werewolves, Demons, Hunters, Changelings (OWoD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:51:23-07:00","id":555884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555869#post555869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the discussion itself has kind of drifted from it, but I'm a little confused why Beast's would stop being related on the grounds that now they're a human fragment that's fused with a fragment of the Primordial Dream. I mean the silliest would of course be arguing the relation is from the human side, as with the exception of Prometheans, the splats tend to have human as part of the initial life phase then the supernatural kicks in.*<br /> <br /> So more likely the relation ,at least from the belief of Beasts, comes from the Horror aspect you've merged with. Which to my knowledge a few of the other splats require you to be made and not born anyway, so discounting Beasts because they weren't always monsters doesn't really work.**<br /> <br /> *Unless you're a wolfwere garou then you were a wolf and one day you gained the power to become human and have thumbs.<br /> **The list as I understand it: Made splats: Vampires, Changelings (NWoD), Geists, Prometheans, Mummies. Born splats: Mages, Werewolves, Demons, Hunters, Changelings (OWoD)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know, the way things are presented, Beasts feel more like a cult than a family. More a group of like-minded individuals than a gathering of people sharing either descent or affection. And yes, I know they now actually have lines of descent, but IMO, the way it's presented feels more like a conversion than an adoption or a siring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:51:48-07:00","id":555925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555814#post555814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover was never a core intention of NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its been said, time and again, that crossover is a core intention of Beast: the Primordial. Every game deviates from the core assumptions in some way. Beast does it by making crossover the default. That's the kind of game it is. There's no way around it. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555828#post555828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Collector's can't really go out of the abusive that easily. They can't just steal random shit. The stuff they steal must be valuable to someone for it to count. And if it's valuable.. well, all the Beasts take away value from you (whenever it's stuff, hp, dignity or whatever else)</div> </div> </div> </div> Theft of precious items do not amount to abuse, however. And that's only at high Satiety. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555852#post555852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Dark Mother is in any way an analogue to the God Machine, but all we have is the introduction and from that it looks like a character could do that. Still, I wouldn't want an entire, new game revolving around fighting the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's actually a fair amount of support for the Dark Mother and God Machine being opposed. Not written into Beast, but in other sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555869#post555869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the discussion itself has kind of drifted from it, but I'm a little confused why Beast's would stop being related on the grounds that now they're a human fragment that's fused with a fragment of the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know either. I suspect its because something else was changed, and the problem is being misidentified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555884#post555884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, the way things are presented, Beasts feel more like a cult than a family. More a group of like-minded individuals than a gathering of people sharing either descent or affection. And yes, I know they now actually have lines of descent, but IMO, the way it's presented feels more like a conversion than an adoption or a siring.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ironically, Werewolf has more in common with an actual cult or religion, but people freak out if you try to say that. So, if Werewolf can't be a cult or religion, I'm not sure why Beasts suddenly are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:00:01-07:00","id":555928,"title":"","content":"So, finally got off call and could read the new intro...<br /> <br /> I am generally sticking with my initial interpretation for if I run a game of Beast, since it still fits the general theme: Beasts reflect the Mythic Arcs recast into the Modern Day, where the legends have been lost to humanity and the Beasts act as a Legend trying to be &quot;remembered&quot;..<br /> <br /> My take (both pre and post revision) is: Each Beast reflects a story given form, a mythic tale being spun around it, with it as the source of the confirm that drives the tale as well as providing the thematic setting via the Lair. Those who become beasts were someone with a tie to the Primordial Dream, and through an event come to accept their role in the story and become the means of perpetuating the Myth in the World. Heroes are those with a sensitivity for the Dream but inability to process it, whose weakened identity results in them being shaped by the Myth into the role of the Heroes.<br /> <br /> The only differences are that Beasts now accept their role as the central element more fully, instead of being forced into it. I think the focus on them as teachers from a school of hard knocks isn't to hard to switch to &quot;Myths manifest that are trying to be remembered&quot;: both have the goal of influencing nightmares, to make mortals aware of the forgotten. It is just one focuses on reminding humanity what it once feared and the lessons tied to those fears, while the Myth is more open (though the purpose of myths is to teach or explain things, the story is equally important). The new Devouring works as an acceptance as a part of the story, choosing to become the role you were cast for and joining the wider family of myths.<br /> <br /> The Hunger, Satiety, and its impact on the world is playing the role needed for any story: conflict. Withough conflict, there is no plot, and thus the beasts Myth cannot be remembered, as there is no Myth. The Beast can choose how it introduces this conflict, such as becoming the masked vigilante who strikes fear into criminals while being hated by that one detective who <i>knows </i> said vigilante is worse than any criminal, or playing the role of the Urban monster who stalks children unseen except on film and causes fear beyond just in those children he takes via the social media. Regardless of the <i>how</i>, the Beast wants his Myth remembered.<br /> <br /> Beasts are driven to one day join the likes of the Hydra or Grendel, becoming well known in the conscious collective, their Myths are cornerstone of human culture, or at the very least leave a mark among the humans they live among. This is my idea for their greater purpose: construction of a Myth. Beyond their Hunger and Archetype, I could see elements of their society derived from the type of mythic arc they seek, from seeking remembered certain through benevolence (or anti-heroism) to infamy for their malevolence, to making a land forever marked by their presence (but their role forgotten) or an urban legend that knows recognizes no borders. Some of those groups seek to weave other supernaturals into their stories, adding different themes into their Myth, while others choose to remain among the monsters.<br /> <br /> As an Aside, the idea of other Beasts facilitating a metamorphosis doesn't bother me too much, versus the original Homecoming. Sine the only connection before was the Primordial Dream, I view that the focus has just shifted on who the family is. The Horrors are all family, and share a kinship within the Primordial Dream. With the unity with the Horror, the Beast is essentially made a part of this network of conceptual terrors given form. Instead of a random human somehow born with a monster inside (remember, monsters didn't follow bloodlines), the focus is on an ancient horror leaving it's place amongst the purely conceptual to manifest in the world among it's kin. The fact that all humans have the ability but only a few forge the needed connection and then a mentor in many cases to transition seems almost a cross between mage and vampire, but I am okay with that.<br /> <br /> As an aside aside... I can't shake the feeling I have seen elements of this all in Mage. Awakening in general, the idea of Astral Journey's leading to a dramatic change due to acceptance of a lesson and modification of the soul? And that Banishers parallel Heroes: those who experienced the trip but failed to accept it, who now seek those who did and destroy these reminders of the Truths they couldn't accept. And the idea of alternations of the soul from Astral trips or connections to gain new powers isn't new; the Morphean Continuity, Tremere (Revised) and Unforgotten Scion legacies, to name a few. Now, not saying these parallels are bad or discredit either one. Just an observation I found interesting, especially with the new intro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":".  I wish I could type on my phone better...Damn these tiny keyboards! 06-15-2015, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:10:35-07:00","id":555958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555925#post555925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its been said, time and again, that crossover is a core intention of Beast: the Primordial. Every game deviates from the core assumptions in some way. Beast does it by making crossover the default. That's the kind of game it is. There's no way around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's great that Beast insists that it's awesome friends with most of the other splats. But those other splats were not written with the intention of being great friends with anyone else. Those splats are not even balanced against each other in a way that makes crossover very fair. Beast doesn't make those issues go away, especially since Beast is already stepping on so many other thematic toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:16:00-07:00","id":555962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555958#post555958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's great that Beast insists that it's awesome friends with most of the other splats. But those other splats were not written with the intention of being great friends with anyone else. Those splats are not even balanced against each other in a way that makes crossover very fair. Beast doesn't make those issues go away, especially since Beast is already stepping on so many other thematic toes.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) Beast works fine with all PCs as Beasts, and other supernats as NPCs. That, too, is a form of crossover. 2) Balance is overrated, overshadowing each other is the key issue. 3) Your opinion on crossovers still doesn't change that the fact that Beast was designed with crossover as the default.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it sounds like you have some issues with crossovers here, but there's a lot of people who want it and do play it, and Beast was specifically made for that kind of play. I'm sorry if you don't like it, but that's kind of what this game is meant for. If you don't want it at all, then Beast may not be for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-15-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:26:07-07:00","id":555992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555928#post555928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside aside... I can't shake the feeling I have seen elements of this all in Mage. Awakening in general, the idea of Astral Journey's leading to a dramatic change due to acceptance of a lesson and modification of the soul? And that Banishers parrallel Heroes: those who experienced the trip but failed to accept it, who now seek those who did and destroy these reminders of the Truths they couldn't accept. And the idea of alterinations of the soul from Astral trips or connections to gain new powers isnt new; the Morphean Continuity, Tremere (Revised) and Unforgotten Scion legacies, to name a few. Now, not saying these parallels are bad or discredit either one. Just an observation I found interesting, especially with the new intro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Repetitive themes and parallels among PC and antagonist types and options is common in both the nWoD and cWoD. For instance, how many spats are metaphors for oppressed or alienated minorities? The test is how well the authors executed the premise and how interesting and integrated the unique setting elements are in the new game line. Besides, if an idea works, there's nothing really wrong with reusing it with a little polish or twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:36:12-07:00","id":555999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555925#post555925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ironically, Werewolf has more in common with an actual cult or religion, but people freak out if you try to say that. So, if Werewolf can't be a cult or religion, I'm not sure why Beasts suddenly are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken and the Pure of 1st Edition were pretty cult-like in some aspects, what with the elaborate mythos, clannishness and quasi-sacred purposes. I don't know about 2E, since I haven't read it yet. Don't really see what this has to do with the discussion, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:38:22-07:00","id":556026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555962#post555962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Beast works fine with all PCs as Beasts, and other supernats as NPCs. That, too, is a form of crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Beast games would need to explore the themes and relationships of the other splat in some depth before it should be considered a crossover.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555962#post555962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3) Your opinion on crossovers still doesn't change that the fact that Beast was designed with crossover as the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that doesn't mean those splats were designed for crossover with Beast.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555962#post555962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, it sounds like you have some issues with crossovers here, but there's a lot of people who want it and do play it, and Beast was specifically made for that kind of play. I'm sorry if you don't like it, but that's kind of what this game is meant for. If you don't want it at all, then Beast may not be for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Internet discussions often go down some pretty distant tangents that are not necessarily representative of the more moderate views we would normally take in a real life situation. We've gotten off the important topic of most Beasts being abusers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:50:21-07:00","id":556035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555999#post555999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Forsaken and the Pure of 1st Edition were pretty cult-like in some aspects, what with the elaborate mythos, clannishness and quasi-sacred purposes. I don't know about 2E, since I haven't read it yet. Don't really see what this has to do with the discussion, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit different, for the reasons I pointed out above. The reason I find it relevant is that the social and origin changes that happened between 1e and 2e reflect the changes between the first Kickstarter draft and the revision, that making Beasts become rather than realize allows for more potential societal mixture than hanging everything on being born into a particular group.<br /> <br /> It also leaves open the possibility of a demi-splat, that could even be encouraged into coming into existence.<br /> <br /> <b>Idea:</b> instead of having both extremes of the Inflicting Nightmares roll produce Heroes, have the Extraordinary Success awaken nascent Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:55:41-07:00","id":556036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555992#post555992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Repetitive themes and parallels among PC and antagonist types and options is common in both the nWoD and cWoD. For instance, how many spats are metaphors for oppressed or alienated minorities? The test is how well the authors executed the premise and how interesting and integrated the unique setting elements are in the new game line. Besides, if an idea works, there's nothing really wrong with reusing it with a little polish or twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree fully. I realize that it doesn't come across this way, but I actually like those things, especially since it helps tie mages in to the Beast setting even more.I could see mages asking questions about the parrallels between the Devouring and Awakening, and taking notes. And if a mage who escaped the Morphean Continuity legacy encountered a Beast and heard it's story, the mage likely would see a parrallel and possibly want to &quot;help it&quot;. And it means that the Mage and Beast team up doesn't bug me as much when it comes to Heroes: While I can see a mage who relies the truth might try to intercede on the Heroes behalf to facilitate treatment (of that remains post revision), I also can get them coming at it as &quot;ahhh, Heroes are your Banishers... carry on.&quot;<br /> <br /> In a more general sense, it helps frame the idea of &quot;Astral force in human body&quot; as a thing when a mage encounters the Beast: their lore supports these things. Note, I am not saying the Mages are right or that I am trying to work on a universal cosmos, but it helps piece things together enough for an in setting encounter for me as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:05:23-07:00","id":556045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555884#post555884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know, the way things are presented, Beasts feel more like a cult than a family. More a group of like-minded individuals than a gathering of people sharing either descent or affection. And yes, I know they now actually have lines of descent, but IMO, the way it's presented feels more like a conversion than an adoption or a siring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The Homecoming, to me, always seemed like kid from an adopted family, finally meeting their birth parents. There was that sense of relief, and familiarity to it that seemed really poignant to me, even if the metaphor was being applied in the form of a monstrous transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:07:04-07:00","id":556049,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly interested in the possibilities of Hunter/Beast crossovers, as much for Hunter's monsters (e.g., Mortal Remains pp.161\u2013165) as for the hunters themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:08:02-07:00","id":556050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556036#post556036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I agree fully. I realize that it doesn't come across this way, but I actually like those things, especially since it helps tie mages in to the Beast setting even more.I could see mages asking questions about the parrallels between the Devouring and Awakening, and taking notes. And if a mage who escaped the Morphean Continuity legacy encountered a Beast and heard it's story, the mage likely would see a parrallel and possibly want to &quot;help it&quot;. And it means that the Mage and Beast team up doesn't bug me as much when it comes to Heroes: While I can see a mage who relies the truth might try to intercede on the Heroes behalf to facilitate treatment (of that remains post revision), I also can get them coming at it as &quot;ahhh, Heroes are your Banishers... carry on.&quot;<br /> <br /> In a more general sense, it helps frame the idea of &quot;Astral force in human body&quot; as a thing when a mage encounters the Beast: their lore supports these things. Note, I am not saying the Mages are right or that I am trying to work on a universal cosmos, but it helps piece things together enough for an in setting encounter for me as an ST.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about the entire Mastigos Path for Mage crossover material. <br /> <br /> The Mastigos are all about confronting, learning from and overcoming fear. As Mind is one of their Ruling Arcana, they additionally have ready access to and influence in the astral realms, presumably including the Primordial Dream which is in (near? below? two doors down?) the Temenos. It also looks to me that Beasts actually could learn a thing or two about fear from Pandemonium. What nasty Nightmares could Beasts develop watching (feeding from?) a Mastigos engaging in a summoning of a supernal demon? <br /> <br /> Beasts and Mastigos should be kicking back a few cold ones and comparing notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:15:05-07:00","id":556053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555999#post555999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Forsaken and the Pure of 1st Edition were pretty cult-like in some aspects, what with the elaborate mythos, clannishness and quasi-sacred purposes. I don't know about 2E, since I haven't read it yet. Don't really see what this has to do with the discussion, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And mage... don't forget mage. Both we and 2e are predicated on joining Mystery Cults. 2e doesn't even hide that and expressly calls them out as such. The entire thing reads as a crossover of Plato and Gnostic theory, with a smattering of Kaballah, Alchemy and Hermeticism. <br /> <br /> It doesn't make it bad, and I don't know why it bothers people to point it out at times (maybe due to the negative connotations associated with cults). It makes sense that Supernaturals will have their own cultures. And due to their exclusive and isolated natures, combined with the nature of their abilities along with questions of origins and history, these organizations are going to take on relgious/cult-like manifestations. <br /> <br /> That said, it also makes sense for them not to have such organizations. Cults, religions and networks imply that you both have the numbers and enough unity of ideas to support an organization, amd not every splat does. Promethean offers a good example, as while the transmutation and origins can define them, their quest is too personal for more then generalities of organized beliefs. Depending on how Beast goes with their social structures, such as a low population, and I could get lower level of social complexity.<br /> <br /> As for Family versus Cult for the Beasts creation, it depends on which side you look at it: Human vs Horror. For Humans, it definitely is cultish, as it is having unusual experiences that results in an existing member facilitating your entrance. But from the Horror side, the unity of the Primordial Dream and their origin as children of the Dark Mother makes me think family: they trace a common lineage and origin, and as part of the realm of concepts, their physical appearance is less important than what they represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-15-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:19:06-07:00","id":556055,"title":"","content":"RE: &quot;abuse&quot;<br /> This is the World of Darkness, there's no shortage of people who deserve a little trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:25:47-07:00","id":556084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556050#post556050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How about the entire Mastigos Path for Mage crossover material. <br /> <br /> The Mastigos are all about confronting, learning from and overcoming fear. As Mind is one of their Ruling Arcana, they additionally have ready access to and influence in the astral realms, presumably including the Primordial Dream which is in (near? below? two doors down?) the Temenos. It also looks to me that Beasts actually could learn a thing or two about fear from Pandemonium. What nasty Nightmares could Beasts develop watching (feeding from?) a Mastigos engaging in a summoning of a supernal demon? <br /> <br /> Beasts and Mastigos should be kicking back a few cold ones and comparing notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that the book highlighted this. I also will admit though that I started playing the &quot;how would things backfire&quot; game too, where I looked at how mage interpetation of the actions of Beast's could lead to, ahem, unpleasantness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For example, the Mastigos Thearch who sees the Beast as a tool of the Lie, meant to keep people distracted and fearful, and thus preventing them from Awakening. Or an Obrimos... anything, really, who sees them as foul monsters who have possessed a human host. <br /> <br /> Actually... I do wonder how mages are going to take the whole &quot;and then my soul was devoured by the Horror that now resides within me&quot; bit. I mean, they are one of the only splats beyond Demons to deal with the soul extensively, and have a more personal take on it (vs. Demons, where it is a placeholder they jump into when needed). So how would they feel when they hear that someone's soul was eaten by a Astral Monster, especially when there are things like the Abyss who have entities that float in the Astral as well, and the idea of something eating and replacing something with a dark and monsterous force might place some mages on edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-15-2015, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:33:06-07:00","id":556089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555149#post555149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess one could use the Incarnate, Unfettered and Rampant as antagonists as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they have the placement in the book where they do for a reason... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Although insert standard disclaimer here of &quot;Use this how you want.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:33:23-07:00","id":556090,"title":"","content":"I don't know about anyone else but &quot;abuse&quot; to me generally requires some sort of familiarity and a breach of trust. Not just jumping people at random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:38:22-07:00","id":556093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556084#post556084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked that the book highlighted this. I also will admit though that I started playing the &quot;how would things backfire&quot; game too, where I looked at how mage interpetation of the actions of Beast's could lead to, ahem, unpleasantness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For example, the Mastigos Thearch who sees the Beast as a tool of the Lie, meant to keep people distracted and fearful, and thus preventing them from Awakening. Or an Obrimos... anything, really, who sees them as foul monsters who have possessed a human host.<br /> <br /> Actually... I do wonder how mages are going to take the whole &quot;and then my soul was devoured by the Horror that now resides within me&quot; bit. I mean, they are one of the only splats beyond Demons to deal with the soul extensively, and have a more personal take on it (vs. Demons, where it is a placeholder they jump into when needed). So how would they feel when they hear that someone's soul was eaten by a Astral Monster, especially when there are things like the Abyss who have entities that float in the Astral as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages are used to beings that have or had <i>not quite human</i> souls, such as werewolves, vampires and changelings. I believe attitudes will vary widely and depend both on the individual mages or cabals as well as the behavior and attitudes of the individual Beasts. For better or worse, Beasts will present a real <i>mystery</i> to explore.<br /> <br /> Absent using their Nightmares to steal or &quot;suppress&quot; souls or other similarly &quot;unpleasant&quot; conduct, I imagine most consilia would take a laissez faire attitude to Beasts in general. However, if local Beasts did engage in any widespread &quot;unpleasantness,&quot; I believe mages may very well be at the vanguard of the torches and pitchforks contingent.<br /> <br /> The soul issue actually makes me more curious how any Forsaken werewolf could positively view Beasts. Under their cosmology and priorities, they appear to be little more than particularly devious and dangerous Claimed or Hosts. I would think that most Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords would be ready to call a Sacred Hunt after meeting a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:44:07-07:00","id":556096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556035#post556035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit different, for the reasons I pointed out above. The reason I find it relevant is that the social and origin changes that happened between 1e and 2e reflect the changes between the first Kickstarter draft and the revision, that making Beasts become rather than realize allows for more potential societal mixture than hanging everything on being born into a particular group.<br /> <br /> It also leaves open the possibility of a demi-splat, that could even be encouraged into coming into existence.<br /> <br /> <b>Idea:</b> instead of having both extremes of the Inflicting Nightmares roll produce Heroes, have the Extraordinary Success awaken nascent Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>My remark doesn't come from he fact that the Begotten are now made rahter than born; it comes from HOW they are made. They have a few weird dreams, a guy appears, tell them &quot;This is hat yis going on, wanna join?&quot; and poof! Their soul get eaten and they're now a Beast. What in this scenario makes you think about family? To me, it's more like a visit by a demonic version of the Jehovah's Witnesses. Could be a cultural, thing, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:46:22-07:00","id":556097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556090#post556090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about anyone else but &quot;abuse&quot; to me generally requires some sort of familiarity and a breach of trust. Not just jumping people at random.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basing a game on some people purportedly deserving abuse appears rife with potential problems, and risks becoming little more than a juvenile power revenge fantasy where abused becomes abuser. I and my fellow players are not particularly sensitive, but even we would strenuously avoid this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:09:27-07:00","id":556117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556090#post556090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about anyone else but &quot;abuse&quot; to me generally requires some sort of familiarity and a breach of trust. Not just jumping people at random.</div> </div> </div> </div>We often think of abuse as a long term thing, but it can definitely be short term. The vampire who charms someone into handing over some cash is a minor abuse. The boss who uses her position of authority to convince someone to sleep with her is a pretty notable abuse. The bully at school who always takes your lunch money is a moderate abuse. It can take all shapes and sizes. Beast definitely has strong themes of religion and abuse that make for some rather unfortunate comparisons. But those unfortunate comparisons are pretty good fodder for an RPG. And I'm not sure it would be possible to run a WoD game that was fun without touching on unfortunate comparisons to something.<br /> <br /> <b>No matter what you do, someone will take offense.<br /> The important question is <i>how many.</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:11:54-07:00","id":556120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556055#post556055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: &quot;abuse&quot;<br /> This is the World of Darkness, there's no shortage of people who deserve a little trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be careful. These terms are thrown around and there is a lot of nuances with them that are other societal and personal.<br /> <br /> Abuse* is an improper affliction of physical or emotional injury onto another. It usually implies uneven power dynamics or predation, but doesn't have to. What it doesn't implies is success either. <br /> <br /> Trauma* is harm of the emotional or physical being of an individual. While it is synonymous to injury and it doesn't refer to abuse, many people associate the two. However, psychological harm can come from non-abuse situations, such as loss of a family member to cancer or severe anxiety from exams. <br /> <br /> What is clear to make the delineation here is that <i>harm of an individual by another </i>does not equal <i>abuse</i>, which I think is the point here. As noted, abuse is <u>improper</u> harm, and there are justifiable uses of it. For example, a cop who shoots a rabid dog threatening a child certainly harmed it, but it is not animal abuse: the use of force and resulting harm were justified. Meanwhile, the cop that shoots a dog because he hates its owner... that is abuse of both the animal and owner. Context defines whether such harm is abusive, and even then, it can be nuanced: being called an asshole and beaten is abusive when it is some random guy, but when it is part of your military training to resist capture and interrogation (SERE), it is not. And while you can argue ad nauseum as to where the line gets drawn, there is a difference.<br /> <br /> For Beasts, I think this line can exist. The thing is, Beasts need to cause fear. People can fear things without the element of abuse. I fear the ocean because I saw Jaws at a formative point (and live in an area with lots of great whites...damn it). Psychologically harmful? Sure. Abusive? No. Abuse is a means to propogate fear, but as the book and others pointed out, not the only one. <br /> <br /> For example, how about the Beast police detective who does everything by the books and feeds off the fear of questioning suspects? Is that abusive, if she acts no differently than any other upstanding cop should**? Heck, switch out punishment for prey, and a cop still works: chase down the criminal, with clamping down the cuffs as akin to going for the throat. Or how about a prosecutor? Have prey or punishment, and have him sate it by putting away crooks?<br /> <br /> Sure, I am focusing on the legal system (us Docs view lawyers in a... particular light). But there are a huge number of positions where those hungers can be fed and thus the Horror sated where the Beast doesn't need to abuse anyone, just play a role in society where is hunger is sated. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Note, when either are attached to &quot;sexual&quot;, they are essentially synonymous by legal, medical, and societal standards. Injury due to sex (and yes, I have seen it... God help me) is just called trauma in most documentations to make sure such confusion doesn't occur... I make this distinction here so no one thinks I am ignoring it or belittling it.<br /> **Yes, I know there is police brutality. I know people abuse their power in general. My example is assuming the Beast <i>doesn't, nor do they need to to fulfill their hunger. </i> Of course, doesn't mean a Beast can't be an abusive cop...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-15-2015, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:15:26-07:00","id":556124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556053#post556053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And mage... don't forget mage. Both we and 2e are predicated on joining Mystery Cults. 2e doesn't even hide that and expressly calls them out as such. The entire thing reads as a crossover of Plato and Gnostic theory, with a smattering of Kaballah, Alchemy and Hermeticism.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make it bad, and I don't know why it bothers people to point it out at times (maybe due to the negative connotations associated with cults). It makes sense that Supernaturals will have their own cultures. And due to their exclusive and isolated natures, combined with the nature of their abilities along with questions of origins and history, these organizations are going to take on relgious/cult-like manifestations.<br /> <br /> That said, it also makes sense for them not to have such organizations. Cults, religions and networks imply that you both have the numbers and enough unity of ideas to support an organization, amd not every splat does. Promethean offers a good example, as while the transmutation and origins can define them, their quest is too personal for more then generalities of organized beliefs. Depending on how Beast goes with their social structures, such as a low population, and I could get lower level of social complexity.<br /> <br /> As for Family versus Cult for the Beasts creation, it depends on which side you look at it: Human vs Horror. For Humans, it definitely is cultish, as it is having unusual experiences that results in an existing member facilitating your entrance. But from the Horror side, the unity of the Primordial Dream and their origin as children of the Dark Mother makes me think family: they trace a common lineage and origin, and as part of the realm of concepts, their physical appearance is less important than what they represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, as written, all we know about Horrors is that they come from the Primordial Dream, that makes them neighbours or compatriots, not family. This is disappointing, since the Dark Mother offers an obvious mean to make Beasts feel truly related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:34:10-07:00","id":556146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556124#post556124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, as written, all we know about Horrors is that they come from the Primordial Dream, that makes them neighbours or compatriots, not family. This is disappointing, since the Dark Mother offers an obvious mean to make Beasts feel truly related.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-revision, Souls also came from the Primordial Dream, and the relation of the Dark Mother to Horrors doesn't really seem to be any different, so I don't actually see your point in this? Horrors are no less related to each other than Souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:35:51-07:00","id":556147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555744#post555744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debates about morality, agency, etc aside my problem with the whole Devouring angle boils down to this: nobody in their right mind is going to say yes to the question &quot;is it cool if I <i>eat your soul</i> and turn you into a living Scared Straight program?&quot; The mechanical necessity/function of a soul in the NWoD notwithstanding, the popular conception of what constitutes your soul is a pretty big deal, enough so that most people aren't going to use it as a bargaining chip regardless of the payoff.<br /> <br /> At least with Vampires the pitch is a relatively easy sell. You can see how someone would be willing to change their diet and give up tanning in exchange for wealth, immortality and some incidental super powers. With Beast though? &quot;In addition to having your soul replaced with a Horror From Man's Darkest Imaginings, you'll have a slightly extended lifespan, some powers that are mostly good for smashing things and/or scaring the poo out of people, and sometimes the neighborhood loser will spontaneously come unglued and obsessively try to murder you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point, so rare these days in this thread. The presentation of the &quot;job&quot; could use some work. However, quite a few people that are considered to be in their right mind would actually say yes. The &quot;pitch&quot; could use some work. Of course, this is basically an early draft we're looking at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:46:49-07:00","id":556159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556097#post556097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basing a game on some people purportedly deserving abuse appears rife with potential problems, and risks becoming little more than a juvenile power revenge fantasy where abused becomes abuser. I and my fellow players are not particularly sensitive, but even we would strenuously avoid this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My perception of the original version actually had me seeing the game like that. It wasn't the intention for the game to be like that, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:50:31-07:00","id":556162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556093#post556093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mages are used to beings that have or had <i>not quite human</i> souls, such as werewolves, vampires and changelings. I believe attitudes will vary widely and depend both on the individual mages or cabals as well as the behavior and attitudes of the individual Beasts. For better or worse, Beasts will present a real <i>mystery</i> to explore.<br /> <br /> Absent using their Nightmares to steal or &quot;suppress&quot; souls or other similarly &quot;unpleasant&quot; conduct, I imagine most consilia would take a laissez faire attitude to Beasts in general. However, if local Beasts did engage in any widespread &quot;unpleasantness,&quot; I believe mages may very well be at the vanguard of the torches and pitchforks contingent.<br /> <br /> The soul issue actually makes me more curious how any Forsaken werewolf could positively view Beasts. Under their cosmology and priorities, they appear to be little more than particularly devious and dangerous Claimed or Hosts. I would think that most Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords would be ready to call a Sacred Hunt after meeting a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book mentions the views of Werewolves of Beast's can sometimes put them into the category of the Claimed, which.... can definitely sour relations. <br /> <br /> And I was speaking more of the fact that there is that choice component that darkly mirrors their own. Changlings were taken, wolf blooded are born or &quot;infected&quot; by exposure to Lunacy and transform randomly, Vampires are twisted by a curse. Prometheans are made and lack a true soul, hunters are (mostly) people. Demons are... something weird. And I don't remember mummies. <br /> <br /> But Beasts are similar enough in their origin that I feel a mage could see it as a dark parrallel of their own journey... and what conclusions they draw from it can be added to my 1001 story hooks for both games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556124#post556124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, as written, all we know about Horrors is that they come from the Primordial Dream, that makes them neighbours or compatriots, not family. This is disappointing, since the Dark Mother offers an obvious mean to make Beasts feel truly related.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if I follow. You mean the repeated lore about how the primordial dream and it's creaturds are her spawn or that Beasts claim to see her during the Devouring doesn't at least imply something more?<br /> <br /> Or ignoring that as IC fluff, how about just by how the Astral works? But if you assume that the PD follows the same rules as laid down in Astral Realms (the book), then if they view themselves and hold themselves to be kin in a Realm of Concepts, then they are. Even if it was once just a philosophy that held Beasts together at one point and mostly used as a metaphor, the Astral gives embodiment to philosophies and metaphors as actual things, and this likely lead to the Horrors being shaped into the family they are now. It is why mages can explore a Mars that both reflects the real one as well as one where Martians exist: the concepts of each exist and thus manifest as actual things in the Astral. Regardless of the origin, the fact that Horrors and Beasts draw on such symbolism (both culturally and for their powers) means that the concept exists within their realm at more than just a &quot;theory&quot; level, and their beliefs also then reinforces said concept.<br /> <br /> Now, if someone messed with their astral realms concepts, theoretically this could change...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:54:59-07:00","id":556164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556117#post556117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We often think of abuse as a long term thing, but it can definitely be short term. The vampire who charms someone into handing over some cash is a minor abuse. The boss who uses her position of authority to convince someone to sleep with her is a pretty notable abuse. The bully at school who always takes your lunch money is a moderate abuse. It can take all shapes and sizes. Beast definitely has strong themes of religion and abuse that make for some rather unfortunate comparisons. But those unfortunate comparisons are pretty good fodder for an RPG. And I'm not sure it would be possible to run a WoD game that was fun without touching on unfortunate comparisons to something.<br /> <br /> <b>No matter what you do, someone will take offense.<br /> The important question is <i>how many.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think it has strong themes of religion. You're filling in gaps because the game hasn't actually explained this Beast Religion, or whatever a person wants to call it. Religion is comparable to culture. Adding culture means you can begin to compare it to religion. At no point does this seem to represent any religion, except maybe the one specifically made for/by Beasts. Also, I would like to point out that Werewolves have their own religion. Mages have a couple. Basically, every game line has religion or something like it. So far, it is more appropriate to compare the Beast stuff to the Autumn Court rather than the Lancea Sanctum. The comparison is more fair so you would get less resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:56:06-07:00","id":556165,"title":"","content":"I really wish I could say that this revision leaves me more excited for Beast: The Primordial than before, but if I'm honest, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> I feel like Homecoming had significantly more emotional heft to it than Devouring does. I much prefer Homecoming to Devouring.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the opening fiction preceding the Introduction makes far less sense, if the Devouring was something accepted later in life, rather than Ben having been a Beast all along.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I think that what you're experimenting with in Beast may be the root of some of the difficulties.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think a Beast's Hungers are any worse than, say, a Vampire's need to feed on blood. I'm not sure why people find Hungers so objectionable but not feeding on blood. I, personally, have no objection to the lack of an Integrity/Humanity analogue, but I feel like without it, the people who find Hungers objectionable see a vampire with the brakes torn out.<br /> <br /> I can't say I'm all that excited for the new angle in a Beast's purpose. I realize Beast is supposed to be a game without social splats/a social splat axis (forgive me if I'm not using the right terminology here), but its introduction leaves me feeling a little like in lieu of that, we've been given just one social splat for the whole gameline, leaving out even the choice Masquerade Vampires had between Camarilla, Sabbat, and the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> If I have more specific thoughts about Heroes and the Primordial Dream as I digest the Introduction, I'll add my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:06:22-07:00","id":556197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556164#post556164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it has strong themes of religion. You're filling in gaps because the game hasn't actually explained this Beast Religion, or whatever a person wants to call it. Religion is comparable to culture. Adding culture means you can begin to compare it to religion. At no point does this seem to represent any religion, except maybe the one specifically made for/by Beasts. Also, I would like to point out that Werewolves have their own religion. Mages have a couple. Basically, every game line has religion or something like it. So far, it is more appropriate to compare the Beast stuff to the Autumn Court rather than the Lancea Sanctum. The comparison is more fair so you would get less resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to repost this since it sounds like you missed my response to this objection several pages back.<br /> <br /> <b>Please consider the following:</b><ul><li><b>A (hopefully) benevolent member of Beast society discovers you because you went searching for answers or you are the kind of person they want to join them.</b></li> <li><b>Said member of Beast society attempts to convert you by explaining their system of beliefs and offering supernatural perks.</b></li> <li><b>You agree to their belief system and undergo a process where you are reborn.</b></li> <li><b>Your new job requires you to seek out others and teach them your system of beliefs (at least the basic tenets).</b></li> <li><b>While you do so, you are also on the look out for potential converts.</b></li> </ul><b>There are probably numerous different systems of belief across the various types of beasts and geographical locations, so this does not suggest similarity to any <u><i><b>singular</b></i></u> religion. But it is quite similar to the behavior of <i><u><b>many</b></u></i> throughout history.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:25:04-07:00","id":556206,"title":"","content":"So there's something I'm still not clear on.<br /> <br /> Are Beasts kids? <i> Or are they squids?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:28:10-07:00","id":556208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556096#post556096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My remark doesn't come from he fact that the Begotten are now made rahter than born; it comes from HOW they are made. They have a few weird dreams, a guy appears, tell them &quot;This is hat yis going on, wanna join?&quot; and poof! Their soul get eaten and they're now a Beast. What in this scenario makes you think about family? To me, it's more like a visit by a demonic version of the Jehovah's Witnesses. Could be a cultural, thing, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Demonic Jehovah's Witnesses, you say? This comes to mind:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HiWfNsWa7d0\" data-code=\"HiWfNsWa7d0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HiWfNsWa7d0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That aside, I prefer stories where the traditional view of family, as being predicated upon the members having blood relations (or a suitable metaphysical equivalent) are challenged. The first draft did this fine, but lacked a catalyst for dropping out of a traditional family arrangement into this newer, self-selected model. The new introduction, in contrast, uses the Devouring to create the anomie necessary to make that leap. Part of that comes from knowing that staying with unchanged humans would be almost guaranteed to devolve into a vicious cycle of victimization and not entirely unjustified fratricide, while the other part comes from knowing that your fellow Begotten, and to a lesser extent, your Supernatural Kin, are hardly susceptible to the depredations of the thing that ate your soul the way your old friends would be, and more to the point, they get what you're going through in a way your old family never could. That acceptance is what makes that new family far superior to the traditional one, as is the lack of forced deference that arises in conventional families.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:49:13-07:00","id":556221,"title":"","content":"Okay, being born a beast was a big selling point for me. Creepy kids whose friends and family instinctively feel there's something off about, who are troubled by strange desires and unwholesome urges and terrible nightmares? Kids who always feel uncomfortable and out of place among other people, until one day the realization cones to them that it's because they're NOT people, they never were, they were always something ELSE, something dark and terrible and ancient, something that suddenly explains all the weirdness growing up? <br /> <br /> That is a powerful story. It's powerful because it's a mythic chosen one narrative common to our culture inverted (what if your parents are not your real parents? What if you're really royalty?). It's powerful because it's a story many players will feel resonance with- beasts aren't queer kids (well, some of 'me might be), but I can see some similarities, especially in the whole &quot;my family is the other freaks who know who and what I really am and accept me warts and fangs and dripping toxic ichor and all thing.<br /> <br /> A the new story is less powerful. It's not a bad story, but it's roots aren't as deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:04:29-07:00","id":556229,"title":"","content":"Where would a Esmaki with a hunger for prey who hunts adults to give children a fear of growing up fit in the new narrative focus?<br /> <br /> If the writers would come out and say that a beast is essentially a nightmare Claimed and sold it as that I think I would feel better about the changes. As I understand it Beasts are somewhere between a Sin-Eater and Claimed leaning more towards the Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:09:12-07:00","id":556233,"title":"","content":"There's certainly overlap, but there's a lot of overlap with Claimed in general. Even vampires and mages could be considered claimed. They are a far cry from the traditional claimed, whose personalities and even physical form are overwhelmed by something else. Beasts do seem to have a life outside of their hunger for fear. But a foreign entity has joined with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:34:05-07:00","id":556242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556233#post556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's certainly overlap, but there's a lot of overlap with Claimed in general. Even vampires and mages could be considered claimed. They are a far cry from the traditional claimed, whose personalities and even physical form are overwhelmed by something else. Beasts do seem to have a life outside of their hunger for fear. But a foreign entity has joined with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claimed fuse into a new individual. From what you describe is a Fear Sin-Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:37:43-07:00","id":556288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556242#post556242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Claimed fuse into a new individual. From what you describe is a Fear Sin-Eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Claimed by the dead is still Claimed&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, they're closer to Sin-Eaters as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:45:35-07:00","id":556293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555814#post555814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover was never a core intention of NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Oh, is that why they all work off of the same basic system and same vocabulary and have included direct references to other gamelines rather than an in-setting version of them?<br /> <br /> I've heard a lot of off the wall comments in this thread, but this one has earned a straight up Back To The Future reference. Think, McFly, think!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:48:01-07:00","id":556294,"title":"","con