 like you missed my response to this objection several pages back.<br /> <br /> <b>Please consider the following:</b><ul><li><b>A (hopefully) benevolent member of Beast society discovers you because you went searching for answers or you are the kind of person they want to join them.</b></li> <li><b>Said member of Beast society attempts to convert you by explaining their system of beliefs and offering supernatural perks.</b></li> <li><b>You agree to their belief system and undergo a process where you are reborn.</b></li> <li><b>Your new job requires you to seek out others and teach them your system of beliefs (at least the basic tenets).</b></li> <li><b>While you do so, you are also on the look out for potential converts.</b></li> </ul><b>There are probably numerous different systems of belief across the various types of beasts and geographical locations, so this does not suggest similarity to any <u><i><b>singular</b></i></u> religion. But it is quite similar to the behavior of <i><u><b>many</b></u></i> throughout history.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't miss it. I was responding to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:07:14-07:00","id":556315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556221#post556221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, being born a beast was a big selling point for me. Creepy kids whose friends and family instinctively feel there's something off about, who are troubled by strange desires and unwholesome urges and terrible nightmares? Kids who always feel uncomfortable and out of place among other people, until one day the realization cones to them that it's because they're NOT people, they never were, they were always something ELSE, something dark and terrible and ancient, something that suddenly explains all the weirdness growing up?<br /> <br /> That is a powerful story. It's powerful because it's a mythic chosen one narrative common to our culture inverted (what if your parents are not your real parents? What if you're really royalty?). It's powerful because it's a story many players will feel resonance with- beasts aren't queer kids (well, some of 'me might be), but I can see some similarities, especially in the whole &quot;my family is the other freaks who know who and what I really am and accept me warts and fangs and dripping toxic ichor and all thing.<br /> <br /> A the new story is less powerful. It's not a bad story, but it's roots aren't as deep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, too many people didn't see the intent of the story as you, and I, did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:56:06-07:00","id":556364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556315#post556315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, too many people didn't see the intent of the story as you, and I, did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less that intent and more people decided and started having an outcry about how clearly* this game represented oppressed minorities or the LGBT community.Which coupled with the initial lack of purpose to Beasts outside of feeding their own hunger made people argue how the game was basically representing the LGBT community as psychotic monsters out to make the world worse. Thus the whining and then somewhere along the line people started arguing how killing Heroes was wrong because it basically amounted to victim blaming** <br /> <br /> *Always sounded bloody stupid and insane to me, but there were a few people who liked that angle and I won't begrudge them it if they had more fun with the idea that way.<br /> ** I don't know the internet gets weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:03:12-07:00","id":556367,"title":"","content":"I will note that the text of the original draft does specifically site the &quot;stories of marginalized people&quot; as an inspirational source to draw on, and how Beasts are tied to &quot;the other&quot;. And there's A TON of treaded ground on using &quot;monsters&quot; to serve that purpose in fiction. So people weren't seeing it out of nowhere. It just wasn't ever supposed to be the central theme.<br /> <br /> I'll quote Rose over on the Kickstarter...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">At 14, I had a terrible secret. I knew I was a monster, and there was no one I could tell. Vampire: The Masquerade told me there was a world of people like me. It was tremendously liberating.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">But that's a double-edged identification. Because in the World of Darkness, vampires actually are monsters. They hurt and they kill and they break hearts and they're mostly not held to account for it. So at what point is the metaphor liberating and at what point is it shaming, stigmatizing? At what point is it saying that queer 14-year-old Rose really _is_ a monster?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Each World of Darkness game has to walk that line for itself. Sometimes we have to meander from side to side a little before we find the line.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is how art works. It's messy and it's dangerous and your message isn't always what you thought it was.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:09:08-07:00","id":556371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556229#post556229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would a Esmaki with a hunger for prey who hunts adults to give children a fear of growing up fit in the new narrative focus?<br /> <br /> If the writers would come out and say that a beast is essentially a nightmare Claimed and sold it as that I think I would feel better about the changes. As I understand it Beasts are somewhere between a Sin-Eater and Claimed leaning more towards the Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it, and I <b>wanted</b> Claimed to get their own splat.<br /> <br /> As to your concept, you're leaning dangerously close to Slasher territory. I'd require you to analyze your potential prey before going all murder-happy. Generally, you'd need to pick workaholics, absentee parents, or career bachelors, although, to be honest, the kids themselves seem to be a more appropriate target for the fear you are engendering. For your low to mid-Satiety Feedings, you'd want to use social programming attacks, framed to look like inconveniences stemming from adult problems, i.e.: Identity Theft, Credit Scams, forcing Demotions or Firings, out-fighting them for promotion, anything that would demonstrate the folly of abandoning childishness for adulthood. It wouldn't be undoable, but it would take a meticulous level of detail to do right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:17:52-07:00","id":556377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556367#post556367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that the text of the original draft does specifically site the &quot;stories of marginalized people&quot; as an inspirational source to draw on, and how Beasts are tied to &quot;the other&quot;. And there's A TON of treaded ground on using &quot;monsters&quot; to serve that purpose in fiction. So people weren't seeing it out of nowhere. It just wasn't ever supposed to be the central theme.<br /> <br /> I'll quote Rose over on the Kickstarter...<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm just mostly saying I never really saw it and how when I said &quot;clearly the game represents [etc]&quot; it was more on the grounds that people kept acting like it was on the first page in size 32 bold font as opposed to saying that it obviously did that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:20:45-07:00","id":556381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556371#post556371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see it, and I <b>wanted</b> Claimed to get their own splat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see how they are Claimed? A human soul and an ephemeral entity merge and become a completely new creature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:21:10-07:00","id":556382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556367#post556367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that the text of the original draft does specifically site the &quot;stories of marginalized people&quot; as an inspirational source to draw on, and how Beasts are tied to &quot;the other&quot;. <b>And there's A TON of treaded ground on using &quot;monsters&quot; to serve that purpose in fiction</b>. So people weren't seeing it out of nowhere. It just wasn't ever supposed to be the central theme.<br /> <br /> I'll quote Rose over on the Kickstarter...<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just fiction in general, it's most of the WOD protagonists!!! Given the very obvious and admitted politics of the authors and developers, and the themes within almost every WOD game line and book, analogizing the protagonists as minorities, the oppressed or alienated is the default reader perspective with WW products, even before any admissions by the writers in the text and elsewhere or interpretation by the audience. <br /> <br /> As noted by Rose, these metaphors are always a little risky, and sometimes they miss or the message is muddled or confused. If this wasn't the case with Beast, Matt, Rich and everyone else at OPP would certainly not have conceded some points and now engaged in a mad rush for revisions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:26:25-07:00","id":556385,"title":"","content":"Beasts are outsiders seemed to be intentional a theme. Outsider is a broad term. People were making it more narrow. I believe it was intended for Beasts to represent the <i>individual</i> as an outsider. If a player was LGBT then Beast could represent that through the player. The crazies came out to try and say Beasts represent outsiders as <i>groups</i>. It is a fine line. Beast can represent LGBT on an individual basis, but not symbolically. Beasts don't stand in for the LGBT community. Too many people blurred the line so then you have the problem that Beasts are monsters. Now the writers are supposed to try to manage writing the game as not to offend this one or that one? Bullshit. They would rather just kill off any notion of that. It does dilute the Beast concept and that is a shame, but I can't blame anyone for not wanting to write under those conditions. People really did seem to think Beasts were the LGBT game in WoD. *SMH* I don't know where these people come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:05:30-07:00","id":556408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556381#post556381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't see how they are Claimed? A human soul and an ephemeral entity merge and become a completely new creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is most assuredly by force, the other is presented with some degree of consent.<br /> One completely subsumes the personality of the host, the other doesn't.<br /> One is completely reversible, the other really isn't.<br /> <br /> Also, the powers design and fuel system are completely different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:07:32-07:00","id":556410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556385#post556385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are outsiders seemed to be intentional a theme. Outsider is a broad term. People were making it more narrow. I believe it was intended for Beasts to represent the <i>individual</i> as an outsider. If a player was LGBT then Beast could represent that through the player. <b>The crazies came out to try and say Beasts represent outsiders as <i>groups</i>.</b> It is a fine line. Beast can represent LGBT on an individual basis, but not symbolically. Beasts don't stand in for the LGBT community. Too many people blurred the line so then you have the problem that Beasts are monsters. Now the writers are supposed to try to manage writing the game as not to offend this one or that one? Bullshit. They would rather just kill off any notion of that. It does dilute the Beast concept and that is a shame, but I can't blame anyone for not wanting to write under those conditions. People really did seem to think Beasts were the LGBT game in WoD. *SMH* I don't know where these people come from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, the significant number of people who saw clear, uncomfortable and unfortunate parallels between Beasts and marginalized <i>groups</i> are &quot;crazies?&quot; Wow! <br /> <br /> WW protagonists have represented oppressed groups and minorities since the early 1990's, and they have been at the cutting edge of this social narrative among RPG manufacturers. In fact, they have received significant criticism for the actual inclusion and acknowledgement of these groups and often obvious left-wing political narrative in many of their products, including by me, One needs only to casually peruse the various sidebars and fiction throughout virtually all recent WW products to understand how the alienated and minority <i>group</i> viewpoints have been repeatedly emphasized and incorporated. <br /> <br /> Your argument is that Beast somehow totally broke the mold. The Beast authors certainly may have tried, but as both Rose and Matt explicitly acknowledged multiple times, good faith intent does not always equal success and sometimes metaphors and themes just don't work as written. You and some others may indeed <i>believe</i> Beasts in the first draft represented <i>individual</i> outsiders, but a great many here and elsewhere respectfully disagree.<br /> <br /> Now, you and anyone else are of course entitled to your own perspectives on both Beast drafts and related matters. This debate, while contentious, has generally remained polite, thoughtful and well-meaning, to say nothing of the fact that it has resulted in continuing major revisions to the book. Accordingly, your tone and insult are out of place, unwelcome and rude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:16:21-07:00","id":556416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556410#post556410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, the significant number of people who saw clear, uncomfortable and unfortunate parallels between Beasts and marginalized <i>groups</i> are &quot;crazies?&quot; Wow!<br /> <br /> WW protagonists have represented oppressed groups and minorities since the early 1990's, and they have been at the cutting edge of this social narrative among RPG manufacturers. In fact, they have received significant criticism for the actual inclusion and acknowledgement of these groups and often obvious left-wing political narrative in many of their products, including by me, One needs only to casually peruse the various sidebars and fiction throughout virtually all recent WW products to understand how the alienated and minority <i>group</i> viewpoints have been repeatedly emphasized and incorporated.<br /> <br /> Your argument is that Beast somehow totally broke the mold. The Beast authors certainly may have tried, but as both Rose and Matt explicitly acknowledged multiple times, good faith intent does not always equal success and sometimes metaphors and themes just don't work as written. You and some others may indeed <i>believe</i> Beasts in the first draft represented <i>individual</i> outsiders, but a great many here and elsewhere respectfully disagree.<br /> <br /> Now, you and anyone else are of course entitled to your own perspectives on both Beast drafts and related matters. This debate, while contentious, has generally remained polite, thoughtful and well-meaning, to say nothing of the fact that it has resulted in continuing major revisions to the book. Accordingly, your tone and insult are out of place, unwelcome and rude.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. Crazy is thinking Beast is the LGBT game and Beasts are the LGBT monsters so if Beasts are sadistic then that means LGBT must be sadistic, or at least the writers think that. It was valid to think there was too much LGBT stuff even though I didn't really agree. It was valid for an individual to to make the connections on an individual level, not my bag though. The opinion you just expressed and that many share are perfectly reasonable. It is when it is taken even further that people seem like loons. There is no grand conspiracy by Onyx Path to turn us all gay. I think it is obvious that Onyx Path doesn't have a problem with the LGBT community and is not trying to underhandedly portray them as monstrous. At most they might portray that community as feeling like they are monsters or get treated like monsters. Basically, anybody that thinks OP are gaybashers is crazy. I'll stand by that even if it is rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:42:46-07:00","id":556438,"title":"","content":"Beasts are outsiders. This is intentional. They are not like humans. To behave as the humans around them do would be wrong, would feel wrong, for them. There's a purposeful thematic resonance here.<br /> <br /> But the fear of the Other is one of our oldest, strongest fears as a species. It makes sense that our nightmares would look like trans people, or members of ethnic or racial or religious groups we see as outsiders. We fear these people, as a culture! They are the out group! Our Heroes, on the other hand, are usually righteous defenders of our tribe, whatever tribe we identify with.<br /> <br /> But you shouldn't identify beasts as trans kids, or women, or illegal immigrants, or whatever human out group you see them as resembling. Their only similarity to these &quot;alien&quot; groups is that they are &quot;not like us.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you are a trans person, the Other that your tribe fears is a neonazi shithead, or a conservative Christian doctor who wants to &quot;cure&quot; you, or harsh parental figures who deny your existence or put you out on the street.<br /> <br /> If you are a black kid, you fear teachers who talk down at you, or police, or scared white folk with guns.<br /> <br /> If you're a Jew, the Beast is gonna stalk your dreams in an SS uniform. If you're a parent, there's a nightmare out there that preys on kids. Sure, if you're from a certain demographic the Beast is gonna be a transgender atheist communist dragon with dreadlocks and a fondness for hooking your kids on drugs, but this is missing the point.<br /> <br /> You- yes you, real world human people- shouldn't take the Beast as too much of an analogy for oppressed groups. They're the Other, and there's some overlap there, but restricting living avatars of human nightmares to the Other with which you know and identify is a mistake. Serial killers are a Others. Cannibals are a Others. Abusers are Others. Violent zealots are Others. Cult leaders and drug dealers and thieves and rapists and kidnappers are Others. <br /> <br /> Beasts have as much in common with the Others you don't like as the ones you do. Maybe more! They are monsters, after all!<br /> <br /> The most important thing to me about Beasts is that they should be scary. Stating up my first Beast character according to the first rules we got, I had trouble sleeping that night! That's a good thing! (and she was a bloody unicorn, it's not like I was trying for a horror show here!)<br /> <br /> The idea that some thing inhuman and monstrous could be walking around thinking it's a child, like some horrible human cuckoo? That's powerful. Don't look at that story and decide it's saying that gay people are monsters walking around in human skins! I mean, the themes of hate are there, but that's just because all our fears and hatreds play out the same way. Vampires are gay people. Werewolves are people with mental illnesses. The God Machine is the big scary guv-mint. All monsters are allegories one way or another, but it's important not to let the allegory take over the monster story unless you want an allegorical story.<br /> <br /> I don't want the things we're afraid of (and maybe shouldn't be) to get in the way of my playing as Fear Itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:48:58-07:00","id":556441,"title":"","content":"The thing about metaphors, people should keep in mind, is that there's a message and a messenger to them, and that the largest trouble we have in communication is that we both run the risk of mistaking the message for the messenger as well as only seeing the messenger.<br /> <br /> The icons at work are broad idea forms that encapsulate a lot. Some flexibility in interpretation is required.<br /> <br /> Or, in old tired words, please remember to be generous in your reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:57:20-07:00","id":556445,"title":"","content":"In the interests of keeping the thread above a certain threshold of discussion enjoyability\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyone else hoping the fluff for how the Unchained interact with the Begotten gets a little less mutually hands-off?<br /> <br /> After all, we're talking about a species whose sole dead zone of metaphysical connection is the very thing demons are trying to hide from, with a forbidding mobile pocket realm inhabited by a terrifying guardian and capable of reaching some of the most hostile places in the universe with comparative ease <i>and</i> the ability to liaise with some of their more powerful denizens on nominally friendly terms. For a lot of constructivist Tempters, that seems like it'd be Hell in all but name.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, demons may not have much to offer in the way of worldly resources to the Begotten, but this <i>is</i> a group whose toolkit can easily produce gateways to other worlds, and whose innate capabilities include a couple of the main holes in the Beastly powerset vis-a-vis translation and outfitting; Beasts are the first supernatural gameline since Changeling to lack an innate linguistic workaround and gadgets help a fair bit to offset the potential complications of being Gorged or Slumbering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-16-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:31:48-07:00","id":556503,"title":"","content":"With Rip the Gates, Demons can travel to the Astral Realm, is it possible to travel directly to a Lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:32:42-07:00","id":556505,"title":"","content":"I've realized some parallels with other game lines are unavoidable no matter how they do the origin.<br /> <br /> If you were always &quot;different&quot; until your true nature presents itself, it's like Werewolf.<br /> <br /> If your transformed by other Beasts, it's like Vampire.<br /> <br /> If you were human but always had the potential to be &quot;more&quot; that you seized for yourself via embracing the incarnation of your fear as your self, it's like an Awakening.<br /> <br /> So some redundancy is unavoidable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:38:29-07:00","id":556514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556503#post556503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Rip the Gates, Demons can travel to the Astral Realm, is it possible to travel directly to a Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all likelihood, but the Dream in general seems like the more readily accessible locale, particularly given what little the existence of free-floating Chambers tells us.<br /> <br /> Sermon would be handy for Beasts looking to make new Chambers, too, I'd imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:38:52-07:00","id":556515,"title":"","content":"You can be transformed by others in Werewolf, too. More as a side-effect than as a reliable method of expanding the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:41:37-07:00","id":556521,"title":"","content":"I finally read the revised introduction. I would have read it sooner, but keeping up with this thread is work enough.<br /> <br /> It just seems kind of scattered, but here are a couple of thoughts.<br /> <br /> -The new reason for being seems to remove or lesson the kinship to other supernats. You seem less like a cousin or long lost sibling and more like a Teaching Assistant/Work Inspector who comes to tell you you're not doing it right.<br /> -If the Beast in question chose to become what they, then why would they care about &quot;Society tells them that monsters are villains&quot; exactly? They knew what they were getting into when they agreed to get nibbled and even had &quot;Gratitude&quot; when faced with the monster who had been stalking it.<br /> -The Begotten's conflictedness about their monstrous natures/hunger and their role to Teach with Fear seems off, because again they chose this.<br /> -Are the Children Claimed, Fear Sin-Eaters, or not even the original person to begin with? After reading about the devouring I got a Buffyverse vampire vibe, &quot;You have to remember that when you see <i>him</i>, <i>you</i>'<i>re not</i> looking at <i>your friend</i>. <i>You</i>'<i>re looking</i> at the <i>thing that killed him</i>.&quot; Are they one? Are they two? A specific statement on this matter is needed. All of the other supernats have it.<br /> <br /> -Overall I am not keen on the Beast no longer being born beasts. It goes against the original stated premise of the game. A suggestion that no one asked for: Make the Homecoming the default and keep the Devouring for those who are adopted or marry into the Family, allowing for non standard beasts. It allows for more options and story ideas and even Beast on Beast conflict &quot;You're not my real Brother&quot; or &quot;Hello, Canadian&quot;* Heck, maybe that's how the Primordial Dream allows for sudden or rapid change?<br /> -I think the Teaching by Fear reason works as one philosophy (Not covenant/tribe/order mind you) within the Beast community(?) feels limiting. Like there's only one way to be a &quot;Good&quot; or less hostile Beast. Another philosophy or would have added variety and even having no philosophy would add to the possibilities.<br /> <br /> I did like what was done to the Heroes though. Becoming what they are from being Integrity 4 and gazing too long into the Primordial Dream is interesting and not the roving of Beasts is interesting. Also, it makes the Beasts dislike of them more justified and the at times the Hero more tragic and we can avoid the victimization discussion from earlier. So, I like the Heroes and the Devouring and Teaching as options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:47:09-07:00","id":556527,"title":"","content":"Metaphors are great until somebody forgets they aren't to be taken literally.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering why Demons seem to be forced into an antagonist role since the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:51:10-07:00","id":556530,"title":"","content":"To drag that nearly dead horse back up, re: harmfulness of Beast vs Vampires.<br /> Is there anything that requires Beast's victims not to have given their consent to what happens to them?<br /> Reliably getting cool nightmares alone is something a lot of people would pay a lot for.<br /> Nearly every hunger is something a simple Craigslist ad would find you entire cities worth of people desperate to have you feed your Hunger on them.<br /> <br /> So no, Vampires being less harmful is something that falls flat in regards to agreed consent as well, as Beast's can get that too and they are even better about it because they don't need to inflict physical harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:55:19-07:00","id":556533,"title":"","content":"As Matt explained, I fully understand that Beasts were intended to represent more generic &quot;outsiders,&quot; rather than as a stand-ins for certain minority or oppressed groups. As a very long-time fan, who is well aware of the work of Matt, Rose, DaveB, DavidH and others, I'm additionally quite aware that they would never <i>intentionally</i> analogize these groups as monsters inherently inimical to society. As a political moderate with a thick skin who many would consider &quot;privileged&quot; (straight, white, male, Jewish, NYC attorney), I'm also not personally affected or extremely sensitive to these issues in the context of the RPG's I enjoy, and often don't like it when these themes are conveyed in a heavy-handed manner, even when I basically agree with the authors' viewpoints, because I find it distracting and preachy. Nevertheless, I still clearly read and understood Beasts as uncomfortably analogous to societally alienated groups, and thought revisions were appropriate in order to achieve what I assumed was Matt's original vision (my reasons are detailed at length in earlier posts). In the final analysis, good faith intentions are irrelevant if the final text conveys a different or confused message.<br /> <br /> I understand and respect that some may not share my perspective or liked the original draft of Beast for precisely the very reasons I thought negatively impacted upon its quality. It's impossible to please everyone all the time, and debates about WW products are the norm, not the exception. I certainly did not take these discussions personally, enjoyed the relatively peaceful and thoughtful analysis, and was appreciative that Matt, Rich and others were responding to fan feedback, one of the primary reasons for open development and the early release of the draft.<br /> <br /> I simply wish to keep the ongoing discussion as amicable as possible, and believed that accusing people who find the minority group parallels in Beast troublesome and strongly encouring change as &quot;crazies&quot; was unfortunate, unhelpful and risked derailing the discourse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typos 06-16-2015, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:05:55-07:00","id":556541,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a link to a cohesive critique or whatever set off the revisions? I think fora and social media have finally fragmented beyond my Google-fu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:08:41-07:00","id":556542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556527#post556527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaphors are great until somebody forgets they aren't to be taken literally.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering why Demons seem to be forced into an antagonist role since the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If a game has certain pervasive metaphors as part of its primary setting and themes, it sets the tone for the entire work. These metaphors need not be taken literally to be objectionable and impact the overall quality of the book.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert about Demon (I'm not personally enamored with the God Machine as a plot device), so cannot speak to why they might always be considered antagonists. However, while the comparisons of Beast to other WW game lines is quite informative and entertaining, Beast must still stand on its own (even with its expressly crossover-friendly setting and mechanics). The strengths, weaknesses and related issues with other WW games do not excuse or absolve Beast's perceived failings or shortfalls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:09:01-07:00","id":556543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556371#post556371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see it, and I <b>wanted</b> Claimed to get their own splat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, I too would like the Claimed to get their own splat or demi-splat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:11:21-07:00","id":556545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556541#post556541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a link to a cohesive critique or whatever set off the revisions? I think fora and social media have finally fragmented beyond my Google-fu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, some more verbose Dev commentary at some point would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:17:07-07:00","id":556548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556545#post556545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, some more verbose Dev commentary at some point would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would probably only set off more arguments. The partisan camps of Draft 1 vs Draft 2 have already formed. <br /> <br /> However, a simply review of the Kickstarter general comments and those connected to the update for new Introduction by Matt, Rich and Rose, as well as reviewing Matt's relatively few comments here and on rpg.net, should prove very informative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:17:34-07:00","id":556549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556527#post556527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been wondering why Demons seem to be forced into an antagonist role since the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing its a mix of Demons not being like anything else in the setting normally. I mean part of the thing with Demons is that the GM is huge and very confusing and not understood, so linking it with the Beghotten would be rather awkward on dealing with it there. Probably also the fact that one of the major things to deal with in Demon is paranoia and spy stuff. I know there's at least one or two threads I've seen where the issue in a game is detecting other Demons or Angels. Beasts being able to pick out another splat at glance almost would be rather devastating for trying to add into the worry on whether or not a person ,or persons, nearby are Angels or enemy Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:18:55-07:00","id":556550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556527#post556527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaphors are great until somebody forgets they aren't to be taken literally.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering why Demons seem to be forced into an antagonist role since the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really antagonistic. More like they're both Homer Simpson, and they see each other as Ned Flanders. They dislike each other on an instinctual, mostly irrational level, but they don't really fight outright.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Which, in restrospect, is still antagonistic, but a <i>different</i> antagonism than, say, Forsaken v. Pure or Hunter v. Everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:24:15-07:00","id":556552,"title":"","content":"I really think if we, as a group demand the Homecoming we will get it. There is no feel for family in the Devouring. You don't really choose family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","name":"imposterzilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:33:30-07:00","id":556555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imposterzilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556552#post556552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think if we, as a group demand the Homecoming we will get it. There is no feel for family in the Devouring. You don't really choose family.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although I do not agree, I would note that Rose and Matt stated that this issue and others will soon be addressed in the upcoming revisions. We've only seen the new Introduction, and the Devouring complaints may prove premature. There should be much more in the pipeline. Matt can only write so fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:35:18-07:00","id":556556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imposterzilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556552#post556552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think if we, as a group demand the Homecoming we will get it. There is no feel for family in the Devouring. You don't really choose family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think that's fair to say in an absolute statement.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm for the &quot;Two States&quot; solution. Natural Beasts are &quot;born&quot; through the Homecoming, normal humans can &quot;marry in&quot; via Devouring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:38:15-07:00","id":556557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556548#post556548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a simply review of the Kickstarter general comments and those connected to the update for new Introduction by Matt, Rich and Rose, as well as reviewing Matt's relatively few comments here and on rpg.net, should prove very informative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be, but isn't, because they are all over the place and buried deep in 250-page threads on other topics. Like here...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:40:41-07:00","id":556562,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for comprehensive then I think you are out of luck, Verge. Generally, the changes are clarifications.<br /> <br /> I doubt demanding will get you anywhere. You could try a well thought out argument. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-16-2015, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:48:43-07:00","id":556563,"title":"","content":"Here, Verge, this is probably the most comprehensive response you will get about the changes.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-beastly-process/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-beastly-process/\" target=\"_blank\"> A Beastly Process [Monday Meeting Notes] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> 