/div> </div><br /> It would be great if OPP added a separate Beast sub-forum. It would certainly help break-down and organize the different discussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:03:40-07:00","id":556579,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, the person that would work on the forums is busy with Beast. It could be said they should have done it before the kickstarter, but not much anyone can do about that now. It is annoying not having a Beast forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:05:34-07:00","id":556581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556567#post556567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, think I caught you between edits. It's the well-thought-out arguments I'm trying to find. Guess I'll have to settle for tough luck...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well-thought-out arguments about what exactly? There are plenty in this thread, but we are at page 248.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:07:18-07:00","id":556583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556579#post556579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the person that would work on the forums is busy with Beast. It could be said they should have done it before the kickstarter, but not much anyone can do about that now. It is annoying not having a Beast forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe a sub-forum will be the next announced Stretch Goal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:10:11-07:00","id":556588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556583#post556583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe a sub-forum will be the next announced Stretch Goal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd buy that for a dollar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:15:36-07:00","id":556591,"title":"","content":"Suppose I could have been more specific: I'm looking for the too-close-to-home-for-LGBT+ metaphor, but I don't think I'd do anything constructive with it at the moment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: &quot;well-thought-out&quot; was quoting what you, Diggs, had written, which I cut out of the quote, because it had read as a dig that you had edited out (rather than in), and I was ribbing you with an in-joke, rather than taking offense...<br /> <br /> EDIT THE SECOND: or giving offense! Didn't mean to summarily dismiss the whole of the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":". 06-16-2015, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:01:44-07:00","id":556637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556313#post556313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't miss it. I was responding to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, then I am not sure what to say. All my points seem to address and overcome your points, but you probably feel the same way about your own points. Maybe we should agree to disagree? There are lots of people who have commented on the religious similarities in this thread, so I feel pretty confident in my position.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:14:03-07:00","id":556643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556591#post556591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose I could have been more specific: I'm looking for the too-close-to-home-for-LGBT+ metaphor, but I don't think I'd do anything constructive with it at the moment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: &quot;well-thought-out&quot; was quoting what you, Diggs, had written, which I cut out of the quote, because it had read as a dig that you had edited out (rather than in), and I was ribbing you with an in-joke, rather than taking offense...<br /> <br /> EDIT THE SECOND: or giving offense! Didn't mean to summarily dismiss the whole of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that I can't think of any, but that sounds suggestive that I have seen and found some wanting. I don't recall any good posts that might have convinced the authors. I suspect the number of voices pointing it out led to another look at the text and they starting pulling it away. I also think I might have misspoke earlier by saying I disagree. I disagree that all the LGBT characters, allusions and metaphors were too much that it was a problem, not that they didn't exist. I probably did a better job when I was defending someone getting piled on for pointing out the references. There are tons of people with opinions expressing their like or dislike of all the LGBT tone. I don't think any one person convinced the writers.<br /> <br /> This thread has long since numbed me to taking offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-16-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:15:42-07:00","id":556645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Mettings</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>REASON TO DRINK: To Matt McF and Rose. All kidding aside, they had a hell of a week and comported themselves professionally throughout.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You're damn right!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:37:34-07:00","id":556654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556637#post556637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, then I am not sure what to say. All my points seem to address and overcome your points, but you probably feel the same way about your own points. Maybe we should agree to disagree? There are lots of people who have commented on the religious similarities in this thread, so I feel pretty confident in my position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our difference results in me talking about religion and you about religious practices. There is also your bullet points, half of which is not actually in the book. If you want my opinion of your bullet points then I would agree you seem to be working on a religion there. I don't think your assessment is necessarily wrong. I think it is only one of many possible interpretations so it would be premature to choose your version. We have a few sentences on a subject that will be explained later in the book. I'm not sure how to address your bullet points since I believe we are not supposed to go into religion much. I can't give an analysis of religion. I don't see any reason to tear apart your points at this time.<br /> <br /> An actual religion is not something I would suspect Matt is going to make this Beast thing, but it is possible. Your version of what Beasts would be doing is certainly religious. The Autumn Court could be viewed in a similar way so that would be a better thing to compare instead of the Lancea Sanctum. The Lancea Sanctum has a Christian veneer. I don't see how anyone can see the Beast thing as Christian. That is what is controversial and why people keep saying to drop that aspect. The Autumn Court has no basis in real world religion. If Beasts have religion it would be the same. In that way it would be nothing like the LGBT issues so it was not a trade like that. The trade was no culture to fear teacher, LGBT heavy to light (presumably). They are unrelated in every way. The last point would be I can't see why it matters if Beasts have religion since every game line does, or something comparable.<br /> <br /> You see religious similarities but that does not necessarily mean a religion exists. I avoid stepping on cracks. It is not out of a superstitious belief that it will hurt my mother. It is a OC manifestation. My actions might seem superstitious, but they are not. A Beast's actions might seem religious, but not be carried out in the name of a religion. They would not be <i>actually</i> religious.<br /> <br /> Unless you change your premise, I really don't see how I can respond. Most of your points can be used to describe the Autumn Court or there would be a parallel. I can give your opinion another look if you want to come at it from that angle. I'm not sure how relevant it would be since in about a week we should have more information on what Beasts are doing and why. You might change your mind then, maybe not about it being religious, but I can't tell you about what I haven't seen yet.<br /> <br /> I can agree to disagree though. I was of the mind that there was nowhere to go with the discussion. If you see a path, I don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:46:16-07:00","id":556655,"title":"","content":"That I gathered. My first read was that the change to Devouring and the adding of Teaching was more of a retreat to a politically neutral ground, but MattRichRose have said it was never their intention to be there in the first place. I'm glad they're mindful, but lurches in theme at a fetal stage of the game worry me.<br /> <br /> I guess since I'm on the topic: Satiety. I think tinkering here would have addressed a lot of the &quot;too monstrous&quot; complaints. It's an Integrity analog, but unlike most others, it doesn't define risky behaviors. Satiety both rises and falls on being monstrous, meaning that trying to remain a little bit human is only ever a matter of convenience. That's thematically appropriate, but why not have some behaviors that tempt the Horror, whet its appetite, so to speak? For example, a Makara hungering for Ruin might be ill-advised to work in construction, where as a Giant hungering for Punishment should avoid any contact with the prison system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:47:59-07:00","id":556658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556549#post556549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing its a mix of Demons not being like anything else in the setting normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many things in the NWoD aren't like anything else, that's one of the biggest selling points. It's a huge world filled to the brim with weird and impossible horrors.<br /> Chosing to define the GM as the &quot;outer border&quot; of weirdness in the NWoD makes the whole setting suffer. Fun as it is, the GM should not be the apex of unique weirdness the setting has to offer.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556549#post556549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean part of the thing with Demons is that the GM is huge and very confusing and not understood</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, many things in the setting are huge, very confusing and not understood. This is not a special, unique quality of the GM and it shouldn't be, for the sake of the larger setting. I am fully okay with making this specialness apply within a Demon only game, but once you include the larger NWoD the setting's larger concerns should take precedence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556549#post556549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts being able to pick out another splat at glance almost would be rather devastating for trying to add into the worry on whether or not a person ,or persons, nearby are Angels or enemy Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nearly every single splat out there can do this, and Spoofing has always been more than enough to deal with this. Beasts really don't require special treatment in this regard. Just have the rules state how often Demons have to 're-spoof' to be protected from a Beast's super-sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-16-2015, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:54:24-07:00","id":556662,"title":"","content":"The intention is for Beasts to be monstrous. I think they got focused on that and forgot about the rest of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There will always be complaints. My position and what I heard from many others was the issue was feeling forced to be that monstrous. It also felt like you had no real choice in the matter. The Devouring actually fixed all of that, although I'm not convinced that was the way to go. There were other reasons for the Devouring too though. Interesting idea on Hunger triggers, but I don't think we can really expect anything (more) new at this point.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm okay with playing a sadistic monster as long as I know I'm choosing it every step of the way. If I feel like I have to play it that way then I'm not interested. I felt the game before was restrictive. I know it wasn't, but the tone matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:34:58-07:00","id":556675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556658#post556658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many things in the NWoD aren't like anything else, that's one of the biggest selling points. It's a huge world filled to the brim with weird and impossible horrors.<br /> Chosing to define the GM as the &quot;outer border&quot; of weirdness in the NWoD makes the whole setting suffer. Fun as it is, the GM should not be the apex of unique weirdness the setting has to offer.<br /> <br /> Similarly, many things in the setting are huge, very confusing and not understood. This is not a special, unique quality of the GM and it shouldn't be, for the sake of the larger setting. I am fully okay with making this specialness apply within a Demon only game, but once you include the larger NWoD the setting's larger concerns should take precedence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nearly every single splat out there can do this, and Spoofing has always been more than enough to deal with this. Beasts really don't require special treatment in this regard. Just have the rules state how often Demons have to 're-spoof' to be protected from a Beast's super-sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say nothing else was unique or special. Look later in the Beast book part of the explanation with Demons was mentioned as the GM being alien. This is not to say nothing else is alien more that the GM is something that is alien from the perspective of Beasts. Everything else has survival, life, and the details that come from actually being a living thing. (For the value of saying living when dealing with vampires and the like.) The GM lacks those desires to survive or any recognizable similarities to a living thing.<br /> <br /> I'm also saying that GM is rather central to Demon and defining it in more broad strokes is probably something best avoided lest you cause problems by conflicting with the primary antagonist needed for the entire Demon splat. It isn't a case of this being the only thing allowed to be too big and complex to understand. It is case of the GM and its creations being a blindspot in the sense of familiarity they have with everything else.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge the ability of other splats to recognize other splats tend to be abilities one would have to have and usually have cost associations.( Auspex, or some spell from a mage.) Unless you're just seeing the supernatural stuff that crops up like magic, disquiet, chrinos, etc. It's kind of just a passive power for Beasts.<br /> <br /> To put it in a simpler analogy just assume Demons lack a presence in the Primordial Dream. It makes sense, they weren't designed by humans, when they ran properly they were just programs that might have had to interact with people and so used a really complex people disguise, they are literally a quantum matrix/computer. Wouldn't be too hard to assume that the Unchained lack a presence in the Dream. After that it comes off rather similar to an encounter between a psyker and a blank in a Caiphus Caine story I once read.*<br /> <br /> *The psyker started screaming bloody murder about how the blank was nothing and shouldn't exist.Psykers are literally insane though, so no real complications arose from it after the psyker's freak out led to her passing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:53:22-07:00","id":556681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556675#post556675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything else has survival, life, and the details that come from actually being a living thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lost me here.<br /> I don't see that as correct even for the small number of creatures that NWoD has already described to us. It becomes doubly hard to swallow when you consider just how much is implied to be out there in the NWoD that hasn't been described yet.<br /> <br /> Some other splats can recognize you without requiring activation. By a strict reading for example, passive mage sight should ping a Demon's cover as an active supernatural effect. If it doesn't because cover is handwave'd as not being an active supernatural thing, then the same reasoning could be used to explain that a Demon in Cover automatically counts as human to a Beasts senses. No extra specialness or deeper explanation needed.<br /> <br /> Demons may or may not lack presence in the Primordial Dream, but so should lots of other things out there, that doesn't make them unique either.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-16-2015, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:05:43-07:00","id":556683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556681#post556681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other splats can recognize you without requiring activation. By a strict reading for example, passive mage sight should ping a Demon's cover as an active supernatural effect. </div> </div> </div> </div>Peripheral Mage Sight doesn't work on effects that are designed to cloak themselves. A mage has to suspect that you're a demon and then scan you to see if you're human, which would result in a difficult roll-off taking several turns for most mages. If the mage is particularly powerful, or your Cover particularly weak, it might be over more quickly, but <i>in general[</i>, if the wizard starts looking at you funny, run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:19:22-07:00","id":556701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556683#post556683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Peripheral Mage Sight doesn't work on effects that are designed to cloak themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked up Cover rules to make sure, but Cover's inbuild 'hide itself from being identified as a supernatural effect' effect is Spoofing. It doesn't have another effect that would hide the Cover's nature as a supernatural effect from passive mage sight outside of that.<br /> By RAW, to be immune to being detected by passive mage sight without having to spoof it would have to have a passive &quot;hide itself&quot; effect that Spoofing then works in addition to. I may have missed that on my quick read, but I cannot see any such base effect in its description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":".  and the mistakes keep on coming 06-16-2015, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:19:33-07:00","id":556702,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to playing a sadistic monster myself. My bone with Devouring is that it's a bizarre and senseless choice, <i>given what we know</i>. It's not that dreams lack wisdom or fear isn't wise, but nightmares are irrational and fear is learned. Anyone who thinks that inflicting anxieties and worse on people who offend some dream-monster's sense of propriety is worth giving over their own soul as victuals is already a monster, choice or not. And this makes it harder to relate, for me, to a Devoured. Homecoming is bittersweet, because you have an understanding of who you are, and you have people who understand you now, but through no fault of your own you are hunted and despised. A Devoured basically buys a white elephant of Hunger and isolation, and then is tenuously bound not to be too much of a monster.<br /> <br /> And while I guess that reads as agency, I still don't see how the Horror closes the deal. They either find people with dubious moral compasses and give them their sick hearts' desires, or they somehow convince Joe Dreamer that being a sadistic monster is actually a calling on par with pedagogy and mentoring. And while that's interesting, those motives are in line with these sorts of characters, while the choice (as described so far) filters out the people who should find conflict with their own nature and the depredations of their kindred. I'm not crying paradox, but there seems a circle needs squaring here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:37:56-07:00","id":556707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556681#post556681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You lost me here.<br /> I don't see that as correct even for the small number of creatures that NWoD has already described to us. It becomes doubly hard to swallow when you consider just how much is implied to be out there in the NWoD that hasn't been described yet.<br /> <br /> Some other splats can recognize you without requiring activation. By a strict reading for example, passive mage sight should ping a Demon's cover as an active supernatural effect. If it doesn't because cover is handwave'd as not being an active supernatural thing, then the same reasoning could be used to explain that a Demon in Cover automatically counts as human to a Beasts senses. No extra specialness or deeper explanation needed.<br /> <br /> Demons may or may not lack presence in the Primordial Dream, but so should lots of other things out there, that doesn't make them unique either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Demons aren't human and never will be. As such, they have never been touched by the Primordial Dream. The demon's use for souls are as Covers, disposable lives that they never truly inhabit. As such, they are invisible to the Horrors in the Astral Realms, and difficult for the Beasts to find. Other splats have more earthly roots than the debris of a pan-dimensional construct capable of using all magical energies ever, allowing the Beasts to forge connections the Unchained refuse.<br /> <br /> Also, as a crossover game, Beast has a responsibility to honor <i>all </i>of the other games' assumptions. Demons are assumed to be paranoid, soulless biomechanical horrors constructed to be cogs in a cosmic machine who now fear discovery above all else. <i>Of course</i> these social butterflies who ingratiate themselves with the monsters the God-Machine exploits present a real and immediate risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:40:59-07:00","id":556710,"title":"","content":"Because I looked up the Revelations blog and to better explain my reasoning, the blog says&quot;Any form of concealment magic defeats it <i>without a Clash of Wills</i>&quot; (emphasis mine).<br /> <br /> So, by the rules I assume the following<br /> Peripheral Mage Sight: &quot;hey there, are you an ongoing supernatural effect? Don't worry, if you are hiding from me you automatically succeed on the Clash of Wills!&quot;<br /> Demon's Cover: &quot;No Clash of Wills necessary, let me see if my power to try and stay hidden from you can activate. *rolls Spoof, fails* Oh, looks like I failed to activate the power that would hide me from you. I am an onging supernatural effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the effect that hides the Cover fails to activate against Peripheral Mage Sight, then there is no active camouflage effect against that Peripheral Mage Sight could automatically fail the Clash of Wills.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:45:06-07:00","id":556713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556707#post556707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons aren't human and never will be. As such, they have never been touched by the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that makes them unique in the wider NWoD?<br /> I don't buy that there aren't other creatures that share this in the vastness of the NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:49:00-07:00","id":556715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556701#post556701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked up Cover rules to make sure, but Cover's inbuild 'hide itself from being identified as a supernatural effect' effect is Spoofing. It doesn't have another effect that would hide the Cover's nature as a supernatural effect from passive mage sight outside of that.<br /> By RAW, to be immune to being detected by passive mage sight without having to spoof it would have to have a passive &quot;hide itself&quot; effect that Spoofing then works in addition to. I may have missed that on my quick read, but I cannot see any such base effect in its description.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine, considering the point of a cover is to prevent the unchained from being picked up by the GM, that a cover is kind of a cloaking effect. With spoofing being used to handle more ground level specific targeting like mind reading. The RAW does actually mention mind reading magic when it was discussing spoofing, because well a spell designed to read minds doesn't work to read hard drives.<br /> <br /> As for your whole thing on there being lots of things that shouldn't connect with the Primordial Dream. You'll have to explain that since I'm not drawing a large pool that wouldn't require part of the explanation for one showing up being, &quot;and then someone broke the universe.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:53:20-07:00","id":556716,"title":"","content":"Well, that did actually happen a couple of times, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:59:10-07:00","id":556717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556715#post556715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for your whole thing on there being lots of things that shouldn't connect with the Primordial Dream. You'll have to explain that since I'm not drawing a large pool that wouldn't require part of the explanation for one showing up being, &quot;and then someone broke the universe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that there are Abyssal creatures that are explicidly the result of someone breaking the Universe?<br /> Thing is, no matter what example I bring, because we have so little material you could come up with some reasoning for why they could be connected. Example: Unfleshed. There is no more reason why they should be connected to the Primordial Dream than Demons, but if you give me five minutes I could come up with a dozen reasons why they might be connected. <i>Which doesn't </i><i>matter</i>, because I could do the same for Demon. They disconnect is a conscious decision the designer made, because if they wanted to they could have made the decision to link them up.<br /> <br /> I am not against Demons being non-kin to Beasts, because I understand the need to keep their themes of staying hidden intact. I am against having them explicidly be the <i>only</i> creatures in the setting that are, because it makes the NWoD smaller and gives a limit to how weird and out there the supernaturals the Beast meets can be. NWoD should have more mysteries to offer that leave Beasts stumped and stlightly freaked out than just Demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, why would other Creatures that don't connect to the Primordial Dream have to be the result of someone breaking the Universe at all? The GM is not that special!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-16-2015, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T03:03:53-07:00","id":556718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556713#post556713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that makes them unique in the wider NWoD?<br /> I don't buy that there aren't other creatures that share this in the vastness of the NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is theme.<br /> <br /> Demon is a spy game with trapping of demonology mixed in with an antagonist which is basically God.<br /> <br /> Fluff can sort it's out but in theme, it makes sense in the context that Demons are cut off in their own little world of paranoia and trust issues and more importantly, Beasts can't ID Demons on sight.<br /> <br /> Because if they could...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T03:57:28-07:00","id":556725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556718#post556718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the issue is theme.<br /> <br /> Demon is a spy game with trapping of demonology mixed in with an antagonist which is basically God.<br /> <br /> Fluff can sort it's out but in theme, it makes sense in the context that Demons are cut off in their own little world of paranoia and trust issues and more importantly, Beasts can't ID Demons on sight.<br /> <br /> Because if they could...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I absolutely agree with this. I have no problem with Demon requiring some thematic extra protection. But the way to implement it and chose to make Demons the <i>only</i> non kin and what that says about the rest of the NWoD is the problem.<br /> A simple sentence like &quot;the World of Darkness is a vast place of unknowable horrors, some of which leave even Beasts at a loss and are not kin to them. Beasts feel instinctive revulsion towards these and see them as unnatural beings that shouldn't be part of the Universe, often making it their objective to fight them whenever they can to protect their family. Most well known among these horrors are the former servants of the God Machine, described in Demon: the Descent... [rules follow]&quot; would make me completely okay with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T04:27:50-07:00","id":556728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556527#post556527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering why Demons seem to be forced into an antagonist role since the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're not. Its just thematically inappropriate for the Unchained to be associated with the Dark Mother. Demon is predicated on the assumption that the God Machine is their Creator; you can't make the D.M. their mother without making the DM give birth to the GM, and that's a very large statement to make. They're also called &quot;unchained&quot; because they don't have any chains - any natural bonds - to reality or people, making it a stretch to assume they'd be connected to Beasts by default.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, it also provides a very nice &quot;WTF, there are supernaturals who AREN'T tied to the Dark Mother?&quot; moment for the Beasts, and eventually a plot hook, not antagonists. Demons provide the exception that leads to greater exploration instead of merely accepting the myths and stories. Its something different that breaks their happy little boxes that they put everyone in.<br /> <br /> In short, its really just unthematic for Demons to be considered Kin, and they make good plot hooks as the exception. There's no reason to assume that they're the only exception out there, but Beast, as a game, is focusing on the PC splats to cross over with, and most of those other exceptions aren't part of that focus. Its also thought provoking - all this argument about how they should not be the only exception?<br /> <br /> <i>That's what the Beasts should be arguing about in character!</i> &quot;Holy shit, guys! The Dark Mother didn't mother everything! What else is out there? And what does that make us?&quot; Ah, drama and plot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-16-2015, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T04:32:13-07:00","id":556732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imposterzilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556552#post556552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't really choose family.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, contrare! I think that's exactly the message of the game. You DO choose your family. I feel like that's a major part of the game, why we're calling everyone Kin and Family. We're choosing these new people that understand us for our family, and leaving the blood relations who don't quite get us behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:37:57-07:00","id":556780,"title":"","content":"You know, a Nightmare developed in a way akin to Kinship Nightmares with a Demon could be pretty fun. Something like They're Not Who They Appear to Be, which convinces the target that some of their allies were replaced with imposters. Admittedly it would probably take a good deal more work than an actual Kinship Nightmare since you effectively have to make it from whole cloth instead of tapping your Social Link for guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1965-joebobjoe","name":"joebobjoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:13:46-07:00","id":556812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joebobjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556780#post556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, a Nightmare developed in a way akin to Kinship Nightmares with a Demon could be pretty fun. Something like They're Not Who They Appear to Be, which convinces the target that some of their allies were replaced with imposters. Admittedly it would probably take a good deal more work than an actual Kinship Nightmare since you effectively have to make it from whole cloth instead of tapping your Social Link for guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it could be, but to play devil's advocate (ha!) couldn't you develop the same nightmare from a Changeling or, even better, from a Fetch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:23:37-07:00","id":556822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556683#post556683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>In general[</i>, if the wizard starts looking at you funny, run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid advice for a happier, substantially longer, life right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:24:15-07:00","id":556823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=555814#post555814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover was never a core intention of NWoD..</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yeah it was. That's why the core the system is basically the same, everyone has the same Skills, and so forth. It doesn't always work and it's been a bigger priority to some people than others, but as someone who was there during the initial design process, making crossover possible without breaking anything was always a goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:39:52-07:00","id":556836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556812#post556812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it could be, but to play devil's advocate (ha!) couldn't you develop the same nightmare from a Changeling or, even better, from a Fetch?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, one thing I'd run if I introduced a demon into a Beast game would be to allow the players to eventually figure out a way to claim Kinship somehow, in some way, if they wanted. It'd be tied to their way of finding Hell. And I'd allow a unique Nightmare as a reward for finishing up such a challenging plot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:51:00-07:00","id":556853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556823#post556823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, yeah it was. That's why the core the system is basically the same, everyone has the same Skills, and so forth. It doesn't always work and it's been a bigger priority to some people than others, but as someone who was there during the initial design process, making crossover possible without breaking anything was always a goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I remember it being flatly stated that it was a major goal of the NWoD back when things were first being announced. The whole idea of having the systems all start on the same page instead of flailing in one another's general direction was huge. (I think that for the most part it's been a great success, esp. compared to some of the classic WoD stuff. The conversion rules were arguably the worst thing about CWoD that didn't involve Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand or Sam Haight.) It might not be a major <i>theme</i> in some of the games or as heavily supported in canon fluff, but that has more to do with the focus on particular types of story the devs and authors want to encourage than the actual nuts and bolts of the thing.<br /> <br /> One of the things I've loved about the NWoD is how easily I can mix in different critters and not have to worry about making a small mountain of house rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556812#post556812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it could be, but to play devil's advocate (ha!) couldn't you develop the same nightmare from a Changeling or, even better, from a Fetch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think a Fetch would be the <i>perfect</i> template for that sort of 'They Aren't Who You Think' or 'World of Evil Dolls' type of Nightmare... this raises an interesting question though: does something like a Fetch count as Kin? They're a pseudo-creature created by another supernatural to serve a pre-programmed purpose, and in that respect they have more in common with an Angel than they do with the Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:52:03-07:00","id":556855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556836#post556836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, one thing I'd run if I introduced a demon into a Beast game would be to allow the players to eventually figure out a way to claim Kinship somehow, in some way, if they wanted. It'd be tied to their way of finding Hell. And I'd allow a unique Nightmare as a reward for finishing up such a challenging plot.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a awesome idea! That would be tons of fun for a chronicle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:11:10-07:00","id":556860,"title":"","content":"So... I just had this nightmare that a female clown with blonde hair and twin-tails, wearing a white shirt and burgundy pants, stalked my grandparents' old house at exactly 3AM at night. <br /> <br /> What the fuck kind of Beast is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:11:39-07:00","id":556862,"title":"","content":"Re: the idea of the God Machine as the outer edge of Weird (or not) in the WoD, I think the intent isn't that Demons and their parent/designer/Clockwork Dickhead Machine are unique in being unfamiliar to the Beasts, just that they are a definitive Other in comparison to the other critters who have their own games.<br /> <br /> It makes sense if you think about it. All the other major supernatural splats are a human base with a template of strangeness stamped onto them, whether by infection or fate or external meddling. The Demons are a malfunctioning thing that was never human, hiding behind a ghillie suit of person-bits they've woven together. A fair number of the other splats are natives of, or have a strong connection to, another realm of some kind while Demons and their ilk are explicitly native to the material world. In some respects they are the least alien thing in the WoD because they are as native as something can get.<br /> <br /> The Beasts and Demons potentially have a number of things to offer one another, but the Demons are paranoid by necessity and Beasts are so used to having a relatively effortless connection with their cousins that someone who doesn't read as familiar stands out as more of a monster than any werebeast or bloodsucker will. Simple fear and caution will make them wary of one another, and they will inevitably clash over resources and misunderstood intent, but that doesn't mean it can't be overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:38:37-07:00","id":556917,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's about humanity, although at one point I did, because unfleshed prometheans and even strix apparently count as kin.<br /> <br /> I have two theories.<br /> <br /> One- Demons are kin, but kinship breaks their cover, so they innately deny the kinship as a defense mechanism (and demons do resist being sensed through kinship). Cover is life for a demon. Of course unless a demon finds their hell there is no way to prove that one way or another. Basically, the unchained have a firewall and a cookie erasing feature which is why kinship never gets that far. <br /> <br /> Secondly- Kinship is based on fear, beasts are nightmares made flesh, they tie in to the fear that monsters generate. How many people have nightmares about reality hacking quantum supercomputer former energy constructs? Not a lot of people. Even when the unchained let the mask slip, Joe Q Public is going to attribute the supernatural to the powers of Inferno. <br /> <br /> Of course unless demons and the unchained get outed, one can't test that theory either. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:53:03-07:00","id":556948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556917#post556917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think it's about humanity, although at one point I did, because unfleshed prometheans and even strix apparently count as kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, of course. I forgot to account for the Prometheans. (I know exactly nothing about the Strix beyond their name, so I'll take your word that they're a similar gap in the theory.) The Prometheans are still trying to BE human though, and Demons just want/need to look like one so you could argue that there's still a tenuous thematic thread of sorts there.<br /> <br /> (Quick edit to add this. The cover argument re: Demons would make sense, except that I believe Angels are explicitly noted as non-Kin as well and IIRC they don't have quite the same Cover/Exposure rules that Demons do.)<br /> <br /> The overall thought is pretty much the same regardless of the IC reasons: I don't think the intent was to mark Demons as Important Special Snowflakes, just to have at least one outlying Other as a canonical exception that proves the rule, and the God Machine makes a relatively logical place to draw that line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":". 06-16-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:57:11-07:00","id":556952,"title":"","content":"I still say its because the God Machine is still the Unchained's Creator. It simply ruins the themes of the game if we suddenly have them as the Dark Mother's grandkids, or make the GM one of her children; the mystery of the GM is a huge part of the setting, and ties to the Dark Mother ruin that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:00:59-07:00","id":556955,"title":"","content":"The strix are evil bird monsters made out of shadow that possess people or corpses (or undead corpses), and drink life energy as either breath or blood, they use modified ephemeral rules even though they're made out of shadow instead of essence. Basically, they're vampires without the baseline humanity, and their beef with the kindred is that they're too human, they want vampires to be pure monsters like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:02:53-07:00","id":556957,"title":"","content":"I don't actually disagree MCN, I was speculating as to possible in-character reasons, but you're almost certainly right that at least part of the reason was just that it spoils some of the setting if everything can be neatly tied back to a single origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:04:52-07:00","id":556958,"title":"","content":"They consider spirits kin, too. And the old ones of Werewolf lore, though they shouldn't really know much about them, such as the Plague King and the Spinner-Hag, and would include the beshilu and azlu, who aren't remotely human.<br /> <br /> Of course, things they consider kin aren't necessarily kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-16-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:10:21-07:00","id":556979,"title":"","content":"Most things may have a connection to the dark mother, but that doesn't mean said connection is anything like what beasts think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:20:50-07:00","id":556987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556860#post556860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I just had this nightmare that a female clown with blonde hair and twin-tails, wearing a white shirt and burgundy pants, stalked my grandparents' old house at exactly 3AM at night.<br /> <br /> What the fuck kind of Beast is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Namtaru. Totes Namtaru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:26:21-07:00","id":556993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556957#post556957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually disagree MCN, I was speculating as to possible in-character reasons, but you're almost certainly right that at least part of the reason was just that it spoils some of the setting if everything can be neatly tied back to a single origin.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was actually addressing St Sword. Sorry about the mix up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556955#post556955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The strix are evil bird monsters made out of shadow that possess people or corpses (or undead corpses), and drink life energy as either breath or blood, they use modified ephemeral rules even though they're made out of shadow instead of essence. Basically, they're vampires without the baseline humanity, and their beef with the kindred is that they're too human, they want vampires to be pure monsters like them.</div> </div> </div> </div> That doesn't mean we can't consider the strix to be the children of the Mother. Doesn't mess up their story at all. Plus, there's the CotC, who explicitly worship a Dark Mother figure as the mother of the vampire race, and they account for the strix as well. So, that's all tied together already.<br /> <br /> They claim that Father Wolf is one of the Mother's kids as well the original Gentry. Who the heck knows how Mages feature into this. Prometheans, they just flat out adopt - they don't claim direct decent there. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:26:41-07:00","id":556994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556979#post556979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most things may have a connection to the dark mother, but that doesn't mean said connection is anything like what beasts think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. We're talking passed down myths and legends, not empirically provable facts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:37:44-07:00","id":557010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556993#post556993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was actually addressing St Sword. Sorry about the mix up.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we can't consider the strix to be the children of the Mother. Doesn't mess up their story at all. Plus, there's the CotC, who explicitly worship a Dark Mother figure as the mother of the vampire race, and they account for the strix as well. So, that's all tied together already.<br /> <br /> They claim that Father Wolf is one of the Mother's kids as well the original Gentry. Who the heck knows how Mages feature into this. Prometheans, they just flat out adopt - they don't claim direct decent there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree a little on the prometheans on the fact that their are some stories of titans or giants making people one famous one is prometheus and pandora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:47:54-07:00","id":557013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557010#post557010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree a little on the prometheans on the fact that their are some stories of titans or giants making people one famous one is prometheus and pandora.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beast Kickstarter Preview, page 314. &quot;If kinship describes a family relationship between monsters, then Prometheans are adopted children of the Dark Mother rather than sharing her direct bloodline.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:59:01-07:00","id":557040,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine and it's ilk are 'divine' and therefore apart from the natural order. They're an artificial element in a way that that Prometheans aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T10:37:36-07:00","id":557051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556717#post556717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that there are Abyssal creatures that are explicidly the result of someone breaking the Universe?<br /> Thing is, no matter what example I bring, because we have so little material you could come up with some reasoning for why they could be connected. Example: Unfleshed. There is no more reason why they should be connected to the Primordial Dream than Demons, but if you give me five minutes I could come up with a dozen reasons why they might be connected. <i>Which doesn't </i><i>matter</i>, because I could do the same for Demon. They disconnect is a conscious decision the designer made, because if they wanted to they could have made the decision to link them up.<br /> <br /> I am not against Demons being non-kin to Beasts, because I understand the need to keep their themes of staying hidden intact. I am against having them explicidly be the <i>only</i> creatures in the setting that are, because it makes the NWoD smaller and gives a limit to how weird and out there the supernaturals the Beast meets can be. NWoD should have more mysteries to offer that leave Beasts stumped and stlightly freaked out than just Demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, why would other Creatures that don't connect to the Primordial Dream have to be the result of someone breaking the Universe at all? The GM is not that special!</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it required breaking the universe I said nothing comes to mind that doesn't involve basically breaking reality. You said you could think of lots of other creatures that shouldn't have any resonance in the Primordial Dream. I asked what they were since the only ones I could think of were the result of reality breaking. This isn't me saying &quot;The GM is so special nothing else can compare without breaking the universe.&quot; This is me saying,&quot; Really you say this isn't an abnormal situation? Where else does it occur because I've never heard of it happening outside of specifically designed lab conditions?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T10:55:59-07:00","id":557057,"title":"","content":"And as I pointed out earlier, Beasts draw their abilities from a part of the Astral Realms, a place where concepts and beliefs take tangible form or manifest as actualities. Metaphors exist as real things, ideas take flesh and symbols embody what they represent. The Astral is flexible and adjusts as ideas and beliefs change, meaning that Realms shift in both prominence and what they manifest as changes occur within the world and Humanity's views of things. And these realms and entities are capable of interacting with other Realms, including the material, and have their powers and influences manifest in those worlds. What's more, we know that in 1e at least that the splat that spent the most time in the Astral, mages, that their powers changed to conform to the Astral: space magic worked differently, for example, to conform to humanities collective view of distance (this might change in 2e). What's more, we know astral entities associated with Arcana, the Abyss and Mages as a whole could influence mage powers and physical abilities in both the Astral and other Realms (Looking at you Acamoths and Aeons), at least within the purview of what they represented.<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is a substrate of the Astral Realms, and seems to sit as part of the area between the Tenemos and Anima Mundi (maybe). This likely means that it represents more base elements of human thoughts and emotions due to its positions on the border of the collective unconciousness of Humanity and the World's Soul, which matches it's role as the Realm of Humanity's base fears. Everything in that Realm is a symbolic reflection of these fears, as well as everything associated with these fears. For example, the Horrors are fears and related concepts made manifest as individual monsters. It also means that the line between symbolism and actualities are blurred. Thus the idea of Kinship and the metaphor of the Dark Mother as the link between Kin may be simply that in any other Realm: an idea, a metaphor to explain the WoD and what the Primoral Dream and it's denizens are. But the Astral gives these concepts substance, and thus in the Primordial Dream, the idea of Kinship and the Dark Mothers Family defines how the Realm functions, as well as how any Astral entity of the Realm would interact with things.<br /> <br /> So in other words: the Beasts are actually Kin and everyone is a descendent or draws from the Dark Mother <i>when operating by the rules of the Primordial Dream </i>. It doesn't mean Mages actually use her power or Werewolves are truly descendent from one of her wayward offspring. What it means is that when the Primordial Dream and the entities from it interact with the other splats as according to how their realm defines such interactions, and their realm defines most splats as Kin. <br /> <br /> Essentially, the Primordial Dream contains it's own self-contained cosmology of the WoD by which it operates. For all intents and purposes, this cosmology is <i>true </i>for the realm and it's denizens, as it is made manifest as an actuality within this Astral Realm. It could be that the Realm was once different, and was shaped by the collective interactions and beliefs of the Beasts to now embody Kinship and the Dark Mother as a means to explain themselves and the different splats, or the Realm always manifested this idea. Regardless of the orogin, all of the Realms influences and powers stem from this cosmology and the Realms nature as the collective embodiment of base fears, and this in turn governs it's interactions with everything both with and beyond itself. Thus, a Beast is going to see the Vampires as Kin and have powers that bond off of that because the source of its powers and the realm in which it operates defines Vampires as such. It doesn't over-write or even need to match up with any other splats cosmology, as it doesn't mean that either is &quot;wrong&quot; when there is an incinsistency: it is just the difference between the Primordial Dream's representation of what happened and the actual event. It is also why their powers based on other splats are more thematically tied to the splat rather than just straight duplications: they are drawing on and making manifest the <i>concepts </i> tied to that splat and shaped through the lens of the Primordial Dream. It also means that they can't use Supernal magic, the Abyss, Numina, Keys, etc. but can reflect what those things represent.<br /> <br /> As for the GM and Demons? I am not sure. It could be that the GM and it's workings fall outside the Primordial Dream because their lore says it does, and thus this theory is reinforced by its manifestations as an actuality in the PD. Maybe there is a disconnect between the GM and the Astral such that it is incapable of a true representation within it. Maybe the GM is an alien physical force from outside of our reality and thus in opposition with the Astral, which is a abstract reflection of it. Maybe it is because all the other splats at least influence the Astral in some way (without physically invading it) via having some form of (proto-)soul (or reflect one, such as Ghosts and Spirits), while demons and GM can only interact by invading it. It could be that the GM and it's entities are so interwoven within the material reality that their presence doesn't register as anything supernatural, and this is just part of everyday mundane fears. Maybe it is an Astral realm manifest in our world, reflecting technology and Humanity's interactions with it, and thus it exists parrallel but opposite the Primordial Dream. Or maybe...the GM has so much mystery surrounding it, I can only guess. But no matter why, if the Primordial Dream doesn't recognize them as Kin, then it makes sense for this to manifest as a lack of ability to tap kinship abilities. Depending on the &quot;why&quot; you choose to fill in, maybe this could change or maybe it is a fixed feature. I actually don't mind this lack of specifics though as it means I can add it in as a ST. <br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and I do wonder if the denizens of the Lower Depths, Supernal, Abyss, Outer Realms (the Cthullu space in <i>Summoners </i>) can interact with Beasts as Kin. We only know that Demons can't be kin, but most of the focus of who could be was on the splats and common non-PC supernaturals (ghosts and spirits). While I would assume Astral entities are similar to ghosts/spirits, a part of me wonders how you could tie beings that represent the defining aspects of reality/anti-reality (supernal or abyssal entities, respectively) or fractured/incomplete aspects of reality (lower depths) as Kin when Demons aren't due to their association with the GM. <br /> <br /> (Posted from my phone so I apologize for the many typos that I am sure are present)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-16-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:19:04-07:00","id":557100,"title":"","content":"Demons being the odd ones out simply because they have absolutely no connection to the astral would make the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:38:33-07:00","id":557134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557057#post557057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Primordial Dream is a substrate of the Astral Realms, and seems to sit as part of the area between the Tenemos and Anima Mundi (maybe).</b> This likely means that it represents more base elements of human thoughts and emotions due to its positions on the border of the collective unconciousness of Humanity and the World's Soul, which matches it's role as the Realm of Humanity's base fears. Everything in that Realm is a symbolic reflection of these fears, as well as everything associated with these fears. For example, the Horrors are fears and related concepts made manifest as individual monsters. It also means that the line between symbolism and actualities are blurred. Thus the idea of Kinship and the metaphor of the Dark Mother as the link between Kin may be simply that in any other Realm: an idea, a metaphor to explain the WoD and what the Primoral Dream and it's denizens are. But the Astral gives these concepts substance, and thus in the Primordial Dream, the idea of Kinship and the Dark Mothers Family defines how the Realm functions, as well as how any Astral entity of the Realm would interact with things.<br /> <br /> (Posted from my phone so I apologize for the many typos that I am sure are present)</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you're truly a glutton for punishment for typing such long posts concerning metaphysical topics on your phone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Note that Beast actually referred to the location of the Primordial Dream in the Lexicon section of the draft (both old and new Introduction). It seems like the PD is &quot;closer&quot; to the layer between individual Oneiros' and the Temenos, assuming &quot;above&quot; refers to &quot;higher&quot; astral realms like the Anima Mundi and &quot;below&quot; is closer to an individual's dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordial Dream: A layer of the collective soul of the world, perhaps \u201cbelow\u201d the Temenos, in which the nightmares of humanity are given life. The Lairs of the Primordial Selves of all Beasts are here. Beasts can grant access to this Dream to other supernatural beings through Kinship. </div> </div> </div><br /> Edit: As another poster mentioned in another thread, I'm also curious if the Dream Steed and Midnight Train from Astral Realms are capable of bringing a mage (or anyone else) to locations (Lairs?) in the Primordial Dream","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 06-16-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:46:30-07:00","id":557140,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1 explained it was between the Anima Mundi and the Temenos though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast Kickstarter Preview Page 74</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts know another aspect of the Astral Realms, the Primordial Dream, lurks in the twilight between the Temenos and the Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although later on it's implied it stretches through every layer of the Astral anyways (which makes sense since Lairs probably exist on the same level as the Oneiros for the Begotten who own them), I'll take the extended explanations over the lexicon in importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-16-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:46:50-07:00","id":557141,"title":"","content":"The Primordial Dream is basically the Beast version of the Boundry Stone that mages use to cross from the Temnos to the Anima Mundi. Kind of like how the Gauntlet and Hedge are actually just spaces between realms instead of worlds themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:53:45-07:00","id":557175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557134#post557134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, you're truly a glutton for punishment for typing such long posts concerning metaphysical topics on your phone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, Beast actually referred to the location of the Primordial Dream in the Lexicon section of the draft (both old and new Introduction). It seems like the PD is &quot;closer&quot; to the layer between individual Oneiros' and the Temenos, assuming &quot;above&quot; refers to &quot;higher&quot; astral realms like the Anima Mundi and &quot;below&quot; is closer to an individual's dreams. <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But I lacknowledged access at my computer due to network controls and I am REALLY bored with still 0 patients on my service (everyone is healthy or got transfered to the local children's hospital). Also means I can't access my reference material, so i am trying to get this all from memory (or what i can get to on my saved PDFs). I definitely need a better device for this though. <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I must have misinterpreted that. In my mind, a Realm of Primordial Fear feels like it should sit closer to the Anima Mundi and Tenemos to me, since it reflects things that unite all of humanity but can be found as Archtypes beyond Humanity (Certain species can experience fear). Plus, the concepts of it being a Realm reflecting the WoD cosmology, including other Realms and non-humans like spirits, made me feel it would be closer to the Anima Mundi, which is what I always felt would encompass these reflections (it is where Wolf Dreams happen, after all).<br /> <br /> But then again, it makes sense for the Realm of Nightmares to rest close to the Onieros: the Onieros is the reflection of an individual's soul in the Astral, and it manifests as Dreams. So I could the Realm of Nightmares having close ties to it. Thanks for pointing that out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the book seems to go back and forth on where it rests (as pointed out by YeOfLittleFaith), and the Primordial pathways play all sorts of wierdness. But considering the nature of the Astral, wackiness is part for the course.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I do still hold that the Beasts power stems from the nature of their Astral Realm, amd the concepts thr Primordial Dream has come to embody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-16-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:55:20-07:00","id":557179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557140#post557140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 1 explained it was between the Anima Mundi and the Temenos though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Although later on it's implied it stretches through every layer of the Astral anyways (which makes sense since Lairs probably exist on the same level as the Oneiros for the Begotten who own them), I'll take the extended explanations over the lexicon in importance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Terms like &quot;below&quot; and &quot;above&quot; really aren't that helpful when referring to astral space. As I noted, I interpreted &quot;below the Temenos&quot; as &quot;farther&quot; from the Anima Mundi, although p.74 does indeed place the PD &quot;between&quot; the Temenos and Animan Mundi, and assume that the reference to &quot;lurks in the twilight&quot; was simply a rhetorical flourish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:04:43-07:00","id":557190,"title":"","content":"The &quot;below&quot; in the lexicon could be easily interpreted as below in the sense the Temenos is the 'surface' and the Primordial Dream is 'beneath' it, but they're still in the same level of the Astral.<br /> <br /> Frankly the exact location of the Primordial Dream there defies easy charting, and the lexicon does say &quot;perhaps&quot;, so eh. I think it's more interesting that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:16:06-07:00","id":557191,"title":"","content":"Although mapping the astral realms is clearly a fools errand, the (metaphysical) location of the Primordial Dream does matter since, unlike the supernal realms, PC's are actually meant to find and enter it on occasion. Moreover, given the explicit crossover potential with mages, who have very distinct rules for entering and traveling in astral space (at least in 1e), where the PD is might determine which mages can actually get there (and rescue poor comatose Melanie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)**.<br /> <br /> Since DaveB wrote both the section on Lairs and is the developer for Mage 2e, I assume there is a <i>relatively</i> straightforward canon answer.<br /> <br /> This is obviously one of the problems with encouraging crossover as part of the Beast setting. It's sometimes necessary to reference the unique rules of other game lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: ** What's the Adamantine Arrow equivalent for Seal Team 6 or Delta Force?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 06-16-2015, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:14:55-07:00","id":557236,"title":"","content":"Regardless of its exact location, the nature of the Primordial Dream and Horrors as part of the Astral means that they belong to a dimension is a place where the Abstract, Theoretical, Real, Dreams and Emotions all find manifestation as actual things, where each Realm within it a place that operates based on its collection of Concepts. It doesn't matter if the rules or elements contradict the rest the non-Astral Realms, or even other Astral Realms (See &quot;Real Mars&quot; vs. &quot;Pulp Mars&quot;). Each individual realm functons according to its own internal rules that in turn reflect the concepts and ideas that brought said realm into existence, and thus within that Realm, those Concepts and Ideas are <i>True </i>. Once you look at it that way, the Beasts, their powers and their cosmology make way more sense. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I wouldn't mind some clarification on how I would use astral travel to get there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557191#post557191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: ** What's the Adamantine Arrow equivalent for Seal Team 6 or Delta Force?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would half jokingly say &quot;The Adamantine Arrow&quot;, since their whole philosophy is based on being the ideal warrior-sage, able to function perfectly as either a grunt or tactician, warrior or philosopher, and effective in any type of combat and able to readily adapt. So it is hard to really pick anyone subset.<br /> That said, the order has a rank for &quot;specialists&quot; in the form of Thunderbolt Guardians, who are called on for certain missions that fall into their realm of expertise... so maybe what ever group of Thunderbolt Guardians who specialize in Astral escapades can rescue her :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:33:35-07:00","id":557272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557236#post557236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of its exact location, the nature of the Primordial Dream and Horrors as part of the Astral means that they belong to a dimension is a place where the Abstract, Theoretical, Real, Dreams and Emotions all find manifestation as actual things, where each Realm within it a place that operates based on its collection of Concepts. It doesn't matter if the rules or elements contradict the rest the non-Astral Realms, or even other Astral Realms (See &quot;Real Mars&quot; vs. &quot;Pulp Mars&quot;). Each individual realm functons according to its own internal rules that in turn reflect the concepts and ideas that brought said realm into existence, and thus within that Realm, those Concepts and Ideas are <i>True </i>. Once you look at it that way, the Beasts, their powers and their cosmology make way more sense.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I wouldn't mind some clarification on how I would use astral travel to get there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would half jokingly say &quot;The Adamantine Arrow&quot;, since their whole philosophy is based on being the ideal warrior-sage, able to function perfectly as either a grunt or tactician, warrior or philosopher, and effective in any type of combat and able to readily adapt. So it is hard to really pick anyone subset.<br /> That said, the order has a rank for &quot;specialists&quot; in the form of Thunderbolt Guardians, who are called on for certain missions that fall into their realm of expertise... so maybe what ever group of Thunderbolt Guardians who specialize in Astral escapades can rescue her :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have no problem with the rules of various astral realms being different, my concern was only about which &quot;layer&quot; of the astral the PD resides in order to apply mage rules to travel there.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, I would love to run a 1980's style &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_MVonyVSQoM\" target=\"_blank\">A-Team</a>&quot; game where the player cabal tries to rescue Melanie. Beasts would make great 80's villains!<br /> <br /> What would be the Paths and Order for the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_The_A-Team_characters\" target=\"_blank\">A-Team characters</a> (they apparently already have shadow names)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:48:09-07:00","id":557299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557191#post557191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although mapping the astral realms is clearly a fools errand, the (metaphysical) location of the Primordial Dream does matter since, unlike the supernal realms, PC's are actually meant to find and enter it on occasion. Moreover, given the explicit crossover potential with mages, who have very distinct rules for entering and traveling in astral space (at least in 1e), where the PD is might determine which mages can actually get there (and rescue poor comatose Melanie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)**.<br /> <br /> Since DaveB wrote both the section on Lairs and is the developer for Mage 2e, I assume there is a <i>relatively</i> straightforward canon answer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Straight from the Mysterious World section of Awakening second edition, in the part about the Astral Realms;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a mage rises through the Temenos, cultural skin flakes off collective ideas until she reaches the border of the Anima Mundi, the Omphalos or Boundary Stone: the liminal realm of High Speech that represents the highest form of human language. From here, mages can either travel through tunnels in the stone into the Anima Mundi, or skirt its edge to walk into the Primordial realms containing humanity\u2019s essential emotions and fears. These realms, representing the animal instincts of the human race, are poorly understood. Their inhabitants are typically monstrous and highly protective of their territory. </div> </div> </div>In Mage terms (and I must stress that these are Mage terms) the Primordial Dream is the very oldest part of the Temenos, where the evolutionary memory of humans takes shape. Humanity's soul is sharply divided from that of the rest of the world by the Omphalos, which represents both magic and language; a dream-logic representation of the one thing that truly sets us apart from other animals. <br /> <br /> So, in terms of difficulty to get there for mages, it's firmly in the middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 06-16-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:52:13-07:00","id":557304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557299#post557299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Straight from the Mysterious World section of Awakening second edition, in the part about the Astral Realms;<br /> <br /> [/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave, are you simply not going to release Awakened 2nd edition but instead throw out these tidbits throw various forum postings that require one to go track down all the tidbits to get the cohesive whole of the game?<br /> <br /> Because that would be hilariously evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:07:53-07:00","id":557419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557299#post557299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Straight from the Mysterious World section of Awakening second edition, in the part about the Astral Realms;<br /> <br /> In Mage terms (and I must stress that these are Mage terms) the Primordial Dream is the very oldest part of the Temenos, where the evolutionary memory of humans takes shape. Humanity's soul is sharply divided from that of the rest of the world by the Omphalos, which represents both magic and language; a dream-logic representation of the one thing that truly sets us apart from other animals.<br /> <br /> So, in terms of difficulty to get there for mages, it's firmly in the middle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Dave.<br /> <br /> I guess that's one advantage of releasing Mage after Beast, it can anticipate and incorporate some crossover issues and questions.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also hope the Midnight Train from Astral Realms is still viable in 2e and can reach the Primordial Dream. I can certainly envision a very powerful Beast whose Lair contained a Chamber that was a spooky and abandoned train station, and where you most definitely would not want to be waiting in at midnight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 06-16-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:09:43-07:00","id":557490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imposterzilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556552#post556552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't really choose family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather vehemently disagree. Being bound by blood does not necessarily make two people &quot;family,&quot; in my mind. The word family has deeper connotations to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:29:48-07:00","id":557495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557490#post557490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I rather vehemently disagree. Being bound by blood does not necessarily make two people &quot;family,&quot; in my mind. The word family has deeper connotations to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'm bound by blood to my dad's family, but I've actively cheered two of them being put into the ground(they were not good people) and I wouldn't let them in my house if any of them came knocking. Counter wise, there are folks I've only known for three months I'd house without question.<br /> <br /> Family's always a choice. The failure to see that and act accordingly is the source of much tragedy in the world. Part of the terror of Beasts is that they sometimes push the 'blood-bond' as part of their ideology. They've got some rough lessons to learn too, that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:44:35-07:00","id":557513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557495#post557495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I'm bound by blood to my dad's family, but I've actively cheered two of them being put into the ground(they were not good people) and I wouldn't let them in my house if any of them came knocking. Counter wise, there are folks I've only known for three months I'd house without question.<br /> <br /> Family's always a choice. The failure to see that and act accordingly is the source of much tragedy in the world. Part of the terror of Beasts is that they sometimes push the 'blood-bond' as part of their ideology. They've got some rough lessons to learn too, that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You most certainly do not have to like or respect family, but these people are still family. Hypothetical Uncle Earl might be a bigoted serial killer, but he's still your uncle, even if you loathe his very existence.<br /> <br /> The concept of &quot;family&quot; is diverse and, for good or ill, includes both ties of blood and voluntary association. The importance and themes of both clearly resonate in Beast (e.g., nature and genetics vs. nurture issues, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:45:21-07:00","id":557514,"title":"","content":"I think family is a concept meant to be examined in the game. It isn't like Beasts were ever related by blood, or anything like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:54:49-07:00","id":557519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557513#post557513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You most certainly do not have to like or respect family, but these people are still family. Hypothetical Uncle Earl might be a bigoted serial killer, but he's still your uncle, even if you loathe his very existence.<br /> <br /> The concept of &quot;family&quot; is diverse and, for good or ill, includes both ties of blood and voluntary association. The importance and themes of both clearly resonate in Beast (e.g., nature and genetics vs. nurture issues, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood only matters if you think blood is cause for reflection on yourself. Which, again, is a problem with Beasts(a good one).<br /> <br /> But beyond that, saying someone is, for instance, my uncle doesn't mean anything to me personally. My Uncle Bruce was a womanizer, if not a rapist, a conman, and an abuser. He died a few years ago, but if he were alive and came to my door, I'd shoot him without question. Because those things mean something and his being my uncle does not.<br /> <br /> The Steele family supporting him despite all of that is why I've largely written them all off. Well, that and the other load of dick moves they've done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T17:05:46-07:00","id":557577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557495#post557495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Counter wise, there are folks I've only known for three months I'd house without question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of that, if you ever find yourself in my neck of the woods, give me a shout. You can come hang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T17:06:33-07:00","id":557584,"title":"","content":"Basically &quot;family&quot; can actually mean one of two homophones that mean very different things. There's the good family, people you'd trust with your life, and the &quot;family&quot; of people you share recent genetic ancestors with.<br /> <br /> If you're <i>very</i> lucky, these might even be the same group of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T17:11:29-07:00","id":557585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557577#post557577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of that, if you ever find yourself in my neck of the woods, give me a shout. You can come hang.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I get a job in New York next year, I was planning on making a roadtrip of it and stopping by. I need someone to get me a good Philly Cheesesteak, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Basically &quot;family&quot; can actually mean one of two homophones that mean very different things. There's the good family, people you'd trust with your life, and the &quot;family&quot; of people you share recent genetic ancestors with.<br /> <br /> If you're <i>very</i> lucky, these might even be the same group of people.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Yes, this. Beast asks questions of both of those meanings, and a common struggle for them is being both of these things in the face of their struggles.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.t