0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T17:47:16-07:00","id":557617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557609#post557609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough. Plus, don't you have some kind of amazing scotch? Or was that a friend's?<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm planning on good food and good drinks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's my roommate's - Glenlivet 21 Heritage Collection. It's transcendent.<br /> <br /> But anyway, we're derailing the thread. Sorry, folks! *Amnesia dust!*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T17:50:24-07:00","id":557618,"title":"","content":"Man, I don't remember ordering peppers on my taco. What were we talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:16:41-07:00","id":557677,"title":"","content":"As ive already started integrating beasts into my ongoing chronicle (so far, queen bee, killer croc, killer moth, and batsy himself), Ive found that my initial wariness over the devouring has cleared up quite a bit. indeed, someone pointed out IC that hes never met a monster who chose to be one(he doesnt know any sineaters). the devouring brought up lots of good nuances, and the whole &quot;big brother is watching you&quot; vibe of the Lessons is actually kinda cool (croc doesnt care, but his broodmate tries to clean up his brother's mess and teach him control.) One thing i'd REALLY love to know, however... during the Devouring, does your Older Sibling have to be the same Family as you, or end up giving you a matching Lair Trait? does the sibling influence what the Beast becomes, or are they wholly unique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:43:04-07:00","id":557747,"title":"","content":"From the Monday Meeting notes, I think they may be backpeddling on the Devouring aspect. For fans of the Homecoming, keep the emails and comments coming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","name":"imposterzilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:51:17-07:00","id":557753,"title":"","content":"After reading the most recent draft, especially the new intro, I am coming away feeling even more like these guys are the perfect Freddy Kruegers, both while alive(where he would be a proper PC Beast) and after his death(where he becomes Freddy Unfettered). He's got cool dream powers and arbitrary dream weaknesses, deviant appetites that he lives to fill, scary phantom dream-damage Atavisms, and even though he's an unrelentingly evil maniac, he's still the real star of the show. The audience loves Freddy and has nothing but contempt for the mostly innocent teens he slashes. And if ever there were a guy who would look into the face of Darkness and say &quot;yes please&quot;, it's the son of 100 maniacs. I'm sure other people have mentioned this before, but for me it is what makes the game. Totally liking the Devouring, guys. Thumbs up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:00:23-07:00","id":557758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557677#post557677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">indeed, someone pointed out IC that hes never met a monster who chose to be one(he doesnt know any sineaters).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if he did know any of the Bound, a significant proportion don't make that choice while lucid and the stunning majority make it under duress \u2014 remember that the alternative to accepting the Bargain is generally <i>death.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:08:39-07:00","id":557762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557495#post557495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I'm bound by blood to my dad's family, but I've actively cheered two of them being put into the ground(they were not good people) and I wouldn't let them in my house if any of them came knocking. Counter wise, there are folks I've only known for three months I'd house without question.<br /> <br /> Family's always a choice. The failure to see that and act accordingly is the source of much tragedy in the world. Part of the terror of Beasts is that they sometimes push the 'blood-bond' as part of their ideology. They've got some rough lessons to learn too, that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. My dad is a literal psychopath from a long line of them, he somehow manages to show all the signs EXCEPT cruelty to animals (animals seem to be the ONLY creatures he has empathy for, I wonder if there is a reason for that), which is why I have a lodge's worth of evil werewolf characters in both versions of the WoD (a mafia Ivory Claw, a seductive serial killer Bale Hound, a Black Spiral Dancer executive in charge of Pentax's version of autotrader.com and that's just the WoD versions of him) and many other settings based off him, he's basically one of my muses for evil werewolves. I wrote him out of my life last year after he threatened to kill me, and yet he blames my mom for turning me against him and has been harassing her over it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At the same time, I have a couple of close friends that I consider family, including an older fellow I met at the library who is helping me write my novel, who I consider something of a subsitute father figure. He's awesome.<br /> <br /> So yeah, family is a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:54:24-07:00","id":557797,"title":"","content":"P<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556146#post556146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pre-revision, Souls also came from the Primordial Dream, and the relation of the Dark Mother to Horrors doesn't really seem to be any different, so I don't actually see your point in this? Horrors are no less related to each other than Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>re-revision, you were <i>born</i> with a soul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:10:26-07:00","id":557804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557797#post557797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P<br /> re-revision, you were <i>born</i> with a soul</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you meant &quot;Soul&quot;, where did it say that? I don't remember reading it that way. If a Beast was born with a Soul then the Homecoming would seem to have served no purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:37:13-07:00","id":557856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557804#post557804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you meant &quot;Soul&quot;, where did it say that? I don't remember reading it that way. If a Beast was born with a Soul then the Homecoming would seem to have served no purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Homecoming was facing and accepting that; your Soul is not human but Beastial, a primordial nightmare born into the waking world. It was as if you were finally were coming home after a lifetime of away from it. It was always a metaphor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:48:14-07:00","id":557864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557856#post557856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Homecoming was facing and accepting that; your Soul is not human but Beastial, a primordial nightmare born into the waking world. It was as if you were finally were coming home after a lifetime of away from it. It was always a metaphor</div> </div> </div> </div>The conundrum here is that Esmee Childress didn't have nightmares of her Soul until a year before her Homecoming, Ling Chen only had a month of preamble, and Boleslav's Homecoming only mentions the stone giant in the context of the Homecoming dream itself, so it's clear that even in the first drafts the recurring dreams of your Soul aren't necessarily a lifelong thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:50:45-07:00","id":557865,"title":"","content":"&quot;Beast: A human being born with an ancestral connection to the Dark Mother, as expressed by the Soul.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:04:02-07:00","id":557893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557865#post557865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Beast: A human being born with an ancestral connection to the Dark Mother, as expressed by the Soul.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Beasts aren\u2019t human: True. Beasts are born like humans and seem human until their<br /> Homecoming, when they discover a spiritual link to nightmare monsters \u2014 their Souls. That is<br /> when they truly become Beasts, but even before that they are not really human.&quot;<br /> <br /> Contradicts that Beasts are born with a Soul. The Lexicon could be talking about just the Beasts after a Homecoming, so a human being could be born with a connection to the Dark Mother then after the Homecoming that connection is expressed by the Soul. The Lexicon is a bit unclear all other things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T00:06:25-07:00","id":557954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556993#post556993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was actually addressing St Sword. Sorry about the mix up.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we can't consider the strix to be the children of the Mother. Doesn't mess up their story at all. Plus, there's the CotC, who explicitly worship a Dark Mother figure as the mother of the vampire race, and they account for the strix as well. So, that's all tied together already.<br /> <br /> They claim that Father Wolf is one of the Mother's kids as well the original Gentry. Who the heck knows how Mages feature into this. Prometheans, they just flat out adopt - they don't claim direct decent there.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you had read more closely you would have noticed that I only mentioned the kinship with strix from the angle that strix have no connection to humanity- They aren't part human, they aren't former humans, so the theory that kinship is limited by connections to humanity being why demons are exempt doesn't fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T01:37:29-07:00","id":558023,"title":"","content":"Anyone thought about a Beast crossover with Innocents? It seems like a natural fit to me.<br /> <br /> I've been chewing on the idea that perhaps something happens to children that allows them to form a connection to the Primordial Dream. The ones that have problems with nightmares can end up becoming Beasts. The ones that don't might end up as Heroes if they don't hold it together later in life, assuming the Integrity requirement isn't changed. I can't wait to see more about the Primordial Dream. Maybe I can think of what might cause a connection to form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T02:17:53-07:00","id":558027,"title":"","content":"I think there's a lot of potential for Innocents as Prelude. Like the original text demonstrated, Ben essentially created his own nemesis through things that are a by-product of natural childhood traumas and interactions.<br /> <br /> Even though Beasts no longer create Heroes through their actions, the idea of two children destined to be on opposite sides of things, and both touched by the power of the Dream, ties in to the overall idea of narratives and narrative subversions.<br /> <br /> And now for some reason all I can think of is the start of Maleficent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T03:36:18-07:00","id":558077,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to pop in and say that despite my misgivings about the revisions I really think you've got something good here Matt. Thanks for your hard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T03:56:36-07:00","id":558079,"title":"","content":"Maybe remove Beasts out of it directly. It is just Horrors, proto-Horrors, and Unfettered that enter the dreams of a child for the first time in the child's life. The kid has a natural fight or flight response. Those that choose to run or cower live on to potentially become Heroes. Those that stand their ground or try to fight earn the respect of the monster and can grow up to become Beasts. The kids forget the dream as people usually do, but after Innocents end, around puberty, they have either connected to the PD or not.<br /> <br /> They also instinctively remember the experience so nascent Beasts are never as alarmed by the strange nightmares they might have. They remember in their heart it will work out fine whether they are predator or prey in the dream. Would be Heroes remember they were afraid. Their moment of weakness haunts them and turns into self-loathing. Should they lose their grip and are exposed to something similar all they hate they have built up over years gets projected upon the Beast that &quot;awakens&quot; the Hero. But the Hero's heart knows that it never actually saw what caused the initial incident. The Hero only knows that it had a feeling to it that is the same feeling they get from any Beast. So the cycle of hate never ends as long as the Hero lives.<br /> <br /> Beasts dare not unleash their Horrors. The Horror must be sated because most children would run. Trying to create more nascent Beasts would create more nascent Heroes, and Heroes in greater numbers. Beasts learn to teach through fear because it is what they know and they have to try to keep people stable and productive. It seems to keep the number of Heroes down. If Beasts could only keep all the nascent Heroes on the straight and narrow then they wouldn't have to face them, but there are never enough Beasts. Beasts &quot;recruit&quot; all the nascent Beasts that they can. They try to teach the newbies the program. It isn't pretty, but surviving never is.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Beast isn't hereditary, but it does seem like children that grow up around Beasts end up Heroes or Beasts themselves. Beasts can't see this connection that people have unless they are ripe to become Beasts so it might be best to stay away from family. It is the only way to keep them from ever becoming Heroes. It is better to create a new family. It will have members that are &quot;safe.&quot; Members that aren't really human, but that's okay because Beasts aren't really human either anymore. They might be monsters, but nobody is perfect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> Seems to be all nicely tied with a bow and no religious overtones. The whole thing is purely self-serving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T04:16:58-07:00","id":558106,"title":"","content":"I mean not even thinking about the mechanics, Beast is THE material that would go best with Innocents.<br /> <br /> I will not personally do crossover games with Beast, nor I do think I will run Beast game at all, but I will indeed run Beast/Innocent game, because I do think it is the splat that really really works best within Innocent worldview. Either as antagonists, mysterious NPC, or even PC.<br /> <br /> That's why, upon realization of the Innocent potential, I am actuially backing a lot more money that I was planning to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T05:34:03-07:00","id":558116,"title":"","content":"Did you suggest such Innocent book for Beast as a Stretch Goal? They are almost to the last one listed. Might be worth a shot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was just messing around with that writeup to show how the information in the introduction could be interpreted as something other than Beast: The Jehovah's Witness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-17-2015, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:21:22-07:00","id":558225,"title":"","content":"Okay, yeah, Beast and Innocents go together like peanut butter and chocolate.<br /> <br /> Wanna run that game now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:56:43-07:00","id":558251,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Homecoming vs Devouring, on the RPG forum, I said this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll probably end up fusing the two concepts. You were always the Horror, but the Homecoming (where acceptance of this happens spontaneously) or Devouring (where it's catalysed by another Beast) involves it essentially devouring your dream self (going from fearing it to becoming part of the fear it inspires). </div> </div> </div>And Matt said &quot;way ahead of you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:07:59-07:00","id":558277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558251#post558251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Homecoming vs Devouring, on the RPG forum, I said this:And Matt said &quot;way ahead of you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My little suggestion brick a few days back had a similar approach. I'm looking forward to seeing how this all takes shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:20:28-07:00","id":558329,"title":"","content":"Since I just finished my part on Chapter Two, I can now be blunt about this:<br /> <br /> Beasts are &quot;different&quot; their whole lives long. They dream deep. They are set apart. They are, in many ways, already Beasts. Their final encounter with the Horror puts all of this into context, but it's not their first brush with their own weird selves. And while a mentor-Beast may facilitate that (it's probably the easiest way), you can realize your Beastly potential all on your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:35:45-07:00","id":558348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558329#post558329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I just finished my part on Chapter Two, I can now be blunt about this:<br /> <br /> Beasts are &quot;different&quot; their whole lives long. They dream deep. They are set apart. They are, in many ways, already Beasts. Their final encounter with the Horror puts all of this into context, but it's not their first brush with their own weird selves. And while a mentor-Beast may facilitate that (it's probably the easiest way), you can realize your Beastly potential all on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it the Homecoming and I'm satisfied with this compromise! I prefer the original version of things still, but that isn't coming back from the sounds of it. No point in complaining at this point.<br /> <br /> Wait, we're still calling a Beast's inner monster the Soul though, right? Because I don't see a reason why it shouldn't still be called the Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 06-17-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:39:11-07:00","id":558351,"title":"","content":"Honestly, they can keep the names. They're just a shell over a concept, and it was the concept I cared about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:42:02-07:00","id":558362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558351#post558351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, they can keep the names. They're just a shell over a concept, and it was the concept I cared about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I care about both, but you're right in that there is a priority there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:52:03-07:00","id":558375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=557893#post557893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Beasts aren\u2019t human: True. Beasts are born like humans and seem human until their<br /> Homecoming, when they discover a spiritual link to nightmare monsters \u2014 their Souls. That is<br /> when they truly become Beasts, but even before that they are not really human.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Contradicts that Beasts are born with a Soul. The Lexicon could be talking about just the Beasts after a Homecoming, so a human being could be born with a connection to the Dark Mother then after the Homecoming that connection is expressed by the Soul. The Lexicon is a bit unclear all other things considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. It says the discover the link, which is the Soul, not that they gain it. There is no contridiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:53:48-07:00","id":558376,"title":"","content":"So the way it basically works is that you've got this connection to the Primordial Dream. At some point in your life, you face the reality of the situation,* and you either realize your potential or you don't. You're different, but you're not doomed to monstrosity (whether Beastly or Heroic) because of that difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Or at least part of it. Once you're a true Beast you've still got your whole life ahead of you, with lots more lessons left to learn and lots more late nights to ponder what it is you're <i>really </i>supposed to be doing. Remember that the Devouring usually happens <i>before </i>the start of the game, and that we expect characters and their broods to have many long story arcs after.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:55:17-07:00","id":558377,"title":"","content":"Though, I do prefer the Soul to the Horror, truth be told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:58:56-07:00","id":558384,"title":"","content":"I think it would work best with both terms. Beasts generally refer to it as their Soul, but use Horror when they want to be specific and mean &quot;a soul like what a beast got&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:04:14-07:00","id":558589,"title":"","content":"Just want to pop in to offer my support to the devs. Beast was not the game I initially thought it to be, but it still looks like it's shaping up to be a great one. And better that the text of the game shake out now for clarity than later, or worse never be realized as it was intended. I'm sure you don't need validation, but if nothing else the heat of the arguments in various places show that people do care about what you're doing. Keep on keeping on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6513-maltry","name":"Maltry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:34:37-07:00","id":558804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maltry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558589#post558589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just want to pop in to offer my support to the devs. Beast was not the game I initially thought it to be, but it still looks like it's shaping up to be a great one. And better that the text of the game shake out now for clarity than later, or worse never be realized as it was intended. I'm sure you don't need validation, but if nothing else the heat of the arguments in various places show that people do care about what you're doing. Keep on keeping on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:39:00-07:00","id":558837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558329#post558329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I just finished my part on Chapter Two, I can now be blunt about this:<br /> <br /> Beasts are &quot;different&quot; their whole lives long. They dream deep. They are set apart. They are, in many ways, already Beasts. Their final encounter with the Horror puts all of this into context, but it's not their first brush with their own weird selves. And while a mentor-Beast may facilitate that (it's probably the easiest way), you can realize your Beastly potential all on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like how I always thought it worked, now with an additional option of a mentor to help at the end stage. Clarity is always nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To be honest, I think people have gone into the realm of arguing over semantics and going hyper-technical. Your swift progress is commendable. I can't say that enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:55:18-07:00","id":558863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558225#post558225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, yeah, Beast and Innocents go together like peanut butter and chocolate.<br /> <br /> Wanna run that game now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I realize I made a Splatoon joke earlier but this would literally be squidkids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:27:50-07:00","id":558881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558863#post558863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I realize I made a Splatoon joke earlier but this would literally be squidkids.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or <i>Nightmare on Elm Street</i> YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:04:37-07:00","id":559007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we pass $93,000 of contributions, we will create a Beast supplement PDF for Hunter: the Vigil's Mortal Remains book that contains such things as a Conspiracy that co-opts Beast Lairs, and hunters that deal with Heroes. The PDF will be sent to every backer who pledged for a Reward Tier that includes a PDF of Beast: The Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesssssssssssss! <br /> <br /> Also, I notice that one of the $750 pledges has opened up. I'm almost tempted by it, but I already spent way too much money on the Dark Eras Kickstarter, so am unlikely to snap it up. If anyone else is interested, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:21:48-07:00","id":559013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maltry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=558589#post558589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just want to pop in to offer my support to the devs. Beast was not the game I initially thought it to be, but it still looks like it's shaping up to be a great one. And better that the text of the game shake out now for clarity than later, or worse never be realized as it was intended. I'm sure you don't need validation, but if nothing else the heat of the arguments in various places show that people do care about what you're doing. Keep on keeping on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also want to add my support. I know that Rose and Matt and all the rest of the Devs are working to make this an awesome game, and I want to second that I like that we are getting things aired out to make sure that the game is recognized by us, the public, as you, the artists, intended.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I am going to see if I can convince anyone else from my gaming group to get some pledges in.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am getting more pledges because I A) want the Hunter expansion and B) want to stop being the only one who buys the books and then has to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T22:12:52-07:00","id":559070,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm quote myself from the Kickstarter comments, but I do think its highly relevant: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">@Jason I don't know about other cases, but what happened this time was one of the $750 backers either pulled out entirely or dropped to another tier. Give that that's a hell of a lot of money, I don't think that there's anything to worry about, likely someone just reassessed their financial state. I fully expect we'll get that pledge back before the Kickstarter ends, albeit from a different person. I also think it's worth noting that despite that big dollar drop from a single pledge, the Kickstarter is only at -$89 according to kicktraqs from yesterday, which means there has been a significant influx of money as well that is being hidden by the drop of one person who pledge a lot. It also bears noting that the number of backers every day has been positive, so either people are dropping to lower reward tiers, or we are taking in more backers than are dropping out. Either way you look at it, and as frustrating as it is, there is still positive growth in this project.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'm amazed how the impact of one person, likely deciding that they don't have a spare grand to spend on an RPG project (which is what it would be for me given the current USD to CAD exchange rate), can cause people to take such a negative viewpoint. Especially once you consider that that reward tier will definitely get filled back in by the end of the kickstarter, if not by the end of tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T22:39:27-07:00","id":559075,"title":"","content":"This here reminds me of Beasts<br /> <br /> Even eagles need a push<br /> <br /> The eagle gently coaxed her offspring toward the edge of the nest. Her heart quivered with conflicting emotions as she felt their resistance to her persistent nudging. \u201cWhy does the thrill of soaring have to begin with the fear of falling?\u201d she thought. This ageless question was still unanswered for her. As in tradition of the species, her nest was located high on the shelf of a sheer rock face. Below there was nothing but air to support the wings of each child. \u201cIs it possible that this time it will not work?\u201d she thought. Despite her fears, the eagle knew it was time, her parental mission was all but complete. There remained one final task \u2013 THE PUSH. The eagle drew courage from an innate wisdom. Until her children discovered their wings, there was no purpose for their lives outside the nest. Until they learned to soar, they would fail to understand the privilege it was to have been born an eagle. The push was the greatest gift she had to offer. It was her supreme act of love. And so, one by one, she pushed them and they flew. - David McNally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-18-2015, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T02:19:09-07:00","id":559161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559070#post559070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm quote myself from the Kickstarter comments, but I do think its highly relevant: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm amazed how the impact of one person, likely deciding that they don't have a spare grand to spend on an RPG project (which is what it would be for me given the current USD to CAD exchange rate), can cause people to take such a negative viewpoint. Especially once you consider that that reward tier will definitely get filled back in by the end of the kickstarter, if not by the end of tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there's an unfortunate tendency to want to grasp onto things and cry &quot;Ah ha!&quot; with things like this. Personally I actually took a step back from the KS comments, just because things were getting so hyperbolic. Things see, to be simmering down all across the board, especially as things are made clearer by the Devs.<br /> <br /> I have to echo the praise found elsewhere on this page. You have all comported yourselves with grace and dignity, despite the Scylla and Charybdis of circumstances that has set in. Everyone knows that you guys are determined to make Beast the best game it can be, and also the game that Matt set out to create. <br /> <br /> Watching this makes me glad to support, and continue to support, Onyx Path- precisely because of their open and frank approach to game design and their willingness to listen to the concerns of the community. And if any game deserved a &quot;reward our staff&quot; stretch goal, then it would be Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T02:30:52-07:00","id":559169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559161#post559161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching this makes me glad to support, and continue to support, Onyx Path- precisely because of their open and frank approach to game design and their willingness to listen to the concerns of the community. And if any game deserved a &quot;reward our staff&quot; stretch goal, then it would be Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agreed! You've pushed yourself to the limit, but everyone, everyone involved in this project has helped to produce something amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:30:32-07:00","id":559272,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the support. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We really do give these games our all, and it's great when that gets noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:49:31-07:00","id":559282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=556146#post556146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pre-revision, Souls also came from the Primordial Dream, and the relation of the Dark Mother to Horrors doesn't really seem to be any different, so I don't actually see your point in this? Horrors are no less related to each other than Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls were described as being an inborn part of the Beast, not some alien body-snatching invader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:08:56-07:00","id":559291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559282#post559282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls were described as being an inborn part of the Beast, not some alien body-snatching invader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. The process was just more drawn out.<br /> <br /> 'It is important to understand that the Soul is not a flesh-and-blood monster. The Soul is much more iconic than that, existing primarily as a dread spirit entity in the darkest depths of the Primordial Dream...Whatever its form, whatever its origins, however, the Soul chooses the Beast for reasons known only in its terrible heart. It stalks her and ultimately claims her, creating something no longer human but not fully of the Soul: a Beast.'<br /> <br /> 'Still, the process of actually becoming one with the Soul and becoming a true Beast begins early, sometimes even in early childhood. The nascent Beast has terrible recurring nightmares, glimpses of the Lair that awaits her in the Primordial Dream, nightmares made all the worse because she is more often than the predator than the prey, especially as the time draws close. She feels a terrible, consuming need that is never sated and that she tries unflinchingly to fulfill, even if she is wracked with guilt afterward by her actions. Sometimes she feels as though some unknowable thing is casting a vast, terrible shadow over her life\u2026but she takes comfort in that in shadow nonetheless, knowing that somewhere out there, someone understands her.<br /> When the moment finally comes \u2014 when the Soul claims the mortal and the Beast is born \u2014 the horror of the monstrous is almost always accompanied by a sense of relief.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:44:09-07:00","id":559309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559291#post559291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. The process was just more drawn out.<br /> <br /> 'It is important to understand that the Soul is not a flesh-and-blood monster. The Soul is much more iconic than that, existing primarily as a dread spirit entity in the darkest depths of the Primordial Dream...Whatever its form, whatever its origins, however, the Soul chooses the Beast for reasons known only in its terrible heart. It stalks her and ultimately claims her, creating something no longer human but not fully of the Soul: a Beast.'<br /> <br /> 'Still, the process of actually becoming one with the Soul and becoming a true Beast begins early, sometimes even in early childhood. The nascent Beast has terrible recurring nightmares, glimpses of the Lair that awaits her in the Primordial Dream, nightmares made all the worse because she is more often than the predator than the prey, especially as the time draws close. She feels a terrible, consuming need that is never sated and that she tries unflinchingly to fulfill, even if she is wracked with guilt afterward by her actions. Sometimes she feels as though some unknowable thing is casting a vast, terrible shadow over her life\u2026but she takes comfort in that in shadow nonetheless, knowing that somewhere out there, someone understands her.<br /> When the moment finally comes \u2014 when the Soul claims the mortal and the Beast is born \u2014 the horror of the monstrous is almost always accompanied by a sense of relief.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly took this part as being symbolic but perhaps you're right.<br /> Still, when you compare:<br /> <br /> -&quot;Beasts are born like humans and seem human until their Homecoming, when they <b>discover a spiritual link to nightmare monsters</b> \u2014 their Souls. That is when they truly become Beasts, but even before that they are not really human.&quot;<br /> to:<br /> -&quot;Beasts are born human, though most of them experience deep, primal nightmares throughout their lives \u2014 an intrinsic connection to the Primordial Dream. At some point, another of the Children finds the incipient Beast and offers to change her through Devouring. From that point on, the person is no longer fully human,<b> having lost her soul and replaced it with a Horror</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't sound like the same process at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 06-18-2015, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:55:54-07:00","id":559327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559291#post559291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. The process was just more drawn out.<br /> <br /> 'It is important to understand that the Soul is not a flesh-and-blood monster. The Soul is much more iconic than that, existing primarily as a dread spirit entity in the darkest depths of the Primordial Dream...Whatever its form, whatever its origins, however, the Soul chooses the Beast for reasons known only in its terrible heart. It stalks her and ultimately claims her, creating something no longer human but not fully of the Soul: a Beast.'<br /> <br /> 'Still, the process of actually becoming one with the Soul and becoming a true Beast begins early, sometimes even in early childhood. The nascent Beast has terrible recurring nightmares, glimpses of the Lair that awaits her in the Primordial Dream, nightmares made all the worse because she is more often than the predator than the prey, especially as the time draws close. She feels a terrible, consuming need that is never sated and that she tries unflinchingly to fulfill, even if she is wracked with guilt afterward by her actions. Sometimes she feels as though some unknowable thing is casting a vast, terrible shadow over her life\u2026but she takes comfort in that in shadow nonetheless, knowing that somewhere out there, someone understands her.<br /> When the moment finally comes \u2014 when the Soul claims the mortal and the Beast is born \u2014 the horror of the monstrous is almost always accompanied by a sense of relief.'</div> </div> </div> </div>We might change the language some, but that's basically still how it works. The Horror replaces your human soul, creating a hybrid myth/person.<br /> <br /> It's important to note that in the World of Darkness, the soul is not the seat of consciousness or conscience. If you have a look at the Soulless Condition, for example, you'll notice that the character stays themselves... they just start to run out of psychological juice and may behave oddly due to the effects on Virtue and Vice. And vampires have intact souls, despite the strains on self that Humanity loss models.*<br /> <br /> A soul's kind of like a fire burning in a hearth. You can put it out, then start a new one with a different kind of wood, but the room around it is still warm, and more to the point is still the same building. So no, no body snatching.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Vampires sometimes don't describe this accurately -- most of them don't understand the metaphysics. But in actual supernatural terms, that's how it is.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:18:05-07:00","id":559347,"title":"","content":"With the input from Rose, about how the Beast always had the deep connection to the Primordial Dream that eventually grew till you faced that connection and accept your role, I feel like we need something between Devouring and homecoming. Both terms imply an interaction and change, but some of the implocations are not quite on point or confusing. Devouring implies a destructive element and loss, while Homecoming implies that there is no choice. Even if the concepts are explained well, the words used to encapsulate them are going to shape people's opinions of them. <br /> <br /> I almost feel like something more akin to &quot;self-realization&quot; from Analytical Psychology (Jung's theories about thr concious/unconcious, which the Astral Realms are based off of). It would encapsulate both the developmental aspect, the fact that the connection always existed, and the idea of choice, as self-realization is that: choosing to unite your disparate parts, including those you don't like or aren't aware of, over a prolonged period with eventual realization and acceptance. At the same time, it keeps the idea of this always being a part of you, as such self-realization is based on what is already there. Beast as mentors that guide this development matches the idea of parents or psychotherapists helping someone achieve their own realiztion. And the idea that Heroes are those with a deep connection to the Primordial but fail to connect makes because they cannot unify the Self would also fit what we know, and match the idea of what happens when you don't embrace the full self. <br /> <br /> So maybe something like &quot;Consummation&quot;, &quot;Completion&quot; or &quot;The Culmination&quot;? I am sure there are much more evocative ways to put that (I need a thesaurus), but something to unify the idea that this is process that starts early and reaches a final confrontation where the person makes the choice and accepts their darkness, their connection to the Primordial Dream, forming their new and fuller self. <br /> <br /> (Or I am full of it and am just thinking of my CME lecture from last week on this stuff.)<br /> <br /> Also, one thing to note: the Astral is the collective unconciousness and possibly soul of both humanity and the World. You could potentially theorize that all human souls are just a part of it and share a common energy/sourcewhatever that is mostly ibterchangeable. Thus the Horror and the human who becomes the Beast aren't destroying one another so much pouring some of that energy out of a human vessel and then shifting some new energy from one part of that collective pool into the human vessel. It is just like emptying a water bottle: that bottle still has its shape and purpose, even when empty. When you then refill it from the tap, it is still a bottle full of water, and is essentially the same as before, even if the water isn't the same you poured out. The water just might taste different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Rose beat me to the metaphor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":".  Typos 06-18-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:21:27-07:00","id":559348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559327#post559327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We might change the language some, but that's basically still how it works. The Horror replaces your human soul, creating a hybrid myth/person.<br /> <br /> It's important to note that in the World of Darkness, the soul is not the seat of consciousness or conscience. If you have a look at the Soulless Condition, for example, you'll notice that the character stays themselves... they just start to run out of psychological juice and may behave oddly due to the effects on Virtue and Vice. And vampires have intact souls, despite the strains on self that Humanity loss models.*<br /> <br /> A soul's kind of like a fire burning in a hearth. You can put it out, then start a new one with a different kind of wood, but the room around it is still warm, and more to the point is still the same building. So no, no body snatching.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Vampires sometimes don't describe this accurately -- most of them don't understand the metaphysics. But in actual supernatural terms, that's how it is.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:28:10-07:00","id":559350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559348#post559348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the soul pact seems to do more than steal the soul or consume it. Mage Reapers do that all the tone and it just leaves husks of human beings. What the demons seem to do is literally co-opt all the material aspects of the person (including external social connections aND resources) but destroy most of the persons innate ephemeral qualities in the process, including the soul. It is more that they are getting permission for such obliteration, rather than actually taking possession of the soul itself (I think the book describes it as destroying the person and soul when they fulfill the pact, and stepping into that void before reality rushes in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:34:22-07:00","id":559357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559348#post559348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly that's it. But also partly the &quot;soul&quot; pact actually mucks with a lot more than the soul. Depending on how you view it, it also can include destruction of the physical body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:35:52-07:00","id":559360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559327#post559327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We might change the language some, but that's basically still how it works. The Horror replaces your human soul, creating a hybrid myth/person.<br /> <br /> It's important to note that in the World of Darkness, the soul is not the seat of consciousness or conscience. If you have a look at the Soulless Condition, for example, you'll notice that the character stays themselves... they just start to run out of psychological juice and may behave oddly due to the effects on Virtue and Vice. And vampires have intact souls, despite the strains on self that Humanity loss models.*<br /> <br /> A soul's kind of like a fire burning in a hearth. You can put it out, then start a new one with a different kind of wood, but the room around it is still warm, and more to the point is still the same building. So no, no body snatching.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Vampires sometimes don't describe this accurately -- most of them don't understand the metaphysics. But in actual supernatural terms, that's how it is.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>If the process is still one of self-discovery rather than one of being taken over, then I personally am reassured on this point, but changing the wording to better reflect it would indeed be a excellent idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:40:29-07:00","id":559364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559348#post559348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, Demons don't really have the memories of the people they take over. They might have the social connections and history of said people, but its not something they know innately after claiming a person. <br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean anything. Absorbing the &quot;Infrastructure&quot; that makes up human lives might very well be an innate ability of the Unchained, and the pesky soul acts as a bulwark against it. So, by claiming the soul, a demon can get around the defenses and absorb the new Cover, killing the person in the process. <br /> <br /> Soul pacts really don't have anything to do with souls, when you get right down to it. There's a few powers that interact with souls, mind you, but mostly indirectly. Raising a person from the dead &quot;restores their soul&quot; but the demons can't see, interact with, or do anything with the soul other than repair a vessel for it and hope it hops in. Demons are pretty much all about the physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:40:41-07:00","id":559365,"title":"","content":"Looking at the different splats, I would probably say that Mages have the best knowledge of the soul, and that is usually only enough to say &quot;we can muck around with it, but we aren't 100% sure what it is or what it does, but it definitely seems important!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:45:14-07:00","id":559366,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm curious about is exploring the Onerios pre- and post- Devouring, actually. If the original soul is devoured by the Horror and replaces it, how much of the inside of that soul going to change? Do we still have a daimon and demon inside? What if we say that the Horror is from previous Beasts, and is now rebonding to a physical body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:45:58-07:00","id":559367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559364#post559364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, Demons don't really have the memories of the people they take over. They might have the social connections and history of said people, but its not something they know innately after claiming a person.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean anything. Absorbing the &quot;Infrastructure&quot; that makes up human lives might very well be an innate ability of the Unchained, and the pesky soul acts as a bulwark against it. So, by claiming the soul, a demon can get around the defenses and absorb the new Cover, killing the person in the process.<br /> <br /> Soul pacts really don't have anything to do with souls, when you get right down to it. There's a few powers that interact with souls, mind you, but mostly indirectly. Raising a person from the dead &quot;restores their soul&quot; but the demons can't see, interact with, or do anything with the soul other than repair a vessel for it and hope it hops in. Demons are pretty much all about the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take this as 100% canon or anything, but I always liked the idea that the pact takes the soul out sorta like you turn off the power before you fool with wiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:57:23-07:00","id":559381,"title":"","content":"I am not sure about the Onieros changes (but those a RE really good questions) but I feel that each Horror is new, or I hope they are. To me, the idea that the Beast-to-Be's (BtB) confrontation is a crystallizing moment that makes the Horror more than just a primordial fear but a unique facet if the Primordial Dream, after years of being shaped by the BtB's long term connection to thr primordial. Essentially, it was honed as much by thr BtB's connection as the BtB was shaped by it. <br /> <br /> Though I do wonder what happens to those Beasts that undergo retreat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:06:04-07:00","id":559384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559365#post559365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the different splats, I would probably say that Mages have the best knowledge of the soul, and that is usually only enough to say &quot;we can muck around with it, but we aren't 100% sure what it is or what it does, but it definitely seems important!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>According to 1e Mage cosmology, the souls are intimately tied to the Supernal. They flow from it, and return to it once we die. The creation of ghosts, while theoretically not having a soul itself (debatable), does prevent the soul from moving on. Sin-Eaters, while some might argue that ghosts have/are souls, don't know souls move on to, they only know its not the Underworld and they have nothing to do with it beyond setting them loose. <br /> <br /> So, if we assume that the 1e cosmology holds true, then mages do, in fact, deal more with souls than anyone else because its more intimately tied into their existance than any other game, save possibly Beast. And, even then, mages were the ones who went to college in the family, while Beast Mama stayed at home, caring for all the kids. Really, if only Camilla would put as much effort into her future as Moony; at least Moony spends his time keeping the place safe instead of playing around and staying out all night! And don't get me started on Frankie - always complaining that everyone hates him. We love him very much, but he's always talking about going off on his own, moving to a new city,s tarting a new life, as if the one we provided wasn't good enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:07:04-07:00","id":559388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559367#post559367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't take this as 100% canon or anything, but I always liked the idea that the pact takes the soul out sorta like you turn off the power before you fool with wiring.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I likes! *steals!*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:34:04-07:00","id":559405,"title":"","content":"Seems like the soul works similarly to how it did in the Mekhet clan book, where it was your Morality baseline. Except now it's Integrity. I guess it's like your soul's health.<br /> <br /> It certainly explains how the Harmony sins affect werewolf souls, since theirs isn't just human. Low Harmony means the spirit half is strong with the human side weak, high the human half with the spirit part faded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-18-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:48:31-07:00","id":559417,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... thinking about it... <br /> <br /> If mages are the ones that went to college, Prommies are the adopted kids, and vamps are the night owls that party all the time... what are the other supernaturals in the Beast family set up? Unchained would be the Stranger Danger...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:00:00-07:00","id":559424,"title":"","content":"Changeling's the sensitive kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:10:36-07:00","id":559432,"title":"","content":"Possibility. Continue to call it Homecoming but say that you were born with a soul that wanders the Primordial Dream. Another Beast (or a self realization) reveals that your soul is that of an ancient monster. Then you make the choice to continue with your life and never become a Beast, or to guide your soul back to your body where the two unite and you become a true Beast.<br /> <br /> This enables the 'born this way' and 'family' supporters, AND the 'choice' supporters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:33:15-07:00","id":559488,"title":"","content":"O, what's in a name? That which we call a monster's birth/ by any other name would scare as deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:43:27-07:00","id":559493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559488#post559488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O, what's in a name? That which we call a monster's birth/ by any other name would scare as deep.</div> </div> </div> </div> If we prick them, do they not bleed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But good point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:13:35-07:00","id":559504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559348#post559348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies too seem to use Soul for something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:14:03-07:00","id":559505,"title":"","content":"Sometimes a lot. :P Homecoming has connotations of reassurance; Devouring implies something swallowing up the you-that-was and what is left is the Beast. But from what Rose has been saying about it, it seems to be fine as what it actually is, so I'm not hugely fussed over it. Especially as terminology is flexible both in the draft at this point and at the table.<br /> <br /> Horror is a more notable change, though. Changing it from being a Soul has some major thematic implications that were covered up-thread.<br /> <br /> ...On the other hand I'm probably getting dangerously close to opening a can of worms larger than a Beast whose Soul/Horror is made of them, so. &lt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6527-fleshcrafterangel","name":"FleshcrafterAngel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:38:01-07:00","id":559535,"title":"","content":"I rather like the idea that the soul is this weird little black box that people interact with in different ways. That said, Beast sits close to Mage's metaphysics, so it makes sense for them to follow that structure.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Except I'm forgetting that what's described is default, not mage. Still works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:44:45-07:00","id":559550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559348#post559348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it Unchained don't really understand these metaphysics either, since what they call a soul pact actually does usurp the person's consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it doesn't really give the conciousness of the target just their identity. Actually the Unchained define the soul as all aspects of a person that make them a recognizable individual, so outside of raising the dead I think the unchained really don't care too much about the metaphysical soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:55:55-07:00","id":559565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559327#post559327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A soul's kind of like a fire burning in a hearth. You can put it out, then start a new one with a different kind of wood, but the room around it is still warm, and more to the point is still the same building. So no, no body snatching.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, the <i>Howl's Moving Castle</i> version of a soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:09:27-07:00","id":559573,"title":"","content":"whelp leauge of legends just gave us an example of a beast and it is a interesting beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9RM4HwwoKs\" data-code=\"u9RM4HwwoKs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u9RM4HwwoKs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:15:40-07:00","id":559576,"title":"","content":"Quote The Blackhat: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt, on Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;In this moment of epiphany, she sees the face of the Dark Mother. She joins her new Family, a word rich with bittersweet connotations. For the first time, the Beast knows what she is and where the dreams came from. She is not a defective human being. She is not insane. She is a creature of legend.<br /> The Beast\u2019s eyes snap open. She and the nightmare are one.&quot;<br /> \u202a#\u200eamwriting\u202c \u202a#\u200ewip\u202c \u202a#\u200eBeast\u202c</div> </div> </div> 