east-the-primordial?p=559161#post559161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to echo the praise found elsewhere on this page. You have all comported yourselves with grace and dignity, despite the Scylla and Charybdis of circumstances that has set in. Everyone knows that you guys are determined to make Beast the best game it can be, and also the game that Matt set out to create.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note to self: Stat Scylla and Charybdis as picky internet nerds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:19:38-07:00","id":559665,"title":"","content":"Oh, yes. That too. And, notably, Rose and Matt (though especially Rose, for me, just due to, y'know, her addressing my specific areas of concern) have been good at clarifying contended points here while also having to juggle working on the rewrite; it wouldn't have surprised me for them to be far too busy to address matters here directly, and it's awesome that they've been able to do so while still having to rewrite it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6527-fleshcrafterangel","name":"FleshcrafterAngel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:33:25-07:00","id":559673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559625#post559625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note to self: Stat Scylla and Charybdis as picky internet nerds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking and choosing points that the other one won't have; screeching and roaring at all who pass. People desperate to avoid them.<br /> <br /> These local Beasts do not get on; and some damn fool gave them wi-fi <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:43:39-07:00","id":559870,"title":"","content":"So, if someone wanted to do something like, for example, create a Beast based off the fear of God how do you guys think would be the best way to go about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:45:02-07:00","id":559873,"title":"","content":"Anakim, Hunger for Punishment, possibly Ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:08:52-07:00","id":559942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lovecraft lite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=559870#post559870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if someone wanted to do something like, for example, create a Beast based off the fear of God how do you guys think would be the best way to go about that?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, been stewin' on this for a while. I'd go with an Anakim, focusing on the sheer vastness of Him(unless you want to focus on His aspect of &quot;All-Knowing&quot;, in which case I'd go Ugallu). Of all the Hungers, I'd go with Punishment, reflecting the whole &quot;Fire and Brimstone&quot;/&quot;I am a Jealous God&quot; shtick, not to mention it looks like the most &quot;moral&quot; Hunger(even if it's not). In my particular case, I'm shaping his Soul/Horror as a massive angel, a vaguely- humanoid pillar of fire with eight wings and a blazing sword, covered in &quot;eyes&quot; made of small spheres of light. My idea is that his &quot;Heart Chamber&quot; takes the form of the idea of Fluffy Cloud Heaven... except it's perpetually on fire and generally a roiling, chaotic storm surrounding a vast, unreachable constant. At least one of his Chambers will be a cathedral. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:51:38-07:00","id":559967,"title":"","content":"See Old Testament. Pillars of fire, turning people to salt, plagues, rivers of blood, the parting of seas. Punishment would be the obvious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:01:06-07:00","id":559974,"title":"","content":"I am SO happy over the new Stretch Goal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:46:31-07:00","id":560039,"title":"","content":"The Hunter supplement is looking mighty appealing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:57:31-07:00","id":560046,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I have a question about the mechanics of a Beast's Soul. In the Soul Itself passage, the text states that a Soul can use any aspect of an Atavism. Does this follow the normal rules for Atavisms or can the Soul use them freely regardless of Satiety?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:59:07-07:00","id":560049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560046#post560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I have a question about the mechanics of a Beast's Soul. In the Soul Itself passage, the text states that a Soul can use any aspect of an Atavism. Does this follow the normal rules for Atavisms or can the Soul use them freely regardless of Satiety?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncertain, but remember Lair Resonance is universal for the Soul due to its confinement to the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:07:14-07:00","id":560057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560046#post560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I have a question about the mechanics of a Beast's Soul. In the Soul Itself passage, the text states that a Soul can use any aspect of an Atavism. Does this follow the normal rules for Atavisms or can the Soul use them freely regardless of Satiety?</div> </div> </div> </div>This part remains unclear. Very vaguely worded text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:41:28-07:00","id":560164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560049#post560049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uncertain, but remember Lair Resonance is universal for the Soul due to its confinement to the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560057#post560057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part remains unclear. Very vaguely worded text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers guys, I guess we'll have to wait for official clarification on this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:43:30-07:00","id":560169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560046#post560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I have a question about the mechanics of a Beast's Soul. In the Soul Itself passage, the text states that a Soul can use any aspect of an Atavism. Does this follow the normal rules for Atavisms or can the Soul use them freely regardless of Satiety?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it got brought up in the Kickstarter comments Matt indicated it was the latter. He said it was likely not going to get changed but they were planning on clarifying the text.<br /> <br /> Best wait until after the revisions to ask again though, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-18-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T19:20:43-07:00","id":560208,"title":"","content":"I thought it was clear the soul could use any effect of an Atavism no matter what Satiety it had. What was unclear to me was if the Satiety expenditure still cost anything when it was the soul using it. If it does then the Beast can find their Satiety dropping against their will in a sense as the Horror goes on a rampage around the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T01:21:33-07:00","id":560520,"title":"","content":"I had a thought about beasts and their lairs- That they're the beastly equivalent of influences.<br /> <br /> Ephemerals, presumably including goetia, use natural conditions or influence to make the right conditions to manifest.<br /> <br /> Beasts use natural conditions or impose their lair traits to manifest their inner horror.<br /> <br /> Beasts, so far, lack a real versatile power set like vampire blood magic, mage arcana, changeling goblin vows, or networking with ephemerals with influences like sin-eaters and werewolves can do.<br /> <br /> So what about an option along the lines of a martial art-like series of merits to enable beasts to make their lair traits more versatile along the lines of ephemeral influences?<br /> <br /> Anyone think say the idea of say a sea serpent that can manipulate water or a dragon that can manipulate fire as too out there?<br /> <br /> Oh and for the record I didn't mean one merit for making every lair trait more versatile, but something they have to buy for each lair they want to specialize in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T04:23:37-07:00","id":560621,"title":"","content":"I don't know. The beasts influence isn't an elemental force or species, it is Fear and their hungers. I think they already have plenty of influences along those lines, which are extremely powerful. <br /> <br /> All the other stuff is there to facilitate that primary influence. The Dragon Breath isn't part if their influence ovet fire, bur part of humanities fear of being burned (and giant, firebreathing lizards). Considering they can bring their Lairs to overlap with physical reality, and that atavisms effects are real and nightmares effects are real for the target, it isn't like they can't draw on the thematic elements that support the central fears they represent.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and remember they represent concepts. So that Sea Serpent isn't representing the Ocean, but the Fears of the Unknown, Drowning, Aquatic Life, etc. His powers are going to be reflective of those Fears, and may have elements of salt water, but he isn't representing the Ocean as a concept itself, which would give him power over water. A fire spirit doesn't gain essence from fear, but from causing fires, hence it's influence over fire (unless it consumes/merges with a spirit of fear or was born out of an amalgamation of human fear of burning and the fire itself... but then it is a spirit representing both).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-19-2015, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:24:22-07:00","id":560654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560520#post560520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought about beasts and their lairs- That they're the beastly equivalent of influences.<br /> <br /> Ephemerals, presumably including goetia, use natural conditions or influence to make the right conditions to manifest.<br /> <br /> Beasts use natural conditions or impose their lair traits to manifest their inner horror.<br /> <br /> Beasts, so far, lack a real versatile power set like vampire blood magic, mage arcana, changeling goblin vows, or networking with ephemerals with influences like sin-eaters and werewolves can do.<br /> <br /> So what about an option along the lines of a martial art-like series of merits to enable beasts to make their lair traits more versatile along the lines of ephemeral influences?<br /> <br /> Anyone think say the idea of say a sea serpent that can manipulate water or a dragon that can manipulate fire as too out there?<br /> <br /> Oh and for the record I didn't mean one merit for making every lair trait more versatile, but something they have to buy for each lair they want to specialize in.</div> </div> </div> </div> A few thoughts. The first is that the Lair is a lot like the ultimate Safe Place (the traps are waaaay better). Its got a lot of flexibility where you call up this Safe Place, but that's the only flexibility involved. You can't really change what you're invoking here, you can't influence or direct the fires of your home. Its not really meant to represent a kind of flexible magic to influence things. Its meant to reflect that Beasts almost always can have the home ground advantage. <br /> <br /> We already have &quot;manipulate water&quot; and &quot;manipulate fire&quot; powers. They're both Atavisms. Remember, Beasts aren't mages or elementals, nor are they actual spirits. Is it thematically appropriate for a dragon to control an existing blaze with his mind? No, not at all. Its appropriate for him to take a bath in burning lava without issue, but not extinguish or raise flames at whim. <br /> <br /> Its a question of what's thematically appropriate here. Legendary monsters are renowned for spreading terror, their dungeons, their strength, their unusual forms. They're not renowned for flexible magic. I don't think that expanding the existing things would help the game at all, and would actually dilute the impact. <br /> <br /> Plus, not really interested in dealing with more &quot;OMG~ Beasts are OP!&quot; complaints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:37:06-07:00","id":560809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560654#post560654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A few thoughts. The first is that the Lair is a lot like the ultimate Safe Place (the traps are waaaay better). Its got a lot of flexibility where you call up this Safe Place, but that's the only flexibility involved. You can't really change what you're invoking here, you can't influence or direct the fires of your home. Its not really meant to represent a kind of flexible magic to influence things. Its meant to reflect that Beasts almost always can have the home ground advantage. <br /> <br /> We already have &amp;quot;manipulate water&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;manipulate fire&amp;quot; powers. They're both Atavisms. Remember, Beasts aren't mages or elementals, nor are they actual spirits. Is it thematically appropriate for a dragon to control an existing blaze with his mind? No, not at all. Its appropriate for him to take a bath in burning lava without issue, but not extinguish or raise flames at whim. <br /> <br /> Its a question of what's thematically appropriate here. Legendary monsters are renowned for spreading terror, their dungeons, their strength, their unusual forms. They're not renowned for flexible magic. I don't think that expanding the existing things would help the game at all, and would actually dilute the impact. <br /> <br /> Plus, not really interested in dealing with more &amp;quot;OMG~ Beasts are OP!&amp;quot; complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't control fire or water they can breath fire but they can't control the flame","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:52:29-07:00","id":560831,"title":"","content":"Huh... I wonder. Can you buy merits to reflect stuff in your Lair? Can you populate your Lair with Staff and Retainers? Can you buy Safe Place targeting your Lair? I think Library explicitly can be in your Lair, but I'm not sure if that's an exception or a note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:58:05-07:00","id":560837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560831#post560831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I wonder. Can you buy merits to reflect stuff in your Lair? Can you populate your Lair with Staff and Retainers? Can you buy Safe Place targeting your Lair? I think Library explicitly can be in your Lair, but I'm not sure if that's an exception or a note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha. Can the Horror be your True Friend? Naruto style!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:59:50-07:00","id":560839,"title":"","content":"Probably better to buy safe place targeting lair <i>entrances. </i>That said, I can't help but wonder how close a chamber copies it's source material. If you make one out of somewhere with an electrical supply, can you get electricity in your lair? <br /> <br /> Could you lay an extension cord across a burrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:41:57-07:00","id":560879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560831#post560831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I wonder. Can you buy merits to reflect stuff in your Lair? Can you populate your Lair with Staff and Retainers? Can you buy Safe Place targeting your Lair? I think Library explicitly can be in your Lair, but I'm not sure if that's an exception or a note.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, with the caveats that without True Friend for your supporting NPC Merits, you'd be setting yourself up for being murdered the moment you hit Satiety 10, and that you would need to add the Library, Arsenal, Torture Suite, or whathaveyou, to the Lair through the usual process, while Safe Place is somewhat redundant within the Lair, and really works better for securing locations with perfect Lair Sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:25:08-07:00","id":560900,"title":"","content":"Wut? You have your PC's Retainers murder them the moment they are weak? That's pretty harsh.<br /> <br /> And I'm half picturing &quot;people who are allowed to go to your Lair&quot; and half picturing &quot;a dragon cave, but with Kobolds in it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:30:43-07:00","id":560903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560900#post560900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wut? You have your PC's Retainers murder them the moment they are weak? That's pretty harsh.<br /> <br /> And I'm half picturing &quot;people who are allowed to go to your Lair&quot; and half picturing &quot;a dragon cave, but with Kobolds in it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So that makes me wonder, can you take Hobgoblin Retainers? Because I imagine that Kobolds would be a type of Hobgoblin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:46:22-07:00","id":560912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560831#post560831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I wonder. Can you buy merits to reflect stuff in your Lair? Can you populate your Lair with Staff and Retainers? Can you buy Safe Place targeting your Lair? I think Library explicitly can be in your Lair, but I'm not sure if that's an exception or a note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, no I am going to be sad if they don't patch in a merit for hordes of lesser servant creatures taking care of your lair.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/WOuh7u3.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Seriously though, we need a Beast merit for hordes of lesser servant creatures! NWoD doesn't have that yet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:46:39-07:00","id":560913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560903#post560903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that makes me wonder, can you take Hobgoblin Retainers? Because I imagine that Kobolds would be a type of Hobgoblin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Animals can be retainers too. A Beast who's Soul connects to the Wild Hunt could easily have wolves and bears as retainers within its lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:59:13-07:00","id":560917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560809#post560809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't control fire or water they can breath fire but they can't control the flame</div> </div> </div> </div> That was kind of the tongue-in-cheek point I was making. There are powers that exist for dealing with the elements, and that's really the extent we should expect from a Beast. More than that really isn't very iconic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:02:38-07:00","id":560918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560654#post560654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A few thoughts. The first is that the Lair is a lot like the ultimate Safe Place (the traps are waaaay better). Its got a lot of flexibility where you call up this Safe Place, but that's the only flexibility involved. You can't really change what you're invoking here, you can't influence or direct the fires of your home. Its not really meant to represent a kind of flexible magic to influence things. Its meant to reflect that Beasts almost always can have the home ground advantage.<br /> <br /> We already have &quot;manipulate water&quot; and &quot;manipulate fire&quot; powers. They're both Atavisms. Remember, Beasts aren't mages or elementals, nor are they actual spirits. Is it thematically appropriate for a dragon to control an existing blaze with his mind? No, not at all. Its appropriate for him to take a bath in burning lava without issue, but not extinguish or raise flames at whim.<br /> <br /> Its a question of what's thematically appropriate here. Legendary monsters are renowned for spreading terror, their dungeons, their strength, their unusual forms. They're not renowned for flexible magic. I don't think that expanding the existing things would help the game at all, and would actually dilute the impact.<br /> <br /> Plus, not really interested in dealing with more &quot;OMG~ Beasts are OP!&quot; complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div> Monsters aren't known for magic? Then how did dragons teach mages magic over in Mage? Did you know that there are two gods of magic that happen to be dragons? Not to mention of course other draconic gods, being a god of something usually includes having control over something in myth. Or of course all those myths in which dragons control the weather, using lair doesn't really cut it when the dragons are specifically known for stopping bad weather too. <br /> <br /> Or how about hags? Are you saying that someone who wants to play something like Baba Yaga is wrong? <br /> <br /> Did you fail to notice that beast souls without there bodies are ephemeral beings covered by all those rules, including having influences such as grief and water? And an unfettered looking to manifest physically? Why, arrange an open condition with their influence so they can use the materialize manifestation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:06:01-07:00","id":560921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560831#post560831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I wonder. Can you buy merits to reflect stuff in your Lair? Can you populate your Lair with Staff and Retainers? Can you buy Safe Place targeting your Lair? I think Library explicitly can be in your Lair, but I'm not sure if that's an exception or a note.</div> </div> </div> </div> No reason you can't have a Safe Place as one of the Chambers from your Lair. I'm actually discussing a shared Safe Place that all the brood have as a Chamber, and we all link with the Traits, being able to combine our Lairs through this point.<br /> <br /> Staffing the Lair is a bit trickier, since you'll need to give an open invitation to them, which is something most Beasts are leery of doing with non-Kinship folk.<br /> <br /> Zero reason Library can't be in one of your Chambers either (I'd suggest the Heart). Be careful the environmental Tilts you have don't ruin the books, however.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560839#post560839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably better to buy safe place targeting lair <i>entrances. </i>That said, I can't help but wonder how close a chamber copies it's source material. If you make one out of somewhere with an electrical supply, can you get electricity in your lair?<br /> <br /> Could you lay an extension cord across a burrow?</div> </div> </div> </div> I see no reason. Remember, burrows are just passageways through the Astral. Its not like you actually need electricity to run appliances in the Astral, though you'll probably need to plug it in.<br /> <br /> As for how close? I imagine that depends entirely on how much you want it to. You're going to be blending the Lair traits with the Chamber, don't forget, so there's going to be some differences. A volcanic lair is going to have an effect on that wintery mountain you just added as a chamber. And vice versa. The bigger your Lair, the more the Chambers bleed into each other, I imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=560903#post560903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that makes me wonder, can you take Hobgoblin Retainers? Because I imagine that Kobolds would be a type of Hobgoblin.</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling had a Hedgebeast Companion merit that worked like that. Not sure if it'll hold in 2e, but it was a thing in 1e. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:07:15-07:00","id":561016,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Heroes might dream of grand climactic battles in the Lair, but when push comes to shove, they\u2019ll settle for a shotgun blast or an IED in the Beast\u2019s doorway. Despite the Hero\u2019s grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the Beast dead.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strip down the layers of a Hero\u2019s ego, and all one finds is murder. Murder is his only end, regardless of bystanders. He\u2019ll bloviate about the innocents he saves, but at the best of times, protecting the innocent is incidental. He pursues the Beast because his dreams are the surface of the Primordial Dream, and he sees monsters below. He pursues the Beast because <i>he cannot wake up.</i>&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:18:03-07:00","id":561036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=561016#post561016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Heroes might dream of grand climactic battles in the Lair, but when push comes to shove, they\u2019ll settle for a shotgun blast or an IED in the Beast\u2019s doorway. Despite the Hero\u2019s grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the Beast dead.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strip down the layers of a Hero\u2019s ego, and all one finds is murder. Murder is his only end, regardless of bystanders. He\u2019ll bloviate about the innocents he saves, but at the best of times, protecting the innocent is incidental. He pursues the Beast because his dreams are the surface of the Primordial Dream, and he sees monsters below. He pursues the Beast because <i>he cannot wake up.</i>&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Love it! Delightfully creepy. It also sets up a nice parallel with Hunter. Hunters keep the Vigil, staying awake in the dark of the night, trying desperately to keep the light burning. Heroes are wrapped up in their dreams and illusions of grandeur, unaware of what is actually going on around them, fixated on the only thing that seems real. <br /> <br /> It also suggests the best ways for Beasts to truly break the narrative and save the Hero. <i>Make the Hero wake up</i>. There are wonderful metaphors and analogues loaded within that simple concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:19:25-07:00","id":561039,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, those are some good paragraphs. I have to admit that last bit is quite... evocative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:27:42-07:00","id":561046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=561036#post561036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Make the Hero wake up</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>*mage's ears perk up*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:28:06-07:00","id":561080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Claimed - they use Dread Powers, not Influences and Numina.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The claimed still have their influences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:30:56-07:00","id":561092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=561036#post561036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also suggests the best ways for Beasts to truly break the narrative and save the Hero. <i>Make the Hero wake up</i>. There are wonderful metaphors and analogues loaded within that simple concept.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, Beast really does remind me of Overlord and Dungeon Keeper style games, and I've got a soft spot in my heart for making Fallen Heroes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beas