eword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:12:25-07:00","id":564642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564623#post564623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pulled out of my ass in three seconds</div> </div> </div> </div>Your honor, the prosecution rests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:16:29-07:00","id":564649,"title":"","content":"The point is it's <i>easy</i> to spin it how you want. I put barely any thought into that and yet I think it holds up fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:22:49-07:00","id":564651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564649#post564649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is it's <i>easy</i> to spin it how you want. I put barely any thought into that and yet I think it holds up fairly well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is, this thing you made up has exactly one line of support and only if you squint.<br /> <br /> Your interpretation is not canon.<br /> <br /> Only the literal wording of the book is canon, unless the authors say otherwise.<br /> <br /> And the literal wording of the book is that the horror was not part of you until your soul was ripped out and eaten to make room for you.<br /> <br /> Meaning that sidebar about home comings does not make sense in context as anything but a case of certain beasts deluding themselves about what happened to them because it makes themselves feel better about themself from before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:31:54-07:00","id":564654,"title":"","content":"Dude, you've got to relax. It's hard to have a good discussion about the game when you're bringing in courtroom lingo (you're making it awkward and uncomfortable for <i>everyone </i>by being this confrontational) and getting into page after page of arguments with people.<br /> <br /> Please, for the sake of having useful discussions about Beast, take a deep breath and try to not be so intensely adversarial with other people.<br /> <br /> Elfive's point seems pretty reasonable to me. I think the Devouring is awkwardly worded, fine, but the <i>intent </i>and the <i>idea </i>seem to be pretty clear, <i>especially </i>in light of comments made by Matt and Rose about the Homecoming, the Devouring and how the two ideas are woven together.<br /> <br /> I think you're taking a really myopic view of the text, possibly because you seem so intensely invested in it. Maybe give it some time to think about it, and maybe ask for clarification from the Developers and writers to try and make sure you're understanding the text correctly rather than declaring that yours is the One True Way. Maybe if you took a more constructive approach, it'd be easier to parse the valid complaints, and how your feedback could help refine the concepts being discussed for the final product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:32:20-07:00","id":564655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very occasionally, the dreamer spots a Beast first, and follows her, trying to make sense of the odd connection she feels, eventually realizing she is, in a sense, chasing herself. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> new Beasts invariably feel that by becoming a Beast, they have not lost their humanity but gained something they were missing all along. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The objective truth of how a Beast becomes a Beast is left deliberately murky </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the moment of the Devouring, though, the Horror understands the connection to the dreamer just as the dreamer realizes her connection to the Horror. In order for it to fully join with the dreamer, the human soul must be cleared away, <b>symbolically</b> consumed, and <b>reimagined</b>. </div> </div> </div>That is the sound of literally the entire section on the Devouring contradicting you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:41:25-07:00","id":564662,"title":"","content":"The first one isn't conclusive, the second can bea side effect of the Horror gaining a physical body, the third has no bearing as it's an out of character side note, we're going by what the text says, and the third flat out says that the soul has to be cleared away to make room for the horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:50:56-07:00","id":564668,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/927/298/d4e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">athousandpicturescannolongerexpressmylevelofdisbel eifwiththisthread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:54:13-07:00","id":564673,"title":"","content":"The third is a direct refutation of this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564651#post564651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the literal wording of the book is that the horror was not part of you until your soul was ripped out and eaten to make room for you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They said they were being murky on purpose. I presented you with said murkyness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:12:23-07:00","id":564683,"title":"","content":"I think after a hundred pages or so of dialogue that it's readily apparent which people should be listened to and which should be ignored.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:22:04-07:00","id":564725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564594#post564594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain that please.<br /> <br /> Am I not screaming about problems that don't exist?<br /> <br /> Or am I not making valid criticism?</div> </div> </div> </div>First your statement on &quot;not screaming about problems that don't exist&quot; is terribly written. Copy-editor needed to get that out of the way.<br /> <br /> You aren't making a good case for your arguments, you aren't making arguments, you are complaining about things which are not problems.<br /> <br /> Flaw the first &quot;Beast's teaching a lesson is too restrictive to character creation.&quot; You've never explained this. Since feeding can happen independently of any lesson a Beast wants to teach and since Beasts can teach whatever bloody lesson they want including not teaching one at all this is not restrictive. Certainly not in the same way Epic motivation was in Exalted 2nd which was actually removed because of the limitations and problems in the way it functioned.<br /> <br /> Flaw the second &quot;The Horror devours your soul thus making you a pod person.&quot; This was a fair question when it was just the introduction due to lack of information. At this point though it doesn't work as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the dream, in that final nightmare, when the last shred of the dreamer\u2019s soul is Devoured and the character experiences a pure moment of nothing, then that dreamer must make the choice.Only when she is no longer afraid can she be whole. Thrown into the monster\u2019s jaws, the Beast triumphs over fear by becoming it. She steps into the monster\u2019s role and takes control.<br /> In this moment of epiphany, she sees the face of the Dark Mother. She joins her new Family, a word rich with bittersweet connotations. For the first time, the Beast knows what she is and where the dreams came from. She is not a defective human being. She is not insane. She is a creature of legend. The Beast\u2019s eyes snap open. She and the nightmare are one. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Lost part of a line in the quote 06-22-2015, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:35:01-07:00","id":564736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564673#post564673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They said they were being murky on purpose. I presented you with said murkyness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well maybe <i>you</i> should be more clear about their purposeful murkiness. We don't need ambiguity mucking up the concrete, definitive list of uncontradictory bullet points that define the WoD.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, I don't think you're going to get Rater to understand where you're coming and what you're trying to say unless you're agreeing with him. Those heels be dug in hard, and it seems like the only thing that will change his mind is putting the words &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot; back in, and removing &quot;Devouring&quot; and &quot;Horror&quot;. Since that's unlikely to happen, what is to be gained here?<br /> <br /> I'm hijacking this argument to talk about dancing. Specifically, what would you guys do to define a Hunger for Disco Fever? Like, what would a Satiety 10 act of funkalicious grooving look like? And what would a good Family/Hunger for this Jive Titan to be possessed of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:35:20-07:00","id":564737,"title":"","content":"Man, I think the new chapters are fantastic. They mesh in a more interesting way with other supernaturals, for one (the Views From Without are fantastic, the stereotypes are great).<br /> <br /> I also dig the Ugallu's Birthright, and I hope it doesn't get changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:41:40-07:00","id":564739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564736#post564736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hijacking this argument to talk about dancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to harsh your moxie, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/459089-dance-off-bro-best-supernatural-dancer\">we have a thread for that</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Specifically, what would you guys do to define a Hunger for Disco Fever? </div> </div> </div>I can only call that a Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:46:52-07:00","id":564743,"title":"","content":"The section that says it explains what the &quot;truth&quot; is has no relevance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:18:41-07:00","id":564771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564739#post564739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to harsh your moxie, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/459089-dance-off-bro-best-supernatural-dancer\">we have a thread for that</a>.<br /> <br /> I can only call that a Nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still haveto skip the second page, because that one thing Shock put up still really fucks me up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:46:43-07:00","id":564784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564737#post564737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I think the new chapters are fantastic. They mesh in a more interesting way with other supernaturals, for one (the Views From Without are fantastic, the stereotypes are great).<br /> <br /> I also dig the Ugallu's Birthright, and I hope it doesn't get changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even notice. I do think the revised birthright is more appropriate for the family. The old one was okay but I was scratching my head as to how it really fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:54:15-07:00","id":564789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564784#post564784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't even notice. I do think the revised birthright is more appropriate for the family. The old one was okay but I was scratching my head as to how it really fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new version has many things to recommend it, not least being actual mechanical distinction, but I feel like one of the neater things about it is that the Anakim Birthright is no longer in this weird otherspace as the only Birthright that potentially costs Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:02:52-07:00","id":564793,"title":"","content":"Can I get some clarity here: Epic Fame is the Merit that represents your character's Horror coming with a history and name... why do only already famous/powerful people get those horrors? Is it supposed to be your Horror pushing you to do greater things, because I'm just not seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:04:33-07:00","id":564796,"title":"","content":"The Ugallu birthright could use a small clarification. I'm not sure it they would be searching for a specific hidden or any hidden something. I guess it can be cleared up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:09:51-07:00","id":564799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564793#post564793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get some clarity here: Epic Fame is the Merit that represents your character's Horror coming with a history and name... why do only already famous/powerful people get those horrors? Is it supposed to be your Horror pushing you to do greater things, because I'm just not seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think </i>the intent is the other way around. Your mythology is driving you to become famous in reality as well as in legend. <br /> <br /> It kinda feels like its meant to be a simultaneous thing. Like, with the Coils in the Ordo Dracul. You need Status to buy Coils, but the justification for buying Status 1 is having a Coil... So, the solution is to buy them simultaneously. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:30:25-07:00","id":564808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564673#post564673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third is a direct refutation of this:<br /> <br /> They said they were being murky on purpose. I presented you with said murkyness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be great if it was actually murky.<br /> <br /> Explictly saying the soul is removed to make room for something else is not murky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:39:10-07:00","id":564816,"title":"","content":"So what did you guys think about the lessons my three favorite ones are effort cooperation and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:40:28-07:00","id":564817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564725#post564725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> you are complaining about things which are not problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unnecessary changes that take the game away from the game that was promised are not a problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flaw the first &quot;Beast's teaching a lesson is too restrictive to character creation.&quot; You've never explained this. </div> </div> </div>Beast culture is supposedly about Beasts teaching people lessons through fear.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have to do this horrible thing, to teach you a lesson&quot; is the justification given for like, half of all domestic abusers.<br /> <br /> And since teaching lessons is apparently the cornerstone of Beast culture, presumably the majority of Beasts are going to be doing it.<br /> <br /> And when the majority of a population is doing one thing, and that one thing is the cornerstone of their culture, then anyone in the culture who does not like it is at best looked down on an at worst prosecuted. That is a fact that is backed by historical evidence.<br /> <br /> When my only two options are &quot;Abuser&quot; and &quot;Guy who get's looked down on or prosecuted because he doen'st want to be an asshole&quot;, I consider myself to not have enough options.<br /> <br /> Beasts are, culturally, encouraged to be abusers now.<br /> <br /> So where are all the people who were bitching about &quot;All Beasts are abusers&quot; back when it wasn't culturally mandatory? Why are they not complaining about it now, since it's actually a legitimate critism now?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flaw the second &quot;The Horror devours your soul thus making you a pod person.&quot; This was a fair question when it was just the introduction due to lack of information. At this point though it doesn't work as well. </div> </div> </div>I think since, with this update making it quite explicit that a Horror is an entity separate from the original, the Beasts are pod people criticism is more valid.<br /> <br /> But really, you ignored my third argument: A Best is no longer part of a family.<br /> <br /> A BEast is now somebody who just so happened to have weird dreams up until he got invited to or forced to join a club, and some of them just so happen to have deluded themselves into thinking they were always part of the club.<br /> <br /> That right there utterly murders Beasts selling point-you're not family anymore, you're just the mortal who decided to ape everybody's shit at once.<br /> <br /> I could have sworn I explained all of this before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:49:02-07:00","id":564829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564736#post564736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well maybe <i>you</i> should be more clear about their purposeful murkiness. We don't need ambiguity mucking up the concrete, definitive list of uncontradictory bullet points that define the WoD.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, I don't think you're going to get Rater to understand where you're coming and what you're trying to say unless you're agreeing with him. Those heels be dug in hard, and it seems like the only thing that will change his mind is putting the words &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot; back in, and removing &quot;Devouring&quot; and &quot;Horror&quot;. Since that's unlikely to happen, what is to be gained here?<br /> <br /> I'm hijacking this argument to talk about dancing. Specifically, what would you guys do to define a Hunger for Disco Fever? Like, what would a Satiety 10 act of funkalicious grooving look like? And what would a good Family/Hunger for this Jive Titan to be possessed of?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that my heals are dug in.<br /> <br /> It's that those two changes are completely unnecessary and utterly murder the game.<br /> <br /> &quot;Guy who had his soul ripped out and let a monster crawl inside just so he could join a club&quot; Is not the game we were promised by all of those previews.<br /> <br /> Nor did those previews promise us a game about &quot;Being culturally mandated to go out and scare the shit out of mortals, probably hurting them in the process, in order to &quot;teach them lesson.&quot;&quot;<br /> <br /> The previews promised us a game about being the older brother in a ancient family, feeding, and about exploring the world of darkness to learn more about yourself and your family.<br /> <br /> The two changes, the two, huge, unnecessary changes, the only two things I complained about, kill that game dead.<br /> <br /> Put back homecoming and the Soul, and so far we've got a really good WoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:59:20-07:00","id":564834,"title":"","content":"I don't know that I'd go so far but the choosing to be eaten and the (more or less) official move that another Beast does it is not as evocative a choice as the original narrative. I also think the whole wisdom / lesson teaching angle is a little weak sauce. I could see teaching a lesson with regards to the Beast is the matriarch / patriarch and humans need to remember their place in the greater scheme of things but &quot;because Wisdom&quot; is a little too deus ex machina...it's thematically languid. Begs the question of who died and left Beasts in charge of that activity.<br /> <br /> Of course the whole notion of family is still underdeveloped. While I get that Horrors consuming / replacing the Beast-to-be's soul makes her non-human it completely begs the question of what happens with her relationships to her all to human relatives. Where does her mother fit in her narrative? What about her siblings? What about her children?<br /> <br /> Forestalling the whole &quot;there's not enough page count argument&quot; the entire ephemeral beings section of the book actually serves no purpose in the Beast context, using 2 or 3 pages to account for the mortal side of the family still leaves plenty of page count left for other things,<br /> <br /> Like, what about the entire obligation factor of family relationships? Really, the family aspect really needs some additional development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:50:03-07:00","id":564879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unnecessary changes that take the game away from the game that was promised are not a problem?.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, but then your complaints have never been particularly good.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast culture is supposedly about Beasts teaching people lessons through fear.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have to do this horrible thing, to teach you a lesson&quot; is the justification given for like, half of all domestic abusers.<br /> <br /> And since teaching lessons is apparently the cornerstone of Beast culture, presumably the majority of Beasts are going to be doing it.<br /> <br /> And when the majority of a population is doing one thing, and that one thing is the cornerstone of their culture, then anyone in the culture who does not like it is at best looked down on an at worst prosecuted. That is a fact that is backed by historical evidence.<br /> <br /> When my only two options are &quot;Abuser&quot; and &quot;Guy who get's looked down on or prosecuted because he doen'st want to be an asshole&quot;, I consider myself to not have enough options.<br /> <br /> Beasts are, culturally, encouraged to be abusers now.</div> </div> </div> </div> And you're wrong. The update explicitly points out that Beasts are not required to abuse or the like. Hell they don't even have to do anything outside of stuff normal people might be commended for doing. Lawyer, cop, school administrator, health inspector, person attempting to get a promotion at work. All viable, all acceptable, none require becoming an abuser, and yes there are other bloody jobs one can take that would allow one to teach lessons without becoming an abusive git.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So where are all the people who were bitching about &quot;All Beasts are abusers&quot; back when it wasn't culturally mandatory? Why are they not complaining about it now, since it's actually a legitimate critism now?</div> </div> </div> </div> Originally Beasts had no purpose there was no point to anything a Beast did outside of its own self satisfaction. This meant that a Beasts feeding was just done to keep the inner horror under control, or because feeding was enjoyed. Keeping the Horror under control was therefore primarily done because it going on a rampage increased the odds of a Hero being created drastically. Meaning feeding was primarily done to avoid consequences for feeding because you had to feed.<br /> <br /> This cultural mandate you keep whining about is asinine. Essentially when a Beast comes into its own it is told to teach. After that there is no restriction that forces it outside of other Beasts, who view the idea as a debate on pragmatism mixed with philosophy. Which also means the ramifications will change from region to region.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think since, with this update making it quite explicit that a Horror is an entity separate from the original, the Beasts are pod people criticism is more valid.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. Especially since there's the whole question on what causes a Beast to become the particular Beast they are. Beasts are described as feeling more whole after the Devouring, facing oblivion and accepting yourself, becoming the Nightmare. Sounds more like coming into your own than being swapped out. As in you stop viewing the incomplete fragments you have that you deemed a soul were just the human parts of the rest and the Devouring is when it all comes back together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, you ignored my third argument: A Best is no longer part of a family.<br /> <br /> A BEast is now somebody who just so happened to have weird dreams up until he got invited to or forced to join a club, and some of them just so happen to have deluded themselves into thinking they were always part of the club.<br /> <br /> That right there utterly murders Beasts selling point-you're not family anymore, you're just the mortal who decided to ape everybody's shit at once.<br /> <br /> I could have sworn I explained all of this before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is wrong. After you've had your Devouring you're part of the family, you're accepted into it. They're things from the Primordial Dream who are pretty sure they descend from something called the Dark Mother. Whether or not they would have called you family before you really came into your own isn't stated, but then they never said you were treated as kin by others before you had the Homecoming either.<br /> And no you've not stated these things. Most of the time you just moan about how they changed it and now it sucks, or whined about how you can't do anything due to utterly absurd restrictions, and argued that anything that directly contradicts your interpretations doesn't count.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:06:59-07:00","id":564916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I have to do this horrible thing, to teach you a lesson&quot; is the justification given for like, half of all domestic abusers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cart before horse. &quot;I have to do something that is to some degree accepted to be horrible regardless, so I may as well try to channel that horrible-thing-doing to constructive ends by ensuring that one or more other people learn from it&quot; is not the thought process of an abuser, it's the thought process of the people who are responsible for there being warning signs around dangerous places and pamphlets on Avoiding A Repeat Of This Horrible Tragic Occurrence.<br /> <br /> That failing to do this in favor of murdering people for possessions, transgressions, positions or prominence without even the pretense of a greater point is one of the few things that consistently tends to lead to Begotten censure is kind of the exact opposite of a mark in favor of the argument that the culture of the Family supports abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:13:05-07:00","id":564921,"title":"","content":"The Views From Without are pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, having fully read the new text now, I have to say that overall it feels too rushed and doesn't mesh well with itself. There's pages of going on about Wisdom and teaching through fear being their purpose and such and then you get this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Teaching a lesson through terror is, to most people, morally reprehensible...but<br /> Beasts are not people. They use lessons to give context and purpose to their feeding <br /> practices. <b>If Beasts are honest, they admit they use the concept of \u201clessons\u201d to make <br /> what they do more palatable.</b> Some Beasts rail at that notion, claiming divine <br /> purpose. Others try to make the lessons matter, to improve humanity \u2014 whether <br /> the Dark Mother charges them with it or not, it\u2019s a noble pursuit. Still others shrug, <br /> cast off even the ideas of a higher calling, and feast.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that Rater is being a bit more strident and interpreting things more narrowly than I would, but they've also raised some pretty valid points. Not every person who's said something to the effect of &quot;I'm doing this for your own good&quot; is an abuser, but nearly all abusive people have said or implied it at some point. The notions of kinship and family mesh badly with the idea of the Devouring, especially as it is presented in much of the text, and the mentions of self-realized Beasts <i>definitely</i> come across as almost certainly untrue.<br /> <br /> For that matter the original text had, and the updated version still has, a monster of a problem with consistency in re: to how it refers to the Soul/Horror (take your pick) and it's relation to the rest of the Beast. Depending on what paragraph you're reading it can be either the whole being is one unified constant, or it might treat the Soul as though it's a completely separate entity that just happens to be barely leashed to your hindbrain. The Lair suffers the same issues, being either an extended part of the Beast's Soul or just a hunk of the Primordial Dream that you liked and moved into.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think the game needs to take a step back and regroup. Trying to scramble something together to quickly patch the holes is only going to cause more issues, and ultimately I think they can do better than this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:34:29-07:00","id":564928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564817#post564817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I have to do this horrible thing, to teach you a lesson&quot; is the justification given for like, half of all domestic abusers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game isn't saying that's a morally correct thing to do though - they're saying it's part of the nature of the psychological horror that these Jungian monsters represent. The Vampire ideologies are pretty fucked up and abusive too, also built around justifying their need to feed - it's the nature of their monstrosity. What Demons do to people to maintain their Cover is absolutely horrific, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:50:09-07:00","id":564994,"title":"","content":"Well, gone through the Chapter 1 and 2 revisions. I like much of what was added and expanded upon, like the additional material on the Primordial Dream. A lot of The View From Without sidebars are actually fantastic. I am relieved the nature of the Begotten hasn't really changed and that the Devouring has retained the spirit of the Homecoming for the most part, unlike what the revised Introduction seemed to suggest. But the devil (or the Horror, so to speak) is in the details.<br /> <br /> I seriously do not follow how the most common way of undergoing the Devouring (that one may come face to face with their Horror and finally realize it is them) involves another Beast inflicting a nightmare on the Begotten-to-be that is not their own and feasting on what is left of their human soulstuff, rather than the Beast's own Horror performing that act, tormenting and killing the dreamer one final time as they become the monster. I'm aware many details are intentionally murky to allow interpretation and supposition, but I don't get why the event is so commonly induced by another Beast and their Horror as opposed to the nascent Beast's own.<br /> <br /> The teaching through fear angle has an interesting place between intended ancient byproduct of how the predations of Beasts affect humans, and culturally encouraged prerogrative, giving a focus to their Hunger not to justify it, but to make something positive of it. And I do like it, particularly when it is explained in the context of what the Primordial Dream is and how important it was for the early survival and progression of mankind. But the topic feels a bit clumsy in how it's presented. I'm not even sure why, it's just the feeling I get from my reading.<br /> <br /> The new Ugallu birthright is good though. I think it captures their role as nightmares of exposure better, and has more potential in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-23-2015, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:58:19-07:00","id":564998,"title":"","content":"Wow, People kept talking up the View from Without sections and they were right. they really helped the idea of the 'wisdom' gel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T22:24:53-07:00","id":565005,"title":"","content":"I think it feels clumsy because we went from text that took months to prepare and had a laser like focus to a revision that was done in about a week. I consider the revision to be before final editing and the original preview as a final draft. Obviously, they would seem a bit out of balance. I think the main point of previewing the revision is to make sure their intent actually comes across this time. The last thing they would want to do is miss again. They might ask the backers to vote on delaying the book a little to tidy it up some more. It is a tough spot. Business concerns have to be taken into consideration. I wasn't worried about the details getting it right. Introductions are never very clear. I say have a little faith everyone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:25:12-07:00","id":565055,"title":"","content":"Dear Matt: you have hit the bullseye.<br /> AWESOME.<br /> I first disliked some revision, but now i LOVE THEM.<br /> Very very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:44:55-07:00","id":565061,"title":"","content":"I too like the new Ugallu Birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:56:55-07:00","id":565066,"title":"","content":"I too love the Views from Without sections. They actually make Beasts feel like they hang around other Supernaturals. It's more show than tell, unlike before.<br /> <br /> But I'd have to love these changes anyway, because Matt changed the part about the Oneiros' interaction with dreams that I pointed out a while ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T01:18:26-07:00","id":565088,"title":"","content":"I'm slightly positive after few pages readied when Eshmaki become Nightmares of Darkness now, instead of Destruction they were before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T05:35:39-07:00","id":565260,"title":"","content":"Just adding my voice to the &quot;I really enjoy the revisions&quot; to Beast: The Primordial. I would have been perfectly fine with the Beasts being portrayed as slightly more dark of course... I feel like Matt may haver over corrected slightly, but then again he wrote this all in the flurry of a weak and can revise it to tighten things down further.<br /> <br /> That being said, I want to give the product tremendous praise over all..<br /> <br /> In particular, my problems with Heroes have been addressed, and I understand them much better now. They've been turned into tragic compelling Anatagonists that yet also do DESERVE to be taught a &quot;Lesson&quot; by our Beasts, even if it's a fatal one. Gone is the strange nonsensical dichotomy from before, and in it's place, a set of Antagonists I can really get behind and vary from being tragic, to being the enemy my Players will REALLY want to take down.<br /> <br /> The interactions between the Supernatural are also much better and have changed my mine from not wanting someone to play a Beast in my games to welcoming a player who doesn't mind playing a Beast in one of my other Wod campaigns.<br /> <br /> Overall excellent improvements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T05:46:53-07:00","id":565266,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who &quot;got it&quot; in the first draft, the main thing I like is that it really feels like it has a new dimension and angle. It's still what I knew and came to love, but it has more vectors and an added heart. It feels more...dichotomous, I suppose is a good word to use in a good way. There's a new tug in the o'war going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:08:56-07:00","id":565289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564928#post564928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game isn't saying that's a morally correct thing to do though - they're saying it's part of the nature of the psychological horror that these Jungian monsters represent. The Vampire ideologies are pretty fucked up and abusive too, also built around justifying their need to feed - it's the nature of their monstrosity. What Demons do to people to maintain their Cover is absolutely horrific, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is, Vampires have mortals to keep them in line. Violate the Masquerade to much and there is a lot of burninatin' going on. Beast's don't fear the man the same way. There's nothing to keep them from consuming the whole world besides the deus ex machina of &quot;lessons&quot; and &quot;wisdom&quot; and the very weak sauce threat of Heroes. This is pretty much the first supernatural with no incentive to hide it's true nature from humanity, which begs a lot of questions about how the whole metastory won't instantly devolve into open warfare between humans and Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:11:36-07:00","id":565303,"title":"","content":"One hero isn't much of a threat. Six dozen and an angry mob of normal humans probably are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:23:08-07:00","id":565326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565289#post565289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty much the first supernatural with no incentive to hide it's true nature from humanity, which begs a lot of questions about how the whole metastory won't instantly devolve into open warfare between humans and Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call them the first. Sin-Eaters have no real reason to keep hidden either, and Mummies? There is a reason why the World War Mummy threads came about. Mummies have little reason to keep hidden and their powers are so over the top they pretty much can't.<br /> Dragonfire is pretty obvious, but compared to how Masquerade wrecking a meteor shower or earthquake are it's nothing to write home about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:42:39-07:00","id":565346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565303#post565303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One hero isn't much of a threat. Six dozen and an angry mob of normal humans probably are.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that a Promethean style mob is the answer here. The monomyth is typically about a lone hero, or perhaps a modern variant where we have a hero party (ala D&amp;D or other fantasy games) of four or five. Thematically, Heroes should be a threat on their own. If they're not, then that is an issue with the mechanics. <br /> <br /> I think we need to look at things through the scope of the new, deadlier combat system, and weapons that do heavy damage at a single hit. Violence is the answer, not an epic battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-23-2015, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:51:22-07:00","id":565349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565326#post565326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call them the first. Sin-Eaters have no real reason to keep hidden either, and Mummies? There is a reason why the World War Mummy threads came about. Mummies have little reason to keep hidden and their powers are so over the top they pretty much can't.<br /> Dragonfire is pretty obvious, but compared to how Masquerade wrecking a meteor shower or earthquake are it's nothing to write home about.</div> </div> </div> </div>. This is true. Staying hidden is basically just an assumption at this point. Other than the fact that, even if you dismiss hereos, regular hunters are still a threat. <br /> <br /> The threat of losing your daily life alone is worrisome enough to suggest staying hidden. Who wants that level of media attention when you occasionally get the Hunger to take someone's life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:55:18-07:00","id":565355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565326#post565326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call them the first. Sin-Eaters have no real reason to keep hidden either, and Mummies? There is a reason why the World War Mummy threads came about. Mummies have little reason to keep hidden and their powers are so over the top they pretty much can't.<br /> Dragonfire is pretty obvious, but compared to how Masquerade wrecking a meteor shower or earthquake are it's nothing to write home about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. It's been a problem in many of the more recent game lines. The developers keep forgetting to ask questions about the consequences. What happens if people find out? What incentives are there to cling to the shadows? What incentives are there not to just be a psycho?<br /> <br /> I think where Beast's fit into the world needs to be better addressed before they can really give a good treatment of concepts like Family and being crossover friendly.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 2nd ed versions of Geist and Mummy will address the &quot;superheroes&quot; problems that both game lines have. Mummy should be a relatively simple fix. The Judges are already a built-in deus ex machina, and a more compelling one than &quot;because wisdom&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:58:10-07:00","id":565358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565349#post565349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. This is true. Staying hidden is basically just an assumption at this point. Other than the fact that, even if you dismiss hereos, regular hunters are still a threat.<br /> <br /> The threat of losing your daily life alone is worrisome enough to suggest staying hidden. Who wants that level of media attention when you occasionally get the Hunger to take someone's life?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is nice in theory but it simply doesn't work out in the reality of RPG game play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:08:23-07:00","id":565365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565346#post565346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think that a Promethean style mob is the answer here. The monomyth is typically about a lone hero, or perhaps a modern variant where we have a hero party (ala D&amp;D or other fantasy games) of four or five. Thematically, Heroes should be a threat on their own. If they're not, then that is an issue with the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I think we need to look at things through the scope of the new, deadlier combat system, and weapons that do heavy damage at a single hit. Violence is the answer, not an epic battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One problem is that the monomyth is a story-telling structure that operates best for small cultures. It really doesn't scale very well to today's highly integrated, highly social, highly globalized world. Pretty much every Hero should be bringing an army (unless Heroes are essentially imbeciles which then begs the question of how they could ever be a threat). Numbers always win (unless someone has nukes). The developers need to think through the logical consequences or we're likely to end up with a game that will be on par with some of the most universally reviled things out there, like the Prequels. <br /> <br /> Demon, Vampire, and Werewolf have set the bar for quality for nWoD 2nd ed. I'd like to see this game at least approximate those. Serious engagement with questions about what happens when mortals find out about Beasts needs to be addressed. How do Beasts hide themselves from the masses? Who enforces the whole &quot;we do what we do to teach humans lessons&quot; schtick? What are the consequences for not teaching lessons and just acting like a Beast? If hunters and heroes are the foils, then they need some history that describes why Beasts should fear them. <br /> <br /> This is a game with a lot of potential but it still has a rather long road of development work to go. The revised chapters need yet more revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:16:33-07:00","id":565371,"title":"","content":"We haven't seen the Hero section yet. Maybe they got buffed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:29:34-07:00","id":565383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565365#post565365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem is that the monomyth is a story-telling structure that operates best for small cultures. It really doesn't scale very well to today's highly integrated, highly social, highly globalized world. Pretty much every Hero should be bringing an army (unless Heroes are essentially imbeciles which then begs the question of how they could ever be a threat).</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that goes against the very themes. You can argue that the monomyth hasn't scaled well, but that doesn't change that heroes are described in the book as lone gunmen or commandos. Don't forget that they're there for personal glory. Its how the game is devised.<br /> <br /> That's putting aside that we have times in the real world about a lone or pair of criminals with the right equipment and training taking on the police and casually walking down the street after a bank robbery, no concern of being caught... and getting away. Surprise, shock and awe tactics, and having the right equipment does let small groups of people overcome the more powerful. If anything, the technology is making it EASIER to pull off these kinds of attacks in reality. <br /> <br /> Plus, we're dealing with a fantasy story here. We're already involved with creatures with fantastical powers. Why should people gifted with the power of heroes to slay monsters on their own suddenly be unrealistic in the face of <i>playing as a dragon that can turn an apartment complex in New York into part of a volcano?!</i> <br /> <br /> Heroes might be slightly underpowered compared to their nemesis, but they do have magic to back them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Numbers always win (unless someone has nukes). The developers need to think through the logical consequences or we're likely to end up with a game that will be on par with some of the most universally reviled things out there, like the Prequels. </div> </div> </div> Actually, with how combat and supernatural powers work in 2e, mobs are actually less of a threat to magic defenses than they were in the past. You need banes (or anathema, which is effectively the same thing) to win against powerful supers. Or supernatural powers of your own.<br /> <br /> That's one of the things that separate magic from technology - where technology increases the power of the whole, magic is entirely based on making the individual more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:29:36-07:00","id":565384,"title":"","content":"Once again I feel the need to point out that supplement books exist for a reason. I'm nagging, I know, but that's a side of me that comes out when I'm frustrated. Not pointing fingers specifically but yeah, this thread can be quite exhausting at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:42:41-07:00","id":565396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565355#post565355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. It's been a problem in many of the more recent game lines. The developers keep forgetting to ask questions about the consequences. What happens if people find out? What incentives are there to cling to the shadows? What incentives are there not to just be a psycho?<br /> <br /> I think where Beast's fit into the world needs to be better addressed before they can really give a good treatment of concepts like Family and being crossover friendly.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 2nd ed versions of Geist and Mummy will address the &quot;superheroes&quot; problems that both game lines have. Mummy should be a relatively simple fix. The Judges are already a built-in deus ex machina, and a more compelling one than &quot;because wisdom&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers shouldn't need to peel the apple, slice it, and feed it to you. They and the writers really ask every question they <i>need</i> to. The rest is not up to them. It's up to the players and the ST. We don't need to have them go on about the logical consequences of monsters humanity has already largely objectified as evil being revealed as something real. I'd rather they assume their players have brains and can think about things, than write their books under the idea that we can't understand why it should be a bad idea to destroy a public plaza with supernatural powers in broad daylight, so they should spell out every little possible backlash from that for us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565358#post565358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is nice in theory but it simply doesn't work out in the reality of RPG game play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow. The perspective MCN mentioned is something you <i>cannot separate from play</i> because of the nature of Beast and every WoD game as a character-driven game, whether your Beast is someone who cares for their human life, or doesn't. If you ignore the in-character, in-setting reasoning for things, you're doing it wrong. We really shouldn't need to add unnecessary mechanics or anything to strongly encourage players to not go nuts - that's putting the cart before the horse and treating them like they can't understand narrative consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565365#post565365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon, Vampire, and Werewolf have set the bar for quality for nWoD 2nd ed. I'd like to see this game at least approximate those. Serious engagement with questions about what happens when mortals find out about Beasts needs to be addressed. How do Beasts hide themselves from the masses? Who enforces the whole &quot;we do what we do to teach humans lessons&quot; schtick? What are the consequences for not teaching lessons and just acting like a Beast? If hunters and heroes are the foils, then they need some history that describes why Beasts should fear them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The self-policing (and lack thereof) of Beasts <i>is </i>discussed in the book already, so are the reasons why many do stick to the idea of teaching through fear rather than only feasting, and we're given substantial implications why Beasts have interest in remaining hidden (aside from the implicit fact that you know, many other supernaturals would probably not like Beasts drawing so much attention themselves). Also see my points above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-23-2015, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:57:00-07:00","id":565409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565365#post565365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem is that the monomyth is a story-telling structure that operates best for small cultures. It really doesn't scale very well to today's highly integrated, highly social, highly globalized world. Pretty much every Hero should be bringing an army (unless Heroes are essentially imbeciles which then begs the question of how they could ever be a threat). Numbers always win (unless someone has nukes). The developers need to think through the logical consequences or we're likely to end up with a game that will be on par with some of the most universally reviled things out there, like the Prequels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Massachusetts the only place with seemingly-abandoned factories and small towns which are basically run by small groups of people everyone hates (but can't organize an effective campaign against)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:13:20-07:00","id":565423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565355#post565355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True. It's been a problem in many of the more recent game lines. The developers keep forgetting to ask questions about the consequences. What happens if people find out? What incentives are there to cling to the shadows? What incentives are there not to just be a psycho?<br /> <br /> I think where Beast's fit into the world needs to be better addressed before they can really give a good treatment of concepts like Family and being crossover friendly.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 2nd ed versions of Geist and Mummy will address the &quot;superheroes&quot; problems that both game lines have. Mummy should be a relatively simple fix. The Judges are already a built-in deus ex machina, and a more compelling one than &quot;because wisdom&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think I would like a whole entire section detailing the consequences of what would happen if you revealed yourself to the world especially because we already have those consequence already in the core book and with a lot of supplements their called hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:49:44-07:00","id":565449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565358#post565358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is nice in theory but it simply doesn't work out in the reality of RPG game play.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players are constantly worried about the threat of exposure. In fact, I can't think of a WoD game I've been involved in in the past several years that didn't have at least one paranoia-bro enforcing silence of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 06-23-2015, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:54:31-07:00","id":565452,"title":"","content":"Plus, in a lot of ways, the non-exposure stuff is innate, not a social punishment. In vampire, we have the whole Lost Visage and the mind altering Kiss. In Werewolf, Lunacy takes care of it. Mages have to be cautious, because paradox and disbelief (assuming they remain roughly the same). Prometheans know that'd be courting Disquiet attacks. Changelings don't want to paint Huntsman targets on their back. Hunters know that they would suffer from retaliatory attacks from those they hunt. Sin-Eaters already suffer major annoyance from ghosts, plus the voice in their head not liking it. Mummies inflict their fear/cult recruitment mind warping thing from exposure. Demons fear the God Machine. <br /> <br /> It might not be spelled out explicitly, but secrecy is bred into the nature of supernaturals. You really could get rid of all social consequences, and they would stay hidden, just because its what they're made to be. It takes deliberate, concerted effort to be exposed as something more, and even then, its often self correcting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:21:11-07:00","id":565513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565365#post565365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One problem is that the monomyth is a story-telling structure that operates best for small cultures. It really doesn't scale very well to today's highly integrated, highly social, highly globalized world. Pretty much every Hero should be bringing an army (unless Heroes are essentially imbeciles which then begs the question of how they could ever be a threat). <b>Numbers always win (unless someone has nukes).</b> The developers need to think through the logical consequences or we're likely to end up with a game that will be on par with some of the most universally reviled things out there, like the Prequels.<br /> <br /> Demon, Vampire, and Werewolf have set the bar for quality for nWoD 2nd ed. I'd like to see this game at least approximate those. Serious engagement with questions about what happens when mortals find out about Beasts needs to be addressed. How do Beasts hide themselves from the masses? Who enforces the whole &quot;we do what we do to teach humans lessons&quot; schtick? What are the consequences for not teaching lessons and just acting like a Beast? If hunters and heroes are the foils, then they need some history that describes why Beasts should fear them.<br /> <br /> This is a game with a lot of potential but it still has a rather long road of development work to go. The revised chapters need yet more revisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have 75 years and counting of World History that says you're wrong there. It would be more accurate to say that will to fight and something to fight over are what always wins. And, as I have pointed out before on this thread, you only throw a Hero at the Troupe when it's dramatically apropos, and you adjust the Hero's power level accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:34:07-07:00","id":565519,"title":"","content":"Glaring error in the Introduction revision: Hannibal tv series not added. Especially with the addition of &quot;lessons&quot;. The whole show is a case study of an elder Beast attempting to cultivate an equal, or, perhaps in Will's case, to redeem a Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:48:56-07:00","id":565543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565519#post565519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glaring error in the Introduction revision: Hannibal tv series not added. Especially with the addition of &quot;lessons&quot;. The whole show is a case study of an elder Beast attempting to cultivate an equal, or, perhaps in Will's case, to redeem a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen Hannibal as a Beast archetype for quite a while now; had settled on a Namtaru Tyrant- thanks to the inherent revulsion that comes with the cannibalism taboo. The Wendigo, of course, strides into prominence as his Horror <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:11:54-07:00","id":565603,"title":"","content":"For those that question the whole 'teaching through fear thing', it was recently pointed out to me (completely unrelatedly) that the word monster actually come from the latin <i>mon</i>, which means 'to warn'. Monsters and teaching through fear have literally always been connected to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:43:06-07:00","id":565633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565383#post565383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that goes against the very themes. You can argue that the monomyth hasn't scaled well, but that doesn't change that heroes are described in the book as lone gunmen or commandos. Don't forget that they're there for personal glory. Its how the game is devised.<br /> <br /> That's putting aside that we have times in the real world about a lone or pair of criminals with the right equipment and training taking on the police and casually walking down the street after a bank robbery, no concern of being caught... and getting away. Surprise, shock and awe tactics, and having the right equipment does let small groups of people overcome the more powerful. If anything, the technology is making it EASIER to pull off these kinds of attacks in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a short time period yes, but ultimately no. No one publically beats the police for long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565383#post565383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plus, we're dealing with a fantasy story here. We're already involved with creatures with fantastical powers. Why should people gifted with the power of heroes to slay monsters on their own suddenly be unrealistic in the face of <i>playing as a dragon that can turn an apartment complex in New York into part of a volcano?!</i><br /> <br /> Heroes might be slightly underpowered compared to their nemesis, but they do have magic to back them up.<br /> <br /> Actually, with how combat and supernatural powers work in 2e, mobs are actually less of a threat to magic defenses than they were in the past. You need banes (or anathema, which is effectively the same thing) to win against powerful supers. Or supernatural powers of your own.<br /> <br /> That's one of the things that separate magic from technology - where technology increases the power of the whole, magic is entirely based on making the individual more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that this is a bigger problem but I don't have to use the quick and dirty combat rules. Also there are mortals that do have supernatural connections. While the game is being heavily touted as being cross-over friendly I'm having a hard time not seeing how Beasts won't end up as antagonists to Vampires, Werewolves and Demons all of whom have some pretty strong mortal connections through touchstones, wolf-blooded / mortal pack members, and covers. I'm trying to figure out why Beasts would be accepted as family by these groups because the benefits don't seem to outweigh the detriments...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:47:04-07:00","id":565641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565513#post565513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have 75 years and counting of World History that says you're wrong there. It would be more accurate to say that will to fight and something to fight over are what always wins. And, as I have pointed out before on this thread, you only throw a Hero at the Troupe when it's dramatically apropos, and you adjust the Hero's power level accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll give you that will to fight thing.<br /> <br /> Question though, what other story seeds are there other than Heroes or Crossovers or other Beasts (who couldn't really be said to have a society)? Consuming mortals that have it coming doesn't sound very challenging at all. Notions of family and primordial dream are underdeveloped...I'm digging for additional story hooks. Mortal family is an obvious one. Other things that live in the Primordial Dream is another. They can easily fit in place of certain patches of copy-paste-a text...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:48:22-07:00","id":565643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565449#post565449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My players are constantly worried about the threat of exposure. In fact, I can't think of a WoD game I've been involved in in the past several years that didn't have at least one paranoia-bro enforcing silence of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I'm digging for is -- are Beast's worried about exposure? If not, why not? (Because it seems like everyone else is.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:50:06-07:00","id":565645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565423#post565423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think I would like a whole entire section detailing the consequences of what would happen if you revealed yourself to the world especially because we already have those consequence already in the core book and with a lot of supplements their called hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not arguing for a whole section. One to four sentences would do it. I get that they don't have a Masquerade...<br /> <br /> Why aren't they worried about exposure? Is this game going to be a Werewolf: the Apocalypse furry superhero game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:51:05-07:00","id":565648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565409#post565409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Massachusetts the only place with seemingly-abandoned factories and small towns which are basically run by small groups of people everyone hates (but can't organize an effective campaign against)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes but groups so... (not even close to monomyth right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:55:01-07:00","id":565650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565645#post565645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not arguing for a whole section. One to four sentences would do it. I get that they don't have a Masquerade...<br /> <br /> Why aren't they worried about exposure? Is this game going to be a Werewolf: the Apocalypse furry superhero game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe part of it's to do with how much less overt the Beasts are; like, sure there are Atavisms, but they don't properly show through.<br /> <br /> Harder to prove that Steve from down the road is a mythic monster beast, when there's less obvious signs and even Anathema don't kick in normally. the Mortal Remains chapter will go a long way to helping solidify this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:59:11-07:00","id":565675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565396#post565396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The developers shouldn't need to peel the apple, slice it, and feed it to you. They and the writers really ask every question they <i>need</i> to. The rest is not up to them. It's up to the players and the ST. We don't need to have them go on about the logical consequences of monsters humanity has already largely objectified as evil being revealed as something real. I'd rather they assume their players have brains and can think about things, than write their books under the idea that we can't understand why it should be a bad idea to destroy a public plaza with supernatural powers in broad daylight, so they should spell out every little possible backlash from that for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's simple. More story hooks = better game. Very simple. Right now this game is kinda one note (two notes at best).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565396#post565396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow. The perspective MCN mentioned is something you <i>cannot separate from play</i> because of the nature of Beast and every WoD game as a character-driven game, whether your Beast is someone who cares for their human life, or doesn't. If you ignore the in-character, in-setting reasoning for things, you're doing it wrong. We really shouldn't need to add unnecessary mechanics or anything to strongly encourage players to not go nuts - that's putting the cart before the horse and treating them like they can't understand narrative consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>YMMV. Right now there is no setting because the game hasn't been published yet. I'm asking for additional tools. These things really don't take up much space. Just look at the Ghoul and Stigmatic rules in Vampire and Demon. That's 2~4 pages total. I'm not asking for much at all. Yet I can get so much mileage out of so little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565396#post565396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The self-policing (and lack thereof) of Beasts <i>is </i>discussed in the book already, so are the reasons why many do stick to the idea of teaching through fear rather than only feasting, and we're given substantial implications why Beasts have interest in remaining hidden (aside from the implicit fact that you know, many other supernaturals would probably not like Beasts drawing so much attention themselves). Also see my points above.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could eliminate paradox from mage and the masquerade from vampire and see how it alters the game. As a storyteller I'm looking for sufficient tools to avoid a world war z scenario. nWoD is supposed to be a dark interpretation of our world not some post-apocalyptic dystopia. <br /> <br /> Also your point about other supernaturals is well taken but begs the question of how crossover is supposed to work...<br /> <br /> I also not sold on how a Changeling crossover would work...Beast heads look so good over the mantle and all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:59:27-07:00","id":565676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565519#post565519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glaring error in the Introduction revision: Hannibal tv series not added. Especially with the addition of &quot;lessons&quot;. The whole show is a case study of an elder Beast attempting to cultivate an equal, or, perhaps in Will's case, to redeem a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, Will's too nuanced a character to be a Hero - he's a Hunter (actually his abilities are pretty straight-up Teleinformation) who is a potential Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:01:30-07:00","id":565679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565384#post565384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again I feel the need to point out that supplement books exist for a reason. I'm nagging, I know, but that's a side of me that comes out when I'm frustrated. Not pointing fingers specifically but yeah, this thread can be quite exhausting at times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I got that the first time. The copy/pasted spirit rules still don't contribute to the text though... Devouring / hunting spirits is not a Beast past-time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:03:14-07:00","id":565680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565650#post565650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe part of it's to do with how much less overt the Beasts are; like, sure there are Atavisms, but they don't properly show through.<br /> <br /> Harder to prove that Steve from down the road is a mythic monster beast, when there's less obvious signs and even Anathema don't kick in normally. the Mortal Remains chapter will go a long way to helping solidify this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah...but I'm not buying mortal remains so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:14:11-07:00","id":565689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565679#post565679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, I got that the first time. The copy/pasted spirit rules still don't contribute to the text though... Devouring / hunting spirits is not a Beast past-time...</div> </div> </div> </div>How...how is that related to the fact that we are getting a more detailed insight of Beast's mentality, their place in the world and all sorts of other stuff in supplements? That's a non sequitur if I ever saw one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565680#post565680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah...but I'm not buying mortal remains so...</div> </div> </div> </div>But you'll still get the Beast chapter for free if you pledged for a reward tier including a Beast PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:15:08-07:00","id":565690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565633#post565633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a short time period yes, but ultimately no. No one publically beats the police for long.</div> </div> </div> </div> The long term existence of organized crime begs to differ. As well, a single Beast can produce more than one Hero - and the heroes just need to win once. The Beast needs to survive every single time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that this is a bigger problem but I don't have to use the quick and dirty combat rules. Also there are mortals that do have supernatural connections. </div> </div> </div> This has nothing to do with Q&amp;D combat. This has to do with the fact that supernaturals are powerful against random mobs of mortals pure mortals. Vampires, wolves, and demons all have very good defenses in the face of groups of mortal antagonists. In the past, combat was grossly weighed to the mob; not so much in 2e. Ancillae-level gangrel are exceedingly terrifying in the current edition. A werewolf in Garou form alone can handle several mortals without dying; they just can't gather enough damage to kill it in one turn, and that's before we start bringing in Gifts to really make it a lopsided slaughter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the game is being heavily touted as being cross-over friendly I'm having a hard time not seeing how Beasts won't end up as antagonists to Vampires, Werewolves and Demons all of whom have some pretty strong mortal connections through touchstones, wolf-blooded / mortal pack members, and covers. I'm trying to figure out why Beasts would be accepted as family by these groups because the benefits don't seem to outweigh the detriments... </div> </div> </div> 1) Because your average Beast isn't going around threatening those connections. In fact, they can often choose to target the vamp/wolf/demon's enemies to feed on. Mutual benefit. 2) They often will end up in conflict. That, too, is part of the game design. There's some benefit, some drawback, and there's a good chance of things going either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565641#post565641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question though, what other story seeds are there other than Heroes or Crossovers or other Beasts (who couldn't really be said to have a society)? Consuming mortals that have it coming doesn't sound very challenging at all. Notions of family and primordial dream are underdeveloped...I'm digging for additional story hooks. Mortal family is an obvious one. Other things that live in the Primordial Dream is another. They can easily fit in place of certain patches of copy-paste-a text...</div> </div> </div> </div> First, fighting heroes, dealing with supernaturals, and territorial fights between the Begotten are the main storyhooks; that's the main source of conflict in the game. Getting caught up in the other supers drama. Exploring the Astral is another. Expanding the Lair and building your mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565643#post565643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm digging for is -- are Beast's worried about exposure? If not, why not? (Because it seems like everyone else is.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, because it makes Heroes, and they're a pain in the ass. All you need is one to succeed, one slip up, and you're dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565648#post565648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but groups so... (not even close to monomyth right?)</div> </div> </div> </div> There's some changes, but lets be honest. The entire game is about <i>deconstructing</i> the monomyth. Its not a perfect recreation, nor is it meant to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565675#post565675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's simple. More story hooks = better game. Very simple. Right now this game is kinda one note (two notes at best).</div> </div> </div> </div> More like 12 notes. Heroes (and hunters), other Beasts, vamps, wolves, mages, prommies, changelings, sin-eaters, mummies, demons. Followed by astral stuff and building your Lair by scaring people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> YMMV. Right now there is no setting because the game hasn't been published yet. I'm asking for additional tools. These things really don't take up much space. Just look at the Ghoul and Stigmatic rules in Vampire and Demon. That's 2~4 pages total. I'm not asking for much at all. Yet I can get so much mileage out of so little. </div> </div> </div> The devs said it wasn't really thematic for mini-Beasts, which is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We could eliminate paradox from mage and the masquerade from vampire and see how it alters the game. As a storyteller I'm looking for sufficient tools to avoid a world war z scenario. nWoD is supposed to be a dark interpretation of our world not some post-apocalyptic dystopia. </div> </div> </div> Actually, that's a fun style game, explored in some Mirror shards. As it is, make heroes a constant threat to reinforce why its a bad idea. &quot;Mortals coming to kill us&quot; is generally a good answer. The fact most of their abilities are also invisible and can't be traced helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also your point about other supernaturals is well taken but begs the question of how crossover is supposed to work...<br /> <br /> I also not sold on how a Changeling crossover would work...Beast heads look so good over the mantle and all... </div> </div> </div> I think you're so sold on the idea that they must be enemies and automatically antagonistic, your'e missing the potential. Frankly, this is rather overly bloodthirsty. The game is written that most supernaturals don't see killing as the natural, or even best, response.<br /> <br /> The default assumption with crossover is &quot;wariness&quot; not &quot;OMG! Kill it!&quot; And Beasts tend to have a Good Impression, meaning most supers will be less wary than they normally would be as the Children naturally puts them at ease. From there, its all up to social manuevers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-23-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:27:44-07:00","id":565712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565679#post565679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I got that the first time. The copy/pasted spirit rules still don't contribute to the text though... Devouring / hunting spirits is not a Beast past-time...</div> </div> </div> </div> No, but helping and watching werewolves hunt down and devour spirits is a Beast past-time. Remember, they get two Satiety from the hunt and then the eating. Same with vamps and blood, mages and mysteries, changelings and emotions, demons and aether, Sin-eaters and plasm, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:30:21-07:00","id":565713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565675#post565675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's simple. More story hooks = better game. Very simple. Right now this game is kinda one note (two notes at best).<br /> <br /> YMMV. Right now there is no setting because the game hasn't been published yet. I'm asking for additional tools.<br /> (...)<br /> As a storyteller I'm looking for sufficient tools to avoid a world war z scenario. nWoD is supposed to be a dark interpretation of our world not some post-apocalyptic dystopia.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>You weren't asking for more tools, you were asking to be spoonfed details you could not bother to grasp, or that are in the prerogrative of the players and the ST to consider and logically take into account. And there is absolutely a setting already, with every incentive and self-sustaining impetus for the characters to not shatter the masquerade, and with every natural backlash to come from it at the disposal of the ST.<br /> <br /> I don't want to degrade this into an argument and continue with what may be us talking past each other though, so I'll bow out of the discussion now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-23-2015, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:55:05-07:00","id":565734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565648#post565648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes but groups so... (not even close to monomyth right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think struggles with groups cannot adhere to the monomyth? It's not a terribly restrictive pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:22:27-07:00","id":565753,"title":"","content":"Beasts have less to fear from exposure. When a Beast gets shot in the head, it falls down and doesn't get back up again. Beasts have a whole subset of powers that are only in a victim's mind. <br /> <br /> Yes, officer. My neighbor has been causing me to have nightmares for weeks now. Yesterday, he did it while I was awake during the day. He made me believe bugs were crawling all over me. What do you mean &quot;am I on any medication?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Atavisms are almost all subtle. You can see the effect but not the cause in most cases. Mortals don't get to see the tentacles that grab them. Even if any of a Beasts shenanigans were caught on video, people would assume it was a hoax. Beast supernatural powers are just not something an average person would believe even if they were there to witness it. They would say it was a trick. Video evidence would be even less credible.<br /> <br /> The only worry is a Beast going around purposefully trying to expose their supernatural nature. That is when the mages, vampires, and everyone else come in to deal with any credible witnesses <i>and</i> the Beast causing the problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:32:36-07:00","id":565758,"title":"","content":"*Flies around carrying a car whilst breathing fire*<br /> <br /> Subtle, you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:40:11-07:00","id":565763,"title":"","content":"You can see that in a movie. I bet a magician could pull it off too. I also said <i>most</i> of a Beast's powers were subtle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:55:49-07:00","id":565784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565758#post565758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Flies around carrying a car whilst breathing fire*<br /> <br /> Subtle, you say?</div> </div> </div> </div> If a player did this, I'd make a Hero or two automatically. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:59:07-07:00","id":565786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565641#post565641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll give you that will to fight thing.<br /> <br /> Question though, what other story seeds are there other than Heroes or Crossovers or other Beasts (who couldn't really be said to have a society)? Consuming mortals that have it coming doesn't sound very challenging at all. Notions of family and primordial dream are underdeveloped...I'm digging for additional story hooks. Mortal family is an obvious one. Other things that live in the Primordial Dream is another. They can easily fit in place of certain patches of copy-paste-a text...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always the &quot;Lost in the World Geometry&quot; angle, which is where I'm going with the Chronicle I'll be running. Dodgy Interplanar Travel mechanics FTW!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:36:09-07:00","id":565801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565645#post565645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not arguing for a whole section. One to four sentences would do it. I get that they don't have a Masquerade...<br /> <br /> Why aren't they worried about exposure? Is this game going to be a Werewolf: the Apocalypse furry superhero game?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's exposure and then there's <i>exposure</i>. When it comes to other Supes, with a few noted exceptions, being forthright but circumspect with whom Beast's trust the nature of their power is just good manners. There are only so many Vampires, Mages, or Werewolves you can bluff your way around until someone reads your mind or examines your Aura and decides whether to let you explain truthfully or just out &amp; out murder you.<br /> <br /> As for mortal exposure, your going to have your factions that take a &quot;Change'em all, and let the Dark Mother decide who's worthy&quot; approach, and then your going to have a more moderate majority that advocates secrecy, if not outright apartheid with mortals. And of course, you have rogue elements that treat their &quot;duty&quot; as justification to turn satisfying their Hunger into a criminal enterprise. The impetus exists precisely because there's no Masquerade to enforce, nor is their some metaphysical exploit that facilitates secrecy, beyond the separation from the Horror and psychosomatic nature of Nightmares. It's also a forgone conclusion that most Beasts burn down the lives they had before at the first available opportunity, to avoid hurting their family, if not to avoid the possibility of having to kill a blood relation, either to sate a Hunger, or to stop a Hero.<br /> <br /> And I doubt it would become a <i>furry superhero game</i> unless the ST designs it as such.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:39:09-07:00","id":565806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565784#post565784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a player did this, I'd make a Hero or two automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point when the ST forks over a suspiciously large amount of dice and through a too big smile says that that was awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:48:33-07:00","id":565815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565679#post565679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, I got that the first time. The copy/pasted spirit rules still don't contribute to the text though... Devouring / hunting spirits is not a Beast past-time...</div> </div> </div> </div>But buddying up with them and gatecrashing the Hisil can be. As can plumbing the depths of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:12:27-07:00","id":565832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565679#post565679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, I got that the first time. The copy/pasted spirit rules still don't contribute to the text though... Devouring / hunting spirits is not a Beast past-time...</div> </div> </div> </div> Says who? Not the book, it mentions that some beasts hunt in other worlds. <br /> <br /> Regardless, spirits are also kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:38:43-07:00","id":565852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565676#post565676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, Will's too nuanced a character to be a Hero - he's a Hunter (actually his abilities are pretty straight-up Teleinformation) who is a potential Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone has the Mind of a Madman merit...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:59:58-07:00","id":565902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565603#post565603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those that question the whole 'teaching through fear thing', it was recently pointed out to me (completely unrelatedly) that the word monster actually come from the latin <i>mon</i>, which means 'to warn'. Monsters and teaching through fear have literally always been connected to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This dovetails nicely with a point I'd been contemplating bringing up: <a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/118713990730/astronautcastiel-railehatesfun-the-hilarious\" target=\"_blank\">medieval bestiaries are super weird for a reason</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:35:06-07:00","id":565995,"title":"","content":"So, read the new chapters and I like what I've seen. The teaching angle still feels a bit tacked on (edit: in presentation not theme) but it's workable and I don't hate the idea of spontaneous Devourings. All in all this is something I could have fun with. Still a bit sour about the Homecoming thing but I can live with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:44:58-07:00","id":566013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=565902#post565902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This dovetails nicely with a point I'd been contemplating bringing up: <a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/118713990730/astronautcastiel-railehatesfun-the-hilarious\" target=\"_blank\">medieval bestiaries are super weird for a reason</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear god now I need to figure out how to do an atavism of boiling blood that can melt diamonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T21:41:39-07:00","id":566087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=566013#post566013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dear god now I need to figure out how to do an atavism of boiling blood that can melt diamonds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> .... I.... I just don't understand why they would think that about goats... they regularly killed and ate goats!<br /> <br /> Ok, maybe it was meant to be purely allegory and anyone who read it at the time would have understood that - but if so, what was it an allegory for?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T23:09:52-07:00","id":566143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=566087#post566087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> .... I.... I just don't understand why they would think that about goats... they regularly killed and ate goats!<br /> <br /> Ok, maybe it was meant to be purely allegory and anyone who read it at the time would have understood that - but if so, what was it an allegory for?!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't use goat blood as soap?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T00:06:47-07:00","id":566151,"title":"","content":"Read the two revised chapters. The good thing is that despite the changes it's still possible to play most concepts possible with the 1st version. That was a relief. Unfortunately, the lesson part still feel tacked on and not completely integrated with the rest, and the whole message at the moment of the Devouring feels wrong (who would like a message from Longinus at the time of the Embrace?), but it can be ignored without mechanical repercussions, so it's not too bad. The revised text sugest that the Devouring doesn't have to be catalyzed by another Beast; it would be nice if this was more firmly established.<br /> The revised Beasts are much more human than they were in the 1st draft: practicality, responsibility and morality seem much more prevalent themes now. So, Beast mentality basically shows an evolution from callous amorality, to a kind of dharmic immorality.<br /> It kind of makes the stories focus more on the Beast's relatonships with their victims as people, rather than on the Beasts themselves, and the Begotten have mostly moved from amoral predators with an alien mindset and a vague goal of learning from and interacting with the WoD's denizens, to maladjusted people who seek to transcend their Horrors' hungers with a version of the 'righteous devil' brand of evil. It's like having 2 different and competing paths of enlightenment.<br /> One thing I prefer in the revised version is Eshmaki as Nightmares of Darkness. That was a pleasant surprise.<br /> <br /> It's kind of funny how the Hero part says that 'Justification miss the point of having a hunger in the first place'. It's perhaps just my perception but the Lessons feel a lot like justifications.<br /> <br /> Heroes feel more like people and less like mindless Beast-seeking missiles but IMHO they still lack something. The text makes a parallel between Beast and Heroes, but I feel Heroic motivation lacks a similar visceral component, a counterpart to the Beasts' Hunger for te analogy to work. I do hope Heroes don'tt suffer anymore for not hunting. If they are to feel more like antagonists and less like justified victims their actions need to be fueled more by the desire for a kind of reward than the fear of unfortunate consequences.<br /> <br /> All in all, I believe things seem far from being as bad as the revised intro made me think they'd be. Or perhaps I just calmed down. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 06-25-2015, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:13:16-07:00","id":566269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=566087#post566087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> .... I.... I just don't understand why they would think that about goats... they regularly killed and ate goats!<br /> <br /> Ok, maybe it was meant to be purely allegory and anyone who read it at the time would have understood that - but if so, what was it an allegory for?!</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe its related to the bezoar taken from the goat's stomach that could supposedly cure poison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:22:01-07:00","id":566581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564834#post564834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Begs the question of who died and left Beasts in charge of that activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's intentional. The Primordial Dream teaches - like the rest of the Astral - but Horrors don't care about that, they just hunger - and if Beasts do, it's because they're rationalising from that aspect of the Dream to steer their Horror's Hungers in a direction the Beasts can live with. If someone asks, &quot;what gives you the right?&quot; I suspect they're <i>supposed</i> (by the writers, I mean) to not really have a good answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=564921#post564921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Views From Without are pretty awesome.The Views From Without are pretty awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I especially like the Promethean admiring the dragon and the mummy musing on lessons and purpose. I hope we get more of them in later chapters. (I also wish we could get them in other game lines).<br /> <br /> Relatedly, I like the new stereotypes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T02:38:19-07:00","id":568941,"title":"","content":"Before it's too late I'd like to ask to give a second look at the Mummy crossover section. It's not one of the problematic ones, but I'd say it's the one that feels the most anemic.<br /> If nothing else, the relation between Beasts and Mummies that serve specific judges could be mentioned. Mummies following Ker-Uru the Face of Dread are a possible source of conflict. Mummies that follow <i>Keraf-Het </i>could be pointed out as being the most likely to take time and investigate the truth behind a Beast's or Heroe's actions/claims. Mummies following <i>Neheb-Nefert, Ser-Kheru, Hetch-Abhu </i>could all have reasons to clash with Beasts or Heroes, depending on their actions. Mummies in service to <i>Hepet-Khet, Neb-Heru, Ser-Tih </i>and <i>Neheb-Ka</i> are especially likely to clash with Heroes.<br /> The Deceived's desire to stay hidden clashing with the Beasts supersense might also be worth pointing out.<br /> Making Beasts fulfil the &quot; Consume the flesh and soul of a sorcerer or spiritual adept&quot; requisite for Shuankhsen to reset their Descent would also provide additional crossover potential, giving a reason for a Mummy and a Beast to work together to hunt Shuankhsen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T04:40:17-07:00","id":569027,"title":"","content":"Quite pleased with the further revisions to the Devouring, and quite glad that there's unlikely to be anything further done to it. Haven't had a chance to browse 3 and 4 yet, but on the whole I'm content with what's been done.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:33:56-07:00","id":569780,"title":"","content":"Chapters 3 and 4 have been revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T21:36:18-07:00","id":569929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569780#post569780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapters 3 and 4 have been revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to recap:<ul><li>Suppressing Souls is still a thing</li> <li>Our sample feeding still involves torture through poisoning and suffocation</li> </ul><br /> And the changes:<ul><li>There's no longer a double incidence of Hero creation on the Inflicting Nightmares roll, in that new ones only show up on a Dramatic failure (so eat up, eat often, and ensure that you're not picking on Kin); Extraordinary Success just wakes up already existing Heroes.</li> <li>It's been confirmed that you still have to meet the Satiety requirements for Atavism effects while in your Lair; Lair Resonance still only allows you to activate Satiety Expenditure effects with Willpower once per Scene per point of Lair.</li> <li>Any Hunger can recover Satiety, but satisfying your specific Hunger exactly is more satisfying. All that matters is the shock created.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T21:45:37-07:00","id":569933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569929#post569929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no longer a double incidence of Hero creation on the Inflicting Nightmares roll, in that new ones only show up on a Dramatic failure (so eat up, eat often, and ensure that you're not picking on Kin); Extraordinary Success just wakes up already existing Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Every</i> instance of creating Heroes has been either removed or changed to a reference to pinging Heroic tracking attempts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any Hunger can recover Satiety, but satisfying your specific Hunger exactly is more satisfying. All that matters is the shock created. </div> </div> </div>That's\u2026 not a thing the revisions say. They clarify that the moment of shock is what the feeding roll generally corresponds to, but there's nothing in there about stepping outside the broader umbrella of your Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T21:50:56-07:00","id":569936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569929#post569929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Our sample feeding still involves torture through poisoning and suffocation</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I read it wrong I believe the beginning of chapter four the beast and vampire was using family dinner to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:14:17-07:00","id":569963,"title":"","content":"I believe hex is talking about the sample character made named Mrs. Winters played by Magda. Specifically the instance of feeding on the guy that steals candy on Halloween.<br /> <br /> I think it is fine if they go dark sometimes. I think the overall tone has changed enough. Leaving the darker examples helps to keep the right balance. They were going for monstrous.<br /> <br /> We have to wait for Chapter 5 for Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-27-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:20:28-07:00","id":569965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569929#post569929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our sample feeding still involves torture through poisoning and suffocation</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a large difference in execution though: Brent is explicitly a college man (a frat boy) and there's nothing in there about making players uncomfortable,<br /> <br /> So it's still massively dark, but it doesn't have the over the top grotesque of child abuse accidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:39:46-07:00","id":569972,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it was reader bias creating the confusion about Brent before, but it is always good to have it spelled out better. It was an easy mistake to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Any Hunger can recover Satiety, but satisfying your specific Hunger exactly is more satisfying. All that matters is the shock created.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>If this is referring to the chart then I believe it means specific within the chosen Hunger. Mrs. Winters has Punishment but specifically punishing those that hurt the neighborhood children. She could punish someone that rear ended her, but that would not be specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:47:07-07:00","id":569976,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else bothered that Mother's Kiss can basically be used as an &quot;inflict Dramatic Failures without a Save&quot; power?<br /> Sure, the chance for a dramafail aren't that high, but get low stamina and satiety, and you have a good chance being down to a chance die. Ironically, the more powerful your enemy the more likely you are to get down to the chance die.<br /> Once per scene you can even willingly make the normal failure a dramatic failure, get a Beat for that <b>and</b> inflict a dramatic failure on an opponent without a save.<br /> Mother's Kiss really shouldn't usable on unwilling targets, or maybe even require the Family Ties condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:38:00-07:00","id":570219,"title":"","content":"How do you figure? You can't plan for a dramatic failure, and Storytellers absolutely should not allow players to use the &quot;take a dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; thing as a weapon. That's completely counter to the point of the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:41:36-07:00","id":570223,"title":"","content":"One part that I just noticed, which I really like: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Expanding the Lair</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A location qualifies for inclusion in the Primordial Dream as long as it meets the following <br /> <br /> requirements:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The environment must contain at least one element matching a Lair Trait in the Beast\u2019s Lair.<br /> <br /> And either<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Beast must have achieved an exceptional success on a Nightmare activation roll within the <br /> <br /> scene <br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> \u2022 Another character must have lost Integrity (or some supernatural equivalents; see sidebar) via a <br /> <br /> breaking point with the Beast present<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 A human character must have lost Integrity stemming from encountering the supernatural in the <br /> <br /> location. If the Beast was not present for this occurrence, she needs to learn what happened in the <br /> <br /> location and what supernatural being was involved before she can add the Chamber to her Lair.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely adds to the idea of Beasts being the ones hunting for secrets within the World of Darkness. I could totally see a cop or PI Beast linking their lair to a bunch of old crime scenes that involved the supernatural. Very noir and very cool idea. Great add Matt!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T07:47:07-07:00","id":570249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=570219#post570219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you figure? You can't plan for a dramatic failure, and Storytellers absolutely should not allow players to use the &quot;take a dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; thing as a weapon. That's completely counter to the point of the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's honestly not a big problem, it's not like it's all that overpowered.<br /> <br /> But it's note quite true that you can't plan for a dramatic failure. Even if you disallow the &quot;take a dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; thing (and, agreed, any sane ST will and it's not really worth debating) that leaves any of the many powers that make your next normal failure into a dramatic one. I think several splats get a power like that, my group for example has a Fate Mage.<br /> <br /> Even then I don't think it's all that much of a problem. I think I am mostly bothered because it feels weird to have a power with a dramatic failure effect that can be more beneficial to you than its success effects. If I was a Beast up against a powerful enemy I'd try it at least once. Sure, it's only a 10% chance, but the effect is powerful, it doesn't really take an action, it's not that expensive, you can do it before combat from the other side of the wall, and worst case scenario: you enemy get a single extra die on one roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:04:53-07:00","id":570280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569963#post569963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe hex is talking about the sample character made named Mrs. Winters played by Magda. Specifically the instance of feeding on the guy that steals candy on Halloween.<br /> <br /> I think it is fine if they go dark sometimes. I think the overall tone has changed enough. Leaving the darker examples helps to keep the right balance. They were going for monstrous.<br /> <br /> We have to wait for Chapter 5 for Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I kind of hoped that they'd choose a different example, more to take ammo away from the detractors than anything else, but what we've gotten is what we're getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:23:02-07:00","id":570293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=569972#post569972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it was reader bias creating the confusion about Brent before, but it is always good to have it spelled out better. It was an easy mistake to make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If this is referring to the chart then I believe it means specific within the chosen Hunger. Mrs. Winters has Punishment but specifically punishing those that hurt the neighborhood children. She could punish someone that rear ended her, but that would not be specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial read was that just satisfying the Hunger in a general sense provided neither bonus nor penalty, but I think now that the gradient is more &quot;baseline act \u00bb similar act \u00bb specific act,&quot; so for my Ravager that teaches against pride, the gradient would go from smashing windows, to keying some smug bastard's car, to sabotaging pointless building projects, for example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:12:53-07:00","id":570629,"title":"","content":"I see. I read it the same way now with a bonus when ravaging pride given your example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T18:00:11-07:00","id":570741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=570249#post570249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's note quite true that you can't plan for a dramatic failure. Even if you disallow the &quot;take a dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; thing (and, agreed, any sane ST will and it's not really worth debating) that leaves any of the many powers that make your next normal failure into a dramatic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit tired at present, so that's probably why I'm having a slight issue parsing this. To be clear, you do mean that any sane ST will deny using the Dramatic Failure as a weapon, yes? And not the &quot;Take a Dramatic Failure for a Beat&quot; part?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T02:32:44-07:00","id":571091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=570741#post570741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a bit tired at present, so that's probably why I'm having a slight issue parsing this. To be clear, you do mean that any sane ST will deny using the Dramatic Failure as a weapon, yes? And not the &quot;Take a Dramatic Failure for a Beat&quot; part?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely the latter.<br /> But that's just the result of my games' focus on story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:20:47-07:00","id":571117,"title":"","content":"Okay so I would like to see if I'm understanding the revised mechanics for opening a door to the lair due to location similarities.<br /> <br /> So the most basic is just using the same place I originally created the chamber in. If I created the chamber at the local gym I can ,basically, just focus on opening the path throw my will at the door to the place and open the pathway to the chamber.<br /> <br /> The second is recreating the original chamber's creation just not in the same place. So keeping with the gym example, the original chamber was created because by a tyrant just showing someone who thought they were the toughest how they were completely outclassed they were by the Beast. So by showing how much the tyrant outclasses a person with the same mindset and basically inflict a breaking point they can open the path in the new gym, but they get a -2 since it is still a different place so the pathway doesn't sync exactly.<br /> <br /> Third I'm a little confused by. It reads the same as the second only its a -4 because you don't succeed at causing the breaking point?<br /> <br /> The last being just, &quot;The chamber was created in a gym. Ergo I can open a path here because it is a gym,&quot; but since it lacks any other similarities there's a -5 on the check because the pathway is barely managing to sync at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:54:05-07:00","id":571234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=570249#post570249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly not a big problem, it's not like it's all that overpowered.<br /> <br /> But it's note quite true that you can't plan for a dramatic failure. Even if you disallow the &quot;take a dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; thing (and, agreed, any sane ST will and it's not really worth debating) that leaves any of the many powers that make your next normal failure into a dramatic one. I think several splats get a power like that, my group for example has a Fate Mage.<br /> <br /> Even then I don't think it's all that much of a problem. I think I am mostly bothered because it feels weird to have a power with a dramatic failure effect that can be more beneficial to you than its success effects. If I was a Beast up against a powerful enemy I'd try it at least once. Sure, it's only a 10% chance, but the effect is powerful, it doesn't really take an action, it's not that expensive, you can do it before combat from the other side of the wall, and worst case scenario: you enemy get a single extra die on one roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you disallow that rule? That's a great rule. <br /> <br /> I think maybe the problem is that you're thinking people will roll on dice pools that are low, deliberately try and fail, and then pick up the Beat and try and use the dramatic failure effect as a deliberate power. But that's completely counter to the idea behind the &quot;dramatic failure for a Beat&quot; rule. The idea there is that the player digs a deeper hole for the character, making things <i>worse</i> for the character, and gets a reward for doing that because it makes things more interesting. If that's not what's happening, then the Storyteller needs to either a) disallow <i>that particular use</i> of the rule (not the whole thing, man, talk about throwing out the baby with the bathwater) or b) change the dramatic failure effect on the fly and make is something that's going to make everyone's life complicated. &quot;Sorry, were you trying to game the system and deliberately fail, even though that's totally not how this power works? Well, squids. On your face.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T06:19:32-07:00","id":571243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571234#post571234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you disallow that rule? That's a great rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I meant that particular use of that rule, like your option a). Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T07:19:04-07:00","id":571274,"title":"","content":"Okay, the &quot;you are just meat&quot; thing working on creatures without souls bothers me for a practical reason, it can be made permanent, and it's undone by going questing.<br /> <br /> So has anyone come up with a quest idea for a creature to regain something they never had in the first place without seeming like it was written by someone either stoned or stupid, because I'm drawing a blank. <br /> <br /> Or I suppose it could be fixed by not allowing the soul suppression trick from working permanently on creatures without souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:27:08-07:00","id":571411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571274#post571274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay, the &quot;you are just meat&quot; thing working on creatures without souls bothers me for a practical reason, it can be made permanent, and it's undone by going questing.<br /> <br /> So has anyone come up with a quest idea for a creature to regain something they never had in the first place without seeming like it was written by someone either stoned or stupid, because I'm drawing a blank.<br /> <br /> Or I suppose it could be fixed by not allowing the soul suppression trick from working permanently on creatures without souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the nature of the target of You Are Meat.<br /> <br /> Pilgrimage is the simplest non-soul to simulate recovering, as it represents building a soul out of whole cloth. Cover is harder, as the soul in question is borrowed and/or embellished, so approach recovering it as reinhabiting that role rather than physically recovering the Cover (although this doesn't preclude Burning that Cover and choosing a new one). Synergy and Harmony are the hardest, but should take similar approaches to recovery. Recovering Synergy should be akin to trying to find a lost pet, or getting back in touch with an old friend, where the focus is on reestablishing the connection with the Geist. Using You Are Meat on Uratha should take into account which side of the Gauntlet the character is on when targeted, and force the character toward the extreme that leaves them stranded. The quest for them is about reversing the imbalance and regaining their purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:36:13-07:00","id":571458,"title":"","content":"Actually I think it makes sense for it to push werewolves towards spirit. That's the half which is most like beings with no integrity trait whatsoever, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:40:05-07:00","id":571461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571234#post571234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Sorry, were you trying to game the system and deliberately fail, even though that's totally not how this power works? Well, squids. On your face.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And now this is going to happen whenever someone tries that. Squids forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:46:08-07:00","id":571463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571461#post571461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now this is going to happen whenever someone tries that. Squids forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Octopi Wallstreet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:42:54-07:00","id":571903,"title":"","content":"I'm a die hard OWoD/exalted fan but damn, this has me wanting to get into the NWoD stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T18:34:33-07:00","id":572060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571411#post571411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the nature of the target of You Are Meat.<br /> <br /> Pilgrimage is the simplest non-soul to simulate recovering, as it represents building a soul out of whole cloth. Cover is harder, as the soul in question is borrowed and/or embellished, so approach recovering it as reinhabiting that role rather than physically recovering the Cover (although this doesn't preclude Burning that Cover and choosing a new one). Synergy and Harmony are the hardest, but should take similar approaches to recovery. Recovering Synergy should be akin to trying to find a lost pet, or getting back in touch with an old friend, where the focus is on reestablishing the connection with the Geist. Using You Are Meat on Uratha should take into account which side of the Gauntlet the character is on when targeted, and force the character toward the extreme that leaves them stranded. The quest for them is about reversing the imbalance and regaining their purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well maybe it's just me, but that's not treating the disease, that's treating the symptom. I wouldn't allow a supernatural to regain their soul by buying up their integrity equivalent any more than I'd allow a human to regain their soul by buying up integrity.<br /> <br /> For that matter, saying that indulging your vice automatically attracts the G-M's attention or alienates ones Geist doesn't really work for me either. <br /> <br /> Of course, your solution only works on beings with an integrity score, while all the recommended player types have such, what exactly is a PC imbued or fetch suppose to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T21:24:30-07:00","id":572166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=572060#post572060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well maybe it's just me, but that's not treating the disease, that's treating the symptom. I wouldn't allow a supernatural to regain their soul by buying up their integrity equivalent any more than I'd allow a human to regain their soul by buying up integrity.<br /> <br /> For that matter, saying that indulging your vice automatically attracts the G-M's attention or alienates ones Geist doesn't really work for me either.<br /> <br /> Of course, your solution only works on beings with an integrity score, while all the recommended player types have such, what exactly is a PC imbued or fetch suppose to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not suggesting a hard buyback; I'm saying that the Role-playing challenges should be similar for some templates to the normal processes they go through to improve their analogues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:16:17-07:00","id":572324,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://nwodsecondchances2e.tumblr.com/post/122737255513/joshua-wright-everyone-knows-what-a-cockatrice\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a rather positive spin on what Beast is all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:15:18-07:00","id":572451,"title":"","content":"So, I have two big problems with You are Meat. They don\u2019t really have anything to do with balance or clarity of the rules\u2019, and I don\u2019t want to get these confused with the points I have been making about those aspects. Which is why I am posting them here, not on rpg.net, where I have been posting more about the balance side of things.<br /> <br /> So, we have already been told that the Doylist reason for why You are Meat doesn\u2019t work on Beasts is that it would just outright kill Beasts. Which is an okay reason, I can buy that. But then they the same isn\u2019t true for any other splat!? <i>What?</i> For some reason the Beast book decided for all other splats that stealing the closest equivalent for a soul that they have doesn\u2019t kill them? Prometheans, Sin-Eaters, Deceived/Mummies, probably some others. There are at least several splats that should be just as dead as Beasts (or at least demoted to ST controlled NPCs in the case of Sin-Eaters and Deceived) if they got the closest equivalent to their soul stolen. Take Prometheans for example. The closest equivalent to a soul they have is the fire animating them. You take that away, and you get a pile of stitched together body parts lying on the ground.<br /> So sorry, no. Not only doesn\u2019t that make sense, it\u2019s also a statement about the metaphysics of other splats that Beast should not be allowed to make. If You are Meat can handwave away soul stealing killing, say, Prometheans, then it can do the same for Beasts. And if the book wants Beasts to stay immune, then it should accept that it shouldn\u2019t work on some other splats either.<br /> <br /> And then you get the Watsonian explanation for You are Meat not working on Beasts: \u201cBeasts are immune to the effect, as their \u201csouls\u201d (Horrors) are <b>far too powerful and vicious</b> to be thus affected\u201d. <i>Again, what?</i> The book goes ahead and uses rules text to make Horrors the canon most powerful and vicious \u2018soul equivalents in the entire setting?? Well, that one hell of a no-sell right there. No buildup, no textual support, not even the slightest attempt to make this really over the top statement believable to the reader. By now we have a truckload of books for the WoD, we the readers have read about beings and weird shit in the WoD that, by comparison, make even the most horrific descriptions of Horrors that the Beast book has to offer look like fluffy cuddle-kittens meowing to get some attention. Horrors lack any support at all for this statement outside that one sentence in the power's description. And somehow this explanation, just like the Doylist one, tries to make a statement about the metaphysics of other splats in an absolute, 3<sup>rd</sup>-person rules voice that the Beast book shouldn\u2019t make. That\u2019s just not a statement it should get to make about other splats outside in-character opinion pieces.<br /> <br /> These two are exactly the kind of stuff that makes people dislike the way Beast treats crossover. Because it likes to use rules text for Beast powers to say stuff about other splats that it has no business ruling on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-29-2015, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:47:30-07:00","id":572484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=572451#post572451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we have already been told that the Doylist reason for why You are Meat doesn\u2019t work on Beasts is that it would just outright kill Beasts. Which is an okay reason, I can buy that. But then they the same isn\u2019t true for any other splat!? <i>What?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Other splats don't have a literal mechanic of &quot;if the thing that is acting as your soul is killed or destroyed, you die.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For some reason the Beast book decided for all other splats that stealing the closest equivalent for a soul that they have doesn\u2019t kill them? </div> </div> </div>You appear to be operating under a different definition of &quot;soul&quot; than any of the books actually use and also freely substituting &quot;suppress&quot; with &quot;steal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prometheans, Sin-Eaters, Deceived/Mummies, probably some others. There are at least several splats that should be just as dead as Beasts (or at least demoted to ST controlled NPCs in the case of Sin-Eaters and Deceived) if they got the closest equivalent to their soul stolen. Take Prometheans for example. The closest equivalent to a soul they have is the fire animating them. You take that away, and you get a pile of stitched together body parts lying on the ground. </div> </div> </div>Funny how &quot;set the Integrity stat up to fall no further than 1 before one's Willpower starts shouldering the load of your flagging self-image&quot; and &quot;suppress the soul or its nearest functional equivalent in a fashion that means it is still present <i>in the collective unconscious that touches all souls</i>&quot; means something different than &quot;kill a supernatural character or render them an NPC.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So sorry, no. Not only doesn\u2019t that make sense, it\u2019s also a statement about the metaphysics of other splats that Beast should not be allowed to make. If You are Meat can handwave away soul stealing killing, say, Prometheans, then it can do the same for Beasts. And if the book wants Beasts to stay immune, then it should accept that it shouldn\u2019t work on some other splats either. </div> </div> </div>Beasts are the only non-mage splat that is vulnerable to soul-theft through Awakened magic, which still kills them even if the process is more involved than it would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then you get the Watsonian explanation for You are Meat not working on Beasts: \u201cBeasts are immune to the effect, as their \u201csouls\u201d (Horrors) are <b>far too powerful and vicious</b> to be thus affected\u201d. <i>Again, what?</i> The book goes ahead and uses rules text to make Horrors the canon most powerful and vicious \u2018soul equivalents in the entire setting?? Well, that one hell of a no-sell right there. No buildup, no textual support, not even the slightest attempt to make this really over the top statement believable to the reader. </div> </div> </div>When what is effectively a passive battery in any other character-type is instead a semiautonomous embodiment of fundamental human terror, you do indeed get to make the statement that that thing is a vicious and potent thing.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that we have a term for a soul-equivalent banished to deep within the Primordial Dream that belongs to a Beast, and that's &quot;Unfettered.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I should think the fact that You Are Meat is a Common Nightmare that basically allows you to circumvent most of the difficulty of forming a Chamber would be a greater concern than trying to trump up a poor understanding of the presented metaphysics of the other gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-29-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T03:43:53-07:00","id":572497,"title":"","content":"Read through the revised Chapter 3 and the edits to Chapters 1 and 2. Have belated thoughts to share.<br /> <br /> <b>What I like:</b><ul><li>The change to Expanding The Lair that was already pointed out. It's a neat addition that encourages investigating old horrors and delving into old supernatural history. Really good in that it's a mechanical and flavorful incentive for Beasts to explore the World Of Darkness.</li> <li>The tweaks made to the Devouring. Matt's second take on it, in which the event happening on its own is just as common as it being <i>facilited</i> by another Beast, makes the whole thing far more palatable. The text is just noticeably more accepting and inclusive of both perspectives now, and I can appreciate that. The clarified wording of what happens exactly also makes me much less hung up on the matter of another Beast's involvement in the process (because it's essentially giving a push on an inevitable requirement for the moment of revelation).</li> </ul><br /> <b>What I don't like:</b><ul><li>The change of how Atavisms work for the Horror. I think it significantly takes away from its rightful oomph that the Horror on its own doesn't have free access to the Satiety Expenditure effect, and while merged with the Beast atavisms work entirely as normal. Paraphrasing Matt's explanation from the kickstarter comments, the logic for the latter is that you are essentially burdening your Horror with your human body/nature when you merge with it, which works but feels a bit restrictive. The way I would do it is: While merged with the Horror you always have access to Low Satiety effects but must expend Satiety for the last effect; and when it's by itself it just uses every effect for free (working cooldown times applied as appropriate).</li> <li>The softening in a few examples of Beasts through Chapters 1, 2 and 3. Some of the text might've benefitted from a less antagonistic or monstrous bent on the portrayal of Beasts, but I think there was more than one case that really didn't needed to be changed.</li> </ul><br /> <b>What I'm not sure about<b></b>:</b><ul><li>I'm curious about how the workings of Heroes might have changed with the revised fluff, because it appears feeding through dreams now draws Heroes in and attracts the notice of any in the area rather than creating them; on a first read of the revised chapters 1 and 2, I still had the impression Beasts created Heroes, or were implied to. I understand the reasoning behind editing that out, since as it was it probably leaned too much on the abuser/abused angle for some people. And drawing every Hero in the vicinity to them rather than creating one might actually be <i>more dangerous</i> (and more danger is good). We might be missing context on this since Heroes are elaborated on in Chapter 5, so for now I'mma wait on this topic. Slightly concerned about how the apparent removal of &quot;Beasts unwittingly create Heroes&quot; might affect the conflict between them, but I may be worrying for nothing.</li> </ul><br /> (On a side-note, I kinda want to run a side by side comparison of the old and new sterotypes in the Families, because some felt better than others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-29-2015, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T04:24:20-07:00","id":572504,"title":"","content":"Well, getting everything all the time in the lair did make beasts a touch OP. We need heroes to be a threat, after all.<br /> <br /> It's more of an exchange really, anyway. When you merge your horror loses access to the atavism powers that don't match its satiety, but it also gains the ability to use nightmares. That seems a pretty fair trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T05:18:22-07:00","id":572529,"title":"","content":"Oh, mechanically I understand it. But flavor-wise it feels off. I'm not as bothered by Atavisms working normally when you merge compared to the Horror on its own lacking the unrestrained access to the entirety of its power.<br /> <br /> Should a thundering, looming roc in its stormy mountain perch that is in fact a hungering nightmare one cannot overtake not be able to fly without concern in that dream realm? Should a shapeless, amorphous stalker of tearing darkness not be able to meld and travel through the shadows at the blink of an eye? Should a titan of stone armor not be in truth as tough and impervious as it has every right to be, an unstoppable force of nature chasing its victims?<br /> <br /> My concern is not really a mechanical one. It's a narrative one. It's that the Horror feels offputtingly <i>smaller</i> than it should by all rights be in the revised framework.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(When you consider Lair Traits, this shrinking of the Horror also doesn't really do much for the &quot;Heroes need to be a threat&quot; argument, since fighting in the Lair on your own continues to be at best very difficult and exceedingly impractical, and at worst suicidal. If the idea there was balancing the danger Heroes pose by giving them more of a chance inside the Lair, there are better ways to do it. A Gift that grants resistance to Lair Traits. A Gift that allows them to collapse Chambers much faster. A Gift that grants bonuses to the Hero's every action when facing the heart of fear itself. Some inherent characteristic or mechanic that gives Heroes an advantage when invading the Lair.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-29-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T06:03:39-07:00","id":572554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=572529#post572529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, mechanically I understand it. But flavor-wise it feels off. I'm not as bothered by Atavisms working normally when you merge compared to the Horror on its own lacking the unrestrained access to the entirety of its power.<br /> <br /> Should a thundering, looming roc in its stormy mountain perch that is in fact a hungering nightmare one cannot overtake not be able to fly without concern in that dream realm? Should a shapeless, amorphous stalker of tearing darkness not be able to meld and travel through the shadows at the blink of an eye? Should a titan of stone armor not be in truth as tough and impervious as it has every right to be, an unstoppable force of nature chasing its victims?<br /> <br /> My concern is not really a mechanical one. It's a narrative one. It's that the Horror feels offputtingly <i>smaller</i> than it should by all rights be in the revised framework.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(When you consider Lair Traits, this shrinking of the Horror also doesn't really do much for the &quot;Heroes need to be a threat&quot; argument, since fighting in the Lair on your own continues to be at best very difficult and exceedingly impractical, and at worst suicidal. If the idea there was balancing the danger Heroes pose by giving them more of a chance inside the Lair, there are better ways to do it. A Gift that grants resistance to Lair Traits. A Gift that allows them to collapse Chambers much faster. A Gift that grants bonuses to the Hero's every action when facing the heart of fear itself. Some inherent characteristic or mechanic that gives Heroes an advantage when invading the Lair.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree entirely with the above. I'm probably going to houserule this one so that the Horror gets access to the standard and low Satiety effects of Atavisms but still needs to expend Satiety to use the powers that require fuel. Something that requires an effort still requires an effort, after all.<br /> <br /> The feel I'm getting so far re: Heroes is that they're functioning very much like Hunter: The Reckoning style hunters. Once their particular type of psychic landmine goes off and they're active as a Hero then any Beast that bumps up against their dreams will draw attention, even if it wasn't the one that triggered them. Really their biggest problem mechanically is that they're supposedly terrible team players, but their chances are downright dismal solo and doubly so if they're in a Lair.<br /> <br /> (As a passing thought, one advantage they may have is that if a Hero can collapse Lair chambers as a dream-presence rather than needing to be there in the flesh, the Hero can potentially spawn-rush a Lair by making repeated attacks on the same Beast, probably with rests in between to recharge their spiritual batteries. The Beast will be left with little idea who and where the Hero is in the physical world and would need to race to find and neutralize the threat before Zealot McInfiniteLives overwhelms them or gets lucky.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:16:55-07:00","id":572616,"title":"","content":"Well, we've been waiting on it for a while. The chapter on Heroes is now in the Drive folder and we are free to sate our hunger!<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Wow, we knew it was coming, but big changes none the less to the chapter right off the bat in terms of tone. This is a good very early on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Good Hero</b><br /> <br /> What, then, about the Hero that listens to reason? What about the Hero that chooses to follow her better angels, as it were, trying to soothe the Primordial Dream by providing therapy to troubled individuals, by hunting down violent or destructive supernatural creatures, or by taking on an advisory role such as clergy? Surely these Heroes exist? They do, but Beasts don\u2019t tend to cross paths with them, because they resist the urge to hunt down the Children, or because, for whatever reason, they never find any of the Children. In game terms, the Heroes that stalk Beasts tend to have low Integrity ratings \u2014 their souls are weak and ill-defined. Being a Hero is, like being a Beast, something that a person is born with. Also like being a Beast, being a Hero is what one makes of it. The Hero\u2019s narrative role in a Beast chronicle is discussed in more detailed in Chapter Seven. Heroes discussed in this chapter, however, are the Heroes that react with violence and hatred to the Children. Other Heroes exist, yes, but we\u2019re not talking about them right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that a lot. The negative sanity implications of Heroes are removed, there is now a lot more design space for Heroes, and you still get to keep your obsessive style Hero. Tough to please everyone, but that's about as close as I can see anyone coming for this particular antagonist.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT 2</b>: I skipped ahead for another reason, but I just checked out Melanie's entry. The same basic idea is there, but its been greatly reworked and all of the uncertain implications have been removed. I actually like it much, much better now. Melanie is much more unique and becomes that much more of living plothook. I'd be very interested to see a campaign were a group of Beasts actually help her and she becomes one of the &quot;wise&quot; Heroes instead of the obsessive ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-29-2015, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:39:50-07:00","id":572627,"title":"","content":"Well, actually, the negatime sanity is still present, just different: the Heroes in games who hunt Beasts are those who are far enough off the deep end they don't care. I mean, it still has rhe whole &quot;below integrity 4: kill the Beast!&quot; element. The difference now is that being a hero itself isn't tied to being unhinged, but the axe-crazy heroes are defined by being unstable compared to their saner kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:08:21-07:00","id":572644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571461#post571461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now this is going to happen whenever someone tries that. Squids forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the most amusing things about Beast is that I keep wanting to turn these offhand phrases into nightmares. There's A Squid On Your Face. You Are About To Be Suplexed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:23:47-07:00","id":572681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=572644#post572644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most amusing things about Beast is that I keep wanting to turn these offhand phrases into nightmares. There's A Squid On Your Face. You Are About To Be Suplexed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kinship: Cthulhu and The People's Champion respectively? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:29:24-07:00","id":572691,"title":"","content":"Done with the first reading (or, well, re-reading I suppose) of Chapter 5. Still not sure what to feel about the changes to Heroes.<br /> <br /> The fact Beasts were responsible for the creation of Heroes was genuinely one of the most interesting facets of their conflict to me. Of course, the Begotten still drive Heroes to action - they cause the disturbances that lead them down the slippery slope, and in many ways they're still unwittingly responsible for the cycle of violence. Heroes are still tragic figures who can nonetheless be the antagonists Beasts love to hate, but I think they've lost some considerable part of what originally made them so tragic.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's for the best overall, since they have more room to be multi-dimensional even within the heroic mindset, and they are less straddled down by the possibility of people reading unfortunate implications into them. But the relationship between Heroes and Beasts suffers a bit for it in the distillment of its grim inevitability. Sure, their role in the cosmology is expanded and they have a wider place in things, but what was most significant about their existence seems to have suffered for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-29-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:45:39-07:00","id":572817,"title":"","content":"Do like the changes to Melanie's backstory, I'm just a little confused about how effective her Gifts will be in a fight. I also like how they reinforced how Heroes haunt dreams similarly to Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:57:21-07:00","id":572825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=572681#post572681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship: Cthulhu and The People's Champion respectively? :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think it's the Beast Incarnate, Brock Lesnar, AKA, Mayor of <a href=\"http://www.talkingbaws.com/2015/03/31/brock-lesnar-buys-small-us-town-renames-it-suplex-city/\" target=\"_blank\">Suplex City</a>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://botchedspot.com/wp-content/blogs.dir/1/files/2015/04/2015-04-06-suplex-city.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:16:10-07:00","id":572841,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there is narrative space for Heroes who kill Beasts in more symbolic manners? Impeaching the Tyrant, stealing the Collector's hoard, and such. Other forms of subjugation and humiliation (though that does carry the chance for things to get much darker than straight-up murder). Attempting to separate the human from the Horror, like some sort of pray-away-the-monster program. The point of it all, of course, is still to be an act of self-aggrandizement at the expense of another living, thinking, feeling being. On the other hand, metaphorical deaths might take away something important from the game. What do other people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:10:07-07:00","id":572929,"title":"","content":"Even if heroes don't get new gifts out of those methods, nothing stops a hero from doing such things, so as a story element I can't say I see it as very necessary. Heroes are ST characters anyway, if a ST wants a hero that wants to do a hostile takeover of a beast's company or what not, nothing is stopping them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:43:26-07:00","id":573195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=571091#post571091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely the latter.<br /> But that's just the result of my games' focus on story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Okay.<br /> <br /> I mean, my games focus on story, too, and we love the rule and it's in play constantly. One of my players has adopted the phrase &quot;Embrace failure!&quot; at this point.<br /> <br /> YMMV, I suppose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T00:36:24-07:00","id":573646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If we pass </span></span></span><b>$107,000</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> of contributions, we will create a </span></span></span><b>Building a Legend</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> PDF: A &quot;quickstart your chronicle&quot; book. Everyone makes characters, but then collaboratively designs the city, the setting, and the Brood, and comes away with a fun first session and a bunch of dangling plot hooks for the Storyteller to grab. The PDF will be sent to every backer who pledged for a Reward Tier that includes a physical copy of </span></span></span><b>Beast: The Primordial Prestige Edition</b><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>OMGWTFBBQ!!!!<br /> <br /> This sounds like a super awesome idea for a book. Hopefully we can hit both this one and the &quot;Interface&quot; for the Anthology later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T00:53:01-07:00","id":573649,"title":"","content":"So are there still people fighting over this game? I suppose the one with someone being tortured over candy is a bit dark, but it seems a tad over reactive from what I have seen. I have to ask how much worse is that than a vampire forcing themselves on someone. So what got everyone so worked up? I am kind of late the discussion so I have only heard snippets here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5383-lonesomewanderer1982","name":"Lonesomewanderer1982","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T01:16:41-07:00","id":573658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lonesomewanderer1982</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=573649#post573649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are there still people fighting over this game? I suppose the one with someone being tortured over candy is a bit dark, but it seems a tad over reactive from what I have seen. I have to ask how much worse is that than a vampire forcing themselves on someone. So what got everyone so worked up? I am kind of late the discussion so I have only heard snippets here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh it's calmed down significantly ,at least on these boards, since so much has been handled over the course of the Kickstarter. Not to mention some of the complaints had a tendency to not even be close to accurate, be missing important details, or in some cases be ignoring the fact that the individual probably is not meant to be viewed as a good person. Like there was one where people would say the Beast that was ,I think, the VP at a school was abusing children and all we got in description was that people were freaked out by her and she had a scorpion as a pet in her office.<br /> <br /> The one you mention showed up often as a case of missing details. For start he wasn't tortured it was just poisoning some of the candy enough that he would get exceptionally sick and then using a Nightmare to hammer in that he brought it on himself. Also it was less &quot;over candy&quot; and more because he was a college age student , specified as being a frat boy in the revision, who beat up little kids for their Halloween candy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:09:44-07:00","id":573853,"title":"","content":"The critics are still going strong in Rpg.net, yes. Apparently people who dissaprove of BtP are anxious to see people wanting to play a Beast (because they are cross-over friendly) at their table.<br /> <br /> Bur then compared to Omage flame wars, it is nothing to worry about :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:54:39-07:00","id":573879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=573658#post573658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh it's calmed down significantly ,at least on these boards, since so much has been handled over the course of the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Onyx Path has been really graceful about all the changes, and it's pretty cool how responsive they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T07:18:30-07:00","id":573909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=573853#post573853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The critics are still going strong in Rpg.net, yes. Apparently people who dissaprove of BtP are anxious to see people wanting to play a Beast (because they are cross-over friendly) at their table.<br /> <br /> Bur then compared to Omage flame wars, it is nothing to worry about :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely refuse to go to that board. The constant whining, close-mindedness, and people that generally have nothing in common with myself are the reasons. It's just, so much negativity by the same people over and over and over and over and over again. Literally. The same people. Same complaints. Same cries. <br /> <br /> I prefer the Onyx Path board, anyway. Since 99% of the rpgs that I play come from and are made from OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T07:55:16-07:00","id":573962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=573646#post573646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OMGWTFBBQ!!!!<br /> <br /> This sounds like a super awesome idea for a book. Hopefully we can hit both this one and the &quot;Interface&quot; for the Anthology later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesssssss. I agree. I want this. I want this so bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T08:26:19-07:00","id":573978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div