<div class=\"message\">So, I just finished Marvel's Daredevil. If it's not a Hunter story, It's a Beast story. Matt himself has gotta be an Eshmaki Nemesis, Fisk/Kingpin is an Anakim Tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beast seems particularly easy to make superhero stories for- Daredevil, Batman, the Hulk, etc,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T06:38:43-07:00","id":575153,"title":"","content":"so would that make Joker a &quot;Hero&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2080-protector152","name":"Protector152","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T06:46:52-07:00","id":575159,"title":"","content":"That or he's a particularly enthusiastic Beast who has quite forgotten the lesson. Gluttony for the sake of it, maybe trying to become Incarnate.<br /> I mean, at the end of the day, wouldn't he rather keep Batman around and keep the dance going than destroy him?<br /> <br /> It makes you wonder, out of the two of them, who would be the Apex. Batman or the Joker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T06:56:35-07:00","id":575164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Protector152</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=575153#post575153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so would that make Joker a &quot;Hero&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's not a perfect fit - but it is worth noting he defines himself by his opposition to Batman, unlike Batman who'd just as rather never have to deal with him again. That's very &quot;Hero&quot;-y.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you go with a version off of Heath Ledger's Joker, there's definite &quot;dark teacher of society&quot; elements going on. If he's a Beast, I'd say Hunger for Ruin? Definite Namtaru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":