View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WOOOO!!! *Kermit flail*<br /> <br /> Er, um... *cough* Nothing to see here, folks. But good job anyway! *high fives all around*</div> </div> </div> </div>Dignified, solemn high fives for all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T20:23:15-07:00","id":577026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=575712#post575712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to agree with Joss Whedon on this one (and, please, for folks who either love him or hate him, let's just leave it and focus on this one idea): the Hulk is a werewolf story.<br /> <br /> He's fine, he's fine, he's fine, he gets angry, loses control, changes form, and a lot of people almost certainly get hurt or die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stan Lee has said his inspirations for the Hulk were Frankenstein and Mr. Hyde. Although I <i>do</i> find it amusing that one of his minor antagonists is named <u>Talbot</u>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T00:49:31-07:00","id":577130,"title":"","content":"A fairly neat thing I just realized with B:tP when regarding Heroes...Redeemed Prometheans. Those who have completed the pilgrimage and became mortal. So if a Redeemed becomes a Hero because of a Beast, they will hunt the supernatural; a somewhat tragic twist. However it doesn't stop there. Prometheans get a very unique gift when becoming Redeemed, a redeemed-version of their Athanor.<br /> <br /> Example of this could be a Frakenstein who becomes a Redeemed and had prior to this the Lion Athanor which does...<br /> <b>Promethean</b>: May spend Willpower to ignore supernatural or mundane effects that hinder the accomplishment of goals<br /> <b>Redeemed</b>: Retains Promethean boon.<br /> <br /> So what happens now when a redeemed has this? Well think what a Beast's Lair has...supernatural or mundane effects that hinder the Hero and impede them from reaching the Beast. Suddenly the Redeemed Hero pops a willpower point and can traverse a beast's lair and ignore all effects that <u>hinder</u>. So a Redeemed Hero could very well pop a willpower point and traverse the labyrinth with ease as they make their way to the beast.<br /> If you really want to make an intimidating hero for a beast player, I would honestly give the Redeemed Prometheans and their Anathors a good look at.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Athanors\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Athanors\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Athanors\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Athanors </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Like for instance in the spoiler below for a Hero that is also a Redeemed. I left things like skills, attributes and merits blank intentionally as I wanted to focus on more of what makes the Hero who they are fluff-wise.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Name:[/b] Micheal Ravios<br /> <b>Virtue/Vice:</b> Justice &amp; Pride<br /> <b>Concept:</b> The Honorable Paladin<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4<br /> <b>Heroic Gifts:</b> Champion's Endurance (x2), Legendary Hunter, Open Gate<br /> <b>Redeemed Boon:</b> Machine*<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Law enforcement officer<br /> <b>Formerly:</b> Zeka Promthean<br /> <b>Age: </b> 39<br /> <b>Mythic hero as inspiration:</b> Sauska<br /> <br /> * = <b>Redeemed:</b> Maintains the benefit of the 9-Again rule when following an order that benefits another individual, or when performing any action that directly protects another individual from violence or harm.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Micheal is driven by purpose and duty as a Hero. However, Micheal is not some murderer on a kill spree like his fellow heroes. He tries to be rational and reasonable with the beasts. Not out of foolishness or naivety but because deep down he searches for the good in supernaturals; even beasts. He feels a comfortable almost nostalgic kinship with the supernatural entities and that they don't automatically deserve death for what they are. Which in truth is a small remnant of his old memory. Him remembering what it was like to be a Promethean who was hated by humans.<br /> <br /> He has stopped many beasts from their rampages of harm and shown them the error of their ways. He has only been forced to kill two beasts in his ten years as a hero. As a law enforcement officer even when beast hunting he knew his role and limits. He was a mediator and protector...not a executioner. To kill is a last resort when all other options become useless. He would be no better than the beasts that roam the night if he mindlessly killed.<br /> <br /> Micheal is currently a happy married man who has been married for nine years. His beautiful wife named Lindsy, age 37. They have two lovely daughters. Merrill age nine. Christie age six. Micheal's household has two pets. A golden retriever, age five, named Rocket. A calico cat, age two, named Patches.<br /> <br /> This household has two cars, A blue family van and a red volkswagen. He and his family live in a two story house, colored white. It has a white picket fence, green grass that has been mowed correctly, a grey mailbox at the curve with a green trashcan next to it. The neighborhood is middle class and located at a cul-de-sac.<br /> <br /> Micheal acknowledges the urge to go and fulfill the Hero's Quest everyday. Yet he restrains himself from acting upon it with narrow mindedness. He patrols during the days or nights he get as an officer in case of beasts. He has considered retirement from hunting monsters, yet he knows he cannot just quit and it would all be over. There are always going to beasts and there is always going to need to be a mediator and a protector. Even if that means he must be a mediator or even a protector to an innocent beast who may be falling prey to other supernaturals...or worse another hero who has the intent to kill.<br /> <br /> The first was a fledgling beast who had not only caused Micheal to become a hero but had also killed two people. Yet this beast wasn't some nobody, it was a close friend of Micheal's and a fellow police officer. After some time of trying to track this beast he found him in a back alley at night and was about to kill a third person. His friend panicked when confronted by Micheal who had pulled out his gun. Micheal tried to get his friend to surrender peacefully yet the beast gave chase that winded through several alleyways and eventually led Micheal into a construction site. His friend, not knowing his own strength, tried to slam Micheal yet had missed; Micheal was intentionally holding back as he tried to not kill his friend. The mighty slam had caused part of the concrete roof and a steel girder from an above floor to fall onto Micheal's friend. His friend was not dead yet could not escape as it bled out. Micheal tried and tried to help his friend by removing the debris and girder with all of his strength and ingenuity...yet to no avail. In the end his friend pleaded with Micheal to end its life and so he did by performing a mercy killing. Later on during the next morning, Micheal managed to get the body from the wreckage and helped give his friend a proper funeral. One he himself even attended.<br /> <br /> The second was a beast that had been on a kill spree and had reached a kill streak of twenty-two victims. Micheal spared the beast a certain death in its very own lair. He searched in his backpack for a pair of handcuffs when the beast tried to kill him as well when his guard was down. The beast got a good stab into his arm with a knife. He defended himself and although he tried talking to the beast again it was to no avail as the beast had entered a blind rage as far as Micheal could tell and it was far beyond reason. He pulled out his taser yet the beast knocked it out of his hands as skittered far across the floor. It eventually gave him no other choice than to slay the beast right then and there with his sidearm. After the fight he dragged the beast out of its lair and called for backup on his police radio. Later on he was celebrated in the news and by his peers for taking down the serial killer. Yet deep down, Micheal felt his victory was pyrrhic at best for in the end he secretly knows it was his fault as well for so many deaths for he was the one who sparred the beast in its own lair. It had happened early on after it had killed a single person. He still followed his code and cuffed it, drove it to jail, threw it in the slammer and did the paperwork. Yet the court could not prove with substantial enough evidence to convict the beast, so it was let off the hook free to go. This same beast became an elusive serial killer.&quot;</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T01:47:01-07:00","id":577145,"title":"","content":"Heroes have a gift that lets them cancel out lair traits now anyway though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T02:19:25-07:00","id":577169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577145#post577145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes have a gift that lets them cancel out lair traits now anyway though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they now? They must have added more gifts to the book.<br /> The version I am reading here: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7F...h3V19rSms/view</a><br /> Doesn't have any gifts that allow Heroes to bypass lair traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T02:32:13-07:00","id":577176,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's version 1. If you go to the kickstarter page there's a link to updated versions of the first 6 chapters, which makes some pretty hefty revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T03:02:52-07:00","id":577187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577176#post577176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's version 1. If you go to the kickstarter page there's a link to updated versions of the first 6 chapters, which makes some pretty hefty revisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the info. I will have to go and give it a good read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T03:35:44-07:00","id":577197,"title":"","content":"Will new revisions come now, after the Kickstarter? If there are 6 chapters now, it still like 3 short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T04:47:54-07:00","id":577234,"title":"","content":"Every revised chapter, appendix included, is in the folder now.<br /> <br /> Some bits might still see editing though. The introduction is likely to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-03-2015, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T04:58:30-07:00","id":577238,"title":"","content":"A couple of the earlier ones have changed about three times already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T05:37:48-07:00","id":577273,"title":"","content":"And just now my credit card was suspended of paying in other countries and on internet so there goes my pledge<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So much hate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:40:33-07:00","id":577303,"title":"","content":"I was checking out the updated Appendixes and found something interesting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slumbering Condition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She loses access to all her Atavisms, Nightmares, Beast-specific Merits, and<i><b> Birthrights</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed it before; what are Birthrights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:56:34-07:00","id":577312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577303#post577303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed it before; what are Birthrights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Special powers of each Family. See in detail write-ups of Families in 1st Chapter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T12:51:12-07:00","id":577634,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... I've been audiobooking a lot of Tanith Lee lately... would a character inspired by Azrahrn the Beautiful, Prince of Demons, Night's Master, Who Is Wickedness - be better represented as Raptor or Gorgon. Tyrant is a certainty, obviously.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Raptor for Azrahrn, and Gorgon for Chuz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:09:31-07:00","id":577823,"title":"","content":"There is a link for a pdf version on the kickstarter page? Cannot seem to find it.<br /> <br /> I wonder. Can a promethean who completes the pilgrimage to become human become a beast?<br /> EDIT: Also makes me wonder if an arisen who has went through apotheosis can become a beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","user":"Goblin Engineer","date":". 07-03-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:16:39-07:00","id":577831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577823#post577823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a link for a pdf version on the kickstarter page? Cannot seem to find it.<br /> <br /> I wonder. Can a promethean who completes the pilgrimage to become human become a beast?<br /> EDIT: Also makes me wonder if an arisen who has went through apotheosis can become a beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first: Unknown. The exact rules on who the Devouring will and won't work on are unknown in-setting. A preexisting connection to the Primordial Dream and a potential Horror must exist. Creating that potential for your human self might be the subject of an Athanor (though if you screw up, it could result in your human self becoming a Hero).<br /> <br /> The second: No. They're still Arisen Mummies - just ones unbound by the chains of the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:39:21-07:00","id":577881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577831#post577831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The first: Unknown. The exact rules on who the Devouring will and won't work on are unknown in-setting. A preexisting connection to the Primordial Dream and a potential Horror must exist. Creating that potential for your human self might be the subject of an Athanor (though if you screw up, it could result in your human self becoming a Hero).<br /> <br /> The second: No. They're still Arisen Mummies - just ones unbound by the chains of the Judges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, that figures for mummies.<br /> No surprise with prometheans becoming heroes.<br /> However I still ponder about promethean to human to beast.<br /> I am not 100% familiar with beasts but if I remember reading correctly they are born as a beast or just as a human.<br /> Which makes me wonder if the pilgrimage taken by prometheans to become as a human counts as being born as a human; to be eligible to become a beast.<br /> I assume athanors are maintained when going supernatural-mortal-supernatural as there is nothing I remember reading that states that becoming supernatural removes the athanor in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T16:42:31-07:00","id":577948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577881#post577881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume athanors are maintained when going supernatural-mortal-supernatural as there is nothing I remember reading that states that becoming supernatural removes the athanor in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is indeed the case, but PtC warns storytellers not to let Prometheans go template-hopping unless people know what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Although, I could see an Argentum Created developing an Athanor specifically centered around the supernatural (maybe one that grants a Mage-like universal Unseen Sense as the Redeemed Boon?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T16:55:26-07:00","id":577957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577881#post577881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not 100% familiar with beasts but if I remember reading correctly they are born as a beast or just as a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but a preexisting potential needs to exist in said humans that the Devouring works upon. It can't just be used on anyone at random. So cultivating that connection to the Primordial Dream is something I'm suggesting a Promethean can do with an Athanor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T18:12:08-07:00","id":578019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577948#post577948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that is indeed the case, but PtC warns storytellers not to let Prometheans go template-hopping unless people know what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Although, I could see an Argentum Created developing an Athanor specifically centered around the supernatural (maybe one that grants a Mage-like universal Unseen Sense as the Redeemed Boon?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable and it should always be run by the ST unless the ST is the also the template-hopper.<br /> <br /> Yes there is a athanor for that sort of universal Unseen Sense. It is from the fox athanor of the ulgan family for prometheans. Do not fret or worry though, you can still have a non-ulgan pick up a ulgan athanor as for them it just requires four azoth instead of three.<br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/ptc/RolePlayA.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/ptc/RolePlayA.html</a><br /> <br /> Plus if you are not happy with the pre-existing athanors, you just need five azoth to make your own athanor. Of course you must run it by your ST and work with your ST when developing it.<br /> <br /> Also just a happy coincidence in my eyes, but a Frakenstein with the Caladrius Athanor and is a Hero can take away all mundane illnesses even HIV and be immune to it as well. Yes I am reading the version posted by Psychic Monkey, still cannot find the final version and missed the train for kickstarter. Where it talked about how Heroes being immune to all mundane illnesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=577957#post577957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but a preexisting potential needs to exist in said humans that the Devouring works upon. It can't just be used on anyone at random. So cultivating that connection to the Primordial Dream is something I'm suggesting a Promethean can do with an Athanor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm I now see what your talking about glamourweaver, was not sure before. I can agree with this method by using the Athanor to allow a Promthean to become a Beast when Redeemed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T21:33:28-07:00","id":578138,"title":"","content":"I just had a thought about Heroes. Do you guys think that a heroes legend can be influenced/reflected by the kind of historical, fictional and mythological heroes they looked up to before they were activated? Obviously Thaddeus was big into stories about fantasy warriors and the stories he grew up with were a big influence on his hero behavior.<br /> <br /> Maybe that is another thing that seperates heroes like Thaddeus from the more self aware/less violent heroes that beasts usually don't encounter, the ones that don't hunt beasts were raised on stories of heroes that DIDN'T solve all their problems with violence.<br /> <br /> Which begs the question, what a about a person with a connection to the Primordial Dream whose role models growing up were &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FriendToAllLivingThings\" target=\"_blank\">friend to all living things</a>/ <a href=\"http://FluffyTamer\" target=\"_blank\">fluffy tamer</a>&quot; types? What kind of relationship with Beasts would would THAT result in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T21:47:47-07:00","id":578145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=578138#post578138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a thought about Heroes. Do you guys think that a heroes legend can be influenced/reflected by the kind of historical, fictional and mythological heroes they looked up to before they were activated? Obviously Thaddeus was big into stories about fantasy warriors and the stories he grew up with were a big influence on his hero behavior.<br /> <br /> Maybe that is another thing that seperates heroes like Thaddeus from the more self aware/less violent heroes that beasts usually don't encounter, the ones that don't hunt beasts were raised on stories of heroes that DIDN'T solve all their problems with violence.<br /> <br /> Which begs the question, what a about a person with a connection to the Primordial Dream whose role models growing up were &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FriendToAllLivingThings\" target=\"_blank\">friend to all living things</a>/ <a href=\"http://FluffyTamer\" target=\"_blank\">fluffy tamer</a>&quot; types? What kind of relationship with Beasts would would THAT result in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. Either...<br /> A) The two can understand each other and come to a peaceful resolution.<br /> B) Hero dies.<br /> <br /> With the framework you provided for that that type of hero, it really depends on the beast. How reasonable or dangerous is the beast in question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T21:57:21-07:00","id":578177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=578145#post578145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simple. Either...<br /> A) The two can understand each other and come to a peaceful resolution.<br /> B) Hero dies.<br /> <br /> With the framework you provided for that that type of hero, it really depends on the beast. How reasonable or dangerous is the beast in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying. I was thinking fluffy tamers could be a support splat to beasts, capable of buffing and otherwise helping beasts, but being effectively normal without a Beast to channal their powers through. They would also act a sort of a link to humanity that Beasts have, keeping them from going off the deep end while simultaneously to realize their full potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-04-2015, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:03:50-07:00","id":578275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=578177#post578177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you're saying. I was thinking fluffy tamers could be a support splat to beasts, capable of buffing and otherwise helping beasts, but being effectively normal without a Beast to channel their powers through. They would also act a sort of a link to humanity that Beasts have, keeping them from going off the deep end while simultaneously to realize their full potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again the only thing this hero got to worry about then is the beast itself and how deranged that beast is. The beasts that are more human would be skeptical but wouldn't &quot;shoot first ask later&quot; if your not doing anything aggressive like let yourself enter uninvited to a beast's lair. If the hero did that, they would most likely die as the beast is probably thinking the hero is there to kill it.<br /> <br /> If your ST is fine with that or your the storyteller, I don't see a problem with adding a splat like that. Its refreshing to see a spin like that in where its more a ray of hope and sunshine in a world of darkness. No pun intended.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:09:56-07:00","id":578355,"title":"","content":"Does it mention anywhere what a Beast gets when they devour the &quot;soul&quot; of a nascent beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T03:10:52-07:00","id":578487,"title":"","content":"I'm a tad concerned that we may be getting into the writers' heads, with all of our criticism. Personally, I love the tone of the first draft. But I'm making my way through the re-draft . . . and some of the rewrites seem like they're trying to soft-pedal some of the more dramatic &quot;cut scenes&quot;, and spend a lot of time trying to justify themselves. Too many cooks, and all that.<br /> <br /> For example, I think its entirely appropriate for Brent (in the feeding/trick-or-treat cut scene) to be a high school student . . .and <i>not </i>a frat boy. There are tons of horror and ghost stories focusing on kids . . . and stealing trick-or-treat candy is such a high school thing to do. Maybe its changed, but when I was a kid, it was always the high schoolers who got into that kind of trouble. Too old to trick-or-treat themselves, but not old enough to hit the bars with the college kids . . .<br /> <br /> As a frat boy, he'd have been out clubbing on Halloween, trying to hit on the girls in their skimpy costumes. And if he did steal some kid's candy . . . well, he'd be old enough to justify calling the cops. And in the suburbs (where this scene seems to be set), they'd definitely would call the cops.<br /> <br /> But as a high school/mid-older teen, he'd be likely to get away with it. Oh, sure, his mother might make him apologize . . . but he'd have already eaten the candy by then. And he might well track down the &quot;little brats who squealed&quot; on him, and beat them up. A little monstrous fear might well be the only justice possible. And he'd be young to still feel some of the fear of a childhood boogeyman like Mrs. Winter . . . but old enough to be really angry about it later.<br /> <br /> As for it being child abuse . . . someone has to punish kids. And enforce some degree of order (kids tend to be a little . . . Darwinian, otherwise). Is it child abuse to ground a kid, or spank him (remember, this is the World of Darkness we're talking about)? Plus, there's a huge difference between a six year old, and a sixteen year old.<br /> <br /> If the morality of the situation is bothering people, I'd rather see a follow-up scene, where Brent goes Hero, and breaks into her house to slay the monster. Decked out in football pads, carrying a tire iron . . .and his grandfather's old service revolver, loaded with the three bullets he brought from the war - just in case he ever &quot;ran across a monster like them Nazis&quot; again . . .<br /> <br /> And if that's still not enough, maybe a third excerpt - this time in the form of a news reporter. About how a local teen has just been arrested for beating old Mrs. Winters to death. And - after hearing disturbing stories from the other neighbors - the police are investigating whether Mrs. Winters may have been sexually abusing Brent and the other kids in the neighborhood. Which would make the whole thing a pyrrhic victory for both Hero and Beast - the Beast's lesson is lost, but so is the Hero's glory and reputation (not much panache in being a suspected abuse victim).<br /> <br /> But the main point is that I like the tone of the original draft. This is a game that <i>needs</i> to go dark. So, <i>Beast </i>writers, if you're reading this? Take all of our criticisms with a grain of salt, and try to build the world you originally wanted to. Being a little controversial is <i>not</i> a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Let me join the chorus, though, and say that I do like the outsider view sidebars. Great way to add some color. However, I'm also one of the guys who liked the old Soul/Homecoming idea, over this new Devouring/Horror stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 07-04-2015, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:47:59-07:00","id":578684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=578355#post578355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mention anywhere what a Beast gets when they devour the &quot;soul&quot; of a nascent beast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A new Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:43:14-07:00","id":579408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=578684#post578684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A new Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question was &quot;How does it benefit the one doing the Devouring?&quot;, not &quot;What happens to the one Devoured?&quot;. More of a &quot;What's in it for me?&quot; type of question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:51:29-07:00","id":579416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=579408#post579408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the question was &quot;How does it benefit the one doing the Devouring?&quot;, not &quot;What happens to the one Devoured?&quot;. More of a &quot;What's in it for me?&quot; type of question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I stand by my answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:07:10-07:00","id":579421,"title":"","content":"Well there is the Feeding thing that happens, but aside from that you get to mentor a new member of the family?<br /> I imagine it is sort of like a pack finding someone who about to/is/has just undergone the First Change; if you leave them to it they might muddle through, odds are it won't be pretty and it'll cause more problems. Or a vamp who didn't get the 411 from her sire going all about town without any regard for the (unknown to her) All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Take some of the Inheritance sample NPCs. Most of them seem to have no contact with other Begotten. The Mournng Owl fell to despair because she couldn't come to terms with herself on her own. The Greedy Squid did what came naturally but no one told him about Heroes, (so there is also a Hero in Wayne's area). Starless was all alone, or else her decision wouldn't have been made in haste.<br /> I admit, it could be that they were all just loners but...<br /> <br /> Since someone mentioned having the 'Self-Devoured' treated differently, I thought about why that would be. That was my answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:08:11-07:00","id":579423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=579408#post579408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the question was &quot;How does it benefit the one doing the Devouring?&quot;, not &quot;What happens to the one Devoured?&quot;. More of a &quot;What's in it for me?&quot; type of question.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Still dozy from [devouring their younger sibling's soul]&quot; would seem to indicate it's a fairly hefty Satiety boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:55:32-07:00","id":579490,"title":"","content":"I was contemplating a Sphinx based character. Is there an existing Nightmare that can work well for forcing people to answer riddles - or should I design a new one... likely based off Mage Kinship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:57:21-07:00","id":579492,"title":"","content":"You Must Obey is a good one, but I think a Mage Kinship Nightmare has more fun baked in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:18:39-07:00","id":579500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=579492#post579492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You Must Obey is a good one, but I think a Mage Kinship Nightmare has more fun baked in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking the Satiety expenditure version of You Are Not Alone could also work, as it forces blind monofocus on some distraction in front of the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T21:51:11-07:00","id":580538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=579490#post579490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was contemplating a Sphinx based character. Is there an existing Nightmare that can work well for forcing people to answer riddles - or should I design a new one... likely based off Mage Kinship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alien Allure, Looming Presence, or Siren's Treacherous Song is your setup power, but Everything You Do Is Worthless and We Know All of Your Secrets are the payoff.<br /> <br /> Sounds like an Eshmaki or Ugallu Tyrant to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:34:23-07:00","id":580935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=579490#post579490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was contemplating a Sphinx based character. Is there an existing Nightmare that can work well for forcing people to answer riddles - or should I design a new one... likely based off Mage Kinship?</div> </div> </div> </div> A bit of a side question but... what's the Hunger here? That might help with ideas. The traditional sphinx ate the people that failed her questions. That something you want to go with?<br /> <br /> I'd also say a riddle power is more of a changeling thing, I think. Or maybe Mastigos. I'm thinking about a mental-maze type thing here, along with a bit of a benefit if pass, and penalty if fail, which is like a pledge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2015, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:40:26-07:00","id":580980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=580935#post580935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A bit of a side question but... what's the Hunger here? That might help with ideas. The traditional sphinx ate the people that failed her questions. That something you want to go with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to make it power - but an alternate idea occurred to me, that I could make it Horde, in which case she actually WANTS ANSWERS, and uses the threat of death to compel them. She collects answers to esoteric engimas. The idea she killed herself over getting a correct answer is a LIE! A HERO BORN SLANDER!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:49:20-07:00","id":581390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=580980#post580980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to make it power - but an alternate idea occurred to me, that I could make it Horde, in which case she actually WANTS ANSWERS, and uses the threat of death to compel them. She collects answers to esoteric engimas. The idea she killed herself over getting a correct answer is a LIE! A HERO BORN SLANDER!</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even that she was returning to her lair to celebrate and the puzzled bystander just misunderstood. It's a neat idea though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:43:19-07:00","id":581837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=581390#post581390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or even that she was returning to her lair to celebrate and the puzzled bystander just misunderstood. It's a neat idea though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm imagining the walls of her Lair are carved with text...<br /> <br /> &quot;The Universe Trying to Understand Itself&quot;<br /> &quot;Man&quot;<br /> &quot;Everything That Is Not&quot;<br /> &quot;A Circle Has Neither Beginning Nor Ending&quot;<br /> &quot;Hope&quot;<br /> &quot;Zero&q