226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:49:47-07:00","id":587115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=587038#post587038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is that? The rules for the Horror's form in Chapter 4 (Dev Pass 2) say nothing of the sort...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chapter Four doesn't really mention the Horror much at all, though. Sure you're not thinking of Chapter Three?<br /> <br /> And we haven't changed anything since the end of the KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:27:09-07:00","id":587238,"title":"","content":"So does anyone else find it a bit... lets say non-intuitive... that a very strong but dim Beast can become a genius in their Horror form by virtue of their muscular strength in the physical world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:45:24-07:00","id":587284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=587238#post587238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does anyone else find it a bit... lets say non-intuitive... that a very strong but dim Beast can become a genius in their Horror form by virtue of their muscular strength in the physical world?</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome to ephemeral rules. They've always been counter-intuitive in my opinion. Someone dumb as a brick and socially inept but physically powerful would become both smart and charismatic upon turning into a ghost. <br /> <br /> Thankfully, the only time that they'll come up is in astral combat, I think, so it won't be too much of a problem - you're not exactly working out complex mathematics, exploring deep into other realms, or social engagements in your Lair, where you use those traits. So, its more that a mentally strong person uses it to compensate for a weak body. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T12:39:20-07:00","id":587343,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to play it is that they get an intelligence boost, but only in relation to things associated with their horror.<br /> <br /> Like, an ugallu will become a savant at working out trajectories for the purposes of dive-bombing, but still can't use a computer all that well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T12:55:14-07:00","id":587348,"title":"","content":"Which sounds hilarious to me. A beast with the same intelligence as a dog and just as savage and ill-mannered. Yet their horror is this learned, eloquent speaking and well-mannered oracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T13:00:17-07:00","id":587353,"title":"","content":"Humans do get this unwritten sapience bonus, so 1 dot for us and 1 dot for a dog don't mean the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:36:57-07:00","id":587466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=587238#post587238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does anyone else find it a bit... lets say non-intuitive... that a very strong but dim Beast can become a genius in their Horror form by virtue of their muscular strength in the physical world?</div> </div> </div> </div>More a case of a Powerful Horror being generally imposing, regardless of whether than power comes from knowledge, force of personality, or brute strength. His Horror doesn't so much know more as it can leverage that metaphysical power against a given problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:54:28-07:00","id":588185,"title":"","content":"Given all the talk about Hannibal-as-Beast-inspiration a while back, I really felt that this merited a share, though there are spoilers for those unfamiliar with the books, I suppose;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=loOgfXNs-VI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=loOgfXNs-VI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=loOgfXNs-VI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=loOgfXNs-VI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:36:09-07:00","id":588491,"title":"","content":"Excuse me, I'm trying to find where the dream walking rules are, if anywhere? I heard them being mentioned upthread, but I couldn't find any such actual rules in the document. Did I miss them, or are they not actually in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:53:35-07:00","id":589509,"title":"","content":"Read the next few chapters of the revision.<br /> <br /> So far, nothing that addresses my concerns, but I do like the new heroes.<br /> <br /> I seriously hope the last few chapters of the revision address my issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T07:45:02-07:00","id":590195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=587284#post587284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Welcome to ephemeral rules. They've always been counter-intuitive in my opinion. Someone dumb as a brick and socially inept but physically powerful would become both smart and charismatic upon turning into a ghost.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the only time that they'll come up is in astral combat, I think, so it won't be too much of a problem - you're not exactly working out complex mathematics, exploring deep into other realms, or social engagements in your Lair, where you use those traits. So, its more that a mentally strong person uses it to compensate for a weak body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I always thought that the notion of maths and logics were pretty useless to ephemeral beings like spirits, much like getting any sense of how much weight they could clean and jerk, or how good their con artistry was. Just conglomerating these things into a single stat, <i>Power</i>, does a pretty good job of reinforcing the completely alien nature of ephemeral beings to corporeal things.<br /> <br /> &lt;mini-rant&gt; Of course these rules also made making a nWoD version of Wraith &quot;impossible&quot; which resulted in the odd duck that is Geist. (Which itself is a silly name -- it's just German for &quot;Ghost&quot;, imo calling the game Revenant would have made more sense... sorry, bonus rant over.) The Strix do show us a potential alternative for &quot;ephemeral&quot; beings by which a new version of Wraith could be built but folks wouldn't be too satisfied by it because Geist already scavenged so many of its central themes, e.g., Ego/Id as Psyche/Geist, Underworld setting, among other things. &lt;/mini-rant&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T01:23:11-07:00","id":591018,"title":"","content":"Looking back over Dragonfire, I love how its use as a throwing attack means if you have a shield your ST could allow you to use the rules for catching projectiles to 'catch' the flame with your shield. Instant iconic awesome movie scene recreation, no house rules necessary. You can actually have the knight in shining armour block the Dragon's gout of flame with their shield as a basic feature of the power!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T07:42:52-08:00","id":1021564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=544120#post544120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am kind of surprised that no one has mentioned bloodborne what with all the monsters and beasts in that game. The enemies are literally<br /> called beasts<br /> <img src=\"https://psmedia.playstation.com/is/image/psmedia/bloodborne-bestiary-blood-starved-beast-two-column-01-ps4-us-20mar15?$TwoColumn_Image$\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mehhh, in Bloodborne, the beasts are created through drinking the blood of elder gods, rather than through some spiritual incarnation. Although, I do believe there would be home brewed ways to tweak this into the game somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:43:07-08:00","id":1021580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=1021564#post1021564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Mehhh, in Bloodborne, the beasts are created through drinking the blood of elder gods, rather than through some spiritual incarnation. Although, I do believe there would be home brewed ways to tweak this into the game somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps as denizens of the Primordial Dream? Or the offspring of such entities? Beasts (and most supernaturals, in their opinion) <i>do</i> descend from one, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:42:27-08:00","id":1021646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=1021580#post1021580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps as denizens of the Primordial Dream? Or the offspring of such entities? Beasts (and most supernaturals, in their opinion) <i>do</i> descend from one, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, vampires already reproduce through feeding blood to others. Maybe these guys have a similar ability; creating B